window.REFINED={"Genesis":{"1":{"1":[{"m":"From time immemorial man has been held spellbound by the question of the beginning. The beginning of man and the world.\n\nNow here in the word of God, we have the answer — what happened at the very beginning.\n\nIn the beginning God. So that answers the question men from all ages have asked. \"What happened at the very beginning, who was there at the very beginning?\"\n\nIn the beginning was God. I have heard the arguments being made that in the beginning was nothing and out of that nothing came something.\n\nBut now we are informed as to what was in the beginning. God was in the beginning.\n\nInterestingly, this verse was not addressing so much what was there in the beginning as much as what was happening in the beginning.\n\nIt is a sentence stating what was happening in the beginning and that is, in the beginning the heavens and the earth were created.\n\nWe are not only told that in the beginning heaven and earth were created but who did the creation, i.e. God. This therefore lets us in on the fact that there was a being doing the creation and by implication existed before the creation of the heaven and the earth.","dt":"2021-12-30T18:39:35","s":["826jrljkwc","44235db49e"]}],"2":[{"m":"And the earth became without form... Dake's commentary bible, which is what I use personally, explained that the word \"was\" actually means to become.\n\nI thus checked the strong 💪 definition of the word 'was' in Hebrew and here is what I got...\"to be, become, come to pass, exist, happen, fall out (Qal)-----to happen, fall out, occur, take place, come about, come to pass, to come about, come to pass, to come into being, become, to arise, appear, come to be, to become, to become like, to be instituted, be established, to be, to exist, be in existence, to abide, remain, continue (with word of place or time) to stand, lie, be in, be at, be situated (with word of locality) to accompany, be with...\"\n\nThat’s quite a tall order, but the point is this. \"The earth came to be without form.\" We see God create heaven and earth 🌎 and then the earth, part of his creation, becomes without form and void. What happened? What caused such waste and destruction..???\n\nSome theorize that that is the flood of Lucifer and the pre-adamite world 🗺. I have not personally done much research into that, so I will leave that hanging till I'm personally convinced about this, but it's worth mentioning.","dt":"2021-12-30T20:33:01","s":["8md6ehx8g1","988e80c89c","9858a8af5b"]}],"3":[{"m":"God called 🌩 light to be and it was so. Where did the light come from and how was it formed? We are not told in scripture but one thing we notice is that the light came after God spoke. To emphasise this, we are told \"God said... and there was light\", emphasizing that the observance of the light was after the speaking forth of it.\n\nThis is so important because all through the rest of the Bible we see this pattern set in stone: God executes his will through speaking forth of words.\n\nAmos 3:7-8 KJV Surely the Lord God will do nothing, but he revealeth his secret unto his servants the prophets. [8] The lion hath roared, who will not fear? the Lord God hath spoken, who can but prophesy?\n\nAnd this theme of God requiring his servants to prophesy, and speak forth recurs 🔁 severally in all of scripture.","dt":"2021-12-31T11:51:20","s":["06uj7pn3yj","13ba910f74","a8b8184d91"]}],"4":[{"m":"After the spirit hovers on the waters, God speaks forth light and then God goes to work to separate light from darkness. I'll see if this forms a pattern in the rest of the creation narrative or was only applied here. That is the pattern of speaking forth before actually going ahead to make what was spoken from word matter (non-existent matter or matter made from words).","dt":"2021-12-31T12:02:44","s":["1uim2fpwfr","5068a5dab5","d514274ebf"]},{"m":"Scientifically we know it's the Sun's ☀ shadow which is cast upon the earth 🌎.\n\nBut why is that so to start with? Why does the earth cast a shadow on its other half 🌗?\n\nThat is how God chose to divide light and darkness.\n\nThe laws of physics were created to be so.\n\nFor instance, we have gravity on the earth 🌎 but not in space.\n\nThis shows gravity is not the default. It's only part of, or natural to, earth 🌎 but not natural to heaven.\n\nThere is no gravity in space. So here on earth we should know that the things we have were not automatically meant to be.\n\nNo, it was deliberately created to be so.","dt":"2024-01-05T10:42:46","s":["xz5i1dxqkp"]}],"5":[{"m":"God again begins to name everything he created.","dt":"2021-12-31T17:17:57","s":["cade735c59"]}],"6":[{"m":"We see a repetition of the same format. That is God calls forth what he wants, then he goes ahead to work on it and makes it. He then gives the finished product a name.\n\nLet's call this the law of creative process.","dt":"2023-02-24T09:12:21","s":["e0036a97c2","599ee3aa32"]}],"9":[{"m":"Let's see if the law of creative process is followed here...\n\n1. God calls forth or commands what he wants to see\n\n2. The things appear and God goes ahead to work out and create what he spoke forth\n\n3. He names the final product","dt":"2021-12-31T17:32:41","s":["vrggxg7h35","85f24c5578"]}],"13":[{"m":"The evening and morning. Is it not interesting that evening is mentioned before morning and called day? This order is followed in the Jewish Sabbath where a day is from sunset in the evening to sunset the following evening.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:25:23","s":["w2m4t8npak","7744146f2e"]}],"28":[{"m":"Be Fruitful: be productive, create and produce something of worth out of the resources available to you. The principle/blessing is akin to a seed harnessing the resources of the soil and sunlight etc to grow to a giant tree and then to produce fruit. Something creative and beneficial as a result of harnessing resources available and one's own internal giftings and abilities.\n\nSo a mango seed produces a unique fruit different from an orange based on its natural inherent abilities.\n\nMultiply: it's akin to fruitfulness but in this case you duplicate yourself, the fruit has within it the seed: the multiplier. We as men are expected to multiply ourselves.\n\nReplenish: means to fill a vacant space - in other words GOD is telling man, don’t just multiply, but do so till you fill the entire container: the earth. Multiply without limit, restraint, complacency. Fill the entire container. The limit is till the earth is full.\n\nAnd Subdue it: so you are to fill the entire earth but not only that. Be the dominant force. This therefore suggests opposing forces to one's dominance. You see you can multiply and replenish and yet still be subdued. The fact that you’ve filled the earth and have multiplied greatly doesn’t mean you are the dominant force.\n\nFor instance in the slave trade and colonisation era, the masters who subdued these colonies were not necessarily the majority yet they subdued all else.\n\nSo man is to subdue.\n\nThe rest of the verses go on to some specifics of man's dominion. However it is interesting that man was not to have dominion over other men; over his offspring. At least that was not stated before the fall.","dt":"","s":["5956eaed8a"]},{"m":"In all of history we see only one man 👨 who was able to successfully accomplish this mandate... i.e. the man Jesus Christ... Absolute mastery over sea land and air.. He walked on water, stopped the tempestuous wind, healed the sick, repaired eyes.\n\nCast out demons and other trespassers and intruders in the earth realm.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:36:27","s":["j8p0lgdgx1","b284a5f2d3"]},{"m":"Why did man have to have rulership or dominion over these creatures?\n\nEspecially that in the beginning they were harmless.\n\nAlso that, as we can see 🌊, nature when left alone does well and thrives by itself.\n\nWhat exactly did God have in mind when he asked man to rule over all?\n\nOne such intent of God was for man to have oversight responsibility and to ensure that things function as God intended.\n\nAnd more specifically since there were the enemies of God in the earth 🌎, the dominion of man was very much needed in that light.\n\nSee, the devil 👿 was out there to destroy man and God's creation.\n\nMan's responsibility was to prevent that and ensure the systems functioned as God had intended.\n\nThis concept of an enemy being out there was not hidden from man 👨.\n\nAs seen in the very statement of man replenishing the earth 🌎, having dominion and keeping the garden.","dt":"2024-01-05T11:09:22","s":["qmzvxsal24"]}],"16":[{"m":"rulership is not dominance over others, it is you being your best self every day in constant growth and helping others be the same way.\n\nI got this statement above as I read this verse and started feeling sleepy then I heard it in my sleepiness\nremember there was already day and night before the sun and moon the two great lights were created, there was in fact evening and morning and the existence of lights before the two great lights were created.","dt":"2026-01-01T15:06:30","s":["is2xsovdjd"]}],"30":[{"m":"From the beginning we were all vegetarians.","dt":"2024-01-05T11:10:42","s":["7wvwnpsl2c"]}],"8":[{"m":"We see a repetition of the same format.\n\nGod calls forth what he wants, then he goes ahead to work on it and makes it...\n\nThen gives the finished product a name.\n\nLet's call this the law of creative process.","dt":"2021-12-31T17:29:08","s":["0dxbd1hxop"]}]},"2":{"4":[{"m":"Strange hmm 🤔. So what exactly happened in Chapter 1? What was all that activity about? Was it a mere charade? God calls forth creation, makes the sky earth 🌎 sea 🌊 etc and even blesses them. And now we look at the earth in chapter 2 and there is nothing visible, because the earth 🌎 was waiting for rain ☔, which understandably is what causes stuff to grow.\n\nFair enough but now we see that there was no man and that is the reason given for no visible growth of anything. What exactly was going on?\n\nThis brings us to a great principle. God is a God of order, wisdom and processes. Within a simple seed is a wonderful tree 🎄 which can nest birds, feed animals etc. All that activity is hidden in a simple seed. And it is the same thing we see here. Process and order, not just random creation and calling forth of things to be.\n\nMan, for whom all these were created, needed to be around before any of the things created matured to fullness. The caretaker of the earth needed to be present first.\n\nTwo reasons why the work which the lord had completed and rested from had not yet materialised:\n\n1. There was not yet rain which was to trigger growth: there was a set order and principle of growth and the rain would do that job.\n\n2. The man for whom all these things were created was not yet present to till the earth 🌎. So God formed a fully grown man 👨🏿 and planted him in the garden and caused the trees 🎄 to also grow abnormally and have fruits for the man. And from there left everything to its natural course.","dt":"2023-10-27T12:16:27","s":["d3b91d2a57"]}],"8":[{"m":"A perfect chicken 🐥 and egg 🥚 scenario. Which one did God create first? Here we see God created both.\n\nHe laid the foundation for the earth 🌎. That is, plants, animals and all productive living organisms and hid it in the seed awaiting rain ☔.\n\nThen he goes ahead and plants a complete fully grown garden and a fully formed man 👨 to tend the garden.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:47:11","s":["2hc7mbcv9b","0d8c95d42a"]}],"15":[{"m":"To dress? Well understood but to keep it? Keep it from who and what?\n\nFrom the onset of creation, there has been this subtle suggestion of an enemy. An enemy put in the earth who needed to be kept out. For instance in Genesis 1:28 man was commanded to subdue the earth. Why subdue if there is no rebellion or possibility of it?\n\n28 And God blessed them, and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:50:05","s":["m931ft50sk","2a110e2b62"]}],"17":[{"m":"The nature 🏞 of the tree could not be imparted by communicating it, though it was a tree of knowledge. Quite ironic right? How else was knowledge to be imparted? It was to be imparted by eating it. It was almost like a pen drive containing malware that is transmitted through the hardware.\n\nSee, God mentioned that the tree 🎄 held the knowledge of good and evil 😈 though evil was not in the lives of Adam and Eve. That means the desire for evil was not in them.\n\nGod could actually mention that there was good and evil and they still did not have knowledge of the distinction. They knew only good. They were good by nature 🏞.\n\nBut the tree would introduce a knowledge. The fruit 🥝 was actually one that imparted knowledge. Does that mean they did not know good either? I don't think so.\n\nThey knew good and because that was all they knew there was nothing to compare it to for them to even say that something was good and another evil.\n\nYou can only distinguish the two if you know both... For example, for most of us in Africa 🌍 who grew up in a poor community, we did not know we were poor. We just lived and knew things were hard but we were happy 😊.\n\nUntil we probably moved out of our community as we grew up and realized we were poor.\n\nThe tree 🎄 made knowledge of evil part of us. In our flesh and our souls, even our spirit. We were contaminated. This was why, the moment they ate the fruit, they saw they were naked. In the sense that they felt the shame of it.\n\nInterestingly, God's reaction to their hiding was a strange question 🙋...\nMove to the notes on chapter three, verses 10 and 11.","dt":"2022-01-03T11:15:07","s":["6lhwgfx0yt","3c9b16d389"]}],"18":[{"m":"What God saw that was good, indeed very good, was the created things and the creation of man and woman respectively.\n\nAnd now he sees the man alone and says \"not good\".\n\nHe then goes ahead to bring good to him. That is the various animal forms and shapes.\n\nHe gave names to them all and none was comparable to him.\n\nHe then puts man to sleep and forms another creature and brings her to him to which Adam himself confirmed that this was comparable to him for she was\n\n\"his bone and flesh\". He gives her the name woman 👩🏽.\n\nThis was indeed \"very good\".","dt":"2023-09-10T07:26:59","s":["egodgh0dx6","e9ab20f842"]}],"19":[{"m":"Adam was so highly intelligent and super smart.\n\nHis language was already fully formed.\n\nHe had such vastness of understanding that he could create and coin language.\n\nThus he named the animals. Creating new non-existent language as he named them.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:52:01","s":["n1sqem5vtm","477a1054e8"]}],"20":[{"m":"So there was found help for Adam but not comparable/meet for him. Note that animals were not eating each other and neither was man eating animals. So then the purpose of other creatures was for variety and as a support system for man. To help man 👨🏿.\n\nBut none was like him. So God went back to work, looking for help meet for him and when he finished 🏁 he brought this creature to Adam just as he had done with all the other creatures.\n\nAnd there Adam himself saw that this was bone 🍖 of his and flesh of his, unlike the others. And he gave her the name Woman 👩🏽.","dt":"2023-09-10T07:33:50","s":["hn5a9uju1e","aeb14ccd63"]}],"21":[{"m":"And hence the popular expression said of a man 👨 who finds a wife... You have found your missing rib.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:53:14","s":["f3a7f64d33"]}],"25":[{"m":"This point is worth noting because it ties in with the eating of the tree of good and evil 😈 in chapter three.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:54:21","s":["dd59nj2sef","27e99e1b9d"]}],"5":[{"m":"Two reasons why the work which the lord had completed and rested from had not yet materialized.\n\n1. There was not yet rain which was to trigger growth - there was a set order and principle of growth and the rain would do that job.\n\n2. The man for whom all these things were created was not yet present to till the earth 🌎.\n\nSo God formed a fully grown man 👨🏿 and planted him in the garden and caused the trees 🎄 to also grow abnormally and have fruits for the man and from there left everything to its natural course.","dt":"2023-09-10T07:05:00","s":["psb32m8nsl"]},{"m":"Strange hmm 🤔. So what exactly happened in chapter 1?\n\nWhat was all that activity about? Was it a mere charade?\n\nGod calls forth creation, makes the sky earth 🌎 sea 🌊 etc and even blesses them and we look at the earth and there is nothing.\n\nI.e. the earth 🌎 was waiting for rain ☔. Which understandably is what causes stuff to grow.\n\nTo make matters worse there was no man.\n\nWhat exactly was going on?\n\nThis brings us to a great principle. God is a God of order wisdom and processes.\n\nWithin a simple seed is a wonderful tree 🎄 which can nest birds feed animals etc etc. All that activity is hidden in a simple seed.\n\nAnd it is the same thing we see here.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:43:36","s":["ac9xso0f9d"]}],"24":[{"m":"Marriage was thus instituted the moment Adam named his wife after him.\n\nBone of my bone and flesh of my flesh.. She shall be called woman aka Mrs Adam in modern day.\n\nAnd God instituted the law regarding marriage.","dt":"2024-01-05T11:25:35","s":["6er8i1g8md"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"How did the serpent 🐍 enter the garden?","dt":"2022-01-03T11:45:58","s":["af28f356b5"]}],"6":[{"m":"This has been the problem of man 👨🏿 since. We want to do what we've been asked not to do without being caught even when we've been told what would happen after.","dt":"2023-08-06T03:39:34","s":["399307947e"]}],"7":[{"m":"There is a certain wisdom (lesson) that is learnt only after temptation.\n\nEither you succumb to it and learn wisdom the hard way by facing the consequences or you escape the consequences by not succumbing and behold with wisdom what could have happened to you if you had defied wisdom.\n\nThat is what happened to Adam and continues to happen to us his children.\n\nOf course, you can gain wisdom by observance, seeing what others are going through and avoiding them. Even though seeing what is happening to others does not mean you would heed.\n\nThat's how foolish and deceptive our hearts can be.","dt":"2023-09-15T08:08:22","s":["wcv2mderz5","0118eee316"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh, my lord and my God. Only God knows how that moment felt for them. These sudden berserk torrents of information and emotions.\n\nFor the first time, they felt fear 😱 and dread. They had broken the pot and it could not be repaired. They realized they had just attempted a failed coup. To usurp the powers of the God of the universe and failed.\n\nThey saw the deception of their ways and realized their own nakedness, and hid from the Lord.","dt":"2023-08-06T03:50:19","s":["7hww24akq6","ca9ddc9078"]}],"11":[{"m":"THIS QUESTION 🙋.. \"who told you that thou wast naked\" is THE KEY 🗝 TO UNDERSTANDING THE TREE 🎄. A strange question 🙋.","dt":"2022-01-01T17:56:11","s":["vpirslcthe","204dd52da6"]}],"12":[{"m":"Really. Of all the excuses that Adam could come up with he blamed his wife.\n\nTo stoop so low rather than man up... That should tell you how scared out of his pants 👖 Adam was.\n\nHe was dead scared and was willing to clutch at anything to gain pardon.","dt":"2022-01-03T09:28:51","s":["g0vpkgn6fq","001faf29ad"]}],"21":[{"m":"Such a loving God","dt":"2022-01-03T11:51:12","s":["371b5e782a"]}],"23":[{"m":"Man had rebelled and committed high treason; he could no longer enjoy the privileges of the father. He was living in a garden already planted 🌿 by God. A garden he did not in any way contribute to yet enjoyed the fruits 🥝 thereof and only needed to tend and keep it.\n\nNow he was driven out to go start his own. He wanted to be God. That was the allure of the temptation and now he was left on his own, to be his own god and see what life without the one true God was like.","dt":"2022-01-02T17:48:54","s":["99syfzc3e4","54936525c5"]}],"24":[{"m":"How far did God drive them out? Also, the cherubims kept specifically the way to the Tree of Life at the east of the garden.... Could not someone go through the west and enter?\n\n3rd January 2022 UPDATE: This sounds like a bit of an overkill. Cherubims and a flashing sword just to keep Adam and his wife out..??\n\n 😳 Yes. It showed and emphasized their complete rejection. They were now outcasts 🏰.\n\nWe've had the experience of visiting someone and suddenly wild dogs 🐶 bark at us from nowhere and you might even have a gun 🔫 pointing at you from the owners.\n\n What did you do wrong?... You needn't have done anything wrong. You just do not belong there. However, see the sudden change in reception when they realise you are a friend to the family... 👪 Suddenly the dogs are put to rest, and guns disappear because you are family 👪.\n\nSame thing with Adam. He was now an outcast and a potentially dangerous enemy. What would have been the consequences of Adam eating the fruit 🥝 and living forever in the sin nature 🏞?\n\nMost likely — or should I rather say most definitely — unhindered wickedness. See how much wickedness man exhibits in a lifetime.\n\nNow imagine the wickedness man 👨 would exhibit if he lived forever. This will bear more thinking...","dt":"2022-01-02T18:03:02","s":["dbitz746on","9c9891f7e3"]},{"m":"Despite the complete and outright rejection of man, God was not going to let the devil 👿 win.\n\nHe was going to show the devil an aspect of God he, Satan, could not comprehend.\n\nHe was coming back for man in love 😍. Unrestrained love.\n\nAnd he, God, was going to win.","dt":"2022-01-03T12:13:48","s":["rvah871s0q","n77l8rvq6c"]}],"22":[{"m":"So it was true, man would be as God knowing good and evil 😈 but not as God ruling his own affairs and the universe 🌌 without consequences.\n\nMan was frail and the decision to have knowledge was going to come at a terrible cost.\n\nAnd man was without excuse. God told man the cost of knowledge i.e. death ☠.\n\nBut man chose to believe another than God.\n\nIt was such a big risk.\n\nA bad choice man made and he reaped the consequences even to date.","dt":"2024-01-05T11:38:51","s":["zhqvs0bkft"]},{"m":"Taking of the tree of life 🎄 to live forever would be another terrible blow to the universe 🌌.\n\nMan would have literally become like Satan - living forever in wickedness and evil 😈.","dt":"2024-01-05T11:44:14","s":["yh5wzl0ctt"]}],"15":[{"m":"It is not only snakes 🐍 whose head we bruise.\n\nLiterally every animal harmful to us, we would bruise its head.\n\nSo what makes this case of the snake 🐍 unique?\n\nExcept that it did not make reference to just the natural enmity between man and snake but the seed of the woman, Jesus Christ and Satan.","dt":"2024-01-05T11:31:09","s":["5yx5bh6c0v"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"The same creative element of naming is unveiled here, she calls her son Cain... A name with specific meaning.","dt":"2022-01-02T18:04:39","s":["jjq6l1tdom","5aca96359e"]}],"3":[{"m":"Where is this coming from? Why does God need an offering? When did God instruct them to start giving an offering? Cain's offering was rejected. Why? Cain brought based on the work he did as did Abel.","dt":"2022-01-03T09:45:41","s":["a1oe4ayfsg","f12a424fc6"]}],"4":[{"m":"How did Cain and Abel know to sacrifice? Who initiated it for them to know to follow? In subsequent chapters we see the descendants of Adam showing skill in many crafts including tent-making, metal crafts etc. Who taught them all these?\n\nProbably Adam or they just had the sense to. Considering the fact that Adam was born with super intelligence and lost his place of dominion when he sinned. From these facts, man was not born as a cave man and started to evolve into a more intelligent life form.\n\nMan was created fully intelligent and knowing many things let’s say instinctively.","dt":"","s":["56a3a910f5"]},{"m":"Wait oo... GOD HAD respect as in how? What did God do to show respect?\n\nThis is the book of beginnings. So we see a lot of first mention of things.\n\nHow did God show he preferred Abel's offering to Cain's? We are not told. Why did God prefer Abel's over Cain's? We are not told.","dt":"2022-01-03T10:15:43","s":["7fjglwp9tp","3f6dfd84fd"]}],"5":[{"m":"Why was Cain angry 😡 especially considering that he knew what was right? Was he angry at God or his brother or both? He was not just angry... He was very angry. Probably he felt, after all the hard work from the cursed 🤬 ground which would only yield after much sweat and toil, his work was all to no avail.\n\nAlso, he had lost the fruits 🥝 for no reason.","dt":"2023-10-27T12:18:15","s":["cc8e249e54"]}],"8":[{"m":"Why didn’t God protect Abel from Cain?","dt":"2022-01-03T11:52:55","s":["0xb5vec08v","8mi3amke4a"]}],"14":[{"m":"note 1\n\nHe was in the earth 🌎, walked in it yet was driven away from it. How was that possible 🙆? In a sense to walk and plant 🌿 yet the earth would not yield anything to you. Then Cain indeed was an outcast.\n\nnote 2\n\nHe was walking in the earth yet had been driven from the face of the earth. In the sense that the earth 🌎 no longer responded to and supported him. He was like an outcast so even when he sows, it will yield nothing.\n\nThat's strange, so how was he to eat?","dt":"2022-01-03T11:56:46","d":[["Oct 2023","note 1\n\nHe was in the earth 🌎, walked in it yet was driven away from it. How was that possible 🙆.In a sense to walk and plant 🌿 yet the earth would not yield anything to you. Then Cain indeed was an outcast.\n\nnote 2\n\nHe was walking in the earth yet had been driven from the face of the earth. In the sense that the earth 🌎 no Longer responded to and supported him. He was like an outcast so even when he sows it will yield nothing.\n\nThat strange, so how was he to eat?"]],"s":["4fbwb0m0kp","0d3317s780"]},{"m":"Cain immediately knew the implication of God's curse upon him.\n\nHe knew that the pronouncements of God against him were invariably the death sentence.\n\nBecause to lose favour from the face of God and to be rejected from the earth yet have to live the rest of your life on the earth 🌎.\n\nHe was done for.\n\nIt's like when you are given a prison sentence. You immediately know the implications of that for your family 👪, children, your life and career.\n\nIt's so many things in one.\n\nLord give us the wisdom and discernment to hear and understand your voice.","dt":"2024-01-05T16:41:37","s":["ebxhz8jnps"]}],"15":[{"m":"I don't get the conversation going on here.. Why would anyone finding Cain kill him?\n\nWas such wickedness already on the earth 🌎? It seems that Cain and Co were receiving some solace, protection and favour by being close to God and seeking his face through offerings etc.\n\nElse why would he complain of losing out by the lord's face being hid from him?\n\nAlso it seems by this time men had really multiplied... For one to chance on Cain out there.\n\nOr could it mean the sons of the angels were already here?","dt":"2022-01-03T12:06:47","s":["dgroom8j5x","8e5352ef9b"]},{"m":"So what if Cain hadn't appealed his sentence?\n\nThe kind of father son relationship and dialogue that these ancient ones had with God.\n\nHow come we do differently and approach God, even as new testament saints, with such ungodly fear 😱.\n\nMeanwhile we can dialogue and reason with him.","dt":"2024-01-05T16:44:26","s":["pt8pz0buv1"]}],"16":[{"m":"Ei... How and when?\n\nWhere was the presence of the lord?? 😳 It seems that although they had been driven out of the garden they had some form of communication going on between them and God. And that constant fellowship in his presence brought them protection from the world out there. Cain went east of Eden.. So where was he prior?\n\nWere they hanging around the garden with the hope of getting back? Because so far it looks like the family 👪 of Adam was together. Adam, Eve and Cain and Abel.","dt":"2022-01-03T12:09:53","s":["uw3fypg9p4","tike8sgbxz","13f3364780"]}],"7":[{"m":"From this statement it seems Cain knew what he was supposed to have done but just refused to do it.\n\nIt desired to have Cain. Sin's desire was to have Cain. Control 🎮 him to do as it pleases.\n\nNow that makes me wonder, what is sin? Is it a spirit or is it a property, like a programming which is part of the human being? Like the way wrong software (viruses) can be introduced to a computer 🖥 system.\n\nIt hacks the program and causes the hardware as well as software to malfunction.\n\nSin is everything evil, man was created to love, have joy happiness, help each other grow their family 👪 etc.\n\nThat is man's programming. It's inherent. Then comes sin introduced into man's programming. So now we do good and do evil.","dt":"2022-01-03T10:23:15","s":["72tefzo7hd"]},{"m":"Why was Cain angry 😡 especially considering that he knew what was right? Was he angry at God or his brother or both?\n\nHe was not just angry... He was very angry.\n\nProbably he felt after all the hard work from the cursed 🤬 ground which will only yield after much sacrifice, his work was all to no avail.\n\nAnd he had also lost the fruits 🥝 for no reason.","dt":"2022-01-03T10:31:15","s":["qa1kjtmbn7"]}],"9":[{"m":"GOD was still in active conversation with them.\n\nWhy does God not do anything to interrupt the world 🗺 and this gruesome murder of an innocent man 👨?\n\nSame thing when Adam was eating the fruit. 🍏 It was like God didn't care.","dt":"2022-01-03T11:32:37","s":["pi857yohbp"]}],"10":[{"m":"Despite God's warning Cain let sin in and killed his brother.\n\nGod told Cain what was about to happen to him. That sin was lying at the door 🚪.\n\nDOOR?? 😳 What door, Adam and his generation seem very advanced and rightly so considering that they lived in paradise in the garden of Eden.\n\nI wouldn't be surprised if ADAM lived in a mansion in the garden. He knew much from his interactions with God.\n\nBack to the door, God paints 🎨 the picture 🖼 of sin being separate from the man 👨.\n\nSo Cain is wroth over nothing and sin comes to lie at the door 🚪. And it eventually was let in.\n\nWas this not what God wanted to avoid that was why man was not to eat of the fruit?\n\nSo also Cain was wroth for no reason at all, well for a completely wrong reason. Yet he felt justified.\n\nSIN brings along with it a lot of negative emotional surges and to deal with that emotion we go ahead and act the way we feel so we can feel better and get rid of the negative feelings.\n\nThe door also shows us that in man is a door 🚪 a door to the soul I believe which before the fall was shut to sin but after the fall could be opened 🔓 and closed 🔐 by sin.","dt":"2022-01-03T10:53:02","s":["dc6kbfkbol"]}],"23":[{"m":"Was the curse only in Cain or his generations?\n\nGod being just I believe the curse 🤬 stayed with Cain only.","dt":"2024-01-05T16:46:57","s":["l4kzqwmkiw"]}],"21":[{"m":"Uuuu","dt":"2022-01-03T11:59:16","s":["wyzo69wai8"]}]},"5":{"6":[{"m":"Here again we see the genealogy given to the youngest not the oldest.\n\nLand was so free at these very early stages.","dt":"2022-01-03T12:18:25","s":["cus7dhywnj","af8fbe43aa"]}],"13":[{"m":"Can we say based on the example of the genealogy counting from Seth instead of Cain that the names given here are not necessarily first born but rather those through whom the messiah was traced???","dt":"2022-01-03T12:21:10","s":["7e33qquym3","45ff2bed7f"]}],"29":[{"m":"Prior to the curse 🤬, earth was supposed to be like Eden.\n\nParadise and full of good food 🍲 fruits and vegetables. Anything grew when planted.\n\nIndeed, things grew before man even planted till the ground was cursed.","dt":"2024-01-06T08:41:34","s":["r567yg6laf"]}],"24":[{"m":"That early in the history of man 👨 men already had such intimate relationship with God that God took them away.\n\nThey were fulfilling the mandate of Adam in the earth 🌎 to the full 🌕.\n\nAnd we can see that they were unfriendlies in the earth ie sons of God who needed to be kept at bay hence the dominion mandate but man failed.","dt":"2024-01-06T08:38:06","s":["8eopqeiz46"]}]},"6":{"15":[{"m":"Why did God give these specific dimensions? Why not smaller? Well let's see verses 17-19.","dt":"","s":["2aaf98a89f"]}],"2":[{"m":"This was not meant to be so.\n\nMan was to have the dominion but was now fallen, dead and apart from God.\n\nWithout constant unhindered flow of fellowship with God, man was vulnerable, weak willed and minded.\n\nNow the enemies of God and man took advantage to wreak havoc.\n\nAnd man could do little. We were a disjointed breed and ununited.\n\nWe were to be one but we were not all of one mind. Some were murderers and covetous.\n\nWe formed much smaller communities because you knew not whom to trust.\n\nThus we became easy prey for the devil 👿.","dt":"2024-01-06T08:46:43","s":["3ca6dhc0md"]}],"3":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 this scripture...\n\nDid the 120 refer to the new age of man ie that man will no longer be living that long on the earth 🌎 or as some suggest was in reference to the number of years left for God to cut off mankind through the flood.","dt":"2022-01-04T07:01:57","s":["4ofjwdwjxd"]}],"20":[{"m":"Shall come unto thee... So there was some supernatural element that brought these animals to Noah and to the ark.","dt":"2024-01-06T09:24:54","s":["d116yhtakr"]}],"1":[{"m":"We are not told when this began... Maybe right after the first women were born??","dt":"2022-01-03T12:24:20","s":["ea9si5kk90"]}]},"7":{"17":[{"m":"It was at this point that it dawned on me that the specific dimensions of the ark were so it could stand the storm that was to come. I believe there were boats and ships at the time, so guess what, when the flood rose I guess some tried to escape on canoes but the nature of the storm was such that only a ship of the calibre of Noah’s ark could survive the storm and since there was only one of such a kind, it was only NOAH and his family that survived.\n\nO the manifold wisdom of God.","dt":"","s":["a8c02a7fac"]}],"15":[{"m":"It seems to connote that the beast followed or at least cooperated with Noah of their own accord in a divine way.","dt":"2026-01-03T11:54:50","s":["pjg9z73855"]}],"9":[{"m":"These beasts were first created for man and now as last man was about to enter the ark, they follow him.\n\nThe earth indeed was made for man 👨.","dt":"2024-01-06T09:26:41","s":["1mlwoq6vyg"]}]},"8":{"2":[{"m":"The flood was not just caused by the rain ☔ but also water gushed up from the earth and seas to flood the main land. A tsunami of a sort.\n\nI wonder, really, how was Noah able to get all of each species in pairs? Could all of the various species of animals in the entire world fill one ark… How did he get every species represented?","dt":"2022-01-03T20:18:32","s":["2ab6ddc898","68nbntft0h"]}],"21":[{"m":"Does that mean the curse was lifted from the earth or did it mean it was not going to be made worse?","dt":"2024-01-06T09:41:44","s":["za92h0ywv1"]}],"22":[{"m":"Does this mean during the period of the floods these natural events were abated? Yes.\n\nBecause the floods itself was for 40 days + the 150 days it took to subside, making 190 days which is about 6 months ie half the year. 🙏\n\nSo for half of the year the regular patterns were held in check and now God promises... That never again.","dt":"2022-01-03T20:27:26","s":["qiokx12q36"]}]},"10":{"1":[{"m":"Shem was the line through whom the messiah was reckoned...\n\nThough not emphatically stated, I wonder who the eldest was.","dt":"2022-01-04T07:29:59","s":["hb2krqxf9a","7f6f1975c6"]}],"5":[{"m":"The people described as gentiles by Israel are actually of the same father with Israel. When you trace the genealogy, they all have the same father, Noah.","dt":"","s":["e19e011576"]},{"m":"The isles of the Gentiles, as at this point in history there was no Israel 🇮🇱 for there to be Gentiles.\n\nThey being called gentiles at that stage indicates the position of the author and the narrative as at when this was being written.","dt":"2022-01-04T07:47:17","s":["ub4mkdweoz","9d52cadc4a"]}],"21":[{"m":"The children of Eber (meaning from the other side) are the Hebrews. They came from the other side of the Euphrates according to Dake's commentary.","dt":"2022-01-04T08:56:26","s":["k55ypw4xem","5be25ec1d9"]}],"32":[{"m":"So from the beginning we were all one people.","dt":"2022-01-04T09:01:44","s":["2c4c1326a6"]}]},"11":{"2":[{"m":"Journeyed from which east, was it in rebellion to God, moving away from the garden of Eden around which the world before hung on in hope of returning to God?\n\nNow the lord had said to Abraham...., when did the lord say unto him? Let me check other versions.. I'll be back.\n\nI'm back and several versions maintained the \"had said\" and some just used \"said\".\n\nEither way we are not told when God said to him.\n\nHowever we see earlier that Abraham's father had set off to go to the land of Canaan. Some say he had the calling first but did not fulfill it hence it was transferred to Abraham. It's an inference from","dt":"2022-01-04T09:02:57","s":["f1ht9sco1b","157abea193"]},{"m":"What happened to Eden after the flood or during the flood?\n\nA thought just came to mind, if Eden was on earth 🌎 and the tree of knowledge of good and evil 😈 and the tree 🎄 of life were natural trees.\n\nThen the nutrients of the tree of life are natural in origin.\n\nThen given the right information one can constitute the nutrients of the tree to give one eternal life.\n\nBut alas, what nutrient it is in the tree of life remains a mystery or maybe that nutrient of the tree of life can only be found in that tree and in none else.\n\nOr its constituents could be in other trees in different measures. But who can know these things?\n\nAnyway this is just conjecture...\n\nBack to the garden, so was the garden destroyed in the flood and the angels thus relieved 😌 of their duty of preventing man from accessing the tree 🎄?\n\nOr God hid and protected it from the flood?\n\nWho knows these things?\n\nWhat do you think 🤔 I hear the spirit asking me?\n\nI think 🤔 God preserved the garden from the flood.\n\nA flood of several months can kill animals, but what about seeds 🌱, leaves and bark of trees?\n\nThe tree of life, if I'm right, has its leaves for the healing of the nations.\n\nI'm sure its bark could also do something. I don't think God would risk flooding the garden and the seeds and parts of this tree scattered in the earth 🌎 and found by man accidentally.\n\nAnd now suddenly we have men that do not die?\n\nAnd now I can imagine the carnage and destruction left behind after the flood waters receded.\n\nA sad case for man.\n\nYet another thought, I think 🤔 the animals followed Adam out of the garden 🌿, how else was Abel a shepherd?\n\nUnless we mean to say God created again animals for man - which, seeing that God had finished the work of creation, would mean creating again when there were living animals in the garden.\n\nAs these thoughts come to me I'm beginning to understand why many of the books of the Bible move from one subject matter to the next in a single flow of thought or paragraph without separation into books 📚.\n\nIndeed early writing had no paragraphs. It was just one continuous writing and it required the wisdom of man to separate them into the different topics and thoughts.","dt":"2024-01-06T10:11:44","s":["azv5y6kmzb"]}],"6":[{"m":"So the concept of multiple languages did exist but the lord did not use it till this moment.\n\nI am sure that concept did not even exist in the minds of the people because no such thing existed.\n\nbut it did in the mind of God and he used it when he had to.\n\nOnly God knows what other tools there are in the mind of God that man knows nothing about nor can even fathom it until God introduces it to the scene.","dt":"2026-01-03T16:45:19","s":["y876gfletf"]}],"28":[{"m":"This may explain the soft spot Abraham had for his nephew Lot.\n\nHis father Haran died leaving them to take care of his son Lot.","dt":"2024-01-06T10:16:41","s":["96vt7cmd7s"]}],"31":[{"m":"Did Terah leave Nahor behind?","dt":"2024-01-06T10:17:58","s":["eordwkbdhp"]}]},"12":{"5":[{"m":"And into the land of Canaan they came indeed.\n\nIt was as if to say that Terah had set off to go into the land of Canaan and they ended up settling in Haran but in Abraham's case he completed the journey.","dt":"2022-01-20T08:07:09","s":["37zzxjpaz1","7d7541baa1"]},{"m":"Abraham separating himself to go to Canaan was no new thought.\n\nThat was his father Terah's goal the whole time but it seems Terah could not accomplish that.\n\nMaybe the sheer numbers of his family 👪 with other accompanying responsibilities prevented him from moving the entire tribe to a distant unknown land.\n\nMaybe just maybe in the course of Terah's journey with his family to go to Canaan, they found a comfortable place with good land and settled.\n\nHowever Abraham heeded this difficult call and gathered his family and left.\n\nGod had a plan for Abraham's lineage in Canaan and needed them to be willing to cross over from their comfort zone to Canaan, the land of promise.\n\nAnd of course today we see and know how that grand plan unfolded.","dt":"2024-01-06T10:24:11","s":["d3sy2c7kzb"]}],"7":[{"m":"Having completed his obedience, God now appears to him to give further specifics.\n\nOur walk with God is a journey.\n\nAs we complete one quest of obedience, he comes with the next update. In between times he nudges, watches, observes, repeats the instruction as need be till we complete the command and then fresh orders and updates come. Till then we would go in circles on the same track 🏁","dt":"2022-01-20T08:11:06","s":["49v07uhvs8","7d4312c245"]}],"16":[{"m":"This looks like fresh assets that had been acquired whiles in Egypt.","dt":"2022-01-23T06:48:51","s":["795ls8d5qd","0b852dec1f"]}],"1":[{"m":"Now the lord had said to Abraham… when did the lord say unto him? Let me check other versions.. I'll be back\n\nI'm back, and several versions maintain the \"had said\" and some just used \"said\".\n\nEither ways we are not told when God said to him.\n\nHowever, we see earlier that Abraham's father had set off to go to the land of Canaan.\n\nSome say he had the calling first but did not fulfil it, hence it was transferred to Abraham.\n\nIt's an inference from Genesis 11:31 KJV\nAnd Terah took Abram his son, and Lot the son of Haran his son's son, and Sarai his daughter in law, his son Abram's wife; and they went forth with them from Ur of the Chaldees, to go into the land of Canaan; and they came unto Haran, and dwelt there.","dt":"2022-01-20T07:44:01","s":["tc5bf4qxhh"]}],"8":[{"m":"Here again he called upon the name of the Lord.","dt":"2022-01-23T06:47:40","s":["2k5slaifs4"]}],"19":[{"m":"This event so simply written in a few verses must have taken days of squabble …maybe Abraham was summoned to a judgment sitting or a hearing of some sorts, before eventually being sent away.","dt":"2026-01-16T06:31:21","s":["n5c5ttmfit"]}],"15":[{"m":"Maybe it was common in those days to have women keep their youth and beauty way into their old age.. Sarah was in her mid sixties at least.","dt":"2024-01-06T10:27:10","s":["ygjw380idv"]}],"20":[{"m":"Egypt 🇪🇬 and Pharaoh, they were to play a pivotal role again in the lives of Abraham's descendants centuries later.","dt":"2024-01-06T10:28:31","s":["f87gkdo047"]}]},"13":{"2":[{"m":"Abraham was very rich, scripture says, but it doesn’t leave it blank but goes ahead and states the areas of Abraham's riches: cattle, gold and silver.","dt":"2023-10-01T00:00:00","d":[["Oct 2023","Note 1\n\nFrom Egypt, this was the testimony - a man 👨 rich in cattle and silver and God.He sojourned in Egypt, likely left his massive wealth behind and yet came out a very rich man 👨.\n\nYes I perceive, that is what happened 😊...Because same thing happened in Isaac's Era and out of it came so much riches\n\nNote 2\n\nProbably Abraham sold some or all of his men-servants and asses he got in Egypt to lighten his journey back to Egypt"]],"s":["70cfac0226"]},{"m":"From Egypt, this was the testimony — a man 👨 rich in cattle and silver and God.\n\nHe sojourned in Egypt, likely left his massive wealth behind and yet came out a very rich man 👨.\n\nYes I perceive, that is what happened 😊...\n\nBecause the same thing happened in Isaac's era and out of it came so much riches.","dt":"2022-01-20T16:35:31","s":["dfe93cqyvp"]},{"m":"Probably Abraham sold some or all of his menservants and asses he got in Egypt to lighten his journey back from Egypt.","dt":"2022-01-23T06:51:59","s":["iteacbvs9x"]}],"4":[{"m":"In calling on the name of the Lord, what did Abraham say and with what name did he call on him 🤙?\n\nWhat were his prayer topics? For such a very rich man 👨, what were his thoughts, requests?\n\nMaybe, yes obviously he prayed concerning a seed for himself. And other generational prayers.\n\nHe, Abraham, had a need, he was broken in somewhere and it was out of that need God was to set an example of faith and faithfulness.","dt":"2022-01-20T16:29:39","s":["wutavio71y","608fb0108f"]},{"m":"After having gone through what he had gone through in Egypt, he had to go back to base.\n\nTo where the place of covenant was, trusting God for alignment and guidance.","dt":"2024-01-16T06:23:28","s":["mkiqmvtgpj"]}],"6":[{"m":"In coming they were already rich from Haran but their property was such that they could not live together.\n\nBut for their property to be so great that they could not dwell together in such a vast land. Then they indeed had gained massive wealth.\n\nThey had to go days' journey away from each other. To completely different cities to survive.","dt":"2022-01-23T06:57:51","s":["3z2809nby2","cfb12bb403"]}],"17":[{"m":"What was the significance of this gesture? Was it to survey the land?\n\nIf you look at it even today, when you receive an inheritance, you survey it and check it out.\n\nIt was more like God was saying feel free and walk through the land. It is truly yours.\n\nOkay I get it now.. On 2nd reading, God states why he should walk 🚶 through the land.\n\nBecause he, God, will give it to him. Literally, God was saying it's yours, feel free and walk through it.\n\nThis indeed is faith. A land filled with owners and giants and Abraham walks through it knowing it is his.\n\nWhat a mindset shift this is. He did business 🕴️ with them, traded together and prospered above them all, yet they did not know who he was but he knew.\n\nHe knew he was the actual 📰 landowner. He and God knew. Oh the beauty of spiritual authority and revelation. This in a sense reminds me of modern Israel.","dt":"2022-01-24T08:49:24","s":["ga8exs6px7","aab1c35eb8"]}],"18":[{"m":"Abraham removing his tent was a faith and obedience response to God's command. Anytime God spoke, Abraham acted immediately.","dt":"2022-01-23T07:08:11","s":["701ef767a7"]},{"m":"I can imagine Abram, as leader of his large tribe.\n\nHis people knew that their master was very rich and not through natural means.\n\n\"Our master consults\".\n\nAnd so they are there one day and their master comes and says, 'we are moving tents'. \"What is the reason?\" they may wonder.\n\nThen someone whispers, \"He went to consult his God again yesterday and that is the new direction\".\n\nHis people do not understand him but follow anyway because someway somehow his decisions in time past worked and brought great results and protection.\n\nEspecially after he goes to consult.","dt":"2024-01-16T06:40:23","s":["smo2jnv47d"]},{"m":"If indeed Abraham did all these things which he did at the word of the lord, then he is more of a priest than a nomad or a business man. I mean a man who abandons everything and carries only his family to an unknown land because his God said to do so.\n\nAnd now he moves his tent because his God had told him to move through the land because it has been given to his descendants so Abraham does so.\n\nHis every move is at the whims of his God, the God of heaven. I now understand and see Abraham in a different light, he was not just a nomad or a tent dweller or business man.\n\nThat is just the aesthetics. His very life was dependent on instructions from his God.\n\nIncluding even his own children from his loins and what names to give them and who to sack from his presence i.e. Ishmael and who to keep i.e. Isaac.\n\nThe God of Abraham had an agenda and he needed a willing vessel, a willing man to carry out that agenda. There are not that many willing vessels so when the gods find one they protect him and bless him greatly so his loyalty is greatly sustained because it comes with great rewards.","dt":"2026-01-18T09:41:52","s":["7pn7uwwqyc"]}],"9":[{"m":"That Abraham was the one who took the initiative to bring peace shows the spirit and nature of Abraham.","dt":"2024-01-16T06:25:45","s":["zjyppmjlza"]}],"11":[{"m":"Ei, this guy, he chose all the plain. All the good land, what was in his heart was not good.\n\nA very shrewd businessman and did not care that it was Abraham who brought him and took care of him.\n\nLot was fortunate not to have an uncle like Laban who dealt very shrewdly with Jacob.\n\nBut Abraham was not so, and that was why Lot took advantage of his uncle's kindness to loot the good land.","dt":"2024-01-16T06:31:56","s":["mg1q38b53o"]}],"14":[{"m":"The difference between a man lifting up his eyes in the flesh and greed and choosing the best of the land and a man lifting up his eyes in response to a divine call.","dt":"2026-01-16T06:34:32","s":["xl0s8y1tr2"]}],"16":[{"m":"Abraham whom the lord chose was a very good bargain and choice.\n\nGod works with different people, some disappoint him and others do just OK whiles some do phenomenally well.\n\nAbraham was one such great example. In fact he is the father of us all.","dt":"2024-01-16T06:35:31","s":["vw5f8so5qo"]}]},"14":{"12":[{"m":"In one swoop he lost everything. That was the nature 🏞 of wars.\n\nA time of massive wealth 🧐 transfer. Lot, thinking he was wise, was now proven foolish.","dt":"2022-01-24T09:14:02","s":["sggmnfjtnk","ff7a6b227a"]}],"13":[{"m":"Alliances, always important in such dangerous times of attacks and raids. Abraham had his own small personal army.","dt":"2022-01-24T09:15:14","s":["8605a6a8de"]}],"14":[{"m":"Abraham was very generous in helping his nephew Lot. 🧘‍♂️ That may well mean there was no animosity for Lot when he left or Abraham being his uncle was just forgiving and generous.","dt":"2022-01-24T09:20:37","s":["s02trcrnre","d3f16ce1e6"]}],"15":[{"m":"I don't get this. How can 300 trained soldiers rout 4 kings?\n\nEither the soldiers were about three thousand, which is entirely possible 🙆, though that does still not change 💱 the odds of defeat much.\n\nIt could well be the 300 were highly trained and skilled, like the US marines ⛵. Or 🥇 most likely Jehovah helped them mightily.","dt":"2022-01-24T09:17:51","s":["geapczhzy3","c93706885d"]}],"20":[{"m":"Was it tithes of all his wealth or of what he had gotten through this conquest?","dt":"2022-01-24T09:27:09","s":["41de2fd1a2"]},{"m":"Abraham gave tithes of all that he had, I believe this was in reference to all that he had gained from the battle not of all that he had gained his entire lifetime.\n\nI may be wrong but that is the understanding the text gives.","dt":"2024-01-16T08:07:57","s":["0m0f657pw6"]}],"21":[{"m":"Genesis 14:20\n\nLooking at the context, here it means that Abraham paid tithes of the bounty. Obviously, he was returning from battle.\n\nI wonder, did ABRAHAM pay tithes again after this, and also did he pay tithes of all his other properties and to whom?","dt":"2022-01-24T09:33:51","s":["lln4peq0cn","b641ac12e7"]}],"22":[{"m":"What is the covenant name of God doing here?\n\nI thought by his name \"I AM\" he was not known to them.\n\nThat goes to further illustrate the author was one who knew the 'I am'.","dt":"2022-01-24T09:37:02","s":["w0wrn54r4q","d549b381c9"]}],"24":[{"m":"Okay so the others took their portion. It was Abraham's personal decision to not take anything from the king 👑 of Sodom. He detested thinking that the depraved king of a depraved city 🏙 would brag that he made Abram rich.","dt":"2022-01-24T09:39:33","s":["b0zgn4j05u","03d74ae182"]},{"m":"Okay so what was their portion, was it ten percent or some agreed portion in ancient times for loot after a war is won?","dt":"2026-01-16T06:43:25","s":["yona0zk11w"]}],"17":[{"m":"This goes to show that though Abraham did not call himself king, he was one and strong enough to overpower 4 kings.\n\nAgain this goes to show the heritage of the Israelites.\n\nThey go to battle with Jehovah Sabaoth who is able to bring victory with many or few men.\n\nAbraham was not up to four nations but he defeated them in war through tact, strategy and the help of the spirit.","dt":"2024-01-16T06:48:09","s":["q835199n05"]}]},"15":{"2":[{"m":"Childlessness is very painful. This was to be the number one test for the father of faith. Not anything else, think 🤔 of it.\n\nIn order to qualify for the father of faith, the test was Childlessness. Inability to fulfil the dominion mandate of fruitfulness 🥝.\n\nNote 2\n\nLord what wilt thou give me... Nothing was to be compared to a child. Abraham would rather lose everything and have a child and start building his wealth afresh than to die without one and to leave his inheritance for his servant.\n\nIt is a very painful thing to die childless. Lord help 😣","dt":"2022-01-24T11:52:13","d":[["Oct 2023","Childlessness is very painful. This was to be the number one test for the father of faith. Not anything else, think 🤔 of it.\n\nIn order to qualify for the father of faith, the test was Childlessness. Inability to fulfil the dominion mandate of fruitfulness 🥝\n\nNote 2\n\nLord what will thou give me... Nothing was to be compared to a child. Abraham would rather lose everything and have a child and start building his wealth afresh than to die without one and to leave his inheritance for his servant.\n\nIt is a very painful thing to die childless. Lord help 😣"]],"s":["egee54iew5","qkp7ip8u1r"]}],"6":[{"m":"AMEN","dt":"2022-01-24T12:06:47","s":["21de7ca66a"]}],"11":[{"m":"Another typical example of not making assumptions when it comes to spiritual things.\n\nHe could have assumed that since God gave him the order, he could just lay the birds 🐦 and animals out in the open and God would himself protect them.\n\nThat would have been a wrong assumption and we often get hurt as believers because of the many wrong assumptions we make.","dt":"2022-01-24T12:08:56","s":["kapssx81sa","8b268ea990"]}],"18":[{"m":"\"Have I given this land\" not \"will I give\". He had handed it over officially, all other occupants were just waiting for their lease to run out.","dt":"2022-01-25T07:57:35","s":["a0w9ea1vry","81951e5cf0"]}],"4":[{"m":"In reading these passages you might think the events are chapters apart but really they are decades apart.\n\nThe promise was given when he was 75 years and fulfilled 25 years later.","dt":"2024-01-16T08:10:00","s":["3kqmid4t0i"]},{"m":"In which form did the word of the lord come? Was it that he saw a form, or he just heard words coming from no one?","dt":"2026-01-16T06:46:35","s":["yrajzmxx0l"]}],"8":[{"m":"This is an interesting question 🙋, God Almighty says he will cause Abram and his descendants to inherit the land and Abraham asks for proof?\n\n\nAnd God did not reject his question but went ahead to offer elaborate proof by way of a covenant.\n\nSo we can seek the lord and ask for proof, especially in our world 🗺 today where the miracles, power and holiness of the early disciples seem to be absent.\n\nWe walk in literally no power compared to the miracles of Jesus.\n\n\nMeanwhile, the same spirit lives in us.\n\nLord help us.","dt":"2024-01-17T08:41:41","s":["oiulhvin1u"]}],"13":[{"m":"And God did not mention the name of the nation though he knew. Why not?\n\nI guess lest they avoid that nation altogether.\n\nAgain this begs the question: why did Abraham not ask?\n\nAnd I realise that that was the case for a lot of God's visions or talks with Abraham. There were always gaps.\n\nGaps God deliberately leaves for his providence's sake.\n\nSo for instance he tells Abraham Eliezer shall not be his heir but one born out of his loins.\n\nYet he could have added, yours and Sarah's but he kept quiet till the irreversible was done.\n\nAgain I believe before Abraham went in to Hagar, he enquired of the lord and did not get a response.\n\nThe dealings of God with man always have gaps, gaps to strengthen our faith and to learn to obey his word.\n\nOh this God","dt":"2024-01-16T08:20:53","s":["3puf4plssq"]}]},"16":{"2":[{"m":"Well the lord had spoken to Abram and said his seed, so well Sarah's logic kind of holds true.\n\nInterestingly though this was a wrong move, God did not interfere.\n\nHe could have, to save Abraham all that headache subsequently.","dt":"2022-01-25T08:54:38","s":["6vd6psv0pl","356fb5e484"]}],"3":[{"m":"In choosing a surrogate for her husband, she obviously chose the loyal and humble one.\n\nHowever as life sometimes turns out to be, she failed her and turned proud.\n\nWisdom for us.","dt":"2022-01-25T08:56:38","s":["7o3izn0i0v","27dc997fb5"]}],"4":[{"m":"☺ 😇... Women women, human beings... We are just interesting.\n\nDidn't Hagar despise Sarah because she felt used? That she had to go through the pains 🥖 of pregnancy 🤰 only for Sarah to lay claim over the child 🧒. She suddenly became aware that her son was heir to one of the greatest if not the greatest man 👨 in the land.\n\nShe would be a fool to just let her baby be given to this old 🧓 barren woman. Well just thinking aloud for Hagar.","dt":"2022-01-25T08:58:10","d":[["Oct 2023","☺ 😇... Women women, human beings... We are just interesting.\n\nDidn't Hagar despise Sarah because she felt used? That she has to go through the pains 🥖 of pregnancy 🤰 only for Sarah to lay claim over the child 🧒.She suddenly became aware that her son was heir to one of the greatest If not the greatest man 👨 in the land.\n\nShe would be a fool to just let her baby be given to this old 🧓 barren woman. Well just thinking aloud for Hagar"]],"s":["x0j64b9xnv"]},{"m":"What caused such a reaction we are not told. We can only conjecture.\n\nMaybe she realized her mistress was using her, causing her to go through the pain of child birth, breastfeeding 🤱 her own child only for the madam to lay claim to her child as her own.\n\nShe had agreed to this earlier but she did not really understand the sacrifice she had to make having never taken seed before.\n\nNow she has a change of mind and will not let this old 🧓 lady steal her son from her.\n\nAnd now who knows she might become the next madam.\n\nGenesis 16:4 NKJV\nSo he went in to Hagar, and she conceived. And when she saw that she had conceived, her mistress became despised in her eyes.","dt":"2022-01-25T11:22:46","s":["ow0ut552k2","ds2qbk0ata","io3gipc4bi"]}],"5":[{"m":"Very typical blame game... She was to blame, not Abram.\n\nGenesis 16:5 NKJV\nThen Sarai said to Abram, “My wrong be upon you! I gave my maid into your embrace; and when she saw that she had conceived, I became despised in her eyes. The Lord judge between you and me.”","dt":"2024-01-17T08:48:09","s":["nx230ybreb","uscyu0abv3"]}],"6":[{"m":"Maybe it was also her revenge on Sarah by fleeing, she had a child and not by any mean man but by the great Abraham himself.\n\nHowever, at this stage Sarah didn’t care, she had seen her mistake and wanted to get rid of Hagar.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:13:38","s":["rukul4xl3k"]}],"8":[{"m":"Why would the angel address her in this manner - Hagar, Sarah’s maid?\n\nWas it in a sense divine judgement as if to say, we recognize Sarah’s rights over you because you are her maid and ought to submit yourself to her.\n\nShe opened this door for you, so don’t shut it.\n\n\nThis makes me wonder, was it pride or what - that would make a pregnant woman leave her cover to the unknown deserts when all she needed to have done was submit albeit painfully.\n\nAt least for the safety of her child.\n\nBut who knows such things - when we feel ill treated and unloved, we throw all caution to the wind.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:11:32","s":["xom86as97l"]}],"11":[{"m":"The lord the righteous judge not only sided with Sarah because indeed Hagar was in the wrong for spiting her madam.\n\nBut also blessed Hagar because she was afflicted for obeying and choosing to help her madam.\n\nHer intentions in agreeing to Sarah’s proposition initially was not to be spiteful, but as the situation may have it, that is how things turned out.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:16:31","s":["48eocc9by4"]}],"15":[{"m":"Ishmael, the lord will hear. It seemed Abraham had concluded that this was the answer that God had in mind to his prayer.\n\nThough he helped God and under such circumstances one can argue that it wasn’t exactly a miracle.\n\nBut righteous Abraham still recognized the hand of God in the matter.\n\nAfter all GOD had shown him enough for him to believe in his radical power to answer prayers.\n\n\nNot forgetting Hagar’s divine encounter with the angel of the lord.\n\nSo God himself recognized the child and blessed him and spoke of his future.\n\nHowever God wasn’t buying Abraham’s generous offer of Ishmael as a promised heir.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:22:05","s":["wlxwri9r13"]}],"7":[{"m":"Denoting the angel 😇 was searching.\n\nThey could have simply said an angel visited her, but they go to lengths to describe where and how.","dt":"2024-01-17T08:49:42","s":["i5tnyex5yw"]}]},"17":{"1":[{"m":"I am Elshadai, walk before me and be blameless. I am the almighty God. This I believe is the first time God is introducing Abram to His covenant name of Elshadai.\n\nCould God appearing here refer to an open vision? What form did God take? It was no longer the word of the lord coming to Abraham, or Abraham hearing the word of the lord as we see previously, but it was now the lord appearing.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["q8o0obgv9b","dmc3ochdtu","e0481fd85f"]},{"m":"14 years after Ishmael, God comes again.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:23:49","s":["qd80hzbjfj"]},{"m":"Why this introduction and talk of perfection?\n\nI think because he knew what news he was about to break to Abraham- \n\nThat Ishmael though blessed of God and spoken about was not the promised heir.\n\nGod really stretched Abraham- he had to cause the old man to believe again and again and then finally took Isaac from him- a dead man is what Abraham became at the end of the day so when God saw that Abraham had given all to him,\n\nhim he caused to become alive not just in his generation but even forever alive.\n\nWe talk of him even today-\n\nI see the same thing was done to Jacob.. God made him think he had lost Joseph and Benjamin- the two things he had left to hold unto in this life.\n\n\nRachel his beloved was truly dead but the boys were the only ones left whom he thought were dead till they were restored to him.\n\nAfter which now God appears to Jacob and shows him the future - re-affirming his promises once more.\n\nIt seems God is in the business of getting us killed, dying to self and our desires, hopes and the things we hold dear so he can mould us to his form and shape.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:33:37","s":["pxuzawnwb5"]}],"4":[{"m":"I like that, God sounds so much like a man. He says “As for me”. Hmm","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["bjkl1zq2i6","8affe85c56"]}],"6":[{"m":"I'm sure at this stage promises like these of exceeding fruitfulness were beginning to sound like stories of Ananse (a folklore here in Ghana). He had only one child and was ninety-nine years of age for crying out loud. Why was God keeping up this game?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["ml3c3ohqz1","252209bba6"]}],"7":[{"m":"All these plenty promises and Abraham was not even seeing a hint of evidence.\n\nHe indeed was underperforming in this regard because he had only one son.\n\nWhere were the descendants going to come from?","dt":"2026-01-19T07:35:32","s":["yebsoi7jx6"]},{"m":"Looking at how God deals with us, I don’t think I want to predict God and how his plans for my life will pan out.\n\nHe is too unpredictable and his ways pass finding out. I think I will just trust him.\n\nI have tried to understand him and where he was taking my life to. It didn’t make sense, I just got depressed.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:36:37","s":["06ovdelwc6"]}],"11":[{"m":"Can we then say that by extension of this covenant, everyone on his household partook of this covenant by circumcision?\n\nThis kind of lines up with Paul's argument that we are partakers of Israel through faith and not just the natural seed 🌱 of Abraham.","dt":"2024-01-17T08:54:00","s":["efv81vt6ye"]},{"m":"This story of Abraham is the story of a priest, the story of a prophet, the story of a man whom the Gods talk to and instruct.\n\nThat is the story of Abraham… God’s dealings with him are not different from his dealings with, say, the prophet Jeremiah….\n\nThis was the prophet and father of us all, i.e. Father Abraham.. A man whom God appeared to and spoke with.\n\nHe was indeed a prophet, priest and king 👑.","dt":"2024-10-16T16:30:38","s":["20tks20ndo"]}],"14":[{"m":"Can we then say that by extension of this covenant, everyone on his household partook of this covenant by circumcision?\n\nThis kind of lines up with Paul's argument that we are partakers of Israel through faith and not just the natural seed 🌱 of Abraham.","dt":"2024-01-17T08:54:00","s":["vdgtrzf4ux"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why did God wait all this while before telling Abraham this?\n\nThen this old desperate-to-please-God couple would not have involved Hagar to start with.\n\nRather God waits and then comes to tell Abraham that Hagar's son is not the one, because I omitted this detail: the promise is through you and Sarah,\n\nNot just through your seed.","dt":"2024-01-17T09:01:45","s":["s5svnqlz7b"]}],"16":[{"m":"God did not even speak of Sarah's behavior towards Hagar after what she did.\n\nGod at this time was not interested in this domestic issue.\n\nHe had his own plans for human kind.\n\nGod interrupts it seems to champion his one cause. Any other thing he leaves to man to figure it out.\n\nThat's why he made us any ways.","dt":"2024-01-17T09:03:19","s":["905oov24no"]}],"17":[{"m":"It was at this point that God dropped the bombshell and Abraham got it.\n\n\nAll this while he was not talking of Ishmael but Isaac, a new child of Abraham from Sarah.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:42:06","s":["4zf2wz9voz"]}],"20":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔.. It's almost as if God blessed Ishmael for Abraham's sake since Ishmael was not part of God's plan.\n\nBut it so happens that Ishmael sneaked into the plan and being from Abraham's loins he had to be blessed.\n\nBut then again we see the angel of God earlier asking Hagar to come back to Sarah because the blessing was upon Abraham and nothing out of his loins can be cursed 🤬 even if it came by mistake.","dt":"2024-01-17T09:06:28","s":["75oqejx2y6"]}],"22":[{"m":"And he left talking... God had appeared to Abraham I believe in human form. As is repeated later under the Mamre tree. Likely this was in a quiet 🤫 location when God appeared to him.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["ar0h6qgymk","137ad7c4ed"]},{"m":"It's almost like Abraham had had enough. God himself saw that Abraham had come to his wits' end with this promise of God that never seems to happen.\n\nThis time though God had given Abraham a date.\n\nNow God left off talking to Abraham. It's like Abraham was not saying anything again or asking any questions 🙋 so God left off talking to him.","dt":"2024-01-17T20:13:39","s":["nkqc08ylvi"]}],"23":[{"m":"The promptness with which Abram obeyed God is worth emulating.\n\n\nThe heathen and pagans so fear their gods and obey them.\n\nYet we the sons of the kingdom 👑 are not apt in obeying the voice of the lord.\n\nThis is wisdom 🤔 for me.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["kso3gzuodo","5aace6c17e"]},{"m":"Abraham really had control over his households.\nGod speaks in the morning and by evening his will has been executed.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:48:02","s":["5ibxfyq3t0"]}],"24":[{"m":"What kind of a leader was Abraham? For him to have, in the selfsame day he was instructed of God, done the circumcision of his entire household. Slave and free alike.\nI make some assumptions:\nHis household was up to date with his GOD and very likely worshipped Jehovah.\nHis leadership skills and influence over his house was such that he could steer his household in line with the vision and was such a communicator that his followers caught hold of the vision and ran with it.\nI know he was a skilful visionary because in his house he had highly trained servants who could take on kings in battle and come out victorious.\nHe was a nomad who didn’t leave things to chance.\nHe was a peacemaker, and abundance conscious so he could easily part ways with his own nephew giving to him the best of lands. He was both a man of practical wisdom and of faith:\nwhen it came to the things that God had said to him, he believed it and lived in faith with God whilst living a daily practical life and preparing for the challenges of his day. I guess it's this practicality that led to the birth of Ishmael - a mistake though - and to him suggesting God bless Ishmael instead.","dt":null,"s":["4139730c78"]}],"26":[{"m":"Power, wealth and authority don’t come cheap- Abraham circumcised himself the same day and his households.\n\nNo wonder God so mightily blessed him.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:49:20","s":["oxmfu4x8ln"]}],"27":[{"m":"Abram always swift in obeying God.\n\nWas it not the same state the men of, is it Nineveh, found themselves in that they got killed by Jacob's sons?\n\nAbraham could have been attacked at this time easily but the lord's protection was upon them... These are my thoughts, the text does not suggest that in any way.","dt":"2024-01-17T09:09:50","s":["5it24c9k8d"]}],"2":[{"m":"I guess at this age and time ⌚, Abraham was getting tired 😴 of this routine of promises. No wonder he laughed later on in this discourse.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["8p63kym7vx","380254d702"]}],"19":[{"m":"Interesting one there, so the name Isaac came from after Abraham laughed. 😇\n\nI USED TO think it was Sarah's laughter a year later that prompted the name Isaac, rather it was Abraham's... Hmm 😂\n\nInteresting one there","dt":"2024-02-13T06:54:54","s":["it6gdpul4c"]}]},"18":{"1":[{"m":"And the lord appeared — same as chapter 17 verse 1: “And when Abram was ninety years old and nine, the LORD appeared to Abram, and said unto him, I am the Almighty God; walk before me, and be thou perfect…” 👌\n\nHowever, here we see that God's appearing was in physical form. I believe the previous appearances were also physical except otherwise stated by the text.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["645al72wxq","c386dc7146"]},{"m":"This visit was of a short interval from the first, which wasn’t the norm - likely a few months apart.\n\nBecause in a year’s time Abraham was 100 years - and the previous encounter was when Abraham was 99 years.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:50:57","s":["h6glcyxibi"]}],"2":[{"m":"How did he know who they were? Could it be the suddenness of their appearing?\n\nOr could it be that he recognized one of them from previous God encounters? One of which was not too long ago. Barely a year actually because by 100 years of age, Isaac was born and at 99 God had appeared to Abraham so this 2nd appearing was between 99 years and the 9 months preceding Isaac's birth.\n\nEven within the sudden appearance of these men there might have been a semblance to how God had been appearing to him in time past. This MOG ABRAHAM knew God and could therefore tell this was God.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["adb542a147"]},{"m":"In verse one we are told God appeared to Abraham, however the beauty of this passage of scripture is that it explains how God appeared unto him in details.\n\nMost times we are told God appeared to Abraham or someone or say the ‘word of the lord came to or appeared’ to someone.\n\nAnd left blank without going into the intricate details but here we have the intricate details.","dt":"2024-01-17T20:16:12","s":["ch88t09i3h"]},{"m":"What made him know they were divine?\n\nI suspect because of their sudden appearance out of nowhere by him.\n\nThey just appeared out of nowhere.","dt":"2024-01-17T20:17:36","s":["huab5gszsw"]}],"10":[{"m":"He had told Abraham this earlier and privately now he was telling them both in public.\n\nMaybe Abraham did not even tell Sarah what God had said the last time.\n\nThey had had enough. No wonder Sarah laughed 😂.","dt":"2024-01-17T20:21:11","s":["emmvkczot1"]}],"12":[{"m":"“Shall I have pleasure” is what she was thinking of, the process was laughable to her more than the end result.\n\nShe couldn’t imagine herself having sex again.","dt":"2026-01-19T07:53:07","s":["2cc973n7no"]}],"17":[{"m":"Ah but God is God, of course he is under no compulsion to tell Abraham anything. Abraham is but a man.\nThat’s true, but you see, God is logical, humane, emotional and he is like us. There’s a reason in verse 18.","dt":null,"s":["23579c876c"]}],"18":[{"m":"God having made man custodian of the earth and renewed it in Abraham with plenty promises, how could he pass by Abraham’s house, eat, chat and yet keep mute over a matter concerning Abraham’s vicinity?\nThat is not just unfair but disrespectful and breaking of all sane protocol.","dt":null,"s":["d2f3482adb"]}],"21":[{"m":"The Jacob and Esau prophecy at birth is just like the “Gods Are Not to Blame” story.\nWas it because God said what he said that caused Jacob the younger to inherit the promise or was it going to happen anyways?","dt":null,"s":["ff5478e64f"]},{"m":"Interesting read, God says, “I will go down and see” and in the next verse we see rather the two angels going down towards Sodom, and the Lord staying to converse with Abraham. After which scripture tells us the lord went his way. Meanwhile, down in Sodom, Lot welcomes two angels.\nSo God has a kind of oneness with the two angels such that them carrying out his commands was him carrying it out - POWER OF ATTORNEY. And we see many such examples of these in scripture and in visions of the prophets etc. Maybe the other two angels were really God.\nThis brings another question to mind. Why was God walking with two others? Why not come alone?\nI can almost imagine God say, guys let’s go visit Abraham today.\nGenesis 19 talks of the angels of God rescuing Lot from Sodom. This story presents many interesting facts.\nThat Lot was willing to hand over his virgin daughter for the men to rape showed the sacrifice orientals made or were ready to make for their guests.\nIt also shows the degree of control that fathers had over their daughters.\nIn verse 11 it says…","dt":null,"s":["cf8e1568ef"]},{"m":"God said he would go down to Sodom and then his two companions immediately turn and head for Sodom and Gomorrah.\n\nCould the two be the other persons of the trinity?\n\nLater Lot calls them angels 😇 but maybe they were or not.\n\nBoth can be right because we have seen angels referred to as God or the trinity.. For instance the angel 😇 of the lord’s presence is the holy spirit.\n\nIn this case we see God say I will go and then he himself does not go but the others do.\n\nSome food 🍲 for thought 💭.","dt":"2024-01-17T21:02:07","s":["du5qqajcxp"]}],"33":[{"m":"Throughout scripture we see statements like the word of the lord came to someone saying.. but we are not told how… whether it is just a voice they hear or some whirlwind or apparition.\n\nThe descriptions are not given and that may be because they see nothing.\n\nBecause when men see visions of the most high we are clearly told.\n\nHowever, here a vivid description is given because God came in person and bodily, meaning all previous times were as stated: just the word of the lord came, they heard but saw not.\n\n\nLooking at how Abraham negotiated down to 10, it was a very rare privilege for man to relate with God where one could ask literally anything and get immediate answers…seeing God’s mouth and facial expressions as he talked and could hear his voice and tone.\n\nSuch a blessing, it literally lifts you to the realm of the God kind.\n\nNo wonder God rarely appears that way.\n\nNow I wonder did he ever appear that way to any other - directly as the lord… I know Joshua beheld him as the angel of the lord’s army but not as the lord.\n\nI think Moses also did as testified by the lord himself.","dt":"2026-01-19T08:01:35","s":["ryko4c4qi4"]}],"8":[{"m":"God did eat.","dt":"2024-01-17T20:20:00","s":["e4hcfv3geu"]}],"13":[{"m":"God is very mild and gentle in his dealings with man, see how he answered fearful Sarah, he simply said, “Nay but thou didst laugh”\nLike an extremely generous Lord with his favourite servant, no need to fear.\nSee also Abraham’s reasoning with God over Sodom.","dt":null,"s":["66332eff50"]}],"14":[{"m":"Dakes says, the purpose of this earthly visit of God was to see if Sodom was as wicked as God’s scouts had reported to Him. On the way … they visited their friend Abraham.\nSuch imagery. What a thought. See, God had been skyping and video chatting Abraham for decades, through dreams and visions and apparitions.\nAnd now that he was driving through town he came to his friend, yes his friend.","dt":null,"s":["e3c410a6cc"]}],"15":[{"m":"Oh my lord and my God. So loving and understanding, almost human.","dt":"2024-01-17T20:23:08","s":["vetg3wpz13"]}],"23":[{"m":"Of course God was wiser than Abraham and knew not to destroy the righteous with the wicked, yet he expects us to be able to reason with him. That’s how come he created us with his breath in us to function like him. So he appreciated the conversation.\nIn same manner we are each created with different ways of reasoning, we thus should be able to freely reason our thoughts without fear that some other person would differ in opinion. That’s how it’s meant to be because we are all different. There is no conventional way of thinking so long as it can be defended with reason.\nSo God would say, come let us reason together.","dt":null,"s":["21dff40152"]}],"32":[{"m":"Why did Abraham start with fifty, guess he wanted to start with a large respectable number?","dt":"2024-01-17T21:04:52","s":["szgfmtsd7q"]}]},"19":{"3":[{"m":"Is there any uniqueness to the bread being unleavened?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["cfwpz37pfc"]},{"m":"Usually angels are quick to appear and equally quick to disappear.\n\nLess so to think of coming to dwell comfortably in one's home 🏡?\n\nAlso angels do not mingle with men, they come to deliver their message to whoever and just go.\n\nBut these angels were so different, so not angel like.\n\nOne they come suddenly which is usual,\n\nThen they come in and wait publicly in full glare of Abraham, Sarah and their help who prepared the meal. At least these three are mentioned in Abraham's case.\n\nNext they go to gates of an entire city and move in all night to dwell with Lot.\n\nAnd let's presume Lot did not know they were angels? Meaning they still maintained their secrecy.\n\nReminds me of when Jesus, after his resurrection, now divine, and thus moved in and out of mankind rather than dwell as when he was a man,\n\nAs he walked with the men on the road to Emmaus.\n\nThey did not know him yet their heart burned 🔥 when he spoke.\n\nI believe these beings included Jesus or should I say the word. These were no angels or rather no normal angels.\n\nSo let's presume Lot did not know they were angels, so he welcomes complete strangers to his home, how unlikely especially in a city like Sodom and Gomorrah.\n\nHow about if they were sodomites.\n\nOr maybe he had realised how these sodomites treated strangers who did not know the depravity of the city and passed there for the night 🌃.\n\nGranted, then how about when they struck the people with blindness.\n\nHe knew. He knew who they were yet these angels stayed with him.\n\nThey were angels in the same way the holy spirit is called an angel, i.e. the angel of God's presence.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:19:23","s":["50kj23loy3"]},{"m":"This unleavened bread so reminds me of the Passover - death was coming just as it did to Egypt, it was for Sodom.\n\nAnd here also they break unleavened bread.","dt":"2026-01-19T08:03:31","s":["ngg4ovzp4h"]}],"8":[{"m":"I believe after such incessant pleading 🙏 for the angels to come under his roof, he was now under obligation to defend them with all he could.\n\nThough offering his daughters to these beasts was quite extreme.\n\nAnd why did they want these two ✌ new men? Had they had enough of themselves? Were men already finished in the city 🏙?","dt":"2022-01-27T07:17:34","s":["hnd7slc0tz"]}],"9":[{"m":"Did Lot know who they were? I think 🤔 so.","dt":"2022-01-27T06:11:57","s":["2d7r5cckfu"]}],"11":[{"m":"This goes to show the degree of depravity of these men such that even after being struck with blindness, they still persisted in their depravity.\nI believe the blindness spoken about here is as the one in the case of Elisha when the entire army was struck blind such that they saw only what was permitted for them to see. Not that they went completely blind, I think.\nI mean upon realising suddenly Lot's door was no longer visible, they should have realised what was happening but still continued to search for the door.","dt":null,"s":["3e4d6efc18"]}],"12":[{"m":"These did not exhibit omniscience. Could it therefore mean they were mere angels who accompanied the LORD and not the Godhead in bodily forms?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["edqo48gg0w","8a94daece1"]}],"14":[{"m":"Lot believed the angels but his sons did not. How did he know they were divine beings?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["j5g2flddr4","255c6d4d52"]},{"m":"He had no control over his household unlike Abraham whom even the lord recognized his authority over his house.","dt":"2026-01-19T08:05:25","s":["s1xt8bblkb"]}],"16":[{"m":"Why did they not just snap their fingers for them to appear in the mountains?\n\nSpiritual things are not that way it seems. They physically carried them and dragged them literally. I'm sure like Moses, as they left heaven they were given specific gifts and powers to use in case of any hindrance. Also just like the two men who could call down fire 🔥 and famine at the end of time, I guess the angels 😇 also had their limited abilities.\n\nThey could not do as they wished. Same with the spirit's gifts... We don't do as we wish but as given by the Spirit.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["m1afexs7x7","848701efdc"]}],"17":[{"m":"Again limits of the mission.. The plains. The mountain ⛰ was safe but not the plain.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["bn048gxcz8","7022f5110f"]}],"22":[{"m":"So there were limits and briefings of the assignment the angels had.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["d298z85lnn","f355d740ba"]}],"24":[{"m":"God is still God of the whole earth and reigns as he sees fit. He still judges the nations and is God of the earth.","dt":null,"s":["764eb00f9b"]}],"28":[{"m":"A true intercessor, watching over the plain to see if the city 🏙 was saved or salvaged.\n\nHe saw the smoke ascending. To receive such punishment shows the depth of wickedness.\n\nMen who would do such to visitors and there was no law to restrain them.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["4bd55bc7ud","056f269e67"]}],"29":[{"m":"By this time Abraham's faith in God was great, he, God, was showing him his supremacy above all gods.\n\nHe, God, was the true God and monarch 👑 of the universe 🌌.\n\nDestroying cities regardless of the feigned protection other gods had offered\n\n\nLot, though he had left Abraham, was still benefiting from the father of nations.\n\nRelationships are so crucial.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["f8ikblc8ed","ef540fa8f9"]}],"30":[{"m":"See so invariably he went to the mountains mount 🗻\n\nNow Lot 🧘‍♂️, once a very rich man, was left with just his two daughters.\n\nWhat became of his massive wealth 🧐.\n\nAll gone.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["iulkaqvryq","3537666375"]}],"34":[{"m":"Lot at this time I can imagine was an unhappy man, possibly depressed, he had lost his home, wife, properties etc.\n\nDrinking was what was used by his daughters to commit such incest. Likely very common practice in Sodom.","dt":"2026-01-19T08:09:10","s":["xxwr6swnxa"]}],"36":[{"m":"What depravity what an excuse.\n\nThey had so lived among the sodomites that though they had left Sodom, Sodom was still in them.\n\nFor their conscience not to prick them, I can imagine the depravity of the city 🏙.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:30:39","s":["bvzsuo1ye8"]}],"37":[{"m":"Sad sad ending, who says there was no man in the earth 🌎 😔.\n\n\nThey chose the wrong way out. So much depravity had they witnessed so this was easy for them to do.\n\nThe fact that both were of the same mind shows how the entire family 👪 was corrupted.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["bxvbvt36jv","e3245dc610"]}],"10":[{"m":"… And shut to the door.. Is that a typo?","dt":"2024-01-18T06:21:04","s":["dh61k54lmo"]}],"15":[{"m":"Okay so the angels spoke plainly of their divine mission and nature and stayed with Lot till morning.\n\nNo angel 😇 does this nor behaves as such.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:25:56","s":["wn1tza2sa3"]}]},"20":{"2":[{"m":"This verse I suspect is parenthetical and not in chronological order. Because how could Sarah who at this age was 90 years still be youthful and outclass all the younger women.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:38:49","s":["aksedmpws4"]}],"6":[{"m":"It seemed Abimelech believed in God.","dt":"2022-01-27T08:05:06","s":["3d4bb15503"]}],"7":[{"m":"Ei GOD too he know how to do connection oo. See how he is scaring poor Abimelech and advocating for father Abraham.\nBut this scripture confirms that Abraham indeed was a prophet.","dt":null,"s":["791ed81f2f"]},{"m":"And a great prophet he was. I believe these chapters may be parenthetical in the sense that Sarah was now 99 years old. I don't think she was attractive enough to be taken as a wife for the king 👑. But well maybe they maintained their strength 💪 because of their times. Who knows. 😕 🤷‍♂️.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["ntuunrm90m","1d3c078568"]}],"13":[{"m":"O what a memory, this was where it all began from; when he moved out of his home. I know it was one difficult time and with it has come a lot of blessings and pain as well. O this walk with the father. I know because of how Abraham describes it. He does not say I came out of my father’s house but rather that God caused him to wander from his father’s house. It was the move of the spirit.","dt":null,"s":["761679fabd"]}],"14":[{"m":"Abraham prospered every where he went.\n\nMy only question is this. What was the purpose of this sojourning?\n\nAbraham was already very rich and had a large tribe.\n\nWas it to fulfill God's command that he should walk through the land?\n\nWas he exploring the land he had been given in his lifetime before his generation come to inherit it?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["1f13v303t3","bb5438c8dc"]}],"18":[{"m":"Wow... Then she was kept for some time with Abimelech for them to realise their sudden barrenness.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["8dmfnbpxna","a79e083c4c"]}]},"21":{"7":[{"m":"Interestingly, she never gave birth again, and that goes to show the miracle of his birth.\n\nIsaac was indeed a very special child 🧒.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["18464ct0ou"]}],"14":[{"m":"He that is blessed is indeed blessed. With just these emblems of survival. A nation was born. 🤔.","dt":"2022-01-27T10:47:09","s":["266672e4ae"]},{"m":"Abraham rose up early in the morning. As usual prompt to obey the lord.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:47:53","s":["yw3xcxa5wd"]}],"17":[{"m":"Interesting the arrangements and protocols of the spirit realm.\n\nGod heard the child because he was a covenant child of Abraham and an angel does not appear but rather speaks from heaven.\n\nWhy this methodology. Hmm 🤔.","dt":"2022-01-27T10:49:45","s":["3e2ca62307"]}],"20":[{"m":"Woe unto him who contends with Ishmael, for he is blessed and a covenant child.\n\nThere are many requirements to build a nation.\n\nOne of which is length of days for the progenitor of that nation and subsequent unity and preservation of progenies.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:20","s":["u1yrxndk4o","d421ab2812"]}],"25":[{"m":"Which same thing was to repeat itself later in his son's life.","dt":"2022-01-27T10:53:23","s":["699e183869"]}],"12":[{"m":"God sided with Sarah, though Sarah's actions were unfair because she started this whole mess.\n\nBut her jealousy aligned with God's purpose and so Ishmael had to go.\n\nIt's funny how God works. For God to have come into such a very domestic problem as HE did indicates Abraham was not willing to let Ishmael go.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:44:47","s":["5tdt5adddw"]}],"32":[{"m":"Is this not the same place that Isaac covenanted with Abimelech's son? Let me check.\n\nI've checked, the covenant of Isaac with Abimelech was not at Beer-sheba but right after that covenant, Isaac found again the well of Beer-sheba. Abraham's wells had been stopped by the philistines but now discovered again.\n\nWe live in a very strange dispensation, a dispensation of godlessness.\n\nIn our world 🗺 today people do not believe there is a God or gods, and God is silent 😶 among them that believe not, though mightily alive to and in us who believe.\n\nAnd God is not interested in showing himself in a supernatural physical way to the world 🗺.\n\nHe is too big for that, he moves with his own plans.\n\nIn like manner there was a time when the children 🧒 of Israel in the times of Gideon wondered where the God who divided the red Sea was 🌊 and who did so many miracles as told by their fathers was?\n\nThey had heard all these fantastic stories and now they were in oppression and God was silent 😶.\n\nHe, God, will speak when he sees fit to do so.","dt":"2024-01-18T06:51:38","s":["e0bziyvse1"]}]},"22":{"2":[{"m":"What is a burnt 🔥 offering??? A sign of complete surrender. A giving up of that which is offered without any part of it in usable form.\n\n\nA burnt offering is all and wholly given to the LORD.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["pm9q5sns32","b856840305"]},{"m":"I have heard preachers preach that God had to mention specifically that Isaac was his only son so he doesn't go for Ishmael instead.\n\nBut that point of view doesn't hold much water especially because Ishmael and his mother had been sent away from Abraham's family.","dt":"2026-01-19T20:46:21","s":["agt8jv8p5k"]}],"3":[{"m":"This man of God... So apt and prompt to do the spirit's bidding.","dt":"2022-01-27T11:23:01","s":["ec04ddd431"]}],"4":[{"m":"Wow.. So this was a three day journey... Then it indeed was a far place. He had a long time to think through his decision.","dt":"2022-01-27T11:23:39","s":["c9b643d9d2"]}],"5":[{"m":"Story story ☺... To go worship and come??? He was indeed going to worship 🛐 but... 🙄.","dt":"2022-01-27T11:24:42","s":["d1edb26963"]}],"7":[{"m":"Such a heart wrenching question... I can almost see Abraham nearly give up in tears 😭 but kept his face 😔 so he can accomplish this mission.","dt":"2022-01-27T11:27:48","s":["03aa3c4060"]}],"9":[{"m":"How did he get Isaac on the altar.. Okay so this is how he did it. Somehow he bound him up 👆.\n\nSad 😔, even after, how will Isaac ever trust or even relate to his father who listens 👂 to voices that tell him to offer his son.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["uvg1icnz8q","5cce3c3ed6"]},{"m":"I can only imagine this moment, after having told Isaac God would provide himself a lamb, how did he convince him that he was the sacrifice.\n\n\nI can imagine the torment and torture of the three days journey.\n\nLord have mercy.","dt":"2024-01-19T06:49:57","s":["kg0qwy6ia5"]}],"15":[{"m":"Who was this angel 😇 of the lord because he presumes not only to speak for God but speaks as God?\n\nHowever, if this angel was God it would have been plainly stated.\n\nBut then no ordinary angel 😇 speaks as God.\n\n\nThere is no other angel thus who does this.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["wpwbr490cy","9937106537"]}],"16":[{"m":"The angel of the lord spoke in the stead of the lord.\n\nWhy did God not speak himself as he had done in time past?\n\nI believe because of the utmost sacrifice Abraham had done,\n\nGod sat on his throne as king 👑 and commanded by divine decree that the angel 😇 with all power make this strong 💪 blessing and covenant upon Abraham\n\n\nNote the angel called out of heaven, yes this time God wanted the heavens and the earth 🌎 to bear account of what Abraham had done.","dt":"2024-01-19T06:57:25","s":["ho6tqn3r6s"]},{"m":"A second time out of heaven, it looks like the first time was to provide the lamb for Abraham to sacrifice with, and the whiles Abraham did so,\n\nHeaven went for a counsel meeting to discuss this mind blowing sacrifice.\n\nOh Abraham had passed the test, heaven was full of activity at the act of Abraham.\n\nGod has decided, he was going to bless Abraham forever and thus the royal 👑 decree was sent out with all the royal power and might.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:00:28","s":["3qtejrdgl2"]}],"11":[{"m":"Did Isaac hear this voice, I pray he did.\n\nAt least that would in a sense vindicate Abraham as doing this sacrifice for the lord.\n\nMaybe Isaac did maybe not?","dt":"2024-01-19T06:51:17","s":["sdolcbi3gn"]}]},"23":{"6":[{"m":"Abraham at this stage was mighty in wealth.\n\nThe sons of Heth called him not just a prince 🤴, but a mighty prince 🤴.\n\nHe was not just a leader of some large tribe, he was a prince in the land.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:03:38","s":["m66fio3xby"]}]},"24":{"8":[{"m":"Abraham held the command of the lord to leave his father and mother’s house 🏡 prime above else.\n\nIsaac was not to return there and sojourn there under no circumstance. Canaan was theirs.\n\nAbraham indeed was a man of faith to his death.\n\nHe believed God would favour his son’s course for a wife but left a caveat that in case the woman refuses to come Isaac must remain in the land.\n\nHe was going to leave such a turn of events in the hands of God to find a way of honoring the covenant of his seed possessing the land.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:10:19","s":["34535batox"]}],"14":[{"m":"The fleece of this servant was so difficult it would only take the hand of God.\nHe knew he was rich and looked rich with all these camels but to agree to water all the camels was an overkill.\nNo one would do that, not even for this rich looking merchant.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:12:33","s":["gt1rvnshuf"]}],"16":[{"m":"Genesis 21:3 Abraham has at this time forgotten his troubles, all the years of waiting had finally paid off.","dt":null,"s":["954117ea81"]},{"m":"Rebekah had it all, beauty, youth, purity, brains 🧠 and a hard worker 👷.\n\nThese in one is very rare, indeed a wife worthy of a patriarch.\n\nGod had been preparing this damsel years and years ago.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:14:07","s":["hi2nebzj0w"]}],"21":[{"m":"How and why Rebecca would do such a favor to a stranger is remarkable.\n\nWish there was record from Rebecca's perspective as to why she did what she did.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["ni0g6qtmkn","f50667b971"]},{"m":"Awww, what a description! Indeed, a damsel worthy of a patriarch.\n\nShe was not just fair but also very hard working. To have even offered to water all the camels was another thing all together. And Eliezer just watched quietly and thoughtfully: verse 21","dt":null,"d":[["undated","Awww, what a description! Indeed a damsel worthy of a patriarch.\nShe was not just fair but also very hard working. To have even offered to water all the camels was another thing all together. And Eliezer just watched quietly and thoughtfully: verse 21"]]}],"51":[{"m":"The world then was kind and trustworthy.\n\nI can imagine the feeling of Rebekah about such a moment.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:32:57","s":["kfp4wf9jdl"]}],"60":[{"m":"And this her seed did.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:35:53","s":["wpk1g0b13"]}],"63":[{"m":"What was their meditations 🧘‍♂️ like in those days.. I wonder.","dt":"2022-01-28T10:51:54","s":["c7869dfca0"]}],"67":[{"m":"Rebekah was a good wife, she brought Isaac comfort after the death of his mother whom he was mourning.\n\nShe helped the man heal and recover.\n\nHelping him forget his sorrows.","dt":"2026-01-19T21:07:07","s":["rsp65hce9v"]}],"6":[{"m":"Abraham was true to the covenant God had established with him. O what a man. No wonder God testified of Abraham that “I know him”, that he would teach his generations after him to fear the lord. Even his servants and his entire household he had trained in the fear of the lord and they not only worshipped God for fear of their master but actually personally served him as is the case of Eliezer.\nLittle wonder at a point Abraham talked of Eliezer being his heir.","dt":null,"s":["330d394ece"]}],"25":[{"m":"Wealth meets wealth, Abraham's brother had a city.\n\nBut Abraham was greater.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:17:44","s":["pmcyxm7yb4"]}],"30":[{"m":"Ah money talks.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:18:33","s":["8myx4uwil7"]}],"56":[{"m":"It's difficult for family to part ways.\n\nIt's understandable, but also Abraham's servant knew to seize the moments that come to us.","dt":"2024-01-19T07:35:25","s":["6ia15lszhi"]}]},"25":{"11":[{"m":"Was that the same place that Hagar met the angel the first time when pregnant - yes it so happens to be?","dt":"2026-01-20T07:05:50","s":["9o182t8ykm"]}],"22":[{"m":"How did she go about this inquisition?","dt":"2022-01-28T12:04:33","s":["1d532c9212"]}],"23":[{"m":"I believe God just foretold what was going to happen anyways.\nAnd Jacob, that guy is such a schemer. What in the world entered him to make such a request of his brother.\nIt's pretty obvious it wasn’t a chance event. He had been eyeing that birth right from the day he heard of the blessings associated with the birthright. He just bided his time and went for it.","dt":null,"s":["d7500d4b92"]},{"m":"Who taught her the ways of the lord?\n\nBecause now she had so gotten acquainted with the ways of the lord that she could enquire of the lord for herself.","dt":"2024-01-20T16:51:04","s":["uj3ycdczh5"]}],"31":[{"m":"Jacob was a smart crook, he chose his words carefully. He said SELL me, not give me. So it sounded like a trade and so it became. 2ndly he made Esau swear because he sought to just say it in passing, and Jacob would have none of that. So he made Esau swear.","dt":null,"d":[["undated","Jacob was a smart crook, he chose his words carefully. He said SELL me, not give me. So it sounded like a trade and so it became. 2ndly he made Esau swear because he sought to just say it in passing, and Jacob would have non of that. So he made Esau swear"]]}],"12":[{"m":"So Hagar did not remarry.\n\nI doubt 🤷‍♂️ she did especially after being married to a great prince 🤴 as Abraham.\n\nShe remained celibate, the price for trying to please Sarah and align with divine covenant.\n\nOh there is a price to pay for everything and boy 🧒 was it worth it.\n\nYes it was, now the whole world 🗺 talks of Hagar and Ishmeelites still rule our world today.","dt":"2024-01-20T11:17:20","s":["1bs79rvhvx"]}],"21":[{"m":"The ministry of intercession continues. As was in Abraham so Isaac continued therein the ways of the patriarchs.\n\nIndeed Rebecca came to meet Isaac in meditation on their wedding night.","dt":"2024-01-20T11:21:44","s":["0762c7e9j1"]}],"28":[{"m":"Interesting, it's stated why Isaac loved Esau.\n\nBut for Rebecca it is not. I kinda suspect it is because he was a home boy and was available to help.\n\nWe can see how that when Esau came from hunting Jacob was already at home with food in hand and ready.\n\nJacob might have been quite handy 🖐️ for Rebecca.","dt":"2024-01-23T08:54:10","s":["x1t8h2htjq"]}]},"26":{"3":[{"m":"I wonder how Isaac, in response to God's command, sowed in a land and reaped a 100 fold. How is this even possible?\n\nI sense a divine technology like that which Jacob received.\n\nGod might have shown Isaac something or maybe God just on his own supernaturally caused divine increase.","dt":"2024-01-23T20:26:21","s":["43olh8pxpv"]},{"m":"His father Abraham had sojourned in the same land - his footprints were there echoing through time, weighty with blessings.\n\nSo as the foot of his son, his only son Isaac stepped there, it triggered age old blessings, the blessings of the man who was friend of God.","dt":"2026-01-20T07:21:32","s":["ito3rxfj79"]},{"m":"Sojourn in this land. So it was the plan of God for Abraham and the patriarchs to be wanderers.","dt":null,"d":[["undated","Sojourn in this land. So it was the plan of God for Abraham and the patriarchs to be wanderers,"]]}],"5":[{"m":"Abraham had laws, and commands and statutes from the lord.\n\nI thought he was only just obedient to the voice and directions of the lord.\n\nThat goes to show there were many times God told Abraham to do some other things not recorded which go under these four broad headings of statutes, commands etc.","dt":"2024-01-23T20:24:25","s":["ezeml0prxt"]}],"6":[{"m":"Was this chapter after the boys exchange of birth rights or it was way earlier? I doubt this chapter is chronological.","dt":"2024-01-25T06:42:40","s":["z7jq412xoq"]}],"16":[{"m":"A man 👨 moves to a new neighborhood and becomes greater than they all including the king 👑. Isaac had economic might.","dt":"2022-01-28T12:08:35","s":["06eb82119c"]}],"22":[{"m":"Now with this well he can call his own, without contention he can feed his flock, his family and his great wealth.","dt":"2026-01-20T07:31:28","s":["xrd43rrqgf"]}],"24":[{"m":"What is it that prompts God to appear?\n\nWhen Isaac was going through that tough season of litigation with the herdsmen of Gerar God was silent 😶.\n\nNow suddenly he pops up to bless him and give him further instructions.\n\nGOD SEEMS to pop out based on his own agenda and fulfill his desires as he sees fit.","dt":"2024-01-25T06:45:25","s":["riurr3ljtv"]}],"18":[{"m":"Isaac honoured his father…","dt":null,"s":["101edeaaf5"]},{"m":"They waited till this mighty prince was dead and then they stopped all his wells, hoping to later claim it as theirs, as proved by how they strove with Isaac over it.","dt":"2024-01-23T20:29:48","s":["1sdnkcnw3b"]},{"m":"Such honour he gave his father - he kept the same names. Isaac was a good son.","dt":"2026-01-20T07:24:27","s":["hm0j2g5oyr"]}]},"27":{"6":[{"m":"Such mischief. It is worth noting that, Rebekah still had a strong influence over her son even at this stage of his life.\nAll this trickery and fight over the years had just been for “a blessing”. What is there in a blessing we ought to ask ourselves for an entire family to go to such extent to get it? Rebekah as a mother risked tearing apart her family with such devices.","dt":null,"s":["469246c800"]},{"m":"I know this story, yeah... Isaac will end up blessing Jacob but a thought 💭 came to mind. Did same thing happen to Abraham?\n\nBecause it is not recorded that Abraham blessed Isaac.\n\nEither ways Isaac might have learnt this from somewhere or one.\n\nWho did he learn from?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["n7kyv6xwre","6442f9263b"]}],"8":[{"m":"Our women, what at all prompted her to think of swindling both Esau and Isaac in this way.\n\nThe thought 💭 of giving out the blessings to Jacob was bad enough but to think of trickery.\n\nShe did not consider that Isaac was in his prophetic elements and out of honor and respect for that she should not involve deception in the game.\n\nYes she might have been facilitating the word of God that came to her earlier but not this way.\nHmm this gender\nAnd Jacob also joined in the scheming.\n\n\nHowever, doctor 😷 Otabil makes a notable point that God was willing to make a nation out of Jacob despite this trait.\n\nIndeed, he Doc sees it as a positive and desirable trait.\n\nThe trait of seizing the moment, not letting destiny and opportunity pass you by.","dt":"2024-01-25T07:12:47","s":["jrfjpx1pcv"]}],"12":[{"m":"The deceiver doesn't want to be deceived and found out.\n\nIt thus is very difficult to spot deception. We must therefore be very self aware and be quick to pause when something just seems off. We just might be victims of deception.","dt":"2024-02-13T07:23:38","s":["q3lcy1y1x2"]}],"13":[{"m":"Such scheming between mother and child 🧒. It almost destroyed the family 👪 bond forever.\n\nTwo ✌ tricksters, how then could they even trust one another after this shrewd act.","dt":"2024-02-13T07:25:03","s":["rrpdx6bodh"]},{"m":"I’m trying to guess the age of Rebekah. In the previous chapter Esau was 40 years making Isaac 100.\n\nNow in this chapter give or take Isaac was 100 plus a few years.\n\nIsaac is sick from old age but Rebekah is strong likely about 20 to 25 years younger.\n\nSo 80 or 75\n\nI’m just presuming she married Isaac as a young girl 15 to 20 years.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:05:42","s":["woxwx585uf"]}],"17":[{"m":"Interesting, Rebecca at this time knew the nature of her husband’s sickness well.\n\nHis sense of smell and touch were spot on because of the blindness.\n\nNow the only challenge was his hearing which from the story was good.\n\nSo now two senses against one.\n\nIsaac heard the voice that it was Jacob, but smelt and touched and it was Esau.\n\nNow he had to decide. Bear in mind he had spoken to Esau alone he presumed so that added to the evidence that this was truly Esau.\n\nAlso he did not expect nor suspect that Jacob would dare go to the extent of deceiving his own father.\nIndeed, at a point Isaac was uncomfortable and asked if this was truly Esau to which Jacob affirmed.\n\nMaybe Isaac's hearing was beginning to fail him as well, he might have thought 💭.","dt":"2024-02-13T07:31:51","s":["fp7j6nlzfd"]}],"20":[{"m":"Such a lie in the name of God. Yet God did not annul the blessing despite the trickery involved in obtaining it.","dt":null,"s":["1e299bac01"]},{"m":"This terrible lie did not undo the blessing. Ei so good can come out of wrong.\n\nBlessing out of deceptions - of course this is not a blanket statement we have to look at context.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:08:37","s":["afl1qa9qib"]}],"22":[{"m":"Interesting conclusion by Isaac. So now the million dollar question is this, which is stronger evidence, the voice or the flesh (hairy skin)?\n\nWhy did Isaac fall for it? Well, probably he thought, my ears might be failing me just as my sight, but my sense of feeling is still strong.","dt":null,"s":["36be9c3b6f"]},{"m":"He must have been really hairy for the feel of his hair to be like sheep wool.","dt":"2024-02-14T06:54:59","s":["jjycbpvkfq"]},{"m":"Who knows if they went back and forth over this matter, despite just one verse being dedicated to it.\n\nMaybe Isaac reckoned that his hearing was being affected by his age as well.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:10:43","s":["5haaa6ok69"]}],"27":[{"m":"And the anointing came upon him to bless despite the deceptions. Of course we have to take cognizance of the fact that heaven had already chosen Jacob, and the birthright had been legally exchanged between Esau and Jacob, so indeed Jacob was only outwitting the man who tried to steal from him, i.e. Esau.\n\nScripture doesn’t condone wrong so Jacob was the better man.\n\nEsau was the cheat.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:14:33","s":["z8me2mawlp"]}],"33":[{"m":"Damn!!! Isaac was so damn sure of this. Where did he get this insight from?\n\nI mean he uttered words and he said he couldn’t take it back. Wow 🤯 🤯🤯.","dt":"2022-01-28T15:37:57","s":["psvqmj80ma","758b7a0a06"]},{"m":"A fair exchange had taken place: the person had met the requirements, brought venison, and Isaac had eaten all.\n\nAnd the law or rule, it seems, is that the one whose venison you eat qualifies for the blessings; and once that is done, the legal requirement has been met, and could not be reversed once the cycle 🚴 is complete.","dt":"2024-02-17T11:27:48","s":["4oxwxavom2"]},{"m":"It was the eternal nature of things, i.e. the birthright and blessings, that Jacob saw, that made him follow everything within the books to legally obtain it, and he did.\n\nIt could not be said that he stole the blessing and did not have the birthright.\nHe had the birthright; it was Esau who was stealing the blessing after he had sold all rights to it.\n\nHow that Esau sold the rights to the blessings, and did that by swearing before a king 👑, none other than the monarch 👑 of the universe 🌌, yet still thought he would play smart and steal the blessing when he had relinquished all rights to it.\n\nNo wonder the universe conspired against him to thwart his plans and give it to the one who had his eyes on it the whole time.\n\nI can imagine how many years Jacob had been planning and scheming to get the opportunity for the birthright.\n\nHe missed it just because he came out second in natural twin ✨ birth.\n\nYet he knew on the inside that he deserved this blessing and would handle it better than his wild, uncultured and unrestrained brother.\n\nJacob waited and bided his time until the situation was favourable, and then he bought the rights.\n\nHe knew what it was worth more than the profane Esau who got it at zero cost. He got it just by being born.\n\nSame thing we see today, among chiefs and royals 👑 who sell lands for peanuts 🥜 only to become paupers decades later, and their children without any inheritance.\n\nBecause all they did to acquire such massive assets was to be born.\n\nWe see the same for many young beautiful ladies who sell their bodies and future 🔮 for pimps and cash.\n\nSometimes because of life’s challenges, but also because all they did to have their beauty was to be born with it.\n\nWe must be wise in our dealings, especially for things we got by just being born or for doing little.\n\nWe must be careful.","dt":"2024-02-17T11:48:47","s":["ebe0l6c2vy"]},{"m":"I suspect as he blessed Jacob after he had eaten and was full, he might have felt something move in his bowels towards Jacob.\n\nAnd he knew the person had received. Now that something was not something you could just call back to you.\n\nIsaac knew then that indeed he, Jacob, shall indeed be blessed without fail. And truly see how Jacob’s life turned out.\n\nNothing in this life could stop him from coming atop. Nothing, no matter how difficult or overwhelming.\nHe indeed was blessed.","dt":"2024-02-17T12:42:10","s":["zz8feywnrw"]},{"m":"I wonder where Isaac learnt how to bless from. We don’t have a record of Abraham doing this, or maybe he did but it wasn’t recorded.\n\nIsrael also did — maybe it was dependent on the depth of relationship the person had with God.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:21:44","s":["anwxxt1hoe"]}],"35":[{"m":"There was only one blessing for the first born and it couldn’t be given twice. What a law.\n\nCouldn’t Isaac have simply said that he reverses the blessing on Jacob because he stole it? But no.\n\nIsaac understood spiritual law and knew that Jacob followed the rules, which thus rightly qualified him.\n\nAnd Esau confirmed himself that Jacob had taken the birthright again by fair exchange 💱, and through the same he had the blessing.\n\nAnd 4000+ years on, the children of Jacob are here because of that blessing.\n\nWhat a thing for Esau to forfeit — he could not replace it. Isaac understood the implications of what had happened; no wonder the Bible says he trembled, which is bad enough, but not only did he tremble,\n\nBut he trembled very much. And not just very much but very exceedingly.\n\nHe saw through the sands of time and knew what had happened.\n\nYes, Esau in his time became great and a nation ahead of Israel, but that is the short-sighted view which Esau probably used to console himself that he had become greater than Jacob in his lifetime.\n\nThe part he did not see was the eternal covenant — timelessness ⌚ — which Jacob had won for himself.\n\nWe should not be fornicators like Esau and throw away eternal things for the mundane.","dt":"2024-02-17T11:36:31","s":["5tsyfdihry"]}],"36":[{"m":"Esau paa... What is a birthright if no blessing is attached to it?\n\nJacob followed all the legal processes of obtaining the birthright, which then qualified him for the blessing automatically, but even then he had to fight and use subtlety to take what was rightly his.","dt":"2024-02-17T12:44:02","s":["g52qervrie"]},{"m":"This goes to show the mind of Esau. He wanted to sell the birthright, which is the right to the blessings, and then eat the bean soup, and now, after many decades, with his hands 👐 cleaned and his mouth 👄 wiped, would come and take the blessings.\n\nWhen his evil 😈 schemes failed, he rather became bitter and vengeful.\n\nJacob did well to have run away, and his father to have blessed him.","dt":"2024-02-17T12:47:05","s":["vr7wec0ut4"]},{"m":"Ohhh, so Esau knew he did not have the birthrights.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:22:57","s":["rwdgqm59q4"]}],"37":[{"m":"See the statement of Isaac not too long after he had spoken the blessing. He claims that he had already given all of Jacob’s brethren into his hands and had given him corn and wine. Queer line of thinking, in that to Isaac, he had already given to Jacob corn and wine and servants when all he had done was to have just spoken. Yet to Isaac he reckoned it done and was immediately walking in that reality. This belief and reality was so strong and entrenched that Isaac did not see how it was possible to release those same blessings to Esau since he had just given them away.\nWow, wow, the thinking of the ancients, these patriarchs and men of faith and of the spirit.","dt":null,"s":["ecf55e94d8"]}],"40":[{"m":"But Esau never served Jacob in his life, and indeed he did have dominion, so in that wise the blessings on him worked: it was conditional.\n\nFast forward, their descendants had dominion over each other, but eventually Jacob, aka Israel, prevailed.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:33:29","s":["qv4tc4vrio"]}],"41":[{"m":"Esau hated the blessing because it was going to take a hard life of struggle and being quick and witty to take advantage of opportunities.\n\nHe would need to have the dominion in order to break Jacob’s yoke over him.\n\nHis breakthrough and success was not going to come on a silver 🥈 platter, so he hated it.\n\nBut it served him well, as we later on see.\n\nActually it wasn’t the blessing necessarily he hated, but Jacob, for causing him to inherit a hard blessing.\n\nOr maybe it’s the same thing — hating Jacob equals hating the blessing.","dt":"2022-01-29T12:02:11","s":["57fez3w0gq"]}],"46":[{"m":"So the thing runs in families. Rebekah knew that in her home they train their women well for marriage and thus she wanted Jacob to get a wife from her home.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:37:02","s":["w37381080d"]}],"1":[{"m":"How long was the time frame from when Esau sold his birthright to when the blessing was given?","dt":"2024-01-25T07:05:43","s":["9ntjuxqm9y"]}],"4":[{"m":"We have no record of Abraham blessing Isaac. Most likely he did but because he Isaac was the only child there was no contention so it was not dramatic enough to be recorded.\n\nAgain we see that the blessings of Isaac were very spiritual and backed by Power.\n\nHow and who trained Isaac in such matters of the spirit. We see that it was Abraham’s for we have examples of Isaac building altars, going for meditation 🧘‍♂️ walks hearing from God etc.\n\nHe had been well trained and dabbled well in matters of the spirit.","dt":"2024-01-27T12:40:53","s":["4bk8p99k9q"]}],"10":[{"m":"Such trickery, Isaac was a great man 👨 and with greatness comes all manner of scheming around you.\n\nIt is wisdom therefore to be aware that with rank comes these games around you and to avoid them as much as possible 🙆.\n\n\nThough as one rises in greatness one may have to blink an eye to some of them.","dt":"2024-02-13T07:21:08","s":["mkzaqgjlz4"]}]},"28":{"0":[{"m":"Jacob the blessed one; the man who carried upon him the Abrahamic covenant, yet here he was, being cheated like no man's business. Not so long ago whilst going to Laban’s house God Almighty had spoken to him face to face. Now here he was being cheated.\nWhere was God now? It’s interesting how God sometimes deals with us. Certain things happen to us and it's as if there is no God in our lives. There are times you wonder at God and his preferred time for being silent. Silent when you need him most. These are the times you easily doubt the existence of God or if not his existence, His ability to help in time of need.\nNeedless to say, in all of these trying moments, God blessed Jacob with children, many of them. Out of the bad created he the 12 tribes of Israel.\nGuess that shows God has his ways.","dt":null,"s":["23a34f54d8"]}],"4":[{"m":"Here is where Jacob got not just the blessing but that of Abraham with the covenant of nations.","dt":"2026-01-21T07:38:17","s":["e1q4zyybkz"]}],"14":[{"m":"Here was a very rich man's son yet was hardy and lying in the open rather than as kings and princes.\n\n\nThe descendants of Abraham though rich never settled nor lived an easy life though they could have with their riches.\n\nYet they chose to dwell in tents till the time appointed by God for them to be a nation then they inherited nations, lands and buildings and riches they did not build nor toil for.\n\nThey just kept pace with God.","dt":"2026-01-24T08:06:03","s":["tfsa4y1wor"]}],"15":[{"m":"This is the first time God was speaking to Jacob, the blessing and covenant was now officially affirmed by God.\n\nAfter that Isaac had blessed him.\n\nThis could have been Esau.\n\nNow Jacob was the blessed of the lord.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["nytr5umgz5","db92d4eb6b"]},{"m":"God assuring Jacob he was with him so reminds me of the word of the lord to me that he would not leave me...\n\n“Isaiah 41:10 KJV\nFear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.”\n\nHm, I renew my vows again oh my father and walk the path you spoke to me of many years ago in my youth.\n\nI know the promise and blessings on my life and ministry still holds.\n\nI would attain and attend to it. I will fulfill my call oh my father.\n\n\nAs I read the entire Isaiah 41 I see that it is talking about Jacob and how God called him and strengthened him.\n\nIndeed, Isaiah 41 is literally the story of my life.\n\nI shall tread upon the nations and mine enemies. With the lord on my side I shall come out tops.\n\nTheir molten images and their schemes shall be brought to nought because the lord, the I AM is my maker and keeper.\n\nHe would cause me to ride on the high places of the earth 🌎.\n\nHe who called him will not fail, he would answer and keep his promise.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:15:05","s":["cgtnzx1zn6"]},{"m":"This was the blessings Esau wanted but imagine Esau with his character.\n\nHow could God work with him...one who could sell his birth right can't be trusted with eternal purposes?\n\nThough he did change and to his credit built a nation - a great nation.","dt":"2026-01-24T08:08:24","s":["ib8nnz2mqv"]}],"22":[{"m":"Who was he going to pay the tithes to, or he was going to offer them as burnt offering.. Or as a goodwill to men.??","dt":"2022-01-29T14:52:47","s":["71502e80b5"]},{"m":"In my notes 4 years ago I asked who he was going to pay tithe to but\n\nRemember he said where the pillar was was going to be the house of God. So likely he set up a place of worship of a sort or as I suggested earlier he offered his flocks as burnt offering.","dt":"2026-01-24T08:12:55","s":["ndi1v8cwli"]}],"11":[{"m":"Here Jacob was alone.\nMan versus nature and he slept, today we are so frail and at variance with nature because of development so called.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:10:31","s":["i7i06xgc32"]}],"12":[{"m":"The blessing was provoked and now began to work. Something was on Jacob.. Oh lord bless me indeed and separate me from my brethren and family 👪 to the land you have shown me.\n\nOh lord help me.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:11:44","s":["0oodr69aaa"]}],"19":[{"m":"And anybody chancing upon these stones with its shiny lustre from the oil would not touch it but know that some divine 🔮 exchange had taken place here.\n\nI can imagine many people crossing this game path and seeing the stones and staying back in respect of divinity.\n\nAnd it's same even in our lands today. Many put pots on crossroads with blood of dead animals and such sacrifices and places are held sacred because spirits guard them.\n\nSo also we as children of God ought to set up sacred memorials, customs and traditions for the divine encounters we have with our God.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:25:34","s":["shlmpn10y4"]}],"20":[{"m":"So prior to this Jacob only served God because he was His father's God but now he through this vow was personalizing God as his God. So our gods ought to live worthy of their name and reputation lest they be no gods.","dt":"2022-01-29T12:12:47","s":["e769fc6e45"]}]},"29":{"2":[{"m":"Another well... Was it the same well Rebecca made her destiny move 🎥?\n\nIt could be.. Because the all seeing eye of God just for providence may well have made it so.\n\n\nIn reading these chapters I am reminded of the 🌎 eternal God who never dies.\n\nHe looks at tired Jacob and he remembers that just a few decades ago Eliezer was also here where he met Rebecca.\n\nTo God who lives forever it's probably like a few minutes ago.\n\nHe is working ⚒ like a master chess player the events of men's lives.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["hfpmeuq2zc","acdd6d946a"]}],"21":[{"m":"Ei seven years of relationship no sex... They indeed were cultured.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:30:23","s":["705nf2awxa"]}],"31":[{"m":"Does that mean God approved of the arrangements of deception?\n\nThough it was not really so bad because Jacob got Rachael immediately for his seven years labour.\n\nIn fact he got 2 sisters for seven years, one on loan which he worked another seven years for.\n\nGod indeed is interesting. Leah could not be blamed and hated because of a culture she did not create.\n\nShe was only a victim of circumstances and God being just blessed Leah with the fruit of the womb.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:34:31","s":["lly5omf4uh"]}],"33":[{"m":"Why did the lord do this? Jacob did not love the lady yet the lord chose that she that was hated will bring forth.","dt":"2026-01-24T08:18:54","s":["rrfkfs527r"]}],"15":[{"m":"Their uncle and nephew relations were seen as brothers.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:29:16","s":["aq8nl9snru"]}],"25":[{"m":"This was possible 🙆 under the cover of darkness because Jacob had never come close to ever seeing Rachael's form and nakedness for him to even discern her.\n\nIt was only during the day that he saw it was Leah.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:31:41","s":["yvxemws148"]}]},"30":{"2":[{"m":"The issues of the fruit 🥝 of the womb carried on for generations but Jacob the swindler hedged his odds with his multiple wives.\n\nTill finally his real love could birth. Though she died out of this same issue of child birth.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["3p6envdxms","637b9fcab7"]}],"3":[{"m":"Two generations ago the same decision was made and it resulted in issues.\n\nThough in this story we are not told that Bilhah detested Rachel.\n\nWell maybe because there were already 4 kids in the house so her child 🧒 was not really so unique.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["2z5f5lxppn","0d1b64deae"]}],"9":[{"m":"Servants in those days were literally your personal property.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:37:07","s":["bzy0nvevup"]}],"10":[{"m":"Ei papa Jacob was really enjoying :lol.","dt":null,"s":["b3436e96a2"]}],"13":[{"m":"See the humility of these maids earned their children a name in the 12 tribes of Israel 🇮🇱; and an eternal heritage because they stayed humble and accepted that their children 🧒 should be reckoned to their mistresses. In making these sacrifices little did they know the eternal ramifications for them. Today 4000 years down the line and the good lord has kept his word.","dt":"2022-01-29T18:06:15","s":["w28vlp467"]}],"15":[{"m":"Eii.. This rivalry... Rachael though barren had succeeded in hijacking Jacob to herself.\n\nHmm asem oo 🤭.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:38:48","s":["l0kdeigfh3"]}],"16":[{"m":"O in this life, one must endure many things, many hardships…","dt":null,"s":["2e6a9a9587"]},{"m":"😇 Interesting proceeding... Already Jacob did not favour Leah and now it appears he had stopped sleeping with her 😴.","dt":"2022-01-29T18:08:18","s":["76a566dbeb"]}],"24":[{"m":"HE WHO WAS SEPARATE FROM HIS BRETHREN.","dt":"2022-01-29T18:09:31","s":["c38a7611c3"]},{"m":"And he did","dt":"2026-01-24T08:50:32","s":["3ejx3jl4k7"]}],"26":[{"m":"Sad, 😔 Jacob had been so cheated and was content 😊 to go back home empty handed except with his wives and children 🧒.\n\nThat was enough for him.","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["exuv4vv3o","e38f76f907"]}],"33":[{"m":"Laban took away all the multi coloured animals. He cheated Jacob so much. So that was the first wage change there.\nSo ever before the 6 years should start counting, on day 1, Laban changed wages - he twisted the deal.","dt":null,"s":["29d38dc751"]}],"41":[{"m":"Where did Jacob get this technology from. It was from heaven.\n\nHis time for the blessings to speak had come.\n\nAnd speaking it did... Massively","dt":"2022-01-29T18:15:06","s":["lp4ivommt"]}],"42":[{"m":"How did Jacob discover this technology ⚙?\n\nWas it something he chanced upon as he took care of the flock all these 14 years?\n\nMaybe maybe not, though most likely or how else did he know... Except the lord showed him.\n\nIn that case or either ways we have to study these plants 🌿 and the system set up.. Who knows, it may open up scientific discoveries in our time ⌚.\n\nNo wonder archaeologists continue to discover technology of antiquity that surpasses that of our time ⌚.\n\nWe have much to learn and must admit we don't know it all.\n\nAlso Laban did not want to lose Jacob, no one wants to lose a hard working worker 👷 who brings in the monies and causes the company to grow.\n\nI know this by experience.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:46:30","s":["vjl2hodryh"]}],"21":[{"m":"As about this time I have not heard of Jacob complaining of not having a female child and just having boys. They reckoned that when it came to conception, it was all in the hands of God.","dt":null,"s":["11c277e685"]}],"43":[{"m":"He was not raising camels and asses and men but with his hire from the sheep and cattle, he expanded into these.","dt":"2026-01-24T08:56:36","s":["0ax2kfq6xi"]}]},"31":{"5":[{"m":"Jacob counts his blessings and sees that the Lord had been with him. In subsequent verses he tells of how God had revealed to him in a vision the method by which he was to be rich.","dt":null,"s":["a6f32dce40"]}],"10":[{"m":"Do we see the source of this technology of producing? It was by revelation in a dream.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:48:31","s":["00p7llklqu"]}],"12":[{"m":"When we go through impossible situations in life, God knows. He may be quiet but knows every single thing we are going through. And in the background he is working things together for our good. Just that in the difficult time it is so hard to remember that God is with you. That’s where faith comes in.\n\n…thou would have sent me away empty handed\nYou see, Laban was such a shrewd and wicked man. After 20 years of working, Jacob might have blessed Laban by at least close to 20,000 flock. And yet he would have sent Jacob away empty.\nInterestingly Laban was no pagan nor atheist. Indeed, he showed faith when he swore by the God of Abraham; he indeed demonstrated such faith in him that he was willing to let his sister go with a stranger, because that stranger, Eliezer, came in the name of God and with presents of course.\nYet Laban could as well demonstrate such wickedness to a fellow brother and kinsman.\n\nThere are many things to be said about the Laban-Jacob relationship. Consider this, that for every increase in the flock of Laban, however wicked he was, it was an increase also into Jacob’s account, because later when Jacob was mating the flock, it was these same large flock that produced the speckled offspring. So the more they were, the more were Jacob’s flock.\nThough at the time of Jacob’s faithfulness, he didn’t know he was working for himself. That’s one good lesson to bear in mind as we work for seemingly wicked and unfair bosses.","dt":null,"s":["b4fe657346"]},{"m":"It is such an easy thing for God to bless. I am an eyewitness to this.\n\nJust keep pace and keep in step with the Lord.\n\nHe will bless. And like in Jacob’s case, God watched on as if he did not care or have any plans, but at just the right time God released his wisdom and blessed Jacob supernaturally.\n\nAnd the proof of the blessing, the proof that there was something supernatural on Jacob, was that 10 good times Laban changed the conditions of Jacob’s contract and ten good times supernaturally God blessed Jacob by causing the animals to birth for him.","dt":"2026-01-24T09:42:38","s":["dvmp6j3v8u"]}],"13":[{"m":"An interesting description. “I am the God of Bethel”. So Jacob, who lived among idolatrous men, knows exactly who it is that is speaking to him.","dt":null,"s":["8707913076"]},{"m":"God takes vows seriously and he tells us not to be rash to vow in his presence, lest we be found fools.\n\nThis is what Esau did and lost his blessings.","dt":"2024-02-17T13:59:30","s":["9667clg9ax"]},{"m":"He was to return to the place of promise.","dt":"2026-01-24T09:32:35","s":["3doj7z9r6t"]},{"m":"Having now overdone His part of the vow, God asked Jacob to return, yes, return to the place of the vow.\n\nIt was time to move. 2 decades had passed and God had been faithful throughout.","dt":"2022-01-30T06:47:35","s":["9x1jwi9idx"]}],"19":[{"m":"The shadows and strongholds of the past.\n\nThis polytheist breed. She saw the God of Bethel obviously as one of the many god options.\n\nShe did not know he was the True God. After Noah, man had so strayed from the truth that now men worshipped all sorts of gods.\n\nIt is believed in the African traditional religion that these gods lead to the Supreme one.\n\nCould it be that Rachael took the gods so her father could not divine 🔮 by these.","dt":"2022-01-30T06:54:40","s":["zoyr5tzwiw"]}],"24":[{"m":"Ah, now God was fighting for his interest.\n\nThe blessing on Jacob was speaking and speaking loud 🔊.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:01:57","s":["qyt0cagyou"]}],"28":[{"m":"Of course this was a lie... He was never going to release Jacob.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:02:39","s":["1xls0t400t"]}],"29":[{"m":"God was just as one of the gods to Laban...\n\nPolytheists do not seem to recognize there is only one God.\n\nWell, that is why they are Polytheists.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:03:55","s":["qv3p7eabuo"]},{"m":"So after this warning ⚠, this is Laban’s version of not speaking good or bad.\n\nHow did Laban know that this was the God of Isaac?\n\nExcept that God might have introduced himself as the God of Abraham, Isaac and Jacob.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:01:17","s":["9dx84s3bep"]}],"37":[{"m":"Now Jacob had a justifiable reason to say all that was in his heart ♥ for once, in the presence of witnesses and brothers.\n\nThe brothers of whom the blessing said they would be under him. And indeed they had become so.\n\nAnd by being under him, it was seen in his material dominance.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:06:16","s":["sqajg7mv5o"]}],"38":[{"m":"Twenty years of honest labour.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:05:47","s":["sanuaps0jf"]}],"41":[{"m":"Changed his wages 10 times in 6 years, hmm? Such a crook. It takes cattle nine months to deliver and they can give birth from age 2 every single year for about 14 to 20 years. Yep.\nSo here’s what I see. After Laban separated all the speckled cattle, he noticed in nine months’ time that the cattle still produced speckled, so he decided to change the deal, i.e. Jacob’s wages. So in a matter of 6 years, that is 72 months, 8 nine-months, he changed his wages 10 times. That is very possible.\nBecause right after the arrangement below.","dt":null,"s":["d4719b05be"]}],"53":[{"m":"What was this fear of Isaac he kept saying?\n\nHe mentions the God of Abraham but says the fear of Isaac.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:10:03","s":["jru66zih79"]}],"55":[{"m":"Laban was a shrewd businessman 👨. He made sure to secure 🔐 what he had gotten through subtlety and to preserve his future 🔮.\n\nJacob also did his. Two shrewd men who understood the need to secure wealth and patents and generations from other shrewd men.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:09:56","s":["q8c6vm9vye"]}],"8":[{"m":"What a blessed man he was. Nature was favouring him.\n\nI now understand the blessing.\n\nFor nature to turn and favour him in this strange way 10 times, there was something upon him.\n\nAnd Laban detested him for that.\n\nLord bless me","dt":"2026-01-24T08:59:57","s":["42q11ry4og"]}],"15":[{"m":"Laban was such a crook, he even cheated his own daughters.","dt":null,"s":["d30642b1e0"]},{"m":"Laban was so profit-conscious and shrewd. He loved gain; he gave Rebecca out after having received some gifts.\n\nNow he gave his two daughters out for service and he was rich by it.","dt":"2022-01-30T06:50:34","s":["830fokc32s"]}],"16":[{"m":"If you treat your wife and family well, they will support you no matter what.\n\nThough family 👪 can give headaches sometimes.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:00:46","s":["d4xu9xri49"]}],"43":[{"m":"Laban, such a liar and so shameless. Let me now check sef what his name meant. Like seriously, LABAN means WHITE, such a contrary. Or maybe it’s in reference to whitewashed tombs.\nAnd such are the people in this world. Liars and deceivers. And I have experienced a few.\nIn fact, I relate so much to the Jacob story. I feel that is how Pentecost hospital has been. But then again, like Jacob, he’s vindicated me and I would be rich on account of Pentecost.\nAfter having served all these years, the best send-off is to begin to deny me my right to a workshop and yet continue to use my license to do trade and business.","dt":null,"s":["9e160b4bab"]}],"52":[{"m":"So 100 years down the line, when descendants of them both or any people passing by saw the heap in this desolate wasteland, though they may not understand what the covenant was, it would suffice them knowing a covenant was made here and the stones ought to be left untouched.\nI wonder if our generation would have left such covenant stones in place. I’m sure we would just destroy it and belittle its significance.","dt":null,"s":["6788949835"]}]},"32":{"2":[{"m":"Indeed, the 🔮 was working for Jacob. The blessing was speaking and loudly 📢.\n\nJacob seemed ordinary until the need for the supernatural, and suddenly the blessing is provoked to speak for him.\n\nHere the host of God came to usher and protect their interest.\n\nI believe they came as men just as they had done in the days of Abraham and Lot.\n\nWe are not told how many, but Jacob recognized them.\n\nThis entrance into Seir was to meet the profane Esau, who had refused and downplayed the sacred.\n\nAnd now he was a nation and a possible threat.\n\nGod protects his interests.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:24:33","s":["9pr18s3iaw"]},{"m":"The divine indeed was working for Jacob. The blessings spoke for him.\n\nHe seemed ordinary until the need for the extraordinary came, and then suddenly things changed for his favour.\n\nSee this host of angels.... I suspect they came in the form of men, like in the days of Abraham.\n\nThey had come to secure 🔐 God’s covenant and to protect it.\n\nIndeed, to protect it from the man who despised it and could now pose as a threat to the covenant.\n\nBut no fears for Jacob; a host of two bands had come to protect and strengthen 💪 him.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:16:10","s":["5kqhpowwqj"]}],"3":[{"m":"I’m sure probably at this time, Jacob had sent spies to spy out the condition of his brother Esau and had been told how great Esau had become.\nI wonder though, was the country at this time called Edom, or was it that it later became known by this name and thus the author referred to the name though in the past (I think there is some literary name given to such construction in literature).","dt":null,"s":["45f46937c4"]},{"m":"Ah, twenty years down the line and Edom was already a nation, a nation born out of restlessness and the sword ⚔, and Mount Seir was his.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:20:43","s":["vtayexe4aq"]}],"6":[{"m":"What was Esau doing with 400 men if not for intimidation and malice?\n\nAbraham had 300 trained soldiers 💂 and Esau has 400.\n\nEsau has become a great man indeed. Taking advantage of every situation and not letting any pass him by.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:12:36","s":["84cquqqi3p","fdff3c2e50"]}],"18":[{"m":"Here, Jacob’s nemesis was here.\nAfter he prayed, Jacob still took all possible practicable steps to appease Esau. Am not implying anything — like trying to help out God. I’m just saying what he did.","dt":null,"s":["a302214e70"]}],"20":[{"m":"I wonder what it might have felt like that night for the entire family as they prepared to meet their fate, not knowing what would befall them. They were to face the consequences of their father/husband’s past errors.\nI wonder how Jacob went about the story of his past life with Esau; how he stole Esau’s birthright. Again, I wonder what words of encouragement he gave them. Maybe he said that God, who had been with him, would rescue them all.\nDespite this, Jacob also took practical physical measures to appease Esau.","dt":null,"s":["a0a386913b"]},{"m":"Whilst taking steps in prayer, Jacob was also taking pragmatic measures.\n\nPractical steps to appease Esau.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:15:17","s":["s43199dzbw","f6db17b940"]}],"26":[{"m":"How did Jacob know who this was? How did he discern it was the angel of the Lord? And how did he discern to ask for blessings?","dt":"2023-10-27T13:14:21","s":["d85cd4ab68"]},{"m":"Why was he time-bound... It seemed the man-God had to make his escape before the day dawned.\n\nWhy was that so?","dt":"2026-01-24T09:55:24","s":["0aqg4b819n"]}],"29":[{"m":"How did Jacob know this man was no man and divine, and how did he know to ask for a blessing?\n\nAlso at this time the name of the angel was not revealed. The angel whom I believe is YAHWEH, the covenant name of God which was not yet to be revealed to man.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:28:23","s":["wgxntc8jin"]}],"32":[{"m":"Oh my God, men have touched God. Interacted with Him.\n\nSpoken face 😔 to face with him and lived.\n\nThese men!!!\n\nOh Lord, give me grace I pray.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:19:05","s":["hgonp7mj39","8b2b9fca44"]},{"m":"How come Israel 🇮🇱 could fight with God, except that God came as a man 👨 with the limited strength 💪 of a man?\n\nThough he “cheated” by dislocating the hip of Jacob miraculously. But God was fully man and fully God.\n\nSo Jacob could prevail over him. And Jacob was indeed a fighter. He had fought all his life and he was not going to lose all he had gained through being laid back.\n\nHe was going to prevail.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:35:10","s":["jsrctdsft7"]}],"28":[{"m":"It's interesting where this great nation of Israel, as we now know currently in world affairs, trace their source from. They were supplanters, cheaters; Jacob.\n\nBefore becoming Israel. And well, what God has changed is changed. They are no longer cheaters but princes: of power with God.","dt":null,"d":[["undated","Its interesting where this great nation of Israel as we now know currently in world affairs trace their source from. They were supplanter, cheaters; Jacob.\nBefore becoming Israel. And well, what God has changed is changed. They are no longer cheaters but princes: of power with God."]]}],"10":[{"m":"Over the course of 20 years, this man had become a blessed man. The blessing was indeed upon his head. Mind you, it was just the beginning of greater things to come.","dt":null,"s":["53633facd2"]}]},"33":{"4":[{"m":"Forgiveness and healing had now taken place.\n\nThe past healed.\n\nOh Jacob 😢 😢 😢.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:21:38","s":["cdom9xv9yy","f4b56c33ac"]},{"m":"I can imagine Esau seeing his brother from afar off... limping and approaching him.\n\nHis heart ♥ swelled with longing for his twin brother...\n\nHis brother with whom they had played together as kids and bullied each other here and there.\n\nNow his brother was limping... Life had happened, and Esau knew too well that life happens to us all...\n\nHe forgave his brother and ran to him.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:37:59","s":["e7dyxv9yrr"]}],"9":[{"m":"To refuse such a gift, Esau must have been very rich then.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:22:28","s":["75ba403f92"]}],"20":[{"m":"El was the general name for all gods, but God had told Israel that he was the prince 🤴 with God.\n\nTo let him know that there was only one El — that is, himself.\n\nSo now Jacob calls the place by the name of his God, i.e. God, the God of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nSo anyone who asks which god he is referencing, he, Jacob, would let them know there is only one El and he is the El of Israel.","dt":"2024-02-17T14:44:19","s":["48dssw9jam"]},{"m":"Rightly so","dt":"2022-01-30T07:24:07","s":["ikzaf1rhek"]}],"10":[{"m":"Esau was walking in the blessing Isaac blessed him with... He was not going to serve Jacob. He had broken the yoke of bondage to Jacob that was placed conditionally on him.\n\nNow that he was free there was no point being bitter against his brother, and the sufferings and lessons he had to go through to become who he was served him well.\n\nHe was wise and blessed and free.\n\nIn good faith there was nothing to hold against his brother.\n\nI’m sure if Esau was still under bondage and not free yet, he would still hold resentment against his brother who was coming back blessed.","dt":"2026-01-24T09:59:52","s":["c75ydo13vh"]}]},"34":{"12":[{"m":"For the man to go to this extent, Dinah was obviously very beautiful and virtuous.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:26:03","s":["5cv382mekj"]}],"26":[{"m":"Such wickedness. Now they had put their father in trouble.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:27:49","s":["dlvbukx69d"]}],"31":[{"m":"These two ✌️, even when they were being corrected, they would hear no rebuke and only saw from their perspective.\n\nYes, justifiably they were ill treated, but was that the solution — jeopardizing everything their father had worked for, and everyone’s life, just to appease their anger?","dt":"2024-02-18T06:16:02","s":["b9w92t7dli"]}]},"35":{"2":[{"m":"He married an idol worshipper’s daughter, who of course believed in the God of their father, for Rachel stole her father’s gods as well.\n\nHis community had idol worshippers and yet they dwelled in peace and feared not each other.\n\nHe being their leader could even order them to put away their gods.\n\nThat is the power of influence.","dt":"2026-01-24T10:06:06","s":["hrg22t9436"]}],"4":[{"m":"So Jacob knew of the jealousy of God against strange gods.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:12:34","s":["e9325b24af"]}],"22":[{"m":"Hm 🤔 he has brought a curse upon himself.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:20:33","s":["p1yv9e9dan"]},{"m":"Even though this is just a verse, it could have been an entire chapter or even book 📙.\n\nHow did he hear about it? Who chanced upon them?\n\nMost definitely Jacob never went in unto her again after that incident.\n\nWho was that spy 🕵️ who reported the case? What were the initial moves of Reuben? When did that love 😍 life begin among them?\n\nLike the story of Absalom, which was several chapters long, so could this particular verse.\n\nWisdom in a man is like deep waters...\n\nSo also is the writing of a book 📙 🙏.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:25:32","s":["032ndxex3m"]}],"29":[{"m":"History indeed repeats itself. Not too long ago, it was Isaac and Ishmael who buried father Abraham. However, this repetition is not some monotonous vicious cycle, because at the end of each man’s life he left behind much more than he came to meet and was given. So the process of nation building was under way. The quest to form national Israel was underway.\nO what a quest — in the course of time and history, Israel grew and became great. And this process continued from generation to generation. All through the Old Testament.\nHowever, in the New Testament it took on a completely different form. The nation building no longer became of the flesh, and in grafting of other nations by circumcision and the adherence to the law. No, it became by the spirit.\nInterestingly, though, the common factor has and always will be this: that the process of nation building and inheritance is by birth. Strictly by birth. For both the new and the old covenants.","dt":null,"s":["a8dd6a0aa8"]},{"m":"Awww.. 😢","dt":"2022-01-31T17:21:50","s":["2a88aadd70"]},{"m":"Dake’s bible explains that Isaac lived over 40 more years from when he expected to die, for which reason he had given his blessings.\n\nI believe that, considering that his blessing — which was supposed to help put his house in order — rather tore his house 🏡 apart, he might have pleaded with the Lord to grant him life and to see his family 👪 together again before he died.\n\nAnd this he did.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:05:58","s":["n0dvd2k1or"]}]},"36":{"8":[{"m":"Esau is Edom.\nEsau is Edom. That’s all I can say by way of commentary for now. “Esau is Edom”. There is something deep about this statement that I am trying to decipher… it’s causing a stir in my spirit; “Esau is Edom”. (6:50 PM). I know the cause of this stirring in my spirit would be explained.\nHe — Esau — had become a nation.","dt":null,"s":["f6bc4d9b97"]},{"m":"Aw, the Bible is a living thing. That last statement in bold just summarises the life of Esau in a phrase. It shows Esau became great, Esau became a conqueror, ESAU BECAME A MIGHTY NATION TO RECKON WITH.\nI feel so stirred up in my spirit. What will my story be? At the end of my tenure, what would be said of me?\nHENRY IS …","dt":null,"s":["09a2f23072"]}]},"37":{"20":[{"m":"Young and reckless","dt":"2022-02-01T14:20:43","s":["788jvc80ba"]},{"m":"These had killed before an entire city and were ready to do so again, even of their own brother.","dt":"2022-02-01T14:21:24","s":["jy4q4729rb"]}],"22":[{"m":"These young lads were very wicked.\n\nHow did they become so hardened and heartless? And it was not just a handful of them but quite a number.\n\nFor they conspired together to do this thing. To kill their own brother.","dt":"2024-02-19T18:11:05","s":["f3yf9czbsd"]}],"27":[{"m":"These brothers were a gang not to be messed with.\n\nYoung rowdy men who killed communities for defiling their sister, and sold their own brother into slavery for not being like them and not hanging out with them in their wicked escapades.\n\nHow did the sons of Jacob the blessed turn out so bad?\n\nBut the Almighty God uses their wickedness and youthful callousness to advance his cause and programme.\n\nNothing takes God by surprise. He is God.","dt":"2026-01-24T11:22:11","s":["yfyyjj3j3"]}],"28":[{"m":"Did Joseph fight? Did he struggle and explain, or was he too tired and weary?","dt":"2024-02-20T06:55:55","s":["gcuez5zgqb"]}],"29":[{"m":"Reuben was the first born, so naturally he felt the responsibility of taking care of everyone.","dt":"2026-01-24T11:29:35","s":["mfl4v7916k"]}],"31":[{"m":"These 11 brothers. Such wickedness in their hearts 💕.\n\nLord help me not to make decisions that in my much older 🧓 years I’ll look back and regret.\n\nHelp me Lord, help me.","dt":"2022-02-01T14:24:09","s":["q4xuwj6e3e","c6fe170260"]}],"32":[{"m":"They were men who had no innocence. Cruel and without heart ♥.","dt":"2022-02-01T14:24:58","s":["78db721477"]}],"34":[{"m":"Leadership is not easy... he had to bear the weight of many losses on his heart.","dt":"2026-01-24T11:30:38","s":["xpebpa3ccf"]}],"35":[{"m":"They knew the truth yet watched their father daily as he wept, and they could not care less.","dt":"2022-02-01T14:26:01","s":["ad9b27b0f9"]},{"m":"I know the feeling of grief for a loved one all too well.\n\nI know how the loss of a child in old age takes a toll on the aged, to speed their death.","dt":"2024-02-20T06:57:23","s":["y5emw4aju9"]}],"9":[{"m":"This boy Joseph. Hmm. Dreamed a dream more.\n\nSAD NEWS. I HAVE JUST BEEN INFORMED THAT KOMLA DUMOR IS DEAD. IT IS ALL OVER THE NEWS — OF CARDIAC ARREST — 19:23:54\nThe thought that comes to mind is that why is it that when we hear of someone’s death, the deception of the living is that we fail to realise that the dead were once alive. And that it could be any of us. In very real terms it could be us.","dt":null,"s":["425022b2df"]},{"m":"Did Joseph not know his brothers hated him and his dreams... Or did they conceal their hatred well from him?\n\nThese brothers were the same who killed an entire township.\n\nThey were young and wild.","dt":"2024-02-19T18:05:28","s":["eayanbx05x"]}],"25":[{"m":"As Joseph lay in the pit, providence started speaking. The Arabians came in at just the right time; the thoughts of Judah that making money was better gain than killing their brother and getting nothing.\n\nThis all fell perfectly into God’s plan.\n\nOh this God","dt":"2024-02-20T06:54:58","s":["3i0np6yiai"]}],"36":[{"m":"Despite Joseph being like a spoilt brat, he was diligent in all his ways. The Lord was with him.","dt":"2022-02-01T14:26:45","s":["03aa775342"]},{"m":"Now let the game begin.\n\nGod was now at liberty to continue his agenda.\n\nThe game was only just beginning — though for Joe that seemed to be the end of his life.","dt":"2026-01-24T11:33:36","s":["7jfwvtsy4t"]}]},"38":{"7":[{"m":"For the Lord to have slain Er, then he indeed was wicked. Because even the brothers of Joseph were kept alive despite their wickedness.\n\nEr must have been wicked indeed.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:10:52","s":["siyxkbw7fk"]}],"10":[{"m":"How did the people know this was the reason for Onan’s death?\n\nMaybe he died on the spot in a strange way the moment he spilled his seed.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:12:10","s":["lqxac9uyhr"]}],"14":[{"m":"How did she know that she could trap him thus...?","dt":"2022-02-24T13:22:59","s":["c012be1255"]},{"m":"What kind of culture is that? Young men could marry much older women.","dt":"2026-01-25T09:01:05","s":["m5tbrkswxh"]}],"23":[{"m":"Judah had such an eventful life, though not good events at such a young age.\n\nLost two of his three sons, impregnated his daughter-in-law... Sold his brother into slavery.\n\nHe had separated himself from his family and was doing his own things at this time.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:17:30","s":["k1o72zg3mb"]}],"8":[{"m":"Oh this was being practiced even before the law.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:12:59","s":["qtyev1g30h"]}],"18":[{"m":"Makes sense — if she could be allowed to take seed by her husband’s younger brother, she could also take seed by her father-in-law, who in any case was much older and more preferred than sleeping with her husband’s younger brothers, or waiting for the young ones to grow.\n\nShe was not growing any younger herself.","dt":"2026-01-25T09:03:32","s":["uh07v5hy76"]}]},"39":{"1":[{"m":"Barely a few generations ago, Abraham, Joseph’s great-grandfather, was with this Pharaoh’s great-grandfather.\n\nThey negotiated on equal terms. Indeed he feared Abraham the Hebrew.\n\nNow barely a few generations, and Abraham’s progeny has been sold to Pharaoh’s.\n\nOh how different things would be if they both knew this... Oh if only we had a historical perspective and revelation.\n\nOur lives would be so much better.\n\nWe bypass our miracle and inheritance daily but do not even know it.\n\nRather we may end up begging for crumbs.\n\nSMH 🤦‍♂️ this life.","dt":"2022-02-24T14:38:33","s":["juf6a1e13r","0652ea3ad7"]},{"m":"This trade of Poti-pherah was to change his life forever.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:20:27","s":["bu6oyllntc"]}],"3":[{"m":"And indeed, like his father Jacob, Joseph was blessed in all that he did. O LORD, make me like one of these.","dt":null,"s":["31e73d10b5"]},{"m":"Joseph was not just hardworking or intelligent.\n\nNo — whatever he did, there seemed to be some divine element that made him prosper.\n\nHis kind of prosperity was so divine that his master could tell that God was with him.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:22:07","s":["t83fjhae7p"]}],"14":[{"m":"They knew the Hebrews at this time.\n\nBecause of how great their fathers were: these men from the other side who dwelt in tents and had much riches because of their trade and shepherding skills.\n\nCenturies had passed and the Hebrews had etched their name in the sands of time with men like Abraham and Isaac.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:29:08","s":["xs26i0baak"]}],"19":[{"m":"Is this the usual way a servant who attempts to have his way with your wife is treated?\n\nI think Potiphar knew who his wife was. Or at least, between Joseph and his wife, he knew he was not hearing the whole truth.\n\nBut then how could he keep Joseph around with such an allegation hanging around him?\n\nHe had to imprison him and keep his own home.\n\nI can also imagine the politics and joy of those who hated this slave who suddenly had it all going well for him.","dt":"2026-01-25T09:19:09","s":["3k5sjz66zl"]}],"20":[{"m":"Is this the usual place Potiphar kept servants...\nThis was a political prison. Or, though a servant, could Joseph have risen that high in the social status and ladder?\n\nI doubt 🤷‍♂️ not","dt":"2022-02-24T14:42:31","s":["y7swflabdl","0234f5a55e"]}],"23":[{"m":"There was something about Joseph: whatever he did prospered. No wonder his father loved him. I think he stood out from his brethren in character and honesty. No wonder the Lord chose him to use him to be the deliverer of his people.","dt":null,"s":["2f4ba07c53"]}],"6":[{"m":"Joseph had become to Potiphar what Eliezer was to Abraham.","dt":null,"s":["d12f960d5d"]},{"m":"What kind of man was Joseph — he was blessed by the 'gods' so supernaturally that he prospered in everything.\n\nAnd he was also very handsome, and with all this he had such high moral standards.\n\nHe had it all.","dt":"2024-02-20T07:25:18","s":["28rghesoo5"]}],"11":[{"m":"As all this was going on, God was very much aware, watching.","dt":null,"s":["57b4608f46"]}]},"40":{"1":[{"m":"Could this incident have been orchestrated by God in the fullness of time? Of course, he did orchestrate it.","dt":null,"s":["11d9ce771f"]}],"4":[{"m":"He charged Joseph with them, and you would think he lorded it over them.\n\nBut we see that in this charge, he served them. He saw to their needs.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:26:56","s":["h7608ewejg","24586346d8"]}],"8":[{"m":"The interruptions of God into our lives in a divine way are not many, and need not be.\nBut in all those times it leads to effects that are life changing, or at the least leaves impact for years to come.\n\nSee Joseph — God shows him a childhood dream that almost got him killed, but God rescued him.\n\nNow he’s so 🌾 blessed of God it lands him in prison, and that same blessing becomes an everyday occurrence that takes him to the height of success even in prison.\n\nNow God intervenes again with three dreams in 2 years:\nThe butler, baker and Pharaoh’s.\n\nThese three permanently change his life.\n\nGod is a wonderful God of process.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:33:16","s":["euh3n294gd","dc006fed3e"]}],"14":[{"m":"A good appeal, but he would not be heard.\n\nHe knew that if he got some pardon, he would do well in the land of Egypt 🇪🇬","dt":"2022-02-24T16:30:53","s":["4sl6k9ya44","adace967e5"]}],"15":[{"m":"Joseph seemed so blessed and yet cursed at the same time.\n\nHe had God’s blessings, so whatever he TOUCHES turns to gold, yet he never rose and stayed risen.\n\nHe rises and is brought very low. I.e. he was the boy with the coat of many colour’s among his brethren, then he went down into a pit and sold into slavery...\n\nHe rose again in the house of Potiphar and then down to prison...\n\nI expect that in his next rise he might be weary and fearful if he does not deal with the shadows from the past.\n\nInstead of enjoying his present blessings, he would constantly be on edge for fear of patterns repeating.\n\nBut once he recognizes the hand of God in all this to preserve life he would be at peace — and he did.\n\nIn our current dispensation we would call it a generational curse, but that was not it.\n\nIt was a blessing in progress.","dt":"2026-01-25T09:42:09","s":["jxbhesr255"]}],"19":[{"m":"How did Joseph know the three branches and three baskets all represented days?\n\nWe know Joseph was a dreamer, but when did he become an interpreter of dreams?\n\nOr maybe his own dreams helped him nurture the gift of dream interpretation.\n\nOnly God knows how many other dreams he has had that were not recorded, which came to pass when he was in his father’s house.","dt":"2024-02-21T06:34:48","s":["oekbvnhfyl"]}],"23":[{"m":"All the better... For in God’s time he made all beautiful.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:29:36","s":["bff9a8ab17"]}],"5":[{"m":"How that God was working behind the scenes to cause things to work in favour of the Jews is simply amazing.\n\nIn retrospect we see the hand 🖐️ of God, but in real time it looks like business as usual; God is delaying, nothing is working... The same old boring life.","dt":"2024-02-21T06:30:09","s":["uo3m0wltcm"]}]},"41":{"1":[{"m":"Parashah 10: Mikketz (At the end) 41:1-44:17\n41:1 At the end of two years, Pharaoh had a dream: he was standing beside the Nile River;\n\nMany times in scripture, matters of the nations are revealed to the kings, however pagan they were. God respects hierarchy and order. I believe our president has certain dreams revealed to him of God — dreams which none of us ordinarily would have.","dt":null,"s":["76ef9ddd07"]},{"m":"Why was it Pharaoh that had this dream? It all falls in the plan of God.\n\nGod had conspired all of this and was just implementing it in due season.\n\nJoseph later recognized that it was the hand of God the whole time.","dt":"2024-02-21T06:55:44","s":["el1p6xn45t"]}],"6":[{"m":"These profane pagan minds and kings 👑 yet had futuristic dreams.\nRevelations of global 🌐 impact.\n\nAt least for the then world.\n\nSame as Nebuchadnezzar, whose dream even took him to the end of the world.\n\nThe point is God can and does use all for his glory. See Cyrus, whom God did lift up.\n\nWhom God called his anointed. So God anoints even pagans for a purpose.\n\nIsaiah 45:1-2 KJV\nThus saith the Lord to his anointed, to Cyrus, whose right hand I have holden, to subdue nations before him; and I will loose the loins of kings, to open before him the two leaved gates; and the gates shall not be shut; [2] I will go before thee, and make the crooked places straight: I will break in pieces the gates of brass, and cut in sunder the bars of iron:","dt":"2022-02-24T16:44:05","s":["yalpe9gkd6","822c4d5a30"]}],"8":[{"m":"It was when all else failed that this butler remembered Joseph - interesting.","dt":"2024-02-21T07:16:10","s":["050ti75sp0"]}],"14":[{"m":"How long had this mystery been out there seeking an answer?\n\nI’m sure weeks had passed and no answer.\n\nAnd Pharaoh sensed within him that this dream was imminent and it had grave implications if not handled well.\n\nSo Joseph had to be brought hastily.","dt":"2024-02-22T06:52:22","s":["63gmvmft8l"]},{"m":"His time had come, and his life, which had been in slow motion, now took off — and very fast.\n\nHis time had come.\n\nPsalm 105:19-21\nKing James Version\n19 Until the time that his word came: the word of the Lord tried him.\n\n20 The king sent and loosed him; even the ruler of the people, and let him go free.\n\n21 He made him lord of his.","dt":"2026-01-26T08:02:17","s":["8nktcbebqt"]}],"33":[{"m":"Joseph not only could interpret dreams but could also recommend the next appropriate response or action to be taken. He had wisdom as a gift as well.\nAfter having served with his gift of excellence in low places, including a prison. Now his gift had brought him high. Where it really belongs? His star now shone.\nI wonder whether Pharaoh asked for the reason for Joseph’s imprisonment. Of course he did, but I guess he… maybe overlooked it.\nI wonder how it might have felt for Joseph, knowing he was so blessed all round, with handsomeness as well as skill and wisdom and divine gifts, to be serving with them in the lowest of places — a prison. No wonder he tried lobbying to get out of there asap.\nSo painful to know you’ve got something of value that the world would celebrate yet lack opportunity to showcase it.","dt":null,"s":["0449213629"]}],"34":[{"m":"I get it that Joseph had wisdom to interpret dreams and lead Potiphar’s house and rule over the prisoners,\n\nbut to have the skill and wisdom to govern a whole nation and later feed that nation and other nations besides, that is a whole new level.\n\nHow did he know to do this?\n\nThis shows that it is the same principles. The same principles that govern a small people well will govern a large people well as well...\n\nNo wonder the master said, he who is faithful in little will also be faithful in much.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:02:28","s":["fzc540jgam"]}],"39":[{"m":"Smart move by Pharaoh. He chose the best in the land for himself and made him no. 2 man of the land.\n\nHow could he let one in whom the spirit of the gods reside go away from him and not serve in his cabinet?","dt":"2024-02-22T07:12:09","s":["k3w330038t"]}],"43":[{"m":"Just like that?\n\nDid Pharaoh not investigate his background, what took him to prison, etc.?\n\nMaybe he did and found only rumors, or maybe he knew how corrupt man is, so who are we to bring judgement on another.\n\nHe knew worse men who ought to be in prison but by virtue of their corruption and influence are walking free.\n\nEither way, he made Joseph number 2 man of the land.","dt":"2024-02-22T07:14:46","s":["hzvo5hm32i"]}],"45":[{"m":"There are seasons and times. Joseph married a pagan priest’s daughter.\n\nAt this stage it was permissible.\n\nThere was to come a time when such alliances were an abomination.\n\nThere are times, and let’s know them to walk in them.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:52:48","s":["p3hmzho6av","ca6abeb16f"]}],"50":[{"m":"Joseph married an unbeliever and idol worshipper.\n\nA polytheist who likely saw Joseph’s God as one of the many gods, yet they remained married.\n\nWhat was the culture and beliefs of that time that could sustain such a union...\n\nThose beliefs have changed, and being unequally yoked with an unbeliever I’ll advise against — and much trouble after....\nI have to think this through.","dt":"2026-01-26T08:14:10","s":["imr74aenmw"]}],"51":[{"m":"Oh only God knows how long he longed for his father without end. It ate him up.\n\nBut now he was restored and had rest even in a strange land. Such rest that he forgot — not literally — his father’s house.","dt":"2024-02-22T07:17:47","s":["6dewa4i3un"]},{"m":"Though married to a priest’s daughter, he named his children after his God.\n\nHe still had authority in his home, though on a foreign land with foreign gods who do not regard the monotheistic God of Joseph as the one and only true God.\n\nHe was still the man over his house.","dt":"2026-01-26T08:15:50","s":["qoua222ww1"]}],"56":[{"m":"Now Joseph’s wisdom was coming to bear.\n\nOthers could have gathered for themselves the same in the times of plenty, and they would not have needed to beg and sell themselves.\n\nIndeed generational wealth would have been built.\n\nI know what the future holds and what is to come.\n\nI will concentrate my energies thus wise.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:55:41","s":["wn536v85y8","c813bd84d4"]}],"57":[{"m":"Egypt was once such a great superpower.","dt":null,"s":["8867ac1aa8"]},{"m":"This famine made Joseph and Egypt rich.\n\nIndeed, it is God who maketh rich, and we have seen how many times God supernaturally made his children very rich.","dt":"2024-02-22T07:22:52","s":["pa9177we6u"]}],"9":[{"m":"Ei, this God is a very big God. He was able to keep all the gods of Egypt at a loss till his man Joseph came with the interpretation.","dt":"2024-02-22T06:49:53","s":["040wv8zi8d"]}],"11":[{"m":"Oh this God of mystery — so the dream of the butler and baker was a set-up for this moment — God knew all along what His plan was.","dt":"2024-02-22T06:53:39","s":["46ix4zlgzu"]}],"22":[{"m":"Such a dream is obviously not a normal dream.","dt":"2024-02-22T07:01:27","s":["htl0v1u26i"]}],"26":[{"m":"How did Joseph know this, or did the understanding just come to mind in thought 💭 flashes?\n\nHow come in Daniel’s case he had to go and wait — in fact 4 of them had to wait for the interpretation.","dt":"2024-02-22T07:03:33","s":["tmsd6kwegv"]}],"31":[{"m":"Oh Pharaoh had the keys right there to rule the world and the challenges coming upon the whole realm.\n\nImagine he did not seek the meaning with all his might.\n\nHe would have lost out big time ⌚ in securing a great future for himself.\n\nHelp me Lord not to be negligent and to not take things for granted.\n\nAnd show me Lord the meaning of the things revealed, I pray.","dt":"2024-02-22T07:06:24","s":["j0aixgsjv1"]}],"40":[{"m":"Was he not afraid of the man’s history? Did he investigate, or did he know that gifted men have flaws too and decide to forgive or overlook it?\n\nI think he might have investigated and made up his mind to work with Joseph.","dt":"2026-01-26T08:08:57","s":["9izeg1563y"]}]},"42":{"2":[{"m":"Dake’s reminds us that Abraham had done the same in the first famine in Genesis 12:10.\nO how countless a time Israel has looked to Egypt for salvation — much to God’s disapproval. Interestingly, the Messiah sought for refuge there and was groomed in Egypt.","dt":null,"s":["5bbb8f3905"]},{"m":"This was how far the news had traveled.... Pharaoh was going to be very powerful.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:57:04","s":["0f4adece5e"]}],"4":[{"m":"Oh, the griefings of life.\n\nJoseph’s death ☠, the 1st of two sons of his beloved Rachael, brought a great blow to Jacob.\n\nNow the only memory and posterity of Rachael was this last son Benjamin, and he wasn’t going to risk it. Meanwhile Benjamin is a ravenous wolf 🐺.\n\nHe cannot be tamed, but the circumstances of life sought to do so to protect him, but by so doing greatly limiting him.\n\nUntil the liberty was brought forth by Joseph, the manifestation of being alive.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:09:54","s":["h32fpz9ds5"]},{"m":"Though called Benjamin — son of my right hand 🖐️ — interestingly most of its people were left handed.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:12:46","s":["kspxagkp0c"]}],"6":[{"m":"😇... Interesting, such a big man like Joseph — so why did he personally sell to the people?\n\nI guess because as a leader you do the most important of things and delegate all others, and at this time bread 🥪 was the most important thing the world needed.","dt":"2022-02-24T16:59:08","s":["tvx7964xx8","fff7b3f7c1"]},{"m":"For a man of such stature, how come he was personally selling to the people, so directly involved in the sales?\n\nBecause that was wisdom. The most important, scarce and expensive commodity in the land was corn, and what else should the greatest man of the land concern himself with than corn?\n\nJoseph was indeed a faithful steward. No wonder Pharaoh and all his masters entrusted all things into his hands.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:07:05","s":["3q0yl6o5vj"]}],"22":[{"m":"Ah, here it is: their life had turned sore over the years, God had had his pound of flesh, and they had concluded that the blood of Joseph is what’s crying 😢 out against them for their much wickedness.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:20:36","s":["l4b89939kv"]},{"m":"Now they were parents and knew the pangs of fathers for the children, especially their sons.\n\nI believe their children were very beautiful and adorable and looked a lot like them.\n\nMy conjecture is that God might have done this, thus causing their souls to be so strongly knit to their own children.\n\nAnd now they remember their own sins of lying to their father and selling their most gifted brother out of jealousy.\n\nThe guilt never left after all these years.","dt":"2024-10-23T12:03:16","s":["pcbn74as02"]},{"m":"It had been 13 years — 13 years of torture, not just for Joseph but for his brethren as well.\n\nAs each of them married and had children of their own, they saw what they had done to their father and their own brother Joseph.\n\nNot to mention the other crimes they had committed in Shechem.\n\nNow they were much older, and each passing moment they remembered their wrong and regretted it.\n\nThe restoration of Joseph was not just a blessing to their father but to the conscience of their brothers as well.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:12:35","s":["1ak34oy15k"]}],"24":[{"m":"Joseph, like David ✡, was wise and soft-hearted, at the same time hard and witty.\nSee how he maximized the famine till the people sold themselves over.\n\nYet wept and forgave his brothers whiles still playing them by not revealing his identity immediately.","dt":"2022-02-24T17:02:32","s":["6z6rwsrwxi","acc817ab12"]}],"28":[{"m":"How were they going to go back for more corn when it seemed they did not pay for the first time for such a super scarce commodity?\n\nThey would need to be served again, and here they were having seemingly swindled the governor.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:24:31","s":["h1e2g734w7"]}],"37":[{"m":"For him to use his own children as collateral showed he was ready to die for his little brother, though of a different mother.","dt":"2024-10-23T11:55:13","s":["7j5deg8urb"]},{"m":"He didn’t trust Reuben, who had failed the first time as the first born to protect Joseph.\n\nThough of course it wasn’t his fault, and it was not as if Joseph was left in his charge.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:16:28","s":["kqqw258utj"]}],"21":[{"m":"It was 13 years and this thing would not go away.\n\nI suspect things had gone against them in their personal lives after they sold Joseph.\n\nAnd then it began to dawn on them the wickedness of their ways.\n\nAt this time most of them were middle-aged men and had their own children and grandchildren.\n\nThey understood life better and now saw the grief they had caused their father in the past.\n\nLife had happened to them and now they were wiser, regretful and pained, but they could not change the past.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:19:12","s":["u1iv03zvw1"]}],"29":[{"m":"Joseph took Simeon as surety, and he knew the famine would last for some more years, so they would definitely come back.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:23:00","s":["ddijccoa93"]}],"32":[{"m":"O I can imagine the guilt and pain the brothers faced as they watched their father, over the course of 22 years, live with the lie they had told him.\nThey were so affected that after many years, they attributed their ill treatment in Egypt to the sin they had committed.\nI think they had repented and were truly sorry. I feel for them.","dt":null,"s":["9c939642eb"]}],"38":[{"m":"Oh old man Jacob, he held on to life for the sake of Benjamin his son. His last born.\n\nIf Benjamin is lost, that is the end of his life.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:26:59","s":["lpalgth3qn"]}]},"43":{"6":[{"m":"I am laughing at this statement by Jacob, I however have tears in my eyes as well. I feel so sad for him.","dt":null,"s":["cd3804bc73"]},{"m":"OUR GREATEST PAIN IS OFTEN TIMES OUR GREATEST JOY AND GAIN.","dt":null,"s":["54b3832194"]}],"8":[{"m":"Now they had little ones; they knew the pangs of fatherhood.\n\nThey knew they had done their father in.\n\nAnd these boys, now men, remained loyal to each other all these decades and none told their father the truth.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:29:46","s":["yg3n2dk3r1"]},{"m":"Jacob might have trusted Judah more than Reuben, for he heeds to him here and releases Benjamin.\n\nMaybe the sins of Reuben were part of his distrust 🤨 for him at this time, though he swore by his 2 children.\n\nOf course their food was finished, so it added to the pressure to release Benjamin for the journey.","dt":"2024-10-23T11:57:25","s":["oi4plljf4i"]}],"14":[{"m":"I am in tears now. For all of his pain, Jacob was soon to receive double honor. He was soon to see both his sons.","dt":null,"s":["e66120bd86"]},{"m":"Amen, and may God almighty give unto all of us mercy. LORD GIVE US MERCY.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:19:48","s":["wkk98biubr"]}],"34":[{"m":"I’m sure they were glad, much as it seems the blessings upon Jacob their father were now beginning to speak for them.\n\nOr so it seemed.","dt":"2024-02-23T08:18:15","s":["g19i4djzhv"]},{"m":"They were happy for their brother.","dt":"2024-10-23T12:05:34","s":["pddj21enw6"]},{"m":"STRANGE things happening to these sons of Jacob. They knew they were in covenant with Jehovah, so these strange but good things happening to them were in their estimation the work of God Almighty.\n\nTheir fathers were idol worshippers, and so by God introducing himself as God almighty, he was etching it deep into their mind his status,\n\nas the only true and mighty God, hence almighty. He was not one of the gods, he was God himself.\n\nIn our African traditional religion for instance we believe in smaller gods, and God himself the father of them all who is accessed via the smaller gods.\n\nSo for a god to say that he is God, there must be undoubted proof.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:27:06","s":["o79z8ciq18"]},{"m":"I’m just thinking in the light of the note on this verse, why is it that the Old Testament servants of God dwelled in peace though they lived among idol worshippers and devils,\n\nyet the New Testament believer is jittery and constantly in fear fighting these spirits and demons, meanwhile we have a greater power, covenant and blessings.\n\nLord why this anomaly — I believe unwavering dedication to our GOD is the problem and difference between us and them.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:29:07","s":["twnmss9vnt"]}],"9":[{"m":"And in all this God was watching.\n\nHis boys were responding to his dealings with them. Now they knew loyalty, sacrifice, love and forgiveness.\n\nThey were men now and better versions of themselves.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:32:52","s":["7vufci0c6d"]}],"12":[{"m":"Ready to offer a gift as he did with Esau to assuage any animosity held against his family 👪.\n\nI can imagine how much Jacob prayed the whole time his sons were on the journey to Egypt.\n\nBut this time God did not show up 👆. There was no host with his sons, neither did the God of Beth-el answer.\n\nGod was just silent 😶 because He, God, was already working — indeed had been working — behind the scenes, and did not need interruptions at this time ⌚.\n\nNeither did he need Jacob to do anything, so there was nothing to tell him.\n\nJacob just needed to continue living blameless before God.","dt":"2024-02-23T07:37:03","s":["du09wnddim"]}],"17":[{"m":"O such guilt every step of the way. I feel for the sons of Israel now.\nGenesis 43\nvs 28: again, they bow themselves to Joseph, fulfilling the dream of Joseph again and again.\n\nCHAPTER 45","dt":null,"s":["78804b28ce"]}]},"44":{"16":[{"m":"They still blamed every evil 😈 that happened to them on their iniquity of killing Joseph and causing their father so much pain.\n\nAnd so it seemed, because the ills that befell them were all too strange.\n\nI believe strongly that from that day they sold Joseph, things went against them.\n\nThey were judged for their ill intent, though it did not happen. I.e. Joseph yet lived.","dt":"2024-02-23T08:24:38","s":["xtppuobays"]},{"m":"Though innocent, they could not defend themselves nor provide proof of it, so they handed themselves over to God as punishment for their iniquities and atrocities of the past. And rightly so it seemed.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:33:47","s":["y0ti4ayop9"]}],"20":[{"m":"They had come to accept that Rachel and her children would forever be their father’s favorite, and their father had a right to that.\n\nNow they themselves were men and understood — they had favorites themselves.","dt":"2024-02-23T08:26:18","s":["rw9laj9zjy"]}],"9":[{"m":"What made them so sure of their integrity and that of their fellow brothers?\n\nSomething had changed.\n\nThe brothers had been together for at least 3 decades.\n\nThey knew each other too well now and could trust their words.","dt":"2024-02-23T08:21:07","s":["sbo77o6d5x"]},{"m":"They had such confidence in their personal morals and that of each other to the extent that they could trust each other with their lives.\n\nThey were blood brothers now indeed.\n\nThey knew each other so well and were so bonded.","dt":"2024-10-23T12:10:06","s":["9e8cxbs8pn"]}]},"45":{"6":[{"m":"THERE IS something about this scripture, i.e. the part talking about “and yet there are five years, in the which there shall neither be earing nor harvest”. THERE IS SOMETHING…","dt":null,"s":["a42bd0abf6"]},{"m":"Here we go again, the dreamer, and he was right.\n\nNow circumstances had changed.\n\nJoseph had changed too.\n\nI kind of think he was a bit over-pampered, but that did not warrant such jealousy from his brothers.","dt":"2022-02-25T14:13:06","s":["ur22ecjha3","2b440fd269"]},{"m":"God had called for a famine. He did not want to see earing nor harvest in the face of the earth for 7 years.\n\nHe is the LORD.","dt":"2024-02-23T08:30:38","s":["dyn8ua2sij"]}],"8":[{"m":"What a moment in history for Joseph and his brethren.","dt":null,"s":["780710c37e"]}],"9":[{"m":"Joseph, that promised child, the dreamer, is now Lord of Egypt: there was always a star on his head.","dt":null,"s":["1da2c94134"]}],"14":[{"m":"Finally, he gets to meet his wise brother the dreamer, and now the greatest and wisest man in the world.\n\nWhat a proud brother Benjamin might have been.\n\nTo have Joseph as his brother — same mother and father...\n\nThe God of his father had proven himself true on their behalf.","dt":"2024-10-23T12:14:49","s":["b2pc3vzof5"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh my oh mine... I’m sure Pharaoh and Egypt knew the story all too well.\n\nThat Joseph was a slave turned president, whose kindred had sold him.\n\nHe was now without family 👪.\n\nAnd now here we are, his family, through the famine had come to him.\n\nWhat a moment, what a story! Word will indeed spread and many a fireside story would be told of Joseph the prince 🤴 of Egypt and his family 👪.","dt":"2024-02-23T08:39:15","s":["83jk6o4iuz"]}],"21":[{"m":"Earlier Joseph said that there will be no harvest until the famine was over, not that there will be no planting; yes, men will plant but there will be no harvest.\n\nI can imagine the eighth year. Just imagine that the whole world plants the year before and the ground is dry, left to the mercy of nature which showed no mercy.\n\nAnd now the eighth year, and finally plants begin to bud all over. The sovereign power of God is seen.\n\nOh the power of God and nature to bring wealth and to take away wealth.\n\nJust the imagery of fresh buds, and flowers and eventually fruiting — oh what a glory to God almighty.\n\nNo wonder the gods were worshipped so much. But in our age and days, instead of science and wisdom strengthening our belief and resolve, we have become more Godless than ever.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:42:59","s":["yned5dnzua"]}],"24":[{"m":"Oh I can imagine the many tears and prayers of Jacob for his children even as they embarked on this many days’ journey.\n\nAnd especially as they delayed because of the debacle, and their meeting Joseph for real now.\n\nHow he often woke up to look over the horizon for his children, just as he had done oftentimes when Joseph was said to have died.\n\nWandering many times into the wild, hoping against hope that he might have lived, or at worst some body part of his be left for burial.\n\nBut to no avail.\n\nNow here he is waiting once more.","dt":"2024-10-23T12:18:55","s":["k5cvk5p78m"]}],"28":[{"m":"O yes, the way of all flesh — a time to be born and a time to die. So it’s not right to die when one’s time to die is not due.","dt":null,"s":["8c1282d92f"]},{"m":"😢 😢 😢","dt":"2022-03-06T16:44:35","s":["7570ffccac"]},{"m":"Ah the blessing. Now he evidently saw it and came alive.\n\nNow he knew for certainty the command and the promise of the Lord was true and certain, and was sure to take place.\n\nAnd today we are spiritual Israelites, and for sure the blessing is upon our heads and would surely happen according to the word of God the LORD.","dt":"2024-02-23T09:07:08","s":["d2cg2tq5uj"]}]},"46":{"0":[{"m":"vs 4\nGod promised going down with Israel. When God sends a man to a place and the man heeds, he, God, goes with the man. O what a pleasure to have God go with you to a place.","dt":null,"s":["548d6af780"]}],"2":[{"m":"So God waited all this while as the drama unfolded and real raw emotions were put to the test; and now that the drama was over and Jacob knew the truth,\n\nGod shows up from behind the curtains and lays forth the next set of plans for the future 🔮.","dt":"2024-10-23T12:21:02","s":["p4o5wequvu"]},{"m":"Lord God almighty, why did you call him twice?","dt":"2026-01-27T07:44:55","s":["2e2fkxtx3f"]}],"3":[{"m":"Why did God have to keep telling Jacob who he was?\n\nI think 🤔 obviously because Jacob barely heard from God. Unlike our days where God is in our hearts, so we easily discern him.\n\nBut from the text it has been over twenty years since God’s last appearance to Jacob, so it was only right to let him know it is not some dream from some spirit, but this is him.\nGod almighty.\n\nThis time God didn’t even mention his signature name of God almighty but rather referenced the covenant he had with Abraham.","dt":"2026-01-28T07:21:04","s":["so289t8odf"]}],"4":[{"m":"Where God sends, he God follows.","dt":null,"s":["da182d1816"]},{"m":"So all the while and years the children of Israel were in Egypt there was a GOD in their midst — through the great initial moments and through the slavery time, there was a God with them.\n\nOh how God dwelleth in our midst, God with us — Immanuel. We are not ordinary — there is a God in our midst.\n\nSo he told me over the weekend, Sunday I think, to taste and see that the Lord is good.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:49:54","s":["0jnwhtw7we"]}],"5":[{"m":"Each passing day of this journey his bowels yearned for his son Joseph, just to meet him.\n\nBenjamin was what had kept him, so for each of us we serve as a treasured reminder and joy to our parents of their love for us, and same for us our children do serve that purpose.\n\nWe must therefore, as much as possible, with all our might make the most of our lives so our memory is greatly cherished and a joy to both our parents and children.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:52:09","s":["sz6m2a0gsb"]}],"7":[{"m":"They were running 🏃 a very huge family business.","dt":"2022-03-06T16:49:17","s":["eaf5a2c914"]},{"m":"I am sure other tribes and families will perch so they can survive. Who would not want to?","dt":"2026-01-27T07:54:53","s":["1wsu78jtn0"]}],"20":[{"m":"Joseph married a fetish priests daughter. And not just any fetish priest but the national priest associated with Pharaoh.","dt":"2022-08-05T07:22:10","s":["1df8236732"]}],"34":[{"m":"Good advice and wisdom. Lord give us good advisers.","dt":"2026-01-27T07:56:38","s":["69zm83wt5t"]}]},"47":{"19":[{"m":"If during the years of abundance, each family had kept enough supplies, they would not have come to this point. They didn’t even have a single grain for food or to sow.","dt":null,"s":["eb5cb51770"]}],"23":[{"m":"The people had been reduced to their lowest possible state.\n\nBare survival mode, and were all too glad to sell themselves and their land so they could survive.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:29:09","s":["jts5gi7eur"]}],"30":[{"m":"Oh men of vision and wisdom,\n\nMen with prophetic insight. He required by oath that he be buried ⚰ in the land of covenant, by his fathers who passed in the divine blessings.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:31:58","s":["3xwkhk34dx"]}],"18":[{"m":"All this because they lacked revelation and Joseph had revelation.\n\nAnd they did not have connections to the power corridors to have heard how that there was a coming famine, for them to have at least prepared ahead.\n\nOr maybe they heard but did not believe until it was too late.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:26:39","s":["9zoblb10pe"]}],"24":[{"m":"And this has remained till today — men slaves perpetually.\n\nWe pay taxes, some countries up to half.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:30:09","s":["2c5sgpzj0v"]}]},"48":{"4":[{"m":"Oh, so that is how information and knowledge is passed on.\n\nFrom generation to generation the mantle remained.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:33:07","s":["radjwtly4"]}],"5":[{"m":"Right here Joseph has the right of the 1st born, a double portion. Instead of he representing himself, a single tribe, he represented 2.\nSo whiles Esau lost the 1st born through trading it, Joseph gained the first born right through excellence; he demonstrated leadership and the traits of the 1st born.\nAlso it almost looks like Jacob wanted to reward his favourite wife since she had only 2 children, so he gave Joseph 2 slots instead of one. Because right after, he speaks of Rachael.","dt":null,"s":["fe76692fdf"]},{"m":"Ah oo... I now get it... Jacob made Joseph the first born and so gave him two portions in the blessings and of course consequently in the sharing of the land of Canaan.\n\nIn doing this he made Ephraim and Manasseh in place of Reuben and Simeon.\n\nAgain he swapped Manasseh’s place with Ephraim, so Ephraim became the 1st born and Manasseh the 2nd born.\n\nSuch powers the patriarch had and understood.\n\nIt seems also that from his encounters with God almighty and the promise of him becoming a multitude of nations, he knew each son of his would represent a unique tribe... why else would he switch places of the first born if they were not going to be significant nations individually?\n\nSo he blessed and gave the son whom he loved from his wife whom he loved the rights of the first born, just as he had gotten those same rights from his father.","dt":"2026-01-28T07:46:17","s":["7avobwjwzy"]}],"10":[{"m":"Joseph was now about 54 years and his young men in their twenties.\n\nAnd here they witnessed how blessing and mantles are transferred from generation to generation.\n\nIt was a very spiritual moment. And this indeed is the reason we give birth — to pass inheritance across generations and to ensure that your name and legacy remains strong 💪 from generation to generation.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:35:57","s":["u9occs2du8"]},{"m":"He could not see, like his father Isaac, and kissed, embraced and smelled them like when he was taking the blessings from Isaac his father.\n\nThere was no deception here though...\n\nBut wait, there was — he swapped places... the first for the last.","dt":"2026-01-28T07:48:59","s":["sgds9s6nw8"]}],"12":[{"m":"Before his father, in obedience and honour.\n\nThis was his father whom he played with and whom he was favorite of, but at this moment his father was a prophet and in his spiritual elements.\n\nJoseph recognized the moment and bowed down. Ready to be blessed.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:37:42","s":["o39sfw8tbm"]}],"19":[{"m":"Oh what a word, we all want to be great.\n\nHe also shall be great.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:39:35","s":["8b6ebb2ad2"]}],"18":[{"m":"Spiritual moments cannot be missed. You cannot assume it doesn’t matter. You must needs be present, and things must needs be done in a certain way.\nWhelp","dt":null,"s":["d980cca274"]}],"22":[{"m":"Interesting, even before they returned to Canaan and to share the land, Jacob prophetically and in faith gave Joseph additional land and property, and specified which portion was for Joseph for his birthright.\n\nThese men were indeed men of faith who died not having duly inherited the promise but saw it a far way off.","dt":"2024-02-28T07:44:24","s":["xuy42klmkc"]}]},"49":{"1":[{"m":"How did Jacob come about this knowledge?\n\nHow did he know what was to befall his sons in the last days?\n\nWhen did he become a prophet?\n\nBut this should not be surprising. Jacob was a man God spoke to.\n\nIt shouldn’t be a wonder he prophesied concerning the end.","dt":"2024-02-29T06:32:05","s":["q8lh5gixyj"]}],"5":[{"m":"The eldest borns of Jacob, who were to serve as an example unto the younger ones and to ease the burden of their father, rather caused him much pain and trouble.","dt":"2024-02-29T12:28:54","s":["lgexfed4zx"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh my God, the things that Jacob knew, the visions of the most high he had that only he knew.\n\nHere he lets them out.\n\nHe was not just pouring blessing from his mind and heart ♥.\n\nHe knew some things by prophecy... how else could he have known that the scepter shall not depart from Judah until Shiloh comes?","dt":"2026-01-28T07:55:25","s":["yhf668w1hw"]}],"15":[{"m":"He was not just blessing, he was prophesying what he saw.\n\nJacob prophesied what he saw, as in this case with Judah... At the same time he had power to bless whom he will, as Joseph, and curse, as Reuben.\n\nWhat he liked, he sustained the prophecy thereof.\n\nLord have mercy and give us of the water and fountain of the spirit.","dt":"2026-01-28T07:58:20","s":["o725rl1nth"]}],"26":[{"m":"I like Joseph’s blessings. He determined his own fate and destiny as a result of the strength of his character. Though he was not the first born, he far superseded the first. He determined his destiny and consequently, a great blessing was bestowed upon him.","dt":null,"s":["d5d76f2fd5"]},{"m":"O I love this part of the blessings of Joseph so poetic.","dt":null,"s":["26dcd9eef4"]}],"28":[{"m":"He blessed them all... NONE was called cursed. Even Reuben, who seemed cursed, was described as blessed.\n\nJust that some blessings were better than others. And like Esau, even the blessing which seems not the best — much can be made out of it.\n\nReally Reuben was blessed in many ways.","dt":"2026-01-28T08:03:40","s":["zc0t85ry0a"]}],"33":[{"m":"Amen, and now the blessing is hovering around, looking for the next person in line to carry out the will of God.\n\nYes, the blessing was on Joseph now, who took care of all his brethren, but soon enough Joseph was going to die and Israel 🇮🇱, now a nation in a foreign land, lived comfortably.\n\nBut who was going to stand out next in an extraordinary way, in a way that showed the might and power of God?\n\nWho was going to carry the blessings?","dt":"2024-02-29T12:52:44","s":["chtqyvz4hu"]}],"0":[{"m":"In blessing his sons, I wondered: is it Jacob’s blessings that determined the character of his sons, or is it their character which determined the blessing? Well obviously, their character determined the blessings they each got, not just for their lives but for all posterity. They determined their future.","dt":null,"s":["6cb76ce27e"]}],"2":[{"m":"Jacob speaks in the 3rd person.","dt":null,"s":["4495907380"]}],"4":[{"m":"I will not at all be surprised that since then Jacob never knew her again and kept himself from her.\n\nAfter all she was a servant to begin with.","dt":"2024-02-29T12:27:17","s":["9l8cfyzb3v"]}]},"50":{"17":[{"m":"As they aged more and more, they realized the foolishness of their ways and the far-reaching consequences of their actions.\n\nIt haunted them and now they sought forgiveness again, because another dimension of understanding of how wicked their actions were had dawned on them.","dt":"2024-02-29T12:59:47","s":["0kzozskmrs"]}],"18":[{"m":"Joseph was truly powerful; he was ruler of all of Egypt. His brethren had seen men bow to Joseph. They had his power and it had an effect on them.\nJoseph was not a president, he was a king, for life. So his brethren easily bowed to him.","dt":null,"s":["64965bd310"]}],"20":[{"m":"Simeon and Levi knew all too well the power of deception. They themselves had practiced it, as well as the other brethren, and now they feared Joseph was doing same to them.\n\nUsing fair words to hide his true intentions.","dt":"2024-02-29T13:02:20","s":["gefwk9z6rc"]}],"25":[{"m":"And this promise they kept... It’s interesting how this instruction was carried on from generation to generation without losing it until they departed from Egypt 🇪🇬.","dt":"2026-01-30T06:41:19","s":["rhcuzsc7fe"]}],"26":[{"m":"Oh, details were not given as to how grand his burial was.\n\nSee how Jacob was buried ⚰ in grand style that the children of Canaan noticed. How much more the Zaphnath-paaneah.","dt":"2024-02-29T13:04:23","s":["1vge7oqa3d"]}],"11":[{"m":"The man was indeed very great.\nJacob the swindler, now Israel the prince.","dt":"2026-01-30T06:36:47","s":["vmljabtex4"]}],"13":[{"m":"Israel kept good records because they were on a mission, a mission that transcended generations, so each generation carried the mantle.\n\nPeople did not just get up and do what they liked and lived vain and separate lives.\n\nNo, there was always someone who championed the cause, and of course God ensured the preservation of the nation so the vision was not lost.\n\nThese people kept such accurate records, and even up to now they have such a strong sense of history — the average Jew.","dt":"2024-02-29T12:57:24","s":["lc5pfk53dz"]}]},"9":{"2":[{"m":"Unlike the children of Israel who were to take the promised land little by little so the beasts did not overtake them,\n\nNoah and his family received the protection of the lord in that the fear 😱 of them fell on the beasts.\n\nGod uses different strategies at different times.\n\nWe are not to be presumptuous and get ahead of him.","dt":"2024-01-06T09:47:32","s":["0l9ews0jdx"]}],"24":[{"m":"This is one of the mysteries of writings.\n\nHidden in these words is what Ham did.\n\nWe are told he saw his father's nakedness.\n\nBut what is wrong with that, especially considering he told his older brothers and they covered their father.\n\nWhat ham did was more than accidentally chance upon his father.\n\nThere was more to it that we are not told but left to our imagination.\n\nThat is the beauty of scripture and of writings.\n\nI believe that with enough meditation 🧘‍♂️, one can extract the hidden meaning of what Ham really did.","dt":"2024-01-06T09:51:16","s":["h30190uaf4"]}]}},"Matthew":{"1":{"17":[{"m":"14 generations to Jesus, but Jesus had no generations after him as prophesied; rather he chose adoption and truly adopted us all into his family.\n\nBeing born again in him. We are his generation.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:09:38","s":["cabddba3dd"]}],"20":[{"m":"Why was the appearance to Joseph through a dream, but to Mary was a physical angelic 😇 manifestation?\n\nI guess 'cos varying degrees of faith are required for different messages.\n\nTo get pregnant 🤰 as a virgin and you were told that through a dream??\n\nNo, to cement the truth and divinity of it required more tangible evidence, hence Angel Gabriel was sent.\n\nAlso, this was the birth of God's Son; such a VIP message required a heavy dignitary like Gabriel.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:14:59","s":["c2c895f341"]}],"25":[{"m":"Only God knows the shame and mockery Mary experienced.\n\nAs well Joseph, for accepting to take Mary home when everyone knew the child was not his.\n\nWow.\n\nThis must have been some very difficult times for them. Who was going to believe such a cock 🐓 and bull 🐮 story?\n\nSo they suffered in silence 🤫.\n\nCould that have accounted for Joseph's absence in the entire New Testament during Jesus's ministry years? Or he died 😕","dt":"2022-10-02T07:16:36","s":["skl0u2ha6t","ee85ee70e1"]}],"16":[{"m":"Joseph is connected to Jesus only via adoption — there is truly no biological or generational connection.\n\nThis goes to show that one adopted is truly family.","dt":"2025-01-13T07:47:54","s":["2vgq85yqhu"]}]},"2":{"2":[{"m":"To be able to tell the signs of the Christ being born, indeed they were wise men.\n\nSame for Simeon and Anna.\n\nWith such wisdom one is able to position oneself strategically.","dt":"2022-10-04T04:14:37","s":["76ug9bdqvz"]},{"m":"Of all kings born, why did the wise men come to King 👑 Jesus alone?\n\nThere was something they had seen.\n\nAnd they, as a matter of urgency, needed to secure their peace and show their allegiance to the new king 👑.\n\nThey saw something; likely they saw this King of the Jews was going to rule the whole world with a rod of iron.\n\nAnd being wise men, they secured their slot 🎰 of peace with him.\n\nNote they came to worship 🛐 him. Does that not point to the fact that they saw his kingdom to be everlasting?\n\nA God-man 👨🏿 had been born. They knew it.\n\nIndeed they were wise men.\n\nMatthew 2:1-2 NKJV\nNow after Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea in the days of Herod the king, behold, wise men from the East came to Jerusalem, saying, “Where is He who has been born King of the Jews? For we have seen His star in the East and have come to worship Him.”","dt":"2023-01-12T07:29:50","s":["8y6eg7ohxh","g34v2j1vjg"]}],"3":[{"m":"Yes, indeed these politicians would be troubled.\n\nThey know what it is like for a new king 👑 to come and overthrow another.\n\nThey needed to preserve their lot.\n\nThis also shows how much faith Joseph and Mary had, and the weight of responsibility on them.\n\nKnowing they carried the one to overthrow the thrones.","dt":"2023-01-12T07:36:44","s":["a6cd25446c"]},{"m":"Many a time we underestimate the weight 🏋️ of responsibility that was carried by Mary and Joseph in accepting to carry Jesus the Christ.\n\nThere was a sitting and reigning king 👑.\n\nHerod by name, and he was no generous king.\n\nHe was not ready to lose his throne and his entire lineage to another.\n\nYou can see the degree of his wickedness and what Mary and Joseph were coming against by his willingness to kill innocent children just to get to Jesus.\n\nNo wonder the Bible says often that Mary kept all these things in her heart ♥.\n\nAnd Jesus did not disappoint, he was a","dt":"2023-01-27T04:20:33","s":["70d5ic5na1"]},{"m":"Herod was troubled? And all Jerusalem with her.\nI mean the ruling class and all who had interest and benefited one way from the throne or another.\n\nThis must have been quite a number of people, just as we see today.\n\nA lot of people benefit from affiliating with the ruling class, and politicians for that matter.\n\nThe birth of a new king meant a lot politically, and in their time it does not take a lifetime to rule.\n\nThere were kings who ruled by the time they were eight years or 12, as we see in the book of Kings.\n\nHerod indeed had cause to be worried, and all Jerusalem with him.","dt":"2025-01-15T17:36:14","s":["t3z3mgljh3"]}],"9":[{"m":"Was the star a moving star 🌟 or something?","dt":"2022-10-04T06:51:55","s":["dfd7ea3922"]}],"11":[{"m":"I wonder how they, the parents, felt about all these strange visits and sayings.\n\nThey immediately knew he was no ordinary child 🧒.\n\nThe Lord was confirming their faith.","dt":"2022-10-04T06:52:53","s":["7ddbc906h5"]}],"13":[{"m":"Joseph, being head, was the one God spoke to as head.","dt":"2022-10-04T06:52:36","s":["v8jislers4"]}]},"3":{"11":[{"m":"Things had changed, there seems to be something pending.\nWhich prophet comes preaching about another prophet who was to come after him?\n\nA shift had happened, and though he baptized, he knew it was in preparation for the one.\n\nThese were strange times indeed.\n\nAgain, later they sent to ask if he was the Messiah, to which he denied. Where did such rumors gain grounds?\n\nLikely because 30 years back rumors about this wonder child had been spreading and gradually gaining grounds.\n\nThe events of the magi, the shepherds, though long ago, had gained some traction.\n\nAside the fact that there was a general expectation of the Messiah as prophesied in Daniel.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:21:04","s":["t8tcmowhbm"]}],"12":[{"m":"The time had come, that prince who was prophesied about had come, and now more specifics will be unveiled...\n\nWe were given some details in verses and chapters in the OT; now here we are, we shall see the full manifestations.\n\nAh, so we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father.\n\nFull 🌕 of grace and truth.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:25:48","s":["reir9ons8i"]}],"15":[{"m":"The first words of Jesus in Matthew... He was now of full age.\n\nThe devil 👿 was in trouble.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:26:58","s":["nfr2mdaqkr"]},{"m":"Men of the Spirit, men of wisdom. Anybody standing by and listening 👂 would wonder what these two ✌️ are talking about.\n\nJohn is baptising, he sees Jesus and says, no, I can't baptise you, you baptise me.\n\nAnd they seem to understand why John would make an unusual request.\n\nThis was John's territory and he was the Baptist, so why would he make such requests — a bystander would ask.\n\nNow things get weirder when Jesus responds like, permit it to be so for now, you know we have an arrangement from the dateless past.\n\nHaving said that, there was no more arguing.\n\nJohn goes ahead and baptises him. What were these two talking about? They've never met, so what fulfillment of all righteousness was that?\n\nThe way of the Spirit is the way of wisdom.","dt":"2023-01-12T07:51:01","s":["qi2iqjtd44"]}],"3":[{"m":"Prophecy prophecy prophecy, I searched where exactly in Isaiah and the Old Testament that this was written, and it says:\n\nIsaiah 40:3-5\nThe voice of him that crieth in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the LORD,\nmake straight in the desert a highway for our God.\n4 Every valley shall be exalted,\nand every mountain and hill shall be made low:\nand the crooked shall be made straight,\nand the rough places plain:\n5 And the glory of the LORD shall be revealed,\nand all flesh shall see it together:\nfor the mouth of the LORD hath spoken it.\n\nThe Dake's commentary provides an additional scripture in Malachi 3:1:\n\nMalachi 3:1\nBehold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me:\nand the Lord, whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple,\neven the messenger of the covenant, whom ye delight in:\nbehold, he shall come, saith the LORD of hosts.\n\nWhat amazes me is that in just this one verse is a period of over 2000 years.\n\n2000 years between “Behold, I will send my messenger” and “the Lord whom you seek shall suddenly come to his temple”,\n\ntalking of the end times when Christ appears.\n\nThis makes me realise that the books of prophecy, for example Revelation, might have many events happen not written down, or written down but miles apart in their time zone, except where the time is explicitly given.\n\nBut even where timing of events are given, there might be gaps of time not made mention of.\n\nWe have to be very humble and sober whenever we try to predict future events using scripture.\n\nOur firm assurance is that in the fullness of time all things shall align as written.\n\nFor there shall not one jot of the scripture be left unfulfilled.\n\nHeaven and earth shall pass away, but God's word abides forever.","dt":"2025-01-23T07:50:52","s":["kyez303o56"]}],"13":[{"m":"Ah... Then came Jesus...","dt":"2022-10-04T08:26:06","s":["g9yrmqg924"]}]},"4":{"2":[{"m":"I wonder what his prayer topics were at this fasting period.","dt":"2022-10-05T06:04:32","s":["rneftyz8zi"]},{"m":"It is worth noting that Jesus took on the whole cohort of hell by himself, literally.\n\nHe had no prayer partners or support, except his disciples, but we know their input... Very little, if any.\n\nHe forsook home and the jeering of family 👪 to pursue the call.","dt":"2022-10-05T06:06:42","s":["519b5fywex"]}],"6":[{"m":"Questions rise to mind:\n1. What is there about “it is written”, i.e. what is there about the word? — It is the tool, and the true authoritative tool, to govern life.\n\nThat was how Jesus governed his life, and the devils recognize its Power.\n\nGoing contrary to it is what opens doors to devils. 👿\n\nAlso, even the devil quoted “it is written”, so the fact that it is in the Bible does not mean it cannot be twisted.\n\nThis reminds me of some hyper-grace people who sin and quote a scripture on grace.\n\nThey have placed themselves in hearing view of the devil 👿, and he's quoting scriptures to support the flesh.","dt":"2022-10-05T06:18:36","s":["hp17v9x6m5"]}],"8":[{"m":"The devil took Jesus.\n\nSo we can have encounters and spiritual experiences orchestrated by the devil 👿","dt":"2022-10-05T06:33:54","s":["q6tfee0cp8"]}],"9":[{"m":"Once again the devil exposes himself.\n\nIt is worship he wants. The same Godlike traits he desired which led to his fall...\n\nHe's at it again.","dt":"2022-10-05T06:38:46","s":["45sbtmkakc"]}],"11":[{"m":"Where were these angels all this while? They were kept at bay, watching till the temptation was over.\n\nLord, have mercy on us. May we pass the tests of life. For that is what they are... TESTS","dt":"2022-10-05T06:35:04","s":["djgiv4ge5e"]}],"13":[{"m":"He dwelt there. Not he passed through there or spent some days there.\n\nSo this was where his home was now based. And this was in fulfillment of prophecy; no wonder the ancients, in seeing this, knew the city was blessed for such a privilege.","dt":"2025-01-25T10:46:50","s":["p4df8i9ura"]}],"19":[{"m":"Jesus was just a walking miracle; everywhere he went he was performing miracles, so much so that sometimes the writers overlooked his miracles, however amazing they were, and moved on straight to the point,\n\nlest they risk overloading their readers and missing the intent of the writing or that particular passage.\n\nThis passage in Luke tells a different story, one of a catch of fish 🐠, so much so that their ship 🚢 began to sink.\n\nThen when Jesus tells them to follow, it made sense that they did.\n\nBecause if they knew nothing of him, why would they leave their thriving business to follow him?\n\nNo wonder John says Jesus's miracles were not all recorded, in order to save the volumes.","dt":"2025-06-23T08:28:40","s":["9estgh5rjh"]}],"20":[{"m":"Was this not after he had performed the miracle of fish 🐠 without number?","dt":"2023-01-12T07:57:42","s":["mar3dtjuqm"]}],"4":[{"m":"Because man is spirit, soul and body... There is part of us that needs for bread 🥪 of the word of God.\n\nWithout which we are malnourished.","dt":"2023-01-12T07:53:42","s":["59e5hg03cq"]}],"7":[{"m":"The moment you quote and govern your life and decisions by “it is written”, you are recognizing and activating the laws and powers of God set up to rule the world 🗺.\n\nThese laws keep us as men.","dt":"2022-10-05T06:19:52","s":["cw4lxlxnrf"]}],"10":[{"m":"I was wondering why didn't Jesus just say \"NO\" at the request of Satan.\n\nA simple no on all his requests, because you know nothing good can come out of the devil 👿, but rather he stuck to the word.\n\nThe word, I believe, is like a barricade and weapon against the onslaught of the enemy. It is the sword of the Spirit.\n\nAfter three “it is writtens”, the devil was driven away.\n\n\"No\" alone would not be effective. The devil 👿 will keep hammering 🛠 till the flesh gives in.\n\nBut with “it is written”, he knows you are countering with a weapon 🔫, you have a base for your position.","dt":"2022-10-05T06:27:24","s":["d88qqu4i6s"]}]},"5":{"33":[{"m":"Other versions say swear falsely.","dt":"2023-01-13T08:34:59","s":["8xcs2fwj8y"]}],"40":[{"m":"If they take your inner cloth or covering, add your outer coat as well 🧥.\n\nCheck the Strong's definition of these words.","dt":"2023-01-13T08:37:05","s":["qbdkkyco4s"]}],"44":[{"m":"They despitefully use you, knowing you are good and, per your belief and practice in the faith, certain things you cannot do.\n\nThey know you cannot take revenge because your Lord has commanded you to leave vengeance for him.\n\nSo they take advantage and ravage you. Pray for them.\n\nIt doesn't mean you should hand yourself to them if you can avoid them, but pray for them 🙏... Pray 🙏","dt":"2023-01-13T08:40:19","s":["a4jeku6ygk"]}],"12":[{"m":"If you suffer persecution for my sake, it is akin to how the prophets of old suffered persecution for the sake of God.\n\nWere they even listening to what Jesus was saying?\n\nIn many ways, and not so subtle at times, Jesus showed he was more than a prophet and more than their perception of who the Messiah was.\n\nHe showed and said many things reserved for God. Not even angels took such attributes upon themselves, except the fallen ones who desire to be God and are thus so called by other beliefs.","dt":"2025-02-18T08:08:27","s":["lv5pso5xju"]}],"17":[{"m":"Jesus made this statement because he knew the things he was about to say might sound controversial and could be misconstrued, and so he clears the air and right after goes to establish his doctrine.\n\nHe began to unpack the law in the light of God's true nature and intentions.","dt":"2025-06-23T08:32:09","s":["a800kwuaku"]}],"31":[{"m":"On the issue of marriage and the conditions under which divorce takes place, a number of awkward scenarios come to mind.\nWhat happens if your spouse, for some reason best known to him/her, chooses to leave you, and despite all appeals and attempts at making her/him stay, the person leaves? Are you free to marry?\nIf your spouse becomes very abusive, even to the point of danger to one's life, what happens? Separation may take place, but is one justified to divorce and remarry?\nYour spouse for some crime goes to prison for a life tenure or some very long jail sentence. Are you permitted to divorce and remarry?\nErr, let me give the final one: your spouse dies from sickness, in war, or becomes a prisoner of war in a foreign country...\nCould all these be exceptions to the rule, kind of...","dt":null,"s":["6b7a5321c1"]}],"45":[{"m":"So you will be like your Father.\n\nThis is the way of God... So he said we are gods, and all of us children of the Most High, but we shall die like mere men...\n\nIf we forfeit the path and way of deity. Love, forgive and pray for all. Doing good to both good and evil alike.","dt":"2023-01-13T09:47:22","s":["f1ikiiv0kn"]}]},"6":{"1":[{"m":"Oh nice, so there is reward in giving of alms.\n\nWhat is that reward actually?\n\nIn the Old Testament we know God would pour out his blessings.\n\nI do believe the same blessings continue to apply.","dt":"2023-01-13T10:54:29","s":["fseg7do3lj"]}],"7":[{"m":"That is a difficult one, not so much the stopping of vain repetitions as the thinking that one shall be heard for your much speaking.","dt":"2023-01-13T12:55:02","s":["ces1ff99sz"]}],"9":[{"m":"In other accounts the disciples ask Jesus to teach them how to pray, then the Lord's Prayer comes after that.\n\nLuke 11:2","dt":"2023-01-13T12:58:08","s":["788k5wrp4e"]}]},"7":{"6":[{"m":"They learn that you are easy prey, for you trusted them to thrust that which is precious to them.\n\nMeaning you trust them.\n\nNot only are they going to despise what was given them, but would turn against you to your hurt.","dt":"2023-01-13T11:54:25","s":["gr11mwz8uy"]}],"11":[{"m":"So ask, seek and knock was in reference to asking the Father in prayer, and not to asking in general or to life.\n\nOf course some of it may apply to life, but contextually this was in prayer.","dt":"2023-01-13T11:52:01","s":["2c3h430mec"]}],"23":[{"m":"These sayings of Jesus were uttered in a particular context and must be applied in that context.\n\nVery important.\n\nBecause this verse does not mean miracles, signs and wonders are not approved of God; no, in this context these miracle workers were described as people who worked iniquity.\n\nThe supernatural signs they did were not denied, but in addition to it, they worked iniquity.\n\nAll men err, but not in this case; these people practiced iniquity.\n\nWe see in later scriptures Jesus mentioning signs and wonders as part of the proof of those who believe in him.","dt":"2022-10-12T14:40:46","s":["2379gkir3n"]}],"29":[{"m":"Of course 🏇 Of course... No one ever spake as he did.","dt":"2022-10-12T14:42:58","s":["dd4yczzuqt"]}]},"8":{"1":[{"m":"Jesus was a walking mass of authority and power; he comes down from the mountain after such power-packed teachings and men began to worship him.\n\nThe leper worships him and prays him for healing. Jesus heals him.\n\nRight after, a centurion, a man amongst men who commanded a 100 strong men, came pleading with him to heal his servant.\n\nYes, Jesus was and is King of kings, and he demonstrated that here in the earth.\n\nNow we look at his story and many men desire his authority, Power and anointing, and go back empty.\n\nWhy should God give such authority to men just because we read it in his book, the holy scriptures?\n\nIf men were given the authority of Christ, and to demonstrate it in full measure, men would require to be worshipped.\n\nYes, Jesus himself promised that this power was for all who believe, but why should he give it to men who were unworthy and who would trample it under foot?\n\nJust look at our world today, the little power we have and make ourselves God.\n\nSad, but till we as believers subject ourselves truly to God and to his Spirit, we will wait for a real long whiles to see the power of the Christ demonstrated in our world today.","dt":"2025-06-23T08:39:52","s":["5lqdxs6q12"]}],"13":[{"m":"As thou has believed.\nIn other words, what and how you believe is what and how it will happen to you.\n\nIt's not just what you believe, but you can actually determine how what you believe should turn out for your good.","dt":"2023-01-14T01:56:56","s":["nr5t4ai4m4"]},{"m":"The centurion was a man of power and knew how to communicate with men of power — he spoke boldly and truly what he believed, but was not pompous or high-minded about it.\n\nBecause scripture says he beseeched Jesus, meaning he started off with pleading and respect and all humility before stating his opinion.\n\nThat is a lesson right there about speaking to authority and getting results.\n\nThose with power love men who are bold but know their limits and give utmost respect as due.","dt":"2025-06-23T08:44:09","s":["hgni6vpftw"]}],"17":[{"m":"It seems, on observation, when it comes to healing and answered prayer, that\n\nthere are some constants and some prerogatives.\n\nTo man belongs the constants, and to God belongs the prerogatives.\n\nIt is a constant to pray,\nto have faith, and\nto continue in belief for God to answer prayers,\n\nand it is the prerogative of God to answer when all these are met, or to not answer despite these constants being met.\n\nIt is also God's prerogative, despite the constants, to heal and answer prayers without them being met.\n\nI.e. where people just say they were healed in a meeting though they did not expect nor believe it.\n\nThe above is not doctrine but my observation, very much subject to change and truth.\n\nHaving said this, some individuals get more results and certainty of answers to prayer than others, and that on the basis of having established a strong relationship with the Lord.\n\nJust like Moses, who could even tell God whose prayer to answer and whose to reject.\n\nMoses knew God, and vice versa. He knew God beyond writings, to the point of a one-on-one personal relationship.\n\nAnd yet even with him, he was not always guaranteed answers. But he knew how to move the hand of God to secure answers.","dt":"2025-06-23T09:04:08","s":["066hfbou1y"]}],"18":[{"m":"It seems Jesus was just wary. Of men, he did not trust man.\n\nWhenever it seems crowds are gathering, he just smartly moves on.\n\nWhen they want to keep him at a place, he relocates.","dt":"2021-12-15T09:33:49","s":["dcptlfbcvh"]}],"20":[{"m":"Jesus, I believe, here was helping the people count the cost of following him.\n\nHe wanted the scribe to know that it was not all healing and miracles. There was a price to pay of homelessness 🏡 and danger. In peril of the weather. Etc.","dt":"2021-12-15T09:31:19","s":["ur5z47gq2m"]}],"22":[{"m":"Another price to pay. Many things you cannot participate in.","dt":"2021-12-15T09:32:00","s":["neg2tjrwgw"]},{"m":"Why did Jesus deny one and yet accepted another...\nIs that where the call comes in?\n\nOne was called and chosen and another was not?","dt":"2023-01-14T02:06:29","s":["ohgcx29wsr"]},{"m":"I have often wondered why Jesus would refuse one who wanted to follow him wholeheartedly in one breath, and yet turn in the next and compel another who had a genuine reason to defer commitment to the right time.\n\nI have often wondered about this, and as I read this passage today I wondered the same thing; then a thought 💭 came to mind to read the passage again, but more carefully this time...\n\nAs I did, I realized the following...\n\n1. Do you realize that Jesus never denied the scribe or prevented the scribe from following him... No, Jesus did not, just read it carefully.\n\nHe did not, but rather he cautioned him that it was not as rosy a journey as it seems on the surface — it was a journey of many sleepless nights, and indeed many nights spent in the open fields because of nowhere to lay one's head 🤕.\n\nHe was forewarning him of what the journey to follow him really entailed.\n\nYes, there were miracles, many great miracles; yes, there were signs and wonders and the foretaste of the kingdom, but there were also many great trials that can cause one to be offended, wounded and to fall off... Jesus was forewarning him.\n\nTo the second, he was:\n\n1. Already a disciple of Jesus, so we can assume he knew the cost, especially since Jesus had just raised the challenges of following him, and yet this disciple was willing to follow him.\n\nHowever, this disciple had an urgent family 👪 responsibility of burying his own father in honour and respect, as commanded by the law.\n\nHere Jesus teaches this disciple the second lesson... We must deny many things and people and pleasures to follow Jesus.\n\nIncluding family — he was not teaching negligence of family and children, but priorities — the dead should bury the dead, but to them that are alive and have the light of life and the Son of righteousness with them, nothing was worth exchanging time for...\n\nEspecially the dead whose time was past.\n\nIn both cases Jesus taught lessons and left the decision to them.\n\nOf course we can say one was compelled to follow and the other discouraged... But that in no way makes it easier for the disciple than the scribe...\n\nThey both had a hard decision to make... We are not told their choices though...\n\nWhat do you think they chose?","dt":"2025-02-02T15:06:40","s":["kvrw3weqmh"]}],"25":[{"m":"Who does that, who cries to another man to save them?\n\nNormally men in such a situation of life and death cry out to God, or their gods, as was the case of Jonah.\n\nNo man goes crying to another man for salvation in such matters.\n\nIn fact, when you cry out to God in such instances, you are pleading for mercy, knowing very well that he may or may not save you.\n\nBut here was a man — God in the flesh — who by all means will save when cried out to.\n\nIt was not a matter of he may or may not. It was a matter of he will save them.\n\nOh, such surety to have God in the flesh — Jesus Christ.\n\nAnd when he left, he left us a promise that as sure as he was with us, and we could count on him even in such dire times, he was sending us another like himself — even the Holy Spirit.\n\nSo why then are we not experiencing the Holy Spirit like the way the disciples experienced Jesus?\n\nOne of the reasons is that he is spirit and not flesh — and that is our limitation — relating to spirit.\n\nWe fail many times in such respect; many, many times the flesh excels than the spirit.\n\nAnd even when the Spirit forewarns us or guides us, we are negligent and thus unable to yield.\n\nI think that is the main deal and limitation — for instance, Jesus at every instance could heal any sickness and disease using different techniques; how does he know what to do in each situation?\n\nBy the guidance of the Holy Spirit. For some he laid hands, others he asked to go wash in a pool, and yet others he just spoke.\n\nBy knowing the mind and will of the Spirit, he is able to produce results.\n\nI will not be presumptuous to think that is the only reason for our failure to walk in constant power and victory, but I believe that is a major reason.","dt":"2025-02-04T08:25:13","s":["14pepdz005"]}],"26":[{"m":"Funny, but Jesus actually expected his disciples to know better.\n\nHe's like, why disturb me over this matter, why are you so frantic... as you of all people should have known better.","dt":"2021-12-15T09:37:01","s":["kd6b3nkb5j"]}],"4":[{"m":"As a testimony to who? To the priests, because according to the law of Moses, the priest examines people who have recovered from their illness and declares them clean.\n\nSo the priests and Co kept receiving testimony after testimony, and by their own mouths 👄 💋 declaring and authenticating the miracles of Jesus, yet they did not believe.\n\nNo wonder Jesus made this statement...\n\nJohn 15:23-25 KJV\nHe that hateth me hateth my Father also. [24] If I had not done among them the works which none other man did, they had not had sin: but now have they both seen and hated both me and my Father. [25] But this cometh to pass, that the word might be fulfilled that is written in their law, They hated me without a cause.","dt":"2021-12-15T09:24:32","s":["7eko9cot9l"]}]},"9":{"8":[{"m":"Yes, to men, but Jesus was no ordinary man 👨. Was Jesus even a man?","dt":"2021-12-16T21:51:48","s":["l0z61c7bw3"]}],"9":[{"m":"Jesus, the rabbi whose fame had spread far and near, now calls to this \"sinful\" tax collector. And immediately he heeds to the call 🤙.\n\nIs this how it happened, or it took a while for Matthew to warm up into the role of a disciple?\n\nI think it happened as stated. Jesus calls Matthew, and what a great privilege to follow such a man of God.\n\nMatthew saw the blessedness of the calling and heeded. I can imagine Matthew looking at Jesus as he passed with such a glow in his eyes 👀; Matthew's eyes 👀 sparkled ✨ with admiration of this prophet whom some believed was the Messiah.\n\nAs he passed, Matthew watched. Ah, alas he can catch 🤼‍♂️ a glimpse close up of Jesus. That wonderful man from Nazareth.\n\nThen to his amazement Jesus inches closer. This can't be happening 😊. He really is passing this close to my collector's booth.\n\nSuddenly he stops and says 👄 \"Follow me\". What, did I hear right...? But then Jesus is not moving either, looking straight at Matthew with such love 😍, he nods his head.\n\nYes, follow me, his smile ☺ seems to say. So I heard right. Oh, this can't be happening, and like in the case of Zacchaeus: tonight I will be dining in your house 🏡","dt":"2021-12-16T22:15:11","s":["ly9kj6yu95"]}],"11":[{"m":"What were Pharisees doing in Matthew's house 🏡? I understand the many tax collectors and sinners were Matthew's friends.\n\nBut the Pharisees, who invited them? And why did it seem they were everywhere Jesus was, including in people's homes?\n\nIt's likely this was a party 🎉 opened to all. And Jesus present in anyone's home naturally drew crowds.\n\nAnd the Pharisees, I guess, invited themselves in.\nThey had become like the custodians of the traditions of the fathers.\n\nAnd Jesus was just messing their theology up and winning 🥇 the common people over. They just hated it.","dt":"2021-12-16T22:22:13","s":["jvpz3ir5wr"]},{"m":"Again, all of scripture is within a certain context.\n\nThis does not mean men of God should go about eating in the houses of sinners because Jesus did so.\n\nIt's all within a context, and the context must be understood in order not to misapply the holy scriptures.\n\nThis is very important.","dt":"2022-10-12T14:54:29","s":["e1q27j8n4r"]}],"13":[{"m":"What a punch 👊.\n\nGo and learn paa. Sometimes, in fact many times, as we read the Bible we miss the import of what is being said because we just glance.\n\nI mean, these are teachers of the law ⚖, scribes et al. And Jesus makes a statement that they should go and learn. What a 👊. They just hated Jesus some more after this, I believe.\n\nJesus actually took that verse from Hos 6:6... Now this raises another question 🙋 or observation — Jesus was well-versed in the scriptures. He read them and memorised his own words/scripture.","dt":"2021-12-17T04:07:05","s":["hrc8n2azvd"]},{"m":"This verse seems akin to the scripture that talks about the kind of fast God requires:\n\nIsaiah 58:6 KJV\nIs not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke?\n\nSo also, sacrifices are important, but mercy really is what God requires.","dt":"2022-10-12T14:57:48","s":["ezicv3s7tr"]}],"19":[{"m":"We are fake... All Jesus required of men was to have faith that he could heal, and based often on the people's own faith, Jesus healed them.\n\nAlways.\n\nHowever, in our days and times, the people come to us with their needs, trusting the anointing upon our lives we have so often made reference to.\n\nAnd many times we fail to deliver. Indeed, most times for most acclaimed men of God.\n\nWe are so fake 😤 😒 🙄 😔 😪 😑 😤","dt":"2025-02-19T06:17:50","s":["g7js3d3z5t"]}],"22":[{"m":"Matthew's account makes it sound like the woman intended to touch Jesus's garment, and just when she did, Jesus turns around and proclaims healing and wholeness to her.\n\nBut this is not the full story. Matthew sums it up beautifully, whiles the other accounts give us the details.","dt":"2022-10-12T15:01:00","s":["x2uqt2wgmd"]},{"m":"Matthew's account gives the impression of the woman getting healed after Jesus had turned because of her touch and told her her faith had made her whole.\n\nBut other accounts fill in the gaps and bring the meaning out clearer.\n\nThat is, the woman got her own healing when she touched the hem of his garment.\n\nSo strong was the power that Jesus noticed virtue had gone out of him.","dt":"2023-01-14T08:11:03","s":["ly5je7nrss"]}],"28":[{"m":"Which house 🏡, or rather whose?? Is it Matthew's still, or Peter's?","dt":"2021-12-16T22:28:12","s":["c8th3ysju1"]}],"29":[{"m":"I believe the blind men following Jesus all the way to the house was to test their faith and readiness to be healed.\n\nHow blind men can follow a man all the way home... They likely had helpers, I guess.","dt":"2022-10-12T15:05:56","s":["3z9achuyv4"]}],"33":[{"m":"No mention of devils being cast out is mentioned in the old scriptures.\n\nThen comes Jesus, and suddenly devils 👿 are manifesting and being cast out everywhere.\n\nWhat happened, what changed?? 😳\n\nWhy was this never mentioned before?\n\nAnd even the people themselves confirmed that it was never so seen in Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nSo what was happening? It seemed devils 👿 possessed people, but no one knew what to do about it effectively.","dt":"2022-10-12T15:09:32","s":["pi2vhiywmz"]}],"36":[{"m":"Jesus was so unconventional, crowds did not move him. Fame and popularity he avoided, and when he healed the sick 🤮 he hid it.\n\nI know in that light ☀ it is easy to draw comparisons with now, where we advertise miracles and draw crowds by them.\n\nBut let's not forget the times and dispensations. Jesus at this time was a Lamb, yet to be slain.\n\nIt was not time to reign as king, yet the people wanted to make him king 👑.\n\nNot to mention how the very leaders sought to kill him.\n\nHe had to bide his time wisely. Not to attract attention or do anything before the time.\n\nBut after he rose up from the dead, he himself gave command to make disciples of the whole world 🗺, and the whole world we will disciple into truth.","dt":"2021-12-17T04:51:56","s":["ypviy5x982"]}],"38":[{"m":"Why did Jesus ignore them? A commentary I was reading online said so he could enter into the secret place of his home and heal them without the crowds.\n\nSome commentaries also say it was to build/try their faith.","dt":"2021-12-17T04:43:41","s":["dzcb7q2ccv"]},{"m":"Yes, more labourers like himself into the field, hence the disciples and hence ministry callings.\n\nAnd yet today we say we can't fulfill our calling because we are hindered by system in churches, or men of God so called not willing to release their members etc.\n\nStrange times indeed. Strange times. Let's take advantage of whatever resource God has given us 🙏 in diverse ways to spread the word of the kingdom.","dt":"2022-10-12T15:13:12","s":["dnp72xwqtb"]}],"14":[{"m":"Wei nyinaa Y3 asem, as we would say in Ghana. Did they feel that if Jesus was indeed the Christ, he ought to be more spiritual?\n\nSeems so. Jesus and his followers were too carnal. Yet in this carnality he got results that none other did get.\n\nHe 🧗‍♂️ graciously gave them a good answer.","dt":"2021-12-17T04:18:49","s":["dt1bq3oohe"]}],"18":[{"m":"He believed God enough that he is able to raise the dead.\n\nWhy can't we believe God enough for some things? Lord, help me... Help us.","dt":"2023-01-14T08:05:38","s":["jiwno39k7p"]}],"34":[{"m":"😼 😏\n\nThey were just seeking opportunity to discredit him.","dt":"2021-12-16T22:26:02","s":["axnnpo5g0y"]}]},"10":{"1":[{"m":"How did he achieve that? H😕w did he give them the power... Was it by verbal impartation, like after his resurrection when he imparted the Holy Ghost and spirit of understanding the scripture?","dt":"2021-12-18T13:56:08","s":["v79bj4fyg4"]}],"17":[{"m":"He was prepping them up for the woes of ministry.\n\nOccupational hazards. This did not happen at this time, but it happened to them all after he had left...\n\nThe Spirit took over the job of reminding them of what Jesus had said.","dt":"2023-01-14T09:59:32","s":["49uaph8wi3"]}]},"11":{"3":[{"m":"You can't really fault John. I don't think he knew that the Christ was to suffer, die, resurrect and come back after 2000 years to come reign 🙄😱.\n\nWho can know such things?","dt":"2021-12-17T07:24:52","s":["1vmcu43mdi"]}],"12":[{"m":"The kingdom of God is being violently attacked, to hinder it and stop it if possible, but equally violent people are seizing it and advancing it.","dt":"2021-12-17T07:44:01","s":["92sk53soyq"]}],"26":[{"m":"This again shows the wisdom of God and the offense of the gospel.\n\nIf the wise and prudent, rulers and authorities had the gospel revealed to them, things would have churned out pretty differently; obviously the crucifixion would not have happened.\n\nJohn will definitely be out of prison and not offended.\n\nBut no, so are the ways of God.","dt":"2021-12-17T07:49:56","s":["3lshgsrtck"]}],"5":[{"m":"Here also Luke's account says he worked miracles and then told them to go tell John what they see, the blind receive their sight etc.\n\nSo the different accounts complement each other.\n\nLuke 7:21 KJV\nAnd in that same hour he cured many of their infirmities and plagues, and of evil spirits; and unto many that were blind he gave sight.","dt":"2023-01-14T10:08:31","s":["ixuk6z89uv"]}]},"12":{"10":[{"m":"These people just had a set of religious law which they had a blanket application of, without first understanding the law and the moral and spirit of the law.\n\nIn so doing they ended up misapplying the law.\n\nIndeed they were hypocrites, because they were subjective in their application of the law when it suited them.","dt":"2022-10-09T06:08:33","s":["ohcsx1cjn9"]},{"m":"Luke 6:7,9 KJV\nAnd the scribes and Pharisees watched him, whether he would heal on the sabbath day; that they might find an accusation against him.\n\nIn Matthew's account the leaders asked Jesus if it's lawful to heal on the Sabbath.\n\nAnd in Luke's account Jesus answers that question by asking them a question 🙋 as well.\n\n[9] Then said Jesus unto them, I will ask you one thing; Is it lawful on the sabbath days to do good, or to do evil? to save life, or to destroy it?\n\nTo which they hypocritically failed to answer.\n\nOf course Jesus heals the man.","dt":"2023-01-14T13:36:09","s":["9f8wbmab9p"]}],"14":[{"m":"Ah, these Pharisees. I do not understand them.\n\nIf a thing as simple as healing cannot be done on the Sabbath, then what can?\n\nSo they walk on the Sabbath? Yes. Do they eat? Yes. Do they swing their arms when walking 🚶? Yes.\n\nBut the sick cannot stretch forth those same hands 👐 and receive healing...\n\nIt was just a spirit of envy and jealousy that had filled their hearts to the point of wanting to kill.\n\nThe heart ♥ of man can be so wicked.","dt":"2021-12-16T07:41:18","s":["jdsy1phjvl"]}],"15":[{"m":"Lord, when will we again experience such? When all are healed.","dt":"2021-12-16T07:42:44","s":["pxmh4x8uwy"]},{"m":"He healed them all —\nNot he healed some.\nAlso take note of the fact that this was not some few people, but rather great multitudes who came with their sick and unwell, and he healed them all.\n\nOh God, when are we going to have such crusades?\n\nGreat healings taking place and all sick being healed.","dt":"2025-02-17T06:45:03","s":["wglwr4fsl3"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh, for such a great crowd I can only imagine the diversity of miracles that took place.\n\nAll manner of ailments must have been present in such a great crowd, and yet he healed them all.\n\nLittle wonder the apostle John says if all the things he did were written down, there would not be enough books to contain them.","dt":"2025-02-17T07:53:09","s":["m6vg1ftbu6"]}],"23":[{"m":"These leaders were devils 👿 themselves.\n\nJust when the people were beginning to realise that this could be the Messiah, the long-awaited King who did works that none other did do,\n\nthe Pharisees tried distorting their viewpoint with lies 🤥.\n\nJesus was apt to counter them.","dt":"2023-01-14T13:42:13","s":["5zxufzh23u"]}],"28":[{"m":"The kingdom of God is come to you. The battle for earth 🌎 rages on.\n\nTo cast out, to take a strong 💪 man's goods, indicates there is war and a struggle.\n\nIndeed the kingdom of God is come to take over the earth 🌎, and there is a raging war ongoing.","dt":"2022-10-09T06:12:59","s":["a62v8fv5bm"]}],"37":[{"m":"Just like in a law court.","dt":"2023-01-14T13:47:52","s":["z03pmxni80"]}],"40":[{"m":"They wanted an immediate sign, but Jesus would have none of that.\n\nThey got a futuristic sign, which would still require them to believe.\n\nIf after all these miracles of Jesus they did not believe, but needed a sign again, then the problem was not with the signs but their heart of unbelief.","dt":"2022-10-09T06:17:12","s":["mpqq3eibe9"]}],"32":[{"m":"Why and what did Jesus mean???","dt":"2022-10-09T06:13:51","s":["j466h9ljy3"]}]},"13":{"12":[{"m":"Then invariably the person who was described as not having really did have something, yet despised it.","dt":"2022-10-16T07:28:30","s":["dfwi2aid51"]}],"13":[{"m":"Oh God, this is so painful.\n\nIt was almost as if Jesus was saying... These are fools, they have eyes but they do not see with them.\n\nAnd their ears 👂 which they have are not for hearing, and of course if you do not hear, how will you understand?\n\nLet us actively seek to see, hear and understand.\n\nAs Christians, if you indeed believe that you are a Christian, meaning the Son of God died for you, imagine that 🤯.\n\nAnd he's given you and I the commission of living the Christian life. Ask yourself how seriously you have taken this commission.\n\nJudge yourself, especially considering that he will be coming to judge our works.\n\nIs your current state of Christian walk truly reflecting wisdom, or are you part of those who have eyes 👀 but see not and ears but hear not?\n\nToday this question 🙋 goes to us all.","dt":"2022-10-16T07:33:54","s":["s82pf9dyru"]}],"23":[{"m":"Luke's account gives only a hundredfold option without stating the others:\n\nLuke 8:8 KJV\nAnd other fell on good ground, and sprang up, and bare fruit an hundredfold. And when he had said these things, he cried, He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.","dt":"2023-01-15T16:08:44","s":["t29456l6q5"]}],"37":[{"m":"He that sowed the seed is Jesus Christ, and whiles men slept 😴.\n\nIt does not say whiles the good man slept, which in that case will be Jesus.\n\nBut whiles men slept 😴, the men who were to keep watch over the good seed slept, an enemy came in.\n\nI liken this to the very beginning when the kingdom of God was established and man put in charge.\n\nAnd man slept, and for that matter men of all ages slept, the enemy came in to sow tares.\n\nUntil the end of time when the error of man is done away with and the evils punished.\n\nIt can also be likened to the good seed being the church, but whiles men, the custodians of the church, i.e. believers, slept, wolves in sheep's clothing were sown in the church, and all such in the church and in the world 🌎 will be flushed out at the end of time.","dt":"2025-02-26T12:45:25","s":["im3rx3qpig"]}],"41":[{"m":"A kingdom is a king 👑 and his domain...\n\nFor now we see the kingdom of heaven expand through preaching and teaching. Soul winning, as we call it.\n\nThrough non-violent conquest of the souls, hearts and bodies of men.\n\nSo the question 🙋 becomes, where is the King's domain?\n\nIt is here answered plainly. The earth 🌎 is the domain.\n\n😇","dt":"2021-12-17T08:22:29","s":["a14qsc2ifs"]},{"m":"The angels shall gather out of his kingdom all evil people 😈.\n\nIn reading the passage carefully, it seems the world 🌎 is his kingdom.\n\nAnd in following the storyline and flow of thoughts, the world will eventually become his kingdom.\n\nThis is the difference: the world has both good and evil, but his kingdom has only good people.\n\nSo when eventually his kingdom takes over the world 🌎, the children of wickedness must be taken out so his kingdom remains true to its characteristics.\n\nI now understand why there will be a war in order for Christ's kingdom to dominate all kings 🤴 and dominions.\n\nThe fact that all eyes see Christ at his coming does not mean all want him or will accept him.\n\nIndeed, many will continue on in rebellion at his commands and precepts.\n\nThat is why after the millennial reign of Christ, a final rebellion will be put out.","dt":"2025-02-26T12:34:14","s":["52wpm0xnlo"]}],"46":[{"m":"These two can be combined in the sense that the treasure in the field is that goodly pearl, for which the man sold all he had and bought it and the field in which it was found.","dt":"2025-02-26T12:47:29","s":["q1q91pmlx1"]}],"33":[{"m":"Interesting analogy.\n\nThe kingdom of heaven is indeed hidden 🫥.\n\nIt began with 12 core disciples and today is the biggest belief system.\n\nAnd yet it is still hidden in the eyes of many, even unto the end of time when it takes over the world 🌎.","dt":"2025-02-26T12:38:57","s":["wfungbjnzx"]}],"55":[{"m":"Sad 😔, so it's no news if your own people hail you not... In fact, be ready to be disdained by your own.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:24:25","s":["ynegbt9njz"]}]},"14":{"13":[{"m":"Likely these were very poor people and could not afford a ship 🛳.\n\nLikely also because it was a multitude, they walked in groups to Jesus.\n\nOf course Jesus, being famous, needed some respite and went alone to a desert 🏜 place away from the public view.","dt":"2022-10-27T11:56:03","s":["tmrx0qpn65"]}],"14":[{"m":"It's almost like he was surprised they had gone to such an extent to track him 🖲, and felt compassion for them.","dt":"2022-10-27T11:57:41","s":["0fgugzbc8x"]}],"15":[{"m":"Today we send the multitudes away with nothing and on an empty stomach.\n\nTo make matters worse, we do not heal them; we fake the power and take from them.\n\nWe have wolves on the pulpit acting 🎭 as sheep 🐑 and devouring them.","dt":"2022-10-22T07:13:41","s":["86qwmf1swi"]}],"23":[{"m":"I'm sure final ministration and prayers. The kind that happens in church after a major revival.","dt":"2022-10-22T07:10:52","s":["yfj0i67ggc"]},{"m":"That was the main point of going into a desert 🏜 place, but there again the multitudes had found him...\n\nSo now, having sent them away, he sought solitude again on the mountain ⛰, and this time he got it.","dt":"2022-10-27T12:01:27","s":["snivxgchcg"]}],"31":[{"m":"I don't even know what to say or where to begin from.\n\nSo the faith it took Peter to walk on water 💦 was little faith to Jesus. So what is great or big faith to Jesus?\n\nLet me run a search global.\n\nMatthew 8:10 KJV\nWhen Jesus heard it, he marvelled, and said to them that followed, Verily I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.\n\nMatthew 15:28 KJV\nThen Jesus answered and said unto her, O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.\n\nSo these are the examples, men and women who exhibited great faith according to Jesus.\n\nA grand total of 2 souls.\n\nIt seems to me that Peter's inability to sustain faith to the end was what earned him little faith.\n\n'Cause I think 🤔 and you'd agree 👍 with me that walking on water is no small feat of faith, but continuing in that faith as the tempest grows stronger 💪 shows how strong one's faith is.\n\nSo if the faith of Peter was great, he would have stood in the midst of the storms and not allowed doubt 🤷‍♂️.\n\n\"Why did you doubt 🤷‍♂️?\" was Jesus's question 🙋 and key 🗝 to grade Peter's faith. On the merit of that question, his faith was little.","dt":"2021-12-20T04:36:32","s":["4mz2dpvhan"]},{"m":"If Peter walking on water had little faith, then we today really have very little faith...\n\nBecause our faith is ever so often shaken by the minutest of opposition.\n\nIf your faith remains whiles everything is cool and rosy 🌹 but shakes when things seem not to work out,\n\nthen indeed you have little faith.\n\nOh Lord, I will have great faith. So help me to.","dt":"2023-01-15T16:50:51","s":["f4c8maigyq"]}],"36":[{"m":"Perfectly 👌 whole...","dt":"2021-12-20T04:37:23","s":["c7uc2yn42k"]}]},"15":{"22":[{"m":"How did she know that Jesus was the Son of David?\n\nShe might have heard of stories of him, and him being the Messiah possibly.\n\nShe had done her homework well before coming to him.\n\nNo wonder she was so incessant on receiving answers to her prayer.","dt":"2025-03-20T11:12:02","s":["9utxlj340q"]}],"24":[{"m":"Her story in a way is akin to that of the centurion who had his child made well with just a word.\n\nHe also was not a Jew.\nYet the Lord did not ignore him like he did this woman.\n\nHis bargaining chip was that he was worthy, for he had built them a synagogue.\n\nThat goes to show there are exceptions to rules.","dt":"2025-03-20T11:14:20","s":["8r6alxc8mz"]}],"28":[{"m":"What an answer, she had gotten Jesus at his weak spot, i.e. the exhibition of great faith.\n\nAnd great faith was seen in what the people spoke.\n\nSame with the centurion who spoke his belief... Faith speaks.","dt":"2021-12-22T06:56:40","s":["se9thkqre4"]},{"m":"There are many things to glean from this story.\n\nHow come this devil was not cast out with a word or addressed directly?\n\nYet there were times that the devils were.\n\nCould that not therefore imply that verbally casting out a devil is not the only way to get them out of a person?","dt":"2025-03-20T11:09:53","s":["xtgadzbzsx"]}],"39":[{"m":"Which place is that, Magdala?","dt":"2021-12-23T07:08:05","s":["18tssredxj"]}],"12":[{"m":"Jesus was courting trouble with his answers. Already the people loved him and saw him as a prophet.\n\nBut the Pharisees thought he deceiveth the people. He had come to usurp their authority in a sense, because the common people now listened 👂 to him.","dt":"2021-12-22T06:40:21","s":["bb8w74jcie"]}]},"16":{"1":[{"m":"😼 Before I even go on to read the response of Jesus to 😏 these guys, let me give them this 😼 wry smile 😼 😏😏😏😏😒😒\n\nI 🤔 mean, really. Are they serious? Raising the dead, feeding 5000, restoring maimed and blind.\n\nAll this is not enough. What will a sign from heaven do to change the hearts 💕 of these people?\n\nIt's an attempt in futility.","dt":"2021-12-23T07:40:50","s":["ec9yl2zxzh"]}],"4":[{"m":"I love that... He left them and departed, of course 🏇 not without telling them his mind.","dt":"2021-12-23T07:42:11","s":["7dxly68ovl"]}],"13":[{"m":"Why did he ask this question 🙋 in Caesarea Philippi?","dt":"2022-10-20T06:12:45","s":["pxnpvsj3e6"]}],"18":[{"m":"You, Peter, a smaller part of the bigger rock.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:14:43","s":["e0vsbxy17n"]}],"20":[{"m":"Yes, they should tell no man, because if all men know, they will destroy the purpose of God... i.e. that the Christ must die.\n\nAnd we know men; there is no way they will allow the Christ to die.\n\nThe only way for Christ to die is for the people to not know that they are crucifying the Lord of glory.\n\nJesus actually actively facilitated his own death ☠.\n\nStrange man he was... Who does that?","dt":"2022-10-20T06:18:05","s":["90twift82o"]}],"21":[{"m":"Having now gained perfect understanding of who Jesus was and confirming what was in their hearts 💕 by vocalizing it,\n\nhe now began to open 🔓 up levels and dimensions of understanding to his disciples.\n\nRevelation thus begets revelation. As you cross over and begin to understand God more and more,\n\nmore is opened up to you.","dt":"2021-12-23T08:10:20","s":["kgga1brpx2"]},{"m":"It's almost as if Jesus was waiting for his disciples to get the revelation of him as the Christ before going to the cross.\n\nIt was important for continuity of the mission after his death.\n\nIt was almost like the cue he was looking for was here, so now he could prepare himself for the cross ➕.\n\nMaybe that was the sign he was to look for; that was the sign that now his mission was done and it was time to move on.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:27:15","s":["jfz31mjcuv"]},{"m":"Such a counteraction.\n\nHe knew that with them knowing he was the Christ, they run the risk of making him king 👑, as the Christ rightly is.\n\nBut he knew that at this time he was a lamb, not a king.\n\nHe was to be slaughtered, not enthroned.\nSo he began immediately to put things in perspective.","dt":"2025-03-21T07:21:07","s":["t3i07lp00e"]}],"23":[{"m":"Why address him as Satan? Was Jesus discerning that Satan had entered into Peter, or he used it like we do when someone does something wrong and we go like, you devil 👿?\n\nBecause really, what Peter was suggesting, that Jesus die not, was very grievous and deserving of being called a devil.\n\nHe was suggesting the whole world 🗺 should continue on in darkness, for which Christ came to save it from death ☠.","dt":"2021-12-23T08:13:09","s":["42axmx5vjm"]}],"24":[{"m":"Hmm... Yes, Jesus had set his mind and face towards the cross.\n\nAnd so he tells his disciples — that is the way of the follower of Christ, denying yourself and setting your face aggressively to the cross ➕.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:20:51","s":["prkle9c8o5"]}],"25":[{"m":"In other words, if you lose your life for me, just as I will be resurrected on the third day, I will resurrect what you lose in your quest for me, both in this life and after your death, eternal life.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:22:54","s":["2jixiuq4z2"]}],"28":[{"m":"What does this mean, and who did it make reference to?\n\nAre","dt":"2021-12-23T07:50:31","s":["v5x3nqmpis"]}],"12":[{"m":"1.\ncause (dough or bread) to rise by adding yeast or another raising agent.\n\"it only takes a little bit of yeast to leaven the bread.\"\n\nLeaven leavens the whole bread 🥪, so wrong doctrine as that of the Pharisees can destroy and corrupt an entire church ⛪.","dt":"2021-12-23T07:46:35","s":["6wq1xonkrw"]}]},"17":{"3":[{"m":"Elias we know was transported to heaven, but Moses...\n\nHe died 😕, or did he? His body also was not found, and we know that the devil 👿 contended for his body.\n\nWas it that he wanted it for necromancy and other witchcraft purposes?\n\nSo now what was Moses doing here? Was he not supposed to be in Abraham's bosom?","dt":"2022-10-21T06:13:43","s":["h8vqnupvuk"]}],"9":[{"m":"To them it was a vision, but in our modern context that was a 3D hologram.","dt":"2021-12-24T07:31:52","s":["4kgg66ejs9"]},{"m":"In my previous comment I described this as a 3D hologram, but that is debatable.\n\nIf Moses and Elias physically came to the mount, then that was no hologram.\n\nIf it was that images and pictures were given them, then we can talk of a hologram, like when Peter saw a great sheet coming down with all manner of animals in it.\n\nThat might have been a hologram. These are just conjectures anyways.","dt":"2023-01-16T08:05:07","s":["nd9glsrhv6"]},{"m":"Why were they not to tell the vision to anyone?\n\nNot even to the other disciples?\n\nMaybe because this vision\n1. Clearly demonstrated that he was the Christ, the Son of God. This was the sign that the Pharisees were asking for.\n\nBut they were not worthy of such a sign, having already attributed the many signs and wonders to the work of demon spirits.\n\nHere we have direct attestation from God that Jesus was his Son.\n\n2. He demonstrated that he was not just man, but he was a divine being.\n\nRemember when he calmed the storms, they asked what manner of man he was?\n\nAnd now he shows what manner of man he was: he was not just a man, the son of Joseph, but he was divine, the Son of God, and radiated forth divine power such as is seen in divine beings.\n\nThese things Jesus wanted hid until after his death on the cross. Else they will not let him die on the cross.\n\nNo, not the king and salvation that the Jews have long awaited for.\n\nAfter his death he would have fulfilled the reason for his coming and be crowned king awaiting his kingdom, so his subjects can now be in the know of such things concerning him, as his radiance on the mountain etc.\n\nThings worthy of a king.\n\nAt this point he was to be a lamb, without honor.\n\nSuch mysteries were therefore the preserve of those who could keep secrets and were close to the king.","dt":"2025-03-22T08:52:32","s":["54s7tlvurb"]}],"18":[{"m":"This casting of demons and the like, i.e. healings.\n\nWhere did Jesus learn them from? From the Holy Ghost 👻, obviously.\n\nBecause he did and understood things in ways that no man did.\n\nIt must have come from the Holy Ghost.","dt":"2021-12-24T08:38:21","s":["ewch7ccmeo"]}],"21":[{"m":"This kind: some say the \"this kind\" refers to unbelief... not to the kind of demon.\n\nI believe it's in reference to the kind of demon 👹. However, either way the result is the same.\n\nWhether fasting to cure the unbelief so you can cast out this demon, or fasting to receive grace 💪 to cast out this specific demon.\n\nHowever, the wording leans more towards 🗼 casting out the demon through fasting.\n\nBecause I have not come across any other scripture talking about unbelief as something to be \"casted out\".","dt":"2021-12-24T09:10:26","s":["72ofxfwul7"]}],"23":[{"m":"The number of times he said this, and yet they did not or could not believe it till it all happened.","dt":"2022-10-21T06:21:10","s":["ogk7kffjd6"]}],"27":[{"m":"Oh my Lord and my Saviour.\n\nI love Jesus. He lived in a dichotomy. He was a servant, yet king 👑.\n\nMore like he was king 👑 but had to live a life of a servant, yet could exercise such kingly dominion of the earth, thus at times betraying his humanness.\n\nHere he, the king 👑, was being asked if he paid tribute. 🙄😁😁😁... I can imagine Jesus just smiling ☺ at the ignorance 🤷‍♂️ of these tribute collectors.\n\nThis whole world 🗺 is in darkness and such a mystery. Mingled with anomalies.\n\nThere are kings living 🛋 as slaves, yet exercising such kingly dominion at times that it blows their slave cover.\n\nThere are also kings by birth who fear 😱 servants and demons, meanwhiles these are their subjects. I'm making reference here to baby 🤱 Christians.\n\nThere is so much lies and deceptions ongoing in the earth 🌎.\n\nAnd it's about time the true sons rise to take their place and help their brethren do the same.","dt":"2021-12-24T09:17:15","s":["qesg92ww73"]}],"11":[{"m":"So the disciples had this nagging question 🙋 at the back of their minds the whole time.\n\nThey knew Jesus was the Christ, but also knew that the scribes had said Elijah was to come first.\n\nAnd he did come, but hid from them.\n\nJust like Jesus the Christ came not as a king but as the son of Joseph, a poor carpenter.\n\nSo also John came, the son of Zechariah, yet carried the spirit of Elijah.\n\nIn all these, the leaders and people knew them not.\n\nBut at the second coming, Elijah would come again as the witness before the second coming of Jesus Christ.","dt":"2025-03-22T09:23:34","s":["141s4whmjt"]}],"13":[{"m":"The disciples walk with Jesus, what did they really want?\n\nHe told them many times that he would die, but they understood it not.\n\nSo in their minds, how was all this going to end?\n\nWith Jesus crowned king 👑 in their presence and they hopefully reigning with him in his kingdom?\n\nTo think that in the end they will reign with him in this world was right, but the road to the throne they least expected.\n\nThat it would include crucifixion? Not not.","dt":"2023-01-16T08:12:06","s":["r0dwemqxvk"]}]},"19":{"9":[{"m":"Adultery, because in the eyes 👀 of the Lord they are still married... So offering a bill of divorce cannot annul what has been established by covenant.\n\nHowever, sleeping with another breaks that marital union.\n\nThat then implies that consummation is the seal of marriage, so sex with a different person breaks the union.","dt":"2023-01-16T14:15:48","s":["lcbxftxwdn"]}],"12":[{"m":"In our current generation, being a eunuch is not even considered, but I suspect a time is coming where it will be common among the believers.","dt":"2023-01-16T14:18:32","s":["u2i7v188r7"]}],"21":[{"m":"With all the rich young ruler had done, he was qualified for the kingdom 👑 of God.\n\nBut if he wanted the ultimate crown 👑 and to be perfect 👌, here were the terms.\n\nAnd now he was too entangled in his wealth to let it go for the kingdom.","dt":"2023-01-16T14:23:23","s":["yzotnrc2fb"]},{"m":"In the Luke 18 account of the same story, Jesus tells him that he lacks one thing, i.e. his riches were his hindrance.\n\nSo then I asked if he will make heaven, since he had done well except in releasing his hard-earned cash for the kingdom.\n\nBut in this account in Matthew, Jesus tells him if he wants to be perfect 👌...\n\nAs if to say, you have done well in keeping all these commands, which will qualify you for eternal life, but if you really want to hit the nail on the head and be sure of having met all requirements, go sell all you have.\n\nThat was the deal breaker for the guy... he couldn't do what Jesus suggested.\n\nI think he would make the kingdom, but narrowly, and if in the kingdom there are different zones based on degrees of sacrifice, he will miss the best of places.\n\nNo wonder Jesus explained how hard it was for the rich to make heaven.\n\nAgain, Paul talks of people whose works will be burned when tried with fire 🔥, but they themselves will make it, but scarcely...\n\nHowever, if our work be of gold or silver, it is purified rather than burned by the fire 🔥...\n\nSo this kinda answers my questions.","dt":"2025-03-30T11:46:49","s":["ioabbg6yz9"]}]},"20":{"27":[{"m":"Both ministers and servants of Mt. 20:26-28 refer to the lowest secular and ecclesiastical office among Christians, as exemplified by Christ Himself. No minister has a right to be a lord over God's people (1Pet. 5:1-9). He is to be least of all and servant of all (Mk. 9:35).\n\nThis is the comment passed by Dake's commentary.\n\nNow note that all this is within a context. Yes, Jesus did state that his people were to serve others and themselves.\n\nThis did not mean they were to walk about sober and naive and be trampled about by all.\n\nLook at the life of Jesus: he was a sacrificial lamb for all, including the Pharisees and elders of the people who were antagonistic to his ministry.\n\nAnd we saw how he dealt with them. He was no meek man allowing himself to be trampled by them.\n\nNo indeed, he was actively rebuking them and calling them out on their hypocrisy. He did not give them a foothold around him or his disciples for them to hurt them.\n\nJesus was tough on them. So yes, we ought to serve people, but that does not mean being naively ill-treated and being messed up with.","dt":"2025-03-31T08:56:49","s":["x0qilbjuqa"]}],"34":[{"m":"They followed him for how long...?\n\nDid these latter become ardent followers of the Lord, or did they go back to their lives as usual?","dt":"2023-01-16T14:29:40","s":["jtwgv7u3v7"]}]},"22":{"21":[{"m":"The trick is not in the answer he gave but how he gave that answer.\n\nHe could have answered the question to mean the same thing as stated in verse 21, but using a different illustration, and that would have led to his destruction.\n\nIndeed, he ended up saying it is right to pay tribute to Caesar, but the way he put it showed his wisdom and helped him escape the wrath of the people.\n\nThis should be wisdom to us.","dt":"2023-11-18T09:37:18","s":["r1hrscq5rm"]}],"37":[{"m":"Oh this Jesus... He was the master of his craft.\n\nHe was the best of the best 🙏.\n\nHe was the nerd, but not nerdy in his behavior, and associated with the common folks.\n\nSee how an entire company came against him, yet he masterfully answers them all.\n\nHe indeed and truly is the Word of God.","dt":"2022-11-04T06:11:31","s":["di8cmzb1un"]}],"42":[{"m":"That is an easy one, they thought, duh...\n\nThey did not know that that question 🙋 was the bait. And they took it in willingly and, I can imagine, almost lackadaisically.\n\nThen he caught them with the real deal 🤝.\n\nNow they were at a loss, because they did not know the answer; it was not that they had forgotten.\n\nIt had never occurred to them. One man, Jesus, against this many teachers and leaders, yet he surpassed them all.","dt":"2023-11-18T09:40:45","s":["1uwzo10uxr"]},{"m":"How does one answer such a 🙋 question without creating doubts 🤷‍♂️ and controversies?\n\nJesus knew that to answer this question right would mean to acknowledge the Christ, the son of David, as being greater than David.\n\nWhich he was, for the Christ was more the Son of God than of David.\n\nIndeed, David is man and Christ is God.","dt":"2025-04-04T07:22:39","s":["jtiszebxhi"]}],"4":[{"m":"Them which are bidden to the wedding feast sounds very much like the Jews.\n\nWho, though to them belong the covenants and promises of God, were not ready for the kingdom when it came to be.","dt":"2025-04-03T10:12:05","s":["g4o6078o7b"]}],"39":[{"m":"He gave them a second 🥈 as a bonus.","dt":"2023-01-17T12:06:42","s":["vhdyz7lusn"]}],"46":[{"m":"I can imagine how long these leaders deliberated over this, his question 🙋, without any answer, till shamefacedly they conceded.\n\nFrom then, to avoid such public embarrassment, they were compelled not to ask him any more questions.\n\nJesus had smeared their face 😔 in the mud and done so publicly.\n\nNo wonder they hated him so much.","dt":"2023-11-18T09:43:29","s":["bhhpu457wb"]}]},"23":{"27":[{"m":"Jesus was really on their case... A whole chapter for them.","dt":"2022-11-04T16:58:12","s":["usbgh1kt5x"]}],"28":[{"m":"Is this not the state of the church ⛪ today...\n\nThe things that Jesus said here 2000 years ago are happening today.","dt":"2022-11-04T16:59:06","s":["0aptt0ap2t"]}]},"24":{"13":[{"m":"But he that shall endure to the end shall be saved — to which end is it referencing?\n\nTo the end of the world immediately preceding the massive preaching of the word to all nations.\n\nSo the enduring to the end is not in hiding but in reaching out despite the risk of death and persecution till he comes. Then shall the end come.","dt":"2025-07-31T08:29:30","s":["9jlq2azzgv"]}],"14":[{"m":"In a sense this has been repeated throughout history; there have been wars and pestilence.\n\nBelievers have had to suffer for their faith in divers forms.\n\nThough not always through death ☠.\n\nThen those who endure to the end of their lives are promised eternal life.\n\nThough all these past generations and cycles do not culminate in the coming of the Christ, it reflects the prophecy of Jesus.\n\nAnd a generation will come that will climax it all and end with the coming of our Lord.","dt":"2025-07-31T08:25:04","s":["rkwdhfgugb"]},{"m":"There have been revivals of the word and gospel in many places in the years gone by, and there will once more be a massive worldwide preaching to usher in the end of the world 🗺.","dt":"2025-07-31T08:26:16","s":["864pqvp6y1"]}],"29":[{"m":"So these happen after the great tribulations. Other books let us know it will happen in a 7-year duration, indeed in the last half of the seven years.\n\nAnd so Christ lets us know the signs in the heavens, as stated in Revelation, occur right after the great tribulations.\n\nIt seems, actually it is, God's judgement on the world.","dt":"2025-04-07T03:34:16","s":["e70b3swdxn"]}],"34":[{"m":"These will take place in a seven-year duration, so yes, that generation that will experience these things will not pass till all be fulfilled.\n\nOnce it starts, that generation will be the same to witness its completion.","dt":"2025-04-07T03:37:01","s":["bndo1ldvga"]}],"36":[{"m":"\"No one knows, however, when that day and hour will come — neither the angels in heaven nor the Son; the Father alone knows.\" (GNT)\nBut come to think of it, what would have been the big deal if Jesus had made known the time? Or better still, why do Jesus and the Father especially not want us to focus so much on the specific date?","dt":null,"s":["d1e3c27680"]},{"m":"When you see these signs, then know that my coming is at the doors and is very close.\n\nHowever, the exact date, the day and hour, knows no man, but only the Father.","dt":"2023-01-20T11:21:17","s":["wp74hq36i4"]}],"41":[{"m":"Those left on the earth will continue on into the new millennium. They will not all be believers, yet will continue on with the resurrected saints.\n\nThis by itself is an act of mercy from the LORD.\n\nThat fallibility of the new millennium residents accounts for why the devil will come in to deceive the nations one more time before he is finally cast into the lake of fire.\n\nHaving said this, I will have to verify if there indeed will be unbelievers during the millennial reign of Christ.\n\nWhat is evident in the scriptures is that the nations during the millennial reign will team up with the devil to fight the saints and the beloved city.","dt":"2025-11-27T09:54:26","s":["jd7z366xqj"]}],"50":[{"m":"For the unprepared servant who was not looking forward to his coming, it will seem his master has come at an hour that he is not aware of.\n\nBut to the prepared, he is ever ready.","dt":"2023-01-20T11:51:56","s":["ixh06ajk3y"]}],"15":[{"m":"Oh, so we would be here to see the abomination of desolation? I thought we were supposed to be raptured by then, so what are we doing seeing this? Except this was a warning not directly to his disciples of his day, but to the future disciples.\n\nJust as Isaiah 6, or is it 9, says, for to us a child is born, to us a son is given. This “to us” was fulfilled after Isaiah’s day, so though it sounded like it was in his days, it was to the future generations.","dt":"2025-06-08T14:58:32","s":["p2nu8vpenq"]}],"40":[{"m":"Jesus had said earlier that his coming will be marked by the gathering of the saints to himself.\n\nAnd now he talks of that hour no one knows, and now he talks of two people being in the field and one taken but the other not.\n\nI believe this is in reference to his gathering of the saints and not to being gathered for the battle of Armageddon like some teach... I think Dake's commentary teaches that.","dt":"2025-04-07T03:40:11","s":["oh5ncv3uxj"]}],"49":[{"m":"So if that servant goes to bed with the world and is not expectant of the Lord's coming, he will be thrown into outer darkness with the wicked.\n\nBecause he was a partaker with them instead of watching.","dt":"2023-01-20T11:32:27","s":["onkpq00ni1"]}],"51":[{"m":"This weeping and gnashing of teeth is not to the unbeliever and sinner oo...\n\nIt is to the servant and believer who was not prepared for him.\n\nThere is a reward for such.\n\nIt is the reward for hypocrites, and it is not pleasant.","dt":"2023-01-20T11:54:09","s":["8mb86lo5ib"]}]},"25":{"13":[{"m":"So here the bridegroom, Jesus, came to take these virgins to the marriage supper, but the others were not allowed in.\n\nThey were left in outer darkness, though not stated directly, except that we are admonished to watch for his coming.\n\nIt is therefore in order to assign to them the same punishment of those who failed to watch, i.e. outer darkness, weeping and teeth gnashing.","dt":"2023-01-20T12:28:04","s":["cgi0egypqb"]}],"30":[{"m":"The same place that the unprepared servants were sent at his coming, these who did not use their talents were sent.\n\nThese parables and that of the 10 virgins illustrate the same point.\n\nThey are different sides of the same coin.","dt":"2023-01-20T12:04:22","s":["y8tobvkd1f"]}],"31":[{"m":"As I read this verse, in my mind I presumed Jesus speaking to the rich or privileged people and telling them what they should have done for the poor and less privileged.\n\nBut that is not what he said; rather he said, you did not do it to the least of these my brethren.\n\nTo these my brothers. Which brothers was he referring to? Was he referencing every poor and underprivileged person as his brother, and those privileged as deserving of death for not visiting the poor and doing them good?","dt":"2025-11-18T11:06:32","s":["hvy6m8qbe3"]}],"32":[{"m":"It appears this judgement — actually at this point Jesus is on the earth 🌎 reigning, and all nations come before Him.\n\nThis judgement seems to be of a different sort from those who were unfaithful and did not meet him at his coming.\n\nThey are now in outer darkness. But here we have the nations being judged, and I believe the saints 😇 are with him in this judgment.\n\nI wonder though how this judgement will be carried out and over what time span.\n\nWill each individual human being be judged here?\n\nThat seems the case; that is why saints will partake of this great judgment of the nations.","dt":"2023-01-20T12:20:52","s":["qs203lzb38"]}],"40":[{"m":"The criteria here was not how many souls were won, but the good and righteous deeds of man to his fellow man 👨🏿.\n\nHmm","dt":"2023-01-20T12:22:42","s":["ekws425fxd"]}]},"26":{"15":[{"m":"What brought Judas to this point? How did he get so hurt or offended that he was ready to betray Jesus, the miracle worker 👷?\n\nMaybe Judas was just tired of this whole messiah business. I doubt 🤷‍♂️ Judas actually believed Jesus was the Messiah — why would he try such betrayal against the Christ?","dt":"2025-04-10T19:33:41","s":["hikh3odulc"]},{"m":"They covenanted with him. What was Judas thinking?\n30 pieces of silver?? When I checked, it was about some plots of land, for when it was later rejected, it was used to buy a field.","dt":"2025-04-11T08:37:06","s":["irmxlce4m6"]}],"38":[{"m":"Jesus was indeed a man.","dt":"2023-01-22T13:34:48","s":["bsdgr7zet4"]}],"44":[{"m":"The time when he needed help the most, he did not receive it.\n\nI guess at the point where even he, Jesus, needed help, then the others who were not that 💪 strong would have crushed and not have the help and energy ⚡ to help.","dt":"2023-01-22T13:42:27","s":["2525fnwj7p"]}],"56":[{"m":"Wow.\nThey forsook Jesus and fled when they realized what was happening; the state was against their master.","dt":"2025-04-11T08:40:03","s":["4r0rkdtreg"]},{"m":"Then the disciples forsook him. I can imagine the leader of this multitude shout, \"ARREST THEM ALL\"...\nThen the disciples forsook him.\n\nOver the past three years they had managed to escape the grip of the crowds and the leaders of the time.\n\nBut this time they were hemmed in.\n\nOne of them had betrayed their hideout. That should show you how tight-lipped and tight-knit the inner circle of Jesus's disciples were.\n\nThey had escaped many such attempts by hiding, sometimes in plain sight among the common people,\n\nsleeping in mounts and secluded places. Sometimes the divine hand of God made a way for them.\n\nBut here they were; finally the arms of the \"law\" had caught up with them.\n\nThey fled.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:34:24","s":["n2kuckrhoh"]}],"63":[{"m":"They knew the Christ will be the Son of God.\n\nWhich verses say this?","dt":"2023-01-22T15:22:29","s":["od0c8ekd7l"]}],"75":[{"m":"He betrayed his Lord and Master. No wonder when he got the chance again he gave a strong testimony of Christ before these same Pharisees.\n\nAnd continued even until he was crucified. And even then he counted not himself worthy of such exemplary death ☠ and requested to die upside 🙃 down.","dt":"2022-11-10T07:10:30","s":["d55lk72r46"]}],"59":[{"m":"A form of justice, yet it was all a setup... Including false witnesses.","dt":"2022-11-10T07:04:17","s":["f8s9xptzip"]}],"65":[{"m":"All this was fake. He just dramatised the confession of Jesus as the Christ to be blasphemy, renting his clothes as a public show of the seriousness of such an offense, and now asks his people what they thought.\n\nOf course this kangaroo court had already passed judgement on him long ago, before they even brought him.\n\nThey just wanted him dead.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:38:00","s":["e4fz8eta02"]}],"69":[{"m":"The high priest had a palace, hmmm.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:39:03","s":["8a7bi9tmel"]}],"74":[{"m":"He cursed; this was a survival tactic. These people sought to have him condemned with Jesus, and he would have none of that.\n\nI can imagine him swear that may God strike him if he was lying, hahah... He was indeed a man of the streets; he knew how to survive.\n\nThis was not the time to die; he had family to take care of.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:41:15","s":["z9ws19rb58"]}]},"27":{"3":[{"m":"When he saw Jesus was condemned.\n\nWas he thinking he would get the money and invariably Jesus would be set free, or he would free himself?\n\nThat way he can still keep the money whiles having kept his end of the bargain.","dt":"2023-01-22T15:27:16","s":["lu2s198lyn"]}],"4":[{"m":"Then the beginning of condemnation and suicidal thoughts started.\n\nHe had betrayed the Messiah; he had become the son of perdition spoken about in the Holy Scriptures.","dt":"2023-01-22T15:29:02","s":["ihl9pgu90l"]}],"32":[{"m":"Was this the same Simon of Cyrene in the Acts of the Apostles?","dt":"2023-01-22T16:58:40","s":["whlzm2k836"]}],"45":[{"m":"About 12 noon to 3pm... A strange time for there to be darkness. It should be sunny, hot 🔥 at this time.","dt":"2023-01-22T17:00:34","s":["6mwpw3fbf5"]}],"46":[{"m":"How come they were confused about what he said? Which language is this?","dt":"2023-01-22T17:01:25","s":["2ug5u4bku0"]}],"53":[{"m":"So the graves were rent when he died, but the saints 😇 came out of them only after his resurrection, to signify victory ✌️ over death ☠, and showed themselves to many, just like he did.","dt":"2023-01-22T17:05:51","s":["6xlrg994vz"]}],"10":[{"m":"Within context, this was a field Jeremiah himself bought, and yet it also alluded to the Messiah.\n\nThere is nothing new under the sun.","dt":"2025-04-17T09:10:24","s":["ai1xf3zoa2"]}],"18":[{"m":"Yes, for envy they had delivered him; he was just doing better in ministry than they were.\n\nBut was that sufficient reason to murder him? Yes, for the envious it was more than sufficient.\n\nLittle wonder Proverbs has this to say about envy:\n\nProverbs 27:4 KJV\nWrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before envy?","dt":"2025-04-17T09:15:17","s":["fvnoepkoh4"]}],"22":[{"m":"This note is a direct copy from Dake's commentary, and it struck my heart so strong 💪.\n\n\"Notes For Verse 22 a [What shall I do then with Jesus which is called Christ?] Question 174. Next, Mt. 27:23. The greatest question of human life. How we answer it determines our destiny.\"","dt":"2023-01-23T06:57:03","s":["8bmd6tcoyr"]}],"62":[{"m":"Which day was this?","dt":"2025-04-17T09:32:07","s":["yrjujxw9oa"]}]},"28":{"10":[{"m":"His disciples were now referred to as brethren... What had changed?\n\nHe, having died, now has raised many sons into glory.","dt":"2022-11-18T15:34:09","s":["3qastjbgs1"]}],"13":[{"m":"These people were children 🧒 of the devil 👿 indeed.\n\nThey had first-hand 🖐️ witness of the resurrection, yet denied it and covered it up 👆... Their own Messiah they denied so they can keep their place up and continue on in their politics...\n\nThis should serve as a lesson for believers today: men who love power and play politics at all cost, one must be wary of... Even if they profess Christ...","dt":"2022-11-18T15:23:03","s":["r2pkhdytx2"]},{"m":"I thought they said should Christ come down from the cross, they will believe.\n\nNow he goes beyond what they requested, in that he actually dies on the cross.\n\nIs buried ⚰ and rises up from the grave with power.\n\nAnd now, rather than repent and be saved, they paid their way to hide the truth.\n\nBrood of vipers they were.","dt":"2023-01-23T08:32:12","s":["jdz58bkl1w"]}],"14":[{"m":"😼 Did they not say that if he comes down from the cross they would believe?\n\nHere he did more than come down from a cross ➕; he came back from the grave.\n\nAnd guess what, they bribed their way to hide the truth.\n\nThey were the messiahs, and no one would be allowed to take their place. Not even the true Messiah.\n\nThey were children of the father, the devil 👿.\n\nJesus was right, and he knew this.\n\nHe was not using this figuratively; they indeed were children of the devil 👿.\n\nFor them to see the acts of God and reject it and hide it from others.\n\nSo they can keep on lording it over others through lies and deception.","dt":"2025-04-19T06:40:58","s":["n2yapus6mg"]}],"17":[{"m":"What did they doubt 🤷‍♂️, that he was the one, or that he was God worthy of worship, or that he did not really die?\n\nWhat was it...?","dt":"2023-01-23T08:29:23","s":["n65f8vt2gi"]}],"20":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-11-18T15:35:36","s":["3d73d8189c"]}]},"18":{"18":[{"m":"So this promise was not just to Simon bar Jonah but to all believers.\n\nIndeed, Simon's promise of the keys came later.\n\nMatthew 16:19 KJV\nAnd I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.","dt":"2023-01-16T13:55:48","s":["jt2pdxi7mf"]}]},"21":{"14":[{"m":"Jesus did not hang around the right crowd most of the time; here the blind and the lame came to him and he attended to their needs.","dt":"2025-03-31T09:34:12","s":["7hwas5p7py"]}]}},"Exodus":{"1":{"14":[{"m":"So hard work, affliction and difficult times only serve to strengthen us and enable us to adapt 🔌 to the hard life.\n\nAnd subsequently triumph 😤 over the sissies who were over-pampered and not taught real discipline.","dt":"2022-01-30T07:32:39","s":["db499c7c5d"]}],"22":[{"m":"We are not told how this policy came about, but such wickedness and terrible season it was for Israel...\n\nSimilar to what happened to Jesus when he was born.","dt":"2026-01-30T06:53:45","s":["iwe5bc6yha"]}],"7":[{"m":"Why? Because there was a God in their midst advancing them and causing them to be fruitful.","dt":"2026-01-30T06:44:53","s":["gtn5s9e6qb"]}]},"2":{"2":[{"m":"I don’t get it, which parent does not see the child as a goodly child 🧒.\n\nEvery parent adores their little ones. Dake’s describes him as “very fair”... Moses was indeed very beautiful even as a baby 🤱","dt":"2022-01-30T09:55:59","s":["fl8k9521lj","aff7f6311b"]}],"4":[{"m":"Aww.. This Miriam who watched over her junior brother and gave her life in essence.\n\n80 years later she was to challenge him only to find out he was a senior in the spirit.","dt":"2022-01-30T09:57:22","s":["3flsqdsu5a","45cdee5061"]}],"8":[{"m":"It was a very wicked and cruel regime.\n\nA slave-master relationship automatically existed between every Egyptian and Israelite, no matter if they were royalty or not.\n\nIt’s much like the slave trade, and all blacks were seen as being inferior.\n\nThis pattern has been etched in the sands of history from time immemorial.","dt":"2026-01-30T06:59:19","s":["t3k7owezee"]}],"9":[{"m":"Oh what divine providence. How many other women hid their children 🧒.\n\nThe mother of the child becomes the nurse. Oh what love would be shown to this child 🧒,\n\nshe knowing that as soon as he is nursed, her own child will be taken away to the castle to learn the culture of kings and royalty 👑.","dt":"2022-01-30T10:00:50","s":["9vfk51h33x","eba3337458"]}],"10":[{"m":"I did not birth him, nor was he in the water of the womb, but birthed from the water 💦 of a river.","dt":"2022-01-30T10:02:13","s":["gnsui25yqr","e47b6dd240"]}],"11":[{"m":"How did he know he was Hebrew? Obviously evidence was given by his mother whiles nursing him that he was a Hebrew.","dt":"2022-01-30T10:03:27","s":["4e73db1a52"]}],"15":[{"m":"This very complex turn of events is explained very simply.\n\nThe investigation that had to be carried out before concluding on Moses as guilty, the confusion in the palace about what Moses had done.\n\nHis mother’s tears 😭. Sad moments — he was going to be a fugitive forever, never to return home 🏡 and never to be seen by both his mothers.\nEgypt 🇪🇬 was the superpower of the time, and if they are on the look out for you, there is no come back.","dt":"2024-03-01T12:52:49","s":["2v0y44y3xl","d54514f2a1"]}],"16":[{"m":"The many stories and happenings that took place by wells.\n\nIncluding that of Jesus.\n\nWell it’s understandable — wells were life, where water was drawn daily for survival.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:01:04","s":["3etulj1b71"]}],"19":[{"m":"Reminds me of Jacob.","dt":"2024-03-01T13:03:51","s":["39gr6kg0kv"]},{"m":"Could not God have revealed himself to Moses and sent him to deliver Israel 🇮🇱?\n\nHe easily could have, but Israel needed to stay in Egypt 🇪🇬 until the fullness of time.","dt":"2024-03-01T13:05:53","s":["hj03ywdeo5"]}],"22":[{"m":"Similar to his father Israel, their history is filled with stories of being in strange lands and marrying and establishing themselves there.\n\nAnd often becoming even greater than the natives.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:03:39","s":["gm3167dzn8"]}],"23":[{"m":"And now a new king 👑 comes to power and continues the enslavement without questioning it or its history.","dt":"2024-03-01T13:38:27","s":["1idnrw1edg"]},{"m":"Was it that they cried to God by reason of their bondage and God heard, or was it that they cried in pain and anguish and God heard their pain though it was not directed at him, yet because of his covenant he remembered?","dt":"2024-03-02T11:42:33","s":["hj9ct2ghzk"]},{"m":"Interestingly God’s covenant was with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob, whiles the rest by birth were participants of the covenant.","dt":"2024-03-02T11:43:19","s":["vw0f6ixbwk"]},{"m":"Even after the death of the old king, the law and system of oppression continues without question because it benefited the oppressor.\n\nWe must stand up for what we believe in even if it has been the norm or we came to meet it.\n\nThe fact that something has been in existence for long and has become the norm doesn’t mean that it is right, nor must be accepted without question.\n\nWe must be bold to stand up for what we believe in.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:05:34","s":["5m4cn6bi9r"]}],"3":[{"m":"This law, it indeed was in force and must have been very stringent for Moses’s parents to take this step. Does that therefore imply that, like Jesus, Moses’s age mates in Egypt had been killed?","dt":"2024-02-29T13:09:54","s":["b31cd48e3a"]}],"6":[{"m":"She gave her son up to another for adoption.\n\nRather than lose him, she was willing to let him go in order to gain him.","dt":"2026-01-30T06:55:07","s":["ihw0wxrho4"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"At the backside of the desert 🏜, the blessing, the covenant of The man who sacrificed his son to obey God was crying out.\n\nYes the time had come and the covenant was starting to speak.\n\nSo loudly was the cry 😢 of this covenant that bushes caught literal fire 🔥","dt":"2024-03-02T11:45:08","s":["skjdadltvx"]}],"2":[{"m":"Of all the children of Israel in Egypt, why Moses?\n\nWhat was unique about him that God skipped all the millions and chose Moses?\n\nHe was very different from his brothers because he was a free man, he grew up in the palace...\n\nBut why did that matter...\n\nHow did that translate to his being chosen?\n\nI think it’s not merely being free and being royalty, but he had the right mentality and heart for his people and for God to use.\n\nIf these attributes existed in one of the slaves, God could have used him, as we see in David.\n\nWho though a shepherd boy and in the fields had God at heart, and the heart of a king who would serve his people in truth and in accordance with God’s will.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:12:46","s":["qvf2hiwf2e"]}],"5":[{"m":"Which place was this?\n\nWhich holy ground? And what was special about those grounds such that it was holy?\n\nTo the last question 🙋 I believe because God had come down 👇 in a manifest form, it made the grounds holy — just like when the anointed priestly garment sanctifies whatever it touches.","dt":"2022-01-30T10:48:21","s":["0848456dd1"]}],"8":[{"m":"I am come down 👇. Hmm 🤔. God was in action. He was going to take charge, for the time he spoke of had come.\n\nMany things happening to us are because their time is due...\nThat which was spoken of, some of which predates us, are due and we see its manifestations.\n\nThis is so with light and darkness.","dt":"2022-01-30T11:00:39","s":["bmokxr72dt","e9a946c349"]},{"m":"Who ordained him a priest? If he was the first generation of priest, who called him? When was his call?\n\nHim being a priest meant he was deeper into God than the average Hebrew.\n\nHe had a special ordination that allowed him access to God in a deeper and intimate way without risk to his life.\n\nIn the Levitical priesthood, only they could go into the holy place.\n\nIn this wise, Reuel had a depth of relationship with God that others had not.","dt":"2022-01-30T10:38:28","s":["6js3qigjy5"]}],"11":[{"m":"Moses was literally saying, God I think you’ve jumped the gun.\n\nI am a nobody, how do I stand before the king 👑 of the world’s super power and deliver such a message.\n\nI do not even have the clearance and weight to stand before him.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:10:38","s":["et5wfwymg4"]},{"m":"Remember he was a fugitive who had escaped, so to now ask him to turn and face what he was running 🏃 from was unfathomable for him.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:19:17","s":["x4x9eofek7"]},{"m":"Moses well remembers the past, how that 40 years ago he attempted what he could to save Israel 🇮🇱 and failed miserably.\n\nBecause of which he was now a fugitive and has had to raise his family 👪 in a strange land.","dt":"2022-01-30T11:04:55","s":["kg5wsfq0ke"]}],"12":[{"m":"God was saying my being with you is all the clearance you need.\n\nBut Moses was not going to buy that. He needed more and better proof, and he got that.\n\nGod being God speaks as he is, i.e. God, and “forgets” we are men and it will take some time and break down to be at his frequency.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:12:56","s":["brn3k0wa4p"]},{"m":"But to say that the proof or token of your words coming to pass is that they will come worship on this exact same mountain is no token.\n\nWe need proof in time, in the present, to assure us of the future — not the other way round.\n\nBut God, who lives not in time, does this strange thing of assuring Moses of present-day success and of his words coming to pass before Pharaoh in bringing the children of Israel out of Egypt, by pointing to the future.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:25:00","s":["zhci35mvbu"]},{"m":"Aah, so that answers the question of the mountain ⛰. Sinai.","dt":"2022-01-30T11:08:55","s":["xpytwoy0pf"]}],"13":[{"m":"Now Moses gives a practical breakdown of what would happen for God to come to terms with the reality on the ground.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:14:00","s":["f440edyz61"]}],"14":[{"m":"The questions we probe God with is what opens up dimensions of revelations to us.","dt":"2022-01-30T11:23:17","s":["suh162lezx"]}],"16":[{"m":"Say to them, the I AM, the God of your fathers, has sent you.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:19:11","s":["v4q5075kh3"]}],"18":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔, that was not exactly true.\n\nAnd Pharaoh read through it and made matters worse.\n\nIt was this and other hindrances like it that Moses tried explaining to God, that God would have none of.\n\nAnd Moses was proven right, but God already had it figured out — it was all part of the plan.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:22:36","s":["3pgx3903cq","1d4b88df93"]}],"19":[{"m":"God knew it won’t work, but it was all part of the plan.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:23:51","s":["bd3575b58b"]}],"20":[{"m":"The kind of wonders it took for Pharaoh to release Israel 🇮🇱 shows Egypt was a land of the supernatural.\n\nPharaoh himself must have thought himself a God-king 👑. His people even replicated some of God’s wonders.\n\nIt really took the extra supernatural and mighty hand 🖐️ of God to release Israel.\n\nIf not for God, Israel 🇮🇱 was never going to be free.\n\nI mean their enslavement was not just physical and through cunning ways, but entangled with sorcery and magic 🧝‍♂️.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:31:44","s":["em96mxcfn8","ac2c8292a8"]}],"15":[{"m":"Moses knew of the history of his people, but like history it’s a vague memory — Abraham died centuries back, so a sudden appearance of his God needs clarification.\n\nMoses asked to know HIS name, and unlike with Jacob, he did reveal himself by his true name.","dt":"2024-03-02T15:17:31","s":["kmfwzincut","774b641248"]}],"6":[{"m":"From day one, Moses saw the Lord face to face.\nThe premise had been set and was to continue throughout his journeys.","dt":"2026-01-30T07:16:52","s":["latqpzx50m"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"I like the negotiation going on. So practical and full of wisdom.\n\nAnd God answered likewise. So the Bible says, come let us reason together.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:26:45","s":["9047f34ad7"]}],"5":[{"m":"Dispensational change — Jehovah El Shaddai did none of these miracles.\n\nBut in this time and generation God was coming in full swing in power.\n\nThat may also be the reason in our time we seem to lack some of the power and miracles we see in scripture... or maybe it is happening in our time but not mainstream among the so-called popular televangelists.","dt":"2026-01-31T09:12:49","s":["pga1bnqv1"]}],"14":[{"m":"The all-knowing God, who knew Aaron was still angry in time about Moses’ unwillingness to trust him completely to go.\n\nIn mercy he provided Aaron as Moses’ mouthpiece.\n\nThe calling of God is without repentance.","dt":"2026-01-31T14:26:13","s":["h6upmp5gqe"]}],"17":[{"m":"So now Moses has his modus operandi drawn out for him. Easy as ABC.\n\nHowever, these days it seems if you want to be a prince 🤴 of power with God and to walk in the supernatural, there is so much suffering with fastings and hours of prayers unend without supernatural support.\n\nIs that how God really intends for access to him and to the supernatural by HIS own children to be like?","dt":"2024-03-02T16:05:43","s":["0c71458c6c"]}],"19":[{"m":"The Lord made sure of that.","dt":"2026-01-31T14:29:53","s":["w19f756jgx"]}],"20":[{"m":"I like this arrangement. Moses asked all the right questions, and got the right answers equipping him for the journey.\n\nHe took the rod for signs and wonders. Thus let’s learn in our walk with God to be true and real with him 🚶.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:31:18","s":["0f6b848647"]}],"22":[{"m":"God dealt with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob on a personal level, but with Israel 🇮🇱 on a national level. Also at this time they were a great host.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:32:48","s":["60cfeb64d8"]}],"31":[{"m":"Afflictions often lead to prayer.\n\nSo we can safely say they prayed and cried out in their affliction, and God answered them.","dt":"2024-03-02T16:09:37","s":["9k8563e5wb"]},{"m":"😇😇.. This is just the beginning.\n\nAt this stage they were glad and smiled. But the worst was yet to come before finally they will realize the victory ✌️. The victory ✌️ which they saw that made them smile ☺.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:37:46","s":["5wt5b37kvy"]}],"25":[{"m":"Strange scripture.\n\n1. Why did the Lord seek to slay MOSES, if even it was for not circumcising his son according to the covenant which he ought to have upheld in a foreign land?\n\n2. Why at this time, seeing he had already met him at the burning bush?\n\n3. How did Zipporah know that this would solve the problem?\n\nAll these cues are left out.","dt":"2026-01-31T14:35:42","s":["iutw7jcb26"]}]},"5":{"9":[{"m":"It has started, the pain before the gain.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:39:17","s":["f0c6ed87ce"]}],"18":[{"m":"How did Pharaoh so masterfully have such control over the people of Israel? It may likely be because of superior military might, and this system had been entrenched for decades so much so that it was in the psyche of the people — slave versus master mentality..\n\nIt likely may be, as in most slave cases, that those who tried to rebel were dealt with brutally and with death.","dt":"2026-01-31T14:50:26","s":["em0eq8stsv"]}],"21":[{"m":"It’s almost like they were cursing 🤬 Moses and Aaron for such ill luck 🤞.\n\nThey were there somewhere, as we say in Ghana, minding their own business and managing their pain.\n\nNow here comes Moses and his brother to give them hope, and now that hope has turned sour.\n\nSuch was the murmurings of the people, and that was to be their continuous trait all through their deliverance, even to their untimely grave.","dt":"2024-03-02T16:31:38","s":["tyhxyb8io6","a94caae21c"]}],"23":[{"m":"I like Moses’ questionings.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:41:01","s":["5072290732"]}]},"6":{"1":[{"m":"Oh my God. Did you not care about the doubling of affliction upon your people when ⚕ Pharaoh was contacted?\n\nWhy did you not just let Moses perform the needed miracles, but the people had to first suffer more?\n\nIt seems the Lord uses suffering as a tool, though we men hate it.\n\nWe see the same in the lives of all men. GOD, it seems, does not involve himself in the affairs of men, rarely until he is contacted, or it was already part of his plans and then he finds a man to use.\n\nSee Abraham, who suffered much, had an additional child 🧒 Ishmael who was not part of the plan originally, but God permitted it.\n\nThe ways of God must be learnt and studied.","dt":"2022-01-31T17:45:22","s":["15020961bc"]},{"m":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Now shalt thou see what I would do to Pharaoh.” It was almost like God was just waiting for this moment so he could demonstrate his greatness against Egypt.","dt":null,"d":[["undated","then the LORD said to Moses, now shall thou see what i would do to Pharaoh,.i t was almost like God was just waiting for this moment so he can demonstrate his greatness against Egypt\n\nGen 17:11-12 \" and it came to pass when Moses held up his hand , that Israel prevailed; and when he let down his hand, amalek prevailed, but Moses hand were heavy;\"\nThis verse is an enigma. The very hands that were providing strength to the army of israel did not receive strength. He Moses needed a rock to support his hands so it could still continue to provide strength to the tiring hands of the children of Israel.\nTruely we have this treasure in earthen vessels that the excellence of the power may be of God and not of man.\nThe workings of the realm of the spirit often is such that it's channelled through physical means. That is why sometimes, we ought to be at certain locations to access certain spiritual blessings. I ln like manner is the doctrine of laying on of hands. Its not that God cannot do it without the physical but just that is how the spiritual law works."]]}],"4":[{"m":"God always plays the long game.\n\nIn the short while he seems to be losing but in the long run he comes out tops.","dt":"2024-03-02T16:34:12","s":["114889b517"]},{"m":"The land where they walked in as strangers, having left what was theirs, where they had a heritage — Ur of the Chaldees and Haran — to a land not their own, so there they could be strangers and pilgrims.\n\nIt was only fair to give them as promised, having forfeited their own to attend to the Lord’s command.\n\nThe only problem with God’s promise was that they were not going to see it fulfilled in their lifetime, though God left enough evidence for them to trust in his words by what he did in their lifetime in their advantage.\n\nBut it still required believing.","dt":"2026-01-31T14:53:02","s":["3zb58rba7z"]}],"8":[{"m":"As I see how impossible 🙅 it would have been for Israel 🇮🇱 to be free from Pharaoh without God, I see also that it would take God for Africa 🌍 to be a liberated people.\n\nLord help us.","dt":"2024-03-02T16:35:58","s":["q3z7qogm1q","e508e9a60d"]}],"12":[{"m":"Moses was reasonable, and this reasoning was valid. Why would God ask Moses to go do the same thing he had done that failed? The message had to be different.\n\nIt was only wise to ask.\n\nThis begs the question: why would God, knowing the first time things did not go well, not come a second time with a new strategy or an enhanced one at least, but comes to give the same old command?\n\nMaybe it was to elicit this response from Moses — he loves to cooperate with man.\n\nHe loves to work with man and hear man’s reasoning and logic. This truly is a father-son relationship. Of course the father knows more than the son and gives command at his high level of reasoning as a father, but by the son speaking up at his own level the father then breaks down the plan to him.\n\nThis ought to be how as Christians we relate with our father in heaven.","dt":"2026-01-31T15:02:36","s":["zh5ogiepo5"]}],"26":[{"m":"It is interesting, the double or rather triple repetition above. Dake’s draws our mind to something: that initially Aaron was placed before Moses and then Moses was placed ahead.\nBut looking carefully, I see Aaron was placed before Moses (A), and then they were placed at par (B), then Moses was ahead (C).\nThe Holy Scriptures are so interesting. Subtle details you would never see if you don’t look closely. If you are not led there.","dt":null,"s":["d56ea399ad"]}],"9":[{"m":"I can imagine the looks and squelching Moses received as he attempted another motivational speech.\n\nHe had trusted the Lord anyway when he first went to see Pharaoh, despite his guts telling him this would not end well.\n\nYet at the word of the Lord he went, and things went badly as suspected, and the Lord unexpectedly did nothing.\n\nI’m sure Moses thought the Lord would work something out at this time, but he didn’t.\n\nGod was following his own calendar.","dt":"2024-03-02T16:39:00","s":["f11svnkqn1","84dae208fe"]}]},"7":{"10":[{"m":"It seems this was the 2nd time when they met Pharaoh, because the first time nothing of the sort is stated.\n\nI’m sure after this display, though he did not let them go, he did not punish them senselessly as before, because this time he was seeing the hand of God at play.\n\nBut at this time he thought of God as one of the gods, and God played along with that at the beginning.\n\nAllowing himself to be introduced as the God of the Hebrews.","dt":"2026-01-31T15:09:12","s":["08v2qzqssk"]}],"11":[{"m":"🇪🇬 Egypt was really a dark place, a nation super powerful and also supported in the corridors of power by witchcraft and enchantments.\n\nWhat manner of power and enchantment is this???\n\nMen who can turn their rods into snakes 🐍 — such deep stuff... And that wasn’t all, they could cause natural disasters like sending fleas etc.\n\nThe men of Egypt were indeed powerhouses, and Pharaoh himself I believe was no exception — how else could he have enchantment around him without being involved himself?","dt":"2024-03-07T12:40:45","s":["ey6wyxta4p"]},{"m":"This was the kind of spirit ruling over the nation; it was going to take spiritual power and backing to take over such a nation.\n\nAnd the same happens now, where strange malevolent spirits rule nations and govern states.\n\nAnd they would not relinquish such sweet control and power. Over their dead bodies — you might as well kill them, and that literally so.\n\nNo wonder they will kill you to keep their thrones of influence.\n\nWe must know that as we enter and take territories for Christ, else we be beaten at the game because we underestimate the enemy and the nature of the game.\n\nIt’s done very clandestinely and like sleight of hand 🖐️ — one moment they are smiling ☺ with you and the next moment voila, you are thrown under the bus 🚍.","dt":"2024-03-07T12:45:05","s":["1vide74bdj"]}],"12":[{"m":"Where did these men learn such magic 🧝‍♂️ and power? Who taught them?","dt":"2022-01-31T17:51:55","s":["mr62y4fkbk"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why did Pharaoh tolerate the presence of Moses and Aaron when he could have just ordered their execution?\nWho knows — these people had tried killing Moses spiritually and physically and failed.\n\nProbably, though not recorded, Moses might have disappeared right before their eyes 👀.\n\nThey knew Moses to be a powerful sorcerer. After multiple attempts they concluded this was but the finger of God.","dt":"2024-03-07T12:48:27","s":["8hgh1rbtlt"]}]},"8":{"7":[{"m":"The magicians 🧝‍♂️ had matched Moses boot for boot so far.\n\nJust that they could not reverse what Moses did. They could just duplicate same, but Moses could reverse whatever he did.","dt":"2024-03-07T12:50:57","s":["4973xf08zr"]}],"19":[{"m":"Pharaoh thought he was a demi God. He saw the finger of God yet hardened his heart. Believers see the finger of man and cower.","dt":null,"s":["ad3927a449"]},{"m":"It was after they could not duplicate what Moses did that they concluded that this was the finger of God, and not the curious charms of men, wise so-called.","dt":"2024-03-07T13:00:37","s":["hg5w7ex8rr"]},{"m":"The Egyptians had many gods — gods of fertility, harvest etc.\n\nI wonder who Elohim was to them, but obviously they knew that aside all the other gods there was this one God who is called Elohim who surpassed all the other gods.\n\nOr it could mean, since they were producing results through enchantments just as Moses was, they thought they were on the same level with Moses, just that he Moses was an advanced wizard 🧙‍♂️.\n\nHowever, at this point they realized that this is not the cunning and curious act of men, neither is it the power of sorcery; rather this was the finger of the Elohim (the gods), because Elohim means Gods.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:29:10","s":["zszgt1w9py"]},{"m":"It was only after their magic failed to work that they realised this was the finger of God. All along they thought it was a contest of power and who knew more magic.\n\nBut this time they realise it was no longer a battle of men who all had access to the realm of the spirit and to magical powers. It was now a contest of God.\n\nGod against man... suddenly it was not that someone’s magic power was more potent than the other, but rather suddenly — Moses had all the power and all of them put together had none.","dt":"2026-01-31T15:43:14","s":["vx9ydoive1"]},{"m":"At the very beginning, God seems to be permitting the 🧝‍♂️ magicians to also counter with their powers.\n\nI suspect it was all part of the agenda to harden Pharaoh’s heart ♥ 🐍.\n\nNow at this time enough was enough. The enchantments 🧙‍♀️ failed.\n\nEven the magicians 🧝‍♂️ concluded that this indeed was the hand 🖐️ or rather finger of God.\n\nThe great God himself who created the other gods was involved here.\n\nThe tricks and games were over.","dt":"2022-02-01T07:35:10","s":["j8xezls53h"]}],"22":[{"m":"I don’t think this implied that the earlier plagues affected both cities. It affected the Egyptians only.\n\nAlso, with so much disruption going on in Egypt 🇪🇬, Israel now had much needed respite from hard labour as their slave masters had their own issues to deal with.","dt":"2024-03-07T12:58:12","s":["8slb0qgy1z"]},{"m":"Does that imply all the previous plagues affected everyone?\n\nBecause it seems from this statement that the separation of Egypt 🇪🇬 from 🇮🇱 Israel itself was a sign 🤘.\n\nI can imagine that by now the confidence of Israel had risen tenfold.\n\nI doubt they were being molested or cruelly treated at this stage by their Egyptian masters.","dt":"2022-02-01T07:38:04","s":["m90u3hmtiw"]}],"23":[{"m":"I believe that in our walk with God, we should just trust the process.\n\nSee, God did not start with killing of the first borns of Egypt.\n\nNo, he did not even start with a miracle. It started with ill favour coming upon Israel.\n\nThen the miracles started — pretty exciting, right 😏 — only for the magicians to produce same results.\n\nSo that neutralises what God was doing as nothing.\n\nThen came miracles which none other could perform.\n\nGod knew what he was doing from the beginning.\n\nThen now he performs the plagues and gives physical boundaries as to how far the plagues could go.\n\nJust like he has given boundaries to the sea 🌊.\n\nThe ways of God. 🤦‍♂️ Beyond searching 🔎.","dt":"2022-02-01T07:43:08","s":["j0qj9un4oi"]},{"m":"And I will sever in that day the land of Goshen, in which my people dwell, that no swarms of flies shall be there; to the end thou mayest know that I am the Lord in the midst of the earth.\nExodus 8:22 KJV\n\nI believe that in our walk with God, we should just trust the process.\n\nWhen it came to liberating Israel from bondage in Egypt, God did not start with killing of the first borns of Egypt.\n\nNo, he did not even start with a miracle. He started with a promise, the birth of Moses and finally their liberation from Egypt.\n\nEven when God started the miracles, I believe it might have been pretty exciting 😏 — only for the magicians to produce same results.\n\nThis sort of neutralises what God was doing as nothing, but God was up to something.\n\nThen came miracles which none other could perform.\n\nIn Exodus 8:23 KJV he says: And I will put a division between my people and thy people: to morrow shall this sign be.\n\nThe ways of God are 🤦‍♂️ beyond searching 🔎. Eventually Pharaoh released the children of Israel. This was the end game, but it followed a design and pathway beyond the thinking of mere mortals.\n\nSO TRUST THE PROCESS: the meanderings and hard-to-grasp ride that your life may be going through.\n\nThe endgame victory and glory to the name of God.","dt":"2022-08-04T15:49:59","s":["1zcbxeb1te"]}],"30":[{"m":"Again Moses uses entreaties, pleading with the Lord, not just waving 👋 his hand and things magically happened.\n\nEven though it was God who sent him, he had to make entreaties of God to reverse it.\n\nHe did not make entreaties of God to send the swarm and the flies, but when it came to wanting God to do his bidding he had to wait on the Lord and make entreaties and cries.\n\nThis shows that in God’s providence, he does not need man’s active involvement, but when man engages God, there is a way to go about it even if man’s request is actually the will of God.\n\nHmm 🤔... Very interesting 🤔.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:36:55","s":["ijdklrdz8h"]},{"m":"It reminds me of Elijah stopping the heavens with a word, and yet to reverse it he had to make great entreaties in prayers for long.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:39:49","s":["40gao4j3nr"]}],"3":[{"m":"What happened to the bloody river?\n\nNatural laws took over, and likely the blood river flowed into the sea and fresh water flowed in.","dt":"2026-01-31T15:12:10","s":["wyt9nv7m2u"]}],"9":[{"m":"Moses was so sure. How?? Because he had such a relationship with God there was no doubt 🤷‍♂️.\n\nI mean he just spoke to God like face to face yesterday, why would the answer be no when it was God who sent him in the first place.","dt":"2022-02-01T08:03:35","s":["rm9uq9akcr"]}],"11":[{"m":"I’m wondering, at this time it was very likely the abuse of the Israelites had ceased — nobody wanted to be in the bad books of this their so-called God.","dt":"2024-03-07T12:52:52","s":["txf566fujq"]}],"12":[{"m":"This was not done at the swinging of a wand like we see on TV.\n\nIt was through cries and intercession until heaven heeded and the Lord showed up.\n\nHow that Moses could intercede for his enemies with cries is a whole different ball game.\n\n⚽ Moses had mastered the art of intercession and entreaty before the Lord.","dt":"2024-03-07T12:55:06","s":["p8oi232hxl"]}],"31":[{"m":"It says the Lord did according to the word of Moses. Left to God alone, probably he would have left the swarms on them all day long.\n\nBut Moses had gone to place a bargain, and God answered according to Moses’ bidding.\n\nMoses was a master intercessor and had mastered how to get answers from God.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:38:51","s":["7tf6ppea6a"]}]},"9":{"8":[{"m":"In the sight of Pharaoh, so he knows it’s not coincidence.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:40:44","s":["nflbptqsvc"]}],"11":[{"m":"With all those boils all over them it would have been so embarrassing to try and stand before Moses.\n\nJust imagine that... Coming in to contest Moses with big boils all over you.\n\nIf you have power, then undo the boils on you.\n\nComing to claim you have power to face Moses yet the boils are on you makes your claim so obviously a lie.","dt":"2026-02-01T09:54:38","s":["jrvmaejvxy"]},{"m":"Does that mean the magicians 🧝‍♂️ attempted to undo the boils, or invoke similar boils to nullify God’s?","dt":"2022-02-01T09:54:28","s":["dcdkqfy9pb"]}],"13":[{"m":"Why early morning? Or was that when he could catch Pharaoh?\n\nI wonder how long all these plagues took place.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:42:18","s":["4ai9s6rls3"]}],"16":[{"m":"The sovereignty, supremacy and omniscience of God.\n\nPharaoh was but a tool in the hands 👐 of the master.","dt":"2022-02-01T09:55:57","s":["bwr7185gnq"]}],"17":[{"m":"God was in full-scale God mode.\n\nMan saw vividly the hand of God and the evidence of God.\n\nMany of us would wish to have seen God on display this way.\n\nThat is how the end of the world would be... God would be in full-scale God mode, displaying his powers, and all men will see.","dt":"2026-02-01T09:56:57","s":["wqv9bqiyl1"]}],"21":[{"m":"God was gradually making believers even out of the Egyptians. Those were wise guys.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:43:30","s":["e7w0orxxp6"]}],"23":[{"m":"It’s as if God wanted it to be clear that the hail was not by some random works, but it happened as Moses stretched his hands 👐 towards heaven.\n\nHe made sure of that.","dt":"2022-02-02T02:25:22","s":["r4gr3z6s19"]}],"28":[{"m":"How did Moses reach Pharaoh... he passed through the hail?\n\nYes, and was divinely protected from it hurting him.\n\nIt would have destroyed him if there was no divine protection upon his life.\n\nBecause once the hail started it followed natural order to destroy anything in its way...\n\nBut the Lord, who severed between Egypt and Israel, protected Moses, a Jew, from the hail as he walked through to see Pharaoh.","dt":"2026-02-01T10:01:02","s":["s0zwg0lw30"]}],"35":[{"m":"How can a man see these signs and yet remain unrepentant?\n\nThis goes to show the nature 🏞 of man 👨. That signs and wonders do not always bring true repentance.","dt":"2022-02-01T09:58:57","s":["q4f1svxvvp"]}],"33":[{"m":"It sounds like Moses went out of the city and out of the hail to the land of Israel, or at least to where there was no hail, so he could pray to the Lord without being knocked down by the very hail he prayed for.\n\nThis is practically wisdom in relating with the supernatural and the divine.\n\nHe kept reason and common sense in relating with the supernatural, i.e. natural laws are not suspended except where God says so.\n\nAnd do not be presumptuous in the supernatural to assume all natural laws are suspended.","dt":"2026-02-01T10:05:00","s":["5wsqf5wcl7"]}]},"10":{"11":[{"m":"He budged a bit, this Pharaoh, and was willing to negotiate, but this was non-negotiable, so he damned them to go away from him.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:47:33","s":["t979enp4up"]}],"13":[{"m":"The miracle of plagues that the Lord brought upon Egypt 🇪🇬 followed a process.\n\nIn the sense that God did not cause locusts to appear everywhere in Egypt.\n\nRather Moses had to stretch his rod and an east wind 🍃 blew all day and night 🌃.\n\nAnd then the wind carried the locusts.\n\nI won’t be surprised 🤨 Moses literally had to stretch his hands 👐 for almost the entire time the wind blew till there was enough, as in Elijah’s prayer for rain ☔, who saw a cloud 🌥 as a hand 🖐️ to signal it was done.\n\nGod is a God of process, not some sporadic 🚶 random and erratic God.\n\nLet’s learn from these things as we walk with God.\n\nThis brings to mind mine own experiences in my walk with God.\n\nHis presence can almost always be guaranteed once you know what to do to get into him.\n\nI can personally tell how to activate his presence and power in my life 😘 keep it.\n\nI know what to do to keep his presence and to literally harvest it for the day’s activities.\n\nI have not experienced certain realms of glory because I have not paid certain prices 🏆 🏆.","dt":"2022-02-02T02:20:41","s":["2r3fqf1kys"]}],"23":[{"m":"How did this happen... how was this achieved?","dt":"2026-02-02T07:46:19","s":["7o3bf33p70"]}],"29":[{"m":"Wow such insolence and stupidity.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:52:51","s":["p7pa0vqd2"]}],"20":[{"m":"When men show themselves shrewd before the Lord, he also would show himself even more shrewd than they are.\n\nHow Pharaoh could see all these and remain adamant is mind-boggling.\n\nSo guess what — where the evidence was too impossible to resist, God hardened Pharaoh’s heart so he resisted the evidence anyway.\n\nThis is akin to when God talks of handing men over to strange lusts since they refused to go by what is natural.\n\nAnd we see same in our world today with the alphabet community.\nLiteral madness held as normalcy.\n\nA strange time we find ourselves in today.","dt":"2024-03-08T06:51:53","s":["p40m724z0b"]}]},"11":{"8":[{"m":"Hol'dit… A man who had brought such destruction to the nation, and after threatening the death ☠ of their first born they still waited for it to happen?? 😳 😳 😳\n\nDid they somehow doubt 🤷‍♂️ because such a thing had never been heard of?\n\nThis itself is a miracle and could only be the finger of God hardening their hearts 💕 in order to completely destroy them and make a name.\n\nThe El Shaddai God of Abraham did not at all seem to be that terrible 😰.\n\nNow he's showing and displaying his full 🌕 wrath, taking his place again as the 👑 monarch of the universe 🌌.","dt":"2022-02-02T02:34:52","s":["3hkyltb2gy","2aa025d8f8"]}],"9":[{"m":"😇 It was almost as if God was feeling sorry for Moses.\n\nThat he was really angry 😡 on God's behalf. Meanwhile God was calm about the whole situation because he knew Pharaoh won't change 💱.\n\nSo he chipped in to Moses: Pharaoh won't listen 👂, just forget him and save your heart ♥.\n\nThis depth of relationship is so enviable. So so enviable and worth emulating.","dt":"2022-02-02T11:40:16","s":["cf8e237521"]}],"10":[{"m":"Looking at the character of Pharaoh, he really deserved the hardening of heart the Lord gave him, so as to bring him down heavily and with a mighty hand.\n\nI mean, such insolence! So, to compound his punishment on Pharaoh and his people, God hardened their leader's heart.\n\nIt was also to punish them for their enslavement of his first born, Israel.\n\nImagine if Pharaoh had given in at the very early stages... then they would have escaped the judgement they deserved.","dt":"2026-02-02T07:52:17","s":["rm4q28jy9a"]}]},"12":{"1":[{"m":"He spoke to them both.\n\nSo they both heard.\n\nDid he come as a person and speak face to face, or did they only hear words?\n\nI am beginning to think he came in a physical form whenever the Bible says God spoke to someone.\n\nAnd when the expression “the word of the Lord came” is used, it is in reference to only hearing the voice but not seeing a person.","dt":"2024-03-09T17:23:26","s":["db73663aa1"]}],"12":[{"m":"Ahh, power and authority has spoken. God was saying: I will execute judgement on all the gods of Egypt 🇪🇬, for I am the ‘I AM’… I love that.","dt":"2022-02-02T03:00:45","s":["4me30lt2wp","d65280e15a"]}],"33":[{"m":"The Egyptians were so stubborn. For it to take such an action for them to release Israel shows how much benefit they were deriving from them.","dt":"2024-03-09T17:28:12","s":["0934ab4779"]}],"36":[{"m":"I can imagine them telling their Egyptian masters, “The Lord requires gold and silver for the sacrifices we would be making to him… Much gold will we require.”\n\nAnd so the word which God had spoken to Moses from the beginning happened.","dt":"2024-03-09T17:30:33","s":["0yy80nvyva"]}],"40":[{"m":"What is the calculation of it? Most say the children of Israel spent 400 full years in slavery, but Dake’s calculates the 400 years from the call of Abraham to the exodus from Egypt, and there are many proofs to that.","dt":"2022-02-02T03:07:38","s":["80aotut72f","a15c8c774e"]}],"41":[{"m":"All the hosts of the Lord obviously referred to the children of Israel, but not just them.\n\nRemember what the Lord told Jacob before he died — that he would go down with them to Egypt.\n\nI believe there was a company of angels who went with the children of Israel in Egypt, to favour their cause and expand them.\n\nThese same hosts now needed to leave Egypt with the children of Israel for the promised land.\n\nIndeed, HOSTS of God left Egypt for Canaan.","dt":"2026-02-02T08:08:27","s":["s1v2wy73o8"]}],"32":[{"m":"How could he have the mind to ask for a blessing in this circumstance? Except to say he probably was so scared he wanted to be prayed for, so his kingdom would be kept from further wrath.","dt":"2022-02-02T03:05:58","s":["81e7ac22a6"]}]},"13":{"9":[{"m":"So the law of God was constantly on their mouth 👄.\n\nWhy? Because the human mind so easily forgets and is easily influenced by information and data from the 5 senses.\n\nBy ensuring that the law of God is before the eyes and on the hands 👐 and on their lips, the mind is constantly aware of God and of his laws.\n\nThis influences behaviour and makes obedience of God's law pretty natural.","dt":"2024-03-11T12:51:59","s":["484790c477"]}],"17":[{"m":"Peradventure is not a word you use for an omniscient God. It sounds unsure and not too certain.\n\nHowever, there are times we see the omniscience of God on display.\n\nFor instance, in the case of Pharaoh, he knew he would not let the people go no matter how much evidence was brought to the fore.\n\nDake’s suggests that God’s omniscience does not mean he knows every single thought and action and possibility.\n\nIn his estimation that would be stretching God's omniscience too far.\n\nThis assertion by Dake’s I disagree with 👎.\n\nI believe the use of peradventure adds some human element to God's nature and his dealings and conversations with man 👨, especially the man Moses.\n\nThis does not mean he had no way of knowing the Israelites would flee at the least hindrance.","dt":"2024-03-13T12:27:56","s":["13jsa15nsa","0be633b480"]}],"19":[{"m":"Over a century had passed since his death ☠, yet they kept the words of covenant of their progenitor Joseph.\n\nFor some of us, sadly, we are lost and have no progenitor blessings or inheritance.\n\nWe must rather set such a system of inheritance and blessings for our children, God being our helper.","dt":"2024-03-13T12:32:50","s":["da0f7e2cf0"]}],"22":[{"m":"Wow.. It was before their eyes day and night 🌃.","dt":"2024-03-13T12:33:44","s":["da972aaf3a"]}],"15":[{"m":"So in reality the first born in the jurisdiction of Egypt were to be killed.\n\nBut the first born of Egypt were killed, and that of Israel was to be redeemed by the death of another.\n\nSo the law of death of the first born was modified for Israel 🇮🇱, in the sense that death was to take place but not immediately.\n\nFor beasts, they were going to have their firstborn sacrificed, and for every male firstborn human it was to be swapped for a lamb — life for life — it is a spiritual law.","dt":"2024-03-11T12:55:49","s":["wop4snvzzs","9ff1224e06"]}],"18":[{"m":"And by so doing, he had them trapped between Egypt and the Red Sea. Thus they could not run in the face of war and death, but had to learn to trust the might of God.\n\nThis way God was gradually training them to rely on him.\n\nA lesson they took too long to learn, to their own detriment.","dt":"2024-03-13T12:31:02","s":["0dva2c7rvb","2115c7de4f"]}]},"14":{"5":[{"m":"This is madness…😡.. A spirit of mental illness was upon them.\n\nWhy would you do that after all that was done to you?\n\nThey had so soon forgotten.\n\nThe note above was in Feb 2022 — to add to it (13th March 2024): the spirit of madness was brought upon them by the Lord, i.e. the hardness of their hearts. I have also dropped a comment on the possible elements accounting for this behaviour of theirs from a natural perspective and a supernatural perspective, and these two ✌️, i.e. the natural and supernatural, merge nicely.","dt":"2022-02-02T14:43:19","s":["30grqn5in7","tq4m7qz76e"]},{"m":"This suggests that:\n\n1. Pharaoh understood that Israel 🇮🇱 was going into the wilderness to serve the Lord, albeit for three days as Moses had said earlier, and to return.\n\n2. He disagreed because he long suspected they ran the risk of taking advantage to flee.\n\n3. Now that he had gotten word that indeed they did flee, his fears were confirmed.\n\n4. Pharaoh had spies and eyes on Israel 🇮🇱 to check out what they were doing and if they would flee.\n\n5. For Pharaoh to have kept eyes on Israel 🇮🇱 despite all the loss he had suffered indicated he wanted them to come back as agreed 🤝 — to let them come back into his domain after their God had killed their first born.\n\n6. For Pharaoh to have pursued Israel 🇮🇱 even after all the loss of his first born and all the loss from the plagues indicates he, Pharaoh, was never going to let Israel go under any circumstance.\n\n7. For Pharaoh's and his subjects' hearts to be so set on never letting Israel go except over their own dead bodies — not that of their sons or property — indicates the grand benefits they were enjoying under their enslavement of 🇮🇱 Israel 🇮🇱.\n\n7b. Israel 🇮🇱 was literally their life, and they couldn't imagine nor live without the contribution of the Israelites.\n\nThey would rather die than give up such a life.\n\nNow I understand why men, the wicked, would kill for fame, riches and material possessions. This is wisdom.\n\n7c. This explains why God told Moses to start off by asking for a three-day journey into the wilderness. He was never going to budge under any circumstances if the reason was for them to just go free to their promised land.\n\n8. This is the heart of man under demonic hardening and divine influence; how much more when men, especially believers, are under the influence of demonic spirits and demon-possessed human beings.\n\nThey will not let us go except by the finger of God. This was a whole nation, so it was the hand 🖐️ of God, but Christ lets us know that he casts out demons by the finger ☝️ of God.","dt":"2024-03-13T12:49:58","s":["bqm9i9xwud","a5da920bdc"]}],"7":[{"m":"So this was the military might by which Egypt kept Israel enslaved.\n\nThey were never going to be free.. no, not in a thousand years.","dt":"2026-02-04T07:27:50","s":["ypz4s3prdl"]}],"12":[{"m":"Their faith, not even just faith but even their memory, failed them.\n\nThey had so soon forgotten. But that is the nature 🏞 of the flesh. It's so powerful and controls us so easily.\n\nThe fear of death and the looming danger of the army of the then super 👌 power.\n\nMoses did exhibit faith though.","dt":"2022-02-02T14:47:30","s":["9df7958bf9"]}],"15":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔.. The Lord was tough on Moses; the days of crying 😢 out were passing... Take action, says the Lord... Move forward.","dt":"2022-02-02T14:51:14","s":["nah4cvs69k","e4adbd3b2a"]}],"16":[{"m":"Not just move forward but stretch out thine hand 🖐️ and divide the sea 🌊.\n\nNow the Moses–God partnership was coming so strong 💪, it seemed it was Moses who was doing the division ➗.","dt":"2022-02-03T05:32:08","s":["5f13e9349c"]}],"19":[{"m":"So there was the pillar of cloud 🌥 and the angel 😇 of the Lord right before their faces, and yet they doubted the Lord.\n\nIt is human nature; we all fall prey to it, and these have been written for our learning.","dt":"2024-03-14T14:03:50","s":["d92140bb25"]}],"21":[{"m":"How long did this take for the sea to begin to be parted?\n\nI don't think 🤔, as soon as Moses stretched his hand 🖐️, the parting began…. It might have taken some time.","dt":"2024-03-14T14:07:06","s":["9xk0mbhnqy","5f2cbd1a7e"]}],"24":[{"m":"At this point it was both at the same time... i.e. the pillar of...","dt":"2024-03-14T14:08:29","s":["oeqk19222e"]}],"26":[{"m":"So God honored the leadership of his servant Moses, causing Moses to do the physical actions and he, God, fulfilling it.\n\nThis way his leadership was greatly honored in the eyes 👀 of Israel.\n\nThis again goes to buttress the point that God is a God of process. He is not erratic.","dt":"2022-02-03T05:38:27","s":["5e6a1ff2bb"]}],"27":[{"m":"Was this an all-night event, i.e. the restoration of the sea? Did he stretch his hand literally all night? Possibly he did, till the sea returned, as we see in the war with Amalek when he stretched his hand till the war was over.\n\nProbably this duration was shorter than that of the war with Amalek, because in the war Moses' hand got so tired it needed support.","dt":"2024-03-14T14:09:52","s":["ofogdo5841","7575e27f8e"]}],"13":[{"m":"Moses had been prior notified that this would happen, so he was bold in the face of death ☠.","dt":"2022-02-02T14:48:55","s":["8abb7a8bf4"]}],"25":[{"m":"Why are they now realizing this... A spirit of stupor was upon them.\n\nAfter all the Lord had done against them all these ten times in Egypt through the plagues, are they now realising this?\n\nWell, it was too late now.\n\nThen I realized in like manner the devil and demons can cast darkness upon a man so that foolishly he digs his own grave.\n\nLet's look at our own lives — we sometimes make some of the most stupid of decisions and wonder what we were thinking when we made them.\n\nThings we could have very easily walked away from, but we continue on in them to our hurt.\n\nLord, deliver us from any demonic bondage and blindness set over our hearts 💕 to our own hurt.\n\nDeliver us, oh God, deliver us.","dt":"2026-02-04T07:37:42","s":["1138fva2u2"]}]},"15":{"4":[{"m":"Pharaoh was such a strong 💪, revered and feared 😱 name on the lips of the Israelites, and now the tyrant has been destroyed.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:32:04","s":["377b0b6140"]}],"13":[{"m":"Indeed, they were a redeemed people, redeemed by the mighty hand of the Lord through miracles, signs and wonders.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:34:03","s":["a23465a3c5"]}],"25":[{"m":"A very effective way to etch his words in their hearts 💕. After three days of thirst — a very difficult experience to forget for a lifetime — Israel 🇮🇱 was told that just as water was healed for them to drink, so also the Lord heals their diseases.","dt":"2022-02-03T06:43:22","s":["f884b8906a"]}],"26":[{"m":"Every chance God had, he took advantage to drive home a point or 2.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:37:27","s":["4a5161d943"]}]},"16":{"1":[{"m":"It took that long for their reserves to run out.\n\nAnd that was exactly the Lord's plan.\n\nJust like the bitter waters of Marah took three days to reach, and the Lord healed the water to implant in their minds that he is their healer.\n\nHere he wants to show them he is their provider and keeper.\n\nUnder such conditions, hopefully the lessons won't be forgotten.\n\nBut 👨 man, they forgot over and over, even under such harsh teaching conditions by which to etch the lessons in memory.","dt":"2026-02-04T08:03:30","s":["u4bn8ic9bf"]}],"2":[{"m":"One month of being in the wilderness, they were hungry and growing lean by now, I suspect.\n\nI understand Israel 🇮🇱. The need to survive. Yes, God worked miracles, we agree.\n\nBut now how do they survive if there is no food 🍲?\n\nIt would have been nice if after crossing the Red Sea there were miracles of water, immediately followed by manna.\n\nThen there would have been no need for murmurings and the like.\n\nThat is only fair 🧚‍♂️, considering that this is a wilderness and God had the ability to feed them.\n\nSo now the million dollar question was, WHY DID GOD TREAT THEM THIS WAY?","dt":"2022-02-05T07:58:51","s":["7b15391549"]}],"4":[{"m":"This was a very difficult situation God put Moses in.\n\nI believe it never crossed the mind of Moses that God would feed them angels' bread 🥪.\n\nI mean, who would have thought of such things?\n\nI'm sure he prayed for provisions and increase for the goods and livelihood of the people.\n\nThe journey was to be 10 days ideally, but they went via a longer route.\n\nIt was already a month and a half, and it was starting to look like the Lord wanted to bring them out to kill them in the wilderness.\n\nThe burden on Moses's head was getting heavier with each passing day, much prayers and fastings, and the Lord had not said anything yet concerning the people's food 🍲.\n\nNow their stock was running 🏃 dry.\n\nAnd Moses and God spoke face to face, so obviously Moses had asked and God had told him to trust him, or maybe he refrained from answering, or maybe God spoke to him face to face but not daily.\n\nAnd it had been a while since the Lord showed forth; the last time he was at the waters of Marah.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:46:37","s":["21bdad468e"]}],"6":[{"m":"Once the Lord spoke, they could speak the same and now become bold.\n\nBut till then they had to wait for the Lord. Not even Moses could just get up and declare anything or any solution at all he wanted.\n\nIt always had to be in concert with the Lord.\n\nThe one time he did deviate from this protocol and assumed to just exercise spiritual power without the Lord, it led to his disqualification from the promise.\n\nHe was cut off from the promised land.\n\nThe Lord takes matters of usurping spiritual authority and protocols very seriously.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:50:37","s":["df4559f92e"]}],"8":[{"m":"They were trying their very best for the people to appreciate how powerful and how much of a provider God is, so as to keep them from murmuring in future challenges.\n\nBut they never learnt till they were totally cast out of the promise.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:52:04","s":["bpqy19m9ep","db16b69683"]}],"28":[{"m":"God was very strict and firm with his commandments.\n\nHe did not entertain disobedience... He may let it slide but will definitely bring it to mind.","dt":"2022-02-03T17:22:34","s":["79e1myb89o","5d93f98d68"]}],"29":[{"m":"Working with man can be so frustrating.. even God was getting tired of them. So as a leader, lead with a heart of patience but diligence.","dt":"2026-02-04T08:07:38","s":["xr08w6cycy"]}],"31":[{"m":"Hmm, I can imagine the taste was nice.","dt":"2024-03-15T14:57:08","s":["45ecab9f2c"]}],"35":[{"m":"?? 😳 😳 😳\n\nForty years.\n\n40 years eating one food 🍲 type, though I suspect they found creative ways of cooking it differently.","dt":"2022-02-03T17:24:31","s":["548abfd468"]}]},"17":{"3":[{"m":"Why did God cause them to hunger and thirst?","dt":"2022-02-03T17:25:43","s":["sqv9h39u2s","681134f613"]}],"6":[{"m":"Is not this Horeb, where Moses was first called in the burning bush?","dt":"2026-02-04T08:11:43","s":["ueiuysu5j5"]}],"8":[{"m":"There is a scripture which talks of Amalek harming the weaker ones at the rear of the camp.\n\nIf this is the same incident, then now Joshua prepared for a proper war.","dt":"2022-02-03T18:06:45","s":["26f9o92m9e","ce3bb0ce80"]}],"12":[{"m":"That is a very long time to have your hand 🖐️ up.\n\nSo it's not whether you gave your best or not... It's if you paid the price required.\n\nThey, i.e. Aaron and Hur, had to find a way of meeting the requirements to ensure victory.\n\nSo our responsibility is to find out what the requirements are and to meet the demands thereof ✌️.","dt":"2022-02-03T18:09:23","s":["5xw95sqq81","69bea3e1f5"]}],"14":[{"m":"Joshua was already being groomed.","dt":"2024-03-15T15:00:00","s":["640ce51cc1"]}],"4":[{"m":"Moses had a real and loving relationship with the Lord.\n\nIt was like a man relating to his father.\n\nAlso I wonder, if God answered Moses this often, why did he not get answers before things got out of hand 🖐️?\n\nThis is my strong belief: Moses often foresaw the need of the people, as any leader would.\n\nBut God delayed until the people were almost ready to do the unthinkable: stone Moses or go back to Egypt.\n\nThis begs the question again. Why?","dt":"2022-02-03T17:28:35","s":["r4t1tylkiy","fd1e721a3a"]}],"11":[{"m":"Ex 17:11–12: “And it came to pass, when Moses held up his hand, that Israel prevailed: and when he let down his hand, Amalek prevailed. But Moses' hands were heavy;”\nThis verse is an enigma. The very hands that were providing strength to the army of Israel did not receive strength. He, Moses, needed a rock to support his hands so they could still continue to provide strength to the tiring hands of the children of Israel.\nTruly we have this treasure in earthen vessels, that the excellence of the power may be of God and not of man.\nThe workings of the realm of the spirit often are such that they're channelled through physical means. That is why sometimes we ought to be at certain locations to access certain spiritual blessings. In like manner is the doctrine of laying on of hands. It's not that God cannot do it without the physical, but just that is how the spiritual law works.","dt":null,"d":[["undated","then the LORD said to Moses, now shall thou see what i would do to Pharaoh,.i t was almost like God was just waiting for this moment so he can demonstrate his greatness against Egypt\n\nGen 17:11-12 \" and it came to pass when Moses held up his hand , that Israel prevailed; and when he let down his hand, amalek prevailed, but Moses hand were heavy;\"\nThis verse is an enigma. The very hands that were providing strength to the army of israel did not receive strength. He Moses needed a rock to support his hands so it could still continue to provide strength to the tiring hands of the children of Israel.\nTruely we have this treasure in earthen vessels that the excellence of the power may be of God and not of man.\nThe workings of the realm of the spirit often is such that it's channelled through physical means. That is why sometimes, we ought to be at certain locations to access certain spiritual blessings. I ln like manner is the doctrine of laying on of hands. Its not that God cannot do it without the physical but just that is how the spiritual law works."]]}]},"18":{"23":[{"m":"It was a good idea how Jethro made sure to add the caveat of “if it 😌 pleased the Lord”.\n\nNot all good ideas please the Lord nor displease him.\n\nWe have to commit our ways to the Lord at all times.","dt":"2026-02-04T08:18:24","s":["zyi090eqxf"]}],"11":[{"m":"I think it's in reference to the many gods of Egypt whom God made a show of...\n\nFor instance, Dake’s commentary suggests that each of the plagues was against a god of Egypt, for Egypt had a god for everything.\n\nThe Nile, which became blood, was contrary to their god.. the locusts, the boils, all these contradicted the power of the gods whose domain it was to protect Egypt and their worshippers from such.","dt":"2026-02-04T08:15:52","s":["8jighjaqnu"]}]},"19":{"20":[{"m":"How? Bodily, or as a cloud 🌥, or bodily and in the cloud 🌥?","dt":"2026-02-06T06:58:24","s":["szc5rw730p"]}]},"20":{"20":[{"m":"Moses, Moses...\n\nHe was in such an intimate relationship with God that he feared not the Lord.\n\nHe understood that he was not to dishonor or disregard God because he was familiar with him.\n\nFamiliarity was not to set in, but then he also knew he was God and needed to be accorded honour..\n\nThere is a proverb in Ghana that if someone is known to you in the day, you do not light a lamp to identify him at night 🌃.\n\nMoses knew God so well that the thunderings and lightning 🌩, the darkness and smoke did not change 💱 his knowledge of God.. He knew it was all a matter of power display, but God was his Lord, father and friend.\n\nHe did not disregard the symbols, but he also did not misinterpret them, despite the fear 😱 it caused.\n\nFear not.","dt":"2022-02-05T18:03:29","s":["f0hv16k9h4","e76ed05750"]}],"22":[{"m":"Interesting.\n\nGod tells them that, as they can see, he spoke to them from heaven, so obviously he is the God of heaven.\n\nIf not, how could he have dominated the heavens to speak from there to them?\n\nHow can a man take another's house except he first binds the strong man?\n\nSo for God to speak from heaven, that is where he stays and rules.\n\nIn that light no one should make other gods beside him... not of silver or gold.\n\nBecause, as he himself said and as observed by the children of Israel, he is from heaven and is of heaven; therefore you cannot make things of the earth to represent him.","dt":"2026-02-06T07:08:15","s":["rqpgwuzwmj"]}],"24":[{"m":"So where he hasn't recorded his name, he will not be there to come and bless.\n\nAnd he shows where his name is recorded.\n\nIn the altars of stone. Thatsoor...\n\nSimplicity is the ultimate sophistication.","dt":"2026-02-06T07:10:00","s":["f4xqxxwf07"]},{"m":"vs 24: “In all places where I record my name, I will come unto thee, and I will bless thee.”\nBy implication, it's not all places that God has recorded his name.","dt":"","s":["fr024jqd57"]}],"0":[{"m":"In this chapter the LORD begins to give the Israelites laws and to establish his covenant with them. I noticed that the dealings of God with Israel as a people are a bit different from those with the patriarchs as individuals.\nHere he gives the people specific laws: laws concerning idolatry, the Sabbath, the use of his name, etc. This was quite different from his dealings with the patriarchs. Jacob even had a wife who stole her father's gods, and his followers at a point had to hide all foreign gods as they approached Jehovah (Gen 35). There was allowance given for these things then. But now that Israel had become a people, the way of dealing with them had to be different, as demonstrated here by the giving of laws.\nThe dealings of God with the patriarchs sound to me like the dealings of God with us under grace.","dt":null,"s":["128a29dde2"]}],"21":[{"m":"Such contrast.","dt":"2026-02-06T07:03:41","s":["0rdekzqzt8"]}]},"21":{"14":[{"m":"“Take him from my altar” — was it in reference to men holding on to the horns of the altar for mercy?\n\nNo such mercy shall he find.","dt":"2024-03-22T07:09:35","s":["6d4401f633"]}],"19":[{"m":"Even then, God wanted him to be compensated for loss of time. That’s interesting.","dt":null,"s":["3ac49d6876"]},{"m":"vs 19: “only he shall pay for the loss of his time and…cause him to be thoroughly healed.”\nThat's interesting. Paying for loss of time. GOD does value people's time. You can't have your time wasted. You've got to get good reward for it.","dt":"","s":["gvk69pwvfb"]}]},"22":{"11":[{"m":"That’s interesting; an oath alone was enough in those days, but in these days when there is no trust, it just may not hold.","dt":null,"s":["d7bf4322e4"]}],"18":[{"m":"No questions, no exceptions, no explanation. The witch must die.","dt":"2026-02-06T07:19:56","s":["iz9f5opxpl"]}]},"23":{"2":[{"m":"Herd mentality is prohibited and not excused.\n\nWe must be independent-minded in obedience to him. Independent of the crowd in our life.","dt":"2026-02-06T07:22:27","s":["2nekvcz7da"]}],"4":[{"m":"It's amazing this is actually Old Testament.\n\nJesus speaks similarly in the New.","dt":"2026-02-06T07:25:08","s":["8ot7sy1non"]}]},"24":{"12":[{"m":"This whole chapter bears more studies.. They were all with the Lord, seeing him, and then he tells Moses to come up to him on the mount.\n\nMeanwhile, it seems the whole mountain ⛰ was on fire 🔥, or the top part where Moses was to come up to.\n\nThis calls for more studies.","dt":"2022-02-08T08:19:07","s":["dce1b0b4e0"]}],"17":[{"m":"Was this not the same fire 🔥 of the burning bush that burnt, yet it consumed it not??\n\nNow it was atop the entire mountain ⛰.","dt":"2022-02-08T09:27:34","s":["sqtbxpefo5","9433a05243"]}]},"25":{"8":[{"m":"God's plan was to move from the mountain, from being on the outskirts, to be amongst them.","dt":"2026-02-07T01:04:48","s":["lamvg37cnh"]}]},"27":{"21":[{"m":"From generation to generation, the light never went out.","dt":"2026-02-07T02:22:11","s":["d60xiet23d"]}],"8":[{"m":"At this point I wonder how God came about such specific measurements.\n\nThe details are so specific, it reeks of someone who has done it before and thus has the blueprint.\n\nAnd indeed He has, because he tells Moses to follow the template he saw on the mountain ⛰.\n\nSo Moses was sent to the mountain, and there he saw the ark of the Lord.\n\nIn modern terminology he might have seen a hologram with such vivid details and so advanced that he could touch and feel and even possibly sacrifices.\n\nI do not think the template he saw was just a blueprint for the earth… because we are later told of the tabernacle in heaven.\n\nIf there is a tabernacle in heaven, then there are sacrifices offered.\n\nThe sort of sacrifice we are not told, but it was of a sort that could accept the blood of Jesus.","dt":"2024-03-25T17:30:18","s":["cimrj7rtwx","371fcdff9e"]}]},"28":{"43":[{"m":"Amen... What was the purpose of all these.. Most of the time it is explained as a cover to ensure their sins are covered and accepted.\n\nSometimes also it was so that Aaron's sons do not die before the Lord; it was a form of cover.\n\nBut the question still holds. What was the purpose? Could God not just do away with all these elements?\n\nWhy go through all these? This brings me to the wisdom of God and again to the processes of God.\n\nHe is the creator of order, system and purpose, and here again we see the order, systems and purposes of God on display.\n\nEverything must follow a logic and wisdom.\n\nThis entire chapter bears more studies.","dt":"2022-02-09T08:07:22","s":["0f7umsv2xv","324c8b7516"]}]},"29":{"9":[{"m":"What a privilege, the priesthood is theirs by an everlasting covenant.\n\nWow.. What a blessing, and we also are priests by an everlasting covenant, the precious blood of Jesus.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:20:28","s":["1f7ebb324a"]}],"26":[{"m":"God eats by fire 🔥, we eat as humans, and here Moses partakes with God in the sacrifice, as well as Aaron and his sons.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:23:50","s":["0ed4dd0c67"]}],"37":[{"m":"WOW","dt":"2022-08-31T07:29:51","s":["7a6b76b1be"]}],"46":[{"m":"So all these laborious processes were to pave the way for God to dwell amongst his own people.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:27:46","s":["34881d5e3d"]}]},"30":{"33":[{"m":"A mystery. So there is a compound whose mixture and composition is public knowledge, and yet it should not be compounded because it attracts spirits, specifically the Lord GOD Almighty.\n\nIt is amazing that it should not be put on any flesh, yet on the flesh of the priests it consecrates them, but on a stranger it banishes them from the land.\n\nGod is indeed a God of structure and order and will not compromise on it.\n\nI am in Dubai at the moment and I see the structure and the uncompromising and elaborate order of the country.\n\nSystems and structures are everything.","dt":"2026-02-11T15:46:15","s":["4hr8woflg4"]}],"38":[{"m":"If you do, your smell becomes like the smell of the house of God; the smell of his divine presence is what you seek to covet after.\nYour crime is coveting not after the property of your neighbour but that of the goods of GOD.","dt":"2026-02-11T15:48:46","s":["xm0nso74tq"]}],"12":[{"m":"What is the point, that numbering the people of God was a trespass?...\n\nBecause it sounds like God is saying that if you allow yourself to be numbered you will be punished, but the money will in a sense atone for it.\n\nThis reminds me of when David chose to number the people and God caused a plague to fall on them.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:32:57","s":["8wqi9wkudi","c0cb17cf30"]}]},"32":{"2":[{"m":"In those times the people were truly rich... The common folks had gold, gold earrings and jewelry.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:38:05","s":["90cx2wqupn","3c50527360"]}],"5":[{"m":"This was not the LORD, so not even Aaron knew how to have access to God and call on him for guidance. Then he would have heard from him and waited for Moses.\n\nMeanwhile the Lord had at least told them they were not to have other gods beside him nor make images to represent him.\n\nIf they were to follow this command, this would mean they would sit down doing nothing but waiting — waiting for Moses and the Lord. And the spirit of man is always in a haste. Waiting is painful and difficult for us.","dt":"2026-02-13T05:15:33","s":["26fe7w95ze"]}],"6":[{"m":"Where did they learn how to do all these things? They even called the calf by the name of the LORD. So they couldn't deny the truth that it was indeed the I AM that brought them out of Egypt.\n\nThis was suddenly their attempt to access the power of the LORD, and they did all they knew, i.e. create other gods from the works of their hands and hope they would then gain their favour to lead them in the way they should go.","dt":"2026-02-13T05:07:35","s":["3stlp24or9"]}],"8":[{"m":"Hm.. I can feel the jealousy of God in how he vividly describes worship due to him being given to demons and man-made objects.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:39:38","s":["9iklaz3nuh","3122118743"]}],"10":[{"m":"Hmm, God was willing to start afresh with Moses; that would have meant only the tribe of Levi would become a nation, but God wasn't bothered.\n\nFor his covenant was with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob. He did not covenant with any of the sons of Jacob; though he blessed Joseph mightily, he did not reveal himself to him by way of covenant.\n\nHe was willing to work with the man Moses, who knew him and obeyed him, to make of him a great nation.\n\nGod makes great nations out of the willing and obedient.","dt":"2026-02-13T05:20:48","s":["uguy1ubpmb"]}],"17":[{"m":"Hm.. JOSHUA also was in the mount all this while.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:41:54","s":["69e6fb18ad"]}],"19":[{"m":"They had broken the commandments of God, and Moses literally breaks the commandments by breaking the tablets.","dt":"2024-03-27T10:39:18","s":["7ea07005c4"]}],"21":[{"m":"He was literally saying, how did these people successfully bewitch 🧙‍♀️ thee?","dt":"2022-02-10T17:52:55","s":["08a58bf11b"]}],"23":[{"m":"So man can make gods by himself. Set up a spirit portal of a sort, and the spirits then come and inhabit them.","dt":"2022-02-10T17:53:49","s":["ad742e93f1"]}],"34":[{"m":"My angel 😇. This was the second time, I think, that God had mentioned this angel 😇.\n\nAnd he further emphasized that when he, God, comes... indicating he was separate from this, his angel 😇.\n\nHowever, I think in the Psalms we are given a clearer description helping us understand the angel was the Holy Ghost 👻.","dt":"2022-02-10T17:57:26","s":["mjyencnmv2","0b5c20219e"]}],"35":[{"m":"So eventually he punished them, though not to completely destroy the entire nation.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:44:05","s":["pzne9k4e2w","113c7a883d"]}],"7":[{"m":"I am currently listening to The Bait of Satan and I am really learning, or being reminded of, some good christian stuff — or should I call them ethics. Well here goes some of the lessons that I have or am learning.\n1. The believer who cannot forgive is a person who has forgotten what he's actually been forgiven of\n\nEx 32:7\nThen the Lord said to Moses, “Go down, because your people, whom you brought up out of Egypt, have become corrupt.”\nGod is not afraid to share his victories with his people. Here he ascribes the coming out of Egypt by Israel to Moses.","dt":"","s":["ngf5jxg4aw"]}],"14":[{"m":"It was not with mere emotions but with wisdom and facts that Moses was able to sway the anger of the Lord.","dt":"2024-03-26T08:41:26","s":["4e30fcccad"]}]},"33":{"5":[{"m":"And that moment they did not know. They were kept on edge. It's like being on death row without knowing the day of your death ☠.\n\nThat itself was torturous.","dt":"2024-03-27T11:12:07","s":["8goycs2i32","8df0fb937e"]}],"6":[{"m":"So they committed these atrocities on none other than Mount 🗻 Horeb, the mount of the Lord, and from where the Lord had spoken not too long ago in an audible voice from Sinai.\n\nHuman beings, we are so someway.\n\nSuch — not just disobedience but blatant disrespect of God and his word.","dt":"2026-02-14T00:58:44","s":["n35a4nilh3"]},{"m":"This was a serious moment.. This was not a time to look pretty, and with the very ornaments of their gross disrespect...\n\nA painful reminder of the sin they had committed before the Lord.","dt":"2026-02-14T01:01:14","s":["zyrosbnknr"]}],"11":[{"m":"No wonder he (Joshua) later inherited Moses.","dt":"2022-02-16T12:42:03","s":["nlbld1pdia","dec31f2680"]},{"m":"God spoke to Moses face to face. Was it that he appeared as a man and spoke to him, or he appeared in the cloud so that his figure is masked in a sense?\n\nIf so, that will not be face to face, will it?\n\nWhatever the case may be, this form in which God appeared to Moses was different from his appearance in glory. I am sure Moses had seen that glorious form faintly or very shortly in time past and wanted a fuller, much more personal encounter with him.\n\nHow did Moses know there was a glorious form different from what the Lord was currently showing him? Or maybe it came up in conversation with God.","dt":"2026-02-14T10:19:30","s":["b8w8xckklf"]}],"12":[{"m":"Of course the Lord had told him who was going with him — an angel — but Moses wanted the Lord himself to go with them.","dt":"2026-02-14T09:29:45","s":["9ew3llsaml"]}],"23":[{"m":"No wonder ever so often visions of God or the Lord are those of bright light. He is shrouded in light.","dt":"2024-03-27T11:18:51","s":["i9eg0dmpls","98c654156e"]}],"20":[{"m":"While Israel's relationship with the Lord had turned sour, Moses's was getting better and deeper.\n\nAwesome indeed.","dt":"2024-03-27T11:19:46","s":["eedtds2667","e398e66eeb"]}],"3":[{"m":"Was the angel therefore more forgiving or considerate than the Lord? Or, probably and more likely, the holiness of the Lord could not coexist with the rebellion of the people.\n\nLetting an angel guide them was an act of mercy, though it meant they lost the privilege of the LORD himself being in the midst of them.\n\nNo wonder they wept when they heard the Lord's decisions.","dt":"2024-03-27T11:10:42","s":["297c88543b"]}]},"34":{"2":[{"m":"This Mount Sinai, how does it relate to Mount Horeb?","dt":"2026-02-14T10:34:49","s":["9n2q618gqd"]}],"5":[{"m":"Hold it, the Lord descending in the cloud is not so strange; the cloud was ever with the camp of Israel, and indeed anytime Moses came to the tabernacle the LORD's pillar of cloud descended and the Lord spoke with Moses.\n\nSo the Lord appearing this way here was normal, but that was not the deal. Let's read further.","dt":"2026-02-14T10:36:36","s":["l2nmpudogc"]}],"28":[{"m":"My GOD, forty days and nights.. What conversations were they having?\n\nBear 🐻 in mind, Moses and God were this close 🔐 🤞🤏👌. They talked face to face, so they really talked.\n\nFor forty days.\n\nIt is safe to assume that they talked for hours. So in forty days, only God knows what was said.\n\nHowever, based on conjecture, I doubt 🤷‍♂️ they spoke for 40 days straight.\n\nBecause in earlier chapters we see Moses had to wait on the mount for some 7 days before God finally showed up.\n\nSo likely in the forty days God did come and go.\n\nMY two ✌️ cents.","dt":"2022-02-16T13:28:09","s":["0i3pe9m6il","bfb5d8bb96"]}],"34":[{"m":"Come to think of it, MOSES spoke to the Lord pretty frequently in the tabernacle, but the moment Moses asked to see the Lord's glory, the encounter had to move from the tabernacle to the mountains.\n\nThis shows the form Moses sees in the tabernacle is different from what he saw or sees in the mountain that quakes and thunders with smoke and fire.","dt":"2026-02-14T12:52:09","s":["l63146shor"]}],"8":[{"m":"This man Moses was a smart guy. He maximized the opportunity as God honored him by passing before him in all HIS GLORY. He quickly bowed down in worship and soon after made his request.","dt":null,"s":["e654a12fd9"]}],"13":[{"m":"These folks would definitely break this command, because they themselves, on their own, were idolatrous. How much more when they come into an environment where such lust is the norm?","dt":"2024-03-27T11:24:31","s":["25b3dd4afc"]}],"18":[{"m":"The Lord reiterates the very things he had told them from the very beginning, after he renewed his covenant with them. It was like a fresh start for all.","dt":"2026-02-14T10:40:13","s":["0l6nwngn03"]}]},"35":{"30":[{"m":"He hath called by name... Interesting.","dt":"2024-03-27T11:30:59","s":["3sz74takwp","f23ce7b17c"]}],"21":[{"m":"After seeing a man whose face lit the earth 🌎, no doubt many hearts will be willing to contribute to the service of the Lord.","dt":"2022-02-16T13:54:04","s":["9c0d69dca0"]}]},"36":{"1":[{"m":"Of all the power acts, signs and wonders that the Lord wrought in Israel — could he not just have caused the tabernacle to descend from the heavens?\n\nI mean, he rained down manna for 40 years, yet he requires them to build a tabernacle in the earth, a replica of the heavenly one, and went through the elaborate how-to process.\n\nThis further proves that God had the template and could have just done it. Yet God chooses to work with man. He has given us abilities, and he loves to partner with us so we do what only we as humans can do and he does only what he as God can do — everyone playing their respective roles beautifully.\n\nHowever, I have a question — in GOD partnering man, is there a way of knowing what God will do and what he expects man to do? I believe this distinction is important so we do not sit aloof expecting God to do something when he also is expecting us to do the same, or we overstep our boundaries into the place of God. What do you expect?","dt":"2026-02-14T13:41:45","s":["rue2cvajgl"]}],"2":[{"m":"So all these people did not make it to the promised land.\n\nWow.. This walk with God bears more study.","dt":"2022-02-16T20:38:20","s":["a536a19a2e"]}]},"39":{"13":[{"m":"We are not told why these specific stones were selected, but knowing who God is, there is a definite reason.\n\nGod throughout scripture is very deliberate in his dealings.\n\nHe even has specific measurements for everything.\n\nHe did not just pick those stones at random by name. He is God.","dt":"2024-03-30T15:49:26","s":["8228fa01eb","fnm6q6ylfh"]}],"31":[{"m":"This was as the Lord had commanded. It followed a pattern — likely that of heaven, because we know there are altars et al. there.","dt":"2022-02-17T07:51:02","s":["e3b3092867"]}]},"40":{"38":[{"m":"Fire 🔥 and 🌥 cloud by day and night, and yet these people did not make the promised land.\n\nThe same is happening to us now. So much power and anointing in the body of Christ, and yet so much sin, unbelief and no thirst 💦 for God.\n\nWe are following the manner of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nLord, have mercy.","dt":"2022-02-17T07:54:59","s":["f3276a54ad"]}]}},"Isaiah":{"1":{"5":[{"m":"A sad state of national Israel. The more they were smitten, the normal and natural expectation is that they will come to repentance.\n\nBut rather they became worse and worse.\n\nGod himself realised these people were sick in the head.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:55:40","s":["puw51ornel"]}],"11":[{"m":"In this wise he told Amos the prophet, that in the many years that Israel walked in the desert, even before the laws and sacrifices were commanded,\n\nthere were no sacrifices; rather, he demanded that they walk in uprightness and holiness towards him.\n\nSacrifices and offerings are nothing to him if we abandon his laws.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:59:19","s":["x5j6456zae"]}],"23":[{"m":"Judges are princes, or rather, in the days of Israel the princes and rulers judged the people.\n\nToday we have judges as a profession, and in a sense they have powers of kings and princes, to put to death and save from death.","dt":"2024-09-12T07:02:01","s":["jx2dj14vo6"]}],"31":[{"m":"This, I believe, was in reference to their many carved idols and groves of idolatrous worship.","dt":"2024-09-12T07:06:26","s":["1j55yss0xq"]}]},"2":{"8":[{"m":"Idols made by their own hands 👐.\n\nAnd this is what prevails in this generation — men have exalted self and made gods of themselves.\n\nIncluding lifting up other men in man worship.\n\nSadly, this also is in the church ⛪","dt":"2024-09-13T18:19:39","s":["ubobuo2reb"]}],"17":[{"m":"Men and the idols they worship alike will bow before the Most High.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:21:13","s":["h5llrclbyc"]}],"22":[{"m":"Interesting. Spirits — do they breathe? If so, where is their breath?","dt":"2024-09-13T18:22:25","s":["15k5gosyvg"]}]},"3":{"11":[{"m":"The seasons and times of life — you reap what you sow.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:24:33","s":["jcbypcz4zq"]}]},"4":{"6":[{"m":"Are we back in the wilderness experience where the Shekinah was seen?\n\nWill those days come again in the end?","dt":"2024-09-13T18:30:48","s":["4wvl3i7pcn"]}]},"5":{"1":[{"m":"Touching his vineyard, i.e. concerning his vineyard.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:32:18","s":["qn2t10e345"]}],"4":[{"m":"God is so logical, so reasonable... No wonder in some place he said, \"Come, let us reason together.\"\n\nMost times we approach God in a strange way, almost weird.\n\nIf the way we pray was the way we talk to people, that would have been pretty weird. Let's just be real with God.\n\nIsaiah 1:18 KJV\nCome now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.","dt":"2022-07-14T13:32:14","s":["9jibs5ouib"]}],"5":[{"m":"This was an allegory to Jerusalem. Is it not interesting that though Jerusalem had physical walls, God speaks of him removing the hedge/wall?\n\nAnd after having done that, having spoken it forth, we see later the walls of Jerusalem being broken.\n\nIn other words, the protection of Jerusalem was God, not their physical representations.","dt":"2022-07-14T13:45:45","s":["zuuii2ivsj"]}],"7":[{"m":"Judgment and righteousness, the fruits that the Lord sought.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:35:43","s":["comfdrc4dk"]}],"20":[{"m":"That sadly is the state of the world today.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:38:12","s":["b76khr10yr"]}],"22":[{"m":"Interesting comparisons here.","dt":"2022-07-12T06:41:32","s":["jfgjo6kv88"]}]},"6":{"11":[{"m":"After their destruction shall their wisdom and their hearts 💕 be given to understand. Till then their heart shall lack understanding.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:07:46","s":["elkoml7l1i"]}],"10":[{"m":"Such bad counsel, but because it is the word of the Lord, it cannot but happen.\n\nThis was meant to be a mockery and warning ⚠ them off their ways...\n\nBut they cared less.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:42:17","s":["trtmacr851"]}]},"7":{"7":[{"m":"When did they say this, and how was it heard? I suspect God's messenger, or in this case a clandestine or spy angel 😇, was behind this.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:11:31","s":["jtc56mow6y"]}],"8":[{"m":"Ephraim of Joseph, the one blessed with the right of the firstborn.","dt":"2024-09-13T18:45:42","s":["9i73247m4c"]}],"14":[{"m":"I don't understand oo...\nWhy is God using a future 🔮 event several centuries to come as a basis for his word being fulfilled?\n\nAhaz would not even be alive to test the potency of the sign, but we will, or we are. 😇","dt":"2022-07-14T14:28:30","s":["8e637bf562","79r1wyjinv"]},{"m":"This sign has double fulfillment, one in Isaiah's time and one in Christ. Earlier I had said, \"Why is God giving a future event as a sign to Ahaz?\" But I checked on this blog https://www.jeanejones.net/2020/12/the-virgin-shall-conceive-why-isaiah-714-confuses-people/\n\nand it explains how that prophecy got fulfilled in Isaiah's time as well.\n\nA virgin did give birth, but it explains that unlike Mary, who was a virgin at conception, this refers to a virgin who got married and gave birth. That was the fulfillment in Ahaz's day, not that a virgin like Mary will be overshadowed by the Spirit of God and give birth.\n\nRead the blog; it explains it beautifully. But I do not endorse it until I have done my own studies.","dt":"2026-07-18T07:02:53","s":["aac58t3gka"]}]},"8":{"8":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 deep stuff... O Emmanuel, what is this doing here?\n\nIn the pages and writings of scripture are hidden meanings.\n\nMysteries that can only be gleaned and squeezed out by meditation 🧘‍♂️ and the Spirit revealing them to you.\n\nMysteries which a man can know just by the Spirit of God.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:35:05","s":["8c58i86glw"]}],"10":[{"m":"Another occurrence of Immanuel: God indeed is with us. Though written as \"God with us\", it is Immanuel.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:36:26","s":["rfm7zme9ey"]}],"15":[{"m":"So the majority can be wrong and can suffer, whiles the minority escape and are blessed.\n\nOh my Father, is this how your coming will be?\nFor Jesus said it, that broad is the way to hell and many go there, but narrow is the way to damnation and few find it. 😢","dt":"2022-07-14T14:38:37","s":["wkykmmi6pf"]}],"16":[{"m":"Wow... Because when the day of judgement shall come, that shall be their vindication.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:47:27","s":["7aobbvp6fy"]}],"17":[{"m":"In the midst of a rebellious people, he was willing to wait on the Lord — how odd he might have looked and felt.","dt":"2024-09-13T19:01:49","s":["1gokev3us8"]}],"18":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-07-14T14:47:47","s":["c555aded83"]}],"20":[{"m":"The law and the prophets are contrasted with wizards that peep and do their enchantment — to us, our power, \"our enchantment\", is the law and prophetic word of our God, and by that we conquer and have the victory.\n\nAs the heathen mutter and peep, we go over to the law and word of our God. For that is our enchantment.","dt":"2026-07-18T07:09:53","s":["iz3pgq675m"]}]},"9":{"5":[{"m":"Here we have another example of mixing present-day realities with a distant occurrence of the Messiah.\n\nOh, this timeless God.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:24:58","s":["7kxkzbqfvz"]}],"12":[{"m":"I just read this whole chapter up to this point in the NLT — and the NLT did a great job of narrating this passage in such a way that it is easy to understand and decipher.\n\nInserted clauses to ensure smooth transition and flow of thought.\n\nThere are even subheadings that ensure you move from context to the next context without getting lost, that there is now a change of topic.\n\nBut the ancient text and writing itself, not only did it lack such headings, but I am told there were no commas or such annotation. The text just continued.\n\nNo wonder it was so difficult to understand such ancient writings, and indeed they were classified as sacred, and it took scribes and scholars to understand and even transcribe the text.\n\nIt was indeed sacred and mysterious in many respects. It (the text) can move from the past right past the present into the future 4000 years without transitioning.\n\nYou just move from a war today to a war millennia later, and you can't tell you have moved until you realise what is being said does not apply to the present time.\n\nI suspect it is also because of the way these sacred writings were revealed.\n\nIt seemed they were written as the prophets saw the vision. So just like in a dream, where you can be in one location and the next moment you are in the next, all merged as one dream, the prophets wrote as they saw and kept it that way without interpreting it.\n\nIndeed, we are told the prophets of old themselves looked into these things and sought to understand it, but they knew it was not for their time. But even they did not fully comprehend it.\n\n1 Peter 1:12 KJV\nUnto whom it was revealed, that not unto themselves, but unto us they did minister the things, which are now reported unto you by them that have preached the gospel unto you with the Holy Ghost sent down from heaven; which things the angels desire to look into.\n\nEven angels desired to look into such things.","dt":"2026-07-20T07:49:54","s":["6b11r07nfr"]}]},"10":{"5":[{"m":"So Assyria at this time was the tool of the Lord to execute his judgment.\n\nSometimes it's like God is not in charge of earth 🌎 because he is so long-suffering.\n\nWe soon form our own doctrines that man is the one in charge of the earth and man must fix it.\n\nWhat we don't know is that God is behind the scenes to fix this earth, and very actively about it.\n\nWe may not see him in action in any significant way for centuries, but he is the Lord and has his timelines and appointment times to execute justice.","dt":"2024-09-14T07:42:23","s":["b1ep8ngn1a"]}],"12":[{"m":"Assyria was just a tool of judgement, and he did not even know it.\n\nWhen they had finished using him, they dumped him, i.e. God did.\n\nWhen in use, the king of Assyria thought himself somebody and had a stout look and proud heart, till he himself was also judged by the Lord.","dt":"2024-09-14T07:45:13","s":["na257uow9l"]}]},"11":{"9":[{"m":"So in the knowledge of God is goodness and purity etc.\n\nThe very thing God is often accused of not doing enough of.\n\nWhy doesn't God end all evil if he really is that good?\n\nEven us men, in our limited knowledge, we know the world could be better.\n\nAnd now here God says the whole earth 🌎 will be filled with his knowledge and understanding.\n\nIn it the lion and bear hung out. We indeed are in a fallen world 🗺.\n\nBut we shall see the glory of the Lord at the end.","dt":"2024-09-14T08:58:22","s":["6u75n81i8k"]}],"13":[{"m":"The Lord is talking here as if the event of the scattering of Israel has completely taken place and now he is in the restoring phase.\n\nOh, our eternal, all-knowing and omnipotent one.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:44:52","s":["b27ensoqq3"]}]},"14":{"12":[{"m":"The Babylonian king was cast down from the earth to hell beneath, and Lucifer from heaven to the ground.","dt":"2026-07-25T18:29:13","s":["eb3blyhwea"]}],"13":[{"m":"This passage is often said to follow the prophetic law of double interpretation, i.e. some portions refer to the human king of Babylon and some to Satan or Lucifer himself.\n\nI believe all that, but just for the purposes of argument, can it be said that it all referred to the natural king of Babylon, but all the extraordinary happenings, like being called Lucifer and being cast out of the heavens, were a hyperbole of a sort?\nThis assertion is difficult to defend, though, in that specific names were mentioned.\n\nMeaning he existed, i.e. Lucifer was mentioned. Who was he? If even the king of Babylon was being called Lucifer, then we can look at the descriptions given of the king of Babylon to help us decipher who Lucifer was and what happened to him, because whatever it was that happened to him was descriptive and fitting enough to have been used to describe the king of Babylon as being the same.","dt":"2026-07-25T18:37:23","s":["0thypncoqu"]}],"29":[{"m":"From bad to worse, I guess.","dt":"2022-07-16T10:56:14","s":["2mki5j8325"]}]},"17":{"6":[{"m":"Mercy, Lord.\n\nSuch strong imagery is used because word pictures communicate stronger to the human soul.\n\nIndeed, word pictures are used throughout these passages in Isaiah.\n\nGod, the creator of man, knows how best to get to him.\n\nJesus also did the same in his parables and stories. No wonder he is the greatest teacher ever.","dt":"2022-07-16T11:03:30","s":["5nvroawhhk"]}],"14":[{"m":"Selah","dt":"2022-07-16T11:04:34","s":["s9fr6tplqa"]}]},"19":{"25":[{"m":"Which day is this strange day, where sworn enemies become confederates, more or less?\n\nThis is the doing of the Lord, and it is marvelous in our sight.","dt":"2022-07-17T06:44:35","s":["rvj131biw9"]}]},"20":{"3":[{"m":"I wonder, was Isaiah's message to the whole of Israel — did the whole nation hear him?\n\nOr he appealed to some, and other prophets to others.\n\nBecause Isaiah had contemporaries who also prophesied.\n\nI believe each was sent to specific towns and on specific tasks to proclaim the word of the Lord.","dt":"2024-09-19T06:33:07","s":["uob49qd88p"]}]},"21":{"9":[{"m":"Babylon also is fallen like the rest of the nations, in its due time.","dt":"2024-09-19T06:35:29","s":["vcyq1ma72p"]}]},"26":{"2":[{"m":"The requirements to enter this gate are righteousness and truth.\n\nI won't be surprised that this gate itself may have a spiritual connotation — maybe righteousness is the name of the gate thereof.","dt":"2024-09-19T07:51:05","s":["4jnrffwfqp"]}],"3":[{"m":"The secret for perfect 👌 peace revealed right there.","dt":"2022-07-18T08:17:50","s":["k0cupql3pt"]}],"10":[{"m":"Truth revealed right there: the wicked thinks himself wise and will likely reward favour with wickedness.\n\nHe seeks advantage over others and misses out on his own salvation.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:30:18","s":["hm9zdxxgv7"]}],"13":[{"m":"Other lords besides thee have had the dominion over us to our destruction, but under your lordship and governance we have had everlasting peace ✌️.\n\nBecause of that we have fond memories of thee, and thus ever make mention of your name, your sweet name, oh Holy Spirit.","dt":"2022-07-18T08:20:06","s":["cyjhivqeow"]}],"1":[{"m":"Salvation is our wall, our strong 💪 defense — not physical protection, but the Lord's protection is our trust.","dt":"2024-09-19T07:49:28","s":["3m6xes33u0"]}],"18":[{"m":"May this never be anyone's lot, I pray, for you to travail in labour and miscarry.\n\nLord, have mercy.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:33:38","s":["3ity01ljsp"]}]},"27":{"6":[{"m":"Because of the covenant he has with this people, he did not slay them like he did unto other nations who are not his people.\n\nIt's not fair, but that is the same with us: when you have a relationship with someone, be it your child, friend... you are not able to deal with them when they do some wrong things as you should.\n\nIt's just that way.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:37:51","s":["2rpixvmmsa"]}]},"28":{"1":[{"m":"Such imagery, such elaborate word pictures to drive home the message and propel a compelling persuasion to this indolent people of Ephraim, yet they would not hear.\n\nBut needless to say, God indeed is an orator and great communicator and spokesperson via his prophets.","dt":"2026-08-01T08:04:36","s":["mu5jnagl8j"]}],"6":[{"m":"The rulers were to be filled with the spirit of judgement, but rather they be full of wine and are intoxicated therewith, yet we be admonished by the Apostle Paul to not be drunk with wine, wherein is excess, but to be filled, as though drunk, but with the Holy Spirit.\n\nYet these rulers would not hear.","dt":"2026-08-01T08:23:00","s":["g2rhj2lwtx"]}],"13":[{"m":"The power of words and the word of God.","dt":"2022-07-22T07:17:25","s":["c7e5cc0ntf"]}],"15":[{"m":"I believe they had cut strange covenants with idols and devils. 👿\n\nBut the Lord annulled it.","dt":"2022-07-22T07:15:37","s":["ec3wtpktuz"]}]},"29":{"13":[{"m":"\"These people come near to me with their mouth\nbut their hearts are far from me.\nTheir worship of me\nis made up only of rules taught by men.\"","dt":null,"s":["84433a1160"]},{"m":"For their recompense, he plays their game and at the end makes their wisdom and prudence foolish, as seen in the next verse.","dt":"2026-08-01T08:31:34","s":["lvlfs6bl47","narezoa2x3"]}]},"30":{"10":[{"m":"Really?? 😳... But this is so real in our times.\n\nThere is indeed nothing new under the sun ☀","dt":"2022-07-22T07:24:53","s":["7k3e7gd9w6"]}],"18":[{"m":"Wait and be blessed.\n\nWhat a promise. You know, many times we love activity, but God is assuring us that making time to wait on him and hear him will indeed bring his blessings.","dt":"2022-07-22T07:29:26","s":["6uyr3nl704"]}],"21":[{"m":"Amen. Waiting on the Lord leads to instruction, guidance & directions.","dt":"2022-07-22T07:30:44","s":["u6poa7efpc"]}]},"32":{"15":[{"m":"All we need is the Spirit. Are you in an impossible place? Do you find yourself entangled and in a web 🕸 of life's many troubles?\n\nTrust in God, give yourself to prayer and seeking after his Spirit's guidance, and he that called the things that be not as though they were will bring life and light to you.\n\nRomans 4:17 KJV\n(As it is written, I have made thee a father of many nations,) before him whom he believed, even God, who quickeneth the dead, and calleth those things which be not as though they were.\n\nI leave you with this final scripture:\n\n2 Corinthians 4:6 KJV\nFor God, who commanded the light to shine out of darkness, hath shined in our hearts, to give the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ.","dt":"2022-07-23T08:13:46","s":["pj62f865kz"]},{"m":"The Spirit of the Lord brings us peace, peace of mind and rest to our minds and our bodies.\n\nThere is a peace that his presence brings.\n\nHe gives us the ability to obey the word of God. To walk according to the precepts of God written 📝 on our hearts 💕 and conscience 🧠.\n\nSometimes you know the right thing to do but just can't do it. Indeed, many times that is the case.\n\nBut the Spirit enables us to do his will. Especially the things that are our weaknesses.\n\nEspecially in our generation, where we have been lured into addictions.\n\nAddictions of sex, drunkenness, lewdness, materialism etc.\n\nHis Spirit helps us break all those yokes and bondages.\n\nIsaiah 10:27 KJV\nAnd it shall come to pass in that day, that his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.\n\nAnd he blesses us, guides us into hidden riches.\n\nAnd shows us our role in the kingdom 👑 and enables us to do it.\n\nHe shows us judgements and wisdom. Just like the spirit upon Moses was given to the 70 elders to enable them to judge Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nNumbers 11:25 KJV\nAnd the LORD came down in a cloud, and spake unto him, and took of the spirit that was upon him, and gave it unto the seventy elders: and it came to pass, that, when the spirit rested upon them, they prophesied, and did not cease.\n\nHis Spirit is all we need. When he, the Spirit of truth, comes, he changes everything and aligns us to his will, his word and his ways.","dt":"2024-05-03T06:54:12","s":["ylxu5upsk4"]}],"20":[{"m":"Good business advice, a blessing for the businessman: the producer who sows beside all waters, which yields fields for the ox 🐂 and donkey.","dt":"2022-07-23T16:19:47","s":["2g0jxqd9a6"]}]},"33":{"17":[{"m":"The reward of the righteous: spared from the coming destruction, accepted into Sion, the beloved city.","dt":"2022-07-23T16:25:35","s":["lygjj5e0oe"]}],"21":[{"m":"A place of largeness, rest and peace.","dt":"2022-07-23T16:28:02","s":["y3kv8m4jji"]}]},"34":{"2":[{"m":"This was a world 🗺 wide event, or at least a great chunk of their world then... Just worth noting.","dt":"2022-07-23T16:34:45","s":["vjxuuti9w6"]}],"15":[{"m":"Such detail of future 🔮 events. GOD INDEED is very detailed in what he intends to do.\n\nHe has a very clear picture of what he wants.","dt":"2022-07-23T16:34:07","s":["6b0ym9jrop"]}],"16":[{"m":"This follows the same creative process of Genesis... The word was spoken and his Spirit gathered the people.\n\nThis created law at work.","dt":"2022-07-23T16:33:17","s":["bs47txj4io"]}]},"35":{"5":[{"m":"The end of this world 🗺 shall be beautiful and glorious.","dt":"2022-07-24T06:09:27","s":["4rfgixi35j"]}],"8":[{"m":"The end of all things shall be glorious.","dt":"2022-07-24T06:08:19","s":["2a2zhenobc"]}]},"36":{"10":[{"m":"God's dealings and doings might have definitely been broadcast all over the place.\n\nNo wonder Rabshakeh lied that he was sent by him and tried usurping the fear that comes with the mere mention of the Lord.\n\nHezekiah, of course, knew he was lying 🤥","dt":"2022-07-24T06:12:44","s":["w0xtxwlvmh"]}],"11":[{"m":"I am sure this request was made in the Syrian language to mask the fears of Hezekiah's leaders.","dt":"2026-08-02T07:04:40","s":["ew10eos1ay"]}],"12":[{"m":"Were they under siege... Was there the risk of famine in the land?\n\nYes, there was the risk of famine once a full siege was mounted.\n\nBut it did not appear there was one yet, but that was a very real threat.","dt":"2026-08-02T07:06:19","s":["908n6x1qsh"]}],"16":[{"m":"Make peace with me, why by a present... Another version says... Show me that you want peace.\nThat would involve an appeasement of some sort.\n\nSo it was not that they were going to present some present, but a sign and show of want of peace; a present would still have been apt, though.","dt":"2026-08-02T07:12:21","s":["xzrpy8mhpl"]}],"17":[{"m":"This was not guaranteed; it might well have been sweet and empty words.","dt":"2024-09-25T09:34:31","s":["d1hu1y4kij"]}]},"40":{"2":[{"m":"The Alpha and Omega, these sayings came even whiles 🇮🇱 Israel was in a backslidden state.\n\nBut he knew this time would come, and indeed it did.","dt":"2022-07-26T06:07:38","s":["cjb38kvo45"]}],"5":[{"m":"God, who is spirit, will reveal his glory, and natural carnal eyes shall see it together.","dt":"2026-08-03T15:32:29","s":["krfpkt6uhu"]}]},"41":{"4":[{"m":"What does he mean by I THE LORD, THE FIRST, AND WITH THE LAST? In Revelations, he is the first and the last, but here he says he is the first and with the last.\n\nOr is he saying he dwells with those who are lowly and not regarded?\n\nBut the context does not suggest that. Contextually, he is saying from generations he is from the beginning and will be with the last of generations. Other verses bring the meaning out clearer.","dt":"2026-08-03T15:41:32","s":["tiar9xugxu"]}],"11":[{"m":"This verse has been my personal rhema for years now.\n\nIt's been a strong 💪 pillar and support even in difficult times.\n\nThe part that I love the most is where he says 'I will help you'.\n\nYou know, generally we think of help as someone coming to support you whiles you bear the greater burden.\n\nBut that is not always so. In fact, it depends on who is offering the help.\n\nSay you are carrying a load and a little child or youth offers to help.\n\nYou know you will bear the greater part of the load.\n\nNow imagine a 7-foot, 120 kg giant offers help.\n\nYou know you carry little, if any, part of the load. Indeed, if you offer to help, the weight 🏋️ might be lopsided, so it's better you let him carry all.\n\nThat is our God for us. He is our help, and he will help us big time.","dt":"2022-07-26T06:30:52","s":["09f80uvelm"]}],"14":[{"m":"Oh, what a privilege when God helps you.","dt":"2022-07-26T06:31:58","s":["lef9hmqe8j"]}],"21":[{"m":"A challenge to the gods and idols, so called, to prove their worth.","dt":"2022-07-26T06:35:47","s":["z9u6r5lrmi"]}],"26":[{"m":"As the Lord talks of these things, I am reminded and aware that there are prophets and priests of other religions, particularly our fathers, who prophesied and it came to pass.\n\nBut then again, the Lord allows these because all things are not yet perfected under his reign, but will be at the end.\n\nAlso, in our traditions, most of these things take place where there is no strong Christian foundation and Christ is not lifted up on high.\n\nHowever, when Christ is lifted in any place, all falsehood disappears and Christ's will and supremacy is established.","dt":"2026-08-03T15:49:35","s":["naebav24wf"]}]},"43":{"2":[{"m":"So we will go through the fire 🔥 and water 💦; we are not exempted from them, but are exempt from its burning 🔥 and destruction by the grace of God.\n\nGod is always faithful.","dt":"2022-07-26T06:44:08","s":["rink9s9uei"]}],"10":[{"m":"He has said it: there is no God besides him. There is no Power, and he has no equals.","dt":"2022-07-26T06:55:27","s":["34fx6mcz7s"]}]},"44":{"20":[{"m":"It takes one who is very self-aware and honest to accept that he has been deluded the whole time.\n\nIt takes humility to say that I have believed in a lie the whole time, and to come to oneself.\n\nIt reminds me of the prodigal son, who came to himself and realized how foolish he had been, and turned back home.","dt":"2022-07-27T07:21:16","s":["arhl6qtyms"]}],"25":[{"m":"Yes Lord, continue to frustrate their omens and lies.\n\nThis is how he brings distinction between his prophets and those who are not his.\n\nIn the New Testament, the prophets are to prophesy whiles another judges.\n\nOf course 🏇, if someone gives a wrong prophecy or speaks out of sync with the scriptures,\n\nit does not make him a false prophet; he might have just missed it, and hence the need to judge.","dt":"2022-07-27T07:26:30","s":["c6howbsmkj"]},{"m":"In the earlier verses, God calls them out on their idols.\n\nHe makes them see the deceptiveness of bowing down to a tree as your God, only to later burn part of that same tree as firewood.\n\nWhen God makes these kinds of statements, it makes me wonder, but these things produce some results, as the spirits around take over such.\n\nBut God is the only God; there is none besides him.\n\nHe has no equals, so he wonders at men when they bow to wood.\n\nEven if and when spirits back these totems, they are not Gods, and their worshippers are still deceived.\n\nThere is no God except JEHOVAH, and beside him there is none.\n\nAll these idols are not gods, and even if they claim and give some powers, they are not God.","dt":"2024-09-27T06:47:40","s":["nqdgoufuvj"]}],"28":[{"m":"Cyrus was prophesied of even before Judah went into captivity.","dt":"2024-09-27T06:51:15","s":["s15dygfqft"]}]},"45":{"7":[{"m":"Obviously, for God to have spoken about all this concerning Cyrus almost a century down the line, he indeed does all things.\n\nThis is not just some vague prophecy, but he actually calls him by name.","dt":"2026-08-04T16:04:30","s":["s4vght947o"]}],"9":[{"m":"Interesting... Yes, let the potsherd strive with the potsherds of the earth 🌎.\n\nIt is such arrogance and ignorance 🤷‍♂️ that makes men challenge God.","dt":"2022-07-27T07:38:41","s":["ej9z52ezxm"]}],"23":[{"m":"And so shall it be that all eyes shall behold him, and their tongues cling to the roof of their mouth as our God and Saviour comes down in the clouds.\n\nAnd every knee shall bow 🙇, even they that pierced him.","dt":"2022-07-27T07:42:34","s":["naznq57i0t"]}],"5":[{"m":"It will have been very strange for Cyrus to grow up and see writings about him from some 70 years back. I believe God did this because he wanted to leave no shadow of doubt that he raised Cyrus up.","dt":"2026-08-04T16:03:10","s":["9vy14kdj3k"]}],"17":[{"m":"World without end","dt":"2024-09-27T08:43:59","s":["vtnwe0fvpj"]}],"22":[{"m":"Fact","dt":"2022-07-27T07:40:24","s":["8c255w5rq9"]}]},"46":{"10":[{"m":"This no other god can do... And them that attempt to do, he frustrates 😤 their signs and omens till they come to nought.","dt":"2022-07-27T07:45:28","s":["786riddqyw"]}]},"47":{"13":[{"m":"This confirms again the earlier word of the Lord: he confuses the sorcerers and them that seek omens.","dt":"2022-07-27T17:47:07","s":["eu6htfanc6"]}]},"48":{"5":[{"m":"God created things anew, such that the idol worshippers could not take credit and say it ahead of time.\n\nI suspect the constellations and other omens carry information which the spirits can tap into and subsequently communicate with man.\n\nBut this time God created the events anew; there was no way anyone could have known who was not a prophet of God.\n\nIf God does all this for his name's sake, so no one takes his glory... he will be even more willing to keep and remain faithful to his children 🧒.\n\nWho have rescinded the things of the world to serve him.","dt":"2022-07-27T17:53:34","s":["nlf5fss87y"]}],"8":[{"m":"Why does God speak in very poetic language, parables almost?\n\nFor instance, \"thou was a transgressor from the womb\" references Jacob.","dt":"2022-07-27T17:50:46","s":["632xw6352x"]}],"21":[{"m":"This verse has erupted solemn thoughts 💭.\n\nIsaiah 48:21 NLT\nThey were not thirsty when he led them through the desert. He divided the rock, and water gushed out for them to drink.\n\nActually, in this singular verse are a lot of hidden meanings.\n\nTo start with, when God led them through the wilderness they did thirst. They thirsted not from lack of water 💦, neither was it that the power of God could not provide them 💦 water.\n\nThey thirsted because it was a test from God.\n\nSo in the eyes 👀 of the Lord, and from the spiritual standpoint, they never thirsted; the provision was always there, even if not manifested when they wanted.\n\nHowever, from the human standpoint, those periods of thirst when they lacked water 💦 and murmured and complained were very significant.\n\nThe temporal need of the flesh for water so made them forget God's eternal supply, such that they lost the God perspective:\n\nA perspective God wanted them to retain — that God always had abundant supply for them.\n\nBut many times when tested they lost that mindset of the spirit. But Joshua and Caleb never did, hence God described them as having a different spirit.\n\nThough difficult and contrary to our human nature 🏞, we must think and maintain the thoughts of God even when circumstances oppose the promises of God.","dt":"2022-07-27T18:15:00","s":["cuepagv2nf"]}]},"49":{"15":[{"m":"God loves us very much.\n\nIsaiah 49:15-16 AMPC\n[And the Lord answered] Can a woman forget her nursing child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? Yes, they may forget, yet I will not forget you. Behold, I have indelibly imprinted (tattooed a picture of) you on the palm of each of My hands; [O Zion] your walls are continually before Me.\n\nSuch blessed assurance of our place in the hands of God.\n\nPsalm 125:2-3 AMPC\nAs the mountains are round about Jerusalem, so the Lord is round about His people from this time forth and forever. For the scepter of wickedness shall not rest upon the land of the [uncompromisingly] righteous, lest the righteous (God's people) stretch forth their hands to iniquity and apostasy.\n\nHe's tattooed us in him (AMPC); our walls, our dwelling places, are continually before him.\n\nAs the mountains surround Jerusalem.","dt":"2022-07-29T07:08:58","s":["pz32yt1hp1"]}],"23":[{"m":"It pays to wait on the Lord... Hear what scripture has to say on waiting on the Lord.\nContextually it has to do with Israel returning to God, but we can appropriate these blessings also.\n\nIsaiah 49:23 AMPC\nAnd kings shall be your foster fathers and guardians, and their queens your nursing mothers. They shall bow down to you with their faces to the earth and lick up the dust of your feet; and you shall know [with an acquaintance and understanding based on and grounded in personal experience] that I am the Lord; for they shall not be put to shame who wait for, look for, hope for, and expect Me.\n\nAmen, they shall not be ashamed that wait for me.\n\nThis is not the only promise for those who wait.\n\nWe who wait are also assured that we shall mount up with wings like eagles 🦅\n\nIsaiah 40:31 AMPC\nBut those who wait for the Lord [who expect, look for, and hope in Him] shall change and renew their strength and power; they shall lift their wings and mount up [close to God] as eagles [mount up to the sun]; they shall run and not be weary, they shall walk and not faint or become tired. [Heb. 12:1-3.]","dt":"2022-07-29T07:07:23","s":["xd9s83tyrb"]}],"6":[{"m":"Initially I thought Isaiah was talking about himself and his calling as a prophet, but this sounds more like Christ.","dt":"2026-08-05T08:33:47","s":["g74gjr06fg"]}]},"50":{"1":[{"m":"So in reality, we face only the natural consequences of our actions or inactions.\n\nYet God still saves us.\n\nImagine a world 🗺 where there was no consequence for our misdeeds — where will the lessons be, etc.? Such chaos we will have.\n\nHowever, there is hope for restoration and rescue. The goodness of the Lord is our lot.","dt":"2022-07-29T07:34:11","s":["up9zy16wr6"]}],"4":[{"m":"One would believe this was Isaiah talking about himself, but on reading the subsequent verses you wonder who was being spoken of?\n\nThe Messiah, because in hindsight we know these things happened to him, not Isaiah, or at least not recorded if it did happen to Isaiah.\nIn that case it carries a double reference:\n\nTo Isaiah and to the Messiah.","dt":"2024-09-30T06:11:32","s":["e6hhwpunbs"]}]},"51":{"1":[{"m":"Back to our core and our foundation.","dt":"2022-07-29T11:52:36","s":["df6z3xb41z"]}]},"53":{"12":[{"m":"Prophecies and prophetic books... We can't know it all.\n\nThis describes Christ, and indeed he fulfilled it to the letter.\n\nBut the thing about prophecies is that as it gets fulfilled, then you understand the prophecy better.\n\nWe see many times in the New Testament that as what prophecies say concerning Jesus was fulfilled in real time, we are told then the disciples remembered what was written.\n\nThis meant they knew what was written but did not exactly 100 percent know how it will play out... Indeed, sometimes it is after it had played out that they remembered that it was prophesied long ago.\n\nIn like manner the prophecies in Revelation concerning the end of the world.\n\nIt will play out in ways many people did not expect, except they that watch and pray.\n\nThat's the beauty of prophecy, so we are not caught unawares.\n\nBut that also calls for humility... We cannot know it all, even the most obvious, until it starts playing out; then we will understand.\n\nWe must therefore be humble, lest prophecy will be fulfilled right before our eyes.\n\nAgain, many expected Jesus to come as a king, only for him to come as a lamb first, which was also part of the prophecy concerning him.\n\nHe will come later as a king.\n\nIn like manner, the book of Revelations may not be fulfilled in chronological order, or it may be.\n\nJust that if you have read the book of Revelations before, you know it is so intertwined.\n\nSo we His children await its fulfilment in earnest expectation.\n\nFor the earnest expectation of the creation eagerly awaits the manifestation of the sons of God.","dt":"2026-08-06T08:26:59","s":["7h3m6lp4j6"]}]},"54":{"10":[{"m":"I feel this scripture speaking directly to me — indeed he was wroth with me for a season — a long season in my estimation, though he says it was for a little while, but now at the last his everlasting kindness and mercy will be with me for all eternity.","dt":"2026-08-07T08:28:21","s":["glq8iez7fv"]}],"16":[{"m":"The Lord says he's created the waster to destroy, so when he says no weapon 🔫 forged against you shall prosper, it's based on solid fact.","dt":"2022-08-01T10:39:54","s":["pz1zfx59cv"]}]},"55":{"1":[{"m":"The counsel of the Lord, the word of the Lord, is likened to free wine 🍷 and milk 🥛.\n\nAnd indeed the word and counsel of the Lord has come to us free of charge. Wisdom without pay, plus a free home tutor in the person of the Holy Ghost 👻.\n\nWisdom calls out to us not to despise him.","dt":"2022-08-01T10:52:06","s":["9rb3cfmvis"]}],"3":[{"m":"I like this passage for one thing.\n\nThe sure mercies of David ✡","dt":"2022-08-01T10:52:40","s":["sa8gljo891"]}],"7":[{"m":"He should forsake his thoughts — it all starts from the thoughts, so the Lord judges and corrects not just the ways, but recognises it all starts from the thoughts.","dt":"2026-08-07T08:33:15","s":["fvfq6nlua4"]}]},"56":{"5":[{"m":"God is indeed no respecter of persons.\nA son or daughter is not one who is by blood, but one who does the will of the Father.\n\nJesus said the same thing when he was told that his mother and brethren seek him.\n\nHe said, them that do listen and do his will are his mother and brethren.","dt":"2022-08-01T11:13:29","s":["p47bzp678w"]}],"8":[{"m":"The roping in of the Gentiles into the gospel program was long predicted in the Old Testament.","dt":"2024-10-02T21:02:58","s":["n9zg1srax"]}],"6":[{"m":"I was wondering what happened to the sons of the stranger, because he mentioned them first in verse 3, only for him to talk more about the eunuch — the dry tree — so I thought he had left off talking about the sons of the stranger, but here we have it.\n\nGod shares his plans for them, for their righteous living towards him.","dt":"2026-08-07T08:37:46","s":["re3ig8n6eq"]}]},"57":{"13":[{"m":"This is trust in God in the face of contrary information.\n\nHere the wind carries the people away and vanity takes them.\n\nThe only natural response will be that I am next; they have called upon their gods, and see, they are carried away.\n\nHow different will my case be? But then, in putting one's trust in the Lord, not only will you escape being carried away, but the very land of destruction you shall possess for an inheritance.\n\nYou shall thrive there.","dt":"2022-08-01T11:20:15","s":["8lo6maunfh"]}],"15":[{"m":"This is like my story. I like the verse 16, lest the spirit should fail before...","dt":"2022-08-01T11:30:41","s":["1uqm5dh6qn"]}],"21":[{"m":"Truth and wisdom to us: there is no peace to the wicked.","dt":"2022-08-01T11:28:17","s":["mlzaix9xj4"]}],"4":[{"m":"Were they making faces at God by scorning his laws and commands, his prophets and seers?","dt":"2026-08-07T08:40:17","s":["nro29fw1uu"]}]},"58":{"1":[{"m":"Is God a man 👨?\n\nThe way he seems to know the emotions and nature of man is amazing. He is omniscient and all-powerful.\n\nThere is no weakness in him. Yet he knows the nature of man and our weaknesses and frailties.\n\nHe commands his prophet to spare not.\n\nDo not hold back. He knows men do hold back, and he did not want that.","dt":"2022-08-01T11:58:18","s":["m8hrtllvy6"]}],"10":[{"m":"What a notable promise.\n\nIn obscurity shall thy light shine.","dt":"2022-08-01T12:00:43","s":["9oma9585ws"]}]},"59":{"1":[{"m":"Remember when we were kids and you did something really naughty and, say, Dad was angry 😡.\n\nYou were expected, and knew you had to make amends and apologize. You couldn't just walk back and pretend nothing happened and expect your favorite toy and game to be given you.\n\nMany times we do what is wrong, our conscience pricks us, but we pretend nothing has happened and we go on living our lives, instead of repenting and coming back to God our Father so our relationship is restored.\n\nSin separates us from God.\n\nThere's a flip side to it.","dt":"2022-08-02T06:39:20","s":["3nph6vzoyv"]}],"15":[{"m":"Is this so much like our time, where he who walks upright becomes the target and the prey?\n\nAs I look at the ills of Israel at this point in their history, I ask myself, why does God continue on with them?\n\nIt is because he has a covenant with Abraham. Looking at his love and dealings with Israel as compared to other nations, it seems unfair.\n\nAnd the demands of justice can be raised against God for his unjust love for Israel, but then God can reference them to their source, Abraham, who literally endured injustice for God and gave his all, including his posterity, to the Lord.\n\nSince Abraham did this, it was no longer unjust for God to constantly keep his eye on them and bring them back to himself when they repent.\n\nIt is the same demands of love and justice that Christ Jesus met on his cross, that through his blood we continue to be forgiven of our sins.\n\nOf course, it doesn't mean we can do what we want, because if we do we will be punished and reap the consequences; just that when we repent, we are restored.\n\nBut why choose such a hard path of suffering, only to repent, when one can be in constant peace with the Lord?","dt":"2024-10-03T07:52:38","s":["uzi06zvit1"]}]},"62":{"11":[{"m":"Alluding to the Christ coming.","dt":"2022-08-06T12:24:31","s":["cdxfdnastv"]}]},"63":{"3":[{"m":"Why was there no one with him? Does it mean there was none righteous with him?","dt":"2022-08-06T12:26:21","s":["ek0nktpeg7"]}],"4":[{"m":"Since it talks of the year of his redeemed, then it meant there was no one with him to help save his people, so his own arm worked out righteousness, i.e. verse 5.","dt":"2022-08-06T12:27:51","s":["0bryvrhwtj"]}],"11":[{"m":"So God led them by the angel of his presence. They grieved his Spirit, so He, God, was turned to be their enemy.\n\nThese verses distinguish him from his Spirit, but we see that his Spirit is kind of part of him.","dt":"2022-08-04T08:18:50","s":["6hk09qikne"]}],"16":[{"m":"What does this passage mean? Is it to say their fathers did not know them?\n\nOf course we don't know our descendants, though they do know us.","dt":"2022-08-04T08:15:52","s":["s8dm5eu8rx"]}],"17":[{"m":"Why are they blaming God?\n\nIsaiah knew that God had the ability to harden hearts, especially when men make up their minds to deliberately go against his laws.\n\nThen God adds up further rebellion by hardening their hearts 💕, such that their disobedience goes beyond any sense.\n\nPaul explained it as God leaves them to a reprobate mind.","dt":"2022-08-04T08:22:21","s":["v3wna06cvy"]}],"7":[{"m":"God is good.","dt":"2022-08-06T12:32:27","s":["l0un3s5sor"]}]},"65":{"3":[{"m":"Love, true love is some way.\n\nGod continued to hold his arm out to a people who continued to spit in his face 😔.\n\nHe still worked out a way for them to get back to him. Because of love.","dt":"2022-08-06T12:35:18","s":["5lul63hka1"]}],"25":[{"m":"Amen... This is a utopia, and it will happen.","dt":"2022-08-06T12:39:41","s":["oaquost1kt"]}]},"16":{"10":[{"m":"Such allegory, especially in the prophets and Psalms.","dt":"2022-07-16T11:00:18","s":["yejuskpthf"]}]},"22":{"11":[{"m":"In the midst of all this, was God hoping that they might somehow come to their senses and call unto him?\n\nI think so.","dt":"2022-07-17T06:56:12","s":["o7fn243jo1"]}],"13":[{"m":"Oh, I see... So this expression was literal.\n\nThe people were really going to die the next day.\n\nThey chose death instead of repentance, and the Lord swore that for that sin they shall have death ☠ as they desired.","dt":"2024-09-19T06:54:44","s":["tej0am6vbu"]}]},"23":{"18":[{"m":"The merchandise of the harlot that reveals her nakedness shall, in contrast, be used for proper covering and clothing.","dt":"2026-07-28T09:51:49","s":["cw75qnv2ml"]}]},"24":{"23":[{"m":"How shall the moon and the sun be ashamed? By the Lord of Hosts being the light thereof in that day. Because in that holy city, Zion, there is no night there. No, there is no night there.","dt":"2026-07-28T09:57:43","s":["hf2rq4pbps"]}]},"31":{"1":[{"m":"See, God is not condemning the horses nor chariots; what he's saying is, putting your trust in them when he, God, is not in the cycle 🚴 is a failed venture.\n\nThe God factor is what completes the cycle 💫.\n\nSo he mocks at them that go to war with incomplete armor. It's like having a gun without bullets... Completely useless.\n\nThis illustration is of war, but it's applicable in all else.\n\nGod is needed in all things to complete it.\n\nThis is akin to the scripture that says:\n\nProverbs 21:31 KJV\nThe horse is prepared against the day of battle: but safety is of the Lord.","dt":"2022-07-23T07:54:23","s":["76bh2jpb2g"]}],"3":[{"m":"In essence, God is superior to man and the spirit far superior to flesh.\n\nIn other words, the life of man is God and the life of the flesh is the spirit.\n\nLike fuel is to a machine is the spirit to the flesh; let us therefore not exalt the flesh above its place, nor man above his honour.\n\nSo Paul exhorts us in\n\nPhilippians 2:3 KJV\nLet nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem others better than themselves.","dt":"2022-07-23T08:05:10","s":["bcsfizpz42"]}]},"37":{"1":[{"m":"This was not a good place to be in at all... I can imagine the fear and the possible insurrection being planned out by people who wanted to escape with their lives.\nThe much fear and sleepless nights the king 👑 had to endure.\n\nHe was a good king 👑.","dt":"2026-08-02T07:16:18","s":["ie6l8fj274"]}],"26":[{"m":"So Assyria was ordained by God from long ago to do what he was doing.\n\nHe thought 💭 it was his own doing and his own strength 💪.\n\nLittle did he know that his pride would be his ruin.","dt":"2024-09-25T09:47:43","s":["1eza7asmna"]}],"38":[{"m":"He was worshipping his gods that failed him.\n\nMaybe he did something wrong, he might have thought, but the 100s of thousands of people who died was a real blow to the king and his kingdom.\n\nWhat did they attribute the death to?\n\nThey definitely knew it was an evil spirit that had done such damage. Obviously they would not credit such atrocities as coming from an angel, and a good one at that.\n\nBut on the side of Judah, that was the good angel of the Lord.","dt":"2026-08-02T07:28:00","s":["z299kyvfju"]}]},"52":{"13":[{"m":"The Christ","dt":"2024-09-30T06:34:24","s":["ndhvbg6uuh"]}]},"61":{"4":[{"m":"If this was in reference to Christ, which it was, for Christ quoted from it, then after HE binds up the broken hearted and restores his people, they now are able to build and restore the ancient ruins.\n\nEven today ancient Israel lies in ruins; there are desolate places that must be raised up, typically the Temple Mount, and many more such places must be raised up, and they will.\n\nJesus began this restorative work described in this chapter, and 2 millennia later he had not yet gotten to verse 4. This tells me that even with prophecy, and with the book of, for instance, Revelations, many events will happen over time periods that the book is silent on.\n\nWho knows, maybe God will in the future give other prophetic words, filling in the gaps and predicting some more specific things that will happen, or at least explaining the current prophecies that the Lord has given in the book of Revelations.","dt":"2026-08-07T22:22:12","s":["ce7mbn63yk"]}]}},"1 Kings":{"1":{"8":[{"m":"Pour réflexion plus tard.","dt":"2020-05-20T08:32:53","s":["of44wt5j9g"]},{"m":"Let the game of politics and of thrones begin.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:10:43","s":["qx5n8otb1l"]},{"m":"How come Joab had separated himself from the mighty men who had been comrades in arms all these decades?\n\nJoab was such a fiercely independent and selfish schemer.\n\nAnd this ultimately led to his demise.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:22:47","s":["rr1t3lc5zr"]}],"14":[{"m":"Many thoughts regarding the politics of the day. But here are my considerations: firstly, God had promised Solomon would be king, and that by the mouth of the prophet Nathan himself.\n\nSo how come now Nathan has become a politician and trying to \"help God\"? Was he not supposed to leave everything to happen by itself?\n\nAnd this is where I think we sometimes miss it as believers. We leave many things to chance. Of course, that is not to say that we are to run off pursuing our own agenda by whatever means possible, be it fair or foul means.\n\nThe point I see here is we are to do what is at all possible within our power to do with regards to the promises of God, and leave the divine part to God.\n\nThat also means God will not do what we must do as men.\n\nAs I muse over this verse, another thing also comes to mind. Remember when David slept with Bathsheba, God did nothing all through David's scheming and murder of Uriah, but rather sent Nathan after the event to call out David.\n\nWhy did God wait till that time? That is something worth pondering about.\n\nAgain, is it not interesting that Solomon, of this wicked union, was chosen by God to be king? Something worth thinking about.","dt":"2022-05-30T11:24:18","s":["t3cyw6upgt"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why was David very old, yet Joab and his mighty men remained relatively stronger?\n\nCould it be the weight and burden of kingship that burdened him so much?\n\nThe burden of a good king 👑.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:24:22","s":["a87940dcyf"]}],"23":[{"m":"Behold Nathan the prophet: the systems of the kingdom were established.\n\nAn announcement 📢 must be made to the king 👑 even before individuals are granted audience with the king 👑.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:12:53","s":["7xfyj9qux4"]}],"26":[{"m":"Where was Solomon at this time?","dt":"2022-05-30T11:25:48","s":["fg7wg38em7"]}],"28":[{"m":"Bathsheba had by this time been excused so Nathan the prophet could be granted audience.\n\nOnly for Nathan the prophet to say the same things.\n\nThis further brought emphasis to the mind of the old king 👑, the severity of the situation, that it was not mere insecurity of the woman but a real threat to their lives and his precious son Solomon.\n\nThe act of Nathan and Bathsheba was wisdom.\n\nLord, grant me wisdom in the Castle and in the corridors of Power.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:18:27","s":["cuaan5blmp"]}],"30":[{"m":"I wonder when David uttered these words, and under which circumstance he made this promise.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:20:17","s":["nwxvbvkie9"]}],"33":[{"m":"Riding upon the king's mule was very significant; it was indicative of the transfer of power.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:37:41","s":["9ddksro0bz"]},{"m":"What was the significance of Gihon?","dt":"2024-07-16T06:40:12","s":["bgkk6lzpd8"]}],"40":[{"m":"'Ei asem oo', to wit 'matter oo', as the Nigerian 🇳🇬 would say.\n\nTWO commemorations happening at the same time.\n\nBut one carried more weight 🏋️ than the other.\n\nAnd the entire people followed the king's choice, Solomon, whiles Adonijah's group were left behind.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:59:53","s":["9qh73k9v53"]}],"47":[{"m":"That sealed it. Anyone can anoint another king 👑 and rejoice in it, as demonstrated by Adonijah,\n\nBut to sit on the throne of David the king, and have his servants bless him, and for him to acknowledge such, was more powerful a symbolism than any other.\n\nAdonijah had all the king's sons backing him up, which in itself was a very powerful symbol.\n\nThe other sons, though stepchildren, had all come together to back up Adonijah, who was the eldest son at this point.\n\nAmnon, the first and eldest son, was dead; the 2nd, no mention is made of his whereabouts; Absalom was dead in his revolt against his father; and now Adonijah was next in command.\n\nAnd all the other sons of different mothers had converged to make Adonijah king.\n\nThis was a very powerful symbol.\n\nHow could Solomon, the youngest son, and of an opportunistic woman 👩 as Bathsheba, be made king 👑?\n\nThey can't let that boy rule over them all. They had hatched a plan and it worked so far.\n\nAnd David their father knew his sons were right to want justice and the right thing to be done...\n\nBut David had sworn by the Lord to Bathsheba, and he would not renounce it.\n\nHe himself said that in\n\nPsalm 15:4 ESV\nin whose eyes a vile person is despised, but who honors those who fear the LORD; who swears to his own hurt and does not change;\n\nThat such an one would dwell in the hill of the Lord.\n\nSo David honored the word of the Lord God concerning Solomon, and honored his word to his wife Bathsheba.\n\nNathan was the one who rebuked David for his sins with Bathsheba, and one would have expected him to be the last to support her, seeing her selfishness.\n\nBut he was firstly a prophet and a man of God, and knew what the word of the Lord was.\n\nAnd he chose the Lord's side, though that wasn't the fairest.\n\nBut God does not judge after appearances, but judges the heart, and also God does not count the sins of the fathers unto the sons.\n\nThe fathers must not eat sour grapes and the children's teeth set on edge.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:12:49","s":["3p4r8v9ial"]}],"53":[{"m":"It was settled, the Lord had established Solomon — for Adonijah to bow 🙇 was symbolic of surrender to the new dynasty.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:14:11","s":["zxay39c1to"]}],"1":[{"m":"David was about 70 years old at this time.\n\nDake's commentary makes an interesting, puzzling yet mind-blowing 🤯 point about the kings after David.\n\nThat none lived more than 60 years. I'll have to investigate this.\nWhat???","dt":"2024-07-16T06:30:46","s":["g2xjhq3zy9"]}],"6":[{"m":"It seems this family 👪 had within them a strong 💪 thirst for power and rulership... Even if it meant usurping them.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:10:14","s":["pbmsdpg0va"]}],"12":[{"m":"The matters of the kingdom are a matter of life and death ☠.\n\nIt was not merely about wielding power for power's sake.\n\nPower has to be protected and all potential threats eliminated.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:21:53","s":["0utpzxpyuc"]}],"27":[{"m":"The Lord had spoken concerning Solomon, but it will take the man, the king 👑 David, to cause the will of the Lord to pass.\n\nAnd David was God's man 👨, and he will cause the Lord's will to happen.\n\nThat is why the Lord loved him so much.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:27:03","s":["06fple8677"]}],"31":[{"m":"Oh, where was Michal, the first true wife of David? She had lost significance in the kingdom 👑, and one of the very few opportunities to continue the name of her father was lost.","dt":"2024-07-16T06:35:57","s":["yqu9zvxqpf"]}],"42":[{"m":"Speaking 🔊 as a king 👑, he didn't know his kingdom never began, for it to be even said that it had ended.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:00:55","s":["dbigyw44v3"]}]},"2":{"8":[{"m":"Was it not just an empty curse 🤬?\nDavid made light of it at the time, but it really got to him and pierced his heart.\n\nHere we see how he still makes bitter reference to it.\n\nHe wanted that man dead.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:20:32","s":["l4c82lba3t"]}],"26":[{"m":"Anathoth, there is something familiar about that name.","dt":"2022-05-30T11:37:48","s":["swtjxxha1k"]},{"m":"Oh, Solomon had been told stories, stories of heroism,\n\nStories of battles and the kingdom and friendships. So he knew who to save and who to kill.\n\nImagine he had not been told and went ahead to kill one who had played such a vital role in his father's kingdom.\n\nLord, help 😣 me make wise choices, and to build in wisdom and not tear down.\n\nHelp me, Lord, help 😣 me 😭.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:30:17","s":["86xzo3ijzh"]}],"27":[{"m":"It took close to 2 centuries thereabout for God's word to be fulfilled. It makes me wonder, how many curses and blessings are hanging on our 👪 families and heads and businesses, awaiting their final and/or complete manifestations?","dt":"2020-05-20T08:55:11","s":["4ghe0mrdsx"]},{"m":"Wow... Such a long time ago, but the word of the Lord will not fail... Until Shiloh comes... Until Shiloh comes 😭","dt":"2024-07-16T07:32:03","s":["vikthx7462"]},{"m":"In the eyes of everyone he was thrust out because of his insurrection, but in the eyes of providence it was long determined, and he was steered into his own exit from the priesthood because of the curse upon his fathers.\n\nHe was a good man, but the old order and curse still had to be fulfilled.\n\nHis goodness, however, spoke for him and spared his life.\n\nI am sure he could have been spared from this and the curse passed on to his son, but this was the time set of the order of divine justice.","dt":"2026-06-01T06:44:31","s":["e82dae495f"]}],"31":[{"m":"Why do I feel sorry for Joab? He knew the Lord, though he did not love him unconditionally.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:33:25","s":["fw9pmoto5x"]}],"41":[{"m":"Hmm, the spies of the king. Solomon had spies everywhere.","dt":"2022-05-30T11:40:53","s":["c5qff0rdvb"]}],"45":[{"m":"Solomon here blesses his throne and that of David his father... Reversing invariably the curse 🤬 of Shimei against David.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:38:27","s":["iq7sl1zk92"]}],"46":[{"m":"Ah, alas, all rebels dealt with and the wicked put to death. I find it interesting, though, that David forgave Shimei at the first, one that posed such a risk to the throne. But David had such a heart of Gold.\n\nHowever, he was a wise man and knew Shimei had to die before he became trouble again, and for his grievous offense of cursing the king.","dt":"2022-05-30T11:43:58","s":["sgger2n5hv"]}],"7":[{"m":"Matters of the heart ♥ weigh in heavily.\n\nAnd now David charges his son to avenge him and do what he, David, couldn't do.\n\nDavid had the upper hand in that, though he dies, he lives on in his son, who was younger and stronger 💪.\n\nAnd his son would continue his works and bring justice to the kingdom.\n\nThis advantage David's enemies did not have.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:18:22","s":["omvlbwgv8n"]}],"20":[{"m":"Yet he said her nay.\n\nWhen one swears or promises, it can be breached, and righteously so, if the terms are not met.\n\nIt is not wisdom to go ahead and honour a promise or vow just for honoring's sake when it will bring harm and danger to you and others.\n\nWe see many such breaches first with God and his covenants — when the terms are breached, he changes his mind, as we see with Saul, and even Israel.\n\nWe see the same with David's promise to Shimei — he did not hurt him in his time but trusted his son to do so.\n\nSolomon promised his own mother but refused to carry it out because other factors had arisen that showed an ill 🤒 intent for asking the vow.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:26:32","s":["mf0fvv628o"]}],"33":[{"m":"There are certain deeds that greatly weigh 🏋️ in and surpass others.\n\nDavid had killed many wicked men for the Lord and for David's throne, but the lives of those two men could not be forgiven nor atoned for by the blood of the evil 😈 men he had slaughtered.\n\nWe ought to be careful, because not all actions carry the same weight.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:35:49","s":["snhdc3of24"]}],"39":[{"m":"Barely three years... This must have had the hand of the Lord in it.\n\nHelp me, Lord, to know who your anointed is, and to submit to your chosen one and authority.","dt":"2024-07-16T07:37:15","s":["8vc9p5cbch"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"Hm, Solomon, Solomon — it is one thing marrying a foreign woman, but now he brings the heathen into the city of his father.\n\nGranted that he married 👰 them for political reasons, he did not need to bring them close to himself to the point of them influencing him.","dt":"2024-07-17T06:47:46","s":["fpvwnjcjlm"]}],"16":[{"m":"These two harlots were not even to be given audience but punished severely, indeed the death sentence for sexual immorality, but the times had changed and the covenant broken many times and ways.\n\nBut the Lord remained merciful.\n\nIndeed, if the terms of the covenant were kept, these women would not even have become harlots in the first place.\n\nBut sadly that was the case.\n\nAnd it's the same in our world 🗺 today. Christianity is weakened so much and so different from what the fathers left for us.\n\nBut again, God is merciful as we continue to journey into him and retrace our steps.","dt":"2024-07-17T07:13:36","s":["cw4qvn0py"]}],"26":[{"m":"Such wickedness of the wicked.","dt":"2024-07-17T07:15:51","s":["u6e5ihnkwj"]}],"28":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔. Indeed wisdom.","dt":"2022-05-31T11:36:04","s":["1wb5akjxuq"]},{"m":"A specific kind of wisdom was upon Solomon... Lord, give us wisdom, even as a church ⛪","dt":"2024-07-17T07:16:27","s":["p702kup035"]}],"12":[{"m":"Solomon, Solomon, no wonder the Lord loved him so much.\n\nHe put God first before his needs.\n\nGod looks at the hearts 💕 of all David's sons who wanted to be kings 👑, and compares it to Solomon's, whose desire was to please 😌 the Lord.\n\nAnd the Lord chooses Solomon, just as he had chosen David before all his brethren.\n\nSolomon's heart was right before the Lord.\n\nThis is a lesson for us to choose God first in all things.\nJesus renders it this way:\n\nMatthew 6:33 ESV\nBut seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness, and all these things will be added to you.","dt":"2024-07-17T07:03:09","s":["1e9ig1qsd6"]}],"14":[{"m":"And this was where God ended with Solomon.\n\nHe would lengthen his days — this could indicate both length of days of his life and length of days of his reign.\n\nAnd knowing God, if Solomon had kept His word, God would not only have lengthened his days but would have upped the terms of the covenant, by possibly guaranteeing him and his children rulership over Israel for generations.\n\nBut sadly, after Solomon the kingdom 👑 was divided.","dt":"2024-07-17T07:09:48","s":["9bnkkzkq8a"]}]},"4":{"32":[{"m":"One thousand and five songs, really... How is that possible?","dt":"2020-05-21T09:07:05","s":["s14a5x4kzd"]}],"34":[{"m":"Lord, give me wisdom, I pray.","dt":"2024-07-17T14:23:55","s":["yuf88257eu"]}],"15":[{"m":"Family 👪 and friends, that's how kingdoms and government are run.\n\nWhat else do you expect?","dt":"2024-07-17T14:20:45","s":["crvqi8lnk9"]}]},"5":{"2":[{"m":"Because his father had laid a good foundation, he could tap into his father's network.\n\nOh, if only the kingdom of Solomon had continued, and every generation stands upon the shoulders of the next.\n\nIndeed, what a mighty kingdom and throne that would have been.","dt":"2024-08-01T07:14:11","s":["675rjpkkz0"]}],"4":[{"m":"So not only was it a divine decision not to let David build a temple for the Lord, it was also a technical decision.\n\nThere were wars on every side; how was he going to make time in the midst of wars for such a grandiose project?\n\nNot to mention invasions of the enemy into the city where the temple was to be built, and possibly breaching the building, breaking it down etc.\n\nIt was a very wise decision to put it on hold until David, now at peace and having put out every rebellion though old, to put up the building 🏢","dt":"2024-08-01T07:20:44","s":["zb6k0c2jeo"]}],"11":[{"m":"Swapping of skill and resources.\n\nHiram made available his skill and got food and oil in payment or in exchange.","dt":"2024-08-01T07:32:20","s":["1voxz62lvm"]}]},"6":{"7":[{"m":"Why was that so? Was it to denote Solomon had created a new way of building, again another sign of his wisdom,\n\nOr was it to ensure constant peace and serenity in reverence to God and the city where he would dwell?\n\n1 Kings 6:7 NLT\nThe stones used in the construction of the Temple were finished at the quarry, so there was no sound of hammer, ax, or any other iron tool at the building site.","dt":"2024-08-01T07:44:04","s":["r5x9yjn04x","l8pznozrsm"]}],"38":[{"m":"It took seven years to perfect all things regarding the temple.","dt":"2024-08-01T07:52:07","s":["e555i61n15"]}],"12":[{"m":"You can see here God's desperate desire to find a man who would obey him and stick to his ways, so he gets blessed by the Almighty himself,\n\nHe so wanted Solomon to be that man.","dt":"2024-08-01T07:47:17","s":["c6se9c2vwt"]},{"m":"Is it not interesting that in building the house for the Lord, and in the Lord commenting on the house, he did not come to give further designs and specifications concerning the building, but rather his instructions concerned obedience to his moral law... His judgements and commandments?\n\nThat was what was most important to the Lord.","dt":"2026-06-12T18:28:29","s":["7f9bca2669"]}]},"7":{"12":[{"m":"Even today, archeological findings show the stones used for the foundations of these massive structures weigh tonnes and are still present — though Solomon's temple was destroyed because of Israel's denial of God, and other more powerful nations than they arose and destroyed them.\n\nBut fast forward: now we have history guiding us — the powerful nations have learnt to monitor other nations, and keep and protect vehemently what they have.\n\nNo one will be fooled again into oblivion, because history has taught us a lot.\n\nWe are now at the end of all things — nations are surviving for long, and technology is making man too powerful for our own good.\n\nUnless the end comes to correct all things, man, with such an evil heart and with such powerful technology, will self-destruct and commit wicked abominations.\n\nThe end of all things is at hand; the end is here.\n\nWe have become like when Adam fell and had to be prevented from getting the tree of life, lest in his fallen and wicked state he lives forever. That will be a disaster for man himself and the world God has created.\n\nWe are there again now, but this time we have the tree of life — our tech has made us too powerful for our good.\n\nThe end is here; it is only the end that can undo this that we find ourselves in.","dt":"2026-06-13T09:03:49","s":["kh9kpsg9ph","f336ccd56f"]}],"17":[{"m":"Solomon himself said,\n\nSeest thou a man skilled in his work? He will stand before kings... He will not stand before mean men.\n\nHe knew this from experience, and now because of his great skill, Huram, though not fully Israel 🇮🇱, is mentioned in the Hebrew scriptures.","dt":"2024-08-02T07:37:07","s":["cbkyrkfmpo"]}]},"8":{"5":[{"m":"Solomon was a very rich man.","dt":"2024-08-03T09:22:09","s":["9cb96jsiil"]}],"9":[{"m":"Solomon, in building the temple, literally redesigned everything, making it bigger and more glamorous than the original tabernacle,\n\nBut the ark of the covenant was not redesigned; the original one was taken from its old place and brought into the new.\n\nYes, the room, i.e. the most holy place itself, was redesigned with cherubims standing with their wings all over the room,\n\nBut the ark itself was not touched. Why?\n\nIt could be that that was the instruction from the Lord, for scripture says the design of the temple David received from the Lord.\n\nBut even if that was the case, why did the Lord choose to keep the original ark of the covenant?\n\nI think the answer is found in verse... As the name suggests, it is the ark of the covenant; it symbolizes the covenant between God and Israel, and so it was not to be touched. The original document, i.e. the ark, is what was kept and put in its place in the temple.\n\nIn verse 21 Solomon says,\n\n1 Kings 8:21 KJV\nAnd I have set there a place for the ark, wherein is the covenant of the LORD, which he made with our fathers, when he brought them out of the land of Egypt.\n\nThis was the original ark and none was made like it, so there was only one ark always.\n\nThe ancients had a very good practice of setting up landmarks. A testimony to the past, and helps to transfer knowledge across generations.","dt":"2024-08-03T09:33:18","s":["kp9l39yuxs"]}],"21":[{"m":"The original ark was kept in its place; there was none like it.","dt":"2024-08-03T09:42:54","s":["8lrwvnrmh8"]}],"25":[{"m":"Solomon recognized that the covenant originally was with his father David and not with him, but he has benefited greatly from it, if not more.","dt":"2024-08-03T09:44:27","s":["lb2jpheusc"]}],"39":[{"m":"No wonder Daniel understood this covenant prayer and harnessed it, and prayed daily to the Lord facing Jerusalem and the temple.\n\nDaniel was indeed a very wise and strategic man.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:09:53","s":["dt5gauvje3"]}],"43":[{"m":"So by extension any one of the heathen nations who gains this wisdom can tap into it and be blessed.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:11:24","s":["jr5ttns6co"]}],"47":[{"m":"Solomon was not presumptuous to think that such a glorious sight and manifest presence of the Lord will mean perpetual submission to the Lord for all generations,\n\nHe knew men will fail and be punished as due them; even he, Solomon, failed in his lifetime to serve the Lord blameless.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:14:31","s":["272qns6kf5"]}],"58":[{"m":"A good plea that the Lord forsake not his people, so that even when they do err,\n\nBecause they are his people, he will still not forsake them but will do all it takes to keep them his people.\n\nAnd this God did, so no matter how much Israel sinned, he punished them sufficiently to bring them back to himself.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:18:37","s":["mh9j9vhnce"]}],"63":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 so here Solomon offered far more than the 1000 sheep 🐑 offering that is often preached about.\n\nObviously because after this offering God did not appear to Solomon as at the first, so this case is not a good preaching point.\n\nI think 🤔 sometimes we are not honest with the scriptures and use them to achieve our own goals.\n\nUpdate to above:\n\nWell actually God did appear to Solomon this second time as well, so I was wrong.","dt":"2022-06-12T06:58:14","s":["0pdqcatwxq"]}],"65":[{"m":"In this verse we can hear 👂 the voice of the author; he says unto the Lord our God, not the Lord their God.\n\nCould it be the author was present at this time of the feast, or he was also expressing his faith as an Israelite in the same God that Solomon and his people had?","dt":"2024-08-03T10:22:33","s":["y56dry7lox"]}],"33":[{"m":"See the condition under which Israel will be smitten before the enemy:\n\nIf they have sinned against the Lord. Outside of that they cannot be defeated; it does not matter the size of their enemies, they cannot be smitten.\n\nWhat a gift, what a people.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:06:20","s":["pu6axtm9b1"]}],"46":[{"m":"So there are sins we commit that the Lord overlooks, and there are sins we commit that anger the Lord and receive just punishment for.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:12:41","s":["5o244wb7hw"]}]},"9":{"16":[{"m":"Wow... These men and kings of those times were heartless and literally god-like, but wicked.\n\nCities and families were destroyed, generations cut off, just to please a man and a king's daughter.\n\nThis goes to show what man does with power.","dt":"2024-08-10T08:19:48","s":["z86ju0fgrh"]}],"19":[{"m":"I guess now that this is the expanse of territory Israel of today eventually wants to conquer and occupy.","dt":"2024-08-10T08:21:14","s":["lv63nefrlu"]}],"25":[{"m":"Three times a year he honored the Lord in a grand way.\n\nSolomon had really just started his journey, and did so on a good note.","dt":"2024-08-10T08:22:57","s":["6egeg8medt"]}],"9":[{"m":"This story has been so well told and documented that it refused to fade into a fable, legend or superstition.\n\nIt became what it truly was, a true and related miracle by a living God who still works amongst his people to this day.","dt":"2024-08-10T08:16:28","s":["0t71k2nenp"]}]},"10":{"1":[{"m":"She heard of his fame as it relates to the name of the Lord.\n\nThe wisdom, success and fame of Solomon were never independent of God.\n\nBecause when it comes to a visibly successful King like Solomon, the obvious question most would ask would be the source of his wisdom.\n\nAnd the answer was always the Lord. That alone was a great tool of evangelism.\n\nAnd when you came to Jerusalem and ISRAEL, there were two great and MIGHTY edifices,\n\nOne of them was Solomon's house and the other was the Lord's temple.\n\nThe Lord was never missing in the display of splendor and the wealth and fame and success of Solomon.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:24:07","s":["63m6kwvnam"]}],"4":[{"m":"Wisdom cannot be hidden.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:25:16","s":["c2ivmz411d"]}],"5":[{"m":"She had fallen in love at this time 🙃","dt":"2024-08-20T06:28:37","s":["b81z2i316c"]}],"9":[{"m":"Immediately she had become a believer. Just by observation, not mere empty words.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:26:48","s":["znx0rkfi2j"]}],"10":[{"m":"This much gold contributed to 20 percent of the gold that Solomon received in a year.\n\nThat is a lot of Gold. Sheba herself was rich in her own right.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:32:53","s":["6cqmseo9pk"]}],"14":[{"m":"Sheba alone in one visit brought 20 percent of the gold Solomon receives in a year.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:31:14","s":["phl70yympe"]}],"24":[{"m":"All these kings and nobles who came to Solomon, the counsel they received,\n\nIs that not what we have written down for us in Proverbs and Ecclesiastes?\n\nOh, the wisdom of royals and of kings have been given to us. Wow\n\nIndeed, these proverbs will make the simple wise and establish a man in his life.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:42:22","s":["fgpflbi8m1"]}],"25":[{"m":"Everyone hearing of the wisdom of Solomon and his riches will themselves bring the very best of the best.\n\nTo catch his eye and outdo the others. Solomon thus kept going higher and higher.\n\nFor Sheba's visit to have been particularly mentioned shows her power and influence and the rareness of her gifts.\n\nHer spices were described as none being in the kingdom.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:39:39","s":["sbb3bnyifg"]}]},"11":{"2":[{"m":"Surely they will turn your heart away — what made it so sure?\n\nWhy was it not the other way? Same thing he told the whole of Israel 🇮🇱, not to intermarry lest they be led after other gods.\n\nWhy could they not intermarry and lead the others to Jehovah?\n\nIt appears sin and evil 😈 and idolatry wield a certain stronger 💪 influence and, I guess, more aggressive drive and lure.\n\nWhiles right and righteousness carries the still small gentle influence. Never surmounting the will. Never deceiving.\n\nBut like a breeze, we are invited in to do good.\n\nSo that is why they and Solomon were forewarned.","dt":"2022-06-23T06:34:00","s":["366xc30z5g"]},{"m":"There is something about idols and the dark side that has this allure to attract and deceive.\n\nSuch that your heart lies to you and the power of darkness leads you astray; to the slaughter.\n\nThat is why the way out is not to entangle or dabble in it, but to stay far.\n\nSolomon, being a man of wisdom, sought strange knowledge and experiences.\n\nAnd even he, though the wisest, could not escape the allure of the darkness.\n\nHe fell, and that without remedy... Not even the voice of God could bring him back.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:47:04","s":["zbynzf6m1n"]}],"7":[{"m":"Oh, and what did the people do, and how did they feel, when they saw their once great king, in the sight of God and man, turn to such disaster?\n\nI can imagine the heaviness of their hearts.\n\nOh why, Solomon, why? I'm sure heads had to roll to make way for such abominations.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:54:57","s":["wx6mnt222w"]}],"12":[{"m":"I'm only wondering, but why would God tell him that he will not do it in his days, and go ahead to tell him that because of David ✡ the throne will not depart from their lineage, no matter how grave the offense?\n\nI guess because God had in time past committed himself to this covenant, and so all knew he was bound to keep it.\n\nSo of course God had to find other ways of beating his people into line...","dt":"2022-06-23T09:37:51","s":["vaqlqv9if4"]}],"33":[{"m":"As I read these verses I ask myself...\n\nHave we and are we worshipping these spirits still, unconsciously and unbeknownst to us?\n\nCould the worship of self, sex, abortions, celebrity worship, abcdef+ etc. be actually directed to these spirits and deities, but in a modern manner and with a touch of class?\n\nYes, I believe so; these demon spirits are still in operation and served, but differently.","dt":"2024-08-21T06:10:17","s":["wenezha21r"]}],"34":[{"m":"All his life?? 😳 So there are people who are messing up and around but seem not completely destroyed because of a previous good done and covenant made that is keeping them.","dt":"2022-06-23T06:49:15","s":["f6us442rt2"]}],"40":[{"m":"Solomon had now become like his father's adversary, aka Saul.\n\nHe persecuted David because of the word of the Lord to make him king 👑, and now ironically David's son Solomon is pursuing someone because the Lord has prophesied to make him king 👑.\n\nInstead of repenting, he sought to use his power to control and alter what God had spoken.\n\nIt seems there is something about power that makes you think 🤔 you're divine of a sort.\n\nThat corruption of power is what destroyed Saul.\n\nThough he knew the word of God, yet he felt he could somehow thwart the word of God.\n\nSuch audacity, but that is how pride and rebellion fill the heart, as witchcraft.\n\nYou see, you have powers and therefore ascribe deity to yourself.","dt":"2024-08-21T06:35:47","s":["l9uex5xe3h"]},{"m":"History repeats. He sought to kill Jeroboam, much like Saul sought to kill his father David. Oh Solomon, Solomon.","dt":"2026-06-26T02:15:17","s":["osf7rrzx5j","a957b8ad84"]}],"4":[{"m":"This was how long it took, a lifetime literally, for him to be brought low.\n\nHe had walked in wisdom and in his prime could not be lured, but as he aged and his sharpness was gone,\n\nHe needed support, and the very people that lay in his bosom to prop him up were daughters of Belial.\n\nThey did him in and destroyed his kingdom.","dt":"2024-08-20T06:52:58","s":["hmd65fnm9g"]}],"38":[{"m":"Eiiiiii... Jeroboam BLEW IT BIG TIME ⌚. Like, today we will be talking about Jeroboam and David ✡ as the twin kings 👑 over national Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nBut alas, it was not to be so. How this man missed an eternal opportunity to do good forever.\n\nBecause see, God promised him an enduring house 🏡 just like David.\n\nSuch perfect timing. Yet he missed it. Joshua, Caleb and Co did not get such a promise.\n\nBut by mere virtue of being born in the times of the kings, he gets the bargain of a lifetime and blows it.\n\nLORD HAVE MERCY","dt":"2022-06-23T06:53:29","s":["d1189azq9e"]}],"39":[{"m":"God was really wroth with Solomon, but he loved David and had respect unto him and to his covenant with him.\n\nHere Jeroboam had the opportunity of a lifetime to do the same for himself and his seed after him.\n\nYet he blew it, and did so big time.\n\nOh Lord, help me seize my defining moments and not miss my time.","dt":"2024-08-21T06:31:55","s":["7cjyr1s687"]}]},"12":{"4":[{"m":"Rehoboam... I wonder why the kingdom had to fall under his watch ⌚.\n\nObviously he did not have any personal leanings and covenant with Jehovah for him to obtain mercy, or at least a deferment of judgements.\n\nHe lost ten tribes, and there was found no pardon nor ransom to help stay the judgements of God. He did not have relationship.","dt":"2022-06-23T11:26:03","s":["v13hxc8t09"]}],"6":[{"m":"These stood before Solomon, so possessed much wisdom and understanding of the times.\n\nThey knew that due to the power, wealth and influence of Solomon, he could afford to put the people under burdensome labour and still wield control over his kingdom.\n\nNot so with his son Rehoboam. He was not Solomon; the times had changed and the old men knew it...\n\nLord, give me wisdom to know and understand the times and seasons of life. So I know what I ought to do.","dt":"2022-06-23T11:23:44","s":["yqthaafreo"]}],"15":[{"m":"The Lord is very active in watching his word to come to pass.\n\nHe was involved in giving foolish counsel to Rehoboam, in order to divide his kingdom.\n\nI believe that Rehoboam himself hated the Lord, else the Lord would have exempted him from this division, but as we will see later, he worshipped other gods.","dt":"2024-08-22T06:42:09","s":["dbv2y5qx1w"]}],"21":[{"m":"A strange alliance.\nHow time changes and flies. Judah and Benjamin, of Saul of Kish, in alliance.\n\nI guess because there was a time when the 10 tribes were of Benjamin, in that Benjamin reigned over Israel and David over Judah.\n\nLikely they wanted their property back.","dt":"2022-06-23T11:31:58","s":["j3iw7048cd"]}],"22":[{"m":"God could directly send men to the kings and directly interfere in matters of the kingdom.\n\nSadly, it is not so anymore in our times.","dt":"2024-08-22T08:14:40","s":["9cvayvo6jc"]}],"33":[{"m":"ABOMINATION","dt":"2022-06-23T11:33:34","s":["t7h73c1uds"]},{"m":"That is exactly what he had done: created a god of his own imaginations and heart.","dt":"2026-06-26T21:22:49","s":["0b38ddf2fe","rkej40nm1e"]}],"14":[{"m":"He lacked understanding and discernment, but not good counsel.\n\nHe got good counsel from the old men, but because he lacked discernment he chose the counsel of the young men rather.\n\nEven if he lacked understanding, which he did, else he would have heeded the old men, but had discernment, which he did not,\n\nHe would have used his discernment to heed the old men, though he might not agree nor understand why they counseled thus.\n\nHe did not know that his kingdom was a shaky one and he needed others to make the kingdom stand.\n\nHe likely thought to supersede the achievements of his father and make a name also for himself.\n\nHe thought his father's kingdom was rock solid and established.\n\nUnlike David his father, who left a good inheritance and preparation and a good transition for his son Solomon,\n\nSolomon could or did not do the same for his son, so right from the beginning of his reign,\n\nRehoboam lost 90 percent of the kingdom.\n\nThe other one percent was even because of David.","dt":"2024-08-21T22:43:52","s":["kag06d75l5"]}],"28":[{"m":"Ah, 🤬 these golden calves have appeared here also.\n\nAfter all these centuries, after the precedence set by Aaron,\n\nThat same image rears its head up again.\n\nThe error once made could not be undone,\n\nSomewhere in the psyche of the people the golden calf stayed.\n\nNow to counter it, the Lord destroyed the image and the people involved and made them drink of it.\n\nSo that whenever the image of the calf appears, the due punishment of God also comes alongside.","dt":"2024-08-23T06:34:02","s":["sl1uvc9k6b"]}]},"13":{"6":[{"m":"Two things... After this, did he repent? 2. How come God chose him? Did he not know that Jeroboam will start a train of idolatry which will transcend several generations?\n\nJust see the lives lost and damage done because God ordained the wrong person.\n\nOr did he? It comes down to the will of man 👨. Which makes us independent of mind.","dt":"2022-06-23T11:37:24","s":["ak77oypfih"]},{"m":"The Lord thy God???\n\nSo the Lord who had made him king 👑 was no longer the Lord his God?\n\nHe had another god found by his own heart and devices.\n\nHe was now very powerful and was not just a god to himself, but he created his own gods and that of his people.","dt":"2024-08-23T06:41:52","s":["6zbovz6dz7"]}],"18":[{"m":"Why did he lie 🤥 to this man of God?\n\nMaybe because the Lord had left use of him because of his moral failures — who knows.\n\nAnd now maybe he sought to acquaint himself with the one whom God has chosen to use.\n\nCome to think of it, why would God send a prophet all the way from Judah if there was one worthy already in Israel 🇮🇱?\n\nIt goes to show that we must keep ourselves sanctified always for the Lord's use.\n\nThis dubious character of the prophet may explain why the Lord would not use him.\n\nAlso, why did the Lord not forgive this MOG, since he was deceived?\n\nBecause the Lord had given him sufficient warning for him to have overcome this lie 🤥 of the old prophet.\n\nIn fact, this was the very warning ⚠ the Lord had given him, and he had fallen prey to it.\nHe let his own desire for food, shelter and respect for man cost him his life and that of his ministry.\n\nLord, have mercy upon me I pray; let not my respect for man and authority cost me my calling and destiny, for I must have respect for you and your words first, Lord.\n\nHave mercy and help me, Lord 🙏","dt":"2024-08-23T06:51:42","s":["x4mz3ja63h"]},{"m":"Was it that the lie coming from an old man made it all the more believable?","dt":"2026-06-26T21:35:01","s":["4215145dbc"]}],"23":[{"m":"So much to say in this passage about the young man 👨.\n\nH... Okay, let's start from — when the Spirit of the Lord came upon the prophet, did it like possess him such that he could not refrain but prophesy?\n\nI believe the unction on the prophet is so strong it's virtually impossible to refrain, as we see in Jeremiah, who described it as burning 🔥 fire 🔥 shut up in his bones.\n\n2ndly, why did God not use the old prophet? Thirdly... I want to see the face 😔 and demeanor of the old prophet now that he had messed things up and he himself was used of God to expose his own lies 🤥.\n\nNow he had caused the death of the young prophet.\n\nTo compensate, he buried him in his own tomb.","dt":"2022-06-23T18:28:06","s":["0ab2d7w0k3"]}],"24":[{"m":"Why did he go back after the word of the Lord had come as to what would happen to him?\n\nMaybe they pleaded with the Lord for forgiveness and handed it all to the Lord to show mercy?\n\nAfter all, he couldn't stay with the old prophet forever.","dt":"2024-08-23T06:46:30","s":["j21tuhr0nb"]}],"33":[{"m":"How come he was unrepentant after such display of God's power?\n\nSad, but such is the nature of man.","dt":"2024-08-24T07:18:30","s":["a24ilozay9"]}],"34":[{"m":"God is no respecter of persons.\n\nJeroboam had such prospects and he messed it up, and his house 🏡 was to be exterminated, i.e. his generations cut off.","dt":"2022-06-23T18:29:19","s":["xnhs1tnjzl"]}],"28":[{"m":"Was this an instruction from the Lord to the old prophet? If not, how did he know that the lion would not devour him also, or he get trampled down by the donkey?\n\nOr could it be that by prophetic insight he knew this was the divine at work, and knew what he could and could not do?\n\nThis particular chapter begs many questions:\n\n1. The young prophet was penalised for disobeying God directly\n\n2. But the old prophet was spared any punishment\n\n3. He got the young man killed to fuel his own interests and curiosity, or maybe he knew he was no longer relevant to God and so wanted to connect by association with the Lord and whom the Lord was currently using\n\n4. This should be wisdom for us young ministers — the old are not necessarily wise or kind or in legacy mode — some are crafty and subtle and are in a take-at-all-cost mode","dt":"2026-06-29T09:06:48","s":["6bd14647f7"]}]},"14":{"2":[{"m":"Why was Ahijah the prophet not sent to Jeroboam to warn him of his evil ways, but rather a young prophet was sent? Just wondering out loud.","dt":"2026-06-30T07:43:45","s":["rp8kg63vg5"]}],"13":[{"m":"As young 🧒 as the child was, God saw the good in him and brought him to death and burial.\n\nHe was to be the only one of the house of Jeroboam to be buried ⚰ peacefully.\n\nGod knows all things.","dt":"2022-06-23T18:36:18","s":["fcouagkwi8"]},{"m":"Wow, so his death was actually a reward from God, because God had found good in him and wanted to spare him from cruel and shameful death.","dt":"2024-08-24T07:25:26","s":["iwv6ltnh8q"]},{"m":"How old was this child? I believe he must have been very young, and so what had he accomplished for the Lord to say that he has found some good thing in him?\n\nHe had not taken the throne nor done some public good; he was but a lad, yet the Lord spoke this way concerning him.\n\nCould it be that the Lord has seen his heart and knew he was a good person, and God, who knows the heart, decided to reward him with honour and respect in letting him die without violence?\n\nI am thinking that just like Jonathan, who was never king yet demonstrated a faith and love in God that his father never had, this young lad might have shown the same, or like David, a man after God's own heart, or like Joseph with his coat of many colours.","dt":"2026-06-30T07:52:29","s":["yy34cmoh3b"]}],"24":[{"m":"There is nothing new under the sun; sodomites have always been around from time immemorial.","dt":"2024-08-24T07:28:00","s":["zp53heiy9q"]},{"m":"Why were the sodomites in particular mentioned — \"there were also sodomites\" — almost making it a stand-alone sin? It was among the abominations the Lord detested.","dt":"2026-06-30T08:01:20","s":["f0tkk6lafn"]}],"26":[{"m":"After all the honor God had given this place, I found it interesting that he allowed the place to be raided and such precious riches taken away.\n\nWell, there was a time he even allowed the ark of testimony to be captured.\n\nHe created all things, so what really can captivate him?","dt":"2022-06-23T18:38:32","s":["v7evorz079"]}],"3":[{"m":"This was the simple gift to the prophet for such a powerful thing as healing a dying son of a king 👑.\n\nYet today, prophets want gifts commensurate with the miracle performed, based on a free gift from God.","dt":"2024-08-24T07:22:50","s":["xeor4q06bf"]}],"31":[{"m":"Abijam and Abijah.","dt":"2026-06-30T08:02:59","s":["pungxgn068"]},{"m":"Same name for both kings' sons — interesting for Israel and Judah to have the same names for their heirs apparent.","dt":"2026-06-30T09:06:50","s":["sxrg2ro15l"]}]},"15":{"7":[{"m":"Likely war over territory, which indeed was a common cause of war and still is.\n\nLikely each made incursions into the territory of the other, and for Jeroboam especially, most of his people were defecting to Israel, so he had reason to worry.","dt":"2024-08-27T07:57:15","s":["usq76dabrk"]}],"9":[{"m":"How come Abijam's reign was so short? Looks like about 2 to 3 years.\n\nFor it began in the 18th year of Jeroboam and ended in his 20th year.\n\nMeaning Rehoboam likely married early and gave birth early and lived long on the throne, so his son took over late in age, as we see in King Charles currently of England.\n\nOr he died in war, though that is not told.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:00:35","s":["4t1wrxumb9"]}],"10":[{"m":"The royal lineage went to the children of the daughter of Absalom. She married her cousin or step cousin for that matter.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:02:39","s":["v23hvok6s2"]}],"13":[{"m":"Wow, really, he did this.\n\nHis heart was really for the Lord and the things of God.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:07:51","s":["m6dy0wg0u5"]}],"21":[{"m":"This doesn't feel right.\n\nAsa's heart was right before the Lord, so the Lord was on his side.\n\nHe could and should have relied on God to defeat Baasha of Israel without such a compromise.\n\nI also noticed that life with God was so predictable:\n\nSo long as we are with the Lord, we prosper and make progress despite the hurdles of life.\n\nHowever, the moment we are deceived into thinking we have attained unto greatness, so we are now stable and independent of God,\nthe moment we drink that Kool-Aid and are deceived, we start the journey of retrogression.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:14:38","s":["cqqsfta4wo"]}],"34":[{"m":"Jeroboam set a terribly bad precedence.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:17:36","s":["q49r6lludr"]}]},"16":{"2":[{"m":"I thought this guy came in through a coup — yet here we see that the Lord was behind it, and so the Lord expected better from him.\n\nBut he did same as his predecessors.\n\nMany times that is the error of man 👨: when we rise in power and strength 💪 we forget the Lord and often think it is by our own strength and doings, and gradually we spiral to our own undoing.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:38:13","s":["fz4bdozsnq"]}],"4":[{"m":"And yet in this curse, if any of the house of Baasha give himself over to the Lord, him the Lord will exempt from the plague and lift him high up.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:39:25","s":["5516uancre"]}],"7":[{"m":"I thought it was of the Lord's word that Jeroboam was killed, but now the Lord is punishing the killer as well.\n\nBecause the killer failed to align with the Lord. Baasha was already in God's bad books, and rightly so, so anything to get rid of him was used.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:47:26","s":["v7rjs6asyq"]}],"23":[{"m":"After 4 years of civil war, Omri prevailed and was made king 👑.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:54:21","s":["2wtxnwclgv"]}],"33":[{"m":"Progressive wickedness and rebellion against the Lord. Just when you thought it couldn't get any worse, somebody comes who does worse.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:56:25","s":["j3fjradomb"]}],"34":[{"m":"There are mysteries in this life. But if we walk with God, he will guide us through it all.\n\nHow could Hiel have known what he was setting himself up for, except he was forewarned that there hangs a curse 🤬 on that city 🏙?\n\nA curse activated only when one begins to build. Hmm 🤔. That is a good preaching point.\n\nEverything seems calm, cool and collected until you begin to build Jericho up, and anon your sons begin to die.","dt":"2022-06-26T13:03:32","s":["q6afzk79ym"]}],"13":[{"m":"God never abandoned Israel or let it go to start afresh.\n\nRather he kept Israel as his own and punished anyone who came against his house.\n\nBecause he is a God of covenants.\n\nIt was the same with man 👨. He could have started afresh without Adam, but no, he kept his word to man and rather sought to redeem man.\n\nThis is one key attribute of God.\n\nHis unchangeableness.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:51:54","s":["v0qkxzkwg7"]}],"19":[{"m":"Zimri reigned for just 7 days, but already evil was in his heart.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:53:06","s":["2jnfolzkb5"]}]},"17":{"14":[{"m":"I wish I could see Elijah in person, his body mannerism and frame...\n\nIndeed the characters of the Bible — sad there are no pictures. It would have helped greatly.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:24:23","s":["shduyp365q"]}],"24":[{"m":"One sign, miracle or supernatural event is not enough to endorse one as a prophet or man of God; there must be consistency in the person's walk in the supernatural.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:35:51","s":["fj8sfjm7id"]}],"7":[{"m":"The natural and supernatural were converging at this point.\n\nThe drying up of the brook was a consequence of there being no rain ☔, and not even Elijah was exempted.\n\nOf course, in a sense the lack of rain was supernatural, as it came by the order of the Lord.\n\nThe ravens feeding Elijah was purely supernatural.\n\nI find it interesting as well that it is not recorded that Elijah prayed for there to be no rain ☔, but had to pray hard to reverse...","dt":"2024-08-29T08:41:44","s":["ciuzwsmfhl"]}],"16":[{"m":"The ways of the Lord are worth studying.\n\nHe could have just continued feeding Elijah by the brook, but here he answers the prayer of this poor widow and her son, thus killing two birds with one stone.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:27:17","s":["2g3xrv1cq2"]},{"m":"It was no luxury meal but sufficient to keep them alive for years — similar to the manna.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:28:12","s":["n8121neqb"]}]},"18":{"6":[{"m":"How come such a righteous man worked for such a wicked king 👑?\n\nIt tells you the nature of the kingdoms of righteousness — we must be everywhere to exert righteous influence in the dark places.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:52:38","s":["ryu6noczy4"]}],"13":[{"m":"To have done thus, he was a man of great substance.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:54:05","s":["ow98c40qb5"]}],"33":[{"m":"Err, before you engage in such a contest, you should know what you are doing.\n\nElijah took 12 stones, built the altar as ordained by God, and the sacrifice was at the time of the evening sacrifice.\n\nYou should have engaged with God at that level and seen results before.\n\nDon't rush in blind faith and zeal lest you be shamed like the prophets of Baal.\n\nIt could actually cost you your life.","dt":"2022-06-28T07:51:47","s":["hiyl2w3cdb"]},{"m":"Ah... I thought there was famine?? 😳 This water 💦 was precious seed 🌱. It was such a great sacrifice.","dt":"2022-06-28T07:51:47","s":["fxv3b7zgvu"]}],"34":[{"m":"In times of such famine and scarcity of water 💦 — this was indeed a sacrifice.","dt":"2024-08-29T10:01:03","s":["lpj1by1cw8"]}],"42":[{"m":"How come he had to pray this into happening — how did he know this will take prayer to pull the rains into reality?\n\nHow did he know that to call down fire he would have to erect altars for the Lord? How did he know what to do when?\n\nWhat if the word of the Lord came to him again and again — instructing and teaching him time and again what to do?","dt":"2024-08-29T10:15:33","s":["kxw7x5o5ke"]}],"43":[{"m":"So Elijah goes up to Mount Carmel to pray, and then his servant had to locate himself strategically and go higher in order to see towards the sea 🌊. How long this took we are not told.\n\nBut that would be laborious and would take time. Seven times Elijah prayed 🙏.\n\nAnd he did till he got the reply. The path from “I hear the sound of abundance” to when the rains ☔ did come was a daunting and laborious work.\n\nThis is a good lesson on prayer.\n\nAlso, how did Elijah know all this? He wasn't doing trial and error. He knew how to engage with God till he got a reply.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:16:29","s":["uywq18xfuo"]}],"46":[{"m":"He ran down the mountainous ridges of Carmel without fall or injury all the way to the entrance of Jezreel.\n\nAbout 50km in all. Wow. He outdid the chariots 🛒 of Ahab.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:20:31","s":["dpv2uwngia"]}],"22":[{"m":"Which was not true, but the Lord did not interrupt him until he now wanted to give up because he thought 💭 he was alone.","dt":"2024-08-29T09:56:22","s":["7ajoyfj4jz"]}],"28":[{"m":"Elijah was so confident that God would answer.\n\nDo we have such men in our times — who know for sure that God will answer?","dt":"2024-08-29T09:58:27","s":["mz9901seqq"]}],"37":[{"m":"All of this was of the Lord's own instructions and evolution, not Elijah's.\n\nThis goes to show that when God gives an instruction, he goes ahead to back it.\n\nAnyone on course in the work of the Lord is divinely backed and must be respected as such.\n\nHe is not acting on his own but on orders. And any obedient servant has the backing of his lord and master.","dt":"2024-08-29T10:05:09","s":["u91czbl4u3"]}],"39":[{"m":"So before, they thought Baalim was God, not some demon spirit lying 🤥 to them and manipulating them.\n\nThey didn't even know they were deceived.\n\nBut with fire 🔥 from heaven it became obvious that the LORD is not one of the divine beings, but he is the real deal —\n\nHe is the God that all know, the creator and ruler of the universe — God is indeed the Lord and the Lord is God.","dt":"2024-08-29T10:10:19","s":["xrhoxbqxqi"]}],"41":[{"m":"There is a sound of abundance, and you would think this was a done 🤝 deal 🤝.\n\nYet it was only a sound 🔊. Elijah was now yet to climb to Mount 🗻 Carmel and pray for hours, seven times.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:09:45","s":["wg7njj5tlr"]}],"44":[{"m":"How did Elijah know that this cloud 🌥, however little, was an indication of a done deal 🤝, and yet the sound of rain ☔ was just the beginning of prayer and spiritual engagement?\n\nOh Lord, how do we know such things? Teach me, Lord, teach me.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:18:43","s":["k7h65di6zi"]}]},"19":{"4":[{"m":"Ah, the way we saw Elijah as a super man 👨. So in all these there were uncertainties, fears, doubts and tiredness.\n\nAt this time Elijah was battle weary 😩. He was a man like us.\n\nUnbelievable?\n\nAfter such victory ✌️, wow, and seeing such demonstrations of power, one would expect great faith and boldness, but rather Elijah ran.\n\nHe fled and asked to be killed. This marked the beginning of the end for him and he transited to heaven.\n\nIn this life we must be strong 💪... Really strong.\n\nThis life is not for sissies and cry babies 🤱. GOD HELP 😣","dt":"2022-06-28T08:26:00","s":["p23s15hrlh"]}],"8":[{"m":"Forty days and nights 🌃. Oh mine, strange men 🚹 have walked 🚶 the earth 🌎. Strange men 🚹","dt":"2022-06-28T08:29:36","s":["xy92bbj7jn"]}],"11":[{"m":"Here Elijah sought the Lord; he waited for him.\n\nSo this begs the question 🙋: where was the Lord all this while?\n\nWhen the angel 😇 came, that was not the Lord; the voice asking him what he was doing here, was that not the Lord?\n\nI believe the waiting on the Lord here was to show him and empower him for what was next.\n\nAngels giving him food and him being questioned did meet the need and requirements for the next level.\n\nThese events were gradual steps to the next level.\n\nThis should teach us not to run ahead of God in waiting for him.\n\nSo help me God 😣","dt":"2022-06-28T08:33:30","s":["ng1wnvu77w"]}],"15":[{"m":"Here God finally instructs Elijah on what the next move was.\n\nHmm 🤔, come to think of it, I don't think we can really fault Elijah nor conclude that his exasperation 🤦‍♂️ led God to take him out of the scene.\n\nIt looks more like God just continued and revealed the next move to Elijah, rather than God taking him out because he was no longer fit for the job or because he complained.\n\nThis very verse begs a lot of meditation.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:38:39","s":["s3dsp5o3mk"]}],"18":[{"m":"Only 7000 people left who were not idolatrous. Oh, how low Israel 🇮🇱 had sunk because of wicked leadership.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:39:15","s":["8mbhijws3c"]}],"10":[{"m":"I suspect maybe God was silent 😶 during these moments and grave danger of death ☠.\n\nWhen Jezebel threatened, likely God was silent 😶, as he sometimes does.\n\nELIJAH felt the weight 🏋️ of being the only person in an entire territory. He felt alone, and he was wrong, but it is understandable, his frustration.","dt":"2022-06-28T08:28:44","s":["mbydbwgu0i"]}],"12":[{"m":"Was this not the same voice of the Lord God walking in the Garden in the cool of the day that Adam heard?","dt":"2022-06-28T08:34:38","s":["4g7dorwbi9"]}]},"20":{"9":[{"m":"2. When you tolerate one thing, the enemy is not content with it... He will come more and more.\n\nThere should come a point when you will say enough is enough... When are you going to get to that point?\n\nWhen irreparable damage has been done, when you've lost it all, when you've made all the mistakes —\n\nWhen are you going to take your Christian life seriously?","dt":"2024-09-02T23:54:08","s":["gv069xxjp8"]}],"11":[{"m":"To wit, the one who takes it off has already ended the battle, so can afford to boast, but the one who is yet to fight, who can tell how the battle will end?","dt":"2024-09-02T08:00:00","s":["fvk7j3fype"]}],"13":[{"m":"How come the Lord came in such a great way for the worst of Israel's kings up to that time?\n\nI believe it was because Ahab took a strong stand against the enemies of God.\n\nThough godless, Ahab chose to fight the Lord's battle, and that aligned with God, and for that, the Lord came through for Ahab.\n\nSomething even those whose heart was upright towards God sometimes failed to do, as we see in Asa and others.\n\nAnd quite understandable, because going to war is a risk to your own life so you can protect others.\n\nThat is why most avoid it.\n\nSo which is better: moral decadence, yet you fight the Lord's battle, or upright, yet fail in warring for the Lord?\n\nIt's best to be upright and war as David did.\n\nBut if a choice must be made, be upright in heart, though that alone will deny you of the Lord's best, and we know the upright love the Lord's best, and most upright in heart also go to war for him.","dt":"2024-09-02T07:57:41","s":["odjq5o38ct"]}],"15":[{"m":"Wow, such a small number. Ahab was wise to have asked by what battle strategy the battle would be won, and he got it.\n\nThis goes to show it is important not to rush off into battle without seeking the strategy of the Lord.","dt":"2024-09-02T08:02:20","s":["j29q94b8s1"]}],"22":[{"m":"He was asked to go prepare this time round; that was the wisdom and strategy of the divine.\n\nIn the first, he was supernaturally helped directly in the war.\n\nIn the second, he was supernaturally counseled, so he prepared.\n\nThus it is imperative to know what the Lord is doing now and follow it step by step.\n\nWe must keep in step with the Lord each and every day.\n\nHaving heeded this advice, the Lord gave them victory supernaturally once again even in the day of battle.","dt":"2024-09-02T08:16:58","s":["eoc6nne4nc"]}],"24":[{"m":"The kings were drunk, so this time warriors and captains were to be in their place.\n\nThey were too overconfident in the first war; no wonder they lost.","dt":"2024-09-02T08:18:13","s":["6n1izumz75"]}],"43":[{"m":"Why is God dealing with Ahab in the first place? He, full of idolatry, has received great favour of the Lord and supernatural victory ✌️.\n\nI think there are several phases to God. He will cause the righteous that strays to lose a war to the end that he might draw him back to himself.\n\nYet he might cause the wicked to triumph in battle that he might know the power of the Lord; peradventure he might repent.\n\nGod indeed is a God of the hills and the valleys. The high points in one's life and the lows.\n\nAnd of course sometimes he does good in keeping with some age-old covenant of the fathers. And in doing evil 😈 to a wicked seed, again in keeping covenant to punish and blot out the name of the wicked.","dt":"2022-06-29T06:47:46","s":["qlctdendff"]}]},"21":{"4":[{"m":"It seems that when Ahab is displeased, it is visibly seen.\n\nAs was the case when the Lord told him by the prophet that he would die for letting Benhadad go.","dt":"2024-09-02T08:25:22","s":["b195rst40i"]},{"m":"Ahab, though evil, had a conscience. It did not even strike him that he could take it by force.\n\nHe knew the laws of ownership in Israel; he could not have it. This was the inheritance of the fathers.\n\nBut he had married a foreign woman who did not have regard for such laws; they were nonsense to her.\n\nIt was because of all such differences that the Lord asked them not to intermarry these foreign women.","dt":"2024-09-04T06:40:52","s":["qglu0r0o3f"]}],"17":[{"m":"At this time many prophets had spoken to Ahab under different conditions.\n\nWhen does God send which prophet? What is the criteria for selecting who goes to deliver a message?","dt":"2022-06-29T06:54:08","s":["y9ncufgj63"]}],"24":[{"m":"God was going to destroy both them and their posterity, just as they had destroyed that of Naboth.\n\nThe evil they had done was going to be recompensed them in due measure, including their family.","dt":"2024-09-04T06:44:27","s":["9ek03lmnrg"]}],"29":[{"m":"Just like that...?? 😳 Ahab is forgiven in the sense that his punishment is deferred.\n\nIn that light I believe this punishment 👊 could have been deferred perpetually if each son of Ahab feared God and set up his own covenant of surrender to God.\n\nThey need not be perfect 👌, no, they just need to be yielded and broken 💔 before God.\n\nSee, Ahab in all his unparalleled wickedness obtained mercy.\n\nNow in this dispensation, especially of the New Testament, what is the nature of our relationship with God?\n\nWhat manner of persons ought we be?","dt":"2022-06-29T06:58:50","s":["d4ilvbo6mi"]}],"27":[{"m":"There are people like Ahab; they know the Lord exists, but they do not hold him or his laws in their thoughts, though they fear him and honour the words of men of God.\n\nBut they love their selfish way too much to give themselves over to God.\n\nYet at his rebuke they turn in repentance. On and off, they are like the flick of a light switch.","dt":"2024-09-04T06:46:55","s":["mid3jl0ya2"]}]},"22":{"6":[{"m":"This continues to happen even now,\n\nwhere rich and powerful people gather to themselves prophets to pray for them and tell them goodly things.","dt":"2024-09-04T06:51:20","s":["zrd1b80aiw"]}],"8":[{"m":"How come Jehoshaphat was friends with Ahab? The animosity between Israel and Judah seems to have been resolved.","dt":"2024-09-04T06:56:26","s":["ay8inj6hu7"]}],"15":[{"m":"I suspect he said this with a very sarcastic tone. Because right after, Ahab insisted he be serious and tell him what is genuinely on his heart.","dt":"2024-09-04T06:59:35","s":["0ckd83cwxz"]}],"18":[{"m":"I wonder, if every word of Micaiah was evil and it all happened exactly and immediately he speaks,\n\nI am sure Ahab would have taken him seriously every time.\n\nBut I suspect many times the Lord sends him with words for Ahab to repent lest he be destroyed, yet Ahab continued to reign on as king.\n\nThe words of Micaiah seem like just rubbish talk. I am sure Micaiah himself at times wondered when the wicked ways of Ahab will be brought to an end and when all that the Lord had spoken concerning Ahab will be fulfilled.\n\nBut the long-suffering of the Lord prevented Ahab until due time.\n\nThis is a lesson in prophecy for us, that until God gives a specific time line, we should not be presumptuous.\n\nAlso God may speak something today but it will be manifest in 20 years' time, not in the period we heard the word, except God gives the time line.","dt":"2024-09-04T07:07:07","s":["rqj1zp7aix"]}],"31":[{"m":"What was there about the Syrians and the number 32?","dt":"2024-09-04T07:10:06","s":["fqcjq7c16a"]}],"34":[{"m":"At a venture indeed. It was pronounced that he needs die in the battle, and I can imagine the spirits whispering to the soldier: draw and hit this man (Ahab). He is a perfect target 🎯, you can't miss.\n\nIt seemed random, but the spirits were behind it.\n\nHow many such spirits were in this battle, and have been in battles, to do good and evil?","dt":"2022-07-02T00:09:33","s":["c17oksgrbt"]}]}},"Ecclesiastes":{"1":{"18":[{"m":"Oh true, how I've experienced this... In much knowledge is sorrow.","dt":"2024-08-15T07:28:11","s":["g2uz72fyz1"]}]},"2":{"10":[{"m":"So in as much as all was vanity, the reward for all one's labour is the rejoicing of the heart, that sense of fulfillment and accomplishment.","dt":"2026-06-19T05:47:44","s":["6bc54d470c"]}],"16":[{"m":"In this he was wrong; he was and continues to be remembered.\n\nYes, it's true not all men are remembered, but some are. Most are not.","dt":"2024-08-15T07:36:12","s":["i6eo9z101m"]},{"m":"Not true, we remember him, Solomon, even till today; in this wise he was wrong. A good name is better than riches, as he himself said. And in that wise he was right.\nOh, the wisdom of God. I can imagine Solomon looking at the world from eternity and marvelling at the wisdom of God to preserve the posterity of those he loved.\n\nAll indeed is not vanity.","dt":"2026-06-19T05:50:42","s":["f830797723","p2hppovs43"]}],"26":[{"m":"May God give to the righteous peace and joy to enjoy the works of his hands.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:20:16","s":["oud5l4b16w"]}],"9":[{"m":"So his wisdom remained with him.\n\nMeaning we can build and do great things but not have the wisdom and presence of mind to understand our ways and what we are doing.","dt":"2024-08-15T07:31:47","s":["qzgzfvrcr5"]}],"21":[{"m":"True, and a great evil indeed.","dt":"2026-06-19T05:55:43","s":["c91c4c8c22"]}]},"3":{"22":[{"m":"True, all go to the dust, and that is the wisdom of Solomon.\n\nI understand his desperation, I get his frustration 😤. Our lives on this earth 🌎 are but vanity.\n\nHowever, after Solomon came a greater than Solomon, who taught us wisdom, and showed us where men go after death ☠, and even gave us of the Spirit of the Ancient One forever.\n\nOh, what blessed hope.","dt":"2022-06-19T16:43:54","s":["rihyg2crvc"]},{"m":"Since we cannot tell for certain who will take over what we have laboured to gain, whether he will be wise or foolish,\n\nit is better to rejoice in our works as well, for that is our portion and that which has been given to us.\n\nWhat will be after we are gone is not in our power to determine.\n\nIt has just not been given to us.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:26:05","s":["rhnheiptmy"]}]},"4":{"8":[{"m":"Maybe it is that thing in man 👨, to want or do something and achieve, that drives him on.","dt":"2022-06-19T16:48:56","s":["svc54de7g9"]},{"m":"Oh yes, indeed it is a sore travail, and indeed a vexation of spirit.\n\nA man who has no family or relation, yet labours on without satisfaction, would not even so much as pause to reflect or even enjoy a bit of his labour and riches.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:28:49","s":["81by5xptdu"]}]},"5":{"4":[{"m":"Then there are many fools in the church today.\n\nBut then again, the argument can be raised: is the church today really a gathering of called-out ones, or is it just a gathering?\n\nIf it is not for called-out ones, as was the original plan, then the application of the above scripture and others cannot be applied hook, line and sinker.\n\nBut then again, though the church and house of God may be corrupted by wrong entrants, it does not cease to be of God nor cease to be recognised in his presence.\n\nSo we must be wise in our dealings and seek God's face for ourselves as to what to do with his church and what grounds of alignment he has for us.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:36:41","s":["ga8tfhw6ms"]}],"7":[{"m":"Hmm, in all dreams and states God remains constant, so we ought to fear him.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:37:43","s":["1z1bipbi46"]}],"10":[{"m":"Indeed this is vanity... That that which you love does not fulfill you. Indeed, that is vanity.\n\nIn other words, in as much as we all love money and wealth, it does not bring fulfillment.\n\nYou will always desire more and not be filled.","dt":"2022-06-19T16:59:10","s":["dvc0060prz"]}],"11":[{"m":"Indeed, so this also is vanity; it is best to serve the Lord and do only what he has ordained rather than seek to please men.\n\nNothing will satisfy man.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:39:40","s":["3r9xmmevxc"]}],"16":[{"m":"Interesting way Solomon puts it: in all points that we came, so shall we go.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:42:55","s":["q1fim56z0q"]}],"20":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-06-19T17:00:47","s":["0039bd4d15"]}]},"6":{"6":[{"m":"It is an evil 😈, therefore, to live long and yet not see good days.\n\nIt indeed is not worth it.","dt":"2022-06-19T17:02:12","s":["3wmisfydgl"]}],"9":[{"m":"NLT says it is better to enjoy what you have before you than to chase and desire vanities and what you do not have.","dt":"2024-08-16T06:46:14","s":["2tlm4ijpxr"]}],"12":[{"m":"The Lord can, the Lord Jesus can tell a man what will happen after his life.","dt":"2022-06-19T17:03:24","s":["ajt1ab6eqd"]}]},"7":{"11":[{"m":"It reminds me of another scripture that says the wisdom of the poor man is despised.","dt":"2022-06-20T08:40:31","s":["lln9wppt6j"]}],"12":[{"m":"Hm, so this is how that expression begins, the expression of wisdom and money being both defences.\n\nIt begins by suggesting that wisdom with inheritance is a good thing.\n\nTo be wise and broke and oppressed is not good; it drives the wise mad and makes the wisdom of his ways doubtful or rubbished.\n\nHe can easily be used and dumped.\n\nIn this wise, wisdom with money is a double-edged sword.","dt":"2024-08-16T07:01:48","s":["u9wnvhlq1i"]}],"28":[{"m":"This proverb is so relevant for life.\n\nNo one is good in absolute terms; we are all foiled one way or another.\n\nWalk with this wisdom and you shall escape many traps of men 🚹 and women 🚺.","dt":"2022-06-20T08:48:37","s":["m9dsuycdol"]},{"m":"It is generally true that good men are few, but here Solomon is suggesting that good women are even fewer.","dt":"2024-08-16T07:04:38","s":["tn1wvj776f"]}]},"10":{"2":[{"m":"It is another way of saying a wise man keeps his heart very diligently, because that is the source of your life.\n\nIt indeed must be guarded with your strength, but the fool holds such a vital organ, an organ for life and emotional health and wisdom etc., with his left hand, with nonchalance and carelessness.","dt":"2024-08-19T06:31:39","s":["ug2a9pd1h7"]}],"3":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. True. Sometimes from my rooftop I see people walk by and past.\n\nAnd you can just almost tell from their posture and predispositions how naive or wise they are, innocent and foolish, how experienced or young 🧒.\n\nSometimes you can even tell the good from the evil 😈.","dt":"2022-06-20T09:15:25","s":["0q50rw68v3"]},{"m":"Just by his walking you know a fool is passing by. There is something about one's demeanor that reeks of his wisdom or folly.","dt":"2024-08-19T06:34:25","s":["p7ra2gxpv8"]}],"4":[{"m":"This wisdom worked for me recently in church and is still working for me, as I did my possible best to remain calm in the midst of false and wrong perceptions.","dt":"2024-08-19T06:36:34","s":["e6gnvvze8v"]}],"11":[{"m":"A babbler will bite with his tongue 😝 if he is not kept at bay.","dt":"2022-06-20T09:20:07","s":["6dehpi3uw4"]},{"m":"If you do not nip in the bud a babbler, he would destroy with his mouth.","dt":"2024-08-19T06:48:08","s":["uwypmew3oa"]}],"17":[{"m":"One of the scriptures I like; such aptness in wisdom.","dt":"2024-08-19T06:51:39","s":["lvjme19xxe"]}],"20":[{"m":"Here King 👑 Solomon reveals a secret of the rich, wealthy and powerful; he reveals it and yet still hides it in a proverb.\n\nThe power players of our time have spies and loyalists. Some known and some unknown.\n\nYou speak against them and a bird 🐦 😊... A herald will inform him.","dt":"2022-06-20T09:24:45","s":["6m76hqhjr8"]},{"m":"I'm sure Solomon as king had access to all manner of information and intel.\n\nAnd he himself was at times shocked as to how the information came about.\n\nMaybe someone was passing by a window and overheard someone probably talking to himself and musing over some sensitive information of the kingdom, and lo, the king gets to know.\n\nNow he knows the heart of his people, or this person in his kingdom, but will still relate to him well, and such an one knows not what the king knows.\n\nA knowledge which will be used against him by the king in due time.","dt":"2024-08-19T06:56:49","s":["lyw1q35ds5"]}]},"11":{"5":[{"m":"I know as Christians we pride ourselves in hearing from God and receiving the Spirit's promptings, but still we are men and not God.\n\nFlesh and not spirits, so we are greatly limited.\n\nLet's not be presumptuous; let's follow natural laws and observations and seek wisdom, and God will show us favour and cause our works to be blessed.","dt":"2024-08-19T07:33:08","s":["xzi15apc5u"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh yes, they indeed are, and that is the season we make some of our gravest mistakes.","dt":"2024-08-19T07:34:14","s":["1yyop29pvv"]}]},"12":{"13":[{"m":"Amen and amen, a worthy conclusion indeed!","dt":"2024-08-19T07:37:15","s":["5d8eo13oab"]}]}},"2 Chronicles":{"2":{"14":[{"m":"The league between the two nations even led to intermarriages.\n\nIt is very possible Solomon might have even had a wife from there.","dt":"2024-08-02T00:40:49","s":["po25zsaeq5"]}]},"5":{"10":[{"m":"So where was the rod of Aaron that budded? How about the manna?\n\nHad these been lost in the capture of the ark??","dt":"2024-08-03T10:24:31","s":["ky0zppvqeu"]},{"m":"What happened to the rest of the tabernacle items in the tabernacle of Moses — did they keep them in the storehouses, or they allowed them to be mixed up with the current things?\n\nHow about the tabernacle itself — the tent and its materials of badgers' skin and fine linen etc. — where was it kept?","dt":"2026-06-13T09:35:13","s":["26ffdfdde9","krm63i6y7b"]}],"14":[{"m":"And so they were in the cloud of the Lord, caught up in glory and within glory.\n\nOh, what a moment, what a moment to be part of and to witness.","dt":"2024-08-03T10:26:28","s":["e4s9pwwhhm"]}]},"7":{"14":[{"m":"Oh OK... So this is the context within which this all-popular verse was said...\n\nNow I get it better.","dt":"2024-08-08T07:50:52","s":["4ad60mew8p"]}],"15":[{"m":"So what does God mean by his ears will be attentive to the place...\n\nWe know he sees & hears everything... I believe it means literal answers to prayers will be heard from that place.\n\nIt's just like we know God hears everything, and yet he does not answer every prayer, even the ones promised in his word.\n\nNot because he can't answer them, but there is a missing ingredient. Just like in the dedication of the temple, the missing ingredient is consecration.\n\nPrayers must be MADE for answers to be given. I say this above within a context.\n\nOf course 🏇 many times we cry on the Lord and he answers us; many times also we seem to have hit a stone wall.\n\nThis calls for prayer, fastings, consecrations etc.","dt":"2022-06-13T15:08:14","s":["dx4fsu9tjc"]}],"16":[{"m":"Okay, so this confirms verse 15, that his eyes and heart shall be inclined to that place forever.\n\nThough he is everywhere, he will be attentive in particular to this place, because that place is sanctified.","dt":"2022-06-13T15:21:19","s":["ms8qtxv66l"]}],"20":[{"m":"When men are serious and hallow the things of God, God also takes those things seriously and hallows them. But God is God and the creator of all things.\n\nHe is not unduly attached to things; when things fail after his constant warnings, he lets it go.\n\nThis great temple became same.\n\nEven his ark of covenant was one time taken away by the enemies.","dt":"2026-06-14T06:43:03","s":["fb4aafbc1d"]}],"22":[{"m":"After all such warning ⚠, Solomon still forsook the Lord.\n\nWhy would anyone do such a thing to their own hurt?\n\nBecause the heart of man can so easily lie 🤥 to the man himself and is so prone to self-deception.\n\nLord, have mercy on us all and help us.","dt":"2024-08-08T07:57:14","s":["4jaw25bxs3"]}],"7":[{"m":"He hallowed the middle court... Like David, Solomon was a king priest... Leading the people to offer sacrifices to the Lord and setting up altars to house the Lord.","dt":"2024-08-06T18:39:02","s":["eixgcgzhx5"]}],"13":[{"m":"It is interesting that the Lord repeated the very words of Solomon back to him and accepted it. Solomon was in sync with the word and will of God, so God aligns with him because he aligned with God.","dt":"2026-06-14T06:45:14","s":["c96c86f347"]}]},"8":{"10":[{"m":"Solomon gave his people freedom and made them great leaders.\n\nUnlike some very prosperous nations in this world who enslave both their own people and foreigners.","dt":"2024-08-10T22:00:24","s":["ym9y0z7i8g"]}],"11":[{"m":"Good decision, though she had been staying in the holy cities for years.\n\nHe was not to have married her in the first place.","dt":"2024-08-10T22:05:06","s":["fz3fjyeboi"]}],"16":[{"m":"He had the full budget e'rr before the foundation.\n\nSolomon was indeed a very blessed man 👨.","dt":"2024-08-10T22:08:13","s":["0ttwgwojpb"]}],"3":[{"m":"He went, as in, his army did. I doubt Solomon was a skilled warrior like his father David.\n\nHe was very wise, however.","dt":"2024-08-10T21:56:52","s":["pot7uu50uj"]}]},"9":{"14":[{"m":"The Arabs submitted to Solomon.","dt":"2024-08-21T06:47:45","s":["nlcerr5sky"]}],"22":[{"m":"What a combo to have, riches and wisdom.\n\nTo be number 1 in both is something else.","dt":"2024-08-21T06:50:01","s":["f7vy7wejzb"]}]},"10":{"19":[{"m":"Unto the days of the writing of the text — i.e. before the captivities of the ten tribes, Dake's says.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:21:50","s":["gydiv10px9"]}],"10":[{"m":"How come all the young men gave the same counsel — what was it that the old men saw, and yet not even one of the young men saw same to give a counter counsel?\n\nLord, give me the wisdom and perspective of the ancients. Amen.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:20:11","s":["ocga9wrdnh"]}]},"12":{"1":[{"m":"Leadership. The king 👑 errs, and all Israel 🇮🇱 with him.","dt":"2022-06-23T20:03:52","s":["hobm304mcb"]},{"m":"That is oftentimes the case: when men become strong and established, our vain and baser selves arise to our own hurt and detriment.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:49:00","s":["yhpxva30v1"]}],"8":[{"m":"Hmm, this lesson, for them to know how different serving the Lord and serving men is.\n\nHow that the burden of the Lord is so light and nothing compared with the treachery and wickedness of men.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:50:42","s":["vk5mir2agm"]}]},"13":{"6":[{"m":"They knew their history well and kept records, both oral and written records,\n\nwhich God in his providence has kept.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:19:31","s":["xt7r4w2l3s"]}],"9":[{"m":"So the priesthood, such a sacred trust, was acquired by bribery.\n\nYet the common people likely knew it not and sacrificed to these priests and thieves.\n\nBeing fooled by them the whole time.\n\nNot to mention the gods of Israel were no god at all.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:21:59","s":["eai6foszoz"]}],"13":[{"m":"Whiles delivering his lengthy speech, he did not know he was being ambushed, but God is faithful.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:24:08","s":["wodnao2tm4"]}],"21":[{"m":"☺ 😊... Is the might in the number of wives...?\n\nNo, I don't think so... But his family size in a way was a sign of strength 💪, though.\n\nThis kind of might in this area comes with many problems.","dt":"2022-06-26T12:24:51","s":["gaa3t0b45e"]},{"m":"Mighty because he had a huge family.\n\nSuch might is replicated in these days by growing an organisation.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:26:27","s":["ci173vmhu0"]}]},"14":{"14":[{"m":"Likely because they aided the Ethiopian and gave them passage through their lands.\n\nNone thought to inform Asa, at least, or resist them.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:30:26","s":["6nit1x9e28"]}]},"15":{"19":[{"m":"Wow, he was blessed.\n\nAnd also I noticed when God sends a prophet to warn and strengthen his servants or people, it was because in their prosperity and abundance\n\nthere was a real risk of deflecting from the Lord because of the blessings. That risk must be mitigated if we intend to make progress and sustain the blessings of the Lord.\n\nAnd many a time men failed despite having been warned.\n\nWe ought therefore to really be careful anytime such word comes.","dt":"2024-08-27T08:35:28","s":["fvomma2rw6"]}]},"17":{"4":[{"m":"David was the standard, just as Jeroboam was the standard for evil 😈.","dt":"2022-06-26T13:05:04","s":["rnhd9tctnc"]}],"19":[{"m":"A 1,160,000-strong army in the city.\n\nNo wonder he was feared greatly.","dt":"2024-08-28T08:35:34","s":["iaosdtyq2p"]},{"m":"As we saw in the preceding verse, the Philistines brought gifts of silver. I have no doubt there were a lot of foreign mercenaries who partnered with him as well.","dt":"2026-07-06T09:46:30","s":["u33tf1u6lz"]}],"11":[{"m":"Hm, just like his grandfather Solomon... Men brought him gifts because he was greatly helped of the Lord.","dt":"2024-08-28T08:31:46","s":["mmkv75171j"]}],"14":[{"m":"We see that with prosperity came proper structure, systems and order. We see numbering of the captains — we see structure and order.\n\nWisdom indeed starts from the fear of the Lord, and with it comes riches and order, and law and order, and knowledge of witty inventions.\n\nThe witty inventions of Jehoshaphat are mentioned later — it always follows the fear of God.","dt":"2026-07-06T09:44:47","s":["pnyi1eti68"]}]},"18":{"3":[{"m":"Maybe it was in keeping with the peace, and strengthening the alliance between these two nations that were once one people, that he chose to fight with Ahab in battle.\n\nHe was establishing a treaty for the future, maybe. For a people who fight in battle bond stronger, for they have risked their lives together.","dt":"2024-09-04T07:23:12","s":["qbrjlnude9"]}],"6":[{"m":"What prompted him to ask for a second opinion? I suspected there was something about all these prophets speaking one language. It smacked of sycophancy, I believe.","dt":"2026-07-06T10:07:59","s":["kh191n3xpa"]}],"7":[{"m":"This was in the times of Elijah; this goes to show that God uses many prophets at a particular time.\n\nSome more prominent than others.","dt":"2024-09-04T07:24:17","s":["xbkpwlvpan"]}],"12":[{"m":"It seemed the kings did not fully rely on the words of the prophets, else why would they seek a second opinion?\n\nIt also seems that the prophecies did not always happen as promised; that is why some prophets were more revered than others.\n\nThose whose words never failed were so revered, for God was with their mouth.","dt":"2024-09-04T07:27:26","s":["2jf98fheej"]}],"16":[{"m":"Was this also assigned to a spirit to do... Causing the people to suddenly become home 🏡 sick 🤮 and just abandon battle and go home...?\n\nEspecially considering the battle did not go so well.","dt":"2022-07-02T00:20:39","s":["ur8m0qe3hl"]}],"24":[{"m":"Was this prophecy from Micaiah to Ahab God's last act of mercy to him? If Ahab had somehow believed this prophecy, he would have lived on. All God required of Ahab was obedience, which he would not.\n\nGod is so merciful eh, so merciful.","dt":"2026-07-06T10:14:00","s":["jiakxnwfum"]}],"27":[{"m":"So what became of Micaiah after the death of Ahab? Did the realisation that he only prophesied truth to the king save him? Did it cause the people to repent and accept him as God's true prophet? Maybe, maybe not; we are not told.","dt":"2026-07-06T10:16:12","s":["gxpxkwm4hn"]}],"31":[{"m":"I suspected that the Lord was behind this, for the same account is in Kings, but it does not say it was the Lord that moved them to not pursue him.","dt":"2024-09-04T07:32:15","s":["w2y86mu9tb"]}],"34":[{"m":"He died slowly and painfully, affording him enough time to reflect on the word of the Lord that had warned him, and the words of Micaiah were unfolding right before his eyes.","dt":"2024-09-04T07:33:40","s":["sxjsa4xt9l"]}]},"19":{"4":[{"m":"This man 👨 loved the Lord, ensuring that his laws are taught through all Israel 🇮🇱.","dt":"2022-07-02T00:25:41","s":["38som51ycv"]}],"11":[{"m":"To do right always takes courage.","dt":"2022-07-02T00:27:10","s":["sqmvhfzhra"]},{"m":"Interesting, it was the clergy, them that feared the Lord, that were in power and governance, not some riffraff.\n\nBut then, alas, there was a point in history that the church was in governance, and we got infiltrated and ended up making a mess of things as if we were heathens.","dt":"2024-09-05T07:47:01","s":["4qs5xkk7lf"]}],"9":[{"m":"The priests were supposed to do righteousness and judge right.\nBoth priests and Levites.\n\nPastors, church leaders and lay ministers must do right by the LORD.","dt":"2024-09-05T07:43:17","s":["yqub5hy8ct"]}]},"20":{"15":[{"m":"I have often wondered, this coming of the Spirit of the Lord upon people who are not prophets and have not been tested in time past,\n\nhow are the people able to tell that it is truly of God?\n\nAlso, why did the king not just call one of the prophets who spoke to him in time past to just tell him the strategy to use, but congregate before the Lord?\n\nCould it be that they heard not the Lord through any of these means, and so had to all come and congregate before the Lord in humility?\n\nOnly he could help them.\n\nSo in time past men went over and beyond to hear the word of the Lord, because they knew that at the word of the Lord every knee and situation would bow.\n\nThis was and still is how powerful the word of the Lord is.\n\nSomething this powerful cannot be so commonplace; no wonder the word of the Lord did not come every day but on occasions as needed.\n\nIndeed, there are times it is so uncommon it becomes rare.\n\nYet,\nironically, in our days everyone seems to hear from God and has the word of God, and yet we are some of the most powerless generations in history.\n\nThere is something wrong with our hearing of the word from the Lord.","dt":"2024-09-05T07:56:18","s":["3sd9d7snoa"]}],"18":[{"m":"A man spoke, and the man was standing right before them, and yet they ignored the man and bowed down their heads to the ground and worshipped the Lord.\n\nCompletely disregarding the man.\n\nBecause the Lord will not give his glory to another, neither share it. The speaker was just a tool and a messenger.\n\nHowever, and ironically, man worship has become the order of the day in our churches because of the gift of God.\n\nWe as ministers of God are treading on dangerous grounds, for he shares not his glory with another.","dt":"2024-09-05T08:00:31","s":["g5tltskhqe"]}],"26":[{"m":"Walking with the Lord in faith is not easy, but it sure has great returns.\n\nIt pays really well. A worthwhile investment indeed.","dt":"2024-09-05T08:06:29","s":["kbla86vexy"]},{"m":"Berachah means blessing, and valley represents lowness, bottom, depression. David, for instance, talks of his valley of the shadow of death; it represents a place of many battles, bleeding and death.\n\nYet in such a place of violence and atrocities, there we find a blessing. Jehoshaphat finds a blessing because he waited on the LORD. He waited on the LORD.\n\nIn similar manner the psalmists tell of the valley of BACA, which means suffering and tears, yet the righteous, as they sojourn through there, they turn it into a pool and springs — a place of fullness and nourishment.\n\nPsalm 84:6 NKJV\nAs they pass through the Valley of Baca, They make it a spring; The rain also covers it with pools.","dt":"2026-07-08T10:10:41","s":["ltimlgd97a"]}],"34":[{"m":"Where are all these books?","dt":"2026-07-08T10:11:49","s":["9sl2jmfmxw"]}],"37":[{"m":"Jehoshaphat was in a very bad habit of joining himself with the enemies of the Lord, though he was a good man and he loved the Lord.","dt":"2024-09-05T08:08:13","s":["fnbmcrs6i4"]}],"5":[{"m":"War is interesting. You are you somewhere, as we say in Ghana; you have troubled no one, nor hurt them. But then they conspire quietly, put together an army greater than your strength, and come attack you and take everything you have got, including your very life if possible.\n\nWar indeed has a lot to teach us about life.","dt":"2026-07-07T09:28:45","s":["9bdsg3krid"]}]},"21":{"6":[{"m":"Like mother, like daughter...\n\nHow women are so powerful. Able to turn the hearts of even their husbands for or against God. Same did they unto Solomon.\n\nThis should be a lesson to all.","dt":"2022-07-02T00:37:51","s":["5bk82uzt8t"]},{"m":"Could this marriage not have come from the many alliances his father had with the evil kings of Israel?\n\nGod had warned him, and now his son the heir had fallen for one of the daughters of King Ahab on one of the trips.\n\nNow fast forward, she lured the righteous throne of Judah into depravity.\n\nEvil is so crafty and many times lures the righteous away rather than the reverse.\n\nHowever, righteousness is a much more powerful tool and has its own way of making impact and showing forth light.\n\nSomething the wicked lack.\n\nBut each force, be it good or evil, light or darkness, must be used in its own right.\n\nThe goal is for righteousness to be used right to overpower evil.","dt":"2024-09-05T08:11:29","s":["211q6hnapz"]},{"m":"Alliance which the Lord warned him about, sometimes with severe punishments and near-death experiences, yet it persisted even to the next generation. Sad.","dt":"2026-07-08T10:22:05","s":["kilj8j93bj"]}],"12":[{"m":"Elijah was a union national prophet — he prophesied the word of the Lord to both kings of the two kingdoms, Israel and Judah.","dt":"2026-07-08T10:40:47","s":["vm02hoj21u"]}],"18":[{"m":"Because righteous altars had been set up in time past by David, Asa and co., when Jehoram desecrated it, the Lord punished him severely.\n\nIronically, their brother nation Israel dealt more foolishly longer than Judah, yet their kings were not smitten this quick as in the case of Jehoram.\n\nThis goes to show that God protects and keeps his own more severely, as he also tries to bring those already in wicked systems to the saving knowledge of his truth.\n\nThis he does through a work-reward system: you work righteously, you get blessed by him, and punished when you wrought wickedly.\n\nHowever, for those who have given themselves over to him and have set up a righteous system, he deals with more vehemently and protects the sanctity till there is submission or utter rejection of God.","dt":"2024-09-05T08:51:48","s":["z37g6enost"]}],"20":[{"m":"A fool he was... In just eight years his folly was displayed.","dt":"2022-07-02T00:43:29","s":["ywflq52f84"]},{"m":"A fool and a reproach he had become, but how come nobody discerned such wickedness could come from him? Abubakar's issues come to mind.\n\nHe was made king after one of the most righteous, and yet none could tell of such folly. Lord, help us with wisdom to hand over and create systems that keep only the righteous in power.","dt":"2024-09-05T08:54:04","s":["xhljqeuhlv"]},{"m":"His reign, though very short, weakened the kingdom. He lived through the times of his father's reign when the Lord wrought mighty signs and wonders through his father, yet he had no regard for the ways and power of the Lord.","dt":"2026-07-08T10:26:14","s":["i0cxmbcc7p"]}]},"22":{"1":[{"m":"It is sad that this youngest son who survived also became evil and continued in the sins of his father, which got the rest of his brothers killed.\n\nHe did not learn from it. Yet just as out of the righteous grandfather Jehoshaphat could come such wicked seed,\n\nGod kept the promise to David because out of these wicked kings could come one as righteous as David.","dt":"2024-09-05T09:11:30","s":["do9qyyr8b1"]},{"m":"Why did the inhabitants of Israel not read in between the lines that his mother's wickedness will influence her son? Or because he was the last of the sons still alive and the dynasty had to continue, a thing more important to them than the unrighteous rule of this king... But I guess that is the way of kingdoms, and the many downsides of it kingdoms have to deal with.\n\nA wicked ruler, when it is his turn, gets to rule because of his royal blood, and same if they are lucky to get a good king.\n\nLord, in my nation Ghana, what times are we living in? A good king or an evil ruler?\n\nInterestingly, a good king can give birth to an evil ruler and vice versa.","dt":"2026-07-08T10:36:55","s":["wjoefbys2t"]}],"10":[{"m":"How can a mother be so wicked as to kill her own son's children so she reigns as queen and render the kingdom a queen regnant?","dt":"2024-09-05T09:04:40","s":["5e9bth94is"]}],"11":[{"m":"The power of righteous union: she was the wife of the priest, and righteousness was in her heart.\n\nShe saved her nephew alive, the son of her brother the king who had just died.","dt":"2024-09-05T09:03:17","s":["ijrabuoj42"]}]},"23":{"1":[{"m":"What exactly does that mean — he strengthened himself? It means he schemed, he planned, he strategised.\n\nThis was politics, a life-and-death matter, and he had to be very shrewd lest his head be on the line, so he had to form strategic alliances with the army commanders.\n\nHe was a priest, which in itself was authority and power, but that alone was not enough — he had to get firepower by his side, and firepower he did get.\n\nAthaliah had games of her own, and she was a heartless brute — she had no rules and had to be feared greatly. She feared neither God, less so man, so being priest alone was not enough.\n\nHe had the oil to genuinely anoint kings, but he needed the sword. Lord, give me wisdom to know the times I live in and to know what I ought to do.\n\nAll those who were part of the alliance at the peril of their lives were definitely going to benefit from their kingdom when their plans succeeded.","dt":"2026-07-08T10:57:08","s":["7s5nawwrkg"]}],"3":[{"m":"Though rebellion had brought them such calamity, they activated a righteous covenant in order to get divine backing, and made the young man king.\n\nGod was with them because they aligned with his will and his word.","dt":"2024-09-05T09:13:36","s":["k1na81g01m"]}],"7":[{"m":"They were going to invade the palace and enthrone the king, and had come up with a strategy.","dt":"2024-09-05T10:13:12","s":["5b72m26nse"]},{"m":"Why the Levites? Because they were the righteous and right custodians of the oracles of the LORD.\n\nThey could be trusted to keep the word of the Lord, because that is what they were born to do.\n\nTo mediate between God and the people. And now that waywardness had taken over the kingdom, it was their prerogative right to enforce and establish the norms of the land.","dt":"2024-09-05T10:16:10","s":["fsnhmrouw5"]}],"13":[{"m":"There was the ascent by which the king went to the house of the Lord. Solomon established this ascent, and it was one of the many things Queen Sheba saw that mesmerised her.\n\nAnd here the king stood by his pillar in the house of the Lord.\n\nIt was over for Athaliah. The coup had been made, and successfully.","dt":"2024-09-05T10:19:23","s":["qu6m3qk6uf"]},{"m":"Dake's says the king's pillar was a place in the house of the Lord where kings sat.\n\nThis was such a strong symbol. No one had sat there for a long while, so to see the king standing there sent such a strong signal to all.\n\nTo Athaliah, this was treason. The wicked know how to take advantage of situations and maximize the opportunities presented to them.\n\nThrough much wickedness she had seized the throne, and now Jehoiada the priest, also seeing the opportunities, seizes the divine opportunities.\n\nI can imagine all the years of silence and scheming Jehoiada had to do.\n\nAs he watched the evil Athaliah reign. He knew something no one else knew: the rightful heir to the throne, the son of Jehoram, was alive but still young.\n\nWhen the time was ripe, he executed his agenda.","dt":"2024-09-05T10:30:25","s":["sosgs21lma"]}],"19":[{"m":"The revival had begun, and Israel knew they were going to be blessed once more.\n\nOh, what a season this was in the house of the Lord... I wish I was there to see it.","dt":"2024-09-05T10:22:08","s":["icjozlidfh"]}],"21":[{"m":"Quite a remarkable statement — after Athaliah was slain with the sword, the city was quiet. Cast out the scorner, and contentions shall cease. In other words, cut off the murderer and quietness shall be restored to the people.","dt":"2026-07-08T11:07:19","s":["w9hg393ay4"]}],"9":[{"m":"This was like so that attention is not drawn should the captains and their people go to the public armoury for weapons; that would have raised suspicion. So they went about nonchalantly whiles secretly getting weapons from the last place anybody suspected.\n\nThe house of the Lord. I now see the wisdom of King David and King Solomon in providing spears and shields for the house of the Lord.","dt":"2026-07-08T11:02:00","s":["dd6qikdeta"]}],"10":[{"m":"This was a house coup, and he succeeded.","dt":"2026-07-08T11:00:05","s":["kpe0es0inf"]}],"11":[{"m":"The king's palace and the temple were connected, as built by Solomon the Great.","dt":"2026-07-08T11:02:27","s":["0rum9tuxr8"]}],"15":[{"m":"It seems there was a part of the king's house hard against that of the Lord.\n\nSo we see kings and priests working together, as ought to be the case, state and religion as one.","dt":"2024-09-05T10:20:41","s":["8agzdvzyrm"]}]},"24":{"15":[{"m":"Extraordinary — for him to have lived that long. Many of the kings were dying in their 60s and seventies, yet this man lived very long. To God be glory.","dt":"2026-07-16T22:20:20","s":["71tpuy1ezr"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh oh oh, seest thou a man who is diligent in his work? He will stand before kings; he will not stand before mean men.","dt":"2024-09-10T07:14:57","s":["lecvcjaaqn"]}],"26":[{"m":"The sons of Lot plotted and killed him.","dt":"2024-09-10T07:17:24","s":["ahnt44ur3v"]}]},"25":{"28":[{"m":"He had the same trait of his father: started well in the Lord but ended up bad, and murdered for his later wickedness and ingratitude.\n\nFor his father it was ingratitude to the priest who made him king, but for his son, ingratitude to God who made him win war, but rather chose the gods of the other nations who lost to him.\n\nEvil is so subtle and so tempting, and yet so foolish in hindsight and with foresight.","dt":"2026-07-16T22:32:07","s":["gatcar86ac"]}]},"26":{"19":[{"m":"He had a censer, meaning he was now in the holy place.\n\nI don't know of any king that did that; even Solomon and David, who loved the Lord, made the priests do their duties.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:07:29","s":["r0a61854pg"]}],"16":[{"m":"In his pride he did not evil 😈 oo.\n\nRather he sought to do what was seemingly good.\n\nThe same sin of Saul did Uzziah.\n\nHe went to offer incense upon the Lord's altar.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:05:56","s":["45i6buupp8"]}]},"28":{"13":[{"m":"They could tell by the great victory against their brethren in Judah that such victory could only be supernatural.\nThey agreed that their own victory came because they got help in a supernatural way; they could tell that God just wanted to punish their brothers in Judah.\n\nSo they complied to the word of the prophet.\n\nOnly I wonder, seeing they themselves were at fault, why did they not repent and fully follow the Lord?\n\nBecause the kind of repentance required to save the entire nation of Israel had to be national, not individual only.\n\nAnd it had to start with the men at the helm of power, the kings, as always, since they controlled the greatest power and authority to influence change.\n\nThat was why God often began from there, and/or schemed to set his own man in power and to do his will.\n\nI believe even now the same thing is happening across the nations.\n\nGod using one nation to defeat and punish another to carry out his cause; some of the nations are no more righteous or better than others, but God uses one against the other to push forward his agenda.","dt":"2026-07-25T04:18:57","s":["gsqpluz7q4"]}],"23":[{"m":"I have not read the end of Ahaz's reign yet, but I would love to see how he is treated on his burial.","dt":"2024-09-17T06:30:31","s":["cwowtymucu"]}],"24":[{"m":"Sadly, this foolish king inherited greatness and riches from his father and grandfathers, who were great examples to follow.\n\nOh, why do the wise inherit such foolish sons?","dt":"2024-09-17T06:35:35","s":["4zfluyk8i9"]}],"27":[{"m":"He was not considered a king 👑, so was not buried amongst them.\n\nIronically, this wicked king gave birth to a very wise son.\n\nAnd it's interesting that in their individual lifetimes, however fleeting they may be, they see the goodness of the Lord and the wrath of the Lord depending on whether they choose to serve him or not.\n\nIs this not the life of the believer...\n\nThat so long as we are with the Lord we are blessed and safe... And he will use the rod of men to chastise us if we drift away from him.","dt":"2024-09-17T06:37:54","s":["dnp71ckvki"]},{"m":"Though the people hated his ways because he brought much trouble and havoc to Judah, the people respected the system that had been set up, and he remained king despite his failures.\n\nThe people respected the set-up institution.\nThen when he finally died, they buried him in an ordinary way, not as a king.\n\nWhy? Because he went away from the ways of God. That goes to show that the kingmakers were a righteous people. They knew and kept the ways of the Lord, but their king 👑 worshipped other gods and brought trouble to Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nThat goes to show that in the corridors of Power are righteous people, and that ought to be the case, so there is always a light burning in the corridors of Power.\n\nIn a nation of much wickedness there are always righteous people in there; though the darkness may be loud and seem everywhere, yet the righteous are there and remain shining their light within the sphere of influence until the time is right for the righteous to rule or seize power.","dt":"2026-07-25T09:50:44","s":["zs6h73glve"]},{"m":"All the while the wicked reigned, the righteous were strategically grooming the future king in righteousness... Sometimes it is too late to change the present, but you can buy the future, and you live through the difficulties of the moment... The least you can do for yourself in your difficulty is to buy the future and secure it in righteousness.","dt":"2026-07-25T09:53:12","s":["qdb1z771d8"]}]},"29":{"12":[{"m":"I can feel the hearts 💕 of these Levites.\n\nThere was hope once again; their hearts swelled with possibilities 💓.\n\nMaybe this time would be different, they would make history with God.\n\nOh, thank God that they find themselves here at this point in time before a wise young king 👑.\n\nOh, the expectation, joy bubbling yet restrained on the inside.\n\nRestrained with the cords of hope: hopefully we can make history and be enjoined with the Lord in covenant and blessings.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:56:38","s":["lbyzz9ak9d"]}],"13":[{"m":"These have been in hiding and rendered useless by Ahaz the former king.\n\nBut now they have been found useful.\n\nTheir hearts' cry has the Lord answered.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:57:37","s":["6zy4u2eyr8"]}],"17":[{"m":"How did the house of the Lord come so low, and the Lord stood and watched? Meanwhile, in time past, men who stood and hallowed his name were struck down for a mild misdemeanor compared to the state of the temple in Hezekiah's day.\n\nWhy was God so hard then, and yet now men could even dare shut the doors of his house and refuse to serve him?\n\nBecause whiles a man chooses to serve the Lord, he must do it right and according to the laws of God. God required strict servitude and obedience, because service of HIM is to man's advantage, not the other way.\n\nSo he won't force anyone to worship him and come to him, but once you do, HE demands you do it right or not at all. He has no respect for them that do not respect or fear his name.","dt":"2026-07-29T06:50:59","s":["2yu4x1bylo"]}],"36":[{"m":"Speedily desiring to do right and doing it.","dt":"2022-07-19T08:00:59","s":["jej3hse43e"]}],"3":[{"m":"He chose God first and chose to set up and restore the worship at the temple first, before all else or embarking on any major works or projects.\n\nHe sought first the kingdom of God and God's righteousness first. No wonder all others were added to him, as we shall see in later chapters.","dt":"2026-07-29T06:44:06","s":["06rp7jx8pv"]}],"6":[{"m":"How come Hezekiah was so different? He did not have a good background. He himself said it, that their fathers had transgressed, so how did he learn to do differently?\n\nThis goes to show we are not trapped by the past; we are not completely helpless 😣.\n\nYou may have a background that seems to have imposed limitations on you, but with God's help you can completely break free from the yoke of the past, as did Hezekiah.\n\nTrust fully on the Lord, and he shall order your steps.\n\nProverbs 3:5-6 KJV\nTrust in the Lord with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. [6] In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:51:58","s":["4iepr0xrs9"]}],"34":[{"m":"Maybe the priests had given up on the Lord and did not believe this will yield any results, or maybe they felt it was going to be a nine-day wonder?","dt":"2026-07-29T06:55:06","s":["dbtffbeoqr"]}]},"30":{"20":[{"m":"Amen 😭. God is not so much interested in outward ceremonies of sanctification as much as the sanctification of the heart.\n\nIn time past failure to be sanctified externally can incur the wrath of God and possible death.\n\nBut God healed them when he saw their heart ♥.\n\nThey had been so backslidden for so long that this attempt at reconciliation with God could not be hindered by failure to cleanse oneself as required.","dt":"2022-07-19T08:05:37","s":["uktcpepadv"]},{"m":"Amen","dt":"2026-07-29T07:02:41","s":["e3182ec483"]}],"27":[{"m":"Amen 🙏 and amen. Thank you, Father, you are a prayer-answering God.","dt":"2022-07-19T08:07:14","s":["lo6kz7gv1d"]}],"6":[{"m":"Ah, so that was one of the reasons why Hezekiah later said he had rebelled against Assyria and should be forgiven, and he gave much treasure to appease the king of Assyria.","dt":"2026-07-29T06:56:54","s":["1are9c9177"]}],"10":[{"m":"Hezekiah's act of faith in believing God was going to do as written in his law was not without hindrance.\n\nThey mocked him to scorn. Probably they said, does he think he is David or Solomon?\n\nOr maybe they laughed at him and said, 'This dude believes all these stories of God delivering his chosen people if they serve him.\n\nWe will be killed and conquered like the other nations and kings, and there is nothing any God can do about it. Hezekiah is just a young ambitious 👨 man.'","dt":"2024-09-20T07:21:43","s":["k2yvthlodo"]}],"15":[{"m":"The priests and the Levites were ashamed in 2 Chronicles 30:15 because their own spiritual apathy, laziness, and ritual impurity had delayed God's worship, while the ordinary people showed immense zeal and readiness to serve — this is Google's interpretation of this verse, and I think rightly so.\n\nThe priests, just like the earlier incident, were not ready and zealous for the things of God anymore — maybe they were just tired or did not care because of the previous king's ills.","dt":"2026-07-29T07:00:53","s":["h415sxqzll"]}],"17":[{"m":"When those who ought to do what is right do not and are not ready, a people, though not the best qualified but ready, will take over the kingdom and rulership of things.","dt":"2026-07-29T07:01:50","s":["tlolqyd90i"]}]},"31":{"13":[{"m":"At this time of them doing this, they did not know that their names would ring true for all eternity.\n\nBut here we are today, still talking of this great deed.\n\nOh omnipotent eternal Father, help me do the right thing and serve you faithfully, for I know now what chords it will ring in eternity.","dt":"2022-07-19T08:10:45","s":["b8cxbo5q31"]}],"17":[{"m":"By bringing in their tithes, the service and house of the Lord came alive once more.\n\nPoverty kills the house of God; failure to give to support the church ⛪ kills it.\n\nIt takes the giving of God's people to keep the house of God alive.","dt":"2022-07-19T08:12:37","s":["i04d1f05zi"]}]},"32":{"7":[{"m":"Amen, such blessed assurance.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:31:46","s":["clao96sp0n"]}],"15":[{"m":"Oh, so the God of Judah was less than other gods? Wow.\n\nNo wonder God really dealt with him.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:33:49","s":["sn88a8khk9"]},{"m":"I guess because he had defeated nations bigger and more powerful than Judah, so then that means those nations' gods were more powerful than Judah's God, and of course, following that logic, Judah's God was far less powerful and therefore much more easy to destroy.","dt":"2026-08-09T08:22:07","s":["iidez7jl75"]}],"20":[{"m":"The narrative in the book of Kings gives more details and perspective as to what went into the prayers and cries of Hezekiah and Isaiah. Putting it this way was a good way to summarise the activities of these two men that produced the deliverance of the nation.\n\nIn crying to heaven, we are given the exact details, including Hezekiah going to the house of the Lord and laying prostrate. This also gives us understanding in the preceding chapters when Isaiah cried for a sign for Hezekiah to know that he will recover from his sickness.\n\nEarlier on I had asked why Manasseh, the son of Hezekiah, though wicked, lived and reigned for so long, and yet Hezekiah, one of the most righteous of God's kings on the throne, was cut off early.\n\nBut there the prophet ISAIAH himself explains it thus —\n\nIsaiah 57:1\nThe righteous perish, and no one takes it to heart; the devout are taken away, and no one understands that the righteous are taken away to be spared from evil.","dt":"2026-08-09T08:28:23","s":["geyzc1zdqe"]}],"23":[{"m":"Of course, who wouldn't want to align with such obvious greatness and support of the God of all flesh, the God of the heavens and the creator of all things?","dt":"2026-08-09T08:30:06","s":["ajhsq99mgd"]}],"25":[{"m":"Oh, now this explains it: it was pride and refusal to acknowledge the hand of God in his recovery and later prosperity that the Lord chose to punish them, but they repented, and it happened not in their time.\n\nThat punishment of the raiding of their riches and properties was a long-pending judgement that God had in store for Judah, but the Lord simply deferred it from happening in Hezekiah's and that of his people's days.","dt":"2026-08-09T08:33:26","s":["94nqvs6vuj"]}],"33":[{"m":"Oh, Hezekiah and Manasseh his son.\n\nLight and darkness in the same space. One was given the chiefest place among kings 👑.\n\nThe other was given a burial in his house.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:37:49","s":["wxipq9zrrx"]}]},"33":{"3":[{"m":"Could it be that it was because of this boy 🧒 that Hezekiah's life was to be cut short by sickness, so this Manasseh was not born at all?\n\nBecause he was born within the period of extension of his life.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:45:44","s":["hep4xcu3i2"]}],"12":[{"m":"God is indeed too merciful.","dt":"2022-08-03T07:28:57","s":["hraqmwie1o"]}],"13":[{"m":"God is so merciful — he gives everyone a chance.\n\nSometimes the wicked thrive and destroy the righteous, but at least God knows the righteous is in a safe place.\n\nBut the wicked's only chance is in this life, so it's part of God's lifeline to them, to give them a chance to repent.","dt":"2024-10-06T15:12:32","s":["pakeen84ba"]}]},"34":{"2":[{"m":"Why were there good and evil kings mixed up?\n\nCould not a pattern be established such that evil people could not reign as kings,\n\nso that this back and forth does not continue?\n\nIt so retards growth.","dt":"2022-08-05T11:06:14","s":["kq20e769l1"]}],"21":[{"m":"Since Israel had gone into captivity, it seems Judah annexed the remaining land of Israel to themselves.\n\nThey were one people anyways.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:33:05","s":["touucxig3l"]},{"m":"So at this time Israel was a wasted land? No, we are told new people were occupying that land, and even God had punished them for not giving him reverence and all.\n\nSo there were people living there, but those people themselves were captives, so Judah more or less was the sovereign state with a standing army within that region.","dt":"2026-08-10T09:38:24","s":["0qparmfe17"]}],"3":[{"m":"I read this account, but I did not know Josiah was so young when he was doing this.\n\nHe was only 20 years of age and began to seek the Lord in his youth at the age of 8 years when he became king.\n\nI am even more impressed now at him.\n\nHe was a wise young man.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:29:46","s":["zvt6gghsl9"]}],"8":[{"m":"6 YEARS, that's how long it took to purge the land of idolatry. That shows how polluted the land was with idol worship.\n\nEven by the decree of the king, it took 6 years.","dt":"2026-08-10T09:33:00","s":["445yzy0igt"]}],"28":[{"m":"He did not die in peace; he was killed in war, unless this peace is in comparison to what would have happened if the wrath of the Lord was allowed to happen in Josiah's time.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:34:55","s":["i54gvjndvf"]}]},"35":{"14":[{"m":"Once more the heavens and the earth 🌎 were filled with smoke and sweet incense to the Lord.\n\nThe atmosphere was being created all over Israel 🇮🇱 once again.\nThat sweet-smelling atmosphere which brought riches and blessings 🌾,\n\nwhich purged away evil, was being created.\n\nOur incense needs to rise up perpetually, and God will handle the rest for us.\n\nJust keep your atmosphere fresh with incense and the presence of God.","dt":"2022-08-05T11:17:17","s":["rwvbo6umyo"]}],"23":[{"m":"Awww... Why did not God save him?","dt":"2022-08-05T11:18:52","s":["avl6yejya6"]},{"m":"Oh Josiah, why did he not listen? Died at a young age of 39 years.\n\nOh, why make such a mistake... He should have enquired.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:42:37","s":["7o94jldc94"]}]},"36":{"10":[{"m":"And he was later to be released some 30+ years later.\n\nNow a thought came to mind about prophecies, for example Jeremiah's 70-year prophecy of the return.\n\nNow how did God know this would happen, and how did he ensure it happened?\n\nHow did he scheme things to work out such that Israel was released some 70 years later?\n\nI believe when the prophecy came, the scribes of heaven wrote it down and mapped up a plot and strategy to cause it to happen according to the pleasure of the king 👑 Jehovah.","dt":"2022-08-18T08:59:44","s":["csavg72q8v"]}],"16":[{"m":"The grave end is coming upon them, you can sense.\n\nEven the house of the Lord was being used for idolatry... Their cup was becoming full, and that quickly.\n\nI fear for the church ⛪ also of today. Judgement will come.","dt":"2022-08-18T08:53:17","s":["wquk2xq466"]}],"15":[{"m":"I noticed that even though GOD prophesied death and gloom to these people, he still provided for them a way of escape.\n\nIt sometimes sounded like GOD was going to kill them and destroy them without mercy, but even in their rebellion and idolatry he would tell them, at the very time of his final judgements on them, to surrender to Nebuchadnezzar so they escape cruel death.\n\nYou can see that he did not really want to kill or destroy them. Even when they failed to repent and worship him, he still gave them a chance to continue being alive in their idolatry, but they would not listen.\n\nGOD is a good father. Indeed, no father will allow his son to go wayward, and even in his waywardness will not want him dead, but at least alive, even if still in rebellion.\n\nThe death of the wicked, it seems, is always the last resort of judgement, not the very first.\n\nGOD always seeks to have men repent so he forgives them.","dt":"2026-08-27T08:57:25.601Z","s":["0b9efvh41t"]}],"21":[{"m":"Sabbath is the seventh day, and in symbolism of sabbath the land kept 70 sabbaths, a sabbath per year.","dt":"2026-08-27T09:05:23.195Z","s":["rodfx491zq"]}],"14":[{"m":"So even the chief priests were partakers in idolatry and abominations...\n\nNo wonder they were slain and killed.","dt":"2024-10-25T09:52:22","s":["uod3cnvwfn"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"Is this not the same mount 🗻 of Abraham their father?\n\nI asked this question in an earlier note, and yes, it is... Both the place Abraham sacrificed Isaac and the place David pacified God and stayed the plague.","dt":"2024-08-02T00:42:24","s":["giwhd0fbkn","8d45c36449","e2cdc87993"]}]},"11":{"3":[{"m":"Suddenly Judah and Benjamin collaborated?\nBenjamin, whose king was Saul, whom Judah through David had overthrown.\n\nWell, at least here they had an unusual alliance for their common interest...\n\nThey can fight their personal battles later, after their personal interests are met.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:25:03","s":["0y7tx1cg42"]},{"m":"Why were Judah and Benjamin together when Benjamin's brother is Joseph? Google AI answers this question:\n\nThe tribes of Judah and Benjamin stayed together under King Rehoboam because of geographical proximity, political alignment, and God's sovereign decree, despite the matriarchal bonds that connected Benjamin to Joseph.\n\nAnd right answer — especially seeing they were also one in politics, for their first king Saul reigned in Jerusalem, and their king and David both ruled from the same territory and were both anointed by Samuel the prophet. Of course, their geographical boundaries also presented a very strong tie to Judah.","dt":"2026-06-30T08:58:02","s":["oc6vf3w50z"]}],"17":[{"m":"When I look at my own life, the years of my walk with the Lord were some of the toughest yet most fulfilling and impactful.\n\nImpactful until the years of my drifting away, which initially seemed uneventful until suddenly tough situations came, and I wasn't prepared nor built myself spiritually for it.\n\nThey were so tough I almost could have died, leaving me empty and unfulfilled.\n\nNow I'm getting back on my feet because the Lord showed me mercy.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:34:42","s":["4otu2w0o9u"]}],"22":[{"m":"The lineage of Absalom, it seemed, continued to be very beautiful, for here we see Rehoboam loved her above them all.\n\nI presume she was of great beauty and character as well to be so loved.","dt":"2024-08-24T11:48:07","s":["lqbvuifs5s"]}]},"16":{"10":[{"m":"The dilemma of the messenger — bad news, and he bears the brunt, though he is but a messenger.","dt":"2024-08-28T07:40:23","s":["4hb84g91ec"]}]}},"Leviticus":{"5":{"5":[{"m":"Confession, the first step to redemption.","dt":"2022-02-19T04:23:14","s":["fe4dbd1b79"]}]},"8":{"4":[{"m":"The tabernacle was about a half plot of land or less, i.e. 100 by 80, so how could 2 million people of Israel gather around it? Most likely a representation of it. If that is the case, could we also then say that some of the happenings in Exodus were representative, in that some of the people participated — likely those closest to the corridors of power?\n\nOf course some of the things represented the entire congregation, for example the plagues they were saved from, the crossing of the sea, the manna, etc. etc.\n\nSome commentaries say the key leaders and elders gathered in the court and the rest of the community were in the know; some might have trooped to the hill and nearby mountains to observe from a good height.\n\nAll these are plausible.","dt":"2026-02-17T20:41:59","s":["wwiqhmc0ks"]}],"35":[{"m":"Yes, I understand that it is so the Lord has commanded, but what was the moral or spiritual significance of this seven-day stay at the door of the Tabernacle?\n\nDid it mean they were to sit at the entrance, or did it mean more like they should stay within the outer court area?\n\nThis area really is at the entrance to the door of the Tabernacle.\n\nAnd if my memory serves me right, there were to be daily sacrifices for each day of the seven.","dt":"2022-02-21T14:01:36","s":["wxvzgt3tad","a26f102b70"]}]},"9":{"5":[{"m":"Stood before the Lord.\n\nWas the cloud 🌥 on the tabernacle at this time? Oh, I can imagine the feeling and the sight.\n\nBut even as I pen down these things, I am reminded that we have it more glorious.\n\nThe cloud 🌥 of glory is right here in us. In our hearts. The Lord himself lives inside of us, not outside in some building, but right in us.\n\nDeeper than our skins. Oh God, it's awesome.","dt":"2024-04-02T07:06:39","s":["ea7ccf9593"]}],"12":[{"m":"I wonder if there is any particular reason the blood was sprinkled round about the altar and not anywhere else.","dt":"2024-04-09T14:20:42","s":["5b9d63e28d"]}],"23":[{"m":"This seems to suggest that the cloud 🌥 of glory was not on the tabernacle at this time and came after the rites were completed, and even fired 🔥 up the altar.","dt":"2024-04-02T07:46:55","s":["b641350022"]}],"24":[{"m":"The people shouted for joy, some versions said.\n\nWas it a cry of fear 😱, and they bowed down in awe, or was it a shout of joy?\n\nEither way, from my perspective, daily seeing that cloud 🌥 of glory was more than enough to inspire awe and confidence in God.\n\nI think it is this confidence in God always that he desires.\n\nCome to think 🤔 of it, this daily cloud 🌥 of glory was present even on the days Israel hungered and thirsted in the wilderness.\n\nHmm 🤔, was this some test from God to see how far they would trust in him?\n\nBecause see, the glory never left 👈; he wanted to know for how long these people would hold on to faith.\n\nHmm 🤔, interesting. The ways of God.\n\nIt's easier said than done, because all of the 2 million plus people failed this test of faith save two.\n\nHmm 🤔... It really is easier said than done.","dt":"2022-02-21T14:16:31","s":["cbu9qyd0i2"]},{"m":"This was one of the challenges of God with Israel.\n\nThey saw his mighty signs and wonders... So in times of want and trials he expected them to wait on him in faith,\n\nbut rather they murmured and complained until God responded, though angry and frustrated 😤 at their murmurings.\n\nGod's nature 🏞 is to respond to faith, faithful waiting, but in Israel's case, and I guess sometimes in our Christian walk,\n\nhe, God, for his name's sake, responds to our unbelief.\n\nThough after a while he started punishing Israel for their murmurings and killed them eventually.\n\nThank you Lord for your goodness and mercy. I choose the way of faith. Thank you 🙏","dt":"2022-02-21T14:29:13","s":["iosrsejprd"]},{"m":"And they were going to betray him later in difficult times, despite having seen the Lord visibly.\n\nHumans are just like that.","dt":"2024-04-02T07:50:57","s":["nf6a7t2j6l"]}]},"14":{"39":[{"m":"I am just wondering, as the priest goes about inspecting such infectious contaminations and diseases, how is he himself being protected? Or would he be exempt from such contaminations because he is doing the Lord's work? I believe so.\n\nIt would be unfair to get contaminated as he goes about the work of the Lord as instructed by God himself. Let's see what subsequent chapters say.","dt":"2026-02-19T10:22:42","s":["lh32mfqakj"]}],"53":[{"m":"This looks so much like African traditional religion.","dt":"2024-04-04T11:36:49","s":["2c4ac59141"]}]},"15":{"18":[{"m":"Eii saa... 😂 This is interesting.","dt":"2022-02-21T16:10:16","s":["p6z105g1bh"]},{"m":"Having sex makes one unclean. Hhhmm 🤔","dt":"2024-04-04T11:41:30","s":["uvg4zrs6g7"]}]},"16":{"3":[{"m":"Coming before God was definitely uncommon and required such copious preparation.\n\nIt hammered home the point that his presence is rare and is to be respected.\n\nIt's the same with the laws of cleanliness: to avoid spreading of disease, and the tedious washing of clothes just because you touched someone or something.\n\nSuch requirements ensured the presence of God and his laws were constantly in their mind.","dt":"2024-04-04T11:46:02","s":["610b77ffc2"]}],"4":[{"m":"Why do I have the feeling that angels and spirit beings have a mechanism that prevents dirt from getting to them?\n\nAnd the shadow of that is the cleansing of the flesh with water 💦. That is the purpose of ceremonial cleansing.\n\nSame also, spirits have their outer garments as part of them; it was part of their glorious bodies. So in like manner Aaron was to be well covered in his flesh:\n\nfrom the breeches to the holy crown 👑.","dt":"2022-02-22T02:11:27","s":["1q899eeqz0","ade64c1cce"]}]},"17":{"11":[{"m":"So immediately God sets a law in motion. Blood gives life, and also “I set in motion an atonement ability for the blood.”\n\nSo now blood not only gives life to the body of the animal but now possesses substitution powers.\n\nEven though at this time this is more of a revelation, because blood sacrifices had been made way before the law.","dt":"2022-02-22T07:01:35","s":["8bdcbbe40f"]}]},"19":{"2":[{"m":"Dead on.","dt":"2022-02-22T23:09:21","s":["05o8ap45x3"]},{"m":"Dead right and straight to the point.","dt":"2024-04-09T15:15:49","s":["76d2e9e1fb"]}],"26":[{"m":"Why were eating blood and enchantments used in the same sentence?\n\nExcept to relate it as eating blood for enchantment.\n\nEven though eating it not for enchantment but for food is still forbidden.","dt":"2024-04-06T05:26:43","s":["pcbixutwew","f6744729b8"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh, this law, it is so beautiful. Imagine this law is common knowledge among Israel's neighbours. That when you visit the land of Israel and are stranded or starving, provision is made by their GOD for the stranger and the poor, so that you do not die of starvation but are preserved until you become independent enough and the land itself is taking care of you.\n\nThen you can refrain from the scraps and in turn help others with the same system that preserved you in time past.","dt":"2026-02-19T11:03:17","s":["ehwd56css3"]}]},"22":{"3":[{"m":"Cut off in this sense does not mean banish, I believe, but death ☠. As seen in Aaron's sons.","dt":"2024-04-06T06:14:02","s":["d8ejx4amj9","2ae4f389de"]}],"33":[{"m":"I am the LORD, I am the LORD, I am the LORD.","dt":"2024-04-06T06:20:20","s":["jh6s3sdizi"]},{"m":"God detested abominations and uncleanliness because he is the LORD.","dt":"2024-04-06T06:21:32","s":["bcc8fa7a58"]}],"9":[{"m":"The priests were holy unto the Lord and so were forbidden from doing certain things.\n\nThe same I see for the man of God: there are ethics we must follow and things we must not do, not because they are sinful but because we are called 🤙.","dt":"2024-04-06T06:17:05","s":["f97858269d"]}]},"25":{"22":[{"m":"This makes so much sense.\n\nThis is the way of the Lord. Yet sometimes blessings are proclaimed in the name of the Lord and yet we see nothing.\n\nEven after the conditions which the man of God states are met.\n\nUsually the only condition given is to sow a seed of money 💵.\n\nThus often making our God seem crafty.","dt":"2022-02-21T15:52:40","s":["baoyfp4se9"]},{"m":"God is not mindless. He makes provision for his people for their obedience.","dt":"2024-04-08T08:53:42","s":["ea1c303840"]}],"23":[{"m":"Okay 👌, that's nice. And that rule is what the kings of the earth use to bear rule.\n\nThey lease the land for 100 years and it comes back to them. Very interesting.","dt":"2024-04-08T08:54:47","s":["113eb54cac"]}],"42":[{"m":"Interesting perspectives. God says the children of Israel are his servants; he redeemed them from bondage so that they cannot be put into bondage again.\n\nHe bought them and put them into bondage as servants, but a good bondage, in that so long as they are with him and his, they are bound to freedom.\n\nThey cannot be bound to bondage again.\n\nHe used the same rules of bondage to purchase them and then bound them to perpetual freedom.","dt":"2024-04-08T08:59:36","s":["a54d2fc50d"]}],"47":[{"m":"Interesting, so that means that the terms of prosperity are not automatic.\n\nEven among God's chosen people, a foreigner can be filthy rich, richer than the natives.\n\nGod is indeed a just God. And it seems that as believers we make so many exceptions for ourselves that make no sense.\n\nTherefore God is not obligated to honour those.","dt":"2022-02-21T15:58:22","s":["7m4slqr81t"]}]},"26":{"9":[{"m":"Oh my Lord and my God, just as we honour and respect people of worth... Here God is saying,\n\nI have my ways… I am not some idol through whom disorder emanates.\n\nNo, if you keep my decrees and honour my laws, I will have respect for you.\n\nWow.","dt":"2022-02-23T19:48:57","s":["fyo76aoafr","0898444be9"]}],"12":[{"m":"Wow.\n\nHere was the ideal situation God was painting 🎨 for them, if perhaps they would desire that and be lured into God's beautiful plan for them.","dt":"2022-02-23T19:50:08","s":["hakglclg5h","059da72013"]}],"14":[{"m":"What is the difference between commands, statutes and judgements?\n\nJudgements are easier, in that they are God's decisions concerning issues and cases that come up, especially from breaking any of his laws.\n\nSo all these burnt offerings, stoning offenders, etc. are his judgements concerning breaking his laws.\n\nI presume then that his statutes are the same as his laws, whiles his commandments may be like decrees.\n\nI would have to search out the original Hebrew words.","dt":"2024-04-09T08:14:27","s":["70366369d7"]}],"19":[{"m":"Since mostly they were farmers and shepherds, an iron heaven represents no rain and intense sunshine ☀, which burns and dries up.\n\nAnd brazen earth 🌎 is as a result of an iron heaven, and not just that, but even that which is planted will yield little, if at all.\n\nFar less than what even a scorched earth 🌎 is supposed to yield.","dt":"2024-04-09T08:17:08","s":["e36c0cc645"]}],"28":[{"m":"I mean, after all these, for a people to refuse to yield and return to the Lord?\n\nWhat kind of a people are those? Such blessedness — blessedness in the sense that God will continue to even more extremes just to win them back to himself.\n\nWhy does he not let them alone till they self-destruct like the other nations? Because they are his covenant people, and he always leaves even a remnant.\n\nOh Lord, bless me by yourself indeed, that I will be a covenant people, that there always will be a remnant to do your will, oh Lord, no matter how far off I or my seed stray from you. This I pray 🙏 oh Lord.","dt":"2024-04-09T08:21:14","s":["hq0z8cjv3s","63b587e8f4"]}],"35":[{"m":"Can we say that the Lord will calculate the years of the land not having her sabbath and send the children of Israel into captivity to make up the sabbaths?\n\nGod is so just, in a funny way.","dt":"2026-02-23T20:54:53","s":["peh1l4wpp3"]}],"40":[{"m":"When I read this passage, I wondered why the repentance of the people attracted the Lord's attention and mercy, meanwhile in the preceding verses he himself said he will not accept their incense or offering.\n\nWhat had changed this time? It is because the first time the people just continued in their ways and sins, business as usual, and yet still maintained a posture of religiosity and holiness.\n\nThis is what the verse says:\n\n“And I will make your cities waste, and bring your sanctuaries unto desolation, and I will not smell the savour of your sweet odours.”\nLeviticus 26:31 KJV\n\nSo these people were offering sweet odours to the Lord as if all was well. Meanwhile they were disobeying his laws.\n\nThey kept the rituals but not his laws and judgements.\n\nHowever, when finally they came to themselves and recognized their wicked ways and humbled themselves, God began their redemption.\n\nHe further states that they have to accept the punishment of their iniquity, in that they deserved it and it was just.\n\nWow.. complete repentance... I have been there before and I'm there even now. Lord, help me... Help us all.\n\nI think, like Daniel, one can repent on his own behalf and that of his nation, family, etc.\n\nLord, have mercy on my family.","dt":"2026-02-24T08:38:03","s":["w0zaacxoyc"]}],"42":[{"m":"In verse 28 I prayed a prayer for covenant, but in this verse I realized that we are already covenant children.\n\nThe covenant of Abraham we covet, and so I know my prayer is heard — not that God needs to consider cutting a new covenant with me, but that the old covenant of Abraham I am a part of, so I covet the blessing of that covenant.\n\nOf course that doesn't mean he does not renew or cut new covenants within covenant.\n\nWe see he cut covenants with David, all within the Abrahamic covenant.","dt":"2024-04-09T08:26:11","s":["3156d83771"]}],"7":[{"m":"Wow… It's almost pure paradise for the children of Israel.\n\nThey were to be the dominant force if they walked with the Lord.","dt":"2024-04-08T19:18:38","s":["y0jno45yv5","56a97f4a77"]}],"46":[{"m":"Amen. I'm still trying to figure out the difference between commandments and statutes.\n\nCould the statutes be the numerous customs and rituals of cleansing etc., whiles commandments are like the Ten Commandments and other laws for daily living?","dt":"2024-04-09T08:26:56","s":["84c5240d0d","vwcaym8mw9","29b8b7b3f3"]}]},"1":{"17":[{"m":"A sweet smell to the Lord. I can imagine the smoke of the whole burnt offering forming its cloud 🌥 and being swallowed up and merged with the pillar of cloud 🌥.\n\nGod was in the cloud 🌥, smelling the sweet savour of the burnt offering. That was God's way — he who is spirit — of smelling and partaking and accepting the offerings of his people.\n\nAs he smelt it, he knew who it belonged to, and atonement was made for the person.","dt":"2024-03-31T17:44:06","s":["7f953ee7cb"]}]},"18":{"28":[{"m":"Not only was the land defiled, but it spewed out those who practised such abomination.\n\nThis is worth studying, how the earth 🌎 abhors such wickedness.\n\nAnd we see later that Israel was spewed out of its own land because of such abominations.\n\nIt is unimaginable why men would commit such wickedness, and yet the people of Canaan did.\n\nIncluding sacrificing their children in their droves to Molech by fire 🔥.\n\nReminds me so much of America 🇺🇸 today and their numerous abortions.\n\nLord, have mercy.","dt":"2024-04-06T02:31:10","s":["tpt2oeooym"]}]},"20":{"0":[{"m":"Interesting.","dt":"2024-04-06T06:12:33","s":["9748a95c36"]}]},"21":{"21":[{"m":"Interesting.","dt":"2024-04-06T06:12:33","s":["779d4e900e"]}]}},"Numbers":{"3":{"9":[{"m":"So by this declaration Aaron and his sons were made automatic leaders and heads over the rest of the Levites.","dt":"2024-04-09T11:22:46","s":["aada9a863a","cbwzk2oprz"]}],"13":[{"m":"That makes sense, because in reality they are dead, or were supposed to be dead.\n\nBut he has kept them alive for himself.\n\nThere is similar stuff in the NT that says we are crucified with Christ, nevertheless we live, yet not I but Christ lives in me.\n\nGalatians 2:20 KJV\nI am crucified with Christ: nevertheless I live; yet not I, but Christ liveth in me: and the life which I now live in the flesh I live by the faith of the Son of God, who loved me, and gave himself for me.\n\nSo since all the first born were his, he chose by the law of substitution to replace them with Levi, and for parents to pay a small token to redeem their first born.\n\nAlso they were to present them to the Lord as a reminder of the works of the Lord.","dt":"2022-02-24T06:56:55","s":["7kr1cwww1d","7666eb1bcd"]},{"m":"All the first born were set aside; death had come upon them and they had survived because they were hallowed — God had set them apart.\n\nThey had been touched by the divine. They could no longer be common; they were hallowed.\n\nThat was how God saved them and preserved their lives from the angel 😇 of death ☠. By hallowing them.","dt":"2024-03-17T18:37:04","s":["lkezacsng5"]}]},"5":{"29":[{"m":"Much to be said.\n\nThis sounds or feels so much like 🧙‍♀️ enchantments.\n\nAnd it's meant to work every single time ⌚. Wow, solid.\n\nNow to the main point: of all the trespasses and sins, this is the only one sin for which such allocation is made.\n\nWhy is that so? Why is that not the case for, say, when someone steals from you or lies concerning something of value?\n\nBut concerning one's wife, a provision is made. This calls for much meditation 🧘‍♂️.\n\nWanted to ask, how about the reverse 🔀? But it was a polygamous society, so I get it.","dt":"2022-02-25T12:59:55","s":["3vnefyct4n","9c888769c7"]}],"28":[{"m":"So in the case of wrong accusation, the curse 🤬 is turned into a blessing.","dt":"2024-03-19T14:01:32","s":["2513122db6"]}]},"6":{"10":[{"m":"The New King 👑 James lets us know it's actually two turtle 🐢 doves 🕊.","dt":"2024-04-12T11:03:15","s":["99bc510549"]}],"14":[{"m":"Such an innocent one-year-old lamb, to be killed for sins and trespasses.\n\nAlso, why is the Nazarite bringing a sin offering when he has done no wrong?\n\nBut it seems that to come into the vicinity of our God, you are already deemed a sinner, whether you have literally sinned or not.\n\nAnd so to have audience you should come atoned for.\n\nThis goes to show that it's not just the mere act of having committed any sins, but our very existence and nature is sin, or sinful.","dt":"2024-04-12T11:07:49","s":["adcaf4ba69"]}],"21":[{"m":"I guess the Nazarite vow is to obtain something within the period.","dt":"2022-02-25T13:05:43","s":["iqdeqjfpz7","dbee945273"]}],"25":[{"m":"Amen and amen.","dt":"2024-04-12T11:09:59","s":["132c0e8f66"]}]},"7":{"89":[{"m":"From the rendering of this, it seems Moses spoke with God in the Tabernacle in the holy place, but this time things were different.\n\nHe heard the voice speaking from the mercy seat.\n\nThe Tabernacle was complete; now God was dwelling in his dedicated place.\n\nInteresting — God indeed is a God of times and seasons.\n\nA quick aside: there were sacrifices, especially for the ordination and sanctification of the sanctuary and the whole Tabernacle.\n\nSo much blood shed. Why? Why these ordinations, and their significance?\n\nAnd I hear in my heart, “because there are laws and sin cannot go unpunished.”\n\nThere are consequences to each action, and we just cannot wish it away or ignore it. The very nature of nature demands it.\n\nSo we fool ourselves, especially this generation, where we believe we can do what we like and suffer nothing.\n\nWe walk in error.","dt":"2022-02-26T09:36:05","s":["9gjnjagzof","0dde5a6419"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why didn't God want anything man-made to touch the sacred things, or even be around them? Even the Levites carrying the ark had to use poles of gold.","dt":"2026-02-28T16:53:14","s":["t1wgy5tgyw"]}]},"8":{"11":[{"m":"There we have it again, the Levites were offered.","dt":"2024-03-21T14:31:52","s":["7m65arq6q6"]},{"m":"So does that mean if Israel had stayed with the original plan of God for them to have been a nation of priests,\n\nthat they would have performed the priestly duties themselves?\n\nYes, and they would have done so in turns, or in courses, just like in the times of King 👑 David.\n\nThe Levites' population then had grown, so service to the Lord was done in turns.\n\nOh, what a joy and privilege. All Israel would have had the chance to enter into the tabernacle — and not just the tabernacle, but to have performed the high priestly duties.\n\nMaybe one might get lucky enough to perform that duty once in their lifetime,\n\nto enter the most holy place. Ah, what glory.\n\nAnd now today the veil is torn in two ✌️.\n\nWe are king 👑 priests and we enter the holy place without limits,\n\nwhere we behold the face of our Father time and again. For he indeed is our Father.\n\nGlory to God 🙌","dt":"2024-04-13T00:16:59","s":["2250bcc7d6"]}],"12":[{"m":"So Moses was exempted from all these himself... i.e. the purification rites, or God made him sacrifice for and cleanse himself earlier.","dt":"2026-02-28T17:33:09","s":["dqny81zmz5"]}],"13":[{"m":"Am I reading right, or is it just my mind?\n\nThe Levites were to be offered to the Lord on behalf of the children of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nJust as Israel offered lambs for sin, they offered the Levites for their first born.\n\nThey were literally dead, because they were substituted for every first male-born son, and every first male-born son was substituted for by a ram 🐏.\n\nInteresting. The Levites were no longer their own.","dt":"2024-03-21T14:29:27","s":["kl1d13qpj1","25227efcaa"]}],"15":[{"m":"There we go again, the Levites were offered for an offering.","dt":"2024-03-21T14:32:42","s":["aad937e816"]}],"19":[{"m":"So this was the purpose of the atonement, so that they are not plagued and likely die as they came near God, i.e. the sanctuary.\n\nAnd their dying was because of sin in the flesh. It was not just because of sin committed, but the very nature of the flesh in housing the sinful nature.","dt":"2022-03-01T09:46:43","s":["ktcgid28j2","4ba9254177"]}]},"9":{"16":[{"m":"Was it not this same fire 🔥 that burnt on the mountain whilst Moses kept the flocks of his father-in-law?\n\nThat same fire burning 🔥 the bush, yet the bush was not consumed.\n\nNow that fire 🔥 dwelt upon this Tabernacle, and yet it also was not consumed.\n\nIndeed, another dimension was revealed. It was fire 🔥 and 🌥 it was water 💦, a cloud 🌥.\n\nAnd so it was always.","dt":"2022-03-01T19:11:03","s":["2cf954691c"]}],"19":[{"m":"Yieldedness. The Lord was bringing them up in the way of the spirit.","dt":"2022-03-01T19:19:21","s":["ca51062375"]}],"21":[{"m":"They journeyed, whether it was by day or by night 🌃; they were ever so yielded.\n\nI knew there was more to the divine hand of God upon these ones. The supernatural victories, the protection.\n\nThey couldn't be cursed, or any harm brought upon them.\n\nThey lived a fasted life, eating the bread from heaven — one-way food, which itself was a form of fast, a discipline of the flesh.","dt":"2022-03-01T19:23:13","s":["kpbfv0k2ia","945c5ed201"]}],"7":[{"m":"This is a typical example of “the law was made for man, not man for the law”.\n\nThough they had been defiled by the dead, they could not be denied partaking in the sabbath...\n\nThe law was modified to accommodate this.\n\nGod is just.\n\nSome say they had gone to bury the dead, according to Dake’s.\n\nSo then why should they be denied partaking when they were doing their due? Somebody has to bury the dead, so if they did, why are they being punished?\n\nAnd they were right and just, and this God made provision for.","dt":"2024-03-21T15:01:36","s":["th8qw03dxe","d4010b0617"]}]},"10":{"9":[{"m":"Interesting ritual. So you see the children of Israel blowing the trumpet during war and you presume it is a war cry, or to charge the people, but little do you know that it is a call.\n\nIt is a call to their God. And now suddenly the battle turns in their favour.\n\nThis reminds me of our traditional priests who dance during their rituals, shake some cowries here and there. Only they know the exact code or mystery of the gods they are communicating with.\n\nThis makes me wonder: if another person follows the exact same routine after careful study but does not know what it means, would they yield the same results?\n\nI don't know. Maybe, maybe not. Remember the gods are living, intelligent beings. Maybe they may choose to overlook the lack of knowledge and show up, or maybe, like any machine, once you follow the process and press any button it will respond as expected, even if you don't know what it was for. Once more, I don't know.","dt":"2026-03-02T05:49:53","s":["5xf38edw67"]}],"11":[{"m":"This pillar of cloud 🌥, and of fire 🔥, was literal and physical.\n\nWas that why the covering of the tent was not just of blue, scarlet 🧣 and fine linen, but also of badgers' and goats' skin? So it could physically hold the fire and the cloud 🌥 without being affected or marred.\n\nGod knew what he was going to do all along. That he would descend in literal fashion when all was said and done.\n\nLittle wonder his presence started affecting Moses. His entering the cloudy ⛅ and smoky mountain ⛰ and being in the presence of God changed him.","dt":"2024-04-13T07:10:56","s":["h3cigueivy","680979f515"]}],"12":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔, so he determined when the cloud 🌥 lifts, and where it settles, and how long it stays where it settles.\n\nOh, I know there is a reason, though it's not stated. I'd love 😍 to know why.","dt":"2024-03-22T05:04:19","s":["e14e252396"]}],"35":[{"m":"Who are they that hate thee... Is it not the workers 👷 of darkness and iniquity,\n\nwho will not serve the Lord?","dt":"2022-03-02T07:30:40","s":["4okorzyl7x"]},{"m":"Was this expression a mere chant and slogan, or was it a reflection of reality?\n\nWho were the enemies of God at this time?\n\nIsrael had had no wars, no attempted taking over of any nation, for them to have enemies.\n\nThey had left Egypt 🇪🇬, who was their chief enemy. So now in the wilderness, who was their enemy, for Moses to say at the rising of the Lord that his enemies be scattered?\n\nThe question 🙋 actually is: what accounted for God moving when he did?\n\nWhat was he seeing or foreseeing that made him cause all of Israel 🇮🇱 to change locations?\n\nKnowing God for who he is, there was intelligence and wisdom and design behind his movements.\n\nThey were not erratic. God, I believe, moved to test Israel 🇮🇱, to try them, and to keep them safe from invading enemies or plans of the enemy to invade these wanderers with no place they could call home 🏡.\n\nIt is actually possible, and more likely, that God moved to both save Israel from enemy nations who had heard of Israel's goal of returning to their land and destroying all current occupants.\n\nOf course no nation would sit aloof; some might attempt to invade them. Though 💭 the fear 😱 of God was upon the nations round about, so they mostly dared not attack.\n\nWho attacks a nation in whom God is visibly present and who had wrecked the mighty Egypt?\n\nAlso, in God's moving he could be saving Israel from invaders and at the same time testing their loyalty with lack, or even making provision for them in a miraculous way.\n\nIndeed the tests of God are actually not tests of lack but tests of his provisions.\n\nWhat initially seems like lack was actually divine provision and abundance. Just that the process that led to the provision involves suffering some lack for a while.","dt":"2024-04-13T08:04:16","s":["r6wlvoyvb1"]}]},"11":{"2":[{"m":"Why did the people cry to Moses? Why did they not cry out to the Lord themselves?\n\nThey did not know how to access God... Moses was their mediator — sad 😔, when that was not the initial plan.","dt":"2024-03-22T06:00:27","s":["2d1wi9b4ht"]},{"m":"Moses often pleaded for the people.\n\nOn Mount 🗻 Sinai, when God made up his mind to start a new nation with Moses,\n\nMoses advised God against it. Who was Moses to make suggestions to God? And interestingly, God did rescind his decision and heeded Moses's advice.\n\nThis tells us a lot about God and about us. We are indeed his sons, and sons do reason kingdom 👑 business with their father the king.\n\nEven when sons are not of age, their father is delighted to hear out their innocent counsel.\n\nAnd when they are of age, then truly their counsel is heeded.\n\nBut their father the king 👑 encourages them to speak up on kingdom matters and to reason with them. Indeed it delights him to hear their thoughts 💭 on issues.\n\nSo it is with us. Yet religion preaches things to the contrary.. So we fear 😱 God our father and we barely speak to him or reason things out.\n\nWe just cry and grope and plead always, and that has its place, as we saw with Moses, but there is the place of reasoning with the Lord, which most of us never do because of religious indoctrination and lack of knowledge of the Lord and who he is to us and we to him.","dt":"2024-04-13T08:59:23","s":["aeoczj7550"]}],"9":[{"m":"Oh, I wonder how it looked — not the manna, but when it appeared.\n\nI can imagine waking up early dawn before the dew settles and sitting to see the formation of the manna,\n\nwatching as the dew dried up, and as it did, the manna began forming.\n\nExodus 16:14 KJV\nAnd when the dew that lay was gone up, behold, upon the face of the wilderness there lay a small round thing, as small as the hoar frost on the ground.\n\nA whole new law of matter and water evaporation existed in the camp of Israel 🇮🇱 — their dew turned not into water vapour but into manna, the bread of angels.\n\nOh, how I would love to see that moment and the transformation right before my eyes 👀","dt":"2024-04-15T07:47:47","s":["m71uz95qav"]},{"m":"Here we are told the manna fell upon the dew.\n\nBut I don't think 🤔 it fell in the sense that you could see the manna dropping from heaven physically.\n\nTo the eyes 👀, it appeared on the dew out of the blue, and as the dew dried up you had the manna.\n\nExodus 16:14 KJV\nAnd when the dew that lay was gone up, behold, upon the face of the wilderness there lay a small round thing, as small as the hoar frost on the ground.\n\nSo combining all these pieces of information,\n\nwe see that the manna appeared with the dew, and just as you don't see the dew falling from heaven, so you do not see the manna fall.\n\nBut knowing the manna is from God, who is in heaven, and manna is the bread of angels 😇,\n\nit is right to describe it as falling on the earth from heaven 🌎, just as the dew falls on the earth.\n\nHowever, in appearance to the eyes 👀, it seems to appear when the dew appears, and especially as the dew dries up, the manna is revealed.\n\nThis is how we piece together scripture to derive interpretation and understanding.\n\nAnd I trust the Lord that he would give me understanding of the trinity also, with all the divers 🕊 seemingly contradictory scriptures.","dt":"2024-04-15T07:58:34","s":["n0sr1d07uf"]}],"21":[{"m":"The people wanted flesh to eat, but they had livestock. I don't get it.","dt":"2026-03-02T06:13:19","s":["xx4vjy4aqc"]}],"22":[{"m":"Moses had so gotten into God and his realm that he could have a face to face conversation and even question 🙋 the ways of God.","dt":"2022-03-02T08:50:46","s":["805b79f926"]}],"25":[{"m":"A few key 🗝 things to note 🗒:\n\n1. God came down 👇 into the cloud 🌥.\n\n2. God took of the spirit upon Moses.\n\n3. The spirit upon Moses was given to Moses by God; in other words, the spirit of God was upon Moses.\n\n4. That same spirit is now given among the 70, with the evidence of their prophesying.\n\n5. The same spirit is not divided into seventy parts just because he is upon 70 people, but that spirit is omnipresent and thus can rest on 70 people at a time.\n\n6. The one spirit gives them utterance in prophecy.\n\n7. God, who is spirit and gives his spirit to be upon Moses, at that same time speaks to Moses, and Moses speaks back to him.\n\n8. This is much like Jesus in Jordan during his baptism: the spirit descends upon Jesus and God speaks to Jesus.\n\n9. In point 7 we see a duality, whiles in 8 we see a trinity.\n\n10. Even though God's spirit is upon Moses and he teaches Moses the voice of God, justice, judgements, discernment etc., Moses recognizes that there is one God, and the fact of God's spirit upon him does not produce another God.\n\n11. The spirit is an extension of the many possibilities, powers and/or attributes of God, so he continues in his conversation with God.\n\n12. Same with Jesus, who often refers to, talks to and prays to the Father, though many times he also teaches about the spirit of the Father.\n\nGod is one, and he is Father, Son and Holy Spirit, but in the Old Testament he is Father and Spirit.\n\nAnother quick thought 💭.\n\nWhen God was on with Moses literally, and manifested even physically, who was on his throne? When God comes down in the cloud 🌥 and perpetually was with Israel 🇮🇱,\n\nwas his throne empty, or was he seated?\n\nGod is spirit, so he is omnipresent, and even his manifest presence, so called, can be at many places; indeed his manifest presence is omnipresent, or better put, can be omnipresent if he chooses to.","dt":"2024-04-15T08:48:04","s":["4fp008auzr","c1997f1145"]}],"34":[{"m":"Wasn't 1000 kilograms of meat, as some versions put it, a bit too much meat 🥩 for a month per household?\n\nThey were literally picking for months.\n\nThey doubted when again there would be such a miracle. And God saw their hearts 💕 and evil faithless ways...\n\nAnd he struck them.","dt":"2022-03-02T09:00:00","s":["c2l2rcm62e"]}],"28":[{"m":"One of the young men... I wonder, what was there about Joshua that first caught the eye 👁‍🗨 of Moses?\n\nDid he at one time make a bold statement of absolute trust in the Lord that caught his attention??","dt":"2022-03-02T08:53:16","s":["rbkvelu0wt","de7754f630"]}],"29":[{"m":"Wow, glory.\n\nAnd this desire is fulfilled in us as believers today.\n\nWe all have the spirit and we all do prophesy.","dt":"2024-04-15T08:49:19","s":["gur0frzhsb","7ujka916ub","5d6194b094"]}]},"12":{"2":[{"m":"Were they trying to say that Moses was taking too much upon himself and lording it over them,\n\ndespite the fact that he, Moses, had married 👰 a foreigner and a stranger, thus breaking the law of God?\n\nLikely they used his mixed marriage as a case against Moses, and maybe expected him to acknowledge that he had broken the law of God and thus was not an exemplary leader.\n\nThis was unfair, considering that Moses had married before even the law and his calling.\n\nWhy would they use that against their brother?\n\nMaybe they felt their junior brother had become too much for them; after all, God speaks to them as well.\n\nBut in this they were wrong, and were going to have a rude awakening when God educates them that there are realms of communication with God depending on your rank.\n\nAnd some men need to be feared by virtue of their intimacy with the Father, even if they are your brother.","dt":"2024-04-16T06:48:30","s":["a17bfd1584"]},{"m":"I am just wondering, why did Moses record all these happenings?\n\nI get it that he had to record the tabernacle's structure and how to build it, and the rituals, but the happenings and these events — why?\n\nIt was to preserve knowledge, wisdom and posterity.\n\nSo the future descendants would gain wisdom from the past and know where they came from and whose they are. That is in itself wisdom — penning down all these thoughts.","dt":"2026-03-02T19:44:03","s":["fc0d5jwr65"]}],"13":[{"m":"Heal her now — such audacity.... Oh my God, such intimacy. And at this realm of intimacy one cannot but get an answer.\n\nMoses was so intimate with God, God said, I will, but not now, maybe later. 😼\n\nI reckon that there is a certain realm and level of intimacy where it's like you asking your fellow man face to face to do you a favour.\n\nEven if he will not, he won't ignore you; you will get an answer of no, because of such and such.\n\nThere are times in prayer and fellowship where we experience such intimacy.\n\nFor Moses, he lived there. Always with God.\nAnd Jesus too.","dt":"2022-03-02T16:19:34","s":["wjemzv4zfi"]},{"m":"The relationship of Moses we have much to learn from, in terms of the ways and mind of God.\n\nMoses said to heal her now.\n\nIf it was some other person or prophet, the answer of no, as given in this case, would be realised when Miriam is not healed of her leprosy, and then one continues in prayer, and likely fasting, and realizes the answer on the seventh day.\n\nHowever, with Moses, whom the Lord speaks to mouth to mouth 👄,\nthe Lord tells him, I won't heal her now as you have requested, because I'm really mad 😡 about this situation and would let her be in this situation for a few days to drive home 🏡 the lesson.\n\nThat is relationship and intimacy.","dt":"2024-04-16T06:57:11","s":["ko6jzdiulq"]}],"14":[{"m":"This analogy is not just that, but truth.\n\nGod was their father, Miriam was a prophetess, and the Lord loved her as a father loves his daughter, but she needed to be corrected.\n\nWhat a relationship. This is mind-blowing.","dt":"2024-03-22T06:19:49","s":["1b9co3q8ul","0cba0455f2"]}],"8":[{"m":"He speaks to Moses mouth to mouth.\nSo literally God speaks and he answers, and he speaks and God also answers.\n\nHe was at that level with God.\n\nWhiles with others God just speaks, or even shows them pictures 🖼 and images and leaves them to ponder the meaning.\n\nIt is not less powerful or effective necessarily, but it is less intimate.\n\nAfter all, some sections of scripture came by such means, i.e. visions and dreams, and it does not make them less authentic.","dt":"2024-04-16T06:52:42","s":["e136dma2b8","a8dc9cde08"]}],"10":[{"m":"The Lord departed in anger, and in a sense from the leprosy that was immediately to come on Miriam.\n\nAll lepers were not to come into the congregation of the Lord, and with Miriam's leprosy as white as snow, our holy God departed.\n\nIn anger and in holiness.","dt":"2024-03-22T06:14:09","s":["1pnvh4mehh","08d474b4a2"]}],"15":[{"m":"She wasted everybody's time.\n\nThe Lord wanted her case to be public ridicule. Now everyone knew why they were not moving.\n\nThe whole nation is waiting for Miriam.\n\nThe Lord did this so she learns not to blaspheme next time.","dt":"2024-04-16T07:00:43","s":["07c23dab15"]}]},"13":{"28":[{"m":"God took them by a longer route, lest they see war and flee.\n\nYet after all this while of God teaching them his great wonders, they see not war but giants, and could already imagine defeat in war.\n\nThe children of Israel were just impossible 🙅.","dt":"2024-04-16T07:08:11","s":["km0n309jn8","3966671c42"]}],"32":[{"m":"Was this the faithlessness and faintness of heart ♥ the Lord was trying to change all this while?\n\nAlas, the people's hearts were still empty and devoid of God.\n\nThey rejected God and his promise, not through inability but through unbelief.","dt":"2022-03-02T09:17:56","s":["ohl2lr6ekv"]}],"2":[{"m":"How long after Miriam's leprosy were the spies sent out?\n\nIf not too long, then the lesson was really driven home 🏡.\n\nThat the people were just days away from the promised land and had to wait for the sister of Moses, for her disregard for God's servant.\n\nI can imagine the gossip and mockery going on from tent to tent 🎪.\n\nAnd these Israelites 🇮🇱, masters of murmurings even against God, would by no means spare Miriam.. God knew 😊 and wanted her to learn the lesson hard.","dt":"2024-04-16T07:03:44","s":["8e07c29e1e"]}]},"14":{"1":[{"m":"Yeah, I understand their weeping; now they were stuck in the wilderness.","dt":"2022-03-02T16:20:52","s":["c86a5d645b"]}],"3":[{"m":"Wait right there, something doesn't add up.\n\nWas not the sword upon them when Pharaoh came against them whilst hedged in by the sea 🌊?\n\nYes, the Lord delivered them mightily.\n\nThey had so soon forgotten. The problem with Israel 🇮🇱 was remembrance and faithlessness.\n\nWas it something in the culture, or the slave mentality?\n\nThey had been so used to oppression that they thought 💭 they wanted freedom but were not ready for it.\n\nSomething was wrong, and this affected the entire nation, save a handful of people.\n\nIs it not interesting that they who saw the miracles were unbelieving, yet their children 🧒, who never saw, or those who did but were young, rather could trust God enough to enter the promised land?","dt":"2024-04-17T06:19:58","s":["wwhtnezh52","c4041b2043"]}],"4":[{"m":"What was wrong with them? Something was wrong with them, mightily wrong with them.\n\nNo wonder God knew that even if they entered the promised land, they would not take it nor conquer what was rightfully theirs.\n\nMoses had already won the appeal not to destroy them all and start afresh with him.\n\nSo God did the same thing in a substituted way.\n\nHe made them stay outside the promised land and cut short their life span.\n\nSame thing: if he had killed them as earlier planned and Moses hadn't interrupted, then God would have had to wait till Moses and that generation grew and matured enough to be a matching army to conquer Canaan.\n\nGod executed the same plan, but in a more merciful fashion.\n\nJust like he swapped the first born of Israel 🇮🇱 for the Levites and lambs.\n\nIt's all about substitution. Substitution is an act of mercy and an acceptable form of appeasement of God.","dt":"2024-04-17T06:32:29","s":["4sp5ojk5w2","d8e3fea37b"]}],"10":[{"m":"How did it appear? I thought it was always there. Or did it suddenly glow brighter, or it came ever so often that it almost seemed it was permanently stationed there?\n\nEither way, it appeared out of nowhere.","dt":"2022-03-03T13:50:30","s":["kqt4ma53dh","2da40fda51"]}],"12":[{"m":"This is the second time God had made this statement...\n\nThe first being when they made the golden calf, after the Lord had given them the ten commandments himself by speaking audibly from the mountain ⛰.\n\nFor God to have made this statement at this point shows how hurt he was by them.\n\nHow could they turn back at this crucial stage?\n\nOf all times to be complaining and faithless,\n\nthis was not the time, not when they were this close.\n\nThey really hurt God.\n\nAnd now his mind was made up; he was going to disinherit them.","dt":"2024-04-17T07:38:34","s":["rvtyctryuc","64b3d7fe61"]},{"m":"What was God supposed to do? He had invested time, energy and resources, his power, to bring them out and lead them this far, but now they spoke of going back into slavery rather than fight for the freedom given them.\n\nGod knew that with this mindset, even if he forced them into the land, they would reject him and go a-whoring after the gods of the land. They were not going to stick with the Lord.\n\nThe whole nation was sick. God knew he couldn't make a nation and army he could call his own from these people. Don't forget they had made a golden calf not too long ago, when Moses delayed just a little in coming down from the mountain.\n\nIt is amazing God even used Aaron as high priest, a man who built the people a golden calf and couldn't stand his ground.\n\nBut he had proved to be useful. We just have to use and work with people despite their flaws.","dt":"2026-03-04T05:19:08","s":["gsxnewrjvc"]}],"22":[{"m":"Eiiii, God was taking count and disinherited the people.\n\nAccording to Moses' own words, if he killed them all at once, as one man (vs 15), he would be doubted, so he killed them over a 30-year span.","dt":"2022-03-03T13:53:20","s":["73agz2e26e","7b7b8038a1"]}],"24":[{"m":"So this is how we possess the land: fully following the Lord.","dt":"2022-03-06T09:58:23","s":["3a4f08ccae"]}],"34":[{"m":"🙁 Hm... Ye shall know my breach of promise. God is not a machine or a senseless idol.\n\nHe is real. He does not get up and swear 🤬 senselessly, without conditions.\n\nHe reveals another aspect of him.\n\nThe God who breaches his promise. Though it really took a lot of provoking for him to get to that point.","dt":"2022-03-06T10:01:29","s":["0ec33j6sje","0260123f1c"]}],"16":[{"m":"The situation was terrible 😰, but it had to be managed.\n\nMoses reminded God of what the other nations had heard of:\n\nhow the Lord was visibly in the midst of his people by day and by night 🌃.\n\nIf he killed them as he wanted to, the people would not blame the Israelites but would say he, God, was incapable. A very painful untruth.\n\nBut who was God going to explain it to?\n\nWho would believe it — that it was the people who were incapable and not their God?\n\nIn that light, though painful, God had to endure the people again.\n\nHe had to feed this faithless people with the bread 🥪 of angels.\n\nThey were not worthy, but to save face he had to.\n\nOh my, the things that are happening in the corridors of power and in leadership just to save face.\n\nOnly God knows. This feels like living with an unfaithful spouse, who continues to scorn you by lewdness and fornication, yet to keep the marriage and the children etc. you stay.\n\nIt was like rape — Israel enjoying pleasure and the blessings and the cloud 🌥 cover and the glory of the Lord, and in that pleasure they inflict pain,\n\nterrible pain on the Lord.\n\nOh, our God is indeed very humble — how he could destroy these folks and start afresh, yet he chose to keep the system working ⚒ and live and relate with man as a father and son is unfathomable.","dt":"2024-04-17T07:49:49","s":["xezx3gccel","32077c525c"]}],"7":[{"m":"These Israelites were messing up this long-awaited dream of Joshua and Caleb.\n\nHere they were, with an opportunity of a lifetime to make a name for themselves and their children,\n\netching their names forever in the sands of time,\n\ninheriting whole lands and territories — and these people just couldn't see it and were hindering Joshua and Caleb.\n\nBecause Joshua and Caleb were subject to a system. A system set up by God; the delay of the system was the delay of all, including Caleb and Joshua.\n\nThe system was delayed by a further 38 years, and thus Joshua and Caleb were also delayed by 38 years.\n\nImagine that — that because of human flaws and sluggishness others are delayed terribly.\n\nBut God is faithful, who cannot be mocked; he catches the wicked in their schemes.\n\nHe helped these young Hebrew men (in their forties actually) and kept them young in strength 💪.\n\nSo though it seemed they were delayed, their strength 💪 remained intact for war, both for going out and coming in.\n\nJoshua 14:11 KJV\nAs yet I am as strong this day as I was in the day that Moses sent me: as my strength was then, even so is my strength now, for war, both to go out, and to come in.\n\nSo it doesn't matter the system you are subject to.\n\nGod is faithful, who also will do it and fulfil his promise.\n\n1 Thessalonians 5:24 KJV\nFaithful is he that calleth you, who also will do it.","dt":"2024-04-17T06:42:49","s":["19960612e8"]}],"25":[{"m":"Kai, back to the Red Sea 🌊 🤯. The journey was over. The quest was done.\n\nGod was done with them. He had decided and would not relent: they will not inherit Canaan.\n\nYes, though he would not kill them immediately, as he thought to, because his mercy is great, yet they would not inherit the land.\n\nBoth mercy and judgement were meted to Israel 🇮🇱 at this point.","dt":"2024-04-17T07:52:27","s":["4dd318e2d8"]}]},"15":{"39":[{"m":"The people were to keep the law of God constantly before their eyes 👀 so they obey it.\n\nGod recognizes that what is before a man's eyes and within his environment tends to influence him, whether he likes it or not.\n\n1 Corinthians 15:33 NASB\nDo not be deceived: “Bad company corrupts good morals.”\n\nThat is why we must use this principle and create the right environment and block out the negatives, to enable us to obey the Lord.\n\nIt is also one of the reasons we struggle so much. The enemies of God have worked their way and dominated the environment.\n\nThus we are often led to do the works of the devil 👿, the system of this world 🗺, though in our hearts we do not want to.\n\nAnd we continue to fruitlessly fight sins and battle our weaknesses, whiles yet remaining in the same environment.\n\nWe won't win that way... It's ignorance and self-delusion.\n\nThe portrayal of strength is not being in the wrong environment and forcing to overcome it...\nbut garnering the strength 💪 and discipline to leave the wrong environment and establish oneself deep in the right environment.\n\nIt's all about what we put before our eyes 👀","dt":"2024-04-18T06:57:34","s":["mjrggzt0cz","9fc006d000"]}],"31":[{"m":"Interesting, God continued to give them laws and to instruct them, though they had been rejected and would not inherit the promised land.\n\nBut at least their children would, so it was important to drum home the point.","dt":"2024-04-18T06:37:33","s":["1wcrwbwfpb","1c998bac36"]}],"36":[{"m":"Hmmm... Looks very harsh... Just for gathering sticks.\n\nBut if you look at the context, it was to set a precedent and leave no room for insolence.\n\nThese were a people who saw God visibly; it was not some make-believe.\n\nThey saw the cloud 🌥 by day and fire 🔥 by night.\n\nAnd now this visible, obvious God says not to do something, and you blatantly go ahead, whiles his divine presence blazed visibly, and break his laws.\n\nAside this, the man was not killed immediately, but rather brought before the Lord, who is just.\n\nHe knows the heart, and seeing the heart of this man, he passes justice. We believe his judgements to be right and deserving.","dt":"2024-04-18T06:38:04","s":["u4onw20p08","01dea3ca22"]}]},"16":{"14":[{"m":"Moses was put in a very difficult situation.\n\nIndeed the words of these men carry a semblance of truth.\n\nThey were not in the promised land and they knew they were going to die in the wilderness,\n\nall because of their rebellion when the opportunity was ripe.\n\nThey had brought it upon themselves, and they were only blaming Moses for it.\n\nThey were Levites; they should have taken it up with the Lord.\n\nMoses was the front for God, and God had really put him in a difficult situation.\n\nThere was no reason to listen to Moses, because now the reason for following him all this while was gone.\n\nHow was Moses to govern them? I can imagine the rumors and insults behind his back.\n\nAnd we can sense the conversations they had had in time past from the response of these two men.\n\nNow they had grown so stubborn they told Moses to his face the things they spoke of in his absence..\n\nMoses often pleaded with God for the people, and in this case, though not recorded, I'm sure he went to God time and again to reconsider his decision, or at least reduce the 40 years.\n\nAnd time and again he refused.\n\nThe other thing is, so long as God refused, Moses had to live with reproach like this.\n\nI'm sure he had heard such statements, but it hadn't blown up like this. It was only a matter of time.\n\nAnd now here we are... Open rebellion, towards God and the man of God, Moses.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:20:33","s":["kcgbqk0kcg","68b31797df"]}],"21":[{"m":"Did these rebellious ones hear when the Lord spoke to both Moses and Aaron?\n\nI doubt they did. Next thing they knew, they were consumed. Without warning, seemingly.\n\nThe Lord had acted shrewdly with them.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:39:20","s":["acb87e93ea"]}],"46":[{"m":"How did Moses know this???\n\nIt means Moses not only knew the ordinances and ceremonies but understood why, and what they symbolize.","dt":"2022-03-06T17:52:46","s":["nnl4ub5qdf"]},{"m":"We are not told that the Lord told Moses this... But somehow he knew, and knew what to do about it...\n\nHow did he know?","dt":"2024-04-18T07:43:09","s":["wp08ywmegj"]},{"m":"How come they were all before the presence of the Lord, before the tabernacle, yet Moses by discernment knew that a plague had begun, and also knew how to stop the plague?\n\nThis was because the Lord had shown him. Moses was indeed the prophet and chosen one of the Lord. The Lord really loved him and chose him.","dt":"2026-03-04T06:04:44","s":["kxc2t8u6u"]}],"1":[{"m":"This genealogy, and that of others traced to their fathers, shows that Israel 🇮🇱 was not in slavery 400 years, though they sojourned from Abraham to the exodus 430 years.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:04:18","s":["jy9a7xb055","a1a865397d"]}],"42":[{"m":"Oh.. It has appeared again.\n\nThough the presence of the Lord was constantly dwelling in the tabernacle... it did not always appear for them to see.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:38:11","s":["59keoxj5s6","214bb71c24"]}],"43":[{"m":"It seemed that the appearance of the glory was a summoning to Moses and Aaron.\n\nWhen God shows up it is for a purpose, and it is important we discern the move and stirring of God in our hearts 💕.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:40:37","s":["2jhazixh1k","f0168aee07"]}],"5":[{"m":"This lesson Miriam and Aaron had learnt long ago, but these seem not to have learnt it, or had forgotten.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:09:07","s":["444a6a556f"]}]},"17":{"2":[{"m":"After how many years in the wilderness did these rebellions start?","dt":"2024-04-18T08:22:20","s":["73n3rixfyi","26ce8aed9d"]}],"7":[{"m":"Where did this also come from?\n\nI guess they never heard from the Lord for themselves.\n\nThey were there, and Moses and Aaron came and said, this is what God said.\n\nI think, several years having passed, someone suddenly had an aha moment and thought 💭, don't you think these two brothers came up with this whole Aaronic priesthood thing to lord it over them?\n\nNo wonder Moses bowed down his head in wonder when they challenged him. “Seemeth it a light thing” that you even serve in the Tabernacle of the Lord?\n\nHe, Moses, understood these things.","dt":"2022-03-06T18:00:39","s":["vxmx7nil52","eb39016ce9"]}],"13":[{"m":"Ei!\n\nThese Israelites 🇮🇱 and their constant complaints.","dt":"2024-04-18T08:29:07","s":["519c17c111"]}],"8":[{"m":"😊","dt":"2022-03-06T18:01:04","s":["hszumezuz9","e013386d9e"]}]},"18":{"11":[{"m":"A statute of the most holy things.\n\nSo the statutes are in reference to the ceremonies and rites of the Lord. I need to study more to be conclusive on this thought 💭","dt":"2024-04-18T09:06:21","s":["vz9zedhbyf","093ef93074"]}],"26":[{"m":"Does that mean the Levites did not have any — or should I say, they did not do any form of farming or any work in the fields themselves — because they were partaking of what the children of Israel, or the rest of the children of Israel, offered them?\n\nCome to think of it, I don't think the Levites were prevented from doing any work or owning any business by themselves at all. I think rather, for their labour or their service, and for the offering up of their time in serving in the sanctuary, they had to be paid in a sense for the use of their time, for the use of their strengths 💪.\n\nBecause obviously they could have used that time and that strength to be doing something else which would have brought them some profit, so to make up for that time and that service they received of the tithes and partook in the sacrifices.\n\nSo in essence I believe they also had their own businesses, their own farms, and other things that they owned, because I don't see it clearly stated that they couldn't own anything or any property.\n\nThe only thing clearly stated with regards to inheritance was that they didn't have any portion in the land, and their portion was what was given to them by the children of Israel 🇮🇱; but they themselves as a tribe did not have their own property.","dt":"2024-04-18T10:00:15","s":["4zkwmtyj2l","49fadff2ff"]}],"13":[{"m":"Wow, the priesthood was indeed a very noble and privileged position to find yourself in.\n\nNot only were they close to God, and not only did they have the privilege of drawing close to God, or being closer than any of the other children of Israel, but they had the privilege of enjoying the best of the land, the privilege of enjoying the very first of the fruits of labour of the children of Israel. And aside fruits, when it even comes to the sacrifices offered to the Lord, be it of sheep or herd etc., it had to be without blemish.\n\nThey were the best and the finest; indeed the priesthood, the Levites, were very privileged.\n\nIt was this privileged position that Moses made them understand when they rose up in rebellion against Moses:\n\nthat the Lord had drawn them so closely to himself, and that was not to be taken for granted.","dt":"2024-04-18T09:19:31","s":["90ojc0b9sk","e7c258ff58"]}]},"19":{"16":[{"m":"Okay, I now understand where that law regarding the Nazarite comes from, because in that law God tells the Nazarite that he shall not mourn even for his own dead relative — for his parents, for his siblings — because in mourning definitely you would come close to those you mourn for.\n\nYou will touch the things of the dead, and that would make the Nazarite unclean, and per the law of the Nazarite one shall not make himself or herself unclean for the dead.\n\nSo I get the connection now, in the sense that as you try to mourn for your dead family or relative, you definitely will come in contact with the dead, and if you do, that would make you unclean; and as you see in this case, uncleanliness for coming in contact with the dead is for 7 days. And if you are under a Nazarite vow you cannot be unclean; you cannot mourn the dead.\n\nLess so to think of becoming unclean for as long as 7 days — 7 long days — for the dead.","dt":"2024-04-18T10:09:08","s":["yatiayvdcq","a87e933551"]}]},"20":{"1":[{"m":"Often when they came to a desert, something like this in the subsequent verse would happen,\n\nbecause a desert 🦂 is naturally the place of hunger and thirst.\n\nThey should have gotten the pattern by now, that God will take them through either way.\n\nBut no, they never learnt.","dt":"2022-03-07T06:13:32","s":["dcabe1d1b8"]}],"3":[{"m":"These guys have a character of sarcasm and such gross disrespect.\n\nAnytime they were pushed to the wall and tested, they spoke so badly.\n\nI mean, how can you say that you should have died like your brethren, knowing very well that God is in the camp and would hear and get angry 😡?\n\nAt least complain with some respect.","dt":"2022-03-07T06:11:12","s":["gx9ae6n651"]},{"m":"This time they were no longer making reference to Egypt 🇪🇬.\n\nThough they did a few verses later.","dt":"2024-04-18T10:11:49","s":["5t6ybepp6r"]}],"12":[{"m":"How does this translate into unbelief? Looks more like disobedience. Or could it be that behind this act of disobedience was unbelief?","dt":"2022-03-07T06:17:37","s":["tczq3xfeka","165e183e7d"]}],"29":[{"m":"All the greats were leaving the scene one by one, and in our times also the greats shall pass on, one after the next.","dt":"2026-03-05T05:48:07","s":["1dwvb2cevz"]}],"5":[{"m":"This complaint never left them, even after all these years and punishments.\n\nThey pestered Moses and Aaron so much that they erred in their obedience to the Lord.","dt":"2026-03-05T05:22:16","s":["wxute3qeb"]}],"24":[{"m":"These men had literally become divine.\n\nThey were going to live until the word of the Lord was fulfilled, no matter how long it took.\n\nBut now, alas, the Lord called Aaron.","dt":"2024-04-18T10:15:09","s":["9fe0345aa2"]}]},"21":{"3":[{"m":"And the Lord hearkened to their voice. Why?\n\nBecause it tallied with the plan of God. They had aligned right with God.\n\nThe invasion of the promised land was God's idea 💡 in the first place, and now there comes a people who wanted the same thing as God.\n\nAnd indeed it was further fuelled ⛽ by the capture of their brethren.\n\nIt is interesting that God watched on as some of them, the chosen people of God, were captured.\n\nHow? Impossible 🙅. God's darling choice Israel 🇮🇱 captured?? 😳. Were they not doing the work of God? Was not this whole journey sanctioned by him? How could they be taken prisoners..?\n\nAnd it would have remained so if they did nothing. It kind of aligns with the book of Acts, when James was captured and nothing was done.\n\nThen he was beheaded. Now Peter too was captured, and constant prayers were offered for him by the church.\n\nActs 12:5 KJV\nPeter therefore was kept in prison: but prayer was made without ceasing of the church unto God for him.","dt":"2022-03-04T02:51:27","s":["k827xarw81"]}],"5":[{"m":"Could it be that some of the people actually died because of the difficulty of the journey and the lack of food and water 💦?\n\nVery plausible, and it might well have been a strategy to continue killing the people as the forty years drew nigh.","dt":"2024-04-18T10:20:10","s":["0de7e85edf"]}],"10":[{"m":"What was the point of complaining, when it would not yield any benefit but suffering? At the end of it all they still had to continue the journey to their destination, and their complaining was pointless; indeed it was detrimental, because many of them died because of their murmurings.\n\nGod dealt with them by a strong hand; it looked like God wanted to just rid the earth of them, as he had promised.\n\nHe had wanted to kill them all at once, but Moses pleaded for mercy, so he let them wander for 40 years, and in those days of wandering he killed them all and left their children. They died, but over a time frame instead of all at once.\n\nIt was mercy in a sense — their punishment was deferred.\n\nI wonder if the serpents bit specifically the complainants only — the scripture is silent on that though.","dt":"2026-03-05T05:56:03","s":["16av1fn874"]}],"35":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔, interesting.\n\nThis time it was not captivity that triggered the war and victory, but a direct attack.\n\nEither way, God got himself the victory and his name glorified.\n\nSo in crises, unexpected 😱 or pending doom, whatever the challenge, it's all for his glory.\n\nAmen","dt":"2022-03-04T03:02:21","s":["5fed8b0314"]}]},"22":{"7":[{"m":"It's very interesting that Moses, also a man of God, penned these exact same words concerning another man of God, Balaam.\n\nThat men came to see him with the reward of 📦 divination 🔮 in their hands 👐","dt":"2023-12-18T10:27:55","s":["c080397f60"]}],"8":[{"m":"Wait, how did he know that the Lord would speak by morning, unless of course he had regular daily communion with him, or he had done this consultation for others ever so often and God showed up every time?","dt":"2022-03-04T05:34:53","s":["27621824e9"]}],"9":[{"m":"Balaam consulted with God. Balaam was not of Israel, yet he knew the Lord.\n\nHe was a revered and feared 😱 man of God, or as the heathen understood it, one whose curses 🤬 and blessings 🙌 came to pass.\n\nBear in mind that the book of Numbers was written by Moses — Moses the great prophet and proponent of the Law and the Old Testament.\n\nThis Moses, great and mighty prince 🤴 in Israel 🇮🇱, was here writing about another,\n\nanother man of God who sought to resist Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nA kingdom 👑 divided against itself shall not stand, and so God hindered Balaam.\n\nBut it is interesting to note that these two great men of God lived and encountered each other in this dispensation.\n\nThere are some who say he was not of God.\n\nI beg to differ. All the nations of the promised land were pagans and consulted idols and divined 🔮 perpetually.\n\nWith which of them did the Lord consult before doing anything? None on record. Do you think the occult powers of these nations did not curse Israel 🇮🇱?\n\nOf course they did.\n\nBut now here comes a man coming to curse a people from Egypt 🇪🇬 in the name of the Lord, and the Lord had to intervene.\n\nWhy do such, if Balaam was no man of God?\n\nBehold, there is a people come out of Egypt, which covereth the face of the earth: come now, curse me them; peradventure I shall be able to overcome them, and drive them out.\nNumbers 22:11 KJV","dt":"2023-12-18T07:17:20","s":["uyoectmxdc","f552429f34"]}],"18":[{"m":"He knew that the realm of the spirit was not subject to his beck and call.\n\nIt was subject to the spirits, and here, God himself.","dt":"2022-03-04T06:28:20","s":["66d6af609e"]},{"m":"When and how did Balaam gain the reputation of one who is able to curse and one who is able to bless?\n\nYes, we all do know that prophets carry such power, but Balaam seems to be specially noted for possessing such abilities. This is not a typical way prophets of God are described.\n\nAnd especially for a heathen nation and king to think of buying for his perusal such abilities — it casts a lot of shadow on the reputation of Balaam.\n\nSome say he was a soothsayer and diviner, and others a prophet of God who was just ambitious for money. Either way, he had a relationship with God, and his source of prophecy and modus operandi relied on the God of Israel.","dt":"2026-03-05T08:53:17","s":["738i5f0l2z"]}],"22":[{"m":"Ah, I don't get it — was it not God who gave the approval?\n\nDid he expect him to disobey? Does that mean God expected some form of unwillingness on Balaam's part to go..\n\nHis heart ♥ was not right with God, even though God had released him to go.\n\nJust like he gave Israel 🇮🇱 meat 🥩 to eat, yet he plagued them for eating.\n\nLord have mercy. Be careful of God's yes, when you know his word and will in a matter yet insist on your way,\n\nlest he disapprove of you.","dt":"2022-03-04T06:30:07","s":["e04l7z6afu","5d7ca5229f"]}],"28":[{"m":"🤔 Is this the garden of Eden? Is that a talking animal, like the talking snake 🐍 of Eden?\n\nYou know many have suggested that Eden's events were just figurative. Fair enough, we know animals don't talk and can't reason logically.\n\nBut is that really true? The fact that they don't think in a complex manner does not mean they can't reason at all, nor talk logically if they could.\n\nThink 🤔 about this: if your dog 🐶 could talk, what would it say when hungry, or when a stranger comes to your compound?\n\nWould it not say, I am hungry, or I smell someone I don't know?\n\nHow difficult is that? We have either lost our ability to hear them talk, or, as illustrated here, they have lost the ability to talk. Rather they gesture.\n\nCould it be that there was much communication in Eden?\n\nOh, one can imagine after the fall, and much to the shock of Adam, that all the animals came out mute 🔕.\n\nHe asks for something and they can't understand nor talk back.\n\nToday we train dogs to go pick sticks, balls, search luggage etc. And they do this pretty intelligently.\n\nSomething in the fall just deprived them of the talking ability.","dt":"2022-03-06T01:58:17","s":["87bxcsply0","e4c67ebaab"]}],"29":[{"m":"And Balaam answered? Did he not fear 😱? He indeed was a man of the spirit and had seen many things and understood many spiritual things.","dt":"2023-12-18T07:39:45","s":["5a977a15b7"]}],"32":[{"m":"Great, so that confirms it. It was to protect the donkey that the angel moved, in verses 25 and 26, though he had Balaam cornered.\n\n'Cos if he stood, the donkey, known for their stubbornness, would not move, and Balaam would surely have continued hurting the beast.","dt":"2023-12-18T09:44:31","s":["bltsguzdxy","9f378ab11d"]}],"34":[{"m":"So the thing displeased the Lord the whole time ⌚.\n\nSo though Balaam heard the words “go” from the Lord, the Lord was not really pleased with Balaam's disposition; hence he even sent an angel 😇 to kill him.\n\nA yes from the Lord in this case — and I guess it can repeat itself sometimes — does not mean it's his best intention.","dt":"2022-03-06T02:02:16","s":["cce1d00710"]}],"37":[{"m":"Why did Balak send to attend to this war with Israel 🇮🇱 spiritually?\n\nHad they seen something about Israel 🇮🇱 that suggested that they had spiritual backing?\n\nObviously word had gone out how that Israel's God was with them in all their battles.\n\nHe was wise enough to seek spiritual support.","dt":"2024-04-18T10:47:25","s":["3b66aad75e"]}],"41":[{"m":"Oh man of God, what are you doing here, of all places... What was Balaam doing in the high places of Baal, he who was a man of God?","dt":"2024-04-18T10:48:52","s":["4odsrdrgjz","297dd55ab1"]},{"m":"What was the significance of him showing the utmost part of the people? Because later Balak chooses to let Balaam see just some part of the crowd, so he could curse those people, or that section.\n\nIt seemed Balak felt the reason the curse was turned to a blessing was because he saw the entire nation. I don't understand the spiritual knowledge Balak had, or where he got this idea from. But it did not change a thing.\n\nMaybe in the dark kingdom that was how it worked: if the curse does not work on the entire nation, maybe the enchantment is not strong enough.\n\nSo you target a section of it that the enchantment can handle.","dt":"2026-03-07T08:55:59","s":["2lpuat7fib"]}],"12":[{"m":"By implication, if you are not blessed 🌾, then you deserve, or at least qualify for, a curse.\n\nIt's akin to “he that hath, more will be added”, but he that hath not a blessing, even a curse will be given him.\n\nLife is so not fair: to the blessed, a curse passes over him and he gets more blessed, or at least exempted from the curse,\n\nbut to the ordinary man who has not, even the little is taken away.\n\nHow sad 😔. This life.\n\nMatthew 13:12 KJV\nFor whosoever hath, to him shall be given, and he shall have more abundance: but whosoever hath not, from him shall be taken away even that he hath.","dt":"2022-03-04T06:26:49","s":["fxexisw5jo"]},{"m":"A blessed people must not be cursed 🤬.\n\nIt is an abomination, and not permitted nor proper, for a blessed person to be cursed 🤬.\n\nThat does not mean it cannot happen, but it is not permitted.\n\nIt is hindered, and so we see that as Balak attempted to, he was hindered; he was not permitted.","dt":"2023-12-18T07:04:37","s":["figlqz6r44"]}],"25":[{"m":"It seems the angel went further to prevent Balaam from continuing to hurt the poor animal.","dt":"2023-12-18T07:32:10","s":["13b9329977"]}]},"23":{"1":[{"m":"Who taught him this? How did he know to do this?\n\nHad he done this in time prior? One thing I know:\n\nGod instructed him to.. Whether when they were on their way or in time past, this was a knowledge he had gleaned.","dt":"2023-12-18T10:30:51","s":["7480b2ff39"]}],"3":[{"m":"He, Balaam, could not guarantee that God would meet him; he said, “if peradventure”.\n\nBecause by experience he knew that God shows up when he, God, wants to.\n\nNo one can claim sole control 🎮 over God.\n\nYes, by virtue of relationship one can be sure he is likely to show up or honour your call 🤙.\n\nBut be keenly aware that he is a king 👑, and the prerogative to turn down your request for fellowship still remains his.\n\nThough as sons he doesn't reject fellowship, but he comes on his terms, but there again it's built on relationship.\n\nHe who has an ear 👂, let him hear.","dt":"2023-12-18T10:33:24","s":["gmwi0xnf5s"]},{"m":"He, Balaam, went to an even higher place where he could meet God.\n\nBalaam knew that spirits are secretive. They must be sought for in quiet 🤫 places, and they reveal themselves in signs, patterns and mysteries.\n\nI have met the spirit many times and I know this truth.","dt":"2023-12-18T10:42:47","s":["m89dbp916l"]},{"m":"Peradventure — Balaam had done what was required by way of preparing an altar and sacrifices.\n\nHe even told God that when he met him in verse 4.\n\nMeaning he had fulfilled all that was required for God to meet with him.\n\nBut even then there were no guarantees with God.\n\nIn meeting God there are no guarantees he would show up; you have to do your part to start with, to fulfil the first requirement of sacrifice.\n\nThe second step Balaam took was to go up. He separated himself from the people, because, as God is wont to do, he does not do mass showing up except to demonstrate his power etc.\n\nBut to speak his word, he does so to his prophets in secret, and then they come up to the open 🔓 to declare it.\n\nThe step of God showing up is up to God, and so here Balaam did his part and now waited on the Lord, and he did show up.","dt":"2024-04-19T07:40:46","s":["2dcsx9qj6d"]}],"4":[{"m":"Why tell God this? It was almost as if he was saying to God, I have done what you asked me to do, and in response God gave him a word.\n\nSo then it goes to show that God blesses or curses 🤬, and if God be for you, you are protected from every curse and utterance not from him.\n\nBut if not, woe to you. You shall be cursed 🤬","dt":"2023-12-18T10:35:40","s":["a9788ab3b0"]}],"5":[{"m":"Could we then say that as believers and spiritual Israel 🇮🇱, many have sought by divination to curse us and destroy us, but the Lord hindered them?\n\nBut I have also seen many believers cursed 🤬 and suffer from it. So then the question 🙋 becomes, what kind of believer is cursable?\n\nWhat happened for such a curse to work?\n\nIndeed, using Israel as the prototype, we see how Ai defeated them because they lost alignment and there was an accursed thing in their midst.\n\nSo we must align. Even after we are cursed 🤬, we can recover position through alignment, but then, like the battle with Ai, you will lose something — your time, respect, untold suffering within your trials.","dt":"2023-12-18T10:40:18","s":["3411a38dcb"]}],"7":[{"m":"How did Balaam know this history of the Jews? Oh, could it be that Jacob's greatness and fame in this exact same region had spread far and wide?\n\nBut then again, this was many centuries ago.\n\nWhatever the case may be, Balaam was acquainted with the history of this people whom he had been hired to curse 🤬","dt":"2023-12-20T06:49:51","s":["89cac9280b"]}],"8":[{"m":"There was no way around it: the one whom God had not cursed 🤬 could not be cursed 🤬.\n\nGod was using this as an example to all nations, that his people are sacred and called unto him as a peculiar race, to show forth the glory and life of God to all the earth 🌎.\n\nPeople would take notice of this peculiar treasure that Israel 🇮🇱 had and be converted to the God of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nIsrael 🇮🇱 was on stage; the nations were watching.","dt":"2023-12-20T06:53:18","s":["f7a099ab0e"]}],"10":[{"m":"This was not to be fulfilled, as he loved the wages of mammon more than the treasures of eternal life.\n\nHe did not have faith, unlike Moses, who did esteem the treasures and honor of Egypt a light thing for the glory and life of God,\n\nchoosing rather to suffer affliction with the people of God than to enjoy the pleasures of sin for a moment.\n\nInterestingly, this same Moses did pen this story and saw the latter end of Balaam, and it was not at all glorious.\n\nHe was killed along with these faithless princes of Moab, whom he chose to help and stand with.","dt":"2023-12-20T06:59:38","s":["5e2ac73d2e"]}],"12":[{"m":"It's interesting: just as Balaam followed the instructions of God, he still rejected HIS ways and sought ways around the will of God.\n\nHow did he become a prophet when he was so shrewd and sought ways in the books to hurt God's people?\n\nIt was because he, Balaam, had the gift — the gift of a prophet — and followed the disciplines required to stir up and grow the gifting 📦, yet his heart ♥ was not fully with the Lord.\n\nAnd there are many such Balaams in the church ⛪","dt":"2023-12-20T07:04:13","s":["8lh6epi6kt","44ae7888f9"]}],"13":[{"m":"He, Balak, seems also to have some spiritual knowledge of his own.\n\nElse why would he call for a mystic in the first place?","dt":"2022-03-06T09:09:39","s":["7f07kqnzxs"]},{"m":"And he, Balak, probably had this knowledge from previous encounters with the spiritual, or he just reckoned that a step-by-step strategy of pronouncing curses 🤬 from different angles might yield the desired results.\n\nBut this takes us back to the first assertion 🙋. How had he had previous knowledge?","dt":"2023-12-20T07:08:05","s":["a794jnxg44"]}],"14":[{"m":"This venture was quite labour-intensive as well as financially demanding.\n\nThat is why it is called a sacrifice, and spirits require it for access.","dt":"2023-12-20T07:09:24","s":["vacl3yu6hl"]},{"m":"For us believers today, Christ has made the ultimate sacrifice of his body and blood, but we must make time and fast and wait and focus expectantly whiles waiting.\n\nYet we would not.","dt":"2023-12-20T07:12:46","s":["72q5q1bvna"]}],"15":[{"m":"Here again he goes yonder; how long this whole exercise took we are not told.\n\nThe time between one curse and the next we can only guesstimate.","dt":"2023-12-20T07:14:32","s":["0f56cfced8"]}],"16":[{"m":"It is only when he met with God and got a word that he spoke, and then those words carried power.\n\nHe did not just speak his own goodly words; those would have only carried human power.\n\nBut for it to carry spirit power, the words should be inspired.\n\nThis is wisdom for us 🙏","dt":"2023-12-20T07:17:19","s":["c3dca98206"]}],"17":[{"m":"Why the term “behold”? He stood by his offering as if it was not expected that he would still be there in attention.\n\nThis seems to suggest that it took a while for Balaam to get a word from the Lord and come back.\n\nYet Balak also remained steadfast and waited earnestly on the man of God, hence the statement,\n\n“behold, he stood by his offering”.","dt":"2023-12-20T07:20:18","s":["4b21757efe"]}],"18":[{"m":"Once the Lord had spoken, he feared no man 👨... He did not save face, for he knew the terrible one so well.\n\nLORD, HELP ME FEAR AND KNOW YOU, I PRAY PLS 🙏","dt":"2022-03-06T09:11:05","s":["35ag1ovtye","1910d0360f"]}],"19":[{"m":"So this is where the context of this all-popular scripture is from.\n\nGod had given commandment to bless and not curse in the first encounter, and now Balak tries again by changing strategy, but God sends to tell him that he, God, is not a man that he should lie or repent.\n\nHe will not change his mind concerning Israel.\n\nSee the mindset and determination of a pagan king 👑. He knew that his gods would fail him against the God of 🇮🇱 Israel — the fall of Jericho and Ammon, whose gods were probably greater or the same as that of Moab.\n\nSo he sought help from the Most High himself, pleading 🙏 with him to change his mind concerning Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nHis gods were incapacitated to help here.\n\nSo, like all men, he sought higher power.\n\nSo if the Church ⛪ fails in its mandate, the people, though the people of God, would resort to higher power.\n\nThis is why discipleship and spiritual training is vitally important.","dt":"2023-12-20T07:28:59","s":["uzp7etnx3u"]},{"m":"Balak left his gods and pleaded with the Odumankuma himself, and yet sadly, because the church ⛪ today has forsaken our rock, we leave our rock — God Most High — to seek smaller gods.\n\nWhat is wrong with us?\n\nNow this begs the question 🙋: did Balak know that Balaam called on the same God as did Israel 🇮🇱?\n\nHe, Balak, had his gods, but he knew that the God of Balaam never failed.\n\nAnd now comes Israel, who serve the LORD, the I AM, and now Balak sends for the highest power he knew, i.e. the God of Balaam, who never disappoints.\n\nI believe Balak got informed, likely by Balaam, that he served the same God, and that Israel 🇮🇱 was God's people.\n\nSo to overcome Israel he had to win the God of Israel 🇮🇱 to his side.\n\nBut our God is not like other gods; we are his children 🧒 and the sheep 🐑 of his pasture.\n\nNo father would sell his children.\n\nWhat offer can you make to a father for him to abandon and destroy his own seed 🌱?\n\nBalak's offering and riches could buy man, and could even buy the prophet Balaam, but not God.\n\nMen, these men Balaam and Balak were indeed very shrewd — so shrewd they played their cards well and prevailed against God and Israel 🇮🇱,\n\nin the sense that through knowledge and seduction they lured Israel 🇮🇱 to go and act against their own God — Jehovah — by committing orgies with the daughters of Moab.\n\nThat was how these men, so shrewd, so wise, got God to fight his own people.\n\nBut there were other systems in place; not all Israel disobeyed, so in the end the remnant who stood true to the laws of God destroyed Moab and Balak and Balaam.\n\nWe must be wise as believers and maximize the things and opportunities and the knowledge God has given to us and brought our way.","dt":"2023-12-20T07:31:53","s":["i9ocxvbve8"]},{"m":"Balak wanted to call on God, Elohim, like one calls upon a medium or idol.\n\nHe wanted to use God for his own agenda, but he did not know the God of Israel was not like other gods.\n\nHe cannot be used for evil 😈. He is a good God.","dt":"2023-12-20T08:09:42","s":["ta2gclwwsa"]},{"m":"And to date the game of distracting the children of God and causing them to self-destruct goes on.\n\nWhen Balak realized he could not curse Israel 🇮🇱, he was advised to turn them against their own God by disobeying the laws that kept them under divine power.\n\nThey lusted for Moabite women and were destroyed by God's wrath in the process.\n\nThe wicked rebels had to be purged in order to keep the camp pure.\n\nAnd today as believers we have been fed so many lies 🤥; we have sold our gold for fool's gold.\nAnd so now the church is without power; Christians seek the created things rather than the Creator.\n\nWe have been deceived.","dt":"2023-12-20T08:21:29","s":["ap7incevva"]}],"21":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔, I don't know if I should say what I want to say.\n\nThis statement of not beholding iniquity in Jacob nor perverseness in Israel is more figurative.\n\nI think the man of God means to say he had not beheld such iniquity as deserves a curse — a curse that would mean God turning his back on the covenant he made with Jacob and Isaac and Abraham.\n\nBecause you and I know the many abominations the children of Israel had committed.\n\nBut such abominations were between God and them, and no basis at all for an outsider to use to curse Israel 🇮🇱, especially doing so in the name of God.\n\nGod was not going to allow that.\n\nIt's just like in the New Testament: God chastises us as sons and daughters, but that in no way is grounds for the devil 👿 to accuse us, such that we are no longer worthy of the cleansing blood of Jesus.\n\nOur sins are against God our father, who freely has forgiven 🙏 us.","dt":"2024-04-19T08:09:50","s":["rtdo2ilne3","30be123108"]}],"29":[{"m":"Balaam had done this before; he had cursed people and nations before and it had worked. He was no novice. No wonder Balak trusted him so much.\n\nAnd no wonder Balaam himself tried three solid times until he realised this was not one of those days. So he was compelled to flow along with God.","dt":"2026-03-07T09:02:36","s":["7f1c9s6k1w"]}]},"24":{"1":[{"m":"Okay 👌, 🤦‍♂️ so the whole time, Balaam, understanding spiritual laws, was seeking occasion for God to change his mind, so he, God, would empower Balaam to pronounce a curse.\n\nBalak knew that no people is perfect 👌, so he positioned Balaam at different angles.\n\nPerchance a certain view of Israel 🇮🇱 would arouse the anger of God,\n\nperhaps bring to mind some wrongdoings against the Lord.\n\nAll to no avail. At this time Balaam, being the prophet he was, discerned that God had at this time chosen to bless his people,\nand won't change his mind.\n\nSo he let himself move with the flow.\n\nHmm, interesting spiritual understanding of these people.","dt":"2022-03-06T09:17:24","s":["d38y1db836"]},{"m":"This time he did not go, as at other times, to seek the counsel of the Lord in secret.\n\nNo, he had obtained counsel; he knew what the will of the Lord was.\n\nHe was in alignment and in the spirit, so he set his heart right and looked towards the wilderness and began to let the spirit of the Lord move and speak through him.","dt":"2023-12-20T08:25:12","s":["hx1m8fq1k3"]},{"m":"Balaam obviously worked with God; that was why he was so successful.\n\nBut I wonder why he was said to have gone to seek for enchantment, rather than say he had gone to seek the Lord in prayer, or he went to seek the face of God, or cry out to God — but rather what he did was described as enchantment.\n\nWhat he did was described this way because he was not seeking the will of God; he was seeking how to change the will of God, and that was why what he did was called enchantments.\n\nThink of sorcerers, witches and co. Their craft is described as enchantments because they seek their own will. They seek how to cause what they desire to happen, regardless of whether it was the will of God or not.\n\nThat is why it is called enchantment, and that is why God hates it so much. It is about bending nature and compelling the supernatural to act on the natural to please one's desires.\n\nGod won't do what is contrary to himself, but the devils will. They will do what man desires in exchange for something they want.\n\nBut God will not do what man wants if it contradicts his nature and purpose.\n\nSame way, the devils will not do what will counter their will and purpose; but the devils are not God, so they are usurping authority in rebellion by causing man to seek after enchantments.\n\nIn the long run the devils destroy and cause harm, but God blesses.\n\nThe devil will give you what you desire, seemingly, but it is deception, to end up destroying you, for he is a thief and murderer from the beginning; but God will do what will inure to your benefit in the long run and permanently, whiles in the interim it may seem uncomfortable.\n\nTHIS WAS WHAT SAUL DID, WHO WENT AGAINST THE WILL OF GOD — THAT HIS REBELLION IS THE SAME AS WITCHCRAFT AND IDOLATRY.","dt":"2026-03-07T09:18:03","s":["kl83q3r1vr"]}],"6":[{"m":"As he said all this, Israel was not near water but was in the dry desert 🏜.\nHowever, this prophetically spoke of what was to befall them soon, which had already begun:\n\nthe abundance and the wealth of the promised land.","dt":"2024-04-19T08:18:10","s":["ize592lme5","add25443b6"]}],"10":[{"m":"He smote his hands 👐 together and clapped 👏 him back to reality 🤭.\n\nI don't think Balaam finished his oracle.\n\nBalak woke him out of his trance.","dt":"2023-12-20T08:28:49","s":["9n6phbixlp","07adeed285"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why this repetitive phrase? Or, that was how he readied himself to receive inspiration.\n\nMaybe it was developed over the years of his walk 🚶 with God.","dt":"2024-04-19T08:24:05","s":["663a9ff98c"]}],"17":[{"m":"He was seeing into their future 🔮","dt":"2024-04-19T08:25:40","s":["a3a1738b01"]}],"14":[{"m":"It seemed Balaam did not finish his prophecy 🥠 when Balak clapped 👏 his 👐 🖐️ at him to break the trance.\n\nNow he, Balaam, was going to continue the rest of the prophecy.\n\nThis time it was less of blessing and more of foretelling what lay in the future of both Moab and Israel 🇮🇱.","dt":"2024-04-19T08:22:55","s":["4cit1henxq","d5133b139a"]}],"2":[{"m":"When Balaam readied himself and yielded, the spirit of God came upon him and used him.\n\nWhen he had gone to seek for enchantment (in my own words, seeking a sign 🤘 and some omen concerning ISRAEL 🇮🇱), he met the Lord, who told him what to say.\n\nIt's akin to how many seek the Lord in churches and through men of God, prophets etc.\n\nGod will use all such means to reach his people. But when these same children of his become willing and yield themselves, they are used by God directly, and hear from him and sense his spirit and his impulses themselves.\n\nLet us seek the Lord.","dt":"2024-04-19T08:15:30","s":["f87f0f2ed6"]}],"16":[{"m":"He repeats the same starting lines.\n\nIt's almost like these words were the entryway into the spirit, as he prepares and waits for the spirit of God to take over.","dt":"2023-12-20T08:30:54","s":["9714d6fcb0"]}]},"26":{"65":[{"m":"They mostly died relatively young 🧒... You may not have noticed except you were told, but a generation 20 years old at the time of the first census all died before or at 60 years max.","dt":"2022-03-07T07:02:48","s":["fcab6d7e49"]}]},"27":{"14":[{"m":"Moses disobeyed once 👉. To whom much is given, much is expected.\n\nA disobedience God called rebellion. And he was not forgiven.","dt":"2022-03-09T00:28:23","s":["698ebfc67e"]}],"21":[{"m":"Moses left the scene, and in his place stood two ✌️ men, Joshua and Eleazar the priest.\n\nJoshua to lead the people, and Eleazar to lead in seeking God's counsel.\n\nBoth of these functions Moses did with ease.","dt":"2022-03-09T00:32:49","s":["8f55c8aa7a"]}]},"28":{"7":[{"m":"Is this not libation? Never knew this.","dt":"2024-04-21T16:48:23","s":["dfc30bbc1b"]}],"13":[{"m":"I find it interesting that as the people near the promised land, where they were to inhabit houses they didn't build and fields they didn't plow...\n\nAnd in all this, God was going to have his pound of flesh.\n\nBurnt offerings and others in abundance were to be offered to him at set times.\n\nAs his people prosper, he also is hallowed and worshipped.","dt":"2026-03-08T12:16:20","s":["jhxx3ast7k"]}]},"29":{"6":[{"m":"All these offerings meant the house of God was very wealthy and well taken care of, meaning the Levites also were living very well. This goes to show the mind of God for his people, how God intended to bless his people.\n\nTo bless them so much that his house was also well taken care of. That was his mind, not to impoverish the congregation whiles his house gets blessed.","dt":"2026-03-08T16:23:47","s":["mx8umr7ok9"]}],"40":[{"m":"I can but only imagine the bloodshed and continuous oblation to the Lord.\n\nThat was the cost to endure man dwelt with sinful flesh.\n\nSin always had to be atoned for.\n\nThis ordinance was carefully thought 💭 of and crafted by God and the spirits and the acceptable institution to show the ills of sin and the need for atonement to be made only through such gruesome butchery.\n\nContinual burnt 🔥 offerings and crying of clean beasts to make atonement. That was the only acceptable sacrifice until the perfect sacrifice of Christ was made.","dt":"2022-03-09T01:07:18","s":["10h86kb76t","8b938098c3"]}]},"31":{"17":[{"m":"This was a necessary evil 😈 because of the future 🔮.\n\nSons would likely have taken revenge when they became men.\n\nThe elderly non-virgin women would lure the men into sin and sexual perversions.\n\nMind you, these were pagans who indulged in orgies and had no limits, unlike Israel 🇮🇱 who served God.\n\nTo prevent all these, they were cut off.","dt":"2022-03-09T00:59:35","s":["7na9z8oii4","605fc92933"]}],"49":[{"m":"A living 🛋 wonder.\n\nUnder the watch of Moses and after the death of all rebels, this new generation went to war and none was lost.\n\nThe Lord's perfect 👌 will was being done, and they were kept by the power of God.\n\nI believe if Israel 🇮🇱 had kept wholeheartedly the laws of God, there would be none sick among them, to the end that the laws on leprosy and other diseases would not even be applied.\n\nI personally had a challenge with all these leprosy and disease laws. Why was God Almighty making provisions for such when he was their healer?\n\nWas he going to fail his word? No, but man being man was fallible, and this provision was made for the fallible nature of man.\n\nWow, none was lost... So it is possible 🙆 😇","dt":"2022-03-09T00:55:50","s":["gn3rlo6tga","25153b3aff"]}],"53":[{"m":"There is reward, great reward, in serving the Lord wholeheartedly. And I will serve him with all my heart and soul.","dt":"2022-03-09T01:02:02","s":["toroyysr6y","d682bb409a"]}],"2":[{"m":"God was literally telling Moses, Go and fight this last battle, and after that, die...","dt":"2024-04-22T06:03:04","s":["71d6433951"]}],"47":[{"m":"The Levites also got their portion from these spoils of war.\n\nSuch riches were handed over to Israel 🇮🇱 in just this war.\n\nThey would have partaken of such a long time ago if not for the disobedience of their fathers.","dt":"2022-03-09T00:57:07","s":["8fe6a05380"]}]},"33":{"4":[{"m":"Did they bury their firstborn on the same day or period Israel left Egypt?\n\nI can imagine, whiles Egypt buried ⚰ and mourned, Israel rejoiced and exited Egypt 🇪🇬.\n\nIt was in this state of mourning and fear 😱 that Israel 🇮🇱 spoiled Egypt 🇪🇬 and asked for gifts.\n\nAnd they gave Israel much.","dt":"2024-04-22T07:06:24","s":["o9s4w58bgi","057a627c40"]}],"55":[{"m":"To preserve their own posterity, they needed to drive out the inhabitants.","dt":"2022-03-09T06:41:04","s":["a112b24d6a"]},{"m":"Their destiny was in their own hands; indeed, the extent of their own greatness was in the volume of appetite they could muster.\n\nGod gave them the land, and they had the power to drive all out or some out.\n\nObviously, if we are given the same opportunity, our response will be: we will take all that belongs to us. But it is not that simple.\n\nYes, God was with them to win every battle, but it was still going to be a battle.\n\nAnd most hate battles and the work that goes into conquest. Most people lack the requisite appetite for mass-scale victory and all-round success.\n\nGod's best for them was to conquer all, but they fell short of that. May God give us the grace, and may we have sufficient drive, energy and willingness to conquer all.","dt":"2026-03-09T15:51:01","s":["vtx2d773oq"]}],"56":[{"m":"Simple: God needed his agenda to be fulfilled, and Israel 🇮🇱 was fulfilling that agenda.\n\nThe agenda was cleansing, cleansing the land of the filth of the people.\n\nLater, when Israel became filthy, they were also cleaned off the land by another people.\n\nSo in our world today, God will cleanse this world of the wickedness and moral filth before the great day of our Lord.","dt":"2022-03-09T06:41:15","s":["753387e8d2"]}],"12":[{"m":"Oh my oh my... All these movements were by the Spirit of God; the cloud 🌥 directed where they were to camp and for how long.\n\nAnd not only that, but the Lord asked for Moses to specifically record these journeys, journeys spanning 40 years.\n\nNow come to think of it, did God follow his initial script as intended, or was it influenced and adjusted based on the preparedness of Israel 🇮🇱 to obey him and how willing they were to follow his commands, judgements and statutes?\n\nOh, and many times Israel failed, prolonging their camping 🏕, causing change in directions and eventually leading to 38 extra years of wandering, till they were all dead and their children taking their place.\n\nI wish I saw the places and the pattern these journeys formed and the meaning thereof.\n\nBut alas, the scriptures do not tell us.","dt":"2024-04-22T11:11:24","s":["0bb2d62d3b","oiec1cgtv9"]}],"36":[{"m":"I'm wondering how much preparing had to go into each journey, the scouts that had to be sent ahead, the setting up and setting down 👇.\n\nThe studying of the terrains. Moses at a point required and pleaded with the son of Jethro to be with them, as he knew the wilderness better.\n\nOne would have thought 💭 that for a man 👨 who spoke to God face to face, it was just a matter of asking God.\n\nBut I believe that God was not at the beck and call of Moses, but he had to wait for long in prayer just like we all.\n\nThe only difference being God appeared in person to answer him rather than in shadows and patterns — dreams, impressions etc.\n\nSo he had to rely on his common sense, delegations and counsel from others to successfully lead his people.\n\nThis having to wait on God before he came is seen subtly in many places. For instance, the children of Israel went three days without finding water and were ready to stone Moses before God showed up.\n\nIf Moses could have obtained instant answers from God, why else would he wait until the people were dying from thirst, the weak and elderly convulsing and being feverish, before praying to the Lord?\n\nMoses could not just tell God: where is the nearest water source, the best place to get bread, and the next step to take to receive the miracle of meat 🥩, ahead of the people being hungry and angry 😡.\n\nMoses just could not do that, as God was not that available.\n\nHe was visible, he could be seen and felt, but he was not available until he wanted to talk.\n\nSee how many days and nights Moses spent in the mount to receive the 10 Commandments — 40 days and nights 🌃.","dt":"2024-04-22T11:11:24","s":["73b231645f","c9lq3rl5s9"]}],"38":[{"m":"Oh my God, just at the brink of entering the land.\n\nAt least he lived to the full because of his relationship with God, unlike others who died earlier; just that he did not enter the promised land.","dt":"2024-04-23T06:49:10","s":["9761bb791f"]}]},"34":{"6":[{"m":"Were they even able to occupy all this land?\n\nDid they even have the manpower and military ⚔ might to conquer all?\n\nOr was the idea to show them what was theirs and let them conquer one step at a time, and continue even as their numbers grew?\n\nThey were to pass this information to their children 🧒, who would then continue the conquest.","dt":"2024-04-23T07:11:04","s":["6718be5a28"]}],"11":[{"m":"How did God know all these with such details?","dt":"2026-03-09T15:55:43","s":["08t9kzlupm"]}]},"35":{"28":[{"m":"Stay in the city of refuge until the death of the high priest.\n\nNo, stay under cover of his wings until that storm is over; keep on fighting through prayer etc. until the battle is won... Do not tire, do not give in on the fight and night prayers etc.\n\nUntil you have the absolute victory ✌️","dt":"2022-03-09T06:53:53","s":["n6hig3t2s","00cba75eb0"]},{"m":"There are many permutations in this matter.\n\nImagine fleeing to the city of refuge just a day or week after a new young high priest was installed.\n\nYou will likely die in the city 🏙 of refuge and never be able to return to your property without risk of harm.\n\nBut then, who knows, the avenger of blood might be dead or might have forgiven 🙏 you.\n\nOr you could send a delegation of peace to him.\n\nConversely, what if right after fleeing the high priest dies?\n\nThen God has smiled ☺ on you. You can return home 🏡 safely. Or, out of wisdom, just stay out of sight so you do not trigger memories of the pain on the bereaved family 👪.","dt":"2024-04-24T07:50:55","s":["d0mwnkd7b9"]},{"m":"Edit:\n\nThe previous point: even if a long time has passed and the avenger of blood has forgiven, you cannot return to your possessions again until the death of the high priest...\n\nRansoms and appeasement are not accepted, even for innocently killing someone.\n\nThis is in verse... Numbers 35:32–33 KJV\n[32] And ye shall take no satisfaction for him that is fled to the city of his refuge, that he should come again to dwell in the land, until the death of the priest. [33] So ye shall not pollute the land wherein ye are: for blood it defileth the land: and the land cannot be cleansed of the blood that is shed therein, but by the blood of him that shed it.\n\nFor the Lord says there is a law that blood shed in a land can only be appeased by the blood of the one who shed it, whether intentionally or not.","dt":"2024-04-24T07:54:52","s":["0gw8besmon"]}],"34":[{"m":"What is there about Canaan, of all the world, that God chose for himself and the children of Israel to dwell there?","dt":"2026-03-10T15:58:17","s":["w7yrugzu55"]}],"2":[{"m":"These people hadn't built any cities yet; they were sharing as inheritance cities that others built.\n\nGod was literally ousting the nations of Canaan out of the land; God had had enough of them. Their sins and doings were too much, an abomination to the Lord.\n\nNow he was handing over the nations to a completely new set of people who were obedient and loyal to him.\n\nThe earth is the Lord's in the first place, and the fullness thereof, so he is justified in giving it to whosoever he pleases.","dt":"2026-03-10T12:04:24","s":["eeco45czdf"]}],"32":[{"m":"For the Lord says there is a law that blood shed in a land can only be appeased by the blood of the one who shed it, whether intentionally or not.","dt":"2024-04-22T11:11:24","s":["164e903344"]}]},"25":{"9":[{"m":"Ahhh 😱... 24,000 people had died in such a short time, and counting, and now this abomination was brought into the camp. To add insult to injury, he brings an abomination into the camp.\n\nIt had to be gotten rid of...\n\nI can imagine Phinehas piercing these 2 through and looking down at them with disdain at their selfishness.\n\nBecause of such lust, 24,000 had died...\n\nIt was better that these two die, and quickly, than thousands...","dt":"2024-04-21T15:39:38","s":["dlqj0nw2cv","903061982d"]}],"6":[{"m":"This was not self-imposed religious tears 😢.\n\nTheir very lives were literally at stake here, and they knew how much death had happened because of disobedience.\n\nThey were literally begging and praying for mercy.","dt":"2024-04-21T15:35:21","s":["9mvxooz0b9","0acf2637eb"]}]},"32":{"23":[{"m":"Is this where this expression 😑 is gotten from? Is it a Hebrew expression, or did the King James authors choose this expression because it is most befitting?","dt":"2024-04-22T06:23:50","s":["7itq496p85"]}]}},"Deuteronomy":{"1":{"33":[{"m":"Sad 😔 sad 😔.\n\nSo my earlier commentary was right: God did go ahead of them to search them out a place. They saw the literal Shekinah and turned away from it, and could somehow forget all that and be lured into sin and rebellion.\n\nThey failed themselves and their children 🧒.\n\nAnd truly, so are we all as men. Even now, seeing what the Lord has done for me and us, we continue to struggle to live wholly for him.\n\nThe delusions and lusts of this world have sunk their fangs deep into us.\n\nWe have been poisoned. We are delusional.\n\nWe claim with our mouth 👄 that we serve the Lord, but our hearts 💕 are far away from him.\n\nThat is why we do the things we do.\n\nWe really need help 😣, the help of the Holy Spirit, lest we be done for.\n\nAnd indeed his Spirit helps our infirmities and delivers us from the wickedness of ourselves and the world, and its delusions and entrapments.","dt":"2024-04-26T06:55:04","s":["eltfi0blo6","7ff5801e06"]}],"35":[{"m":"GOD called 🤙 them an evil 😈 generation.\n\nThose are strong 💪 words to use.\n\nAre we to safely assume, then, that the children 🧒 of Israel at this time were actually, literally evil 😈?\n\nYou know, in our time and in everyday usage, calling someone evil meant they really were wicked and cruel and heartless.\n\nWas that the caliber of people Moses was leading, literally?\n\nWow, then that was bad and sad.\n\nMoses really suffered a lot, to lead a people this evil 😈.\n\nGod is kind and merciful; why would he cut short all these people except Joshua and Caleb?\n\nThen the people were indeed evil 😈.\n\nAnd considering all they saw, they were evil also towards the Lord.\n\nThey did not treat him fairly, nor Moses and other leaders who were faithful in service to the Lord.","dt":"2024-04-26T06:49:13","s":["i5n87ug8jm"]},{"m":"It is because of this wickedness of our hearts, common to all men, that the Lord sent his Spirit into our hearts 💕.\n\nTo help our infirmities and wickedness.\n\nWe must not be conceited, but rather rely on his Spirit to help us.\n\nWe must give ourselves wholly to him, and we would be helped.","dt":"2024-04-26T06:59:18","s":["980w9x8b13"]}],"2":[{"m":"Why remind us it is an eleven-day journey? Is it in any way referencing their taking 40 years because of disobedience?","dt":"2026-03-11T13:01:54","s":["4als0wt660"]}]},"2":{"7":[{"m":"Thou hast lacked nothing, though they hungered many times and thirsted many times.\n\nBut God did not count that as lack, because their hunger and thirst was not from lack, neither was it from God's inability to provide, but was a test.\n\nSo truly they lacked nothing.\n\nDo not be surprised 🤨, therefore, on your journeys and assessment from God, that he says you had a good life and lacked nothing.\n\nBecause what you called lack were just tests, and you had to keep rewriting the same tests because of your refusal to learn the lessons.\n\nIt was not God's inability but yours.\n\nLord help us.","dt":"2024-04-26T07:10:31","s":["d5iyq6umjv","8dab590a73"]}],"9":[{"m":"Oookay... So God distributed the lands as he saw fit.\n\nIsrael 🇮🇱 was to skip certain specific lands because it was their lot.\n\nThere was a part of the land of Moab which God had allotted to Moab, and Israel was prevented from taking it.\n\nThe earth indeed is the Lord's, and the fullness thereof.","dt":"2024-04-26T10:18:44","s":["trvq0nns7o","bocyv4ov76","nsx4b3ngep","d814721352"]},{"m":"So God was not only looking out for Israel, but for Esau as well, and Lot. All closely related to Abraham and the promised Israel.","dt":"2026-03-11T20:22:28","s":["rahtfzg68a"]}],"24":[{"m":"I have given it to you, but you have to contend in battle for it.\n\nThe fact that it's been given to you does not mean it will land in your hands on a silver platter.","dt":"2022-03-11T03:45:41","s":["b646etl5uf","81a33d309b"]}],"37":[{"m":"This sounds like the New Testament invasions.\n\nGod separated unto himself Paul and Barnabas for the work among the Gentiles.\n\nEverywhere they went, they literally turned the place upside down.\n\nActs 17:6 KJV\nAnd when they found them not, they drew Jason and certain brethren unto the rulers of the city, crying, These that have turned the world upside down are come hither also;\n\nExcept for where God prohibited them from going.\n\nI see that in this journey we don't choose our path, God does, and once we find that path, there are many activities there and few prohibitions.\n\nWe just have to walk with him.\n\nHow did Moses know where to go and where not to, if he was not in constant communication with the Father?\n\nMoses was a chief servant indeed.","dt":"2022-03-11T03:52:30","s":["0bt0v4q2gh"]}]},"3":{"27":[{"m":"Yet he did go over the Jordan in the Gospels, when he and Elijah appeared.","dt":"2022-03-12T20:24:53","s":["fca1d8c52c"]}]},"4":{"21":[{"m":"A very painful thing... Moses here mentions it again and makes them understand that it is because of them that he, after such greatness, has been dispossessed of what was his.","dt":"2024-04-26T10:45:51","s":["9kzhoxkzmg","562d996e70"]}],"22":[{"m":"The people for whom Moses could not go over, however, did go over... Though their parents did not make it, they did...\n\nThough they were below 20, by no means were they all kids... Indeed, most of them remembered.\n\nFrom whatever age memory is formed to 19 years old, they remembered.\n\nMoses missed it because of their incessant complaints, yet they made it to the promised land.","dt":"2024-04-26T10:48:32","s":["hdm0vfessp","6797130782"]}],"10":[{"m":"Horeb is Sinai.","dt":"2022-03-13T02:41:20","s":["975d2a6c77"]}]},"5":{"27":[{"m":"The fear 😱 of God literally had consumed them and shaken them out of their pants 👖.\n\nThey were willing to obey the voice of man 👨 so long as they would avoid this thunderous ⚡ voice of God.\n\nI'm sure at this point they felt they could make a simple mistake before this awesome God, and that alone could result in their death ☠.\n\nTruly the fear of 😱 God consumed them.\n\nThough not for long, and they were back to their evil ways not too long after.\n\nMan 👨 is such an interesting species... So easily manipulated and subject to change.\n\nThis seeming fear of God did not change much about their character, as we would see in their later dealings with God.","dt":"2024-04-27T06:19:51","s":["4m2sjvl97v","f2ae496f8e"]}],"31":[{"m":"Ah wait oo.. Did God say Moses should “stand here by me”?\n\nWas that how they related? Because if memory serves me right, there was a time or point it was the reverse... i.e. the Lord stood with Moses.\n\nExodus 34:5–6 KJV\nAnd the Lord descended in the cloud, and stood with him there, and proclaimed the name of the Lord. [6] And the Lord passed by before him, and proclaimed, The Lord, The Lord God, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth,\n\nHere he not only stood with him but passed by him...\n\n🤦‍♂️ Godsh... This is mind-blowing.","dt":"2022-03-14T12:42:25","s":["ip30pfsppv","df6ada409e"]}],"29":[{"m":"Hmm, sad 😢","dt":"2022-03-14T12:33:18","s":["jx1ubs22yn","9aade6af3e"]}]},"6":{"23":[{"m":"Oh, I feel stirred in me.\n\nThat God brought us out, that indeed he might bring us in.","dt":"2024-04-27T06:29:00","s":["n0awulyokt","b4d52cad38"]}],"25":[{"m":"Indeed, it was to be their righteousness and wisdom to keep the commandments of Yahweh.","dt":"2024-04-27T06:30:10","s":["j8eadl3yv3","511f604f51"]}]},"7":{"4":[{"m":"What is there about other gods that's more alluring than the worship 🛐 of Jehovah, such that they can turn Israel away from the Lord, and not vice versa?\n\nI think it is because the worship of Jehovah is contrary to our nature and flesh, but the heathen had all these indulgences and still had the blessings of their gods.\n\nNot so with the Lord.","dt":"2022-03-15T05:20:53","s":["6g5vyz4o23","f99e8f86ca"]}],"23":[{"m":"This was going to be a very long war, considering that the land was going to be taken little by little.\n\nThe war could actually be transgenerational if they were to take all that the Lord had given them.","dt":"2024-04-27T06:44:04","s":["ad7f5a1728"]}],"26":[{"m":"Okay 👌, so the gold of idols and shrines was to be destroyed and not taken at all, unlike other spoils of war.","dt":"2024-04-27T06:45:33","s":["bf8f4e8603"]}]},"8":{"3":[{"m":"So in essence, in the absence of food, water and the essentials of life, the word and commands of God remain constant.\n\nEven if life happens, as it does to us all, and lack comes, the word of God, the rule 📐 of God over our life and condition, does not change.\n\nMany times when Israel 🇮🇱 was tempted, they threatened to boycott the mission and go back to Egypt, where they would serve other gods.\n\nAnd the same happens to us in our walk with the Lord.\n\nCompromises as life hits at us, dishonest gain, greed, lusts, just so we can get by or thrive at the expense of others and the word of God.","dt":"2024-04-28T06:14:17","s":["60452281ff"]},{"m":"When the Lord calls or sends you, his word alone is enough. For as you take the steps to walk in his word, he makes the provision for your journey.\n\nMany times we want to make full provision before moving, but not so if you want to walk with the Lord. Many times he will require your step of faith.\n\nThat is not to say do not make provision where you can, but you might often find out nothing is complete; there will always be something lagging.\n\nMaybe all provision might be made, but you find yourself still unsure of yourself.\n\nSome doubt about your ability to do what the Lord has asked, but you must move forward anyways in faith.\n\nThat is how the Lord walks with us.","dt":"2026-03-15T09:10:27","s":["xeap6bc5au"]}],"11":[{"m":"Commandments, judgements and statutes, though subtly different, are in a broad sense commandments, because they are commands to be followed.","dt":"2024-04-28T06:26:55","s":["d5rsgatonw","3a26321bb5"]}],"14":[{"m":"Moses knew that both affliction and abundance can lure us to drift away from God.","dt":"2024-04-28T06:27:40","s":["9aac7b3275"]}],"17":[{"m":"The human heart can be deceptive and foolish. After all these journeys with God, the heart still runs the risk of attributing success to self.\n\nSelf-made men, they would have called themselves.\n\nJust as they did with the golden calf after God had delivered them from Egypt by such mighty works.\n\nAnd now here they were, attributing their success to a new god they just made. Hm 🤔 sad. 😔","dt":"2024-04-28T06:30:52","s":["ca3aba0c57"]}],"9":[{"m":"Oh, so these sufferings were just to be for two years, and from there they would eat bread without scarcity, but alas they did not enter the land and wandered for 40 years.\n\nHow many of us are in a season of wandering and are going about in circles because of disobedience?\n\nWhen in reality our journey of difficulties was to be for just two ✌️ years.\n\nHmm 🥹, Lord help 😣... Help us.","dt":"2024-04-28T06:25:52","s":["d0c9e49858"]}]},"9":{"1":[{"m":"So here were a people great and strong 💪, and heard that a much weaker nation was coming to overthrow them.\n\nIndeed, they saw this weaker nation hanging round their borders for 40 years.\n\nWhy did they not strike at Israel within this period? There were many nations inhabiting the promised land, yet none in forty years, except Amalek and a handful 🖐️, did attempt to strike at Israel.\n\nAt least that was the perspective of the children of Israel 🇮🇱. They were safe under the tabernacle of the Lord.\n\nHowever, every now and then, without any particular formula and pre-notice, the cloud 🌥 of the Lord's presence just lifts, and immediately Israel must pack camp 🏕 and relocate to an unknown place — wherever the cloud would settle.\n\nNow I suspect that the myriads of nations surrounding Israel did plan and attempt to attack Israel, but ere they took action, they heard that Israel had relocated, thus thwarting the efforts of the enemies of God.\n\nRemember, God said he would lead them via the longer route, as they had not seen war yet, and God kept them from war till this moment. After forty years, now they were ready.","dt":"2024-04-29T06:12:49","s":["o405alua3u","d40183effc"]}],"9":[{"m":"For Moses to have stated that he ate not, then that meant he got hungry at least at some point and was kept by the presence of God.","dt":"2022-03-15T05:46:44","s":["b0511f44b5"]}],"19":[{"m":"Moses talked with God face to face, yet he never got familiar.\n\nHe was often afraid for Israel, that they would get destroyed.\n\nI mean, this was a God Moses was close with. Indeed, he knew the personality of God from such closeness, not to mess up.","dt":"2022-03-15T05:52:04","s":["osg44tbhxv","f852a62aed"]}],"20":[{"m":"Wow, deep secrets being unveiled here.\n\nThings Moses had to go through to secure the life of his nation and his only brother.\n\nYet somewhere down the line, Aaron, ungrateful, dared to challenge Moses; maybe he did not know what Moses had done for him in preserving his life.\n\nBut God hadn't forgotten; little wonder God was very wroth and summoned them to judgements.\n\nEven in this, Moses pleaded for them, and they would have gone without any punishment if God had not insisted on keeping leprosy on Miriam for seven days.\n\nLeft to Moses alone, nothing should be done to them.\n\nMoses was one of those overly kind people.\n\nHe had such strong 💪 fellow feeling.","dt":"2024-04-29T06:32:12","s":["n9ufx073nd"]},{"m":"How did Moses know the thoughts 💭 and plans of God concerning Aaron?\n\nBecause he had that kind of relationship going with God.\n\nSo he knew exactly what God was going to do. Very likely God told him.\n\nJust like he told him that he was going to destroy the entire nation and start afresh with Moses.\n\nBut we don't need to hear God and see him face to face like Moses.\n\nGod has given us his mind already through his word — he has said that a witch 🧙‍♀️ should not be allowed to live; he's also said that anyone of their brethren who practises sorcery or tries to lead the people astray into strange gods should be killed immediately.\n\nTheir eyes 👀 were not to pity. And that was exactly what God was implementing here.\n\nHe had already told them not to worship any gods, and that quickly they had broken his law.\n\nNo wonder it took 40 days of dry fasting for God to even consider sparing them.\n\nEven with that, he asked for the camp to be moved whiles he thought 💭 of what to do to them.\n\nEventually he conceded. Oh, this man Moses was indeed the meekest of men. Going to such dire extremes to get to God.\n\nIndeed, he is the meekest. Only a man 👨 like Moses could have freed Israel 🇮🇱 from captivity and led them to the promised land.","dt":"2024-05-03T06:19:16","s":["1qbtx6e7m8"]}],"25":[{"m":"Humility... 40 days fast.","dt":"2022-03-15T06:15:10","s":["j5a1hds8qv","915cd74684"]}],"26":[{"m":"So in a space of two years, Moses had prayed 🙏 for forty days and forty nights, no food 🍲 and water 💦, for 3 times.\n\nHmm... He really loved his people, and yet they were ungrateful every time, and yet Moses never stopped loving them.\n\nThis man 👨 Moses. Very strange man.\n\nNo wonder, yes, no wonder he beheld God face to face; no man did ever have that privilege.","dt":"2024-04-29T06:38:02","s":["a0tzi7x01z","38e32be237"]}],"18":[{"m":"Wow... Two consecutive forty-day fasts.\n\nMoses was a good man 👨 and genuine intercessor for Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nHe humbled himself and begged for pardon for Israel, and he got it.\n\nThat was why in the matter of Korah they had no chance.\n\nHe, Moses, and God were tight.","dt":"2022-03-15T05:50:07","s":["sui41360ow","048ec55958"]},{"m":"You know, we have often been told that because Moses was in the divine presence of God, it preserved him, and he could fast for so long without feeling it.\n\nI believe that is so, but it is also not completely accurate that he did not feel the pangs of hunger and thirst. If he did not feel it, then why would he even make mention of it?\n\nIt was a big sacrifice for him, just like it is for any man. Yes, there was the divine presence and provision that empowered him, but he felt it.\n\nIn fact, in the rest of the chapters he mentions 3 more times he fasted 40 days and nights. The thing was a difficult sacrifice he had to make, but it was so he could deliver a nation of 2 million people from death.","dt":"2026-03-15T09:33:00","s":["nk1ansg7vm"]}],"28":[{"m":"Only God knows how many times he prayed this prayer.\n\nBear in mind, this single verse is a summary of forty days and nights of intercession.\n\nOh, I wish there was a much longer version of the prayers he did pray and repeat.\n\nBut I guess if they wrote down all he said, we would not even read them, or few would, and many would find them boring 💤.","dt":"2024-04-29T06:39:57","s":["f8d986b924"]}]},"10":{"4":[{"m":"What was the point of Moses hewing an ark?\n\nGOD could have just done it.","dt":"2022-03-15T06:16:36","s":["f2f1d21aa8"]}],"14":[{"m":"Moses really wanted Israel 🇮🇱 to obey the Lord.\n\nHe had saved them from total annihilation at least twice and did not want his work to be in vain.\n\nHe truly loved Israel 🇮🇱","dt":"2022-03-15T06:18:29","s":["ohx54rdbj6"]},{"m":"Psalm 146:6 KJV\nWhich made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all that therein is: which keepeth truth for ever:","dt":"2024-04-29T06:45:23","s":["ph5v6pdtyx"]}]},"11":{"1":[{"m":"Jesus put it this way... If you love me, you would keep my commandments.","dt":"2022-03-15T06:36:51","s":["cdb85e29ec"]}],"12":[{"m":"Then the same is true for Africa 🌍. The Lord's eyes are indeed here by way of natural resources.","dt":"2022-03-15T06:50:45","s":["4d40bd27b5"]}],"18":[{"m":"Interesting reference to the spirit, soul and body, i.e. heart ♥, soul, and binding them physically on body parts.","dt":"2022-03-17T03:28:36","s":["14bb1395d6"]}]},"13":{"15":[{"m":"Why the cattle as well? Could it be because such cattle have been dedicated to the worship of false gods?","dt":"2024-04-29T07:14:31","s":["b6a0a06760"]},{"m":"The cattle that was being used to sacrifice to these strange gods was to be destroyed as well, because they, like the people, had become abominable.","dt":"2026-03-15T12:24:44","s":["fxatsgthux"]}],"16":[{"m":"God is a blesser. He indeed blesses. Here we have spoils of war burnt because it belonged to the haters of God.\n\nAnd God promised to bless, because it is technically a loss, organizing and investing in a holy war only to burn out the spoil of war to the Lord.\n\nWhat a loss. And God cannot but bless for such an act.\n\nLet's give our all to the Lord.","dt":"2022-03-17T07:39:55","s":["9683ea9407"]}]},"15":{"4":[{"m":"Two meanings come up from the various translations:\n\n1. Except when there shall be no poor person among you, because the Lord will bless the land\n\n2. Do this so that there shall be no poor person among you; in doing this the Lord will greatly bless you...","dt":"2022-03-17T09:19:56","s":["xehnncqz19","027e297b07"]}],"11":[{"m":"Is this not where Jesus quoted from?","dt":"2026-03-16T07:43:15","s":["3duu1r90q8"]}],"5":[{"m":"God says it is only when one is careful to do his laws that the accompanying blessings come.\n\nIt is not by shabbily doing what one wants, or partial obedience.\n\nGod wants full-scale commitment to him.\n\nSame way, it behoves on us as Christians today to be deliberate in keeping the laws of God and walking in love and holiness.","dt":"2024-04-30T06:28:28","s":["3b43772332"]}]},"16":{"11":[{"m":"The commandments of the Lord seem to address those with means and power, even though it was meant for all.\n\nThey were to ensure that all those under their control and command obeyed the voice of the Lord and observed the required feast.\n\nWith such influence, the others under them would do the right thing in obeying the voice of the Lord.","dt":"2024-04-30T06:54:44","s":["ilsymkiwby"]}]},"17":{"5":[{"m":"This was not to be in the coming years, as the people drifted into apostasy and on a national scale worshipped 🛐 other gods.","dt":"2024-05-01T06:12:09","s":["0rkw7j4o3n","3778afb0db"]}],"10":[{"m":"Here the final judgement is settled by divine direction.\n\nBut that was not to be the norm, but rather the extreme exception.\n\nIt seems, all through God's dealings with Israel 🇮🇱 becoming a nation, that the end goal is not for God to directly oversee and micromanage,\n\nBut rather to set up self-supporting systems controlled by man but governed by God through his laws.\n\nThat was actually why man was created, to rule with God. Our rule is on this earth 🌎.\n\nLook, for instance, at the day Israel entered the promised land and tasted of the fruit thereof, that in that same day the manna ceased.\n\nSo now I ask, in these times of the New Testament, 2000 years down the line of Christ's kingdom 👑 being established, what are the things pertaining to our time that were not pertaining to the early church, and vice versa?\n\nWhat does God want us to take up and establish, and what does God want us to cease doing?\n\nGod is the Creator, and his Spirit is yet alive in us, so we can definitely know the will of God for our time.","dt":"2024-05-01T06:19:27","s":["aefb29b7d5"]}],"17":[{"m":"This exact thing happened to Solomon.\n\nIs it not interesting that God did not attribute multiplying horses 🐴 or gold and silver to the king's heart being turned away from the Lord?\n\nBut when it came to multiplying women, God said it was the women who would turn the king's 👑 heart ♥.\n\nWhy is this so? We are told the consequences of each... That horses 🏇 would mean alliance with Egypt 🇪🇬, which the Lord abhorred.","dt":"2024-05-01T06:24:20","s":["rnzttg7p1w","fcafc3b3d2"]}]},"19":{"5":[{"m":"Why did the Lord their God not prevent this, being present in their midst and seeing all things?\n\nWhy did he not prevent this, but rather has made concessions for what should be done, and for the innocent slayer?\n\nIt is obvious that God was setting up the general principles of guidance for man 👨 to follow without God's direct supervision.\n\nMan was to be governed by the laws of God, and God was setting up the system for that, so it would not require his constant monitoring and interruption.\n\nSo now, with the system set and running 🏃, now God can step in as He pleases to, for instance, prevent the axe head from killing an innocent man 👨, or he can choose to let it happen, because in his providence that man ought to die but justice has eluded him.\n\nOr the innocent slayer would flee to the land, and in that land God has a plan for him or his descendants.\n\nOnce the system is working, God can be God in controlling things behind the scenes in his divine wisdom and judgements.\n\nIt's the same in our world today; many times evil 😈 befalls us and we ask why.\n\nKnowing very well that God could have prevented it. But that is the providence of God.\n\nThough we may not always understand him, that is his providence.","dt":"2024-05-01T07:14:59","s":["7mnrv0oneo","8a4797cd3a"]}],"6":[{"m":"Interestingly, the avenger of blood is not guilty if he succeeds in catching up with the killer, though he be innocent. For the just punishment for shedding blood is to shed blood.\n\nHowever, provision is made so he can escape to the city of refuge, because he is not worthy of death.","dt":"2026-03-17T05:44:01","s":["tbwk81sc2c"]}],"13":[{"m":"By the time we get to the days of David, the people had so neglected the word of the Lord. And so, try as King David did, he could not keep the law to the letter, but he did do very well as a king. He was always the reference point and the best amongst them.\n\nFor instance, in King David's time, Joab his nephew killed many innocent men, but nothing could be done about it at that time till later. He, Joab, was too powerful then.\n\nPoint 2:\nAt this stage the Israelites were in very close alignment with the word of God, so they were really blessed. They could go to war and no one died. Fast forward to David, and many things had been neglected.\n\nSo the people made the most of what they had, including the righteous. I gave the example of a good king like David letting Joab live despite being a murderer twice.\n\nLook at the time of Daniel: such abominations were being committed, and righteous men like Daniel lived in that generation and yet could do nothing, and eventually were taken captive alongside the wicked.\n\nBut God showed mercy to his children. Fast forward, here we are in 21st-century Christendom — we must strive to hold the banner of Christ high, and yet also practically manage the situations we find in our churches.\n\nWe have so strayed from the faith that was once handed down to us. But we will make the most of it, and shine the light of God's word to our brethren.\n\nAnother generation might come who would do better, and maybe restore the first order, near perfect, as was handed down to us.\n\nBut till then we have to make the most of what we have and make do with what flock come to the church.\n\nThat is why today we have all manner of characters serving in church and leading as church leaders. Lord have mercy — we would make the most of it as we trust God to bring change to the hearts of people.","dt":"2026-03-17T05:47:31","s":["ppzeh8jrl9"]}],"14":[{"m":"I'll use this scripture to claim what is rightfully mine in case someone tries to claim my land ☺ 😁","dt":"2024-05-01T07:16:52","s":["85c1c1bb24"]}]},"20":{"4":[{"m":"Again we see here the system of God, which system requires the collaboration of men to function.\n\nGod was going to battle out the enemy and bring victory ✌️.\n\nIndeed, he gives Israel 🇮🇱 assurance of this. You would have expected that Israel can now relax, knowing the battle is the Lord's.\n\nAnd indeed it is the Lord's, but the humans would be the ones fighting it.\n\nAnd not only that, but they would have to be bold and courageous, as is required in war, for them to win.\n\nThey were to put in the preparations required for war, just like any army, and were to have the courage required for war, just like any army,\n\njust that their courage and confidence was not in their numbers and weapons of war, but in the Lord their God.\n\nKnowing this, that the Lord can save with few or with many, with advanced weapons or mundane, so long as the Lord was in the battle, victory ✌️ was assured...\n\n1 Samuel 14:6–7 KJV\nAnd Jonathan said to the young man that bare his armour, Come, and let us go over unto the garrison of these uncircumcised: it may be that the LORD will work for us: for there is no restraint to the LORD to save by many or by few.","dt":"2024-05-01T07:25:45","s":["5wagfto7j2","7cf6ac5ed5"]}],"1":[{"m":"I now see why the Lord would reference Egypt 🇪🇬 in this situation.\n\nIt was to remind them of the might with which he delivered them, so their faith rises in his ability to deliver them again in this case.","dt":"2024-05-01T07:19:59","s":["fb2b645560"]}],"16":[{"m":"Why not treat them like the other nations — at least their young ones? Maybe they had also, one way or the other, seen the abominations committed.\n\nOr the demands of justice were such that their parents were to be cut off, so they themselves were not to be alive in the first place.\n\nOnly God, who is so merciful, will know the extent of the wickedness of these people to deserve such punishments without mercy.","dt":"2026-03-17T06:05:52","s":["uosv2algrl"]}]},"21":{"7":[{"m":"This was very symbolic: innocent blood has been shed, and now the elders kill an innocent heifer and wash their hands over the bloody animal, saying that they have not shed innocent blood.\n\nThe animal here seems to represent the dead, whose blood had been shed just like this heifer.\n\nThe rituals of Israel were full of replacements, substitution and atonements.","dt":"2024-05-02T07:04:05","s":["f90d234af6"]}],"9":[{"m":"Some of the rituals in this part of scriptures feel so much like enchantments of a sort — killing an animal, letting the blood run in a specific valley, etc. etc.\n\nIt is much like African religion, but this was God-ordained. I think it is out of these laws of God that the dark world copies and uses it for their own rituals.","dt":"2026-03-18T05:48:06","s":["v14y2iicy8"]}]},"23":{"8":[{"m":"Was God doing some kind of gene mapping, such that by the 3rd generation the gene pool is pure enough to identify as an Israelite? Does that mean there is something about Israelites, the children of Abraham, that marks them out? Yes, I believe so.\n\nAs for the Ammonite issue, 10 generations later is considered enough to purge the gene pool. Does that also, then, mean that moral failure, or better still, acts we commit in our lifetime, have a way of affecting our genes and staining them, and are transferred to the next generation? As the example given of an illegitimate child, or the Moabites who hired Balaam to curse God's chosen ones. 10 generations is how long it took to purge moral failure of a certain degree.\n\nGenerations literally is connected to one's genes.\n\nDoes physical character or moral character get assimilated in our blood, and eventually into our genes, and to the next generation?","dt":"2026-03-18T06:00:25","s":["aovxdz4ezo"]}],"20":[{"m":"The system they ran did not produce inflation, no currency debasement.","dt":"2022-03-18T01:28:18","s":["5b832c0206"]}],"14":[{"m":"Hmmm 🤔","dt":"2022-03-18T01:27:14","s":["89ssnq935p","40448c5fef"]}]},"24":{"5":[{"m":"Like, what was the significance or reasoning behind this command?","dt":"2022-03-18T01:30:48","s":["5580ffe5c9"]}]},"25":{"15":[{"m":"See how we cut short our lives oo","dt":"2022-03-18T01:34:43","s":["5eptzd24k8"]},{"m":"Honest labour and honest dealings prolong one's life. Just as honoring one's parents...\n\nSo now imagine combining the two ✌️.\n\nHonest labour and obeying parents.","dt":"2024-05-02T21:20:44","s":["me44kqfxn7"]}],"3":[{"m":"Come again?","dt":"2022-03-18T01:33:18","s":["27d40ee0de"]}],"11":[{"m":"Where did God get these ideas from? He has been watching. He indeed was being true when he said he walks in the midst of them in the camp, so they were to remain clean and pure, so he doesn't behold any evil or unclean thing.\n\nThese were God's laws of justice, not just for man but for he, God.\n\nWhen obeyed, he also experiences that sense of justice and blesses accordingly. So these laws are not just for man's legal and justice system and sense, but for God as well.\n\nHe experiences them. In fact, I will say it is for him more than for us. He knows and seems to have a stronger sense of justice and right and wrong than us.\n\nRemember, their eyes were not to pity; man was flawed and could feel pity wrongly, and because we also are at fault oftentimes, and so can have mercy wrongfully.\n\nImagine God walking through the camp, hands at his back, and observing his children get better each day.","dt":"2026-03-18T19:29:35","s":["llqyxkhpvx"]}],"19":[{"m":"Hmmm... Amalek","dt":"2022-03-18T01:35:37","s":["6zu3gfqpn9","f50c4432c0"]}]},"26":{"7":[{"m":"I must trace my heritage.","dt":"2022-03-18T01:37:08","s":["0e64f421d3"]}],"11":[{"m":"Some have labored, and we do enter into their labours.\n\nHere the people were to rejoice in all that the Lord had provided.\n\nA land flowing with milk and honey, which they did not sow, and houses they did not build, and yet they did enjoy.\n\nTheir fathers died in the wilderness seeking out this land, and yet here they are reaping the benefits thereof.\n\nGod made sure that they did remember, so they do not take things for granted.\n\nThis is good advice for us all. That as we sit by the dining table, we teach our children the ways of the Lord that has brought us this far, so that when we are gone, they remember the word of the Lord always.","dt":"2024-05-03T06:40:59","s":["5eh81eu3hr"]},{"m":"The Spirit of the Lord brings us peace, peace of mind and rest to our minds and our bodies.\n\nThere is a peace that his presence brings.\n\nHe gives us the ability to obey the word of God. To walk according to the precepts of God written 📝 on our hearts 💕 and conscience 🧠.\n\nSometimes you know the right thing to do but just can't do it. Indeed, many times that is the case.\n\nBut the Spirit enables us to do his will. Especially the things that are our weaknesses.\n\nEspecially in our generation, where we have been lured into addictions.\n\nAddictions of sex, drunkenness, lewdness, materialism etc.\n\nHis Spirit helps us break all those yokes and bondages.\n\nAnd he blesses us, guides us into hidden riches.\n\nAnd shows us our role in the kingdom 👑 and enables us to do it.\n\nHe shows us judgements and wisdom. Just like the spirit upon Moses was given to the 70 elders to enable them to judge Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nHis Spirit is all we need. When he, the Spirit of truth, comes, he changes everything and aligns us to his will, his word and his ways.","dt":"2024-05-03T06:50:35","s":["5tkyj45yea"]}],"18":[{"m":"You are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, God's own special people — these words of Peter in the New Testament were the very words God used to describe Israel in the wilderness on different occasions.\n\nOh, no wonder Stephen called them the church in the wilderness. Israel was God's special people and church in the wilderness. No wonder he gave them such wonderful and unique laws, because he was so close to them.\n\nMoses even said that if they obey the laws and rules of God, they will be so blessed, and the people around them would call them blessed, and wonder at such wonderful laws God had given them, and wonder at the blessedness of a people whom God is so close to, and lives and walks among.\n\nAnd yes, today we the church are even more blessed, in that not only does the Lord walk among us,\n\nhe is not just so close to us, but actually lives in us as his temple.\n\nThe holy temple of the holy God.\n\nLittle wonder Paul says if you attempt to destroy God's temple, God also will destroy you, which temple we are.","dt":"2026-03-18T19:45:08","s":["8j99lksc91"]}]},"27":{"2":[{"m":"Just imagine the scenery: Moses, the last of his generation, at least 80 years older than the oldest, with the exception of Joshua and Caleb.\n\nAdvising this younger generation. Indeed, Moses was a kind of god to them.\n\nYou could see the hand of divinity on him. Though old, he was strong 💪. And healthy.","dt":"2022-03-18T01:46:06","s":["6eafcef0ec"]}],"3":[{"m":"It was to be etched in stone, a memorial which will never forget them, neither will they forget, or be able to deny if they even forget. For it will be a stone of remembrance.","dt":"2026-03-18T19:47:14","s":["qydrh69mz8"]}],"5":[{"m":"Already God was building 🏢 memorials and images for the promised land.\n\nSo the people do not forget through all generations.\n\nHe was entrenching his name in the land and etching his memory in the sands of time.","dt":"2024-05-03T07:11:00","s":["57d11b371d"]}]},"28":{"15":[{"m":"I was wondering, did Moses really keep repeating the commands of the Lord, as we see him do so many times in the scripture?\n\nDid he have to mention a tall list of blessings and go through its opposites and mention a tall list of curses 🤬?\n\nI believe he did, considering how forgetful the children of Israel were, and how much sacrifice it had taken to finally bring them to this point.\n\nHe was leaving no stone unturned.\n\nHe was going to go through every one of them, blessings and curses 🤬, till it sank deep into their heads 🤕.","dt":"2024-05-04T06:02:47","s":["ab830fabfe"]}],"32":[{"m":"Are these Abraham's children? So the promise to Abraham was not a blanket statement or promise. There were terms and conditions to it.\n\nI mean, for God at a point to be willing to kill all the 2 million or so Israelites and start afresh with Moses alone should tell you something.","dt":"2026-03-20T11:02:37","s":["nxxdsmdput"]}],"49":[{"m":"The Lord told Moses all these?","dt":"2022-03-19T23:16:26","s":["9cj1jy963n","0eaa0db69c"]}],"68":[{"m":"Wow... Why would no man buy them?\n\nWould slavery so abound that procuring of more slaves would be worthless?\n\nOr, more likely, procuring Israelites as slaves would not be worth it, as there would be already so many of them on the slave market.","dt":"2024-05-05T22:31:25","s":["d7efa66d30"]}],"37":[{"m":"But why would any people wait until this point, when literally you've been destroyed — literally your life, your nation, your family, your children, your property, your businesses have come to a standstill?\n\nWhy would you not return to the Lord, but rather wait all the way to this point, and still not repent, and take all of this punishment from the Lord — and it's not even over yet (there's more suffering in store from the Lord for anyone who continues in sin)?\n\nBut why would you go all the way, when at the end of the day you would bend the knee, when at the end of the day you will turn back to the Lord, or be compelled to?\n\nIt doesn't make sense.","dt":"2024-05-04T06:13:41","s":["8e8f94ef9f"]}],"61":[{"m":"Eii","dt":"2022-03-19T23:18:25","s":["8e809b5599"]}]},"29":{"6":[{"m":"Ye have not eaten bread 🥪 (I like this emoji — yummy sandwich), yet have been kept hale and hearty.\n\nYou did not enjoy delicacies that the other nations have enjoyed, yet when they came against you in battle,\n\nI gave you the victory ✌️","dt":"2022-03-20T00:01:03","s":["vzdzxvfgyg"]},{"m":"In other words, God was making the point that the very things in the absence of which man would die...\n\nFood, clothing, wine for joy and happiness...\n\nYes, they lived full, fed, clothed, and experienced peace and joy in the absence of these.","dt":"2024-05-07T07:34:06","s":["bykfm8l5yi"]}],"12":[{"m":"He had made a covenant with their fathers in Horeb, which covenant was also binding on them.\n\nBut now he was making another with them personally. Just like the Abrahamic covenant was binding on Isaac and his son Jacob, and yet God personally appeared to each of them to establish his covenant.\n\nAs I pen this down, a thought came to mind: after Esau lost his birthright, could he not have embarked on a personal journey to search for the God of his father?\n\nHe could have, but did he know how to access God?\n\nJacob, to whom belonged the covenant, had God revealing Himself to him before he could personally commune with God.\n\nWithout God revealing himself, they worshipped as they knew how and followed in the steps of their fathers.\n\nBut when God showed up himself, things changed from impersonal to personal...\n\nHence their personal names of God, like El-bethel etc.\n\nBack to my thought 💭. Maybe if ESAU had embarked on such a journey, just maybe God would have shown up, but alas he did not, so we cannot tell.","dt":"2024-05-07T07:42:42","s":["99tbsz8s7b","be5c9cac69"]}],"23":[{"m":"Admah and Zeboim... Never heard of them.\n\nGoogle commentary says it is one of five cities that formed the plain of Sodom and Gomorrah.","dt":"2022-03-20T00:03:58","s":["ce63bfe660"]}],"15":[{"m":"What does this verse mean by with those not here...\n\nMost translations suggest this covenant was with those present and the descendants not yet present.\n\nWhile some suggest those present, and those not present before Moses but somewhere within the camp, but not here at this time.","dt":"2024-05-07T07:53:54","s":["7kx5lursig","601e55b816"]}],"19":[{"m":"Interesting expression: drunkenness to thirst.\n\nDoes that make you more thirsty?","dt":"2022-03-20T00:03:05","s":["00b514ffe2"]},{"m":"I just checked on Google, and drinking when thirsty, and especially in a wilderness situation, is a recipe for quick dehydration and ultimately death.","dt":"2026-03-20T11:21:40","s":["52tmnf8979"]}],"21":[{"m":"Wait, we have been in service where we are told to establish and cut covenants with the Lord, for he is a God of covenant.\n\nBut indeed we are already truly under covenant, the covenant of Christ and Abraham.\n\nThus whatever covenant we establish even now is not really new, but a covenant under covenant, i.e. under the covenant of Christ.\n\nEven if we do not personally cut covenants with the Lord, we are under one — the New Testament covenant —\n\nthough we are further affirmed when God cuts covenants with us personally, because he wants to do something unique with us and through us.\n\nNot a new covenant, but a unique fulfillment with us of the already established New Testament.","dt":"2024-05-07T07:49:52","s":["531cc22427"]}],"29":[{"m":"AMEN","dt":"2022-03-20T00:07:50","s":["1206e8831d","466d3750b2"]}]},"30":{"2":[{"m":"The blessings of the Lord and his covenant are not automatic. Even in the covenant, it contains blessings and curses, and he treats them according to their actions.\n\nI find the covenant of the Lord with Israel is several layers deep. First he cuts covenant with father Abraham, then with his son Isaac, and then Jacob... We are not told anything about Joseph and Moses, though they were blessed.\n\nBy this time Israel is a nation. Then he cuts covenants with the entire nation. The first covenant with Abraham alone seems not enough for him to impose his will and blessings upon the people.\n\nIn each generation his people must choose to activate the blessings of the covenant in order for it to work for them.\n\nSo what happens if they refuse? That would mean they have refused being blessed, and no one would choose that.\n\nNot to mention, often they find themselves in a bad situation which only the re-enactment of the covenant can pull them out of.\n\nWe see that many times throughout the history of Israel as a nation.\n\nFor the first time we see the introduction of the element of curses in the covenant.\n\nThis was only done when Israel became a nation. Why curses? Because they were in breach of a contract, choosing to turn their back on God after he has blessed them and carried them on eagles' wings to the promised land.\n\nA land flowing with milk and honey. A land where, if there were not curses, God would be on the losing end of the covenant for having fulfilled his part of the deal.\n\nSo if Israel refused to worship and keep him as their God, the curses are activated.","dt":"2026-03-21T06:50:58","s":["0280fpq7eo"]}],"7":[{"m":"So the curses for their disobedience shall now come upon their enemies.\n\nFor they, though not God's people, are judged and cursed for breaking the laws of God, which most are laws of conscience and natural to man.\n\nExcept that we often close 🔐 our minds.\n\nIt also thus means that we can stand on these laws to pass judgment on wicked and evil people 😈","dt":"2022-03-18T01:50:40","s":["ca87d100de"]}],"20":[{"m":"Oww... Indeed he is our life and the length of our days.","dt":"2022-03-18T01:53:13","s":["a68c44a2a3"]}],"4":[{"m":"This seems to be the story of my life. I have returned to the Lord now more than ever, and I see him already aligning my heart and life to his will. Things are lining up by the special grace of God.","dt":"2026-03-21T06:53:42","s":["svin6as0s3"]}],"14":[{"m":"Paul quotes this verse... and applies it to Christ.\n\nRomans 10:6-9 KJV\nBut the righteousness which is of faith speaketh on this wise, Say not in thine heart, Who shall ascend into heaven? (that is, to bring Christ down from above:)\n\n[7] Or, Who shall descend into the deep? (that is, to bring up Christ again from the dead.)\n\n[8] But what saith it? The word is nigh thee, even in thy mouth, and in thy heart: that is, the word of faith, which we preach;\n\n[9] That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved.\n\nIn reality he takes it out of context, but applies it right to Christ.\n\nThough arguably Christ is the word, so in that sense he applied it right, he takes it out of the old covenant and applies it within the New Testament context.\n\nPaul does so with many other scriptures.\n\nIt's almost like when a verse of scripture jumps up at you and speaks to your situation.\n\nIn this case Paul uses it right and establishes doctrine, whiles in our case as believers in general it may be applicable to our situation, but we cannot establish doctrine with it.\n\nThis most people try to do, i.e. make a personal word doctrine, and end up in error.","dt":"2024-05-07T08:12:05","s":["58dda59c82"]}],"19":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-03-18T01:52:44","s":["5488d73445","bc333a16f0"]}]},"31":{"9":[{"m":"I used to think Joshua was a young man, and thus Moses introduced him to the nation and had to stand by him because of his young age. But not so, he was one of the oldest of just two, Caleb and he.\n\nSo that old-age respect was already there, but as proof that he was God's chosen one, Moses stood with him and strengthened his hand.\n\nGod also confirmed that he had called him through signs and wonders later on.","dt":"2026-03-21T07:03:25","s":["q9lykdwxcx"]}],"21":[{"m":"God doth know the hearts of men.","dt":"2022-03-20T08:40:54","s":["gjox4r76fb"]},{"m":"How were Moses and God able to live with this thought 💭?\n\nThat despite all they had done, these people's hearts imagined and desired different things.\n\nThings contrary to God and to themselves. Imaginations that would destroy them and not produce the glorious life God and Moses hoped for them.\n\nIt's sad 😔. No wonder Moses said that a prophet like unto him — great in intercession, compassion, and a great high priest — will arise, and him will the people hear.\n\nDeuteronomy 18:15 ESV\n\"The LORD your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among you, from your brothers—it is to him you shall listen—\n\nAnd in another place he says\n\nGenesis 49:10 KJV\nThe sceptre shall not depart from Judah, nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.\n\n🥹😭","dt":"2024-05-09T07:55:44","s":["6sgj3vpc7i"]}],"29":[{"m":"Ah, the first apostles also said the same thing, that after their passing wolves 🐺 in sheep 🐑 clothing will devour the flock.\n\nActs 20:29 KJV\nFor I know this, that after my departing shall grievous wolves enter in among you, not sparing the flock.\n\nSo there is really nothing new under the sun.","dt":"2024-05-08T02:21:38","s":["cf40d7efce"]}],"30":[{"m":"All these repetitions of instructions and songs and commands.\n\nGoing as far as teaching prophetic songs of rebellion and asking for sacred meetings to read the law,\n\nTying symbols on the forehead and bracelets and hems on clothes, all to bring to remembrance the words of the law in order not to forget them.\n\nDespite these elaborate attempts, Israel 🇮🇱 failed to obey many times,\n\nBut these reminders worked, in that anytime they fell into rebellion, they never forgot the God who brought them out of Egypt.\n\nSo in that sense it worked in bringing them back from rebellion, but it failed in that it did not prevent the rebellion in the first place.\n\nRebellion which led to impossibly difficult circumstances.","dt":"2022-03-22T02:57:03","s":["1cfec6ef48"]}],"8":[{"m":"The Lord, he it is that doth go with you... Oh my word 🥹.\n\nReminding them that it is none other than the I AM.\n\nThe I AM himself and none other that doth go with them into battle.\n\nIf it indeed is the I AM, as it is, then their enemies are done for.","dt":"2024-05-07T21:55:49","s":["8lj1qsxt3m","3328a5b55f"]}],"22":[{"m":"Why a song? Anything that will ingrain the word of the Lord in their hearts so they do not forget, the Lord did.\n\nHe made them build altars on mountains which cannot be moved, so that eternally they remember the blessings and the curses, including generations unborn.\n\nThe law was written on rocks and in a book. They had festivals several times yearly to re-enact the past and remind them constantly of the covenant and whose they were.\n\nNow a song was written.\n\nThis teaches us that we also must set up systems in our lives, and that for our children, so we do not forget the Law of God and his word. We must be very deliberate about this, lest we lose the very thing that is designed to inure to our benefit.\n\nRemember how he told Joshua to meditate on the book of the law day and night. Maybe to literally memorise it, because in it was his sure blessings.","dt":"2026-03-21T07:08:22","s":["h6icasag2y"]}]},"32":{"4":[{"m":"Yes, all his ways are carefully thought 💭 of and planned. When you weigh 🏋️ them, you would realize they are well judged.","dt":"2024-05-09T08:04:31","s":["2d2cd1970c"]}],"14":[{"m":"A lot of symbolism is used in this chapter. Little wonder that in verse 8, some versions actually interpret it to mean that when the Lord divided the boundaries of the nations,\n\nHe set an angel over each.\n\nSuch translation was possible because the word Israel, which means Prince of power with Elohim, was taken literally and translated as Elohim, which is plural and sometimes in scripture refers to angels or gods.\n\nDeuteronomy 32:8 CEB\nWhen God Most High divided up the nations—when he divided up humankind—he decided the people's boundaries based on the number of the gods.\n\nDeuteronomy 32:8 KJV\nWhen the Most High divided to the nations their inheritance, When he separated the sons of Adam, He set the bounds of the people According to the number of the children of Israel.","dt":"2024-05-09T08:18:54","s":["s2mo1xflul","db3376aed6"]}],"34":[{"m":"Lord, is that why Africa is this way, so rich yet so poor? Is it because of our many gods and ills and abominations? Help us God, oh help.\n\nBut other nations like the UAE have also gods, not the LORD, yet they do well for themselves. Then it is the nature of our gods who have influenced our nature, and so together we destroy ourselves and are the most reproached of all men.","dt":"2026-03-21T07:17:07","s":["16c35pk07k"]}],"50":[{"m":"These are strange words. It almost sounds like death is a choice here.\n\nGo to this mountain I'm sending you, and when you get there just die as instructed 🤦‍♂️","dt":"2022-03-22T06:17:55","s":["d3c6111416"]}],"8":[{"m":"I think 🤔 here it meant when he set the bounds of the people from of old 🧓, he, being eternal, foresaw the number of the children of Israel 🇮🇱 and set their boundaries for them, that is the promised land.\n\nHe set those boundaries e'er before Israel was even a nation.\n\nThat's our God.\n\nDeuteronomy 32:8 CEB\nWhen God Most High divided up the nations—when he divided up humankind—he decided the people's boundaries based on the number of the gods.","dt":"2024-05-09T08:08:20","s":["3l263zy8iy","c86f525915"]}],"38":[{"m":"Interesting, so all spirits alike eat the fat of sacrifices and drink wine of drink offerings.\n\nWe still do this today in pouring libations to gods and making sacrifices in African traditional religion.\n\nJust that the wicked spirits of the heathen drink in the blood of humans and even of babies.\n\nBut our God is not so and abhors such.","dt":"2024-05-09T08:28:36","s":["73f6ed1a2d"]}],"49":[{"m":"If at 120 and in so-called old age he could climb a mountain, Moses was not going to die soon, except the Lord killed him, as was the case. He was strong enough to have continued, but he had lived beyond his days. His time was up, and as he handed over the baton to the next generation, it was time to die.","dt":"2026-03-21T07:21:08","s":["g4ztoom8td"]}]},"33":{"3":[{"m":"We see the children of Israel being called saints.","dt":"2022-03-22T07:19:02","s":["lzcxfibo9l"]}],"16":[{"m":"He separated from his brethren.\n\nBut that separation that was meant to be a curse 🤬 and his undoing became his distinction.\n\nHe indeed was the one who was separated from his brethren. His glory, honour and beauty were so distinctly greater and far beyond that of his brethren.\n\nThat his separation was justifiably so, for he was separate from his brethren.","dt":"2024-05-09T13:03:19","s":["ridsemxt72","a34cfcc5fc"]}],"5":[{"m":"A king 👑, yet he did not have the privileges of one, was constantly disrespected, yet uttered not a word.\n\nHe loved his own so much.","dt":"2024-05-09T12:53:00","s":["9a07315604"]}],"25":[{"m":"Ouhhh, so it is the blessings of Asher that we as believers do greatly covet in these our times.\n\nThat as our days, so shall our strength 💪.","dt":"2024-05-09T13:05:09","s":["c6e4e663a0"]}]},"34":{"1":[{"m":"An old man 👨 about to die yet possessed the strength 💪 of his youth and could climb 🧗‍♂️ a mountain ⛰ 🗻 all the way to the top to give up the ghost 👻","dt":"2024-05-09T13:07:22","s":["99107cc8b6"]}],"2":[{"m":"Obviously, either God showed him by a vision, more likely, or by an open vision, so he actually saw it with his eyes 👀, but his vision was greatly enhanced so he could see all the lands.\n\nGod took him, carried him on a trip throughout the land. Awesome 👏","dt":"2024-05-09T13:09:54","s":["1024fee820"]}],"5":[{"m":"Oh OK, this was how Moses died. By the work of the Lord.\n\nAgain God showed Moses all the land of promise before he died. Because after death you exit the earth 🌎 to paradise and have no dealings here.\n\nSo the Lord had to show him before he exited the earth 🌎","dt":"2022-03-22T07:38:20","s":["4feb34d14a"]}]}},"Ruth":{"1":{"4":[{"m":"Were they not supposed to intermarry in the first place, nor dwell amongst them? Well, they had already broken the law of not dwelling with them, so it was only a matter of time they married them. Though ironically, it was through this union that the great King David was born.\n\nSo they not intermarrying was not that the Moabites were inherently evil and unfit for good use by God, but because of their culture and idol worship, it was only a matter of time they would be influenced to drift away from God.\n\nIt was nothing personal.","dt":"2026-04-07T09:56:49","s":["p9nibpkdea"]}],"13":[{"m":"What a relationship between in-laws.\n\nIt was indeed an uncommon love among in-laws.\n\nThere could easily have been accusations and counter-accusations.\n\nMaybe their mother-in-law was a witch 🧙‍♀️, that was why she killed her husband and her two sons.\n\nOr at best she was cursed 🤬, and little wonder there was death ☠ all around her.\n\nOr maybe Ruth and Orpah, being sisters, came into her life to rid her of her two sons, and were likely behind the death of her husband as well.\n\nMaybe they were sent on an evil 😈 assignment.\n\nThis beautiful love story between these in-laws could have so easily gone south, and justifiably so.\n\nMeanwhile, in this relationship and lineage was to be the Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, the great King David and many other great men.\n\nIt could so easily have been marred.\n\nBut God is faithful and cared for and kept 💅 Naomi.\n\nMaking her smile again in her old age.\n\nIt's also quite interesting that Naomi was not branded a witch 🧙‍♀️ when she returned. Unlike here in Africa 🌍.\n\nHaving left with her sons and husband and returning with none of them.\n\nInterestingly, we see very little mention of the power of witchcraft and sorcery in impacting the lives of Israel and God's chosen people in the Bible.\n\nIf anything went wrong, it was because the Lord had allowed it, and they, rather than blame a witch or the power of darkness,\n\nSearched out what they had done wrong that made them incur the displeasure of the Lord.\n\nIt was never about the power of darkness or witch 🧙‍♀️ craft... But the hand 🖐️ of the LORD in all things, good and evil 😈.\n\nWe as believers must also be like-minded. The devil 👿 is a liar 🤥 when he postulates that he is the source of any power or evil happening to us or our family 👪.\n\nIndeed we are the cause, and our great God permitted it because we had gone out of alignment or never were in alignment in the first place.\n\nWe as believers must thus ask and enquire what went wrong and correct it accordingly.\n\nAs David said, and it stands true for us.\n\nPsalm 27:1-2 KJV\nThe LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid? [2] When the wicked, even mine enemies and my foes, came upon me to eat up my flesh, they stumbled and fell.\n\nWe must work the word out in our lives.","dt":"2024-05-23T08:17:41","s":["u0oqiz3s21","e2cc80be72"]}],"17":[{"m":"How did Ruth know the Lord and align with the God of Israel as her God?\n\nMaybe, and in all likelihood, she had heard of the LORD God of Israel 🇮🇱 and longed for him.\n\nAnd now she counted herself divinely blessed to have married an Israelite,\n\nShe had more faith than some who by blood were Israelites.\n\nAnd now that she had found herself connected to the Lord God of Israel, she was not going to go away back to her people.\n\nShe had converted to the God of Israel and was not going back, even if it meant she having less of a life whiles following after Israel's God.\n\nShe was not going to leave Naomi, her last human connection to Israel.\n\nShe would rather die than let go, for she knew that\n\nPsalm 84:10 KJV\nFor a day in thy courts is better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.\n\nOh, now I know and understand why the Lord so blessed Ruth.\n\nShe was indeed a true convert of God and showed more strength, courage, boldness and faith than most naturally born Israelites.\n\nShe represents the new covenant adoption as sons into God's fold 📂.\n\nEven in the Old Testament there were people who had a foretaste of the new covenant life and ways.\n\nOh my. GOD, I FEEL so stirred writing 📝 these things.\n\nOh indeed, the Lord is good and his ways unsearchable.\n\nRomans 11:33 KJV\nO the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of God! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!","dt":"2024-05-23T08:25:59","s":["kx51puq1pw","708c8ad5ff"]},{"m":"Why would she say that? I mean, why would she cleave so hard to her mother-in-law? What had she seen or heard which made her so much want to be a part of the people who crossed the Red Sea on dry ground, whose God was with them in physical form... the children of the man who wrestled with God and prevailed?\n\nShe had married one of them, only for him to die, but she was still going to stick around and stick it out to her death...","dt":"2026-04-07T10:03:06","s":["cyz6l2pyqi"]}],"1":[{"m":"What did he go to do in the land of Moab, a people forbidden from mingling with?\n\nThey were to have been destroyed outrightly from the entering in of the promised land (this point I'm not sure, i.e. about they being among those to be exterminated).\n\nBut Israel had formed leagues and watered 💦 down the command and statutes of the Lord.\n\nThere was to be a way of life of the Jews, but it was overlooked and these people did their own thing.","dt":"2024-05-22T12:50:37","s":["4kdsf4cqij"]},{"m":"These are Dake's notes or commentary on this verse. Very informative, I found it.\n\nTime of the Events of Ruth (Ch. 1:1) One thing is clear--the events of Ruth took place in the early days of the judges, because Ruth 4:21-22 states that Boaz was the son of Salmon who married Rahab the harlot of Jericho (Mt. 1:5). If Salmon married Rahab soon after the conquest of Jericho, the event would have to occur at least during the first 50 to 75 years of the 520 years from Joshua to Saul (for the chronology of this period, see Dispensation of Law). If Boaz was born to Salmon late in life and Boaz himself married late in life, the events would still have to take place in the first 100 years of the 520 years--during the judgeship of Othniel perhaps (Judg. 3:9-11), the 18 years of servitude to Moab (Judg. 3:12-14), or at the latest, during the time of Ehud (Judg. 3:15-20). If this is true, we must acknowledge that not all the names of the men in the genealogy of Christ were given at this point, because we have only four names in the list from Salmon to the birth of David, and the lives of four men would not cover that long a period, with the usual span of life being what it was at that time. It would have required Salmon, Boaz, Obed, and Jesse to have their children in this genealogy at the average age of 125 which is very unlikely. Bible scholars agree that not all the names of royal genealogies were always given, nor were they necessary; so it seems wise to recognize that some names have been omitted (Ruth 4:20-22; Mt. 1:4-6; Lk. 3:31-32). See notes, Mt. 1:8,11.","dt":"2024-05-23T06:27:01","s":["wclpreaq0m"]}],"20":[{"m":"Yep, they never saw misfortunes as the work of the devil 👿 solely, but the providence of God in allowing evil 😈 to befall his people.\n\nWe in Africa 🌍 solely attribute evil to the devil circumventing the plan of God, which gives the devil 👿 more power than is due him.\n\nWe indeed elevate Satan very highly, and the works of darkness highly.","dt":"2024-05-23T11:23:26","s":["dfdf1d4575"]}]},"2":{"12":[{"m":"Hm 🤔 Boaz has described Ruth perfectly 👌. She was a woman 👩 of genuine faith.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:17:34","s":["cbaa99b530"]},{"m":"Little did he know that the recompense would come through his very own hands.","dt":"2026-04-07T10:19:34","s":["yjryauew3h"]}],"19":[{"m":"God's law for the poor was working. See how, by gleaning in the fields of Boaz, she eventually made her mark in history, though poor.","dt":"2026-04-07T10:21:12","s":["1xue4c680y"]}],"23":[{"m":"So she stayed for quite a while in this gleaning business.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:23:01","s":["e32f228746"]}],"15":[{"m":"Boaz was already favoring her.\n\nWho wouldn't?\n\nWho wouldn't find attractive what Ruth had done? It was uncommon, to leave her own heritage for the Lord's, in order to take care of her mother-in-law.\n\nAny single rich man would find such a woman very attractive, a woman of humility and worth dwelling with.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:21:00","s":["2236133a6d"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"When did she make this statement of seeking rest for her daughter? I am sure Ruth had worked hard all harvest, and her mother-in-law was touched at her sincerity of heart in helping her all this while.\n\nAnd now she becomes a destiny helper for the young lady and opens a door of rest for her.","dt":"2026-04-07T10:28:05","s":["1542h1eglv"]}],"2":[{"m":"How did Naomi, who was not in the fields, know what Ruth, who was in the fields, ought to do?\n\nThis shows the power of experience and true mentorship.\n\nShe knew a Good Man like Boaz, if you give him a thousand years, would not make the move, though he was interested.\n\nSo the move had to be made for him.\n\nThese good men.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:25:23","s":["7814c949ed"]}],"11":[{"m":"Boaz, he was interested but 'feared'.\n\nThese kind of men. Hmm","dt":"2024-05-23T20:29:24","s":["o6e3og1hfu","7501a2d4a9"]}],"7":[{"m":"Obviously alcoholic, a drink 🍻 that maketh merry ought to be fermented.\n\nOr?","dt":"2024-05-23T20:28:14","s":["11da37630b"]}],"10":[{"m":"Boaz was a near kinsman to the dead. It was famine that drove them to go to Moab, so how come Boaz was now rich? I suspected he kept some seed and was one of the first to have planted, and he reaped mightily because he had corn, or wheat rather. Then he raked in the returns and planted big the next year, and the Lord rained mightily upon his land and blessed him.\n\nAnd now out of famine came a mighty man of wealth. This is my conjecture, my thoughts.","dt":"2026-04-07T10:32:11","s":["wh9i14nouz"]},{"m":"She showed her true kindness and love for her husband and his family by still seeking that children be raised up in the name of the dead, as required by custom.","dt":"2026-04-07T10:35:36","s":["atcey3t7oc"]}],"17":[{"m":"Oh, a wise woman and mentor for Ruth.\n\nShe knew when to make a move and when to stay put and be quiet.\n\nAnother wisdom piece for us.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:32:07","s":["dc8899e196"]}]},"4":{"12":[{"m":"What was there about the house of Pharez that attracted this blessing, and they being used as a worthy example?\n\nSo Pharez was the son of Judah, and Boaz was from the tribe of Judah.\n\nSo they were using their father Judah's son as reference for this blessing.\n\nThat just as Pharez was born to Judah, may this seed be as one born to Judah.\n\nBlessed Pharez.\n\nMaybe there is more to the house of Pharez which needs to be studied.\n\nIf my memory serves me right... Pharez was a twin who breached and came out before his brother.\n\nAnd it seems from the blessing that Pharez became great and famous among his father's house 🏡. Thus that same blessing was invoked on Ruth's children.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:36:50","s":["xzeh39f4xp","83462cae77"]}],"22":[{"m":"Jesse's grandfather was Boaz, a mighty man of wealth.\n\nHow come then that Jesse was not described in the same manner as his grandfather?\n\nIndeed we are let in on the wealth of Jesse when David's elder brother chastises David for leaving the few sheep 🐑 to come see the battle.\n\n1 Samuel 17:28 KJV\nAnd Eliab his eldest brother heard when he spake unto the men; and Eliab's anger was kindled against David, and he said, Why camest thou down hither? and with whom hast thou left those few sheep in the wilderness? I know thy pride, and the naughtiness of thine heart; for thou art come down that thou mightest see the battle.\n\nHow come Jesse couldn't preserve wealth as Jacob did?\n\nThis is what I mean: Abraham was very rich, he handed his riches to Isaac, who multiplied it.\n\nThis wealth was handed over to Jacob, who also increased it, and out of him came national Israel.\n\nBut not so with Boaz's generation.\n\nThis serves as a good lesson for us to set up systems for wealth creation and to covenant with the Lord, for he is eternal and he is able to preserve that which we have committed to him when we are dead and gone.\n\nPeace, strength, good health, purpose, new identity, forgiven, takes over our needs, takes away fear 😱, gives hope for the future","dt":"2024-05-23T19:15:53","s":["3ka51falxn"]},{"m":"Under the laws of levirate marriage (yibbum), a man fathers his own legal children by continuing to live with the widow after the first son is born. While the first son is legally \"raised up\" to the deceased brother, any subsequent children are typically considered the biological and legal offspring of the living brother.\n\nI got the above from Google, and this is what I make of it: could this be the reason why Jesse was not so rich a man, in that Obed inherited the property of his father, not that of Boaz? This is not stated in the Bible, just my conjecture.","dt":"2026-04-07T10:44:19","s":["khxj8h5s8w"]}],"10":[{"m":"Leaving without a name was terrible. So terrible 😰 the Lord provided an alternative for you — brothers who carry your genes — to raise up children and a generation for you, so your name remains.\n\nIt was not just expected, it was commanded of the Lord, and God actually killed someone for the sin of refusing to raise seed for his brother.","dt":"2024-05-23T20:35:34","s":["02a5482090"]}]}},"1 Samuel":{"1":{"9":[{"m":"What was the temple doing here? We are not told anything about a temple being built to the Lord, or to house the tabernacle of the Lord, so far in the history of Israel.\n\nCould it mean they built a structure to protect the tabernacle proper?\n\nDake's acknowledges that it may be a more permanent structure built for the tabernacle, and adds an extra layer of explanation that it may also be a living quarters for the priests to help in their daily duties.\n\nAnd backs it up with the scripture where God says he has not lived in any dwelling place or temple all this while — 2nd Samuel 7:6,\n\nso it's likely this temple was for the priests, but then,\n\nWhen we study the call of Samuel... \"and ere the lamp of God went out in the temple of the LORD, where the ark of God was, and Samuel was laid down to sleep;\" 1st Samuel 3:3\n\nThis shows Samuel slept in the temple where the ark also was.","dt":"2024-05-24T08:18:05","s":["a9mvvyim1g","b05241d8ce"]}],"16":[{"m":"Yes indeed, for a drunk to come to the temple, such an one definitely had not the fear 😱 of God and qualifies to be a daughter of Belial.","dt":"2024-05-24T08:34:23","s":["e63b5a40e8"]}],"24":[{"m":"Three bullocks? Elkanah was wealthy.","dt":"2024-05-24T08:39:42","s":["2e88a07f61"]}],"5":[{"m":"As stated earlier in my commentary in Ruth, the people of Israel never blamed the devil 👿 or witches 🧙‍♀️ for anything.\n\nBut everything was attributable to God, whether good or evil 😈.\n\nEvil because the Lord did not cause the evil but permitted it to happen, though he could have intruded to stop the evil from happening.\n\nThe devil was given no privileges or place in the happenings of the children of the prince 🤴 of power with God, Israel.\n\nSo low is the devil in the scheme of God's greatness that he did not earn mention in the Old Testament and in God's dealings with his people.\n\nEven in the New Testament, where he is mentioned often, it was because he was being dealt with by the power of God, and we were being let in on the happenings in the realm of spirits.","dt":"2024-05-24T08:14:06","s":["fe76a974ec"]}],"11":[{"m":"Samuel was dedicated a Nazarite from birth, and his mum refused to exercise her right of redemption of her first born son.\n\nShe was going to allow him to fulfill the obligations of the first born as dedicated to the Lord.","dt":"2026-04-08T19:27:49","s":["4t61iltexa"]}],"28":[{"m":"Wow\n\nShe honored her word.","dt":"2024-05-24T08:41:10","s":["4b59a64a94"]}]},"2":{"12":[{"m":"A very strange statement. A statement that makes you wonder how this was possible 🙆.\n\nHow could the sons of Eli, who were priests of the Lord, the mediators and ones set apart to commune with the Lord, not know him?\n\nWhat then were they doing in the priestly office to start with?\n\nBut sadly this statement is true in the times of Eli and is true today.\n\nMany priests and pastors — generally many so-called men of God — do not know the Lord.\n\nThe Lord they serve and teach about — it's a strange paradox.\n\nVery strange indeed.","dt":"2024-05-28T05:49:16","s":["f9d62e5624"]}],"17":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... As I read these parts, I noticed God had become very lenient at this time in his dealings with his people.\n\nThis practice would not have survived one day in the times of Moses.\n\nIt did not mean God was not to be feared 😨. For he was still God.\n\nIndeed, it is wisdom to still FEAR GOD the way they did in the times of Moses, even if you lived in the times of Eli's sons and saw the forbearance of God.\n\nIt did not mean he had changed. Indeed, anytime God's long suffering is demonstrated, it is for this one purpose.\n\n2 Peter 3:9 AMP\nThe Lord does not delay [as though He were unable to act] and is not slow about His promise, as some count slowness, but is [extraordinarily] patient toward you, not wishing for any to perish but for all to come to repentance.\n\nYes, it is to lead to repentance.\n\nAnd as we see from Eli's story, when God suffers us for long and we don't repent, the punishment is worse.\n\nFor the sons of Aaron, they were killed instantly and their generations cut off, because they had no children.\n\nFor Eli and his sons, they were cut off and the entire priesthood taken from them.\n\nAnd God watched over his word all through the descendants till he removed the priesthood from their hands and their lineage.\n\nSo their sins caused a curse 🤬 on their seed 🌱 and their living descendants.\n\nAnd so now I fear 😱, in this light I fear greatly, for our generation has been given a very long leash by the Lord.\n\nAnd we keep praying 🙏 for mercy and extension of time ⌚.\n\nBut when the long suffering of God comes to an end,\n\nWoe to us.\n\nOh Lord, have mercy 😢\n\nI Samuel 2:17 NKJV\nTherefore the sin of the young men was very great before the Lord, for men abhorred the offering of the Lord.","dt":"2024-05-27T07:36:25","s":["n2sel06ub4","iml0kzhgtm","d489b72adf"]}],"18":[{"m":"In time past I used to wonder how that Samuel, who is from Mount 🗻 Ephraim, could be allowed into the priesthood, seeing he was not a Levite.\n\nBut he was the first born, and the Levites were swapped for the first born of all Israelites because of the death of the first born sons of the Egyptians.\n\nLong story short, Samuel was the first born, and instead of a Levite being swapped for him and the family paying a little token to the Lord,\n\nThey chose to give him directly as promised, without swapping him for a Levite.\n\nAnd Hannah's need fell right in line with God's need.\n\nThe priesthood had been corrupted by Eli and his sons.\n\nThe word of the Lord had become scarce in those days, and Israel 🇮🇱 was slowly moving into apostasy.\n\nGod needed a worthy example to use.\n\nAnd there comes Hannah, who had longed for a child all this while.\n\nWhy should God give her a child 🧒, to what end, when he could have a part in her child and give her others later?\n\nAnd so he waited for Hannah till she was so driven with sorrow that she was willing to give birth and give her son to the Lord.\n\nAt least she was used to not having a child, but the shame and public ridicule was something she could never get used to.\n\nShe could bargain with the Lord and give her son out to the Lord — a loss for her, but at least no one could call her barren.\n\nAnd this she did, and God blessed her with some more children 🧒.\n\nImagine she had made this decision earlier... Then Eli's corrupt sons would not have had such a field day for so long.\n\nBut such is the life.","dt":"2024-05-27T07:59:13","s":["dn49ba6w4a","6c3fe905dc"]}],"21":[{"m":"My pastor made a statement that as the first fruit, i.e. Samuel, grew, the blessings (his other brothers and sisters) were provided and multiplied, grew,\n\nTo which I add, no mention ever is made of Samuel's siblings,\n\nIndeed, he was lent out permanently to the Lord; he was the Lord's. He had been cut off from them, and for that the Lord gave Hannah five fold.\n\nShe used her life and womb and the pain of childbirth all to the Lord.\n\nSuch sacrifice could not go unnoticed by the Lord.","dt":"2024-08-11T08:59:00","s":["ylbqbc7gys"]}],"29":[{"m":"The Lord expected him to be stricter on his sons and enforce discipline, but it seems he himself was partaker of their evil ways by just reprimanding them and doing nothing else in such a dangerous matter.\n\nAll he did, or was recorded as doing, was that he advised them and described as transgressions such an abomination as this.\n\nPeople in his lineage died for less. Eli knew this.\n\nHe knows what happened to the two ✌️ sons of Aaron who offered strange fire 🔥 before the Lord.\n\nThey were consumed by strange fire from the Lord 🔥","dt":"2026-04-09T06:00:34","s":["fgzw8zszar"]}],"30":[{"m":"Oh my Lord and my God. A true and just God.","dt":"2024-05-27T08:13:47","s":["obkrphhltj","elwe8tnshc","b4ef0692fd"]}],"35":[{"m":"His anointed — was it referencing the Christ? I believe so.\n\nThe eternal God had plans to reward Samuel's faithfulness into eternity.\n\n1 Samuel 2:30 NKJV\nTherefore the Lord God of Israel says: ‘I said indeed that your house and the house of your father would walk before Me forever.’ But now the Lord says: ‘Far be it from Me; for those who honor Me I will honor, and those who despise Me shall be lightly esteemed.","dt":"2024-05-27T08:13:03","s":["peimqp8f2m","amm7uoy9g9","75bbdf13e3"]}],"36":[{"m":"A sad ending for Eli, his sons and his descendants.","dt":"2024-05-27T08:14:13","s":["1d137fcc07","fsj2slqfn8"]},{"m":"So outside of the ministry work, the descendants of Eli shall starve and suffer want.\n\nIt is only the ministry work that will give them bare survival.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:02:50","s":["idrzx60prf"]}],"5":[{"m":"She was already prophesying about her own future.\n\nShe went on to bear more children 🧒 aside Samuel, though she did not know that.","dt":"2024-05-27T07:20:26","s":["f92bf1de9a"]}],"22":[{"m":"Now they had gotten worse.\n\nFrom stealing meat 🥩 meant for the Lord, and now committing whoredom right 👉 at the door 🚪 of the tabernacle.\n\nIn the very presence of God.\n\nSo it is with every corrupt practice in the Lord's house. It only leads to more and more corruption.\n\nBefore you know it, you are committing wonderful sins you never dreamt possible by you.\n\nSo what we see today in the church ⛪ is not new.\n\nThere is nothing new under the sun.","dt":"2024-05-27T08:02:39","s":["qplgxromua","3797ca6347"]}],"25":[{"m":"Hmm. God cannot be mocked. They thought 💭 to mock God with their actions, but God cannot be mocked.\n\nGalatians 6:7-8 KJV\nBe not deceived; God is not mocked: for whatsoever a man soweth, that shall he also reap. [8] For he that soweth to his flesh shall of the flesh reap corruption; but he that soweth to the Spirit shall of the Spirit reap life everlasting.\n\nAnd they thought to be shrewd with God.\n\nWhat they did not know was that God, being holy, is also very shrewd.\n\nPsalm 18:26 NLT\nTo the pure you show yourself pure, but to the crooked you show yourself shrewd.\n\nAnd this he did to the sons of Eli.","dt":"2024-05-28T05:54:39","s":["4db7ff853f"]}]},"3":{"10":[{"m":"Ah, so refreshing to see God the Father here again being described in almost literal and physical terms, though he is a spirit.\n\nIt has been a while God was described in this way, i.e. appearing in his place at the altar and in the tabernacle, his dwelling place.\n\nIndeed, the word of the Lord was scarce, but God had found himself a man 👨, the boy Samuel.\n\nNow God was back 💪.","dt":"2024-05-28T06:11:15","s":["cb79741801"]}],"17":[{"m":"How did Eli know that the Lord had spoken clearly and it concerned something important?\n\nHow come he seemed so versed in the things of God?\n\nMaybe he himself used to experience same as a boy 🧒, or when he was much younger.\n\nBut now it seems as the Lord had left him.\n\nBut he still knew the ways of God and of his Spirit.\n\nEli was no carnal man, as seen by what even killed him.\n\nThe news of the capture of the ark of the Lord.\n\nThe glory of Israel captured by the uncircumcised Philistines.\n\nAn abomination. He knew at that point that God had abandoned them.\n\nAt that moment he died.\n\nAs terrible as that news and incident of the ark capture was, God was still with Israel.\n\nIndeed, he was now beginning his dealing with Samuel, through whom he dealt with Israel.\n\nSo sometimes, in the worst of moments, seemingly when God has disappeared from the scene...\n\nHe's working something new in the background.\n\nIt was in that same season that the kings were born... Kings such as Saul and David.","dt":"2024-05-28T06:19:21","s":["wubyvti7lv","98980163c6"]}],"21":[{"m":"How does one reveal words? Revealed by the word of the Lord... What or how is this done?","dt":"2022-04-22T11:51:41","s":["6cb5aeff0f"]},{"m":"Some believe “the LORD appeared again” to refer to his visible presence coming down once again in the cloud cover, whiles it could also mean the word of the Lord became more regular, as if God was now back again, though he didn't go anywhere.\n\nIt was their sins that had hidden his face from them.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:24:36","s":["4vovwysln7"]}],"4":[{"m":"In a sense, this goes to show God does speak through the voice of his servants... through preaching, counsel and advice.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:06:04","s":["qt3x2pmtth"]}],"7":[{"m":"He did not know the Lord? Of course he knew the Lord... He was a priest.\n\nHe did not yet know the Lord in knowing his ways and in hearing and identifying his voice.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:10:52","s":["bwso08e65s"]}],"8":[{"m":"Double meaning here.\n\nOne being God had called Samuel as described here, and the second being Samuel had received a calling — i.e. he had been ushered by God into his prophetic office.\n\nEven though, reading contextually, it's in reference to a literal verbal call, as in when one calls another.\n\nBut the second is so right even within the context.","dt":"2024-05-28T06:06:50","s":["650d263a7e"]}],"13":[{"m":"Not the iniquity which he committed, but the one he knoweth and did nothing about.\n\nAn iniquity he called only a transgression. He made light of it, though he knew how grievous it was.\n\nWhy didn't God speak to the boys himself? Maybe he did, though I suspect he did not.\n\nThese were sons of Belial and not worth his time and attention.\n\nHe won't honour them with his voice and word apart from what was written, which they were not obeying anyways.\n\nThat would suffice, and if they refused that one, it was up to them.\n\nIt's like Abraham telling the rich man that the law and the written word was enough, and they need not any to come out of the grave for them to believe.\n\nIf they disobeyed the written word... no miracle would convince them otherwise.\n\nI wonder, so does that mean Eli did not repent even after he was warned by the first man of God?","dt":"2026-04-09T06:17:24","s":["c46fer61ul"]}],"18":[{"m":"He left his fate in the hands of the Lord at this point.","dt":"2024-05-28T06:42:55","s":["e52bd6554c"]}],"19":[{"m":"So God can decide that the words of someone should fall to the ground and become mere empty words, words without substance, by not causing them to happen.\n\nBut with someone, his words came to pass.\n\nWe really have to study this our Father and know his ways and his word.","dt":"2024-05-28T06:46:43","s":["cbf78738fa"]}]},"4":{"4":[{"m":"Look at them... after all their disobedience, they thought God was an idol to be carried around and used to do one's bidding.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:27:39","s":["m1jey4tnir"]}],"7":[{"m":"“The word of Samuel came to all Israel” is an expression of how that Samuel instructed the people.","dt":"2022-04-22T11:52:49","s":["a001824537"]}],"11":[{"m":"They were to guard the ark, and now the Philistines wanted it.\n\nWith their depravity, I'm sure Hophni and Phinehas fled and abandoned the ark...\n\nThe Philistines probably slew them in their flight.\n\nThey did not fear 😱 God; why would they stand in defence of the ark at the peril of their lives?","dt":"2024-05-28T09:37:39","s":["73f1a58b85"]},{"m":"Am sure they guarded the ark with their life, because they knew what it represented.\n\nSo there was some right in them... Some fear of the Lord, and this is where we ought to be very careful.\n\nWe might be doing some things right, i.e. in service, yet rejected by the Lord because we rejected his word to us and were selective in obedience.\n\nServing in his house yet walking in rebellion to his word.\n\nService does not equate obedience.\n\nThey stood to defend the ark from capture...\n\nThe source and tool for their sumptuous feeding and their unbridled lust.\n\nThey didn't know the Lord did not care about the capture of the ark.\n\nHe was going to use its seeming capture to make his name great again.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:33:27","s":["zmrtsngler"]}],"13":[{"m":"Refer to notes in chapter 3 verse 17\n\nHow did Eli know that the Lord had spoken clearly and it concerned something important?\n\nHow come he seemed so versed in the things of God?\n\nMaybe he himself used to experience same as a boy 🧒, or when he was much younger.\n\nBut now it seems as the Lord had left him.\n\nBut he still knew the ways of God and of his Spirit.\n\nEli was no carnal man, as seen by what even killed him.\n\nThe news of the capture of the ark of the Lord.\n\nThe glory of Israel captured by the uncircumcised Philistines.\n\nAn abomination. He knew at that point that God had abandoned them.\n\nAt that moment he died.\n\nAs terrible as that news and incident of the ark capture was, God was still with Israel.\n\nIndeed, he was now beginning his dealing with Samuel, through whom he dealt with Israel.\n\nSo sometimes, in the worst of moments, seemingly when God has disappeared from the scene...\n\nHe's working something new in the background.\n\nIt was in that same season that the kings were born... Kings such as Saul and David.\n\n1 Samuel 3:17 KJV\nAnd he said, What is the thing that the LORD hath said unto thee? I pray thee hide it not from me: God do so to thee, and more also, if thou hide any thing from me of all the things that he said unto thee.\n\nNOTE 2","dt":"2024-06-04T11:57:00","s":["cbcd647a9a"]}],"18":[{"m":"Refer to notes in chapter 3 verse 17\n\nHow did Eli know that the Lord had spoken clearly and it concerned something important?\n\nHow come he seemed so versed in the things of God?\n\nMaybe he himself used to experience same as a boy 🧒, or when he was much younger.\n\nBut now it seems as the Lord had left him.\n\nBut he still knew the ways of God and of his Spirit.\n\nEli was no carnal man, as seen by what even killed him.\n\nThe news of the capture of the ark of the Lord.\n\nThe glory of Israel captured by the uncircumcised Philistines.\n\nAn abomination. He knew at that point that God had abandoned them.\n\nAt that moment he died.\n\nAs terrible as that news and incident of the ark capture was, God was still with Israel.\n\nIndeed, he was now beginning his dealing with Samuel, through whom he dealt with Israel.\n\nSo sometimes, in the worst of moments, seemingly when God has disappeared from the scene...\n\nHe's working something new in the background.\n\nIt was in that same season that the kings were born... Kings such as Saul and David.\n\n1 Samuel 3:17 KJV\nAnd he said, What is the thing that the LORD hath said unto thee? I pray thee hide it not from me: God do so to thee, and more also, if thou hide any thing from me of all the things that he said unto thee.","dt":"2024-05-28T09:39:18","s":["8m4izjvm1a"]},{"m":"At the death ☠ of his sons his heart did not fail; God had already told him.\n\nBut at the capture of the ark he died.\n\nIndeed, this man's heart was on the spiritual.\n\nEven though he had failed God, his heart ♥ was for the Lord.\n\nThe only problem was that he loved the Lord but also loved the flesh, and failed to correct his sons.\n\nHe knew his sons might die, but for the ark of God to be captured was terrible.\n\nThis was worse than he had thought. God did not reveal to Samuel that such a terrible 😰 thing will befall Israel.\n\nAt the thought of this he died, died knowing Israel's glory had departed.","dt":"2024-05-28T09:43:40","s":["72b7400b7a"]},{"m":"It wasn't the news of the death of his sons that killed him, but that of the Lord's ark captured.\n\nSome sons are better dead than alive.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:35:41","s":["fgtu00gxce"]}],"20":[{"m":"She cared more for the ark and the glory of Israel and her husband and her father-in-law than for this new life and hope that was coming into the world 🗺.\n\nShe named him Ichabod — the whole family 👪 of Eli were very spiritual and sensitive to the things of God, though rebellion was found in them.\n\nIt did not exempt them from judgements though.\n\nAnd such is life sometimes, that the dark and terrible things that beset us in this life take away our joy and hope, such that we give up and fail to appreciate the new life and hope around us.\n\nIt is one of the things we must guard against when we go through life's dark alley, lest we run the risk of the seed 🌱 of hopelessness being sown in our hearts 💕.\n\nSuch that we fail to see the new thing that God is doing.\n\nNo matter how terrible 😰 a situation is, there is hope with God.\n\nThe whole glory and power of Israel had been taken; it marked a dark time in the history of Israel, but it was also a new dawn.\n\nMighty kings 👑 were going to be born who would do great and mighty exploits in the absence of the ark of God.\n\nBecause the Spirit 🧚‍♂️ of God was still at work, even as he is today.\n\nThey did not know then that the God of all the earth did not need a tabernacle to dwell in to be present among his people.\n\nOh, if only Eli had known that the God of all flesh dwells in fleshly tabernacles.\n\nThat a time was going to come that God would dwell with man — O Immanuel.\n\nIf only they knew.","dt":"2024-05-28T09:53:23","s":["orxhuj92mm","3fc7ce1dab"]}],"6":[{"m":"They had heard about stories of the ark, strange stories which were told them by their fathers.\n\nThey had been told that Israel had a totem 🗿, an idol shaped as an ark with two ✌️ angels.\n\nIt was made of pure gold. And it produced great victory ✌️ for Israel.\n\nThat was how Israel was rescued from Egypt and annexed Canaan to themselves.\n\nIf not, how else could such a feeble and weak people conquer Anak and the rest of the giant nations?\n\nOh, many a strange and terrible 😰 story had been told of this ark.\n\nAnd now here the ark had been brought to the war front.\n\nThis was terrible news for the Philistines.\n\nBut nevertheless they gingered themselves and trusted in their god Dagon for victory ✌️, and went out against Israel.\n\nIt was altar against altar.\n\nAs I type these words my eyes are teary 😢, as it dawns on me that this is not just a story but a fact of history.\n\nA history which remains relevant to us, because today we have Israel as a nation and we have God still with us.\n\nOh, if only we would give ourselves wholly to him. Oh, what a great work he would do with us and to us and through us.","dt":"2024-05-28T08:22:45","s":["ae5c988b41"]}]},"5":{"5":[{"m":"Instead of learning from this and realizing the supremacy of the God of Israel and converting,\n\nThey formed another religious ritual out of it.\n\nThis was how loyal these Philistines were: just as one cannot change one's parents nor do away with your history and ancestry, these were children 🧒 of Dagon and stayed their allegiance to death ☠.\n\nContrast this with Israel, who were ever so quick to cling unto new gods they know nought of.","dt":"2024-05-28T09:59:23","s":["r5v8kx1utt","14c7179b76"]}],"7":[{"m":"Was this not an appropriate point to repent and serve the one true God?","dt":"2022-04-22T11:59:36","s":["t3m7yu9we6"]},{"m":"It's interesting they noticed that God's hand was not just against them but against their god.\n\nYet they did not repent nor convert to the one true God.","dt":"2024-05-28T10:06:09","s":["4k7pli5a1n"]}],"12":[{"m":"This was a very good strategy. More like a Trojan horse 🐴.\n\nGod took advantage to destroy them and also teach them a lesson in respect for the God of Israel.","dt":"2024-05-28T10:08:28","s":["763401efdb"]},{"m":"Their cry went up to heaven — to do what there? These were Philistines...\n\nMaybe this was just an expression to mean they cried out loud, or really their cry reached heaven, for God heard and answered them in leading the cattle to its place in Israel 🇮🇱","dt":"2026-04-09T06:43:16","s":["lo6392mg7d"]}],"11":[{"m":"Next time","dt":"2024-05-28T10:07:21","s":["c9koj83dye","4cfc9445d2"]}]},"6":{"5":[{"m":"Where did they get this counsel from? Was it really from the Lord, or it was from their own pagan minds?\n\nProbably they had sent for and enquired, and knew that Israel often offered trespass offering to the Lord, so they decided to do likewise.\n\nEven after giving their counsel, the conclusion was that peradventure he might spare them.\n\nSo they themselves were not sure.","dt":"2022-05-06T14:04:10","s":["f5ulq1ng92"]},{"m":"I won't be surprised 😲 after this he lightened his hand upon them, so they know it was the Lord all along and not a mere coincidence.","dt":"2024-05-28T10:10:08","s":["5uaojunnv6"]}],"6":[{"m":"But this was a long time ago. Yet so powerful was the lesson that after over centuries, the story still rages on.","dt":"2022-05-06T14:16:09","s":["61mgzlbche"]}],"18":[{"m":"Numbers do have meaning in spiritual matters.","dt":"2026-04-09T06:49:30","s":["ikwca3nf86"]}],"20":[{"m":"Obviously the law and its reading 📖 to all people had been abolished; there was no structure to ensure that across Israel they knew the laws of God.\n\nOr even if there was, it was mere religious teaching, and the people did not take it to heart ♥.\n\nHad they done so, they would know to stay away from it rather than to go glance into it.\n\nThey had heard it was holy and only the high priest saw it.\n\nNow it was their opportunity to see what no man saw. And so they died.","dt":"2024-05-28T10:15:01","s":["1d548318fe"]}]},"8":{"11":[{"m":"It is interesting, but up to this point in Israel's history they did not know the way of kings in practice. Despite the harshness of having a government, the people still wanted it.\n\nIn my opinion, having a king or kingly tribe to rule them did nothing better.\n\nAt least when a judge ruled, he was righteous and a man of God.\n\nBut how can you guarantee that every seed of the royal line will be righteous or fear God?","dt":"2022-05-06T14:33:09","s":["d0c9de559d"]}],"15":[{"m":"Was the tenth not for the Lord? Well, the Lord would still take his tenth as well as the king. But the king would not tithe the Lord, but vice versa. The two systems would now run concurrently.\n\nBut for the longest time, theocracy and the kingship would clash every now and again.","dt":"2026-04-10T06:30:26","s":["ccrbvwttti"]}],"17":[{"m":"Ah, taxes right there. God knew how corrupt this system was, and no wonder he was against it.","dt":"2022-05-06T14:35:28","s":["tzdcr3ulhr"]},{"m":"God knew the ways of kings, that Israel, who were God's children and not under any form of bondage both physically and economically, warned them of the dangers of a king.\n\nBut their mind was made up; they were God's free men but were willing to come under bondage.\n\n1 Corinthians 7:22 KJV\nFor he that is called in the Lord, being a servant, is the Lord's freeman: likewise also he that is called, being free, is Christ's servant.","dt":"2024-05-30T16:08:56","s":["rbi9so6irq"]}],"18":[{"m":"Hmm, they were warned. As is the case even today, all people cry out against their governments.\n\nSuch madness running the state.","dt":"2022-05-06T14:36:25","s":["6129a4543c"]}],"20":[{"m":"They were offered the flesh and the spirit, and they chose the flesh.","dt":"2024-05-30T16:12:17","s":["eee91e0507"]},{"m":"They didn't want miracles, signs and wonders? They wanted the predictability of human systems they could control, even if it failed in bringing them victory.\n\nIn a way, this was quiet rebellion, in that even if they displeased the LORD and rebelled against him - they and their king - they could still go out to war without waiting on the Lord. Of course, the good kings relied on God and his prophets, and they were victorious.","dt":"2026-04-10T06:33:46","s":["lsrgn4q8g"]}],"6":[{"m":"Samuel was a wise leader, though he was displeased with their request and he knew that theocracy was better than kingship.\n\nHe still took the people's request to the Lord.","dt":"2024-05-29T06:28:22","s":["828c558230"]}],"8":[{"m":"GOD here sounds more empathetic to their demands. He knew this time would come. He had said so himself earlier. They rejected the theocracy. They wanted a kind of continuity they could count on without relying on God, even if that meant the descendants of the king did not fear God.\n\nA thing which they knew would definitely happen. I believe God entertained this new experiment because he himself had a kingdom agenda, where his son would rule as king forever in righteousness, so he let them be.","dt":"2026-04-10T06:25:12","s":["pbdiq6sj0d"]}],"9":[{"m":"God was so wise in his dealings with Israel.\n\nThey wanted something that God himself was not pleased with, because it would not help them.\n\nGod himself knew it was not the better option, and knew that they had made up their minds, yet he suggested that they should be told the truth even though it would be rejected.","dt":"2024-05-30T16:05:50","s":["ed1ffaf50d"]}]},"9":{"6":[{"m":"This servant was under Spirit influence without knowing, and they did just as the Lord had said to Samuel before...\n\nI can imagine the angels of God suggesting thoughts and the right emotions to compel them to come to the man of God.\n\nThey met even the right people to direct them on their course.","dt":"2022-10-27T15:22:01","s":["xfskl924wb"]},{"m":"So all this while they were being led by the divine hand 🖐️ of God to bring them to this point.\n\nAt times when they felt tired, a sudden wave 🌊 of strength and of hope comes to them, and they continue their journey.\n\nThey were thus led until they came to this point of wanting to turn back, but the very thought of having come this far without success was not appealing.\n\nSo once more an idea came 💡, an idea to consult a known seer of the town, and consulting they did.","dt":"2024-05-31T06:12:37","s":["6bf18d34d3"]},{"m":"I just am wondering, who chose this servant? Of all the servants, one was chosen who knew the prophet and his track record. When the hand of God begins his work, it is just so beautiful.","dt":"2026-04-10T06:39:20","s":["ezgmhhv3w0"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh my God.\n\nThe confidence with which the Lord spoke.\n\nThe Father of all flesh, unto whom shall all flesh come.\n\nThey thought they were chasing donkeys but did not know they were under an influence.\n\nI suspect the donkeys themselves were led - Obviously.","dt":"2024-05-31T06:15:23","s":["31a4f9fe9e"]}],"21":[{"m":"God likes using seemingly insignificant people - to fulfill his grand purpose, so all men shall see that this indeed is the Lord's doing.\n\nHe did start off with Saul of Benjamin - a tribe that was almost exterminated, a man of low repute - and he set him up on high.\n\nAfter Saul failed the Lord, God still sought for a man from the backside of the desert 🏜 to fulfill his mandate.\n\nGod is just like that; he is the one who lifts up the low from the dunghill, so he chooses the low in heart as candidates for his lifting.","dt":"2024-05-31T06:24:34","s":["e1cc2509d9"]}],"24":[{"m":"Who were the people invited to dine with the future King? I believe these were men of repute, the very people who had asked for a king from the prophet who was ruling them.\n\nIt is only in a merciful system like that of a theocracy that you can ask your ruler, selected by God, to select his own replacement while he was alive, and expect a fair best choice for you.\n\nIt is interesting. I believe if these were other gods, they would have dealt drastically with such requests.\n\nWere these men even aware that their actions were in fulfillment of a prophecy?","dt":"2026-04-10T07:28:59","s":["jdoz4f8j3o"]}],"27":[{"m":"Wow... This word was not for public consumption","dt":"2024-05-31T06:25:56","s":["jepgdc9f99","879b13a51c"]}],"4":[{"m":"He did not know there was a divine hand upon the whole situation, steering him away from home to the throne. God being in charge of it all.","dt":"2026-04-10T06:37:48","s":["m1ibtxzzyc"]}],"9":[{"m":"Before which time? The author of this book, what time did he live in?","dt":"2026-04-10T06:40:13","s":["45eoddz81i"]}]},"10":{"9":[{"m":"And now the Spirit of the Lord was upon him, and great grace became his portion.\n\nHis path was aligned right 👉 with God, and divinity was with him.","dt":"2022-10-27T16:05:32","s":["5yli5tji0d"]},{"m":"His heart ♥ was first changed, then those signs spoken of began to happen to him.\n\nIt's like the anointing marked him and those things began to be attracted to him.","dt":"2024-05-31T13:18:45","s":["d9v9py38qb"]}],"20":[{"m":"What does the Bible mean by \"was taken\"?\n\nWas it by lot, by the Urim and Thummim, or what?\n\nIt's akin to when Achan brought in the accursed thing to the camp and was taken.","dt":"2024-05-31T14:03:14","s":["yh7x98ji7i","ae3777c672"]}],"22":[{"m":"So this answers the question 🙋 in verse 20 of whether their enquiring was a spiritual activity or purely lots and chance.\n\nHere, after the lot fell on Saul, they could not find him, so they enquired further.\n\nMeaning all this while they were enquiring.\n\nWhat a world 🗺. To watch men enquire of the Lord and immediately get answers, live and in real time ⌚","dt":"2024-05-31T15:36:25","s":["zomnypfsxt","0167d17da3"]}],"25":[{"m":"The manner of royalty 👑 and kings was set up thus.","dt":"2022-10-27T16:04:23","s":["102v2hi1hv"]},{"m":"The manner of the kingdom was scripted for all to see.","dt":"2024-05-31T15:38:20","s":["o9nhbnrvrv"]}],"1":[{"m":"Samuel, the great prophet Samuel, showed respect to Saul, a nobody, by kissing him and anointing him.\n\nThis automatically lifted Saul to a higher pedestal; he was among the great.\n\nAnd his kingship was sealed by an anointing with oil.\n\nThe oil of the Lord.\n\nPreviously God himself anointed the people by his Spirit coming upon them.\n\nWithout any tokens and signs.\n\nBut now the times of the judges were over, and the system of kings was being set up.\n\nA system marked by physical ceremonies, but still ends up being sealed by the Spirit.\n\nHis Spirit comes upon the kings as the human gesture of anointing with oil was done.\n\nSame anointing, different dispensation and methods.","dt":"2024-05-31T06:31:15","s":["nna9wi8124","07257bc62c"]}],"6":[{"m":"The Spirit turns men to other men.\n\nNo wonder David said, \"thou anointedst my head with oil\", and as a result, \"my cup overflows\".","dt":"2024-05-31T06:35:52","s":["b53c168817"]}],"26":[{"m":"God save the King... There went with him men whose heart God had touched. When God calls, he makes available men to help and sustain his purpose and calling upon your life.","dt":"2026-04-10T07:39:25","s":["jgm0yn4u5i"]}]},"11":{"3":[{"m":"Such pomposity from the enemy, and he agreed to their demands. He knew they had no help; they couldn't help themselves, and no one could help them either.\n\nBut they did not know things had changed.","dt":"2026-04-10T07:41:37","s":["n35j2jg04r"]}],"7":[{"m":"Saul acted based on the Spirit coming upon him, and because of that anointing, his fear fell upon the people and they followed him.\n\nJust as Samuel had told him... \"do as occasion serves\"\n\nNow here was an occasion, and God was with him.","dt":"2022-10-29T10:01:50","s":["3qt3j8g14z"]},{"m":"If THE Spirit of God is upon a man 👨, that man can gather for the kingdom of God.\n\nGod here put fear upon the people, and it caused them to join Saul in battle.\n\nThis is not the first time the Spirit of God has come upon a man for him to gather God's people for war and for service.\n\nWe see it in Gideon also, and many other judges.","dt":"2024-05-31T15:48:45","s":["daea269e97"]}],"12":[{"m":"Now the evidence of his calling and anointing was seen.\n\nNow there was zest in the tone and approach of the people.","dt":"2024-05-31T15:50:17","s":["4c2fceb15c"]}],"15":[{"m":"So his kingdom was strengthened further, for proof of his calling was bare for all to see.","dt":"2022-10-29T10:04:51","s":["a36f66b4e5"]}],"14":[{"m":"So really not all the people had accepted Saul as king 👑.\n\nLet's not forget that at such a time, when a new kingdom is being established, there are varied interests and factions.\n\nSamuel's influence, both spiritual and through years of judging, backed Saul.\n\nBut that was not powerful enough to ensure acceptance by the whole nation.\n\nBut now that heaven had responded by helping Saul to gather the people for war, he had expanded his authority and influence.\n\nHe had a standing army with victory ✌️, spoils of war and weaponry on their side.\n\nNow he was king indeed. This was a fine opportunity to consolidate his authority and kingship, and this Samuel did at Gilgal.\n\nThe next question 🙋, however, is, why Gilgal?\n\nDake's commentary explains that it was at Gilgal that they first entered Canaan, so it was befitting in that regard to go renew the kingdom where it all started from.","dt":"2024-06-03T08:05:06","s":["sij4nnsq0b","6f3ff655b4"]}],"5":[{"m":"Saul's kingdom was still new, and he was still following after the herd, and yet so humble.","dt":"2022-10-29T09:59:50","s":["7342a19143"]}]},"12":{"3":[{"m":"And \"before his anointed\" - was that not in reference to king 👑 Saul?","dt":"2024-06-03T08:10:46","s":["517d76a56e"]}],"12":[{"m":"In the text 1 Samuel 8:1 to 6, it is clearly stated that they wanted a king to judge them like the other nations, because Samuel's sons were dubious and not at all like their father.\n\nNo mention was made of the war with Nahash the Ammonite, but Dake's suggests it seemed that war was pending.\n\nWe see here that the fear of Nahash was also a contributing factor to why they wanted a king like the other nations.\n\nOne to lead them to war like the other nations.","dt":"2024-06-03T08:44:07","s":["j2c21q2xsd","0e0851cf3a"]}],"19":[{"m":"Is it not interesting that they did not change their mind about the king after this?\n\nNeedless to say, they were already too deep into the kingdom, and God had given his approval, so there was no turning back.","dt":"2024-06-03T08:46:50","s":["yzkqmxnhvv"]},{"m":"God was displeased with the people's desire for a king,\n\nbut there was no turning back... The people were one, and their hearts yearned for a king.\n\nGod knew that when a people are one, there was no telling what they could do, and indeed it would prosper, whatever their intent was.\n\nExcept God intervened, as was the case in the tower 🗼 of Babel.\n\nGenesis 11:6 KJV\nAnd the LORD said, Behold, the people is one, and they have all one language; and this they begin to do: and now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do.\n\nSo this time the Lord allowed the people to prevail, and even aided their desire.","dt":"2024-06-03T08:52:49","s":["id65i65xdc"]}],"25":[{"m":"Well said: submitting to a king 👑 was no guarantee of victory without submitting to the King 👑 of kings.","dt":"2024-06-03T08:48:35","s":["b029fe83b0"]},{"m":"He made it clear: the king was not going to be a guarantee or surety of anything, or of victory in war. If they disobey the Lord, they will still suffer loss regardless of their king.\n\nCould it then mean that secretly they were hoping their king would be a guarantee of victory even if they strayed away from the Lord their God and did follow after other gods?","dt":"2026-04-10T07:58:20","s":["efuwlo423d"]}],"14":[{"m":"In other words, you will not prosper just because you have a king.\n\nIt will not be an automatic endorsement of God for victory ✌️.\n\nYou still must keep the commandments of the Lord your God in order to continue in prosperity.\n\nNot merely the selection of a king over you.","dt":"2024-06-03T08:30:25","s":["ff35c41df2"]}]},"13":{"5":[{"m":"Having read through Israel's history up to this point,\n\nI can easily tell what this seemingly looming danger from such an impregnable army meant, and what the best response of Israel should be, and how this will turn out.\n\n1. Though the army was impossibly large to defeat with their chariots etc., it was actually a set-up for God to show his great might in the lives of his people, and for He, God, to make a name for himself - something God loves to do.\n\nHe loves to do things that leave a lasting impact transcending generations, and here was a fine opportunity to do so.\n\n2. Israel's 🇮🇱 best response was not to fear but 😱 to wait on the Lord for his instructions and directions as in time past, which they did.\n\n3. And of course it will turn out victorious for them and for God's name to be glorified.\n\nIn practice it is easier said; to not fear 😱 in the face of death is no child's play.\n\nNo wonder when the people waited and Samuel did not show up, they fled.\n\nBut why would Samuel be late when 100s of thousands of lives and the life of the nation were at stake?\n\nMaybe he was praying to hear from God, without whom his coming to make sacrifices was in vain.\n\nThis is my conjecture. In that wait for God, the people began to disperse.\n\nEither ways, Samuel was late for a reason, and Saul could not wait.\n\nMany things would come against us, but as we trust in the Lord our God,\n\nhe would come through for us. Through thick and thin.","dt":"2024-06-03T09:14:32","s":["7g002agnih"]},{"m":"The more one reads about the dealings of God with his people, the more faith is stirred, and the more likely one would face challenges head on, knowing the Lord is with you.\n\nAnd he who has done marvelously in time past for you or others would come through for you as well.\n\nThat is why it is important to read the history of God, for faith cometh by hearing and by hearing the word of God.\n\nRomans 10:17 KJV\nSo then faith cometh by hearing, and hearing by the word of God.\n\nThis battle was not orchestrated by God, but God always came through for his people whenever they took the changing scenes of life and its challenges and made it an attack against God and his covenant children 🧒.\n\nThen, now that God has been made a part of the equation, he comes through for his children.\n\nSo as life happens, as it does to us all, we must wait on the Lord and seek his face 😔, in prayer and in fasting always, and as we do, he comes through for us.\n\nWe must never give up, but continue in all manner of prayers until he pulls through for us.\n\nEphesians 6:18 KJV\nPraying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;","dt":"2024-06-03T09:37:50","s":["yl4ig1icku"]},{"m":"Why did Jonathan attack the garrison of the Philistines and call for such war and trouble?\n\nYet it is not recorded that anyone complained, but naturally it is very likely.\n\nI can imagine the murmurings of why the king's son went to attack the garrison of the Philistines, knowing very well Israel was under control of the Philistines.\n\nAnd I can imagine Jonathan responding that 'we are the children of God, and we cannot continue to allow these uncircumcised Philistines to rule over us.'\n\nI can imagine him saying to his servants, as he did sometime later, that God is able to bring victory ✌️ with little or with few.\n\nHow did Jonathan know such things? Obviously he had heard stories of what God did in time past, and even more recently when God thundered ⚡ against the Philistines in the times of the prophet Samuel, who was still alive to testify.\n\nAnd how his father was anointed through divine orchestrations...\n\nHe was tired of the stories and went straight into action, putting to test the word of the Lord 🙌.\n\nThe land was theirs, given by the God of heaven himself.\n\nWhy had they not taken it all this while?\n\nWhy were the people so cold ❄ and faithless to do the things of God?\n\nHis blood was boiling, and I can imagine the people shutting him up as youthful exuberance.\n\nJonathan was a man of faith, and no wonder when he met David he knew he had met the brother he never had.\n\nTheir bond was immediate and knew no bounds.\n\nDavid was the king 👑 his father could not be, the king he wanted his father to be, but rather disappointingly would not, but rather walked in constant rebellion.","dt":"2024-06-03T09:46:01","s":["3e7088k82l"]}],"12":[{"m":"You can't break the law of God to please 😌 the Lord.\n\nThis is what we see many Christians and Pastors do today.\n\nBreaking the laws of God, dubbing the people of God to build 🏢 a church ⛪ for the Lord.\n\nA church built through deception and lies.\n\nSaul here did foolishly.\n\nNo one ever in the history of Israel after the law offered burnt offering who was not a Levite.\n\nSaul only did this because he was a king 👑 and it had entered his head. 🤕\n\nHe felt he could do anything, and this is obvious in his later posturing whenever he did the wrong thing, and even in his attitude to Samuel - the man who made him king 👑.\n\nEven Samuel was afraid 😨 Saul could kill him at a point.\n\nNot so with David, who, when he was in error, the prophet Nathan, or was it Gad, rebuked him.\n\nAnd when his throne was taken from him, he accepted the fate of God for him and prayed for mercy, whiles of course taking pragmatic measures, as he did not know if it was fully the will of God or not.\n\nHaving mentioned pragmatism, I'm reminded of Nathan, who, though a prophet of God, took practical measures to ensure Solomon was made king 👑 according to the word of the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-03T09:54:47","s":["59pgch76w9","46f65a53a7"]},{"m":"Saul indeed did not know the Lord. For him to think of disobeying the commandment of the Lord in order to please him with an offering, with the excuse that he was under pressure, goes to show his knowledge of God.\n\nHe was treating God like some shrine with no personality, emotions or values or morals.\n\nSaul had indeed done foolishly.","dt":"2026-04-10T21:32:26","s":["07hcgj7wuh"]}],"14":[{"m":"Ah, how did Samuel know this? I mean, how did God search out a man so quickly when Saul had barely just finished sacrificing?\n\nThis goes to show how unpardonable the sin of Saul was.\n\nThe moment he started searching out a lamb or bullock for a burnt offering, the Lord rejected him and searched out a worthy replacement in David.","dt":"2024-06-03T09:57:57","s":["1d9ffe759b"]}],"23":[{"m":"Since Israel did not come out to war, the dominion of Philistia was established once more, and they entrenched their dominion further.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:00:43","s":["5c2010170e"]}]},"14":{"6":[{"m":"Jonathan, though not stated, I believe was anointed, for he also did as occasion served, and he was greatly victorious.","dt":"2022-10-29T10:25:12","s":["c9e31e579a"]}],"10":[{"m":"So it is always good to wait on the Lord rather than act impulsively.\n\nJonathan, being of Israel, already had a promise of victory ✌️ and an instruction to inherit the land.\n\nNow here he waited for a sign 🤘 from the Lord to carry out his intentions, which fell within the broader and general plan of God.\n\nHe did not just rush to do what he thought was right, but did what Israel often did in war... Wait on the Lord.\n\nWait in the face of opportunity, wait in the midst of challenges.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:08:26","s":["lnktj94kf8","87115e8ef5"]}],"21":[{"m":"Some had defected to the side of their own enemies.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:11:20","s":["6q8kuk8la9","a11c0a7bbc"]}],"40":[{"m":"In verses 36, 39 & 40...\n\nThe people's response seems like they were really tired of his ways, but tolerated him anyways because he was king.","dt":"2022-10-29T10:50:22","s":["vg0nqmlycw"]},{"m":"It seems the people were tired of his bizarre leadership and his ways, but hung around for loyalty's sake.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:15:35","s":["k6xjg5lrvz"]}],"45":[{"m":"So this goes to show that not all oaths are binding. Some can be taken back.\n\nWe see Solomon do the same thing in taking back what he swore to his mother.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:17:35","s":["oh1lluiury","2310a19bd5"]}],"46":[{"m":"Saul was one strange, disoriented leader. Firstly, he lost with God by burning offerings when he wasn't a priest. Then, when God through Jonathan still delivered the Philistines into their hand, for all God wanted was someone bold enough to stand with him, Saul asked that no one eat.\n\nWhat a foolish command.\n\nNo wonder the people, in answer to his request, kept telling him that whatever seemed right to him, he should go ahead with it.\n\nThen now he wanted to kill his own son. By this time the people discerned not all was okay with the judgement of the king, so they rescued Jonathan, his son, who would make a more worthy heir and king than his father Saul.\n\nLater on he gave commands to execute the priests of God, which none of his people did, until one Doeg. All the others refused.","dt":"2026-04-10T21:49:32","s":["12e3fhk92w"]}],"52":[{"m":"At least he did good as well and had victories, and these were outlined here.","dt":"2026-04-10T21:51:08","s":["eoh5xs99t9"]}],"1":[{"m":"Likely his father would reject the idea. He did not want any more trouble, as was the case in Michmash.\n\nBut Jonathan was tired 😴 of the Philistines' dominion.\n\nHe was a covenant child of God and had had enough.\n\nHe was a Benjamite, and Benjamin was a ravenous wolf 🐺\n\nGenesis 49:27 ESV\n\"Benjamin is a ravenous wolf, in the morning devouring the prey and at evening dividing the spoil.\"\n\nHe could wait no longer and took matters in his hand 🖐️.\n\nThough he might not have heard directly from God, God had already spoken ages ago of the conquest of Canaan and his promise of victory ✌️.\n\nSo he was doing the Lord's work. He walked in faith.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:04:59","s":["zhagxx5uit","4c044c610c"]}],"24":[{"m":"This guy was so counterproductive and full of strangeness.\n\nThe Lord had started to bring victory by his own hand through Jonathan, and now here he was, taking credit and binding the people to a counterproductive oath.","dt":"2024-06-03T10:13:20","s":["551228824d"]}],"39":[{"m":"Saul's flaw as a leader was coming to bear: his erratic decisions, lack of conviction and faith.\n\nThe people only listened to him because he was their king 👑, not because they necessarily agreed with what he was doing.","dt":"2022-10-29T10:44:42","s":["fdc7960d43"]}]},"15":{"3":[{"m":"God had long been waiting for the best opportunity to avenge him of his enemies. Aside the many abominations of the nations, they also attacked God's people.\n\nFinally the time was ripe; God had the needed resources, the king, his people and their faith in him to deliver. Everything was ripe. Who knows, maybe God had even set prophets to warn them of the coming wrath.\n\nSo all was set in the plan of God. But Saul...\n\nImagine God had said and prophesied through his prophets that he would destroy everything in Amalek, including even every beast, only for Saul to spare them in the name of burnt offerings, including sparing the king.\n\nNow God's word sounds incomplete and someway.\n\nI just checked on Google, and God had indeed said 400 years before that he would destroy the memory of Amalek, though the details about the livestock were given by Samuel the prophet.\n\nSo now imagine, of all the people to spare, Saul spared the king. Who else could have more easily revived the kingdom of Amalek if not the king?\n\nIt was like Saul had no regard to God and his ways. He would not strictly follow anything. He did what he wanted to do. NO wonder he so grieved God till God rejected him.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:05:24","s":["61jrjgxmk4"]}],"4":[{"m":"Saul was now a very powerful king and ruler.","dt":"2022-10-29T11:15:40","s":["0f675cccb9"]}],"16":[{"m":"What a cheeky response, unless I am wrongly putting modern day interpretation to Saul's response.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:07:27","s":["z043sb5z13"]},{"m":"Saul was asked to stay. Could it be he was walking off on him, and trying to maintain his kingly majesty in the midst of his rebellion? Very likely, because the next words of Samuel were to remind him of when he was lowly in his early days. Oh Saul, Saul.\n\nThis is what Google shared with me: \"It highlights the tragedy of Saul's pride: he was 'big in his own eyes' and viewed the prophet of the Most High as a subject who needed permission to speak.\"","dt":"2026-04-10T22:14:58","s":["s0n3qe76wt"]}],"21":[{"m":"Excuses excuses excuses","dt":"2022-10-29T11:17:26","s":["451z9ler9u","dd04fac894"]},{"m":"What? \"Unto the Lord THY God.\" Was the LORD NOT his GOD AS WELL? This Saul.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:17:38","s":["afpggjgdhi"]}],"23":[{"m":"Saul's lows in summary - rebellion and stubbornness","dt":"2024-06-03T13:31:57","s":["0gj3jkloiq","dadc0a6764"]},{"m":"The first rejection of Saul, when he intruded into the priest's office, was that his kingdom would not continue forever as the Lord had planned for him.\n\nMaybe, seeing how God-fearing Jonathan was, it might have ended with him or his son.\n\nBut here God rejects not the descendants of Saul, but he rejects Saul himself as king whiles on the throne. I believe that is why Jonathan might have died in the war. He would have been co-regent with David, his best friend.\n\nThis was not what God said, so Jonathan sadly died in the war; he was not spared.\n\nWe are not so wise; we all ought to be humble before the Lord, because he knows the end from the beginning of all things. We just ought to walk with him in humility in all things.\n\nHe is greater and bigger than we.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:26:58","s":["azzbk1givd"]}],"11":[{"m":"But one could argue that he performed most of the Lord's commandments for this battle.\n\nBut to the Lord, half obedience is no obedience at all.","dt":"2024-06-03T13:29:35","s":["il63ys8i3l","dd85eb8e40"]}],"1":[{"m":"What a premise to start the word of the Lord with. It was as if he knew Saul's heart, and that it was prone to rebellion, so he starts with a very strong premise, probably with the hope that that would make Saul obey completely.\n\nHow wrong he was.","dt":"2026-04-10T21:52:33","s":["tbhv82hhea"]}],"12":[{"m":"I read this in passing, only to be brought back to it. The word used, \"place\", here is actually like a monument of his victory and conquest, meanwhile it was God who had given him the victory. Saul was soo proud and full of it.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:11:28","s":["106nlxf7c9"]}],"33":[{"m":"Hewed him in pieces, very violent and vengeful.\n\nBut Samuel said something interesting, that Agag had made others childless and now he was to reap what he sowed.\n\nAnd so a just recompense was laid upon him, and he was hewed to pieces for all his wickedness.","dt":"2024-06-04T05:34:16","s":["dw1mvvulen","ac5f7014d8"]}]},"16":{"1":[{"m":"I asked myself this morning the difference in punishment between when Saul intruded into the priestly office and when he refused to carry out the instructions to destroy Amalek completely.\n\nWhen he intruded into the priest's office, the Lord said his throne will not continue perpetually, but when he refused to destroy Amalek, even whiles he was still king 👑, God dethroned him.\n\nIn the first instance, likely down the line he would have died, and David would take over his throne after his death ☠.\n\nBut in the second instance, God anointed a new king whiles Saul was still king 👑 and active on the throne, and replaced him with David.\n\nSadly, even Jonathan was killed; maybe he would have been co-regent with David, and that would be contrary to the word of God that Saul's reign had ended.","dt":"2024-06-04T08:03:26","s":["8b2ydm0sdg"]}],"2":[{"m":"It's no child's play being a prophet of the Lord... Such a risky errand.\n\nNo wonder most of them were persecuted and suffered many things.","dt":"2024-06-04T08:11:08","s":["mwyiinf94c"]},{"m":"The Lord had given an instruction, yet Samuel had his reservations, and rightly so. God loves to hear our thoughts, reservations and reasonings. It is not an act of disobedience, but trying to make sense of things. We ought to relate to God more like this, rather than some distant God who doesn't want any contradictions and rebuttals when he talks.\n\nHe is our father.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:29:42","s":["48jfh05fns"]},{"m":"Saul could now kill Samuel. Amazing, the man who made him king. Saul was long lost at this point.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:30:38","s":["lu9vnc6kbj"]}],"7":[{"m":"Does that mean God knew Saul will disobey him later? Or Saul's heart was right initially but changed later? I suspect the former. God knew Saul would mess up, but God used him for the time being.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:39:58","s":["pkw5kr1lgt"]}],"18":[{"m":"Dake's says this is a parenthetical verse, but in chronological order, from the anointing we should have moved to chapter 17, where he did battle Goliath.","dt":"2024-06-04T08:26:11","s":["j784vh1cos"]},{"m":"David must really have been very cunning in playing. Look at all the songs and psalms he composed which we use today. He was the origin, the source. He must have been really very good. Real good, real original. He was of God, inspired by him many times, and even prophetic in his writings.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:48:50","s":["qmqxodj65c"]}],"3":[{"m":"Prophets and priests anoint kings. Meaning the kingship was subject to the priesthood and prophets of God. Though the king now rules as judge over the people, his rulership was to be subject to the theocracy.\n\nHe, the king, was the physical representative of the people, and the prophet was the representative of God, and they both were to govern the people in line with the will of God.\n\nThe prophet shepherds the king, and the king the people.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:33:24","s":["zkfmg3h0d8"]}],"12":[{"m":"What a grand entrance for David - the moment he arrived... It was almost as if God was announcing his cherished handiwork as it is put on display.\n\nNo pressure here, but what a scene.\n\nThat is how I want the Lord to announce me when the time is ready.","dt":"2024-06-04T08:19:23","s":["edfw1xgb6p"]}],"13":[{"m":"It is worth noting that even before the Spirit of the Lord came upon David, his character was pleasing to the Lord, for which the Lord chose him. Then he gave him his Spirit as an advantage and backing.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:41:59","s":["pv4ug472iw"]}],"16":[{"m":"The happenings in the corridors of power: a maniac with evil spirits was ruling the land, yet his own people kept quiet because each had their interest.\n\nSuggesting a new king would be overthrowing their own selves. So they found a way of managing his madness, just to keep up appearances.","dt":"2026-04-10T22:44:55","s":["m4vxd0pu8k"]}]},"17":{"18":[{"m":"David seems such a serviceable and useful lad, who was entrusted of all to carry out such an errand and to do so successfully.\n\nMeanwhile he had elder brothers who should have done that errand, considering that it involved going to the battleground, where there was danger.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:19:43","s":["raulceuddl"]}],"26":[{"m":"It was only David who \"sat there\" thinking 💭 this man was uncircumcised and was therefore not worthy to defy Israel.\n\nThe rest just feared 😱. They had forgotten who and whose they were.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:22:34","s":["35mms4wsuo"]},{"m":"ALL Israel from childhood are told they are children of God and the armies of the living God, but it seemed at this time that it was only David who believed that to be literally true, and rightly so.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:10:42","s":["ygk5q37gtx"]}],"37":[{"m":"What made Saul take such a decision... Putting the entire nation's destiny into one boy's hand 🖐️","dt":"2022-10-29T12:50:15","s":["4smq0ctnxk"]},{"m":"I'm still puzzled as to how Saul got convinced to place the entire nation into David's hand 🖐️.\n\nI believe the Lord played a role here. It could have been the conviction with which David spoke.\n\nWho knows, but it was so risky. No one was willing to go forth, as this was the fortieth day; probably their souls were starting to get wearied 😩 out by the constant defiance of Goliath.\n\nTo get things done and over with, he entrusted the nation into David's hand.\n\nSuch a rash and seemingly reckless decision sounds so much like something Saul would do. And he did, entrusting David to go.\n\nBut it's really strange that of the tens and possibly hundreds of thousands of men, none could lay down their lives for their nation.\n\nYet they had been enrolled in the army.\n\nNot even Saul the king 👑 was willing to go.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:30:54","s":["rus1904r1g"]}],"47":[{"m":"Wow, what a speech 🗨","dt":"2024-06-05T19:33:22","s":["77pku2i932"]}],"49":[{"m":"The battle ended pretty quickly.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:28:04","s":["43poni6pew"]}],"54":[{"m":"David suddenly had a tent allocated to him because he had brought victory and a great awakening to the house 🏡 of the Lord and to his people Israel.\n\nNow they believed once more.\n\nThey had been under a king 👑 who was fearful 😨 and demon possessed, but now they were awakened once more to their true nature and identity.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:37:06","s":["sme54pl51d"]}],"55":[{"m":"Saul was seeing right there a bold, fearless leader in the making.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:30:13","s":["2jstio2ktr"]}],"1":[{"m":"Often the enemies of Israel gather ready for battle with numbers or resources greater than Israel.\n\nIsrael, on the other hand, consults God, goes the way of spirits, and secures the battle ere it is fought.\n\nIsrael was spiritual, and so ought we to be.\n\nThis is not to say the enemy did not consult spirits; they did, but to show how pertinent the spiritual was to Israel... It was a daily part of their lives.","dt":"2024-06-04T10:10:57","s":["lzryrleesc"]}],"10":[{"m":"But Saul and all these warriors had been in many wars —\n\nHow come none could face 😔 Goliath?\n\nHow come none could believe the LORD for victory? Because they had not walked with the Lord in time past, so could not guarantee he would be with them in this battle.\n\nIt would be a game of lottery to attempt to face off 📴 with Goliath in the name of the Lord if this was the first time of doing anything with the Lord.\n\nBut David, he had had his time of testing and training by the Lord already and knew what to do.\n\nHe was not gambling. He had been doing this literally all his youth, and so this was no new sport.\n\nIt was business as usual. He had faced off lions 🦁 and bears 🐻 whose weight and height were comparable to Goliath.\n\nThis was just another fight.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:09:26","s":["myqfw4wixu"]}],"12":[{"m":"David had already been introduced to us in the previous chapter, but here he is reintroduced as if he has not already been mentioned.\n\nAnd this reintroduction was so poetic, symbolizing what he was about to do.\nThis was that David, the now anointed king 👑 of Israel.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:14:14","s":["6tt3edjm7u"]}],"28":[{"m":"This shows the character of David as observed by his brothers — he was good at heart and bold, as we saw in his reign, but his brothers judged that as pride and naughtiness of heart. His boldness and strong confidence in God was judged as pride. He stood for what he believed in, as seen when he said,\n\n\"Is there not a cause?\"\n\nHis refusal to back down on his beliefs was seen as naughtiness of heart. Yet it was he that stayed with the sheep, the few sheep, and defended them with his life as if they were worth an empire. He staked his life on sheep so insignificant compared to his life that God knew he will make a great king.\n\nI think I got the heart part — it is left with the boldness-to-stand-for-what-I-believe-in part.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:21:57","s":["ys1jj2f7v2"]}],"42":[{"m":"Fine boy","dt":"2024-06-05T19:31:46","s":["9cw573n23o"]}],"52":[{"m":"Did David also pursue after them?","dt":"2022-10-29T12:49:31","s":["fhhq7bsex9"]}],"57":[{"m":"How many 17-year-olds can hold the head of another man in their hands?\n\nDAVID seemed made for this. He was born to fight, rule and lead.\n\nThis reminds me of the son of Jerubbaal, aka Gideon. He was told to kill the kings 👑 of Midian, but he could not because he was a lad.\n\nYet David did kill Goliath.\n\nHe was uncompromisingly sold out to the Lord.\n\nThe same word used for youth to describe Gideon's son was used for David.\n\nBut David was already a bold youth at this stage by the Spirit of the Lord.\n\nJudges 8:20 ESV\nSo he said to Jether his firstborn, \"Rise and kill them!\" But the young man did not draw his sword, for he was afraid, because he was still a young man.","dt":"2024-06-05T19:39:45","s":["0ngkrzbuq9"]}]},"18":{"2":[{"m":"He got the job immediately, which he did not apply for, because he delivered. The purpose of applying for a job is to prove you can deliver; if you can prove you can deliver, then you do not need to apply.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:31:57","s":["o0m4nmfskc"]}],"12":[{"m":"How did he know the Lord was with him? Because the Lord had been with him before, and he knew how everything falls in place for you when the Lord is with you.\n\nThose who have tasted of the Lord's power and anointing before and lost it have an eye for fishing out the next anointed person, and wish to draw and have a foretaste of what they lost. They know how precious it was, yet they disdained it, and now want it back, or a foretaste of it, even at the expense and peril of those who now have it.\n\nThe old prophet and the young prophet's story typifies this. The young prophet eventually died just because the old prophet would do anything just to be associated with what the Lord was doing.\n\nHe lost his and helped the young prophet to lose his.\n\nWe see the same with Esau. He lost his birthright and chased Jacob for it, and wanted to kill Jacob even if he could not have it.\n\nEventually Esau was restored because he made the most of what he had left.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:40:06","s":["0h9wi7s2vm"]}],"28":[{"m":"The Lord had been with him before, so he could tell when the Lord was with someone.","dt":"2022-10-30T07:23:24","s":["69al2vb0yg"]},{"m":"Hm... What a strange statement.\n\nIn the sense that when the Lord was with someone, it was obvious.\n\nMeasurable and visible.","dt":"2024-06-05T20:08:10","s":["oola8ls07k"]}],"6":[{"m":"Probably this could have been many days or even weeks later.\n\nBecause in times of war, it could take many days to weeks, even months, for the army to return home 🏡.","dt":"2024-06-05T20:05:09","s":["cxu06ekywv"]}]},"19":{"1":[{"m":"Saul had been told he has been rejected by God and that God has found a man better than him.\n\nFrom Saul's reaction it is obvious that he also had found God's man, and that man was David.\n\nInstead of Saul humbling himself before the Lord, so that, who knows 🤷, he might have obtained mercy,\n\nhe rather chose to actively seek after and to slay God's man and choice for Israel.\n\nHe was using the very authority and power God had given him to fight God and his purposes.\n\nNo wonder God rejected him.\n\nIndeed, it was becoming clearer and clearer, the degree of his character flaws for which the Lord rejected him.","dt":"2024-06-05T21:58:15","s":["o5l580tr9o"]}],"13":[{"m":"What was this image, this idol, doing in the house 🏡, more so in the house of the king's daughter?\n\nThe king who was to ensure only God's worship 🛐, and now behold, in his own household we find an idol.\n\nSometimes in the house of the custodians of traditions and the law of God, or any law, are breaches of the very law they were elected to protect.","dt":"2024-06-05T22:06:34","s":["mwdhxm9e46"]}],"22":[{"m":"What was the distance between where Saul was and Ramah? I wonder.","dt":"2024-06-05T22:03:42","s":["o2kjji8oik"]}],"24":[{"m":"Was this not said of him also at the very start of his ministry as king, when he prophesied?\n\nNow here he was, pursuing the new king.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:55:19","s":["hyt1rvzxcr"]},{"m":"Meaning his kingly clothes and outer coat, I believe, leaving his inner garment or underwear. I have read somewhere that that state in those times was considered nakedness.","dt":"2026-04-12T15:48:29","s":["3fs56b6lec"]}],"14":[{"m":"This goes to show that between verses there can be hours and days. If one is not careful, things will not make sense or be misjudged.\n\nFor instance, we are told that night David escaped out of Saul's presence. Next thing, Michal gives an alibi that David was sick. This could have been possible only if sufficient time had passed for this excuse to make sense.\n\nLater that night David escaped, having bought enough time with his sick excuse.","dt":"2026-04-12T09:53:16","s":["7spw69i4hp"]}]},"20":{"5":[{"m":"He knew the fields all too well from taking care of the sheep.\n\nThree days in the fields was business as usual.","dt":"2024-06-05T23:59:13","s":["8akhtvhf83"]}],"13":[{"m":"He knew the Lord had left his father and was now with David,\n\nand he blesses David for it. No wonder his father cursed 🤬 him and said that he favours David to his own hurt and against his heritage.","dt":"2024-06-06T00:06:19","s":["1oxzoyrjt2"]}],"31":[{"m":"So what God had commanded concerning his throne not continuing was irrelevant to him.\n\nSaul was so rebellious.","dt":"2022-10-30T08:09:13","s":["yi1bd8sf41"]}],"33":[{"m":"Ah, Saul's rage and jealousy","dt":"2024-06-06T00:09:27","s":["u57yijsmj5"]}],"41":[{"m":"In which way did David exceed?","dt":"2024-06-06T00:10:54","s":["t0oweqigtk"]}]},"21":{"5":[{"m":"Why did God tolerate this lie, and allow him to eat his hallowed bread by lying — a lie that would cost the priest his life and that of other priests?\n\nJesus later referenced this eating of hallowed bread as a sign that...\n\ntimes had changed and his people were not following him to the letter. Many laws were broken, and so I believe God excused many things. And why strike he down his man after his own heart, David, who was his next king? Not to mention that God had it in mind to ultimately make all these people holy, and king-priests.\n\nLater we see David go to the king of Moab — a thing which was forbidden, because the Jews were not to have any relations with the people of the land, but that had also been broken.\n\nWe see the same with Ruth, who was a Moabite.\n\nMany things had changed.\n\nNot to mention, the death of Ahimelech was in connection to the curse of the house of ELI prophesied earlier.\n\nNote that in all these laws of God broken, it had to do with rituals and ceremonies, not with his unbendable and infallible moral laws.\n\nThe laws broken were things he himself had instituted with the intention of changing them later.\n\nSo as Christians we ought to really be careful to keep the eternal laws of God, even as we adapt to changing needs and cultures. Many things we can change and adapt to, but not to his infallible law and word.","dt":"2026-04-13T21:26:46","s":["isdstpskrc"]}],"9":[{"m":"How did the sword end up with the priests?\n\nWas it dedicated to God to show the supremacy of the God of Israel to other gods?\n\nLet's not forget Goliath came in the name of his gods, and so did David.","dt":"2024-06-06T07:41:06","s":["h2z1phyp4e"]}],"11":[{"m":"No, far from it, David was the king of the land. :)... Even the enemies knew he was king of the land, and this was no error, for they knew Saul was also king of the land.\n\nThey could discern that David was king material, having won victory for the people of God and for the king.","dt":"2026-04-13T21:08:48","s":["vlgv8ptwx3"]}],"13":[{"m":"Hmm... No be easy.\nAnything to stay alive and survive this world.","dt":"2024-06-06T07:42:17","s":["i1raxrmg89"]}],"4":[{"m":"But is that what the law says? I thought 💭 hallowed bread was for the priests only.\n\nBut at this time, the law of God had been so watered down 👇.\n\nBut the Lord understood that times had changed, so no one died for eating hallowed bread.\n\nJesus actually alluded to this moment to show that he was greater than the Sabbath, and the law was made for man, not the reverse.","dt":"2024-06-06T07:15:32","s":["402vrwiqlm"]}],"7":[{"m":"Doeg, an interesting character. He came to enquire of the Lord, and yet afterwards personally killed the priests of the Lord.\n\nThis shows how men can come before the Lord in seeming worship, but their hearts are far from the Lord.\n\nThis also should be a lesson for pastors and leaders of the flock.\n\nSome seem to love the Lord, but when push comes to shove, will sell out and destroy their own pastor.","dt":"2024-06-06T07:21:15","s":["iq226nrlbp"]},{"m":"Saul was himself a herdsman before he became king, and now he continued in that same business but had someone head it whiles he attended to kingly duties.","dt":"2026-04-13T21:04:47","s":["tbh7iv3izs"]}]},"22":{"2":[{"m":"How was David, the man of God, able to convert men with all these issues to be mighty men and helpers in war and in setting up the kingdom?","dt":"2024-06-06T07:51:34","s":["3tzepttibh"]}],"16":[{"m":"He was mad and unreasonable. This was his son-in-law, whom the priests had enquired of for him.\n\nNow the priesthood stood in peril of their lives because of the king.\n\nMeanwhile the priests and the system of priesthood are to be feared, for they stand before God for the people, but not so. The king had an army and weapons and was thus powerful, and in this case the system of priesthood was subject to the kingdom.\n\nNow I am reminded of the prophets. They were a wildcard, not subject to or part of any of these systems. They spoke in the stead of God and were feared, especially those with signs accompanying their call, like Samuel, who was mighty feared.\n\nHe was both prophet and priest.\n\nAnd now we see Nathan the prophet, not part of any of these systems, and yet was respected by both, and especially the throne and king, as we see later when David sinned with Bathsheba.\n\nOf course, it is also because David feared God, unlike Saul.\n\nIn the case of Samuel, initially, though, the people and Saul feared Samuel. Later Samuel feared Saul, because Saul was now so drifted from God.\n\nGod used Saul to fulfill his curse to the house of Eli, and later killed Saul in war for his wickedness and atrocities.","dt":"2026-04-14T09:37:31","s":["hqx6tw0gy0"]}],"19":[{"m":"Saul was willing to kill everything pertaining to the priests, the Lord's anointed, because he considered them to be his enemies for helping David.\n\nThough they helped David innocently.\n\nYet Saul was not willing to destroy everything pertaining to the enemies of God and all of Israel when instructed to do so, but kept spoil for himself and the people, contrary to the command.\n\nBut here in NKJV he found the dealing of the priests as so detestable that their sheep were not worthy to be taken as loot in the massacre.\n\nIt is becoming clearer and clearer why God rejected Saul.","dt":"2024-06-06T08:02:01","s":["6cv039ltdm"]},{"m":"Why would Saul do this, such wickedness? This was to show what would happen to anyone who stood with David or knew of his whereabouts but kept silent, or even had a little bit of info but did not inform the king.\n\nEven if you did not help David, failure to inform the king was most definitely going to be at the peril of your life. No wonder we later see cities where David dwelt coming to report him before the king. His intention was working.\n\nDake says Saul would destroy every person and animal of the priests through jealousy, but he would not obey the command of God to do this to enemies of both God and Israel (1 Sam. 15).","dt":"2026-04-14T09:44:23","s":["tve432svr4"]}],"3":[{"m":"They were not to intermingle with the Moabites, but the times had changed.","dt":"2026-04-14T09:18:11","s":["o24710w25x"]}],"5":[{"m":"Was the hold the cave of Adullam? If so, many powerful preachings had been made about this cave, yet later the prophet asked him to leave that place because it was not so safe for him.\n\nAs Gad aligned with the new king, God was positioning his servant to have a place in the future, the future kingdom.","dt":"2026-04-13T21:29:43","s":["iil9b23z4r"]}],"8":[{"m":"Such a narcissist Saul was.\n\nManipulating and scheming.","dt":"2024-06-06T07:54:52","s":["g7mbtis2e7"]}],"18":[{"m":"Abominations.\n\nHe touched, and not only that, but killed the anointed of the Lord.\n\nMen anointed to the priesthood were to be revered, but here they were killed without mercy.\n\nAs all this happens, we get to know that there was a curse 🤬 hanging on their fathers, looking for an opportunity to happen.\n\nThe curse on ELI'S house came to bear on them, despite their service to the Lord and actually helping David, the Lord's anointed.\n\nOh Lord, have mercy and deliver me from any curse or anything hindering me from moving to my next level.","dt":"2024-06-06T07:58:46","s":["8okwm1lo74"]}]},"23":{"17":[{"m":"Why did God not allow Jonathan to live, and for him to be co-ruler with David ✡?","dt":"2022-11-01T11:45:26","s":["w6ctu11j8b"]}],"20":[{"m":"Everyone seeks the favour of the king 👑.\n\nEntire cities were ready to give up David just to win the favour of the king 👑, including cities he had helped.\n\nThis shows the nature of man when it comes to power and personal interest.\n\nThey are ready to sell out one who helped them in time past for their own personal convenience in present time ⌚","dt":"2024-06-06T08:39:27","s":["gp26hv5bfo"]}],"28":[{"m":"This narrow escape from the hands of Saul calls 🤙 for a poem on the faithfulness of God and his deliverance from the enemy.","dt":"2024-06-06T08:41:17","s":["igjvwmgj9k"]}]},"24":{"2":[{"m":"Was this not the same number he chose at the very beginning of his kingdom?","dt":"2024-06-06T08:42:00","s":["i9mb2e32m8"]}],"4":[{"m":"Maybe the Lord had spoken in times past that all will bow before him and he will deliver his enemies into his hands 👐","dt":"2024-06-06T08:43:11","s":["fucujumt3p"]}],"16":[{"m":"Hmm 😢 sad 😔.\n\nIndeed Saul wept. David had shown himself to be a man and more righteous than Saul.\n\nSaul wept but did not repent. He still had a heart ♥ and a conscience but had not changed.\n\nWe should not interpret the tears 😭 of men to mean repentance or transformation.","dt":"2024-06-06T08:46:54","s":["wy3lkk5tvl"]}],"21":[{"m":"Saul was unfaithful and wicked, yet he wanted surety for his seed after him, that they should not be cut off.\n\nWicked men always try to prevent the consequences of their wicked ways.\n\nThis reminds me so much of Laban, Jacob's uncle, who sought a covenant that Jacob would not cross over to do him harm, when it was he who had cheated and deceived Jacob.","dt":"2024-06-06T08:55:57","s":["76yum1fx2m"]},{"m":"The ancients knew the power of a good name and living your name as a posterity in the earth.","dt":"2026-04-14T22:28:59","s":["qd522j4ih8"]}],"22":[{"m":"They swore and covenanted with Saul, but were wise enough to still hide themselves.\n\nFor they knew that the wicked cannot be trusted.","dt":"2022-11-01T12:36:02","s":["h6kmuzetgh"]}],"10":[{"m":"They attributed everything to the Lord, and in this case rightly so. But earlier, when news was brought of the whereabouts of David, Saul, the rejected king by God, still attributed this to God.\n\nIt seemed it was part of their language to mention and attribute things to God, just like the way people just mention Jesus, including unbelievers.","dt":"2026-04-14T22:26:05","s":["u7eockcbap"]}]},"25":{"1":[{"m":"So Samuel was alive all this while. No one at this stage could restrain the madness of the king, not even Samuel.","dt":"2026-04-16T07:14:51","s":["k194qooovo"]}],"14":[{"m":"We need young, wise men who notice things.","dt":"2026-04-16T07:18:11","s":["yt7vzpupjw"]}],"17":[{"m":"Nabal, there are some people like that.\n\nThey lack wisdom, and it's further enhanced by the fact that they are rich.\n\nA rich fool is such a lethal combination.","dt":"2024-06-07T08:45:02","s":["a0kx3cazhu"]}],"34":[{"m":"It was expected that your household is with you in counsel, so the consequences of your actions also fall on them.\n\nDavid was going to kill Nabal and all his house.","dt":"2026-04-16T07:27:31","s":["8v4bhz1k5i"]}],"29":[{"m":"Wow... This woman was indeed wise.\n\nThe sling of David was his popular hallmark, his strength and the apex of his skill...\n\nHere Abigail uses it figuratively and poetically to illustrate how the enemies of David will be slinged out.\n\nShe also mentions David's deepest needs and fear 😱.\n\nThat of his master Saul, of which Abigail wishes him the protection of the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-07T08:49:25","s":["zeus4sqjw8"]}],"30":[{"m":"It seems common knowledge now, or maybe the people saw it and desired David to rule over them... How else did Abigail know that\n\nDavid was appointed ruler 📐 over Israel?\n\nThese rumours are what made Saul hate David to start with, and it didn't seem to go away anytime soon.\n\nEspecially since Saul was mad and unstable.\n\nIt made David all the more desirable and a worthy replacement.","dt":"2024-06-07T08:51:37","s":["k9wm7w4r7s"]}],"32":[{"m":"God's people were no cowards. They were men of war — mighty warriors who fearlessly took cities and could completely wipe out entire cities.\n\nThey were to be feared, for they took their lives in their hands and fought the battles of the Lord. Yet they were humble before the LORD and submitted to him.\n\nThis was the nature of the men of God of those times. And I see the same thing in the men of God today. Strong and hardened and well trained for battle.\n\nTaking on nations and systems for the Lord.\n\nSame with the disciples of Jesus, men who could face lions without sword and spear and die a martyr's death.\n\nThis advancement of the Gospel is not for sissies.","dt":"2026-04-16T07:25:01","s":["2nc94uduaj"]}]},"26":{"3":[{"m":"How did David know to watch out for Saul?\n\nAfter all, they had sworn to be at peace ✌️, they and their descendants.\n\nSo what happened to that vow, for David to still be on the lookout for Saul?\n\nThis is wisdom indeed. Saul was a truce breaker; his words were as fickle as the shadows.\n\nDavid had done much for Saul, much to prove his loyalty, but Saul hunted him down 👇.\n\nSo I guess David knew to not trust 100% the dealings with Saul, not even if he swore and covenanted.\n\nLord, give me wisdom, I pray, to know how to deal 🤝 with all men.","dt":"2024-06-08T07:09:45","s":["8wnh7nizyn"]}],"6":[{"m":"These men, later to be reckoned as David's mighty men.\n\nThey were with him from the very beginning.","dt":"2024-06-08T07:19:37","s":["mn7jqs7ewu"]}],"7":[{"m":"Ahimelech did not go, and understandably.\n\nThey had gotten the chance to smite Saul long ago, and they let it pass because of David's own emotional beliefs (seemingly weak).\n\nAnd now Saul was back, and David wanted another risk to be taken. No, not Ahimelech, and rightly so.\n\nLeadership and decisions of leaders are sometimes difficult to decipher, but we must behave ourselves wisely in the corridors of power.\n\nEspecially under a wise and anointed leader.","dt":"2024-06-08T07:22:27","s":["7f1glq4pd0"]},{"m":"David had been an insider before and knew some of the protocol around the king 👑.\n\nWith this knowledge he navigated his way to Saul.","dt":"2024-06-08T07:27:43","s":["gqfqb9o5ct"]}],"12":[{"m":"The Lord's anointed, the Lord was on his side.","dt":"2024-06-08T13:50:27","s":["7z4t78h5im"]},{"m":"I wonder if David enquired of the Lord before attempting this feat.","dt":"2024-06-08T13:58:43","s":["764fst8pbo"]}],"15":[{"m":"Interesting use and play on words","dt":"2024-06-08T15:25:10","s":["fd6vwudft3"]}],"4":[{"m":"David had his own system of security 🔐; he sent his own spies to verify if indeed it was as he heard.","dt":"2024-06-08T07:11:22","s":["7u85o2gbuo"]}],"5":[{"m":"What a move, wow 😱, very risky move, but it carried the element of surprise.\n\nThey least of all expected David to dare come to their camp 🏕.\n\nWhat a risk. David was a very bold and strong 💪 man 👨 to take such a course of action.\n\nAwesome 👏","dt":"2024-06-08T07:18:30","s":["icqmcsoh0h"]}],"8":[{"m":"For Abishai to be willing to do this, Saul indeed was disdained in his eyes 👀.\n\nTo be so easily willing to kill your king 👑, the anointed of the Lord, Saul indeed had lost respect from the people.\n\nHe was erratic, had focused his ill intent on the one who brought him the greatest victories, he was a truce breaker and raving mad 😡 at times.","dt":"2024-06-08T13:01:59","s":["yavs8lhs21"]}],"10":[{"m":"This was so prophetic, and indeed he died in battle.\n\nWhat's strange is that among the options for Saul's death included dying on his appointed day.\n\nMeaning David was willing to wait until Saul was dead, even if it meant waiting until Saul died of old age 🧓.\n\nHe talked of the Lord striking Saul, quite similar to what happened to Nabal.\n\nDavid was quite a man 👨. A man of many parts and capabilities.\n\nIt was not that he was unwilling to be king, for we see that the moment Saul died he was made king 👑.\n\nBut he was a noble man and unwilling to take things by doing evil 😈.\n\nThe same spirit is reflected even in his kingship. Firstly, he was made king of Judah whiles Saul's son reigned as king 👑.\n\nLater, by natural occurrences, he was made king of both realms.","dt":"2024-06-08T13:08:43","s":["1yphymq6vm"]}],"19":[{"m":"Aww aw... Of course David knew the king was filled with jealousy, but chose his words carefully so the king was blameless of any charge.\n\nThis indeed is court manners & palace protocol...\n\nBecause it was obvious to all, the madness of the king 👑, but who dares confront him? And everyone around him had their own agenda and interests.\n\nThe king 👑, kingsmen and courtiers profited much from him being king 👑 and would want that maintained.","dt":"2024-06-08T15:28:37","s":["rg1lygx31p"]},{"m":"If the Lord had stirred thee up against me, let him accept an offering... This sounds like a line that should appear in the Psalms.","dt":"2024-06-08T15:30:53","s":["t5p0r9ev6p"]}],"23":[{"m":"Now, having had the king 👑 accept his faults, David now speaks plainly of having the opportunity to kill the king, yet spared his life...\n\nHe started by courtesies before letting out what had really happened.","dt":"2024-06-08T15:32:27","s":["ifryxtocaz"]}]},"27":{"2":[{"m":"Now his men had increased to 600.\n\nIs this 🤓 the same king under whom Goliath served?\n\nI doubt, as there were many kings at the time.","dt":"2024-06-08T15:34:15","s":["w5f2r2f0j5"]}]},"28":{"2":[{"m":"What made Achish trust David so much? He even added here that David will be keeper of his head. I guess it is also because every leader really needs good and valuable people to help keep the system running and to lighten the burden of the king.\n\nLeaders carry a lot of burden, and skillful people always stand before the king.\n\nUnless Achish was himself playing the game of politics in order for David to fight against his own people with all his might, in which case\n\nDavid also was playing the game very well and promised to do just that.","dt":"2026-04-19T06:13:58","s":["aesnyej76o"]}],"3":[{"m":"So Saul was not all bad, all bad.\n\nHe had even cast out all sorcerers from Israel.\n\nBut his ills were all too many.","dt":"2024-06-09T01:42:25","s":["qj9w2ksadp"]}],"6":[{"m":"Even in rebellion, when Saul enquired of the Lord, the Lord answered. As when he rebelled the first time, and afterward consulted with the Urim and Thummim, and he asked the priest to withdraw his hand because some news came which confirmed what he wanted.\n\nIn such a state of rebellion, and still getting results, he presumed God was an idol and shrine who works as a slot machine, with no personality and emotions.\n\nHe thought God was there to be used and to receive sacrifices and fat of rams. Even devils are smart enough to seek allegiance, even through entrapment, by not telling those who seek after them the full terms of the contract they were getting themselves into.\n\nGod, on the other hand, was true and genuine in service and lays his cards on the table, unlike the devil/s, who hide them and compel people to serve them afterwards by force.","dt":"2026-04-19T06:18:39","s":["cblh8wbigx"]}],"7":[{"m":"When he was told by Samuel that rebellion is as the sin of witchcraft, he thought it was a figure of speech; he thought it was figurative. He did not know that it was literal.\n\nNow here he was, consulting a witch.\n\nGod is quite merciful and understanding, especially when it comes to the context within which things happen and sins are committed.\n\nGod was wroth mightily with Saul and took his throne from him. Yet after Saul came worse kings than him. Indeed, Saul was like an angel compared to these kings, like Ahab, and Manasseh, who was actually a full practicing wizard.\n\nYet God did not take the throne from them. In fact, Manasseh was one of the longest reigning kings of Israel, if my memory serves me right.\n\nWhy was God so seemingly merciful on these more wicked kings? Because of context.\n\nThey did not know better; they inherited the throne as people born into royalty, not as people taken from being nobodies like Saul, and now Saul is rubbing shoulders with God. Same with David, who was picked up from taking care of sheep to being shepherd over God's people.\n\nThe context is very different, and so their punishments for the same sins were very different.\n\nFor instance, Gideon, after being picked up from the winepress and bringing victory to Israel, refused to cement his rule by becoming king, even though the people pressed him for it.\n\nHe recognised it was all God and asked them to continue serving the Lord as their KING.","dt":"2026-04-19T06:51:32","s":["l8q5c6ovq0"]}],"10":[{"m":"Interesting, how could he swear 🤬 by the Lord even as he was about to disobey the command of the Lord?\n\nHe was indeed a very desperate man 👨","dt":"2024-06-09T16:45:57","s":["xm5i5r8k79"]}],"14":[{"m":"I suspect this might not be Saul's first time of using the services of a necromancer.\n\nHow else did he know to discern what the woman 👩 was saying?","dt":"2024-06-11T00:03:49","s":["8xy29tn95l"]}],"19":[{"m":"This was a familiar spirit, and yet her prophecies were accurate and on point.\n\nThis spirit had access to the past, present and future very accurately.\n\nI suspect the spirit spoke through the woman 👩 and not Samuel directly appearing to Saul like some apparition.\n\nNo, it was through the woman.\n\nWe discern this from how that the woman had to describe what she was seeing.\n\nIf it was an apparition visible to Saul and all present, then there was no need asking the woman what she saw.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:11:33","s":["z537o5au7i"]},{"m":"He still went to war with this information. Why so? Was this the real Samuel? He talks of Saul and his sons being with him in the land of the dead.\n\nSamuel mentions being disquieted, as one being woken out of sleep who wants to return back to sleep. But then he mentions Saul being with him as one gone to a place, rather than the grave.\n\nThese terms are figurative, because obviously it was his spirit that was conjured up, and the spirit is alive, at rest in a place.\n\nI do not think spirits are lying down in a place sleeping.","dt":"2026-04-19T07:14:23","s":["dxzsit6kxo"]}],"23":[{"m":"Saul, Saul, so extreme at times. He was very weak from not eating, yet he was going into battle the very next day.\n\nHe was offered and he refused, and had to be coaxed into eating something.\n\nHe did the same to his men when he commanded none to eat till they had won the battle.\n\nMeanwhile, he could have gotten greater victory ✌️ if he had allowed his men to eat.\n\nHere he was again not eating, though this time he did not command the entire army.\n\nBut rather he himself was in a fast. Yet he sought the face of demons.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:14:58","s":["16qkat9cn6"]}],"24":[{"m":"Oh, what a moment! A simple woman, living a life and making a living through witchcraft, has the king of the land with her in her house. The destiny of the nation was unfolding before her, a simple one as herself.\n\nPower play was unfolding right before their eyes.","dt":"2026-04-19T07:20:16","s":["opk34hi4lb"]}],"13":[{"m":"The heavens were closed over Saul, yet the arms of darkness were wide open.\n\nThe dark realm was wide open for him to tap divine secrets. He was not submitted to God really; otherwise, when God refused to reveal anything to him, he would have just conceded and resigned himself to the will of God.\n\nBut not Saul, the man who by his authority intruded and made a breach into spiritual things.\n\nHe lost his throne because of this disregard for spiritual protocol.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:02:12","s":["6jiuy7t7dg"]}],"15":[{"m":"Is this not the same thing he did the first time,\n\nwhiles waiting for Samuel to enquire of the Lord on his behalf before the war?\n\nNow Samuel failed to show up at the appointed time, and Saul himself intruded into the priest's office.\n\nBecause of that, the Lord rejected his kingdom from continuing.\n\nNow fast forward, there is war again; he needs a word from the Lord, and here again there was no word.\n\nNeither from the Lord, from dreams, nor from the Urim and Thummim.\n\nSo what does he do? He seeks a witch doctor and intrudes into the spirit realm.","dt":"2024-06-09T16:52:13","s":["ea4if2eksv"]},{"m":"Saul is like that kind of child or worker who would disregard your instructions in order to have his way, and later come to you expecting you to favour him.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:06:24","s":["6dq07p8gxd"]}],"18":[{"m":"Again, God is not erratic; he stated clearly why Saul was disqualified.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:07:45","s":["axl5fsw5b0"]}],"20":[{"m":"Saul and this his needless and foolish fastings. Being weak even in times of war. Or maybe he was desperate for answers and victory, but he ought to have applied wisdom.","dt":"2026-04-19T07:16:02","s":["80oom0wq1s"]}]},"29":{"3":[{"m":"Why did the writer use \"these days\" and immediately after said \"these years\"? Was he quoting directly as Achish spoke it, or it actually meant these years and some days? Was it the Hebrew way of rendering it?\n\nGoogle just gave me this explanation: In 1 Samuel 29:3, the phrase \"these days, or these years\" is a literal rendering of a Hebrew idiom representing a significant, yet not explicitly defined, period of time. King Achish uses this rhetorical phrasing to emphasize David’s long-term loyalty to the Philistines, even though the actual duration was roughly one year and four months. For further interpretation, visit BibleRef.com.","dt":"2026-04-19T07:23:05","s":["t7k6ugmuxh"]}],"5":[{"m":"Wow... David was indeed a national hero.\n\nThis was a while ago, almost 13 years ago, yet the Philistines too remembered.\n\nIt was a painful loss for them and a memory they wished was not part of their history.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:18:13","s":["a4znpeu26a"]}]},"30":{"3":[{"m":"It was good they returned and did not partake in the battle.\n\nThey would have come back only to realize the loss of their homes and families.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:20:08","s":["wdo8kk1xvu"]}],"6":[{"m":"David encouraged himself in the Lord his God, and therefore sought him even in his troubles.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:21:08","s":["dmdp2pskgu"]}],"8":[{"m":"Shall I pursue? Is this even a question 🙋 to ask?\n\nObviously, I mean, your family has just been taken captive and your home burnt down.\n\nIs pursuing not the obvious step to take?\nOr could this line of questioning hint us as to how David enquired of the Lord?\n\nHis requesting for the ephod meant he likely used the Urim and Thummim.\n\nIn that case, he got a yes and no answer, and not words or sentences.\n\nHe thus had to wisely ask his question 🙋 so the answers make meaning.\n\nThis again lets us in on how spiritual things work.\n\nWe must know and understand how God communicates with us, and his impulses and directions.\n\nIndeed, we must learn to walk with the Lord and know his ways with us personally.","dt":"2024-06-11T00:29:50","s":["uth4f927vw"]}],"25":[{"m":"David had a sense of justice; indeed, he was God's man.","dt":"2024-06-11T02:14:11","s":["wb1p85jsri"]}],"31":[{"m":"The loot was not sent to just some randoms, but strategically, as a thank you to all those areas he often stayed.\n\nA man must show diplomacy and gratitude for the things done for him or her.","dt":"2024-06-11T02:17:10","s":["dp57c3d4sj"]},{"m":"David was wise and very diplomatic. By giving them of the spoil, they would feel a sense of obligation to him to protect and keep him informed of anything, hopefully.\n\nOf course, this is not guaranteed, as we saw with some other towns, including people whom David had rescued from their enemies.","dt":"2026-04-19T07:58:51","s":["7rsay091q9"]}],"26":[{"m":"This indeed might have been such a large loot for him to send some to all the elders?","dt":"2024-06-11T02:15:16","s":["dbwgme2dhf"]}]},"7":{"17":[{"m":"Ramah was his home 🏡.\n\nWhat a proud mother Hannah would be... I can imagine the joy and pride of motherhood.\n\nHer son now a notable prophet and esteemed judge in Israel.","dt":"2024-05-30T15:32:19","s":["7pbm6b4xn1","0b67b03932"]}]},"31":{"8":[{"m":"What do they expect to get on the slain? Like some 💍 jewellery from previous loots, fine swords ⚔ and souvenirs of war.\n\nImagine having the armour of Saul in your custody... The great and feared king 👑.\n\nSaul, who has a warrior called David, a youth who uses slings only to slay giants and then uses the giant's sword to behead them.\n\nOnly God knows the stories and legends formed around Saul and his reign over forty years.\n\nThis reminds me of our own longest serving president, JJ Rawlings, and the stories surrounding him.","dt":"2024-06-11T07:53:43","s":["2qzwk0objy"]}],"9":[{"m":"They thought they had a souvenir and had destroyed the head and star of Israel. They didn't know they had just unlocked their doom in David. They were undone by killing Saul.\n\nThey just didn't know it yet.","dt":"2026-04-19T08:02:25","s":["5i3e1y23i3"]}]}},"Proverbs":{"1":{"18":[{"m":"Spreading the net in the sight of the bird 🐦 will not yield result; the bird will not walk into the trap.\n\nIf you wait, you wait in vain.\n\nAfter this analogy, Solomon further states that not only do such wicked thieves wait in vain, but they wait for the trap to ensnare themselves.\n\nThey will entrap their own lives.","dt":"2024-07-20T06:52:12","s":["letsv2x7yu"]}],"26":[{"m":"It happens to us all. When we refuse to listen 👂 to instructions and end up reaping the consequences of wrong choices.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:01:56","s":["hjxweb4f84"]}],"32":[{"m":"So it happens many times in life that a man, after much struggle, begins to prosper, and then he feeds his lusts with his riches.\n\nDesiring many a strange woman 👩 to the detriment of their own soul and heritage.\n\nNow their children beg in the streets and have no one to attend to them.\n\nTheir father was once rich, yet his children beg for bread 🥪.\n\nFoolishness on display, wisdom to be learnt by others, but too late for them.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:07:25","s":["r75jtd9qe1"]}],"33":[{"m":"Those who listen to wisdom in difficult times are safe and dwell quietly despite the turmoil outside happening to others.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:08:16","s":["q6nimane1b"]}],"13":[{"m":"Sinners here was in reference to armed robbers, for they fill their houses with spoil.","dt":"2024-07-20T06:48:30","s":["oqjfsbcgdo"]}],"22":[{"m":"The scorners scorn wisdom; they make light of the law of God and laugh at instruction of wisdom.\n\nNot only do they reject wisdom, but make mockery of it.\n\nThey know not that it is themselves they mock at. For God cannot be mocked; a man reaps what he sows.","dt":"2024-07-20T06:58:48","s":["8bfqz96wko"]}],"28":[{"m":"When consequences to our actions come, then we learn sense, but it is too late.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:03:02","s":["ug4nk483w1"]}]},"2":{"1":[{"m":"Hide the commandment such that you never lose it.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:01:42","s":["vkl6si9c7x"]}],"4":[{"m":"Wisdom is not obtained passively and lackadaisically.\n\nIt is actively obtained and very deliberately.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:10:22","s":["8vjjhe7pz5"]}],"5":[{"m":"As hidden treasure? This shows the deliberateness that must be applied to get wisdom... Same as one does for riches and wealth 🧐","dt":"2022-06-02T07:03:49","s":["ljszweb9vc"]},{"m":"Quest for wisdom leads to knowledge of God.\n\nSo then, instead of combing the world 🗺 for wisdom and searching the ends of the earth, why don't we search for God, who is more easily attainable?\n\nAnd his words are written and penned down for us all to see.\n\nIt's wisdom to actually fear 😱 God and seek him.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:30:08","s":["msicxryh08"]}],"16":[{"m":"Wisdom delivers us from wicked men and from strange women 🚺","dt":"2024-07-20T07:40:50","s":["qi7rj34lbr"]}],"19":[{"m":"When you unite with a strange woman 👩, there is no turning back.\n\nOnce you sleep with her, it cannot be undone; you have begun to dig your own grave.\n\nIt's like letting trash words out of your mouth; once it's out, we know what is in your heart, and it cannot be unheard again.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:42:38","s":["an3j37yn35"]}],"20":[{"m":"So there is a certain path that is only for the righteous, and that path takes wisdom to be kept.\n\nTo be kept there from the wicked and wayward.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:07:28","s":["qteyoxilb0"]}],"6":[{"m":"The wisdom I seek is not shrouded in some mysterious element out there in the ethos...\n\nIt's right here with us; it proceeds from the mouth 👄 of God; it's in the laws and instructions of righteousness.\n\nWisdom is our portion in the Lord.\n\nWe must seek, therefore, to know and understand the Lord more and more.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:34:46","s":["hk50h0tmez"]}],"7":[{"m":"Ah, there we go! Without reading this verse, I had said in the previous verse that wisdom is found in the instructions of righteousness, and here we have it said clearly.\n\nRighteousness is wisdom.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:35:53","s":["zbpom1xfa0"]}],"8":[{"m":"When one walks in righteous judgement, know that such paths of judgement are kept by the Lord himself.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:39:17","s":["rqh3xsp1th"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"Again, very strong emphasis must be laid on deliberately keeping the law.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:12:49","s":["x0bxf8fdvs"]}],"2":[{"m":"Obviously, something this valuable should not come easy and on the surface.\n\nOne must search deep.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:13:44","s":["ph76labywt"]}],"6":[{"m":"So that is it. Acknowledge him in all you do, so you are directed thus.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:15:32","s":["tds44wx7o7"]}],"10":[{"m":"Wisdom in building the kingdom of God. He is faithful.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:16:19","s":["lelunld99k"]}],"12":[{"m":"This is currently my lot.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:16:47","s":["10aztrr2lh"]}],"15":[{"m":"All that can be desired cannot be compared to her. If that is the case, then any wise person will choose her over everything else. Any wise person will choose her first — ensure she is firmly in his grips and he in hers before going for any other thing.\n\nThough from the sound of things, by the time you get wisdom, you will have riches and every precious thing, so then why would you risk letting her go for other things?\n\nShe is the first and the principal thing. She is the foundation of all things desirable.","dt":"2026-06-05T03:01:11","s":["5dff44cf2b","hmdeq4r8ou"]}],"18":[{"m":"Again, the infinite benefit of wisdom is being released to us-ward.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:17:53","s":["m1ftt5ylp7"]}],"19":[{"m":"Aside moral uprightness and guidance for a good and peaceful life,\n\nwisdom is found in creativity... Creativity requires wisdom, and it's demonstrated by God in his creation of the earth 🌎 by his wisdom.\n\nThe heavens by his understanding, and the beautiful things in the heavens and the earth by knowledge.","dt":"2024-07-20T07:53:11","s":["4byf41nb80"]}],"21":[{"m":"How invaluable wisdom is; we are instructed to never let it out of our eyes.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:19:12","s":["tamxt3dh85"]}],"31":[{"m":"Here we are given some nuggets of wisdom.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:20:41","s":["i25budtv5s"]}],"33":[{"m":"We must therefore be wary of the company of wicked men; who knows, we may be courting with a cursed 🤬 man 👨","dt":"2024-07-20T07:49:59","s":["y113wnlvqd"]}],"35":[{"m":"So a man glorified of God is a man of wisdom.","dt":"2022-06-02T07:21:33","s":["m4isn5lov7"]}]},"6":{"7":[{"m":"Self-rule is the way of wisdom — like the ant, one who rules and deals diligently shall be fat.","dt":"2026-06-05T05:37:06","s":["ffdcb118d2"]}],"22":[{"m":"As we hold on fast to wisdom, wisdom reciprocates by keeping us and teaching us.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:07:40","s":["bb1yh9r2ol"]}],"24":[{"m":"No better person to tell us about the evil 😈 woman than Solomon.\n\nHe had a thousand women at his disposal, though he could not dispose them off like he assumed.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:08:47","s":["xcvx2pl5a9"]}],"32":[{"m":"I don't know if this proverb was deliberately put after the one talking of a thief's ability to restore what was stolen,\n\nin order to create the contrast that he who commits adultery cannot restore nor ransom in any way.\n\nWisdom continues to hammer home the dangers of fornication more than others — this goes to show how important of a role avoiding the strange woman 👩 plays in our overall success in this life.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:12:19","s":["8vj25o34wz"]}],"35":[{"m":"Okay, this confirms my thoughts 💭 in verse 32: the one who commits adultery cannot ransom his soul.\n\nSolomon was king and judge and saw to many cases.\n\nSo he had the rare opportunity to see people's lives grow and blossom 🌸, only to be destroyed by some of these mistakes.\n\nHe saw and judged many cases and gleaned wisdom from them, so we can apply it to our lives. Though we have not that same privilege, we can have the same knowledge.\n\nHe, as judge, had seen how many a man sought to avoid being stoned for adultery, as required by the law, and the many pleadings of such a man 👨, all to no avail.\n\nHe had to be put to death by stoning, as stated in the law of Moses.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:17:24","s":["spd1fi75tz"]}],"21":[{"m":"Wisdom constantly constantly constantly pleads that we never let go of her in our speech and actions.\n\nIt seems that wisdom is easily despised, or it is easier and effortless to walk without wisdom and in folly.\n\nSo wisdom admonishes us to hold on very hard to her, for wisdom is our life.\n\nAnd this indeed is true; no wonder very few wise people are found in our days and times...","dt":"2024-07-24T08:07:08","s":["lbpqtp126p"]}]},"7":{"26":[{"m":"Oh, how true! Strong 💪 men have indeed been slain by her.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:20:22","s":["069oe9hnb2"]}]},"8":{"1":[{"m":"Wisdom is not hidden; it's open 🔓, it's out there where all can partake of.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:21:36","s":["j47f3ud315"]}],"2":[{"m":"Wisdom is in the open, contrasted with the strange woman and folly, who hide in the darkness.","dt":"2026-06-05T05:57:39","s":["ec34249812"]}]},"10":{"12":[{"m":"No wonder lovers are the best of friends.\n\nYou see no wrong,\n\nyou can't even seem to understand when prompted of red flags 🎌","dt":"2024-07-25T06:08:08","s":["hbxr9i43ma"]}],"21":[{"m":"The righteous has transcended feeding himself and feeds many; the fool is not even able to feed himself, talk less of 1 or 2 others, and even less talk of many.","dt":"2026-06-06T03:36:01","s":["e453abd6db"]}]},"11":{"4":[{"m":"In the day of wrath and judgement, it is one's righteousness, not his riches, that shall acquit him.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:28:22","s":["xchrtxpfya"]}],"9":[{"m":"Through knowledge the just shall be delivered from the destruction of the hypocrite.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:29:41","s":["dv85ho379g"]}],"10":[{"m":"Same reaction, one to the rising of one and an even louder one to the downfall of the other, the righteous and the wicked respectively.","dt":"2026-06-06T03:50:46","s":["8de68d03b5"]}],"11":[{"m":"And it is the mouth 👄 of fools that have started many useless and profitless wars.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:31:52","s":["inoxom0usi"]},{"m":"This is so true, so true that ironically his own son divided his own kingdom through his foolish talk and foolish counsel from his peers.","dt":"2026-06-06T03:53:32","s":["532af06ff6"]}],"12":[{"m":"He is thy neighbour; you can never tell when you will need him or what information he has that will help you or deliver you from evil in time to come.","dt":"2026-06-06T03:56:59","s":["99fbd18f43"]}],"15":[{"m":"Hate is a strong word for suretyship, but that goes to explain how that one must flee from being surety for another.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:33:21","s":["aw3ymid3xn"]}]},"12":{"9":[{"m":"Fake life is the order of the day; everyone is pretending to be of some importance they are not of.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:40:58","s":["luukv92zkf"]}],"10":[{"m":"The tender mercies of the wicked are cruel, so do not expect any good or mercy from them.\n\nExpect it from the righteous, but not from the wicked.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:43:41","s":["pp74a4daz3"]}],"12":[{"m":"Seeing the seeming profit of other wicked men, the wicked desire such vain riches.\n\nBut the righteous sows and works with his own hand 🖐️ and yields fruit of himself, rather than to covet what is others'.","dt":"2024-07-25T06:48:57","s":["mm6idk1d7w"]}]},"13":{"10":[{"m":"The proud, therefore, is not well advised or has refused to heed advice.","dt":"2024-07-25T07:06:22","s":["fskz8dh8ke"]}],"12":[{"m":"I just set small achievable targets, so I am refreshed in accomplishing them.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:22:56","s":["h6yh6f46fu"]}],"16":[{"m":"Acquiring knowledge in your field brings wisdom.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:21:40","s":["7cc14eqvje"]}],"18":[{"m":"So another wisdom nugget is to listen to instruction.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:20:57","s":["lbcyyzyr3s"]}],"19":[{"m":"I must accomplish my desire. For the good of my own mental health.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:22:17","s":["46pshybtkx"]}],"20":[{"m":"Hm 🤔... Another wisdom nugget as to how to acquire wisdom.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:24:01","s":["bm2sfxqpw2"]}],"21":[{"m":"So both ways there is pursuit or payback for what is done... be it good or evil.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:24:57","s":["21i094szbo"]},{"m":"As sinners get their due recompense, so the righteous also.","dt":"2024-07-25T07:10:23","s":["hcl5rbxkil"]}],"23":[{"m":"For want of the ability to judge what is good and not, the poor is destroyed.\n\nHe lacks, though there is food.","dt":"2022-06-06T09:26:48","s":["yj0mq3op5w"]}]},"14":{"8":[{"m":"Hhm... The wisdom of the prudent: he judges everything and seeks to understand and be master of his ways, be it business, family, etc.","dt":"2022-06-06T10:18:07","s":["qrwvyjfd8c"]}],"15":[{"m":"One of my personal errors in time past.","dt":"2022-06-06T10:31:57","s":["x9jocsh9ix"]}],"18":[{"m":"Don't be simple-minded or simple-behaved; folly will be yours.\n\nWhen you are prudent and look well into a matter and think deeply, that deep insight will be rewarded... You will be crowned.","dt":"2024-07-25T07:13:26","s":["dwk9fn347m"]}],"19":[{"m":"So if you see one bowing before the other, it may be an example of this proverb.","dt":"2022-06-06T10:54:28","s":["5uk34dnnx7"]}],"23":[{"m":"When you work hard, you definitely profit; talk leads to penury.","dt":"2022-06-06T10:53:08","s":["2ho2mzwyfy"]}],"24":[{"m":"Seeing thou a rich man, he has a certain wisdom which you have not.","dt":"2022-06-06T10:53:38","s":["xq3jl7eaeg"]}],"25":[{"m":"And in speaking lies, a deceitful witness destroys souls.\n\nHe shall not go unpunished.","dt":"2024-07-27T06:42:15","s":["o4df1zmaz1"]}],"29":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔m... Well said, straightforward wisdom.\n\nWrath and haste is not wisdom; temperance in all things shows one's understanding of matters.","dt":"2024-07-25T07:16:47","s":["8yo5cmkq29"]}],"28":[{"m":"Lord, help me grow, I pray...","dt":"2022-06-06T10:55:04","s":["pfeh3sag4u"]}]},"15":{"1":[{"m":"Being easily angered is not wise. Many times Proverbs speaks against it.","dt":"2022-06-06T12:50:40","s":["dr9fs7jldn"]}],"10":[{"m":"Bam. It is done.","dt":"2022-06-06T12:53:11","s":["u46ppfrvef"]}],"14":[{"m":"Knowledge must be sought; that is how it is obtained. It does not just come naturally to us.","dt":"2022-06-06T12:55:06","s":["9dtjy3fth2"]}],"15":[{"m":"Could this then mean that, regardless of the environment, we can choose how we react and remain happy 😊 and of a merry heart in spite of the external factors?","dt":"2024-07-25T09:55:17","s":["mj37jmo3kj"]}],"16":[{"m":"This brings balance to righteousness and wisdom invariably leading to riches.","dt":"2022-06-06T13:07:12","s":["esqocxjsth"]}],"17":[{"m":"Some things are better than others. Of course, we will all prefer a good fatty dinner, but love is better than hatred.","dt":"2022-06-06T13:08:51","s":["zcdwrqqn1m"]}],"18":[{"m":"This is akin to a soft answer turning away wrath.","dt":"2022-06-06T13:09:19","s":["r8ht3yk5r8"]}],"19":[{"m":"You can barely make any progress with the slothful... They will delay you perpetually.","dt":"2024-07-25T09:57:18","s":["wc04635dwn"]}],"22":[{"m":"Wisdom for me. The many things I wish to achieve that seem to have stalled or seem difficult to take off. Wisdom will set them free.","dt":"2022-06-06T13:11:14","s":["cl9pp8ngo2"]},{"m":"Hmm 🤔, the key for establishment is counsel, wise counsel.","dt":"2024-07-25T09:58:26","s":["0317er94wc"]}],"26":[{"m":"Not just the words, but the very thought of the wicked the Lord detests...\n\nAnd again, not just the words, but even the thoughts of the pure are a delight to the Lord.","dt":"2024-07-27T06:57:23","s":["jkvyp6s18z"]}],"28":[{"m":"We should not be quick to answer.","dt":"2022-06-06T13:12:28","s":["6qdh3bytyt"]}],"33":[{"m":"Hmm. This is a key wisdom key. Having respect for God and obeying the dictates of his law gives wisdom.\n\nBefore honour is humility, not rashness and pompousness.\n\nThe question then becomes, what is humility?","dt":"2022-06-06T13:16:22","s":["hzfxt6vn7b"]}],"6":[{"m":"Righteousness equates to wisdom. Because we find riches in the house of the wise, and here we find riches in the house of the righteous.","dt":"2022-06-06T12:52:22","s":["za7wqveue0"]}]},"16":{"3":[{"m":"Wisdom key 🗝 right there for establishment.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:31:08","s":["aiwxapd2ud"]}],"5":[{"m":"Though they unite in evil 😈, they shall not go unpunished.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:32:21","s":["wns1kj5jdf"]}],"8":[{"m":"Most in our day will not agree with this or meet this standard.\n\nIt's all about greed and corruption — making riches at all cost.","dt":"2024-07-27T07:30:54","s":["89rxkkxfsb"]}],"12":[{"m":"No wonder our thrones in Africa 🌍 are not established, and our leaders and their parties can't retain power.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:34:07","s":["h7zul0ncjq"]},{"m":"Abomination is a strong 💪 word to use; this goes to show how anyone in power must avoid wickedness and abuse of power if he/she intends to keep ruling, which all kings do.\n\nYet, contrary to their own desires, they shoot themselves in the foot and end their reign through wickedness.","dt":"2024-07-27T07:33:42","s":["5komy06qlm"]}],"17":[{"m":"Indeed it is a high way... You keep your honor and integrity. You walk confidently without fear. Your soul is preserved.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:42:20","s":["32h8pyqso4"]},{"m":"It is indeed a high way: no distractions, no bends, no entanglement.\n\nRighteousness helps you keep a right path, and your way ahead is clear.\n\nYou move faster in life and you excel above most.","dt":"2024-07-27T07:36:13","s":["h779y4g25j"]}],"31":[{"m":"I love that, terms and conditions? Haha 😄... If it be found in the way of righteousness.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:45:25","s":["xv4lf6yzkw"]},{"m":"So not all grey hair is honorable or a sign of wisdom and honour;\n\nit must be found in the way of righteousness.\n\nLet us therefore have wisdom as we approach the grey-headed.\n\nIt is assumed, but not always so, that the grey-headed are wise.","dt":"2024-07-27T07:40:18","s":["b9y7t0afzg"]}],"32":[{"m":"This proverb, so true! No wonder there are many mighty men and conquerors who can't control their temper nor rule their own spirit.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:46:55","s":["2bgmi6nmyi"]}],"33":[{"m":"This is just like life: we do what we can, because time and chance happens to us all, but as to the kind of outcome... It's in the hands 👐 of the Lord.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:48:22","s":["bf9wo4vriq"]}]},"17":{"3":[{"m":"The Lord is the heart's refinery;\n\nhe's the fire for the heart to purge it.","dt":"2024-07-27T08:19:32","s":["hr2c0g6syf"]}],"10":[{"m":"This is one of those straightforward but interesting Proverbs.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:55:31","s":["pqgtm4038v"]}],"11":[{"m":"Like the cruel messenger Solomon himself sent against Joab, Shimei and Adonijah.","dt":"2024-07-27T08:36:10","s":["u4bqr58num"]}],"16":[{"m":"Then that means wisdom can be and is bought, through paying for books 📚, journeying to the place of wisdom to obtain it for free or at a cost,\n\nto gain audience with the great, or to remain in the assembly of the wise.\n\nFor the rewards thereof are greater than gold and silver.","dt":"2022-06-07T06:59:05","s":["wgu78241qa"]}],"2":[{"m":"What makes such a wise servant? It's not the servant's sweet words; those will be just pretentious.\n\nIt is the servant's skill and dedication and loyalty and leadership.\n\nThe ability to bring profit to the master that gives him such an inheritance.","dt":"2024-07-27T08:13:33","s":["4trswh9iqt"]}],"12":[{"m":"Really?? 😱.\n\nThen we must not treat the foolishness of fools lightly.\n\nIt can cause irreparable damage. As wise, let's walk 🚶 as such.\n\nNot intermeddling our wisdom with folly.","dt":"2024-07-27T08:37:29","s":["9rmstfz19u"]}]},"18":{"15":[{"m":"Wisdom is sought out. Searched for diligently.","dt":"2022-06-08T02:52:56","s":["x3azmbwj3h"]}],"1":[{"m":"The pathway to wisdom:\n1. Desire\n\n2. Separate yourself\n\n3. Seek\n\n4. Find and practice\n\n5. Attain into all manner of wisdom","dt":"2022-06-08T02:42:30","s":["bhg80uqxx0"]}],"22":[{"m":"Another wisdom nugget.","dt":"2022-06-08T02:53:57","s":["ybux332vz0"]}]},"19":{"14":[{"m":"Give grace, Lord... For some things are of men, but that which only you can give, Lord, give them, we pray 🙏","dt":"2022-06-08T11:07:43","s":["db8z5d58l8"]}],"17":[{"m":"How did Solomon know this one? Cause this could not have come by general observation 🔭.\n\nONLY insight into the mind of God can bring such knowledge.","dt":"2022-06-08T12:52:50","s":["fqnt4788u9"]}],"18":[{"m":"Do not let even the crying 😢 and tearing of your son in the time of discipline restrain you.\n\nChasten him whiles there is hope.\n\nThis, I believe, is how God deals with us sometimes too.\n\nDespite our crying 😢 and tears 😭 and pleading 🙏... He ignores and brings us to the right path.\n\nMaybe in this season of my life, this also may be my chastening.","dt":"2022-06-08T12:54:44","s":["3j5wfuoxo6"]}],"20":[{"m":"One of my favorite verses of all time.","dt":"2022-06-08T12:55:40","s":["lh6o0rsk42"]}],"19":[{"m":"True","dt":"2022-06-08T12:54:59","s":["ea9dd54be2"]}]},"20":{"5":[{"m":"It is drawn out by asking and, indeed, provoking the right questions.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:11:20","s":["j15c5rastk"]}],"6":[{"m":"Okay 👌. So true... It is the simple who believes every word he/she hears.\n\nVery few men are indeed faithful. Thus, walk with this wisdom in mind.\n\nVery few men are indeed faithful.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:12:31","s":["q77wm7rk79"]}],"7":[{"m":"There is no negative impact of the father's errors on his children.\n\nIndeed, because of his good name, his children are blessed.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:17:41","s":["4blhnf5gfg"]}],"8":[{"m":"Yes, a good king indeed 👑 scattereth evil in the seat of judgement.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:18:32","s":["hf9rh4ndnc"]}],"11":[{"m":"So watch and know people by their actions, not just their words. Or should I say, not by their words only.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:13:54","s":["frg5g7n9o5"]}],"12":[{"m":"The wise eye and ears 👂 that hear wisdom are from the Lord.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:14:44","s":["e9d0wbrbjj"]}],"15":[{"m":"Does that also mean, then, that the lips of knowledge are indeed very rare?\n\nIs that why so many people are followers rather than leaders?\n\nThe lips of knowledge, is it that rare?\n\nIs that why we are to search for wisdom, because it seems so alien 👾 to our nature 🏞, though abundant everywhere and calling out in the 🔓 open?","dt":"2022-06-08T13:16:56","s":["qeft4x46yi"]}],"18":[{"m":"Okay 👌. Thanks 🙏","dt":"2022-06-08T13:17:50","s":["ubyxqi4l4n"]},{"m":"So it is with good advice and counsel that we embark on a venture and make war.\n\nNot with good intentions would our purposes be established, nor by rage and adrenaline would we win a war.\n\nNot even with a justifiable reason of ill treatment will we win war.\n\nIt is with good counsel.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:31:04","s":["cga5xkaj8r"]}],"20":[{"m":"In the law, such an one could be stoned to death ☠; either this was what King Solomon was referring to, or he was talking of the ill luck that will come to such an one for his cursing 🤬","dt":"2024-07-29T06:33:14","s":["z67ug2fhc1"]}],"24":[{"m":"How can a man then understand his own way without the Lord's counsel and instruction?","dt":"2024-07-29T06:37:29","s":["ysh9a37sa9"]}],"25":[{"m":"Proverbs 20:25 GNT\nThink carefully before you promise an offering to God. You might regret it later.\n\nWill the church ⛪ today ever preach with this verse?","dt":"2022-06-08T13:21:40","s":["0ycoblzslh"]},{"m":"The NKJV brings out the meaning better.\n\nProverbs 20:25 NKJV\nIt is a snare for a man to devote rashly something as holy, And afterward to reconsider his vows.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:39:22","s":["wgisnkf9e6"]}],"29":[{"m":"So years are not lost just because your natural strength 💪 is abated; no, it's replaced with wisdom if you are wise, which is so precious.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:22:47","s":["awwhygfki5"]}],"30":[{"m":"Punishment and facing the consequences of one's actions purges you and cleanses you, helping you to learn wisdom and behave uprightly.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:43:16","s":["qg9er2ckn4"]}],"4":[{"m":"This brings balance once again...\n\nYet we are encouraged to give to the poor and beggar.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:10:48","s":["paoqdsadzp"]}],"26":[{"m":"So therefore a wicked king gathers to himself wicked and vain persons, to the end that he might enrich himself and fulfill his lusts,\n\nat the expense of his own people.\n\nSuch a king is soon hated, and his throne shall not continue.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:40:59","s":["jir27qebgz"]}]},"21":{"5":[{"m":"Because he will follow up on his thoughts 💭 with hard work, so he will reap plenty.\n\nThe hasty will not take time to do what is right, and yet desire results.\n\nThey will have nothing but only want and hunger.","dt":"2024-07-29T06:51:50","s":["4o8ho5hm23"]}],"6":[{"m":"That's quite a harsh consequence of ill-gotten wealth.\n\nBut it does happen, especially death in a figurative sense.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:29:01","s":["qeok20acw6"]}],"13":[{"m":"This does not mean senselessly giving to the poor without doing some due diligence when you can, or asking and pondering to ensure it is a genuine need.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:31:02","s":["qtw41xh6m7"]}],"14":[{"m":"Though anger and wrath are emotions which are intangibles, there are tangible ways to pacify it.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:32:10","s":["wg4rdcsa1r"]}],"15":[{"m":"To the just, it is joy to mete out justice.\n\nIt is the workers of 👷 iniquity, however, who shall suffer.","dt":"2024-07-29T07:13:50","s":["gmohupvtaz"]}],"16":[{"m":"This goes to show how costly lack of understanding can be betimes.\n\nIt can indeed lead to death of family 👪, property, etc. etc.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:33:03","s":["g2gnzhf4qr"]}],"17":[{"m":"And there are so many people with much in hand, but have not made ends meet because of lifestyle.","dt":"2022-06-08T13:33:51","s":["5osp3zi7hz"]}],"18":[{"m":"But such injustice was meted out to the Lord when the Jews, the very custodians of the law of God and such wisdom, did the very opposite.","dt":"2024-07-29T07:17:27","s":["t7nobud49y"]}],"25":[{"m":"Yes, and literally this is what happens: the slothful suffer want and eventually die, no matter how long it takes, in a state of need and lack.","dt":"2024-07-29T07:18:50","s":["53gdqvlpej"]}],"27":[{"m":"Is it a wicked mind, as in to win the favour and blessing of the Lord in his evil endeavors?\n\nI guess that is the case, trusting that God somehow would give blessings to his wicked ways.","dt":"2024-07-29T07:20:57","s":["ug4gwqoz48"]}],"29":[{"m":"You see a hardened face, haughty temperament, winking eyes 👀,\n\nyou be dealing with a wicked man 👨","dt":"2022-06-08T13:36:24","s":["mi65d3wf8n"]}],"11":[{"m":"For the scorner, it takes punishment for him to stop his scorning.\n\nFor the simple, seeing such brute punishment on the scorner now teaches him wisdom.\n\nAs for the wise, words alone are more than enough to set him on the right course and give him knowledge.","dt":"2024-07-29T07:12:33","s":["mckcnfbjpp"]}],"30":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-06-08T13:35:17","s":["5c146531de"]}]},"22":{"4":[{"m":"I like this one.","dt":"2022-06-09T06:56:28","s":["77ktvfrqeg"]}],"12":[{"m":"Because the words of the transgressor seek to destroy knowledge and truth, so the Lord overthrows his words.","dt":"2024-07-30T07:30:05","s":["nn0xld8g2f"]}],"18":[{"m":"Let wisdom continuously enter your heart; soon enough it shall fit your lips 💋","dt":"2022-06-09T07:01:31","s":["90d3y1034v"]}],"15":[{"m":"Far from him... Very far from him. That is the key word.","dt":"2022-06-09T06:59:39","s":["4mp3v4xwhx"]}]},"23":{"2":[{"m":"Why is that so? Why is the meat of the ruler deceitful meat?\n\nIs it that it is a trap for the ruler to observe your conduct when abundance or limitless resources are brought before you?\n\nSuch that by your eating, your motives and character are judged.","dt":"2024-07-30T07:41:35","s":["pc6zs33zdp"]}],"4":[{"m":"Why would wisdom say this, when riches is a good thing?\n\nIronically, he pleads and begs for us to gain wisdom and search for it as we would precious rubies.\n\nYet when it comes to riches, he cautions us about it.\n\nCould it be because of the deceitfulness of riches?\n\nSo the irony is that we seek and labour to be rich, rather than seeking with the same passion for wisdom, and rather disdain wisdom and treat it lightly.\n\nIt seems we have our priorities the other way round.\n\nMay the Lord help us.\n\nIn the next verse we are told why we should not set our eyes on riches: they are so fleeting and uncertain.","dt":"2024-07-30T07:46:57","s":["68f5pegztq"]}],"5":[{"m":"The teacher is not against riches, for he teaches in his many proverbs how to grow in wealth and take care of one's flocks etc.\n\nBut what we are warned about is that riches is not a sure thing; it can disappear any time, so it is not wise to cast your hopes and life upon it.\n\nRather, seek for wisdom, which cannot be taken from you and which will give you life and lead you in the way you should go.\n\nMoney is so fleeting; it cannot be taken to the grave with you, others will inherit it, but wisdom will preserve your life both in this realm and hereafter.","dt":"2024-07-30T07:57:44","s":["haitp1cf6c"]}],"11":[{"m":"So the many people in our times who, through their influence and power, have taken others' property in this country,\n\nwoe to them; they fight against one who is mighty, but they know not.\n\nOne day they will pay for it bad.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:01:08","s":["tqdz4n8c4s"]}],"13":[{"m":"A worthy 🗒 note to all parents.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:06:07","s":["4xfhv7j8pa"]}],"17":[{"m":"It is an easy temptation to fall into, because sinners seem to enjoy life and do so well, but it's only a matter of time.\n\nWe are admonished in the next verse that our expectation shall not be cut off in the end.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:04:06","s":["ecfmaur907"]}],"23":[{"m":"Very apt and beautiful summary of the cry of wisdom.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:07:34","s":["th5ipruvh9"]},{"m":"We are not to let go of wisdom ever; we must accumulate only and never let go of it.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:08:00","s":["9ld8jgpf0y"]}],"33":[{"m":"That is the more grave danger of drunkenness: things you would ordinarily not have done, you will end up doing.\n\nWhen you finally awake out of your stupor, the wisdom of your ways will be before you.\n\nYou will reap the consequences.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:13:25","s":["rbehha6d21"]}],"7":[{"m":"Another wisdom key when it comes to eating with the wicked: his heart is not with thee.\n\nWith every morsel you swallow, he is scheming how he will get back every morsel you have swallowed and more.","dt":"2024-07-30T07:59:17","s":["zlr6xsiyr9"]}]},"24":{"1":[{"m":"It is an easy error of the righteous, where you do all that is right yet seem to reap little, and the wicked and ungodly prosper in their way.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:10:43","s":["9850zfy5g8"]}],"6":[{"m":"So there is physical strength and mental strength 💪","dt":"2022-06-09T07:12:46","s":["mrhsnmlqog"]}],"10":[{"m":"So the measure of one's strength is not when you say you are strong 💪; it is adversity that shall prove it.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:13:54","s":["zcpwptc07j"]}],"11":[{"m":"It is akin to the scripture in Ezekiel admonishing the prophet to forewarn men of their sins, lest their blood be upon his head and he be guilty.\n\nI am reminded of the justice of David all through his life, even the justice he brought to Joab, who somehow seems to have escaped justice.\n\nBut the long arms of the law under David brought justice upon him even in his old age.\n\nDavid executed the will and law of God.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:22:26","s":["ylqemtviu2"]}],"14":[{"m":"Wisdom is so important it cannot be overemphasized.\n\nWe see the writer use so many different allegories just to drive home the point of how eternally vitally important wisdom is.\n\nAnd how we must walk in it always.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:16:15","s":["i12040asir"]}],"16":[{"m":"And by implication, when the wicked fall into mischief, they rise not again.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:23:11","s":["a0pr7xxicr"]}],"20":[{"m":"We have been given that firm assurance: the wicked shall not do well.\n\nThey may seem to get away with it, but no, not at all; their judgement shall come, and come swiftly.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:24:26","s":["reg0lj5efb"]}],"22":[{"m":"Keep a safe distance from wicked men, lest their ruin become yours.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:22:12","s":["986uuian4o"]}],"27":[{"m":"A very practical note 🗒... Worth noting.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:18:57","s":["s4so5ddfth"]}],"29":[{"m":"Do not take revenge.\n\nDo not let the wicked take you down their path of wickedness.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:28:07","s":["80qaskrqbm"]}],"34":[{"m":"The lazy man's end.","dt":"2022-06-09T07:19:49","s":["d70oq7rmvf"]},{"m":"Oh yes, when you travel and you run out of money, and there is no one you know,\n\nit is a terrible thing. Even when you have money but your car breaks down in the middle of nowhere, it is a terrible plight.","dt":"2024-07-30T08:29:46","s":["md5ul8h9h8"]}],"3":[{"m":"What does it mean by it is established???","dt":"2022-06-09T07:11:55","s":["g5al18aby0"]}]},"26":{"5":[{"m":"So the kind of answer you give to a fool is what will determine if you will be like him and be thought a fool also, or if you show his folly for all to see.","dt":"2024-08-12T07:59:47","s":["hxujpmr4qt"]}],"7":[{"m":"The fool and his parable are also not equal.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:00:37","s":["zb91b6xqzn"]}],"12":[{"m":"There is little hope for a fool, but to be self-conceited leaves you with literally no hope.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:03:17","s":["s0zl1qeqal"]}],"22":[{"m":"Another group of people to be wary of: tale bearers.\n\nThey are so good with their craft that they know how to say what they want to say to produce the most painful results.\n\nThey separate friends and families. Avoid them.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:05:01","s":["fxicipiyy4"]}],"24":[{"m":"Never trust the words of someone who is bitter and hurt or hateful; if he speaks fairly, be careful, for deceit may well be in his heart.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:08:18","s":["0mnrs3hwy1"]}],"27":[{"m":"If you seek to hurt and entrap others, you yourself will be hurt and entrapped.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:09:13","s":["jcuh7ydwob"]}],"8":[{"m":"That honour shall be flung out quicker than a stone out of a sling.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:01:50","s":["6wsbdfme7f"]}],"19":[{"m":"Be wary of people who joke with everything, even serious stuff.","dt":"2024-08-12T08:04:18","s":["djgo66yirh"]}]},"27":{"8":[{"m":"You will definitely be ensnared when you wander into a place out of your own.\n\nSo we ought to be aware that out there are wolves and wicked men; stay under your shelter and your place.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:33:00","s":["1rivxumr9v"]}],"11":[{"m":"I can imagine David saying this to Solomon,\n\nhis son born out of wedlock and adultery and murder. Solomon had no choice than to be wise under such circumstances.\n\nAnd wise he became; he understood his peculiar situation and the mockery surrounding him.\n\nHe left nothing to chance.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:39:52","s":["pa2glb0vo7"]}],"22":[{"m":"This is serious; no wonder elsewhere he says answer not a fool according to his folly, lest you become like him.\n\nCounsel is not befitting a fool.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:44:38","s":["yv9rrhacyo"]}],"4":[{"m":"Even evil is in levels; some things are worse than others.\n\nBut we are greatly cautioned here against envy.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:27:31","s":["6jb5pqt2e7"]}],"21":[{"m":"The New King James Version brings the meaning out better; it reads:\n\nProverbs 27:21 NKJV\nThe refining pot is for silver and the furnace for gold, And a man is valued by what others say of him.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:43:19","s":["2vlm1vwp5k"]}]},"28":{"2":[{"m":"The transgressors are many and they lead the nation astray, but only a few men of understanding to prolong the life of the nation.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:50:27","s":["pyirrlq2pf"]}],"4":[{"m":"Hm, no wonder evil thrives where the good people do nothing, and whenever you try to do what is right,\n\nyou would think you would be left alone, if not even praised,\n\nbut rather you will be actively contended with.","dt":"2024-08-13T06:59:15","s":["9e1hjlpczx"]}],"23":[{"m":"Though initially not enjoyable, you shall be appreciated later.","dt":"2024-08-13T07:07:30","s":["a0cmnylrzl"]}],"26":[{"m":"Because the heart, really, is emotional and illogical often.\n\nMany wrong life-changing decisions have been made based on emotions that leave one with regret.\n\nWhy then should one give himself to such unpredictability?","dt":"2024-08-13T07:10:08","s":["unup0c4qp2"]}]},"29":{"5":[{"m":"So be wary of flattery from men; it can set you up for your fall.\n\nYou can easily overestimate yourself and fall.","dt":"2024-08-15T06:59:54","s":["n9n93tnpll"]}],"21":[{"m":"I don't know if this is a good thing or a derogatory statement,\n\nmore like a rhetoric or sarcasm.\n\nI think it is the latter.\n\nOther translations suggest the same.","dt":"2024-08-13T07:23:16","s":["e1wj36fh3h"]}],"8":[{"m":"Where, when faced with opposition, they do not speak right, but damn the consequences and destroy the city.\n\nSuch men start wars which could have been averted; they bring much strife, shame and pain.\n\nBut the wise know how to avert such.","dt":"2024-08-15T07:03:38","s":["7pdphldgrl"]}],"9":[{"m":"The CEV brings out the meaning more clearly:\n\nProverbs 29:9 CEVUK\nBe wise and don't sue a fool. You won't get satisfaction, because all the fool will do is sneer and shout.\n(AND THERE WILL BE NO PEACE — my own additions)","dt":"2024-08-13T07:20:32","s":["5vfujvx05p"]}],"27":[{"m":"So if you walk in righteousness, be wary of the wicked; they are not just unlike you or neutral to you. No, they hate you violently and would get rid of you when the opportunity presents itself.","dt":"2024-08-15T07:25:00","s":["0pypajrcjy"]}]},"4":{"7":[{"m":"Proverbs 4:7 YLT98\nThe first thing [is] wisdom — get wisdom, And with all thy getting get understanding.\n\nWisdom is the principal thing.\n\nIt is the first thing to get, therefore get wisdom. Oh God, help us, help us get you first in our quest for wisdom.\n\nIf wisdom is the first thing to get, and the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom,\n\nthat means as we begin our life's journey, we must seek wisdom. And where do we start this quest for wisdom from? From the fear of God; that is the first step on the wisdom ladder.\n\nYou enter into life and there are many ladders to climb 🧗‍♂️ unto, but oh 😱, this ancient text admonishes us to climb the wisdom ladder first, and on that ladder we are again adjured to climb 🧗‍♂️ from step one, so we don't miss out a step.\n\nAnd step one is the fear of the Lord.","dt":"2024-07-23T06:46:02","s":["fztyn7lyh2"]}]},"9":{"18":[{"m":"Who is this strange woman 👩 that has caused so much harm to many a man, to families 👪 and their children?\n\nLord, give us wisdom to stay far away from the strange woman 👩.","dt":"2024-07-24T08:28:05","s":["b3sxgijpg1"]}]},"25":{"22":[{"m":"This should be applied in context and in wisdom; stay away from your enemy's blows and arrows even as you do him this good.\n\nBecause there are some men who would still recompense you evil for your good and actually kill you when you expose yourself to them.","dt":"2024-08-12T07:31:43","s":["jcepk0nf0o"]}]}},"1 Chronicles":{"3":{"18":[{"m":"The writer of these chronicles obviously lived centuries after David, for him to give this genealogy this far down in history...\n\nALL the way to after the captivity.","dt":"2024-06-14T08:29:50","s":["e4t5raxr4t"]}]},"4":{"40":[{"m":"Which Ham? Is it the Ham of Shem, Ham and Japheth, sons of Noah?\nI believe so. Meaning they of Ham got themselves a good land in their journeys, until they were dispossessed by Israel.","dt":"2024-06-15T00:41:54","s":["nu7igvoeo8"]}],"42":[{"m":"Was Mount Seir not reckoned to Edom...\n\nOr this was just a section of it?","dt":"2024-06-15T00:45:27","s":["qsphd1jojq"]}]},"5":{"26":[{"m":"Which day? The days of the author or authors of the book of Chronicles.\n\nWhich was written after the captivities of the land, or better still, as Dake's says, compiled from various records into one book by multiple authors, including Ezra, Nathan etc.","dt":"2024-06-15T01:03:54","s":["zfbaql6bw7"]}],"2":[{"m":"A very sad and thought 💭 provoking history of these sons.\n\nSimple individual decisions had long-lasting consequences on their generations.\n\nAnd here we see Judah become their chief and head, both of Reuben, who was the natural head 🤕, and Joseph, who was head by birthright.","dt":"2024-06-15T00:49:47","s":["3cb5epb2cw"]},{"m":"Judah prevailed above the natural, and I will dare say the spiritual, birthright and became the dominant tribe, for God is no respecter of persons.\n\nLike Paul, who was the last of the apostles, yet labored more abundantly than they all.\n\nLord, help me labour more abundantly than they all.","dt":"2026-04-26T07:10:48","s":["4xorpbvkci"]}]},"6":{"69":[{"m":"Aijalon & Anathoth sound quite familiar... Would check them out.","dt":"2024-06-16T04:29:21","s":["t9aspl4lpd"]}]},"11":{"6":[{"m":"That guy was damn ambitious and would keep his place at all cost. He took his place as captain by the peril of his life and did everything to keep it. And keeping he did.","dt":"2026-05-03T09:50:33","s":["slektcjl6f"]}],"10":[{"m":"God spoke the word that David would be king 👑, but there were requirements for kingship, and all the pieces had to come together in order for the word of the Lord to be fulfilled.\n\nSo that prophetic word began to pin the pieces together till David became king 👑, and not just king, but a sure house 🏡 was established for him by aid of his mighty men,\n\nwho were uniquely anointed, each in his own right 👉, to help establish the kingdom under David.","dt":"2024-06-19T06:39:18","s":["ga3abkwitx"]},{"m":"They strengthened themselves with him to make him king and to keep him king.","dt":"2026-05-03T09:52:21","s":["j4kb4qpz1v"]}],"22":[{"m":"Such bravado... He went into a pit face to face with a lion 🦁?? 🤯.\n\nIn a pit? 🤯... Meaning there was no turning back for him or the lion... Either he dies or the lion does.\n\nThese men were fearless and the Lord was with them, or because the Lord was with them, they were fearless 😱","dt":"2024-06-19T06:49:21","s":["ca5854mhk7"]}],"46":[{"m":"David had Ammonite and other foreign nationals in his army giving him support.\n\nIndeed, the nations shall serve him was literal in his life.","dt":"2024-06-19T09:08:49","s":["e5tyuhj0xo"]}],"19":[{"m":"Such loyalty these men had. A mighty loyal army, and not just loyal, but they genuinely loved David.\n\nHe had helped raise them from nobodies, disgruntled and cast away, to become strong, mighty, significant and wealthy through the many bounties they had at war.\n\nThis story reminds me so much of the ICGC story and the many other mighty ministries throughout Africa 🌍.\n\nGod was up to something indeed.","dt":"2024-06-19T06:46:49","s":["v5ilqqnebv"]}]},"12":{"40":[{"m":"Indeed, what a great day of rejoicing for them. The children of Israel had their king 👑 who also was God's man.\n\nThey knew this time their kingdom will be valiant and established.","dt":"2024-06-19T09:47:20","s":["633k5wzqtl"]}],"18":[{"m":"Interesting, David was a blessed man, and all who brought him peace themselves received peace ✌️.\n\nAnd thus it is with the man whom God has blessed.","dt":"2024-06-19T09:27:48","s":["nlzgf5dm3h"]},{"m":"What was the proof that it was the Spirit that came upon him for him to utter these words?\n\nWhat sign did they see to know this?","dt":"2024-06-19T09:30:02","s":["73z8u7teh8"]}]},"13":{"3":[{"m":"Seriously?\n\nDavid was indeed a man after God's heart.","dt":"2024-06-20T06:27:05","s":["kyx054m4jc"]}],"5":[{"m":"A good thing, a good thought 💭. Something his predecessor never did in his long 40 years of rulership.\n\nWho would have thought it was not going to end well?\n\nDespite a genuine attempt at pleasing the Lord 😌","dt":"2024-06-20T06:29:39","s":["vmuxziqjjr"]}],"11":[{"m":"So who mounted the ark of the Lord unto the cart?\n\nHow come those who carried the ark from its place unto the cart were not smitten?\n\nOr they held it by the poles as required by the law ⚖. It is safe to presume so.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:38:30","s":["r24j218soc"]}],"14":[{"m":"Strange — what was the process for deciding where the ark, which had just killed a man, should be kept?\n\nWho decided it should be in the home of Obed-edom?\n\nThey knew the ark causes death, and with that experience they dumped the ark. Yet when they got to know that the ark also blesses, they were willing to come for it and learn more about the ways of the ark.\n\nWhen they thought it kills, they were not willing — or at least we are not told — to learn how to stay safe in the service of the ark.\n\nBut now that they had heard of its blessings, they were willing once more to risk it.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:41:46","s":["gnnvh6wb8r"]}]},"14":{"14":[{"m":"He did not presume to know what God would do this time.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:49:26","s":["4b66twrkwm"]}],"8":[{"m":"Such is life, at his ordination and exaltation,\n\nan entire army gathered in unison to weaken greatly the reign of David, if not to completely destroy him.\n\nThey had not too long ago beheaded Saul and left the kingdom weak and divided.\n\nNow all Israel had united to ordain David king 👑.\n\nThis was not good news for their enemies... They, therefore, knowing what was at stake, consolidated their effort for a huge victory over Israel.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:47:09","s":["xc70mtnis5"]}],"10":[{"m":"It was good that David knew that the battle is not won with sword and spear, shield and buckler...\n\nBut won by the Lord.\n\nHe thus enquired in this seemingly impossible 🙅 battle, and twice the Lord came through.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:48:49","s":["ofwubolf5v"]}]},"15":{"15":[{"m":"Does that mean at the first they carried it with bare hands?\n\nIn that case why weren't the first bearers of the ark smitten?\n\nOr could it be that the sound of singing and mighty dancing 🎶 etc... stirred up the presence and power of God, such that under that atmosphere, anything or anyone near the ark ought to have been sanctified.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:53:41","s":["1bk7plflzu"]},{"m":"I perceived that in the times of ignorance and disorder God overlooked many things. As when the Philistines captured the ark — even then he struck them down...\n\nBut now that order was being restored under David, God frowned upon any disorder in his house, as in the case of Uzzah.\n\nMaybe also, pertaining to the ark itself, God held it sacred as before and nothing had changed.\n\nBecause even the ignorance of the Philistines was not excused. God allowed them to capture it without striking them down, only for them to take it to their territory, and it became a Trojan horse... Destroying their god and them.","dt":"2026-05-07T03:42:18","s":["58qxez2919"]}],"27":[{"m":"David had made himself a Levite.","dt":"2024-06-20T17:55:49","s":["ywuldg9idp"]},{"m":"He loved the Lord so much that as king he dressed as one of the servants of the Lord, as a Levite.\n\nThe Levites, though servants, were servants of a great and loving master who protected them from evil 😈 and harm.\n\nDavid was more than pleased; was he not the same person who exclaimed that he would prefer to be a doorkeeper in the house of the Lord...\n\nThis is actually what it says:\n\n\"I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.\" This verse is Psalm 84:10 (KJV).\n\nIt is a psalm of the sons of Korah, who were gatekeepers of the Lord.","dt":"2026-05-07T03:49:28","s":["f8oqj9pc72"]}]},"16":{"22":[{"m":"Ah, so this is the context of this super known and super popular verse.\n\nIt was in reference to the journeys of the patriarchs, particularly Jacob, as he moved from country to country...\n\nGod said unto the nations to not touch Jacob, his anointed, and do his prophet no harm.","dt":"2024-06-20T23:06:40","s":["zqoiokzd9u"]},{"m":"Wait oo... Was this verse not in reference to Abraham and Isaac, concerning Abimelech the king of Gerar, and concerning Pharaoh?\n\nHow come we have covered it for ourselves and done so wrongly against the children of our God?\n\nGenesis 20:7 KJV\nNow therefore restore the man his wife; for he is a prophet, and he shall pray for thee, and thou shalt live: and if thou restore her not, know thou that thou shalt surely die, thou, and all that are thine.","dt":"2026-05-07T03:59:44","s":["y88zicup74"]}],"38":[{"m":"I had rather be a porter in the house of the Lord than to dwell in the tabernacle of wickedness...\n\nI can imagine Obed-edom reciting these words of the psalm.","dt":"2024-06-20T23:15:22","s":["fagfjqcj6u"]}],"5":[{"m":"So Obed-edom will not leave the ark alone?\n\nHaha... He knew what he had profited by it.","dt":"2026-05-07T03:50:50","s":["uwsyhq5u6"]}],"24":[{"m":"So even in the Old Testament, evangelism was a thing.\n\nMany times in the Old Testament we see verses speaking of telling and showing the wondrous works of the Lord.\n\nOf course God's wondrous works by themselves were a powerful evangelist tool that converted individuals... As we see with Rahab the prostitute.\nAll of Jericho and Canaan had heard of the dividing of the Red Sea.\n\nJust like the Spirit of God bears witness of Christ through the working of miracles.","dt":"2024-06-20T23:12:33","s":["0ryj0kcl6c"]}]},"17":{"13":[{"m":"Oh Saul, Saul, he lost mercy with the Lord because of disobedience,\n\nDavid, on the other hand, gained mercy through obedience, such that it was promised him that even if his children are not as submitted to God as he is,\n\nGod will still have mercy upon his children and keep the throne on David forever.","dt":"2024-06-25T00:08:08","s":["pki4tv8dnr"]},{"m":"Lord, take not thy mercy from me, I pray 🙏","dt":"2026-05-13T09:13:48","s":["xr0w0f7cwl"]}],"10":[{"m":"The beginning, when he called Abraham, and their numerous sojourns from place to place, and even in the times of the judges, when different enemies ravaged them and caused them to move from place to place,\n\nravaging them and causing them to hide, just to have some respite from the enemies and to have some food to eat, as we see in the case of Gideon.","dt":"2024-06-25T00:05:36","s":["mpimncfnmf"]}],"27":[{"m":"Amen. And indeed so, whosoever the Lord blesses is blessed indeed.","dt":"2024-06-25T00:10:39","s":["dfon9tfm7p"]}]},"18":{"11":[{"m":"David knew he could carry none of these things to the grave.\n\nRather, he did the wise thing by dedicating it to the Lord, who had lifted him up from the dunghill and made him a king 👑","dt":"2024-06-27T06:39:25","s":["79rutkvk8x"]}],"4":[{"m":"Was this because of the commandment of the Lord not to multiply horses?","dt":"2026-05-14T06:59:49","s":["u61oz8ac5h"]}]},"19":{"6":[{"m":"This extra detail of a thousand talents of silver 🥈 being the price of hire for these mercenaries is not given in the book of Kings account 🏆","dt":"2024-06-27T11:29:47","s":["2njwk4zaji"]}],"7":[{"m":"I don't know what messaging was used for the king to convince his own soldiers to go to war, a needless war.\n\nMeanwhile he had taken a 1000 talents of silver 🥈 and caused men to leave their families for this war.\n\nI can imagine lies 🤥 and propaganda machine at work, to tell the people how much of a danger Israel and king David were to them.\n\nAnd how that intel 🧠 revealed that from Ammon, David was coming for them next.\n\nPolitics at its finest; sadly, many lives were lost in this war.","dt":"2024-06-27T11:33:12","s":["uxdskljnok"]}],"11":[{"m":"A nuclear family of great warriors.","dt":"2024-06-27T11:34:07","s":["gpl3zvjfc3"]}],"17":[{"m":"David was now involved in this battle, David the anointed of the Lord,\n\nDavid the mighty man of war, the man who never lost a war, the slayer of Goliath of Gath.\n\nDavid's name and fame had spread far and wide; I can imagine him riding his royal 👑 horse and entering the battle,\n\nword of his arrival traveling with the wind 🍃 in both camps.\n\nThe morale in the camp of the children of Israel was high, their commander Joab was bad enough, and now their king 👑 was come; the shouting and rejoicing and confidence went up higher.\n\nThe enemy panics, they are frantic but try not to show it, they heard that David was in the camp.\n\nThe fear 😱, the jitteriness of the armies, even the beasts and horses 🐴 could sense the fear 😱.\n\nKING DAVID WAS IN THE BATTLE","dt":"2024-06-27T11:45:32","s":["4lz4d7gkl1"]},{"m":"David the anointed was come into the battle, the presence of the Lord had come into the battle, the name of the Lord had come into the battle.\n\nThis was all that was needed. The weight of David in the battle. And it gave them victory.","dt":"2026-05-15T08:47:08","s":["h1q6zxsfhz"]}]},"20":{"3":[{"m":"Israel was getting rich through conquest and building through slavery.","dt":"2024-06-29T17:33:02","s":["799we9glrj"]}],"8":[{"m":"David started the pattern of giant killers, and it outlived his generation; now their sons were killing giants.\n\nImagine if David hadn't killed Goliath.\n\nThen they, Israel, would have a pattern of defeat and bullying at the hand 🖐️ of the giants.\n\nIt would have been terrible. Just imagine, for 40 days Goliath tormented Israel's army, forty long days, one full month and 10 days.\n\nThe war was halted because there was no worthy man to tackle the giant.\n\nHow many more days was this going to continue? Who knows, it might have continued till supplies ran out, or some fearful 😨 soldier volunteers and gets destroyed.\n\nThen now the children of God would be subject to their enemies.\n\nBut here we have the reverse happening and their children taking over the mantle.","dt":"2024-06-30T01:58:38","s":["cocy8vmmbp"]}]},"21":{"6":[{"m":"Why did Joab omit these two tribes?\n\nLevi I understand because of the priesthood, but why omit Benjamin?\nOr could it be that the Levites dwelt among the Benjamites?","dt":"2024-07-08T06:42:59","s":["811z7tyudl"]}],"13":[{"m":"Man was more wicked than God, and in this wise David chose right.","dt":"2024-07-08T06:45:02","s":["fcqliey8xk"]}],"20":[{"m":"What a scene... How did the angel 😇 look like?\n\nWas he like a man in the air, and or he shone with glory and radiance?","dt":"2024-07-08T06:47:13","s":["p1c6lw94tl"]}],"25":[{"m":"Dake's commentary discloses that the worth of money in gold was about 120,000 USD, which is a lot of money.\n\nThis goes to show the heart of Araunah in willingly offering to give such a valuable land to David to offer burnt offerings.\n\nI mean, he wanted to give this for free??","dt":"2024-07-08T06:53:29","s":["40kaklt1mt"]}]},"22":{"11":[{"m":"The Lord wanted one who had peace round about and had not shed blood to build his holy temple.\n\nO God, thrice holy, perfect in all your ways, even to the utmost bound of the everlasting city and temple. Even Solomon the builder had to be pure and free of bloodshed.\n\nThere was much blood crying at the hands of David for him to partake of the building, but even with that, David, the man after God's heart, prepared all the much needed materials.\n\nHe loved the Lord and wanted to partake anyhow, and he found a way.\n\nJust like Benaiah, if I am not mistaken, who loved to run and run errands; he had no message for the king, but he ran anyways. Though the message was for Cushi.","dt":"2026-05-28T08:24:38","s":["apveqdzweo"]}],"3":[{"m":"A very wise move by David.\n\nRecognizing that God showed all Israel abundant mercy on this land, he decided to build the temple there.\n\nKnowing very well what the place signified, i.e. a place of mercy.\n\nBy this David trusted that in the years to come, when Israel 🇮🇱 needed to obtain mercy, mercy would be made available.\n\nAnd Solomon prayed the same prayer in the dedication of the temple when it was finally done.","dt":"2024-07-08T06:57:02","s":["z25letpmlb"]}]},"25":{"3":[{"m":"Prophesy to give thanks and praise to God...? Interesting.","dt":"2022-05-25T11:34:46","s":["sqyntf5vt1"]}]},"26":{"5":[{"m":"Obed-edom had become quite a household name by this time ⌚.\n\nAnd here again it is recorded that the Lord blessed him.","dt":"2024-07-13T08:13:54","s":["c0oyvifku1"]},{"m":"Decades likely had passed at this time, and his household alone had grown to 62 mighty men — both numerically and in strength.\n\nFrom that one blessing of three months came a legacy.\n\nI used to wonder how three months could be enough to have a blessing so obvious it reaches the ears of the king.\n\nYes, it is possible if suddenly every member of your family, brother and all, with their wives, have all taken seed and birthed, say, boys.\n\nYour field suddenly has yielded much more fruits, way more than other fields of the same size and of previous years.\n\nEven if it wasn't harvest and it was just the beginning of the planting season, yet every seed you planted germinated and your field was mighty green.\n\nSickness and long-standing issues being resolved... lost relatives found, and so many possible miracles.\n\nLanding huge contracts, sales etc.\n\nGOD HAD INDEED BLESSED HIM AND CONTINUED TO DO SO, INCLUDING PLAYING A KEY ROLE IN THE TEMPLE — HE AND HIS SONS","dt":"2026-05-30T11:22:52","s":["alndrcqdoi"]}],"28":[{"m":"We see here that no one is all bad.\n\nJust that some decisions are more critical than others and leave longer lasting impact than others.\n\nWe see that even Saul, though rejected, had the heart to dedicate wealth and riches to the temple of the Lord, or better put, to the house of the Lord, because as at that time there was no temple of Solomon yet.\n\nEven Joab, though wicked and cruel, dedicated things to the temple...\n\nAnd had the presence of mind and knowledge of the ways of God to discourage David from counting the people.\n\nA decision David refused, which became a stain in his reign.","dt":"2024-07-13T09:34:24","s":["z8umwp19oa"]}]},"27":{"1":[{"m":"Such a large number — all this was to ensure excellence and order in all matters.","dt":"2024-07-13T11:13:41","s":["o6s79l2q4q"]},{"m":"There was much work to be done in the kingdom, as is the case in most kingdoms.\n\nGarrisons to be set up for stamping out rebellion,\n\nwatches of the night to prevent enemy attacks.\n\nScouts in the outskirts to prevent surprise attacks, errands and mercenaries etc etc.\n\nDavid himself was an outcast for many years and raided many towns and cities.\n\nHe knew what it took to topple cities and towns.\n\nSo he set up his kingdom strong 💪 based on his experiences.\n\nNot to mention the many wells and other developmental projects he needed to set up 👆","dt":"2024-07-14T01:09:53","s":["tnt2nj99bz"]}],"7":[{"m":"If Asahel was mentioned, then this system was set up at the early years of David's kingdom, when he ruled over Judah only.\n\nFor Asahel was killed later in a war between the two king 👑 doms.","dt":"2024-07-14T01:18:13","s":["3sf2t1fzcr"]},{"m":"Sons modelled their fathers — both were mighty warriors, father and son. Such pride to see your son step into your shoes.","dt":"2026-05-30T11:29:49","s":["nb5mqzb8ay"]}],"24":[{"m":"So the number of the counting was omitted because of the wrath of God against David ✡.\n\nI made a comment that despite the fact that it displeased the Lord, it was still added, but we have it clearly stated here that it was not added.","dt":"2024-07-14T01:24:57","s":["7dg2esd3jx"]},{"m":"Room was left for the divine by making the king uncertain of the total numbers and of his total strength of his people.\n\nThat uncertainty was the grace of God being made sufficient in weakness and uncertainty.\n\nThat is faith.","dt":"2026-05-30T11:33:51","s":["bfccf64157"]}]},"28":{"5":[{"m":"I made a comment to someone that Solomon was chosen by David, and likely that was the promise made to Bathsheba to entice her, but that was a wrong assertion.\n\nIt's stated more than once that he was the Lord's chosen one.","dt":"2024-07-14T01:34:34","s":["3orew9k58n"]}],"12":[{"m":"Though he was not permitted to build the house 🏡 of the Lord, yet he, being a spiritual man, had access to the designs and patterns of the temple 🏛.\n\nAnd this he gave to Solomon, a young prince 🤴 and heir, to follow.","dt":"2024-07-14T01:36:59","s":["wey6vw2854"]},{"m":"He had these by the Spirit, like the man Moses had the pattern of the Tabernacle on the mount.","dt":"2026-05-31T07:55:45","s":["7b3b25962d"]}],"19":[{"m":"So David received the pattern by the Spirit, though God knew very well that David was not to build, but his son was.","dt":"2022-05-27T02:17:44","s":["evb6rrgprq"]},{"m":"David had such a fond relationship with God. Even though he was king, he was also a prophet and priest.\n\nGod loved him, and indeed when he went back against the Lord, the Lord out of love chastised him back in shape.\n\nI accept your rebuke, oh my God, and your chastisement on me for my many foolishness.\n\nThank you Lord.","dt":"2026-05-31T07:59:33","s":["73b4ace372"]}]},"29":{"1":[{"m":"Again another confirmation that God chose Solomon.","dt":"2024-07-14T01:38:49","s":["cqdavmc1i2"]}],"16":[{"m":"David had built his kingdom a great and mighty one, not of his own accord, but with and by the hand of the LORD.\n\nThis is akin to the church today: God has, by the hand of his anointed men of God, built massive churches — likened to kingdoms literally.\n\nChrist Embassy, I am told, now has presidents and prime ministers like a kingdom or nation.\n\nThat was the case of David, but the sad thing was that not long after his death things began to fall apart.\n\nBut the foundation David had laid was so strong it lasted almost 500 years — 424 years according to Google.\n\nI see the church today in the same light — strong mighty churches as kingdoms have been built.\n\nMany, I believe, will stand for long, even though they will be plagued with many ills and almost ungodly rulers and leaders, and brief stints of very God-fearing leaders like their founders, who will bring revivals and restoration, until such a time as fools and sons of Belial destroy what was built.\n\nThis pattern will continue until the eventual overthrow of some churches, kingdoms, culminating in the coming of our Lord and Saviour.\n\nMany new kingdoms and churches will of course rise and be set up, some to replace the old, and the pattern and cycles continue unto the coming of Jesus Christ, as prophesied in the book of Revelation.\n\nUngodliness and wickedness beyond our wildest imaginations will plague the church.\n\nEven now we see the rot in the church and are perplexed. But there still is some fear of God in our midst.\n\nIt will get worse and worse, as prophesied by the early apostles.\n\n2nd Timothy 3\n\n1 But know this, that in the last days perilous times will come: 2 For men will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boasters, proud, blasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy, 3 unloving, unforgiving, slanderers, without self-control, brutal, despisers of good, 4 traitors, headstrong, haughty, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God, 5 having a form of godliness but denying its power. And from such people turn away!\n\n12 Yes, and all who desire to live godly in Christ Jesus will suffer persecution. 13 But evil men and impostors will grow worse and worse, deceiving and being deceived. 14 But you must continue in the things which you have learned and been assured of, knowing from whom you have learned them,","dt":"2026-05-31T08:21:23","s":["cc7ab55f05","48fstnx25f"]}],"23":[{"m":"What an honour, for your son to sit on your throne whiles you are yet alive.\n\nIt did not come easy, but it prospered, for before Solomon the older siblings had usurped the throne, but the ploy failed.","dt":"2026-05-31T08:50:38","s":["e20f743be5"]}],"26":[{"m":"David ✡, still the son of Jesse, David the shepherd boy 🧒.\n\nIn calling him David the son of Jesse rather than David the king 👑 of Israel 🇮🇱... our minds are drawn back to his humble beginning.\n\nThese ancient writers have such a perspective of time and history.","dt":"2022-05-27T02:24:49","s":["rbd4644ydq"]}]}},"2 Kings":{"1":{"6":[{"m":"It seemed the kings, being political and exposed to power and rulership, ended up consulting many gods. They became polytheists, even though the very God of the nation whom they governed for hated polytheism. Indeed, it was for this reason that he formed his own nation for Himself, yet — the error continues on — the kings and the people constantly sought other gods.","dt":"2026-07-12T05:44:10","s":["bb782p78jb"]}],"10":[{"m":"Wait oo... So Elijah could thus perform, and yet fled from Jezebel. I think after all the highs, he was just tired...\n\nTired of all this battle upon battle in attempting to restore Israel 🇮🇱 to the only true God.\n\nYet king after king 👑 continued to frustrate the efforts of God.","dt":"2022-07-02T12:18:52","s":["mq4rez0dh8"]}],"12":[{"m":"Are we serious? These men, the king, feared not God. I mean, to see the hand of God in this manner and still send another — such hard-heartedness — similar to what Pharaoh did.\n\nExposure to power has a way of doing many things to a man, to the degree that men have directly fought against God, knowing very well that he is God. And the same will happen in the end of time, when the Lord comes with his army from the heavens, yet men will rebel.","dt":"2026-07-12T05:46:55","s":["q6bclvp0ev"]}],"15":[{"m":"Wisdom has spoken, a wise captain indeed.","dt":"2022-07-02T12:12:45","s":["4conimhujg"]},{"m":"Why would the angel 😇 tell Elijah not to be afraid 😨?\n\nI mean, he had just burnt a 100 men, what was he afraid of 😨...\n\nIt seemed Elijah did not want to go face the king because he feared for his life, so the angel assured him all was going to be well with him.\n\nSo indeed you may see someone walking in power and strength 💪 but has fears.\n\nCourage and bold acts do not mean necessarily the absence of fear 😱.","dt":"2024-09-06T07:30:26","s":["j2xwrfy5pm"]}]},"2":{"16":[{"m":"Did they not believe their own prophecy?\n\nOr they knew he would be taken, but for how long they did not know.\n\nThis meant, as they themselves had suggested, Elijah and Elisha would be separated, but in their mind they knew man lives and dies on the earth 🌎, not in heaven, so this was perhaps some seasonal visitation. But in this wise they were wrong.\n\nElijah was going to be gone for a loooong time ⌚","dt":"2024-09-06T07:51:40","s":["dbax7irn6f"]}],"23":[{"m":"He was retracing his steps back to where they had started; he was literally walking 🚶 in the steps of Elijah.","dt":"2024-09-06T07:53:05","s":["cg8xejmzby"]}],"25":[{"m":"Okay, so he did not go back to Gilgal, though he had retraced his steps as far back as Bethel.","dt":"2024-09-06T07:54:39","s":["zeg4jvro0l"]}],"3":[{"m":"Elisha had done his work and was also in tune with the Lord, so when the others came to give him the word, he was prepared and ready.","dt":"2024-09-06T07:45:23","s":["4itgtj35cs"]}],"9":[{"m":"Such a powerful man, full of signs and wonders.\n\nIt's amazing he was a man who experienced fear 😱 like all men.\n\nIt's strange indeed, you would expect absolutely constant boldness from him all the time.","dt":"2024-09-06T07:47:45","s":["w49mxgwt15"]}]},"3":{"11":[{"m":"Jehoshaphat had this habit of enquiring of the Lord, even in times of difficulty or error, before he made any move.","dt":"2022-07-02T13:11:30","s":["3gsi7l4mtr"]},{"m":"For Jehoshaphat, everything was spiritual, and he enquired of the Lord often.\n\nHe was like David in this wise.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:01:47","s":["p5d7darhzr"]}],"13":[{"m":"His brother Ahaziah had sent to enquire of Baal in the times of Elijah... They were just pagans.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:02:47","s":["xygaml0mi1"]}],"14":[{"m":"This tells us right there the real relationship that Elisha had with the Lord. It was a similar greeting that Gabriel gave unto Zechariah.\n\nHmm 🤔. For a man to make the same claim that spirits make. Wow.","dt":"2022-07-02T13:14:22","s":["tp2rqie8gz"]}],"19":[{"m":"I see the divine hand of God at work against Moab.\n\nTheir cup was full, and God intended to destroy them, and here he is using the kings of Israel and Edom as his tools for that purpose.","dt":"2022-07-02T13:17:55","s":["qi8bpvfnvx"]}],"23":[{"m":"Why would they think such, except that they had also consulted with their gods, who had promised them victory ✌️?\n\nIndeed, this was not the first time in their history that armies who were confederates had destroyed each other before the enemy, and the enemy just came to loot the spoil.\n\nIsrael had experienced that many times.\n\nBut here Moab was deceived.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:09:03","s":["zsz7ofgr6c"]}],"18":[{"m":"It seems the Lord is vulnerable when men align to do his will and work for him.\n\nHe is just vulnerable. So here these kings, though some hated him, yet because they were aligned with what he, God, wanted to do anyways, and he needed men to do it, he helped them.\n\nJust as he had helped Ahab to overcome 32 kings.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:05:20","s":["9x6w1crvj6"]}],"21":[{"m":"I'm sure this would include men who had never been to battle.\n\nBut at this time all hands were needed.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:09:37","s":["4s21k6mmj6"]}],"26":[{"m":"They planned to cut the head of the snake 🐍 — to kill the king and hence scatter his people.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:10:39","s":["oz6ncnkyub"]}],"27":[{"m":"What exactly happened here... Great indignation as in what?","dt":"2022-07-04T11:05:39","s":["825bfzf7ns"]}]},"4":{"7":[{"m":"She was able to sell the oil and live. That means if someone had given her capital to have started this oil business, she would have been successful, though that would take longer, because she had to pay up the capital and live off the profit.\n\nBut no one was willing to give the poor widow a chance. What if she blows the money, or the creditor comes to seize her business and you lose your capital?\n\nBut God was faithful and gave her divine capital for free — God's stake was in her company now — how could she fail?\n\nIt seems when God gives something, he outsources it permanently, like the earth — he has given it to the children of men forever — as if he never had a stake in there.\n\nHe only required that it is governed according to his will, and his worship given him as offerings and tithes.\n\nObviously the woman was now able to even give her tithes and offerings according to the law.","dt":"2026-07-13T08:10:07","s":["owushp6i77"]}],"14":[{"m":"Why did she not request for a child for herself?\n\nMaybe she did not believe.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:13:18","s":["vxcnfyfzl1"]}],"17":[{"m":"A quick note though, Elijah and Elisha had no children? No record of such.","dt":"2026-07-13T08:12:43","s":["zbajaq2uni"]}],"23":[{"m":"When asked why, she said, nothing really, all is well.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:14:39","s":["05ue2xxiey"]}],"34":[{"m":"Why did the first instruction not work, meanwhile it was as potent and divine as the second???","dt":"2022-07-04T11:16:57","s":["31fv52ryu6"]}],"38":[{"m":"Finally we find Elisha in Gilgal... The first of four places he and his master Elijah journeyed to before his flight to heaven.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:21:09","s":["4q231i2hys"]}],"27":[{"m":"Not that he was not in tune to discern the voice of the Lord, but rather the Lord was quiet about it.\n\nMeaning it is the duty of the prophets to discern things before they happen.\n\nIf not, he has failed to live up to the expectation of his calling.\n\nExcept when the Lord hides it from him.\n\nBut it will be an abomination for the Lord to be looking to speak his word and will, yet no ear 👂 attentive enough to listen.","dt":"2024-09-06T08:17:34","s":["4oxazjniyj"]}],"33":[{"m":"Did not the same thing happen to the widow at Zarephath, and Elijah healed him?","dt":"2024-09-06T08:18:34","s":["xzs6jzqatx"]}]},"5":{"1":[{"m":"By him the Lord had given great deliverance unto Syria — but Syria were not the people of God, so what was God doing in their affairs?\n\nSo God is not just the God of Israel, but also the God of all flesh.","dt":"2026-07-14T09:08:25","s":["i1lp9dzm6f"]}],"5":[{"m":"Though a Syrian and a Gentile, estranged from Israel,\nbecause he had enough faith to believe, he qualified enough to be healed.","dt":"2024-09-07T06:35:02","s":["vxuict87xs"]}],"8":[{"m":"How did Elisha know? I guess because 1. the letter concerned him, and 2. he was politically connected, and 3. he was a prophet.\n\nGOD had probably spoken to him about it.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:19:47","s":["70bwbw8ep2"]},{"m":"The Lord seems to love such challenges,\n\nactions that seek to test if he indeed is God and if he is able to do all things... both great and small.","dt":"2024-09-07T06:37:12","s":["6sz73g74m1"]}],"9":[{"m":"I can imagine him dressed in his full regalia and pride as a commander, covering his leprosy with pride and colour, yet expecting to be healed, with the adamant and terrifying face of an army general.\n\nYet that was not going to impress the prophet nor God. He got humbled — he was asked to strip himself of his armour and go down into the water beneath ground level.\n\nThis was technically worse than prostrating. He went down and then came up cleaned and whole.","dt":"2026-07-14T09:14:47","s":["2emc4q0zpf"]}],"10":[{"m":"I can imagine Naaman, dressed to impress with his army and in his full military ⚔ might and regalia.\n\nThis was not what was needed, because all of his power and position and posturing did not and could not heal him.\n\nElisha was not impressed at all, neither was God, for after all Naaman had nothing that Elisha needed, but Elisha had all that Naaman needed.\n\nThe one to be humble and submit was Naaman, not Elisha and God.\n\nAnd Elisha did well to drum home that point — as to who was superior and in the upper tier. The real G.\n\nAnd many times we don't know how to take our stand and demonstrate that we are the real deal 🤝, but rather let others who are not run roughshod over us.\n\nWe think it humble to keep such a wrong posture and be subdued.","dt":"2024-09-07T06:43:40","s":["7polvlr4b4"]},{"m":"Elisha sent a servant, pure Gold 🥇 of a posture ⌚ for him, wow.\n\nThat was how low on the scale of importance Naaman was to Elisha.","dt":"2024-09-07T06:48:30","s":["0fbs6stvjb"]}],"13":[{"m":"Sometimes we need people who want our own good more than we do ourselves, and would bring perspective to us despite our pride.","dt":"2026-07-14T09:18:35","s":["wqjs6vn33c"]}],"14":[{"m":"We are not told the character or posture with which he dipped, but we can guess he was pretty reluctant and like grumbly and offended.\n\nBut he yet obeyed, and that is the most important thing. Obedience.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:21:30","s":["vwf467o0ye"]},{"m":"At which point did his flesh become clean?","dt":"2024-09-07T06:51:01","s":["omhgnz8ypc"]}],"16":[{"m":"Before whom I stand. This expression again.\n\nThis throws light into the kind of relationship Elisha had with God. He stands in God's presence, same relationship Gabriel spoke of.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:34:31","s":["5g7jeh6jvt"]},{"m":"Now Elisha was ready to meet him face to face, now that he had passed the test of humility and gotten healed.\n\nI guess this is the way God treats us sometimes, after we pass the needed tests of life he had given us.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:08:06","s":["qzbzvg2e7w"]}],"17":[{"m":"How was he going to use that as sacrifice?","dt":"2024-09-09T06:10:16","s":["8liz7ao1fn"]},{"m":"Naaman couldn't believe that he had gotten such a life-changing and a life-transforming miracle for free.\n\nIn fact, even Gehazi, Elisha's servant, couldn't believe it either.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:12:27","s":["sa555iilaf"]}],"22":[{"m":"Such a painful act by Gehazi, in destroying the pure generosity of the Lord. The healing was free, meaning forever Naaman would be indebted to the Lord.\n\nThe Lord's desire was to make the healing completely free, but now Gehazi had stained the whole thing with this gift, and it could not be undone. Even Naaman was more than glad to give.","dt":"2026-07-14T09:22:59","s":["qfhvtqi23m"]}],"27":[{"m":"Sad","dt":"2022-07-04T11:51:57","s":["3jnu4cqq58"]},{"m":"Did he not plead? Did he not beg? I'm sure he did, but to no avail, and being now a leper, he had to quickly leave the city to the outskirts.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:15:15","s":["pp06yhf5mu"]}]},"6":{"6":[{"m":"Elisha was such a man of signs and wonders.\n\nHe was like JESUS, to every situation, he had an answer.\n\nHe was a man of wonders.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:17:22","s":["0iacvwgj3g"]}],"8":[{"m":"Was this the same king of Syria whose servant Naaman had been healed?","dt":"2022-07-04T11:44:37","s":["k9yikjq9rt"]}],"9":[{"m":"Which king 👑 in particular was this?","dt":"2022-07-04T11:43:58","s":["qf10b56uuz"]}],"12":[{"m":"So what if the king had not sought counsel? I guess he would not have known, possibly due to palace protocol; the servants could not have approached the king uninvited, less so to offer counsel.\n\nThis is the power of systems and the need to really set them up right.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:47:11","s":["51sdpdr4w0"]}],"13":[{"m":"What is the logic of this instruction to spy out the prophet who was giving tips of the things the king said in secret? Did he not reckon that Elisha would definitely know and avoid him?\n\nInterestingly enough though, Elisha did not avoid him, and he actually caught up with him.","dt":"2026-07-15T10:00:20","s":["kzt6n06n5m"]}],"15":[{"m":"Was this his new servant after Gehazi the leper?","dt":"2022-07-04T11:48:13","s":["wwtixlbv56"]}],"20":[{"m":"With angels surrounding Elisha, that meant that even if the Syrian army had attacked, they would have found themselves dead, because they would be struck by all these angels in chariots of fire.\n\nOh, when are we going to have men and women like Elijah and Elisha in our days?","dt":"2024-09-09T06:22:24","s":["1ym95h75dn"]}],"21":[{"m":"Which king was this?","dt":"2024-09-09T06:23:02","s":["t5n8dvdu6u"]}],"24":[{"m":"It seems Ben Hadad was the name of all kings of Syria, just as Pharaoh is of Egypt.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:23:46","s":["vfisojnfh1"]}],"25":[{"m":"Oh Lord, have mercy. Anytime I read or hear matters related to famine, I sense we would be experiencing famine soon as a world.\n\nLord, have mercy and save us.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:50:48","s":["r1gtcbz3mj"]}],"27":[{"m":"Did Israel not have a strong standing army to fight? What was the condition of their heart, that they could not wait on the Lord for victory as Jehoshaphat did in his days?","dt":"2024-09-09T06:26:18","s":["d7g3evbpnm"]}],"17":[{"m":"Gehazi was out of the picture at this time; someone else was granted this vision. Gehazi's way and greed, was that possibly why he could not raise the boy from the dead when he placed the staff of Elisha on the boy as instructed?","dt":"2026-07-15T10:02:49","s":["22rissoo1u"]}],"29":[{"m":"God had forewarned them about this if they refused to serve him wholeheartedly, and now here they were.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:27:28","s":["056g0v571t"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"So it really got to the point where women ate their children for the word of the Lord to come — really?\n\nFor Elisha to endure up to this point, when earlier accomplishments of the Lord were almost instant and without delay, like the healing of Naaman.\n\nThis also goes to show that till the word of the Lord came, they did not make a move. He, Elisha, was in the famine, starving and hungry like everyone else, urging the people to wait for the word of the LORD.\n\nI can imagine the king of Israel had been to Elisha many times for him to do something, and Elisha's response might have been something like, \"The Lord has not spoken, we have to wait for the Lord to speak, without which I can do nothing.\"\n\nIt is just like when Balaam was asked to curse Israel and he said, I cannot go beyond what the Lord has spoken.\n\nIt is also akin to when the Shunammite woman came to Elisha and Elisha said, \"The Lord has hidden this from me.\" It also goes to show that as a prophet one has to be sharp always, not to miss the Lord when he is speaking.\n\nBut then when God is not speaking, no matter how sharp you are, you will hear nothing and have to wait on the Lord, lest you move in the flesh and nothing happens, or, like Moses, something happens in disobedience to the Lord, as in when he struck the rock and water gushed out.\n\nBut it seems there were times that the authority of the prophet or man of God comes to bear, as in when he commanded the bears to kill the little ones — but at that time we are not told if it was impulsively. But then even if it was his will, it was subject to what God had told him, because I don't think Elisha called the bear on the kids at his whim.\n\nIf so, why did he have to wait for the Lord to speak subsequently? Maybe he felt some power in him by which he knew that his words will not be empty. That must be it.\n\nIt is similar to when Elijah called down fire — it seemed it was at his will, but then again there was an angel of the Lord with him, who later told him to go with the 3rd captain and fear nothing.\n\nSo then it is always about the Lord and not about us, and we must learn to wait on the Lord always.","dt":"2026-07-15T10:34:52","s":["eyysdlc1um"]}],"4":[{"m":"It always takes an act of faith to serve the Lord and walk in the supernatural.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:31:37","s":["g0twlrg00l"]}],"5":[{"m":"Such serendipity, they took steps just when heaven was looking to bless someone.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:54:50","s":["akxdw3ewto"]}],"8":[{"m":"I used to wonder why soldiers would carry such valuables to war.\n\nBut mostly these are spoils from wars fought before the current one.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:56:00","s":["9ge1hplwnc"]},{"m":"These lepers suddenly became some of the richest men in town, and rightly so, as they had taken their lives into their hands and risked it.\n\nTherefore they got the greatest rewards.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:33:49","s":["rohl5qn6qn"]}],"9":[{"m":"These lepers became very rich, I believe. I can imagine their stories being told of the unlikely manner of how poor lepers became rich.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:56:34","s":["d3weh4z7xt"]}],"10":[{"m":"The porter, because they were not allowed into the city because of their condition.\n\nYet the same God who set the laws of separation used them to bless their entire city and generation.","dt":"2022-07-04T11:59:19","s":["5gdlxk84gw"]},{"m":"Not only did they get food, but horses and mules in abundance. What a loot, and rightly so, because they had suffered in the famine incredibly, and the Lord, when his word finally came, likely months later, compensated every wrong. And that will be my story, for the much missed opportunities and suffering at the hands of brutish men who claim to be of God.","dt":"2026-07-15T10:38:47","s":["souhh4z9ui"]}],"15":[{"m":"In times of famine, God will take care of his own through divine means.","dt":"2022-07-04T12:00:23","s":["3blzpeh7wd"]},{"m":"The garments that were cast away were slowing the fleeing army down. Some sought to save some of their provisions, but it seems, as the lepers drew near, it felt like their perceived army of Egypt and the Hittites were drawing closer and closer, and it was not worth the loot, which was slowing them down.","dt":"2026-07-15T10:44:57","s":["3u7bsf95o1"]}],"20":[{"m":"One man trying to regulate a hungry, famine-stricken mob.","dt":"2026-07-15T10:45:55","s":["owmldcw091"]}],"13":[{"m":"That was all that was left alive of an entire city — incredible. And I am sure they had to be kept alive and fed somehow in the midst of this famine. The Lord had mercy and saved the people of this evil judgement.\n\nIt seems to suggest also that when we fast, we in a way pronounce judgement on ourselves and seek the mercies of the Lord. Maybe that is why it is sometimes referred to as afflicting oneself or humbling oneself. And in such a state the Lord watches with pity upon us and shows his grace.","dt":"2026-07-15T10:42:57","s":["epu5rauo8p"]}]},"8":{"7":[{"m":"When did Elisha gain this title as the man of God, especially among the heathen?\n\nI will run a search on that one.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:37:53","s":["nn2j3f5h5i"]}],"11":[{"m":"Elisha had read into the future and knew that Ben Hadad would have recovered if not for the wickedness of his own right-hand man.\n\nI suspect Hazael had long had it in heart to kill the king and become king.\n\nRight after this word, which gave him assurance of success, he went in and carried out his desires.","dt":"2024-09-09T06:41:37","s":["ve3bdgvrb"]}],"28":[{"m":"Hazael had prophecy 🥠 and the spirits backing him; he could not be destroyed naturally, for there were other factors ensuring his success.","dt":"2022-07-04T12:06:08","s":["cv9a0lv59x"]}]},"9":{"13":[{"m":"At the word of the Lord, the response of the people is quick.\nThey knew that once the Lord had spoken, it was a done deal, so they hastened to perform it.\n\nAnd this was a word from none other than Elisha the man of God. He was no mean prophet.\n\nIs that our response these days to the word?","dt":"2024-09-09T07:09:01","s":["9uchfu5yer"]}],"29":[{"m":"Ahaziah of Judah was Ahab’s grandson through his mother, Athaliah (Jezebel's daughter). From Google.\n\nSo Ahaziah being here at this time was literally visiting his grandmother as well.\n\nJust imagine how this witch of a queen, a Phoenician woman, had managed not just to be princess of her home in Tyre, but also rule as queen in Israel, and extend her claws to Judah, thus ruling over the divided kingdom as one woman.\n\nNo king of either nation has managed to have such rulership and influence after the kingdom divided, but this witch, through her whoredoms, had gained powers and influence beyond imagination.\n\nShe was a powerhouse and master of the game of thrones, until the owner of the universe, God, played his last bit of the chess move.\n\nIs it not interesting that as all this was going on, Elijah and Elisha, as powerful as they were, lived under the influence of such wickedness and were not able to stop it until now?\n\nThis begs the question, what can God do and not do? God had to play the game along as well, until he made his move at this time. Why did he not just kill them?\n\nMany factors — maybe he had to give room for repentance, change, the will of man. Man also has a say in how this world is run. God comes in when invited, and he was invited into Israel via Abraham, and so he is revealed to the world through Israel.\n\nThe Gentiles have not a strong stake in God like Israel does, though the wisdom of God through Christ ensured now he has a strong stake everywhere.\n\nThis needs more study — what can God do and not do in the earth.","dt":"2026-07-16T09:35:16","s":["xlual9gcd1"]}],"1":[{"m":"Was this not why Elijah anointed Elisha? And the timing was just perfect: the king of Judah, the grandson of Ahab, and the king of Israel were gathered together at one place.\n\nThe perfect duo at one location for the perfect assassination, and immediately the word of the Lord went out against them both.","dt":"2026-07-16T07:41:27","s":["w3j2rtbaxj"]}]},"10":{"7":[{"m":"Innocently they walked in the city 🚶 of Jezreel, yet their death ☠ warrant had just been issued.\n\nMany times things happen in the corridors of power, and the ordinary people know not what it is until their death ☠...\n\nUntil they are suddenly caught unawares.","dt":"2022-07-04T12:14:18","s":["tsgaw0bnsl"]}],"11":[{"m":"Oh OK 🙂 so when it was prophesied that his house will be cut off, it meant everyone in it or associated closely 🔐, not just his blood family members.","dt":"2022-07-04T12:15:40","s":["lg700n5oer"]},{"m":"I wondered how the people could be so wicked to not even put up a fight, but slaughtered seventy sons of Ahab. The throne and the corridors of power is a dangerous place, and blood flows so easily.\n\nThey killed all the house of Ahab, their master, to save their lives, and they lost it at the end of the day. They were in their master's house for their interests, and of course wicked begets wicked, so they, being wicked like Ahab, were in it all for themselves.\n\nThe game of thrones everywhere is a deadly game.\n\nLook at when Christ came with his kingdom. HE died. The Divine died. When his disciples attempted to continue his legacy, their blood flowed freely.\n\nAnd fast forward, we seem now at ease, but the game continues. It is still as dangerous as before, and we need not be naive in these times that things seem at ease. There are all manner of agendas and games ongoing, and we must be on the lookout.\n\nThe enemy, the devil, our adversary, has infiltrated our ranks.\n\nThe kingdom is not just in righteousness and doing away with sin; it is a militant force. Brutish, and many will die on both sides when our kingdom is finally established. We must know that.","dt":"2026-07-16T10:57:18","s":["amg68a59su"]}],"15":[{"m":"Is this of the righteous descendants of the Rechabites?","dt":"2022-07-04T12:17:20","s":["jybg92qygf"]}],"16":[{"m":"Words were held in honour in those days. Just by words Jehu held Jehonadab in honour.","dt":"2024-09-09T07:17:05","s":["z5qqpgy9lf"]}],"30":[{"m":"GOD IS A REWARDER, WHEN WE PLEASE HIM 😌 HE REWARDS US GREATLY.\n\nTO HAVE 4 GENERATIONS GUARANTEED YOU. WOW...\n\nI WILL WORSHIP 🛐 YOU FOREVER AND SERVE AT YOUR FEET IN THE HOUSE OF THE LORD 🏡","dt":"2022-07-04T12:20:23","s":["gany3u4ne2"]}],"5":[{"m":"Elders over the city were like governors or senators of today — they seem to have some sort of independence and autonomy. And of course this was a coup, so they had the prerogative to fight back.\n\nA similar occurrence happened in the times of David, when a rebel went to hide in one city and Joab called for the head of the rebel.\n\n2 Samuel 20","dt":"2026-07-16T10:19:24","s":["ifghl2s4te"]}]},"12":{"18":[{"m":"Ah, how sad. Why did he not read the history of his fathers, to know that this was a fine opportunity to strengthen his kingdom and make a name for himself by fighting the LORD'S WAR?\n\nThis was not the first time the kings of Syria had attacked Israel.\n\nEven Ahab, the wicked king, got favour from the Lord for aligning with the will of the Lord.\n\nJehoash should have fought in this battle.\n\nLORD, help us to know your will and grant us the boldness to do it, in Jesus' name.","dt":"2024-09-10T06:52:42","s":["dd0q52w648"]}]},"13":{"19":[{"m":"But why was he not told to strike it more?\n\nIt seemed a prophetic window was opened, and once it was passed, it was passed.\n\nHe may have to wait long for another opportunity, and this time he will be ready.","dt":"2024-09-10T07:01:56","s":["0duxeijbo1"]}],"25":[{"m":"It seemed that sometimes the sons are not able to maintain the victory of their fathers. Here, though it was prophesied that Joash would have victory over Syria, it was not until the death of Hazael that he had victory over his son.","dt":"2026-07-16T22:17:28","s":["h48fwi5odg"]}]},"14":{"6":[{"m":"This was the law of God, yet for certain wickedness, like that of Ahab, he slew all children and all of the house of Ahab. But in a sense these died for their own sins, because they continued on in the sins of their father Ahab, so there is justification in there.\n\nI don't think the Lord will kill righteous sons for the sins of their fathers, no matter how grave the sin was, if the sons were righteous.\n\nThat would be against his nature.","dt":"2026-07-16T22:24:43","s":["0tcn3jzld6"]}],"19":[{"m":"Maybe because of the foolish war he fought with Israel, he lost favour with the people.","dt":"2024-09-10T07:09:09","s":["qnromiods"]}],"27":[{"m":"Because of his covenants, the Lord helped Israel, though their kings were rebellious.","dt":"2024-09-10T07:11:04","s":["umm81hotzu"]}],"12":[{"m":"I think the anointing with which Elisha had anointed Joash was strongly upon him and caused him to win these wars.","dt":"2024-09-10T07:07:49","s":["ji5wjuit85"]}]},"15":{"18":[{"m":"The sin of Jeroboam was very systemic. It never went away and became a snare which lured everyone who came on the throne.\n\nVery few could resist.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:00:27","s":["26ltlydib5"]}],"19":[{"m":"Money answereth all things, and it turned his enemy to be his friend.","dt":"2024-09-11T06:59:27","s":["90yubpaxom"]}]},"17":{"9":[{"m":"How could one turn from the Lord after seeing all the good benefits the Lord brought them?\n\nLogically this does not make sense. And especially reading the history of their kings, and seeing the patterns of obedience and disobedience yielding good and evil 😈 respectively.\n\nIt does not add up, yet Israel 🇮🇱 did evil before the Lord.\n\nThe conclusion I make from this is that evil is very deceptive and subtle; before you know it, you end up ensnared by it.\n\nThis is why we are admonished to be wary and flee from it.\n\nGod told them not to intermarry with them, because they will influence them to do evil 😈, and not the other way around.\n\nLet's be careful as we stand, lest we fall.","dt":"2024-09-17T06:48:05","s":["8qnz3bqznf"]}],"11":[{"m":"Why did God allow all this, and such decadence, to get to this level, until his own people were carried captive?\n\nI believe one of the reasons was to show that all men are prone to sin and the worst of atrocities against God and men.\n\nWho would have thought that Israel would have gone so low, if not that the Lord left them to their ways, to their own detriment?\n\nBut he kept a remnant for himself. However, the point was made... There is none righteous, and men, if left to themselves, would self-destruct and reject God, unless the Lord himself intervenes. And he did, in sending a savior, his man, to redeem men from self-bondage and sin.","dt":"2026-07-25T09:58:19","s":["88ekjxqfna"]}],"26":[{"m":"How did they come about this knowledge? Was it their own prophets and heathen priests who deciphered this from the realm of spirits?\n\nWhich thing God hid not from their priests, because he wanted them to know it was he, the Almighty God, that punished them.\n\nIt is similar to when the Philistines captured the ark of the children of Israel and got punished accordingly, until they sought to appease the LORD and were pardoned after much suffering.","dt":"2026-07-25T10:29:14","s":["1gpozajrrb"]}],"33":[{"m":"Strange 😞 yet interesting. This sounds so much like African traditional religion of today.\n\nWe fear 😱 God but serve him through smaller gods.\n\nThis again is the state of the church.\n\nChristians serve God but have smaller gods, be it idols or habits, patterns etc., they don't want to give up.","dt":"2022-07-15T06:55:57","s":["b9cu8csjq5"]},{"m":"Is this not like African traditional religion and other religions?\n\nThey fear and recognize the Lord, but still serve their gods in addition ➕ to fearing the Lord 😱.\n\nWhile we Christians are monotheists, and fear and serve the one and only true God &\nnot recognizing the others, for they are no gods but devils and the work of men's hands.","dt":"2024-09-17T06:53:06","s":["dykwhsu94j"]}],"41":[{"m":"Strange 😞 times, even up to this day. How did we get here?\n\nThese people served their own gods, and then the Lord punished them for serving idols in his land.\n\nSo they learnt the ways of God and resorted to God worship 🛐.\n\nBut they did not stop at that. They resorted to God worship in addition to their other gods.\n\nThey saw Yahweh as one of the gods. They called him the god of the Israelites.\n\nIn their deception 😞 they combined gods and continued this practice from generation to generation. Hmm","dt":"2022-07-15T06:57:21","s":["sppdgxuxon"]},{"m":"At least the good in all of this is that they recognized the Lord as supreme, the supreme creator of all; at the least they knew he was the most high and the most powerful one.","dt":"2024-09-17T07:00:39","s":["55dn04asch"]},{"m":"African traditional religion... we believe in the supreme being and access to Him via the smaller gods.","dt":"2026-07-25T10:41:52","s":["18ss9i74q2"]}],"2":[{"m":"So the evils of Israel were classified and graded.\n\nHe did evil 😈, but not as bad as his predecessors.\n\nIs that not the state of our leaders here in Africa 🌍?\n\nEven the seeming good ones are those who do not corrupt themselves so much 🙏 as the others.","dt":"2024-09-17T06:42:59","s":["gvq27t3yl1"]}],"36":[{"m":"After such a mighty display of power, God's expectation was that they would serve him and him only.\n\nAfter all, he had demonstrated outright victory over all the so-called powerful gods.\n\nYet strangely enough the people, his own people, lusted after strange gods, the very gods who had just been defeated.\n\nWhat manner of foolishness is that?\n\nThen the Lord introduces his ultimate strategy, for all these issues of man are a heart problem. Hence sending Jesus into our hearts 💕.","dt":"2024-09-17T06:59:18","s":["mxx4rutu9s"]}]},"18":{"16":[{"m":"Oh I thought the lord was with Hezekiah - how come he had to give in at this time?\n\nMaybe the pressure was too great - but in time past others did same and God was not pleased with them.\n\nOr maybe he did wait on the lord and he got no answer, so he went ahead to do the needful and last resort of appeasing the king of Assyria.","dt":"2024-09-19T08:02:40","s":["0nskv1la5o"]}],"33":[{"m":"It seemed here that Hezekiah was appeasing the king of Assyria with gifts of gold, as seen in verse 16, to buy time as he continued to wait on the salvation of the Lord.\n\nUltimately Assyria wanted to take Israel completely captive and carry them to a new place and location.\n\nHezekiah's trust was in the Lord, and even his enemies knew it.\n\nO Lord, come quickly for them who trust in you, and help them.","dt":"2024-09-19T08:08:09","s":["0hp3kk9jiw"]}],"26":[{"m":"Syria 🇸🇾 was the dominant nation in those days; having colonized many, their languages thrived.","dt":"2022-07-19T07:46:13","s":["nx631pugct"]},{"m":"So at this time Syria 🇸🇾 was the prominent nation whose language most did speak.\n\nThey were the conquerors of the time.","dt":"2024-09-19T08:04:19","s":["1go0v9atvx"]}]},"19":{"25":[{"m":"God had pre-planned all this. And he wanted the Assyrian king to not assume that it was by his own power.\n\nGod Almighty had pre-ordained it to be so; he, Sennacherib, was just walking in it.\n\nCould it be that your life is a fulfillment of what has been pre-ordained?\n\nYet of course 🏇... In the volume of the book it is written... says the scriptures.\n\nHe says the very hairs on our head are all numbered.\n\nHe, God, knows our flaws, our faults and our frame.\n\nEven in temptation it is measured.\n\nWhy then are you thinking you are all alone? Your situation is unique to you, and truly so, but not unique to heaven.\n\nI remember a quote I saw online, advising doctors that what may be common to you, because you've seen such cases many times, may be the patient's first and most scary part of his life experiences.","dt":"2022-07-28T08:15:35","s":["umayzq039l"]}],"28":[{"m":"As we remember that our goings are before the Lord, so also are the goings of the enemy.\n\nSometimes evil may happen to us unbeknownst to us, but not to God. That is why we have to come to God in prayer.\n\nIt is only a matter of time; he will put a hook literally in the nose of the enemy, because he knows the goings of the enemy as well.\n\nContextually, the enemy was having a field day, not just because of the ordination of God,\n\nbut because Israel had strayed out of his protection.\n\nIt's important therefore that as we walk this life, we walk with God.","dt":"2022-07-28T08:19:37","s":["do7gbujilh"]}],"29":[{"m":"Wow, what a sign and wonder. For two whole years the curse on the earth 🌎 was lifted.\n\nThey were to eat what grew of itself naturally, and it was not weeds and thorns, but food, grapes, vine.\n\nOnly in the third year were they to sow and reap. The heavens have spoken.","dt":"2022-07-28T08:33:27","s":["o6cz2ehj49"]}]},"20":{"11":[{"m":"Wow, how did he cry to the Lord? Is it that he issued out a cry, like literally crying to the Lord, or is it that he prayed fervently to the Lord?\n\nEither ways, this begs my second question: why did he have to cry to the Lord? Was it not the Lord who sent him? So why did he have to pray again for God to give a sign that he will answer his own words and be true to his own words?\n\nYou know, prayer is hard and can be hard, especially when you have to tarry until the word of the Lord is established.\n\nSo why did Isaiah have to go through the labour of intense prayer, when it was God who sent him in the first place and he orchestrated this whole thing?\n\nThis reminds me of the case of Elijah. He was sent by God to declare the sound of abundance of rain, and yet he had to go through seven agonising levels of prayer — the apostle James describes them as effectual, fervent and heartfelt prayer — in order for the rain to manifest.\n\nThat is the burden the Lord places on his sent ones.\n\nSame thing with Moses, many times he had to pray, and sometimes he spent days praying — including 40 days of fasting, three times in 40 years, with no food and water. Some of these fastings were like days or at best weeks apart. Imagine fasting 40 days and descending from the mountain of the Lord, only to see Israel commit idolatry, and now have to go back up the mountain to plead with the Lord another 40 days.\n\nMeanwhile, he did not call himself; it was the Lord who called him in the first place.","dt":"2026-08-09T07:23:20","s":["kq3td8rjlu"]}]},"21":{"9":[{"m":"God is the creator of the universe. He brings down 👇 one nation and lifts up the other.\n\nHe routed out the Canaanites because of their evil ways and brought in 🇮🇱 Israel.\n\nNow Israel 🇮🇱, though having a covenant, was also replaced because of evil 😈 — though a remnant was left them.\n\nThis is a call to the nations of the world 🗺. God, who is no respecter of persons, will punish sin and judge wrongdoing.\n\nIt is therefore our responsibility, whiles there is time, to tell the world the truth of the gospel...\n\nWe must speak the truth and watch our lives and doctrine closely.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:24:34","s":["w8a2aobfpf"]}],"11":[{"m":"Manasseh was the longest reigning king of Judah.\n\nWhy God did not cut him off, and caused him to live so long, makes me think 🤔. Could it not be a deliberate act to cut the nation off into exile and begin something new with a remnant?\n\nWhy should Manasseh even thrive for so long?","dt":"2024-10-06T14:50:53","s":["2sjnfk7piq"]}],"23":[{"m":"Manasseh escaped such fate, but this abomination in the land had to end.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:27:09","s":["helgcazzet"]},{"m":"Manasseh escaped this fate. He should have died to curtail his abominations, such wickedness, and he was the long-reigning king of Judah. It hurts me that God allowed him to have such a record for such a long time.\nI think in the Chronicles account he repented somehow later, but it was all too little and insignificant and too late.","dt":"2026-08-09T07:58:32","s":["wlerln18qw"]}],"5":[{"m":"And the Lord watched on as the two courts of his house were desecrated; meanwhile HE had killed people for less.\n\nIt seemed God was just allowing all this because he was bent on destroying the people. Their sins had reached a peak that would merit almost total annihilation, leaving a remnant. He had given them more than enough time and chances to repent.\n\nNeedless to say, the program of the law was failing and had to be brought to an end, to introduce a much better program. These were the last days of the law and the Old Testament, the beginning of the end.\n\nSoon enough the New Testament was to be introduced — soon, though, meant another several centuries.","dt":"2026-08-09T07:53:05","s":["dxjzlmw39l"]}]},"22":{"8":[{"m":"In the fifty years of Manasseh, the nation had so deteriorated that they were not even reading the law of the Lord.\n\nIndeed, the house of the Lord was filled with pagan priests and idols.\n\nSuch a sad state of God's nation.","dt":"2024-10-08T09:24:13","s":["cgsb64hgde"]},{"m":"Wait, so all this while, what was guiding their worship? Was it the traditions passed on orally or from memory? Obviously whatever was informing their worship of God without the book was flawed, because we see in later verses that after reading the book of the law they were found greatly wanting.\n\nThey had been in great error the whole time. Indeed, the book prophesied exactly what will happen to those found in error of the law, and that is exactly what happened to them, and so they repented.\n\nBut this is so much like Christianity today. What started often as personal revelations of churches and their leaders soon became a doctrine that plagues the church and drifts them massively away from the truth of the book.\n\nAnd we see it so now in our churches; we have drifted from the faith so far behind, it is terrible.\n\nIf the people of Israel, who had the traditions and systems, needed to go back to the book, then even so we need to go back to the book more than ever before, we who were engrafted into this whole new divine life.\n\nWe must follow the pattern set for us.","dt":"2026-08-10T08:34:15","s":["jdbwyq5wf9"]}],"11":[{"m":"This shows how in touch Josiah was with the things of God. He, upon hearing the law, knew how bad their situation was.\n\nHe knew they were under the wrath of God without even knowing. He at this stage rent his clothes.","dt":"2024-10-08T09:26:22","s":["l7uxkk3e38"]}]},"23":{"3":[{"m":"By cutting covenants with the Lord, he was setting himself up to be helped greatly. His covenant was not mere empty words; Josiah stuck to his words and did well for his people and his reign.","dt":"2024-10-08T09:46:14","s":["zze18z0zxd"]}],"11":[{"m":"All these had become an abomination and a reproach to Israel.\n\nNow I ask, the pagan nations that practiced these things, did these things become a reproach to them, since God was not their God?\n\nDid it matter to God?\n\nYes, it did, as we see in the many times God used Israel to destroy other nations and their evil practices.\n\nAnd when Israel itself went into apostasy, the Lord used the other nations against them.\n\nSo in all lands all over the world, when the fulness of the wrath of God comes, he destroys those nations from under the earth.\n\nSo now I ask, how about nations outside the Middle East Palestine area?\n\nWe do not have written records of these, but I believe God, being God, did this same thing all over the world.\n\nWhen the sins of the people reached its peak (sometimes it takes centuries), the Lord will finally bring an end to their whoredoms and wickedness.\n\nSadly, all who worshipped demons always have practices inimical to human life and benefit.\n\nIt seems only the worship of Jehovah preserved life and advanced humanity in all aspects.\n\nI am yet to study other religions to see if there are any that bring out the best in man in all aspects.\n\nBut the point remains, God is God over all lands and punishes and rewards accordingly.\n\nIndeed, come to think of it, even where God does not directly intervene, the natural laws of good governance determine if a nation prospers or deteriorates.\n\nGod has already set the laws in motion to ensure cause and effects. So we determine what happens to us in the long run by our actions or inactions.","dt":"2024-10-08T09:55:31","s":["ygjh6e510l"]}],"13":[{"m":"The legacy of even Solomon in his sins lived on. After all these years, they had not completely rid the nation of ancient evil altars.\n\nNo wonder Paul in his epistles encourages us to pray for leaders of nations.","dt":"2022-08-05T10:57:35","s":["wvx3melzmj"]}],"15":[{"m":"After all these centuries, nobody had broken down this altar of abomination, of Jeroboam? Maybe it was waiting to fulfill the prophecy spoken by the Lord concerning it.\n\nAnd God watched over an over-500-year prophecy to fulfill it, yet today we have prophets whose words don't even last for a week and it gets debunked on the spot.\n\nThey are no prophets, just charlatans.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:04:37","s":["olu8jugatd"]}],"19":[{"m":"This was outside Judah territory, unless Judah had taken back some land of Israel, or the strength of Judah permitted them to do as they pleased since they were the dominant force.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:19:20","s":["2u5lef3u44"]}],"24":[{"m":"The political power of the day easily overpowered the wizards 🧙‍♂️ and witches 🧙‍♀️ of the time and ended their craft.\n\nYet I am sure if it had come to using spiritual power, like what we do in our days where we kill witches in prayers, it would take a lifetime.\n\nSometimes I wonder, all the witches we kill in prayer... How come they all don't die 🎲 and we keep having to kill them?\n\nSomething does not add up.","dt":"2022-08-05T11:03:06","s":["qy1s7d0dl8"]}],"26":[{"m":"Maybe this was why God permitted Josiah to lose this war; Judah's time was up, there was no more extension of days.\n\nIt was time for Judah also to go. The death of Josiah this way must have been more an act of mercy than vengeance on him for the sins of Israel.\n\nGod saved him from being the one in whose time Judah went into captivity.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:28:10","s":["9sjxcptrg9"]}],"27":[{"m":"Nothing could reverse it; it was the ordination of the Lord and it was established. At best it could be deferred in the era of the righteous ruler, but it was bent on happening, and so it did.\n\nSomething peculiar: that because Josiah did well and walked uprightly as the ruler of the people, his nation was spared the punishment in his time.\n\nHowever, after he died the punishment was unleashed, and here is the unique catch: there were other righteous people and rulers, but so long as the king, the one who carried the great power of the nation, was evil, justice could not be tempered or deferred with mercy,\n\nso we see great men and prophets like Daniel and the three Hebrew boys taken to captivity, as righteous as they were.\n\nWhy? Because the sin of the people was great and the rulers were wicked, so the presence of the righteous, even among the royals and in the corridors of power, could not sway the judgement of the LORD.","dt":"2026-08-10T09:17:26","s":["t3ki4cug93"]}],"29":[{"m":"Why did the Lord not save him, and why did he go into this battle in the first place?\n\nA man with such a strong testimony to be killed this way is not good.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:17:50","s":["krprhrm688"]}],"7":[{"m":"Really, such rot in the house of God. Even sodomites and idolaters affiliated with the house of God.","dt":"2022-08-05T10:55:25","s":["cajm8mx3hr"]}],"16":[{"m":"As he turned, he knew not that there was a divine hand of providence, centuries waiting for this moment, to ensure that every word spoken was going to be fulfilled.\n\nJosiah was anointed for this purpose. He was fulfilling and being helped greatly to do this work of God. And God helped him indeed.\n\nOh, I can imagine the presence and power of God in that place at that time, moving to ensure that every prophetic word spoken all those centuries ago to Jeroboam and penned out will be fulfilled without fail, for God's word never fails and never returns to Him empty.\n\nAs I pen down these thoughts, I am seeing a picture of the book of the law being brought to Josiah, as well as the Chronicles of the kings, and he reading about the prophecy of Jeroboam concerning his very life.\n\nThat one shall arise as him and shall do the Lord's work.\n\nI see Josiah rising up in humility and marching on to do the Lord's work as written about him.\n\nOh, in the volume of the books it is written of me, I have come to do thy will, O God.\n\nPsalms 40:7-9 KJV\nThen said I, Lo, I come: In the volume of the book it is written of me, I delight to do thy will, O my God: Yea, thy law is within my heart. I have preached righteousness in the great congregation: Lo, I have not refrained my lips, O LORD, thou knowest.","dt":"2024-10-08T10:11:51","s":["1b5hdjxmkb"]}]},"24":{"10":[{"m":"Is God and this walk with 🚶 with God this predictable?\n\nAs soon as a king 👑 pleased 😌 the Lord, his kingdom prospered, and as soon as he did otherwise, he suffered, under covenant Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nThis I believe works at the individual level.\n\nAs newborn babies 🤱, if we focus and determine to walk with God, he will doubtless bless us 🙏...\n\nI will put this to the test. I have actually, and I've seen the results.","dt":"2022-08-18T08:12:43","s":["yza1ojtzd5"]}],"20":[{"m":"What may be the possible 🙆 cause of his rebellion... Likely demands from the king 👑 Nebuchadnezzar, like yearly levies etc.","dt":"2022-08-18T08:14:45","s":["kya185cwbs"]}],"16":[{"m":"Wow, taken captive to live as royals or as peasants and commoners.\n\nWe have a bit of an idea what Nebuchadnezzar did to the royals based on the story of Daniel.\n\nLikely the less dangerous and valuable ones were roped into the service of the kingdom like Daniel, or sent off to the quarries to rot if found unworthy.","dt":"2026-08-26T08:25:01.573Z","s":["dwfetxnvm"]}],"4":[{"m":"Wow, not all sins are pardonable by GOD — forgiven but not pardoned from repercussions.\n\nJust as we saw in this exact instance, Manasseh was forgiven and even restored when he repented, but he was not pardoned.\n\nThe punishment for his sin wreaked havoc through the last decades, later after him.","dt":"2026-08-26T08:19:32.960Z","s":["we5l9wk9n9"]}],"8":[{"m":"You know, I wondered how in just three months it could be said that he did that which was wrong in the eyes of the Lord. I felt 3 months was too short a time.\n\nBut the truth is the time of the judgement of GOD has come and there was no more room for wickedness. I am sure if he was righteous as some of the other kings, GOD might have given him more time, or might have sent his prophets to him to make a league with Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon.\n\nBut that was not to be.","dt":"2026-08-27T08:35:57.151Z","s":["tt88ckcy9n"]}]},"25":{"7":[{"m":"There is something about rebellion towards God that brings foolishness to our hearts 💕 and lands us in trouble.\n\nIt is obvious not just in retrospect, but with the knowledge of the Lord's will through prophets like Jeremiah, that rebellion against Nebuchadnezzar was rebellion against God.\n\nIt was so obvious, but this king did not fear the Lord, so obviously he would not heed, even to his own death ☠.\n\nOh Lord, exempt us from the consequences of the reign of foolish kings 👑.","dt":"2022-08-18T08:17:57","s":["tp1kvn45lw"]}],"21":[{"m":"The chief priests and religious leaders were killed, so there was no one to inspire hope and possible rebellion.\n\nIn the same way, the sons of the king Zedekiah were killed before his own eyes 👀, so there was no hope of succession in his heart ♥.\n\nHis hopes were permanently dashed.","dt":"2024-10-25T09:41:47","s":["wjg9ahxs81"]},{"m":"Every important and influential person was taken away. The keepers of the temple and religious worship of Israel were slain. Every hope of Israel and everything that made them great was taken away.\n\nNeedless to say, some of the priests were themselves idol worshippers, so they were not necessarily the custodians of GOD.\n\n2 Chronicles 36:14 KJV\nMoreover all the chief of the priests, and the people, transgressed very much after all the abominations of the heathen; and polluted the house of the LORD which he had hallowed in Jerusalem.\n\nEzekiel 8:16 NIV\nHe then brought me into the inner court of the house of the Lord, and there at the entrance to the temple, between the portico and the altar, were about twenty-five men. With their backs toward the temple of the Lord and their faces toward the east, they were bowing down to the sun in the east.","dt":"2026-08-27T08:46:46.847Z","s":["nu7osie63g"]}],"22":[{"m":"How the selection process... I'm interested... Was it that he had fallen to the Chaldeans earlier?","dt":"2022-08-18T08:27:50","s":["m7juynlepo"]}]}},"Amos":{"2":{"3":[{"m":"Wickedness happening to both the good and bad... The bad as judgement for their wicked ways, and the good being devoured and no one to help them.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:56:31","s":["e6qkiuii4n"]}],"12":[{"m":"Such an abomination — they indeed despised the laws of God.\n\nAs I read these judgements on all these nations, I ask, who then shall survive?\n\nIn time past God used them against each other to punish and enforce the will of God,\n\nbut now they were all in the wrong and were all to be punished.\n\nThis time God brought his winnowing fork from a far-off country, even the king of Assyria and the king of Babylon.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:18:07","s":["no69h5w9r7"]}],"4":[{"m":"We see here that everyone is judged according to the light given them... Israel 🇮🇱 had the law and were thus judged thus.\n\nThe pagans had conscience and natural law to guide them, and they were judged accordingly.\n\nRomans 2:11-12 KJV\nFor there is no respect of persons with God. [12] For as many as have sinned without law shall also perish without law: and as many as have sinned in the law shall be judged by the law;\n\n1 Corinthians 10:13 KJV\nThere hath no temptation taken you but such as is common to man: but God is faithful, who will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape, that ye may be able to bear it.","dt":"2022-07-14T14:57:55","s":["d36hoon5k4"]}]},"4":{"8":[{"m":"God wanted their attention, but to no avail.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:42:23","s":["ig5s5s8bjs"]}]},"5":{"19":[{"m":"Mercy, mercy, mercy, Lord.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:02:50","s":["5resdcfyrr"]},{"m":"I see a picture of a man running 🏃 into his house 🏡, and he enters in exhausted, bends over and leans upon the wall with his hand 🖐️ to catch his breath,\n\nonly for a snake 🐍 to bite him from the very wall he leaned on for support and respite.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:48:31","s":["5jw52r3to9"]}],"13":[{"m":"Hmm... It is an evil 😈 time ⌚.\n\nSo the righteous and wise keep silent 😶.\n\nThere come such seasons in life where it seems there is no God, simply because of the ease with which evil 😈 is executed and the entire system corrupted.","dt":"2024-09-11T07:46:01","s":["qinx96wksk"]}]},"6":{"5":[{"m":"Hmm... This gives us some insight about David, the sweet psalmist of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nHe was not just a psalmist but an inventor of music and musical 🎶 instruments.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:06:01","s":["6gbk5lkabt"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"Was God creating afresh these grasshoppers, or he gathered them? I believe he gathered them, but in a sense it was he creating them. But the verse clearly says he formed them; that goes to show the Lord still creates, and continues to, for his own name's sake and to fulfill HIS desire upon the earth.","dt":"2026-07-18T15:03:16","s":["0kinqbgtud"]}],"5":[{"m":"All God needed was a man to stand in the gap.","dt":"2026-07-18T15:04:37","s":["hnovwjwmr9"]}],"10":[{"m":"I do not think this Amaziah was the Lord's priest.\n\nI suspect he was a Baal worshiper or some idol's priest.\n\nIt is ironic that this Bethel, where Jacob encountered God, now has some strange gods being worshipped there.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:17:14","s":["qcibm6r8h0"]},{"m":"I suspect he was an idol priest.","dt":"2026-07-18T15:05:28","s":["v5pxhqd659"]}],"13":[{"m":"Such a fallen state; they actively abhorred any correction or godliness.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:10:35","s":["49z9gp1wxs"]}]},"8":{"5":[{"m":"This is so much like our land: thievery & wickedness even in the marketplace.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:14:26","s":["ut0g3stjxf"]}],"6":[{"m":"We do this even today, in our marketplaces. False balances and poisoned foods are being sold for money.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:18:57","s":["w2m7u4bbmm"]}],"10":[{"m":"When such statements used to be made, I did not quite understand, till I grew and lost some loved ones,\n\nand oh, imagine the pain of a parent losing their son, their only son.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:20:26","s":["fjee6bxve6"]}],"12":[{"m":"God, have mercy!\n\nThough this is OT, we find the same in the NT. I see that many themes of the OT have parallels in the new.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:15:41","s":["b7bpbtuuha"]},{"m":"It was not the written word these people were going to faint for; it was the spoken word.\n\nThat a word from the Lord through a true prophet will come to them and save them, or guide them at least.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:22:16","s":["80fqjzycm9"]}],"14":[{"m":"Were they attributing the works and power and mercy of GOD to their gods?","dt":"2026-07-18T15:09:38","s":["ltu2sl4v6p"]}]},"9":{"8":[{"m":"You know, our times are like the times of Isaiah when he gave the prophecy of the virgin birth. I guess they expected it to happen in their lifetime;\n\nlittle did they know that the sign was for centuries to come.\n\nSo was the coming of our Lord, and his second coming.\n\nWe see the signs, but then suddenly it is upon us 🙏.\n\nHave mercy, Lord, have mercy on us.","dt":"2022-07-14T17:19:20","s":["i4e5u5dh2h"]}],"14":[{"m":"Israel is such an archeologically rich land.\n\nSo much history, and so many people have lived there over the centuries and millennia.\n\nMany wars fought, whole civilizations brought to the ground, all because of disobedience.","dt":"2024-09-12T06:26:35","s":["r331gwmlso"]}],"15":[{"m":"God is strange a lot. See, whiles he's actively talking of judgement and their reward for wickedness, he is in another breath talking of their redemption from evil and come back to glory 🙏","dt":"2022-07-14T17:21:29","s":["rd96m56nwx"]}]},"3":{"2":[{"m":"This ties in with my comment in Amos 2:4 — we are punished according to the degree of light that we have.","dt":"2026-07-18T14:29:14","s":["t27iatnmkq"]}]}},"Jonah":{"1":{"2":[{"m":"What is there about Nineveh?","dt":"2021-06-13T17:00:02","s":["cd2nx181gy"]}],"3":[{"m":"How is it possible to flee from the presence of the omnipresent God?\n\nUnless to say he was fleeing from where he heard God from, the place of covenant, to a far-off place where he won't hear God.\n\nWe see also that in fleeing from the presence of God, he fled from doing God's will.\n\nThat is, he was disobedient to the word and will of God.\n\nBut Jonah was such a man 👨 of God, to actually be in so close a relationship with God, that he disobeys God and God comes looking for him and does all possible means to reach out to him and bring him back on course 🏇.\n\nIncluding creating an entire storm just for Jonah.\n\nAnd he was proven right, as we see later the repentance of Nineveh at the preaching of Jonah.\n\nJonah's rebellion reminds me of Cain, who again God came looking for in the matter of Abel.\n\nCain denies knowledge of such things, lying 🤥, as if possible, to the omniscient one...\n\nFor he too, God helps and provides some respite from the blood of Abel.","dt":"2022-07-08T07:34:43","s":["wctwhcg7ps"]}],"4":[{"m":"Come on, why is God stressing himself over Jonah?\n\nHe should just send another person, a prophet, to get the job done. There were many prophets in the land in those days, I believe.\n\nBut yet God stuck to the job and went to the extreme to get Jonah to do the work.\n\nGod is not erratic; he follows order, systems and logic.\n\nJudging from the kind of relationship Jonah had with God, he was God's buddy-buddy, and God could not suddenly abandon him. This is the God of love and relationships.","dt":"2022-07-08T09:15:40","s":["am71yudod8"]},{"m":"Hmm, what God does for his friends and those he has a relationship with. Going this extreme for his own prophet, however disobedient he was.\n\nGod knows his children and those who are his, and he loves them as his own. And like any father, he would do anything for his children (an attribute we as men picked up from our heavenly Father).","dt":"2022-07-08T09:18:16","s":["l6gm8lwkn8"]}],"7":[{"m":"Storms in the sea 🌊 were normal for these experienced sailors ⛵.\n\nBut there seems to be something about this storm; I doubt it was just the fierceness of the storm.\n\nI suspect the storms showed signs of intelligence. It was preventing them from sailing in a particular direction — in the direction opposite Nineveh.\n\nThere was something about the storm that made them sense a divine hand 🖐️ behind it.\n\nWhy else would they ask for lots to be cast?","dt":"2024-09-11T06:36:53","s":["go8kcnlnwe"]}],"12":[{"m":"Such a sense of awareness of the presence of God, to the extent that he was ready to be cast away into the sea 🌊.\n\nBut I ask, how did Jonah know he was the cause of the tempest, and how did he know what was to be done?","dt":"2022-07-08T09:43:53","s":["ikvciuu944"]}],"16":[{"m":"Vows as to what they will do once God brings them to land.\n\nWhy do we vow and make sacrifices? Because we want to do something that will catch the attention of the supernatural.\n\nThe earth 🌎 is filled with men going about their activities; the man, therefore, who wants to catch the attention of the gods to himself must do something extra, and hence a sacrifice.","dt":"2022-07-08T09:47:37","s":["ye3grpakic"]}],"9":[{"m":"I am an Hebrew — those people, the people for whom God divided the Red Sea and dealt with Pharaoh and all the gods of Egypt. Who led his own people like no other god does in the wilderness and brought them to the land of Canaan.\n\nA land he had promised their fathers before them. Those strangely blessed people.","dt":"2026-07-17T09:52:57","s":["br2kuqn7jh"]}],"10":[{"m":"They had heard enough stories of this God who divided the Red Sea 🌊 and led his people through the fierce desert 🏜.","dt":"2024-09-11T06:38:24","s":["rdiejhklkm"]}]},"3":{"5":[{"m":"This story of Nineveh has many loop ➿ holes 🕳.\n\nWhy did they fear the Lord in the first place? Who was Jonah to them, for them to even listen 👂 to him?\n\nEven the king 👑 left his throne to fast.\n\nHow did they know Jehovah could do what Jonah had declared?","dt":"2024-09-11T06:46:26","s":["zbl184fj6g"]}],"10":[{"m":"Many times we wonder what was wrong with Jonah for refusing to have people saved. Was he not supposed to be a prophet of God? But I think Jonah's story is like the elder son in the story of the prodigal son.\n\nHe did everything right and yet got little reward, and yet this rebellious son takes his share of the property and blows it, and the father still welcomes him home and has a place in his heart to forgive him.\n\nIt started looking like the father honoured rebellion and did not reward those who did what is right, meanwhile the father had been telling them from childhood to obey him. So why was it that now the disobedient have a party thrown for them?\n\nBut if you have no children, you will not understand the heart of a father. No father wants to lose any of his children. Good or bad, he will find a way of keeping them all.\n\nBut of course he will reward good behaviour over bad behaviour, but then he will also forgive the one who repents and comes back home.\n\nHe was not going to give him property, since he had squandered it, but he was of course in no way going to cast him away.\n\nThat is what Jonah knew but refused to understand. I understand Jonah, but I understand the Lord more and agree with HIS decision.","dt":"2026-07-17T11:16:03","s":["ora02rja1s"]}]},"4":{"5":[{"m":"What was Jonah's grudge with God?\n\nDid he have a personal issue with Nineveh?\n\nHad they done some evil to him in time past, for which he felt and maybe prayed for the Lord's vengeance?\n\nNow it was all tumbling down.","dt":"2024-09-11T06:49:41","s":["fd8qlmatu3"]}],"9":[{"m":"God sometimes uses experiences to teach a lesson and elicit the appropriate response and understanding from us.\n\nJonah wanted the people dead, yet he wanted a plant to have lived — a plant of so little worth compared to a man, yet Jonah did not see it that way till God took from him what he cared about, the gourd, to help Jonah see that he was not being fair and reasonable.\n\nThe story ends with this lesson from God to Jonah.\n\nA strange story of the man, the prophet who wanted an entire nation dead, or maybe they were enemies of Israel — who knows?","dt":"2026-07-17T10:05:06","s":["s8hxvuv6iv"]}],"11":[{"m":"What are cattle doing in here... So this was in reference to the prosperity of the city.","dt":"2022-07-08T10:21:43","s":["q9c1ych9v3"]},{"m":"God was telling him it's a buzzing and economically vibrant city.\n\nThey did not deserve death ☠ without a chance at repentance.","dt":"2024-09-11T06:51:32","s":["rgqk7hjjcx"]}]},"2":{"9":[{"m":"In his situation he could not make animal sacrifice, but he had his voice.\n\nHere again he vowed. I believe his vow was that he would preach the word to Nineveh.\n\nHebrews 13:15 KJV\nBy him therefore let us offer the sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of our lips giving thanks to his name.","dt":"2022-07-08T10:18:38","s":["t2tgxdh2ht"]}]}},"Micah":{"3":{"8":[{"m":"As I come across some of these more familiar scriptures, I see how clear of a difference there is when one reads it in context, as compared to when one just reads the verse and runs off with it.","dt":"2024-09-16T07:59:32","s":["mu2jk6dd3k"]}],"11":[{"m":"Oh, there is nothing new under the sun; in our times this is so rife,\n\nbut so was it in the times of Israel.\n\nHow did they get to this point? Gradually compromise seeped into the church, i.e. the nation of Israel: worship of other gods and much sin and disregard for the commandments of God.\n\nAnd then now they find themselves at this point, where even the priests have become corrupt and prophets do so for hire.","dt":"2024-09-16T08:04:40","s":["7h7hdr9nod"]}]},"5":{"10":[{"m":"Why does the Lord detest multiplying horses and chariots? Especially for Israel.","dt":"2024-09-16T08:10:47","s":["gbvz63k1qd"]}]},"7":{"12":[{"m":"Why is Assyria so prominent in these verses and chapters?\n\nThe same occurs in the book of Isaiah.\n\nBecause Assyria was to be used of God to punish Israel, and in the future an Assyrian will take center stage to attempt to destroy Israel, as they had done in the past.","dt":"2024-09-16T08:17:24","s":["5ctzjne9mv"]}]}},"Hosea":{"3":{"5":[{"m":"Only for the latter days to be millennia later","dt":"2024-09-23T10:32:17","s":["bn5t6ogdpk"]}]},"4":{"6":[{"m":"This truth stands true generally, that for lack of knowledge people perish or suffer many things, though contextually it was referring specifically to the lack of knowledge that the children of God — Israel — had of God's laws and his word. Not that they did not know it.\n\nIt was not even for lack of knowledge but for rejection of knowledge. They knew the word of God, but they just hated it.","dt":"2026-07-30T07:21:59","s":["uwsiv9l8se"]}]},"5":{"15":[{"m":"Hmm, I thought the same thing: in their affliction they will seek the Lord, and early.\n\nIn the verse 4, we are told a spirit of whoredom has taken over them.\n\nHosea 5:4 KJV\nThey will not frame their doings to turn unto their God: for the spirit of whoredoms is in the midst of them, and they have not known the Lord.\n\nIn this state, the way to shake them awake and out of it was affliction.","dt":"2022-07-20T17:14:11","s":["tosqb1bre9"]}]},"6":{"1":[{"m":"This ties in beautifully with the last previous chapter's verse. Indeed, he who tore will heal, because that was the entire purpose of the tearing.\n\nTo heal and bring restoration.","dt":"2022-07-20T17:16:16","s":["b6kt7j5iui"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"See the progression:\n\nGod wanted to heal, but they committed wickedness... then the thief was able to come in, and robbers spoil.","dt":"2022-07-20T17:20:22","s":["14stsnvm77"]}],"16":[{"m":"God did his best to restore these ones without bringing them low, but it did not work out. Eventually affliction was theirs.","dt":"2022-07-20T17:23:10","s":["h38n5on67u"]}]},"8":{"14":[{"m":"Because it is the Lord who is our defence, so building fortified cities without spiritual cover is an activity in vain.","dt":"2022-07-21T08:56:17","s":["14tjbm0484"]}]},"9":{"11":[{"m":"God, we know, is in heaven, but the way he describes activities of men, it is clear that he is very accustomed to our ways.\n\nNot just because of his omniscience, but he watches the ways of man closely.\n\nI have had these thoughts often: why is there so much focus on man and the earth 🌎 from these heavenly spiritual beings?\n\nWhy are we so important to them? It seems heaven's and the spiritual realms' preoccupation is the earth, meanwhile we are here minding our own business.\n\nThis bears more study.","dt":"2022-07-21T09:05:40","s":["l61yqtluvf"]}],"17":[{"m":"Mercy","dt":"2022-07-21T09:06:46","s":["17gkbr2eqx"]}]},"10":{"12":[{"m":"Do you struggle with sin? Are you struggling with being righteous?\n\nWe all do sometimes, and here we are given a key... If you are struggling, then it's a hint that it is time to seek the Lord.\n\nSeek his face in prayer, fastings and scripture meditation 🧘‍♂️; continue till he comes and rains righteousness on you.\n\nWaiting on the Lord is the way to go to receive power over our flesh and its desires.","dt":"2022-07-21T09:16:42","s":["l02a0st0hu"]}],"13":[{"m":"A similar process is repeated here: men plowed wickedness and reaped iniquity, ate the fruit of lies 🥝.\n\nThis law never changes, no matter how advanced and/or civilized a society becomes.\n\nYou can't out-advance the laws of sowing and reaping. You sow wickedness, you will reap iniquity and the consequences thereof.","dt":"2022-07-21T09:21:17","s":["jsd5hm5wke"]}]},"11":{"8":[{"m":"How can he not?\n\nYou can literally sense the affections of a father, the bowels of love of a parent.\n\nGOD knew he could not completely bring an end to Israel 🇮🇱 as he had other nations.\n\nThis father-son love and bond was too great.","dt":"2022-07-21T11:49:13","s":["nm6bufngeh"]}]},"12":{"3":[{"m":"Judah here was in a bad place; they were in a backslidden state, and God, wanting them to turn back to him, reminded them of what made them Israel 🇮🇱 in the first place.\n\nHe said to them: you are Israel, you are the one who wrestled 🤼‍♂️ with both God and man 👨.\n\nWhen you set out to do something, you do it.\n\nReturn to me, because the latent power is still there: you are Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nWhy did God never force his people to change, but often used words, sometimes for decades and even centuries?\n\nHis last resort always was physical harm through abandonment. Taking away his protection so the enemy could get them.","dt":"2022-07-22T06:11:42","s":["2i0a4fmv3n"]}]},"13":{"8":[{"m":"I've heard this expression before... But what is there about a bear 🐻 robbed of her cubs\n\nthat makes it different from, say, a lion or tiger?","dt":"2022-07-22T06:45:06","s":["wmvak5mo9d"]}],"11":[{"m":"God doesn't forget...\n\nHe still remembers their sin and rejection of him in asking for a king 👑.","dt":"2024-09-23T13:00:48","s":["sp25mbr873"]}]},"14":{"2":[{"m":"The calves of our lips. Words of thanksgiving, words of sacrifice. Again we see a New Testament concept in the old 🧓.\n\nWords were going to be accepted in the place of lambs and calves.","dt":"2022-07-22T06:49:53","s":["0q8i7p1v6r"]}],"9":[{"m":"So indeed, inasmuch as it is said that the ways of God are mysteries, there are things he's given for us to understand.\n\nHe therefore calls the wise to understand. These passages, I believe, have to do with the end of time, when Israel will be reconciled to God.\n\nThe same, I believe, applies to the 666; it is said to be the number of a man 👨.","dt":"2022-07-22T06:55:41","s":["b7t137qdo6"]}]},"2":{"8":[{"m":"So the Lord blessed them, and they took those same resources and worshipped Baal.\n\nThey thought, or maybe rather forgot, that it was God who blessed them with those things.\n\nLikely they attributed their blessings to their deity, till God taught them a lesson that he gave it to them.\n\nHe proved so by withdrawing the blessings from them.\n\nBut God","dt":"2024-09-21T07:50:51","s":["jhqgw0d30g"]}]}},"Psalms":{"1":{"2":[{"m":"What did meditating on the law of God look like in their days?\n\nBecause they did not have all these stories making up today's Bible.\n\nThey had the Torah.\n\nIn fact, this same command to meditate was given to Joshua, who at that time was to meditate on the law of God; the Torah was barely complete then, there was no book of Psalms, so he even had less volumes to read then.\n\nWas it that they memorized the law or pondered over all the different ways it could be applied in a practical way every day?","dt":"2024-06-21T07:49:10","s":["4xjatneuui"]}]},"2":{"7":[{"m":"This psalm is a messianic psalm, commonly regarded so.\n\nBut I'm trying to see if it was David musing about himself and his kingdom 👑.\n\nBecause he was indeed the Lord's anointed, his kingdom had been established by God,\n\nHe prospered wherever he went and dashed to pieces his enemies.\n\nGod could have said to him, \"You are my son, this day have I begotten you\", in the sense that he called David, but at a point in his walk with God, God considered him his begotten son.\n\nSimply, this psalm is messianic indeed, though we can apply it to David, but it more easily applies to Christ, but with some extrapolation David can be roped in.\n\nThis is why it is more messianic than a musing about self.","dt":"2024-06-21T08:43:23","s":["dj4xjm2kve"]}]},"4":{"5":[{"m":"The sacrifices of righteousness: not just bulls or animals, but the sacrifice of pain and endurance that come from doing what is right and seeking what is good.","dt":"2026-05-23T07:41:08","s":["8iyssef8ah"]}],"4":[{"m":"Commune with your own heart and be still.\n\nDavid seems to be reasoning that when you really take time and muse, meditating 🧘‍♂️ on the greatness and wisdom of God,\nyou come to a point of rest and stillness.\n\nBecause you know this good, merciful and powerful God is able to make all things work together for good.","dt":"2024-07-01T10:15:57","s":["5tl73ulwa9"]}]},"8":{"5":[{"m":"The word translated angels is actually elohim, the same word for God and the same word translated judges in certain verses.\n\nI have heard some argue, and some say, that it's best translated \"you have made him a little lower than God\"... I think I have believed that myself in time past.\n\nBut looking at the whole passage contextually, translating elohim as angels seems best.\n\nDavid starts off by talking of how frail and insignificant man is in the frame of God's creation when compared to the moon, stars ✨ etc.\n\nYet in his frailness God has made man head of the earth 🌎. And \"had made him lower than angels\" fits best because through the passage, God's covenant name of Lord is used.\n\nSo if David wanted to say he has made him lower than himself, either he would have said \"you have made him lower than yourself\" or \"... lower than the Lord God\",\n\nbut chose to use the word God, and so it's best understood as the angels, who are in a sense considered as divine.","dt":"2024-06-13T08:06:04","s":["fica3h1pan"]}]},"9":{"3":[{"m":"The enemies of David fall at the presence of the Lord even as they fled before him (David).\n\nI thought 💭 David would have said his enemies fell by his sword ⚔ even as they turned to flee.\n\nIt goes to show how David recognizes the hand 🖐️ of God even in his victories gained by his own hand 🖐️","dt":"2024-06-13T08:09:31","s":["acz5me4kgx"]}]},"15":{"5":[{"m":"Interesting that the Jews do not lend to another at interest.","dt":"2024-06-21T08:48:31","s":["wp04eg4eob"]}]},"17":{"3":[{"m":"Oh Lord, help me that I transgress not from my lips 💋","dt":"2024-06-08T15:41:45","s":["9nkd7u1dl4"]}]},"18":{"29":[{"m":"One of the more popular scriptures.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:13:58","s":["a5ra8kixjq"]}],"34":[{"m":"Wow... Extraordinary things are possible 🙆 in battle because of the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:14:52","s":["24rft5xwlc"]}],"37":[{"m":"Here we see the many benefits of serving the Lord and making his word and laws paramount in your life.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:16:12","s":["rwlr6bnugf"]}],"41":[{"m":"Who were these enemies of God who hated him and kept not his commands and laws, yet in times of trouble they cried out to him?\n\nOf course the Lord will not answer.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:19:15","s":["pfne763vmm"]}],"26":[{"m":"This is one of my favorite scriptures of late... with the froward thou will show thyself froward.\n\nGod cannot be mocked, so those who seek to mock him, he has equally devious plans for them.\n\nIn the end God will laugh them to scorn.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:01:43","s":["3ohx3ipnmy"]}],"42":[{"m":"There seems to be a certain delivery of justice on behalf of God in the wars David fought.\n\nGod, the judge of all flesh, seemed to be executing judgements on the wicked people even as David slew them in battle.\n\nAs he did, the judgment of the Lord against those nations was being executed.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:21:10","s":["igpha2qy3k"]}],"47":[{"m":"David recognizes the fact that it was God all through his victories.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:22:13","s":["z5cdlfrbp5"]}]},"19":{"14":[{"m":"Amen. I love this psalm, especially from verse 7, which talks of the benefits of the instruction of God.\n\nStarting from the law of God all the way to his judgments,\n\ngliding from one precept and concept of God to the next.\n\nOh, how I wish I knew distinctly the subtle difference in each instruction that proceeds from the mouth 👄 of God.\n\nLaw, testimony, statutes, commands, fear 😱 & judgements","dt":"2024-06-13T08:25:49","s":["mc4oge398e"]}]},"20":{"7":[{"m":"And indeed David had put to flight the kings of Ammon and Syria in 2nd Samuel 10 & 1 Chronicles 19... and destroyed their chariots.\n\nMaybe this psalm was inspired by that battle.","dt":"2024-06-27T11:49:32","s":["i02xzusafw"]}],"9":[{"m":"The king, the LORD","dt":"2026-05-15T08:49:33","s":["sm59654aua"]}]},"21":{"1":[{"m":"The king 👑, God's king 👑, God's man was on the throne, and the will of God was rightly established.","dt":"2024-06-13T08:29:32","s":["fcaz5b5dg5"]}],"8":[{"m":"Though David was on the throne, he spoke of his enemies as the enemies of God and vice versa.\n\nIndeed he was coregent with God; he was there to represent the agenda of God.\n\nHe was God's man on the throne.","dt":"2024-06-13T08:39:31","s":["zka79zvcuf"]}]},"22":{"10":[{"m":"Another messianic psalm.\n\nFor God to be the writer's God from the mother's womb. This so clearly points to Christ rather than man 👨","dt":"2024-06-21T08:54:12","s":["cftiuk1jo6"]}],"21":[{"m":"Unicorn is translated wild oxen 🐂 in some versions.\nMeaning, he cried when caught between the horns 🤘 of the oxen and was answered by the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-21T08:58:15","s":["htz9lm7bj5"]}],"2":[{"m":"David had these experiences, yet when it comes to him praying and enquiring of the Lord, it's summarized often as\n\n'David enquired of the Lord and God said...'\n\nWe are not told of the many days and nights he cried out without response or help.","dt":"2024-06-21T08:52:16","s":["1tazhd4emc"]}]},"27":{"8":[{"m":"Wow...\n\nWhen the Lord instructed him to seek his face, his response was not lip service, but with his heart ♥ he yearned to know him.","dt":"2024-06-07T06:22:20","s":["cqo10tr7f2"]}],"10":[{"m":"Why would David make up such statements?\n\nWas it figurative or was it literal? Did his parents abandon him?\n\nWas that why he was the one taking care of sheep whiles the rest sought to be anointed king 👑?","dt":"2024-06-07T06:27:17","s":["9detzxx45q"]}]},"28":{"4":[{"m":"Old King James English version is very interesting at times.\n\nIt says for God to render to them their deserts... Hehe 😂... But in plain English it's to render to them what they deserve.","dt":"2024-07-01T10:27:07","s":["zt65bk7o3a"]}],"7":[{"m":"Amen. My heart trusted in him and I am helped.","dt":"2024-07-01T10:27:59","s":["46wyw9ssdu"]}]},"31":{"20":[{"m":"God shall hide his sons in his secret presence from the pride of men.\n\nHe hides them in his presence, where his goodness is.","dt":"2024-06-07T06:42:51","s":["8om44j3txo"]}],"6":[{"m":"Lying 🤥 vanities. The same word or phrase that Jonah used when he prayed from the belly of the whale 🐳\n\nJonah 2:8 KJV\nThey that observe lying vanities forsake their own mercy.","dt":"2024-06-07T06:39:18","s":["j5oj4sryxi"]}]},"33":{"16":[{"m":"This counsel sounds so counterintuitive, but this is the wisdom of Israel and David, with which they defeated their enemies with 100% 💯 certainty.\n\nSo also is the case of the believer who fears and waits on the Lord.","dt":"2022-05-09T13:28:18","s":["4vcngfrbus"]},{"m":"Words of a man of war and much experience.\n\nThey are strange words indeed for an army general to utter.\n\nOne might think 🤔 that after having uttered these words he would then attribute success in warfare to strategy and skill.\n\nNo, none of these. He concludes in subsequent verses that deliverance comes from the Lord.\n\nAnd this is wisdom for us 🙏.","dt":"2024-06-26T06:17:35","s":["5t6myqdgoe"]}],"19":[{"m":"Another wisdom nugget... It is God who keeps alive in famine. He never fails.","dt":"2022-05-09T13:29:01","s":["9veu4kla43"]}],"17":[{"m":"No one knows this better than David, a mighty warrior himself. Even in much strength and valour he knows victory is of the Lord, for he has defeated many a mighty army greater than himself.","dt":"2026-05-14T06:49:37","s":["5fy2jzyxnr"]}],"18":[{"m":"So in war, in trials, in difficult times, it is those who hope in the Lord and their eyes 👀 look upon his mercy that obtain his mercy.\n\nFor horses 🐴 and chariots are prepared for battle, but safety is of God.\n\nProverbs 21:31 KJV\nThe horse is prepared against the day of battle: but safety is of the LORD.","dt":"2024-06-26T06:20:35","s":["zkkw6h2v19"]}]},"36":{"6":[{"m":"He started by talking of the mercies of the Lord that is in heaven,\n\nthen progresses to the clouds 🌥 with his faithfulness, then he descends to the earth 🌎 and mountains ⛰\n\nAnd now down to the deep.\n\nThen to man 👨 and beast.","dt":"2024-06-26T06:46:43","s":["1e6t7gnt91"]}],"9":[{"m":"Amen, because he lighteth upon us, our mouth 👄 is filled with good things and our hearts 💕 are at peace ✌️ and enlarged towards him.","dt":"2024-06-26T06:51:45","s":["iwub5ltfxr"]}]},"37":{"37":[{"m":"Real nuggets of life there.\n\nNuggets for practical everyday living.","dt":"2024-07-17T06:29:11","s":["qs3wluhha8"]}]},"38":{"1":[{"m":"David in his psalms often talks of the end of the wicked and the judgement the Lord brings upon them.\n\nBecause of this insight, whenever he finds himself walking 🚶 in the ways of wickedness, he quickly prays and returns.","dt":"2024-07-04T09:42:41","s":["te9frh2imn"]}],"22":[{"m":"I wonder when in the history of David he wrote this psalm.\n\nIt must indeed have been a very low moment in his life.\n\nHis enemies and friends alike were against him, he was caught in sin...\n\nALL around him things were very bad.","dt":"2024-07-04T09:51:18","s":["qx1gmpr3gd"]}]},"39":{"5":[{"m":"This is a much line indeed.","dt":"2022-05-09T13:33:29","s":["gz225tze4v"]}]},"41":{"5":[{"m":"Wow, really, that's very bad.\n\nThese are the words of someone embittered, vengeful and angry 😡","dt":"2024-07-04T09:54:30","s":["2tj3q14dul"]}]},"44":{"12":[{"m":"A sad state to be in. Where the people of God are so cheap and valueless that they are sold for nought, and those that sell them barely make a thing from their sales. The seller is not made any richer by that sale.\n\nThat should tell you how common of a slave the people of God became. The people of God. That in itself is an irony.","dt":"2026-04-25T08:55:23","s":["m7z75k919y"]}],"19":[{"m":"The New King 👑 James Version uses jackals instead of dragons, and so do many other versions.","dt":"2024-06-14T06:37:51","s":["dug5ah0bho"]}],"20":[{"m":"What point in the history of Israel was this?\n\nWhere they dared God to search their hearts 💕, where their ways were perfect before the Lord, yet they lost battles and they fled before their enemies.\n\nUsually it was when they went out of covenant that the Lord caused them to be afflicted by their enemies.\n\nBut this time they were doing alright, yet they were counted as sheep 🐑 for the slaughter.\n\nAnd the circumstances of this period were also used to allude to the suffering of the church ⛪ and of Christ in his day.\n\nRomans 8:36 KJV\nAs it is written, For thy sake we are killed all the day long; we are accounted as sheep for the slaughter.\n\nMaybe this was penned down for us, that sometimes for no ill 🤒 doing of ours, evil 😈 befalls us.\n\nWe may search our hearts and find no fault; in such times we just trust in the providence of God.\n\nHe is God.","dt":"2024-06-14T06:42:04","s":["v2pyo2t61l"]},{"m":"It gets even more ironic. The people had not abandoned God or his laws, yet they were suffering as a people whose God had abandoned them. So this was their plea and cry to God.\n\nThey did not deserve what they were suffering.","dt":"2026-04-25T09:00:09","s":["qgzho2c9vj"]}],"22":[{"m":"Paul alluded to this in\n\nRomans 8:36 KJV\nAs it is written, For thy sake we are killed all the day long; we are accounted as sheep for the slaughter.","dt":"2024-06-14T06:43:51","s":["wlks4bmvcg"]}]},"46":{"4":[{"m":"The rendering of this verse is so poetic — really it is.","dt":"2024-09-28T07:41:41","s":["9kryte25da"]}],"11":[{"m":"Selah","dt":"2022-07-16T11:04:34","s":["nmuwl37gyr"]}]},"48":{"14":[{"m":"Amen, I'm only wondering, how does this psalm tie in with the chronological reading 📖 of the Bible plan I'm doing?\n\nHow does this tie in with Hezekiah revamping Jehovah worship?","dt":"2022-07-19T08:17:22","s":["veeqkhonle"]}]},"49":{"15":[{"m":"This psalm is very thought-provoking:\n\nDescribing how that we take nothing to the grave with us.\n\nHow we are wasted after life and buried ⚰ like the beasts of the field.\n\nWho would have thought that great men would be brought so low at death ☠?\n\nHowever, in this verse he talks of how that God would redeem his soul from death.\n\nThey had hope of the resurrection from the dead.","dt":"2024-06-14T08:11:05","s":["1pvr1dlf01"]}],"17":[{"m":"This is wisdom for us. We brought nothing into this world, and it is obvious we would take nothing out.\n\nEven as we make a name for ourselves and gain wealth, we must always have that in mind.","dt":"2024-06-14T08:12:39","s":["t5n52sahdv"]}]},"51":{"17":[{"m":"True, sacrifices in the midst of sin and forgoing God's law are an abomination to him.","dt":"2024-07-01T12:05:45","s":["1ui62s0jx4"]}],"4":[{"m":"What did he mean by 'against God only had he sinned'? He had sinned against a lot of people.\n\nUnless it was an expression 😑 in those days, probably to show how that even if no one could challenge him or knew of this sin because he had covered it up well,\n\nit was not against man he had sinned but against God, against God alone who sees all things, that he had sinned.","dt":"2024-07-01T12:00:15","s":["g100t13mlk"]}],"6":[{"m":"He speaks here of truth in hidden parts, which ties in with the earlier commentary on verse... That it was a secret sin which he could use his influence to cover up.\n\nBut here he finds himself having sinned against God; how was he going to cover it up before God's omnipresence?\n\nHe was in a fix and could only confess and beg for mercy.","dt":"2024-07-01T12:02:18","s":["falez72dau"]}],"11":[{"m":"David did not want God to take away his Spirit from him. The very thing that made him the LORD's anointed. This anointed and the anointing was something that David did not take lightly at all. He held it as sacred and rightly so, to the extent that he refused to kill Saul when he had the chance to, a decision that looked very foolish and weak.\n\nBut on account of his understanding of the anointing he kept his hand from evil. God also kept him from evil when he became the anointed of the LORD. God held him as sacred and forgave him and led him in the way he should go.","dt":"2026-05-18T23:20:54","s":["mnk5qeep41"]}],"19":[{"m":"The same God who did not desire burnt offerings and sacrifices in verse 16 is now pleased with them in this verse, because they were the sacrifices of the righteous.\n\nThe heart that offers the sacrifice is more important to God than the sacrifice — like King Saul, who offered sacrifices, yet on account of that offering he lost his kingdom.","dt":"2026-05-18T23:25:03","s":["g5vm76201k"]}]},"52":{"8":[{"m":"Wow, such imagery — such power with words.\n\nIndeed one like a green olive tree 🎄 planted 🌿 in the house of the Lord shall live forever.\n\nEver fresh and fine.","dt":"2024-06-07T08:28:29","s":["ooyfrids2i"]}]},"55":{"14":[{"m":"Could this have been Ahithophel, whose counsel was like God's?\n\nWhat a divine privilege for a man to be described as this...\nBeing given almost a God status.\n\nSadly he eventually destroyed himself... His own wisdom failed him and he committed suicide.","dt":"2024-07-01T11:32:45","s":["m1g9liabo5"]}]},"56":{"4":[{"m":"Warriors and soldiers are indeed very bold.\n\nImagine David had all these fears yet was so valiant in war and battle.\n\nWhen you read the stories about him, you see only the bravery and bravado but not his heart ♥.\n\nThe contents of the heart are difficult to capture through the expressions 😑.\n\nHowever the psalms, his personal writing, tell of the state of his heart ♥.\nThat which no man sees.\n\nThen we see that he was only human... helped by God.","dt":"2024-06-07T08:34:20","s":["7qxb6whpcl"]}]},"57":{"4":[{"m":"I don't know if them that are set on fire 🔥 has anything to do with men literally set on fire 🔥, as happens in war, where fiery darts 🎯 are shot out or coals of fuel poured out and set ablaze on the enemies.\n\nTo be among such men, you risk getting burned and destroyed with them.\n\nNow David finds himself in the midst of such men; being in the midst of fire and not burned will take grace.","dt":"2024-07-06T03:05:55","s":["j1dhq80d8t"]}]},"60":{"11":[{"m":"From this psalm it seemed at a point that the armies of Israel were overpowered and seemed to be losing the war.\n\nDavid cries for help 😣 and pleads with the Lord to come through for Israel.\n\nIf this psalm is a true reflection of what happened, then the summaries of events in the book of Samuel and Chronicles are just a summary and omit how tough the battle was and the numerous challenges, including feelings of despair and defeat.\n\nEventually God came through and Israel won.\n\nThis victory is all that is said, and none of the losses and defeats.\n\nIt doesn't mean it was all conquest... Just that nothing is mentioned of it.","dt":"2024-06-27T09:43:14","s":["92g708vxbl"]}],"12":[{"m":"Selah, and at the end of the day they did triumph — they did valiantly and conquered the enemy.\n\nThis goes to show that in virtually all his battles David did seek the face of the Lord. Especially when things were turned against them, and God heard him.","dt":"2026-05-15T08:01:11","s":["98z48g1u1d"]}]},"61":{"6":[{"m":"Had David by this time received the promise of an eternal throne?","dt":"2024-07-02T13:21:23","s":["vjzw4wp6cj"]}]},"64":{"8":[{"m":"That which they speak of doing will fall on themselves.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:23:19","s":["ji8pw00tyo"]}]},"65":{"2":[{"m":"There is something about poetry that endears the heart ♥.\n\nNo wonder these psalms of David are so popular. They are sweet and truly inspired.\n\nThey are deeper than meets the eyes.\n\nOh God, unto you shall all flesh 💪 come.","dt":"2024-07-01T12:21:35","s":["3gzbossg2o"]}],"7":[{"m":"And Christ did this literally; these words are not mere appellations but words of life and truth.","dt":"2024-07-03T13:00:04","s":["uja8iz352w"]}],"4":[{"m":"I used to wonder how these things pan out, that by being in the courts of God one is satisfied with the goodness in His house 🏡\n\nBut then the story of Obed-edom beautifully sums this up.\n\nThe ark of God was in his house 🏡 and by that fact and proximity his house was so blessed in just three months.\n\nThere seems to be something about the proximity to the house of God that rubs his presence off on you and blesses you mightily.","dt":"2024-07-01T12:33:58","s":["g5l47fg3y5"]}]},"67":{"1":[{"m":"I think a \"may\" should have started the sentence, since from the second statement it's in the 3rd person.","dt":"2024-07-03T14:02:36","s":["iw8uv6rj1k"]}]},"68":{"16":[{"m":"The imagery is like the hills leaping to catch the attention of God, meanwhile he has chosen whom he has chosen... he has chosen the hill of Zion and nothing can change his mind.\n\nNo amount of trying to impress God from the other hills will change his affection for Zion.\n\nHe has already chosen.","dt":"2026-05-09T07:08:31","s":["pjtljhd3lo"]}],"18":[{"m":"I'm trying to get the connection between this verse and the preceding verses.\n\nWho was he referring to in the context of the psalm?","dt":"2024-06-21T09:16:07","s":["vmy3r2cghs"]}],"34":[{"m":"So many different concepts in this particular chapter of Psalms.","dt":"2024-06-21T09:19:50","s":["drw17jmd4p"]}]},"69":{"4":[{"m":"Hmm... How 😔, sad where a man 👨 restores what he did not take.","dt":"2024-07-03T14:07:45","s":["qeqngbd7dg"]}],"9":[{"m":"This is quoted in the New Testament, though I do not see how that connects to the Messiah directly, unlike other messianic psalms that very clearly describe best the Messiah and no one else.","dt":"2024-07-03T14:13:47","s":["k5hvrcp67x"]}],"21":[{"m":"This happened to the Christ and could be applied to the life of the psalmist as well.","dt":"2024-07-03T14:17:00","s":["jeqs9cj9th"]}],"26":[{"m":"This is not reflective of the Christ at all, unlike the preceding verses, which actually happened.\n\nBut unlike this verse, the Christ asked for them to be forgiven.","dt":"2024-07-03T14:22:00","s":["i5axwjdf1r"]}]},"70":{"5":[{"m":"Many a man crieth out for hasty deliverance, but it is the Lord who truly knows those who need hasty deliverance.","dt":"2024-07-03T14:23:43","s":["ks8c7fma9y"]}]},"71":{"11":[{"m":"This sounds like something that would be said when Absalom overthrew him.","dt":"2024-07-17T06:21:13","s":["qyflx6knj0"]}],"7":[{"m":"Yes indeed, David knew he was a wonder unto many, but his secret was God.\n\nGod was his refuge.","dt":"2024-07-17T06:22:43","s":["f5mxqw7wwl"]}]},"72":{"12":[{"m":"Of such a high profile was the king 👑 Solomon, yet he held judgement for the needy and poor.\n\nNo wonder God prospered and blessed him so much 🙏","dt":"2024-07-17T14:31:07","s":["8sxrab43nd"]}],"20":[{"m":"Indeed, amen and amen.","dt":"2024-07-17T14:33:33","s":["0squuj4b0a"]}],"14":[{"m":"For a man of such a high profile, why would the blood of people of low profile be precious in his sight?\n\nBecause he indeed was a righteous ruler.","dt":"2024-07-17T14:32:07","s":["adxfgg0jcm"]}]},"77":{"11":[{"m":"That was a very wise decision made in the midst of difficulties and hardships.\n\nThis Asaph chose to remember the goodness of the Lord and his mighty saving acts in time past, and not just console but counsel himself by it.\n\nKnowing that our God is mighty to save.","dt":"2024-06-16T03:22:06","s":["1abjts8mx6"]},{"m":"It is because of the penchant for man to forget the great works of God, and for man to continuously walk in faith, that we are admonished to meditate on the word day and night.\n\nFaith is required to please the Lord and to continuously be blessed by him.\n\nThis goes to show that our role is vitally needed for God's promises for us to be fulfilled.\n\nCould not the God who divided the Red Sea 🌊 cause Israel to inherit the promised land the first time?\n\nHe could, for all things are possible 🙆 with God, but\n\nthat is not how God works, and those are not his ways — erratic and unstructured.\n\nFaith and action of his people is needed for him to carry them into their inheritance.\n\nFaith in him and action in the direction of his commands is what is needed.\n\nNonchalance and inaction will destroy a people, even if they are named after the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-16T03:51:50","s":["cfjug65xfn"]}]},"78":{"25":[{"m":"Was it angels' food 🍲? It was physical, and angels are spirit, but then again we do know that spirits eat.","dt":"2024-06-16T03:46:41","s":["5yyhechlbj"]}],"26":[{"m":"God was angry at men for seeking a miracle... for throwing a challenge to him to prove himself.\n\nCould it be that today, where Christianity is all about seeking miracles from God, that God is not happy?\n\nWhat have we done with all the signs and wonders the Lord has done for us, he may be asking.\n\nHow we have disdained the opportunities he brought our way, and now here we are asking him to prove himself strong and true in our lives.","dt":"2026-04-26T08:31:22","s":["4w80oaen4a"]}],"51":[{"m":"Oh, it seems that Ham inherited Egypt and its territories.","dt":"2024-06-16T03:57:20","s":["0ksbnxtfwd"]}],"65":[{"m":"This scripture one time brought such hope of restoration for me.\n\nWhen under the weight of life's difficulties, I was assured of the Lord coming to my rescue.\n\nRising up suddenly like a man out of the stupor of wine 🍷.\n\nRising up to my rescue.","dt":"2024-06-16T04:09:31","s":["8zkbb1dz9q"]}],"67":[{"m":"Were the Ephraimites not the nation of sodomites that almost got exterminated?\n\nI wonder if this was a factor in their being rejected.\n\nIf not, what could have accounted for their rejection?","dt":"2024-06-16T04:10:59","s":["cmpl3v8ez6"]}]},"80":{"1":[{"m":"See how The Message puts this verse... completely diluting the substance thereof.","dt":"2022-07-28T08:38:46","s":["jruitxdjhq"]}]},"84":{"11":[{"m":"It is indeed for a very valid reason that David would choose to be a doorkeeper in the house of God than to dwell comfortably in tents 🎪 of the wicked.\n\nHe reveals this in the next verse:\n\nFor the Lord God is a sun ☀ and shield 🛡, he gives grace and glory.\n\nThe benefits of the Lord far surpass the comforts of wickedness.","dt":"2024-06-14T08:22:07","s":["fgig6t8h47"]}]},"86":{"17":[{"m":"Oh yes, we all do need this every now and then.\n\nThat our enemies may see the power of our God and fear 😱... knowing that our God fights for us 🙏","dt":"2024-07-01T12:13:24","s":["wm6vtv6lhz"]}]},"87":{"2":[{"m":"Who wrote this psalm: likely David.\n\nBut at which point was Zion declared the city of God?\n\nThis bears further studies.","dt":"2024-06-14T08:26:11","s":["0x619v1o4x"]}]},"88":{"1":[{"m":"The heading of this psalm says it's by the Ezrahite...\n\nAre we then to presume that the person descended from Ezra? That would then mean this psalm was after the captivity, and the people had returned back to their land, and way after Ezra had died and now his generation after him had multiplied.\n\nIs this assumption right 👉?\n\nI read an article online that confirmed this thought but was quick to add that because of the poetic nature of the psalm it was difficult to come up with a definite date.\nhttps://honorsblog.uark.edu/psalms/#:~:text=Most%20modern%20scholars%20believe%20the,because%20of%20their%20poetic%20nature.\n\nThere is a different and contrasting view that suggests that there was mention of Heman the Ezrahite in the days of Solomon and David, and if this was the same man, then he lived in their time.\n\nhttps://enduringword.com/bible-commentary/psalm-88/\n\nLet's see how this goes.","dt":"2024-06-17T06:57:52","s":["qt8dt6f01j"]}]},"90":{"17":[{"m":"Amen... Satisfy us early, oh God, according to thy mercies.\n\nSatisfy us according to the years wherein thou hast afflicted us.","dt":"2024-04-18T07:02:07","s":["3mees6mvma"]}],"3":[{"m":"Return ye to where?\n\nReturn ye to the dust, for dust you are and to dust ye shall return.\n\nGenesis 3:19 KJV\nIn the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.","dt":"2024-04-18T06:58:54","s":["66l51bwjnv"]}]},"96":{"9":[{"m":"Holiness is not an outmoded thing; holiness is a beautiful thing.\n\nFor our God is holy.","dt":"2024-06-22T06:51:09","s":["5idopz5vnp"]}],"13":[{"m":"The judgement of this world by God has long been known by them of old 🧓","dt":"2024-06-22T06:53:23","s":["xy6enwp19b"]}]},"98":{"3":[{"m":"Indeed the psalmist is proud to have the Lord as his God.\n\nAnd declares that the ends of the earth 🌎 have seen the glory of the Lord.\n\nIndeed the Jews must be a very proud people, for them to be the only nation of all the earth 🌎 that the Lord has chosen.","dt":"2024-07-06T18:29:13","s":["jr61d32ajg"]}],"9":[{"m":"These psalms in these chapters, i.e. 90 to 98, 99, talk of the Lord coming to judge the earth.\n\nYes, it is symbolic, but then it is actually also literal. The LORD through Jesus physically will come down to rule the earth.","dt":"2026-10-07T10:51:58.460Z","s":["t1ux55su23"]}]},"101":{"8":[{"m":"No wonder the Lord loved him. He had come to do God's work, and that he did.\n\nPromoting the good and demoting the wicked.","dt":"2024-06-22T06:59:07","s":["ogk3oxb7kg"]},{"m":"This sounds like a psalm of David.","dt":"2026-10-07T10:56:11.980Z","s":["usuvas777r"]}],"6":[{"m":"David was a good king 👑; he sought to promote the good and righteous ones and to demote them that have a high look and haughty in spirit.","dt":"2024-06-22T06:57:48","s":["1pzfp30o6d"]}]},"102":{"9":[{"m":"The imagery... He holding his cup 🥤 to drink and at the same time ⌚ his tears 😭 falling into the cup.\n\nIn their culture, when sad, they put ashes upon the head 😩 and wear sack clothes... The psalmist must have been so grieved and so full of ashes, so much so that he literally tasted of it daily.","dt":"2024-06-18T08:17:51","s":["un65xggsjj"]}],"26":[{"m":"Very prophetic and apocalyptic.\nSame description is given in the book of Revelation.","dt":"2024-06-18T08:25:22","s":["nvwldnrd2l"]}],"13":[{"m":"Wow, is this the backdrop 💧 to this verse? A very popular verse of scripture that has spoken to me in time past.\n\nYet in context the psalmist was in grief and pain untold, so much so that he describes his tears 😭 as his drink...\n\nPsalm 102:9 KJV\nFor I have eaten ashes like bread, And mingled my drink with weeping,\n\nYet there was hope coming: God of Zion was going to rise up and have mercy upon Zion, for her appointed time of favour had come.","dt":"2024-06-18T08:22:32","s":["o1bowq1aoi"]}]},"103":{"7":[{"m":"One of the more popular verses often preached from.\n\nTo wit, that Moses understood God, that was why he could walk with God so intimately, but the children of Israel only saw his acts but had no relationship with nor understanding of his ways.\n\nTo determine how accurate this assertion is, we would have to search for the original meaning of the word translated 'ways' and 'acts'.","dt":"2024-06-17T13:13:14","s":["2scza7jg1i"]}]},"105":{"19":[{"m":"Ah, I love 😍 this,\n\n\"until the time that his word came...\"\nUntil his season was due.","dt":"2024-06-22T07:02:55","s":["y7hoqydgyn"]}],"27":[{"m":"EGYPT is being referred to as the land of Ham.","dt":"2024-06-22T07:04:01","s":["jqqv9sypmw"]}]},"106":{"15":[{"m":"He gave them their request: fatness of flesh, yet leanness of souls.","dt":"2024-06-19T21:20:29","s":["25vwztchf0"]},{"m":"These psalms are historical; it seems this is a continuation in a sense of chapter 105.","dt":"2026-10-08T11:00:33.805Z","s":["u4wao6oiim"]}],"20":[{"m":"Ah 🤬, so painful 🤬... This verse states the bluntness of their ways so clearly. Without mincing words.\n\nThey did such a terrible 😰 unfair exchange...\nThis beast for the Lord God Almighty himself.\n\nHidden in splendor and glory.","dt":"2024-06-19T21:24:41","s":["dktukgmk2n"]}],"47":[{"m":"This psalmist wrote like one in captivity, or after they had been scattered from their homeland to other nations.\n\nThis might have been deep in the Assyrian or Babylonian captivity.","dt":"2026-10-08T11:04:31.847Z","s":["s6571mxg6g"]}]},"109":{"4":[{"m":"David really had terrible moments in his life.\n\nNo wonder his psalms were so full of them.\n\nIndeed, such is life, and so it's not so peculiar to him.\n\nJust that to uphold his righteousness he suffered so much 🙏, and through his psalms we gain comfort in this world 🗺.\n\nThis verse ends with the statement, \"but I give myself to prayer\".\n\nIf we take out the italicized portions, which are not part of the original text, it reads:\n\n\"but I prayer\", which can more effectively be translated as \"but I pray\" 🙏","dt":"2024-07-09T09:32:30","s":["zvlabmzbkz"]}],"20":[{"m":"Those were some very damning wishes for one's enemies.\n\nBut the premise justifies it.\n\nHe started by stating how it all began in love, but for his love he, David, was rewarded with evil 😈.\n\nPsalm 109:5 KJV\nAnd they have rewarded me evil for good, And hatred for my love.\n\nNote also that these are wicked men.","dt":"2024-07-09T09:40:05","s":["fq6knqnnny"]}],"21":[{"m":"David was a king 👑 and knew how to make entreaties of one.\n\nHe knew how to use emotional word picture 🖼 to connect his requests to the heart of God.","dt":"2024-07-09T09:36:18","s":["9zadar1z04"]}]},"110":{"5":[{"m":"Which Lord was it that was at the right hand of THE LORD, to whom was given power to strike kings?","dt":"2024-07-09T09:44:22","s":["qwgd3xlorv"]}]},"116":{"10":[{"m":"This verse, specifically the phrase 'I believed, therefore have I spoken...',\n\nwas used of Paul to indicate that when we speak what we believe... as in the word of faith.\n\nBut contextually this verse was talking in the negative confession,\nwhere the psalmist believed God had abandoned him and left him to be afflicted.\n\nOnly to realize the loving kindness of the Lord. So the psalmist was wrong in his assumptions.\n\nNow Paul takes the same concept but applies it to our walk of faith.\n\nThat goes to show it's not necessarily always about context, depending on the point you want to make.\n\nAgain, this whole conversation is premised on the assumption that this is where Paul the apostle picked his thoughts 💭 from.","dt":"2024-07-15T07:00:07","s":["lclwme1c8s"]}]},"118":{"27":[{"m":"Continuous verses of psalms that are so popular in Christianity.\n\nAnd they all reside here in one chapter.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:07:55","s":["n0xh0mnkvg"]}]},"119":{"37":[{"m":"Instead of beholding vanities he desires to be quickened and made alive in the ways of God.\n\nIs it not interesting that the same instrument or part of our body for sinning is the same for doing good and obeying the laws of God?\n\nWe must direct our heart, habits and desire right 👉 so our members serve the law of God.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:33:26","s":["3jh0j35r9k"]}],"40":[{"m":"The precepts of the Lord lead to righteousness.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:41:31","s":["nxthb7kf2v"]}],"41":[{"m":"Mercy and salvation is found in his word.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:41:58","s":["i2cn7yan6f"]}],"43":[{"m":"His word and judgements are the hope we hold unto.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:42:39","s":["zveqamjfz1"]}],"45":[{"m":"His word brings peace ✌️. So many countless benefits of the word.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:43:36","s":["kh9e4kzynr"]}],"46":[{"m":"Amen — his word and truths are an opportunity to share them without shame, for so precious are they that it is worth sharing, and will be valued every bit by the kings.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:45:02","s":["l3urvwf9y9"]}],"47":[{"m":"His word is delightful and loveable.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:46:07","s":["rdo604on5t"]}],"50":[{"m":"His word brings comfort. So many benefits of the word of God.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:46:55","s":["7t6tx1p6wf"]}],"51":[{"m":"Humility is found in the law.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:55:10","s":["x4egbm8v4n"]}],"61":[{"m":"Loss of material possession, and for that matter gain of same, did not cause him to forget the law.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:57:32","s":["efa6lu7nvw"]}],"62":[{"m":"The law of the Lord must occupy us at all times, even in the night season, and fill our minds.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:58:21","s":["1ushx654an"]}],"64":[{"m":"Indeed the whole earth speaks of and demonstrates the wisdom and word of God.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:59:33","s":["lv4pv9e1ol"]}],"36":[{"m":"I like this comparison, comparing the desires of his heart for the testimonies of God to covetousness.\n\nSo rather than the secret desire for his neighbor's goods, the psalmist prays for a heart that desires the testimonies of the Lord.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:31:04","s":["cypiedulko"]}],"39":[{"m":"The law of the Lord turns away our reproach, because our steps are directed right in the ways of God.\n\nHis judgements are good, so we choose what is right and not what would bring us shame and reproach.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:35:42","s":["r3gc9jdym7"]}],"60":[{"m":"Promptness to obey God's word is required.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:56:50","s":["3op4fedwib"]}],"63":[{"m":"Those who fear the Lord and have this in common must unite to push the agenda of God into fruition.","dt":"2024-07-19T06:59:02","s":["d4n0zioa3z"]}]},"123":{"3":[{"m":"This is the state of many in our day, and thus this should be the prayer of many, and I guess it is.\n\nYet it needs to be prayed more often, and many more ought to pray 🙏 in such manner.","dt":"2024-06-12T06:23:48","s":["e2fcmkzh92"]}]},"130":{"6":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. Did David or the psalmist mean this literally?\n\nWho are they that wait for the morning...\n\nOther versions bring clarity: they that watch for the morning as watchmen.\n\nNow I get it. Indeed, when you are on night watch, you battle sleep to keep your watch, you battle time as the clock 🕒 barely seems to move.\n\nIndeed there is yearning and desiring for the morning and the dawn of light.\n\nDavid, being in the army, had kept the watches severally, for the rest of your comrades' lives depend on it, so you must keep watch.\n\nI can imagine David keeping the watches and yearning for the morning, and then he begins to think upon the goodness of the Lord.\n\nHe then compares his love and yearning for the Lord with his yearning for the break of day when his watches would end.\n\nHe knows that just as the brink of day matches with freedom and rest from the watches, so when God breaks forth upon him like the morning lights, his rest would come and all this labour would end.\n\nAs he meditated upon the Lord, he realized his need and yearning for the Lord actually supersedes that of the yearning for the day...\n\nIndeed his soul waits and is willing to wait for the Lord more than they that watch for the night.\n\nNow I wonder what prompted such thoughts 💭 and ideas in David's mind to start with.\n\nHe was just there and such fantastic and wonderful thoughts about God come to his mind...\n\nIndeed he was a man after God's own heart 💕","dt":"2024-06-12T07:28:36","s":["1vh5topv1e"]}]},"131":{"1":[{"m":"What a psalm.\nShort, concise and straight to the point.\n\nI'm surprised I don't remember coming across this psalm ever.\n\nMaybe because it is not preached about often.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:11:50","s":["l9acbevyhk"]}]},"136":{"26":[{"m":"Why does this psalm end at the entering in of the promised land?\n\nIt doesn't continue to Joshua and the judges and David and Solomon.\n\nMaybe those events hadn't yet happened, or the psalmist just decided to end there, or\n\nthe events of particularly David and Solomon were never thought of as sacred, especially by those living in those times.\n\nThey were spectacular, but not sacred enough for them to have thought of it as scripture.\n\nThe psalmist might have lived in those times, and you know, when one is making history, you may not even be aware.\n\nThey were making history, but in their own psalms they did not consider their times worthy, yet generations after would consider those events so.","dt":"2024-08-08T08:03:35","s":["dw9vlj3doj"]}]},"138":{"8":[{"m":"Two of the more popular verses of scripture.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:27:32","s":["ao9259ld6x"]}]},"139":{"10":[{"m":"David asks a question of fleeing from the presence of the Lord.\n\nMaybe fleeing in disobedience like Jonah.\n\nYet when the hand of the Lord found him, he was not chastised nor rejected, but the loving arm 🙋 of the Lord guided and comforted him.\n\nThat is the nature of God: full of love and mercy.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:30:40","s":["u9dlbgan56"]}],"12":[{"m":"The Lord has long had night vision eyes 👀 😇","dt":"2024-07-10T09:34:37","s":["ocyvdpbzco"]}],"15":[{"m":"Most translations retain the lowest part of the earth 🌎, but a few say the dark of the womb.\n\nIs this an example of where all the original text says earth 🌎, but because the translators don't agree 👍 with a person being formed in the earth 🌎, they chose to use their knowledge of biology to render it womb?","dt":"2022-05-27T06:39:46","s":["wz3zxd492q"]},{"m":"Could this in a sense allude to Adam?\n\nHe was not born but formed from the earth 🌎.\n\nMen are now all born, yet in referencing the baby in the womb, the writer chose to describe the creative process.\n\nI checked the original Hebrew, and the word used here is 'eret, which means land, earth.\n\nIt is not used differently anywhere else... In all cases it means earth.\n\nAs for the versions that translated it as the dark of the womb, it is an attempt, I believe, to help the reader understand.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:37:56","s":["lusoe1croj"]}],"16":[{"m":"Is David's thinking that we are formed by God before we are formed in the womb, in the sense that did we pre-exist before our birth?\n\nOr, to be more true to the text, were our physical and bodily features known, decided upon and recorded in heaven before our physical birth?\n\nOr does the same apply to our entire person, as in spirit, soul and body?\n\nDavid talks about being formed, and since man is spirit, soul and body, this statement is in reference to the complete man, not just the physical body.\n\nSo even before man was formed in the land of the living, he was known by God.\n\nKnown by the almighty, eternally living God.\n\nWho, being eternal, not only lives forever into the future but also predates time in the past.\n\nHe is the Alpha and Omega. Time to him is not just a continuum but a spectrum.\n\nHas a beginning and end, unlike man 👨.\n\nThat is why he is God.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:52:45","s":["dtxgglr4gq"]}],"22":[{"m":"No wonder the Lord loved David so much... His enemies were David's enemies as well.\n\nIndeed, David fought the Lord's battles at the peril of his life.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:48:51","s":["gfqmz0n04l"]}]},"143":{"5":[{"m":"David is so good at encouraging himself in the days of trouble.\n\nAs he did in Ziklag.","dt":"2024-07-10T09:59:53","s":["vtqp8mnj18"]}]},"144":{"15":[{"m":"Amen 😭... Indeed, happy is such a people that all these good things happen to them.\n\nThis is the desire of every man in this cursed 🤬 earth 🌎.","dt":"2024-07-10T10:46:12","s":["mlm1nfr0be"]}]},"145":{"9":[{"m":"True.\n\nHe causes his sun ☀ to rise on both the good and wicked.","dt":"2024-07-10T10:48:16","s":["lng7zsclgx"]}]},"12":{"3":[{"m":"Yes, flattering lips flatter for the purposes of keeping your heart at ease, whiles they devise wicked plans to overthrow.","dt":"2026-05-23T07:45:18","s":["lspoakr7xx"]}]},"30":{"12":[{"m":"Oh yes, indeed, to the end that my glory will sing your praise and not be silent.\n\nI will give you thanks, oh Lord, I will give you thanks, oh Lord.\n\nMany years ago the Lord spoke these words to me when my expectations were cut off.\n\nWhat I wanted did not come to me, and when I enquired of the Lord, he gave me this word: that what I wanted was going to hinder what he wanted for me.\n\nHe wanted my glory to sing his praise, he wanted my gifts and abilities to bring his glory, which was also what I really wanted more than anything else.\n\nAnd now in this season of my life I feel this scripture remains relevant to me.\n\nI have weathered many storms over the past decades because indeed he wants my glory to sing his praise and not be silent.\n\nAnd that will be done.","dt":"2024-07-08T07:11:12","s":["mdd48uhgv6"]}]},"32":{"2":[{"m":"After talking of a man whose sins are forgiven and iniquity not imputed.\n\nYou would have thought that the man's heart was full of sin, but in further describing the man,\n\nhe describes him as one in whose spirit is no guile.\n\nWhat kind of man is that? 😲\n\nThat is a righteous man 👨, but even a righteous man does sin and fall short of God's glory and needs God's unconditional love and mercy to keep him in the love of God.\n\nRomans 3:23 KJV\nFor all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;\n\nJohn 3:16 KJV\nFor God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","dt":"2024-07-01T11:52:19","s":["zo5fglz1qu"]}]},"43":{"5":[{"m":"David stands at a place outside himself and speaks to his downcast soul, encouraging it to hope in God.\n\nDavid had learnt to be talking to himself in such a manner.\n\nI believe that is what is meant when scripture says in\n\n1 Samuel 30:6 KJV\nAnd David was greatly distressed; for the people spake of stoning him, because the soul of all the people was grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters: but David encouraged himself in the LORD his God.","dt":"2024-06-14T06:33:01","s":["dp7wzycy6k"]}]},"50":{"11":[{"m":"Really!? He knows. It sounds so much like the teaching of Jesus when he says every sparrow is numbered. And even the very hairs of our head are known and numbered.\n\nThis is very possible and is actually the case. Looking especially at how advanced we have become and we are able to keep very detailed records.\n\nHow much more the heavens and the systems God has set in place. Giving his creation structures and abilities to ensure that the systems are working. So there are actually heavenly scribes, recorders, recordings and systems of record for all these.\n\nI am beginning to understand why God created man in the first place. Being a businessman myself, I see all the possibilities and the need for people to do all the little things you delegate to them, so that you can do only what you can do.\n\nSo God created man, and he, God, does only what he as God can do.\nIn this light, we messed things up, and the nature of the relationship and our mandate is being mended? But we still are man, and created in the image of God to build and to maintain and grow what has been committed to us.\n\nLet me jump ahead.\n\nThis begs the question: what does God expect us to do, and what does he expect us to ask him to do, and what needs no asking but he, God, will do?","dt":"2026-05-15T08:07:23","s":["iu8mi4ieqn"]}]},"53":{"5":[{"m":"The spirit of fright had come upon the people... causing them to fear needlessly.","dt":"2024-06-27T09:35:17","s":["nqvgemsevv"]}]},"66":{"12":[{"m":"Through the fire 🔥 and through the 💦 waters God delivers.\n\nThe interesting thing is that when men rode over us, he actually allowed it.\n\nIt was not on his blind side, nor was he taken unawares.\n\nIt is very interesting that God is very much involved in our conflicts and hardships.\n\nHe is in the know paa. Every one of the difficulties we face 😔 was allowed by him.\n\nHe has not been nonchalant about our afflictions nor ignorant of them.\n\nWe have to trust his judgments as knowing what's best for us, and keep in sync with his wisdom and ways by daily prayer and seeking his face.","dt":"2024-07-03T13:53:15","s":["rdp20gm6ns"]}]},"73":{"28":[{"m":"An interesting conclusion, when he thought 💭 the wicked seem to do well in this life and go unpunished; same was Job's thoughts.\n\nAnd it seems generally the righteous observe the wicked and think such.\n\nBut after living for a while the righteous observe the wicked and see that in the end the wicked perish without hope, neither in this earth 🌎 nor in the life after.","dt":"2024-06-15T01:08:05","s":["4p7jw28f30"]}]},"75":{"8":[{"m":"😊 Interesting imagery this is.","dt":"2024-06-27T10:56:31","s":["iuoogziu4g"]}]},"85":{"8":[{"m":"☺ A very good reprimand there.\n\nLet us not return to foolishness after the Lord rescues and restores us.","dt":"2024-06-14T08:24:10","s":["1l44e5jqbj"]}]},"91":{"6":[{"m":"I have a sense this psalm of Moses was written in the times after the plagues of Egypt 🇪🇬.\n\nIt resonates so much with the destruction at noonday and the terror 😰 of the night that came upon Egypt, and yet none on Israel, who were in such close proximity to Egypt.","dt":"2024-05-09T14:37:50","s":["1kxv12v3hd"]}]},"94":{"13":[{"m":"Amen.\n\nIf the Lord chasteneth thee, then indeed he loves thee.\n\nHe could have left thee to fall after the manner of the wicked...\n\nBut because he loveth thee, he suffereth not thee to perish but chasteneth thee unto righteousness.","dt":"2024-07-17T06:36:04","s":["g8ji1zykcm"]}]},"100":{"3":[{"m":"This scripture is much akin to Jesus saying in\n\nJohn 15:16 ESV\nYou did not choose me, but I chose you and appointed you that you should go and bear fruit and that your fruit should abide, so that whatever you ask the Father in my name, he may give it to you.","dt":"2024-06-22T06:54:53","s":["2hgamdet5g"]}]},"115":{"3":[{"m":"AWWW... my heart wells up at this very thought 💭...\n\nWhere the heathen think 🤔 to mock us and ask to see our God...\n\nThen we rather laugh out loud at them and say, our God is in heaven.\n\nYours have mouth 👄, nose 👃, ears 👂 and other appendages but are without function... How sad 😔.","dt":"2024-07-15T18:01:02","s":["ltuzu3a7ab"]}]},"122":{"6":[{"m":"Oh, this is where that popular verse comes from.\n\nBut indeed this is not a command from God for us, the heathen that have now laid hold of the covenant of God.\n\nIt's a prayer of David.","dt":"2024-07-01T12:17:46","s":["33fdz2weai"]}]},"132":{"1":[{"m":"Although not titled a psalm of David like the other psalms, we see right from the beginning the involvement of David in the psalm.","dt":"2024-06-22T07:07:34","s":["t094fscc6c"]}]},"135":{"21":[{"m":"Amen 🙏","dt":"2022-07-28T08:41:30","s":["6uyn2otkpd"]}]},"137":{"9":[{"m":"This goes to show what was done to them, and they wished the same upon their enemies.\n\nWhat a pain they entered captivity with.\n\nWar is not good.","dt":"2024-12-23T08:03:12","s":["tae815ul4j"]}]},"140":{"7":[{"m":"Anyone could be hit by the enemy's arrows from afar as you focus on the enemy before you. So if the Lord had not been on his side to shield him from those arrows, he would have long been dead.","dt":"2026-04-16T06:23:44","s":["6a17c0pp81"]}]}},"Nahum":{"1":{"3":[{"m":"He has his way in the nature... using it to do his bidding and display his glory and majestic power and presence.","dt":"2026-08-09T09:59:44","s":["1rk396dl4t"]}],"9":[{"m":"He will make an utter and complete end, so much so that there would be no room for a comeback or recovery.\n\nOne-time defeat of evil 😈 and affliction. It will make no recovery.","dt":"2022-08-03T06:54:57","s":["xytzq826ja"]},{"m":"Other translations render it to mean affliction which the Assyrians inflict on the people of God will not arise a second time.\n\nNahum 1:9 AMP\n“Whatever [plot] you [Assyrians] devise against the Lord, He will make a complete end of it; Affliction [of God’s people by the hand of Assyria] will not occur twice.”","dt":"2026-08-09T10:04:33","s":["8u3t5t9sg6"]}]},"2":{"2":[{"m":"The emptiers, from Assyria to Syria to Babylon etc.","dt":"2022-08-03T07:04:42","s":["uaaion0i49"]}]},"3":{"19":[{"m":"THY bruit — bruit, according to Google, means 2 things — bruit (pronounced broot or broo-ee) is primarily a medical term for an abnormal blowing or swishing sound heard with a stethoscope over a blood vessel, caused by turbulent blood flow. In older or literary English, it can also act as a noun or verb meaning a rumor or to spread a rumor.\n\nThe time of their casting out had come... they had performed many wonderful evils... Overthrowing and ousting out nations, yet it was only a time they also will be ravaged...","dt":"2026-08-09T10:20:14","s":["qwm9j0vcjk"]}]}},"Zephaniah":{"1":{"12":[{"m":"Same thing when the day of the Lord comes.\n\nNow people are tired of the message of the Lord's coming.\n\nIt's now become just a story.","dt":"2022-08-06T11:52:12","s":["3elrsl77zf"]},{"m":"The Lord was going to do a thorough job on this one.\n\nThe picture of a man in the dark with candlelight searching out every nook and cranny for something.\n\nIn like manner, the Lord was going to flush out every evil man from the house.","dt":"2024-10-09T07:41:37","s":["o6e4dltg3p"]}],"14":[{"m":"Interestingly, it is called the day of the Lord, not the day of Assyria attacking Judah or the day of Babylon.\n\nIt was, or more specifically will be, the Lord behind it the whole time.","dt":"2024-10-09T08:17:41","s":["wdra6e12an"]}],"17":[{"m":"I find it amazing that these prophecies came in the time of Josiah, a time of prosperity and righteousness, yet the prophets prophesied of gloom and doom.\n\nWho would have expected or heard or even believed such?\n\nI look at our nations today, and Ghana my own motherland, and I ask, who will be able to see such visions in the times of prosperity and abundance, and especially in the days of a righteous king?\n\nAll will prophesy of prosperity and riches forever. Alas, who will hear the true cry and warning of the Lord?\n\nLORD, GIVE US YOUR WORD AND DISCERNMENT AND TRUTH IN THE SPIRIT OF PROPHECY.","dt":"2026-08-10T20:34:25","s":["prcd4uscyw"]}]},"2":{"3":[{"m":"Amen. Yes, there is escape for the righteous in the day of the Lord's wrath.","dt":"2022-08-06T11:55:01","s":["yjw36p7yd5"]}],"9":[{"m":"Interesting. Meanwhiles, Moab and Ammon were birthed after the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah. Indeed, they were birthed as a result of the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah.\n\nAnd fast forward, their end was to be the same as the place they hailed from, the place that birthed them. They were the sons of Lot's daughters, who slept with their father to birth them.","dt":"2026-08-11T08:54:44","s":["513d8fmldn"]}],"11":[{"m":"Famish??? 🤯\n\nZephaniah 2:11 AMP\nThe Lord will be terrifying and awesome to them, for He will starve all the gods of the earth; and all the coastlands of the nations will bow down and worship Him, everyone from his own place.\n\nAnd he alone will be worshipped. It almost sounds like the gods thrive and are empowered by worship 🛐, i.e. sacrifices, blood and following their doctrine.\n\nIn a sense this is true; the gods live off these. It is true in that it is through these that they are empowered and granted access to have authority on the earth 🌎.\n\nIt does not mean they die or lose or diminish in existence, but in influence in the earth realm.\n\nAnd of course, since all gods want a stake in the earth 🌎, they do all they can to have an entrenched position.\n\nA permanent ♾ stake if possible.\n\nAnd in this wise will God outsmart all others.\n\nHe will have it all and famish all others.","dt":"2022-08-06T11:59:33","s":["lrod86y2vh"]}],"10":[{"m":"Just as their father Lot lifted himself in pride and chose the best part of the land in his own eyes, and left the father of Israel, Abraham, to feed on the rest. Yet Lot did not reckon that the blessing was on Abraham, so wherever the soles of his feet would tread there would be a blessing.\n\nAnd now we see the children of Lot reproach the children of Abraham — the people of Israel.","dt":"2026-08-11T08:58:05","s":["g728or2j5j"]}]},"3":{"9":[{"m":"So the end game is so all flesh fears him and worships.\n\nHe is a jealous one and will not tolerate any other gods.\n\nSo great is his jealousy that he will exterminate all.","dt":"2022-08-06T12:10:20","s":["tccnxvcs0u"]}],"20":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-01-24T12:06:47","s":["cbkqru2y1o"]}]}},"Jeremiah":{"1":{"4":[{"m":"In verse 4 he says the word of the Lord came to him, but in verse 9 he says and the hand of the Lord touched his mouth.\n\nThis goes to show that the word of the Lord is the Lord in person.\n\nIt is not a voice or sound. It is a personal being.\n\nSaying the word of the Lord came is more of an expression for saying the Lord came to him.\n\nRevelation 19:13 KJV\nAnd he was clothed with a vesture dipped in blood: and his name is called The Word of God.\n\nAnd his name is the word of God.\n\nIs that not the name given to Jesus the Christ — does that mean this expression is actually referencing Christ in his pre-incarnate form?\n\nWhy else would he be called the word of God if he is not the word of God?\n\nThat expression often confused 😕 me. But it doesn't mean he was in the past in the form of words; rather, it's an expression describing his function.\n\nBecause when he shows up he speaks the mind of God.\n\nHe is the logos.","dt":"2024-10-09T09:21:16","s":["ee7060iiek"]}],"16":[{"m":"Does that mean the righteous were spared... Not necessarily, not automatically, not all.\n\nFor instance, Daniel and his brethren were spared, but we can't definitively say all righteous people were spared.\n\nExample: Jonathan was killed, though so righteous, in the war in which his father died... So it's not always the case.\n\nI wish I knew the criteria in the case of such selection, as to which righteous person lives and which one is spared the wickedness of this world.\n\nMaybe the righteous that run the risk of turning evil if given more time... Who knows, or those who are so pure hearted and love God that the world is not worthy of them, as stated in the New Testament.","dt":"2026-08-13T21:35:35","s":["hllpd3zqir"]}],"18":[{"m":"Literally fenced in city 🏙. Such a city is fortified with iron pillars and walls made of bronze.","dt":"2022-08-07T07:36:44","s":["o67u71y9lt"]}],"6":[{"m":"This issue of I cannot speak.\n\nIt seems the Lord sees differently from how we see ourselves.\n\nMoses complained of the exact same thing.\n\nAnd I, even I, have pleaded for a mouth 👄 that can speak and for God to be with my mouth like he was with Moses, so I can speak and teach his word.","dt":"2024-10-09T08:53:44","s":["3c3dtt68b4"]}],"8":[{"m":"And you would think 🤔 after having said this, the ride will be smooth, or at worst when trouble comes, immediately God comes in to save the day.\n\nJeremiah was put in a pit and almost died, he was imprisoned, and at a point he himself testified that he said he would no more speak the word...\n\nYeah, that's how bad it got.\n\nNo, it's more like you will go through the challenges, there will be doubts 🤷‍♂️, pain 🥖 and at a point you might wonder if God is alive.\n\nBut our God, just at your threshold, he comes to the rescue.\n\nAnd you know the thing about God is that when he steps in, he does a beautiful job of cleaning up every mess.\n\nOh, when he, God, steps in, as we say, he \"ebaa fée Tami sini\".\n\nLike when the good cop shows up in the movie at the last moment, you know help has come and it doesn't matter how messed up the situation. He's gonna do a good job.","dt":"2022-08-07T07:29:37","s":["yztc9wnt51"]}]},"2":{"2":[{"m":"I know they used to murmur and complain a lot in the wilderness, but that was their best days yet.\n\nFast forward, the Lord remembers those days and calls them holiness to the Lord.\nThe wilderness was one of the closest a nation en masse had experienced God and divinity.\n\nIndeed they were holiness to the Lord.","dt":"2024-10-11T19:43:17","s":["3kln1w7jvx"]}],"10":[{"m":"Hm... Why is it so... They that have the truth often sell it cheaply for falsehood...\n\nWhy do evil 😈 people, and in this case other nations, stay true to their false god and to evil, but Israel 🇮🇱 did not show the same but converted to other gods?\n\nI think part of it is the deception 😞 of evil 😈.\n\nIt is for this same reason, I believe, that God commanded Israel not to intermarry with the other nations, lest they lead them astray, and not vice versa.\n\nSee how Solomon the wisest, even he was led astray.\n\nWhat is there about other gods? Is it the thrill of wickedness and the controlling power, that you can have power over others, as is practiced in witchcraft?\n\nBut in Christ Jesus we are told to go out and witness, but are cautioned not to be unequally yoked.\n\nWe are also cautioned about marriage with unbelievers.\n\nThe same thing applies here also. I think it requires more tact, since we are to be in the world 🗺 and win the world over without being of the world.\n\nWe are to be innocent as doves whiles wise as serpents, in order to fulfill the great commission.","dt":"2022-08-07T08:02:53","s":["srkr7rbq2f"]}],"32":[{"m":"Hmmm... Can a bride forget her attire?\n\nSuch vivid description.\n\nGod was saying, I am your cover, that which you feel and experience, for which you think you are great and you are in charge of the happenings of your life... Your successes and all...\n\nI am actually behind it. Like the attire of a bride 👰, God was their glory and beauty.","dt":"2024-10-12T11:02:43","s":["f4ynvk88c5"]},{"m":"He was their cover, their beauty, their apparel, yet they walk on in shame; they choose the darkness and nakedness and once more shame.","dt":"2026-08-14T05:17:17","s":["6o0etgbs3r"]}],"27":[{"m":"The way God debunks and utterly destroys and exposes the foolishness of idol worship is so apt.","dt":"2024-10-12T10:59:57","s":["4usvovctih"]}],"28":[{"m":"Numerous","dt":"2024-10-11T19:46:29","s":["2j2v5sgq04"]}]},"3":{"3":[{"m":"😊 🤭... What does that look like... A whore's forehead.\n\nAm sure it's that look of defiance and stubbornness.","dt":"2022-08-07T08:04:49","s":["66183dk6k1"]}],"8":[{"m":"Such imagery, such practical storytelling to illustrate his point.\n\nGood example of how to teach using emotional word pictures.","dt":"2024-10-12T11:37:10","s":["kec4oupcuc"]}],"15":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-01-24T12:06:47","s":["oot2qmwa50"]}]},"4":{"3":[{"m":"Sow not among thorns.","dt":"2022-08-08T06:26:19","s":["o7awnk67r4"]}],"10":[{"m":"This reminds me of the lying spirit sent in the times of Ahab to bring his destruction.\n\nWas God doing the same thing in this time ⌚?\n\nBut Jeremiah, being a true prophet, was privy to God's real intent and end game.","dt":"2024-10-12T11:44:57","s":["h0hibdev6p"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why would the priest and the prophets wonder, a people who were supposed to foresee events... They are taken by surprise; they had betrayed their purpose and function.","dt":"2026-08-14T05:28:49","s":["b6bx2ldmcq"]},{"m":"Interesting, no wonder the prophets and the priest were surprised and taken aback.\n\nBecause they had heard a word seemingly from the Lord of peace and prosperity, but Jeremiah knew otherwise, and he realized how the Lord was deceiving them.","dt":"2026-08-14T05:42:04","s":["p92qks7nzt"]}]},"5":{"1":[{"m":"Really, was it that bad? That not one righteous person.\n\nThe story of Lot in Sodom comes to mind.\n\nWhat can account for such? One possibility is when injustice prevails and there seems to be no reward for doing right and obeying the laws.\n\nThe psalmist foresaw this and said:\n\nPsalms 125:3 NIV\nThe scepter of the wicked will not remain over the land allotted to the righteous, for then the righteous might use their hands to do evil. 😈\n\nWe have to keep praying and staying under God's grace. We are all fallible and have a breaking point, no matter how righteous we may seem to be.\n\nBecause of this God makes provision in the New Testament with these promises.\n\nThe days shall be cut short, and there is no temptation...\n\nMatthew 24:22 KJV\nAnd except those days should be shortened, there should no flesh be saved: but for the elect's sake those days shall be shortened.\n\n1 Corinthians 10:13 KJV\nThere hath no temptation taken you but such as is common to man: but God is faithful, who will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape, that ye may be able to bear it.","dt":"2022-08-08T07:42:45","s":["has3jrgjp8"]},{"m":"Was this figurative or was this literally true?\n\nI mean, it had happened before in Sodom and Gomorrah, where up to 5 righteous people were not found.","dt":"2024-10-13T05:54:01","s":["210l8inctx"]}],"30":[{"m":"You would think 🤔 he was talking of our times today in 2024...\n\nSo many false prophets, and sadly God's people love it so.","dt":"2024-10-14T06:20:42","s":["63u5wqe8sa"]}],"12":[{"m":"They said it was the Lord that blessed them and prospered them.\n\nSo they knew he could do them no harm. Oh, how wrong they were.\n\nBut for them to come to this point... Their new gods felt more like the real deal than Jehovah... Because these gods more likely appealed to their flesh and senses and thus felt more real.","dt":"2026-08-14T06:07:35","s":["03c8pnfecn"]}],"19":[{"m":"Hm... Interesting comparisons.","dt":"2022-08-08T07:26:02","s":["g9mdq14k0s"]}]},"7":{"3":[{"m":"Very interesting instruction here... Stand not on the streets or where the harlots and brawlers are lined up.\n\nNo, stand at the entryway to the temple 🏛.\n\nThat is how backslidden the nation had become.","dt":"2022-08-10T00:38:18","s":["0lpp1nf3ko"]}]},"8":{"7":[{"m":"What times are we living in today?","dt":"2022-08-10T00:49:06","s":["pvk7399msh"]}],"14":[{"m":"This was going to be the reaction of the people when God finally destroyed them out of their land, yet the Bible writes this verse in the present tense, as if it had already happened and the people lament in real time.\n\nBut that was going to be their fate in the near future. The Bible is an interesting masterpiece.","dt":"2026-08-15T06:11:11","s":["u9j55s36i7"]}]},"9":{"23":[{"m":"Amen...\n\nEven though his judgement had come upon Israel 🇮🇱, he reminds them first of all of his loving kindness...\n\nGod is so balanced ⚖... Exercising all these attributes as appropriate per the situation.\n\nHe exercises all these in the earth 🌎. This again begs the question: why is heaven and the spirit realm and world so earth conscious?\n\nThere is something to the earth and man.\n\nNo wonder earth is the only habitable planet 🌏 in our galaxy 🌌.\n\nAnd man is the very image of God.\n\nNo wonder through deception 😞 the enemy reigns here. There is something... This bears more pondering.","dt":"2022-08-10T08:10:44","s":["03sbyjrbg8"]},{"m":"I believe Paul the Apostle quoted this verse in one of his writings:\n\n1 Corinthians 1:31 KJV\nThat, according as it is written, He that glorieth, let him glory in the Lord.","dt":"2026-08-15T06:24:39","s":["an00um09x6"]}],"26":[{"m":"Interesting connotation.\n\nPhysical circumcision was a sign of sanctification.\n\nBut here we have Israel, who are physically circumcised yet are unholy, and the Gentiles, also unholy but not physically circumcised.\n\nHere God says, in reality you are both the same, and Israel, though physically circumcised, are uncircumcised in their hearts.","dt":"2024-10-14T07:32:36","s":["oypaaaw21s"]},{"m":"Truth","dt":"2026-08-15T17:24:33","s":["29e2nl2et9"]}]},"10":{"5":[{"m":"Do not be afraid of them — they cannot do evil... This verse must be pondered over.","dt":"2021-10-25T06:28:39","s":["giotkpep95"]},{"m":"Paul says the same things... That to us an idol is nothing.\n\nHere we are told they cannot do evil 😈 nor good.","dt":"2022-08-11T07:29:17","s":["yljtz9vgt5"]}],"8":[{"m":"A worthless doctrine??? 😳 What does this mean?","dt":"2021-10-25T06:45:47","s":["9vwwf84yom"]}],"16":[{"m":"Israel is the tribe of his inheritance.","dt":"2021-10-25T06:49:39","s":["bl314ij88t"]}],"23":[{"m":"So true...\n\nBecause in all of human history, when left alone we act so stupidly, even to our own hurt.\n\nWho does that? Who bites off his own tongue 😝 or shoots himself in the foot?\n\nThere is a species that does that.\n\nMan","dt":"2022-08-11T07:38:39","s":["vkc3eqk0se"]}]},"11":{"4":[{"m":"We cannot out-advance the commandments of God.\n\nThis covenant was signed when they came out of Egypt, almost getting to a millennium, and God called it to remembrance and expected them to stay with it.\n\nTime, advancements and tech ⚙ could not fade out God or his commandments.","dt":"2022-08-12T06:49:28","s":["aam1p0gktf"]}],"9":[{"m":"How come in the reading of the words of the Bible specifically, the Spirit gives understanding, as compared to reading other books?","dt":"2021-10-25T07:22:36","s":["nxhpikidlp"]}],"21":[{"m":"Anathoth, a land of Levites, a holy land, and yet they plot the evil of the prophet Jeremiah.\n\nIf the Lord had not been merciful to deliver Jeremiah and even reveal this evil to him, he would not have known.","dt":"2022-08-12T07:33:53","s":["sgps3xs2pv"]},{"m":"Anathoth was supposed to be the land reserved for the Levites, and yet they were the very people devising evil against Jeremiah for prophesying truth to them...\n\nInteresting","dt":"2024-10-15T06:52:30","s":["e5g0j0zf6o"]}],"6":[{"m":"Jeremiah was to walk all the streets of Jerusalem and Judah proclaiming the word of the Lord. This reminds me of when we used to do dawn broadcasts as young men and women in our late teens, 18-19. What we were doing is not very far-fetched at all from what Jeremiah was doing.\n\nJeremiah is a great and well-known prophet of God even in our times, so his works seem huge, but he was about 17, according to some scholars, when God called him.\n\nAnd he was to fill the nation with his words, and that is exactly what he did. Imagine young Jeremiah preaching the word; it seemed ordinary and even annoying, rising up early and warning the people of God.\n\nWe did the same thing in our youth, and fast forward, here we are. For Jeremiah, fast forward, his words are still living with us and warning us of the grace and wrath of God.","dt":"2026-08-16T06:43:41","s":["c4ydbnc183"]}],"14":[{"m":"Two things:\n1. Why is Baal called a shameful thing?\n\n2. There is a time to cry out to God that he will hear; there is a time when he will not hear, and in this context, in the time of their trouble, he will not hear.","dt":"2021-10-25T07:25:39","s":["nhl7pm8rqz"]}]},"12":{"1":[{"m":"This is a very valid question 🙋.\n\nAnd the response is similar to the response of God to Job.\n\nHe did not directly answer the question, but made him understand that it was even worse than he thought.","dt":"2022-08-12T09:51:28","s":["ntexr3u1bu"]}],"10":[{"m":"I thought, how come these pastors are behaving this way if it is God who called them?\n\nBut herein the free will and choice of man is revealed. And we are not told these pastors were called by God as in Jeremiah's case.\n\nThey were called by the systems and structures set up.\n\nJust like in the New Testament, it says that if any desires to be a bishop...\n\n1 Timothy 3:1 KJV\nThis is a true saying, If a man desire the office of a bishop, he desireth a good work.\n\nIt is purely a desire, but of course there are those God himself directly calls.","dt":"2022-08-12T09:56:34","s":["r6v9lfkpyi"]},{"m":"Hmm, sad.","dt":"2024-10-15T07:03:04","s":["3z7tefge9r"]}]},"14":{"22":[{"m":"The argument can be made that the heathen gods give them showers and do similar to what God does, as we see in the case of Moses against the wise men of Egypt.\n\nBut when the contest begins, then we see that the power of the heathen gods is rendered useless.\n\nIn that God is proven supreme over all and as the one true God. Without this, the curious acts of the wicked idols will confuse the mind of the novice believer.","dt":"2026-08-19T20:09:20","s":["vhyogguntd"]}],"14":[{"m":"So the prophets were seeing alright and hearing alright, but it was after their own fantasies and the deceit of their hearts.\n\nYet they did not know it and presumed to prophesy for the Lord.\n\nIt was a similar thing in the days of Micaiah; the prophets prophesied lies to the detriment and death of Ahab.","dt":"2026-08-19T09:12:51","s":["v5clabu28a"]}],"18":[{"m":"To prophesy ill concerning the people is one thing, but to do so against the other prophets and leaders — the priests — is another ball game, then the rulers and king.\n\nAnyone who has done that is eventually conspired against and most times killed; talk of John the Baptist, talk of Jesus.","dt":"2026-08-19T20:05:03","s":["m6kxy3dv1q"]}]},"15":{"1":[{"m":"Why Moses and Samuel...\n\nHmm... So there are men whom God has respect for.\n\nJust like the way when you mess up and you have to apologize, you look for people whom the other party greatly respects.\n\nHere God says, these two great intercessors I respect, they could move my heart to change towards an entire nation many times.\n\nBut this time not even they combined can change my mind.\n\nEither one of them could have changed God's mind, but so grievous is the offense that both of them will yield no results.","dt":"2022-08-13T06:34:52","s":["2bv8aqf5nb"]}],"4":[{"m":"This man of whom it is spoken here was actually forgiven of his sins, because he repented eventually, but the consequences of his sins needed to happen still.","dt":"2024-10-16T13:02:18","s":["3w3akdj6ln"]},{"m":"This prophecy was in the times of Josiah, and we read earlier that Manasseh repented, but his wicked sins could not be blotted out despite his repentance and restoration to his throne by God after.\n\nHis wickedness had repercussions, and that could not be blotted out.\n\nMany times in the Old Testament we see the generosity and grace of God. When men most wicked, like Ahab and Manasseh, repented, he even forgave them and restored or pardoned them.\n\nGod is that gracious even to the wicked, how much more the righteous sons — if only they will acknowledge their wrongs and repent.","dt":"2026-08-19T20:14:18","s":["mov3lhvsb1"]}],"21":[{"m":"After having said this, you'd expect that things would fall in place beautifully for Jeremiah... Not too long after, he was arrested, cast in a pit to die.\n\nHe himself confessed that it was like God had deceived him.\n\nJeremiah 20:7 KJV\nO Lord, thou hast deceived me, and I was deceived: thou art stronger than I, and hast prevailed: I am in derision daily, every one mocketh me.\n\nBut in the end he was set free and was not taken in the captivity.","dt":"2022-08-13T06:48:19","s":["wtrdd1dxno"]}]},"16":{"3":[{"m":"Privileged information led to abstinence... In the short term Jeremiah seemed a fool and late in life...\n\nBut his wisdom was to be made known in the years to come, when destruction came upon all.","dt":"2024-10-16T13:07:59","s":["v6zo82gx54"]}],"9":[{"m":"God had been speaking of doom all these years, yet nothing happened.\n\nTo the extent that the people even made fun of the coming of the Lord:\n\nJeremiah 17:15 KJV\nBehold, they say unto me, Where is the word of the Lord? let it come now.\n\nBut here God gives a specific date... In your lifetime.\nSame thing for Abraham... He promised Isaac, and when the man was now 99 years, God gave a date.\n\nCould it be that some promises of God we think have delayed have not? It could just be that God has not given us the date yet.","dt":"2022-08-13T06:55:28","s":["ozu9hsvqwy"]}]},"18":{"11":[{"m":"Like a potter or craftsman framing a device, the Lord was framing evil against this people, but like the potter, if they repent of their sins, God will change what he was framing against them to frame good towards them.\n\nPreviously I thought the potter's story was that of God working on one's destiny, but then things went wrong in the hands of God. It made me wonder how an all-powerful God can have things go wrong in his hand; it made me doubt HIM a bit.\n\nTill I realised things going wrong in the hands of GOD was not a GOD problem, but man in our many schemes go contrary to the word of God, but he, God, is able to restore, like the potter is able to restore a damaged product.","dt":"2026-08-21T05:44:29","s":["5u1zvmuswg"]}],"17":[{"m":"This is very similar to an earlier commentary, where in the time of trouble there is no time to be helped. The time for help is over in the time of trouble.","dt":"2021-10-28T06:37:16","s":["8lo7a131ux"]}],"18":[{"m":"I won't be surprised God revealed these wicked devices to Jeremiah as before.","dt":"2022-08-13T07:52:48","s":["youmtssf0d"]}],"21":[{"m":"This prayer that Jeremiah prayed was from a position of privileged information.\n\nHe knew the coming drought and captivity and prayed in that regard.\n\nSo it's not just a wishy prayer, but one in line with prophecy.","dt":"2022-08-13T07:51:33","s":["z99evmplb4"]}],"23":[{"m":"It is so painful when good is recompensed with evil.\n\nBy virtue of being a prophet, he saw through their schemes.\n\nPeople he had just preserved their lives through his prayer now sought for his own.","dt":"2024-10-17T08:22:02","s":["aj2wxtiyj1"]}],"4":[{"m":"How come he got there just in time to see the clay marred?\n\nThat was the hand of God at work,\n\nOr he was literally there the whole day, and at just the point where the clay was marred, the word of the Lord came to him.","dt":"2024-10-17T07:36:56","s":["i8fd18be92"]}]},"19":{"14":[{"m":"I'm getting the feeling that Jeremiah would soon be ambushed because of the constant bad news and chastisement of the sins of the people.\n\nWe see same in our world today; we hate correction, and Christianity is now being persecuted in the world today.\n\nThe voice of reason and truth is being silenced.","dt":"2024-10-17T08:26:03","s":["vlw1i2ga94"]}],"15":[{"m":"Isn't it interesting that these prophecies were given in no other place than the house of God? He spoke to the people of God in the house of God, yet they hated him.\n\nIf it was that he prophesied to strangers and they hated him, fair enough, but he prophesied to God's people and his children and they hated him.\n\nSometimes, as in this case, he prophesied in the church and the hatred was even more.","dt":"2026-08-21T06:08:35","s":["eysl7icu47"]}]},"20":{"2":[{"m":"It is well... Being imprisoned for the truth.","dt":"2022-08-13T08:03:09","s":["pyeuk1680j"]}],"18":[{"m":"Jeremiah really suffered and was persecuted sore for him to have prayed this way.","dt":"2024-10-17T08:29:51","s":["3xajs7trlj"]},{"m":"This prayer in so many respects is like the prayer and wishes of JOB.\n\nJob 3:3: \"Let the day perish on which I was born, and the night that said, 'A man is conceived.'\"\n\nJob 3:11: \"Why did I not die at birth, come out from the womb and expire?\"\n\nJob 3:16: \"Or why was I not as a hidden stillborn child, as infants who never see the light?\"\n\nIndeed the whole chapter 3 was him cursing his birth and his very existence.","dt":"2026-08-21T06:33:18","s":["hkoympxl2y"]}],"11":[{"m":"But the Lord is with me, despite what my enemies seek for my soul.\n\nTo bring to destruction.","dt":"2022-08-13T13:13:11","s":["pq5obwess"]}]},"21":{"10":[{"m":"It really takes boldness to say these things.\n\nJeremiah could have been slain for speaking so boldly to the kings and rulers.\n\nHe spoke the truth to their face, that they will die.","dt":"2024-10-17T08:32:36","s":["ja48c3v86n"]}]},"22":{"2":[{"m":"Were they sitting on the literal throne that David sat on — just wondering. Of course, by ascending the throne as king the expression is used, but it is possible they sat also on the literal throne. I remember Solomon building a formidable throne that the Bible describes as there being none like it.\n\nI wonder if it replaced David's? Logically it did. It is implied, though not stated, but obviously.","dt":"2026-08-21T06:42:46","s":["7pgh9qvxvz","1szhjf004t"]}],"4":[{"m":"This is the 2nd time Jeremiah has prophesied thus. Say the same things.","dt":"2022-08-13T13:39:21","s":["k51ph88thc"]}],"12":[{"m":"So this prophecy was after the death of Josiah and in the times of the reign of his son.\n\nHe was carried away captive because of his wicked ways.","dt":"2024-10-17T13:59:00","s":["u6fde3luo0"]}],"19":[{"m":"Did Jeremiah really go and say this? This was literally suicide; which king would hear this and ignore it, or which servant of a royal or of the king's guards will hear this and let it pass?\n\nEven if the king ignored such insult, definitely not his servants and courtiers.","dt":"2024-10-17T14:01:47","s":["jrekixiyk3"]}],"21":[{"m":"Until we learn to self-humble, we would go on in wrongdoings and not repent.\n\nAnd end up self-destructing.\n\nIt is in humility that we obtain mercy to change and do better.\n\nIt is better to seek God in humility in our prosperity than to go down because of our evil ways and sin and end up humbled anyways, but with shame.","dt":"2022-08-13T13:48:18","s":["6hrgsroh5h"]}],"29":[{"m":"😢 What a curse 🤬... The earth being called to witness.","dt":"2022-08-13T13:49:45","s":["epas011vrg"]}],"30":[{"m":"It seemed these particular prophecies were cried out not to the animate but to the inanimate, and yet it did hear.\n\nReminds me so much of when Jesus spoke to the fig tree.","dt":"2024-10-17T14:04:25","s":["byg0iy8rwx"]}]},"23":{"35":[{"m":"I'm not quite getting this verse, though the Message translations seem to bring out the meaning better.","dt":"2022-08-13T14:06:19","s":["5ff9hn5au2"]}],"6":[{"m":"This is none other than the Messiah.\n\nThe word translated LORD here is YAHWEH, i.e. the covenant name of God.\n\nNo human king 👑 can take upon himself the name Yahweh except the I Am himself.","dt":"2024-10-18T14:33:28","s":["745a4ao3ls"]}],"10":[{"m":"So sin and wickedness affect nature and the dwelling places of these men.\n\nSo the dwelling places of the wicked will vomit themselves out of the way.","dt":"2026-08-22T06:34:21","s":["4cwr4sd8mu"]}],"20":[{"m":"So these prophets did not wait on the Lord to hear his counsel. They prophesy lies 🤥.\n\nIf only they had waited. But I guess it is not in them to speak the truth, so they wait not.","dt":"2022-08-13T14:01:56","s":["eskiuyzmcr"]}]},"24":{"5":[{"m":"God is so just; he warned the people, but they will not listen 👂.\n\nYet he caused some to be taken captive to Babylon, not to punish them further, but for their good.\n\nLikely he caused a number of his righteous ones to survive, as we see with Daniel and his friends, for instance.","dt":"2024-10-18T14:46:22","s":["t9vw4fk09o"]}],"6":[{"m":"Sometimes we just need to pray to God for a new heart, because we in ourselves are so vile and difficult to change.\n\nLord, give us a new heart I pray, a new heart, Lord, I pray 🙏","dt":"2022-08-13T14:08:03","s":["vucmz2najo"]}],"10":[{"m":"It seems from this verse that the Lord divided the captives in two.\n\nThe righteous to Babylon for their good, and the wicked to remain in Judah and to Egypt for the overthrow.","dt":"2024-10-18T14:49:37","s":["f26p3davyh"]}]},"25":{"8":[{"m":"Many people wonder why God, if he is all good, doesn't prevent evil but allows it to happen and then punishes evil and rewards the good.\n\nIt is because that is the current regime we are in and under.\n\nThe regime of man in control of his own governance.\n\nHowever, a time is going to come under the direct rulership of God where good prevails and evil is prevented from even happening.\n\nIndeed this question 🙋 is a good one and futuristic.\n\nWe will have the opportunity to compare the two governments and appreciate which is indeed best.","dt":"2024-10-18T14:53:42","s":["5kefi4mnmz"]}],"17":[{"m":"How did he cause them to drink 🍻 in the vision?","dt":"2022-08-13T14:11:55","s":["z5u49j4ajv"]}],"28":[{"m":"Wait oo 😩... Was God expecting them to really take and drink 🍻 and partake in the prophetic symbolism of their own demise?\n\nBut God knew they won't, so he had his own plan of compelling them to drink.","dt":"2024-10-18T14:57:18","s":["2s9fltclw5"]}],"29":[{"m":"Mercy, mercy, but how can there be mercy at this time, when even his own children drank of the cup of his fury?","dt":"2022-08-13T14:13:33","s":["nvf7uxb3wc"]}],"26":[{"m":"God's punishment was upon all the earth 🌎... Moving from nation to nation, not just Palestine and the Middle East as I used to think.\n\nSo if God has sent his punishment upon the whole earth 🌎 before, and not once but time and again, what makes us think that this is far off in this our time, when the world 🗺 is one global connected village?\n\nJust that because of the connectivity, wars easily become global, and so will the end time war which God would wage, and again, because of how connected we have become, his words as taught in the book of Revelations are no longer left to the imagination, as they carry literal meanings and are literally possible in our time and with our tech.","dt":"2024-10-18T15:00:47","s":["yfjgyrk56h"]}],"33":[{"m":"This seems more futuristic and fits the Armageddon more than God's punishment of nations in Jeremiah's day.","dt":"2024-10-18T15:07:11","s":["ccbwgx4dcg"]}]},"26":{"3":[{"m":"GOD IS SO MERCIFUL. The master communicator he is.\n\nHe did everything to prevent Israel from going into captivity.","dt":"2022-08-13T14:25:10","s":["0pnb06lwpu"]},{"m":"Even up until the last moments God wanted to save them and rescue them from the coming wrath.\n\nHowever, I wonder why God continued to warn them when he himself had prophesied that he would take them into captivity.\n\nI believe it was to fulfill all righteousness and leave them without excuse.\n\nWe see from the wording of the verse that it was to fulfill all righteousness, because he says\n\n\"if so be they will hearken...\"","dt":"2024-10-19T09:44:08","s":["8yg1y5im6d"]}],"9":[{"m":"God specifically told him not to diminish what he was about to say, only for him to be arrested, and God did nothing about it nor stopped it.\n\nObedience to God's word doesn't always exempt you from its negative consequences.\n\nI have had such moments in my life, and the consequences were not the best.\n\nI then began to gradually be weary 😩 of God subconsciously without even knowing.\n\nEventually I backslid and learnt my lesson the hard way, that the tough reproaches we face 😔 because of God and the hard training in our walking with God are far better than any abundance or pleasures the world has to offer.","dt":"2024-10-19T09:49:33","s":["uc1dhskln8"]}],"16":[{"m":"IS IT NOT FUNNY that the politicians rather appealed to the religious leaders for pardon 🙏?\n\nThey were more reasonable than the priest and saw the sense and good in what Jeremiah was saying.\n\nHe was not worthy of death ☠, but the priests thought 💭 otherwise.\n\nThis is just like Jesus; Pilate saw him not worthy of death, but the high priests and his team saw otherwise.","dt":"2022-08-15T06:53:04","s":["mphp83682t"]},{"m":"What an irony, that it took the princes, i.e. the politicians, to bring the voice of reason to the priests and the prophets, who were the religious leaders — what an irony indeed.","dt":"2024-10-19T09:51:52","s":["dlm3mg72bz"]}],"19":[{"m":"The politicians were more sensible and spiritually honest and humble than the priest and prophets — what an irony.","dt":"2026-08-23T08:33:10.263Z","s":["l4j8laoaks"]}],"23":[{"m":"Was this verse a counter to the first illustration, that a certain precedent had also been set historically, where a man who claimed to have prophesied in the name of the Lord was murdered by the king?\n\nSo they were justified in killing Jeremiah?","dt":"2024-10-19T10:05:29","s":["jz8tddfd0p"]}]},"27":{"3":[{"m":"So Jeremiah indeed prophesied to nations and to kingdoms.","dt":"2024-10-19T10:06:38","s":["j205vg33xo"]}],"6":[{"m":"There are times when a man seems invincible and almost godlike.\n\nI mean, God was so with Nebuchadnezzar that even the beasts of the field serve him.\n\nLiterally everything was at his beck and call, and things fell in place and worked out for him.\n\nNo wonder he thought he was a god.\n\nWhen we come to that point in life where things work for our good and it's like we have the touch of Midas... Let's remember heaven is smiling at us, and we ought to give God the glory.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:03:30","s":["w4po3mjacq"]}],"9":[{"m":"This Jeremiah had just barely escaped death threats, and indeed he himself was ready to die 🎲 if that was his end.\n\nNow here he goes again. I can imagine the difficulty in having to face the prospects of death and not knowing when next God was going to come up with another life-threatening message.\n\nNo wonder God told him to set his face like a flint and be strong 💪.\n\nThese death threats here were very real, because other prophets before him had prophesied such and died.\n\nEven the one who sought asylum in another country was tracked down and brought back to die.\n\nThis was how determined King Jehoiakim was to bring down any opposition to his throne.\n\nHe did not want any negative news to dampen the spirit of his people.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:05:53","s":["3fjyc54rch"]},{"m":"So everyone has their prophets; the heathen nations also have their prophets and fortune tellers.\n\nTherefore, the demonstration of power is not the only proof of GOD, lest anyone also who shows power will be misconstrued as coming from GOD.","dt":"2026-08-24T05:57:31.236Z","s":["v9eyj1h076"]}],"11":[{"m":"So God did not just out of the blue bring the nations under bondage to Nebuchadnezzar; he forewarned them.\n\nHe even gave them the opportunity for self-preservation.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:07:54","s":["pbe1084gwa"]}],"16":[{"m":"Virtually every strategic leader was given the message. Jeremiah was using all possible means to get his message across and save his people.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:17:59","s":["a2f8bfiy5s"]}],"22":[{"m":"Oh Lord God, who is praying for Africa 🌍 and our nations, for restoration of that which the nations have looted and plundered from us?\n\nSend help, Lord; help, you send help 😣","dt":"2022-08-15T07:20:24","s":["l211b3l9ea"]},{"m":"The temple was such a rich source of wealth for Israel.\n\nIt was such a strong 💪 national symbol for them.\n\nLittle wonder when the nation was being built the gold and other treasures were returned.","dt":"2024-10-19T10:24:11","s":["m8ucykzooc"]},{"m":"Now I am wondering, since there were so many prophets, some prophesying the safety of Judah and others its exile, how were the ruling class supposed to determine who was really speaking for GOD? Just wondering.","dt":"2026-08-24T06:24:45.506Z","s":["00fswkqtm6"]}]},"28":{"10":[{"m":"Was Jeremiah carrying this yoke still around?\n\nIt wasn't easy to be a prophet of old, carrying with you the burdens and symbols of your prophecies.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:23:21","s":["mcjov8zon3"]}],"14":[{"m":"The beast also. The same point is re-emphasized here.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:41:42","s":["hh3f9dkpuc"]}],"16":[{"m":"And it happened.\n\nMy only challenge with Hananiah... Why would you deliberately forge a lie 🤥?\n\nI mean, it's so cruel, but human nature.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:41:11","s":["aqyzh9ee8z"]}],"17":[{"m":"So what if Jeremiah hadn't prophesied his death?\n\nMany would have thought it a natural death.\n\nHow many deaths occasioned by rebellion and misrepresentation of God have taken lives, and many took it for death by natural causes?","dt":"2024-10-19T10:28:38","s":["qeyb0p6s0w"]}],"15":[{"m":"The prophet said to the prophet — interesting, but since he was false, why was he being called a prophet? Oh, maybe the title had come to stay, or he used to prophesy accurately in time past.\n\nThis makes me wonder, was Hananiah just being dubious, or he genuinely was hearing voices, voices of his own heart or a deceptive spirit which he thought were GOD's?\n\nWe ought therefore to be careful, because in an attempt to represent GOD, we can be genuinely wrong.","dt":"2026-08-24T06:35:34.815Z","s":["thj7e8v0ru"]}],"11":[{"m":"Does that mean Jeremiah was carrying this yoke on his head everywhere he went?","dt":"2024-10-19T10:26:09","s":["x2k9qnsr1t"]}]},"29":{"10":[{"m":"So if anything at all, the people who want to return should pray for long life, so when the seventy years are over, they can come back in line with God's word.\n\nOh Lord, let me not stray off and be outside your domain because of lack of foresight.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:48:51","s":["byrx4ymwxt"]}],"23":[{"m":"Of their many sins, I think the main thing was that they prophesied lies in the name of the Lord.\n\nYou can almost tell from God's tonations.","dt":"2022-08-15T07:58:58","s":["75rju7rort"]}],"32":[{"m":"The judgements beginning from the house of the Lord had started.","dt":"2022-08-15T08:01:36","s":["6s70356lej"]},{"m":"The Lord specifically punished false prophets because what they said not only tarnished the image of GOD, but it led entire nations and rulers astray, thus affecting the ordinary people.\n\nIn this case the nation listened to the false prophets and myriads died, so the Lord punished all those false prophets.\n\nWe see the same things today; many have caused the people of GOD to die in their sins because they excuse them, and have caused many to die in their sickness because they lied to them that they had been healed when they had not.\n\nThe Lord will not hold them guiltless, for He is GOD and He is Judge.","dt":"2026-08-24T06:52:16.419Z","s":["msom764iuw"]}],"4":[{"m":"The war and takeover of Judah seemed random, the killing of the people when Nebuchadnezzar took over the nations seemed arbitrary, yet in all of it GOD had prepared for himself a remnant to survive him and hold true his word.\n\nI wonder, though, what criteria the Lord used to select his elect: was it covenant, was it some ancient pact their father made, and/or was it according to his own pre-ordination and future plans for future generations?\n\nI believe all these applied.","dt":"2026-08-24T06:41:34.857Z","s":["yufltw4l1a"]}],"9":[{"m":"The Lord had not sent them, so who did? The Lord did not speak to them, so whom were they hearing?","dt":"2026-08-24T06:43:45.127Z","s":["jeh2aj5oiv"]}]},"30":{"9":[{"m":"Was this in reference to the Christ and David literally being raised up?","dt":"2022-08-15T08:04:24","s":["om399qwhhy"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why is God explaining himself? He had forewarned these people.\n\nBut it's understandable; it's the way of love.\n\nThese were his children 🧒 👪.\n\nI now understand when God says Israel is his firstborn.\n\nAnd how that, though he had completely destroyed other nations, he only punished Israel as deserved, but unfairly left a remnant.\n\nBut hey, you can't say it's unfair, these are his children and his nation.\n\nThis beautifully translates to the New Testament: every believer is a child 🧒 of God, and he, God, watches over us and helps us.\n\nEven in our backslidden state he draws us to him.","dt":"2022-08-15T08:13:17","s":["4zp42ws1k3"]}]},"31":{"4":[{"m":"She was no virgin, but Israel had been pronounced to be one.","dt":"2024-10-22T13:19:27","s":["ub42q9d8n8"]}],"15":[{"m":"This referred to the times of restoration after Ramah had suffered much, but the Lord was to restore them.\n\nNow fast forward, in the New Testament it is repeated as prophecy relevant to the time...\n\nThere is nothing new under the sun ☀.\n\nGod is so deep, and such hidden wisdom even in his words.\n\nIt's just like when God speaks to you through the pages of the book 📙. Though contextually it's for a certain time.\n\nYet practically it also speaks to you.","dt":"2022-08-15T08:22:58","s":["oxxrhljppq"]}],"22":[{"m":"And in our world today, indeed we have women protecting men and taking care of them literally.","dt":"2024-10-22T19:12:04","s":["65k9vafl36"]}],"33":[{"m":"Was not this promise made also in the book of Ezekiel?\n\nEzekiel 36:26 KJV\nA new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.\n\nYes, it is the same promise.","dt":"2026-08-25T09:40:24.634Z","s":["7o8dadc7xu"]}],"37":[{"m":"Such a strong 💪 covenant Israel has and knows they have.\n\nAnd God was not afraid 😨 they will misbehave, because if they did, he will chastise them sore.","dt":"2024-10-22T19:32:22","s":["hb2yage367"]}]},"32":{"3":[{"m":"Such proclamations from Jeremiah were not good politically... He was spreading fear and panic and possible treason.\n\nYet he was speaking the truth from God. For he showed them the way out of trouble, but they would not heed.","dt":"2022-08-16T07:41:16","s":["m9ypqyfnbv"]}],"5":[{"m":"I guess this was to say until I grant him pardon and cause his release.\n\nBecause of the gap between these events, you might not see the hand of God at work.\n\nThat is the nature of the spiritual: it's eternal, so we in time tend to forget such things.\n\nThat is why we are often urged to write these things down, so we mortals who live in time can follow it and understand it.","dt":"2022-08-16T07:44:08","s":["okm50cuedu"]}],"17":[{"m":"The things of God and the Spirit are interesting.\n\nJeremiah spoke boldly in vs 15. His was to say what God said to say, and separate himself from how unbelievable and possibly stupid it sounds.\n\nThis is seen in verse 17, when his true struggles and heart are revealed in his prayer.\n\nYou can see Jeremiah fighting hard to not believe.\n\nSo God assures him: is there anything too hard for him?","dt":"2022-08-16T07:51:57","s":["jt6q482glw"]}],"33":[{"m":"Because of their mass idolatry, God wiped them from his sight as a nation.\n\nThis was the state of the continent of Africa 🌍. We did not have an alternative; we only knew to worship other gods.\n\nUntil God in his great mercy brought us the gospel, for He saw how great a people we will be to champion the gospel of Jesus.","dt":"2022-08-16T07:56:48","s":["1ali3jih21"]}],"37":[{"m":"God indeed knows and plans out the end from the beginning.\n\nEven in his whirlwind 🍃 like fury he had a redemption plan.","dt":"2022-08-16T07:58:05","s":["njd4aopaph"]}],"44":[{"m":"And it did happen many times over, even up to today.\n\nAnd God says he would give them a heart that would obey him forever.\n\nSo there is a state of heart that is geared towards God and good.\n\nYou know how sometimes we wish to do what is right but just can't, because we are broken 💔 and of the sinful nature 🏞.\n\nThis God will take away and give us a new heart ♥","dt":"2022-08-16T08:00:37","s":["x4dujp8icz"]}],"4":[{"m":"He was going to see the great king Nebuchadnezzar face to face, and that was going to be one of the last things he sees.\n\nNebuchadnezzar knows how to make a statement. It was no ordinary thing to come into his presence and to see his face.","dt":"2026-08-26T05:59:18.390Z","s":["vetlsnq2xq"]}],"9":[{"m":"He did this knowing full well Judah was going into captivity. But this was a sign of faith that his people would come back from captivity.\n\nThis indeed was great faith.","dt":"2026-08-26T06:01:41.340Z","s":["bowuxni7n3"]}],"29":[{"m":"Their idolatry was in the open, in the full glare of the GOD of heavens, as if to provoke him.\n\nThey set up their idolatry upon their roofs in the direct glare of GOD of the heavens. True, GOD is omnipresent, but in a figurative sense they were showing their idolatry directly to GOD. And they cared less.","dt":"2026-08-26T06:06:11.814Z","s":["ai8ewkocuo"]}]},"33":{"7":[{"m":"These words might have been consoling to Jeremiah to know, though it seems unbelievable considering the present circumstances.\n\nI can imagine Jeremiah's pain as he saw the very things he spoke about come to pass.\n\nYou know how painful it can be, and the emotional turmoil of such mixed messages.","dt":"2022-08-16T08:02:52","s":["khla0fyn4d"]}],"15":[{"m":"When I look at all these messianic verses, I begin to wonder, how come they missed Jesus?\n\nMany say it was because they expect the king of righteousness to come and rule and destroy Israel's enemies once and for all.\n\nGood, I understand that, but it also says the Messiah will suffer in a way that doesn't make sense or befit someone of his stature.\n\nA saviour who is almost God-like in his functions couldn't possibly suffer that way. I believe they then began to conjecture the meaning of the suffering part to be more metaphorical than the literal.\n\nBut in this wise they were wrong.\n\nThe Messiah's suffering was literal.\n\nBut either ways, God's plan was for the Messiah to come once to fulfill the suffering part and once more to rule in glory. This resurrection and ascension is what the Jews could not decipher.\n\nEither ways, we both wait — Christians and Jews alike — for the coming of the Messiah.\n\nOne for his first coming and the other for his second and last.\n\nIn like manner, as there are many end-time prophecies, we would witness the plan of God unfold in ways not so predicted and expected by man, especially the seemingly confusing and contradictory portions of scripture.\n\nThose days will be beautiful.","dt":"2024-10-23T08:17:35","s":["9ahqaghebj"]}],"22":[{"m":"Awww... And we are part of that spiritual priesthood.","dt":"2022-08-16T08:09:40","s":["rod78gxadx"]}],"26":[{"m":"It is easy to say that the word of GOD concerned the ancient times and that it was fulfilled in the times of the ancients.\n\nBut we see many of the things GOD says were not fulfilled and could possibly not be fulfilled in those times.","dt":"2026-08-26T08:17:16.137Z","s":["v69jc7ybho"]}],"21":[{"m":"We see now in our days, as it were, that the throne of David is vacant and non-existent, so then how do we interpret this saying and promise of GOD?\n\nIs GOD lying? No. Then what is it then? It means the throne of David will once more be set up and established, and one from his loins shall sit on it.\n\nWe see Israel being scattered for centuries, and finally now in their gathering the tribes are lost mostly.\n\nSo then how do we know who the descendants of David are, not just Judah but specifically of David? How can this word be truly fulfilled?\n\nWill GOD come down and set up a man as the true heir of David by some means? NO.\n\nIt is as if GOD, knowing these times will come and Israel will not be divisible in their tribes, set up a man who never dies, to live forever, a true son of David whose genealogy can be traced, and that son, since he lives forever, will appear on the scene at the right time to reclaim his throne.\n\nHe only waits and bides his time and will come at the right time.\n\nWhen is the right time? When the knowledge of GOD covers the earth as the waters the sea, and all know of the Christ and the gospel.\n\nIt seems that as yet that has not been attained, and the course is on to do so; when that is done and his kingdom ready, he will come.\n\nThis morning I was listening to Rick Warren talk of how many movements have attempted to reach the whole world with the gospel over the centuries, and none has quite gotten it right, always lagging behind the growth of the world and the spread of the gospel.\n\nHe has started a movement to achieve that by 2033, so let's see. But we must hasten the Lord's coming, and by hasten, really it is not of us but of the Lord and of his Spirit.\n\nHe shall, and that real soon.","dt":"2026-08-26T08:13:43.208Z","s":["p8mkb9d6u5"]}],"5":[{"m":"They came to fight in the physical, but they only came to fulfil what GOD had already established in his fury towards them.\n\nIn the natural lay slain bodies of men, but in the spirit raged the anger and the fury of GOD.","dt":"2026-08-26T06:12:14.782Z","s":["2tyh99ge49"]}],"11":[{"m":"As I read this verse, there is this sense of awareness and awakening, that this Jerusalem that is being spoken about here is the real Jerusalem that we see being spoken of every day in the news.\n\nThis prophecy is concerning a real place we are living in in our days. So it means this prophecy can be tested, if it be true or it is just some ancient story and text.\n\nIf the things spoken concerning it come to pass, we can attest to it even if not in our lifetime; the point is it is verifiable.","dt":"2026-08-26T08:03:07.161Z","s":["mkshf4z3zd"]}]},"34":{"2":[{"m":"Oh, again, this work which God had given to Jeremiah was very difficult.\n\nMen of God really go through a lot of impossible things.\nHe, Jeremiah, had suffered so much already.\n\nWas it now, in the middle of battle, that Jeremiah was going to tell Zedekiah that his battle was useless because he would lose?\n\nWas this the time for such statements? Was this the time to weaken the hands of the soldiers and leaders?\n\nThis work was no easy task.","dt":"2022-08-16T08:13:05","s":["eq518i91n9"]}],"14":[{"m":"In their backsliding, God had still not forgotten the laws he made for them.\n\nAnd he was happy they were now obeying them.","dt":"2022-08-16T08:15:16","s":["qq0hjlzpoa"]}],"18":[{"m":"Okay, so it seems the release was something they did by oath, and yet they broke that oath.","dt":"2022-08-16T08:16:38","s":["rj1u7fvl6h"]}]},"35":{"7":[{"m":"God was looking for a worthy example of consistency to make an illustration with, and he found the Rechabites.\n\nMay the good Lord find us when he comes in search of one to use his or her life for an example. Amen","dt":"2024-10-24T07:31:41","s":["b0en7d0l75"]}],"19":[{"m":"Wow... Who were the Rechabites... How were they to survive without owning fields etc.?\n\nWhat was their main occupation?","dt":"2022-08-16T08:30:00","s":["srfxbok0xj"]},{"m":"Wow, what an honour and a covenant.\n\nI wonder where the Rechabites are today though. God being God, I know, will continue to keep them and their generations as he has ISRAEL to this date.","dt":"2024-10-24T07:34:45","s":["4p40zf1fd7"]}]},"36":{"28":[{"m":"Another work? I can imagine how difficult it was to pen 🖋 down the first, and now having to do it all again.\n\nThe dilemmas of men of God.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:00:41","s":["6znllis9k8"]},{"m":"What kind of work is this? In our time we would just copy and paste the same thing and print, but here Jeremiah and Baruch would have to painstakingly record the same things all over again.\n\nInk, feather or whatever writer they used then, and scroll. They used a cut reed in their times, according to Google.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:22:40.809Z","s":["s2r1fjy5oc"]}],"32":[{"m":"So it is this book that we now read.\n\n2ndly, all these words were in the head 🤕 of Jeremiah.\n\nIt must have to be divinely inspired. Not just out of memory.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:03:25","s":["c5xa5iwyzq"]}],"7":[{"m":"The Lord is the only one who is angry and can cause damage, yet pleads with the people to avoid the damage he is about to cause.\n\nHe even tells them how to avoid his wrath and judgement. Indeed, the Lord does not want to destroy his people.\n\nLittle wonder Jonah got frustrated and refused to preach to Nineveh.\n\nI also see the pain of Jeremiah when his people went into captivity despite all the warnings he had given them.\n\nNo wonder he wrote a whole book of Lamentations.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:12:45.779Z","s":["fpdvlgn9b9"]}],"21":[{"m":"There are princes on the outside and there are princes near the king — different levels of intimacy with the corridors of power.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:20:46.389Z","s":["f498ik2l2j"]}],"12":[{"m":"Is this the same Zedekiah who later became king? No, he was not the Zedekiah who became king. The Zedekiah who became king was brother to the current king.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:14:24.942Z","s":["nf6230yczc"]}],"3":[{"m":"GOD really had a long rope and a good heart towards his people. He did all that was humanly possible in diverse ways and literally exhausted all options so his people would be saved, but they would not.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:04:28.887Z","s":["gszct3dh28"]}],"31":[{"m":"He would be killed if he attempted this. But I guess, having survived this long, the Lord would keep him.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:25:14.410Z","s":["70b4kd082m"]}]},"37":{"12":[{"m":"Most versions explain this to mean he went for his portion of inheritance.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:06:16","s":["zngv1bf58y"]}],"21":[{"m":"Wow, the famine had already started. Lord have mercy on us, for a similar fate befalleth our world in these times... 17th August 2022... It has begun ever so subtly.\n\nThe imprisonment became a survival opportunity for Jeremiah.\n\nEven in the famine, the king's 👑 household will be the last to feel it, and this God used to feed his servant.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:09:56","s":["ileduxqvvy"]}]},"38":{"3":[{"m":"The Lord of hosts, the mighty man of war... had by his wisdom and watchers and divine beings on the ground assessed all the data and knew that surely Jerusalem and Judah shall fall.\n\nI believe data on the size of the army of the Chaldeans, other battles to be fought aside Jerusalem, ammunition and supplies left etc. had been provided, and it was obvious Jerusalem would fall.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:13:18","s":["nv1oxouvx6"]}],"5":[{"m":"After all the good Jeremiah had done in warning the king 👑, and at this time that his warnings ⚠ were being fulfilled right before their eyes,\n\nhe allows the leaders to have their way, as such weak-willed politicians tend to be.\n\nWith the truth staring at him, all he needed to do was repent and ask the way out.\n\nHe should have put on ashes and sackcloth and fasted so the Lord has mercy on him.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:16:52","s":["v2s26dpuu9"]},{"m":"Was he not the same king that secretly desired of a word from Jeremiah, yet he wanted not to repent, so turned a deaf ear to the Lord?\n\nNow he hands over Jeremiah to these wicked people, though Jeremiah had pleaded not to be sent back there.\n\nThat request was granted, but for a while, it seemed.","dt":"2024-10-24T07:48:39","s":["gjyxicy4xu"]}],"10":[{"m":"Hmm. This king... He was in a quagmire... Everything was falling apart, so he himself approved something and later another thing else.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:23:55","s":["ylcsrwdqqb"]},{"m":"The game of politics: after having approved the imprisonment of Jeremiah, now he commands his release to a different group of people, to go with thirty men in case there was hindrance.\n\nWhy couldn't or didn't he ask the first group to go release Jeremiah? Because the game of politics must be well played, lest you destroy your kingdom and that which you have built.","dt":"2024-10-24T07:51:16","s":["dvnlx841li"]},{"m":"The same king that agreed for Jeremiah to be put to death, barely days later agreed to have him freed. He who has the ears of the king must be feared.\n\nI see also the pressures of the kingdom. His city and rulership was under threat, and he was going to do all in his power to keep power. He had many voices speaking to him, and he had to, in the midst of the myriads of suggestions, choose what was best.\n\nUneasy lies the head that wears the crown.\n\nI am beginning to understand why he would not heed Jeremiah's words. There were many different voices, including other prophets, saying the opposite.\n\nNot to mention the fact that he was an idolater, and succumbing to Jehovah would mean him worshipping him only.\n\nSo in the corridors of power, the fact that you are right and have the truth does not mean you will be heard. So you have got to be smart and work your way for your truth to be heard and taken.\n\nThis indeed is the corridors of power. The forces are many there.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:47:25.175Z","s":["xyg3tbhwb5"]}],"17":[{"m":"Ah... The way out was given, but it was not to be heeded.\n\nHe was too far down the pit of self-hope and the delusion of kingship to heed this warning.\n\nJeremiah knew by now that they would not heed, but he had to try at least.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:26:04","s":["praxenuwdg"]}],"25":[{"m":"The king's hands and reign was faint and not as it ought to be. Some of his own people, the Jews, had defected to the Chaldeans, and he had to be tactful with the rest of the people who were still with him.\n\nSimilar events happened in David's time, where he had to find a smart way of getting rid of Joab, though Joab was heartless and killed all potential successors.","dt":"2024-10-24T08:06:38","s":["8hzrsx6zdw"]},{"m":"The games of power: kings may have the appearance of omnipotence, but power is indeed fragile and must be handled and harnessed wisely, lest you lose it all.\nIt can be very fragile.\n\nWhen his predecessor was captured (Jehoiakim), he was chained and put in prison; he was suddenly rendered to nothing and indeed made to feel that way. All his resolve and kingliness was taken from him. The point was to render him hopeless.","dt":"2026-08-28T08:56:32.275Z","s":["xtpa0v59gc"]}],"28":[{"m":"Again another strategic imprisonment... i.e. he was in the prison, and by now, after all these years, the Chaldeans might have heard of this prophet who had been prophesying in their favour, or\n\nwhen they invaded the king's house and asked what Jeremiah's crime was, it was told them that he prophesied of this day, and thus they set him free.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:29:05","s":["qrty1fjf7q"]}]},"39":{"9":[{"m":"At this time this man might have felt invincible, and so he was.\n\nFor the God of the whole universe was with him. Little did he know that he was walking 🚶 in the dictates of God.","dt":"2022-08-17T07:56:52","s":["tyz149n2py"]}],"18":[{"m":"Because he trusted in me — Psalm 91.\n\nIt was not everyone who died in the invasion of Jerusalem.\n\nThis above lets us in on one of the criteria for exemption.\n\nI remember reading the many times Israel goes to war, and we are told God was with them and gave them the victory, and yet many people die 🎲...\nSo I ask, what qualifies for one to live and others to die?\n\nI was not expecting any deaths when God was with a nation to war.","dt":"2022-08-17T08:01:15","s":["znm30y57kd"]}],"11":[{"m":"How did he know him? Likely he had heard of his many prophecies over the years, which prophecies had come to pass.\n\nSo he respected the Spirit of GOD with him and honoured him as a true prophet of GOD.\n\nSometimes politicians know how to honour and work with genuine ministers of GOD more than some religious priests and clergy.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:24:48.054Z","s":["jehp12i3j9"]}],"10":[{"m":"Why were the poor of the people given the resources of the wealth to work in it?\n\nBecause they would know how to till and work in it, but lack the skills and complexity to grow it and harness it to have dominion and might for themselves.\n\nThey were the poor of the people.\n\nIt is the same thing even now. Many people have resources and gifts, abilities, but can only work it; they can work it but not grow it and harness it for greatness and influence.\n\nThat is the poor of the people.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:18:47.923Z","s":["pax339lcxx"]}],"16":[{"m":"He helped Jeremiah escape from the pit, and GOD honoured him. Indeed, GOD honoured the righteous who dwelt among the wicked people of the land and kept them according to his many mercies.\n\nThey held high up their righteousness despite the many wicked intentions of the people, and GOD honoured them.\n\nWe see the same for Daniel and his friends as well. GOD kept them.\n\nGOD has his own plans. He allowed these boys to be carried into captivity as eunuchs, a painful process; they lost so much, and yet in all that GOD was fulfilling his agenda — he blessed them in a strange land.\n\nIndeed, to put it another way, GOD blessed what he, GOD, was already doing, and anyone who helped advance his cause got blessed alongside.\n\nThis is the doing of the Lord, and it is marvellous in our eyes.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:30:38.291Z","s":["1hi7qjs9rs"]}],"14":[{"m":"Jeremiah, was he among the poor of the people, because those were the ones left behind?\n\nMaybe he was, maybe not, but at least we do know that he was kept not because he was poor but because he spoke the word of the Lord, which word was favourable to Nebuchadnezzar.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:26:23.699Z","s":["pnchgz8hni"]}]},"40":{"3":[{"m":"How did the captain know this? Babylon and the Chaldeans were not worshippers of Jehovah.\n\nUnless, of course, they thought of Jehovah as one of the many gods, and had heard how that the God of Israel 🇮🇱 is so jealous that if you go after other gods he would abandon you.\n\nAs we see in Africa 🌍, where certain gods must be appeased if displeased, lest they bring a plague or something.\n\nI suppose this was the context of the captain speaking.\n\nAlso, Israel 🇮🇱 went a-whoring after other gods, but how come we never read of one other nation taking up the God of Israel 🇮🇱, even after the many mighty works God had done?\n\nWe know of individual converts like Naaman and Rahab, but national conversions were never recorded.\n\nDoes this not teach us the nature of man 👨 and sin? Nations just naturally deteriorate and lose moral values... but do not pick up good moral values without some radical revival.\n\nEven when sin brings self-destruction, we are just inclined to go on in sin, because the motivations and pleasure of sin is addictive and compelling.","dt":"2022-08-18T06:36:35","s":["cyrsii2bgs"]}],"7":[{"m":"Who was Gedaliah? Was he of the seed royal 👑, or maybe one of those who very early on had fallen aside unto the king of Babylon and now had a strategic position under the new kingdom?","dt":"2024-10-25T09:23:05","s":["j9o845d08d"]}],"12":[{"m":"Is this not what Jeremiah prophesied?","dt":"2024-10-25T09:28:14","s":["o5redot8vt"]}]},"41":{"2":[{"m":"Do not be ignorant, Gedaliah was so innocent, naive and almost stupid 😲.\n\nAnd this really gets to me, because me and most Christians and, I guess, humans in general tend to be naive.\n\nIt seems to take, and I guess it's true, a certain level of subtlety and shrewdness to be in power and to keep it.","dt":"2022-08-20T06:46:20","s":["s2iur8c743"]},{"m":"Gedaliah was a man of peace and naive, probably the likely reason Babylon appointed him.\n\nThere was no rebellion in him. He wanted peace and good for all.\n\nSame reasoning for which the poor of the land were left behind.\n\nBut naivety will lead to grave losses; you can be good and not naive.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:46:21.429Z","s":["scdjw4wih3"]}],"8":[{"m":"What wealth 🧐 and money 💵 can do.\n\nThe rich man's wealth is his fortified city 🏙. It saved them their lives. That means the others, though devout men, were broke ass guys 🙊.\n\nAnd they had nothing to negotiate with; indeed, they did not even know to negotiate, because they did not have wealth.\n\nBy the time you get rich, you know that you can buy your way out of many predicaments, as did the others.\n\nIt's sad that though devout and so God-fearing, they did not have weight 🏋️ in this world 🗺.\n\nLord have mercy.\n\nAnother quick thought... Wealth abounds, actually looking for opportunity to grow and increase.\n\nSo if you prove yourself worth your salt and can multiply riches, money from all manner of places will come to you. As we see with the 3AC case in crypto.\n\nSo Henry, solve money problems and people will give you their money.\nSolve problems that will take a million dollars 💵 to solve and people will give you a million.\n\nSolve a problem that will take a billion and men will give you that.\n\nBecause there is not a lack of money; indeed, money is in excess.\n\nNeither is there a lack of problems or needs... They abound.\n\nIt is a lack of enough solutions to these, or ideas that will multiply these monies.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:09:15","s":["sclocm32f6"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why was this being described? Was it that it came to fulfil a certain prophecy, or it was just an observation? Google explains it was a historical observation — an underground water cistern large enough to hold so many bodies goes to show how vast it was. It was supposed to hold water for the people in times of wars, where sometimes siege prevented food and water from coming into walled cities.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:39:17.432Z","s":["1knugg33kr"]}],"7":[{"m":"He did this likely to prevent the conspiracy and murder from being known.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:55:15.730Z","s":["ndobfst5fe"]}],"18":[{"m":"How that the governor's naivety had cost everyone.\n\nIshmael was able to achieve this feat because he had killed the few men who had weapons, and all smiths etc. had been taken out of the land, save the poorest of the poor.\n\nIsrael 🇮🇱, once so great, is now feeding on crumbs. A once great, or greatest, of nations.\n\nIt is important to know our heritage and where we have come from, so we can fight for what belongs to us or aim to bring back the gallant years of our heritage.\n\nIt is this knowledge that has kept the Jews over these millennia and helped them to always bounce back.\n\nRecouping the lost years.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:13:34","s":["5uuk5u6w7j"]}]},"42":{"7":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 ten days, these men knew how to locate God. Who taught Jeremiah?\n\nAnd how does he know God will answer? Because the signs of a prophet were evident in him, i.e. God had spoken multiple times to him.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:18:52","s":["uh0fgln3jo"]},{"m":"That is how long it took a great prophet like Jeremiah to hear from the Lord. Many a time we think that because these major prophets wrote copious volumes of God's word to them, so GOD spoke to them easily and frequently.\n\nBut it was not so; even great Moses, who spoke to GOD face to face, spent 40 days and nights in fasting to receive the Ten Commandments and to have his encounters sometimes.\n\nThat is why they...\n\nIsaiah 40:31\nThey that wait upon the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.","dt":"2026-08-31T09:59:32.821Z","s":["s8lq9656gi"]}],"22":[{"m":"It is understandable why they refused the counsel of the Lord.\n\nIt sounds quite counterproductive to stay in the land where such atrocities have been committed.\n\nVery likely Nebuchadnezzar will come and exact his revenge.\n\nYet the Lord insists they stay in that same place, and there he will have mercy on them.\n\nThe Lord's instruction and wisdom can sometimes be so counterproductive, it seems... Though it will all work out well.\n\nLORD HELP us heed your wisdom.","dt":"2024-10-28T16:10:36","s":["93iblu9rdf"]}],"20":[{"m":"They asked for the word of the Lord GOD, but what they wanted really was for GOD to endorse their ways.\n\nIt was not for GOD to tell them the right way to go.\n\nSee how in the next chapter they vehemently resisted and rebelled against the word of the Lord.\n\nAs for Jeremiah, he being under the control of these people, he went with them.\n\nI don't think they would have allowed him to go back otherwise.","dt":"2026-08-31T10:15:15.860Z","s":["ftu4lnb2in"]}]},"43":{"1":[{"m":"They had been told the word of the Lord and had even been told that they will not listen 👂. And truly they refused.\n\nIn their wisdom they said that Jeremiah had conspired with the Chaldeans to do them evil 😈.\n\nWhat they failed to remember was that Jeremiah had never failed in any of his words of prophecy.\n\nThese people's hearts 💕 were so full 🌕 of deception. They had sworn that, be it good or evil 😈, they will obey the voice of the Lord.\n\nBut that was not to be so.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:24:33","s":["y4p9mpbaup"]}],"3":[{"m":"So what they really wanted was not to obey the word and direction of the Lord, but for God to bless the decision they had already taken in their hearts to do. They should have just said that from the very beginning.\n\nSometimes we just want to do our thing, but we come to God sanctimonious, as if we desire his will, but in reality we want to rope him into our own quest, or at least he should sanction our desires.","dt":"2024-10-28T17:41:31","s":["jfud5i9568"]}],"10":[{"m":"Who was he going to send? His spirits...\n\nSpirits seem to have such great interest in human affairs, and are greatly involved.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:26:32","s":["7kvm196jg7"]}],"11":[{"m":"So even in war and disaster there is some order.\n\nIt seems random 🚶, but in reality some have been assigned to die and others to be captive.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:28:03","s":["ahjdjmquwp"]}],"13":[{"m":"Completely rendering them, i.e. their gods, useless. It's sad that God made his own temple 🏛, which was so great, to be completely destroyed.\n\nJust like other nations. However, the difference being he had told his people that he would destroy them and the land because they had turned against him.\n\nIndeed, they had turned his temple for idol worship.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:30:32","s":["s01gel414q"]}]},"44":{"19":[{"m":"In the long-suffering of God Almighty, they thought 💭 it was their gods still prospering them.\n\nBut by the time they had stopped, according to their own account, evil came to them.\n\nBut Jeremiah tells them that by then their sins had so polluted the land that judgement had already been declared against the land.\n\nWhen we do not understand spiritual things, we can so easily get deceived.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:36:39","s":["nl4272tknj"]},{"m":"Such deception by these evil spirits. Whiles the Lord in his great patience prevented and held back his punishment, they took that as a time of prosperity by their gods.\n\nAnd when finally GOD's wrath hit, they had then stopped their wicked ways, but their wicked heart was still with their idol; but then it was too late, because the Lord was bent on destroying the people.\n\nThey took that as a bad omen from their gods for abandoning them. So now they were back to their evil ways.","dt":"2026-08-31T10:21:55.826Z","s":["hj7v6r6nej"]}],"23":[{"m":"It seems that the people repented for a while to serve the Lord, only for this disaster to come upon them, and they lost their land.\n\nSo their reasoning was that it was because they stopped that was why the queen of the heavens caused them to go into captivity.\n\nSuch foolish deception they were walking.\n\nTheir temporal repentance in following the Lord was a little too late. The Lord had already decided, and nothing was going to change it.\n\nJudah was going to go into captivity regardless of their repentance. It was this decision of God to send them into captivity despite their repentance that they judged as the idol being angry at them and casting them out of their sight.\n\nMany times some things have already been predetermined by God regardless, and it happens despite our prayers and our good intentions.\n\nAnd so when evil happens to good people we question the Lord, we question the Lord, but sometimes God permits evil to happen and out of it he shows forth his glory.\n\nIt's just like when he said that even if Moses and Samuel stood before him, he would not change his mind.\n\nSome things have been determined to happen, but our consolation is in the fact that all things work together for our good.","dt":"2024-10-28T18:05:19","s":["wt4zkafyw9"]}],"28":[{"m":"The remnant, I believe, would mostly be the righteous ones who continue to serve the Lord despite the hindrances and challenges in a foreign land.\n\nThem the Lord will cause to escape from the sword and famine and pestilence of the land.","dt":"2024-10-28T17:58:11","s":["l9w1ae2my4"]}],"30":[{"m":"Case closed and settled. This will settle their confusion, but they need not be confused 😕.\n\nThey were not honest and just self-absorbed in their delusions. I'm sure the demon 👹 calling itself the queen of heaven had told them the lie that it's because they stopped serving her.\n\nSo it was this demon's words of deception 😞 against God's true words.\n\nThese people's hearts were bent on evil 😈, and they were just giving excuses, because\n\neven if they were confused 😕, which God is better: the gods who require them to sacrifice their children and commit whoredoms, or the one who demands righteousness from them?\n\nThey were just self-deluded, selfish and deceived.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:43:03","s":["lppmzxwq8p"]},{"m":"These people were so blessed, really they were, to have a prophet whose words never failed and who could hear from the Lord for them and tell them what was about to happen.\n\nThey were indeed so blessed.","dt":"2024-10-28T18:10:52","s":["he7het17vl"]}],"8":[{"m":"So even in a foreign land God still keeps his eyes on his children and expects them to worship him and keep his laws.\n\nThis goes to show that regardless of the land and the location, God judges all men and expects men to do what is right and keep his laws.\n\nEven in pagan lands.","dt":"2024-10-28T17:51:14","s":["vvrfrjg9ir"]}],"9":[{"m":"Obviously committing whoredoms.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:32:13","s":["1n59n9t4x4"]}]},"45":{"5":[{"m":"What a great promise for service to the Lord.","dt":"2022-08-20T07:44:04","s":["2idxa2k1mh"]},{"m":"Baruch sought rest for himself.\n\nHe had gone through much and suffered much for the sake of the Lord and in defence of Jeremiah the prophet.\n\nHe sought, like all men, to probably build a good house for himself and to come to retirement and rest from all his labour and suffering.\n\nBut the wisdom of God spoke to him: why would you want to build when God was about to destroy everything? That would be work in futility.\n\nRather, God promised him the most important thing: that when the time of destruction comes, he will save him from it.","dt":"2024-10-28T18:14:49","s":["9jhksb45wd"]}]},"46":{"14":[{"m":"Indeed, the word of the Lord to Jeremiah, that before his birth he was ordained a prophet to the nations, was being fulfilled.\n\nNow here his calling had brought him to Egypt.","dt":"2024-10-29T20:27:34","s":["3x50y10ksg"]}]},"48":{"10":[{"m":"Shabajfodjenwldjiooa... So this is where this scripture is...\nIt is not a New Testament scripture.\n\nGOD calls this invasion by non-believers his work.","dt":"2022-08-22T08:06:58","s":["pu2u5vphix"]}],"13":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 Lord have mercy and bring not the wanderer, if possible.","dt":"2022-08-22T08:10:47","s":["qfhrz6oojr"]}]},"50":{"11":[{"m":"This teaches us not to rejoice at the punishment of others, even if justified.","dt":"2022-08-23T15:36:21","s":["a1ul5dtrg5"]}],"38":[{"m":"Here we see the reason for this famine and drying of waters.","dt":"2022-08-23T15:42:06","s":["7k3l9sr064"]}],"16":[{"m":"Is it not the same thing that GOD used Israel to do against the inhabitants of the promised land that GOD now used Babylon to do to Israel and its surrounding nations, and now it's been done to Babylon herself?\n\nIndeed, when GOD was using Babylon to destroy other nations, he called Babylon and Nebuchadnezzar his servant. Wow","dt":"2026-09-07T09:45:51.592Z","s":["neu38jxki5"]}],"4":[{"m":"The fall of Babylon at that time will be the deliverance of Israel and Judah, the city the Lord loves.","dt":"2026-09-05T13:36:07.112Z","s":["dlqbwhj0nl"]}],"28":[{"m":"His temple was destroyed by Babylon, and now is the time to take vengeance. Initially I wondered why GOD allowed such a rich and powerful imagery of his presence as GOD in Israel to be taken.\n\nWhy did he allow it, and why did he do nothing after? But here we see his plan to exact revenge for that act, though he allowed it to allow Israel to see that he, GOD, cares less about physical things if his people will reject worship of him and think that because they have his temple, they are alright.","dt":"2026-09-07T09:56:18.732Z","s":["0loprw8l7b"]}],"18":[{"m":"Anytime a nation is taken, reference is made to their gods, not their armoury or strength 💪.\n\nYes, some allusion may be made to these, but ultimately their gods are mentioned as failing their people.","dt":"2022-08-23T15:17:08","s":["7rywt5ewu5"]}]},"51":{"11":[{"m":"As I read these verses, I think 🤔 to myself how lucky these people were.\n\nTo read, decades ahead, events that would happen way before they ever did.\n\nIndeed they were blessed.\n\nBut then I realized that we are equally, if not more, blessed.\n\nTo see their lives and learn from their stories, and we also have prophecies of future events.\n\nSo we are even more blessed. Prophecies of the end of time.\n\nAnd the end is nearer now than when we first believed.","dt":"2024-10-30T16:14:47","s":["c9pmfb6m2a"]}],"13":[{"m":"Why so? Is Babylon indeed in the midst of waters? It's an expression.\n\nBecause in Revelation mention is made of the woman that sitteth upon waters, and it was in reference to Babylon, if I'm not mistaken.","dt":"2024-10-30T16:17:19","s":["eymj428ul4"]},{"m":"She that dwells upon many waters — is that not the description of the mystery Babylon in the book of Revelation 17:1?\n\nRevelation 17:1 NKJV\nThen one of the seven angels who had the seven bowls came and talked with me, saying to me, “Come, I will show you the judgment of the great harlot who sits on many waters,","dt":"2026-09-08T08:48:07.581Z","s":["368rv5wwrg"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh, this earth 🌎, so beautifully designed by God.\n\nTo reflect his mindset and wisdom.","dt":"2022-08-24T21:13:51","s":["jpulsu31v6"]}],"30":[{"m":"All these shall happen after the seventy years completed...\n\nThis prophecy came whiles Babylon was busy capturing other nations.\n\nLittle did they know that their own captivity was at hand 🖐️.\nAnd of course, in the God realm, at hand can be many years.","dt":"2022-08-26T06:19:26","s":["70ghnyj3nc"]}],"47":[{"m":"As these prophecies and judgements come upon Babylon, I wonder, in our days where are the prophecies against the nations?\n\nWhere are the prophets who would speak the mind of God concerning the USA 🇺🇸, RUSSIA 🇷🇺 in these our days?","dt":"2022-08-26T06:27:06","s":["r9jocz1fs6"]}],"64":[{"m":"So this prophecy against Babylon was not to be uttered before any king or princes 🤴. It was to be read in the land of Babylon, and a curse 🤬 it became unto them.\n\nBound up into the sea, and its fulfillment would happen in due time ⌚.\n\nOnly God knows the words spoken against men and nations in the quiet 🤫, and no one knows.\n\nYet it speaks against the nations and people.\n\nOh Lord, deliver us from evil curses 🤬 and bless us. Amen","dt":"2022-08-26T06:34:28","s":["qllnf93i3l"]}],"49":[{"m":"Babylon destroyed many nations, yet for none of them is GOD exacting this revenge, but for his own people Israel, as if they are the only ones to suffer at the hand of Babylon.\n\nBut that is GOD showing he is the one true GOD.","dt":"2026-09-08T10:19:43.889Z","s":["8tfk2ixqj8"]}],"24":[{"m":"Was this Jeremiah?","dt":"2022-08-24T21:18:13","s":["rw9ja68xqi"]}],"63":[{"m":"Wow, the all-seeing eye of GOD. In the peak of their prosperity and conquest, GOD was already seeing their destruction and end.","dt":"2026-09-08T10:22:50.602Z","s":["actgatna4x"]}]},"52":{"10":[{"m":"When a king 👑 is taken, his courtiers are taken with him. So princes 🤴 must ensure the strength 💪 of their king and kingdom.\n\nLest when they are broken 💔 through, they will all suffer.","dt":"2022-08-26T06:39:12","s":["yjnva09xz4"]}]},"49":{"12":[{"m":"This reminds me of the New Testament passage that says, If the righteous are scarcely saved, how much more the sinner — let me just drop the quote here.\n\n1 Peter 4:18 KJV\nAnd if the righteous scarcely be saved, where shall the ungodly and the sinner appear?","dt":"2026-09-05T13:30:39.688Z","s":["9p2vaqwh10"]}]},"47":{"2":[{"m":"Egypt is likened to a flood that overflowed; it was so described of him in the previous chapter and here also.\nIn the previous chapter he lost his ambition to overflow the earth to the army from the North — the army of Nebuchadnezzar.\n\nHere, however, like a flood, he is victorious over Gaza and over the Philistines.\n\nEgypt seems to have had a world conquest mission to dominate the world that then was.\n\nBut it was aborted by King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon.","dt":"2026-09-04T09:14:20.979Z","s":["qyxvxh14zm"]}]},"6":{"15":[{"m":"I fear 😱, I fear greatly — that the judgement of the whole world is coming, and this is how it will pan out.\n\nThis has happened before in the times of Israel; they were corrupt to the core, and God sent his judgments upon them after many warnings.\n\nToday Christianity is all over the world 🗺, bearing worldwide witness to all.\n\nAnd yet the world continues in depravity and is setting itself up for worldwide judgment.\n\nAnd the world will be without excuse because of Christianity and the preaching of the gospel.\n\nThe nations around Israel were pagan, and though they knew not the word of the Lord, were punished in due time.\n\nIsrael, who knew the word, were punished as such after many warnings.\n\nOur world today is like Israel then; the word of the Lord is gone out, and soon men would be without excuse as the judgement of the Lord comes upon them, because they have been preached to as Israel was.\n\nAnd the punishment would be absolute and would end the world 🗺, but the gospel must be preached before the eternal judgements so that God would be just.","dt":"2024-10-14T06:40:47","s":["81vyz3jhy0"]}],"20":[{"m":"So the sacrifices and offerings from a disobedient people are not acceptable.","dt":"2022-08-09T21:40:27","s":["w4pteg9tkv"]}]}},"2 Samuel":{"1":{"2":[{"m":"The politicking had begun. Saul was dead, and now people wanted to take up and win favour before the king 👑 through lies 🤥, sycophancy and all means fair and foul.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:23:54","s":["940twts17i"]}],"5":[{"m":"He did not react immediately, because many are tale bearers and liars. So he had to be sure of this information source.","dt":"2026-04-21T07:59:50","s":["t4ll8141nu"]}],"10":[{"m":"So he took some loot for himself even before the Philistines did.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:32:21","s":["tyaxum2e6b"]},{"m":"He brought these souvenirs to the new king, with the hope that he will be in the upcoming king's good books, which will likely get him a place in the new kingdom. Politics, hm.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:02:25","s":["t03x8k4mxi"]}],"21":[{"m":"So one anointed should not have his shield violently cast away, vilely cast away. There is a protection upon one who is anointed. I am anointed. I am protected.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:06:23","s":["88rmjysdqc"]}],"26":[{"m":"Oh, why did Jonathan die? 😭","dt":"2024-06-11T08:35:22","s":["7bas8tecsj"]}],"12":[{"m":"A strange reaction indeed. David did not let bitterness take a hold of his heart ♥.\n\nHe loved Saul through and through, and now that he who had chosen him as his enemy had died, he mourned deeply, and all his men with him.\n\nI wonder the reaction of this informant to David and his men.\n\nMaybe he understood that they likely mourned for the loss that had befallen the nation.\n\nWhat he likely did not phantom 👻 was that David actually mourned for Saul as well.\n\nThis informant's end was near, but he knew it not.\n\nJust as the wicked cannot phantom 👻 the ways of the righteous, also the righteous underestimate the ways of wickedness.\n\nThat is why we are admonished by the Lord to be wise as serpents but innocent as doves 🕊\n\nMatthew 10:16 ESV\nBehold, I am sending you out as sheep in the midst of wolves, so be wise as serpents and innocent as doves.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:30:22","s":["8uj1ozf9hn"]}]},"2":{"4":[{"m":"David was already very popular at this time. I don't know how he managed to balance knowing he was the next king whiles at the same time serving the current king.\n\nEspecially knowing he was not of royal blood and descent. God has a way of sometimes putting us in very precarious positions. But David handled himself well.\n\nI wonder how his family also felt about this. I am sure they were wise enough to keep it secret — top secret — because any such leakage of information was going to be at the peril of their lives.\n\nDavid was not going to be the last king to be anointed this way and to live at the peril of his life and that of his family.\n\nJesus, the King of kings, also was born whiles another king was alive. Unfortunately, many innocent people died as well because of who he was.\n\nEventually his parents had to go hide in another country. It is not easy to be blessed and called whiles another person already occupies the place you have been called to occupy.\n\nNo wonder even in the church today, leaders are wary of people who are called and have exceptional or obvious grace from God.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:23:45","s":["s98ulh699b"]}],"23":[{"m":"Abner was a skilled general, and obtaining his armour would be a great feat for Asahel.\n\nHe would have cemented his name as one of the young greats of his times.\n\nBut that was never to be.\n\nThe technique with which Abner killed Asahel was so unexpected.\n\nWho would have expected such?\n\nAbner's hands were very strong 💪, and he likely had rehearsed this countlessly, and it had given him success many times.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:42:48","s":["c7hgmiqf2c"]}],"5":[{"m":"He had studied and learnt well and already knew the ways of kings and the kingdom.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:36:27","s":["onhnq3wlo3"]}]},"3":{"9":[{"m":"So Abner knew the word of the Lord 🙌, yet stood against the Lord because of his power and influence.\n\nHe did not fear the Lord, and indeed he furthered his own interests against that of God and his word.\n\nIf he had from the very beginning heeded to the word of the Lord, many lives of the house of Saul would not have been lost, and in all likelihood he would not have lost his life either.\n\nBut then again, God was against the house of Saul and wanted them weaker and weaker.\n\nHe did not want a coregency between the house of Saul and David.\n\nHe had declared that he was taking the kingdom from Saul.\n\nMaybe that was also why Jonathan also died in battle.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:48:07","s":["f4klsh694m"]},{"m":"Even in the background, God was working to establish David as king over all Israel.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:31:14","s":["8s3jzl4nz0"]}],"16":[{"m":"She must have been a very good wife for a man in a polygamous culture to cry behind her...","dt":"2022-04-21T06:40:01","s":["k54g1pbn44"]},{"m":"Hmm 🤔. She might have been a very good wife for him to cry thus after her.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:49:18","s":["wujdjqzym1"]},{"m":"These military ⚔ men, see how he humbled the man.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:50:12","s":["ljjwt0xb6c"]}],"19":[{"m":"I am sure some lobbying and sharing of power went on. Who would become what in the new kingdom?\n\nThe power brokers were brokering power.\n\nEveryone was juggling for position and power in the setting up of the joint kingdom.\n\nBut it seems at the end of the day God wanted to really strengthen the hand of David in the kingdom, so there are no possible threats to this new king and kingdom.\n\nGod indeed loved David, and David had proven himself in the wilderness to be a man who really loved the Lord and whose heart was for him.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:33:39","s":["rag45a0647"]}],"27":[{"m":"Even Abner in all his cruelty could not have phantomed such wickedness from Joab.\n\nHe thought 💭 Joab was as loyal to the word of the king 👑 as he, Abner, was.\n\nHe had stood with Saul even throughout his madness. And even remained loyal to the house of Saul after Saul's death ☠.\n\nHe thought the same of Joab, and in this he was mistaken, a mistake that cost him his life.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:53:51","s":["nycwqo5o2f"]}],"29":[{"m":"This curse, should it work, will forever be a reproach in Joab's family.\n\nCould it be that even today there are families with multi-dimensional curses? Families that you cannot see a specific pattern of, say, a sickness or death, but a general pattern where there seems to be one misfortune or another. Nothing specific, but always one very bad news or another.\n\nJoab lacked morals and character.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:40:17","s":["c2x2hkcdjb"]}],"31":[{"m":"Joab the murderer was forced to mourn for the very man he killed. A good punishment for his wickedness. He was too powerful to be taken out, so David made him mourn for the very man he killed.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:43:15","s":["sbz4xlbple"]}],"33":[{"m":"Let me not be a fool, O God, let me not be.","dt":"2026-04-21T08:41:41","s":["yoa0wcd5lw"]}],"39":[{"m":"He cursed them for their wickedness.","dt":"2024-06-11T08:55:19","s":["u8excwpq58"]}]},"4":{"12":[{"m":"A sad 😔 day indeed in Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nEven though all these worked to establish the throne of David, he executed justice against the sons of Belial.\n\nOh, the wisdom of God, whiles executing righteousness, he was at the same time using the acts of wickedness to establish a good thing... An eternal and perpetual throne for the man after his own heart ♥","dt":"2024-06-11T08:59:08","s":["th94zogh60"]}]},"5":{"2":[{"m":"How and when did it become common knowledge that the Lord had spoken concerning David that he would become king 👑?\n\nCould the secret anointing of DAVID by Samuel have become an open 🔓 secret?","dt":"2024-06-18T21:15:37","s":["3wt8oi9kou"]}],"10":[{"m":"The Lord of hosts was with him, the Lord of armies was with him in helping him to win his wars. This particular title of God was aptly chosen to fit the context of the passage.","dt":"2026-05-03T09:39:44","s":["5r5cudv4yr"]}],"17":[{"m":"I'm sure this includes the Philistines among whom he had lived.\n\nNow they realized David had deceived them the whole time ⌚.\n\nThey knew the dangers of David becoming king for long.\n\nHe was going to dominate them all. The earlier they nipped him in the bud, the better for them.","dt":"2024-06-18T21:38:45","s":["m2ml9m0ugg"]},{"m":"Which hold?","dt":"2024-06-18T21:39:58","s":["r1kl9djb17"]},{"m":"Israel had a king and successor over them in place of Saul. Their enemies, the Philistines, saw that Israel was trying to strengthen themselves. They can have none of that.\n\nSo they gathered to weaken the new king and exert their control and influence over Israel. In time past they had garrisons and a strong presence in Israel. They had also taken cities after defeating Saul in battle.\n\nA loss to the children of God that God permitted. Of course, God knew he could take all that back in due time, so that wasn't a problem.\n\nNow the Philistines, with David on the throne, risked losing all they had consolidated.","dt":"2026-05-03T09:45:20","s":["pkd5tbugqc"]}],"24":[{"m":"Why move quickly? Because this move of God was time bound.\n\nIt was not at David's discretion as to when to attack.\n\nHe was to attack when God prompts, and he was to do it quickly.\n\nHe was to seize the moment.","dt":"2024-06-18T22:05:49","s":["w3quq295qo"]}],"1":[{"m":"It was easy to see that the hand of the Lord was upon David.\n\nThe way situations conspired for his help was obviously the divine at work.\n\nThe people recognized this and aligned to make him king 👑 of the whole realm.\n\nIt was a long walk to freedom.","dt":"2024-06-11T09:04:10","s":["xx0m2faj86"]}],"19":[{"m":"How did David enquire... If by the Urim and Thummim, he would get yes and no answers.\n\nBut God spoke to him clearly that he would doubtless be victorious over them.\n\nLikely the Lord spoke to him, or through the priests?\n\nNo details are given as to the enquiry process.","dt":"2024-06-18T22:01:39","s":["fzz7xctlka"]}]},"6":{"2":[{"m":"Why such a long description? The LORD (I AM that I am) of the hosts (he) that dwelleth between the cherubims.\n\nThe brackets are my own additions.","dt":"2024-06-23T14:44:13","s":["iemymctalg"]}],"3":[{"m":"So Uzzah was the son of a priest; he was not an ordinary man.","dt":"2024-06-23T22:14:52","s":["mztcsp5xx6"]}],"11":[{"m":"When I was much younger, I used to wonder how a man can get so blessed in just three months that it attracts the attention of the number one man in the land...\n\nBut as I grew older, I see how that could have happened even in just a day.\n\nHe chanced upon something of value in their time, as an oil well is in our times, or a gold mine or some contract or idea.","dt":"2024-06-23T22:19:30","s":["p32ro8tlfe"]}],"23":[{"m":"Is it that David no longer went in unto her, which is a very easy thing for him considering his numerous wives?\n\nOr she became barren of God?","dt":"2024-06-23T22:23:34","s":["ja2c4ynpw2"]}],"10":[{"m":"Because of a wisdom problem, that which was meant to be a blessing to David and his city was transferred to the home of a single individual and his household.\n\nAnd boy 🧒 did they get blessed.\n\nThey indeed got blessed to the envy and hearing of even the king 👑.","dt":"2024-06-23T22:17:22","s":["22abphc1r3"]}]},"7":{"10":[{"m":"The nations around Israel were called the children of wickedness.\n\nFor their gods, being demons, taught them wickedness and demanded such from them.","dt":"2024-06-24T23:55:11","s":["ozs54ecb52"]},{"m":"Why are they not called wicked people... but children of wickedness? Who then is their father?\n\nBy the sound of this, it's almost as if their wickedness was hereditary. And indeed it was, in the sense that fathers pass it on to their children, and children their children.\n\nThus a generation, a nation, a seed can stem from the root of wickedness.","dt":"2026-05-13T08:40:55","s":["9ss94tg5f1"]}],"18":[{"m":"I believe he sat before the Lord in the house of God.\n\nThis is the man who said he would rather be a door 🚪 keeper in the Lord's house than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.\n\nHe said better is a day in the house of the Lord than a thousand elsewhere.\n\nIndeed, King 👑 David loved the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-24T23:58:31","s":["59xzx5011j"]}],"20":[{"m":"He could have prayed all this prayer in his room, but he went down into the house of the Lord, his King 👑.\n\nAnd in humility sat as a nobody before the Lord.\n\nAcknowledging that the Lord took him from being a shepherd to make him king.\n\nThat alone was too much, and to now add an eternal kingdom?","dt":"2026-05-13T08:47:54","s":["hq12q7kteo"]}],"23":[{"m":"Israel was not just redeemed from Egypt, that is the people of Egypt, but was redeemed from their gods.\n\nYou saw how their gods also displayed to counter Moses and the power of God.\n\nIf Israel had attempted escaping without power from on high... without divine power.\n\nThey would not in any way have escaped.\n\nEven with the power of God, see how long it took.","dt":"2026-05-13T08:50:32","s":["x9dg6iephd"]}],"27":[{"m":"One of the main names and attributes of God is that he is a man of war, the Lord of hosts.\n\nHow come then that as Christians we lack warlike attributes and posture in the face of trouble?\n\nOur God is a man of war, so every challenge, no matter the size and ferocity, is bread for us.","dt":"2024-06-25T00:01:42","s":["e095dykf1m"]}]},"8":{"4":[{"m":"Why an hundred chariots, when he could have kept them all?\n\nChariots were the thing at the time, an advanced transport system for war and the envy of any army.\n\nI suspect David destroyed the majority of them in keeping with the law against multiplying horses 🏇.","dt":"2024-06-27T06:21:57","s":["8tyxy5tqfn"]}]},"9":{"10":[{"m":"Ziba was a leader under a leader.\n\nHe had 20 servants and was himself a servant of Saul.","dt":"2024-06-27T06:36:37","s":["egqspk6pmh"]}],"8":[{"m":"This story, this sudden change in destiny and purpose. There were many highlights in David's life, but for this particular story to be chosen above all else,\n\nThis goes to show it was one of the high moments of David, to show his heart for covenant and friendship.","dt":"2024-06-27T06:35:41","s":["goquh0g3h2"]}]},"10":{"6":[{"m":"Such foolish counsel.\n\nIt was after they had heeded the counsel that they realized the implications of their decisions, and now hired an army for war?\n\nFools, but all too often this is repeated even in our days. Men go to war over foolish and often selfish reasons.\n\nMarriages are at war over very little and trivial things we could have overlooked.\n\nSad, sad 😔. Lord, give us wisdom to deal wisely as a people.","dt":"2024-06-27T11:07:50","s":["ebgtwxhf9o"]},{"m":"This feels like a setup by God to judge the children of Ammon and their allies and to destroy them. David and his men were not afraid of war.\n\nThey were apt and ready for it. In a sense this reminds me of some of the later kings of Israel, who, when war came, instead of fighting, rather gave out the treasures of the house of God in order to secure peace.\n\nAs the case of Asa.\n\nIf there was trust in God, they would have had the victory.\n\nThis I see to be one such fine opportunity, and David took full advantage.","dt":"2026-05-15T08:20:07","s":["ozmfozz5d9"]}],"12":[{"m":"Even Joab, though wicked, trusted in the Lord of war, El Gibbor, to come through, and he did.\n\nWar is such an uncertain venture, and at this moment Joab left all in the hands of God to do what is good in his eyes 👀.","dt":"2024-06-27T11:13:40","s":["ppgdb2xmma"]},{"m":"They were fighting for their own, their people and for their God, the cities of their God. God was an intricate part of all they did, even things done by their own might and at the peril of their own lives. They attributed it all to God, and it was not a vain attribution, for God indeed worked through them supernaturally to bring victory.\n\nYes, they themselves were well trained and skilled, but that cum God was an undefeatable force.","dt":"2026-05-15T08:42:36","s":["nvu4fx6uzg"]}],"19":[{"m":"It seems, using the example of happenings in Saul's era, the 12 spies of Moses and other kings who faced impossible 🙅 armies and warfare,\n\nThat God loved such moments, as it serves as an occasion for him to take vengeance in a big way on his enemies, who also are enemies of his people.\n\nThat is why when his people fear 😱 and don't trust him because of the size of the battle, he punished them, because it was a sweet opportunity for him to display his power and show what only HE can do.\n\nSuch wasted moments for grand victory take a while, sometimes decades or generations, for such fine opportunities to come on such a grand scale as to bring the LORD glory.","dt":"2024-06-27T11:18:36","s":["iymms02r6x"]}]},"11":{"11":[{"m":"This was what David should have considered.\n\nUriah was more righteous and honorable by miles than David.\n\nHe considered that his own brothers' lives were in jeopardy and great discomfort.\nHow could he then, with this knowledge, be at ease?\n\nBut David considered none of these.\n\nNot only was he at ease in his palace, he ate and slept, not with his wives, but polluted himself with another.","dt":"2024-06-28T07:00:36","s":["s57ukkbxs4"]}],"16":[{"m":"How and when did David get to this place?\n\nSuch a low point, he was now a murderer.","dt":"2024-06-28T07:05:32","s":["useerth90v"]}],"17":[{"m":"He not only killed Uriah the Hittite but also others needlessly... Families lost their breadwinners, not in service of the nation, but in cover-up for someone else's sins.","dt":"2024-06-28T07:30:06","s":["ru5fo0mbpp"]}],"20":[{"m":"David knew people died in war, as well as Joab, but careless mistakes that cost lives needlessly would definitely attract the anger of the king 👑.\n\nUnlike in some armies where suicide missions were a strategy, it seems here that David did all he could to save his people from such needless deaths.","dt":"2024-06-29T11:27:28","s":["3ku23yese8"]}],"22":[{"m":"I can imagine these servants who delivered this message: after delivering the message and seeing the anger of the king subside upon hearing about the death of Uriah, they would be left wondering why the king seemed pleased about the death of one of his most faithful generals.\n\nBut being trained messengers, they will keep silent and secret the conversation.\n\nFast forward a few weeks later, they see the king has taken the man's wife. They can't believe it — is that why he killed his friend, for his wife?\n\nThen next thing, they see the woman already pregnant.\n\nThey now understand.\n\nBut they stay hushed — they focus on their job and move on — wiser now.\n\nIt is such wisdom of the workings of the corridors of power that made the servant of Joab refuse to strike down Absalom when Joab tried compelling him to with a gift.\n\nHe plainly told him the king commanded otherwise, and it would have been he, Joab, who would at the end of the day expose him, though now he speaks comfortably to him.","dt":"2026-05-16T06:48:17","s":["srqsuwuqz7"]}],"26":[{"m":"She mourned and just moved on. Just like that.\n\nHer character is revealed by the fact that she did not refuse the king but chose to be entered into. No report is made of her resisting or objecting.\n\nAnd now she mourns, as ought to be the case, and moves on to be the wife of the great King David.\n\nOr maybe she had little power or choice to object — I doubt, though.","dt":"2026-05-16T06:50:56","s":["ycvoou2bh3"]}],"4":[{"m":"What message did the messengers of King 👑 David convey that could lure and convince Bathsheba to give up on her marital vow, dishonor her marital bed 🛏 in a culture where adulterers are stoned to death ☠?\n\nThe Shunammite woman faced an even stronger temptation from an even more powerful, rich and attractive king, King Solomon.\n\nYet Solomon in all his allure could neither captivate nor convince the Shulamite woman to abandon her betrothal to follow him,\n\nA betrothal to a man she was barely married to 👰, yet Solomon could not draw her away.\n\nBut Bathsheba could be lured with sweet words and promises, so she succumbed.\n\nHmm 🤔.","dt":"2024-06-28T06:45:48","s":["l4enybb2l2"]},{"m":"She was ceremonially clean; that was important to her and David.\n\nShe had to be ceremonially clean in order to break the law of God.\n\nSuch confusion and mockery of God.\n\nProbably she was cleansing herself from her menstrual flow when David spied her.","dt":"2024-06-28T06:54:13","s":["pg42e87vue"]}],"13":[{"m":"The man's righteousness cost him his life but got him a name before the Lord.\n\nEven in his drunken state, his subconscious held high the morals of a warrior and the respect for God, his ark and his people.","dt":"2024-06-28T07:04:21","s":["rt68r5yba2"]}],"24":[{"m":"It was not just Uriah who died; many more did, all to cover for the sins of the king 👑.","dt":"2024-06-29T11:24:52","s":["ycbcf8gqyy"]}]},"12":{"8":[{"m":"The ways of the kings of the time... They take their masters' wives and all.","dt":"2024-06-29T17:19:10","s":["mu2bvstca9"]}],"11":[{"m":"Why didn't God destroy David immediately? Because of the consequences upon Israel if David were to die immediately and suddenly. So he spread the punishment over years and generations and dispensed them accordingly, according to his many mercies.","dt":"2026-05-16T06:56:09","s":["kijp9altu9"]},{"m":"He had already promised him an eternal house, so he could not take the kingdom from him forever, but God knew how to serve justice accordingly.","dt":"2026-05-16T06:57:06","s":["7pnyhm0rph"]}],"13":[{"m":"So the original and requisite punishment for David was death, but the Lord spared him.","dt":"2024-06-29T17:21:28","s":["o25lrmu4z"]}],"23":[{"m":"Oh death ☠...\n\nDeath is the great equalizer and final enemy of all men.","dt":"2024-06-29T17:24:02","s":["brxmrneicq"]}],"24":[{"m":"The sins of the father are not to transfer to the child in the law of our God.","dt":"2026-05-16T07:02:45","s":["lgxaaelc6e"]}],"10":[{"m":"This sin was not against Uriah but against God, as all sins are.","dt":"2024-06-29T17:20:12","s":["l69rzfqne6"]}],"14":[{"m":"It is like when men of God fall or are caught in scandals, the world condemns us all and our God. David, the servant of the Lord, or so he was touted, now doing worse than the average blasphemer of God.\n\nI can imagine the ridicule and gossip on the streets.","dt":"2026-05-16T06:58:42","s":["yy0eo4h2an"]}]},"13":{"15":[{"m":"Such lusts were likely demon driven, and right after that he hated her.\n\nThe curse of the Lord on his family had started.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:05:44","s":["n0ejo3xtus"]}],"17":[{"m":"A foolish man 👨","dt":"2024-06-30T02:11:12","s":["99acipr9iy"]}],"29":[{"m":"It seems the servants of each prince were loyal to the prince — because for them to kill another prince at the command of another, damning the consequences, shows the extent of loyalty.","dt":"2026-05-20T03:47:40","s":["xqu48jhl03"]}],"31":[{"m":"What a scene in the palace that day, David rent and in his ashes, and all his servants as well...\n\nTerrible 😰 moment, much commotion in the palace, only for the news that it was Amnon alone who was killed...\n\nAt least this was better than the earlier news. A little embarrassed 😳 but still pained, they weep and cry 😢.\n\nThe following day, the general populace get a wind 🍃 of the happenings in the palace.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:27:06","s":["6yhpstexr9"]},{"m":"Out of solidarity, and not just that, but also these were boys they had lived with in the palace; for them all to be dead was so painful.\n\nBut they could not lie in the dirt like the king — so they stood but had their garments rent.","dt":"2026-05-20T02:35:41","s":["ptr5jxmdbj"]}],"35":[{"m":"This guy was really shrewd, appeasing and easing the pain of the king 👑... Who knows, he might be added to the king's confidants.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:29:17","s":["032elo3z9l"]}],"3":[{"m":"They were cousins. The royal 👑 palace was occupied by family 👪 and friends.\n\nDavid had opened a huge door 🚪 for his entire family and their friends.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:02:16","s":["wkck5m878v"]}],"16":[{"m":"After having fed his lusts with her, the least she wanted was dignity.\n\nShe reckoned that if he loved her so uncontrollably, then he would be at least so kind to talk to her softly and keep her in his house until the right thing has been done.\n\nMaybe it would be agreed 🤝 for him to take her home as his wife, as was the case between Shechem and Jacob's daughter Dinah.\n\nBut that was not to be; the lusts were suddenly replaced by hate, she was repulsive to him.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:10:44","s":["8rxryv39no"]}],"20":[{"m":"Did anyone marry her after that?","dt":"2024-06-30T02:13:51","s":["qxkv7wxbdd"]}],"28":[{"m":"Each prince 🤴 had his own personal servants and soldiers loyal to him.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:18:23","s":["a1qs6gb2vv"]}],"39":[{"m":"The law of Moses had been fulfilled by Absalom; life goes on.\n\nIf a man shall take his sister, his father's daughter, or his mother's daughter, and see her nakedness, and she see his nakedness; it is a wicked thing; and they shall be cut off in the sight of their people: he hath uncovered his sister's nakedness; he shall bear his iniquity.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:32:55","s":["kdg0cvdrdw"]}]},"14":{"20":[{"m":"Such wisdom with words. Lord, give me such wisdom in speech, I pray.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:42:16","s":["pe9zwnsfn2"]},{"m":"David was a psalmist, and such wisdom and dexterity with words moved him to do the needful.\n\nLord, give wisdom.","dt":"2026-05-20T03:13:23","s":["q6nk5uqh26"]}],"1":[{"m":"The family was full of family, and that is how the kingdom is run, then and even now. Even in so-called democracies.","dt":"2026-05-20T02:38:53","s":["ib1rk677wh"]}],"5":[{"m":"The kings were both the legislature and the judiciary. I think in a sense modern-day presidents do the same; yes, they are more of the legislature, but can appoint new judges in order to control the judiciary.","dt":"2026-05-20T02:40:23","s":["9cot2f7s27"]}],"23":[{"m":"Joab had a soft spot for Absalom.\n\nHe went to lengths to have Absalom restored.\n\nOr maybe his soft spot was for DAVID, his uncle.\n\nHe saw how worried 😯 David was about his son and how his soul longed for him,\n\nBut righteous David would not use his powers to bring back his son who had broken caused much pain.\n\nJoab saw the dilemma of his king 👑 and intervened.","dt":"2024-06-30T02:41:41","s":["tuq39raerb"]}]},"15":{"13":[{"m":"God allowed this. Fear 😱 seized David and his servants. God's word was coming to pass; thus a divine element was backing all of this conspiracy.\n\nFear and uncertainty were in the air; David and his men had to escape quick.\n\nIn such moments I'm reminded of the book of Revelations, where God takes peace 🌎 from the earth 😱.\n\nSame thing in Israel's conquest of the promised land, that a spirit of fear was released upon the inhabitants, that they could do them no harm.\n\nGenesis 35:5 KJV\nAnd they journeyed: and the terror of God was upon the cities that were round about them, and they did not pursue after the sons of Jacob.\n\nThere are many examples of such moments.\n\nSame when Jacob escaped from Shechem.\n\nGenesis 35:5 KJV\nAnd they journeyed: and the terror of God was upon the cities that were round about them, and they did not pursue after the sons of Jacob.","dt":"2024-06-30T05:24:26","s":["ja764n7jpn"]}],"23":[{"m":"Meaning the people's heart ♥ was still with David, just that he seems to have fallen out of favour with those in the corridors of power and the kingmakers.\n\nThe entire army was beside Absalom, and so were some of David's trusted men and counselors.\n\nDavid had lost favour with the key people.","dt":"2024-06-30T18:50:37","s":["sw3ffb5rpu"]}],"12":[{"m":"He offered sacrifices, Ahithophel — the wise man of Israel.\n\nSacrifices mean nothing if one's heart is not with the Lord.\n\nI believe Ahithophel thought he was doing right in revolting against the king 👑.\n\nMaybe he was seeking the favour of the Lord in the matters of the overthrow of the king 👑.\n\nWhat he didn't know was that David was the Lord's man.\n\nDavid had done stuff for God for which God was going to give him an everlasting kingdom 👑.","dt":"2024-06-30T05:17:44","s":["ph4eoux8v"]}],"18":[{"m":"Were these not the same 600 who were with him in the wilderness wandering?\n\nMen who were outcasts, disgruntled, rejected, and now mighty men, helpers in war,\n\nLegends, literally.","dt":"2024-06-30T18:46:53","s":["cxkv46mby1"]}],"30":[{"m":"Is it the same Mount Olivet that Jesus reclined at ever so often... The same mount 🗻 he was arrested on after the Last Supper?\n\nDake's commentary brings a strong 💪 comparison, that just as David wept on this mount as he went up, the same way Jesus wept on his last night 🌃 of the supper.","dt":"2024-06-30T19:05:32","s":["hvemzsefjd"]}],"35":[{"m":"In as much as David trusted the Lord for restoration and also knew it was the hand of God against him for his sins.\n\nHe took practical measures to dethrone the new king 👑 and topple his kingdom.\n\nHe was not presumptuous and did not claim knowledge of the whole counsel of God.\n\nHe only trusted God to keep him or reject him.\n\nBut did all that was practically possible 🙆, and God used those measures to restore him.\n\nThe lesson is not to be presumptuous in our dealing with God.\n\nHe is God and too big... We as believers must accept that we only know in part, and that knowledge is so infinitesimal.\n\nWe are men, not God, so let's do what is practical and humanly possible 🙆 within all our abilities to make things work, whiles trusting the Lord.","dt":"2024-06-30T19:15:41","s":["8m7214u9x9"]}]},"16":{"3":[{"m":"Such a wicked lie 🤥. We must all indeed be very wise and careful in the corridors of power.\n\nInnocence and naivety cannot be tolerated; it is the bane of fools.\n\nAnd one would die if he or she chooses the path of innocence without wisdom.\n\nSo for the righteous, Jesus tells us to keep our innocence as doves 🕊 but be wise as serpents 🐍.\n\nWhy all these analogies? Because Ziba hated that he worked for a crippled son of a dead and defeated king 👑.\n\nHe was doing fine, enjoying the wealth of the dead, when suddenly Mephibosheth is discovered as an heir, and David's love for truth and covenant restores all that pertaineth to Jonathan and his descendants.\n\nI can imagine how shamed Ziba was. Imagine a caretaker flaunting the wealth of his dead masters.\n\nAnd then suddenly there comes an heir to lay claim of his inheritance; to make matters worse, he was a cripple.\n\nThat was the state of Ziba when Mephibosheth suddenly popped out of nowhere.\n\nIronically, Ziba knew all along where Mephibosheth was but never mentioned it.\n\nHe, Ziba, himself had fifteen sons and servants as well — he was great himself, and now the tables had turned and he had been made a servant again.\n\n2 Samuel 9:9-11 KJV\nThen the king called to Ziba, Saul's servant, and said unto him, I have given unto thy master's son all that pertained to Saul and to all his house.\n\n[10] Thou therefore, and thy sons, and thy servants, shall till the land for him, and thou shalt bring in the fruits, that thy master's son may have food to eat: but Mephibosheth thy master's son shall eat bread alway at my table. Now Ziba had fifteen sons and twenty servants.\n\n[11] Then said Ziba unto the king, According to all that my lord the king hath commanded his servant, so shall thy servant do. As for Mephibosheth, said the king, he shall eat at my table, as one of the king's sons.\n\nDAVID was a wise king 👑 and read the situation very well and knew what challenges such demotion would cause,\n\nSo he kept Mephibosheth in his palace always, and he ate at his table whiles Ziba slaved away for Mephibosheth.\n\nZiba didn't really slave away; he had sons and servants himself, but his pride was wounded.\n\nHe had no choice.\n\nAnd now here comes such an opportunity to discredit this crippled heir.\n\nAnd he did that skillfully and regained his stolen wealth.\n\nAnd this is where wisdom comes in.\n\nMephibosheth would not be beaten in the game. He was crippled, so was pushed aside by Ziba — such gross disrespect from a servant to a prince 🤴.\n\nHow dare Ziba even touch him, but who cares, he did and took occasion to steal generational wealth.\n\nMephibosheth also played his cards and left his beard unshaved for all the period the king 👑 was in exile.\n\nAnd his overgrown bushy beard 🧔 was evidence. A grown beard cannot be faked.\n\nHe saved his skin and kept his life and even got half the property.\n\nJustice was served. David knew he had been a bit unfair to Ziba in not giving him anything when his master's son — Mephibosheth — was introduced into the scene.\n\nTo prevent any future contests, he divided the land and held no animosity against Mephibosheth, as evidenced when he spared him from death ☠\n\n2 Samuel 21:7 KJV\nBut the king spared Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan the son of Saul, because of the LORD'S oath that was between them, between David and Jonathan the son of Saul.","dt":"2024-07-02T08:23:25","s":["cloarkmvou"]},{"m":"David had restored Mephibosheth and saved the man from untold pain and hardships and shame.\n\nIt was because of acts like this that endeared David to the Lord's heart.\n\nHe was a good man. Just imagine how a man like Jonathan, so anointed, one whom the Lord used to grant great victories to Israel, dies and his generation is suddenly treated like scumbags.\n\nHis son, his only son, was crippled, and thus his entire generation rendered useless and cut short.\n\nLife can be so cruel and painful and unfair. But David changed those fortunes.\n\nHe loved the Lord and his work and laws, and the Lord loved him, for he kept his commands and executed the Lord's will and laws and judgements.","dt":"2024-07-02T08:49:33","s":["acppe2qqlj"]}],"8":[{"m":"Though it is not stated directly in the scriptures, whenever there is the dethronement of a king 👑, much bloodshed happens as people clamor for the power and the throne.\n\nAnd the death of Saul was no different, hence Shimei's curse 🤬","dt":"2024-07-02T08:45:29","s":["p02hk25abv"]}],"15":[{"m":"I was wondering why they did not immediately chase after David and his men, because others were able to reach David and co and help them with food.\n\nWhy did not Absalom and his team chase after David?\n\nThen I realized that that would require mobilizing the army, which takes time.\n\nAt this time Joab and other key leaders had vacated post.\n\nA new leader was in place, and it would take him time to organize himself.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:14:52","s":["380f547fcg"]}],"19":[{"m":"Interesting response.\n\nIt's all agendas and games. Absalom heard and understood Hushai's response of betrayal to his father as Hushai seeking his own interests.\n\nAbsalom knew that all who were around him sought each their own good, not that they loved him, but at this time he was in power, so of course many would default to him and seek their interests in the new kingdom 👑 he had set up 👆","dt":"2024-07-02T12:18:16","s":["oy7qkoz0qg"]}],"20":[{"m":"Just as people were around him to use and benefit from him, and not necessarily because they are loyal to him, so also he immediately began to use them, their abilities, time and skill.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:19:19","s":["nigwau1o83"]}],"21":[{"m":"By this singular act, all Israel knew that forever the cords of blood between father and son were severed; there was no way any would obtain mercy from the other because of blood, seeing the abomination King Absalom had committed.\n\nDavid was definitely not going to be welcomed back by any chance.\n\nThis was the new kingdom, and it was about time the whole of Israel became forward looking and focused on the new king.\n\nThis was the whole purpose of the act of incest and abomination.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:26:10","s":["hs6fs59ckp"]},{"m":"What did Hushai do in this case? We are not told what his counter suggestion was.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:30:03","s":["zsxyvwerpd"]}],"23":[{"m":"And this testimony of Ahithophel is proved right in his counsel to Absalom about such abomination of sleeping with his father's concubines.\n\nThis was actually the word God had prophesied, and we are not told if Ahithophel knew this word or not, but he here counsels in line with the word of the Lord.\n\nThis Ahithophel a while ago was seeking the face of the Lord, and now here he was counseling contrary to the law of God.\n\n2 Samuel 15:12 KJV\nAnd Absalom sent for Ahithophel the Gilonite, David's counsellor, from his city, even from Giloh, while he offered sacrifices. And the conspiracy was strong; for the people increased continually with Absalom.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:23:36","s":["d64n9wab1w"]},{"m":"Why was this statement made after Ahithophel had given such a wicked counsel? Was that counsel also of God? In a sense it was, for the Lord had told David that that would happen.\n\nSo though that counsel was wicked, it was of God.","dt":"2026-05-21T09:06:38","s":["15fm27kcpc"]}]},"17":{"3":[{"m":"Even though some had left with David, they still had interests in Israel: land, property, friends, wives, business partners etc. Their death will have repercussions and rippling effects.\n\nSo it would be good to have all of them back in one piece, and peace upon the land, even as Absalom reigned.","dt":"2026-05-21T09:11:48","s":["mq0gafquvy"]}],"5":[{"m":"Could that have been what happened in the first case, when Ahithophel gave that wicked advice to sleep with his father's concubines?\n\nMaybe Hushai was not called for his opinion.\n\nEven though from chapter 16 verse 20 it sounds like both advisors were present, but we see that after the first advice was given, Ahithophel was asked for more advice.\n\nAfter which Hushai was called in, so though from chapter 16 verse 20 it sounds like both were present, we see from here that they more likely than not were called in, in order","dt":"2024-07-02T12:34:54","s":["f90whcrui1"]}],"8":[{"m":"Chafed in their minds... I like that expression.\n\nOther verses say they are enraged.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:37:03","s":["f50mi3jg44"]}],"12":[{"m":"I can imagine Absalom recollecting the many victories and stories of David his father in the wilderness, stories he had heard since childhood.\n\nI can imagine the counselors of Absalom agreeing with Hushai, that David can play the game of hide and seek all day long. He did it for 13 years with Saul.\n\nAbsalom wouldn't want to play that game with David. His reign was new, and so long as David was alive, his reign would never be cemented. This was not the time for the kingdom to be fragile.\n\nAll these disloyal servants wanted David dead so they know they are secure.\n\nIf not, some of the people might eventually default to the side of David, and now the kingdom will be divided.\n\nInterestingly enough — when David came back he just continued his reign with these same officers in place — no mention is made of him destroying any.\n\nHe continued working even with all these disloyal officers... the games and agendas in the corridors of power.\n\nLeading people is no joke; even the most robust and strong systems are so fragile. One moment David was king, the next moment he wasn't, and next he is back as king with these same people saluting him.\n\nI am sure a few heads rolled, especially of the obviously disloyal ones; why else did Ahithophel take his life?","dt":"2026-05-21T09:21:10","s":["36ot58ssxe"]}],"13":[{"m":"Hushai justified his advice of gathering the whole army, which of course will buy time for David to escape.\n\nAlso, if a counter argument is raised that gathering the whole of Israel is an overkill, he argued that if he gets into a particular walled city, the entire army can then fight that city without needing to remobilise.\n\nThis campaign was meant to kill David and his men at all cost, regardless.\n\nBut Hushai knew he was lying 🤥, and yet it made more sense than Ahithophel's counsel.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:43:59","s":["uktn9eh2bc"]}],"17":[{"m":"A wench — a female servant","dt":"2024-07-02T12:45:16","s":["tleqk0qvrt"]}],"22":[{"m":"As at this time, it was not known yet what the decision of the king 👑 was.\n\nMaybe Ahithophel was still lobbying very hard to ensure his counsel was taken and implemented.\n\nIt was not known what the final decision of the king would be.\n\nAhithophel's life depended on this counsel being taken, and he knew the consequences.\n\nSo likely he lobbied hard, but alas, time was spent; David and his men escaped.\n\nIt was too late.\n\nIn the wisdom of the gods it was over. In the wisdom of God it was over, and Ahithophel — the man who had access to the wisdom of God — knew so too...\n\nHe walked off, shoulders slumped. He gathered his house 🏡 hold, put his house in order.\n\nDivided his inheritance — ended his life — he was not ready to become a fugitive running 🏃 everywhere when David returned as king 👑.\n\nIt was over.\n\nThe 😔 ending of the man of wisdom.\n\nHis wisdom killed him.\n\nHe was too wise for his own good.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:56:04","s":["wahn3evju8"]}],"23":[{"m":"With such cold, calculated, almost cruel focus and straightness. He understood the implication of his decision, he foresaw what was about to happen, he weighed all the angles and possible outcomes.\n\nAnd he chose the best, or the least worst option — to preserve his posterity by putting his house in order and end his life. Maybe he risked himself and his entire family being ostracised or worse killed for his disloyalty, so he did it himself and saved them.\n\nThat man had understanding.","dt":"2026-05-21T09:25:15","s":["vk08gilkot"]}],"29":[{"m":"They were connecting themselves strategically, though their intentions were right and not for manipulation, for there was no guarantee of success. But when success did come, David rewarded his family.\n\nIt is like politics of today: when you stick your neck out for any aspirant, he rewards you when he comes into power, because of the risk you took. If he failed to come into power, you will be wrecked for a long time; you and your family will be ill treated by the opponent who won.","dt":"2026-05-21T09:30:16","s":["9rhn8a9pxw"]}],"19":[{"m":"This is all too familiar and is as when Rahab the prostitute of Jericho hid the spies.\n\nThough she used a different technique.\n\nJoshua 2:5-6 KJV\nAnd it came to pass about the time of shutting of the gate, when it was dark, that the men went out: whither the men went I wot not: pursue after them quickly; for ye shall overtake them. [6] But she had brought them up to the roof of the house, and hid them with the stalks of flax, which she had laid in order upon the roof.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:45:57","s":["t32o7eqelc"]}],"24":[{"m":"Was that not where Jacob met the host of angels? 😇\n\nGenesis 32:1-2 KJV\nAnd Jacob went on his way, and the angels of God met him. [2] And when Jacob saw them, he said, This is God's host: and he called the name of that place Mahanaim.","dt":"2024-07-02T12:57:55","s":["xy3hl72b1h"]}]},"18":{"3":[{"m":"Which city was this, and why were they faithful to David?","dt":"2026-05-21T09:32:00","s":["813hupgedw"]}],"12":[{"m":"David's men truly loved him and were loyal.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:10:13","s":["7ibmp77ujw"]}],"18":[{"m":"Ah 🤬 what a foolish exit, no name, no inheritor, no genealogy, and his story was one of rebellion and death ☠.\n\nAn example for all to learn from.\n\nHe was not even buried properly.\n\nA byword and a reproach even on death ☠.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:12:31","s":["dj0xozzku0"]}],"22":[{"m":"Sometimes, because of the transliteration of the KJV, it opens up for varied interpretation, and in this wise, only the original speakers could have told us the exact meaning, or...\n\nOf course the Holy Spirit.","dt":"2022-05-19T06:50:47","s":["7mxxg7r5em"]}],"33":[{"m":"King David was quite a sentimental and emotional leader... crying aloud so much for his son who had died from battle, which was the logical expected consequence of going to war, especially a war of this type, where rebellion and insurrection had to be snuffed out.","dt":"2026-05-22T04:39:42","s":["rh5m00ahvi"]}],"4":[{"m":"I wonder how the army of David felt, how insignificant their size was compared to the entire army of Israel.\n\nBut this was not their first time of winning a battle with the odds against them.\n\nBut they knew that to win such a battle when you are clearly outnumbered, the Lord had to be with you.\n\nThis was a battle of their lives, a do or die affair.\n\nThey stayed with David because they were loyal. As to whether he was still the Lord's anointed and favored king 👑, only time will tell.\n\nOh, these mighty loyal men of David, they began with him and now they would die with him.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:06:22","s":["w3gi8cpo3l"]}],"5":[{"m":"He loved Absalom, as only a father can love a son.\n\nI understand this father's love 😍 for his children 🧒.\n\nEven one who sought his own life.\n\nThe situation David found himself in was so very sad 😔, an abomination.\n\nFor your own son whom you love to thrust you out.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:01:40","s":["sg98ikrw1n"]}],"9":[{"m":"But what kind of battle strategy was this that Amasa and Absalom chose?\n\nLikely they thought it would favour their course, or maybe they looked at their sheer number and thought it did not matter.\n\nEven if the woods took some lives, it would not be skewed in anyone's favour, and they had more than enough men to take the city where David was lodging.\n\nWhat they didn't know was that the woods had chosen a side.\n\nThe woods were in favour of David, something Israel's army hadn't factored into their strategic plan.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:09:32","s":["9kzx05ud0g"]}],"15":[{"m":"I am sure these classified themselves as the wicked killers of Joab — young and ruthless like their master Joab. Loyal to him against the word of the king.\n\nIt is such loyalty to a subject in a kingdom against the king that breeds insurrections etc.\n\nIt happens in churches and organisations and business. No wonder churches are now so strict on loyalty and fish around for any hints of disloyalty and exterminate it. Such has become an obsession, it is no longer Christian.","dt":"2026-05-21T09:42:16","s":["77k5dfdmj9"]}]},"19":{"5":[{"m":"David was a very emotional person and a great mighty warrior.\n\nA very contrarian attribute in one.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:24:50","s":["idcsdet9k6"]}],"7":[{"m":"Only Joab, David's nephew, could thus speak to him.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:25:32","s":["ynwv14fjdh"]}],"11":[{"m":"Why are ye the last to bring the king back to his house?\n\nDavid had reinstated himself as king; the game of thrones had begun once more. And with a renewed kingdom, David took advantage to rid himself of those who had troubled him much in his first reign, namely JOAB.\n\nThough that backfired, Joab was so wicked and power drunk, he would do anything to hold on to the reins of power. David, a man of his calibre, would do anything to rid himself of such wicked men from his camp.\n\nBut that was not to be so, and JOAB stayed significantly powerful in the courts of the king even unto the death of the king.","dt":"2026-05-22T05:46:04","s":["x01dql97lq"]}],"17":[{"m":"Ziba had played his cards well: even if David did not come back, he could quickly switch allegiance to Absalom; if he came back, which he did, he had already sowed his seed of helping David with food on his exile.\n\nSo now that David was back, he was still in David's good books.","dt":"2026-05-22T05:48:40","s":["rpnk0n3lvv"]},{"m":"Shimei was wise to have first come to meet the king, and not only that, but with a 1000 men; that is quite a number and goes to show how influential the man was.","dt":"2026-05-22T05:51:05","s":["leooe06r2x"]}],"18":[{"m":"Despite everything else, Shimei was a wise person, quickly appeasing the king 👑 because he feared for his life now that David was back as king 👑.\n\nHe also came at a strategic time when the king was all too glad to be back home 🏡 and in a good mood.\n\nHe thus obtained mercy from David.\n\nKing David was battle weary 😩 and was not in the mood for vengefulness.\n\nHe just wanted to go home 🏡.\n\nIn this wise Shimei prevailed.\n\nAnd David showed mercy, but here again we see the wisdom of David.\n\nHe knew Shimei had played him, but he just couldn't help but forgive 🙏 Shimei and extend mercy.\n\nBut David was no fool; he knew his good heart ♥ was being taken advantage of, but he kept his wisdom with him.\n\nHe forgave but did not forget Shimei's dealings with him.\n\nHe knew Shimei only repented because David won the battle and was now back.\n\nBut Shimei was still a potential threat to the kingdom, especially of his son Solomon.\n\nShimei could organize a thousand men to come with him to appeal to David??? 🤯 for his life.\n\nThat is an entire army...\nShimei was no mean man 👨, he was a man of influence.\n\nA potential threat in the future 🔮 🙆.\n\nSo he left a charge to his son Solomon to devise a way to deal with Shimei, and he did.\n\nAnd it worked: Shimei died from his own way.\n\nDavid was indeed God's man; things just worked for his good.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:38:42","s":["3ldc86chd3"]}],"20":[{"m":"To come first, before the king settled down and began to take record and exact revenge, was a very wise move to save his own life.","dt":"2026-05-22T05:51:53","s":["aail91vujx"]}],"14":[{"m":"DAVID was a very wise statesman.\n\nHe knew when to be assertive and proactive and when to restrain and watch what God does.\n\nHe was indeed very wise. No wonder his son Solomon took after same.\n\nMostly wisdom is attributed to Solomon, but David was a very wise king 👑.\n\nIndeed Solomon gives us a hint of this when he talks of how his father showed him the ways of wisdom.\n\nProverbs 4:3 KJV\nFor I was my father's son, tender and only beloved in the sight of my mother.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:29:31","s":["7kjse9zoeh"]}],"22":[{"m":"Same thing Saul said when he was first king, but then he became proud at heart and in his later years was very wicked and heartless. David maintained his humility and frame all through his reign.\n\nSo the Lord loved him to the end, and he was a man after God's own heart.","dt":"2026-05-22T05:53:34","s":["f96svyn65t"]}],"37":[{"m":"These indeed honored their parents, and rightly so.\n\nParents literally lay down their lives that their sons and daughters can have a life...","dt":"2024-07-02T13:41:11","s":["vyzzlbyq9q"]}],"43":[{"m":"Ei asem oo, matter. I am sure the posturing of the men of Judah started all this. It was a posture of “David is our king and the rest of you are subject to us”, but Israel indeed had ten parts in David, even though Judah could have argued that Israel conspired to dethrone the king. But that can be countered by the fact that the king's own son, of Judah, headed the revolt.","dt":"2026-05-22T06:01:22","s":["ol8p208qvm"]}]},"20":{"20":[{"m":"However fierce and wicked they were, these warriors and Joab... There is some room for reason in their heart.\n\nAnd this room this wise woman was bold to enter.\n\nIt takes boldness and tact so you do not offend when trying to access the heart and ears of the great.\n\nLord, grant me such wisdom, I pray.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:49:33","s":["e9pt01pedu"]}],"22":[{"m":"That is wisdom, they sacrificed one to preserve all...\n\nUnlike the men of Ephraim who chose to stand with the sodomites of the land till they were almost foolishly exterminated.\n\nI don't know how the woman 👩 convinced the elders of the land to disown Sheba.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:55:28","s":["8lan0qrx7y"]}]},"21":{"9":[{"m":"Aside Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, with whom David had a covenant, and was thus spared, what other criteria was used in selecting the others?\n\nGrace, grace. May Grace locate us.\n\nYou notice the other 5 were sons of concubines, like the main wives of Saul were spared. This was indeed a tough call.\n\nMay God grant us grace that when the sword falls in the time of adversity, may we be spared in the mighty name of Jesus, we and our children.","dt":"2026-05-23T06:44:20","s":["bj0lwojzgd"]}],"10":[{"m":"The one with two children fought for them in their death, yet the one with 5 children has no record of her. That is not to say she was not grieved or did not mourn for them, but what Rizpah did was out of the ordinary.","dt":"2026-05-23T06:41:33","s":["mjpl3czz8v"]}],"14":[{"m":"Why would David do this?\n\nSee what the audacity of one woman produced: a befitting burial not just for her sons but for her ancestors.","dt":"2026-05-23T06:45:37","s":["q2kncvde29"]}],"21":[{"m":"The warrior spirit runs in the family.","dt":"2024-07-02T14:03:05","s":["qiczjpif04"]}],"4":[{"m":"Strange things happen in this world 🗺.\nMay we find favour before the Lord so he gives us the wisdom and grace we need to be victorious.","dt":"2024-07-02T13:57:36","s":["ebdu1wkl9j"]}]},"23":{"19":[{"m":"There was rank and order among David's mighty men.","dt":"2024-07-06T02:55:17","s":["15butmb0l0"]}]},"24":{"2":[{"m":"Joab, Joab, the good, the bad and the ugly, or more appropriately the ugliest.\n\nJoab really played dirty and would do anything to keep his rank.\n\nHe was also very useful and beneficial to the king 👑.\n\nHe did the king's dirty jobs at times, as in the case of Uriah, and could talk truth to power, as in when the king 👑 wept over Absalom to the detriment of his own people, and now here in restraining the king 👑 from numbering the people, though he was unsuccessful.\n\nHe played all kinds of roles in this kingdom.\n\nDavid being a king, handling Joab was indeed a thorn in the flesh he could not seem to get rid of no matter what.\n\nJoab played the game of politics really well and could not be replaced.\n\nDespite the pain Joab caused to David, he had to use him here.\n\nLeadership is not easy. David had much suffering because of Joab's excesses, but he had to manage him; despite the pain, he sent Joab to do this errand.\n\nI can imagine the pain in David's heart ♥, yet all the while he sent and spoke with Joab.\n\nJoab had killed many innocent lives, and it was a stain on David's reign.\n\nDavid had to go to lengths to mourn such dead so that it becomes evident he had no hand in it.\n\nDespite all this pain, David managed to live and work with Joab.\n\nLord, make me a wise leader, help me excel in all I do.","dt":"2024-07-08T06:28:02","s":["nz73v7s133"]}],"6":[{"m":"This thing which displeased the Lord so much 🙏 will inure to the benefit of the Lord in helping keep proper records.\n\nGod has a way of turning and making good that which was meant for evil 😈.\n\nDavid and Israel got punished for this, but the records were not burnt or destroyed but kept for future use, as we see in the verse preceding.","dt":"2024-07-08T06:30:24","s":["8yvp9cwtf7"]}],"13":[{"m":"The question 🙋 I ask is this: how in the world 🗺 could God orchestrate these things, being a spirit?\n\nI get the famine part and the pestilence, but David fleeing before his enemies 🏃?\n\nDoes that mean the so-called enemies of David were actually stooges and tools in the hands 👐 of God to bring him glory?\n\nSo by implication all the wars of David and his victories were just God choosing which side should win, and this was easy since he had both sides of the divide ➗ in his pocket and chooses what he wants for each side.\n\nJust that because David pleased 😌 him, he chose always.\n\nThat was a very rare feat, for one to win always.\n\nDavid was indeed special in the heart of the Lord.\n\nOh Lord, help me walk in wisdom before thee all the days of my life.","dt":"2024-07-08T06:35:27","s":["1q08g9ul09"]}],"24":[{"m":"This verse, used of many to raise support in the Church and compel congregants to give over and above their comfortabilities.","dt":"2024-07-08T06:40:45","s":["ah4h6z3dsm"]}],"11":[{"m":"When did Gad become David's seer? Where was Nathan? Meaning there was more than one active prophet in David's time to the palace and the throne.\n\nBecause later we see Nathan at David's deathbed, meaning they were still cordial and there was no animosity.","dt":"2026-05-28T07:57:46","s":["1tb1v9tyhe"]}]},"22":{"42":[{"m":"Even his enemies 🚶, the enemies of God, called him in the day of trouble, but David destroyed them.\n\nReminds me of the expression: there is no atheist in the pit.","dt":"2024-07-05T20:22:45","s":["jmjgrtxm8n"]}]}},"Judges":{"1":{"1":[{"m":"So the promise of them taking the land continued even after Joshua. God's words indeed are sure.\n\nAnd come to think of it, how could the words of the Lord end with Joshua?\n\nWords that started centuries before Joshua could in no wise die with him, though he was a great leader.\n\nIndeed the words of the Lord never failed, and even millennia down the line the word continues to hold 👫.\n\nAnd the generations that serve him wholeheartedly, he deals 🤝 truly with them, and they lay claim of their inheritance, but the next generation, or whichever generation is shrewd and unfaithful, he abandons, so they know that it is not by might, neither by power, but by his Spirit and Spirit alone.\n\nIndeed the timelines can even be shorter.\n\nIn a lifetime, when a generation or individual serves the Lord, all goes well, but in that same lifetime things can go horribly off if one turns away from the Lord.\n\nWhen we turn away he turns away, but when we are faithless he remains faithful, for he cannot deny himself.\n\n2 Timothy 2:12-13 KJV\nIf we suffer, we shall also reign with him: if we deny him, he also will deny us: [13] If we believe not, yet he abideth faithful: he cannot deny himself.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:55:04","s":["hc2lalaebh"]}],"18":[{"m":"Gaza was of Israel in times past.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:57:00","s":["x66w4kh9f"]}],"34":[{"m":"This was the failure of the tribes; they should have had a long-term plan to completely drive the people out, such that if they could not do it in a particular period, they ought to have a plan to continue.\n\nBut alas, they did not obey the Lord fully.\n\nThough somewhere it says the Lord did not completely drive the people out in order to test them.\n\nOK, I've found the verse.\n\nJudges 2:2-3 KJV\nAnd ye shall make no league with the inhabitants of this land; ye shall throw down their altars: but ye have not obeyed my voice: why have ye done this? [3] Wherefore I also said, I will not drive them out from before you; but they shall be as thorns in your sides, and their gods shall be a snare unto you.\n\nSo the reason God did not drive the people out was because Israel themselves failed to obey the voice of the Lord.\n\nSo he let them reap the natural consequences of their actions.","dt":"2024-05-14T10:00:16","s":["nj9f1f14bi"]}],"35":[{"m":"After the death of Joshua, things began to go south. I wonder why Joshua did not have a protégé whom he was to hand over to. Maybe the dynamics this time were different.\n\nNow they were each settled according to their tribe in their respective inheritance, so to raise one person from a tribe over the others was a challenge. Or MAYBE not, because they have always dwelt in tribes, even when Moses was their head. Though that was in the wilderness.\n\nWe see a similar thing in the times of the kings: under Saul and David and Solomon there was unity, and the hand of God selected people, but after a whiles it also failed.\n\nIt seems God is not interested in permanently setting up systems and rulers for his people, even though that works best when he is in charge. But he sets up systems and expects his people to take over and continue with the system he has set up.\n\nBut man, in our flaws, messes things up.\nBut God is good.","dt":"2026-03-30T06:14:48","s":["ekm5lteqvn"]}],"26":[{"m":"😢... He carried the memory of his beloved lost city 🏙 with him.\n\nIt's almost like me losing Accra and being the only survivor and resettling in, say, Kumasi.\n\nAnd renaming my settlement Accra. I might live in a state of perpetual sadness and retell my children stories of Accra.\n\nOh, I can imagine the man's great loss... His friends, favorite spots etc.\n\nIt is well.","dt":"2022-04-14T02:15:20","s":["6i7xj59z0f"]}]},"2":{"11":[{"m":"Why was it easier to serve other gods? I think 🤔 it's because, one, the other nations had been formed ages ahead of Israel, and their gods had set up traditions and customs that kept their people in service.\n\nThey had the benefit of time, and secondly, and a stronger reason, other gods appealed to the flesh and its lusts.\n\nSexual immorality was rife among some gods, or the practice of it did not affect the relations of the god with his people.","dt":"2022-04-14T02:31:49","s":["n2ym8kpxgk"]}],"23":[{"m":"A good summary of the book of Judges.","dt":"2022-04-14T02:33:48","s":["sjlygl83zb"]},{"m":"Oh OK... So this started even from the days of Joshua.\n\nJoshua did his best, but the people had their own way.","dt":"2024-05-14T10:04:49","s":["bvcw7idl9a"]}],"10":[{"m":"I'm trying to understand this statement.\n\nThey knew not the Lord in the sense that they had not experienced him for themselves.\n\nThey knew not his works because now they were at rest and had not seen the works of the Lord.\n\nThe generation that saw the works were all dead.\n\nThrough his works and dealings with them via punishment etc., the generation knew his works and knew the Lord.\n\nIt is possible to know the works of the Lord yet not know him, as we see in the 1st generation of Israel from Egypt.\n\nTheir children did better in knowing both the Lord and his works.\n\nThis current generation knew none except stories told them by the fathers.\n\nThey were at ease and in the promised land.\n\nNo wonder God commanded all enemies of God be destroyed, so they teach not their children their way, thus deceiving them.","dt":"2022-04-14T02:20:41","s":["23gx5om45l"]}]},"3":{"2":[{"m":"Aside to test them and keep them in line, yet another reason for leaving some enemies behind.\n\nGod is very logical.","dt":"2022-04-14T08:04:29","s":["5o1z1udtg0"]}],"30":[{"m":"How one event of killing ten thousand valiant men rang through time and produced an impact lasting 80 years — literally two ✌️ generations.\n\nCertain occurrences in life ring through the sands of time...","dt":"2024-05-15T10:17:18","s":["f4b55phe7d"]}],"31":[{"m":"How did just his feat silence the Philistines? I suspect stories of Shamgar began to travel around, and no one wanted to mess up with him or Israel. It was a psychological defeat.","dt":"2026-04-01T06:27:23","s":["3mskrsx48w"]}],"12":[{"m":"Ah, God strengthens the enemies of Israel so they could turn back to him.\n\nSo it's not true that the devil only uses the enemies of God.\n\nGod can and does use them for his own purposes and intent.","dt":"2024-05-15T08:15:59","s":["jlbfi2cts6"]}]},"4":{"11":[{"m":"This insert just pops up out of nowhere but will play a role 11 or so verses later in the passage.\n\nIt seems out of place but has its purpose.","dt":"2024-05-15T10:20:46","s":["9w4jnjermk"]}],"16":[{"m":"Wow, this is what we call complete and outright victory ✌️.\n\nThe army was completely vanquished.","dt":"2024-05-15T10:22:22","s":["qb0baddd9m"]}],"18":[{"m":"Was it late at night 🌃 and the weather cold ❄, or was it the weather conditions at the time...\nHe needed rest, but why the cover if it was afternoon?\n\nI presume it was cold weather.","dt":"2024-05-15T10:24:40","s":["x6q5h2xxb7"]}]},"6":{"9":[{"m":"The people had forgotten their covenant with the Lord... Life happened, but the Lord did not forget. It is understandable that the people were not there when the covenant was made, but that did not matter; their very existence is tied to that covenant, so in that wise the covenant was legally binding on them.\n\nGod had protected and kept them alive on account of that, so they having not been part of it did not matter.","dt":"2026-04-01T18:52:07","s":["ff2ntqnl2v"]}],"23":[{"m":"This happens. Many times... It appears the Lord detests his children fearing because of him or something supernatural.\nHe always brings that assurance needed.\n\nNow that awareness of the supernatural had been created, and that God was with him and had chosen him.\n\nGod could now directly speak to him.\n\nHe, Gideon, was now aware that the supernatural is close.","dt":"2024-05-17T06:04:50","s":["bqagv0gm6g"]}],"30":[{"m":"Oh, when did they get in so low an estate that the worshippers of Baal rather crucified the worshippers of Jehovah?","dt":"2022-04-15T20:09:01","s":["89onba2z9x"]}],"31":[{"m":"It seems Joash was a leader in a sense in his family 👪 for the people to have even given him attention.\n\nIt also goes to show how backslidden the people had become.","dt":"2024-05-17T06:07:43","s":["1u2zm3oemd"]}],"33":[{"m":"It seems that a spirit or some unseen force had gathered the enemy for this battle, so the Lord can destroy them.\n\nLooking at the order of events, the Midianites ravaged Israel for years,\n\nThen now the Lord tells Gideon he would use him mightily to save Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nNext thing we see, Midian gather in their number with other enemies for a full-fledged war.\n\nIdeally Israel would have fled, but next we see the Spirit of the Lord come upon Gideon with an anointing to gather.\n\nThis scene reminds me of the gathering to Armageddon, where a final death ☠ blow was to be dealt the enemies of God.\n\nAnd we see that same spirit gather the enemies and the people of God for to destroy the enemy.","dt":"2023-11-22T04:01:50","s":["j7nat93m0v"]}],"34":[{"m":"One of my personal all-time favorite verses.","dt":"2022-04-15T22:45:25","s":["yi91pq3maa"]},{"m":"Anytime the Spirit of the Lord comes upon his people, they are endued with extraordinary ability.\n\nThey know something different has come upon them, and they know it is the Lord.\n\nAnd with the Lord upon them, they can do anything and will be victorious in their wars and overcome the challenges and their enemies.\n\nThey had heard of men and women who did great things because the Lord was with them.\n\nNow here they were, almost like a dream, the Spirit of the Lord has come upon them too, and they can do mighty works.\n\nThere is much the Holy Ghost 👻 endues us with which we underutilize because we do not recognize the import of his Spirit upon us.\n\nWe often jump and roll on the floor and get up and do nothing with such an ability of a lifetime.\n\nHere in Gideon is wisdom for us. The Spirit of the Lord came upon him, and he blew the trumpet 🎺, and Abiezer was gathered to him.\nHis people and kinsmen were gathered to him.","dt":"2024-05-17T06:25:42","s":["rrc66d8sjn"]}],"39":[{"m":"He knew God could do anything, so such fleecing was doable by him.","dt":"2024-05-17T06:32:26","s":["o7mn358v35"]}],"8":[{"m":"How come they always remember the Lord?\n\nMeaning not that they had forgotten him, but wanted to chase their own lusts.\n\nThen when they began to reap the consequences of their action, they repented.\n\nMeaning they would not have if there were no consequences, but how can there be no consequences for actions not just contrary to God's word and ordinances, as the ceremonial cleansing and rituals,\n\nBut actions contrary to nature itself, as homosexuality, bestiality and child molestation through sacrifice.\n\nNature will itself reject the people. The land will vomit 🤮 them out.\n\nThe sicknesses and diseases from illicit sex.\n\nThe confusion from whorish lifestyle.\n\nThe deaths and wickedness from demonic worship 🛐, including that of babies 🤱.\n\nHere in Africa 🌍, where juju is common.\nSo much wickedness is committed by it, including death of the innocent and what have you.\n\nThe laws of God are indeed perfect 👌\n\nPsalm 19:7-10,14 KJV\nThe law of the LORD is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of the LORD is sure, making wise the simple. [8] The statutes of the LORD are right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the LORD is pure, enlightening the eyes. [9] The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the LORD are true and righteous altogether. [10] More to be desired are they than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb. [14] Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.","dt":"2024-05-16T06:46:41","s":["6l0upd4dmb"]}],"18":[{"m":"See Gideon's reaction and response; it was almost as if they expected miracles and the supernatural.\n\nBased on the stories they had been told, they knew it was not unusual for the supernatural to happen to them.\n\nBut each generation really finds it difficult to connect and relate to the stories of the supernatural because it did not happen to them.\n\nBut to the eternal God, who lives through all time, he can and does connect the dots.\n\nThat is why our trust is in him.","dt":"2024-05-17T05:56:51","s":["6q4ha4zwvh"]}],"21":[{"m":"This is how a sacrifice is accepted before the Lord. He set it ablaze, causing the fire 🔥 to consume it.\n\nIn such difficult times, for Gideon to prepare such a meal for the Lord shows the extent of sacrifice.","dt":"2024-05-17T06:02:02","s":["6oiqhv3uwl"]}]},"7":{"2":[{"m":"God's strategy differs in times and seasons.\n\nWith Gideon the people were too many.\n\nWith Joshua against Ai, he asked for the entire army to go against a few people.\n\nWe must know what the will of the Lord is and to follow it.","dt":"2024-05-17T06:35:47","s":["z7qa7f2izz"]}],"10":[{"m":"Here it wasn't even Gideon who asked for help 😣 with his fears.\n\nIt was God who suggested, and all too gladly he accepted.","dt":"2024-05-17T08:30:59","s":["zeh6qwdd0h"]}],"13":[{"m":"Israel in their state were more than capable of overcoming their enemies, but sadly they were under the enemy, and they ruled over them.\n\nALL they needed was a commander, someone who could gather them and whom the people were willing to rally behind.","dt":"2024-05-17T08:33:29","s":["ucnsg15471"]}],"17":[{"m":"Where did Gideon get this strategy from?\n\nLikely the Lord told him, cos it doesn't make sense.","dt":"2024-05-17T08:36:12","s":["wapitr7uer"]}],"18":[{"m":"Who gave him this strategy... Likely the Lord himself, though it was not stated.","dt":"2026-04-01T20:07:36","s":["9a5gjfjm64"]}],"24":[{"m":"It seems in the time of old, whenever there was such close border war, the fields and property of the losing party were loot for all for the winning side.","dt":"2024-05-17T17:07:17","s":["segsxq8yz1"]}],"8":[{"m":"When God asks you to do something extraordinary and possibly dangerous or out of the ordinary,\n\nYou have got to wait on him for the way out and the plans each step of the way.\n\nGideon could have run off with the fact that the Spirit of the Lord is upon him.\n\nBut rather, where he felt doubt 🤷‍♂️ he asked for further clarity,\n\nWhere he feared he asked God for help.","dt":"2024-05-17T08:29:35","s":["byhxt4s73o"]}]},"8":{"1":[{"m":"Ephraim and Manasseh were brothers, sons of Joseph, so I guess they expected their brother to call 🤙 on them for this war.","dt":"2024-05-17T17:14:37","s":["38lemmfrlo"]}],"11":[{"m":"How could just three smite 15000?\nExcept that the Lord was with them.\n\nOr maybe the Lord confounded 😖 them once more, and they turned on themselves as at the first.","dt":"2024-05-17T17:17:02","s":["7tbg5q18z1"]}],"16":[{"m":"The elders should have known better and, being elders 🧓, should have ensured the right 👉 thing was done.\n\nI don't justify the beatings though... But this was ancient warfare.","dt":"2024-05-17T17:18:55","s":["4xly5c5khb"]}],"18":[{"m":"How do the children of a king look like? Likely had royal regalia and had this regal appearance about them.","dt":"2026-04-02T05:44:33","s":["epi6682p32"]}],"20":[{"m":"Probably Gideon wanted to give his firstborn exposure of war.\n\nHe wanted to let him have his first kill, and that being a king 👑.\n\nThat would have been something to brag about in his later days.\n\nIndeed word would have gone round and legends spun of the man who killed two kings at a go, Zebah and Zalmunna, when he was only a boy 🧒.\n\nYada Yada Yada","dt":"2024-05-18T06:31:10","s":["ofp6ur2ebe"]}],"24":[{"m":"Dake explains that all Midianites were called Ishmeelites, but not vice versa.\n\nHe goes to further explain that that clarifies the confusion in Genesis chapter 24 where Ishmaelites and Midianites were used interchangeably.","dt":"2024-05-18T06:40:33","s":["9qlzpu42dg"]}],"32":[{"m":"Would Gideon be in heaven? Yes, I believe so. Would he be chided for his error of creating an ephod that led the people astray? Yes.\n\nIf so, then what kind of people make heaven? What criteria is used in selecting Old Testament saints with all these atrocities hanging around their neck? They must love the Lord their God and their heart set on him despite their mistakes and wrongs.\n\nSome of these Old Testament folks were not so hyper-spiritual, but they loved the Lord... So now this makes me wonder — how about New Testament saints?\n\nWe have our flaws and weaknesses, but we love the Lord — I believe we would make heaven, but there are different reward systems for different levels of commitment.","dt":"2026-04-02T05:51:09","s":["s874t1xnnf"]}],"34":[{"m":"They had forgotten the conquest of Midian by the hand of 300 men.\n\nThis was not a story of men centuries ago, of some Red Sea 🌊 crossing and escape from Pharaoh,\n\nThis was the story of Gideon, which had happened not too long ago and was fresh in their minds.\n\nBut it doesn't matter to a people whose heart is bent on harlotry.\n\nJust that God made sure to do his part of leaving them without excuse.\n\nAnd thus God deals with us; he is spirit and gives us opportunity always, so we will be without excuse all the days of our lives.\n\nGiving everyone opportunity one way or another. He is spirit and cannot do what flesh must do, so he would open doors and give opportunities, trusting that we would maximize it.\n\nHe would do his part, but we must do ours.","dt":"2024-05-18T06:46:21","s":["7gghmdvxg4"]}],"10":[{"m":"That is such a huge number of men; no wonder after such great victories it takes decades for the enemy to recover, and usually by which a new generation arises that know not the LORD and rebel against him.\n\nCreating a perfect time bomb for the enemy to beat them into submission.","dt":"2026-04-02T05:42:13","s":["056p0t6wgf"]}]},"9":{"5":[{"m":"Aww, so painful.\nGideon should have accepted the offer to be king 👑.\n\nBut that would be contrary to God's ideal theocracy.\n\nBut then again, if they had read the book of the law day and night as instructed, they would have known that God spoke of a time ⌚ of kings 👑 for the children 🧒 of Israel.\n\nMaybe this was the time.\n\nAn aside: where are men used of God mightily like Gideon etc.?\n\nAre they in hell or heaven?\n\nConsidering some went astray like Solomon, Samson etc. Though some repented in their last days.\n\nWell, I don't know. It was just a thought 💭","dt":"2024-05-18T07:00:55","s":["snu7nr1pnu"]}],"50":[{"m":"The conspiracy of Gaal had really spread far, from city to city, and now Abimelech was coming for them all.","dt":"2026-04-02T05:59:08","s":["c398li3vfg"]}],"57":[{"m":"So it worked; the curse of JOTHAM worked.","dt":"2026-04-02T06:00:43","s":["j5ih78dkhb"]}],"7":[{"m":"Was Mount 🗻 Gerizim not one of the mountains ⛰ of witness against Israel... For curses 🤬 and blessings?\n\nJust checked. Yep, it is. Though it is the one of blessings.\n\nDeuteronomy 11:29 KJV\nAnd it shall come to pass, when the LORD thy God hath brought thee in unto the land whither thou goest to possess it, that thou shalt put the blessing upon mount Gerizim, and the curse upon mount Ebal.","dt":"2024-05-18T07:03:05","s":["n8m5twn7ls"]}]},"10":{"6":[{"m":"The gods of other lands had the effect of bringing the children 🧒 of Israel into poverty whiles prospering surrounding nations.\n\nThe God of Israel, Jehovah, had the opposite effect: he made rich the people and helped Israel triumph 😤 over their enemies.","dt":"2024-05-18T11:14:07","s":["spec2ul5ck"]}],"14":[{"m":"Hold on, that is a valid point. Why didn't the gods whom they had chosen over God deliver them?\n\nI get it that if God was now siding with their enemies, and say these new gods of theirs were now siding with Israel, God will win since he is God of all gods.\n\nHowever, if God was neutral, which he is not, how come then Israel lost against their enemies?\n\nBecause it is obvious that though the other nations did not worship God, God uses them to punish Israel his people, whom he had procured by covenant and would therefore not and cannot leave them for another people.\n\nI also wonder, why did not somehow the people of other nations change their gods and somehow worship Jehovah,\n\nEspecially seeing the miracles and power he demonstrates on behalf of his people?\n\nI think it is because the laws of God are contrary to our very human nature, and so to be tempted to do what is right is so not possible.\n\nServing God must be a deliberate decision to go against what is natural.\n\nYou cannot be tempted to do what is right, but you can always be tempted to do wrong, and that so easily, because it lines up with our sinful nature.","dt":"2026-04-03T05:32:22","s":["dy74113m71"]}]},"11":{"36":[{"m":"His daughter was well brought up in the beliefs of her father.","dt":"2026-04-03T07:57:38","s":["bpan6k2zq7"]}],"40":[{"m":"This was the cost of her victory... Yet after all these the people went a-whoring after other gods, but at least for the period the people served the Lord.\n\nShe was a worthy sacrifice.","dt":"2026-04-03T07:59:57","s":["ozlxwnh0in"]}],"33":[{"m":"As God gave Jephthah victory ✌️, he knew who would be coming out of his house to meet him, yet he both gave the victory ✌️ to Jephthah and allowed his daughter to come out to meet him.\n\nI believe God did not interfere but rather allowed things to take their natural course.\n\nHe knew Jephthah's daughter would come out, much to his regret, but he permitted it.\n\nIt was a vow.","dt":"2024-05-19T05:52:02","s":["rppxr0qoml"]}],"39":[{"m":"Wow, very painful indeed.\n\nSo here we see that his offering his daughter as a burnt offering was not literally burning 🔥 her, but she was to be dedicated to the Lord all the days of her life forever.\n\nIt was a Nazarite vow, but forever.","dt":"2024-05-19T05:49:00","s":["rrgt80yt4s"]}]},"12":{"1":[{"m":"These men of Ephraim seem such litigants. They had the same issue with their brother Manasseh in the times of Gideon.","dt":"2024-05-19T05:53:07","s":["mhgo4gb4vp"]}],"12":[{"m":"They judged Israel for a pretty short time... Was it that they were selected judges in their old age? Very likely.","dt":"2026-04-03T08:04:19","s":["f6v30pl5t3"]}],"14":[{"m":"Everyone had their peculiarities... What story do I want said of me when I pass?","dt":"2024-05-19T05:55:03","s":["42fwr3xkuw"]},{"m":"They had large family size, which was a sign of respect in their day... Just as having a large business with many workers is in our days.","dt":"2026-04-03T08:07:10","s":["3riswbczo2"]}]},"13":{"8":[{"m":"Because in the culture and commands the man had the power and right to overrule his wife, the Lord came again to confirm to the husband also.\n\nIs it not however interesting that even the second time he came to the woman again, who then went to call the man?\n\nI think throughout scripture, with the exception of Abraham, when it came to barrenness God dealt with the women, not the men, mostly.","dt":"2026-04-04T08:03:57","s":["ce5wdnrs1k"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why did he not come when the man was around? But yet again Manoah was not around, even though this coming was in answer to prayer.\n\nHe was later called for though.","dt":"2022-04-20T02:06:06","s":["n853ab7zo9"]}],"18":[{"m":"It sounds more like the 😇 angel was saying, \"Why do you ask my name, seeing it is divine and not of the earth 🌎?\"","dt":"2022-04-20T02:10:02","s":["3hj90ou99a"]},{"m":"Indeed it was Gabriel who mentioned his name. But this angel 😇 behaved just like the one who wrestled with God and refused to reveal his name.\n\nWhy he refused is a mystery.","dt":"2024-05-19T05:59:28","s":["wj631mziqk"]}],"25":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔\nWhat is the meaning of this sentence?\n\nIn which way did the Spirit of the Lord begin to move him?\n\nIs it that sometimes he felt a stirring and thus began to go wild and into the caves and dens to be all by himself?\n\nOr he began to prophesy?","dt":"2024-05-19T12:39:57","s":["9qiegqv0hu"]}]},"15":{"10":[{"m":"They had such a superman in their midst, yet sadly did not face up to the Philistines in a war they would have won easily.\n\nHmm 🤔 such is life... When people are presented with the opportunity of a lifetime but blow it, and the next generation or opportunity has to be worked harder for.\n\nSo much harder for.","dt":"2024-05-19T18:40:25","s":["ldybzc3qtb"]}],"14":[{"m":"It seemed their shouts against him was what triggered the anointing and stirred him up to slay them with a great slaughter.","dt":"2024-05-19T18:36:24","s":["ymjg45v0ai"]}],"17":[{"m":"I can only imagine. I wish I was there to see how one man killed a thousand. Was he super fast and super strong 💪, or both? Like Flash? Naa, I don't think that fast, to the point of stopping time.","dt":"2022-04-20T07:54:25","s":["tlag0xbzw2"]}],"20":[{"m":"He judged Israel 20 years... We are not told the age at his death, but Samson's super power stayed with him all through his adult years to his death.","dt":"2024-05-19T18:38:34","s":["mjxuigin81"]}]},"16":{"5":[{"m":"How did they know to ask? What made them think his strength had a source and a weakness or way about it?\n\nI suspect partly because Samson's physique was like any normal man 👨.\n\nIt did not make sense, the strength 💪 he displayed.\n\nI'm sure they had also noticed that something seems to come on Samson and he shakes himself in a certain way.\n\nOr the reverse: he shakes himself in a certain way, then something, some super strength 💪, comes on him.\n\nAgain it appears Samson could rely on his strength 💪 constantly; it never failed.\n\nHe could rely on the spirit of might to be at work, be it when a lion 🦁 pounces on him surprisingly or when an army awaits him.\n\nNow back to the point, it took the Philistines 20 years to come to this conclusion and strategy.\n\nCouldn't they have arrived at this conclusion earlier??\n\nThey just kept piling on men after men, dead after dead, piles of their people, before they realized it's not in the numbers.\n\nSomehow we all often are slow to learn.","dt":"2022-04-20T08:05:06","s":["w693aetm0b"]}],"12":[{"m":"What became of the liers in wait?\n\nMaybe they ran off after they realized the deception.\n\nBut this makes you wonder, why did they not just run at him with a dagger or spear?\n\nMaybe his skin did not get pierced through with spear or any weapon 🔫.\n\nHow else did he defeat 1000 men?\n\nThis is a very strange ability; not only was he physically very strong 💪 but impregnable as a person.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:13:49","s":["c77e5jfilq"]}],"17":[{"m":"So Samson obviously was not like any other man.\n\nHe did not speak of not drinking 🍻 or eating unclean things in his Nazarite vow.\n\nHis focus was on the hair 💇. Could it be that things eased up a little bit and the vow was on the hair only?","dt":"2022-04-20T08:39:51","s":["pil7eoxr6d"]},{"m":"Obviously the no drinking part and keeping the very laws of God, he was exempted from consequences, though it's a part of the Nazarite vows.\n\nOr should we say it was delayed consequences?\n\nIf Samson had lived right, loved his own people and kept the laws of God, he would have lived longer and gotten greater victories for Israel.\n\nBut he wasn't interested in that. He wanted fun.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:32:10","s":["xdjxma2xlo"]}],"21":[{"m":"So the vow was on the hair 💇, not the other conditions of the Nazarite vow.\n\nHe was even intermarrying with the Philistines, and yet his strength remained.","dt":"2022-04-20T08:44:05","s":["bmhumc12i"]}],"23":[{"m":"This did not look much like divine intervention; it was their own wits, but of course they gave honour to their gods.","dt":"2022-04-20T08:45:22","s":["ioxbdgh2je"]},{"m":"It was not their god but the use of their head 🤕.\n\nBut well, I guess their very lives belonged to their god, so by extension their brains 🧠","dt":"2024-05-20T07:33:57","s":["0ylm54wnx3"]}],"31":[{"m":"Oh Samson, the mighty judge of Israel. He should not have died thus.\n\nHe was brought back to his heritage — his spiritual heritage, where the Lord moved him betimes by his Spirit in the land of Dan, between Zorah and Eshtaol.","dt":"2022-04-20T08:48:41","s":["se7es2gjr9"]},{"m":"In the very same place where the Spirit of the Lord began to move him.\n\nOh, what an ending. What a waste and sad ending of this man 👨 of God.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:37:10","s":["ftedprmtnp"]},{"m":"So his father had died knowing his son was just playing around.\n\nAnointed but with strange lusts.\n\nOnly God knew the kind of complaints he had to endure because of his son Samson.\n\nI life.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:43:43","s":["t9l699lp5i"]}],"3":[{"m":"The reason I suspect the posts were lifted with the gate was because of how strongly attached the gate was to the posts.\n\nIt was supposed to be impenetrable.\n\nThis was a city gate after all.\n\nAnd yet Samson carried gate, posts, bar and all.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:01:32","s":["bpuv0e46iz"]}],"6":[{"m":"Strange contrarian circumstances.\n\nSamson was so much in love, his heart was captivated by Delilah, and in return yet her love was for money.\n\nObviously she in no way loved Samson, or she loved money more than she did Samson.\n\nWhy Samson decided to play on the devil's turf is difficult to understand.\n\nBreaking the very laws of God with his promiscuous lifestyle.\n\nI don't know if this also was of the Lord, his falling for Delilah.\n\nThe Bible is silent 😶 on that, so we can presume otherwise.\n\nIt was not God's will, but it still turned out to bring God victory ✌️.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:06:16","s":["tqggaep2fu"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why would Samson continue with this woman 👩 after this event?\n\nHe had become so comfortable and very careless.\n\nIn fact, beyond careless with his life.\n\nNo wonder scripture says take heed, you who think you stand.\n\n1 Corinthians 10:12 KJV\nWherefore let him that thinketh he standeth take heed lest he fall.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:09:30","s":["c6jjgwpjy3"]}],"11":[{"m":"So they knew his strength was supernatural, and it would take something supernatural to defeat him... It took them at least 20 years to figure out that he must have a weakness which they can then use to defeat him.\n\nAlso it seems Samson never married... He just loved women, and foreign women were his preference and undoing.","dt":"2026-04-05T09:48:00","s":["w3ixkz5g45"]}],"13":[{"m":"Now he was getting closer to the truth, i.e. his hair.","dt":"2022-04-20T08:37:07","s":["slrss02yh2"]},{"m":"Now he was getting dangerously closer to home 🏡, his lock of hair.\n\nIt was the same way he was pestered into revealing his riddle.\n\nHis weakness was women.\n\nFor Samson to be giving these outrageous suggestions, yet he was believed, goes to show that the Philistines believed Samson's strength 💪 was a power from the gods.\n\nIt's very likely they might have even enchanted and tried to weaken him spiritually, but all to no avail.\n\nThese men were idol worshipers; only God knows how much enchantment has been made against Samson to either destroy or decipher the truth and mystery of his strength 💪, but nothing worked.\n\nBecause the God of Israel was with him. He was his source.\n\nSo I believe that if we are sold out to the Lord,\n\nWe are protected.\n\nNo enchantment can overcome us.\n\nBut even as I type these words, my eyes 👀 are teary 😢.\n\nMany of us are destroyed by the works and enchantment of this world 🗺.\n\nBy juju and other witchcraft 🧙‍♀️ activities.\n\nVery sad 😔. Lord, why?\n\nThese Israelites did not pray in tongues. Neither knew they what we know now in our days.\n\nSo why?","dt":"2024-05-20T07:14:54","s":["jpicydf7hw"]}],"28":[{"m":"Though his hair 💇 began to grow again, it did not mean the Spirit of the Lord was automatically going to be on him.\n\nYes, the requirements for the anointing of strength 💪 to be upon him were met.\n\nI.e. his hair grew; yes, he had fulfilled his part, and his consecration — his hair 💇 — was in place, but the Spirit of the Lord showing up and enduing him with strength 💪 was the Lord's prerogative, not the other way round.\n\nIt's just like when Balaam son of Beor showed up with seven bulls as sacrifice to the Lord, hoping to hear a word from him.\n\nHe had done his part of sacrificing the bulls, but the showing up was the prerogative of the Lord.\n\nOh Samson, Samson.","dt":"2024-05-20T07:42:25","s":["getgird3nq"]}]},"17":{"6":[{"m":"Is the purpose of this story to show the state of Israel at this time without a king 👑?\n\nIt means Israel did better with a king 👑.\n\nWhy then did God not set up a system of continuity, since he did not set up kingship for Israel?\n\nI always wondered why after the death of Moses and Joshua there was no one whom Joshua handed over to, so no one does what he wants as in this case.\n\nBut indeed God did set up a system.\n\nA system where he was king 👑 and they were his priests, so he could commune directly with them, but they refused.\n\nSo he set up the Levitical priesthood. So he as king 👑 would govern through his priests and prophets.\n\nBut that system was collapsed by the people themselves.\n\nOne generation held on to God's system and won wars and received directions from God.\n\nTill another generation arose that went into idol worship 🛐\nThus tarnishing the system of God and leading to such chaos where everyone did as he saw fit.\n\nBut God had done well to give them the law in written format.\n\nThere were priests and tribe heads, but they could not hold the system God had created in place.\n\nFinally God gave them a human lineage, i.e. kingship 👑.\n\nBut as we see later, this system is plagued with a lot of flaws.\n\nAnd barely lasted two generations till chaos broke out.\n\nIndeed the first king, Saul, had no continuity to his throne.\n\nThe 2nd, David, had his kingdom divided by the third generation, and even lasted that long because God oversaw its survival.\n\nBut in the coming kingdom 👑,\n\nThe king 👑 fuses these two systems, where he reigns as king and also through his human representative, but the twist being his human rep is himself a God man — Jesus. 👑.\n\nThus benefiting from the advantages of both systems without the disadvantages.\n\nNo wonder God allowed Israel to have a king despite its being in rebellion to him.\n\nHe knew it had some advantages and benefits to it. And he intended to harness it in the times to come.\n\nAnd we await that time. Oh, what a moment of glory that will be.\n\nWhen we all see Jesus... Our King, our God and God's man 👨...\n\n😇\nCan't wait.","dt":"2024-05-20T08:19:20","s":["y9okw9h3q2"]},{"m":"In continuity to the notes on this topic about why God let the system run amok. I think God could have selected leaders like he did Moses and his successor Joshua, who would rise up and take care of his people so they do not go astray.\n\nBut even as I type this, I realised God did. All through the book of Judges God personally selected men to lead Israel at various points in time.\n\nBut the same thing kept happening, i.e. as soon as the leader or judge died, the next generation, who saw not the acts of the Lord, went a-whoring after other gods, and the cycle continues.\n\nUntil the people themselves recognise their need for God, he let them suffer under their enemies. There was no way the people would accept God's man unless they were in pain and suffering.\n\nMostly slavery and abuse, just like in Egypt. So Egypt had to keep repeating itself in Israel until the people cried out, then God raised them up a leader.\n\nThe next question and challenge is, how many MOSESES are there in a generation, how many Joshuas and how many Calebs?\n\nWe see that even in the Judges he raised, many had flaws. Many flaws, but God's love for his people made him use them anyways.\n\nHe continued this way until the people asked for a king, which ensured there was no break in leadership upon the death of the leader. His son naturally took over.\n\nWhich in itself was a flaw in the system.\n\nBecause not all natural descendants follow after their fathers' godliness.\n\nIn the judge system, there was a problem of continuity, because not every generation will have God's man to lead, and in the kings not every heir is godly, though it ensured continuity.","dt":"2026-04-05T10:23:41","s":["32z4g196zy"]}]},"18":{"20":[{"m":"This guy was such an opportunist.\n\nPriestly blood ran through him, so he took full advantage to better his cause in life.","dt":"2024-05-20T08:23:40","s":["4ashxprxmu"]}],"28":[{"m":"Wisdoms for us...\nBecause they had no league or business with anyone, there was no one to help.\n\nToo naive they were, too naive.","dt":"2024-05-20T08:24:56","s":["093ujdkj2i"]}]},"19":{"1":[{"m":"Why have the past few chapters been concentrated in and around the land of Ephraim?","dt":"2026-04-06T09:04:09","s":["jhiixa1519"]}],"30":[{"m":"Such immorality, same as in Sodom and Gomorrah.\n\nIs it not interesting that despite many sexual atrocities committed, we can have an entire city of homosexuals thirsty for innocent blood?\n\nWe do not have such examples among heterosexuals. Where a city was so drunk with lust that they gather to sleep 😴 with the latest visitor to the town.\n\nThey were bored with lying with themselves.\n\nThis goes to show the spirit 🧚‍♂️ behind such lusts.\n\nIt's abnormal and immoral.","dt":"2024-05-21T07:39:46","s":["iucyxac4kq"]}],"23":[{"m":"This kind of violence of same-sex passions was never heard of or recorded in scripture. It was a similar thing in Sodom, and now here as well.\n\nAlso why they would offer their daughters and concubines to these beasts goes to show how women were considered second-class citizens who bore the brunt of collateral damage in this situation.","dt":"2026-04-06T09:23:05","s":["f6eu27fqxs"]}]},"20":{"14":[{"m":"Sad 😔... They were not willing to bring out the thugs who committed such.\n\nThe Benjamites had come to terms with this and could thus be willing to defend such abominations with their own lives.","dt":"2024-05-21T07:42:10","s":["dzce4h9g4j"]}],"16":[{"m":"This skill was common to the Benjamites, being left-handed and sling masters.","dt":"2024-05-21T07:43:22","s":["5jdvjudhm2"]},{"m":"They could aim and not miss — Google explains that in Hebrew, the word translated as \"miss\" (chata) is the same word used for \"sin\". Just as a slinger might \"miss the mark\" of his target, sin is defined as \"missing the mark\" of God's moral standard.\n\nIn reading this it dawned on me that just as it is very easy for a slinger to miss the mark of his target, so it is so easy to miss God's high standards.\n\nI mean, imagine being asked to sling at a hair; the likelihood of missing is sooo high. Same way, God's mark is so high we all miss his mark and fall into sin.","dt":"2026-04-06T10:12:44","s":["fz356elt4q"]}],"26":[{"m":"This time they did not just weep and pray 🙏 but went up to the house of God, wept, prayed, fasted, burnt offerings and all.\n\nThey exhausted every possible option.\n\nThey couldn't afford to lose again.\n\nNow my question 🙋 is, why did God cause them to lose, and twice so, when they had enquired of him?\n\nHe was not silent when they enquired, but answered positively that they should go.","dt":"2024-05-21T07:47:02","s":["bbzof9cgtm"]}],"28":[{"m":"This time God spoke with specifics, that he would deliver them.\n\nThe first and second time he said they should go.\n\nBut this time he guaranteed them victory ✌️.\n\nIt's a lesson to not just wait for the go-ahead from God, but to also get the firm, guaranteed assurance they would have the victory ✌️.","dt":"2024-05-21T07:49:47","s":["11sdjdokat"]}]},"21":{"2":[{"m":"It was like God was exacting vengeance on Israel through this Civil War.\n\nIt's interesting that this story was not centuries after the death of Joshua, but in the times of Phinehas the high priest, who lived even in the days of Moses.\n\nSo no wonder the children of Israel were so resolute to wipe out the evil 😈 from their midst.\n\nIn this time they were very committed to the Lord.\n\nIt's amazing that Benjamin could have stooped so deep in sin in such times.","dt":"2024-05-21T08:11:05","s":["n9sexyx7to"]}],"23":[{"m":"This was a very technical way of going around their vow without breaking it. 😇","dt":"2024-05-22T12:48:13","s":["iqvebmkolq"]}],"25":[{"m":"How many times would this statement be repeated? I noticed also that Israel was smitten before Benjamin twice before the Lord finally gave them victory.\n\nWhy was that the case? Meanwhile the Lord had commanded them to go to battle, and they were fighting in the name of the LORD, yet they lost sorely before finally victory came to them.\n\nCould it be the case that because they were no longer such an upright people, God also had limited his might and power towards them?\n\nI mean, think of it, barely two generations after Aaron, and an entire tribe had corrupted themselves so much that they were sodomites and were willing to die to defend the wrong amongst them rather than to give their brethren up.\n\nThey saw nothing wrong with them. Sin can be so pervasive it becomes the norm. LORD HAVE MERCY ON US ALL.","dt":"2026-04-06T11:04:47","s":["b5wfg8yxu1"]}],"14":[{"m":"Strange, these men of war. These ancient warriors.\n\nAfter such massacre of their tribes, they could still stare each other in the face 😔.\n\nBut that is the nature of wars, after we have finished destroying each other.\n\nWe come to that common ground of realization that we are all human beings with same needs.\n\nThat we are not each other's enemies.\n\nBut rather greed, lies 🤥 and selfishness...","dt":"2024-05-22T12:46:21","s":["sfj592c9yf"]}]},"5":{"31":[{"m":"A powerful song and poem, a powerful and informative song and poem.\n\nAnd I love the part in the middle of the song, of Dan and Asher not coming to help but resting on their oars.\n\nYet Zebulun and Naphtali joined forces to fight.","dt":"2024-05-16T06:40:40","s":["ekvkzx55ux"]}]},"14":{"4":[{"m":"The Philistines had dominion over Israel, and with all this anointing, Samson did nothing about it.\n\nHe did not fight nor gather his people to war.\n\nYet the Lord used that to still stir up trouble between Samson and the Philistines.","dt":"2024-05-19T12:46:25","s":["xrtb99q17"]}],"17":[{"m":"Samson's weakness with women did not start with Delilah...","dt":"2026-04-04T08:11:33","s":["5rp769gige"]}]}},"1 Corinthians":{"1":{"17":[{"m":"By words of wisdom Paul is here referencing man's wisdom. No, he declared the gospel not with human wisdom but with divine wisdom, which to those who are perishing it is foolishness.","dt":"2025-04-28T15:42:37","s":["5vdkqrr0kc"]}],"23":[{"m":"The confusion of the Jews was their reconciling what the word of God said with what traditions and their elders taught.\n\nThey expected a king Messiah, only to be presented with Jesus, the Lamb of God.\n\nAnd yet, it was revealed in the scriptures that the Christ had to suffer, something the elders of the day seem not to have deciphered yet.\n\nSo they and the Jews rejected the salvation of the Messiah.\n\nNo wonder after the ascension the disciples by wisdom used the scriptures to prove that Christ was indeed the Messiah.","dt":"2025-04-28T15:46:45","s":["ptwfje5xhq"]}],"28":[{"m":"This is akin to Jesus thanking God for revealing the truth to babes, for so the Father had ordained it to be.","dt":"2025-04-28T15:49:06","s":["n3cp88psh6"]}]},"3":{"11":[{"m":"I think Paul's word here was not just a caution to the church but a gentle caution to Apollos also. That the foundation is Christ and that which is built thereon must align with Christ.\n\nIt was also to sensitize the Corinthian church to discern truth from falsehood.","dt":"2025-04-28T15:55:48","s":["aynjvqqbzr"]}],"16":[{"m":"So the building that Paul is talking about is building the people of God. That makes sense, because the gospel is to men.","dt":"2025-04-28T15:56:51","s":["zpex00ci45"]}]},"4":{"15":[{"m":"I think there is a bit of politics going on. Paul letting them know he birthed them and not Apollos. He said so without naming names.","dt":"2025-04-28T16:14:34","s":["pl3o5q869e"]}]},"5":{"7":[{"m":"Indeed a little leaven affects the whole lump... The reason fornication and grave sins have become so common is that we have not purged them out, even when we do know the truth.\n\nIndeed the leaders and elders themselves are caught in such enticement. How then can we judge rightly?\n\nLord have mercy.","dt":"2022-11-27T05:48:42","s":["5jrajphzxd"]}]},"7":{"6":[{"m":"Interesting choice of words.\n\nWe are not commanded as Christians to marry but rather permitted to marry.\n\nIndeed Paul argues that it is good for a man not to marry.\n\nSo then it is bad for a man to marry? No, not exactly.\n\nIndeed marriage was ordained by God, so it is good.\n\nInterestingly though, in the beginning, remember what God said about a man being alone.\n\nHe said it is not good, but now we see Paul commending being alone as a good thing.\n\nI guess because a lot has changed over the millennia. Man has become corrupted.\n\nSo like Jesus said, from the beginning it was not so... But a lot of things have changed.\n\nSo then what is the conclusion? Marrying or not marrying is both good, but like Paul concluded, he wished all were as he is, so then being single is preferred.\n\nHowever, being single and sleeping around is worse. It is better then to marry.","dt":"2025-04-30T08:25:38","s":["j2ehz854qd"]}],"12":[{"m":"Such depth of FELLOWSHIP. BROTHER Paul could tell a command and say this is what God says.\n\nBut in our day we say one thing and it turns out to be false 😔.\n\nIt seems the word of the Lord is misty and foggy 🌁 🌫... We just cannot tell.\n\nOh Lord, help 😣 us.","dt":"2023-09-15T08:12:29","s":["2zt1mrq8zm"]}],"19":[{"m":"Oh, so there is such a thing as the commandments of God... Some say we are born free in Christ means we do as the flesh pleases 😌","dt":"2023-09-15T08:13:43","s":["sf8r1k7w2s"]}],"34":[{"m":"In the times of the early church they so loved the Lord. Ready to give over themselves to the service of the Lord.\n\nNot just by way of service but by service of their body in true holiness and righteousness.\n\nThey indeed gave themselves over in spirit, soul and body.","dt":"2023-09-16T09:34:01","s":["z43puq8qw8"]}],"40":[{"m":"Indeed this is a well rounded topic on whether we should marry or not.\n\nIt seems the best option is not to marry and to focus on the Lord.\n\nThe above is best only if you do not have feelings 😝.\n\nIf you have feelings, as most humans do... Then marry simplicita.","dt":"2022-11-28T06:16:19","s":["jms8bmwdd0"]},{"m":"It is preferred that one remains unmarried.\n\nIt is better actually. Marriage is also good.\nBut extrapolating Paul's reasoning to our world today? In the face of sexual exploitation, porn and the like, it is better to marry, more so in our world today.","dt":"2025-04-30T08:32:45","s":["m1vvfs2a6z"]}],"29":[{"m":"The time is short is in reference to the coming of the Lord, I believe, and the load of work to be covered.\n\nI believe the apostles expected the Lord in their lifetime.","dt":"2025-04-30T08:35:11","s":["dmhf4i9jfk"]}],"36":[{"m":"There seem to be different interpretations of this verse, but I like the Wycliffe translation in modern English, as it attempts to give the different possible interpretations.\n\n1 Corinthians 7:36 WBMS\nAnd if any man guesseth himself to be seen foul on his virgin, that she is full waxen [or is well old], and so it behooveth to be done, do she that that she will [or what he will]; she sinneth not, if she be wedded, [+or s/he sinneth not, if s/he be wedded].","dt":"2023-09-16T09:39:26","s":["exwth1gyrg"]}]},"8":{"1":[{"m":"The Corinthians are an interesting church ⛪. They have a lot of questions...\n\nFornication issues, marriage, now idol-dedicated foods.\n\nIt is good they sought clarity.","dt":"2022-11-27T14:33:28","s":["n7nw5cmtt4"]}],"4":[{"m":"This scripture often bothered me... Why Paul would say that an idol is nothing in the world 🗺.\n\nI'm from Africa 🌍 and here we see \"things\".\n\nWe see the power of idols and \"gods\" in real time ⌚.\n\nSo I often was confused 😕. It's different if he said they were not as powerful as our God, but nothing?\n\nHerein lies the truth: we are seated with Christ Jesus far above principalities and powers, and there is only one God, Jehovah.\n\nAll others are only making false claims of Godship to deceive and receive god worship that is not due them.\n\nIndeed there is no God but our God. With this consciousness, the deception of idols as gods is broken and we walk in freedom and liberty 🗽.\n\nBut for the weak mind and believers, their belief in idols and other gods weakens their own conscience and thus affects their faith and even their walk with God.\n\nThey may even be snared by attacks spiritually and dreams etc.\n\nYou see, what you believe does affect you. See Peter, who walked on water comfortably. However, the moment he saw the boisterous winds 🍃, he feared and doubted 🤷‍♂️, i.e. he believed that he would drown.\n\nAnd immediately his belief was manifested. He came again under natural law, though he was doing fine believing in the word of Jesus that he should come to him.\n\nSame thing, as we walk with God, we may be doing just fine until we believe something else or someone introduces a thought, and suddenly we find ourselves snared and the power of God becomes of non effect.\n\nIn such times we need a rescue mission on our case; we have to cry out to the Lord like Peter did. We have to go back to the Lord in prayer so we are realigned and our spirits, souls and bodies reset.","dt":"2022-11-28T06:43:31","s":["khrjpqkt34"]}]},"9":{"14":[{"m":"It is an ordination from the Lord himself. Ministers must be supported.","dt":"2023-09-16T09:56:28","s":["u10ehhs2vi"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh, a bond servant indeed.","dt":"2023-09-16T09:58:25","s":["ndzxcqpsc2"]}],"18":[{"m":"This is how and what I want to do and be. Give the gospel without charge and no personal benefit.","dt":"2023-09-16T09:57:34","s":["e352qwjmm4"]}],"24":[{"m":"Indeed Paul ran in such a way as to obtain. He indeed had mastery in all things, to the extent that he refrained from marriage so he could serve the gospel work maximally.\n\nHe was truly a master.","dt":"2022-11-28T10:01:26","s":["12hnxal31b"]}],"27":[{"m":"Is it not interesting that after all this allegory and spiritual examples, it comes down 👇 to one thing?\n\nPutting the body under. An area where many fail, because it is the culmination of all our spirituality.\n\nThe ULTIMATE AND HIGHEST proof indeed of our spirituality.\n\nIt's like when we are told of the power and gifts of the Spirit, and then we are given THE MOST EXCELLENT WAY, I.E. LOVE.\n\nMany want the gifts but detest the most excellent gift of all... LOVE.\n\nHow come this is so? Because it kills the flesh, that's how come.","dt":"2023-09-16T10:03:13","s":["hkipvk9bgw"]}]},"10":{"11":[{"m":"Further proof that indeed they expected the coming of the Lord to be imminent.","dt":"2025-04-30T09:11:53","s":["sih6vxtaod"]}],"15":[{"m":"Paul seems to say that, I am speaking to wise people who would not take what I say out of context, or as an accusation that I'm calling you idol worshippers.\n\nThen he goes ahead and explains how that an idol is nothing but just that; though an idol is nothing, the sacrifices are to devils, and so why would believers have fellowship with devils?","dt":"2023-09-19T09:15:29","s":["xslhc7gkz1"]}],"19":[{"m":"Time and again Paul makes us understand that idols are nothing, empty, and can do nothing.\n\nHe recognizes, however, that the sacrifices done are to devils 👿, and he would not have them dine with devils.\n\nIndeed they cannot partake of the Lord's offering and go partake of the devils'.\n\nPaul does not even recognize that devils are anything or have power over the Christian, so we ought to be careful etc.\n\nThese early believers were full of the Holy Ghost and raw power. No devil could rob them of the gift of redemption nor keep them in bondage.\n\nThey were properly aligned and just needed correct doctrine, that's all. However, the church today is devoid of power, and even now our doctrine is so off.\n\nGod have mercy. And where there seems to be right doctrine, the doctrine of power is lacking.\n\nLord help 😣, Lord have mercy, we have lost alignment.","dt":"2023-09-19T09:22:56","s":["xz7mudt1b8"]}]},"11":{"22":[{"m":"All manner of characters in the church ⛪, and as a minister of grace, one must be really patient and long suffering to bring order without destroying the very work one is building.","dt":"2022-11-28T10:09:27","s":["vv85wh76ra"]}],"34":[{"m":"The Corinthian church had many issues which could not be addressed in one letter, so Paul advised he will set the others straight when he visits them in person.\n\nI'm sure the church was also growing up numerically for them to be experiencing so many different issues.","dt":"2022-11-28T10:13:12","s":["jn0ouvzotx"]}]},"12":{"31":[{"m":"Which gifts are the best?","dt":"2023-09-21T07:32:12","s":["ys4wqjkkdm"]}]},"13":{"2":[{"m":"I used to wonder how one could have faith to move mountains ⛰ and yet not have love.\n\nHow could one attain the heights of such mighty works without having passed the foundational rudiments of the fruit of the Holy Spirit?\n\nThen as I matured in Christ I realized that it actually is possible 🙆.\n\nOne can be spiritually gifted and yet lack the spiritual fruit of love, joy, peace, as stated in Gal 5:22.\n\nThis is actually the sign of maturity in Christ, not the gifts, because as the name suggested they are gifts of the Spirit.\n\nAnd we all do know people who have gifts incommensurate with their character, but that is why it is a gift 📦","dt":"2022-11-29T06:19:52","s":["hsx5rcewff"]}],"3":[{"m":"How can one give his body to be burned 🔥 and not have love?\n\nIt actually is possible to make sacrifices because of pride, to prove a point etc, and yet lack love.\n\nWe know people who are very hard working and sacrifice so much for their job and others, yet are narcissistic and violent on others.","dt":"2022-11-29T06:23:49","s":["09e4u3021w"]}],"8":[{"m":"Love never fails; you can walk 🚶 in love perpetually, but with tongues, prophecies and knowledge (gift of knowledge etc) it will cease at a point, because you receive as the Spirit gives.\n\nAnd you are given these gifts in part; you don't know all there is, but only what the Spirit wills.\n\nSo all these gifts will cease at a point, but LOVE doesn't.\n\nSo is FAITH AND Hope, but love is the greatest.","dt":"2023-09-21T08:28:25","s":["af8ml5wib2"]}],"10":[{"m":"Paul argues that love never fails (in that it never ceases or comes to an end), and earlier he had mentioned that love was the more excellent way.\n\nNow he goes ahead to make the point that things like prophecy are not complete, tongues are not complete, in the sense that with prophecy and tongues it will come to an end eventually, because you have some knowledge but not all knowledge. You prophesy in part.\n\nWhen prophecies and tongues cease, which they will, love will continue to exist.\n\nLOVE is forever.","dt":"2023-09-21T08:14:41","s":["vybfldtvfs"]},{"m":"In other words, when that which is perfect 👌 is come, you choose that over the imperfect... i.e. you choose love always over the gifts, because as we have seen the gifts can be exercised outside of love.\n\nAnd that is childish 🧒. So we have a lot of childish believers and leaders actually.\n\nGifted but childish... Again the manipulation and mind control is real even in the church.\n\nWe give all these children such high regard in the church and suppress the real men.","dt":"2023-09-21T09:52:55","s":["v5hxzlfaac"]}],"13":[{"m":"Where did Paul get this system of priority from? Who even gave him the knowledge of these three things?\n\nWhere did such knowledge come from, and what metric was used to graduate them in order of importance?\n\nIn fact, how do you even measure three such vast and awesome attributes?","dt":"2023-09-22T07:27:27","s":["w5s4o31qfc"]}],"11":[{"m":"Ei, am I hearing this right, that gifts are childish things compared to love ♥?\n\nThat love is so superior to the gifts that it is like a full grown man compared to a child 🧒...\n\nOr in other words, those young in the faith chase the gifts at the expense of love, but as we mature we walk in love more and more, because we realise that is the most excellent way.","dt":"2023-09-21T08:21:47","s":["muxdmr56y5"]}]},"14":{"29":[{"m":"Even with prophecy, there is supposed to be one on standby who judges.\n\nJust as with speaking in tongues, there is supposed to be one who interprets.\n\nBut none of that happens in the church today.","dt":"2023-09-22T08:25:03","s":["pla7oawj2o"]}],"40":[{"m":"Yet we see disorder in the church, and especially when there is a spiritual move.\n\nThe very activity we are commanded to do in order, we do it disorderly.\n\nIt was as if the apostle knew, and he did, that on matters of the Spirit there are many excesses.","dt":"2022-11-29T06:40:32","s":["wrkeac7y86"]}]},"16":{"9":[{"m":"And not but... And there are many adversaries.\n\nWow, it's an acceptable part of the call.","dt":"2022-11-29T10:45:55","s":["hmjvmldi2p"]}],"22":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-11-29T10:58:19","s":["55f046c3d8"]}]},"6":{"1":[{"m":"So here Paul is suggesting that when we have disputes, we resolve it before the saints.\n\nBut that is under the assumption that the individual would submit himself to the saints and church as the final authority in their life.\n\nI ask, can this be executed in the church today?\n\nNo, I doubt 🤷🏾‍♂️. So much has changed in the church ⛪. And you better take the case to court, as people will not submit to church authorities, or just move on to another church ⛪.\n\nBut we must go back to those days again.","dt":"2023-09-13T06:01:35","s":["8ttbmfd0u7"]}],"2":[{"m":"We would judge the world 🤯? I thought God would, but I see Paul is likely talking of the millennial reign, when we reign with Christ.","dt":"2023-09-13T06:03:36","s":["x92gq52723"]}],"4":[{"m":"The least esteemed is in reference to the Gentiles or the world 🗺 outside the church ⛪.","dt":"2025-04-30T07:39:33","s":["0u0ynr89sb"]}],"7":[{"m":"Okay, so Paul is bringing up another angle to the problem, that even if there is no justice or system of judgement in the church,\n\npermit your fellow Christian to get away with having cheated you.\n\nFor the sake of the gospel. You see, Paul was dead to many things of this world, and rightly so. And urges others to.\n\nNot an easy command to keep. And especially in these times you might end up allowing a charlatan to run amok.","dt":"2023-09-13T06:11:57","s":["hy437ca63g"]}]},"15":{"45":[{"m":"Ah, finally I've gained some understanding of this scripture.\n\nThe first Adam was natural bodied, a living soul, but the second Adam is a spirit — a quickening spirit.","dt":"2023-09-28T06:54:15","s":["e441bpbkza"]}]}},"2 Corinthians":{"3":{"18":[{"m":"The entire Christian life, as we behold the face of God through prayer, word study, afflictions and persecution, we are transformed from Glory to GLORY.","dt":"2022-11-30T07:11:31","s":["yj73mm229m"]}],"9":[{"m":"The ministration of condemnation, which condemns all and makes atonement every time it is committed,\n\nas compared to the ministration of righteousness, which from start passes all as righteous without the need for atonement.","dt":"2022-11-30T06:42:45","s":["5sio9ws06a"]}]},"4":{"6":[{"m":"Glory Hallelujah 🙌. GOD HATH SHINED IN OUR HEARTS 💕","dt":"2023-10-07T10:44:01","s":["lv6e338er8"]}],"13":[{"m":"We speak what we believe, not what the circumstances say... We are moved by the word of God.","dt":"2023-10-07T10:48:24","s":["uisg1jqmve"]}],"7":[{"m":"Another popular scripture reflecting the power and glory of God. This treasure in earth 🌎 vessels means the vessel is subject to break, to crack, to tarnish, yet it still contains the raw, pure and unadulterated power of God and his Spirit.\n\nWow... No wonder we are God's men, many times so frail, and yet the power shows forth so radiantly we are literally invincible.\n\nWe have become a paradox almost. And yet this power in us also works on us.","dt":"2023-10-07T10:44:36","s":["6izbt1zsqx"]}],"18":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2023-10-07T10:49:10","s":["5c5f8bfeed"]}]},"5":{"21":[{"m":"The doctrine of the New Testament, the thinking and logic thereof.\n\nWhich is hammered 🛠 home by the Holy Spirit bearing witness.\n\nIt is therefore important not to miss the doctrine, lest excesses come in.\n\nIf we do not follow doctrine, we might end up giving our own interpretation to the Christian walk and to the ministry of the Spirit.\n\nThus we risk gradually moving away from the truth and then suddenly completely away from the truth.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:07:13","s":["b7zvsjprn3"]}],"18":[{"m":"To emphasize the certainty of the new creature, he says old things are passed, ALL things are new...\n\nThen hammers home the point that now all things are of God.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:04:51","s":["gjyxv2nyvy"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"Oh, so holiness need be perfected 👌","dt":"2023-10-07T10:57:38","s":["9sfsf54ous"]}],"15":[{"m":"A true man of God, received with fear and trembling, and yet the fakes also desire this. Hmm, sad 😔","dt":"2023-10-07T11:00:39","s":["z2ozits1hj"]}],"3":[{"m":"Oh, the love of a father, the dilemma of true men of God... They die daily for the flock.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:15:50","s":["e8r9nlvmm7"]}]},"8":{"13":[{"m":"Interesting...\n\nWe give out of what we have, not out of what we have not. This ties in with the state of the church, in people feeling compelled to give outrageously, even of what they do not have...\n\nIt is not proper doctrine and should not be taught as such and encouraged using scriptural support.\n\nIf someone does give in such manner, it should be left at that, i.e. his personal choice and action.\n\nIt should not be touted for others to follow suit 💼","dt":"2022-12-01T06:22:18","s":["v8rki8we3c"]}],"14":[{"m":"Doctrine is sensible and logical, as we see here in the Corinthian church giving out of their abundance to other saints 😇","dt":"2022-12-01T06:23:20","s":["03d711vv66"]}]},"9":{"5":[{"m":"I love that, practical and pragmatic steps to avoid any embarrassment when it came to giving.\n\nWe bless God for wisdom.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:25:49","s":["2xp0kl5jvt"]}],"6":[{"m":"In other words, and looking at the context from the previous verse stating that they were being pre-informed so they give out bountifully and not grudgingly, as the NKJV says,\n\nthey that sow bountifully would reap bountifully, and they that sow sparingly (not that they did not have but are compelled to give, but have and yet are stingy and withhold) will reap sparingly.\n\nThis does not mean we should compel people to give what they don't have to their own hurt.\n\nSee the widow who gave 2 mites at the temple 🏛.\n\nJesus said she had given more than those who had given so much.\n\nSo let's all give according to what we have in our hearts 💕 and 👐 hands to give.\n\nWe should always give bountifully and, where we can, give over and beyond, as exemplified by some of the early church.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:36:32","s":["lii41sz6os"]}],"8":[{"m":"We can see the Apostle Paul nudging the believer towards giving more and bountifully, so they get blessed through their giving, whilst also maintaining sound doctrine so they do not feel compelled to give in a wrong way or out of compulsion.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:38:16","s":["vwe9lhd0ju"]}]},"10":{"2":[{"m":"Paul had walked among the Corinthians in simplicity, and they thus began to take that for granted.\n\nHe did not exalt himself nor the great achievements he had achieved, so they held him in contempt.\n\nThis is common human behavior: when people act simply despite their status, they are disdained, yet when others who have achieved far less hype themselves and carry themselves with pomp, they are treated highly.\n\nNow these Corinthians wondered why Paul's words were heavy in his letters towards them.\n\nThey did not think he should have such audacity, being so simple and ordinary in person.\nWhat right did he think he had to speak to them with such authority?\n\nThus he began to outline his authority and power with which he walked.\n\nHe even further pleaded that those who spoke against him should not compel him to speak boldly towards them when he comes in person. They wouldn't want that.\n\nSo now he drops a few bombshells 🐚 of his great achievements, which thus gave him the audacity and authority despite his simple demeanor.\n\n2 Corinthians 11:16 KJV\nI say again, Let no man think me a fool; if otherwise, yet as a fool receive me, that I may boast myself a little.","dt":"2023-10-26T01:41:26","s":["8k1l34eoec"]},{"m":"Paul pleaded with the Corinthians not to compel him to be bold when he comes, not only because they wouldn't want that, but because he, Paul, wanted to keep in line with the godly example of humility set by Christ for his servants and disciples to follow.","dt":"2023-10-26T02:30:16","s":["3kt16035dl"]}],"4":[{"m":"In essence Paul is saying, though there are some who view things from the natural standpoint and think we the servants of Christ walk after the natural order and do things naturally,\n\nyes, though you see us walk about just like anyone, we do have a warfare going on, and in that warfare we do not use natural, human and fleshly weapons 🔫.\n\nThese weapons are given to us by God for the pulling down of strong mental fortresses and holds, imaginations and high things.\n\nThese weapons are for the mental prisons the enemy has set up, and his schemes by which he puts man into bondage.","dt":"2023-10-26T01:26:51","s":["qmu6zgiaa7"]},{"m":"Though you see us walking about in simplicity and meekness, there is a war ongoing, and in this war we are fighting principalities and powers, mental strongholds among others...\n\nWe do not want to seem to scare you by our letters, for we know you say\n\n2 Corinthians 10:10 KJV\nFor his letters, say they, are weighty and powerful; but his bodily presence is weak, and his speech contemptible.\n\nBut do not let us be bold towards you in person; you would not like it.","dt":"2023-10-26T02:04:49","s":["b4z637gj9m"]}],"6":[{"m":"The NLT makes this verse clearer...\n\n2 Corinthians 10:6 NLT\nAnd after you have become fully obedient, we will punish everyone who remains disobedient.\n\nI resonate with this translation. It's like how that Christ will come for his church when we are perfected in the fullness of time.\n\nHe is coming for a bride without spot and blemish. Yet having said that, he will punish them that are rebellious and sinful after he comes for his obedient ones.","dt":"2022-12-01T06:52:51","s":["l6t0txf4ot"]},{"m":"How did he intend to do this? Was it going to be like he did with the fornicator, i.e.\n\nostracizing and handing the disobedient ones to Satan for the destruction of the flesh, so the spirit is preserved unto God?\n\nI think so.","dt":"2022-12-01T07:01:08","s":["x9xd7tulib"]},{"m":"I am ready to punish every disobedience, when the very things I have asked you to do, you do them.\n\nThen those who rebel I will punish.","dt":"2023-10-26T01:30:07","s":["v7dymqhvns"]}],"8":[{"m":"Hmm, I think as stated in the note in verse 6, he might use this method. Because he says here that the authority they have is for edification, not destruction...\n\nSo he would prefer to build up than to punish by such means as ostracizing others and handing them over to Satan for torment.","dt":"2022-12-01T07:02:57","s":["dzym2nr2ab"]}],"11":[{"m":"So those who think we only write authoritative letters, we can actually be bold and authoritative in person, but we want to spare you that.\n\nSo permit it to be that way, because you wouldn't like it when we start using our authority, which God gave us to build, and use it to punish.","dt":"2023-10-26T01:45:23","s":["3fb3rwugfh"]}],"16":[{"m":"Paul was letting them know that he boasts in what he has achieved, whiles those speaking against him do so not based on their own achievements but on what he, Paul, had achieved among them, the Corinthians.\n\nHe was by this drawing their minds to something — to how fake these people were.\n\nHe, Paul, was trusting that through the Corinthians' support, he would do even more and preach the gospel to other regions beyond them...\n\nAs I pen 🖋 these words above, I see the essence of the teaching gift 📦.\n\nWritings, or things put in writing, often have deep meaning compressed in short words and sentences, and it's up to the teacher to break it down and arrange it into its full length for easy comprehension.\n\nSuch an ability is given by God to the teacher.\n\nThe scriptures were deliberately written the way they were, to house and hide in letters deep mysteries.\n\nThe goal of the writings of scripture really is not so much to hide as it is to communicate as much truths as possible in few words.\n\nThus the need for the teachers to expand and expound truth from letters.","dt":"2023-10-26T01:59:19","s":["1wltw738q3"]}],"18":[{"m":"There is some politics going on here, it seems, and rather than get mixed up with it, Paul draws the mind of the Corinthians, that it is not good to boast in another man's works.\n\nHe had come all the way to Corinth to preach the gospel and win souls, and now here were others who just came to enjoy the fruit of his labour, and not just so, but sought to exert themselves as some authority over what they did not build.\n\nIn Paul's absence some have sought to gain undue influence.\n\nNo wonder in the churches today many pastors are so sensitive and put hindrances to such rebellion, indeed undue hindrances, even to the harm of their own people.\n\nControlling the flock like they own the church ⛪.\n\nPaul understood the sacredness of his calling and knew that at the end of the day, the church was the Lord's.\n\nSo as much as it depended on him, he did not seek any gain from it.","dt":"2025-05-09T07:58:57","s":["0jn2n7dc77"]}]},"11":{"4":[{"m":"This corruption of the gospel from its simplicity seems to be a key 🗝 and common problem in the early church.\n\nThe good news was too good, so often people feel naturally more inclined to accept excesses.","dt":"2023-10-16T12:23:01","s":["v3tucowmwk"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh OK, so not that Paul did not take support for the ministry work — he did.\n\nBut not from all churches; here he for some reason had decided to do ministry freely for all the regions of Achaia.\n\nAnd the other churches in other regions knew his needs and funded them.","dt":"2025-05-09T08:08:25","s":["xngy9wvxtp"]}],"13":[{"m":"Okay, so they were false apostles, meaning of course true apostles existed.\n\nThat also means the assertion that there were and can only be 12 apostles of Christ in all of Christianity is false.","dt":"2023-10-16T12:25:58","s":["l2tvwcnia8"]}],"32":[{"m":"For the king to personally want him arrested shows the extent to which Paul was breaking and destroying set systems, cultures and thinking 💭 which kept the peace ✌️ for the rulers to rule.\n\nWhether such rulership was usurped or through malice and lies 🤥, they still exerted influence.\n\nAnd now here comes Paul the trouble maker.\n\nNo wonder he came to the realization that the weapons of this battle are mighty through God to pull down strong holds etc.\n\nIndeed his enemies testified that the people who have turned the world upside down are here also.","dt":"2025-05-09T08:18:07","s":["j7jfszvyn0"]}],"20":[{"m":"Oh my Lord and my God, these things are now so common in the church in Africa 🌍 these days.\n\nLiterally so-called men of God smiting the flock, and that physically, devouring them and manipulating themselves beyond measure.","dt":"2025-05-09T08:11:31","s":["czf80fylfe"]}]},"12":{"18":[{"m":"It seems some people had taken financial advantage and exerted undue authority over the church ⛪, yet the people still praised and hailed them as of God.\n\nBut Paul and his comrades, who did not do this, were rejected. What an irony.","dt":"2023-10-16T12:33:09","s":["bamp0mzjeq"]}],"21":[{"m":"Paul was a true man of God, and with open hearts he related with the people.\n\nIs that the same thing we have in the church today?","dt":"2022-12-03T18:38:49","s":["bcdu0regvj"]}],"9":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2023-10-16T12:30:35","s":["7ee810d64a"]}]},"13":{"3":[{"m":"Wow, is this how bad things had gotten?\n\nThey sought proof that Christ spoke through Paul.","dt":"2023-10-16T12:35:06","s":["8rw6gkohey"]}],"8":[{"m":"True words 💯... Truth will win.","dt":"2022-12-03T18:50:57","s":["yd5n9ysofl"]}],"10":[{"m":"I still wonder, what did Paul intend to do when he comes to meet them unrepented?","dt":"2023-10-16T12:36:38","s":["9nvvc0rbeb"]}],"14":[{"m":"Ahh... So it was in this letter to the Corinthians, the church with many diverse issues and questions 🙋, that the apostle wrote these ever gracious words...","dt":"2022-12-03T18:52:25","s":["ikeu1sqcem"]},{"m":"Oh, how I wish there was a third epistle we could read to find out how Paul faced the Corinthians when he met them in person.","dt":"2023-10-26T02:12:31","s":["7701dkvkwm"]}]}},"Romans":{"1":{"22":[{"m":"They became fools for giving the glory and worship of the God to idols.\n\nHow much more foolish are they that completely deny the existence of anything deity.\n\nRomans 1:22 NKJV\nProfessing to be wise, they became fools,","dt":"2022-12-04T12:27:02","s":["4o5833of8c","1ct4l10lj1"]}],"24":[{"m":"In like manner, or even worse, them that deny the existence of God completely.\n\nRomans 1:24 NKJV\nTherefore God also gave them up to uncleanness, in the lusts of their hearts, to dishonor their bodies among themselves,","dt":"2022-12-04T12:27:49","s":["bpx1umuwff","35g89cw7xn"]}],"28":[{"m":"Soon America and the West will reap the recompense of their ways and their deliberate folly.","dt":"2022-12-04T12:33:46","s":["qoemu2l3pa"]}]},"2":{"15":[{"m":"This begs the great question 🙋: will someone who never heard the gospel but kept a right conscience go to hell because they did not receive Christ, or will they be given some opportunity in the afterlife to choose or refuse the Christ??\n\nBecause here in this verse we see judgement on the Gentiles based on conscience rather than the law ⚖ of righteousness.","dt":"2022-12-04T12:40:16","s":["0zuytktrxi"]}],"24":[{"m":"This is not different from today.\n\nUnbelievers mock Christians because we do the same things, if not worse than what unbelievers do.","dt":"2023-08-14T07:40:18","s":["drhkj6a91h"]}],"29":[{"m":"Okay, good and logically coherent points so far...\n\nSo will the righteous Gentile who knows not Christ be condemned...? Following this line of logic, his righteousness shall speak for him apart from the law.","dt":"2022-12-04T12:43:10","s":["fecri454of"]}]},"3":{"24":[{"m":"Well, since all have sinned and fallen short, there is none that can claim absolute righteousness according to their conscience or the law.\n\nAll have fallen short and sentenced to salvation by Jesus or be damned.","dt":"2022-12-04T12:49:44","s":["dulaqjz2xy"]}],"31":[{"m":"In which way then do we establish the law?\n\nBy meeting the righteous requirements of the law through the death of Christ.\n\nWe fulfill what is required in the law.","dt":"2022-12-04T12:52:27","s":["0umpd8xl1k"]}]},"5":{"15":[{"m":"Not unlike the offense is the free gift... Simply, the pattern of the offence is like the free gift.\n\nIt came by one man, so also righteousness came by one man.","dt":"2022-12-04T13:01:18","s":["x5awlsizjy"]}],"17":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-12-05T11:51:03","s":["f7fb398b5b"]}]},"6":{"14":[{"m":"And so we have legal grounds to denounce sin and fight against it in our members.\n\nSo we are not dominated by it, but rather that we dominate.","dt":"2022-12-05T12:32:41","s":["vo4qx0sc61"]}],"23":[{"m":"So we exercise that eternal life now because Christ is risen from the dead.","dt":"2022-12-05T12:34:25","s":["2skl328wh5"]}],"19":[{"m":"What did he mean by \"because of the infirmity of the flesh\"?","dt":"2023-08-23T02:41:26","s":["zzjbplfund"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"CONCERNING CHAPTER 7,\n\nDake's commentary gives a beautiful summary -\n\nCHAPTER 7 Old relationship to sin: new relationship to God illustrated by marriage. Paul's experience bound by sin under the law illustrates bondage to sin and the law (Rom. 7:7-25). The law itself is not sinful but I am. Sin controlled me before law came but it was inactive. I was alive before the law came but then sin that controlled me would not let me obey the law so I incurred its penalty. The law was just in its demands but it could not deliver me from sin so I had to pay the penalty. I consented to the law but I could not obey it because sin was my master. I was not a willing slave. I was a wretched slave until I found a new master.","dt":"2023-08-11T06:52:51","s":["cz86chpxzc"]}],"6":[{"m":"So we can by this verse appreciate that the letter refers to the law, and the spirit to the dictates of the grace life.","dt":"2022-12-05T13:12:51","s":["2zbjmx947b"]}],"20":[{"m":"Hmm... Hence addictions and habits die hard.","dt":"2022-12-05T13:15:22","s":["dmtm1gvh98"]}]},"8":{"11":[{"m":"If the Spirit of him who raised Christ Jesus from the dead, the body dieth no more because of sin but is made alive because of the Spirit that raises the dead.\n\nThis life-giving Spirit gives life to our mortal bodies.\n\nWhat does this life constitute?\n\nLife: quickening - to cause to live, make alive, give life\nby spiritual power to arouse and invigorate\nto restore to life\nto give increase of life: thus of physical life\n\nOur mortal bodies receive quickening.","dt":"2022-12-06T07:14:58","s":["hn7vnrt6tx"]}],"12":[{"m":"In the light of the Spirit having quickened our mortal bodies, we are no longer debtors to the flesh.","dt":"2022-12-06T07:17:42","s":["26k04r2u0z"]}],"13":[{"m":"There are several sides and angles to the sin in the flesh issue.\n\nBy God's grace we have his quickening Spirit, which quickens our mortal bodies so we can live after the Spirit.\n\nBecause of this ability, we are no longer obligated to the flesh.\n\nAnd because that compelling force of sin and the flesh is no longer there, we can kill and mortify sin in the flesh by the Spirit.","dt":"2022-12-06T07:24:11","s":["uodyvcl66s"]}],"23":[{"m":"Hm... Indeed we await the redemption of the body, for though sin is dead within the body,\n\nWe see not the body fully redeemed, but dominated rather by the Spirit.\n\nWe groan and await the complete redemption of body, where we are clothed anew with immortality in our new bodies.","dt":"2022-12-06T09:55:25","s":["9j6mqd8l9k"]}],"28":[{"m":"Amen, and this promise is not in isolation but against the background of groanings and the Spirit's cry 😢 in intercession.","dt":"2022-12-06T09:57:12","s":["230xo5nsav"]}],"31":[{"m":"Again, this promise is against a backdrop of Spirit walk, prayer and calling of the Father and proper alignment...\n\nWe cannot just claim it and profess it without proper alignment... Of course it remains true even if we do not align ourselves with the walk 🚶 of the Spirit, just that it won't work for us 🙏.\n\nGOD doesn't offer blanket promises. It is always with a condition met.","dt":"2022-12-06T10:01:36","s":["7rkijvfkw4"]}],"34":[{"m":"So there is one great judge, the Father of all.\n\nSatan does not judge; he rather accuses.\n\nGod in his judgment must be fair, and he met the requirements of divine justice ⚖ through the death of his Son Jesus for the accused man.\n\nWe cannot be condemned, nor any accusation brought against us successfully.","dt":"2022-12-07T07:45:05","s":["ee1q0omlcd"]},{"m":"So Christ makes intercession for us, and the Spirit also makes intercession for us.\n\nIndeed, who can separate us from the love of God... All things work together for good.","dt":"2025-05-12T09:14:59","s":["46bl85ri33"]}],"37":[{"m":"A worth-noting scripture","dt":"2022-12-07T07:46:04","s":["p0teqwjtz7"]}],"10":[{"m":"If Christ is in you, the body is dead because of sin, for when Christ died we died with him; our bodies were crucified with him.\n\nBut the Spirit is life because of righteousness, for when he died he rose again by the Spirit, and we also rose with him, and our bodies received life by the Spirit unto righteousness.\n\nThis is an expansion of what I believe Paul was saying.\n\nThe next verse highlights this further.","dt":"2025-05-12T09:11:43","s":["c1ia0pbae0"]}]},"9":{"4":[{"m":"See what passion that Paul speaks with... He has seen the glory and the power, and knows how that his own people, to whom these things originally belong, are missing out big time.\n\nIt's like a great king and prince leaving his estate to his sons and some servants adopted as sons,\n\nyet the sons have absconded and lured into vanities, whiles the servants enjoy the pleasures of royalty 👑,\n\nJustifiably so, but sadly the sons themselves miss out.","dt":"2022-12-06T10:05:41","s":["4yjkvb5fts"]}],"33":[{"m":"Isaiah 28:16\nTherefore thus says the Lord GOD: “Behold, I lay in Zion a stone for a foundation, A tried stone, a precious cornerstone, a sure foundation; Whoever believes will not act hastily.\n\nIsaiah 8:14\nHe will be as a sanctuary, But a stone of stumbling and a rock of offense To both the houses of Israel, As a trap and a snare to the inhabitants of Jerusalem.\n\nIn searching 🔎 out the Old Testament from which Paul quoted, I came across the above verse.\n\nTo get the context I read from surrounding verses, and I came across this in verse 19:\n\nAnd when they say to you, “Seek those who are mediums and wizards, who whisper and mutter,” should not a people seek their God? Should they seek the dead on behalf of the living? To the law and to the testimony! If they do not speak according to this word, it is because there is no light in them.\n\nThe Amplified renders it best for me as:\n\nIsaiah 8:19-20 AMP\nWhen the people [instead of trusting God] say to you, “Consult the mediums [who try to talk to the dead] and the soothsayers who chirp and whisper and mutter,” should not a people consult their God? Should they consult the dead on behalf of the living? [Direct those people] to the law and to the testimony! If their teachings are not in accord with this word, it is because they have no dawn.\n\nSo, seeking mediums, spirits and peeping into the spirit realm for instructions and guidance,\n\nGOD, who is the Father of all spirits, tells them and us a more effective and precise route to spiritual knowledge. If we wish to not only peep but have vast knowledge of the spirit,\n\nHere is GOD'S instruction to access such hidden knowledge and mysteries -\n\n\"TO THE LAW AND PROPHETS\"\n\nThere is no need for mundane practices; he, God, has brought the hidden spiritual things to light and put it in writing for public consumption.\n\nOya ➡ 👉 to the Law and prophets -\n\nSo indeed the word of God is mysteries revealed, but we tend to take it for granted because it's too easily accessible.\n\nHence we continue to dabble in the occultic etc., because those require hidden practices and so are more appealing.\n\nAnd these have such an allure men shed blood and get entrapped.\n\nFrom the times of Adam man has sought to access the unknown, but it is obvious we were not designed to access such knowledge through other agencies except God. We are God-breathed.\n\nHe is our source, and anytime we go outside of him, we crash.","dt":"2022-12-07T11:42:43","s":["o789ic3tsd"]}],"3":[{"m":"I understand and can imagine the pain of Paul.\n\nAs he outlines all these benefits and blessedness of knowing the Lord, only to be reminded that his own people,\n\nThe first selected nation to do the will of God, missed it, and continue to miss such high hopes and blessings.\n\nI understand.","dt":"2023-08-23T04:40:46","s":["a7ue317i0t"]}]},"10":{"9":[{"m":"Very ABC of salvation","dt":"2022-12-07T13:02:16","s":["yfedk1sxou"]}],"16":[{"m":"The way Paul quotes scripture in his writings.\n\nAnd I noticed that he quotes from the OT, obviously in a context of his letters, even though when you read the OT, its context of use is for its particular situation.\n\nI know the law of double interpretation may be used in this case, but when Paul was using it he literally was lifting it and using it for his own use.\n\nThat suggests that context is good, and God can also give you words out of the context of its use and apply it to your situation, as Paul does here.","dt":"2022-12-07T13:06:37","s":["dksv2fsf73"]}]},"11":{"5":[{"m":"So a remnant have been saved by grace, to the end that they might reach out to the Gentiles, and later the entire national Israel will be saved - verse 26.","dt":"2023-08-28T01:49:28","s":["ej4say2j7l"]}],"12":[{"m":"Ah, I now see how this will and is panning out in our time, 2000+ years past.\n\nChristianity is all over the world 🗺; Israel will definitely be provoked to jealousy and their revival shall come.\n\nAmen... I can't wait to see those times... If I'm still around.","dt":"2022-12-07T14:17:16","s":["yzz6dw0pq4"]}],"15":[{"m":"Interesting line of reasoning","dt":"2022-12-07T14:18:22","s":["h8snxq4hii"]}],"22":[{"m":"Did he just say cut off... There goes out the window the 'once saved, forever saved' argument.","dt":"2023-08-28T01:41:53","s":["138ijml3zs"]}],"23":[{"m":"Amen 🙏... He is able to graft in again.","dt":"2022-12-07T14:19:08","s":["80nau669t0"]}],"25":[{"m":"So it's possible to be cut off, and Paul calls it a mystery.\n\nAnd to act contrary to this is to be self-conceited.","dt":"2023-08-28T01:43:02","s":["ptghfajkzd"]}],"26":[{"m":"This is one of those verses with the use of synecdoche — all Israel shall be saved was in reference to national Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nBut that is not to say that every individual, including the wicked and rebellious, will be saved.\n\nThat is not how it works.","dt":"2023-08-28T01:35:38","s":["capyy10nm0"]}]},"14":{"8":[{"m":"Ah, so this popular verse of scripture contextually had to do with food.","dt":"2023-08-30T08:54:18","s":["ma5570ngp6"]}],"13":[{"m":"We are admonished not to judge one another -\n\nWe see that contextually he was not talking of sin but of food and observing special days or festivities...\n\nIn such matters we are each to do according to his faith.\n\nBut in matters of sin which has been clearly judged for us in the scriptures, that we should avoid them, and strong rebukes are given of such, we know what the judgement of scripture is already.\n\nSo we just apply it. Calling out sin is not you judging someone.\n\nIndeed, we are given example of one caught in fornication who is cast out and ostracized from the church ⛪.\n\nSuch things are in order.\n\nAgain, this is different from when a brother is caught up in sin and you are helping restore him or her.\n\nIn such matters we are admonished to also be careful not to be lured into that same sin we counsel others about.\n\nSo different situations require different sets of rules and approaches.","dt":"2022-12-08T06:54:21","s":["t83smluub2"]}],"23":[{"m":"For whatsoever is not of faith is sin","dt":"2022-12-08T06:49:35","s":["gowy46qxiu"]}]},"15":{"30":[{"m":"Strive in prayer; prayer is work. Hard work 👷.\n\nThis kind of prayer was not just saying a prayer of protection in passing.\n\nBut staying in prayer until you get the clearance that indeed all is well and the Lord has answered.\n\nMaybe a word of knowledge may even come to confirm what the Lord is doing. Example: he's sent his angels 😇 to take charge.","dt":"2023-08-31T16:18:53","s":["5vlxros2kb"]}],"31":[{"m":"The NKJV says I beg of you...\n\nI hope they took his plea seriously and prayed with him... Because he was delivered over to the heathen and they took him as their prisoner.","dt":"2022-12-08T08:08:26","s":["0jws86gt1g"]}],"13":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2023-08-31T05:13:11","s":["bktdx7gy05"]}]},"12":{"1":[{"m":"Ah, after having read the verse prior, I now understand this verse better...\n\nThe mercies of God here is in reference to how that God has shown his mercies to the Gentiles and they now have redemption.\n\nHe shows mercies to whom he will, and the Gentiles have become abundant recipients.\n\nIn view of this Paul urges them to offer their bodies as a living sacrifice.","dt":"2022-12-07T18:56:46","s":["8vvc2257xd"]}]}},"Acts":{"1":{"3":[{"m":"Indeed it was his passion, for He was as a lamb silent 😶... He was determined, passionate about the cross, about his dying.\n\nHe longed for it; it's almost as if he schemed and set up his own death ☠","dt":"2022-11-18T17:49:28","s":["xc6514pwjj"]}],"6":[{"m":"John heard in prison of Jesus. That shows how far and wide his works had reached.\n\nNow I'm still trying to get the reason for John's offense.\n\nWas he also expecting Jesus to bring redemption to Israel through conquest, like most expected of the Messiah?\n\nAfter having pronounced Jesus the Lamb of God and Messiah, was John wondering, like the disciples did wonder even after the resurrection, when will these things be?\n\nWhen will Jesus sit on the throne as judge and the kingdom be restored to Israel?\n\nBut I love Jesus. Rather than respond in words, he responded in works.","dt":"2021-12-17T07:09:50","s":["tvlwqxw2io"]}],"15":[{"m":"So where were all the others, the crowds, the multitudes?\n\nThe people he healed, the five thousand he fed at one time, and the four thousand.\n\nThey were partakers of his ministry and the supernatural.\n\nSo what happened? How come, in the face of so great a promise, they failed to be partakers?","dt":"2023-06-15T19:52:43","s":["vd2n6uymw1"]}],"25":[{"m":"In all the Gospels, all we heard mostly were the words of Jesus.\n\nAfter his death, suddenly we hear the words of the disciples.\n\nNot that they did not speak in the times of Jesus, but the Gospels focus on Jesus, whiles the Acts focuses on the apostles.","dt":"2025-04-19T08:04:31","s":["juqfaxwp4k"]}]},"2":{"16":[{"m":"How knew Peter these letters all of a sudden?","dt":"2023-02-22T09:39:57","s":["zin7estynx"]}],"17":[{"m":"I believe these scriptures and understanding were inspired by the Holy Spirit. Oh, Peter was full of power, by the Spirit of the Lord...","dt":"2023-06-20T06:59:27","s":["67c6jujr0b"]}],"24":[{"m":"This testimony of Peter led to 3000 souls being saved.\n\nYou know, Jesus testified of himself through signs and the Old Testament's words concerning him.\n\nBut you see, it is one thing to testify of yourself, but for someone to testify of you is a whole different ball ⚽ game.\n\nIt adds dynamics, weight 🏋️, and solidifies the truth of what was said.","dt":"2023-02-22T09:43:28","s":["qnalsestdv"]}],"34":[{"m":"This was the same question he asked the Pharisees that they could not answer.\n\nAnd obviously in private Jesus had explained this scripture to them.\n\nCould it not be that even all the scriptures that Peter spoke of in this sermon of his were derived from Jesus?\n\nBecause indeed the Bible says that Jesus opened the eyes 👀 of their understanding and showed them what was written concerning him.","dt":"2023-02-22T09:52:53","s":["wo7k8ueoa7"]}],"47":[{"m":"These were expecting the Christ soon, per their actions.\n\nDid they expect it would take another 2000 years, and would they have behaved thus if they knew it was not going to be any time soon? Would that sense of urgency still have been present 📦?\n\nAnd why did God hide the date and time, or at least the period?\n\nHe did not in scripture hint that it would take centuries — even when the people's prayer, behavior, expenditure etc. showed imminent preparation.\n\nTheir expectation was not to be.\n\nWhy did God behave that way in hiding truth?\n\nThough in God's defence, he did tell them not to try and forecast, and he also did tell them that the whole world 🗺 must be evangelised before he comes.\n\nSo truly, if you heed God's words above, you would be in haste, and you would take your mind off dates as advised.\n\nSo with God we must think 🤔, reason and argue out.\n\nThat's the walk of the Spirit 🚶","dt":"2023-06-21T11:06:53","s":["i2lnrxsn0x"]}]},"4":{"3":[{"m":"The Sadducees did not believe in the resurrection of the dead; the priest and others killed Jesus.\n\nBoth classes knew not the scriptures, else all these would not have happened.\n\nThis is so much a reflection of the church ⛪ today...\nPriests who know not the word or the Lord and manipulate the flock of the living God.\n\nThey lie 🤥, cheat and kill so they can have their way rather than the will of God fulfilled.","dt":"2022-11-19T06:33:52","s":["o4x1dnar5n"]}],"4":[{"m":"First preaching was 3000 souls, and now 5000.\n\nThe power of God was self-evident for the people to see; there was no denying that God was with them.\n\nThis miracle which won souls also hardened others.\n\nMiracles are needed in the body of Christ because they win souls.\n\nBut then also there are those 🤭 whom no amount of miracles will transform, sadly though.","dt":"2023-02-24T07:49:29","s":["vlwni2i1fr"]}],"11":[{"m":"These are some very strong 💪 words there. Peter minced no words in accusing them directly of their failures and sins.\n\nGosh, a fiery 🔥 message that was.","dt":"2023-02-24T08:22:41","s":["r7p2yteenn"]}],"12":[{"m":"This answers their question of by what name...\n\nTo which Peter emphatically states that by the name of Jesus 🙏, and goes ahead to say that it's not like this miracle was done in the name of Jesus and that ends it,\n\nbut Peter goes ahead to explain that when it comes to salvation, it's in the name of Jesus and there is no other that can bring salvation.\n\nTherefore them that are Christians and believe in other ways to God are in error.","dt":"2023-06-26T06:43:44","s":["v9hg8m1lww"]}],"13":[{"m":"Yes, indeed these were very bold statements.","dt":"2023-02-24T08:23:04","s":["xhtso6d8lm"]},{"m":"They were surprised that 😲 Peter and John were not afraid 😨 of their faces.","dt":"2023-06-26T06:44:53","s":["8xslaqqy7t"]}],"26":[{"m":"I believe that contextually this scripture was in reference to the Christ in the last days, as the nations come against him.\n\nBut here Peter and his company appropriated it for themselves in this situation.\n\nAnd same we do even in our days.\nHmm 🤔\n\nUpon further reading of subsequent verses, the disciples actually understood it to have been fulfilled when Herod and Pilate and Co crucified Jesus.\n\nAnd that makes sense. They were not calling themselves God's anointed.\n\nEven though its application to the end of time is right, as we see him destroy the future kings and antichrist.","dt":"2023-06-26T06:50:23","s":["xzvku40io0"]}],"16":[{"m":"They could not deny it, but they wouldn't accept the Messiah either.","dt":"2022-11-19T07:36:03","s":["76go4ec3bz"]},{"m":"I wonder, just out of curiosity, where was Nicodemus, or even Joseph of Arimathea?\n\nHad they now abandoned the sect of leaders because they were not willing to walk in the midst of sinful men?\n\nOr had all who were sympathetic towards Jesus at this time, or his followers later on, been taken out of the leaders?\n\nI genuinely wonder where these were.","dt":"2023-02-24T08:26:02","s":["qy8rtfgfi6"]}]},"5":{"4":[{"m":"It seems this couple 👫 wanted the praise and honour of sacrificing what belongs to you for others, whiles still holding on to part of the money 💵, and yet lying that they had sold everything for the sake of the brethren.\n\nI conjecture that when they sold the land and they got the money, they couldn't believe that such a huge amount was going to the church.\n\nThey conspired to lie about it after they had likely promised the church they would sell their land to support the ministry.\n\nThey could have changed their minds at any time but chose this path.","dt":"2023-02-25T08:57:22","s":["xdosji2mf9"]}],"9":[{"m":"It's sad 😔, sad that in the times of the apostles, as we see in this case, the apostles literally stood in the place of God.\n\nPeter did not say you have lied to the apostle of Christ, but that they have lied directly to God.\nThe people in the early church were like the children of Israel 🇮🇱, in that God was literally in their midst and they were aware of it.\n\nIt was this awareness and presence, I believe, of God that resulted in the death of this couple 👫.\n\nThis was the epitome, more or less, of what church should be: love, sharing, forgiveness, the fear of God both by the church ⛪ and those without.\n\nThere was true Power and presence.\n\nIt's sad, sad that today's church lacks all of these things, yet the pastors of today want to claim the honour and privileges the early apostles had.\n\nPastors coerce members to give using biblical examples, when these pastors will dip their hands 🖐️ into the offertory.\n\nThey require honour and unchallenged respect when they take advantage of that to enrich themselves and have their own way with the flock 🐑.\n\nSometimes ravaging them. Sad 😔, real sad 😔. The truth must be told that we all, pulpit to pew, aspire to be like Jesus and the apostles, but we are not yet there.\n\nTill we get there, we must be wise and careful, even in the house 🏡 of God, the church ⛪","dt":"2023-06-27T14:30:24","s":["78wxfxj49v"]}],"13":[{"m":"Of course you would want to be cautious of such a community of holy people, where lying can have you struck down, especially when you know you are fake and just want the benefits of the community without genuine conversion 👇. 😌","dt":"2023-02-25T08:59:57","s":["b9yvz8e712"]}],"19":[{"m":"They had their plans, the Pharisees, but God had better counter plans. This act of the angel of God should have melted their hearts 💕.\n\nBut no, it did not; these were so hardened and would not be moved by miracles, neither by words.\n\nIt seems nothing would change their stands. Indeed, brood of vipers they were, and they would not escape the coming wrath of God.\n\nMatthew 23:33 KJV\nYe serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?","dt":"2023-02-27T09:00:07","s":["r84i6st1qu"]},{"m":"What is this? So humorous.\n\nThere was no stopping them. Even when in anger the disciples were locked 🔒 up,\n\nalmost immediately an angel comes to supernaturally rescue them.\n\nHow do you deal with such things?\n\nThe evidence of the divine hand of God was too strong 💪 and real to deny.","dt":"2025-04-19T09:26:06","s":["fpsdol15hf"]}],"20":[{"m":"See the instruction of the angel 😇 after making mockery of the attempted imprisonment of the disciples...\n\nHe tells them to go stand back in the temple doing exactly what caused their arrest — preaching Jesus.\n\nIt was almost as if God wanted to leave no room for them to doubt 🤷‍♂️ that indeed Jesus was whom he said he was.\n\nSo much so that they themselves, without doubt 🤷‍♂️, would acknowledge that it is God and his Christ they hate, and not that there was lack of evidence that Jesus was the Christ.\n\nThis was so glaring in how they dealt with the truth presented to them.\n\nThey were indeed children of the devil 👿","dt":"2025-04-19T09:30:58","s":["yzlsp6wip2"]}],"21":[{"m":"Ha 😁, what a slap in the face. God has a sense of humor.","dt":"2023-02-27T09:01:19","s":["jlybf7j90e"]},{"m":"They taught in the temple 🏛. Such defiance, but in a sense it was not for the same reason Jesus cleansed and taught in the temple.\n\nThis was the house of God, not of man 👨🏿. So they had more right to teach the truth of God's word, even if the leaders disagreed.\n\nBut years to come, and they had to flee the temple and synagogues because of persecution.","dt":"2023-02-27T09:05:06","s":["7xu3xh5zn9"]}],"24":[{"m":"No amount of proof or signs 🤘 would change these people.\n\nThey were hardened beyond help... They would not even concede their mistakes... Indeed, children of the devil 👿.\n\nNo wonder Jesus was ever so often on their case and never gave them much chance.","dt":"2022-11-19T08:49:59","s":["t7bykg8ofb"]},{"m":"Didn't their conscience then prick ⛏ them that this thing was of God?\n\nThis goes to show how hardened and wicked they were. Any attempts at converting them or reasoning with them unto repentance would be a pipe dream 🚭.\n\nNot all men have faith, O Lord, give us the wisdom to distinguish these, we pray 🙏","dt":"2023-06-27T14:33:39","s":["k7zg2g4cto"]}],"28":[{"m":"So Jesus the Messiah was just this man 👨🏿 to them. He meant nothing to them.\n\nEven if they did not recognize he was the Messiah, at least they should have conceded he was of God, or a prophet.\n\nBut no, rather they conceded he was of the devil 👿","dt":"2023-06-27T14:35:26","s":["3033pzacxo"]}],"29":[{"m":"These same men had been brought before the council when they attracted a huge multitude after the healing of the man at the gate of Beautiful.\n\nThey had created a scene and distracted the normal order of activities of the temple worship that day.\n\nThey were immediately seized from continuing and even threatened.\n\nBut as is evidenced here, they could not and would not stop.","dt":"2023-02-27T09:14:01","s":["huflntzc0t"]}],"33":[{"m":"These men were too hardened. I am beginning to believe Joshua Selman's message that they were probably of the seed of the serpent 🐍.\n\nHow could men be this corrupted and defiant to truth?\n\nThey were the ones who were learned and had the law.\n\nAll they needed to do was to go read 📖 and they would be convinced.\n\nBut no, indeed generation of serpents.\n\nMatthew 23:33 KJV\nYe serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?","dt":"2023-02-27T09:16:52","s":["63fa6ivzqv"]},{"m":"They were going to do the same thing they did to Jesus to them.","dt":"2023-06-27T14:38:00","s":["pszcdgugle"]}],"34":[{"m":"If we look at the actions of wicked and ruthless men as these, you would not want to have anything to do with them.\n\nBut this is rather where we good men need to rise to the occasion and not leave power to such evil 😈 hearts 💕.\n\nSee, among these was Gamaliel, who had grown in influence and brought some sanity to these mad men.\n\nSo good people, rather than run from power because it is corrupted 🧞‍♂️ by evil, ought to run toward it and engage, so the force 💪 of good and of God is also felt.\n\nDespite the interjection of Gamaliel, these men could not let it slide just like that and free them.\n\nThey still flogged these men. Which of course is better than death ☠","dt":"2023-02-27T09:25:27","s":["of6wzf517j"]}],"39":[{"m":"Finally one of their own had concluded right 👉 — they indeed were fighting God.","dt":"2025-04-19T09:35:02","s":["m1s0nt6dia"]}],"40":[{"m":"So after all this counsel, they still threatened them not to speak in the name of Jesus. Or maybe it was to save face 😔.\n\nLet me see if they were ever arrayed before them again after this.\n\nBut hold on, I remember Stephen was killed after this. Was it before them? Let me see.","dt":"2023-06-27T16:29:01","s":["kffpcza8up"]}],"42":[{"m":"Ei, these guys were stubborn paa oo...\n\nSo I believe true believers ought to begin to invade the churches once more with truth and doctrine.\n\nTrue worship 🛐 and doctrine ought to be restored in the house 🏡 of the Lord.\n\nIn the place of lies, we ought to engage the church ⛪ back to God.\n\nSo help 😣 me, Lord.","dt":"2023-02-27T09:28:15","s":["o61omwz9ef"]},{"m":"There was no stopping this.","dt":"2025-04-19T09:34:27","s":["2ikckq21jo"]}],"10":[{"m":"Did they have a family 👪?","dt":"2023-02-25T08:58:27","s":["9f8lgk73ep"]}],"17":[{"m":"This fresh wave 🌊 of revival and the spread of the gospel was definitely not going to keep going this unhindered.\n\nWithout the devil 👿 stepping in to stop, or at least hinder, this blazing work of revival.","dt":"2023-02-27T08:56:00","s":["vfrvprtw43"]}],"26":[{"m":"☺, interesting. The Jews were not a religious group that could be taken for granted.\n\nInasmuch as they were listening 👂 to the truth of God's word, they were not calm, have-mercy kind of people.\n\nIf you should mess up against their beliefs, they would stone you.\n\nIs this allowed in Christianity? For Christians to physically defend themselves if attacked or confronted?\n\nI think it depends on the context.","dt":"2023-02-27T09:11:17","s":["9mkazya28a"]}]},"6":{"15":[{"m":"True was the saying of Abraham to the rich man... They have Moses and the prophets.\n\nIf they would not hear them, neither would they heed if one were to rise from the dead.\n\nHere a man's face shone as an angel, and yet they killed him and still boldly deny the Christ.","dt":"2022-11-19T09:22:28","s":["59yk40sl84"]},{"m":"And thus marked the beginning of his demise and exaltation to heaven.","dt":"2023-06-28T08:23:45","s":["l6ekd86v0g"]}]},"7":{"57":[{"m":"They were raving mad at that point.","dt":"2023-02-28T16:42:24","s":["4tvand2x9z"]},{"m":"These wicked people and their children did not love the Lord, nor were they deserving of him.\n\nTheir deeds and acts showed they hated the Lord and his truth and his ways.\n\nYet them the Lord wanted to deliver and bring salvation to, as well as the rest of the world.","dt":"2023-07-01T11:48:59","s":["7x8etsl9pb"]}],"58":[{"m":"Oh, the brain 🧠 washing was so strong 💪.\n\nHere was Saul, so zealous for God that he followed the traditions of men taught him rather than what God himself had taught in his word.\n\nIt took the divine intervention of God to bring him to his senses and wake him up.\n\nThis was what the miracles of Jesus were supposed to do. Wake them that slept out of their stupor.\n\nBut it did for some, and others would just not repent.","dt":"2025-04-19T09:53:57","s":["dskbxm1m9k"]}]},"8":{"13":[{"m":"Simon believed also and was baptized, yet he still had in him the shrewdness and the spirit of manipulation.\n\nWe should be careful; there is a standard in Christ — for not all men have faith.\n\nThe moment people walk in the flesh, though born again, we should neither accord to them nor expect from them the nature of Christ.\n\nLest we be fooled over and over again.","dt":"2023-07-04T10:22:53","s":["hw0k29dnwg"]}],"20":[{"m":"But don't we buy prayer and the hearts 💕 of men of God, so called, with money 💵?\n\nAnd oh, they gladly accept it.","dt":"2025-04-19T10:00:23","s":["ru4zs8lqan"]}],"23":[{"m":"Yes, he indeed was in the bond of iniquity. Though born again, he was in the gall of bitterness, another aspect of his character that had not been dealt with.","dt":"2023-07-04T10:25:02","s":["t4u30b6xv8"]}],"30":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. Imagine this scene. The eunuch was in the desert 🏜, no one else was around. And that's understandable since it's a desert 🏜.\n\nThen coincidentally another man 👨🏿 was also traveling, but on foot.\n\nThis man joins himself to the chariot 🛒 and they have a discussion.\n\nAt the end of which the man disappears in plain sight.\n\nWhat would his conclusion be, except that he had seen an angel 😇 of God?\n\nBut it was a man. Could it be that many a man have beheld other men 🚹 but were thought of as angels?\n\nMen so yielded to the Spirit that they could be passed for divine beings.","dt":"2023-07-04T10:30:23","s":["qvjcy604xn"]}],"34":[{"m":"Reading 📖 the prophets often leads to this dilemma... As to whom the words apply to.\n\nSuch is the nature of the prophetic writings.","dt":"2025-04-19T10:04:06","s":["exasdo5jja"]}],"19":[{"m":"He wanted to buy it and later sell it to the highest bidder, likely gain worldwide fame as he gained audience before kings and the greats of the earth 🌎.\n\nHe saw opportunities that the apostles did not see, because he was corrupt at heart ♥.\n\nAnd we see many such sorcerers in our time ⌚.\n\nMaking great merchandise of the kingdom and the gospel.\n\nFulfilling all the lusts of the flesh without restraint.","dt":"2025-04-19T09:58:49","s":["nvtiyf6h4b"]}],"39":[{"m":"Oh, what joy as this eunuch heads home for Ethiopia 🇪🇹. Sending the gospel home 🏡.\n\nThis miraculous disappearance of Philip further comes to cement that indeed Jesus is the Son of God and he indeed is Lord and Christ.\n\nOh, what a moment, oh, what joy...","dt":"2023-03-01T12:20:28","s":["rx8sm2i6cs"]},{"m":"I'm sure he would go home 🏡 knowing he had met an angel 😇 of the Lord who preached to him the gospel.\n\nThis vivid supernatural experience was necessary to entrench the belief of the eunuch in what had just happened to him.\n\nNo man-taught wild doctrines can bring any confusion to his heart ♥ or thoughts 💭.\n\nFor he had experienced it himself.","dt":"2025-04-19T10:06:34","s":["1nqt9lfuvh"]}]},"9":{"5":[{"m":"At this point he realized, or maybe his later analysis of the experience showed, that Jesus was not a man.\n\nHow could the man who came blaspheming 🤬 against the temple 🏛 and God, who was killed, and rightly so, be speaking from heaven?\n\nThen he was no man; the claims he said about himself were true.","dt":"2023-07-05T06:18:55","s":["fzr6f9cxld"]},{"m":"This statement by Jesus is so revelatory.\n\nIt shows the end of this entire Christian 🚶 experience.\n\nVictory is assured. So here Jesus advises Paul that his taking sides against the truth rather than for the truth is self-destructive and counterproductive.\n\nI read that the expression \"it is hard for thee to kick against the pricks/goads\" was a Roman idiom.\n\nHere's what Google search reveals: To \"kick against the goads\" is nothing less than an exercise in vanity; futile and pointless. The Greeks and Romans used this saying to imply \"ruinous resistance.\"\n\nWow, Paul was truly lucky to be handpicked and saved from such an end.\n\nPaul himself called it mercy.","dt":"2023-07-09T16:06:00","s":["asvsn3x377"]}],"6":[{"m":"At this divine encounter Paul is changed, and yet his sect of Pharisees saw not spiritual but physical manifestations of the divine, yet would not believe.","dt":"2025-04-19T19:46:51","s":["jda7zmpp3u"]}],"7":[{"m":"What became of these men who were there with Paul? Did they believe after or not?\n\nDid they become fiery Christians like Paul? No, not likely, else they would have been mentioned.\n\nOh, how close one can be to greatness and yet far away because of apathy and lack of discernment.\n\nThis reminds me of James and John's mother. She discerned the kingdom so much that she desired a good place for her children 🧒.\n\nNot even for herself but for her children.","dt":"2022-11-20T05:24:51","s":["aovqaf66mf"]}],"8":[{"m":"Irony of ironies.\n\nI would not be surprised 🤨 that the night before his journey to Damascus,\n\nhe might have prayed for Godspeed and favour to capture this sect which was provoking God with their idolatry.\n\nBecause of their rejection of God, they, Israel 🇮🇱, once a powerful nation, were now servants to the Romans.\n\nNow to add insult 🤬 to injury, in captivity they were starting a new religion and calling this Jesus the Messiah.\n\nGod knew he did all this in ignorance, hence this conversion.","dt":"2023-03-02T06:39:57","s":["3odknvfphd"]},{"m":"Maybe these men who were with Paul became Christians also. Maybe not as great as he, but believers all the same.\n\nMaybe they became great but were just not mentioned in any text of scripture.","dt":"2023-03-02T06:43:21","s":["x3k39xwb9d"]}],"14":[{"m":"See how Ananias freely expressed himself and his objections before the Lord. The Lord does not gag anyone, so why do we see so much manipulation in our churches today?\n\nNot even God hinders us. So we should not allow men to do so to us, especially in the name of the Lord.","dt":"2023-03-02T07:23:46","s":["xopknswbh1"]}],"17":[{"m":"Wow... Strange times ⌚. Indeed these were strange times for Saul.\n\nIt took such an obvious, undeniable supernatural event for Saul to be transformed into a disciple.\n\nHowever, we know that not all will change, even at the most powerful witness of Christ.\n\nAs we can see from the many examples of the Pharisees...\n\nSo in soul winning, we ought to plant the seed and leave God to be God.\n\nWe need not be disappointed if people change not.","dt":"2022-11-20T05:30:21","s":["dgsbx6yieq"]}],"28":[{"m":"How did Paul feel walking 🚶 among the believers? How did he overcome the regrets, knowing full well he killed a vital tool and pillar in the church — Stephen?","dt":"2023-07-11T07:09:20","s":["887w74ee4j"]}],"29":[{"m":"Not surprisingly... Stephen started off by disputing with certain of the Jews, and that ultimately led to his demise.","dt":"2022-11-20T05:40:27","s":["omykjn3wja"]},{"m":"Were the Jews just interested in killing anyone who did not side with them, or were they just ignorantly defending what they believed to be true in keeping with the commandments of God?\n\nThe latter seems more likely, even though the former is also true.\n\nBecause the leaders, chief priests etc., in the face of undeniable evidence kept their stance to protect their place and interest rather than God's.","dt":"2023-07-09T16:17:31","s":["z030g1z6mq"]}],"31":[{"m":"So what did the Pharisees say about Saul's conversion? How many priests believed because of Paul, and how many remained adamant? Hmm 🤔","dt":"2023-03-02T07:29:43","s":["8wzpi6ypio"]}],"32":[{"m":"As an itinerant preacher of a sort, he moved from place to place to strengthen the churches.","dt":"2022-11-20T05:45:45","s":["vdreb8gv5d"]}],"24":[{"m":"When he was on their side, they cherished him because they believed he was on the side of truth.\n\nAfter his conversion, they did not ask, \"What happened to our brother Paul?\" Rather they sought to kill him.\n\nThat tells you they followed blind faith and religion and would hear no reason.\n\nHaving gone through such a phase ourselves as believers, we should be ready and prepared to answer reasonably our faith and why we believe what we believe.\n\nFaith is the start of Christian belief. But it is not good to have faith that is blind, without any reason at all.","dt":"2022-11-20T05:38:47","s":["ktbfg13t4t"]}],"43":[{"m":"Only thinking out loud: what happened to all these who were brought back from the dead, in the sense that decades later in life they died again?\n\nInteresting.","dt":"2025-04-20T10:31:04","s":["69mcmml8sl"]}]},"10":{"9":[{"m":"What if Peter had not prayed...? Would God have had to wait till he was in prayer?\nInterestingly, it was on the day they took their journey that Peter saw the vision.\n\nOur Lord was right: \"Men ought always to pray and not faint.\"","dt":"2023-03-06T12:28:00","s":["8o83z9fir7"]}],"24":[{"m":"Oh, that we would have such friends, who would lead us on the path to eternal life.\n\nThe importance of right friendships.","dt":"2023-03-07T07:21:37","s":["cqq57hgj4k"]}],"31":[{"m":"When the decision was being made to rope the Gentiles into the salvation program, a search had to be made.\n\nJust like when the fullness of time had come and the Messiah was to be born, a search was made and Mary was found.\n\nSo Cornelius was chosen not as a random event but through, I believe, painstaking search.\n\nHe fitted the kind of person, home and personality needed for the job.","dt":"2023-03-07T07:52:44","s":["nx73x18g4v"]}],"38":[{"m":"How God anointed Jesus of Nazareth... Who went about doing good.\n\nThe good news that Jesus preached covered all of Judea and Galilee.\n\nHe literally fulfilled his ministry to all Israel 🇮🇱 as a witness to them.\n\nHis name was commonplace. He indeed, like John the Baptist, was a burning 🔥 and shining light.","dt":"2022-11-20T13:43:59","s":["fu6p62epvq"]}],"39":[{"m":"So the death ☠ of Jesus was common knowledge among both Jews and Gentiles.","dt":"2023-07-10T07:29:23","s":["o7sj8aggsn"]}],"42":[{"m":"This instruction to preach in the early stages of Christianity was basically to proclaim what they had witnessed.\n\nAs the church grew and was established, deeper doctrines of the Holy Ghost, baptism etc. were taught.\n\nOf course, these Paul calls fundamental doctrines.","dt":"2023-03-07T11:23:38","s":["5f50pb4b1t"]}],"43":[{"m":"Which specific Old Testament scriptures and prophets give this witness, that whoever believes in him shall receive remission of sins?","dt":"2025-04-20T11:50:54","s":["dw318m9cj7"]}],"17":[{"m":"He sees a vision and immediately seeks the meaning.\n\nIt was not some random occurrence; no, there was a purpose to it.\n\nAnd that purpose was not hidden; that is why in no time men from Cornelius came to him.\n\nThe lesson is to seek to know and understand what the visions, dreams etc. that God gives us mean.","dt":"2023-03-07T06:55:05","s":["igs5udpgnl"]}],"28":[{"m":"It took much graphic detail to get Peter to go to a non-Jewish home...\n\nGod had to make it undoubtedly clear what his agenda was in a very obvious way before Peter could heed, knowing very well the laws God himself had instituted.\n\nTo indicate there was a change of laws required making it so obvious his hand was in it.\nHence the many confirmations and signs.","dt":"2023-03-07T07:50:15","s":["njf6oh4534"]}]},"11":{"7":[{"m":"Why this imagery? Why did not an angel 😇 just come and say, the gospel must go to the Gentiles also?\n\nThis has been part of the plan always.\n\nBut no, God is a master communicator — and knows how to paint the right picture to drum home the message 🥁","dt":"2023-07-11T06:47:28","s":["fnt65emx3d"]}],"12":[{"m":"Meaning, do not be afraid 😨 to go with them; do not doubt their word or intentions, that their master indeed sent for you, as a command from God.\n\nGo, nothing doubting, for it is my will.\n\nThis begs another question: why does God have to go through such elaborate means to have the Spirit poured on Cornelius?\n\nCould he not have asked that they gather and, just as he did in the upper room, fall on them?\n\nBut then that would mean being baptized without being preached to.\n\nOkay... It appears God has set up systems, and it is through these systems that he works.\n\nWhy the angel 😇 did not preach the gospel shows the system God has set up for salvation and for dominion in the earth 🌎.\n\nHe always must use man... the lord of the earth 🌎, and God the Lord of man.","dt":"2022-11-20T13:52:42","s":["50wxpu9t39"]}],"15":[{"m":"The day of Pentecost to the disciples marked the beginning for them.\n\nWhy so, why not the day they met Christ? Because of the context he was using this.\n\nAnd indeed it was the beginning, and when their lives changed.","dt":"2023-03-08T05:21:09","s":["4y13gpt4d2"]}]},"12":{"2":[{"m":"What exactly happened here we are not told.\n\nWhat triggered this sudden onslaught against the church ⛪ we are not told.\n\nOr maybe something happened and it was attributed to the Christians, or there was a Jewish riot in the temple due to some confrontation over doctrine with the Christians.\n\nWe are not told.","dt":"2023-07-12T07:06:54","s":["qjnmcxluz8"]}],"3":[{"m":"So it pleased the Jews, so likely the cause of this fresh onslaught against believers had something to do with the Jews.","dt":"2023-07-12T07:07:53","s":["f0rc4fbv1w"]}],"6":[{"m":"Prayer was part of his everyday life... No wonder he could sleep a night before his death ☠... Likely he had committed himself to the Lord to do as he pleased 😌","dt":"2022-11-20T14:30:52","s":["e098ghse3x"]},{"m":"He was sleeping 😴 between two ✌️ soldiers; that's quite unusual.\n\nPeter was indeed thought a high-profile criminal.\n\nHe had garnered a large following that was teaching new things and championing a new religion; he could possibly start an insurrection.","dt":"2023-07-14T06:55:12","s":["dabno1a3wj"]},{"m":"This tight security protocol is standard procedure, I believe, for high-profile, hardened criminals.","dt":"2023-07-15T09:43:24","s":["bf3na2sxeu"]},{"m":"God waited saa till the night 🌃 of his trial.","dt":"2023-07-15T09:44:58","s":["7tdmjd1xgd"]}],"7":[{"m":"Arise up quickly. But why the haste? Because he did not have all night. He could not suspend time, but could cause deep sleep or blind the eyes 👀 from seeing them.\n\nI'm sure he was time-bound, because angels are not when supposed to in the physical realm.\n\nOr maybe in all of this he was visible only to Peter.","dt":"2023-07-14T07:04:51","s":["m98z8uzbbr"]}],"9":[{"m":"Of course he thought it was a vision.\n\nThe turn of events was too unnatural to be real.","dt":"2023-07-15T09:46:58","s":["pucg0b89tp"]}],"10":[{"m":"Did they walk through the people at the posts, or did they just walk past them without them noticing? Either ways, no wonder Peter thought it was a vision.","dt":"2023-07-14T07:12:09","s":["sl4cacd7b4"]}],"11":[{"m":"The Lord Jesus... Faithful to his word and ever with his children, came to the rescue of Peter.\n\nOh, how real he was to them, and even now he is so real.","dt":"2022-11-20T14:33:29","s":["ne5aq9n8pl"]}],"12":[{"m":"So where were the men and husbands of these women?\n\nMen in general were plentiful in the followers of Jesus, but I'm just wondering about the women and their husbands.","dt":"2023-07-14T07:14:09","s":["d8nmbqmt2n"]}],"15":[{"m":"Maybe in their prayers they were expecting that when Peter is arrayed before Herod, mercy would be shown him.\n\nDoes that not therefore imply that we can be praying one thing and having a particular expectation, but God would answer differently or give the best answer to the prayers?\n\nWe indeed sometimes do not know how to pray as we ought 🙏, but the Spirit helps us.","dt":"2023-07-14T07:18:12","s":["l65a6c7rm4"]}],"17":[{"m":"How God can astonish 🤯 us with the methodology he uses to answer our prayers.","dt":"2023-07-14T07:19:19","s":["n2vth0zxlx"]}],"23":[{"m":"Well deserving for the numerous innocent deaths.","dt":"2023-07-15T09:49:42","s":["odtleu7oms"]}],"4":[{"m":"This kind of security for a nobody and harmless person like Peter.\n\nThis shows the kind of information and perception Herod had been given about Peter and the Christians.\n\nIt's also very likely that he knew the Christian population was quite large and Peter was the head, so he was a high-profile person.","dt":"2023-07-12T07:28:36","s":["ffkei0cq0v"]}],"18":[{"m":"Oh, I can imagine the scene, the confusion, the fear 😱 of Herod, and what he would think of such rubbish of an excuse.\n\nHm, maybe they took bribes, but...\nDid they all take bribes, all sixteen of them? 🤔 Then this Christian sect has some really powerful people backing them.\n\nAll this still did not change the hardened leaders.\n\nI'm sure some others of the prison guards 💂 would convert to Christianity, as happened in Paul's case.\n\nGod has so many ways of ensuring his word gets out there and people surrender to him.","dt":"2023-07-14T08:48:49","s":["okfxbh9yu9"]}]},"13":{"13":[{"m":"Why didn't Luke state the cause of John Mark's departure?\n\nI believe it was to protect him. Because if it was a valid reason, why would Paul refuse to take him along?\n\nWell, Luke was penning history and did not want to paint a brother in bad light, especially now that John Mark had become useful in the ministry work again.\n\nOr maybe he thought 💭 it not wise to reveal some of Paul's extreme demands and standards.\n\nIf what Mark did was so bad, why was Barnabas willing to take him?\n\nBut then again Barnabas is that way, always believing and always trusting.","dt":"2023-07-22T06:47:47","s":["sm0l038q51"]}],"14":[{"m":"Who was sponsoring these trips and journeys to distant lands?","dt":"2023-07-19T06:42:55","s":["i1d5rx92eh"]}],"27":[{"m":"Is it possible 🙆 that the same thing is happening in our times today...\n\nWhere the reading of scriptures and preaching is going on day after day, and yet the Christians do not know the Lord nor his voice.\n\nIndeed the same thing is happening in our times today.","dt":"2022-11-21T06:33:30","s":["nh0ors76p7"]}],"36":[{"m":"Same message that Peter preached, and he used this exact same psalm.\n\nEvidence-based preaching, more or less.","dt":"2023-07-19T06:48:41","s":["20r07tp12u"]}],"39":[{"m":"How compelling were these words.\n\nPaul's speech of Jesus suggests word about him and the way had traveled far and wide.\n\nThat the long-awaited Messiah was Jesus, just that he is gone and will come later to liberate the people of God.","dt":"2023-07-19T06:56:14","s":["jpd3kdo8b4"]},{"m":"Is this teaching of being justified in Christ from things the law could not justify not the same he teaches in his writings?\n\nWhat things was he making reference to?","dt":"2023-07-20T05:54:25","s":["0wvz8aw0kn"]}],"42":[{"m":"Why were the Gentiles more responsive?\n\nMaybe because from childhood they had not been as indoctrinated as the core Jews.","dt":"2023-07-19T06:57:26","s":["vywe4asueb"]}],"52":[{"m":"Ah, with joy and the Holy Ghost, meaning them that had accepted the word went through the Holy Ghost baptism and promise of the Father.\n\nA full church ⛪ had been formed.\n\nSo Lord, what do we do now in the churches?\n\nThere is no joy; we are cold ❄; we can pray in tongues one moment whiles still in hatred and dissension towards one another.\n\nHaving the form of godliness but denying the power.","dt":"2023-07-19T07:01:25","s":["01kkuln2by"]}],"25":[{"m":"Who told Paul about John and his sayings?\n\nBecause Paul himself was not there, likely John or the other disciples had been telling the story orally and word had gone round.","dt":"2023-07-19T06:46:18","s":["gkzy1dhdz9"]}],"50":[{"m":"So the growth and sustenance of religion was not by some supernatural means, but men have stood and defended their religion in the name of God, and yet it seems the God of that religion has not shown himself true.\n\nYou would easily have thought the God that the Jews so vehemently fight for would also fight for his own cause.\n\nMany religions indeed are not God-ordained but rather man-made.\n\nTo appease our own senses and fulfill our needs of prominence and self-importance, even our survival.","dt":"2025-04-21T09:27:36","s":["aj7wkntq8a"]}]},"14":{"19":[{"m":"How come a verse ago they hailed him as God and the next they stoned him?\nI believe it was not in the same breath.\n\nIt had to be sometime later; the Jews through conspiracy sought to kill him as they did the Lord.","dt":"2023-07-22T06:54:06","s":["avizy11wrc"]}],"21":[{"m":"They went there again? This Paul and his group.\n\nThis time they went low-key 🗝 and spoke to only the brethren, not an evangelistic effort.","dt":"2023-07-22T06:57:20","s":["i6uh3pgehs"]}]},"15":{"6":[{"m":"Could they not have prayed for God to have given a simple answer, and that would end all the disputes?","dt":"2022-11-23T10:34:30","s":["me3wgnibke"]}],"11":[{"m":"So here we see the grace of Jesus.\n\nThe Jews kept the laws, but even they could not, and now the Gentiles were being compelled to bear that same yoke of the law which the Jews themselves struggled with.\n\nBut thanks be to the grace of Jesus, which exempted them from such laws, yet provided them even better access to God apart from the law.\n\nGod, give me grace to serve you, grace for ministry.","dt":"2025-04-24T07:16:17","s":["vpeminbclh"]}],"13":[{"m":"So the Christian faith is progressive, in line with what God by his Spirit revealed to his people.\n\n2000 years down the line, and we have the New Testament and 2000 years of church history to make sense of the faith...\n\nOf course it does not mean every question has been answered, but then it helps us know how to arrive at a consensus concerning the mind of God, especially when controversy comes up.\n\nWe weigh 🏋️ and judge and look at what God, by his Spirit's work and move, is signaling to us.\n\nAnd of course he will not signal anything contrary to his word.","dt":"2022-11-23T10:53:48","s":["lvqzsnkqsx"]}],"20":[{"m":"Even this command, we see Paul explain it further and even clarify how that an idol is nothing, and that we abstain not for the sake of the idol but for the conscience of weaker brethren.","dt":"2022-11-23T10:56:23","s":["qjeve3nz91"]}],"29":[{"m":"Even these instructions Paul later debunked: the eating of meat sacrificed to idols.\n\nIt goes to show that we work with God, and that even the early disciples observed what the Lord was doing and then inferred from it.","dt":"2023-07-21T10:48:43","s":["bhk3aktshl"]},{"m":"Now to my question: why didn't God just show by revelation or some divine way the answer to this divisive yet important topic of Gentiles observing the law?\n\nBut made Paul and Co go through this arduous journey back and have this debate, which itself was not very conclusive, as we would see later.\n\nBecause Paul had to still deal with issues related to eating food sacrificed to idols.","dt":"2023-07-21T10:53:10","s":["0cqzxrji0p"]},{"m":"It seems the staying from blood and things strangled, which is part of the law of Moses, was a concession that James made so as not to outrightly dismiss the other side of the argument, who wanted the whole law of Moses kept.\n\nIt was a harmless concession really, and maybe a healthy one.\n\nBut it was not a requirement under grace; that is why, as the church evolved, it has been scraped off.\n\nIndeed in some of Paul's letters he debunks them.","dt":"2025-04-24T07:22:10","s":["evbjx4zxw5"]}],"39":[{"m":"Barnabas, ever generous and forgiving. It was his good heart ♥ that got him to admit Paul, even when the rest of the disciples were wary of him.\n\nAnd now that same good heart wanted John Mark back, but Paul, who himself was a beneficiary of Barnabas's generosity, would have none of it.\n\nWe do good not expecting anything back, lest we ourselves would be highly disappointed 😥","dt":"2025-04-24T07:26:59","s":["x5uylnrtt2"]}],"40":[{"m":"Eish... I hope this is not church politics.","dt":"2022-11-23T11:01:59","s":["j1e5609476"]}]},"16":{"3":[{"m":"Wow... Practical Christianity... Not because it would justify him before God, but so they can have audience among the Jews to even speak to them the truth of the gospel.","dt":"2022-11-23T11:17:21","s":["jw9n4t1ikp"]},{"m":"So Paul needed an assistant, someone who would attend to him and minister to their needs.\n\nAs we would say, someone who would do small small rounds.\n\nHe couldn't send Silas; he was a grown man.\n\nSo in effect Paul needed John Mark, despite his too known.\n\nBut John was unreliable in a sense, and Paul, like me, needed someone stable.","dt":"2023-07-22T07:04:54","s":["0g19qvnvyw"]}],"6":[{"m":"This is new; they did not come to Galatia the last time.","dt":"2023-07-22T07:07:39","s":["zelcp1r132"]}],"7":[{"m":"So Paul was not just going about his journey carnally. No, he kept in sync with the Spirit for constant prompting and guidance.","dt":"2022-11-23T11:18:31","s":["m8zqxd9827"]}],"13":[{"m":"The modus operandi was to go to the synagogue 🕍, particularly on the sabbath, but in this case\n\nit appeared they had not a synagogue but some spiritual place of worship.","dt":"2022-11-23T15:16:48","s":["qxljaviawo"]}],"25":[{"m":"Ei, these guys don't sleep... Why at midnight? What informed them to pray at such an hour, and praise?","dt":"2022-11-23T11:23:44","s":["u5b7733pwp"]}],"27":[{"m":"The presence of the Lord was there, and where the presence of the Lord is, there is liberty 🗽.\n\nAll were loosed from their chains ⛓.\n\nAnd this is very symbolic, because obviously most of the people there had committed crimes and offenses, yet the Lord freed everyone regardless of his offense.\n\nSo we all can come to the Lord. He will forgive and set free regardless of the weight of the sin.","dt":"2023-07-22T07:42:50","s":["g3lb0wlc8x"]}],"31":[{"m":"It was not just an earthquake. Because earthquakes do not bring repentance.\n\nBut I can imagine the chains falling off one after another and the prison door screeching 😱 open of their own accord.\n\nAnd the presence of the Lord heavy in that place.\n\nEven the prisoners were too afraid 😨 to escape.\n\nBut the Lord could have done all this, and yet he let them be beaten?","dt":"2023-07-22T07:45:42","s":["nv9r3wi2mt"]}],"40":[{"m":"All that was needed was for a seed of a church, no matter how small, to be sown, and with the right foundations the churches grew.","dt":"2022-11-23T11:26:14","s":["oawcs3xpjx"]}]},"17":{"2":[{"m":"As his modus operandi was... ☺","dt":"2022-11-25T12:00:38","s":["6er1pnv5o2"]}],"6":[{"m":"An interesting description... It's like soul winning men and women into righteousness was now a mark of notoriety.","dt":"2022-11-25T12:02:43","s":["umaami7upe"]},{"m":"These that have turned the world upside down 👇 — obviously referring to the entire gospel movement and the massive work that has been done, beginning from Jesus and the days of Pentecost, over some two decades back.\n\nWord had traveled far, and now these people on mission had arrived here in Thessalonica as well.\n\nReminds me much of the journey of the children of Israel 🇮🇱 in the desert.\n\nNow, as Rahab the prostitute testified, they had heard of the God of Israel 🇮🇱 who opened the Red Sea, and now these ones had arrived in Jericho.\nA foreboding presence before them all.","dt":"2022-11-26T06:28:20","s":["6uhdwpqf2m"]}],"11":[{"m":"Oh, how I wish there was a letter of Paul to the churches in Berea.\n\nThey were more noble than others.\n\nIndeed, here it talks of the Jews of this city; somehow they were open-minded and were not afraid at all to have their minds changed on an opinion, so long as it was grounded in the scriptures.","dt":"2025-04-27T01:23:15","s":["4j7v5n0jez"]}],"13":[{"m":"These whitewashed graves... They would not receive the truth... Neither yet permit others to receive same.","dt":"2022-11-25T12:03:53","s":["sbyn3dhel8"]}],"14":[{"m":"The brethren sending Paul away, did that not mean possibly raising seed 🌱 for him to take on his journey?\n\nI don't think they just sent him away empty-handed.\n\nAnd a quick thought: mention is not made of miracles taking place here.\n\nThat does not mean it did not, though.","dt":"2023-07-25T06:47:16","s":["b7i02bksfv"]}],"22":[{"m":"A church in the US took this name...\n\nBerea church also in my hood... I understand why they named themselves thus.","dt":"2022-11-25T12:07:32","s":["u5z6gwfxo9"]}],"28":[{"m":"Wow... This is quoted in Christian circles as referring to our oneness and close union we Christians have with God.\n\nBut contextually he was not talking about the Christian way of life but of man's/humanity's way of life with God.","dt":"2022-11-25T12:09:58","s":["tg5ijep2z3"]}]},"18":{"4":[{"m":"The methods of Paul included his reasoning and persuasive abilities.\n\nA skill he used much to advance the gospel.\n\nInterestingly, his persuasive abilities in no way imply he was without power; indeed, he was a man of immense powers.\n\nIn this wise the Holy Spirit really has hit a home run in sending Paul out to the Gentiles.\n\nIt's interesting again that though Paul's calling was to Gentile lands, he often and almost always started off in the synagogue of the Jews.\n\nA method which then attracted the Gentiles.\n\nHe had discovered what works 💪 and was sticking with it.","dt":"2025-04-27T01:42:31","s":["od843iaill"]}]},"19":{"9":[{"m":"The school of Tyrannus","dt":"2022-11-26T12:41:44","s":["scb8ersawz"]},{"m":"At this time he was not just involved in evangelistic effort of making Christ known, but Christ was already known, so a church was started and the gospel advanced through church ministry.","dt":"2023-07-25T15:23:40","s":["3dul8sde9a"]}]},"20":{"4":[{"m":"How far apart were these cities that these disciples came from, for them to accompany Paul?","dt":"2022-12-09T07:04:18","s":["j0qijrby94"]}],"25":[{"m":"Sad 😔, how could Paul tell of these things?","dt":"2023-07-30T06:56:40","s":["5z0ko52nfn"]}],"32":[{"m":"The word of his grace, his free gift of self-offering, his own blood.","dt":"2023-07-30T06:54:16","s":["k6a6g8jzri"]}],"33":[{"m":"Lord, may that be my testimony in your vineyard.","dt":"2022-12-09T07:17:37","s":["vsvqpp00ll"]}]},"21":{"4":[{"m":"How can Paul, who serves the Lord with all his heart, disobey the voice of God?\n\nTwo ✌️ things\n1. It was a word of knowledge of what was to happen at Jerusalem, not necessarily a command for him not to go. As his going would glorify God anyways.\n\n2. It was a word of knowledge to Paul, so he does with it as he wills, according to his own free choice.","dt":"2023-07-30T07:02:07","s":["qdh9qi4i9c"]}],"9":[{"m":"If he had four daughters of age, then he wasn't a young man. If he was the same as the Philip appointed to oversee the affairs of the widows, then it means they did not appoint novices as leaders.","dt":"2023-07-30T11:34:16","s":["b6mwx3l8r3"]}],"10":[{"m":"In Acts 11 verse 28, “Then one of them, named Agabus, stood up and showed by the Spirit that there was going to be a great famine throughout all the world, which also happened in the days of Claudius Caesar.” Acts 11:28\n\nThis same Agabus had prophesied about the famine and it happened, so his words did not fall to the ground.\n\nNo wonder after his prophecy, they knew for a fact that it was going to happen, so they pleaded with him.","dt":"2023-07-30T07:10:29","s":["k84b5uxv33"]}],"25":[{"m":"I wonder what went on in Paul's head as the brethren talked of the command to the Gentiles concerning eating food sacrificed to idols,\n\nHe knowing full well he had told them that, and further clarified that an idol is nothing, so you may eat or desist in accordance with the word of God.\n\nFor he would rather obey God and give the Gentiles their true liberties with understanding than bind them with the commands of men.","dt":"2022-12-10T08:09:37","s":["m0csx1zax2"]}],"26":[{"m":"This was animal sacrifice — as if he was under the law. Little wonder he said that he had done all manner of things so that he might at least save some.","dt":"2023-07-30T11:39:36","s":["zv3bbj55q"]}],"8":[{"m":"Who is he?","dt":"2023-07-30T07:02:39","s":["yemmtm46py"]}]},"23":{"11":[{"m":"Though prophecy came that he would suffer at Jerusalem, so by interpretation he was not to go.\n\nSo what was this man doing hearing the voice of God and a good word as that?","dt":"2022-12-10T12:08:51","s":["ybdm277b0k"]}],"21":[{"m":"This was a serious thing, very serious. These men, under an oath and a curse 🤬 on themselves, would go to whatever extent to free themselves from the oath and curse.\n\nOnly God knows how many days they had already been fasting.\n\nThe seriousness of the issue is seen in the steps the captain took to protect Saul.\n\nIt was not an overkill in the light of the intelligence gathered.","dt":"2022-12-11T05:52:48","s":["vze5w0eumh"]}]},"24":{"27":[{"m":"Is it not possible that the Jews had paid Felix money 💵, which Paul refused to pay, thus he did them the favour of leaving Paul bound before leaving office?","dt":"2023-08-05T11:45:25","s":["sz3lnqytyj"]}]},"25":{"5":[{"m":"Here Festus sounds like he had a hint that Paul was a righteous man. The tone of his reply suggests so.","dt":"2022-12-13T06:24:39","s":["ayxpcwmo66"]}],"11":[{"m":"Wow, this new religious sect was going everywhere.\n\nBoth among the common people and poor, and the elite royal 👑.\n\nGod had told him he would testify also in Rome, and what finer opportunity than now?\n\nHe, Paul, would stand before the great Caesar to testify of the Christ among the corridors of power.\n\nPAUL was very strategic with his impact.","dt":"2022-12-13T06:28:34","s":["pl2itcy277"]},{"m":"The beauty of divine counsel and walking 🚶 by the wisdom of God.\n\nHis appeal to Caesar was actually in alignment with God's word. To man he might have seemed to appeal to Caesar, but he was on assignment.\n\nAnd that funded by the state. Kingdom work, state-funded.","dt":"2022-12-13T06:34:34","s":["mlr92fraw3"]}],"15":[{"m":"This meant they actually wanted him handed over to them and killed, as seen in the next verse.\n\nSo it was not just a matter of asking Festus to put him on trial; they wanted him killed.","dt":"2022-12-13T06:42:26","s":["4ayjmcwc2v"]}],"16":[{"m":"Ah, so this was what happened to Jesus. Yet he was silent 😶 and 🤫 said nothing.\n\nThis rule was broken in the case of Stephen, who was stoned to death, and Paul stood, giving his approval and ready to answer any matters that arose as a result of this action.\n\nIn the case of Jesus, he was too popular to be stoned; the Pharisees would have gotten into trouble had they attempted anything against Jesus.\n\nThat is why they came for him in the night, in secret.\n\nAnd they could not kill him without breaking the law, hence their appeal to Pilate.","dt":"2022-12-13T06:49:02","s":["darnyuejdt"]}],"19":[{"m":"Those in power are sometimes so clueless as they sit on their high horses.\n\nThat is why leaders must surround themselves with people who would tell them the truth and help them keep touch with base.\n\nHere Festus talks of Jesus as superstition. He actually says 'one Jesus'.\n\nHe had no idea of such common knowledge. 'Are you the only stranger in Jerusalem?', which was asked on the road to Emmaus, shows how commonplace Jesus' name was.\n\nEven in his preachings to Cornelius after the Holy Ghost baptism, Peter starts off by telling the people that this story about Jesus, they know...\n\nActs 10:36-37 KJV\nThe word which God sent unto the children of Israel, preaching peace by Jesus Christ: (he is Lord of all:)\n[37] That word, I say, ye know, which was published throughout all Judaea, and began from Galilee, after the baptism which John preached;\n\nThe people knew, whiles their rulers were so absent-minded.","dt":"2022-12-13T06:59:37","s":["bhdq17abwa"]}],"23":[{"m":"Christianity was going everywhere — and before all social groups.","dt":"2023-08-05T12:01:38","s":["pxtbbdrf3c"]}],"26":[{"m":"Paul's appeal to Caesar was so strategic. Now the great Caesar himself will hear the gospel, though likely will not believe.\n\nBut the testimony will be borne before kings and royals, as prophesied.","dt":"2023-08-05T12:19:20","s":["9vo5osqluz"]}],"24":[{"m":"Have dealt with me... Through much pressure from multitudes and possible 🙆 threat of further chaos and reporting to Caesar possibly.\n\nThese mad zealots.","dt":"2022-12-13T07:33:11","s":["5ektvhokkm"]}]},"26":{"11":[{"m":"I never took notice of this. I had seen it in movies and read accounts in church history of men and women being compelled to denounce and blaspheme the name of Christ.\n\nBut Paul also did same against the people of the Way in his early days.","dt":"2025-05-17T08:30:25","s":["istqzb37vo"]}],"12":[{"m":"These kings were listening to his story and testimony as royals and politicians.\n\nElite men who knew how scheming and untruthful man was.\n\nSo their instincts were alert, so as not to be lured or manipulated, as is often the case among the common people.\n\nAnd such posture was rightly so, considering the deception of man. How can we win such people over? Easily: the power of God by his Spirit would bring them to the point of true repentance.\n\nThe gospel is the power of God for a people, not just the poor sinner but the king 👑.\n\nIndeed, after all, our Lord himself is King 👑 also, actually King of kings, and knows how to deal with royalty 👑","dt":"2022-12-13T07:38:43","s":["hrey14l0mc"]}],"17":[{"m":"I don't think this part of the instructions of Jesus to Paul was in the early book of Acts account.","dt":"2025-05-17T08:40:17","s":["uk8u8v2tqy"]}],"24":[{"m":"Indeed, with the right posture of asking questions 🙋 and judging what a person says intelligently 🧠 without being swayed emotionally,\n\nKing 👑 Agrippa, seeing the passion and obvious conviction with which Paul spoke, concluded that too much learning was driving 🚘 him mad.\n\nHe himself would have been convinced, except that he knew it was just fairy tales to believe in resurrection of dead men, and something for the masses to grapple on to.\n\nThe appeal to our base senses to believe in some Messiah. Religion was the opium of the masses, and he, King Agrippa, would obviously not be lured into such.","dt":"2022-12-13T07:46:14","s":["1kgrzfkyfz"]}],"30":[{"m":"Well done, brother Paul; he had borne good witness of Christ, and these nobles had heard the gospel.\n\nMaybe later on they would get a second prompting from a different person, and soon enough their hearts might be ready to receive the Christ.","dt":"2022-12-13T07:48:59","s":["nknpytq6ky"]}],"32":[{"m":"This was no mistake; Paul was aligning to the instructions of God. And having testified before these two kings, he was going to testify before the great Caesar himself.","dt":"2025-05-17T08:43:53","s":["lzk2pqjccq"]}]},"27":{"1":[{"m":"Paul was innocent, a free man, and would have been set free, yet he chose to be among prisoners and suffer the fate of such for the gospel's sake.\n\nHe could have been home with his family but chose to be among people, and as we know, where people are — there, there is opportunity for harvest of souls.","dt":"2025-05-17T08:48:49","s":["so3ej0d8a9"]}],"31":[{"m":"The word of the Lord had come assuring the safety of all, yet they continued to take all practical steps to ensure their personal safety and that of the ship.\n\nPractical works do not nullify nor imply lack of faith.\n\nPaul could have gone like, well, God would do what he wants to do; since he had promised us we would be safe, we can sit and do nothing.\n\nIf the sailors had escaped, who was going to steer the ship to safety?\n\nPractical spirituality at work here.","dt":"2023-08-08T06:41:28","s":["1cs7sdm4lo"]}],"35":[{"m":"That was church right there. Paul was very much aware of his calling and mission, and took advantage of every opportunity to make Christ known.","dt":"2025-05-17T08:56:12","s":["sdherkhpzt"]}],"24":[{"m":"Wow, because Paul was aligned, all of the people around him were protected.","dt":"2023-08-08T06:37:54","s":["wklv9byzob"]}]},"28":{"14":[{"m":"Who brought the gospel to these brethren...? Ah, far and wide the gospel prospered.","dt":"2022-12-13T18:05:37","s":["bh6p0x8vwx"]}],"16":[{"m":"So was it after this visit that he later wrote to the Romans? I guess so.","dt":"2022-12-13T18:06:32","s":["vtxj5zc55x"]}],"19":[{"m":"Very similar story to what happened to Jesus, and the testimony Peter gave about him when the Pharisees arrested him.","dt":"2022-12-13T18:07:34","s":["il8flghgyv"]}],"23":[{"m":"In the early days of the church, the synagogue was a great place to start ministry.\n\nEverywhere one went in the Roman Empire and the world there were synagogues, which provided a fine avenue to start ministry and grow from there to the Gentiles.\n\nMost of whom had heard of the God of Israel one way or the other.\n\nPaul, being a Jew, took advantage of this to witness Christ in all places he went.\n\nThe synagogues were the right place to exalt Christ. He did not see this ministry opportunity as a way to exalt himself but to exalt Christ.\n\nToday in the churches, we have become so entitled that men think the churches are theirs and that of their families.\n\nTo the extent of fighting the truth to keep their places of power. Same thing the Pharisees did.\n\nBut like then, the same opportunity is presented to us to do ministry in the churches. For there many gather in the name of Christ, though sadly Christ is not exalted in most churches,\n\nRather men and the flesh is what is exalted. Yet in the midst of the anomaly lies the opportunity for true ministry and to exalt Christ again.\n\nSo we as true Christians must position ourselves and be apt to share the truth of Christ, particularly in and among our church friends.\n\nWe should be ready to seize the moment and opportunities to do genuine ministry.\n\nAs pastors and lay workers, genuine ministry should be the goal.\n\nThere is more to be done by way of evangelism, and that must be started in the church.","dt":"2025-05-17T09:08:54","s":["oi47v5nekf"]}],"28":[{"m":"Funny enough, the Gentiles who had no ties with the Jews and had never even heard Jesus believed.\n\nJust as we in Africa 🌍 do believe now.","dt":"2022-12-14T07:42:45","s":["109mxgm8zo"]}],"10":[{"m":"Souls were won everywhere, to God's glory...\n\nAnd one would dare say that out of the storms came something good.","dt":"2023-08-09T13:27:15","s":["9i5bmd807t"]}],"22":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔. Christianity was a sect... Today it is the biggest religion and we continue to expand...\n\nHumble beginnings.","dt":"2022-12-13T18:08:40","s":["0ijvjy7da9"]}],"27":[{"m":"For Paul to say these words meant he knew he had provided proof beyond all reasonable doubt 🤷‍♂️ of Jesus, but they would not hear.","dt":"2022-12-14T07:41:23","s":["q8br9e6ajm"]}]}},"Colossians":{"1":{"13":[{"m":"Translated us... This reminds me of translation in mathematics.","dt":"2023-10-09T09:54:29","s":["g6p8tac1s6"]}],"16":[{"m":"How did Paul know this? For nowhere in the Old Testament, or even in the words of Jesus, are these things directly said, though it alludes to them.\n\nBear in mind the apostles did not leave together, so though later John gave a similar truth, this knowledge did not come from preexisting data or literature.\n\nSo then Paul received these things directly from the Lord.","dt":"2025-05-17T15:59:11","s":["l5hjmzp0y9"]}],"20":[{"m":"Paul here seems to be alluding that by him, Christ Jesus, the reconciliation was not just of man to God, but all things on earth 🌎 and\n\nnow things in heaven.\n\nThis really opens up the scope of the work of Christ to include reconciliation of heavenly things.\nNow I wonder 🤔 what specific things in heaven did God reconcile?","dt":"2023-10-09T10:05:45","s":["xirhtkbaa3"]}],"23":[{"m":"If ye continue — now out the window goes the argument of once saved, forever saved.\n\nHe leaves a condition for inheriting the kingdom 👑","dt":"2023-10-09T09:58:04","s":["kgdvx9ef9m"]}]},"2":{"19":[{"m":"These are very strong 💪 words from Paul.\n\nThe simplicity of the gospel is so. Simply you can despise the freedom and liberty 🗽 of Christ and be caught up in winding disputes and rituals.\n\nSuch rituals of men feel more spiritual, but we have not so learned Christ.\n\nIn him we are complete; we need no more additions.\n\nOh Lord, help 😣 us stay in the simplicity of your word.","dt":"2023-10-10T14:08:20","s":["yw9x4a3auj"]}]},"3":{"5":[{"m":"Kill your members, Paul is saying, but how do you do that? By engaging the Spirit. And such conversations are what must be had in our days, especially as sin is taking a strong hold over the church.\n\nWe must have more of such conversations. They are so needed. How to kill the members of the flesh practically.","dt":"2025-05-17T16:26:36","s":["ncpzcqor4l"]}],"12":[{"m":"The elect of God, the saints of God.\n\nThe elite and high ones.\n\nWe have become the holy ones... Like the watchers and sons of God of old 🧓,\n\nwe have been given a high place in Christ Jesus.\n\nJust think 🤔 and meditate on these. Our high hope and calling in God.","dt":"2022-12-14T12:37:43","s":["m2j3g0ebct"]}],"25":[{"m":"Yet we think there is no accountability with God, and thus repent not, even when we are clearly at fault.\n\nWe continue in such until our conscience becomes seared.","dt":"2025-05-17T16:31:24","s":["urh25gbetm"]}]},"4":{"3":[{"m":"My prayer also. Lord, open unto us a door 🚪 of utterance wherever we go... For my wife and I 🙏","dt":"2023-10-10T14:12:46","s":["qnhgnmn7d1"]}]}},"Philemon":{"1":{"6":[{"m":"How do we make the gospel we have heard and the life of Christ real in our walk in this life?\n\nThere is a process or processes that move the gospel from the pages of the Bible to become real and manifest in power, healing, peace, joy etc.\n\nWhat are some of these processes of making it effectual?\n\n1. By knowledge","dt":"2022-12-14T12:47:28","s":["8j5h73mh6p"]}],"18":[{"m":"For Paul to vouch so much for Onesimus as to have his wrongs charged to his account, then Paul was really saying the former servant and sinner was truly repented and transformed by the power of Christ in him.\n\nWow, that's quite some bold moves from Paul, to vouch for a runaway slave.\n\nWe are not told how long Onesimus was with Paul, but long enough for Paul to speak so highly of him. Hmm. It is well.","dt":"2023-11-01T07:39:38","s":["1oihfn776u"]}],"19":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 Paul... Bullying Philemon a little 😇","dt":"2022-12-14T12:49:28","s":["ucu5m9resi"]}],"16":[{"m":"The early church ⛪ truly and indeed preached LOVE and lived it.\n\nSee how a stubborn runaway slave was now repented and converted.\n\nAnd could now be treated by his believing master as a brother. And you can see the affection in the letter from Paul to Philemon.\n\nThey were really full of love for each other.\n\nToday such love seems rare; everyone is on guard and on edge, because you do not know who to trust or who may feign love to take advantage of you.\n\nSo now we have all adapted; we show love, but with wisdom and caution, even in the church, lest you be taken advantage of.\n\nLord have mercy and restore true and genuine love of God and of the Holy Ghost.","dt":"2023-11-01T07:30:16","s":["6snjlyl7in"]}]}},"Ephesians":{"5":{"3":[{"m":"Hmm... This command... We are to be that perfect when it comes to the issue of sexual immorality.","dt":"2022-12-16T01:37:34","s":["jxrbm65l8x"]}],"30":[{"m":"What is the meaning of this? Is it literal, and if it is, in what sense? Explain.","dt":"2023-10-04T11:58:23","s":["6ysv3opdlv"]},{"m":"We are members of his body — the church ⛪, of his flesh — his literal body, flesh through partaking in the communion and his exchange 💱 on the cross ➕, and of his bones...\n\nBones literally through his exchange in the cross and communion...\n\nNot blood, because all of it was shed. For the remission of our sins, and presented to the Father for us 🙏","dt":"2023-10-04T12:22:29","s":["av0z3nhhal"]}],"32":[{"m":"It indeed is a great mystery, because husband and wife don't walk attached to each other like Siamese.\n\nSo how this oneness of flesh, not of spirit but of flesh, is achieved is a mystery.\n\nNow the fact that our relationship and literally oneness with Christ is exemplified by marriage could mean that if we are able to decipher how the marriage oneness works, then we can apply that to decipher how our oneness with Christ is achieved.","dt":"2023-10-04T12:35:54","s":["lnulbp4lz2"]}]},"6":{"17":[{"m":"Take the helmet of salvation, the helmet that says we are free men, and so we will not be bound again, nor lied 🤥 to that we are bound or are not completely free.","dt":"2024-12-19T02:48:44","s":["g37u84x0d3"]}],"24":[{"m":"An interesting ending... Grace to those who genuinely love the Lord Jesus. Wow","dt":"2022-12-17T11:52:52","s":["1orlp7h361"]}]},"3":{"21":[{"m":"Ephesians 1:17-23 KJV\nthat the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give unto you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him: the eyes of your understanding being enlightened; that ye may know what is the hope of his calling, and what the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints, and what is the exceeding greatness of his power to us-ward who believe, according to the working of his mighty power, which he wrought in Christ, when he raised him from the dead, and set him at his own right hand in the heavenly places, far above all principality, and power, and might, and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this world, but also in that which is to come: and hath put all things under his feet, and gave him to be the head over all things to the church, which is his body, the fulness of him that filleth all in all.\n\nEphesians 3:10 KJV\nto the intent that now unto the principalities and powers in heavenly places might be known by the church the manifold wisdom of God,\n\nEphesians 3:14-21 KJV\nFor this cause I bow my knees unto the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, of whom the whole family in heaven and earth is named, that he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, to be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man; that Christ may dwell in your hearts by faith; that ye, being rooted and grounded in love, may be able to comprehend with all saints what is the breadth, and length, and depth, and height; and to know the love of Christ, which passeth knowledge, that ye might be filled with all the fulness of God. Now unto him that is able to do exceeding abundantly above all that we ask or think, according to the power that worketh in us, unto him be glory in the church by Christ Jesus throughout all ages, world without end. Amen.","dt":"2023-10-01T07:20:35","s":["6q66sqx06p"]}]}},"Philippians":{"1":{"9":[{"m":"His prayer was that this love the Philippian church had for God and his Son Jesus Christ may abound more in knowledge.\n\nHe did not want them to be ignorant zealots, but full of spiritual wisdom and knowledge.","dt":"2022-12-17T12:24:23","s":["5njmxpnujt"]}],"16":[{"m":"Oh, such envy... Envy indeed is very evil, as the book of Proverbs suggests, i.e. who can stand before envy?\n\nI say this because Paul was in such affliction because of the gospel, and to think that another believer would seek to add more affliction to his already unbearable situation is sad and difficult to decipher.\n\nBut that is the nature of men, of men who are born again and profess Christ.","dt":"2025-05-20T09:24:43","s":["xmgjiheyie"]}],"17":[{"m":"So there was some politics and contentions going on in the preaching of the gospel.\n\nNothing new under the sun ☀; the same is true in our churches today.","dt":"2022-12-17T13:45:09","s":["q68f2a3w06"]}],"19":[{"m":"Such a strange thing to rejoice in. In his bonds and people doing him in, he rejoices.\n\nBut we understand why his strange joying, seeing the reason he gives, that is... knowing very well that it will work out for the furtherance of the gospel, and not just that, but\n\nit will work out for his own salvation as the saints pray 🙏.","dt":"2023-10-05T12:08:29","s":["xv6095ykyh"]}],"23":[{"m":"Strange talk, whiles most men fear 😱 death ☠,\n\nPaul is contemplating death so he meets Christ.\n\nIndeed his life was full and complete, less how else could he have desired death ☠?\n\nThere are two ✌️ things, indeed two opposites, that cause a man to desire ☠ death.\n\n1. Complete hopelessness in life & 2. Complete fullness and fulfillment in this life.\n\nOh, what a life Paul had. Lord help me have a full life, a hope full life. Amen","dt":"2023-10-05T12:13:46","s":["cff3rco2xg"]}]},"3":{"3":[{"m":"The concision — referring to those advocating for circumcision before one is accepted in Christ.\n\nThese Paul condemned and said to be wary of them.\n\nFor they take away their liberties in Christ.","dt":"2022-12-17T17:17:10","s":["gz6vluvjfx"]}],"20":[{"m":"Other versions say our citizenship is in heaven... Wow... Glory","dt":"2022-12-17T17:21:03","s":["uqv8b32zex"]}],"21":[{"m":"Oh, indeed these our bodies are vile indeed... Full of lusts, envy and the fleshly things...\n\nSo much work constantly must be put to keep it subdued.\n\nIt is indeed a vile thing.","dt":"2022-12-17T17:25:25","s":["jvtzh6vo4s"]}]},"4":{"10":[{"m":"The language of the New Testament, especially the old King James language, you would think the phrase\n\n\"ye were careful\" means they were not willing to, but it rather meant they were...\n\nIt's like when you say... Do you care for a drink?... If you want the drink, your response should be no, and if you don't want the drink 🍻, you say yes.","dt":"2022-12-17T17:48:37","s":["rxkb9ondpe"]}],"12":[{"m":"I am instructed??? 😳 So this was not just a mindset or good thing he just wanted to do.\n\nIt was a directive he was given... God required it of him.","dt":"2023-10-06T17:43:26","s":["7yirynebva"]}]}},"1 Timothy":{"1":{"4":[{"m":"What is the doctrine of endless genealogy that is being spoken about here?","dt":"2023-10-22T05:40:45","s":["paikgsr2l8"]}],"5":[{"m":"Same as the sum of all the law and commandment is love.","dt":"2022-12-18T12:30:52","s":["n1w84jjdjq"]}],"20":[{"m":"Hmm\n\nWhat is the meaning of this verse... Because this is not the first time a believer has been delivered to Satan for punishment in the flesh.\n\nIt happened in the church of Corinthians by the instruction of Paul.\n\nDoes it involve removing spiritual cover so that the person is tortured in the flesh to some extent till true repentance is born?","dt":"2022-12-19T06:16:26","s":["uebbregj4c"]}]},"2":{"10":[{"m":"Is Paul saying women should not wear broided hair and jewelry? YES he is.\n\nBut he said that within a context, and the context is that of \"women professing godliness\".\n\nSo for women professing godliness and sobriety, loud adornment communicated otherwise.\n\nIn essence this was purely a cultural thing, and to put up the right posture not just at heart but in appearance.\n\nCulture has changed and these are not needed, as wearing adornment is now the norm.\n\nWe cannot say that not wearing gold and other jewelry 💍 is Christian doctrine.\n\nStudying the rest of scripture, we see no such doctrine, and this cannot form the basic tenets of the Christian faith.\n\nAlso there were many nobles and royals 👑 who came to the faith.\n\nWere they to suddenly take off their gold and beautiful adornment? No, and that did not hinder their profession of faith, because for their social status anyone they witnessed to would not accuse or judge them as not being sober or godly.\n\nChristianity indeed must be approached logically and not with a set of hard rules, lest we gradually sink into error.","dt":"2023-10-23T07:54:07","s":["sl56sogjv9"]}],"11":[{"m":"Another context to this verse.\n\nIt does not say let the women be silent 🤫.\n\nIt says let them learn, meaning there is something to teach which they do not know.\n\nEver had to teach someone who does not know, and yet postures as if they do and would not learn in silence 🤫?\n\nThis is what is being referred to here.\n\nAnd we know Paul is not introducing a doctrine of masking 😷 women not to talk,\n\nbecause we see he's worked with several women in ministry, and we see other confirmatory scriptures of women prophets who are the mouth 👄 piece of God.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:16:43","s":["t7a4sne8q4"]}],"12":[{"m":"What is the meaning of the word to be in silence 🤫?\n\nObviously it does not mean to not talk. But to be measured in speech and not to over talk or talk over the man,\n\nas is demonstrated by the next instruction of not usurping authority over the man 👨.\n\nIt was expected that godly women be not found to be loud and domineering over their man.\n\nIndeed in society in general such behaviour of women is frowned 🙁 upon, and much more on the believers, who were held to a much higher standard.\n\nJust imagine seeing a woman calling her husband and saying, come let me teach you a few things about so and so.\n\nThe utter shock 🤯 and disgust 🤢 of those watching in that society and culture.\n\nFrom the way Paul talks, you can see he is looking at it from a societal, cultural and public view of such an occurrence.\n\nIndeed even now in our 21st century, imagine a worker 👷 calling out to his manager or supervisor in full 🌕 view of others, trying to talk over or teach his leader.\n\nSee, we know leaders everywhere don't know it all, and their team always helps them.\n\nBut even then you know there is an appropriate way to teach and correct your leader.\n\nNow the man/husband is the head of the home — the team leader —\n\nhow and what do you think is the appropriate manner for a wife to talk to, correct, and particularly when it comes to having to teach him, to do so?\n\nHow do you think 🤔 it ought to be done in the home 🏡 privately? How about before the kids?\n\nHow, what about when neighbours are around?\n\nYou see, the point I believe Paul was making is still apt and appropriate in our times and age, and even much more in their cultural setting, where proper behaviour was stricter and expected.\n\nFor those of us in Africa, and I believe non-western nations, we understand this better.\n\nA lot of the confusion in marriages, the arguments and fights, is as a result of these things.","dt":"2022-12-19T06:58:25","s":["8i9ryvt7va"]},{"m":"I do not permit a woman to teach or exercise authority over the man; nature even teaches us so, as we see in the case of man being created first before woman.\n\nGenerally men are more assertive than women, and this natural tendency has been accepted and ingrained in culture.\n\nI can imagine in the times of Paul, under such a culture, for women in the church to be seen towering tall over men and teaching them whiles the men sit in silence 🤫.\n\nThat whole scenery is a shock 🤯 to the cultural sense of the time ⌚.\n\nFor the church not to be seen in that light, and also for ensuring what is proper, since the church is part of society and culture, and this culture of men leading lines up with scripture, it was only wise to set things in order in that manner.\n\nThe church is cultural.\n\nHowever, after many centuries, gradually that mindset is being wiped out of culture to a large extent, though the nature of things still stands.\n\nThe church therefore needs to be wise in and change with the times, but also we need to be cautious and not go against or deny natural order, by putting in support systems to help women teachers and leaders.\n\nIt is a slippery ground, but we can navigate that path if we tread cautiously.","dt":"2023-10-23T09:21:17","s":["s82iadfjby"]}],"13":[{"m":"An order is being set here of headship and leadership.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:21:04","s":["13gbkzfd2i"]}],"14":[{"m":"Was this not illustrating the general susceptibility of women to being deceived and lured or distracted generally, because of their emotional nature?\n\nI believe Paul, in foreseeing all these limits, gave this instruction.\n\nOf course it does not make the woman inferior, no, because women have strengths that men do not have.\n\nWomen, because of their emotions, are more intuitive.\n\nThis verse indicates men and women are just different, and the greater should each stay in their strength 💪 area.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:25:58","s":["mc939lp5zv"]},{"m":"So brother Paul, what has Adam not being deceived and being formed first got to do with anything?\n\nHe seems to be saying the man is head and should lead in church ⛪; he also seems to be suggesting the vulnerability of women and it seeping out into their leadership if they are left to do as they feel.\n\nSo Paul is saying to let the men lead. And I think 🤔 we all know in a practical sense that women are more emotionally driven and sometimes erratic.\n\nSo I see Paul saying to not let this happen, let the women learn in silence 🤫 (which is not typical of women 😉), also let the men lead, because in the natural order man was created first, and women rather than men are more susceptible to influences.\n\nHaving said this, does this therefore not imply that\n\n1. If there are women teachers, well learned and behaved, they cannot be kept silent 🤫 but must be allowed to teach, as in other examples we see in scripture.\n\n2. If a woman is a natural leader or can learn to lead, she should be allowed, or if structures can be put in place that counter the natural inhibitions against women, so their gifts and talents are brought to bear, it is wisest to do so.\n\n3. Eve was cursed to endure much pain in pregnancy, but today due to modern medicine 😷 women can literally have pain-free birth. Should we then say that since pain in childbirth is a natural process, women should be left to suffer though there is a way out...\n\nOf course we know the advantages of natural birth, but there is no need imposing that on a woman 👩 when there are alternatives, especially where there is risk.\n\nSo also in the positive, we should help women shine as much as men in the church without hindering the work of ministry.","dt":"2023-10-23T08:11:46","s":["8c8qba7n75"]},{"m":"When Paul gives a command, even if it is not doctrine, here he ensures there is scriptural backing, i.e. that it lines up with the scriptures.","dt":"2023-10-23T09:45:00","s":["4w15wqxhjw"]}],"15":[{"m":"These entire verses require study, much study and clarification.","dt":"2022-12-19T06:45:15","s":["t3pf6oi20g"]},{"m":"This points to a supernatural benefit to women for living in godliness and meekness.\n\nThat in childbirth she shall be preserved... Her life and that of her young one shall be saved from harm and the dangers of childbirth.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:30:23","s":["rto72lvbpt"]}],"2":[{"m":"It's an interesting mindset that Paul had.\n\nChristianity was under persecution all over, and instead of probably praying for the death or destruction of these authorities, he asked for them to be prayed for, for peace.\n\nWhich is what every leader wants in their realm.\n\nBut not just for the peace of the leaders, but for the peace of believers.\n\nThis was more like pray that we may have peace, rather than tag these rulers as evil 😈 and when they go rogue on us we pray for our deliverance.\n\nSmart approach 👍","dt":"2023-10-23T07:40:01","s":["6d9heza202"]}]},"3":{"5":[{"m":"And his own house, and by extension his body, which is God's house 🏡.\n\nSo the requirements for housekeeping are stated in the verse before.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:38:14","s":["qw2zxb62gv"]}],"10":[{"m":"Deacons must be worthy of respect; the ability to teach was not required, but the ability to hold true the tenets of the faith was required.\n\nThe bishops were to be teachers and the deacons offer support.","dt":"2023-10-23T09:41:33","s":["wehw77myct"]}],"15":[{"m":"Ah, yes indeed, the church ⛪ is the ground and pillar of the truth.","dt":"2023-10-23T09:42:31","s":["laavd98klw"]}],"16":[{"m":"Paul always has a way of linking 🔗 instructions to some bigger spiritual truth.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:40:12","s":["h165bud14w"]},{"m":"Seen of angels? 😇. You know, we presume angels see God all the time, but here we see otherwise.\n\nYes, angels are in God's presence, but he lives in an unapproachable light.\n\nWhen Christ was manifested, now the angels saw God's form in the flesh.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:42:24","s":["h0qj1ecn3i"]},{"m":"A great mystery indeed.","dt":"2023-10-23T09:46:21","s":["vrl8ioozgm"]}]},"4":{"4":[{"m":"This issue of food seems prevalent in the churches. Somehow the believers were becoming spooky over food sold in the market places, and couldn't just eat freely, but had to try and decipher the sources of the food and whether it be dedicated to devils 👿.\n\nBut Paul makes a remarkable statement, that just eat what is in the market places without asking questions. Just receive it with thanksgiving.\n\nThe people pushing this doctrine of certain foods as evil, you would think, are hyper spiritual, but rather, ironically, were controlled by lusts and deceiving spirits.","dt":"2023-10-25T07:51:52","s":["r0dik51l3x"]}],"7":[{"m":"So the problem of stories, personal experiences and cultural superstitions\n\nbeing mingled with the gospel to the detriment of the church ⛪ did not start from now.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:44:41","s":["6s5uzuiaaq"]}],"5":[{"m":"Simplicita... Amen","dt":"2022-12-19T07:43:13","s":["oqiabsiv27"]}]},"5":{"2":[{"m":"When it came to the sisters, all purity had to be added to the conditions.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:46:34","s":["rqq0s2r4ca"]}],"5":[{"m":"The church is not perfect 👌 and has never been, not even in the times of the Apostles.\n\nHere we see some widows just taking advantage of the church system, meanwhile they had help elsewhere.","dt":"2023-10-25T07:54:28","s":["cttac2zs6m"]}],"10":[{"m":"So in helping widows, they ought to have contributed to the gospel work one way or another...\n\nSo doing same in our churches today is in order.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:48:08","s":["2hykp2yhxz"]}],"13":[{"m":"Ei hehehe... The gossip and busybodiness is everywhere.","dt":"2023-10-25T07:58:34","s":["rx2o5v0lxj"]}],"15":[{"m":"Ei really, like they were now serving Satan actively... Not just lured to sin, but now have given themselves over for Satan to use. LORD have mercy.","dt":"2023-10-25T07:59:52","s":["wqur0o8kix"]}],"17":[{"m":"Amen... The labourer is worthy of his wages.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:49:14","s":["par3prl7zg"]}],"23":[{"m":"This instruction was purely for medicinal purposes and nothing else...\n\nIt is no excuse for Christians to get drunk.","dt":"2022-12-19T08:10:45","s":["22d2s15tf9"]}],"25":[{"m":"In essence, they that do evil and are not found out in this life would be in the afterlife.\n\nThe same with them that do good.\n\nAt the end of the day, we will all be brought to the light.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:51:56","s":["rvcict5k42"]}],"20":[{"m":"Public rebuke of sin is also sound doctrine, but of course should be done in wisdom and love.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:50:12","s":["mlbkxefpqn"]}],"22":[{"m":"Purity is expected of the men of God.\n\nSo I pray, oh Lord, why do men of God fall and often completely drift from the faith by the time they've been in ministry some years?","dt":"2022-12-19T07:52:59","s":["rqvf5v12ay"]}]},"6":{"1":[{"m":"Not so in our days; believers cheat and destroy the work of their masters...\n\nThey practice not the faith.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:54:43","s":["sefo1g941l"]}],"5":[{"m":"We see that drifting away from sound doctrine comes with it many errors.\n\nSee, those greedy for gain have accompanying flaws and errors.\n\nWe must seek to stay in sound doctrine, else we risk falling into much error.","dt":"2023-10-25T08:43:57","s":["87sl9d0vp0"]}],"10":[{"m":"True, and I know that personally.","dt":"2022-12-19T07:56:59","s":["feotgl8e8h"]},{"m":"The love of money is the root of all evil 😈. Many have tried justifying and explaining this scripture by saying the love of money, not money itself, is the root of all evil 😈.\n\nBut then we all need money, so how do we pursue the need for money without falling into this error?\n\nThe answer is in the subsequent statement. It says some so pursued and loved money that they erred from the faith.\n\nThat was how the love of money had entered their hearts and taken the place of even their faith. At that point you should know that you are no longer just trying to make a living,\n\nmoney has taken hold of you. It's a slippery ground, so as believers we ought to be careful.\n\nNo believer starts out to be controlled by mammon, but rather to have enough and some more, with maybe the intention of supporting the church ⛪.\n\nBut soon enough a little more becomes just too much.\n\nThis road is so slippery, we have seen men of God taken over and possessed by it. It really is a slippery slope.\n\nSo Paul admonishes, having food and raiment we are content. For those with families, I would add, and shelter we are content.\n\nLord help 😣 Lord have mercy","dt":"2023-10-25T08:53:48","s":["gzuv1em9sj"]}],"6":[{"m":"Amen 🙏","dt":"2022-12-19T07:55:33","s":["b914269500"]}],"21":[{"m":"Amen 🙏","dt":"2022-12-19T07:58:50","s":["558a558a21"]}]}},"Titus":{"1":{"13":[{"m":"Hehehe... The Cretans by this description were quite a handful.\n\nBringing their cultural failures into the faith.\n\nThese Paul says should be rebuked accordingly.","dt":"2022-12-19T08:03:19","s":["xc5np8co4i"]}],"14":[{"m":"We have to stay with the truth always and be wary of the commandments of men.","dt":"2022-12-19T08:06:29","s":["nsdrfqysz7"]}],"15":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔.\n\nThis sounds like what is often the case with us.\n\nThe way we are is the way we tend to see things and others.\n\nMost good people seem to think 🤔 others are also good and walk 🚶 on in naivety, whiles the wicked would think no good of others.\n\nAlways walking in deception 😞","dt":"2022-12-19T08:05:24","s":["7mq5kqx5tc"]}],"16":[{"m":"Hmm... They say one thing but do others.","dt":"2022-12-19T08:05:48","s":["v89ndkbwj"]}]},"2":{"13":[{"m":"Jesus is our great God and saviour...\n\nHe is described as God here.","dt":"2022-12-19T08:09:07","s":["y91jf7u3jj"]}],"15":[{"m":"The church hasn't changed much in terms of the moral problems of ministry.\n\nSame greed, sexual perversion 🙄, doctrinal error etc.","dt":"2023-10-31T09:16:40","s":["axvwqosrw2"]},{"m":"Let no man despise thee. Same thing he said to Timothy...\n\nThat means it's easy to be despised when you are young in the ministry.","dt":"2023-10-31T09:17:48","s":["j5ndsgjof1"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"Human leaders and judges.\n\nSame word is used of spiritual as well.\n\nMeaning there are judges, magistrates, principalities and powers.","dt":"2022-12-19T08:12:11","s":["urrjsftp81"]},{"m":"So as it is in the natural, so it is in the spirit.\n\nPrincipalities, powers and magistrates... Intelligent 🧠 beings who sit at table to set in order what should take place among men.\n\nMeaning they have agents whom they reward if they will carry out their will.\n\nWillingly obedient humans to spirits, who in turn empower them and prosper them.\n\nSuch men come out with results and technology ahead of their time, giving them literally deity-like presence and results.\n\nAnd so our Father in heaven rewards even with blessings, not just in this world but for all eternity... Oh, God indeed is love ♥... Blessings perpetually, whiles these deceptive spirits hide truth and take men to hell.","dt":"2023-10-31T09:26:07","s":["9ypg75innc"]}],"7":[{"m":"These writings of Paul concerning the finished works of Christ and the blessings of this new life were written from encounters and daily walk 🚶 with the Lord.\n\nIt was from experience translated into writings and instructions called doctrine.\n\nBear in mind there were no New Testament writings in the times of Paul, so these are fresh insights from the knowledge of God and his ways.\n\nSo doctrine must be experienced; it is not mere words to be memorized... It's the dictates of the spirit life that must be lived.\n\nAnd that is the error of our days: we have doctrine as head knowledge, whiles others walked in doctrine.","dt":"2023-10-31T09:51:48","s":["9bwcd6txg7"]}]}},"1 Peter":{"1":{"18":[{"m":"You were not redeemed with corruptible things as gold and silver; you did not receive this redemption through the traditions of your fathers.","dt":"2022-12-19T15:09:24","s":["4zb1l9e2vc"]}],"23":[{"m":"Being born not of corruptible sperm but of the incorruptible sperm of the word of God, which is Christ Jesus.","dt":"2022-12-19T15:11:51","s":["85028di036"]}]},"3":{"7":[{"m":"There seems to be a revelation here. That a man's prayers are hindered if he refuses to dwell in wisdom with his wife and honour her as the weaker vessel.","dt":"2022-12-19T15:17:34","s":["mx2kdil9ov"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh Lord, grant, I pray, my tongue refrain from evil 😈 and my lips 💋 that they speak no guile. 🙏","dt":"2023-11-28T16:14:06","s":["o9xpv4rbj1"]}],"19":[{"m":"When was this?","dt":"2022-12-19T15:25:08","s":["g0p9yqczwi"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"PAUL said similar words.","dt":"2022-12-19T15:25:41","s":["31cnp1j1mr"]}],"3":[{"m":"The will of the Gentiles, and he goes ahead to describe sinful actions...\n\nMeaning the Jews were a separate and holy people. Indeed, the commands of God even in the OT were for them to be this holy people.\n\nRighteousness and holiness to the Lord was what the Lord envisioned for national Israel 🇮🇱, though it did not manifest.","dt":"2022-12-19T18:10:36","s":["kjulpqdfs4"]}],"6":[{"m":"I don't understand: to what end is the preaching of the true gospel to the dead?\n\nI believe this is making reference to the dead righteous ones who died before the gospel work of Christ began.","dt":"2023-11-29T13:56:32","s":["h2n9vysgr5"]}],"18":[{"m":"A very grave situation indeed.","dt":"2023-11-29T14:01:54","s":["tnxulfl0v4"]}]},"5":{"9":[{"m":"It seems it was common knowledge and commonly accepted among the early church ⛪ that suffering for Christ was part of the call 🤙.","dt":"2023-11-29T14:03:52","s":["i06q99bnfk"]}],"10":[{"m":"Persecution and suffering produce perfection and patience in us believers.","dt":"2023-11-29T14:04:48","s":["wggef3g9ei"]}],"1":[{"m":"Peter, the great Peter himself, calls himself an elder along with the other believers.\n\nHe did not see himself as some exalted special one.\n\nHe was an elder, as were the others, and he recognized their office as such.","dt":"2023-11-29T14:06:14","s":["ba27b61pqd"]}]}},"Hebrews":{"2":{"14":[{"m":"When did the devil 👿 get this power of death ☠ and how did he get it?","dt":"2022-12-20T16:28:02","s":["q3i5rrwufg"]}]},"4":{"10":[{"m":"He that has entered into His rest has ceased from his own works into the works of the LORD.\n\nHis life is not his own; his life is the LORD'S and the LORD'S his.\n\nHe has taken the yoke of the Lord, and the Lord's yoke is not burdensome.\n\nThis is actually what the Lord spoke to me about — that I should bear his yoke as he takes my heavy yoke from me by the power of the anointing.\n\nIsaiah 10:27 KJV\nAnd it shall come to pass in that day, that his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.\n\nAs I began to pray a few minutes ago, at about 1am — 15th November 2023 — the words of Isaiah came to mind. I was reminded by the Spirit of it, as that was the impression I had had the previous day in my prayers.\n\nNow as I took my phone, I somehow decided to read my Bible plan from the YouVersion Bible app, but using Olives Bible, since that has the Dake's commentary...\n\nMyself I was wondering why I was reading the Bible instead of praying.\n\nThen I started by reading the book of Hebrews talking about the rest of God, only for it to link 🔗 perfectly 👌 with the scripture in Isaiah about the anointing breaking the yoke, and how that we need to learn from the Lord as he takes our heavy yoke in exchange for our light one.\n\nMatthew 11:28-30 KJV\nCome unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. [29] Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls. [30] For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.\n\nThe Lord is indeed speaking to me through these verses.","dt":"2023-11-15T01:40:58","s":["mgij08ip8l","wugrpe18oy"]}],"8":[{"m":"Initially I presumed that the people born after the generation that wasted in the wilderness are the ones that entered into his rest.\n\nBut Paul's exposition is that even they did not. Because if indeed they did, we would not have David here in Psalm speaking of another day of rest,\n\nTo day if ye will hear his voice, Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, and as in the day of temptation in the wilderness: When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work. Forty years long was I grieved with this generation, and said, It is a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:\n\nAs to whether the people in David's day heeded his warning and entered in, it is not likely, as we see how the people and their kings rebelled constantly against the LORD.\n\nHebrews 4:8 NKJV\nFor if Joshua had given them rest, then He would not afterward have spoken of another day.","dt":"2023-11-15T01:29:22","s":["tvruo4avr7","54jsd5xlcb"]}]},"6":{"18":[{"m":"What are the two immutable things?\n\n1. God himself is immutable, so his saying anything is sure.\n\n2. An oath is immutable...\n\nSo God swearing an oath by himself = two immutable things\n\nHebrews 6:18 NKJV\nthat by two immutable things, in which it is impossible for God to lie, we might have strong consolation, who have fled for refuge to lay hold of the hope set before us.","dt":"2022-12-21T11:16:23","s":["gi4kho2qoe","dl72ggu9ip"]},{"m":"Most versions state the two unchangeable things to be\n\n1. His promise and\n\n2. His oath\n\nHebrews 6:18 NKJV\nthat by two immutable things, in which it is impossible for God to lie, we might have strong consolation, who have fled for refuge to lay hold of the hope set before us.","dt":"2022-12-21T11:19:09","s":["3en1fgqq4s","pxth7xpez9"]}]},"9":{"14":[{"m":"Yes indeed, how much more.","dt":"2022-12-21T11:32:46","s":["z95slaygbk"]}],"26":[{"m":"In the end of the world has this been offered.","dt":"2022-12-21T11:35:39","s":["3ugimcqxha"]}],"27":[{"m":"What is the meaning of this... That is, as it is appointed unto man to die, so Jesus also died for us once...\n\nOK, I get it now... We die once, not many times, for our sins, so Jesus also died once for all sins of mankind... 👌","dt":"2023-12-06T12:14:03","s":["lt9jq45jal"]}]},"10":{"14":[{"m":"This kind of contradicts Dake's commentary Bible assertion that sacrifices will be offered in the new earth 🌎 as a memorial.\n\nI'll recheck this, because if as a memorial, well, then it's okay, since it's not to wash sins but to serve as a memorial.\n\nThat commentary by Dake's was made not on this verse of scripture, but on another verse I do not quite remember, but it had to do with priesthood in the new earth 🌎 and temple.","dt":"2023-12-06T12:21:09","s":["qwy3721eg1"]}],"18":[{"m":"Since their sins are no more remembered and they are washed, there is no more offering for sin.","dt":"2022-12-21T11:52:45","s":["89vdspv3cn"]}],"22":[{"m":"He's picking allegory from the Old Testament rituals of sprinkling and washing and applying it to what Christ has done for US.","dt":"2023-12-06T12:24:05","s":["qizqba2u3q"]}],"34":[{"m":"I understand why this book is attributed to Paul.\n\nHe often talked of his bonds in his writings, and the general style of the writing so resembles Paul.","dt":"2023-12-06T12:38:23","s":["3vhyhgyvlf"]}],"27":[{"m":"Paul is clearly saying we are wiped clean and pure from all sins, past, present and future.\n\nAnd he has explained how this was achieved in Christ.\n\nNow having this knowledge that Christ's blood is so efficacious, we run the risk of deliberately sinning, and if we do, there is no more sacrifice for us.\n\nGod does not delight in sacrifice of fools. Lord have mercy...\n\nALL this is in scripture, yet we still go about saying we can sin willfully and just lay claim of Jesus' blood. Because we are under grace.","dt":"2023-12-06T12:28:23","s":["2vzdb90int","o9mtcrz2w5"]}],"12":[{"m":"Every priest standeth daily to offer sacrifices, but this Jesus Christ offered once the perfect 👌 sacrifice, and since stands no longer, but rather sat down and remains seated at the right hand of glory.\n\nAwaiting his enemies be made his footstool.","dt":"2023-12-06T12:18:00","s":["9dakhf0e1e"]}],"37":[{"m":"With all sobriety, it's been 2000 years?","dt":"2023-12-06T12:25:49","s":["7noipgb5fg"]}],"38":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-12-21T11:56:31","s":["9f93c1adeb"]}]},"11":{"6":[{"m":"Faith is not so complex when we look at the examples that Paul gave of people acting in faith.\n\nThey simply believed God and thus acted in accordance with their belief.","dt":"2022-12-21T11:59:03","s":["yv5w4n84hr"]}],"7":[{"m":"Noah was forewarned by God; he acted in obedience and earned his place in the annals of faith.","dt":"2022-12-21T12:02:06","s":["wqq5e5kpxz"]}],"11":[{"m":"If you have faith, you will act on what you believe.\n\nIf you do not act, then you do not really believe.\n\nI understand why Abraham is the father of faith.\n\nHe did not obtain what was promised him in his lifetime.\n\nThough God, who is faithful, supplied enough proof of what the future will be for his children, for Abraham to hold on in belief unto death ☠","dt":"2022-12-21T12:05:05","s":["vvrevb1s6s"]}],"22":[{"m":"Such faith in God.","dt":"2022-12-21T12:07:11","s":["xjewwv8qp5"]}],"35":[{"m":"Who were those? Who refused deliverance?","dt":"2025-05-23T11:17:54","s":["g5cj9w1hvm"]}],"39":[{"m":"Oh what a people... Who are these of whom the world is not worthy...\n\nThese, having obtained a good report through faith, received not the promise.\n\nOh what a people 🙏","dt":"2022-12-21T12:13:09","s":["9xmlgltxc9"]}]},"12":{"1":[{"m":"So the cloud 🌥 of witnesses often spoken about are not some random beings in the heavenlies.\n\nThey are the Old Testament saints, who while here on the earth 🌎 demonstrated faith, and now are in glory, having served their due. It is now our turn.","dt":"2023-12-08T06:26:47","s":["8s32mzxvey"]}],"3":[{"m":"If they did this to even the master... How much more worse treatment will they give to his disciples?","dt":"2022-12-21T12:17:50","s":["cg9mgw2wpd"]}],"14":[{"m":"Ah... Holiness","dt":"2022-12-21T12:19:08","s":["h5axo26xlo"]}]},"13":{"9":[{"m":"This verse and others point to why many believe Hebrews was written by Paul...\n\nHe peculiarly talked of meats not defiling us and of righteousness by faith alone.\n\nAnd in preceding verses he talks of his bonds... All this was peculiar to him in his writings.","dt":"2025-05-23T11:25:18","s":["rjqzenxm21"]}],"14":[{"m":"Glory!!! 😲","dt":"2022-12-21T12:22:31","s":["0es2o4czoi"]},{"m":"Very sobering statement and thought-provoking\n😢😭\nIt's akin to Peter talking of us being pilgrims in this life.","dt":"2025-05-23T11:27:53","s":["t2llrqsqdy"]}],"15":[{"m":"Not blood of animals, but the fruit 🥝 of our lips...\n\nIt looks simple and not powerful, but that is the believer's power and \"enchantment\" before God.\n\nNot some blood or oil or fleshly symbol, but faith in obedience.\n\nIt's faithlessness in the simple provisions that God has given in his word that makes us go for excess and symbols and tokens.","dt":"2022-12-21T12:27:22","s":["ut2xf8r6fr"]}],"18":[{"m":"This asking for prayers is also so peculiar to Paul.\n\nHis footprints 👣 are all over it.","dt":"2025-05-23T11:30:06","s":["hcr2vejxqy"]}],"23":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 this letter is more likely than not written by Paul.","dt":"2025-05-23T11:31:34","s":["awfaugsg8x"]}],"25":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-12-21T12:24:37","s":["84e58ebb40"]}]}},"2 Timothy":{"1":{"6":[{"m":"How was he to do this? How was he to stir it up...\n\nIf he was to remember to stir it up, then it means it's 💯 percent in his control.","dt":"2022-12-23T06:55:42","s":["wda0uca5nx"]},{"m":"We are told in Corinthians of the gifts of the Spirit, the administrations of Christ and operations of God.\n\n1 Corinthians 12:4-6 KJV\nNow there are diversities of gifts, but the same Spirit. [5] And there are differences of administrations, but the same Lord. [6] And there are diversities of operations, but it is the same God which worketh all in all.\n\nIf we extend that here, the gifts of God in that sense are the fivefold gifts, i.e.\n\n1 Corinthians 12:28 KJV\nAnd God hath set some in the church, first apostles, secondarily prophets, thirdly teachers, after that miracles, then gifts of healings, helps, governments, diversities of tongues.\n\nWill need to clarify this concept above... More to be added as revealed.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:11:45","s":["89gorw4in7"]}],"7":[{"m":"So fear can hinder us from going ahead to exercise the gift of God in us.\n\nWe may feel inadequate or ashamed to do the ministry work, but it is a gift; we must put it to use, to stir it up.","dt":"2022-12-23T06:57:05","s":["wz5at2hgwz"]}],"9":[{"m":"Before the world began... How did Paul know this plan was before the world began?\n\nJohn also testifies of the same thing, as Christ being the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:13:46","s":["w2n8l40rof"]}],"10":[{"m":"Immortality, oh that elixir of life that men have long craved for... Oh if only they knew it was here 😢","dt":"2022-12-23T07:16:32","s":["m2min46u8p"]},{"m":"Amen","dt":"2023-10-27T10:18:20","s":["8015e52682"]}],"8":[{"m":"Paul says he's Jesus's prisoner. So his being in prison, he sees it not as man having imprisoned him, but as God.\n\nIn a sense he was casting his cares and affliction on the Lord, knowing full well that it could not have happened to him if God did not permit it.\n\nThis was a good thing to do; rather than worry, he trusted in the Lord his master.","dt":"2023-10-27T10:16:05","s":["ykp3wcbr1a"]}]},"2":{"15":[{"m":"The man of God must learn.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:20:16","s":["x9f2n22yki"]}],"18":[{"m":"Is this not the same awful doctrine the Thessalonians were peddling, for which Paul wrote volumes to correct the error?\n\nNow it was here too. If they who were barely a century after Jesus' death had these issues, then we, 2 millennia down the line, would have more issues in that stead.","dt":"2023-10-28T07:41:12","s":["8jkx4asviu"]}]},"3":{"8":[{"m":"This caution was more to the church ⛪ than the world.\n\nAgain, who are those who have a form of godliness yet deny its power, if not believers? (verse 5)\n\nIndeed in the last days there will be much onslaught against the church ⛪ from within.","dt":"2023-10-28T07:46:12","s":["tuu7zhpybw"]}],"12":[{"m":"A grave warning to all true believers. So we do not get surprised when those persecutions arise.\n\nYou as a believer are a soldier for life, so have that mindset in your head 🤕.\n\nIt is for lack or refusal of this knowledge that many believers have chosen the broad path. The easy way.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:26:04","s":["cj6kzk70d7"]}],"13":[{"m":"Some of the things Paul describes here, if this plumb line is used as the standard, many will fall short.\n\nMany will fail the test.\n\nLord have mercy, heal me and help 😣 me.\n\nFor the kingdom's 👑 calling and standard is indeed a high one.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:33:30","s":["r33g3nyw1y"]}]},"4":{"4":[{"m":"This is happening now in our times before our very eyes 👀.\n\nMen telling fables to a willing congregation.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:45:32","s":["zix705nbpu"]}],"8":[{"m":"If you are alive and you love the Lord and his appearing, be rest assured... You shall receive from the Lord the crown 👑 of righteousness.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:51:39","s":["ge447ykb22"]}],"7":[{"m":"Lord, let this be my story...\n\nThat I also will at the end of my time be ready to be offered.\n\nThough I suspect this offering was the martyrdom of the saints, he will be thrown to the lions or burnt 🔥 like most of his companions.\n\nHe will be offered up and the smoke of his burning body will be a sweet smelling incense to the Lord.","dt":"2022-12-23T07:50:14","s":["3pw74obc9c"]}],"22":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-12-23T07:53:17","s":["dcec16ea95"]}]}},"2 Peter":{"1":{"8":[{"m":"I love this: if these things are in you and abound, THEY MAKE YOU... It's as simple as that.\n\nGet these things in you and let them abound, and you wouldn't need to try anything.\n\nThey would make you by themselves.","dt":"2022-12-25T15:36:46","s":["eyv92me1fz"]}],"14":[{"m":"😢... He knew his time... He knew this body is just a tabernacle.\n\nBut for most of us it's just head knowledge.","dt":"2022-12-25T15:44:33","s":["7zwg0wgz1m"]},{"m":"What exactly did the Lord Jesus show him? And it makes me wonder, if the Lord Jesus showed Peter he had to go,\n\ndid that mean there was no more good Peter could have done if he lived longer?\n\nOf course not; there was plenty of good Peter staying alive could do, but it was time ⌚; others would step in.\n\nThe Lord knew it was time.","dt":"2023-12-01T16:44:00","s":["8vpdcqlqn9"]},{"m":"I just finished reading 2nd Timothy, where Paul talks of his time being near to leave the earth 🌎.\n\nAnd here Peter says the same thing.\n\nGod help us to serve our all as we await for the life thereafter.\n\nIt would be nice to know when your time draws near.","dt":"2025-05-25T06:30:44","s":["385e8zl5se"]}],"19":[{"m":"Aside we hearing the voice of God testifying that Jesus is his Son,\n\nthere is a more sure witness and testimony, and that is the scriptures.\n\nWhich prophesied of his coming, the good thing being scriptures are not of any one private interpretation,\n\nso we can all read the scriptures and verify for ourselves if indeed he, Jesus, is the Christ.","dt":"2022-12-25T16:17:25","s":["8lhk7tb79s"]}],"9":[{"m":"If you lack these things, then you are still walking in sin and in your old ways.\n\nYou have forgotten you were purged and are now a new creature...","dt":"2022-12-25T15:42:36","s":["nrwzolorjw"]}],"10":[{"m":"Here Peter admonishes the disciples not to be lukewarm, but to make their calling into the faith sure and steadfast.\n\nAs solid as a rock (my own expression), by following the traits of virtue, knowledge, temperance, love etc.\n\nIf these things are done, one will never fall.","dt":"2023-12-01T16:41:31","s":["ndb0fv8i5u"]}],"15":[{"m":"This letter is almost like his will; in his dying days he sought to establish the kingdom of God.\n\nNot his riches or houses etc., maybe he did if he had any.\n\nOh, these early disciples were sold out to the King 👑.","dt":"2023-12-01T16:45:16","s":["7kd55l3b8c"]}]},"2":{"19":[{"m":"This almost sounds like being ensnared into sin in the name of grace abounds, so there is no such thing as sin.\n\nAll the while entangled and cannot but fulfill the lust of the flesh.\n\nWe have to be careful... Lest we end up in the error the earlier disciples forewarned us of.","dt":"2022-12-25T16:25:11","s":["3argg1f4fo"]}],"3":[{"m":"And this we find happening now in our times; we were forewarned from the very beginning.\n\nMen who would make merchandise of the flock because of covetousness.\n\nLord, have mercy and help us discern, I pray, true from false teachers.","dt":"2022-12-25T22:16:02","s":["plsbsqz3tv"]},{"m":"See the very strong 💪 words of Peter for false teachers who were making merchandise of God's flock.\n\nPeter says their judgment will not delay.\n\nI doubt 🤷‍♂️ the so-called men of God of today know what hell 🔥 they are unleashing on themselves as they make merchandise of the Lord's people and deny his holy name.","dt":"2023-12-01T16:51:11","s":["oo6984hw5m"]}]},"3":{"7":[{"m":"Was this making reference to the pre-Adamite flood, so called, or was it in reference to the flood of Noah?\n\nThree reasons I believe it's in reference to the pre-Adamite flood rather than the flood of Noah.\n\n1. If it was the flood of Noah, Noah would have been mentioned, as we see in the previous chapter.\n\n2. The flood of Noah was a flood from rain ☔, not the earth 🌎 standing out of water and ending up in water, i.e. over flooded, as we see in Genesis chapter one.\n\n3. This particular flood is in reference to the heavens and the earth being created by the word of the Lord, and later the world 🗺 that then was, was destroyed by the water 💦. We see also that there was no sun ☀ or stars ✨.\n\nThe heavens and the earth 🌎 were destroyed, and it is this destruction that was compared to the future destruction of the heavens and the earth, thus we would have a new heaven and a new earth 🌎.\n\nNot a flood that did not even destroy the earth but drowned all living things save some.\n\nThe illustration of a new heaven and a new earth 🌎 better fits the pre-Adamite flood than the flood of Noah.\n\nIf that is the case, then this begs the question 🙋: how did Peter know about this flood?...\nOr was it common knowledge at the time?","dt":"2023-12-01T17:09:21","s":["92wctwkx8y"]}]}},"1 John":{"2":{"2":[{"m":"The standards for Christian living are high ✋ indeed.\n\nWe must abundantly leave room for love to abound one for each other, for we are flawed in many ways.\n\nHowever, we should be wise so our love is not taken advantage of.","dt":"2022-12-26T08:55:40","s":["h67tyznpx9"]}],"12":[{"m":"There is room for stumbling as little children, the room of forgiveness.\n\nThe apostle John indeed is preaching a balanced Gospel.","dt":"2022-12-26T08:56:55","s":["d6ey291tpe"]}],"18":[{"m":"This is where I have some concerns: the early apostles preached the imminent coming of the Lord.\n\nBut now, alas, they were aging and the Lord had not yet come; Peter had to address this issue in his second letter.\n\nThe Apostle Paul also had to address similar issues; some even said the Lord had already come.\n\nPaul refuted this claim on the basis that the antichrist hadn't yet come, and he had to come before the Lord's coming.\n\nWe see that through the preaching of Christ there is this imminent, pending and looming coming of the Lord, for which our response is that of watching and waiting.\n\nHowever, after a while men become weary 😩.\n\nIt's been 2000 years now... The only consolation is that a day is like a 1000 years before the Lord, and a thousand years a day...\nWhat is 2000 years to an eternal God?\n\nSo we continue to wait.\n\nBut why through our time has the Lord made his coming so imminent, when all the apostles and early church ⛪ would pass on?\n\nMaybe because the Lord knows the heart of man and kept the time of this coming away from us, to keep us in check and in line.\n\nAnd to keep us fervent and evangelistic. This our Lord.\n\nIn this same vein, the coming of the antichrist and the prophecy of the end times would pan out in a way that may be beyond our human thinking and any assumptions we have of the end.","dt":"2023-12-02T10:09:52","s":["ksq6ajvzg3"]}],"20":[{"m":"Indeed, we know all things by the unction.\n\nThe Spirit of truth.","dt":"2022-12-26T08:59:16","s":["f2fycx2sft"]}],"27":[{"m":"The witness of the Spirit teaches us all things... And so we can know what is true from falsehood.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:00:43","s":["5tv47557nf"]}],"6":[{"m":"This is the standard for Christianity. You cannot profess Christ and not walk 🚶 thus.\n\nEither such an one is a liar 🤥 and deceiver, or is a novice in the faith.","dt":"2022-12-26T08:53:24","s":["uaztha0sv"]}],"19":[{"m":"In this vein, the false teachers who have come out of good and sound churches are walking 🚶 in the spirit of the antichrist.\n\nIf we follow this logic, does that not mean the antichrist would come out of the church ⛪, or at the very least be religious and like the Christ?\n\nThis ties in with his description in Revelations.\n\nAnd indeed the spirit of the antichrist is very much alive now.","dt":"2023-12-02T10:00:21","s":["sfsk5inqlf"]}]},"3":{"15":[{"m":"Because out of hate cometh murder.\n\nIndeed, by the standards of Christ, he who calls his brother “you fool” is worthy of hell fire 🔥.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:24:54","s":["ooltj7srjd"]}],"24":[{"m":"Proof of Christ in us is his Spirit.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:26:12","s":["kzmvilavwc"]}],"1":[{"m":"GOD did not just adopt us, legally as seen in the Roman law and culture of the time, but paid our debts. So unlike the Roman adoption process, that very poor and debt-ridden families can use to technically escape the weight of debt,\n\nGOD actually paid the past debts in full, and legally adopted us, and then biologically transformed us by giving us the Spirit of his dear Son Jesus Christ; thus we became not just legal heirs but natural heirs.\n\nWhy would he do that if not love?","dt":"2026-10-03T05:10:04.987Z","s":["xbbpukanw5"]}],"7":[{"m":"This statement seems so obvious. Yet John says it.\n\nAnd warns them not to be deceived.\n\nCould it be they were being deceived that it matters not whether one sins or not?","dt":"2022-12-26T09:23:14","s":["0i6wer0evw"]}]},"4":{"4":[{"m":"Mind blowing 🤯.\n\nDid John really mean that we have a Spirit in us, and that Spirit is greater than the spirit of the world and the world system?\n\nThen why are we so weak and beggarly?","dt":"2023-12-04T07:34:13","s":["iutm1clai4"]}],"10":[{"m":"Wow 😲... Mind blowing 🤯, not that we love God but he first loved us.\n\nIn fact, we detested him. Such love is humanly not possible 🙆.\n\nWhere you show love to one who hates you, and there is no guarantee the person would reciprocate your love or accept it.","dt":"2023-12-04T07:43:50","s":["pu2ot90cy6"]}],"17":[{"m":"Such cause for boldness. We are exhibiting his traits even here on the earth, so in the day of judgement we know our stand in him whom we love.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:32:36","s":["28rlp0bsli"]}],"20":[{"m":"True","dt":"2022-06-08T12:54:59","s":["fs7mi4k3k9"]}]},"5":{"1":[{"m":"This was some 60 years after Christ's death ☠, and so such fundamental truths had to be reiterated, because many lies were now being touted.\n\nMany false doctrines were out there, as is now even in our world 🗺.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:39:41","s":["2it37nkyzt"]}],"8":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 interesting...\n\nNeed more meditating 🧘‍♂️ and study.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:41:22","s":["a4fbp3a2bu"]}],"18":[{"m":"It's clearly stated here that if we keep ourselves, the enemy cannot touch us.\n\nIt's about time as believers we move on from the issue of sin and struggling and laden with so much sin, to the realm where we walk in power and fulness of the God life.\n\nWe must completely, once for all, turn our backs on sin and fundamental doctrines to greater heights in the Spirit. So help me God.","dt":"2023-12-04T07:48:46","s":["uu86r52po2"]}],"6":[{"m":"Could this refer to his baptism and shed blood?","dt":"2022-12-26T09:40:42","s":["q7oomoq11a"]}],"19":[{"m":"We know, we know, not we think. These last concluding statements from John are statements of truth and knowings.","dt":"2022-12-26T09:43:34","s":["vxocvsenbr"]}],"21":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-12-26T09:43:48","s":["0da4e3992f"]}]},"1":{"3":[{"m":"I can imagine the early church receiving such letters from the revered John.\n\nThis was 90 AD, and so to receive a letter from one of those who saw the Lord face to face in his full 🌕 bodily manifestation was a sight to behold and a gem 💎.\n\nIt was scarce; at this time John might have been the only living Apostle at the time...\n\nWith much tears 😭 I believe these letters were received, read and heard.\n\nIn this letter he bears witness to physically seeing Jesus. With these eyes 👀.\n\nThat tells us, in a sense, the controversies of the time ⌚.\n\nMaybe some were already denying the truth, saying Christianity was craftily designed fables.","dt":"2022-12-26T08:50:43","s":["bzdrpk3tjh"]}]}},"2 John":{"1":{"2":[{"m":"The truth which dwelleth in us and shall be with us forever is Jesus.\n\n60 years earlier, the truth which dwelleth with us and shall be in us was and is the Holy Spirit.\n\nJohn 14:17 KJV\nEven the Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him; for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you.\n\nWhat is the link between these? Jesus is in us by the Holy Spirit forever, and now in the end of the age, he that is in us shall be with us forever.\n\nDoes not that therefore imply that Jesus is the Spirit of truth, who is the Holy Spirit?","dt":"2022-12-26T10:47:11","s":["movghckzgz"]},{"m":"Interestingly enough, this truth in us, which is the Spirit of truth, i.e. the Holy Spirit, shall be with us in the person of Jesus, but that does not mean the Spirit will cease living in us.\n\nSame vein, the truth dwelt with us in the person of Jesus and shall be with us forever, i.e. the Holy Ghost 👻 coming on the day of Pentecost.\n\nYet Jesus liveth on still, even after he came into us through the Holy Ghost.\n\nThis indeed is a mystery.","dt":"2022-12-26T13:33:50","s":["3atgekeyld"]},{"m":"If the truth dwells in us and the truth is Jesus Christ (the way, the truth and the life),\nthen who is it that dwells in us if not Jesus —\nthe living truth?\n\nThen how about the Holy Ghost, who also dwells in us as the Spirit of truth — which Spirit is Jesus,\n\nand the Lord is that Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.","dt":"2022-12-26T13:39:03","s":["85a8wak870"]},{"m":"The truth in us is Jesus... For he is the way, the truth and the life...\n\nJohn 14:6 KJV\nJesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.\n\nThe truth in us is how we become born again, not of corruptible seed but of incorruptible, by the word of truth...\n\n1 Peter 1:23 KJV\nBeing born again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, by the word of God, which liveth and abideth for ever.\n\nThat same seed... 🌱 which did not need man to be birthed but brought about the virgin birth,\n\nbrought about our rebirth, our being born again.\n\nAgain, this seed which brought a full-grown Jesus to Jordan, and was baptized by the Holy Ghost, brings us into baptism of the Holy Ghost.\n\nAs first seen on the day of Pentecost.\n\nWe also receive the Holy Ghost after the same pattern.\n\nSo in us is the truth, of which seed we 🌱 were born again, our spirits being new.\n\nAnd now we have the Holy Ghost; we literally have become duplicates of the Christ Jesus.\n\nSo this truth which lives in us, not just lives in us forever but actually birthed us,\n\nhim we shall see and meet with him forever.\n\nAnd we have the Holy Spirit of promise also in us forever.\n\nWe are a new creature, clones of the Lord. No wonder we are sons of God as Jesus is.\n\nFor we are made of the same matter and composition that Jesus is.\n\n😢\n\nSons of God, yet live so weak and beggarly.\n\nNo wonder Jesus said,\n\nJohn 16:12-13 KJV\nI have yet many things to say unto you, but ye cannot bear them now.\n\n[13] Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come.\n\nThe whole born-again, Spirit-filled, Gentile-inclusive experience had to be unpacked in bite sizes for the entire Christian experience to be possible.\n\nLest it be too confusing.\n\nSo Jesus unpacked some and left the rest for the Holy Ghost to do, so he does and continues on until this day.","dt":"2022-12-27T07:13:29","s":["zxsyfizwea"]}]}},"Revelation":{"1":{"5":[{"m":"The prince of the kings of the earth, to wit, he is the crown and the head of the kings of the earth.","dt":"2025-05-27T08:36:08","s":["01axjdbhl2"]},{"m":"The faithful witness: he came to witness to us of the love of God. He taught us of the extent of God's love, and being from heaven, gave us first-hand witness of the love of God.\n\nAnd further demonstrated it by dying a shameful death on the cross, to show to us the extent of the love of God.\n\nHe remained faithful to his call and mandate; he remained true to his call to witness the love of God to us.","dt":"2025-06-02T19:46:09","s":["ztpj1x89sq"]}],"18":[{"m":"The keys 🗝 of hell and death ☠. Keys signifying a place.\n\nSo death is not just an event, it is also a place that people go after they die.","dt":"2022-12-27T08:39:34","s":["shpjortbib"]},{"m":"This is such a sharp deviation from the man Jesus.\n\nMany times Jesus spoke in parables and sayings to shroud the truth, so only those with ears can hear.\n\nHowever, here we see so clearly him taking upon himself the attributes of God.\n\nIn appearance and even in his speech. He was no longer hiding who he was.\n\nIndeed, he received an inheritance for the things done on the cross...\n\nHe had paid the full price of the sacrifice.","dt":"2025-05-27T08:48:43","s":["ap3wwo3sza"]}],"7":[{"m":"Shortly come to pass, and it's been 2000 years.\n\nAnd they also which pierced him, but they are in hell, and yet it says all eyes shall see him.\n\nAnd that is true in the sense of all will be brought before him, both dead and alive, and even they which pierced him.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:04:35","s":["g2tk9a0jfl"]}],"19":[{"m":"Write what you have seen so far, and the things that are happening now, currently, and the things that shall happen in the future, hereafter...","dt":"2022-12-27T08:42:00","s":["02ixs4vogp"]}]},"2":{"10":[{"m":"Having now properly ID'd them as the synagogue of Satan, Jesus minces no words in letting his church know that the devil would cast them into prison.\n\nHe could have said that the Jews would cast them in prison, but he knew these were no Jews. They were devils, and rightly so.\n\nThere was no point in keeping up appearances. He called those brute beasts out.","dt":"2025-05-27T09:01:58","s":["lkeh3yisen"]}],"14":[{"m":"This issue of things sacrificed to idols has come again here too.\n\nAnd the Lord detests eating things offered to idols. He is a jealous God.\n\nPaul addresses a similar issue, and his solution is within a particular context.\n\nWe see here that it seems the eating of things offered to idols tied in with their committing whoredom, yet still claiming to be part of the church ⛪.\n\nWe see the same in today's church. There is nothing new under the sun ☀.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:26:53","s":["ie1s636jn8"]}],"17":[{"m":"What will be the purpose of having a name which no man knoweth? It is obviously not a title or appellation to give one some honour whenever it is mentioned.\n\nLike we do have doctors etc.\nSo to have a secret name may mean it worked like a code, which could open certain doors. So this code will grant privileged access to some places in heaven.","dt":"2025-06-04T15:05:09","s":["awc3whca1v"]}],"19":[{"m":"Wow, this was a good church ⛪, into a lot of works and service.\n\nIt kinda reminds me of today's new wine 🍷 church.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:29:37","s":["7iyvsmwxeb"]}],"20":[{"m":"Again we see fornication tying in with idol worship, or at least participating in their food.\n\nAnd it seemed this woman was preaching that it is OK to be sinning though we are for the Lord.\n\nGod is gracious and gave time for them to repent.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:31:44","s":["u8yek8vhfq"]},{"m":"Even in the early church a lot of strange things were happening, as is the case even today.","dt":"2025-05-27T09:04:45","s":["8zj8sivm2d"]}],"25":[{"m":"Hold fast till I come.","dt":"2022-12-27T09:21:23","s":["mzd0jo1e4u"]},{"m":"Hold fast till I come, not hold fast till you come up to me, as is signified in the rapture.\n\nYes, we will be caught up with him in the clouds, and then we will come down with him to rule and reign with him.\n\nIf there is any catching up into the heavens without coming down with the Lord, then it is us being with him at death.\n\nThen we will be caught up to him and will be with him until he comes.","dt":"2025-05-27T09:07:47","s":["1dz2gc7riq"]}],"2":[{"m":"So other apostles arise after the 12, whose claims were found false.","dt":"2022-12-27T08:46:17","s":["bfwahu5lgo"]}],"9":[{"m":"Synagogue 🕍 of Satan 👿?? 😳 ?? 😳\n\nIt's almost like saying the whiteness of black.\n\nA synagogue 🕍 to start with is not of Satan, so how did they get there...","dt":"2022-12-27T09:00:06","s":["vcpguu1ay9"]}]},"3":{"5":[{"m":"So, to him who overcomes. The Christian walk is warfare.\n\nThere is much to overcome, so we cannot take it casually and cool.\n\nWe are in a real war.\n\nWe must be strong, alert ⚠ and vigilant.","dt":"2022-12-27T09:27:46","s":["sv2h76w3qh"]}],"12":[{"m":"This is an interesting verse. In chapter 1, after Jesus having boldly taken upon himself the attributes of God,\n\nhe here calls God his God. The wording of scripture is interesting — this shows the depth of the wisdom of God, even in his make-up and Godhead.","dt":"2025-06-04T15:13:51","s":["vywq08n1vy"]}],"20":[{"m":"This is to believers, even though it is quoted often for evangelistic work among unbelievers.","dt":"2022-12-27T09:32:56","s":["bq4ub9bzkg"]}],"21":[{"m":"He is seated with the Father in his throne: in his rulership and dominion.\n\nNot that there is one throne and they are thronging about in it to find space.\n\nEven though, as spirits, they can sit together on one throne, considering the fact that the Father is in the Son and the Son in the Father.","dt":"2022-12-27T10:02:53","s":["c58cfql1ae"]}],"14":[{"m":"This is how DAKES describes this verse, and I think that should suffice.\n\n[beginning of the creation of God] That is, the One who began creating all things in the very beginning (Jn. 1:3; Eph. 3:9; Col. 1:15-18; Heb. 1:2; 11:3). It could not mean that He was the first to be created by God, for He is an uncreated and eternal being (Isa. 9:6-7; Mic. 5:2; Jn. 1:1-2; Heb. 1:8; Rev. 1:8, note).","dt":"2025-06-04T15:15:43","s":["pwnebl89vd"]}],"19":[{"m":"This sounds like a modern, rich, educated church ⛪ for the elite.\n\nThey needed to be more zealous and do more.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:37:56","s":["6nik5o6gub"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"Okay, so we had the things which thou hast seen, i.e. the Son of Man appearing in his glory,\n\nThen we had the things which are, that is the current issues pertaining to the churches and the mind of God for them, and now,\n\nWithout ambiguity, the passage here says these are the things that must be hereafter.\n\nThese 3 distinctions are so clear.\n\nThe things which are was sandwiched 🥪 between the things which were seen by John and this proclamation commencing that which must be hereafter.","dt":"2022-12-27T10:27:26","s":["bbn355cuur"]},{"m":"There is a way to hide in plain sight truths through the letters of the ink 🖋.\n\nIn writing, much can be hidden in plain sight, such that the discerning and wise of heart —\n\ni.e. the one willing to spend some more time in 📖 reading 📖 and meditating 🧘‍♂️ on that which is written — ends up receiving and 🔓 unlocking the hidden gems 💎 in the text.\n\nIn writing you can hide your pearls from the swine and give it to him that is truly deserving.","dt":"2022-12-27T10:30:16","s":["vemydlgf5f"]},{"m":"There are many interpretations that can be inferred from what 'hereafter' meant.\n\nIt's worth noting that when it came to events of hereafter, John leaves the 🌎 earth and journeys to the heavens...\n\n1. So firstly, the visions of the Son of Man 👨 refer to what thou hast seen.\n\n2. The visions of what is concerns the interpretation of the vision John saw and the issues of the churches.\n\n3. Now he is told this part of the revelation has to do with what shall be hereafter.\n\nThe question is, 'hereafter what?'\n\nDakes says it's the things after the church age, i.e. the church is raptured and not here when these things happen.\n\nOne thing is clear though: John was caught up to heaven to see events in heaven and as they affect the earth 🌎.\n\nAnd these events are after the message to the church and the events of the church ⛪.\n\nI do not know if that meant it happened after the rapture, but we see that it happens after the church has been given warnings for earth and blessing in the end of time ⌚.\n\nAnd the next thing we see is the end of time activities. So then the church's time on earth 🌎 to prove their obedience is over. There is no more time to do any more works or heed any more instructions.\n\nIt's now time for the blessings or punishment as need be.\n\nThis does not necessarily mean the church vanishes from the earth and appears in heaven.\n\nEven though we see saints in heaven by the time John is told to Come up hither.\n\nBut those could be dead saints.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:50:27","s":["g4dqwgf6ad"]},{"m":"DAKES argues that there is no mention of the church in the book of Revelation from after chapter 4. Thus proving the church has been raptured to heaven.\nBut it is worthy of note that the church was not mentioned as being in heaven either. The church is neither named in heaven nor earth.\n\nRather, we see mention of saints, both in the heavens and in the earth. I think the word church is missing in heaven because by definition church is the term for ecclesia, i.e. the called-out ones.\n\nBut in heaven we are all called out; that is why we made it there in the first place. So then why is the name church not maintained in the earth?\nI don't know. Maybe that may be alluding to the church no longer being on earth but has been raptured, maybe, maybe not. So Dakes may be right, but that only alludes to it but doesn't provide evidence to the rapture.","dt":"2025-06-08T14:54:09","s":["w1rkjlsoxj"]}],"2":[{"m":"His being in the spirit immediately was because he was called up 👆","dt":"2022-12-27T10:43:01","s":["5an7k77pm2"]}],"5":[{"m":"Voices — was it that he who sat in the throne, as he speaks, he speaks with multiple voices, or is it that there is more than one person in that glorious light?","dt":"2022-12-27T10:45:47","s":["qijzfc2cpk"]}],"10":[{"m":"In a sense, this anointing on the beasts in a form rests on music ministers today; as they give praise and glory and worship, we sense the power of God and we lie prostrate before him.","dt":"2025-05-28T08:52:28","s":["69jqmxnt6t"]}]},"5":{"4":[{"m":"Why was he weeping thus? Except that he knew the contents of the book were critical to the salvation of the saints and to bring all matters to an end.\nHe sensed the book was mighty important.","dt":"2023-12-12T11:56:16","s":["ih7gl8rk5a"]},{"m":"No man could open the book. I used to think that it meant no creature, i.e. angels, beasts etc. could open it.\n\nBut no, the opening of the book was the purview of man; it was only a man who qualifies to open the book.\n\nHowever, being a man is only the first qualification.\n\nThe man, however, must be a worthy man. And when the entirety of God's created places was searched, places where men could be found,\n\nThere was none worthy.\n\nThe earth was searched, the heavens were searched, under the earth — Hades and the land of dead spirits of men were searched — none was worthy.\n\nUntil the Lion of the tribe of Judah showed forth. He was a lion but showed forth as a lamb; that sacrifice was what made him the worthy one.","dt":"2025-05-28T08:57:36","s":["ewp4cqlpq4"]},{"m":"Without the opening of this book, how will the righteous be vindicated, how will all things and the suffering and the persecutions and the hope of the righteous be met, if the book is not opened?\n\nThen had we laboured in vain, and we are of all men most miserable.","dt":"2025-05-28T09:00:03","s":["i8dlfzrkq5"]}],"7":[{"m":"Wait oo, and he came. Did he come as a man, or he came as the lamb to take the scroll?\n\nOr maybe he took it with his mouth, since when John looked he saw a lamb and not a man.","dt":"2025-05-28T09:09:24","s":["ur0x4qgwcl"]}],"8":[{"m":"We have seen the elders before bowing before the throne and casting their crowns; however, here the imagery we are given is that after the book was taken by the lamb, we see the elders and beasts with golden vials full of odours, and we are told those are the prayers of the saints.\n\nWhy would that be mentioned at this particular time, except there is a connection between the taking of the book by the lamb in order to break its seals and the prayers of the saints?\n\nAnd I believe that is exactly that: there is a connection, in that the book contains answers to the prayers of the saints.\n\nPrayers to the injustice, the murders and martyrdom of their families, friends. The untold hardships of the persecutions they faced.\n\nThe book, as we see subsequently, contains the judgement of God upon the wicked.\n\nLittle wonder when earlier there was no one to open the book, that John wept. Without the seals being broken, there will continue to be further delay, and the wickedness will continue.\n\nWhen you genuinely serve the Lord, you so wish for the coming of the Lord. The world is not worthy of you.\n\nYou have no taste for the things of the world. Literally you are enduring this world and groaning constantly in this world, waiting for the redemption of your body.\n\nThis is further corroborated when later in the succeeding chapters we see the saints cry for justice, and they are told to wait for the rest of their brethren to be martyred like them; then when the numbers add up, justice will be meted out.\n\nRevelation 6:9-11 KJV\n9 And when he had opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of them that were slain for the word of God, and for the testimony which they held: 10 And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Lord, holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth? 11 And white robes were given unto every one of them; and it was said unto them, that they should rest yet for a little season, until their fellowservants also and their brethren, that should be killed as they were, should be fulfilled.","dt":"2025-06-07T10:42:30","s":["ffvwsw01bz"]}],"10":[{"m":"This did not just apply to the elders here, who were saints, but to all the saints who were in heaven at this time.\n\nAs the song of the elders reveals, they were redeemed from all over the world... Every kindred.","dt":"2022-12-28T09:35:42","s":["5p84jklman"]},{"m":"So this was a season of reigning for the redeemed of the Lord. The golden vials contained the prayers of the saints.\n\nFor the elders and all creatures to sing that we are king 👑 priests and we shall reign on the earth 🌎, then it indeed was time for the saints to reign, and the saints were in heaven at this time...\n\nBut this does not necessarily mean that there were zero saints in the earth 🌎, neither does that prove a rapture had relocated the saints rather than death.","dt":"2023-12-12T12:00:19","s":["dvl9337232"]},{"m":"This king 👑 priest status was not just for the elders but all saints, as we see John quote same in chapter one, and Peter talks of us being a royal 👑 priesthood.","dt":"2023-12-12T12:16:35","s":["ob5zggvtw"]}]},"6":{"10":[{"m":"So these were in heaven, awaiting justice and vengeance on the wicked.","dt":"2025-05-28T09:25:01","s":["bau9ujeqoy"]}],"16":[{"m":"Who told them this was God and his wrath... How did they know?","dt":"2022-12-28T13:19:19","s":["ari3s2wx27"]},{"m":"How did men of all classes know that the movement of the heavens was not some cosmic incident but the wrath of HIM who sits on the throne and of his lamb?\n\nOr could it be that, as they themselves said, the one who sits on the throne is seen from the earth?\n\nBecause men sought to be hidden from him and his face.\n\nOh, I can imagine a great throne of the Lord being seen in the heavens from the earth.","dt":"2025-06-27T16:28:48","s":["61w11dt3l9"]}],"1":[{"m":"Was it the voice of the beast that sounded like thunder, or as the beast spoke, thunder accompanied this very word?","dt":"2025-05-28T09:14:44","s":["bzodztu1yl"]}],"8":[{"m":"It seemed the fourth horse carried with him all the powers of the first three horses, plus an extra one of his own, i.e. ability to destroy with beasts of the earth.","dt":"2025-06-21T09:32:56","s":["d65x0qbfca"]}],"14":[{"m":"I believe the parting of the heavens as a scroll 📜 will be the gateway for the tribulation saints to be raptured into the heavens.\n\nFor they are seen in the next chapter in heaven.","dt":"2025-07-31T08:21:52","s":["6pcoqteom3"]}]},"7":{"14":[{"m":"They have washed their robes; their sins have they been cleansed from by the blood of Jesus, and have proved themselves worthy by the purging of the flesh through the tribulation.","dt":"2022-12-28T20:41:52","s":["xokpbujoff"]},{"m":"To have such a large crowd out of tribulations, then indeed it was such a great tribulation. The saints martyred in unfathomable numbers without pity.\n\nSomebody wanted to obliterate Christianity out of the earth.","dt":"2025-05-28T09:46:38","s":["z5xa9p783w"]}]},"8":{"7":[{"m":"Why blood? Likely because they had shed the blood of the saints in abundance.","dt":"2025-05-28T10:04:20","s":["xc13y5r0hd"]}],"9":[{"m":"Could the sea becoming blood mean that the sea literally became blood,\n\nor the animals that were crushed by the meteor bled out, and it was so much that a third of the sea became blood?","dt":"2025-07-06T10:47:41","s":["4z3trc1wxm"]}],"12":[{"m":"How does this pan out, that a third part of the earth did not have day and another third part did not have nights?","dt":"2025-05-28T10:05:28","s":["sxikqurfun"]}]},"9":{"14":[{"m":"There are many mysteries and hidden places on the earth containing creatures beyond our wildest imaginations.\n\nSee for instance the bottomless pit: where exactly is it?\n\nThese angels bound in the Euphrates: which exact part of this river are they in?","dt":"2025-05-28T10:11:00","s":["ybz0xpffft"]}],"21":[{"m":"Men number about seven billion today; a third will be 2.5 billion. That is a lot.\n\nNot to mention these numbers will be higher in the future.","dt":"2025-05-28T10:15:48","s":["k958c27g6i"]}]},"10":{"1":[{"m":"His feet as pillars of fire, yet were not quenched by the water he stood in.","dt":"2025-07-09T06:42:06","s":["qyfmkjsw0c"]}],"4":[{"m":"Ahhh 😱... My heart ♥ burns 🔥 to know what it was that was uttered.\n\nWhat is it at all that God thought it best for us not to know?","dt":"2023-12-19T06:54:47","s":["6xqfmu70eg"]},{"m":"It was not for us to know, but for John; he knew but could not speak openly of them.\n\nThere indeed are mysteries in the life.\n\nOh Lord, grant me some.\n\nRevelation 10:4 ASV\nAnd when the seven thunders uttered their voices, I was about to write: and I heard a voice from heaven saying, Seal up the things which the seven thunders uttered, and write them not.","dt":"2023-12-19T07:04:05","s":["vzppla6gff"]}],"6":[{"m":"How is that even possible... That there should be time no longer?","dt":"2023-12-19T07:09:18","s":["f8edn2hrq3"]}],"7":[{"m":"I believe part of the mystery of God that should be finished in the days of the voice of the seventh angel 😇 is the mystery of time ⌚.\n\nAnd time ⌚ would be no more.","dt":"2023-12-19T07:11:31","s":["0cle9q0zpe"]}]},"11":{"3":[{"m":"Will they really be clothed in sackcloth in the modern world 🗺 of that future 🔮 day? Well, it's totally possible 🤷","dt":"2023-12-22T07:39:23","s":["f459dekbq6"]}],"4":[{"m":"How do they arrive on the scene — are they born... Because we see that after their death and resurrection they are called up to the heavens in a cloud like Jesus.","dt":"2025-07-09T07:06:59","s":["butnu6jj3x"]}],"9":[{"m":"This is literally true: the whole world 🗺 would see their bodies.\n\nIn time past it was wondered how, but now with our modern tech, it's a no-brainer 🧠","dt":"2023-12-19T07:30:48","s":["fjkqnj5xan"]}],"10":[{"m":"I am wondering, where are Christians at this point in time?\n\nHow will Christians be exempted from these plagues upon the earth?\n\nIsrael will still be here in those times, so people will continue to give their lives to Christ, and so the church will also continue here.","dt":"2025-05-28T10:29:29","s":["7v8835ou7r"]}],"15":[{"m":"When the seventh seal was broken, there was silence 🤫 in heaven for half an hour, but when the seventh trumpet 🎺 sounded there were great voices in heaven.","dt":"2025-07-09T07:08:23","s":["nfedj6kv2l"]}],"18":[{"m":"The nations were angry 😡 and God was also angry 😡 — His wrath is come.","dt":"2025-07-09T07:13:41","s":["4t1n2rze1z"]}]},"12":{"3":[{"m":"Such imagery.\n\nWhat an anomaly — in the perfect kingdom of God in the heavens, the heavens of our holy God, there appeared a great red dragon.\n\nSo out of place. The dark son in the place of light... And with him stood an army of rebellious luminaries.\n\nStars, yet dark — another anomaly.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:01:46","s":["qc9e1z6q5b"]}],"11":[{"m":"At this time all saints were in heaven, and so spoke from a heavenly perspective.\n\nThey were glad that the devil's 👿 place in heaven, which he still has access to even now, was taken from him.\n\nNow heaven had permanently gotten rid of this accuser, whose access to heaven was a perpetual pain to the saints of God, the never-ending railings of accusations against us.\n\nNow the saints are in heaven, and heaven has rid itself of the devil 👿 and his cohorts forever by an act of war.\n\nMeaning if the angels of God tried to eject Satan from his current place in the realm of God, there would be war.\n\nNow the saints, and heaven for that matter, could rejoice greatly because the devil has been ousted.","dt":"2023-12-25T11:38:13","s":["sdo5wbkm68"]},{"m":"Why would the devil accuse us before God,\nexcept to obtain judgement against us, or to justify his persecution and abuse of the saints?\n\nIn his accusations it is stated that the saints overcame him by the blood of the lamb,\n\nwhich is in reference to the shed blood of Christ, thus justifying us and making us righteous before God,\n\nbut despite our sins and right standing with God being paid for, the devil still accuses us and seeks condemnation against us.\n\nSo the word of our testimony comes into play, and we confess that we have accepted the shed blood of the lamb and are in alignment with his finished works on the cross.\n\nWe acknowledge what has been done by Christ for us and keep to that testimony. We refuse to be condemned nor pay for what Christ has already paid for.\n\nHowever, that is not enough for the devil; he would not budge and continues to persecute the saints using his power and human agencies on the earth.\n\nHe causes us pain because of our acknowledgement of Christ and his finished works in our lives.\n\nHe still accuses us and insists that we are not only not worthy but have not really received Christ for real in our hearts and lives 💕, and this we refute by not loving our own lives even to the death.\n\nWe hold firm our confessions and stand our ground and our belief even unto death.\n\nAnd these accusations and persecution of the devil Christ forewarns us about. He says in this life we would have trouble, but we must be of good cheer, for he has overcome the world.\n\nIt is therefore actually counter-Christian to teach that in Christ we have all things and no pain or suffering.\n\nIndeed, the pain and suffering and our standing our ground is the proof of Christ in us, and not the opposite: that Christ in us means no pain or afflictions.\n\nThat belief is a lie of the devil to validate his accusations of us before God and win his case that we are fake and are hovering around just for convenience; thus we are not worthy of the kingdom and to stand before the presence of God and his holy angels.\n\nWho wants fake subjects before him or serving in his castle, in this case his temple and presence?\n\nAnd I think the devil wins his case sometimes; why else would he keep at it this long if it didn't really matter, because after all Christ has completed his work and finished it?\n\nBut he wins sometimes, I think, and his evidence is our change of allegiance from service of God to compromise because of discomfort.\n\nNot just some random compromise or falling into temptation, but a perpetual and permanent drift from God, and thus his face, to follow after vanity.\n\nI'm sure sometimes the devil brings an accusation, seeking to take the life of a believer in apostasy and claim him for himself as having rejected God and followed the devil.\n\nBut God overrules the accusation and gives the person more time to repent, and sure enough the person turns over and is on fire more than ever before, and with the enemy fuming because he lost.\nHe wins some other cases as well.\n\nWhy he has taken the posture of condemning God's people is a subject for another teaching.","dt":"2025-08-01T06:58:08","s":["26fuylgko0","rbuxx53lty"]}],"12":[{"m":"Who are the inhabitants of the sea? 🌊","dt":"2023-12-25T11:38:39","s":["y54hloq5cn"]},{"m":"I believe that as a result of this great work of accusation of the enemy,\n\nMany a strong 💪 Christian has been lost, lost through pain and affliction, and some even from the faith, all because of the work of the accuser who must be disproved.\nSo we must suffer even unto death for the Lord in order to meet the demands of divine justice.","dt":"2023-12-25T15:57:21","s":["mqqv20bjrj"]},{"m":"He has a short time to do what? To convert many to his ways and deceive men, as many as possible, to their own doom and rebellion towards God.\n\nThe time for him to do this before he is finally judged and ostracized is short. Time was coming to an end, and his time was thus far running 🏃 out on him.","dt":"2023-12-26T09:23:20","s":["go0lnpef9u"]},{"m":"Who are the inhabitants of the sea?\n\nI want to know.","dt":"2025-08-01T07:08:15","s":["77pqt58hvy"]},{"m":"His time is short for what? I have explained some of the reasons for which his time was short, as time coming to an end as prophesied, but not just that but also because,\n\nHis place in the heavens has been cleared, so the space was vacant for the taking, and the victor in the war would take all the strategic positions, mount their defence and finally usher in the coming of Christ with his host of saints and angels.\n\nAs things stand now, the third heavens are taken by the enemy and his angels, but in the end it will be for Michael and his angels to finally usher in the descent of Christ with his vast host.\n\nOh, what a moment, what a triumphant entry.","dt":"2025-08-01T07:21:06","s":["6i0zazhad6"]}],"4":[{"m":"So all of the drama in heaven was because of a small planet 🌏 called earth 🌎.\n\nEarth 🌎 then must indeed be very important.\n\nI suspect there may be none like it in the universe 🌌.\n\nI mean, for the God of the whole universe to give us such attention and personal touch, including his own Son's death ☠ for us.\n\nEarth 🌎 is one of a kind in my estimation.","dt":"2023-12-25T11:30:51","s":["cpdd0dzg2v"]}],"13":[{"m":"Why didn't the dragon pursue the woman but rather fought Michael in the heavens?\n\nBecause his target was the man child, who was now caught up to God in the heavens.\n\nSo he had to go for him in the heavens.\n\nIt was upon failure to win the heavenly war that he came for the woman. And when that failed too, he went for the rest of her seed.\n\nThe heavens were the first priority, because once he conquered the heavens, the earth was his for the taking.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:12:03","s":["4q8o7rasiw"]}]},"13":{"1":[{"m":"This marked the beginning of the war with the remnant of the seed of the woman and the righteous saints in the earth.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:37:54","s":["22ymt8bzhb"]}],"6":[{"m":"His blasphemy was directed to the heavens. The people of the earth were deceived into wondering who could make war against the beast.\n\nWhat they did not know was that the head of the beast, the dragon, had already been defeated in heaven.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:16:41","s":["cxu56f6e8s"]},{"m":"I wonder what blasphemies he said against them that dwell in heaven. Or maybe he disdained them and lied that they were no more than just aliens and deceitful beings who want to lord it over humans.\n\nAt this point it could be anything.","dt":"2025-08-25T01:40:14","s":["zwzdu8p79b"]}],"10":[{"m":"Here is where the saints are tried and tested to show themselves true to Christ.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:19:00","s":["s35y71618g"]}],"11":[{"m":"The first beast came out of the sea. This one out of the earth.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:19:26","s":["gplxkbuwmt"]},{"m":"This beast mimicked the lamb, but his voice betrayed him. There is always something about the enemy that betrays him, even when they disguise themselves as angels of light.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:20:34","s":["4y4ko6av8m"]}],"17":[{"m":"The second beast came to make worse the policies of the first beast, that is the antichrist, by taking the beast's policies down to every street corner and every human being.\n\nHe ensured compliance by his systems, even tying the worship of the beast to the food we eat.\n\nI won't be surprised that in worship a portion of one's food would have to be given as an oblation to the image.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:24:21","s":["jqajbt4szf"]}],"18":[{"m":"In giving us wisdom, we are not given it in line with the image of the beast nor his mark, but the number of the beast, and we are told it is the number of a man, i.e. the name of a known man — and that man's number is 666.\n\nThe people of wisdom in the times of John definitely could judge who the man was.\n\nNow that makes me wonder: after writing the letters to the churches, John by all means would give them the book of Revelations, of the things after the specific churches.\n\nAnd there will be many discussions amongst them of the number of the beast.\n\nMaybe we also can know if we apply wisdom; after all, it is the number of a man.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:29:03","s":["vzyccnur2o"]},{"m":"Three things are given: the name, the mark and the number, yet no clue is given of any save the number.\n\nBased on which, we can get the name, ID the beast, and I guess from there we can know how the image or mark of the beast is like.","dt":"2025-08-04T08:56:59","s":["i4yu1cghnv"]}],"8":[{"m":"He had become the god of this world. Now he is, but through subtlety and hidden; but then he will be publicly.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:17:45","s":["u7w5icxzuw"]}]},"14":{"4":[{"m":"Aww, what a people, in whose mouth is no guile; they are his personal protocol.\n\nFollowing the lamb everywhere he goes.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:31:10","s":["phrn2spbrf"]}],"8":[{"m":"They drank of the wine of her fornication, and therefore when the wrath of God came on all fornication,\n\nall the other nations who were partakers with her drank as well of their iniquities.","dt":"2022-12-30T06:09:37","s":["rr9abbwyib"]}],"11":[{"m":"For angels to announce this, it would indeed have been a very trying moment for the saints here.\n\nOh God, have mercy on our brethren, and help, help, Lord... help.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:33:02","s":["q9c7vb30eu"]}],"12":[{"m":"Saints in the future will have to take their stance for Christ at the peril of their lives in order to enter the kingdom.\n\nJust as the early church did suffer much for Christ.\n\nAnd yet today we are told we need not suffer nothing, nor take a stand for him, yet we will still be given an entrance into the kingdom.\n\nSuch lies and deception we have believed in.","dt":"2025-08-01T07:29:29","s":["uf2ygu0o9b"]}],"13":[{"m":"Amen, rest, and their works follow them to eternity.","dt":"2022-12-28T23:08:14","s":["v1uedwzc57"]},{"m":"People in all ages will continue to give their life to the Lord and serve him.\n\nAt this point in history, the rapture of the saints had long taken place, including the 144k.\n\nYet people continue to believe in the Lord and die in him.\n\nIndeed, because of the rapture of these saints, people give their life to the Lord.","dt":"2023-12-29T07:02:54","s":["ur8fxzz129"]},{"m":"This shows many were about to die; the great tribulation was yet unfolding, but in death was victory.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:34:07","s":["rjravjxbpj"]}],"19":[{"m":"The first harvest was of the righteous, but this second harvest was that of the wicked, to be destroyed in the winepress of the wrath of God.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:35:53","s":["sz8p2a5obl"]}],"20":[{"m":"This battle between Christ and his saints and the antichrist and his armies,\n\nIt takes place in the earth 🌎 and it is a physical battle.\n\nHow does it occur, or does the Lord throw in the supernatural to champion his own cause?\n\nThe enemies are destroyed.","dt":"2023-12-29T07:09:49","s":["v87nce4t22"]}]},"16":{"6":[{"m":"Hm...\nThe judgement of the Lord, his justice system, is right.","dt":"2022-12-28T23:10:32","s":["sukyc9yp2t"]}],"11":[{"m":"How did darkness cause the people pain?\n\nWe see in the next verse that their pain was related to the sores.\nIt could even be possible that the darkness worsened their pain from the sores, or maybe it was solely in reference to the sores and the darkness did not directly cause the pain.","dt":"2023-12-29T08:17:03","s":["f5nbw4dilx"]}],"14":[{"m":"Was this literal, or did these spirits possess ambassadors for the dragon 🐲 who then did work miracles?\n\nIt could be literal spirits who took on bodies. At this point in time there was no doubt 🤷‍♂️ of the existence of the supernatural and of God and godlike beings.\n\nSuch spirits made literal would not be unusual.","dt":"2023-12-29T08:21:16","s":["vvuf0d7xhc"]},{"m":"The nations of the earth 🌎 are gathered to battle the coming invasion of the sky people;\n\nOf the aliens from the sky, whom some earthlings have defected to, much to their shame.\n\nSo now all earth 🌎 needs to unite for that great battle.\n\nSuch a narrative as above is very likely the alibi 🙆.\n\nEarth 🌎 and men at war to save the earth 🌎. Whiles the truth is that it is the antichrist who is the enemy of man and the earth 🌎.\n\nSuch deception and wickedness from the devil 👿. Turning men against their own salvation and making them fight in a war against their own side.\n\nHe is indeed the father of lies 🤥.","dt":"2023-12-29T08:29:41","s":["1viwrcw9gv"]}],"18":[{"m":"These earthquakes and the words 'It is done' came to finalize all things.\n\nMeanwhile, there were earlier great earthquakes which men might assume was the earthquake to end all things... Just like we have been expecting the end and the coming of the Lord, and there have been many points in history that some of these end-time events happened and men were quick to jump at it and assume the end.\n\nSo also with these revelations we must constantly watch, so we keep in pace with God and His promptings through his Spirit, lest we jump ahead of ourselves.","dt":"2025-05-29T12:44:40","s":["zirffvdsmg"]}],"13":[{"m":"Three frogs, one from each mouth 👄 of the three persons.","dt":"2023-12-29T08:18:39","s":["sq5uvxeq3m"]}],"15":[{"m":"Even as close to the end of time as this period in time is, Jesus yet comes as a thief, because his coming is in a few years — maximum three and a half — yet the exact time is not known.\n\nBelievers must be on the watch to the end. Unto his appearing.","dt":"2023-12-29T08:25:23","s":["9m2071ey1k"]}]},"17":{"10":[{"m":"Is it not amazing that these prophecies are in plain sight, so you would expect that as these prophecies are fulfilled,\n\nThe world will believe because it is happening exactly as prophesied...\n\nBut the devil 👿 and his cohorts are clandestine in their approach and will hide as much as possible 🙆 so these words can't be linked to him.\n\nThis way he can continue his agenda unhindered.","dt":"2022-12-30T08:42:44","s":["t8q8tn17qr"]}]},"19":{"14":[{"m":"These armies in heaven and their clothing point to them being the saints 😇","dt":"2022-12-30T09:58:47","s":["i233gxh5dp"]}],"16":[{"m":"Jesus is King of kings 👑 and Lord of lords...\n\nAnd what better place to affirm this than in the book of Revelations.","dt":"2022-12-30T09:41:09","s":["xltgqcibu7"]}],"17":[{"m":"Oh, the heavens and the ways of spirit influence on the earth 🌎 and matter.\n\nSee how the birds of the air are called to this feast.\n\nIn the natural, you would see and wonder about where all these birds came from. It would seem as if they were summoned.\n\nAnd indeed they were. In the spirit there was a clear summons, but in the natural you think they came by themselves.","dt":"2022-12-30T09:57:05","s":["178gwoanwf"]}]},"20":{"4":[{"m":"A glimpse into eternity\n\nWhy was it possible for the devil in Rev 20:4-10 to come back and deceive the nations after a thousand years? And this was under the Christ and the saints.\n\nAnd I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years. But the rest of the dead lived not again until the thousand years were finished. This is the first resurrection. Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign with him a thousand years.\nAnd when the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison, And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea. And they went up on the breadth of the earth, and compassed the camp of the saints about, and the beloved city: and fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them. And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.\n\nThe question I ask is this: what kind of system was being run that allowed such rebellion, even to the point of the devil amassing an army for himself? Only for that army and the devil to be destroyed once and for all with all evil men.\n\nI think it is a similar system, in a sense, that God is running now, where we live in a world where men call the shots. We have free will and freely exercise it.\n\nIt seems evil is running amok perpetually, but in the scheme of God this will come to an end. We are flesh and mortal, so this evil world seems to go on and on, but to God it is but just a few moments in time and it will all be over.\n\nSo also in the reign of Christ and the saints we see the reign a thousand years. Yes, wow, a thousand years is a long time, but it is mentioned in just a single verse as if it is nothing.\n\nAnd during those thousand years there will be order and righteousness and the goodness of the Lord, but men will still be free-willed.\n\nThat is why after the thousand years, when the devil is let loose one more time, he is able to deceive the nations again.\n\nThis shows in the rule of God and his Christ men could still choose to rebel. And they did when the opportunity came.\n\nSo it is not truly that God will wave some magic wand and all men will be righteous and holy and love him.\n\nNo, not at all, just that under his reign, righteousness and justice will be the order of the day.\n\nUntil once more the devil is let loose and he begins his deception. I just wonder, will the men of that time know about the prophecy in the book of Revelations?\n\nWill they know that they are just part of a play book, and the devil himself is also within that play book? And that the words of the devil and the seeming liberty with which he is running amok and gathering the nations is only being allowed by God? He, the devil, is really not powerful and independent as he postulates.\n\nThat he has actually been allowed, and this allowance was prophesied thousands of years ago. Will men even be aware of that prophecy for them to resist the devil?\n\nThis makes me wonder, our world we live in today, could it not be the same thing that is going on?\n\nThat we are all just part of God’s play book that was prophesied to the world that then was, and we that are alive today are just acting players in the book.\n\nAnd the devil is only doing so much as he is allowed to. We know the story of the future of our world through prophecies like Revelations, yet the past of our world is shrouded in mystery and shadows. So many unanswered questions, and it seems we just dropped in the middle of nowhere, with no sense of history and of the past to know exactly what is going on.\n\nThere are some hints here and there, but mostly it is just theories.\n\nI believe we are part of a prophecy that was given to a world that lived, and now we, looking into the future, see another world coming and what their own play book will be like, but they will not have that awareness like we do. We are looking into the future and will be alive to witness it, but they will be looking at the past and what will be at that time their present.\n\nHowever, the Spirit of God will continue to give wisdom and prompt men of the future, so men are kept in the ways of righteousness, just as he does in our world today.","dt":"2025-08-21T20:39:32","s":["jqiwh13o4a"]}],"7":[{"m":"Is it not interesting that this was not the first time that the devil was going to gather an army unsuccessfully against God's chosen ones?\n\nHe did that in the battle at Megiddo,\n\ndid same when he tried to pursue the man child,\n\nhe did same in the dateless past when he tried to be like the Most High and was cast down.\n\nIn all these he led armies of angels and of men.\n\nIt is the case that the devil has been leading men and nations for a really long time, and the cycles keep repeating themselves.\n\nHe has become skilled at deceiving nations of men and leading them against the Lord, in constant rebellion and in final grand wars that end his reign.\n\nBut at the end of time there will be one final battle to end and permanently break this cycle.\n\nAnd a stark memory will be left in the annals of history that rebellion against God does not pay.","dt":"2025-08-21T20:46:42","s":["8cb0cwve35"]}],"9":[{"m":"So the living people of the earth did not like the government of Christ. Imagine a world of strict adherence to the tenets of Christianity. I can only imagine how many people will hate that.","dt":"2025-05-30T11:09:18","s":["m0v6ssu3rn"]}],"15":[{"m":"Will some people escape who were in hell prior? I doubt. But if none escape, why go through the whole judgement process and setting up thrones, if the verdict was final and already known?\n\nI guess it is the same reason for which we hold court sessions today: so the guilty have a fair trial and are proved guilty. Before finally being punished eternally.","dt":"2025-08-21T20:54:03","s":["bxl2gdmauq"]},{"m":"Under this judgement, does that mean some were found written in the book of life? If not, and they were all not found in the book of life, then what was the point of judgement, when obviously they were going to end up all in the lake of fire?\n\nThe counter-argument is that it will be unjust to cast people into the lake of fire without judgement.\n\nThe fact that you are before the all-knowing God who knows you are guilty doesn't make it right that you are condemned without trial and judgement.\n\nFrom the reading of this passage, it seems all righteous resurrected in the first resurrection and reigned a thousand years with Christ, whiles the wicked were reserved for the moment.\n\nWorth noting also is the fact that there will be people alive when Christ first comes — what happens to all those nations who are alive?\n\nDefinitely there will be righteous and wicked amongst them, and the apathetic.\n\nBut at the coming of the Lord the righteous will be taken, the wicked destroyed, and Christ with the saints will rule over this world.\n\nThere will still be wickedness and good, but there will be a general sense of peace and good righteous governance under Christ and his ministers and parliamentarians, i.e. the saints.\n\nBut men will have the choice to be good or wicked, but the wicked will hide because of the righteous reign of Christ.\n\nThat is why after a thousand years, when the devil is released, he is still able to gather nations unto him.\n\nWe see again later in chapter 21 that after the wicked are condemned after the thousand years, the living nations will have the chance to bring their glory to the New Jerusalem. It even says their kings will do that.\n\nI believe these kings will be saints.","dt":"2025-11-25T08:56:17","s":["a6ke9j9z2b"]},{"m":"Why in the world would other books be opened, when at the end of the day it is the book of life that will be the determining factor?\n\nJust imagine this, that a court session and accused persons are brought in; immediately a book is opened and you are told your name is not found in the book, thus you are guilty.\n\nYou are also told the book is not wrong.\n\nYour response would be: at least I have got to know what my crime is, where I erred against the law, rather than to be slapped with such a sentence.\n\nSo therefore other books are opened, which show all the works of men. Then finally the book of life is opened, and whosoever was not found written therein is cast in the lake of fire.\n\nI wonder how long this whole process will take, considering the billions of people to be judged.","dt":"2025-11-28T13:37:59","s":["7m7mhmcf1p"]}],"5":[{"m":"So what becomes of those who were righteous but died before the tribulation? What happens to them? Considering that mention is specifically made of those who were martyred in the tribulation.\n\nBut I think it goes without saying that this resurrection of the martyrs includes the resurrection of all righteous people.\n\nThe same applies to the great white throne judgement. All the wicked dead in all ages time past will be resurrected and judged.","dt":"2025-11-25T08:45:37","s":["3hfgrunk17"]}],"11":[{"m":"From the sound of this verse, the judgement was completed within a period, because the earth and the heavens fled away, then the judgement, after which the new heavens and earth were formed, in which is no evil or anything that defileth.\n\nSo all of these judgements must have been completed before the new heavens and earth, but after the old earth and heaven fled away.","dt":"2025-11-28T14:01:08","s":["48tr5qva4d"]}]},"21":{"3":[{"m":"AMEEENNNNN... LET GOD DWELL WITH US AND...","dt":"2022-12-30T10:15:22","s":["6of379qpzk"]}],"5":[{"m":"True and faithful, true and enduring... Will come true for sure.","dt":"2022-12-30T10:12:03","s":["xbaybc3ezn"]}],"7":[{"m":"Kaiyaaa... We are sons of God oo 🤭... But here he says he shall be our Father and we his son...\n\nAt this time it was not just mere profession, but this statement has been proven true by all the hardships of the end time. And not just the end time, but our own hardship in all of Christian history.","dt":"2022-12-30T10:14:18","s":["ccpggrr5ij"]}],"24":[{"m":"So there will be saved nations outside the New Jerusalem who will enjoy the reign of Christ because they are saved as well.\n\nWhat then is the criteria for being a citizen of the New Jerusalem compared to being among the nations?\n\nMartyrdom for Christ during the tribulation, and I think having given your all and your very life in the service of Christ.\n\nI had wanted to type that having died believing in Jesus.\n\nBut as we see today, there are many Christians who believe but are not too serious with their Christian lives.\n\nI believe God will decide who goes where.\n\nBut I believe those who really give their lives to God will inherit the kingdom, as taught in the Holy Scriptures severally.","dt":"2025-11-25T09:02:57","s":["3gjc373dkm"]}],"12":[{"m":"The supernatural and the natural interplay now. It is totally possible that these angels did not manifest physically but were on guard even as spirits.\n\nThat is more likely; however, it is also likely that glorified saints see angels now, so indeed the natural and spiritual are no longer hidden from us but now seen as one.","dt":"2025-05-30T11:23:11","s":["bf2mwh93i3"]}]}},"John":{"1":{"4":[{"m":"In him was life and light — why need him except that there is death ☠ and darkness?\n\nAnd indeed this world is full of death and darkness.","dt":"2023-01-02T06:42:56","s":["pps0bblgdf"]}],"13":[{"m":"We claim to be the sons of God, and this claim is mere words if not backed by power...\n\nAnyone can claim to be a son of royalty 👑, but till you prove it with wealth, riches and a kingdom,\n\nyou are speaking mere words...\n\nSame thing: we can claim to be the sons of deities. But do we have divine power to back it?\n\nIf not, all would just laugh 😂 and mock at us till we prove it.","dt":"2023-01-02T06:48:07","s":["5ord0xafyl"]}],"15":[{"m":"This was John; he and Jesus were cousins, and yet the divine reverence he had for him.\n\nThis was because John walked by revelation and the Spirit.\n\nIt is just like James and Jude. The brothers of Jesus, yet they called themselves servants of the Lord.\n\nThey knew Jesus by the Spirit.","dt":"2022-10-01T12:24:22","s":["2bhvbrmdhp"]}],"22":[{"m":"The religious leaders and power-drunk leaders of the time sent to quiz John and to find out his true intent.\n\nThey did not seek the truth; they sought to protect their influence at all cost...\n\nIf John had claimed he was Messiah, he would be a threat, and only a matter of time they would have killed him.\n\nSee what they did to Jesus, their Messiah.","dt":"2023-01-02T06:52:01","s":["t0swt6ffuw"]}],"25":[{"m":"Why? What was there about baptism that it was the reserve of prophets or the Christ?\n\nI ran a test and Elijah did not baptize; indeed there is no mention of baptism in the Old Testament.\n\nSo what were these people talking about?\n\nAnd where did John know how to baptize from?\n\nWill need further studies.","dt":"2022-10-01T12:29:12","s":["qwzkpajacq"]},{"m":"In reality they were saying, you are too successful for our liking.\n\nWhy do you baptise successfully when we cannot, because we are not that influential?\n\nWe are actually harboring some jealousy.","dt":"2023-01-02T06:54:23","s":["702jy9jz4o"]},{"m":"What is there about these three people that makes baptism their preserve?\n\nIs there a prophecy that said that the Christ will baptize?\n\nI don't remember Elijah baptizing anyone.\n\nWill search 🔎","dt":"2023-05-07T14:36:07","s":["31gqrdxh13"]}],"26":[{"m":"Who was that prophet referring to?","dt":"2025-01-11T10:14:13","s":["zmx9irdbnt"]}],"31":[{"m":"So all this was to wait for Jesus.\n\nHow long had he been baptising... Jesus was the climax of his ministry; indeed, baptizing Jesus was the fulfillment of his ministry.","dt":"2023-01-02T06:56:31","s":["ausz2mer02"]},{"m":"But they were cousins, so how come he says he knew him not?\n\nThat could likely be because they did not grow up together nor meet each other till this moment in time.\n\nFrom the records we have, the babies 🤱 last met each other when they were in the womb.","dt":"2023-05-09T08:51:13","s":["g8qvycrt7t"]}],"33":[{"m":"Two ✌️ things: upon whom the Spirit descends and remains.\n\nDoes that imply that for some, the Spirit descends and lifts back up, maybe as a sign to them of God's approval...?\n\nBut for the Christ the Spirit stayed with him forever.","dt":"2023-05-09T08:57:18","s":["3etmoqlxys"]},{"m":"What in the world did he mean? They were cousins.\n\nBut this is understandable; they did not live or grow together.\n\nSo he knew him not, except by the Spirit, which is reality.","dt":"2025-01-11T10:18:14","s":["jfer942zdc"]}],"36":[{"m":"These two were eyewitnesses and probably helped give this information for the gospel story.\n\nI'm sure Mary the mother of Jesus and his family, who later became believers, also gave some account of their elder brother.","dt":"2025-01-11T10:20:10","s":["6u7yieh1ko"]}],"43":[{"m":"How was the relationship built earlier for him to go looking for and finding him?","dt":"2023-01-02T09:15:58","s":["tpi88es7ji"]}],"45":[{"m":"How did they know Joseph? Or because Joseph was more or less his surname, it was just a way of calling his full name...\n\nnot necessarily that they knew Joseph.","dt":"2025-01-11T10:22:28","s":["4ooe474rep"]}],"51":[{"m":"When did he see this? We don't know, or maybe it was in reference to his future coming.","dt":"2025-01-11T10:23:45","s":["xlcyxqa0jh"]}],"21":[{"m":"These questions asked of John go to show that\n\n1. they were expecting the Messiah, the Christ\n2. the signs of the Christ were known to them, for instance that Elijah must come first\n\nThey were a colony of Rome at this time and needed to know if their salvation was here.","dt":"2025-01-11T10:10:52","s":["h23w27lkz5"]}]},"2":{"4":[{"m":"Wait oo... What hour was ⏳ he talking about? He had been baptized in the Holy Ghost 👻 already in Jordan.\n\nI'm missing something here.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:08:22","s":["oxir527ssr"]}],"5":[{"m":"How did Mary know this?\n\nDoesn't this debunk the theory that Jesus never performed a single miracle till he was baptized and started his public ministry?\n\nThis statement, it indicates Mary knew that he would likely give some senseless instruction, as the case is with most supernatural instruction.\n\nIf you are not of faith you won't even bother doing it.\n\nShe prepped them up for it.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:09:28","s":["tt8xtv2say"]}],"8":[{"m":"So at which point did the water turn to wine 🍷?\n\nI suspect not when they filled the pots, not when they fetched from the pots, but when they bore the water and en route to the governor.\n\nThat is when the miracle took place.\n\nThere is always that faith element, that additional impulse and action that does not make sense.\nIt is at that point the Lord always shows up.\n\nLike the blind men, cripples and lepers — he would often ask, do you believe I am able to do this?\n\nThe moment they affirm, bam 🤯 the miracle would take place.\n\nFor the 10 lepers, when they were on their way, then the miracle took place.","dt":"2023-05-09T09:46:40","s":["p8k2tq7fo2"]}],"12":[{"m":"John does not give us the many happenings in Capernaum, but the other gospels do.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:19:32","s":["n7tpx3nq8y"]},{"m":"So in this account by John, at which point did Jesus fast the forty days and nights of the other accounts?\n\nAnd we see John give a chronological order of events from day one to day three after baptism.\n\nSo when did Jesus go fasting?","dt":"2023-05-09T09:49:33","s":["edn7j3pg9x"]}],"19":[{"m":"What was the point of this parable... Jesus hid the meaning of what he actually wanted to say in this parable, and of course they misunderstood him...\n\nHe did not bother correcting their error or clarifying his statement.\n\nIt thus means that Jesus hid the things of the kingdom in plain sight.\n\nThe question then is WHY. Was it a case of not casting your pearls before swine 🐽... Because these people either ways will not listen 👂 to him.\n\nRaising the dead and all these miracles did not change them.","dt":"2021-12-14T17:35:26","s":["bl9xwardjc"]},{"m":"These parables of Jesus. He publicly told them exactly what would happen to him, but it was hidden in a mystery.\n\nA mystery only his disciples would later understand, and this strengthened their faith more.\n\nHe that hath will more be given.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:18:14","s":["azdcba5rxb"]},{"m":"Jesus knew from the very beginning what was going to happen to him and what he was going to do about it.\n\nThere was no one like Jesus.\n\nWho was lord over every situation from start to finish 🏁.\n\nHe indeed is the author and finisher 🏁 of our faith.\n\nNot even John the Baptist could be steadfast in faith, for at a point he was offended and questioned the Christ.\n\nSame with Elijah, who gave up at a point in his ministry, of whose power and spirit John was.\n\nThere was none like Jesus.","dt":"2023-05-09T09:56:36","s":["mtabfs4oks"]}],"21":[{"m":"Is this where Paul got the thought of our bodies being the temple of God?\n\nBut the book of Corinthians was written before John; however, the oral tradition was definitely in circulation before any writings were even done.","dt":"2025-01-28T08:45:53","s":["zni5yockq4"]}]},"3":{"3":[{"m":"You are right in your observation that I am sent from God.\n\nThis I tell you, most definitely no man can enter into the kingdom of God except he is born again.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:23:14","s":["au5kj911go"]}],"8":[{"m":"So is everyone born of the wind 🍃. This verse I believe talks of oneness with the wind / the Spirit.\n\nI am not the one replacing wind with 🧚‍♂️ spirit or vice versa.\n\nIn the Greek, the word spirit is pneuma, and is the same word used for wind.\n\nI can relate to this because in my language, Ga, the word for spirit is similar to the word for breath.\n\nJesus is saying that just as you can only hear the sound of the wind but cannot tell its path, so are the ways of the Spirit and the one born of the Spirit.\n\nIn essence, the one born of the Spirit is spirit — he acts, moves and exhibits the same traits as the Spirit.","dt":"2021-12-15T07:30:49","s":["ys334gwasu"]},{"m":"Oh Jesus, the things he knew, the understanding he had and the revelations — these came in his personal dealing with God in prayer.\n\nOnly God knows what other things he had to say, but no one could bear them.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:27:02","s":["khhpdf64ze"]}],"12":[{"m":"I understand Nicodemus. It is not easy to believe that a man can or must be born again... even if it is implied in some esoteric way.","dt":"2021-12-15T07:47:51","s":["vktcez2xcf"]},{"m":"These things pertain to man and the earth 🌎.\n\nHe did not believe, being a teacher of the law, because he did not understand it.\n\nThough understanding is not a prerequisite to believing.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:29:28","s":["ywcz1ograq"]},{"m":"This could mean that the answer to Nicodemus's question as to how one could be born again pertains to heavenly things.\n\nThe how part of the question was more intriguing, for lack of a better word, than just merely stating the facts.\n\nIt was in response to the question of how that Jesus begins to talk of heavenly things and the movement of the Spirit-born being akin to that of the wind.","dt":"2025-01-29T07:47:56","s":["pzespq4tvp"]}],"13":[{"m":"What does Jesus mean by he is in heaven?\n\nThe Amplified explains it as the Son of Man who dwells, has his home in heaven.\n\nJohn 3:13 AMPC\nAnd yet no one has ever gone up to heaven, but there is One Who has come down from heaven–the Son of Man [Himself], Who is (dwells, has His home) in heaven.","dt":"2021-12-15T07:59:34","s":["c8e0ebdrq9"]},{"m":"Jesus was not just aware by some revelation that he came from heaven, in the sense of the way men of God or prophets are sent from God, so in a sense they are from God.\n\nNo, he, Jesus, lived there, had memories and was just continuing his eternal life temporarily in the earth 🌎 and eternally in the heavens.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:33:58","s":["gnmmsv59io"]},{"m":"Little wonder some people thought he was Elijah come down again.","dt":"2025-01-29T07:41:51","s":["2jy9kw33hl"]}],"15":[{"m":"It's almost like Jesus had the complete script of his life.\n\nHe knew what was to happen to him from the very beginning.\n\nIt was all outlined in scripture, and he had read them and had understanding of them that none other had, because he was part of the inspiration behind the writings.\n\nHe was the word of God.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:36:18","s":["hbxs761z3y"]}],"18":[{"m":"Just like Adam, the son of God, had what we would now consider as superhuman in strength 💪, and mind, in that he named all animals without being taught.\n\nSo Jesus was God on earth 🌎 and knew so much but spoke little compared to what he knew.\n\nHe was full of grace, as John said.\n\nJesus was likely melchor, considering his straightforwardness at times, combined with his compassion.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:41:37","s":["ayt71npibf"]}],"29":[{"m":"John alludes to himself as being the friend of the bridegroom, yet when he was in trouble he was not helped by his friend, until eventually he was beheaded.\n\nNo wonder John became offended in him...\n\nIn reality John and Jesus were not friends in ministry.\n\nThey did not even complement each other's ministry — John's ministry was to be subject to that of Christ's.\n\nIndeed in the beginning it looked like John's ministry was meant to last, but alas it was cut short after having finished his assignment of ushering in the ministry of Jesus.\n\nWe have to be careful and understand our roles in people's lives and ministries without pushing it too far.","dt":"2025-01-30T08:11:42","s":["09xjjxjtor"]}],"30":[{"m":"Wow... Such a sense of self. Such self-awareness... He knew he must decrease.\n\nWho wants to decrease and actually accepts his lot is to decrease?","dt":"2021-12-15T08:39:25","s":["ygt83ftrmv"]},{"m":"Oh, such depth of understanding of his calling.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:43:03","s":["7nmdadwu63"]},{"m":"In essence Jesus was going to end John's ministry, and John was more than glad that was happening right before his eyes.\n\nHe must decrease and Jesus increase.\n\nNow John was in prison, and Jesus, who was healing the sick, raising the dead, even men dead for days, watched on as John was beheaded and did nothing.\n\nMaybe indeed John's ministry had come to an end and did not need any resurrection back to life.\n\nI understand why John was offended in him. Maybe John himself was expecting Jesus to manifest his kingship at his first coming. I can imagine John's pain in prison as he heard of the Christ, and yet nothing was done to liberate Jesus's own forerunner.\n\nWho knows these things. That also goes to show that no matter how accurate our relationship with God is, we only know in part always and never complete.\n\nThis is indeed a word of caution to the prophets who assume an omniscient posture but are only men, not God.","dt":"2025-01-29T08:25:25","s":["q4ns00mmqk"]}],"31":[{"m":"How did John get these words of John the Baptist? I believe John himself, being a disciple of John the Baptist, heard from those who remained with the Baptist.","dt":"2023-01-02T17:56:29","s":["kfe3qblhwt"]}],"32":[{"m":"This confirms what I was saying earlier.\n\nJesus lived in heaven, has memories and continued to see and hear the dealings of heaven concerning the earth 🌎, and he testifies of them.\n\nSo men know, believe and know what God's plan is for them.","dt":"2022-10-06T06:45:25","s":["9th0lpm51c"]}],"36":[{"m":"Jesus the Son of Man epitomized the model of and for the redeemed man.\n\nSo now that we are born again, we follow the same example.\n\nJesus did not need the Spirit to do any miracles... He himself is the creator, yet when he became man he needed the Holy Spirit like those of us to be redeemed later.\n\nHe did all this for us, and cleansed us with his one blood for the remission of sins.","dt":"2023-01-02T17:58:55","s":["7lkjwb5rab"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"Hm... Then this whole baptism thing became an issue of public opinion.","dt":"2022-10-06T08:11:29","s":["0o8cjxakx8"]}],"6":[{"m":"The history of the very places they walked was common knowledge.\n\nBut we find ourselves lost as Ghanaians... The stories have died; we have let urbanization and so-called education deny us of our heritage.","dt":"2022-10-06T08:16:49","s":["648l3smn1v"]}],"12":[{"m":"The woman obviously understood Jesus to be implying that he had something better than what they had.\n\nIt was not really about the water 💦, it was about eternal life.","dt":"2023-01-03T06:45:14","s":["qonuhgwgt3"]}],"17":[{"m":"Ah, now Jesus was about to hit the home 🏡 run 🏃.\n\nHe had her where he wanted her.","dt":"2023-01-03T06:46:48","s":["glow3knwz0"]}],"22":[{"m":"So here he corrected her doctrine but quickly brought her up to speed with the latest event, which even the Jews did not know, that is, now the true believers worship in spirit & truth.","dt":"2023-01-03T06:49:06","s":["hi8a6q2xx5"]}],"26":[{"m":"He easily revealed his identity to the humble and lowly in state.\n\nHe would not cast his pearls before swine. To those who would receive it he told them plainly.","dt":"2022-10-06T08:21:14","s":["bbngf3i3is"]}],"30":[{"m":"Oh, the pain when they heard of his death ☠.\n\nAt his death, the last thing anyone wanted was to be associated with Jesus in any way.\n\nOh, I can imagine the pain, fear 😱 and mockery the disciples experienced.","dt":"2023-05-12T06:44:48","s":["ko9djp1y3k"]}],"34":[{"m":"This woman had run into the city and was bringing the town people to meet him.\n\nThis was not the time to eat, though very hungry.\n\nThe people were coming to meet the Messiah and he was going to wait on them; they were coming to find him ready and in expectancy.\n\nIndeed they would likely host him and feed him more lavishly than his disciples could, which was just a fringe benefit.\n\nHis meat was to do the will of him that sent him.","dt":"2023-01-03T07:55:22","s":["9bopw0pk8r"]}],"38":[{"m":"Is it that the prophets labored and we enter into their labour?","dt":"2022-10-06T08:22:19","s":["9fv7sedyv5"]},{"m":"I asked in my previous notes: is it that the prophets and men of old labored and we enter into their labours?\n\nAnd the answer is yes, they labored in the sense that they yearned and waited for the coming Messiah and died waiting, whiles we just inherited their wait without labour.\n\nAnd now, much more, the early church and apostles have labored and suffered martyrdom etc., and we walk in their labour and doctrine (which through much affliction they learnt).\n\nAnd now it's our turn to labour and others reap our labour.","dt":"2023-08-11T07:40:22","s":["jyigpd718y"]}],"54":[{"m":"This is the second miracle, not of Jesus' ministry, but in Galilee.","dt":"2025-01-30T08:56:27","s":["f21v60arwl"]},{"m":"This is the second miracle in Galilee which he did, for he had done many in Jerusalem.\n\nAll this while, in his own home town he had done only 2 miracles.\n\nThis means the first miracle of Jesus in turning water to wine was his first miracle in his home town, not necessarily the first in his ministry.","dt":"2025-02-01T07:37:54","s":["1jm62hx7qo"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why did she believe this story of water that is everlasting?...","dt":"2023-05-12T06:40:38","s":["mbytbhbysl"]},{"m":"How come she believed such a fantabulous story?\n\nOf eternal waters.","dt":"2025-01-30T08:45:03","s":["878lefarwg"]}],"25":[{"m":"...the meshiak, transliterated Messiah and translated Christ in Greek, when he comes...","dt":"2023-01-03T06:55:09","s":["tsdaypsrpm"]}],"42":[{"m":"Jesus was not tied down too much by itinerary.","dt":"2023-05-12T06:47:41","s":["n5l0uju0w0"]}]},"5":{"9":[{"m":"What triggered this move by Jesus... Many people have sought him and exercised great faith for their miracles.\n\nAnd this man gets his handed down to him more or less.\n\nWhat was the mind of God in this?","dt":"2023-01-03T11:33:36","s":["du3b7vwnpv"]},{"m":"Why did he listen 👂 to a random man 👨 who just told him to rise?\n\nUnless he knew Jesus already through the fame of him.\n\nWe are not told, but at this stage of his ministry his fame had spread abroad.\n\nNeedless to say, he did not need to know Jesus to get his healing though. He just needed to believe the words.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:44:11","s":["5g616s9ay6"]},{"m":"Update: subsequent verses let us know the man did not know Jesus, but others did, because a crowd already began forming because of the miracle.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:45:40","s":["8e7zvl32ec"]}],"11":[{"m":"Your religious laws and rites could not cleanse me; now comes a man who heals me regardless of your rites, and in so doing one of your laws is broken.\n\nWho am I to deny my own miracles for your laws, which carried no power to save?\n\nI would rather obey my saviour than your laws.","dt":"2023-05-16T07:28:49","s":["efbf5pg770"]}],"12":[{"m":"Funny...\n\nThese religion hooligans. Their interest was not in the fact that somebody had been healed after 38 years of bondage, but the fact that the person was messing up with their religion laws by carrying his bed of affliction.\n\nIn this life everyone has interests. It is therefore an error on one's part to assume interests for others.\n\nIt might shock 🤯 you: what you think is best for someone, the person might spite and spite you if you insist.","dt":"2022-10-08T07:20:06","s":["6uhnqss988"]}],"14":[{"m":"So here we see the likely cause of the man's infirmity for 38 years... Wow. Sin... smh 🤦‍♂️","dt":"2021-12-16T07:12:00","s":["6x4bj6cc1g"]},{"m":"We see here a possible 🙆 cause of sickness 🤮 — sin.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:47:47","s":["up9slgezq0"]},{"m":"This man had suffered for thirty-eight years.\n\nIf it was sin, what kind of sin was it?\n\nProbably he committed this sin in his younger days. This man may well be in his 60s at this time.","dt":"2023-05-12T07:04:50","s":["5sgv8mwisa"]}],"15":[{"m":"Thur 16th Dec 2021\n\nWhere do I start from? To start with, the man did not know it was Jesus. Does that mean he did not know who Jesus was?\n\nI 🤷‍♂️ doubt.\n\nHe likely might have heard of the teacher who heals the sick 🤮 but did not know who he was in physique.\n\nSo having established the fact that he did not know it was Jesus who was standing before him, how was his response when \"the man\" told him to rise up and walk 🚶?\n\nDid he feel some power run through him for him to know that the power of God was at work? How did he know to take Jesus serious?\n\nPicture this: here was the man by the pool, awaiting the stirring of the waters. And some random rabbi-looking guy asks him to take up his mat and 🚶.\n\nHow likely was he to obey such a command? Only if he felt well. And feeling well he felt, because the verse says\n\nJohn 5:9 NKJV\nAnd immediately the man was made well, took up his bed, and walked. And that day was the Sabbath.\n\nHe was made well.\n\nWhy all this going back and forth? It's because sometimes a lot of stress is made on the faith response needed by the sick to the word of God to make them well.\n\nBut here we see Jesus giving the word and immediately the healing taking place.","dt":"2021-12-16T07:05:40","s":["gev6cmtjyt"]}],"16":[{"m":"They persecuted Jesus and sought to slay him.\n\nI wonder how else they persecuted him.","dt":"2025-02-15T12:04:34","s":["gukbyx35pc"]}],"18":[{"m":"We all call ourselves children of God, but nobody implies in essence to have the attributes or function like God as Jesus was claiming here.\n\nHe was directly saying he functions like God: God works and he does in the same manner.\n\nSuch blasphemy from a common man, or so they thought 💭.","dt":"2023-05-16T07:34:23","s":["drq57oqfhj"]}],"20":[{"m":"Oh, Jesus was indeed the Son of God, the firstborn of God... He sees ALL that the Father does.\n\nNo wonder he was a 🚶 walking wonder.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:49:47","s":["1eov5tbfkl"]}],"23":[{"m":"We see the authority of the Father and the Son and their joint powers.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:51:31","s":["483e23qc0b"]},{"m":"The kind of comparisons Jesus makes of himself with the Father are not the claims of a man 👨🏿.\n\nHe's claiming divinity not with the other gods of the heathen 🔥 but with God Almighty.\n\nIncluding claims of divine judgement and life sources.","dt":"2023-05-16T07:50:47","s":["op3ru545ch"]}],"25":[{"m":"The dead that hear — if they are dead, how do they hear?\n\nThis was spiritual death, I believe. The call to come to life in Christ, and as many as heed will live.","dt":"2022-10-08T07:27:47","s":["cd0j3wcgjq"]}],"27":[{"m":"He had been given this authority to judge because he also is man 👨 and understands human beings better.\n\nOur weaknesses and flaws.","dt":"2022-10-08T07:28:54","s":["lvf1r84620"]}],"30":[{"m":"As I hear, I judge.","dt":"2021-12-16T07:17:25","s":["ja58hvwv16"]},{"m":"This Jesus, as he hears he judges, and as he sees his Father do, he does.\n\nHe could not do anything of his own accord. And it's the same with us.\n\nWe don't have the power in ourselves. This God has not given to us.\n\nBut rather what we see and hear him do we also do, and that is where the supernatural becomes natural.","dt":"2022-10-08T07:29:56","s":["caa7otmrl6"]},{"m":"We also can do nothing of ourselves except what he gives to us to do.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:53:43","s":["8zsdfzufy2"]},{"m":"By this statement we see the separation of Divinity.\n\nThe separation of God and his will from Jesus and his will.\n\nWe also see his humanity in that he, Jesus, cannot do anything on his own. He relies on seeing what the Father is doing so he can do likewise.\n\nSo he relies on the Father and has no power of his own.\n\nThis was why he spent much time in prayer.\n\nHowever, after his resurrection all power was given unto him.","dt":"2023-05-16T07:59:55","s":["bee1y538qi"]}],"37":[{"m":"What was Jesus implying?\n\nThat he had heard the voice of the Father, and not only that, had seen what no man yet sees and lived — his form or shape.","dt":"2023-09-01T06:23:07","s":["39yx3f7rz6"]}],"44":[{"m":"They were too self-important in their self-dignity one to another to believe this carpenter's son and Nazarene.\n\nThey would have none of his teaching out of envy.\n\nThey did not so much as bother to check the scriptures to confirm; they would have none of him.\n\nHe was in their estimation too small for them, and to think of him as their Messiah. No no.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:56:27","s":["fu7fx5cwuj"]}],"46":[{"m":"He has stated the truth. Even if they did not believe him but believed Moses, they would have been compelled to believe him, because he is plainly spoken of in the law and the prophets.\n\nSo these representatives of God were just seat 💺 occupiers and incompetent, yet will not relinquish their power.\n\nThe devil 👿 had infiltrated the church / synagogue.","dt":"2023-01-03T12:00:15","s":["f0w2n1d51h"]}],"47":[{"m":"The leaders were full of lies 🤥 and hypocrisy.\n\nThey claimed to believe in him, yet their actions prove otherwise.\n\nMoses testified of Jesus; they believe Moses but deny Jesus.","dt":"2023-05-16T08:07:35","s":["zgo84z9chu"]}],"4":[{"m":"What season, we are not told; what triggered the season, we do not know.\n\nHow this pool came about, and if it exists today, again we are not told.","dt":"2023-01-03T11:29:14","s":["oj0atlj87j"]}],"13":[{"m":"Jesus, like any normal person, had limited time, strength 💪 and resources.\nHe came to heal this guy and go do some other stuff.\n\nHe did not come to do a crusade or teaching service.\n\nThere would be time for that. His mission here in healing the man was done.\n\nHe had to go do other stuff.\n\nIn this case he was in the temple area, likely teaching some folks who by now were waiting on him.\n\nNow imagine him going ahead and, being overwhelmed by the crowd, starting another crusade.\n\nSuch erratic behavior, unpredictable, and a total disrespect to those waiting on him.","dt":"2022-10-08T07:24:00","s":["tedql1tttn"]}],"19":[{"m":"The way Jesus spoke and the things he said show how much info he had about GOD and from GOD.\n\nI believe, and scripture witnesses to it, before Jesus came he was with GOD (John 1:1), so they spoke and planned out all this... What he was to do and how he was to go about it.\n\nNow when he came, even as a child he remembered who he was and whose he was the moment he had conscience and was self-aware.\n\nHe was the carpenter's son and played the part all along, knowing who he was. He was GOD.\n\nWe see this all the time... Men playing the average person when indeed they are of immense wealth.\nI have done that myself sometimes, including the knowledge of scriptures I have, yet few know this.","dt":"2026-10-03T05:03:33.924Z","s":["18719mecgj"]}],"39":[{"m":"In essence eternal life is in Jesus.\n\nIf you believe eternal life is in the scriptures, fair enough; they point to me as the one to look up to for eternal life.","dt":"2023-05-16T08:04:59","s":["pyyk645hj3"]}]},"6":{"12":[{"m":"There always seems to be the human factor in the supernatural.\n\nThis verse about Jesus asking for the pieces to be taken and nothing lost bears more study.\n\nSo many questions arise. God gave in abundance for man 👨 to have excess, not to waste it but to save it for future usage.","dt":"2021-12-21T13:30:39","s":["j4uvivntab"]}],"15":[{"m":"Now we see why Jesus often controlled crowds and expectations by telling those healed to keep mute 🔕.\n\nJesus was so complete in himself.","dt":"2021-12-21T13:35:43","s":["62uel2xr7k"]},{"m":"Jesus had the full picture in his glare... Kingship at this time was nothing compared to the glory of suffering on the cross, the reign over the whole world 🗺.","dt":"2023-01-03T13:59:42","s":["nmt4jq9znr"]}],"20":[{"m":"Did Jesus really mean it?\n\nWe see angels say the same thing when strange appearances do take 🥡 place.\n\nEven Moses told Israel 🇮🇱 not to fear 😱 at Mount Sinai.\n\nThis goes to show that we are not to fear 😱, cos fear is not of God but rather of the fallen man 👨.\n\nThis is so key 🗝: we are to rise above fear of any super 👌 natural 🏞 occurrence.\nFor we are sons of God. Created in his image 🖼 and likeness.\n\nWe fear no evil 😈. Cos fear is of the evil one.\n\nWhy fear at the appearance of a divine 🔮 being, if not that we would get punishment one way or the other?","dt":"2021-12-21T13:45:23","s":["mwnn3gbj4v"]}],"25":[{"m":"I see another angle to this whole Jesus walking 🚶 on water 🌊 stance.\n\nIt was a good way to have some respite, especially from these crowds who wanted to make him king.\n\nBecause they saw the disciples go alone, Jesus not with them, so they hung around presuming he was up the mountain ⛰.","dt":"2023-05-17T08:01:39","s":["ox2ti15mzq"]}],"26":[{"m":"Jesus was wary of being made king 👑 and knew what they wanted.\n\nHe was soon going to drive them away with his doctrine when he started telling them hard truths.\n\nThese same people suddenly abandoned him.","dt":"2023-01-03T14:02:43","s":["0rqm9eeeja"]}],"29":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 Believing itself is work. That is the work of God. It's akin to salvation. A concept in which lie many doors and packages 📦","dt":"2021-12-21T13:47:59","s":["qzy0kc1dg4"]}],"44":[{"m":"Unless he draws us.","dt":"2023-01-03T14:04:07","s":["unrrgp8ij3"]}],"45":[{"m":"I'm sure some before this time might have argued that this verse is not literal but figurative.\n\nBecause how in the world 🗺 can God Almighty come down to teach men?\n\nYet it was literal and was fulfilled in Christ.\n\nIndeed we need to be guided by the Spirit of God to understand the words of God.","dt":"2023-12-27T04:46:57","s":["xk7e16g7b8"]}],"53":[{"m":"Ah... That's the punch 👊 line that drove most of them away.\n\nIt seems almost that Jesus did this deliberately to drive them away from him and from making him king, by teaching them hard doctrine which, though true, is difficult to accept according to their culture and beliefs.","dt":"2023-01-03T14:05:31","s":["9m2zmgmjn7"]}],"55":[{"m":"Ei Jesus, making matters worse... His coming from heaven was bad enough, but to give his flesh? 😕","dt":"2021-12-21T14:01:01","s":["9sy1h1yftt"]}],"57":[{"m":"Jesus lives by the Father, his source, and has learnt to fully depend on him to live even his daily life.\n\nSo also we live by the flesh and blood of Jesus and so ought to learn to live dependent on him.","dt":"2023-05-19T06:54:41","s":["a68wq67a1h"]}],"60":[{"m":"It appeared Jesus was saying things that might offend them and reveal the true state of their heart.\n\nThese people wanted to make him king 👑 after he fed them, and they concluded he was the Messiah.\n\nJesus knew this all along; that was why he was careful in fully disclosing his identity.\n\nHere they were getting offended at him.\n\nPeople who a while ago were going to make him king 👑.","dt":"2022-10-27T12:41:37","s":["tpcnf40y0p"]}],"63":[{"m":"Spirit words, not flesh, not carnal.","dt":"2021-12-21T14:02:26","s":["n5g1y7z2ha"]}],"66":[{"m":"The moment Jesus started showing them that he wasn't just some great prophet to be just followed and emulated but was the source of eternal life and must depend on him as a man depends on God, they began to leave...\n\nWho did he think he was to claim such divine traits?\n\nPeter and Co. stayed because they had already discerned who he was. He was the Messiah.","dt":"2023-05-19T07:05:20","s":["o2pe8iy4mg"]},{"m":"It seems Jesus was teaching heresies and making himself some divine being.\n\nNo wonder the leaders said he \"deceiveth the people\", the common people.\n\nThe only problem was that he had such undeniable proof backing what he was saying.\n\nSo strong and undeniable was the power he wielded that they now had to attribute it to the prince 🤴 of demons 👹... Beelzebub.","dt":"2023-05-19T07:19:34","s":["0av4z39mdd"]}],"71":[{"m":"Why were they hanging around when they knew they did not believe him?\n\nProbably to see what would become of this braggart who claims to be the Messiah.\n\nThey knew the Messiah would come, but he was to be a ruler, and this Jesus was no ruler.\n\nThere was nothing noble about him. They had checked him out and his background, and he was a carpenter, the son of a carpenter.\n\nBut Jesus is so gracious, so in all this he did the works that no other did do, so that all would be without excuse.\n\nHe himself said that if you do not believe me for me, at least let my works speak for me.\n\nJohn 15:24 KJV\nIf I had not done among them the works which none other man did, they had not had sin: but now have they both seen and hated both me and my Father.\n\nBelieve the works, he appealed to them.\n\nJohn 10:38 KJV\nBut if I do, though ye believe not me, believe the works: that ye may know, and believe, that the Father is in me, and I in him.","dt":"2023-01-05T03:43:43","s":["mjl3i03yby"]}],"14":[{"m":"Could this be making reference to the words of Moses in\nDeuteronomy 18:15 KJV\nThe LORD thy God will raise up unto thee a Prophet from the midst of thee, of thy brethren, like unto me; unto him ye shall hearken;\n\nAnd yes, those are words this crowd is making reference to.\n\nFor in Acts Peter quotes the same.\n\nActs 3:22 KJV\nFor Moses truly said unto the fathers, A prophet shall the Lord your God raise up unto you of your brethren, like unto me; him shall ye hear in all things whatsoever he shall say unto you.","dt":"2023-12-27T04:44:52","s":["f4g94bf5ac"]}],"42":[{"m":"Jesus ever spoke to them in parables. He never cast his pearls 🍐 before swine.\n\nAnd Jesus insists he is from heaven though he was born here. He predates his birth.\n\nHow about us?","dt":"2021-12-21T13:56:32","s":["revyu4o1an"]}],"62":[{"m":"What was Jesus doing when he was up where he used to be before?","dt":"2023-01-03T14:07:56","s":["o459ul6890"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"John 7:1-2 KJV\nAfter these things Jesus walked in Galilee: for he would not walk in Jewry, because the Jews sought to kill him. Now the Jews' feast of tabernacles was at hand.\n\nSee how ironic these 2 verses are... They wanted to kill their salvation in verse one, and then right in verse two they go through a laborious ritual to please the Lord, trusting that he would send their salvation.\n\nMeanwhile their salvation was right with them — what an irony.\n\nAnd in many ways in life this happens to us. Say you struggle with prayerlessness and you look around, guy, and you have no prayerful friends.\n\nAnd those who try getting you to prayer meetings, you hate and stonewall them.\n\nSame with, say, drinking 🍻. You want to stop, yet your social circle 😶 is filled with drunks.\n\nYou wishfully want to change but are not taking the needed steps.","dt":"2023-09-28T17:38:44","s":["myaihdwb5u"]}],"4":[{"m":"I guess his brethren not believing in him is expected.\n\nFamily 👪 sometimes is not the most supportive, and anyways they played together as kids 🧒 and now their elder brother claims to be Messiah??\n\nAnd in this wise they were wrong. Jesus did not seek to be known. Rather he hid and did many secret miracles.\n\nPer his SOP, the view the world and crowds had of Jesus was short 🍰 term. They did not know of all his miracles because he hid them, lest they obviously would have made him king 👑.","dt":"2021-12-26T04:23:48","s":["cm3vwukgm8"]}],"11":[{"m":"As if they believed or longed for him.\n\nThey just hated him.","dt":"2021-12-26T04:30:06","s":["ag6in1l3o4"]},{"m":"Where was he hiding the whole time?\n\nI can imagine Jesus covering his head with his hood to avoid being recognized.\n\nHe must have done a pretty good job for him not to have been seen, considering how popular he was.\n\nThe very thought of Jesus moving in and out of the people in secrecy is quite a thought 💭.","dt":"2025-03-24T07:05:02","s":["8ijsgrrm12"]}],"36":[{"m":"Jesus was often speaking one hidden thing or another, leaving much room open for all kinds of interpretation, and sometimes he taught them the truth, or at least did so to his disciples.","dt":"2023-05-19T07:46:59","s":["lhjowc3z2b"]}],"38":[{"m":"Kabado... Glory to God.\n\nThe Holy Spirit to be poured forth like rivers... In abundance to fill the thirst of the hungry.","dt":"2023-01-05T03:56:50","s":["ovufmum6g9"]},{"m":"Jesus could not have stayed in active ministry for too long.\n\nHe being the Christ would have been made king 👑 by force by the people.\n\nHe was too powerful to be left walking about for years just reaching out to the poor and destitute.\n\nNo wonder after just 3 years he died.\n\nHis purpose on earth at this time was to be a sacrificial lamb. And which he did.","dt":"2025-03-24T07:19:04","s":["dgqoj5t3g5"]}],"41":[{"m":"He indeed is the Christ; who else can make such bold claims of himself?\n\nTelling men to come to him... No ordinary man or even prophet can say such things.\n\nMoses never asked that if any thirsts he should come to him.\n\nThough Jesus avoided saying it directly, especially in public, his words pointed to none other than the Christ.","dt":"2023-01-05T08:18:11","s":["bhnfc3srkr"]}],"42":[{"m":"All manner of interpretation and standards being used to determine if he was the Messiah.\n\nSome who were knowledgeable knew he was to be born in Bethlehem if he was Messiah.\n\nAnd in this wise they were wrong, and Jesus also did not correct them.","dt":"2023-01-05T03:58:54","s":["a0cs6p6a9s"]}],"48":[{"m":"When people have no logical explanation or argument, they just want you to believe them for belief's sake.\n\nSee their line of reasoning: because they were an authority, even if what they were saying was not logical or there was contrary evidence, they still expected to be believed.","dt":"2023-01-05T08:28:21","s":["9ndocztv5b"]}],"52":[{"m":"Now their logic for disbelief 🤨 was that it had never happened before, so even if it was happening, it was not true.","dt":"2023-01-05T08:29:10","s":["ipixniosn3"]},{"m":"The topic of Jesus had successfully dispersed them.","dt":"2025-03-24T07:20:50","s":["wz9fcah7hv"]}],"2":[{"m":"They were still celebrating these things, and by things I mean Passover etc. and other feasts.\n\nThese their fathers, in keeping, won favour before God and wrought many mighty works for them.\n\nIn keeping with these laws, obviously they looked forward to the day their redemption would come.\nWhen a mighty revivalist or king 👑 would be 🐝 raised by God.\n\nTo set them free from the control of the Romans. Yes, they had Herod as king, shrewd and hated, but he was a king who still reported to the Romans.\n\nSo in keeping with these festivals they looked forward to their redemption and Messiah.","dt":"2021-12-26T04:17:53","s":["45m72s7xce"]}],"12":[{"m":"Some loved him, others hated him.\n\nHis haters believed he deceiveth the people, i.e. the common people, who they felt did not know the laws of God and were not as learned as they.\n\nBut the logic of the masses and poor and seemingly not so educated was simple: a man cannot do such mighty works except God be with him,\n\nand if the Messiah comes, is he going to do mightier works than these?","dt":"2021-12-26T04:34:39","s":["lgckjt5h5f"]}],"14":[{"m":"This Jesus...","dt":"2025-03-24T07:05:39","s":["j7fcb8qlv5"]}],"53":[{"m":"😀😃😃","dt":"2023-05-19T07:48:59","s":["1kzx419jpd"]}]},"8":{"5":[{"m":"They had so studied Jesus, his words and his doctrine, they knew he would not want to condemn the woman to death ☠.\n\nHaving such knowledge of Jesus, a knowledge that powerful to bring eternal life, yet they were not changed.\nSad 😔\n\nRather they sought to use it as a form of entrapment.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:13:36","s":["bbfzrm4lx8"]},{"m":"They thought to trap him, but what they didn't envisage was that with every test they were placing him on a higher pedestal.\n\nIn this instance, by testing him this way, they were unconsciously placing him on the same pedestal with Moses.\n\nOf course he was greater, but they did not think he was even a true prophet, so to do this and promote Jesus.","dt":"2023-05-20T08:28:24","s":["oaznr51cw7"]}],"7":[{"m":"They had handed over their authority to Jesus, because here without Jesus's go-ahead they would not act, and upon Jesus's answer they turned away — that was how powerful his influence was.\n\nIn reality they did not hand over their authority; Jesus demonstrated greater authority than them, both in word and backed by deeds of miracles.\n\nSuch a powerful combination could not be countered by these powerless leaders.\n\nThey hated him the more.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:17:21","s":["h2umi1defn"]}],"9":[{"m":"Are we not sure these people's sins that were called to mind might have been sexual sins as well, just that they had not been caught?","dt":"2022-10-23T07:43:50","s":["iobzk2466e"]}],"11":[{"m":"He let her go, in public and in the full glare of temple onlookers. Wow, such powerful scenery to show that he came to save that which was lost.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:18:49","s":["977vgyd1y4"]},{"m":"She had had her punishment. She had come this close to death and had gained pardon from this most holy prophet and the Christos himself.","dt":"2023-05-20T08:36:02","s":["nmjwn7psuu"]}],"28":[{"m":"So the things he says he was taught by the Father. He had to be enlightened because he came as a man.","dt":"2022-10-23T07:46:51","s":["71p420ygo3"]},{"m":"This is akin to Paul saying that had they known these things, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.","dt":"2023-05-22T06:27:45","s":["pbura0s25o"]}],"29":[{"m":"So God is with us 🙏 as we are with him. He doesn't leave us alone.","dt":"2022-10-23T07:47:43","s":["lucil9ty8t"]}],"30":[{"m":"The spirit and conviction of these words struck the heart and many believed.\n\nIndeed it is the Spirit that quickeneth and gives life... The flesh counts for nothing.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:29:57","s":["noa75jjnmz"]}],"48":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔. What was it about Jesus that made him look like or sound like one with a devil 👿?\n\nI think because he said words which no man ever did speak. And you know how, when people can't seem to fathom a thing, they attribute it to the supernatural.\n\nIn this case they did not want to attribute it to God, because that would mean them admitting he was the Messiah.\n\nSo they attributed the good things and gracious words he spoke to the devil.","dt":"2023-05-22T06:40:57","s":["vjetagfxns"]}],"53":[{"m":"Interesting question 🙋: whom maketh thou thyself?\n\nThey still could not discern him, and even if they could, as the Messiah, they did not think the Messiah was a divine being who predated Abraham.\n\nEven until now that problem exists, to accept that Jesus was divine and God.","dt":"2023-05-22T06:49:54","s":["7bykrw4vmu"]}],"54":[{"m":"The ability to not taste death ☠ if one followed Jesus was an honour the Father had given to him.","dt":"2023-05-22T06:52:23","s":["0uo2igl4k5"]}],"55":[{"m":"Jesus knew the Father, that's one, and he kept the Father's sayings.\n\nIt's one thing to know the truth and a completely different ball game to keep it, as we see here.","dt":"2023-05-22T06:54:04","s":["59uhugh4j5"]}],"59":[{"m":"How did he do this? Is it that they were blinded from recognizing him, or he disguised 🤢 himself?","dt":"2022-10-23T07:51:43","s":["hwr0loap57"]},{"m":"The latter seems likely from the wording of the verse.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:41:09","s":["dwvqh43wjx"]}],"24":[{"m":"Here also he said it plainly... Pleading his case before these people... yet some would not heed.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:28:08","s":["i4bgi1fjjc"]}]},"9":{"2":[{"m":"Sin can lead to sickness 🤮.","dt":"2023-01-05T09:49:15","s":["gw7yhv6fn0"]}],"18":[{"m":"Why did they not believe? It's not like this was Jesus's first miracle.\n\nThey had earlier accused him of casting out spirits by the power of the devil 👿.\n\nThis miracle could not be attributed to such. He had performed other notable miracles, so what was their problem?","dt":"2023-01-05T15:21:42","s":["pxjti9ure8"]}],"22":[{"m":"Because of 😱 fear and lack of influence and power, they could not give praise to God for the man who had healed their grown-up son who was born blind.\n\nThey could not rejoice and confess the goodness of God because of fear 😱 of the Jews and for public acceptance.\n\nNo wonder Jesus said that he who is ashamed of him in this world, the Lord would also be ashamed of him before his Father.","dt":"2025-03-25T06:37:24","s":["uabkq6k32e"]}],"24":[{"m":"They were trying to force things down his throat and discredit Jesus at all cost.\n\nBut the blind man will have none of that hypocrisy; he was not yet a part of the system.","dt":"2022-10-25T02:34:21","s":["262i1eyg3v"]}],"30":[{"m":"It took such blind honesty to shake these guys awake to the folly of their own logic.","dt":"2023-01-05T15:23:57","s":["gwy5yu6dex"]},{"m":"He wasn't part of the system yet; he was blind and was managing on his own.\n\nSo he hadn't yet been corrupted by the system.\n\nNo wonder, coming in with a clear conscience and possessing his own thoughts without being a man-pleaser, he stated the obvious and most logical conclusion.\n\nBut these people were self-deluded and simply dishonest.\n\nLet's be careful, be it in the corporation or the world, lest we be gagged into submission and dishonesty.\n\nLest our consciences be hurt and weakened till we no longer speak the truth, not even to ourselves.\n\nAnd you couldn't blame the people in Jesus's time who kept mute 🔕. The leaders were ready to cast anyone out and ban him from the system and privileges if they spoke about Jesus as the Messiah.\n\nIf they believed otherwise, that they could freely speak.","dt":"2023-05-24T06:34:44","s":["jbzv7mrju1"]}],"34":[{"m":"He did not even confess Jesus as the Christ; he only reasoned logically that he was of God.\n\nAnd these wicked people cast the man out. A rude awakening for him as to how the world works, and how the so-called custodians of the law of God were more corrupt than any.","dt":"2025-03-25T06:39:59","s":["qjansdj3yn"]},{"m":"Were they not themselves born in sin, as we all are?\n\nOr because he was born blind, they presumed, just as the disciples of Christ asked earlier, that because of sin that was why he was born blind.\n\nYet we all are born in sin. Though of course they meant that it was some really grave sin that was committed which led to him being born blind.","dt":"2025-03-25T06:41:58","s":["iqzkwbkc2f"]}],"37":[{"m":"JESUS did not cast his pearls before swine 🐽...\n\nTo those who were of open, willing and receptive hearts 💕 he plainly told them he was the Christ, but of them that were hardened hypocrites,\n\nhe spoke in parables and confused them all the more... That seeing they may not see...","dt":"2022-10-25T02:38:12","s":["nxk80ls0lq"]}],"40":[{"m":"These guys really hang around Jesus. While some of their colleagues had thrown this man out, others hang around him.\n\nMostly not for good, but to entrap him.","dt":"2023-05-24T06:36:48","s":["ow0rmj8p1a"]}]},"10":{"21":[{"m":"Jesus was an enigma — the people had a certain fixed mindset about how the Messiah ought to be, and this Jesus did not fit.\n\nHowever, he did works which were undeniable, that no man ever did.\n\nSo now they were caught in a dilemma — he did not quite fit the perfect 👌 picture 🖼 they had created.\n\nLord, help us to walk in your truth even when we are at a loss by the deceptions and illusions of the enemy.","dt":"2023-05-24T06:56:47","s":["eblkmr05es"]}],"24":[{"m":"How come it took revelation to know this?\n\nThat means Jesus in his teachings and preaching did not make that his emphasis.\n\nIn fact, rather than talk about who he was, he rather did the works of God and taught about the kingdom of God 👑 from the perspective and with the authority of someone who had been 🐝 there 🤒.\n\nThus Jesus ✝ left the final conclusion as to who he was to the people to judge for themselves, rather than he emphasizing it.\n\nIn fact, Jesus so stuck to this method that the Jewish leaders in their frustration 😤 asked him to tell them plainly if he was the Christ.\n\nJohn 10:24-27,29-33 KJV\nThen came the Jews round about him, and said unto him, How long dost thou make us to doubt? If thou be the Christ, tell us plainly.\n\n[25] Jesus answered them, I told you, and ye believed not: the works that I do in my Father's name, they bear witness of me.\n\n[26] But ye believe not, because ye are not of my sheep, as I said unto you.\n\n[27] My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me:\n\n[29] My Father, which gave them me, is greater than all; and no man is able to pluck them out of my Father's hand.\n\n[30] I and my Father are one.\n\n[31] Then the Jews took up stones again to stone him.\n\n[32] Jesus answered them, Many good works have I shewed you from my Father; for which of those works do ye stone me?\n\n[33] The Jews answered him, saying, For a good work we stone thee not; but for blasphemy; and because that thou, being a man, makest thyself God.\n\nIn the end he told them of his methods. It is better to prove who you are than to just say it without proof. Apparently \"talk is cheap\" is not a modern concept.\n\nWhen he finally told them that I and my Father are one, they sought to stone him... Smh 🤦‍♂️.\n\nThought they wanted to know if he is the Christ???\n\nAnd they knew very well that the Christ is no ordinary man, and yet when he emphasizes his divinity they sought to kill him.\n\nThat shows they did not really want to believe him. Jesus knew this and never gave them attention.\n\nThey were crooks and liars, yet they were the religious heads of the time. Broken heads 🤕","dt":"2021-12-23T08:05:50","s":["0ubjs6qf9o"]}],"33":[{"m":"The Jews understood this statement to mean oneness with God in his deity, not unity of purpose or mind or character.\n\nAnd thus they sought to stone him.\n\nJesus in his response did not deny that he was making reference to his deity, and went further to use Psalms 82:6.","dt":"2023-01-05T16:08:15","s":["3c8pyhmz75"]}],"41":[{"m":"Those who were willing did remember and consider the evidence that came from John about Jesus.\n\nIt was not for lack of evidence that people did not believe he was the Christ,\n\nit was a stony and stubborn heart ♥","dt":"2023-01-05T16:03:01","s":["b7zsk9acwq"]}],"18":[{"m":"Jesus's laying down of his life was not by compulsion.\n\nIt was a free-will offering. He decided to lay it down, though he could have decided otherwise.\n\nIt was part of the bargain.","dt":"2025-03-25T06:47:56","s":["r94d4r69dg"]}],"29":[{"m":"And this saying was put to the test when they finally killed him.\n\nOnly to make matters \"worse\", for they unleashed and released him to live in the heart of many more hundreds who believed in him.","dt":"2025-03-25T06:50:23","s":["hfmc04tucx"]}]},"11":{"9":[{"m":"Jesus indeed faced grave danger even in fulfilling his ministry here in the 🌎.\n\nSo why did he do it?","dt":"2023-05-27T10:56:41","s":["57h31amsrs"]}],"22":[{"m":"That was faith right there.","dt":"2023-01-06T03:40:01","s":["xyfknbedaj"]}],"24":[{"m":"GOD is often accused of taking too long before vindicating his own or answering.\n\nHowever, that is not always the case, as we see here.\n\nMartha thought Jesus was talking about the future resurrection, but Jesus was talking of just a few minutes away.","dt":"2023-06-01T07:04:20","s":["rl4uchfqjf"]}],"26":[{"m":"This statement is true and will be the criteria in the last day for both the dead and the living.\n\nThe key here at this time was that the one who would cause all this to happen was himself present.\n\nSo he could front-load the resurrection and cause it to happen now and not later.\n\n\"I am the resurrection and the life.\"","dt":"2023-01-06T03:44:30","s":["utv2ujk7ya"]}],"36":[{"m":"He might really have wept bad... For them to have concluded his love 😍 for Lazarus by how deep the weeping was.","dt":"2022-10-29T08:24:55","s":["9k0u8v0qza"]},{"m":"Somehow I used to imagine him shed a tear 😢 rather than weep 😭. I guess because I couldn't imagine a Jesus being who he was really weeping.\n\nBut that seems the case as described here.\nIt really was tears of how fallen the natural man had become.","dt":"2023-05-28T09:55:54","s":["79bh3ix22l"]}],"38":[{"m":"Groaned in anger (G 1690), not out of pain of loss but the pain of the suffering that the thief Satan was causing his creation.\n\nHe groaned in his spirit how that man, the master of the earth, the one who was to have dominion in the earth 🌎, was now so weak and beggarly.\n\nMan had been deceived and continues to be.\n\nBut alas, he was here, and here to crush the head of the serpent 🐍.","dt":"2023-01-06T03:49:35","s":["u1igr05h1w"]}],"41":[{"m":"Oh, Jesus was in his full elements... ready to take on the challenge and demonstrate what belief in God produces and the power of the Christ who is the resurrection and the life.\n\nHe was issuing commands and was readying himself for the grand miracle.\n\nHe was groaning in him because of the state of man. Man was fallen and was now reduced to a piece of bread 🍞.\n\nBut he was come to restore all things and man to his previous glory.","dt":"2025-03-28T18:30:02","s":["jz60jxiado"]},{"m":"I thank thee that thou hast heard me?\n\nSo Jesus had already prayed about the situation and had received a hearing from God and knew exactly what to do.\n\nThis was just a replay of what was already discussed.","dt":"2025-03-28T18:37:01","s":["64x3uop9jm"]}],"42":[{"m":"Jesus had already prayed for Lazarus, and now it was time for the prayer to manifest.","dt":"2023-01-06T03:53:42","s":["mwmnrw03oa"]}],"48":[{"m":"So this was what this was all about: their place in the nation.\n\nTo the extent that they seared their conscience against the Messiah and denied the validity of vivid miracles.\n\nHow great their judgement will be.","dt":"2022-10-29T08:28:28","s":["vsyqvopqpo"]},{"m":"They believed more in the power of the Romans to take their place and nation than in the power of God to keep their place and nation.","dt":"2022-10-29T09:36:14","s":["idoxk8v8lb"]},{"m":"The Messiah was to end all rule against Israel 🇮🇱 and to establish God's rule.\n\nThey did not believe Jesus was the Messiah, else this would not have been their concern.\n\nThey had convinced themselves that he did miracles by devils.\n\nThey were evil 😈 men, else even if they did not believe in Jesus, his works would have made them re-think, and even his resurrection.\n\nAs we see in Nicodemus and Joseph of Arimathea.\n\nBut these children of the devil stuck to their ways after all contrary evidence to their claims.","dt":"2023-05-29T06:45:40","s":["slit1lnx9o"]}],"54":[{"m":"Jesus the Son of David ✡ was adapting the ways of David.\n\nHe also stayed around the wilderness even as an escape strategy from his enemies, just as David his father did.","dt":"2023-05-29T06:47:46","s":["y623zu2vqe"]},{"m":"Jesus is the son of David, but he is David's Lord.\n\nBoth are true, but though David is his ancestor, he is not subject to David, but rather the opposite.\n\nJesus is our elder brother, but he is not our buddy-buddy brother; no, he is our saviour and God.\n\nJesus is the son of God as we are sons of God, but he is more than that; he is God.\n\nSo when the Bible makes two statements which sound contrary but are both true,\n\nthere is a greater truth hidden in these seemingly contrary statements, in that both are true, but one truth supersedes the other in manifestation.\n\nSo for instance, Jesus is David's son is true, but Jesus is not subject to David as sons are to fathers. He is David's son only in ancestry but not functionally.\n\nDavid rather is subject to him as his Lord and God, and not just as a statement but in deed and all the ways of divine worship 🛐 and subjection.","dt":"2023-05-29T06:57:02","s":["gu2xsoahz3"]}],"57":[{"m":"Oh, then Jesus's guise really worked.","dt":"2023-05-29T06:58:08","s":["l9fvhwwaek"]},{"m":"Jesus seemed very adept at hiding himself.\n\nNo wonder that even on the day of his arrest Judas had to identify him to them, so they don't miss him.","dt":"2025-03-28T18:40:33","s":["6mkfuvltp0"]}],"8":[{"m":"They were afraid 😨 for their lives and that of their master.\n\nJesus could care less. But I think actually he did care.\n\nHe was human after all.","dt":"2023-05-27T10:58:12","s":["ccfgmesog0"]}],"35":[{"m":"Such a mix of emotions, groaning yet weeping. Groaning in the spirit at death and its pangs against mankind.\n\nJesus knew that one day he would collect the keys from this beast that has caused so much 🙏 pain.","dt":"2023-06-01T07:06:51","s":["4edx8i9u1r"]},{"m":"Of course Jesus did not weep because Lazarus was dead.\n\nHe was weeping at the state of mankind and the pain and tears 😢 brought on by death.\n\nDeath, which had no power over man, had now gained mastery over man.","dt":"2025-03-28T18:33:46","s":["3jn5up0atm"]}]},"12":{"10":[{"m":"Sad 😔 sad 😔.\n\nThese people were just devils 👿 in priest clothing. How could such thoughts come to mind if not that one is controlled by the devil 👿?","dt":"2023-01-06T07:48:03","s":["jcf9tipycy"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why does it start with the salutation 🤝 of \"fear not\"?","dt":"2023-06-01T06:56:48","s":["iiej0zfjoh"]},{"m":"Ei, this Jesus, what a way to enter Jerusalem. This sent a very strong 💪 signal to his enemies.\n\nYou see, he had always remained low and humble in predisposition.\n\nNow here it seems he had stepped up to the challenge and was riding as a king 👑. Though on a colt, which is not kingly.\n\nSuch contrasting scenery, but still it was enough to provoke anger among the leaders and his eventual death ☠","dt":"2023-06-01T07:20:37","s":["kbsgtodpcm"]}],"17":[{"m":"The miracle of raising Lazarus from the dead did great damage to the darkness and affirmed the gospel work more.\n\nNotable miracles are a great way to advance the kingdom 👑","dt":"2023-01-06T09:11:28","s":["yerlxstrsi"]}],"24":[{"m":"How does a corn die 🌽? I mean, do seeds die before germinating?","dt":"2023-01-06T09:13:42","s":["clahqs766q"]},{"m":"Oh, this Jesus... He was full of matter; his tongue 😝 was like the pen 🖋 of a ready writer 📝...\n\nHe uses such beautiful imagery.\n\nThe time of his death ☠ was at hand and the weight 🏋️ of it heavy on his spirit, yet he grew strong and was full of doctrine and the Spirit.\n\nNo wonder in these last days he uttered some of the most powerful words in Christendom.","dt":"2023-01-06T09:17:54","s":["eynw0wqc3m"]}],"30":[{"m":"Jesus did not need assurances that the Father was with him, but the people did.\n\nTo strengthen their faith did the voice come.","dt":"2023-06-01T07:25:13","s":["mylqw7877q"]}],"49":[{"m":"Amen... What I should say and speak","dt":"2022-11-03T06:48:49","s":["n4a5yzgn2z"]}],"3":[{"m":"Have to investigate the cultural significance of this practice, because a woman in the other gospels had done the same, who was a sinner.\n\nI don't want to straightway buy the interpretation that it was their wedding gift to the bridegroom literally.\n\nMeaning they forfeited ever marrying.\n\nEven though 💭 the whole scenery of a woman breaking the alabaster box before her husband-to-be is that of being vulnerable before your suitor, knowing he would understand and take care of you in your vulnerability.","dt":"2023-06-01T07:16:48","s":["u9sg7rpl63"]}]},"13":{"11":[{"m":"So Judas also partook in this feet washing and even the communion.","dt":"2025-04-14T07:19:40","s":["d0dmqyw9t3"]}],"25":[{"m":"This disciple... Actually lay on God Almighty. In this life and in this earth 🌎.\n\nThese ones had such intimate fellowship with God. They beheld his glory and power.\n\nThis Jesus, the son of God... Oh, how I wish Jesus had written 📝 an autobiography for us to know his inner personal thoughts that none of the disciples could even apprehend.\n\nHow did he know he was the son of God if not by the Spirit?\n\nAnd he said that whatever he says and does is according to the Father's will.\n\nThis reminds me of Moses, who spoke face to face with God.\n\nOh, and a greater than Moses is here.","dt":"2023-01-06T14:33:58","s":["mn8m8sfyhp"]}],"31":[{"m":"Wow... The omniscient one.\n\nNow is the Son of man glorified?\n😳 Now after Judas was devil 👿 possessed and maximum damage was about to be unleashed against he, Jesus.\n\nThat was when he confessed this,\nbecause he knew his end would be glorious.","dt":"2023-01-06T14:28:09","s":["u9t9gnpq99"]}]},"14":{"2":[{"m":"So up until this time ⌚, there was no place for man in God's house 🏡.\n\nBut now he goes to prepare a place for man 👨","dt":"2022-11-15T06:57:29","s":["s18jk1mu1c"]},{"m":"What a privilege, to have a dwelling place prepared by Christ himself for us.","dt":"2023-06-06T06:39:10","s":["azq8l6e7id"]}],"6":[{"m":"So to answer where he was going — he was going to the Father.\n\nAnd the way to the Father for us is him.","dt":"2023-01-06T17:58:37","s":["2716jxdyv9"]},{"m":"The way and the place are neither a pathway nor a place; they are persons who are the way and destination.","dt":"2023-01-07T08:14:29","s":["lpd1b0prp6"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why didn't Jesus say here, or even in\nJohn 10:30 (I and my Father are one), or anywhere else in scripture,\n\nthat \"I am the Father\", but rather says whoever has seen me has seen the Father?\n\nIt is this separation of Father and Son that has become the basis for the debate regarding the definition of the Trinity.\n\nBecause Jesus never stated it explicitly, and neither did Paul or the other disciples, that tells us they are different.\n\nIndeed, they being different and the same is explicitly implied by varied scriptures, hence the confusion 😕\n\nHere are my personal conclusions, subject to change upon evidence.\n\nI think Jesus is God. Now imagine this: God wants to come to earth 🌎 and talk to man.\n\nBut God is a Spirit, yet he wants to talk to man face 😔 face... Man to man.\n\nSo now he has to come in a human form, and that is exactly what he does.\n\nBut whiles in human form he still is Spirit on the throne... He created all things including angels and holds everything together by his power.\n\nSo to take on flesh and human form and still be on his throne is the easiest thing ever.\n\nWith this theory, that means the God Abraham saw and ate with was Jesus, or more appropriately Immanuel would be a more apt name.\n\nThat also means that the one who ate with Moses and the elders of Israel 🇮🇱 was Immanuel.\n\nHe it was that spoke to Moses face to face in the tent 🎪 outside the camp.\n\nHe told Aaron and Miriam in their rebellion that Moses, I speak to him face to face; he, Moses, alone has this revelation.\n\nI believe many more things Moses knew of but did not write about in the Pentateuch. He knew this face-to-face God he is experiencing will one day be experienced by all, but they would not know him.\n\nSo in the transfiguration he meets Moses the man of God once more on the mount 🗻. They knew each other already.\n\nI suspect the same came to the three Hebrew boys in the fires of Nebuchadnezzar.\n\nAnd now he is with us, born this time, not just appearing to his prophets but to all.\n\nHe came through birth, the son of man and God, so that he could be legally seen by all.\n\nHe took on himself our infirmities and so qualified to die... A shameful death of the sinful man 👨.\n\nAnd now he is arisen and we have risen with him too. We have exchanged places and carry in us the divine nature 🏞.\n\nWe have become him, sons of man and sons of God.\n\nHe that makes all this possible is the man Jesus by his Spirit. We have become one — literally.","dt":"2023-01-07T09:21:00","s":["ypca2mpxcx"]}],"10":[{"m":"So the notion of oneness with the Father not being literal but referring to attributes goes down the drain.\n\nPhilip asks to see the Father with these his eyes 👀, and the Lord says I am the physical representation of the Father.\n\nThe Father lives in me; my union with the Father is so synchronised that the words and works are actually the Father speaking and doing them.\n\nSuch oneness goes beyond just mere agreement of the Son with the Father.","dt":"2023-01-06T18:05:31","s":["dcejfiip7i"]},{"m":"The Father doeth the works that my words represent.","dt":"2023-06-06T06:41:23","s":["1e55yn89cd"]}],"11":[{"m":"Now the Lord is saying, just believe me, though it sounds unbelievable. At least I have extraordinary works to prove that what I say is true.\n\nIf it were not so, how could I do works that only God can do?","dt":"2023-01-06T18:06:59","s":["yn5wo0oi9h"]},{"m":"This union was the best that words could offer.\n\nAs we draw more and more into God, we would understand these things.\n\nAnd when we finally meet him, our understanding shall be complete and we would know more and more.","dt":"2023-01-07T07:25:32","s":["eiq4ioqc5g"]}],"12":[{"m":"Because I go to my Father, and I will come back to them who believe in me by the Holy Spirit.\n\nAnd that is when they will be endued with power to do greater works.","dt":"2023-01-07T07:29:46","s":["8ipx4ce3td"]}],"17":[{"m":"Why didn't the disciples ask the same questions Thomas and Philip asked when Jesus told them that they know and have seen the Father...\n\nJohn 14:7 KJV\nIf ye had known me, ye should have known my Father also: and from henceforth ye know him, and have seen him.\n\nBecause he had corrected them earlier when they asked that question 🙋,\n\nhe was surprised 🤨 😲 they did not know the Father when he, Jesus, had been with them all this while.\n\nJohn 14:9 KJV\nJesus saith unto him, Have I been so long time with you, and yet hast thou not known me, Philip? he that hath seen me hath seen the Father; and how sayest thou then, Shew us the Father?\n\nAnd now he tells them he will send another person like himself (allos)...\n\nA person they know and obviously have seen (though not stated, but obviously they see him because he dwells with them, and the world cannot see him, implying they could).\n\nAnd they dared not ask the same question they had asked earlier, that \"they know him not, nor have seen him, so he should show him to them\".\n\nEspecially now that Jesus had repeated in an eerily similar way the words 'seeth him, know him and dwelleth in you'.\n\nJohn 14:17 KJV\nEven the Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him; for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you.","dt":"2023-01-07T07:52:00","s":["oj85vep1p4"]},{"m":"The Spirit of truth, the Holy Spirit, was not a topic Christ spoke about until now.\n\nIndeed, in the New Testament it is only John who talks of the Spirit in depth, even in this chapter onwards.\n\nSo a topic and personality Jesus had rarely spoken about, and suddenly he tells his disciples that not only do they know him already but have seen him.\n\nBut he reveals what he means by saying he dwells with them. At this time, who was dwelling with the disciples? He, Jesus.\n\nHe was the Spirit seen in flesh and shall be in them. Remember he said another comforter.\n\nOne like himself. Him in another form, in other words.","dt":"2023-01-08T01:53:53","s":["4y0nu07v07"]}],"18":[{"m":"I will not leave you comfortless.\n\nI will come to you as the Spirit.","dt":"2023-01-08T01:55:03","s":["ce4o69pkuz"]}],"19":[{"m":"And indeed the world saw him no more for good, but his disciples saw him in his physical body, and after his ascension in the person of the Holy Ghost.","dt":"2023-06-06T06:46:55","s":["xj2rseg8ei"]}],"20":[{"m":"After having talked of the Holy Spirit, now he ropes in another dimension of the oneness he and the Father have.\n\nThat is, now there is a oneness of he and the Father that involves man 👨.\n\nNow man 👨🏿 was part of that oneness.\n\nThis additional oneness was spoken of after he spoke of the Spirit, and he himself said in the verse before that it is the day when the Spirit comes to indwell in them that they will understand beyond all doubt 🤷‍♂️ how this oneness is possible 🙆\n\nSo possibly it includes them.","dt":"2023-01-08T01:59:14","s":["t24yyzf194"]}],"26":[{"m":"The wise are spoken to in proverbs and they understand. The Spirit is one with the Father and the Son.\n\nThe Son is one with the Father and they are in perfect agreement one with another...\n\nThe Holy Spirit is sent in the name of the Father.\n\nHe is with the disciples and shall be on them.\n\nAnd yet in heaven we never see three persons sitting on three thrones, or even the Father sitting on his throne with Jesus at his right hand and the Holy Spirit by his side.\n\nNo, we see one throne with one person sitting on it...\n\nHowever, we see symbolism of Christ and symbolisms of the Spirit, but not persons.\n\nCheck the book of Revelation.\n\nIndeed, the times that Christ is seen in bodily form, he is not in or by the throne.\n\nHe is en route to the second coming...\n\nHe that hath ears 👂.","dt":"2022-11-15T07:14:35","s":["lnumukkhkl"]},{"m":"Whom the Father will send — once more bringing the separation between Christ and God.\n\nBut he will send in my name — in my stead — showing once more the oneness; the Father will not send without me.\n\nHe is sending in my name, under my authority.","dt":"2023-01-08T02:04:55","s":["u1yr3c9l6c"]}],"7":[{"m":"If you have known me, the way, ye should have known the place as well.\n\nHe who knows the way knows the destination; he who knows the path knows the place also.\n\nFor every path leads to a place, so if anyone claims to know the path, then he knows where the path leads to.\n\nThat is what knowing the path means in the first place.","dt":"2023-01-08T01:06:12","s":["gjl1qvzbvo"]}],"16":[{"m":"The beginning of the reverse relationship.\n\nJesus was going to the Father & upon arrival another person just like him will also come to the disciples.","dt":"2023-01-07T07:49:39","s":["56e42anpwt"]}],"28":[{"m":"I go away and come again unto you as the Holy Ghost. Twice he has said or insinuated his coming back as the Holy Ghost.\n\nJohn 14:18 KJV\nI will not leave you comfortless: I will come to you.","dt":"2023-01-08T02:06:32","s":["ldjzqvmbwh"]}]},"15":{"3":[{"m":"What does this mean?","dt":"2022-11-15T07:32:22","s":["fzp881jqeo"]}],"8":[{"m":"The Father's glory is that we be disciples... And we have the examples of discipleship in scriptures.\n\nSo today in our world we have to be disciples.","dt":"2022-11-15T07:47:33","s":["b56e5efmzv"]}],"24":[{"m":"Now they are without excuse","dt":"2023-01-08T02:59:00","s":["jxyxlt26up"]}]},"16":{"4":[{"m":"At the beginning he was with them, defending, arguing with the Pharisees etc. His disciples only watching and learning.\n\nBut now he was going; they were going to be on their own.\n\nHe needed to let them know some key 🗝 truth and reemphasise others.\n\nAnd indeed in these final moments he spoke some things that he had never ever spoken of. Setting the foundation for some of the core doctrines of Christ.","dt":"2023-06-07T06:58:30","s":["kgzyq6kucb"]}],"13":[{"m":"Just like Jesus, what he hears he shall speak.","dt":"2023-01-08T03:11:08","s":["do8vg34xbj"]}],"23":[{"m":"Once more he makes reference to that day, when he is gone and comes back as the Spirit.","dt":"2023-01-08T03:13:51","s":["wgil67556d"]}]},"17":{"3":[{"m":"Eternal life defined","dt":"2023-01-08T03:25:25","s":["mcdcri3f39"]},{"m":"And this is life eternal, that they might know thee...\n\nSo eternal life is knowledge, a specific knowledge.\n\nThe knowledge of JESUS","dt":"2025-04-17T09:03:25","s":["6gx7qerj7q"]}],"13":[{"m":"Jesus was going to the Father as planned by them before he ever came.\n\nNow he says this prayer to their hearing; the purpose was to affirm their faith and educate them, so they have joy about this new way of life.","dt":"2023-06-09T06:24:15","s":["jac3h47qk7"]}],"17":[{"m":"God's word is truth.","dt":"2023-01-08T10:57:19","s":["czgulx4gzh"]}],"24":[{"m":"So again confirming Jesus existed before the foundation of the world...","dt":"2022-11-16T12:36:41","s":["bkwzet518m"]},{"m":"So this Jesus, the Father made flesh, the Father incarnate, did not exist when the world 🗺 began.\n\nBut pre-existed the foundation of the world.\n\nI will not be surprised if this is not the first time that God in the flesh has been used by God to reach out to his creation.\n\nWhatever the situation may be, the Word had a purpose before the foundation of the world.\n\nMaybe he did not go by the name Jesus but served his purpose.","dt":"2023-01-08T11:14:28","s":["jkbf94cu5j"]}]},"18":{"8":[{"m":"All through his life Jesus had the absolute control and mastery over every situation. Even his death ☠","dt":"2023-06-09T06:58:20","s":["jdpe9u200v"]}],"19":[{"m":"Why his disciples? Was he not allowed to have disciples?\n\nOr they wanted to imply he was gathering a people to start an insurrection. Hm 🤔, possibly.\n\nThey had accused him of many things, including his claim of king 👑","dt":"2023-06-09T06:56:37","s":["qn8jhksu2z"]}],"26":[{"m":"If his testimony is true, then he saw also the miraculous healing of his kinsman's ear 👂.\n\nWhy then did he not believe? Unless he had bought the narrative of the Pharisees, i.e.\n\nJesus worked miracles by Beelzebub. Smh 🤦🏾","dt":"2022-11-18T13:06:52","s":["970jj4esn2"]}],"28":[{"m":"As for their external religious rites to keep them ceremonially clean, they would not forfeit.\n\nSuch hypocrisy, but to kill an innocent man they definitely would.","dt":"2022-11-18T13:05:23","s":["nwf1v65a38"]}],"5":[{"m":"His betrayal was so obvious, he stood with the enemy.\n\nHe did not even stand aside, let alone think of hiding his betrayal by hanging with the disciples.\n\nRather he stood with the enemy.","dt":"2025-04-18T05:43:58","s":["j91yasu1kz"]}],"12":[{"m":"They bound my savior... Tied him up like a criminal.\n\nAll he ever did was to do good.","dt":"2025-04-18T05:45:33","s":["27nzkl30c4"]},{"m":"Really they did not bind him... he let them do it.\n\nJust like Samson made his own people bind him and take him to the Philistines, and though he could have freed himself, he allowed them to.\n\nEven so Jesus allowed all that happened to him to have happened.","dt":"2025-08-14T08:15:11","s":["xpw2syx5qq"]}],"15":[{"m":"These disciples had normal everyday lives with the people.","dt":"2023-06-09T06:57:26","s":["zvrj83e6ij"]}],"17":[{"m":"John brings more details to this part of the story.\n\nThe different eyewitnesses helped to bring the story of Jesus to light and help us see the historical Jesus and his disciples better.\n\nThey were human.","dt":"2025-04-18T05:47:30","s":["baghrvjzm1"]}],"22":[{"m":"Why didn't Peter and John do anything? Or at least, since John had some influence here, speak up for Jesus?\n\n1. These disciples were ordinary fishermen with not much power and influence; they couldn't even call on lawyers to rise up to the task for Jesus.\n\n2. They were so young 🧒. John was a teenager; maybe it was his innocence that gave him access to the high priest's palace without being pestered like Peter, who likely was much older 🧓. For he had a wife and kids.","dt":"2023-06-09T07:02:29","s":["gzfsgajk81"]}]},"19":{"11":[{"m":"This whole trial of Jesus feels so wrong and so rushed, just to get him killed.","dt":"2023-01-08T17:28:45","s":["lpdf2ws9m5"]}],"18":[{"m":"Was it a mere coincidence that others were to be crucified alongside Jesus, or were these in prison awaiting the day of their crucifixion?\n\nAnd then came Jesus opportunistically, so they had to add them up to him for crucifixion.","dt":"2023-06-10T13:26:27","s":["zpnnaflslv"]}],"28":[{"m":"This makes it sound like he said it out of obligation to fulfill scripture than of true thirst.","dt":"2023-01-08T17:38:26","s":["p4e23bf2ce"]}],"38":[{"m":"Jesus had secret disciples. He could have been a good politician with such connections in places of power.\n\nBut no, he knew his mission.","dt":"2023-01-08T17:40:17","s":["poqfsf2dik"]}],"24":[{"m":"Were they keeping the souvenirs for themselves, as having something belonging to Jesus the Christ?\n\nOr they were just doing it because the material was good quality and they just wanted a piece of it.","dt":"2023-06-11T04:17:34","s":["262pwoqs3u"]}]},"20":{"27":[{"m":"Even at this time they were still not ready to do the gospel work.\n\nThey believed in him, but still were a bunch of fearful Jews who were following this new leader who had just died.\n\nHow could they go out and testify of him to these same Jews?\nThey were ill 🤒 prepared.\n\nWhen Jesus was present, they were powerful because they were under his covering, but now who would cover them...\n\nThat is why he sent the Holy Ghost 👻, their new cover.","dt":"2023-01-08T18:05:25","s":["hp64mu4kb3"]}],"17":[{"m":"Jesus could have given them a detailed breakdown of his death and resurrection, but that would not in any way increase their faith.\n\nThey were just not ready, and he himself left the rest of the work to the Holy Spirit to do.","dt":"2023-01-08T17:59:51","s":["m7xhpx55oh"]}]},"21":{"3":[{"m":"Déjà vu... We have toiled all night and caught nothing.\n\nIt was this similar event that marked their call to be fishers of men, and here we are again... Same thing happening.","dt":"2022-11-18T17:28:39","s":["imliltlq1h"]}],"4":[{"m":"An eerie reminder of their start of ministry with Jesus when he made them fishers of men.\n\nAfter all that had happened the whole week, they were ready to forget all that and go back to their past life.\n\nIt happens to us all. When the reality of life dawns on us.\n\nAnd we being men are more inclined to settle for what we see and sense naturally rather than spiritually.","dt":"2023-01-08T18:09:35","s":["n1rlpypi5o"]}],"5":[{"m":"I 🤔 think at this point, the disciples did not know what to do with this whole Jesus resurrection stuff.\n\nThey were glad he was back, but was he 🙄?\n\nHe did not stay with them like he used to; they were sort of on their own and lacked direction as to what to specifically do.\n\nSo here, they went a-fishing.\nJesus again went pursuing them and caught up with them.","dt":"2023-06-13T05:35:29","s":["x1cy35vj3i"]}],"19":[{"m":"Where did Jesus take him to, and what did they discuss?\n\nLikely Peter's leadership role in the gospel work, and how the others looked up to him, seeing he is likely the older or one of the older.\n\nIndeed John was right in mentioning that the whole world's books cannot contain them.","dt":"2023-06-13T05:49:32","s":["w6n9aftn4j"]}]}},"Luke":{"1":{"6":[{"m":"Walking 🚶 in the ordinances of God blameless did not mean they were without sin.\n\nNo one is without sin, but in the ordinances of God is provision made for cleansing of sins, so anyone who follows the ordinances of God can be blameless.\n\nBlameless in that when you sin, you follow the ordinances laid out for cleansing sin, so you remain blameless.","dt":"2023-03-20T07:35:36","s":["e86ghmkpkb"]}],"13":[{"m":"Is it really that when angels do appear they don't expect you to fear?","dt":"2021-12-04T11:30:36","s":["ffnqgw1g17"]}],"17":[{"m":"We know Elijah worked a lot of miracles but John did not; however, we see that John's life showed us what else Elijah did aside the miracles.\n\nHe turned the hearts 💕 of the fathers to the children and brought many to God.\n\nFor this to have been mentioned, then it was a remarkable and distinct and prominent ministry of his.\n\nI mean, of all the prophets, from Samuel to Malachi, Elijah's reconciliation ministry must have been unique for his spirit to be what John operated in.\n\nWhat is your call? What spirit 🤽‍♂️ are you operating in?","dt":"2023-03-20T07:46:33","s":["d9ni3hkk2l"]}],"20":[{"m":"Punished for his unbelief, yet the words of the angel did not require belief to be fulfilled.\n\nYet Jesus did not many miracles in his hometown because of unbelief.\n\nUnbelief did not stop the miracles, but it did hinder it from happening.\n\nWas that why he put everyone out when raising the dead?\n\nWhether unbelief hindered the supernatural or not, it seems a bad thing. Gabriel, though not hindered by it, punished it.","dt":"2023-03-20T09:18:03","s":["3bbpchcmpx"]}],"24":[{"m":"These were the beginning of strange times in Israel. After centuries of prophetic silence 🤫... Things were taking off again.","dt":"2021-12-04T11:31:55","s":["sqkwqoui6l"]}],"27":[{"m":"Mary, I hear, was about 14 years old at this time.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:15:49","s":["ymlk4kjvdh"]}],"30":[{"m":"What was there about Mary and Joseph that made them the perfect couple 👫 God could use?\n\nJust like Samson's parents, maybe the obscurity of their life and poverty, the virgin Mary, the obedient Joseph etc. met the criteria for the Lamb.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:18:05","s":["l1ypez6g6v"]}],"31":[{"m":"Just like Samson, the angel appeared not to the man but to the woman, the carrier of the seed, and then later to the man.\n\nWhy not to the man first?","dt":"2025-01-08T06:55:32","s":["c3aaw2o1uy"]}],"33":[{"m":"Gabriel said these words so simply, yet they were to span a period of over 2000 years, yet unfulfilled.","dt":"2023-03-20T09:25:04","s":["8luxkcuqtn"]},{"m":"Why did Mary not ask how he was to reign forever, unless she understood that to mean his generations shall forever be the ones on the throne?\n\nI do not know if she understood that to mean he was going to be an immortal, a God-man, so he would have no successor and thus he would reign forever.\n\nI doubt that was how she understood it, even though that is actually exactly what God meant.","dt":"2025-01-08T06:54:20","s":["pjj2r6vkvq"]}],"35":[{"m":"Following customs and traditions, Mary was very young at this time — likely in her teens, early to mid teens.\n\nIt's about time we go back to the youth and let them know the truth of the Bible stories so they rise up to the task.\n\nMany take charge of their life and purpose too late.\n\nYouthfulness is for a purpose. It's the time of your greatest strength 💪","dt":"2023-03-20T09:28:13","s":["in5zm8926f"]},{"m":"This so reminds me of when the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men. This resulted in the birth of men of renown of old.\n\nHere God himself overshadowed Mary and birthed his own son.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:21:12","s":["xn2qg8wh9n"]},{"m":"I wonder if the Old Testament prophets really knew the Messiah would be born and ascend into heaven and come back later as king.\n\nNo one knew that, not even the scribes of the time. No wonder many did not and have still not accepted their Christ.\n\nSo also I believe the book of Revelation and the end times would have many elements not recorded; we may be in for many surprises concerning the end of time.","dt":"2025-01-08T07:00:05","s":["ii7nx21tdt"]}],"38":[{"m":"What a bold statement to be made by a virgin lady, to accept to carry a child whiles a virgin and not married 👰.\n\nIt's so shameful and comes with untold hardships even in these our times, how much more in their strict cultural setup 👆.\n\nShe risked possibly stoning to death and unimaginable shame on her family 👪, yet she accepted.\n\nWhat faith and submission to the plan of God.\n\nShe indeed is blessed.\n\nBut as we count the cost of this acceptance declaration, let's not forget the prize 🏆","dt":"2021-12-04T12:22:13","s":["lm8yvxvptx"]},{"m":"Hmm 🤔. Her receptivity to the word of God was also one of her qualifying features.\n\nBe it unto me according to thy word.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:24:54","s":["pj1xgwk4xm"]}],"44":[{"m":"She felt it. She felt the joy of the baby 🤱. Oh, what a moment, what a day.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:26:35","s":["7gygyr6377"]}],"48":[{"m":"Ah... This is faith. Already she was seeing the generations that would honour him.","dt":"2023-01-08T18:38:46","s":["h8ldy4xwfg"]},{"m":"She knew she carried the Messiah. The long-awaited and promised king 👑.\n\nGod, who knows the reins, sought for a woman who would handle the coming suffering upon her so gallantly.\n\nA woman whose personal needs will not interfere with the work of the Lord.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:33:33","s":["hglgag3a7z"]},{"m":"Yes indeed, knowing that her son was to be the future king of Israel and the long-awaited Christ.\n\nOh, what joy of a mother, indeed of the two mothers, Elizabeth knowing her son was to be forerunner to the Messiah.","dt":"2025-01-08T07:03:00","s":["z7to97u6h7"]}],"50":[{"m":"This goes to show the character of Mary: she feared God.","dt":"2025-01-08T07:01:40","s":["0vj6kigvd3"]}],"62":[{"m":"They made signs to him; was he both deaf and dumb now? It seems so. How else were they making signs for him, if he could hear?","dt":"2025-01-08T07:05:16","s":["kr00uzwvrb"]}],"65":[{"m":"And I believe it was from these sources that Luke got his story.\n\nLike it had become an everyday conversation at a point about the miracle child.\n\nAnd there were some of the people still alive to re-enact the story for Luke to record.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:36:08","s":["f2nbmway4k"]}],"66":[{"m":"And 30 years later John was in the wilderness preaching the kingdom of God, a famous and great man of God.\n\nAt about that time his parents and their compatriots who heard and witnessed these strange things were dead.\n\nBut like all stories, it had been handed down 👇 to the younger generation. Indeed, John's comrades were alive at this time to bear 🍷 witness of these strange times.\n\nHe was indeed a burning 🔥 and shining light.","dt":"2021-12-04T12:38:03","s":["be1wnvrga4"]}],"78":[{"m":"Did they fully understand who the Christ was, that he was God incarnate? Again, from the words of Zechariah, they expected deliverance in their days.\n\nI think Jesus did really disappoint a lot of people's expectations.\n\nAs I think of these things, I can't help but wonder about his second coming; many would be disappointed, as we see already, that he has really delayed.\n\nBut we see already the groundwork being laid for his coming and that of the antichrist.\n\nWhere all eyes will see him. Initially we thought that was figurative, but no, that is now literally possible... All eyes will see him.","dt":"2025-01-08T07:11:12","s":["b01jro423s"]}],"18":[{"m":"You know, sometimes we believe for so long and get disappointed for so many years, that even if an angel 😇 or God himself were to bring us word of hope again, we are too broken to believe.\n\nWe gave up on hope long ago. A similar thing happened to Abraham, and the Bible says he fell on his face and laughed and said, O that Ishmael might live before thee.","dt":"2023-03-20T08:55:37","s":["y8988q6zsa"]}],"47":[{"m":"This song of Mary, her appreciation of God's goodness upon her despite the present shame of pre-marital pregnancy 🤰 and sex.\n\nHer understanding and perspective of the promises of God... Makes me marvel at Mary's age. If she is as young as some theories suggest, because virgin and unmarried 👰 most likely indicated youthfulness.\n\nThen she indeed was a wise young woman. This makes me wonder, what kind of character and person was Mary?\n\nMary the mother of God. Indeed I wonder, what kind of personality was God looking for to be the mother of his son 🤔 Hmm.","dt":"2021-12-04T12:32:27","s":["efeif4e2r2"]}],"56":[{"m":"She abode till Elisabeth delivered John the Baptist.\n\nLikely that was one of the last times they saw each other. By the time John was baptizing, he did not even know his own cousin.\n\nThey did not seem to have any relationship.\n\nI believe the old man Zacharias and Elisabeth died along the line.\n\nThis Spirit-filled John grew and, like Samson, began to be moved by the Holy Ghost.\n\nThe boy Jesus also grew in wisdom and in stature.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:31:30","s":["b8nb8eqesa"]}],"76":[{"m":"This is where the antichrist stole his ideas from.\n\nHe also will have a prophet. Hmm 🤔, indeed.","dt":"2023-03-21T07:37:41","s":["n9hhj4qxe5"]}]},"2":{"7":[{"m":"This verse so simply said — \"there was no room for them in the inn\" — carries with it such depth.\n\nImagine the pain and difficulty of traveling with a wife who is full and is due. The nights of pre-labour and labour pains.\n\nThe search 🔎 for an inn whiles she screamed 😱 in pain.\n\nThe need for a midwife or other women to help.\n\nTo finally settle in a manger, likely a sheep or cow 🐮 shed. There was no room, and no one was willing to sacrifice their place for this woman in labour pains.\n\nThe innkeepers were not ready to have blood in their beautiful rooms, too much work etc., coupled with a woman screaming in pain to disturb their guests.\n\nFor Mary to deliver into a manger really suggests the baby was literally coming and some place, any place at all, needed to be found.\n\nSo in the heat of things she was rushed to the animal shed.\n\nNot to mention the spiritual implications. The devil 👿 doing his best and throwing his worst arsenals to hinder the birth of this child 🧒 who was to be saviour.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:29:38","s":["et95xc4ieg"]},{"m":"Not just her son but her FIRST born son, meaning she was to have others or had others after.","dt":"2023-03-23T12:05:25","s":["mg5nieydsv"]}],"10":[{"m":"Good tidings, the gospel, the good news 📰 to all people.\n\nAnd yet there were some others in pain and discomfort to bring the good news.\n\nMary just delivered this bundle of joy in extraordinary circumstances. The king 👑 of the time was going to come for their heads and bring such never-to-be-forgotten misery upon them and others.\n\nOh, what it takes to bring good news. But it does not take away the goodness of the news 📰, and the angels knew this.\n\nLesson: do not let your joy be stolen and the goodness of a moment be taken away because of suffering and pain that birthed it.\n\nJust as we love and cherish our babies 🤱 despite the pain of birth. So also, because of the reward ahead, we forsake the pain.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:45:33","s":["gdreu57ipe"]}],"12":[{"m":"The symbol of their pain, their scars, was the sign of their glory.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:47:01","s":["smddnu0zqy"]}],"16":[{"m":"Where was the midwife??","dt":"2022-10-02T07:55:10","s":["zhertrvg9a"]},{"m":"They found — only God knows how long they might have searched.","dt":"2025-01-14T08:01:29","s":["85akkxu52i"]},{"m":"Mary takes precedence over Joseph — why is that?","dt":"2025-12-28T05:59:15","s":["4e2p3dxj25"]}],"19":[{"m":"Matters of the heart are as deep waters.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:57:19","s":["gjlp5fvyu3"]},{"m":"Mary kept all these in her heart? How about Joseph? Is something being communicated to us here subtly? Later in the story Joseph completely disappears.\n\nWe are not even told when he did. If he died, at least it should have been mentioned. I mean, who would not want to be actively involved and give their all for a wonderful child like Jesus?\n\nHis absence in the gospels without sufficient evidence is quite deafening.\n\nDid he boycott the family later — did he become aloof and estranged from the whole process later? If so, why was mention not made of it?","dt":"2025-12-28T06:03:10","s":["ut6ww51rj2"]}],"20":[{"m":"Where were all these people when Jesus began his public relations ministry? I just wonder.","dt":"2023-03-23T12:15:53","s":["75uijvtvjn"]},{"m":"Let's imagine these were young teenage shepherds... Isn't it amazing how God uses young people, just like David, a shepherd boy, yet anointed king 👑.\n\nWhiles all these were going on, Israel 🇮🇱 was asleep, oblivious to that which was taking place and about to change their future. I say this of both David ✡ anointed as king 👑 and Jesus born in a manger.\n\nOh Lord, even as an adult use me, and let me not be oblivious to your move of the future among the youth.\n\nNow let's fast forward 33 years, when Jesus was at the peak of his ministry. These were in their 50s.\n\nThey had waited 30 long years. Had they closed 🔐 their hearts 💕 long ago because they awaited the military ⚔ style salvation of Jesus, and no signs of that had taken place?\n\nMaybe they were even nonchalant to Jesus' ministry, or could not place the link that this was the same manger boy.\n\nJesus did not go telling his story of being the manger boy.\n\nIndeed, he did hide himself many times so he wasn't made a ruler of the people.\n\nHe was a lamb. It is this part of the mystery of God as a lamb 🐑 that might have eluded all these eye 👁‍🗨 witnesses of his birth.\n\nI'm sure these early witnesses, after waiting for years for the salvation of Israel, began to question 🙋 their experiences and when these things they so vividly saw would come to pass.\n\nTheir experience was too real to be denied, yet its fulfillment being delayed was also too real to deny.\n\nIf this boy was the Messiah, why no show after 30 years?\n\nThen now they hear of rumors and probably were touched by Jesus's ministry.\n\nNow he too dies and no show. Most of the witnesses at this stage, except the younger ones, were dead or dying.\n\nI guess some of the early witnesses, like Jesus' own mother, stayed close enough and followed through in faith till they saw the glory of his son and his resurrection. She had no choice.\n\nBut the others, did they? Maybe life happened to them.\n\nNow here comes faith... The faith of the people who would hold on to God.\n\nThe faith of Abraham, who died yet believing in the city he did not see in this life but had seen with his spirit... 👻\n\nThis is the faith we are called to... Seeing in the spirit is enough because the spirit is a real world 🗺.\n\nA world 🗺 which cannot be negated by the happenings or otherwise of our material & physical world 🗺.\n\nSo let's hold on to God and his prompting in the spirit.\n\nNow over 2000 years, and that which seemed as no show in the first eyewitnesses of the salvation of the Lord is no news in our days.\n\nWho doesn't know Jesus or his name or claim of deity?\n\nIt has worked according to the word of the Lord.\n\nThe fathers of faith have prevailed in the world. Though dead, their faith has provided the evidence of things not seen 👀 👀.","dt":"2023-03-23T13:15:30","s":["jsjco5qwbw"]}],"25":[{"m":"Ah, another man of faith, another man of the Spirit... Who believes what he has seen, not with his 👀 eyes but with his heart ♥ — the eyes 👀 of faith.","dt":"2023-03-23T13:17:33","s":["3iqkht5sg8"]}],"33":[{"m":"They wondered how these things would be, seeing they were just some poor folks and nowhere near the current political and ruling class.","dt":"2023-03-23T13:21:13","s":["3lhspecc7h"]},{"m":"This was confirmation upon confirmation — I can imagine how exciting yet humbling the experience might have been for this poor couple.\n\nFirst the strange pregnancy of his betrothed wife, then the angelic visitation and Joseph's own dream, and now external parties start confirming the word of the LORD.\n\nAnd now this — I'm sure they wondered what next, and truly what manner of child Jesus was.","dt":"2025-01-14T08:05:36","s":["uqne028e7b"]}],"41":[{"m":"This same Passover was to become a routine even in his adult years and ultimately culminate in his death ☠","dt":"2023-01-09T05:36:09","s":["nxu8qvnilo"]}],"1":[{"m":"What an annoying decree that must have been.\n\nWhen we were kids we were told it was a census, and rightly so, but we were never told or explained to us the tax bit.\n\nBut to ask everyone to undertake such a journey and leave all engagements only to be taxed.\n\nBut who could do otherwise, seeing they were a colony and Rome was the superpower then.","dt":"2025-01-14T07:49:44","s":["8xyur4lv14"]}],"5":[{"m":"Such a shame, carrying this Mary around. He was likely mocked as a fool.\n\nOnly he knew what the Lord had spoken to him. It was etched in his heart... O, this walk of faith.","dt":"2022-10-02T07:22:52","s":["kzcbbwxstd"]}],"26":[{"m":"Oh, so though Elijah, Malachi, Zechariah and others had died, there were prophets still moved by the Spirit.\n\nWe may not have their books, but nonetheless they were there...","dt":"2023-03-23T13:19:25","s":["dpxjqgm93i"]}],"32":[{"m":"Ah, I'm edging closer; I see the error of John. He was offended at the methods of Jesus.\n\nHe was not necessarily doing anything majestic. Nothing really kingly for a Messiah and leader of the chosen race.\n\nFor one who was a light to the Gentiles and who would draw all men to national Israel 🇮🇱, hanging around the poor, sick, lame etc. alone did not quite fit it.\n\nSo Jesus says, tell John what you see and hear, and tell him that blessed is he who is not offended in me, my ways and my methods.","dt":"2021-12-17T07:31:39","s":["pj9z4cpotv"]}],"35":[{"m":"Hmmm 😢","dt":"2023-03-23T13:22:10","s":["w2vfpb996l"]}],"46":[{"m":"What did he eat, what did he drink, how did he survive?\n\nAs I pen down these thoughts, I am reminded of His own words decades later, that worry not over what you will eat or drink or wear, for the Father knows you need all these.\n\nBut we are to seek first the kingdom and his righteousness, and all others shall be added unto us.\n\nHmmm🤔","dt":"2025-01-14T08:09:49","s":["t406fa1cyi"]}],"49":[{"m":"At this age he knew.\n\nI wonder, when did he know he was the son of God?\n\nFrom Mary and Joseph's reaction, they were surprised at his words.\n\nMeaning they hadn't been pumping it to him that he was the son of God and that he was the redeemer etc.\n\nIf they had, they would not have been surprised that he was saying this.","dt":"2023-03-23T15:52:22","s":["0b1bb4c6ok"]},{"m":"This statement and voice does not sound like the voice of a twelve-year-old 🧓.\n\nIt sounds like a full-grown man. 🤔.\n\nAn aside... Again I ask, where were all these teachers who were astonished 😲 at his wisdom?\n\nDid they die before his fame spread?","dt":"2023-04-28T11:06:19","s":["wmceprrj5v"]}]},"3":{"6":[{"m":"And it was literally fulfilled. All flesh saw him because salvation had put on flesh.","dt":"2022-10-04T10:03:38","s":["ai8wu9a8j4"]},{"m":"The word flesh was used by God here to let us know that this salvation will be physical. It was going to be visible.","dt":"2023-01-09T07:31:41","s":["8a73co1cme"]}],"7":[{"m":"This lets us know the state of the country and people, for them to be described as a generation of vipers.\n\nThe country was fallen; God's people were backslidden.\n\nHe reprimanded them this way because they, though wicked, somehow came to a place of repentance, which is quite 🤫 uncharacteristic of their nature.\n\nRepentance was not expected of such snakes 🐍\n\nJesus uses a similar expression and was in the same state of wonder 🤯 at their ways.\n\nMatthew 12:34 KJV\nO generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.\n\nHow that they were evil yet could speak good things.","dt":"2023-03-25T08:22:24","s":["7c95iibfzn"]}],"8":[{"m":"God is able to raise up children through stones to Abraham, because the children of Abraham are not just those who are his children of natural descent, but those of faith.\n\nSo raising up children through stones would still be in proper alignments with his justice and righteousness.\n\nHe could literally do so and still be right and within parameters of his set order.","dt":"2023-01-09T07:34:09","s":["6069r0vcbp"]},{"m":"This might have been a common saying among the people at the time, hence his referencing it.\n\nThat it is not enough to be biologically connected to Abraham.\n\nHis figure of speech of stones sounded like a hyperbole, but no, it was not.\n\nIt was literal, and it literally happened, in that a people who were not of Abraham — the Gentiles — were made children of Abraham.\n\nJohn saw and knew what God was capable of doing; he spake not these things on his own.\n\nEven if he was not capable of understanding it, he knew it was possible with God.\n\nRomans 9:26 KJV\nAnd it shall come to pass, that in the place where it was said unto them, Ye are not my people; there shall they be called the children of the living God.\n\nAnd so true and literal was this statement that he raised up that many sons, such that the biological Israel 🇮🇱 were fewer in number.\n\nRomans 9:29 KJV\nAnd as Esaias said before, Except the Lord of Sabaoth had left us a seed, we had been as Sodoma, and been made like unto Gomorrha.","dt":"2023-03-25T08:39:04","s":["2q6x185ox3"]}],"15":[{"m":"A very important verse... They were anticipating the manifestation of the Christ...\n\nCould it be that 30 years ago, when the strange happenings surrounding the birth of 2 babies 🤱, Jesus and John, were publicized, it reached peak circulation?\n\nThus creating this kind of expectation.","dt":"2021-12-08T17:09:30","s":["d3ubmj8204"]},{"m":"John was a good pastor and preacher as well.","dt":"2022-10-04T10:12:06","s":["fanttwfa49"]}],"16":[{"m":"John's ministry was full of power, for the people were struck at heart ♥ and sought his counsel...\n\nHe did not perform any miracles on record, but this ability to bring to repentance shows you the strength 💪 of his calling.","dt":"2023-01-09T07:36:29","s":["2v7ihaspbo"]}],"38":[{"m":"We are all indeed children of God.\n\nWhen you trace all of us, our history, we end up in our progenitor, our Father in heaven.\n\nSo it's biological ☣. We are children of God 😭","dt":"2023-03-25T08:45:09","s":["mhr5l6ejwr"]}],"22":[{"m":"Oh Lord, that I will be a beloved son...","dt":"2023-03-25T09:19:57","s":["19mjachhgw"]}]},"4":{"3":[{"m":"Jesus had not yet started his public ministry, so how did the devil know he was the son of God?\n\nObviously there are things in the spirit that those in the spirit can tell.\n\nAnd later in his ministry we see demons confessing same.\n\nIt was we in the earth 🌎 who did not know him.\n\nHe was already a center of talk and attention in the spirit realm.\n\nThis is interesting, that a man 👨🏿 most popular in the realm of the spirit and known by all was completely unknown in the natural.\n\nHow did they know? Obviously the abundance of spiritual activity around his birth could not go unnoticed.\n\nThe same with us and any man who begins his spiritual journey.\n\nWe begin to ring bells depending on the depth of spiritual activity we are engaged in.\n\nThough unknown in the earth 🌎, we presume same spiritually and can shipwreck when we take things for granted and fall off.\n\nThe enemy would then throw all his arsenals at us so we do not recover at all.\n\nBecause our recovery is a headache for the dark world 🗺.\n\nSo personally, in my falling away, I was greatly attacked in mind and body.\n\nI was dying, felt God I had committed irredeemable offense and thrown away ten years.\n\nA lie 🤥 from hell.\n\nRecently, as I held my son, a thought came to mind that we are sons of God.\n\nThen another thought came: what at all can my son do against me when he grows that I won't forgive him, when especially it was a mistake he did not deliberately intend?\n\nThen my own case came to mind, and I realized 🤭 how much the enemy had deceived me to keep me bound.\n\nIndeed, when a runaway son or employee returns, you know they would not go back, considering their bitter taste of outlawed life.\n\nFor those who never left, you know they would not, but that unknown factor is always a source of temptation.","dt":"2023-01-09T08:25:36","s":["q9ksjw8xs1"]}],"14":[{"m":"Having conquered, he now was endued with power for the next level.","dt":"2023-03-25T10:23:12","s":["dqtatjc28i"]},{"m":"Oh, just realized Jesus returned to his home in Galilee, which was some days' journey from Jordan 🇯🇴 river.\n\nIt's easy to think that \"from Jordan he came out in power to Galilee\" was in reference to a place nearby.","dt":"2023-03-25T10:41:30","s":["cpw85myns7"]}],"15":[{"m":"Did the devil foresee that such power would show up, and thus sought to distract the Lord?\n\nHence the timing of this temptation.","dt":"2022-10-05T07:18:49","s":["3f5ygq5tzy"]}],"28":[{"m":"Everywhere Jesus went, he spoke truth to power without fear 😱, and it caused a lot of rumblings and shake-up, because truth is power.\n\nThis ultimately led to his death ☠ and crucifixion.","dt":"2023-01-09T08:33:19","s":["vaviphsn4"]}],"30":[{"m":"This Jesus...\n\nThe Jews hadn't changed. Once again they were about to destroy their own saviour.","dt":"2022-10-05T07:20:51","s":["lojl61sv2f"]}],"31":[{"m":"I believe, even though this is a verse, the activity of going down to Capernaum, looking for a place to reside and settle. Planning the next move and which synagogue to enter and how to be given access to read or teach that day.\n\nProbably Jesus had to make mention of his qualifications, having understudied rabbi so-and-so, in order to be granted audience that day.\n\nYet it's all summed up in just a verse.","dt":"2021-12-13T13:41:38","s":["uirtlqnzs9"]}],"32":[{"m":"So it is OK to start ministry not where you stay, where the people are familiar with you, but elsewhere.\n\nWhere your ministry would be accepted and the people blessed.","dt":"2023-01-09T08:30:44","s":["helqr7d9we"]}],"34":[{"m":"Jesus had defeated their boss the devil 👿, and they were being exposed and cast out everywhere Jesus went.","dt":"2023-03-28T20:11:40","s":["nzrzmvjj86"]}],"35":[{"m":"There was not much mention of demon possession in the Old Testament and never a mention of any being cast out.\n\nThe example we have is that of Saul and being soothed with music, but not the kind of thing Jesus was doing.\n\nThis does not mean there were no such demon issues, but Jesus's presence with the kingdom 👑 demonstrated his power over the kingdom of the devil 👿.\n\nNo wonder he later said that if he casts out devils by the finger of God, then indeed the kingdom of God has come to them.","dt":"2023-03-28T20:41:28","s":["dv7rmnpmuc"]}],"37":[{"m":"Just like the way word about Jesus went out among men for this miracle.\n\nSo also among the spirits word had gone out.\n\nHow else did this demon spirit know who Jesus was?","dt":"2022-10-05T07:32:19","s":["f79rplqxnd"]}],"41":[{"m":"How did they know he was the Christ, when as yet the people he was with, even the disciples, knew not yet?\n\nAnd it was not just one demon... The demons knew.... How??\n\nAnd he silences them. I guess it's because he knew the uproar that will erupt if Jewry knew he was the Christ ✝...\n\nHis presence at this time was not to be king but Lamb; on his return he will come as king 👑 with pomp ⛽ and pageantry.","dt":"2021-12-09T12:33:15","s":["psi5scnya7"]},{"m":"How did they know?","dt":"2025-01-25T11:48:46","s":["akujs8ktz1"]}],"9":[{"m":"And our temptations as men run parallel to this pattern.","dt":"2023-03-25T10:20:15","s":["3bq11cyzg3"]}]},"5":{"16":[{"m":"In the midst of the crowd and ministry success, so called, he kept the main thing the main thing, i.e. his relationship with the Father.","dt":"2022-10-05T09:49:24","s":["xtsi98svms"]}],"17":[{"m":"An eerie replay of when he was 12 years old and was surrounded by the teachers of the law and doctors.\n\nNow he himself was of full age and the same continued.","dt":"2023-03-29T07:09:07","s":["u2lvw04h42"]},{"m":"They had heard of a new and great prophet, a man rumoured to be possibly the Christ.\n\nAnd they, being self-appointed custodians of the laws of God in a sense, came to watch for themselves.","dt":"2025-01-25T11:55:26","s":["67xs4t6czt"]}],"19":[{"m":"Jesus had such mastery of the spirit... In the midst of skeptics and doubters he still performed miracles.\n\nSome would usually say people's doubts poison the atmosphere.","dt":"2023-01-09T11:08:52","s":["h2lx1o7nee"]}],"21":[{"m":"Not really, Jesus could forgive sins... Indeed, later his disciples could forgive men their sins — a power given them by Christ.","dt":"2025-01-25T11:57:26","s":["g5cv13gmdw"]}],"24":[{"m":"Refer to earlier notes... The proof that Jesus had power to forgive was that he got results.","dt":"2021-12-09T12:40:26","s":["qrmopfiob4"]}],"28":[{"m":"This was the common response of the apostles to Jesus... They forsook all, rose 🌹 up and followed him.","dt":"2022-10-05T09:53:52","s":["sj7znk15g1"]},{"m":"I am interested in knowing the conversion story of Levi — what miracle compelled him to follow the master.","dt":"2025-01-25T12:01:51","s":["nmqym6zz0k"]}],"29":[{"m":"Levi was a man of substance. To have thrown such a great feast.\n\nI'm sure he wanted to impress his friends, that guess who my special guest is for today.\n\nNone other than Jesus, the acclaimed Messiah and miracle worker 👷.\n\nAnd he left all and followed Jesus.\n\nWhat am I leaving to follow Jesus?","dt":"2023-03-29T07:13:53","s":["0nvvltl5im"]}],"30":[{"m":"These were there to keep the status quo, so they kept a close eye on Jesus and killed him eventually.\n\nAnd Jesus knew it, yet indulged them.","dt":"2022-10-05T09:55:28","s":["7zzka2xb9n"]}],"32":[{"m":"It is said that bad company corrupts good character, but then how did Jesus protect himself from being corrupted...\n\nIndeed, he ended up affecting them positively.\n\nReason being:\n1. One, he did not keep them as company.\n2. He was completely and full in himself. He did not need to impress anyone for someone else to influence him... Was it their riches etc. that he desired?? No, he had no such intentions.\n\nJesus was larger than life itself... How can the creator be influenced by the creation?","dt":"2021-12-09T12:45:05","s":["pdfd1l0v7x"]}],"34":[{"m":"Jesus the bridegroom 🤵, adorned in beautiful apparel and splendor. The church ⛪ his beautiful bride 👰.\n\nSuch were the descriptions Jesus gave of himself.\n\nThough simple-looking and with simple associations, he was full of grace and truth.","dt":"2023-03-29T07:15:44","s":["5zwayfcnql"]}],"35":[{"m":"The physical presence of Jesus was such strong cover for the disciples. They were protected by him.\n\nBut when he left, Jesus sent down another cover in the person of the Spirit, but he worked and had to be related in a different fashion than the physical Jesus, since he was Spirit.\n\nThe disciples fasted often after Christ left.","dt":"2025-01-25T12:01:01","s":["9py499jd59"]}],"10":[{"m":"This verse explains why they left all and followed after him.\n\nIn the other accounts, Matthew and Mark, Jesus calls them to follow him, and they forsook all and did.\n\nBut here in Luke we see that the miracle of multiplied fishes and overwhelming success in business made them know that he was no man, and they were secured in him.\n\nSo they followed him to become fishers of men.","dt":"2025-01-25T11:53:03","s":["1i68ebkexp"]}]},"6":{"2":[{"m":"The Pharisees seem to be everywhere.\n\nWere they spying on them?","dt":"2023-01-09T11:13:06","s":["12oxcuchez"]}],"35":[{"m":"Hm... This is so difficult to do.\n\nBut we are told our reward shall be great in heaven.","dt":"2023-03-29T08:02:08","s":["lq1ruyhoke"]}]},"7":{"4":[{"m":"Why did Jesus have to be besought?\n\nCould be that, like the Syrophenician woman, this man was not a Jew, and thus Jesus was not compelled to help him.\n\nBut he had a compelling reason, in that he helped the people of God.\n\nJust like the sons of Midian helped Moses in the desert 🏜 and partook in the blessings,\n\nhere this man was worthy of partaking in the Jewish blessing.","dt":"2025-02-19T06:27:18","s":["vzwfmuf0ix"]}],"8":[{"m":"What did this centurion see about Jesus for him to conclude that Jesus had authority to command his servants to go and come at will, just like himself?\n\nJesus did not have any servants,\nbut he had authority, and he had command and power over creation and angels.\n\nIndeed all these were subject to him. But how did this man know this?","dt":"2023-03-30T06:56:36","s":["9gwl9cf6sd"]}],"11":[{"m":"Jesus often traveled with a convoy. Not of his own making, but because of the grace he carried.","dt":"2021-12-17T04:54:05","s":["8s5y0ffp3p"]}],"16":[{"m":"A great prophet had risen, but Jesus was more than a prophet, and this is proven in the next sentence when they said,\n\nGod has visited his people 🙏, and indeed he had.\n\nThe people meant it figuratively, but it was literal.\n\nAlso, there was a general expectation of the Messiah to come, so for this to be said could be in reference to that expectation, and this would mean they believed Jesus was the Christ to come.","dt":"2025-02-19T06:34:00","s":["nw2b8mxhpw"]}],"18":[{"m":"What exactly was the nature of the report for John to question 🙋 Jesus thus ⚡?","dt":"2021-12-17T05:54:33","s":["ib6897jsva"]}],"23":[{"m":"Here we have John's disciples again. This time not questioning 🙋 about fasting, but the authenticity of Jesus as Messiah.\n\nWhy would John, the forerunner of Jesus, act thus?\n\nWas it that he expected Jesus to be more accommodating? To come around more often for them to do ministry together?\n\nI have heard some preachers say that John was at this time in prison and was surprised 🤨 Jesus did not visit and seek to set him free.\n\nWhatever the case may be 🐝, he was offended about something.\n\nOffended enough to send to Jesus to question 🙋 the very ministry that he had helped authenticate and establish.\n\nYes, that might have been it. After all that he had done and sacrificed for the ministry of Jesus, he was being ignored 🤷‍♂️.\n\nHe was growing less significant by the day.","dt":"2021-12-17T05:04:07","s":["x92v2p06jn"]}],"37":[{"m":"Why was she called specifically a sinner, seeing we are all sinners?\n\nLikely it was an obvious public sin or sexually related.\n\nHow else could Simon the Pharisee have known she was one?","dt":"2023-03-31T12:41:18","s":["sydswetheq"]},{"m":"She being a sinner was common knowledge, for Simon knew.\n\nI can imagine how ostracized she might have felt.\n\nBeing shunned by everyone because they knew her sins.\n\nNow she came to Jesus, this holy man of God.\n\nTo take away her reproach and shame.","dt":"2023-04-04T06:26:47","s":["y9pmrbnyyu"]}],"40":[{"m":"Jesus was unusually good at reading 📖 man... Both their thoughts 💭 and intentions.","dt":"2021-12-17T06:10:33","s":["8tobju6yvl"]}],"48":[{"m":"Here again we have another example of Jesus forgiving sins and associating with sinners.","dt":"2021-12-17T06:29:19","s":["3ruwnioych"]},{"m":"Hm 🤔... So she might have heard that the son of David ✡, the Messiah, had come.\n\nShe being a sinner needed this prophet and man of God to set her free from her guilt and shame.\n\nAnd she came with an offering in hand 🖐️... Oh, what a beautiful thought 💭 and heart ♥.\n\nShe knew she was a sinner, and this holy man of God, whom she was not worthy of, was in town.\n\nShe came in her humility of heart ♥ and brought an offering... Not just the oil, but also a broken 💔 and contrite heart.","dt":"2022-10-12T15:26:22","s":["5v4dpameom"]},{"m":"This woman 👨🏿, this sinner, what did she really want that she came thus to Jesus?\n\nThe whole scene is disconcerting and quite uncomfortable, kissing 😘, crying and using her hair all over Jesus.\n\nI do not know if it's a cultural thing, will check it; looks sensual in a sense.\n\nDid she come because of her sins being many? So she needed forgiveness.\n\nIf so, who did she think Jesus was, God?\n\nHow then did she come to such a conclusion?\n\nMore likely she knew Jesus was a holy man of God and needed him to pray for her possibly and intercede to God on her behalf.\n\nOr she had heard he was likely the Messiah and had come to seek pardon 🙏","dt":"2023-03-31T14:19:03","s":["afpspe9jz6"]}],"50":[{"m":"She came to be forgiven of her sins and set free from the guilt of it.\n\nThis Jesus discerned and restored her and brought salvation and peace to her.\n\nOnly God knows how much guilt and trouble of mind she had.\n\nNow she was set free, and he whom the Son sets free is free. Indeed.","dt":"2023-04-04T06:36:08","s":["7ultwvxgbz"]},{"m":"Her situation is so much like the paralytic man who was also forgiven and made whole from his sickness.\n\nThis woman had broken protocol and come in contact with a holy man like Jesus, and faced shame being a known sinner.\n\nBut her faith made her whole.","dt":"2025-02-19T06:45:06","s":["xmu877ieug"]}],"5":[{"m":"They besought and pressed Jesus that he had to go heal this man's servant.\n\nYou get the idea that it was not everywhere that Jesus went.\n\nHe was being pulled everywhere, and he couldn't be everywhere at once, so he went where he could.","dt":"2023-03-30T06:51:14","s":["agxcej3aj3"]}],"10":[{"m":"Oh, the value of a good servant.\n\nOrdinarily the servant would likely have died, but his master, whom he had helped, now used all of his influence to procure healing for his servant.\n\nLeaving a mark in the lives of others is a very strong bargaining chip.","dt":"2025-02-19T06:30:08","s":["yce8miyzcm"]}]},"8":{"4":[{"m":"First he went out to every city and village preaching; now after that, the people started coming to him.\n\nFirst the announcement and proclamation of the kingdom 👑 had to be made.\n\nHow else were the people to know there was salvation for them?\n\nNow after that, the people, seeing the results, started coming of their own accord.\n\nJesus was deliberate and strategic in his ventures.\n\nHe knew how to dine with the high and mighty, like he did in Simon's house.\n\nHe also knew how to go to the low and abased.\n\nHe was indeed the people's Messiah.","dt":"2023-04-04T06:57:06","s":["azjtye9ppx"]}],"10":[{"m":"What manner of teaching style is this? Imagine a preacher who comes to your church and shares very interesting stories, yet refuses to explain, and yet you love his stories and the miracles he does, and even multiplying bread.\n\nBut his teachings are full of strange illustrations, difficult to decipher, yet he refuses to explain them.\n\nThat was Jesus: some loved him, some hated him, and some just did not know what to make of him.\n\nHe himself knew he had become somewhat of a mystery.\n\nNo wonder he at a point asked to know what people thought of him.\n\nHe was indeed a mighty wonder.","dt":"2025-02-27T18:00:06","s":["rvj05d2l9x"]}],"12":[{"m":"So the devil 👿 has such powers.\n\nNo wonder we ought to arrest every thought 💭 and make them subject to Christ.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:26:17","s":["4a53e6kvk8"]}],"13":[{"m":"Matthew's account says when persecutions arise on account of the word; Luke here says temptation. I think they line up and complement each other well.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:27:50","s":["1x4ub9akqw"]}],"16":[{"m":"These two verses line up well... The good ground hears the word and bears fruit in many folds.\n\nJust like a light is not hidden but shines forth, bears fruit 🥝","dt":"2021-12-17T08:29:35","s":["928vxkowsi"]}],"18":[{"m":"In other words, he that hears and heeds, by paying attention to and doing what the word says, shall more be given...\n\nBut the one who does not have, even the little he/she has is taken away.","dt":"2022-10-19T11:06:37","s":["iqsqfnd3o8"]}],"21":[{"m":"He was speaking forth a mystery here. It might have sounded almost like an insult 🤬 or high-mindedness for him to have said this.\n\nBut that was truth. We are his brethren. We are his family 👪","dt":"2023-04-04T07:01:39","s":["jk0v27a4lo"]}],"25":[{"m":"I love this... What manner of man is this?","dt":"2021-12-17T08:30:40","s":["tl4225m4bn"]},{"m":"Ah, so was Jesus expecting them to, like, do something about the storm? 😕 😤 🤦🏾 🤷🏻‍♂️\n\nIf this was his expectation of his followers during a storm, then I won't be surprised 🤨 that if JESUS was in our individual situations, he would say the same thing.\n\nWhere is your faith? 😳 Yes, we all go through storms in life. And the storms are to bring out the best in us 🙏.\n\nSo like Jesus, I ask us, you and I, where is your faith?","dt":"2023-04-05T07:30:48","s":["gx21w35n6v"]}],"29":[{"m":"Spirits drive men. Here is an example of an evil 😈 spirit driving 🚘 a man.\n\nIn the case of Jesus, he was thus so filled with the Spirit it drove him to the desert 🏜 to fast.\n\nWe are commanded to be full of the Holy Ghost 👻 till he controls us 🎮\n\nEphesians 5:18-19 KJV\nAnd be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit; [19] Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;","dt":"2021-12-17T08:33:06","s":["t926uensd4"]}],"37":[{"m":"But why did they do this? What were they afraid 😨 of...\n\nThat Jesus would bring judgement upon them, or that the devils will come for revenge?\n\nOr they were just afraid at the entire turn of events.","dt":"2023-04-05T07:34:32","s":["thnuq2udjq"]}],"44":[{"m":"This touch of faith, which many have preached about as an example of great faith, is not entirely new.\n\nIn\n\nLuke 6:19 KJV\nAnd the whole multitude sought to touch him: for there went virtue out of him, and healed them all.\n\nWe see many have been doing this kind of thing even before the woman with the issue of blood.\n\nWhat makes her case unique was that she thought to herself, I do not need to touch his body or even cling to his clothes.\n\nNo, I just need a little something; just the hem is enough.\n\nSecondly, so strong was her faith, she literally seems to have drained so much power that even Jesus felt it.\n\nJesus, the repository of power, felt it when power was taken out by this woman; she indeed may have really pulled from him.","dt":"2023-01-10T06:07:00","s":["l1ny64fuwa"]}],"54":[{"m":"In this walk 🚶 of faith, speak no evil; speak only faith and that which you want to see.\n\nJesus refused to speak any contrary view, even when the circumstances indicated otherwise.\n\nIt was the same in the case of Lazarus. From when he was sick to when he died...\n\nSpiritual principles at work here.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:39:07","s":["tvv6evdas5"]}],"14":[{"m":"Many unfulfilled ministries find themselves here.\n\nMark 4:18-19 KJV\nAnd these are they which are sown among thorns; such as hear the word,\nAnd the cares of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, and the lusts of other things entering in, choke the word, and it becometh unfruitful.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:28:31","s":["j8wb08zldy"]}],"33":[{"m":"They caused massive economic damage... 100% destroying someone's business, these demons.\n\nBut I wonder what was the moral (as if they have any) for desiring to leave the man, enter into pigs 🐽, only to destroy them.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:37:13","s":["upk9cecl07"]}],"42":[{"m":"Jairus's faith needed Jesus physically present, but the centurion's did not.\n\nIt would have saved both him and Jesus the time if Jairus's faith was great enough.\n\nIt is interesting that Jesus could not have great faith for the people he ministered to, but had to meet them where their faith was, and not lord his great faith over theirs.","dt":"2023-01-09T21:26:24","s":["a73zq1wbxi"]},{"m":"If Jairus had the faith of the centurion, then maybe we would never have had the story of the woman with the issue of blood, because it was en route to Jairus's house that the woman with the issue of blood showed us great faith.\n\nThe faith of touching the hem of Jesus's garment. A faith many a song has been written about.","dt":"2023-01-10T06:01:14","s":["brivy1ewa6"]}],"46":[{"m":"This lets us in on the kind of things that went through and out and inside of Jesus as he ministered to people.\n\nThis is the only one time we have on record Jesus commenting on what he felt.\n\nIt's almost like today when we say we feel the presence of God.\n\nLord, help us to discern your impulses... Lord, help us.","dt":"2023-04-05T07:41:39","s":["rgiega7bcr"]}],"56":[{"m":"Why should no one know what was done?","dt":"2023-04-05T07:43:17","s":["n95irk489n"]}]},"9":{"2":[{"m":"How did he do this? How did he give or impart this power?\n\nI believe by proclamation or speaking. He might have said something like this:\n\nGo, I give you power to trample upon serpents and scorpions and over all the power of the Enemy, and nothing shall by any means hurt thee.\n\nJust like he gave the Great Commission, so here he sends his disciples two by two, though alive...\n\nIn the Acts of the Apostles, such commissioning was by laying on of hands... Just like Paul was commissioned by laying on of hands of his friends.\n\nOr I think the church commissioned some people by laying on of hands and praying, if I'm not mistaken.","dt":"2023-04-08T06:54:27","s":["1laekstlur"]}],"9":[{"m":"Jesus's fame had now spread to the corridors of power... Herod now desired him.","dt":"2023-01-10T08:52:32","s":["3n7vrbtc4v"]}],"11":[{"m":"The kingdom of God is so vast... There was always something new to teach... Even up until this moment.","dt":"2023-01-10T10:05:40","s":["d0adbd8yca"]}],"12":[{"m":"These people came to a desert place, where they had no acquaintance, to hear Jesus and to hear the truth of the kingdom 👑.\n\nThe word of truth was indeed rare.\n\nYet today the word is all over, and even disdained, and the enemy steals the word out of people's hearts 💕 a lot, so it bears not fruit 🥝.","dt":"2022-10-27T12:15:31","s":["tb2a757qvu"]}],"18":[{"m":"He was alone praying 🙏; were his disciples also praying 🙏 themselves, or were they just there?\n\nBut that shows you the sacrifice of a leader.","dt":"2023-01-10T10:09:47","s":["o297vu71wh"]}],"21":[{"m":"Why such a command, when that was the whole idea of his coming?\n\nAt this stage people had different perceptions about him, but none was really sure where to classify him.\n\nSome suspected he was the Messiah, none was too sure, and he himself did not emphasize that.\n\nEven up until the point of his death, the Pharisees had to ask him if he was the Christ... Laughable.\n\nNow to the point: the reason for his command is seen in the next verse.\n\nLuke 9:22 KJV\nSaying, The Son of man must suffer many things, and be rejected of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be slain, and be raised the third day.\n\nYes, he must; it was necessary that he suffers and dies. How could he have gone through all this if he is believed as the Messiah?\n\nJESUS was sent with a plan and specific mission, and he was not going to fail.\n\nHe needed to be rejected and killed. It was all part of the plan.\n\nHow did Jesus know all of this? The Father has revealed it to him.","dt":"2023-04-10T06:34:05","s":["0yeup1z4ut"]}],"22":[{"m":"Strange, so the so-called teachers and scribes did not have what it takes to know the Messiah, though he was right before their eyes.\n\nThis is a true lesson for us.\n\nThe experts, so-called, are sometimes just title holders. Seek the truth yourself.","dt":"2022-10-27T12:20:32","s":["nx0ar09pms"]},{"m":"Must suffer??? 😳 He said it like it was ordained to be so.\n\nYes, it was ordained; in Isaiah 53 it was so prophesied.","dt":"2023-01-10T10:12:12","s":["30ko7faj69"]}],"26":[{"m":"So there is the glory of the Father, and the glory of the Son, and that of angels 😇.\n\nEach radiating their own glory in their own right.","dt":"2023-04-13T01:31:02","s":["xnelc7pr1q"]}],"28":[{"m":"He took these three to pray... He prayed often with his disciples, but with these three he was taking them the extra mile...\n\nThey spent all night on the mountains ⛰.\n\nHow cold was it, or was it warm enough? Insects? Flies? Who knows.\n\nWhy did Jesus isolate these three, who became pillars in the early church ⛪?\n\nIt was not for nothing; they had gained extra grounding because they went the extra mile.\n\nBut these were not the only ones of weight, as we see in the Acts of the Apostles.","dt":"2023-04-13T01:39:03","s":["tj0jyg8kqx"]}],"29":[{"m":"Was it that his natural clothes took on a new nature 🏞, or was it that his glorified body, which comes clothed, overshadows the natural body and clothes?\n\nThe latter seems so.","dt":"2023-01-10T10:48:20","s":["63ndqkln4r"]}],"30":[{"m":"How did they know it was Moses and Elias?","dt":"2021-12-21T11:19:01","s":["ul2vvtrx4"]}],"37":[{"m":"They spent all night on the hill.","dt":"2023-01-10T10:50:03","s":["l0oavpjdzq"]}],"41":[{"m":"So Jesus expected them to be able to cast the devil 👿 out.\n\nAnd he blamed it on their faithlessness.","dt":"2023-01-10T11:03:34","s":["b10r9lfjre"]}],"45":[{"m":"So it was hid from them...\nBecause Jesus on numerous occasions and times told them, without mincing words, of his death, but they understood it not, though it was right before their eyes 👀.\n\nThis is akin to the parable of the sower and of the seed that the birds took.\n\nThese, the devil 👿 stole the word from their heart, err, before it could even take ground.","dt":"2023-01-10T11:05:58","s":["y4d93mapt8"]}],"46":[{"m":"Where did such reasoning come from?\n\nThey knew they were in a privileged position, being in such close proximity to the Christ.\n\nThey knew that history was unfolding right before their eyes 👀.\n\nAnd now they wondered how they might maximise it.","dt":"2025-03-19T09:53:32","s":["1so5l65dtw"]}],"51":[{"m":"Such in tune 🎶 with the Spirit. LORD GRANT ME yieldedness.","dt":"2021-12-21T11:39:08","s":["vwx4b1okig"]}],"53":[{"m":"Why was this the case? Was it because they realised that his ultimate goal was to head for Jerusalem, and was only transiting through their town?\n\nAnd since they, the Jews, have no dealings with Samaritans, why should they make preparations for him to transit?\n\nThey were not going to be treated second place.\n\nSo they refused to help him.","dt":"2025-03-19T09:58:37","s":["pvoho8yjhv"]}],"54":[{"m":"We all know how Jesus sent for the Last Supper to be prepared and how he sent for the donkey for the triumphant entry.\n\nWhat happened here?\n\nDid he not know that it was the wrong choice to make?\n\nThis shows the humanness of Jesus. He knew only as revealed by the Spirit of God.\n\nHe was indeed fully man and worked the supernatural not based on his ability but based on that of the Spirit.\n\nHe was limited in knowledge and power like any other man and could do the supernatural only by the power of God.\n\nHe could do anything he wanted only in the sense of receiving answers to prayer, which he did receive always.\n\nFor instance, whiles on earth as a man, he could have changed his mind at any time and aborted mission, and he would immediately be in his divine role and form, full of the glory and power he had with the Father before he came on the 🌎 earth.\n\nJohn 17:5 KJV\nAnd now, O Father, glorify thou me with thine own self with the glory which I had with thee before the world was.\n\nBut there was a script to be followed, and he did, to the letter, despite the pain and shame of being in the flesh and following the script.\n\nIndeed, the moment he came in the flesh and accepted the role, he was limited and constrained until his glorification.","dt":"2023-04-15T10:07:45","s":["1tbq7eg5z8"]}],"56":[{"m":"The kind of spirit we are of destroyeth not, but saveth. This bears more study, to clarify when we are permitted to pass judgment on the wicked and death ☠","dt":"2021-12-21T11:38:15","s":["lkz09t35pd"]}],"13":[{"m":"Likely this was for the disciples themselves for the evening 🌃.\n\nThey were in a desert 🏜 place so they could retreat and rest, but that was not to be... But by evening everyone has to go home...","dt":"2023-01-10T10:07:26","s":["09yx24a5ll"]}],"15":[{"m":"These people had not bothered about food 🍲; they just wanted to hear the truth and to hear this prophet, Christ.\n\nThey indeed sought the kingdom first. And they did get bread to eat as well. For Jesus had taught men to give up all for the sake of the kingdom, and here they were putting it into practice.","dt":"2022-10-27T12:18:14","s":["dpwmnebsk4"]}],"31":[{"m":"I'm tempted to wonder what the exact details of this divine chit-chat were.","dt":"2021-12-21T11:25:27","s":["eu92h0azeb"]}],"33":[{"m":"Not knowing what he said, indeed, yet he spoke truth, reality.\n\nThat still begs the question: how did he know it was Moses and Elias, if not by the Spirit?","dt":"2021-12-21T11:28:47","s":["jsaytepebr"]}]},"10":{"17":[{"m":"At this stage they were already using the name of Jesus to cast out devils.","dt":"2023-04-17T07:49:39","s":["tyk9a5qex5"]}],"24":[{"m":"It is like the family and friends of royalty 👑 or very renowned people.\n\nThey have access so much that it is taken for granted.\n\nMeanwhile, others are actively lobbying for opportunity.","dt":"2023-01-10T12:03:16","s":["u08hgd9vls"]}],"37":[{"m":"JESUS, by this parable, was saying: you ask who is your neighbor, but that is the wrong way to put it.\n\nRather, go and be that neighbor you seek.","dt":"2023-04-17T08:00:38","s":["b53imxvstt"]}]},"11":{"1":[{"m":"Who was this disciple who made this all-important question, which today has given us the most popular prayer in all of history?\n\nInterestingly, the disciple here is not named; I checked online, neither was it there.\n\nWho could it be?","dt":"2025-02-22T15:41:15","s":["h7nxtvxstt"]}],"13":[{"m":"Oh, what blessed assurance.","dt":"2021-12-17T07:54:24","s":["41y5yo8e7b"]}],"20":[{"m":"Evidence of the kingdom is demonstrated by Christ in this.\n\nThat is, by his casting out of demons 👹. Of course there are other evidences. His other mighty works also demonstrate the kingdom is come.","dt":"2022-10-13T06:51:00","s":["1gwj1l4kt0"]}],"28":[{"m":"Jesus Dat, small fans and the something turn teaching.\n\nJesus took advantage of the least of moments to horn 📯 home a lesson or 2.","dt":"2021-12-17T07:57:05","s":["t6321zdnbv"]}],"53":[{"m":"See, the same wickedness that Jesus was speaking of was showing forth.","dt":"2021-12-17T08:03:45","s":["ktrvm36wm8"]}],"2":[{"m":"This couldn't get any clearer: Jesus said that when you pray, say...\n\nMeaning these are the things we have to say.\n\nAnd that is the beginning of wrong Bible doctrine.\n\nThis is how people take a verse of scripture and make doctrines and laws out of it.\n\nWhen we look at this verse in the light of all other teachings and examples of Jesus praying, as well as other writings of the early disciples,\n\nWe see that we are not being commanded to always say and repeat these same exact words.\n\nIt reads so, it sounds like that is what is being said, but in the light of other scriptures we get better clarity...\n\nObviously there are other prayers to be prayed, as demonstrated by Jesus in other passages...\nSo what is it saying... It's teaching us what the content of prayer should surround. It should be about the word and will of God and his kingdom 👑...","dt":"2023-01-10T15:19:16","s":["7r30j682rh"]}]},"12":{"19":[{"m":"The soul was addressed and personified here.","dt":"2023-01-10T17:45:42","s":["li13ef8srz"]}],"35":[{"m":"Ever ready, and ever set to redeem the times and champion the kingdom agenda.\n\nConstantly training ourselves and acquiring the skills requisite for kingdom service, for preaching, teaching, healing and service in the kingdom 👑","dt":"2023-01-10T17:51:06","s":["b42rhhk3g2"]}],"50":[{"m":"The Amplified translates straitened as distressed.\n\nThe NIV says how 'constrained' I am.\n\nOh, indeed I can imagine the weight 🏋️ and burden of the call of Jesus.\n\nKnowing what manner of death he was to accomplish, and that shortly, in a few years.\n\nAnd for all these years he carried the weight of a burden.\n\nHe could share it with no one, and indeed he spoke about it often in parables, and even when he spoke plainly his disciples did not understand him and likely thought it another parable.\n\nOh, the burden of the Messiah.","dt":"2025-03-26T06:48:44","s":["a5s4fkkr47"]}],"51":[{"m":"What mean these things?","dt":"2022-10-27T11:33:17","s":["7p94w9akat"]}],"8":[{"m":"Hm 🤔, what a thought 💭.\n\nImagine Jesus discussing you by name before the angels 😇 of God.\nSuch a profound and exciting thought — that the Son of God has you on his lips.\n\nThen obviously you would be on the lips of his Father as well.","dt":"2025-03-26T06:38:35","s":["q70f4a9w9w"]}]},"13":{"17":[{"m":"Was it in the rejoicing and the seeming commotion that comes with such healings that the temple officers and elders felt it disturbed the Sabbath?\n\nMaybe they wanted the solemnness and quietness 🤫 of the Sabbath to be maintained, or maybe not; either ways, that was not reason enough for someone not to be healed or set free.","dt":"2023-01-10T17:58:02","s":["p370adacza"]}],"5":[{"m":"Was he speaking of the coming massacre in AD 70?\n\nWas he alluding to that?","dt":"2025-03-26T06:54:01","s":["0me2akwzfu"]}]},"14":{"4":[{"m":"These guys have become so hardened that no more could miracles move them.\n\nSo hardened have they become that, to appease their conscience, they attribute the works of Christ to the devil 😈, so they could stand against Christ and his works.\n\nThey preferred denying the works of Christ so they could keep their man-made doctrines.","dt":"2025-03-27T07:18:03","s":["wsrokxvug2"]}],"15":[{"m":"🤔 Hmm 🤔. These men sat with God and ate, yet could not discern him.\n\nMoses and the elders of Israel also sat at meat with the Lord in Mount Sinai and ate with him.\n\nHim did they discern as the I am. But yet could not continue on with him, and so died in their sins in the wilderness.\n\nOh, the things of the Spirit... Lord, wash and purge me and save me from self. 🤳\n\nThat I might be counted worthy, oh Lord... Counted worthy.","dt":"2022-10-27T11:42:24","s":["t969g9zy69"]}],"7":[{"m":"Who did Jesus think he was?\n\nHe was only thirty years and was instructing people far older than him and had more experience and influence.\n\nLittle wonder they killed him. He was too much for them.\n\nHe was usurping their authority, wielding influence over the common people, setting new doctrines and calling out the leaders of the time as hypocrites.\n\nAnd after his death ☠, his disciples followed after him.\n\nThere was no stopping him.","dt":"2023-04-20T09:02:00","s":["0lw1to9dxz"]}]},"15":{"32":[{"m":"A kind of love only a father could conceive and fathom.\n\nIt was his son; he could not deny his own offspring.","dt":"2023-04-21T08:38:07","s":["6h772fghic"]}]},"16":{"24":[{"m":"Many thoughts to share here, if this story is not a parable but literal:\n\n1. The gulf separating — is it just a wide expanse, or is it filled with liquid fire 🔥 like the lake of fire?\n\n2. How come the rich man knew it was Abraham? This shows the power of the soul in the afterlife... It's similar to Peter knowing Moses and Elias when Jesus transfigured.\n\n3. How did Abraham know about Moses and the prophets, and the power and possibility of resurrection? That should tell you paradise is not just a place where people hang around and do nothing. It seems from here that there were regular updates given to father Abraham and others likely.\n\n4. It seems Abraham was the boss or lead person here. The rich man did not even address Lazarus but Abraham, and passed every request through him.\n\n5. Was reference to Abraham's bosom implying a place of rest?\n\nWhy Abraham? Because other righteous men, as Abel and Noah, predate him... It's because to him belongs the covenant of the father of many nations.\n\n6. How come one in torments of fire 🔥 could have such coherent discussion with Abraham?\n\nCould it be that the spirit realm has more stamina and other attributes?\n\n7. The torments are eternal, so, unlike flesh that would burn 🔥 to ashes, the spirit is not so, because it is spirit and eternal.","dt":"2023-01-10T19:14:07","s":["undaybjldd"]}],"31":[{"m":"Jesus was with them raising men from the dead, and they did not believe.\n\nAnother person rising from the dead would not change anything for those who refuse to believe.","dt":"2025-03-28T17:56:15","s":["3a4x0a4yxs"]}],"10":[{"m":"Bears more studies.","dt":"2022-10-28T12:20:07","s":["uw7r1zgaur"]}]},"17":{"19":[{"m":"The others would continue going to the priest and meet all requirements before being declared whole to enter the community, but he was declared to be whole to go his way without meeting any of these religious cleansing rituals.","dt":"2023-04-24T06:59:56","s":["8swfyi39oq"]}],"22":[{"m":"Oh yes, the days when everyone's prayer and any request was answered 🙏.\n\nOh, the disciples of Jesus indeed beheld glory as of the only Son of God.\n\nAnd indeed, even in our times we seek to see the power once more,\n\nThe real authentic power of God, as demonstrated by Christ and the early church.","dt":"2025-03-28T18:06:06","s":["922du5z99o"]}],"34":[{"m":"I do not quite understand these verses, but in the day men will have time to escape...\n\nBut in the night 🌃 one will be taken suddenly and another left.\n\nSome will be grinding and some in the field, so this is not making reference to a literal night season, but to a time of great darkness in a figurative sense, where there will be no mercy or time to escape.","dt":"2023-01-10T19:23:44","s":["yfp3bhen9b"]}],"37":[{"m":"Where, Lord?\n\n\"Where I am, there you will be also\"\n\n\"Where the body is, there the eagles 🦅 will be gathered\"\n\nAnd He will send His angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they will gather together His elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.","dt":"2023-04-28T09:07:52","s":["3k5hxdjnfv"]}]},"18":{"25":[{"m":"Mark gives more clarity to this statement.\n\nMark 10:23-24 KJV\nAnd Jesus looked round about, and saith unto his disciples, How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God! [24] And the disciples were astonished at his words. But Jesus answereth again, and saith unto them, Children, how hard is it for them that trust in riches to enter into the kingdom of God!","dt":"2023-01-10T22:49:18","s":["j0qpfc4g3v"]},{"m":"I don't understand: the man wanted to know how to inherit eternal life, and he had kept all the laws of God from his youth.\n\nBut he lacked one thing: he trusted in his riches to the extent that he could not give it up for God.\n\nBut I thought obeying the commands of God qualifies you for a place in the kingdom.\n\nBut here it seems we must really be sold out to enter the kingdom.\n\nThis man was a good man, but his riches were the only thing in his way.\n\nAnd he was not ready to exchange it for eternal life.\n\nSo now I wonder, when time comes to an end, where will this rich young ruler be?\n\nThis makes me wonder how the majority of us Christians will enter the kingdom, considering our current lifestyle.\n\nWe have been told all we need to do is to believe. But there seems to be more: we must not just believe in our Lord Jesus, we must be sold out to him.\n\nThe other thing is, this man asked for eternal life, and Jesus talks of it being hard to enter the kingdom of God.\n\nSo eternal life is in the kingdom of God, or is akin to the kingdom... By eternal life I believe it's in reference to the quality of life after death, where that quality is experienced in the presence of God.\n\nI believe eternal life is quality of life, because all souls live forever but are affected by the quality of life.\n\nSo now back to the earlier question 🙋: where will the rich young ruler be if he can't make the kingdom?\n\nHe will be outside the kingdom 👑, but where exactly?\n\nI don't think he'd go to hell... He'd likely be in the fringes in the earth 🌎, but not part of the New Jerusalem.","dt":"2025-03-29T08:40:38","s":["bx6nomsi1g"]}],"33":[{"m":"Even though Jesus knew these things beforehand 🖐️, it did not make it easier for him.\n\nHe almost gave up; it was good he knew these things ahead of time.\n\nElse it would have been very difficult for him to go through without knowing the glory to be revealed afterwards.","dt":"2025-03-29T09:35:28","s":["pwlrjrq5xg"]}],"38":[{"m":"He probably might have heard that the Messiah, the Christos, the Son of David ✡ was here and healing many.\n\nNow his opportunity was here, and he was not going to let it go.","dt":"2022-10-29T09:43:34","s":["dsexfytgyg"]}],"42":[{"m":"I can imagine, after such crying out, now Jesus tells him to receive his sight — he then begins to squint and try seeing, and lo, his sight cleared and he was healed.","dt":"2025-03-29T09:40:36","s":["bwfurm6itq"]}],"43":[{"m":"Ei, so these standers-by had no needs that Jesus could have met?\n\nRather, they were watching another man receive his miracle right before them, without them taking advantage to receive theirs.","dt":"2023-01-10T22:45:59","s":["ix97gltsup"]}]},"19":{"3":[{"m":"Why would such a chief publican want to see Jesus?\n\nThese publicans were public enemy no. 1. Yet somewhere in their hearts 💕 they longed to do what was right.\n\nThey had a place for God in their hearts, just that the system offered them the opportunity to get ahead by foul means.\n\nBut they had that desire for God still in their heart.\n\nHence Jesus was able to reach out to them.\n\nOf course, not all of them had this desire. As disciples, we reach out to all without prejudice, but in wisdom.","dt":"2022-11-01T06:07:59","s":["yy6a36ho1y"]}],"4":[{"m":"He ran before; being the shrewd businessman he was, he ran ahead of the pack, prepared as he waited for the opportunity.\n\nSecondly, how that a rich man like Zacchaeus was not bothered about keeping up appearances, but could climb 🧗‍♂️ a tree 🎄 and join the ordinary folks and seek to see Jesus.\nThat tells you about his personality — he was willing to stoop low in order to get what he wanted.\n\nJesus was indeed a big deal 🤝 for him to attract such a following. And for his stature to cause Zacchaeus to do all these.\n\nAnd indeed there is no shame in doing the most base of things in order to see God... To see the Son of God 🙂","dt":"2025-04-01T07:21:49","s":["tnxfsl4ip7"]}],"5":[{"m":"Oh, I can imagine the pride he must have had to not just catch a glimpse of the Son of God but to host him as well.\n\nOh, what an honour.","dt":"2025-04-01T07:22:47","s":["b3l5glwwi9"]}],"8":[{"m":"Once more Zacchaeus hits the nail on the head and cements his name in the annals of history and Christianity, and till today we tell the story of Zacchaeus.","dt":"2025-04-01T07:26:23","s":["2uda7w1lm8"]},{"m":"He must indeed have been very rich to give half his goods to the poor and restore fourfold the things he had taken.\n\nHe indeed was very rich, and that also goes to show that when he took anything not due him, he did not just spend it, but he multiplied it.\n\nAn interesting man he was.","dt":"2025-04-01T07:28:33","s":["umlcqy3j0a"]}],"6":[{"m":"😢 I can imagine the joy of Zacchaeus and the honour brought to him by Jesus visiting and dining at his house.\n\nI can imagine the bragging rights, especially before his friends, as they discuss how he managed to get this all-popular prophet, the acclaimed Messiah, to his house.","dt":"2022-11-01T06:22:45","s":["rh9xqfz1qv"]},{"m":"What a story he would have to tell his friends,\nwhen they enquire as to how he managed to get to host Jesus.","dt":"2025-04-01T07:23:46","s":["quazkx04nz"]}],"11":[{"m":"The kingdom should suddenly appear; they knew what the scriptures talk about concerning the Christ coming in the clouds 🌥 of glory.\n\nBut Jesus knew that time was not yet due.\n\nBut then why is it that Jesus says the kingdom of God cometh not with observation, but it's in our hearts?\n\nBecause the kingdom of God is us and the people and the earth 🌎, which would be inherited by the righteous.\n\nThat is the kingdom. It is not just his glorious appearing that makes the kingdom — that appearing is only descriptive of how he comes in grand style to inherit the kingdom.\n\nBut in reality we build and prepare the kingdom for him to inherit and sit on his throne as king 👑, for he is worthy.\n\nAs I typed these words, I said in my heart ♥ that, Oh God, I want to be a builder and contributor of the kingdom of God, so Christ comes to inherit of my works.\n\nI also want to build the kingdom.","dt":"2025-04-01T07:33:04","s":["tgye2lse7k"]}]},"20":{"2":[{"m":"He had come into their space and taken over.\n\nThe people listened to him more than any other.\n\nHe heals on the Sabbath; he had disciples and multitudes, which the Pharisees had not.\n\nHe strutted about with audacity (at least in the eyes of the Pharisees).\n\nWho gave him such powers?","dt":"2023-01-11T06:09:05","s":["r2ifbgy1os"]}],"3":[{"m":"By this time he had taken over the temple, in that the people paid attention to him and what he said ought to be.\n\nThat was why he could cleanse the temple 🏛 as he did.\n\nHe had become too powerful.","dt":"2023-04-28T10:00:47","s":["zxuxc90m1o"]}],"8":[{"m":"Even though, if they were really following his sermons and teachings, they would know.","dt":"2023-01-11T06:09:54","s":["mqoypych3v"]}],"16":[{"m":"They somehow knew he spoke this against them.\n\nThey loved their privileges and place so much to give it up.\n\nGod forbid indeed 🤧","dt":"2023-01-11T06:12:42","s":["56poboa6a"]}],"22":[{"m":"Why such a question 🙋?\n\nIf he said yes, they knew the Jews hated the Romans and did not want to pay taxes, and this would make him lose favour with the people.\n\nIf he said no, then it meant he was revolting against the king 👑 and would be arrested.\n\nSo he answered wisely.","dt":"2022-11-05T11:52:49","s":["3a9knkfr9u"]}],"31":[{"m":"How come these people did not see this as an evil 😈 pattern to be dealt with 👿, but watched until all these seven 7⃣ brothers died whiles the woman lived?\n\nBut you see, that goes to show that we need discernment to judge these things of patterns and evil bloodlines.\n\nFor instance, Naomi — she lost her husband, and her two sons all died in a foreign land.\n\nWas she a witch? Were there undealt-with patterns, or was it just ill luck — to the end that glory would be brought to her at the last?\n\nAnd her bond with her daughters-in-law shows her genuine spirit and heart ♥.\n\nLord, give us wisdom for these times, we pray.","dt":"2023-01-11T06:17:19","s":["q4jytjula3"]}],"35":[{"m":"Not all would obtain that world and the resurrection from the dead.","dt":"2023-01-11T06:18:34","s":["kljgj0aq5u"]}],"20":[{"m":"Chief priests, but had access to thieves, rogues, bearers of false news, who were at their beck and call 🤙.\n\nReady to please them. Are these priests really?","dt":"2023-05-02T06:40:22","s":["r3wb4vas9f"]}],"47":[{"m":"I love how the NLT puts this verse:\n\nLuke 20:47 NLT\n\"... Yet they shamelessly cheat widows out of their property and then pretend to be pious by making long prayers in public. Because of this, they will be severely punished.\"","dt":"2022-11-05T11:59:03","s":["birzxzurvd"]}]},"22":{"6":[{"m":"This connotes that in the absence of the multitudes, Jesus and his disciples literally hid themselves.\n\nThe whereabouts and ways were not known.\n\nJesus knew they wanted to kill him, so he smartly hid in plain sight with the multitudes during the day and slipped out of plain sight during the night, when the multitudes were not there.","dt":"2022-11-13T07:20:08","s":["fnutonjjrx"]},{"m":"So that was the key 🗝, how to get Jesus in the absence of the crowd.\n\nAnd their plan was to try him by night and have him on course to death before the crowds rose up by day.\n\nSuch injustice.","dt":"2023-01-11T06:35:05","s":["1bhwvrpfys"]}],"15":[{"m":"Why did he desire this moment?\n\nI guess because he was going to annul the Old Testament and establish the New.","dt":"2022-11-13T07:28:23","s":["e3xyhkzobt"]}],"22":[{"m":"Did Judas hear all of this?\n\nOr he was too far gone to change his mind.\n\nOr he deemed the words of Jesus irrelevant and gibberish.\n\nHe had had enough of this Messiah with his stories.\n\nIf the others were easy to be fooled, he wasn't.\n\nWho made Jesus his master? They were all somewhere minding their business when Jesus called them, and now he was lording it over them.\n\nHe was going to do what he wanted to do regardless!\n\nEven when Jesus looked at him and told him to go ahead with what he wanted, he still did.","dt":"2023-05-02T08:04:52","s":["mn05jk2ouo"]}],"36":[{"m":"Why such an instruction... I guess because the times had changed.\n\nHe was about to be numbered among the transgressors. Darkness was coming, and they would not be able to walk 🚶 about as at the first.\n\nDangerous times were coming, and he was going to be killed.\n\nIn such times his disciples needed to protect themselves physically.\n\nUnder such circumstances, preaching was not going to happen for them to live off their labours.\n\nThey had to get their own purse for their survival.","dt":"2022-11-13T07:37:34","s":["shqtsz5q4w"]},{"m":"Yes, because the times had changed; evil 😈 was now upon them and the hour of darkness had come.\n\nIn this time and era they would have to hide, because their Saviour and Messiah would be killed.\n\nThis was not the time to go out in twos where you will be welcomed to dinner; no, that time will come again, but not now.\n\nSo he asked them to brace themselves for physical defence. Not to go attacking, but to defend themselves.","dt":"2023-01-11T06:54:51","s":["hcuulbdqat"]}],"40":[{"m":"Prayer is important to keep in step with the Spirit and to receive divine enablement to even live the Christ life in the face of evil.\n\nSame admonition he gave concerning his coming.\n\nThat we should watch and pray, so we don't miss it and it come on us unawares.","dt":"2023-01-11T07:00:18","s":["391auyptle"]}],"46":[{"m":"This statement is very instructive: in sorrow, pain and affliction it is very difficult to pray, but that is when we must.","dt":"2022-11-13T07:39:46","s":["cqwdulfgfb"]},{"m":"Jesus Christ kept himself in the love of God through constant prayer 🙏, and he was here teaching his disciples the same.","dt":"2025-04-14T07:06:56","s":["lm33ugy2w2"]}],"58":[{"m":"He would have been caught as a spy... He had to save his skin.","dt":"2025-04-14T07:10:32","s":["hlrxebasmn"]}],"61":[{"m":"How Jesus, who was undergoing trial and was about to die,\n\nhow Jesus, who a few hours ago almost gave up the course 🏇,\n\ncould remember to keep track of the crowing of a cock 🐓 and turn to look upon Peter is itself supernatural.\n\nLord, help 😣 Lord, have mercy, Lord, strengthen and give grace.","dt":"2023-02-16T11:37:35","s":["xah7fq76n9"]}]},"23":{"2":[{"m":"But were they not expecting Christ to be the king 👑... Such hypocrisy.\n\nThey knew the Christ will be a king 👑, and yet they used that same line as witness against him, to accuse him of treason.","dt":"2023-01-11T07:06:58","s":["8vyzpw8wzs"]}],"25":[{"m":"So what did they do to Barabbas upon his release?\n\nHe was a murderer. Did they not fear 😱 for their lives and that of their kids 🧒?\n\nDid they not fear another sedition, which runs the risk of the Romans coming to destroy them to cut out all rebellion?\n\nTheir hatred for this innocent man was unreasonable.","dt":"2023-01-11T07:11:53","s":["8k41xbu7un"]}],"26":[{"m":"Why did Luke leave out the details of him being scourged before, en route to the road of crucifixion?","dt":"2023-05-05T06:34:29","s":["or1667yz9r"]}],"42":[{"m":"By this request he already affirmed his belief in Jesus as the Christ, in the kingdom of God and his teachings concerning the kingdom 👑.\n\nHe so believed, he wanted to be part.\n\nProbably he had heard Jesus teaching whilst he was on operation in the market or temple, stealing.\n\nIt pierced his heart ♥ and brought regret, but not repentance.\n\nBut now he acknowledges Jesus as Lord.","dt":"2023-05-05T06:42:54","s":["6co22fuyvs"]}],"43":[{"m":"Just like that, and this guy was allowed into paradise...\n\nHe knew Jesus had a kingdom, so in all likelihood he had heard the gospel but refused to accept, though his heart ♥ pierced him.\n\nAnd now here he was; God graciously had given him another chance 🤞, side by side with the Christos.\n\nAnd he accepted and repented, and God graciously accepted him.","dt":"2022-11-18T12:58:51","s":["y6pu948x95"]},{"m":"Just like that, he did not say the sinner's prayer; he did repent and confess Christ.\n\nHe was not born again nor Spirit-filled, but he was repentant.\n\nAnd that was all that was needed; he went into paradise to meet Abraham and other righteous 🎎 folks.","dt":"2023-01-11T07:22:01","s":["0z3gr82dl0"]}],"46":[{"m":"Why did he cry out with a loud voice?\n\nIt was after this that he commended his spirit to God.","dt":"2025-04-14T06:35:56","s":["f6p9v7sgoo"]}],"54":[{"m":"The Sabbath starting at 6pm that day.","dt":"2025-04-17T12:37:52","s":["r8zh9jgd1p"]}],"49":[{"m":"Wickedness had had its way.\n\nThe leaders had, by trickery and subtlety, killed Jesus faster than the people could react or bring a case in a just court of law.","dt":"2023-01-11T07:25:03","s":["1ikq327tcc"]}]},"24":{"4":[{"m":"This grave site became a heaven of angelic 👼 beings long time.","dt":"2023-05-05T07:38:06","s":["43hkk1ofrc"]}],"45":[{"m":"So the obvious can be before our 👀, but we will not see nor understand it.\n\nThat is why it's possible for the word to be stolen by the evil one.\n\nThat is also why we must keep praying 🙏 for all, because unbelief is real.","dt":"2023-01-11T08:04:27","s":["sp180oc6cq"]}]},"21":{"34":[{"m":"In Lk. 21:34-36 we have the promise of Jesus that the saved will be accounted worthy to escape all these things, and to stand before the Son of Man. The things they will escape are those of Mt. 24:4-26 Lk. 21:4-19 and Rev. 6--Rev. 19. – the above is what Dake's says, but I think differently...\nI think this means as we watch and pray always, God will guide our hearts and enable us to escape the plagues and judgement that will come upon the earth. I don't think it means God will rapture us even before these things happen, so we don't even experience them to begin with.","dt":"2025-06-08T16:49:23","s":["1tuinu6uc1"]}]}},"Mark":{"1":{"5":[{"m":"John must have been a very powerful preacher.\n\nTo bring people to that point of repentance.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:29:41","s":["nn75ulnn0o"]}],"13":[{"m":"Satan himself tempted him. He knew him.\n\nWell, even men like Simon, Anna and Co knew him... How much more Satan and the dark world 🗺 saw the signs that he had come.\n\nNow what could they do about it, within the limits of the laws of God and of the spirit and material world 🗺 that God had set up?","dt":"2022-10-04T08:46:58","s":["mxncfv2ueo"]}],"15":[{"m":"The time is fulfilled indeed... He, Jesus, was now here.\n\nThe kingdom is at hand 🖐️. He","dt":"2022-10-04T08:35:34","s":["gx0v9yrwav"]},{"m":"This kingdom of God was the long-awaited kingdom that the prophets had spoken of.\n\nThe kingdom of God by his Christ, where God would dwell with men.\n\nJESUS tells them it is near.\n\nPreceding Jesus's Gospel was that of John, who preached repentance.\n\nFor through repentance and a contrite heart one enters the coming kingdom.\n\nJohn was indeed a forerunner to the Christ, and his message was apt to prepare men for the good news.","dt":"2025-01-23T08:16:35","s":["zo8ib0m0k6"]}],"17":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 I don't get it... There's something missing. No one just gets up and starts following a man who randomly walks up to them and tells them to follow him...\n\nIn John's account we see why Philip, Nathaniel and Peter followed him. They were disciples of John, so obviously knew he was the Christ, and they informed their brethren, who then joined them in the course.\n\nCould it be that they had already heard of this miracle-working rabbi who was possibly the Saviour?\n\nThus providing a premise for them to choose to follow him? That sounds more like it.","dt":"2021-12-08T09:24:03","s":["xth5x0avsz"]}],"20":[{"m":"In Luke's account these helped Peter with the large catch... That account is not stated in Mark.\n\nHowever, I believe all these contributed to their saying yes to the call. Which Mark just only makes mention of.\n\nYou see, sometimes in this life God touches and meets us at our point of need, then we realise how much more there is in God to receive and how little our need is... We break down and surrender to his course.\n\nWe realise how irrelevant our own course 🏇 is, and we choose to align ourselves with a greater good 👋, indeed the best course 🏇.","dt":"2021-12-08T09:37:36","s":["9i2sy65gra"]}],"21":[{"m":"Straightaway... He had focus and a sense of mission and purpose.\n\nNo time to waste 🗑","dt":"2022-10-04T08:36:54","s":["m2dy5886un"]}],"28":[{"m":"Immediate fame and popularity... But he was long prepared for this season.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:40:19","s":["dka3cd38sa"]}],"32":[{"m":"Word had traveled, word had gone round very quickly about this miracle worker 👷.\n\nPeople want results, that's all. Results, nothing else... You provide it and they come to you... Not for you, but for the results.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:42:20","s":["y696ifj0tr"]}],"34":[{"m":"But these devils 👿, why were they interested in exposing him... Was it to buy time, or they spoke because they had been caught?\n\nAlso, how did these devils know him, and yet the very people he came to did not?\n\nThat means the dark kingdom and spirit realm is well organized.\n\nWord had gone round even amongst them, and they knew him.","dt":"2022-10-04T08:44:18","s":["n9otbnhb48"]},{"m":"The agenda at this time was not to reign as king, but to die as a lamb.\n\nThat would have been compromised if the crowds knew who he was.\n\nThey obviously would have fought the Romans, knowing very well that their time had come.\n\nSo Jesus hid himself, but at his second coming there will be no more hiding; all eyes will see him.","dt":"2025-01-23T08:26:40","s":["9qd6vkf2wo"]}],"45":[{"m":"The crowds were great indeed. He tried to contain it, but it did not work.\n\nHe was indeed a city set on a hill.","dt":"2022-10-04T09:51:51","s":["r52s56reu9"]},{"m":"Now the new protocol to control the crowds was to be in desert places.\n\nSo I guess unless your situation is really that dire and your hunger pure, you will not follow him to the wilderness.","dt":"2023-01-26T10:33:30","s":["5zrjtpvqa1"]}],"25":[{"m":"There were and have been many mysteries hidden from men of all ages, and now they were being revealed by Christ.\n\nWhere in the world did this come from? They seem to know each other.\n\nIn other scenarios the spirits asked if he had come out to destroy them before the time.\n\nSuch conversations are never revealed in the Old Testament, and now we are seeing Jesus with knowledge of spirits and ancient agreements and times.\n\nHe indeed was before he was born.","dt":"2025-01-23T08:23:31","s":["rfwrxb1np1"]}]},"2":{"5":[{"m":"We have exhibited such audacious faith, and yet our sick have not been made well.\n\nThey have rather gotten worse and worse beyond remedy and died.\n\nAnd we were left wondering if the word of God was true.\n\nInstead of wondering at the men who claimed to represent what the word of God stood for.\n\nWe wondered at the wrong thing; our wonder should have been if the so-called men of God and disciples of Christ were true.\n\nGod's word was and remains true; the men who claim to be sent from him were false.\n\nFalse in that they feigned having his power when they did not.","dt":"2025-02-01T07:55:34","s":["ijxbcy63x"]}],"7":[{"m":"That was their thinking.\n\nSo for Jesus to have publicly said that he was forgiving the man's sin\n\nwas alluding to his deity.","dt":"2023-01-26T10:35:09","s":["jgni8h0h51"]}],"12":[{"m":"Indeed, they had never seen power exercised in such fashion.\n\nAll they knew prior were the teachings of the Pharisees,\n\nwords without power.\n\nToday, we have the same teachings of men of God, words without power. Worse than that is words with feigned power,\nwolves in sheep's clothing who devour the flock, and use their wool for clothing; they take the milk for themselves and eat the young ones as well...\n\nI can imagine Peter and Co coming to our world today, to see that some of the richest people in a country are not Christians but the pastors who lead them.\n\nThey take from them their money in the name of God to amass riches for themselves;\nthey devour the flock by sleeping with the members, and those who refuse are raped and gagged or ostracised.\n\nThere is an anomaly in the body and among the called.\n\nSomething is amiss.\n\nPeter and Co would not recognise Christianity if they were to come live in our times.","dt":"2025-02-01T08:19:20","s":["pgzt4y9mu5"]}],"13":[{"m":"What was he teaching them? ☺","dt":"2021-12-15T09:40:27","s":["qh7fpx99hn"]}],"14":[{"m":"Jesus had quite 🤫 an interesting way of calling people. He seems to speak once and move on as if nothing happened.\n\nNot much cajoling and pleading 🙏.\n\nI think it is pretty simple. If you have seen all the signs and his great fame about him, and how he bids you come... you have all you need to make an informed decision.","dt":"2021-12-15T09:42:43","s":["66npg6vjul"]},{"m":"The way Jesus calls people... Simply follow me, and that's that.","dt":"2023-01-27T10:52:52","s":["1wsdj3cwwh"]}],"17":[{"m":"This was not to say the Pharisees were righteous, but they SELF-claimed to be, and so, playing along with them, Jesus made them understand that they needed not him nor his company.\n\nHe knew their evil heart and ways.","dt":"2025-02-07T07:11:12","s":["ikm5j4a74k"]}],"22":[{"m":"The new and the old covenants cannot mix up. The old must go for the new to come.","dt":"2022-10-07T09:20:04","s":["dy4x9ki6xc"]},{"m":"In the days when the bridegroom is taken away, they will fast.\n\nBut for now the bridegroom 🤵 is here, so they celebrate 🎉 and make merry.\n\nThese my disciples are like old wine 🍷 skins.\nThey must be renewed to contain the new wine of Christianity which I'll pour out on them.\n\nFor now their happy-go-lucky selves must undergo changes to meet the future responsibility of Christianity.\n\nJust as you will not sew a new cloth on an old, lest you injure the old and the tear is made worse, so my disciples are undergoing the requisite training.\n\nEven after such times of power and glory with Christ, they went back to fishing when he died.\n\nThey were still not ready, till after his resurrection Jesus had to show himself to them bodily.\n\nEven then they still did not know what to do, till Jesus came back to their hearts 💕 and entered their spirit in the person of the Holy Spirit.\n\nThen they knew what to do and could actually do it.\n\nThe Holy Spirit is all we need.","dt":"2023-01-27T11:05:21","s":["ylog9fn7ly"]}],"27":[{"m":"Jesus knew his exact mission and what he was here to do.\n\nHe knew what would be abolished in his death and what new thing would be established from his rising forth.","dt":"2022-10-07T09:19:17","s":["o4ss1mb7ps"]}]},"3":{"30":[{"m":"So herein lies the blasphemy. Jesus had the Spirit of God, yet they said he had an unclean spirit.\n\nAnd it was not for lack of knowledge or ignorance 🤷‍♂️ that the Pharisees said what they said.\n\nNo, it was to discredit Jesus - the Son and Saviour.\n\nTheir hearts were too filled with jealousy to see any good in the good.","dt":"2021-12-16T07:55:31","s":["e3v49mtumz"]}],"6":[{"m":"Such wickedness, even in the religious circles.\n\nThat they wanted to kill a man for doing good.\n\nThese guys were pure evil.","dt":"2022-10-09T06:57:13","s":["sso2k12hd7"]}]},"4":{"40":[{"m":"These things bear more study...\nJesus, in asking this question, was surprised they were fearful 😨...\n\nThis is not casting a devil out oo. This is a storm, a life and ☠ death ☠ matter, but to Jesus it was all the same matter of faith.","dt":"2021-12-17T22:29:34","s":["mvse1hnyy9"]}],"12":[{"m":"But why... Why would God not want them to see, hear, for them to be converted and their sins forgiven them?\n\nIs it that the Lord did not want them converted? Because it seems that once the people reach the point of conversion, there is none else hindering but for them to be healed, for their sins to be forgiven...\n\nOf course he wants them, but their own ways hindered them... Thus the Lord will not cast his pearls before swine 🐽.\n\nCos how come some received the understanding of mysteries whiles others did not?","dt":"2021-12-17T15:47:31","s":["iz5ob1nsat"]}]},"5":{"2":[{"m":"The issue of people with unclean spirits seems quite commonplace in Jesus's time.\n\nOr rather, because one showed up with such power, they were coming out of their hiding before they be exposed.","dt":"2023-02-01T10:52:21","s":["sqm6rtzh0n"]}],"7":[{"m":"How did these spirits know these things? What meeting had been held discussing Jesus and how not to mess with him?","dt":"2021-12-17T22:31:21","s":["xnt4x5si9g"]}],"13":[{"m":"What was the point of asking to possess the pigs, only to drown them in the river?\n\nAnd why did Jesus allow such destruction?","dt":"2023-02-02T11:46:59","s":["ae274ksv8l"]}],"36":[{"m":"Jesus knew that sometimes a word is all that is needed to destroy one's faith and walk of progress in faith.\n\nA lot of damage can be done.\n\nSee how Peter almost drowned if Jesus had not been there.\n\nMay have shipwrecked because of misinformation and seeds of doubt.\n\nJesus had to stop this seed err before it gained root.","dt":"2023-02-02T11:52:48","s":["uha3dbpbdh"]}],"37":[{"m":"Could it be that because he was so sure the damsel will rise, he deliberately sacked the crowd so the miracle could be done in private, and so he controls the crowds that will follow after such a miracle?","dt":"2021-12-17T22:34:57","s":["qnkwj8agvi"]}],"39":[{"m":"Faith remains true and living and working.","dt":"2021-12-17T22:35:23","s":["qlcxz6ym32"]}],"43":[{"m":"Hmm... 🤔 Interesting, real interesting. Once the miracle was done, she needed to do that.\n\nThis is where as believers we err often. After the miraculous, or even in the course of the miraculous, we overstep our boundaries and leave everything to the supernatural, even where we have not been commanded.\n\nLet's not go beyond what is written or spoken. Lest we hurt ourselves on this journey.","dt":"2021-12-17T22:38:13","s":["ge51ajnxhk"]}],"17":[{"m":"Why did they plead with the master to leave? Were they afraid the devils would come back with revenge or something... Well.","dt":"2025-03-08T07:04:08","s":["wqp1719o5w"]}]},"6":{"3":[{"m":"Obviously these knew not of the virgin birth, nor of the other miraculous events surrounding the birth of Jesus.\n\nMary and Joseph had kept these in their hearts 💕 and wondered at what those signs meant, as scripture says.\n\nThose who knew, the shepherds, the wise men, the priests of Herod who gave the location of Jesus for several babies 🤱 to be killed, were all likely dead or very old 🧓.\n\nSome may have relocated and heard of this miracle-working teacher and prophet, but just couldn't draw the correlation...\n\nSee, even his own brethren and those in his home 🏡, who should have drawn the correlation, couldn't, and walked 🚶 on in unbelief.\n\nNot even John the Baptist recognized him as that his cousin, who when he was a child a prophecy was spoken of them both.\n\nIt took the Spirit to help him make Jesus out as the Messiah.\n\nThis shows that life happens to all... People just move on. There are yet, though, a few people, really real few people, who are able to keep the linkage 🔗 and the words spoken.\n\nTo see the full manifestations of prophecies and keep walking in it.\n\nThese are so few that in this case we see only Mary the mother of Jesus being the only common factor 🏭 from when Jesus received the messianic prophecies to his full manifestation.\n\nThis makes me wonder, what happened to Joseph? It's surprising 😲, particularly considering the culture, to call 🤙 Jesus the son of Mary without mentioning Joseph.\n\nProbably Joseph also was dead at the time ⌚. How that happened we know not.\n\nInterestingly, his brothers and sisters did not believe him. The million dollar question 🙋 was why.\n\nWas Jesus too human for such a claim of deity? Or 🥇 they were all playing childhood games and climbing 🧗‍♂️ trees 🎄 to working together as carpenters.\n\nThey just couldn't and did not appreciate the transition.\n\nTheir elder brother, the book 📙 worm and rabbi in the making, goes to Judea, gets baptized by the popular preacher John the Baptist, and suddenly everything changes 💱.\n\n'Yeah, we know our brother was the spiritual rabbi 🐰 type, but 🥅 where from this whole Messiah drift...\nAnd o, mummy seems to be in on this whole Messiah thing.\n\nNow she's telling us some stuff about our elder brother's birth, which she had kept secret all these years for \"our safety\", she claims.\n\nAt one time Herod wanted to kill us, I mean kill our brother, way before we were born, and all this was kept hidden from us.\n\nSo we were that important to the king 👑. That makes sense as to why it's now that mum is telling us all this - after our brother's sudden manifestation of miracle and crowd-pulling stunts - let's wait and see 👁‍🗨'\n\nThis kinda sums the state of Mary, Jesus, his brothers and country men.","dt":"2021-12-20T07:53:16","s":["s6zte5tn5m"]}],"6":[{"m":"I believe they hindered and limited the Holy One of God through their unbelief.","dt":"2023-02-04T15:03:19","s":["b6e3bzc6mx"]}],"14":[{"m":"Hi, how did the apostles know this? Unless it is public knowledge, then it sure should have a record elsewhere, aside the Gospels.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:34:33","s":["65111uyruj"]}],"16":[{"m":"Funny how gossip goes... Jesus had a home and a family 👪. He was called Jesus of Nazareth, yet he was being called John the Baptist, Elias etc. from the dead...\n\nHow could that possibly happen? But well, rumors and gossips are so.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:37:39","s":["oubh35l36t"]}],"20":[{"m":"He heard John gladly, yet killed him because of politics. And vainness.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:48:40","s":["511hbt3jlz"]},{"m":"What many things did Herod do?\n\nCould it be that John gave him some specific instructions or prophetic word from God to govern his realm?\n\nIt could well be so.\n\nIt is interesting that a man like John, though imprisoned, was heard by Herod because of his divine connection to God.\n\nIt seems that as men of God, we are ordinary and like all men, we are castigated and imprisoned.\n\nWe are ordinary men until we are not.\n\nUntil suddenly God shows up in us and we are extraordinary.","dt":"2023-02-04T15:06:28","s":["qrdf0sdkz8"]}],"22":[{"m":"One can't be too sure and too careless in the corridors of power.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:39:30","s":["xjys9r0ehk"]}],"24":[{"m":"This woman was such a bloodthirsty schemer and seductress. Not caring how her husband, who seems to love this prophet 🥀, will feel.\n\nAnd how it will affect his kingdom.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:50:55","s":["b7ourykrqi"]}],"41":[{"m":"It is good to bless what we eat.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:46:07","s":["ofcy5xw005"]}],"23":[{"m":"Unto half 🌗 of my kingdom...? What an innocent request. Obviously his stepdaughter was not going to ask for half the kingdom.\n\nBut she did ask for something that shook even the king himself.\n\nSee how vain men can be 🐝. In his merriment he played careless.\n\nThat is how the people of this world 🗺 are. So vain in their dictates. Just because of a dance he loses something so valuable.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:43:15","s":["jj4kdcu8n6"]}],"25":[{"m":"She came with haste... So she was in on this. And what a moment of joy and glee for these two ✌️.","dt":"2021-12-20T10:44:33","s":["vw9dbdohqv"]}],"48":[{"m":"Really 🤯 😳😳😳... He would have walked 🚶 past?","dt":"2022-10-27T12:10:25","s":["2uttzaeke4"]}]},"7":{"8":[{"m":"Isn't this what is happening in our churches today?\n\nThe traditions of the elders as described here, though not commanded by God, was not exactly sinful.\n\nIn fact, it was not sinful. The challenge came in, however, when the law of God was conveniently replaced by these traditions.\n\nIt became an excuse justifiable to break the laws of God.\n\nFunny enough, they would go to as far as possible 🙆 to keep and hold on to the traditions, yet when it came to the laws of God they let it go.\nThey laid it aside.\n\nTraditions and structuring and church culture and systems are good.\n\nTo build a large and formidable organization you need these.\n\nBut 🥅 for these to replace or counteract the very laws of God. Hmm 🤔 no, no.\n\nSome of the traditions of men: women should not wear jeans 👖, not perm ♾ hair, not wear jewelry 💍, must read the founder's or organization's books 📚, yet the Bible is not equally emphasized.\n\nHoly living 🛋 and purity is not equally stressed and checked as much as dyed or permed hair etc.\n\nI really feel strongly about these things. It must be checked.","dt":"2021-12-23T07:23:41","s":["882w2yelj3"]}],"9":[{"m":"In order to keep organizations and churches growing, we sacrifice people. Hurt them; some people leave the church ⛪ and abandon God, never to return, because of hurts by church members and leaders of churches.\n\nPeople are sacrificed, lied upon and isolated to keep truth about a man of God or ministry from coming out.\n\nYet after these the error is not even corrected. And lies 🤥 keep being peddled in order to save face 😔 of men 🚹.","dt":"2021-12-23T07:28:18","s":["dkjwcp3cez"]}],"22":[{"m":"Yet we make so many external laws in our churches, and yes, that's for good reason, but as we do that we should focus on what's inside the man or woman 👩.\n\nFocus should be made on building 🏢 the spirit of men and women.\n\nAnd caution and constant internalisation should be done to ensure we build right 👉, so we don't replace the laws of God with our traditions.","dt":"2021-12-23T07:34:16","s":["o1oohoqahs"]}],"33":[{"m":"He took him aside to prevent uncontrollable crowds, who, the more they saw such miracles, the more prone they were to make him king 👑.\n\nAlso, he needed to have a life; there were times they could not even eat because of the crowds.\n\nThis miracle was a bit unpalatable, the whole spitting into someone's mouth 👄.","dt":"2023-02-06T08:51:20","s":["624esbr5xx"]}],"37":[{"m":"Amen, he hath indeed done all things well.","dt":"2022-10-27T12:54:26","s":["3jy4lvh6j"]}],"30":[{"m":"Long-distance demon casting.\n\nThat was how wonderful Jesus was.\n\nThis demonstrates devils can be dealt with from afar.\n\nHmm 🤔, interesting.","dt":"2023-02-06T08:52:49","s":["up7pzxeihi"]}]},"8":{"2":[{"m":"Wow... Jesus did a camp meeting... Three days of word fest.\n\nSo the feeding of the 4000 was as a result of 3 days of hunger, not because they skipped lunch.\n\nMiracles are in most cases indeed to meet needs that otherwise cannot be met naturally.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:39:06","s":["so4gsf7pod"]}],"3":[{"m":"Jesus was up to speed with the needs of his people and knew who came from where, and the state of his people.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:40:03","s":["hrfdn82w8n"]}],"10":[{"m":"Which place is this too?","dt":"2021-12-23T08:14:56","s":["c4sccjfqyd"]}],"21":[{"m":"Jesus could discern the state of people's hearts 💕.\n\nHe saw that their hearts were hardened, and by this he meant they, seeing, refused to see and understand and remember.\n\nHe had fed 5000, so obviously what would a lack of bread for a few people be to him? It was no task at all.\n\nSo he wondered why his disciples took his words carnally to mean he, Jesus, was concerned about scarcity of bread 🥪.\n\nHe expected them to know better and to understand.\n\nSo hardness of heart happens when the evidence for believing and submitting to spiritual wisdom and instruction is glaring at you in the face, yet you refuse to accept the truth.","dt":"2022-10-20T06:50:07","s":["wl3zctcicv"]}],"26":[{"m":"Why did Jesus keep up this game?\n\nHe did not want crowds gathering. But why?\n\nYou know why... He was not here to be king 👑, which the people really wanted to.\n\nAnd every miracle inched him closer.\n\nSo he had to navigate his way to continue doing good without inciting the people.","dt":"2021-12-23T08:18:15","s":["4nread5694"]}],"33":[{"m":"I thought Satan did not know God's plan, so contributed actively in killing Jesus.\n\nBut if here he's rebuking Jesus from going to the cross, then why did he later have him killed????😎\n\nHmm 🤔... Calls for more thinking and study 💭","dt":"2022-10-20T06:53:26","s":["gg85yfjl0m"]}]},"9":{"4":[{"m":"The question 🙋 yet arises... How did they know?","dt":"2021-12-24T10:04:56","s":["r47o5iwsmg"]}],"5":[{"m":"How did he know?","dt":"2021-12-24T10:05:19","s":["asprh6ec41"]}],"10":[{"m":"Though Jesus had plainly stated that he would be killed and he will rise up, they still seem not to get it.\n\nIn retrospect and out of hindsight, it is easy for us to understand that this was no parable.\n\nHe meant it literally. He had often talked about how he would come back in clouds ⛅ of glory to judge the living 🛋 and dead,\n\nhow he would have to die and be risen in three days' time.\n\nI guess all these had some long distant, not so near future 🔮 application.\n\nAfter all, Jesus was now just about 33 years. So why is he talking of death and rising, if not in some very distant future 🔮?","dt":"2021-12-24T10:15:02","s":["fcx95prphy"]}],"25":[{"m":"So the spirit was not only cast out, but an embargo was placed in him not to enter him no more.\n\nThis spirit had had access from childhood of this lad and could come in again after he's driven out, so was prevented from doing so.","dt":"2022-10-21T06:36:04","s":["xc8c8paq66"]},{"m":"When Jesus saw that crowds were gathering for a spectacle and showdown, he delayed no further in casting out the spirit.\n\nHe did not want a scene and crowds.","dt":"2023-02-10T09:05:10","s":["dsnd3m1ou9"]}],"31":[{"m":"Would his more public and direct stating of his death ☠ and resurrection have prevented his death?\n\nThis the Pharisees might do to prevent his prediction from happening.","dt":"2021-12-24T22:25:34","s":["pujas72js2"]}],"50":[{"m":"Akin to you are the salt of the earth and the light of the world 🗺","dt":"2022-10-21T06:39:47","s":["q66e08pwkp"]}],"2":[{"m":"If by the kingdom of God come with power was in reference to the transfiguration, then indeed it was with power.\n\nMoses, Elijah and Jesus in one boat 🛥.\nCrazy...","dt":"2022-10-21T06:25:07","s":["pwiqsmk6zd"]}],"13":[{"m":"Where is it written of the suffering of Elias, aka John the Baptist?","dt":"2025-03-22T10:01:03","s":["8b7r9kuz7t"]}]},"10":{"2":[{"m":"Why such a question? What prompted this thought process for them to tempt him with this particular question of all questions 🙋?\n\nHad Jesus made a statement indicating his stand on divorce, hence this angle of questioning used against him?","dt":"2023-02-11T10:29:05","s":["whp6cte3hc"]}],"5":[{"m":"Wow, this Jesus... Imagine this young 30 year old man 👨🏿 teaching and instructing these learned leaders and elders, doctors and teachers of the law.\n\nNo wonder they detested him so much.\n\nHe was disdainful... Such a young man commanding such authority.\n\nIndeed, is this not Joseph the carpenter's son?","dt":"2023-02-11T10:33:42","s":["mlrocz50qv"]}],"8":[{"m":"I think children are a good depiction of the one flesh.\n\nSharing the chromosomes of both parents.\n\nIs that what happens when you have sex?\n\nYou share your body and yourselves. You intertwine in a way.","dt":"2023-02-11T10:38:57","s":["ix4ve1y29h"]},{"m":"1 Corinthians 6:18 KJV\nFlee fornication. Every sin that a man doeth is without the body; but he that committeth fornication sinneth against his own body.\n\n1 Corinthians 6:16 KJV\nWhat? know ye not that he which is joined to an harlot is one body? for two, saith he, shall be one flesh.\n\nI'm trying to figure out how the one flesh is accomplished, but it seems there is something about sex that makes people exchange of themselves.","dt":"2023-02-11T10:52:55","s":["nkhs37a0nl"]}],"11":[{"m":"So after giving his public view on the matter, he tells his private view to his disciples.","dt":"2025-03-30T11:51:43","s":["sdpatdy8lx"]}],"22":[{"m":"He couldn't forgo the great possessions for the eternal life he so claimed he wanted, and which laws he had kept from childhood.\n\nNow Jesus was offering him something greater than the eternal.\n\nA place with him, God.\n\nWhat can be compared to God? But he missed it.\n\nLord, have mercy and let us not miss you, we pray.","dt":"2023-02-11T12:07:04","s":["usd92nca09"]}],"26":[{"m":"So obviously, like is natural to men, we all want some comfort.\n\nAnd indeed it is not anti-Christ to desire good things.\n\nSo Jesus saying it could hinder their part in the kingdom bothered them.\n\nFor they loved the kingdom also very much 🙏.\n\nSo Jesus clarified and brought balance to the discussion.","dt":"2023-02-11T12:11:12","s":["uhetdbn58m"]}],"34":[{"m":"Jesus had seen his own death many times.\n\nHow else could he have so vividly described what was about to happen to him?","dt":"2022-10-30T07:12:15","s":["7pm9xyim5v"]}],"41":[{"m":"Such faith, they so trusted Jesus that they were already sharing heavenly inheritance they were yet to see.\n\nThis was how compelling the evidence for Jesus as Messiah was.\n\nYet this same evidence for others meant he needed to die, lest they lose their place, i.e. the Pharisees.","dt":"2022-10-30T07:14:42","s":["bjiibcypri"]}],"52":[{"m":"Go thy way is the command, but after receiving his healing, as is the case for most of us 🙏... Go thy way becomes a voluntary I will rather follow your way, because there is something you know that I don't know.\n\nSo obviously you know a better way than my way.","dt":"2022-10-30T07:17:23","s":["sa95q0e4gf"]}],"47":[{"m":"It seems the common man on the streets knew about the Messiah and certain key attributes he was to possess.\n\nFor example, here the blind man knew he was to be a son of David.\n\nThe disciples after the transfiguration on the mountains knew that Elijah was to come first.\n\nSo they knew the signs of the Messiah in general, just that at times Jesus confused them a bit, but all in all he chose to demonstrate and prove who he was rather than to make verbal claims.","dt":"2025-03-29T09:39:03","s":["nsex46p5yw"]}],"3":[{"m":"He sends them back to the law ⚖.\n\nHe knew these Pharisees, else they start to spread rumors that Jesus teaches the people against the law of Moses.\n\nIt seems they had tried this before, because somewhere Jesus drives home the point that he had come not to break the law but to fulfill it.","dt":"2023-02-11T10:31:27","s":["5r1i11ysie"]}]},"11":{"11":[{"m":"Was this not where in other accounts he cleansed the temple?\n\nHowever, Dake's Study Bible gives some notes worth looking at.\n\n\"Notes For Verse 45 a [cast out them that sold therein, and them that bought] This is the third purification of the temple. The first one is earlier in His ministry (Jn. 2:15). The second is a few days earlier than this at the first triumphal entry (Mt. 21:12; Mk. 11:15) taking place Friday before the crucifixion. After spending Thursday night at the home of Zacchaeus in Jericho (Lk. 19:1-21), Jesus goes to Jerusalem on Friday and makes His first entry (Mt. 21:1-16). He returns to Bethany where He passes the Sabbath, where He eats the first of three suppers, and where the first of two anointings takes place (Mt. 21:17 Jn. 12:1-11). On Sunday He makes His second triumphal entry and returns to Bethany (Mk. 11:1-11 Lk. 19:29-44 Jn. 12:12-19). On Monday He returns to Jerusalem, cleanses the temple, teaches, curses the fig tree, and goes out of the city (Mt. 21:18-22 Mk. 11:12-19 Lk. 19:45-48 Jn. 12:20-50). On Tuesday He goes back to Jerusalem, teaches, gives the prophecies of Mt. 24-25 Mk. 13; Lk. 21 and returns to Bethany to have the second supper and second anointing (Mt. 21:23--Mt. 26:13; Mk. 11:20--Mk. 14:9; Lk. 20:1--Lk. 21:38). On Wednesday, which is from Tuesday sunset to Wednesday sunset, or on our Tuesday night the last supper is held and Judas betrays Jesus. The Gethsemane prayer, the arrest, the trials throughout Tuesday night (or the first part of their Wednesday) and all the events of the crucifixion and burial end on Wednesday at sunset (Mt. 26:14--Mt. 27:66; Mk. 14:10--Mk. 15:47; Lk. 22:1--Lk. 23:56; Jn. 12:1--Jn. 19:42). Thursday, beginning at Wednesday sunset, is the first day of the feast, the high day and a special sabbath (not the weekly sabbath, Lev. 23:7,24,35; Jn. 19:31). Christ's body is in the tomb and His soul and spirit in hell for three full days and nights (Mt. 12:40, note). Notes For Verse 46\"\n\nThe above in quotes are worth studying in depth later personally.","dt":"2023-02-13T09:05:14","s":["86x8ke9hww"]}],"18":[{"m":"Yes, they sought how they might destroy him, this small boy 🧒, 33 years barely, and he had such influence over the people.\n\nHow long were they going to allow this to continue? It was only a matter of time they would be rendered redundant.\n\nThese leaders and elders 🧓 of the people, so called, were only interested in keeping their positions of power.\n\nThey were willing to kill to keep their place.\n\nTheir interest was not the things of God; they were only there to please themselves and would do anything to keep things that way.\n\nThis is the state of the church today ⛪.\n\nA mixture of good and evil, righteous and wicked alike. A sad 😔 state to be in.\n\nSo we the righteous must arise and take our place, lest evil 😈 prevail over the house 🏡 of our God.","dt":"2023-02-13T10:41:40","s":["nk2y1to2df"]},{"m":"This Jesus, he was getting too powerful and influential.\n\nTo the point he could lash people out of the temple.\n\nAnd his teachings, who did he think he was, claiming some special relationship with the divine?\n\nDon't forget these Pharisees were hypocrites, and so saw things in that light - that he was deceiving the people just like the way they also deceived the people.\n\nBut then Jesus worked miracles, miracles which no man nor prophet ever worked, to show clearly that he was of God.","dt":"2025-04-01T07:56:20","s":["hv2emxqep3"]}],"28":[{"m":"By what authority do you do these things?\n\nThis small boy 🧒, 33 years of age, had usurped their authority.\n\nThis was his house, his temple 🏛. Built with his resources to honour him.\n\nNow men, wicked men, had ravaged it and turned it into a place of merchandise.\n\nHe was not going to look on unconcerned, especially now that he was physically present.\n\nThis kind of merchandise had gone on over the years.\n\nEven from childhood he had seen these things, and his heart burned 🔥 within him.\n\nBut now he was of full age; he had the authority and influence to do as fit.\n\nHe drove these wicked ones out of his house 🏡.","dt":"2023-02-13T10:31:48","s":["ngebfs0ax1"]}],"31":[{"m":"So I say on the behalf of Jesus, why did ye not believe him?\n\nBecause you cared less if he was a prophet or not, if he was from God or not.\n\nHe was not of your camp, so you would not endorse him.\n\nNot that John needed any endorsement from man 👨🏿, for he himself was a burning 🔥 and shining light ☀.\n\nNo wonder John was in the wilderness and had a vibrant ministry from there.\n\nThough he was from the tribe of Levites 😢, he walked 🚶 away from the temple 🏛 and your practices and filthy ways.\n\nSo he went to the wilderness by the Spirit of God, a voice, a voice of one crying 😢 in the wilderness 🏜 to prepare the way of the Lord.\n\nHe indeed was a burning and shining light.\n\nSo now to the matter at hand 🖐️, why did you not believe him?\n\nYou loved your own ways and place and would not give it up for the truth of God's ways.\n\nYou liars and brood of vipers... Ye are of your father the devil 👿","dt":"2023-02-13T10:29:19","s":["j2qmhbwh4q"]}],"33":[{"m":"Such cheek 😝.\n\nThis was the high priest of all people.\n\nJesus so provoked them and showed them what hypocrites they were.","dt":"2022-11-03T06:24:52","s":["htozj04zx5"]},{"m":"Cast not your pearls before swine; he was not going to tell them by what authority he did what he did.\n\nHe would not let them know that this temple 🏛 was built for him and with his resources he provided, i.e. the earth 🌎 and all that therein is.\n\nHe was not.","dt":"2023-02-15T02:11:40","s":["27ipl6e1k4"]}]},"12":{"12":[{"m":"Hmm... This game of power... It seems that the righteous are often not at the top of it because of the shrewdness of the wicked.\n\nYet God is and has been in power for all eternity. We ought to learn of him.","dt":"2022-11-04T06:29:24","s":["qm5681c80g"]}],"15":[{"m":"It's interesting how they rendered the question:\n\nShall we give or not give - meaning they wanted a yes or no answer, knowing very well that either answer will court trouble for Jesus.\n\nThey came with the Herodians in case he said no; they can have him arrested for refusing to pay taxes.\n\nIf he said yes, he will be in disfavor with the people, because they hated Caesar and his tax regime propagated by the corrupt publicans.\n\nThe hatred of which is seen by their distaste for his dining with tax collectors & sinners etc.","dt":"2023-03-09T07:16:33","s":["o82ie04zlf"]}],"17":[{"m":"And that is fair, to give to Caesar what is due him and belongs to him, and to God what is due him.\n\nIn other words, he answered the question of the taxes as yes, and as to whether God approved of it as yes, but whiles doing that you keep the law of God without breaking one for another.","dt":"2023-03-09T07:20:32","s":["kjen9l63jv"]}],"37":[{"m":"With such thought-provoking sermons and ideas, of course they would love to hear him.","dt":"2025-04-04T08:04:25","s":["gs4fp10xv2"]}],"38":[{"m":"Why would Jesus choose such young people for disciples? It's in line with culture.\n\nBut why would he choose those not already in training and having the gift, showing promise of being learned?\n\nOr was it that those boys would have already been deeply indoctrinated?\n\nLike Paul of Tarsus? Whom it took a strong divine encounter to change.\n\nhttps://ac3.org/2017/04/how-old-were-the-disciples\n\nhttp://historyworld.net/wrldhis/PlainTextHistoriesResponsive.asp?historyid=aa11","dt":"2023-03-13T10:36:30","s":["grforlwlxq"]}],"40":[{"m":"So having such traits and character, what kind of tuition were they giving to their young disciples, who were at this time mostly in their teens?\n\nSetting a very bad example for them and misleading them in the way of the Lord.\n\nCould that be why Jesus, being a rabbi, went out of their system to raise his own disciples?\n\nHe wanted nothing to have with them. He started his own movement, more or less.","dt":"2023-03-13T11:46:48","s":["x6mak1ij64"]}],"44":[{"m":"And Jesus did not ask that this poor widow return her money 💵","dt":"2025-04-04T08:06:09","s":["trx53yjmcn"]}],"34":[{"m":"Thou art not far from the kingdom of God? What then is the kingdom of God, and what did Jesus mean by this statement?","dt":"2023-03-11T07:56:08","s":["q63n17b9ov"]},{"m":"Jesus appreciated intelligence 🧠 and understanding.\n\nAnd for this he knew it was only a matter of time, or at least with a bit more seeking he would enter the kingdom - this scribe.\n\nJust like how he loved the rich young ruler for seeking the things that pertain to eternal life.","dt":"2025-04-04T07:17:41","s":["p8y3nrmdmd"]}],"35":[{"m":"They had brought to him their hard and difficult to answer questions, and he had answered well.\n\nNow it was his turn to ask them. Of course none of them could answer his difficult question, because he was the answer, and till they discerned him there was no way they could answer this question of the son of David being his Lord at the same time.","dt":"2023-02-15T02:45:53","s":["cb2twbdefw"]}]},"14":{"21":[{"m":"Good were it for him if he had never been born, and today we all talk of Judas.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:45:07","s":["uvf1mkd25i"]}],"24":[{"m":"Jesus's disciples had grown in faith towards him and strongly believed everything he said and taught.\n\nBecause to have people eat bread 🥪 and say this is your body, and drink wine 🍷 and say it's your blood?\n\nIn our day and age it would be called cult-like behavior. Especially he doing it on a festive occasion where the Passover Lamb was killed.\n\nBut that was not the case, because he indeed died and was indeed the sacrificial Lamb and mediator of the new covenant.","dt":"2022-11-11T06:11:55","s":["w1vh5vwj8q"]}],"33":[{"m":"How did they know he was deeply 😩 distressed?\n\nIt was not just because he said it.\n\nIt was also because he expressed 😑 it. He looked visibly sorrowful 😔 and shaken.\n\nYou know, over the years I have imagined Jesus standing tall and bold, yet speaking to his disciples that he was distressed.\n\nThat the only sign 🤘 of his trouble was the words 'My soul is exceedingly sorrowful 😔'.\n\nBut that could not have been the case.\n\nHis physique and facial expression and all showed he was deeply sorrowful.\n\nMark 14:34 KJV\nAnd saith unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful unto death: tarry ye here, and watch.\n\nWhat was the cause of such sorrow? Obviously the things he was about to suffer.\n\nNo one can take on such suffering and say he was not affected by it in any way.\n\nThis shows the humanness of Christ.\n\nBut he handled this moment well.\n\nYou know, the curse of knowledge was that he knew exactly what was going to happen to him e'er it happened.\n\nThat alone is such a weight 🏋️ to carry around.","dt":"2023-03-15T07:39:22","s":["h6we2a8yve"]}],"34":[{"m":"His soul sorrowful 😔 unto death ☠? No one wants to die, and I can imagine the weight of it, especially on this night.\n\nKnowing full well he was going to die a long, painful death.","dt":"2022-11-11T06:25:43","s":["94owqde17g"]}],"36":[{"m":"Wow, at this point Jesus was so troubled he was willing and ready to abandon the mission...\n\nHis will at this point was to abandon humanity to our fate; the task was too daunting...\n\nOh, we came that close to not being redeemed.\n\nLet us serve the Lord our God and not trample underfoot again the Lord Jesus.","dt":"2023-02-15T17:42:31","s":["q7w07jr3qv"]},{"m":"Is it possible that Jesus had many such 'take this cup away' moments in his life?\n\nYou see, don't forget that Jesus was their rabbi and leader and had to be strong 💪 for them always.\n\nSo the picture of Jesus painted in the gospels is the picture of Jesus they saw.\n\nFull of grace and truth, who went about doing good and healing all them oppressed of the devil 👿.\n\nThey saw no weakness or sorrow except at this moment.\n\nBut the prophet Isaiah saw his many moments of sorrow and grief, so he said:\n\nIsaiah 53:3 KJV\nHe is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief: and we hid as it were our faces from him; he was despised, and we esteemed him not.","dt":"2023-03-15T07:49:38","s":["zp6y0g8gl5"]},{"m":"At this point, it wasn't the will of Jesus to die.\n\nJesus did not want to, but he did it anyways because of his Father.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:48:12","s":["hd6181jo79"]}],"38":[{"m":"Prayerlessness leads to falling to temptation.","dt":"2023-02-15T17:39:21","s":["i8onuoyrm3"]}],"41":[{"m":"At this point it was settled; an angel 😇 had come to strengthen him...\nHe was ready to take on his worst fears 😱","dt":"2023-02-15T17:40:46","s":["ydjjs4jjz7"]}],"44":[{"m":"Wait oo... 😩 Did Judas say after the kiss 😘 Jesus should be taken away safely?\n\nAs in safely so the other disciples are not hurt, or safely like how?","dt":"2023-02-16T10:57:37","s":["5slkpsdwjx"]}],"48":[{"m":"Oh the shame, and disgrace. A whole Son of God being dragged literally for trial.\n\nOh the shame, knowing who he was, and yet had to endure it.\n\nAnd indeed, for all of us, our moment of shame would come, to humble us and teach us obedience, as Christ learned obedience by the things he suffered.\n\nHebrews 5:8-9 KJV\nThough he were a Son, yet learned he obedience by the things which he suffered; [9] And being made perfect, he became the author of eternal salvation unto all them that obey him;","dt":"2023-03-15T08:02:39","s":["gn979lgm44"]}],"52":[{"m":"Was this like literally naked, or he had an undergarment?","dt":"2023-03-15T08:03:26","s":["2mnqc7og8n"]}],"54":[{"m":"What was going on in Peter's mind at this time ⌚?\n\nWas he remembering his promise that he won't forsake the Lord no matter what?\n\nI can imagine the fear 😱 even as he entered the palace and the den of his enemies.\n\nHe could be found out, but he kept at it.\n\nHe did well, till he was brought face to face with possible 🙆 arrest and death ☠ for being partners with Jesus in his alleged crimes.\n\nThen he buckled. He broke.","dt":"2023-03-15T08:16:48","s":["9lpebrja01"]}],"61":[{"m":"Why answer such concocted lies 🤥 of false witnesses?\n\nEven under arrest he had the dominion.","dt":"2023-03-15T08:32:04","s":["k4uc0p69cw"]}],"62":[{"m":"Even though he prophesied that \"ye shall see\", they all died without seeing him come down.\n\nBut they will literally see him come down in glory in the 2nd advent.\n\nSo the \"ye shall see\" was not talking of them necessarily, but their kind and stock shall see him when he comes down.\n\nI am making this point because of the saying, for instance, of Jesus concerning the end of time, that\n\n\"this generation shall not pass till all the signs be fulfilled\" — this was not in reference to that generation but to them, the generation who would see those things.\n\nSame as when he spoke of his disciples being persecuted and seeing the signs of heaven.\n\nHe was not referencing his current disciples but the future ones.","dt":"2022-11-11T06:39:20","s":["b6be0vfigp"]},{"m":"And with this they found the testimony they needed to kill him.\n\nWas this not the same words used by Stephen, for which they clogged their ears and stoned him?\n\nIndeed they did not seek the truth. If this was blasphemy as they claimed, then when Stephen now saw the manifestation of this blasphemy, they should have thought twice and reconsidered their actions before killing Stephen.\n\nBut their minds were made up.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:53:25","s":["olpryg0grl"]}],"68":[{"m":"At this stage the disciples were also quite popular themselves, having been with Jesus everywhere.","dt":"2025-04-13T11:54:33","s":["76bdgo03cy"]}],"72":[{"m":"Such scenery, it was almost like the denial of Jesus was tied to the vocal cords of the cock 🐓.\n\nThe moment the first denial was made the cock crew,\n\nWhen the second and third were done, the cock 🐓 crew again.\n\nAnd Luke's account says that then the Lord turned and looked upon Peter.\n\nOn my word, in the midst of the trial that was to lead to his demise, Jesus was ever sensitive to the spirit.\n\nThe chief priests and Co did not know that in the midst of their trial, there was another conversation going on between Peter and Jesus.\n\nA whole different engagement was going on right in their midst and they did not know it.\n\nOh my Lord God, he was indeed full of glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father...","dt":"2023-02-18T12:45:58","s":["nwmfzyrl2q"]},{"m":"Luke's account says:\n\nLuke 22:61 KJV\nAnd the Lord turned, and looked upon Peter. And Peter remembered the word of the Lord, how he had said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.\n\nThis behavior of Jesus, who was undergoing trial to his death ☠, and not just any death ☠ but death by crucifixion, reminds me later of Peter himself.\n\nWhen he in the book of Acts was between 4 squadrons of soldiers awaiting his death ☠.\n\nAnd in the midst of it he was asleep; who sleeps the night before death ☠ roll?\n\nIndeed, so deep in sleep he was that when the angel shone in such bright radiance he did not still wake.\n\nHe had to be awoken by the angel 😇 himself.\n\nActs 12:7 KJV\nAnd, behold, the angel of the Lord came upon him, and a light shined in the prison: and he smote Peter on the side, and raised him up, saying, Arise up quickly. And his chains fell off from his hands.","dt":"2023-02-18T12:49:59","s":["ywhdjz2vs6"]},{"m":"Was the timing of the cock crowing not the regular time for cocks to crow?\n\nIf cocks 🐓 were crowing all over, then it would have been even difficult to count.\n\nSo this single cock pops out to fulfill prophecy.","dt":"2023-03-15T08:44:47","s":["o6qen770s1"]},{"m":"He just could not help it... He knew the prophecy; he tried not to deny the master, but alas he underestimated the situation.\n\nOr rather he overestimated himself, and now he had failed the master.\n\nSometimes we just cannot help ourselves.","dt":"2023-03-15T08:47:52","s":["z1jdiecq41"]}],"25":[{"m":"Did Judas also partake of this communion?","dt":"2025-04-13T11:46:01","s":["ixi61imksb"]}],"27":[{"m":"Jesus was so up to date with the events of his life.","dt":"2022-11-11T06:21:38","s":["bzhtr0udxh"]}],"37":[{"m":"Oh, I can imagine the disappointment; in his most trying moments they were not strong 💪 for him.\n\nBut he understood and made an excuse for them: they were tired 😴.","dt":"2023-03-15T07:58:50","s":["iu73ijcwyp"]}],"55":[{"m":"How, when did the priests come to such a low place of depravity, so as to bear false witness in order to kill another person?\n\nAnyways, just like their fathers who even served idols in the temple in the times of Ezekiel, I believe... These people were no worshippers of God.","dt":"2023-03-15T08:30:01","s":["thtvqi07gj"]}],"67":[{"m":"At this time Jesus was being condemned or had been condemned to death and was being abused.\n\nNow the time was ripe;\n\nPeter's master was condemned, and so any associates of his also stood to be condemned with him.","dt":"2023-03-15T08:38:40","s":["q05p7p795r"]}]},"15":{"10":[{"m":"Even Pilate knew that it was for envy that they had delivered him up, but he still went ahead and did their bidding because of politics.\n\nThey threatened to report","dt":"2023-03-16T09:20:38","s":["57kas4h3mk"]}],"11":[{"m":"Jesus had many disciples and followers, and it seems this miracle worker 👷 could have no enemies.\n\nBut there were many who felt he was breaking the traditions of the fathers and misleading the people.\n\nThis was the thinking of the crowd — the common people, a thinking fueled by their leaders.\nBut for the Pharisees and Co, they were more concerned about power and keeping their place of authority given them by the Romans.","dt":"2023-03-16T09:23:48","s":["hp3ixsk1t3"]}],"21":[{"m":"Of all the people, why Simon the Cyrenian?\n\nDid he have compassion in his eyes 👀 at the pains of Jesus as he fainted under the weight 🏋️ of the cross?","dt":"2023-03-16T09:27:29","s":["a3p6fstqtf"]}],"31":[{"m":"These children 🧒 of the devil 👿, what were they doing there?\n\nThey had followed him throughout his ministry, seen to his wicked crucifixion, and were now at the cross ➕\n\nTo ensure they watch him die with their own eyes 👀, whiles mocking him.\n\nSuch wickedness!! 😲\n\nBecause he had claimed deity. Now they follow him to his tomb to get it secured, because he had told his disciples of his resurrection the 3rd day.\n\nIndeed it seems the enemies of the Lord paid more attention to his words than his disciples.\n\nSo they secured his tomb to ensure they don't steal his body.\n\nAfter having gone to this extreme, Jesus resurrected, the soldiers testified, and their leaders showed the true state of their hearts 💕.\n\nThey did not want a messiah; they wanted to stay in their sin and wickedness.\n\nThis should serve as a lesson for us regarding the wicked in heart.\n\nThey can't be appeased. They are wicked and ruthless and unrepentant.","dt":"2023-03-16T09:40:06","s":["5jqm3xnfky"]}],"32":[{"m":"And maybe they would have believed, because they presumed that Christ was to come as a triumphant king at this time, yet he was to be a lamb for the sins of the world.\n\nBut we also know that, considering all the miracles including raising the dead, they would not have believed really if even Jesus came down from the grave.\n\nIt's akin to Lazarus and the rich man, whom Abraham admonished that if his brothers believed not the prophets, neither will they believe if one were to come from the grave.","dt":"2025-04-17T09:45:11","s":["iuc3p6r0u7"]}],"33":[{"m":"Three hours of darkness, and gross darkness the people, but our Lord was to rise over them the third day as a light to them.\n\nThe light of the world 🔥 was about to be snuffed off 📴.\n\nNo wonder some say demonic forces were released.\n\nThis was the man who had cast them out and tormented them these three years.\n\nHe alone had cast 6000 of them out of one man 👨🏿.\n\nNow this man was forsaken of God.\n\nDid they come to watch his death ☠, and hell from beneath, they awaited to meet his soul as it descended?","dt":"2023-03-16T09:48:35","s":["7abw1kpi53"]}],"39":[{"m":"He laid down his life.\n\nNo. Man died on the cross by screaming 😱 his last and then expiring.\n\nYes, men breathe their last, but he, he gave up his spirit literally.\n\nAnd this happened so clearly and obviously that the centurion, who might have witnessed this many deaths on the cross ➕, knew this was abnormal.\n\nNo man decides when he wants to die, up to the last breath.","dt":"2023-03-16T09:51:12","s":["pb58ya0m2z"]}],"42":[{"m":"It was evening, i.e. the next day, since in the Jewish calendar the next day starts at 6pm.\n\nThis clarifies the Matthew account, which says early the next day, which was the day of preparation... creating the impression that it was a 24-hour period, but no, it was not, it was in the evening.","dt":"2025-04-17T09:49:31","s":["xueuqr8d7d"]}],"19":[{"m":"I'm sure the soldiers 💂 who were Romans heard that there is a new prisoner whose claim is that he was the King 👑 of the Jews and a God man 👨🏿.\n\nThey began thus to mock him.","dt":"2023-02-18T12:55:32","s":["au8jdp87ue"]}],"26":[{"m":"This superscription sounds more like a mockery of the injustice done him.\nThat he was crucified for this 😩.\n\nNo wonder the Pharisees asked for it to be changed, but Pilate would have none of it.","dt":"2023-02-17T00:15:57","s":["ridfyo57ih"]}],"29":[{"m":"Hm 🤔... These did not know that they prophesied of his resurrection.","dt":"2023-02-17T00:18:32","s":["wldqmfgerj"]}],"47":[{"m":"Their light was snuffed out — Jesus of Nazareth.","dt":"2023-03-16T09:57:40","s":["fs33mnfbye"]}]},"16":{"7":[{"m":"And Peter, yes Peter, so he knows he is not condemned for three times blatant denial after being forewarned.","dt":"2023-03-17T06:50:14","s":["3m3v7yp3mr"]}]},"13":{"22":[{"m":"If falsehood is like the truth, then the Antichrist will be like Christ.\n\nAnd it might not be obvious that he is not.\n\nHere we are told that the elect could be seduced.\n\nSo the Antichrist is not going to be so obviously not Christ, and his false prophet will not be like he is false.\n\nNow is the time to know Christ more than ever before and to get our doctrine right, lest we lose out.","dt":"2023-02-15T13:05:42","s":["19l5xllgmh"]}],"29":[{"m":"Though Jesus spoke to the disciples directly, many of the things he said here outlived them.\n\nIt was not going to be in their time, but Jesus knew that these words would be transferred as disciples are made, such that those to whom it was meant for would be informed.","dt":"2023-03-15T07:20:27","s":["mycvove13u"]}]}},"1 Thessalonians":{"2":{"5":[{"m":"Paul and his team were true men of God. They preached the gospel unfeigned, in truth, without deception or wanting glory over others.\n\nUnlike men of God so called today, the deception and self exaltation is not Christian. And of course sometimes you can't blame them, because the flock seem to exalt and deserve such behaviour.\n\nBut so were some of the flock in Paul's time, yet they did not let that destroy them nor change their way of life.","dt":"2023-10-13T06:25:43","s":["t81jawag3y"]}],"10":[{"m":"Wow... They ensured they were blameless and without spot and blemish.\n\nSo the gospel of Jesus would not be held in disrepute.","dt":"2022-11-26T07:10:11","s":["xux0ltil7q"]}]},"4":{"7":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... I'm here thinking that where do the hyper grace preachers get the whole idea of we can walk in sin and it doesn't matter from?\n\nThey are looking at only one set of scriptures and nullifying others.","dt":"2022-11-26T08:01:07","s":["zo84j36bb4"]}],"17":[{"m":"I earlier in a note asked what's the point of rising up to meet the Lord in the air when he was coming down anyways.\n\nBut that also begs the reverse, that what's the point of Christ coming down only to go back up to heaven?\n\nExcept of course the answer is to take us with him.\n\nI think 🤔 instead of conjecture we should let scripture explain itself.","dt":"2023-10-14T10:25:10","s":["zg50wab2hg"]}]},"5":{"8":[{"m":"In other places it's breastplate of righteousness... Depending on the point Paul wants to make, or maybe better understanding, or what will better communicate reality, he uses different illustrations.","dt":"2022-11-26T08:06:15","s":["ktjpftdgls"]}],"10":[{"m":"How about the teaching that when we die we go to heaven, as in our spirit goes to heaven?\n\nSo if our spirit goes to be in heaven and we are with the Lord,\n\nwhat is the point of we now rising from the grave to meet with him in the air? To what end?\n\nAre we not supposed to rather come down with him?\nThis bears more study.","dt":"2023-10-13T07:08:15","s":["tqsxk40ops"]}],"15":[{"m":"If we do otherwise, rendering evil for evil 😈, we would destroy ourselves.\n\nAnd it's especially true for marriage, lest couples destroy themselves, as is the case in many marriages.\n\nThe key is forgiveness.","dt":"2023-10-13T07:11:42","s":["39aooj3tcg"]}],"16":[{"m":"Is not this verse shorter than \"and Jesus wept\" in John 11:35? Let me check.\n\nJohn 11:35 KJV\nJesus wept.\n\nOkay, there is no \"and\".","dt":"2023-10-13T07:13:43","s":["qgouk8ks12"]}],"19":[{"m":"So the Spirit can be quenched.\n\nWe have got to be careful.","dt":"2023-10-13T07:15:58","s":["pqb0lxp8k8"]}],"24":[{"m":"One of my personal favorites","dt":"2023-10-13T07:15:10","s":["im4nfkh8gt"]}],"13":[{"m":"This is why we honour men of God, but the fakes are also taking of this honour and abusing it.","dt":"2023-10-13T07:09:31","s":["j9qbaetpoq"]}]},"3":{"13":[{"m":"The theme of the coming of the Lord was something they looked forward to constantly, even in their day.","dt":"2022-11-26T07:45:19","s":["iub02pfjdf"]}]}},"2 Thessalonians":{"2":{"1":[{"m":"This was addressing the same event in book one, though Dake's commentary is suggesting the first event in book one is the rapture, whiles this one is in reference to Jesus's second coming.\n\nBut from the text it's the same event he is making reference to.","dt":"2023-10-14T10:27:57","s":["8qj7gpxmkj"]}],"3":[{"m":"If here Paul was addressing the 2nd coming of Christ as different from the rapture, why would he even address the 2nd coming to believers, seeing that we/they would not even be here during the events of the 2nd coming?\n\nI do not think Paul had two different events in mind, at least not according to this writing.\n\nHe, Paul, had one coming only in mind in both books.","dt":"2023-10-14T10:42:00","s":["l3f0lfdnxb"]}]},"1":{"10":[{"m":"Paul talks about the coming of the Lord... In the sense of Christ coming into the earth 🌎, and for judgement and reward.\n\nThat kind of clarifies his point in book one of we being caught up to meet with him in the air.\n\nMy conflict was, what is the point in being caught up in the air to meet him with the dead in Christ if he was coming down anyways?\n\nBible Project explains it to be a kind of welcome procession from us, just as is found in Roman culture.\n\nThough I think we are caught up and transported to heaven.","dt":"2023-10-14T09:08:15","s":["pu42s0am65"]}]}},"Galatians":{"1":{"19":[{"m":"The Lord's brother... i.e. Jesus' blood brothers.\n\nThey were now also believers. Maybe the Lord had showed himself to him in some unique way after his resurrection...\n\nFor one to be convinced that your blood brother is now your God. It must take something...\n\nAsk yourself, what would it take to believe any of your siblings is God 😼","dt":"2022-11-25T10:19:43","s":["yzk3y7pm5d"]}]},"2":{"3":[{"m":"Oh, the early Apostles. Why was Paul explaining himself, men who wrought mighty miracles?\n\nThey were so humble and saw themselves as bond servants and servants of the people.\n\nSo he sought to win the people over to sound doctrine.\n\nBut today there is so much pompousness in the church, because men and women of God have crowds and power.\n\nBut then again, some may argue that the church members then were obedient and listened to the apostles, so they could go down to the people's level and explain themselves as needed.\n\nBut today, there is little reverence for men of God, so men of God stay in their safe places and do what God has called them to do to the best of their abilities.","dt":"2022-11-25T10:26:49","s":["9uxtel76ff"]}],"6":[{"m":"Paul would not be bullied by titles and disobey God, as we are taught today in the church ⛪.\n\nBy these insecure hypnotists. Practicing mind bending on the congregation.\n\nPaul knew the truth and would not allow it to be corrupted, not even by the great apostles.\nAs we see, he did not see them as pillars but described them as \"they seem to be pillars\",\n\nbecause God has not respect of persons.\n\nThis is how the Good News renders it:\n\nGalatians 2:6 GNT\nBut those who seemed to be the leaders—I say this because it makes no difference to me what they were; God does not judge by outward appearances—those leaders, I say, made no new suggestions to me.","dt":"2023-10-17T06:53:09","s":["fza50480sh"]}],"19":[{"m":"The law, by its design and very instruction, was designed to die and to be replaced by Jesus' grace, released by his death and resurrection.","dt":"2022-11-25T10:54:17","s":["8du4qrrreh"]}],"21":[{"m":"These men, being Jews by nature 🏞, contemplated the doctrine of the New Testament deeply in order to really understand what it was all about.\n\nAnd that abolishing the practice of Judaism was not denouncing God but aligning with him.","dt":"2022-11-25T10:56:38","s":["3p4ygskvua"]}]},"3":{"29":[{"m":"Her promise of eternal Prosperous life","dt":"2023-10-17T12:36:02","s":["b3uenmhuhu"]}]},"5":{"11":[{"m":"If all it took to attain salvation was to obey the law, then why were the Jews after Paul...\n\nIt was because he preached freedom from the law.","dt":"2023-10-17T13:32:06","s":["dg2fn3r9g9"]}],"16":[{"m":"Very emphatic and important instructions.","dt":"2023-10-17T13:33:02","s":["3cijjvx6eg"]}],"21":[{"m":"Paul knew that the danger of this liberty 🗽 🗽 was that it would give occasion to the flesh, so we are told to walk in the Spirit.","dt":"2023-10-17T13:36:10","s":["owgfe6q7vj"]}]},"6":{"7":[{"m":"This statement about reaping what we sow is not in relation to giving. Giving is in verse 6; however, verse 7 is not a continuation of verse 6.\n\nIt is easy to assume verse 7 is talking about sowing abundantly into the minister of the word.\n\nThere is a different scripture where that same concept of sowing was in reference to giving. It's:\n\n2 Corinthians 9:5-6 KJV\nTherefore I thought it necessary to exhort the brethren, that they would go before unto you, and make up beforehand your bounty, whereof ye had notice before, that the same might be ready, as a matter of bounty, and not as of covetousness. But this I say, He which soweth sparingly shall reap also sparingly; and he which soweth bountifully shall reap also bountifully.\n\nIn this case, however, it's referencing consequences of our actions, even as believers.","dt":"2023-10-19T14:38:48","s":["q2hmydv6hc"]}],"15":[{"m":"Oh, this wonderful scripture.","dt":"2023-10-17T13:38:49","s":["ihwn6ufi6r"]}]}},"James":{"1":{"12":[{"m":"Did the disciples of Jesus talk thus because they were poor?\n\nWere these doctrines, or at least teachings, a way to remain encouraged in the midst of the difficult circumstances that poverty brings?\n\nWhat if the church was, say, filled with people who have acquired wealth or were born into rich homes or royalty 👑?\n\nWhat would the language have been like?\n\nIn a 🎊 congregation that cannot relate with words of encouragement to the poor, should the rich be made to feel bad about their wealth?\n\nI think that most of the early church were poor, as we see in the writings of the apostles and even Jesus's life itself.\n\nJesus was not rich, but he made the poor know their riches in him.\n\nThe idea was not to condemn riches but to exalt the all-surpassing richness of Christ.","dt":"2023-11-19T13:30:15","s":["zz2hn5x6y3"]}],"27":[{"m":"Unspotted from the world is part of pure religion, not just mere talk of grace and its excuse to sin.","dt":"2023-11-19T13:32:24","s":["klm8kwvovb"]}]},"2":{"6":[{"m":"Ah, there we go. The church generally were poor, or at least not rich.","dt":"2023-11-20T13:48:43","s":["l6hf62wvbs"]}],"12":[{"m":"James quotes from the law but was quick to add that we do not operate the old law but the law of liberty, which is under grace.\n\nAnd in this law of liberty we see that the righteous moral laws of the Old Testament stand.","dt":"2023-11-20T13:50:58","s":["beor5v39zj"]}],"25":[{"m":"I'm sure some hyper-spiritual persons in the church were going about doing nothing in the name of faith, and thus had to be taught that faith is with works.\n\nThat faith is not standalone.","dt":"2025-04-24T06:56:03","s":["4qhtuqb0gw"]}],"16":[{"m":"I am beginning to wonder, what made James address these specific issues?\n\nI believe these were issues that were coming up generally across the churches, and he, being held as a leader, had authority to speak on such matters and express his wisdom concerning them.","dt":"2025-04-24T06:52:17","s":["53f1org4tn"]}]},"3":{"10":[{"m":"Interesting and noteworthy style of writing.\n\nHe earlier said that the tongue 😝 can no man tame, and the one who is able to tame the tongue, the same is a perfect 👌 man 👨.\n\nThen he goes ahead to state that it is wrong that the same mouth 👄 with which we bless God, we curse man, who is the image of God.\n\nThese things ought not to be so. In essence, we are being admonished to strive for perfection and the greater good.\n\nIt's difficult, but that should be our goal, striving for excellence.","dt":"2023-11-20T14:04:20","s":["3i6il3sl55"]}]},"4":{"11":[{"m":"Needs more study. Does it mean do not call out evil 😈 or wrong...? No, not at all.\n\nIt says not to judge, so what does it mean... It means to pass condemnation on a brother...\nMeanwhile there is only one lawgiver and Judge, the Lord Jesus.\n\nSo yes, we need to call out evil, but not pass judgement or sentences on people.\n\nLeave that to God.","dt":"2022-11-22T21:33:28","s":["8m4ve3641t"]}]},"5":{"18":[{"m":"We have the details of Elijah's second prayer.\n\nThat it was a travailing prayer, but we are not given the detail. It is safe to say that he had settled it in prayer, probably the same way, and then came to declare the results of his prayer, i.e.\n\n\"There shall be no rain ☔\", just as he did when he said... \"Go eat and drink, for I hear the sound 🔊 of the abundance of rain ☔\" 1 Kings 18:41","dt":"2023-11-23T07:20:41","s":["rr7mse8swr"]}]}},"3 John":{"1":{"7":[{"m":"The early disciples did not want it to be seen that they sought for money 💵, so they preached the gospel for free, or rather at the expense of the established brethren.\n\nThey did nothing to hinder the gospel.","dt":"2023-12-08T06:39:37","s":["rrzsz5egce"]}],"8":[{"m":"Looks like Gaius was a believer who maybe lived near the church.\n\nAnd the situation was such that the ministers who came to his church from the Gentile church took no offering or any such thing to preach the word of God.\n\nSo Gaius takes them into his house and feeds them, and when they are ready to journey back or on to some other place, gives them some provisions for their journey.\n\nHe was a good man, and such charity is expensive to maintain, but he did all that for the Lord.","dt":"2025-05-26T08:12:33","s":["w74qp2wtc"]}]}},"Job":{"1":{"1":[{"m":"5th Jan 2022\n\nThe land of Uz] The land of Uz was south of Edom and west of Arabia, extending to the borders of Chaldea. In those days it could have comprised even Arabia-Petra itself (Jer. 49:7,20; Lam. 4:21; Ezek. 25:13; Amos 1:11).\n\nJob] Job, afflicted. He was the third son of Issachar, the son of Jacob (Gen. 46:13; Ezek. 14:14,20; Jas. 5:11). He is mentioned 56 times in the book that bears his name.\n\nThis commentary above is from my Dake's Study Bible.","dt":"2022-01-05T17:43:01","s":["byvnro0qp9"]}],"4":[{"m":"The life of the rich kids 🧒. Feasting and merrymaking.\n\nObviously wild partying 🎉, else their father would not have sacrificed on their behalf if he did not have suspicion of their doings.","dt":"2022-01-05T17:02:05","s":["hmtbdvwe5g"]}],"5":[{"m":"Where did Job learn to offer burnt offering from? The same was said of Abel and Cain.\n\nThey offered sacrifices to the Lord. From the book of Job we would move back to Abraham.\n\nWhere he also offered sacrifices. Where did they learn such practices from, as this was before the law?\n\nEspecially considering that this practice started way back as the firstborn Abel.","dt":"2022-01-05T17:45:47","s":["73qlwyszjz"]}],"6":[{"m":"What's he doing here? How did Satan have such access to God?\n\nHow come God is tolerating him?\n\nThe sons of God came to present themselves, and Satan, a son of God also though cast out, also came.","dt":"2022-01-06T06:53:03","s":["1g1k1xjdgo"]},{"m":"I have asked this question before. What was the devil doing here in the presence of God after all the havoc he had caused?\n\nHow come God was allowing him audience, without anger or animosity of any sort?\n\nIndeed the conversation between God and Satan lets us in on the nature of their relationship.\n\nThere is something about God that we really need to understand.\n\nGod's Laws and nature are fixed. God is not evolving or getting better.\n\nWe therefore ought to study what is to understand who he is.\n\nSo for instance, why did God not stop Adam from eating of the tree, knowing full well the untold hardships this would bring on man?\n\nThat lets us in on the nature of God and man.\n\nGod has set the systems in motion. Man was to be the one to have dominion on the earth, not God or another.\n\nIf he stopped man in his tracks, man was no longer an independent being.\n\nMan had literally been made in the image of God; how could he be treated less?\n\nNothing was going to cause God to change his free moral image of himself.\nThat was the whole idea for creating man, so the universe will live with the consequences.\n\nIt was this unchanging, unevolving nature of God that Satan knew; that is why he came before God's presence.\n\nWhy? Because he, Satan, had the right to. He had a place in heaven and he was going to utilize it full well until the time for him to be deposed was up, as we see in Revelation.\n\nBut even then he was not going to give up on the heavens without a fight.\n\nIndeed fights have been had in the heavens, as we see in the book of Daniel when the angel Gabriel was held up until Michael came to his aid.\n\nBut the book of Revelation scene was an entire war.\n\nSo Satan shows up here exercising his full rights to come before God's throne.\n\nHow he got this right we will study some time later.","dt":"2024-01-09T08:06:25","s":["n9r4rmip71"]}],"8":[{"m":"Before asking him of his consideration for Job, what was Satan's original agenda for coming to see God?\n\nWas he presenting a list 📃 of people he wanted to strike at but needed God's informed consent?\n\nIf so, why wasn't Job part of the list 📃? Or could it be that there were some people who could just not be on Satan's list, so he did not bother asking for them.\n\nAgain, if my conjecture is right, God wanted to prove a point that those on the \"can't touch hedge of fire 🔥\" list were there not just by privileged position but have actually earned the right to be there.\n\nSo again, following my conjecture, as Satan went through his hit list 📃, God, in his infinite wisdom and eternal nature, seeking to make an example for all eternity of his faithfulness to the end, suggests and releases Job into Satan's hands 👐","dt":"2022-01-06T07:00:48","s":["0m67hiv9i0"]}],"10":[{"m":"Is this what is on every believer? This hedge 🦔 of protection round about.\n\nI believe Job was not the only one with this protection. Abraham had it, Moses had it.\n\nWe as believers have it. I suspect that the extent of protection is subject to how we remain within the boundaries of his protection. Through obedience and walking in his ways.\n\nWhat we yield to God comes under his watch and protection.\n\nHow do I know this? See how devout Job was. Even making sacrifices for his children 🧒 and 👪, thus they were also under cover.\n\nObviously he did also for his work and property.\n\nAgain, all believers, and I dare say unbelievers. The whole world 🗺 is under a protection of a sort.\n\nHow do we know this? See how swiftly the moment the part of Job's life that was taken out of cover came under complete and merciless destruction.\n\nIf God lifts his cover just a bit, I believe there would be no world 🗺.\n\nWe see in Paul's writings about the man of lawlessness and how that the moment we are taken away such swift destruction will come.\n\n2 Thessalonians 2:5-7 KJV\nRemember ye not, that, when I was yet with you, I told you these things? [6] And now ye know what withholdeth that he might be revealed in his time. [7] For the mystery of iniquity doth already work: only he who now letteth will let, until he be taken out of the way.\n\nEvil 😈 is being held in check ☑ to varying degrees.\n\nAnd in our own lives, if we still have life and no swift destruction has come upon us and that which concerns us,\n\nThen know we that we indeed are under cover. The devil 👿 is not lenient, and full 🌕 of wickedness.\n\nHe will swiftly destroy if given the least chance 🤞 💱","dt":"2022-01-06T08:06:30","s":["e3c5nhq1ww"]},{"m":"So now that which was supposed to be the natural state of the earth 🌎 is now called a blessing.\n\nThe earth was supposed to yield for man, be fruitful and multiply.\n\nBut now when the earth does what it was originally created to do, we call it a blessing.\n\nWe indeed were cursed 🤬","dt":"2024-01-13T13:50:04","s":["0icr3kl7t5"]}],"12":[{"m":"What was the guarantee that Satan 😈 was going to stay within his boundaries?\n\nHow could the devil 🐝 be trusted in this regard?\n\nI guess there was no point in disobeying God; if he took Job's life, God would just bring him back and end the whole arrangement, thus Satan would miss his opportunity to prove his point.\n\nWhy lose such an opportunity to bring down the greatest man in the east?\n\nCould the east mean he was within the promised land territory?","dt":"2022-01-05T18:49:53","s":["kg7ap668tw"]},{"m":"God trusted Satan to not touch Job's life, and this he did. He touched not his life or body.\n\nInteresting thought there.","dt":"2024-01-13T13:50:55","s":["wueguts2jm"]}],"13":[{"m":"So innocently, they did not know their protection was gone.","dt":"2022-01-06T07:37:41","s":["ebfkn9jjsw"]}],"14":[{"m":"Satan leaves God's presence 📦.\n\nThe next thing we see is Job loses all he has... After God speaks, immediately the hedge of fire and blessing etc. is lifted.\n\nWe are not told the process of that happening. That probably the angel in charge of multiplying the flock of Job, the fire 🔥 angel 😇 who keeps everything in check etc., upon hearing the command of God, move into action.\n\nWho knows, likely as soon as God spoke, the angel of his presence who carries forth messages from the throne room to the herald for onward distribution goes into action.\n\nWe are spared all this and just see the effect on Job.\n\nIn verse 14 we see a messenger of Job come to deliver the bad news 📰. In heaven the same thing, I believe, happened.\n\nAn heavenly messenger delivers 🚚 the bad news to the angels who were standing guard over Job's property to protect it.\n\nThat they had to allow evil. I'm sure they might have asked, 'But why?'\n\nIt is the Lord's sovereign will. Job has done no evil btw. So they vacate post.","dt":"2022-01-06T07:36:13","s":["lp5f8z6byz"]}],"17":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 interesting... It's incredible. The devil 👿 had this much power and influence?? 😳\n\nSuch coordinated attack in one 1⃣ day. Through both natural and supernatural means.\n\nHe controlled men, the Sabeans, the Chaldeans, the wind 🍃 and 🔥 fire.","dt":"2022-01-06T08:52:26","s":["ls9ee8yvmb"]}],"19":[{"m":"I get it if, for purely experimental reasons and to prove a point to Satan and for all eternity, Job loses his properties etc.\n\nBut to lose his children 🧒, innocent, just to prove a point.\n\nThat does not sound right.\n\nHere again is my conjecture.\n\nOne can infer the debauchery and kind of life of Job's kids, that they were in no way like their father.\n\nThey just enjoyed his riches. Again we have to look at the nature 🏞 of God. He is righteous and would not suffer the innocent and righteous to perish.\n\nThat is why he did not permit Satan to take the life of Job. If there was righteousness on Job's kids, he obviously would have spared them, or at least the righteous ones.\n\nEither ways, we can trust the righteousness of God to do that which is right.","dt":"2022-01-06T07:10:11","s":["00x0vjdd8b"]}],"22":[{"m":"What a response... What a shock 🤯... I'm sure that was the devil's reaction 🤯. How possible 🙆","dt":"2022-01-06T08:55:28","s":["nd3g01qwi3"]}],"15":[{"m":"Honestly, this arrangement to test Job's faithfulness that involves the life of others... Iiiii...\nIs someway","dt":"2022-01-05T18:54:58","s":["rsqt5zol51"]}]},"2":{"1":[{"m":"Earlier in chpt 1 vs 1...\n\nI was wondering what Satan was doing among the holy and righteous ones.\n\nI felt he was intruding in the space reserved for the sons of God. The holy ones.\n\nBut on reading this verse, it sounds 🔊 more like the presentation 📦 before God was more of a SUMMON and not a casual walk 🚶 in.\n\nLike all kings, you cannot just 🚶 come in at your will.\n\nSo then every now and then Satan either receives a summon or has appointed times within which he is to present himself.\n\nAt such points he makes his accusation etc.\n\nAnd for God to be justified as to why he protects us, as in Job's case, or for our own strength 💪 thening and building perseverance and hope among his children 🧒, as in below:\n\nRomans 5:3-5 KJV\nAnd not only so, but we glory in tribulations also: knowing that tribulation worketh patience; [4] And patience, experience; and experience, hope: [5] And hope maketh not ashamed; because the love of God is shed abroad in our hearts by the Holy Ghost which is given unto us.\n\nHe allows certain trials and tribulations.\n\nOf course we have the promises of God in Christ, and so we resist the devil 👿 any time ⌚ he attempts to cross ➕ boundaries.\n\nWe are not to succumb and assume God has handed us over for testing. No.\n\nIn Christ the only suffering permitted is persecution on account of the gospel, not sickness 🤮, disease.\n\nIn Paul's case of a thorn in the flesh that refused to go away, he knew it was there for his glory, and that was a very personal case, not a norm for every believer.","dt":"2022-01-06T10:06:16","s":["7noa9g2f0r"]},{"m":"I wonder how long after the first plague did this 2nd meeting take place. It seems also that these kinds of meetings and summons were scheduled.\n\nAn appointment of a sort.\n\nAgain Satan, the enemy of God, or is it man 👨, freely spoke with God. It seems Satan was still subject to God in a sense.\n\nWe have to really weigh 🏋️ this God–Satan relationship.\n\nIt seems that there were rules of engagement in this battle for the earth 🌎 and for man.\n\nSo Satan knows God can't, or rather won't, just snap his fingers and vanquish him. There are eternal unchanging laws that keep Satan alive and here to wreak havoc.\n\nAnd there is a time for his overthrow and final casting into the lake of fire 🔥.\n\nTill then he is god of the world.","dt":"2022-01-07T12:55:11","s":["1cusy44rp0"]},{"m":"I am wondering, between the destruction of Job's property and this second visit of Satan, what was God doing about Job's case?\n\nWas he just waiting for Satan to show up so he dialogues with him?\n\nHow long was it between these two situations?","dt":"2026-01-06T08:06:18","s":["fn2ytqqad3"]}],"2":[{"m":"There is a battle going on for the 🌎 earth. Not a direct confrontation between God and the devil. No, far from it, for they are in no way equal.\n\nBut a battle based on rules and laws of the universe 🌌 and the earth, set in iron. It cannot be changed because of the unchangeableness of the word of God.\n\nSo based on that, Satan is wreaking havoc whiles God rules in the affairs 🕴️ of men 🚹 to save them.\n\nAll within the rules of engagement.\n\nSatan knows that if he plays his game well and wins, he can keep this game up perpetually and thereby defer his judgements for all eternity.\n\nGOD doth know that he is bound by his word and also has his agents for good on the earth 🌎, and he knows that he will win.\n\nAnd that victory ✌️ will be attained within the rules set.\n\nGod will reward and rewards all who play on his team.\n\nThis calling business is no joke 🃏... It is a high call 🤙 and a matter of eternal joy or eternal suffering of man.\n\nSo we ought to play and play hard.","dt":"2022-01-06T10:50:14","s":["8lun5s0yiy"]}],"4":[{"m":"How long was God going to put up with this? Either ways, that was the devil's full 🌕 and final arsenal, and it failed.\n\nAfter, we did not see this kind of conversation going on ever between God and Satan in the scriptures.","dt":"2022-01-07T13:01:33","s":["ltrurspukk"]}],"5":[{"m":"This is wisdom from an ancient source. Though we might not like the devil 👿 here, he's shared one of the secrets in bringing down man 👨.\n\nSkin for skin, he says.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:14:39","s":["47r32d8303"]}],"13":[{"m":"Hmm, sad 😔 state.","dt":"2022-01-06T10:52:15","s":["j9mxiwd2fe"]},{"m":"Just on a lighter note,\nthese men lived for so long they had seven days to sit in silence 🤫, doing nothing.","dt":"2024-01-13T13:56:13","s":["qwha3d19sn"]}],"6":[{"m":"How God trusted Satan to do only what he, God, had instructed is something to think about.\n\nThis is God we are talking about — the devil knew better than to disobey.","dt":"2026-01-06T08:08:50","s":["278xdo6xvt"]}]},"3":{"8":[{"m":"Job 3:8 NKJV\nMay those curse it who curse the day, Those who are ready to arouse Leviathan.\n\nThis is how the NKJV and other versions render it. Interesting.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:18:27","s":["u6wk9dzgto"]}],"26":[{"m":"What does it mean... This verse?","dt":"2022-01-07T14:21:02","s":["xhz0u25voa"]}]},"4":{"9":[{"m":"It seems logical, and it's so easy to say of things as seems thought wrong. The things that came upon Job, obviously he can't be innocent. For the fire 🔥 of God signifies divine judgement to come upon Job, smh 🤦‍♂️ he can't be innocent.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:23:55","s":["l77v40wcpe"]}],"17":[{"m":"This again is one of those scriptures we quote so often, and yet it was said by a man who was in the wrong.","dt":"2024-01-15T17:54:47","s":["8habkdwv3y"]}],"10":[{"m":"What manner of friends are these that are so blunt and freely express 😑 their minds to their hurting friend?\n\nThey were indeed true friends. They love their friend and brother Job but were not eye 👁‍🗨 pleasers.\n\nThey were blunt enough and true to their friendship to speak truth to their brother.","dt":"2024-01-15T15:31:57","s":["apqj6mz4vs"]}],"13":[{"m":"So this vision of the night he received, granted it was true, and yea, even its interpretation also true, his personal interpretation & application thereof in Job's situation was wrong, as proved later.\n\nThis teaches us that visions and dreams must be prayerfully thought out and applied.","dt":"2024-01-15T15:36:17","s":["qw47imwmzm"]}]},"5":{"17":[{"m":"Wisdom there, though on a faulty premise and not applicable here.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:27:45","s":["u1wyk3z7dt"]}],"27":[{"m":"Indeed this is wisdom, and his argument ended on a positive note.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:29:51","s":["n00a15mkuf"]}]},"6":{"11":[{"m":"Oh, Job was in pain and he saw no end in sight.\nHe just wished to die 🎲","dt":"2022-01-07T14:31:55","s":["bzga2qt101"]}],"27":[{"m":"Oh... JOB is really baring out his heart and letting his friend know he is hurt.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:35:17","s":["eovmns2h20"]}],"15":[{"m":"Job's trials are lessons of life — though he received his pain as a lump sum, in an instant, we normally have it spread throughout the days of our lives; we learn wisdom from them.\n\nThere will come a time when friends will accuse you and not understand you, family will desert you and deal deceitfully with you.","dt":"2026-01-06T08:26:44","s":["qlv1ol3htt"]}]},"7":{"14":[{"m":"Wow, so the torment was not just physical but mental.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:38:38","s":["s5kou0l4p6"]}],"20":[{"m":"Though Job was not there when Satan placed his bet, he could kind of tell that it was like God has set his eyes upon him to use as an example.\n\nIn this he was right, but he did not know why.","dt":"2026-01-06T08:32:03","s":["h93si2230f"]}],"3":[{"m":"Could this be an indicator of how long he had been under this skin to skin trial??","dt":"2022-01-07T14:37:08","s":["5b7yaqbxiw"]}]},"8":{"6":[{"m":"Another sense knowledge... Very logical argument, but they were wrong.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:40:42","s":["q2hd0mngbo"]}],"7":[{"m":"Ah, so this is where this scripture comes from — from a man whose words were flawed — from a man who condemned his friend wrongly.\n\nThis verse was proven right in Job's life in the long run. Such wisdom in the scriptures.","dt":"2026-01-06T08:39:53","s":["zdsxdm9dz1"]}],"17":[{"m":"Take note that these men were men of wisdom, being friends of the great Job.\n\nAlso they spoke only after 7 days of silence — so their words were full of wisdom and life lessons, yet they were wrong, being applied in the wrong place and time.","dt":"2026-01-06T08:42:26","s":["bqpzput7ek"]}]},"9":{"9":[{"m":"Straight red... What's that?? Meanhijj","dt":"2022-01-07T14:43:31","s":["9awup86ifb"]}],"33":[{"m":"In this Job was right: even if God shows up, he lacks the requisite words to argue with God, and that was exactly how it turned out when God showed up 👆.\n\nEven though elsewhere in scripture God calls us to reason with him.","dt":"2024-01-15T18:01:38","s":["gjm0t74tt6"]}]},"13":{"8":[{"m":"And herein lies the summary of the faults of Job's friends.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:56:02","s":["h335jxlvx3"]}],"16":[{"m":"So Job's point is:\nGOD is just and righteous, so he does not understand why he is suffering, though he is just.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:57:24","s":["uunlg2fw17"]}],"27":[{"m":"He felt he was not being treated fairly. GOD WAS MONITORING him too closely, thus he felt he was being punished even for the sins of his youth.","dt":"2022-01-07T14:59:48","s":["tul119nabk"]}],"3":[{"m":"That was all he wanted, really?","dt":"2022-01-07T14:55:30","s":["h8d4fil0lf"]}],"15":[{"m":"Another popular verse.","dt":"2026-01-06T08:56:30","s":["ik5xq0dk2r"]}]},"14":{"14":[{"m":"Awww... What faith... What blessed him.","dt":"2022-01-07T15:02:06","s":["2erj7cjog8"]}]},"15":{"4":[{"m":"I don't think that is the point he... He is being judged in his righteousness and he questioned that.\n\nAll he desired is to speak to God.","dt":"2022-01-07T15:14:02","s":["xk3wq1ee51"]}],"13":[{"m":"Eliphaz that, the God advocate. Speaking in the place of God and desiring to make God righteous and Job evil 😈","dt":"2022-01-07T15:19:10","s":["qkkoro1484"]}],"30":[{"m":"And Job did depart out of darkness.","dt":"2024-02-05T07:15:40","s":["slr2j2z32r","6wqfmfvedc"]}],"34":[{"m":"Thus ⚡ explaining where the fire 🔥 of God came from.\n\nHe spoke wisely, yet not the wisdom of God.","dt":"2022-01-07T15:21:35","s":["ue24emipxv"]}],"10":[{"m":"Was this literal? Then that meant Job, out of wisdom, kept contact with the aged and the wise so he could pick much from them.","dt":"2024-02-05T07:12:19","s":["kdh73yuwau"]}],"18":[{"m":"So Eliphaz was drawing on the wisdom of the ancients, and rightly so.\n\nJust that he did not know that this time is that one time where things differ from the norm.\n\nJob was no normal man, and that which was happening was indeed beyond any of their wildest imaginations.","dt":"2024-02-05T07:14:28","s":["0r55ez03ef"]}]},"16":{"2":[{"m":"Lol, 😂 indeed they were.\n\nSo the seven days they sat without talking, this was what they were conceiving.\n\nIndeed, as men of wisdom, some older 🧓 than Job, they sought to understand in their silence 🤫 what comfort to give Job and what words to explain his misery.","dt":"2022-01-07T15:23:29","s":["rl7ga2sfo9"]}],"5":[{"m":"Hm 🤔 wisdom spoken: the last thing to do to a man whose soul is weary 😩 is to fault him and bash him more.\n\nAnd that was Job's point here. He was broken down already, and yet they heap up more pain 🥖","dt":"2022-01-07T15:24:51","s":["va828zqo8q"]}],"20":[{"m":"His friends and family 👪, who were to comfort him, mock him.","dt":"2022-01-07T15:27:42","s":["lawgntkumm"]}],"22":[{"m":"Aww... So sad 😔.\n\nIndeed these are the words of a man in pain 🥖","dt":"2022-01-07T15:28:32","s":["zi5n0hqm1q"]}],"6":[{"m":"This was indeed torture upon torture.\n\nNot only was Satan inflicting physical and heart-wrenching emotional pain.\n\nBut here he was going through psychological pain. His own friends blaming him for the troubles that had befallen him.\n\nAnd wanted him to accept something he wasn't guilty of.\n\nSuch wickedness from evil 😈. The devil, when given a chance, will release maximum onslaught.\n\nThis goes to show how wicked Satan is.","dt":"2024-02-05T07:19:02","s":["yxfk5civn3"]}],"13":[{"m":"After such trials, I can imagine the strength 💪 of Job's family 👪, friends and business, and even his army of servants.\n\nThey had gone through much together, and as we know, persecution strengthens a people.","dt":"2024-02-05T07:21:19","s":["is3guwbypq"]}],"14":[{"m":"Like a giant?","dt":"2022-01-07T15:26:24","s":["fzmjlprsfa"]}]},"18":{"21":[{"m":"It seems Job's friends have concluded that his wickedness was the cause of his much suffering.\n\nAnd you can't really blame them. The circumstances of Job's downfall were not just natural but supernatural.\n\nIncluding the fire 🔥 from heaven. Obviously symbolic of God's judgement.\n\nMY only reservation was that his friend was suffering, so the least to do was to provide him with some respite.\n\nEven if Job was in the wrong, this was not the time ⌚","dt":"2022-01-08T07:41:42","s":["4ch0dalzjp"]}]},"19":{"3":[{"m":"A man in pain... He was counting.","dt":"2022-01-08T08:33:54","s":["akvf893nh4"]}],"14":[{"m":"The rich have many friends but the poor,\n\nProverbs 14:20 KJV\nThe poor is hated even of his own neighbour: but the rich hath many friends.\n\nIt's sad 😔. His own wife even asked him to curse 🤬 God and die.\n\nThis indeed is wisdom to us 🙏...\n\nDo we really have true friends? Which of them will stick with us through thick and thin?","dt":"2022-01-08T08:40:08","s":["eakdlvl0uw"]}],"17":[{"m":"What??? 😳 Job suffered, indeed he did.\n\nAnd you know, a thought 💭 struck. The people of the Bible, though we claim we are more developed and advanced than they are, I suspect that might not be the case.\n\nWhere it seems they were limited, we see the supernatural technology at work.\n\nWe have computers today, but they have scrolls and writings whose content our most advanced research and knowledge cannot fathom.\n\nSee, for instance, the prophecies of the Bible that unfold right before our eyes 👀.\n\nSee the kind of miracles and supernatural events that shook their world then. We don't see them today.\n\nAnyways, this is just premonition, back to Job.","dt":"2022-01-08T08:50:11","s":["lnv1ygbbch"]}],"25":[{"m":"Just imagine Job in the terrible situation, and God, the devil 👿 and the rest of the host of heaven watch as Job begins to speak 🔊 thus.\n\nOh, what a moment, how proud God might have felt as the devil 👿 is disgraced.\n\nJob making God so proud, and the host of heaven learn of the sons of God — man 👨.\n\nHow that a people, despite the pain and afflictions which the Lord could have prevented but did not, continue in relentless love to the Lord.","dt":"2024-02-06T07:30:07","s":["x8kschqx4k"]}],"27":[{"m":"These words are so prophetic.\n\nIt was almost as if he knew he prophesied, so he asked for it to be engraved on a rock 🚀.\n\nThat was how dead sure Job was.","dt":"2022-01-08T08:54:02","s":["igsyfd2b5z"]},{"m":"HOW dare he, he was being touted as a wicked man by the best of his friends, yet he has the nerves to not just deny but talk of seeing God in his flesh.\n\nBut he was right, they wrong.","dt":"2026-01-08T18:25:58","s":["4rdf2uyxch"]}],"2":[{"m":"True... Words are weapons. They have creative ability.\n\nIt was with words that the world 🗺 as we know it was created.\n\nIn Psalms it says God sent his word and healed them.\n\nPsalm 107:20 KJV\nHe sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them from their destructions.\n\nIn Isaiah he talks of his word performing that for which he, God, sent it.\n\nIsaiah 55:11 KJV\nSo shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper in the thing whereto I sent it.","dt":"2022-01-08T07:58:58","s":["nv383or5yp"]}],"29":[{"m":"Well noted, Naamathite.\n\nSo what is the portion of the righteous then??","dt":"2022-01-08T08:58:44","s":["ucgf8seds8"]}]},"20":{"29":[{"m":"It seemed that the strong belief in that era was that the wicked are them that go through untold sufferings, as what Job was suffering, and there was no way Job was going through this much suffering as a righteous man.\n\nAnd rightly so.","dt":"2026-01-08T18:33:28","s":["vw0vyclopi"]}]},"21":{"3":[{"m":"Job now properly classifies what he's suffering from his friends as pure mockery.","dt":"2022-01-09T16:05:34","s":["ifg3c15fun"]}],"34":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 that's a solid point made by Job. His friends make the point that his punishment is because of his wickedness.\n\nYet he shows them wicked men 🚹 whose children 🧒 dance about happily and die in the grave in peace ✌️.\n\nSo now where is their point that he's suffering 🏄 for his wickedness?","dt":"2022-01-09T16:11:29","s":["1gkly6gvpd"]}]},"22":{"3":[{"m":"Now they are gradually warming themselves up to Job's point that he is righteous and is not being punished for any wicked deeds of his.","dt":"2022-01-09T18:48:38","s":["sndjmykrpr"]}],"23":[{"m":"I am beginning to wonder, these friends of Job, did they really know him?\n\nWe are told they travelled to come see him, so maybe they are childhood friends.\n\nNot really dwelling with each other to know each other's ways and character.","dt":"2026-01-10T05:39:37","s":["v9tvja939l"]}],"25":[{"m":"Funny, but money, i.e. gold and silver in abundance, was a sign of God's blessing and approval for the righteous.","dt":"2022-01-09T20:38:01","s":["9morpf566h"]}],"28":[{"m":"Amen — but this statement or blessing is conditional — it is subject to obeying the Lord as stated in the verses prior.\n\nWhen we align with the Lord, he makes silver abundant in our lives and gold like the dust to us.","dt":"2026-01-10T05:45:44","s":["07q9i6d597"]}],"29":[{"m":"Two very popular scriptures... It's interesting that it wasn't spoken by God, neither by Job, but by his friends who were in the wrong.\n\nThis does not put these verses ♒ in disrepute, because these men were indeed wise.\n\nThey just got it wrong this time when it came to Job.\n\nThere were factors at stake way beyond them.","dt":"2022-01-09T20:41:45","s":["qy7aozgj13"]}]},"23":{"12":[{"m":"This is akin to Jesus telling his disciples, in the story of the Samaritan woman 👩, that he has food 🍲 to eat that they know not of.","dt":"2022-01-09T20:43:38","s":["9aisq31ek4"]}]},"24":{"24":[{"m":"Was it not Job who said the wicked go unharmed and live long etc.?\n\nYes, but that does not contradict this statement he's made here.\n\nThey are parallel truths... Co-existing though they seem contradictory, yet both are true.\n\nWe see the wicked fall many times before their time and see the law of God at work to cut them short.\n\nThere are also times when the wicked thrive and do well whiles the righteous suffer from want, the poor and fatherless oppressed without justice ⚖\n\nTruths that co-exist.","dt":"2022-01-10T06:30:48","s":["wdxiqe6tkk"]}]},"26":{"14":[{"m":"What we know of God is nothing compared to what is yet to be known, Job seems to be saying.","dt":"2022-01-10T06:33:24","s":["3vg4kbkhso"]}]},"27":{"6":[{"m":"Job stayed true to his words and convictions.\n\nHe would not let others lure his mind away from that truth.","dt":"2022-01-10T06:34:48","s":["dk4wp9bffx"]}],"17":[{"m":"Here we see the justice of the Lord in recompensing evil to the wicked.\n\nAnd Job, through the years, had seen this.\n\nHowever, in previous verses he complains of how the wicked grow old and seem not to be rewarded for their wicked ways.\n\nSo we see that in this life the wicked sometimes get the due reward for their wickedness and hypocrisy.\n\nAnd there are times they seem to get away with it, but of course eternal judgement awaits all.\n\nBut why some get recompensed in the earth 🌎 and others don't, and what criteria is used to judge thus, only God knows.\n\nJust as the righteous get blessed and may prosper materially and for all to see,\n\nThere are times the righteous suffer loss for their righteousness' sake.\n\nBut like David says, I was young and now I am old, and I've not seen the righteous forsaken or their children begging bread.","dt":"2024-01-10T07:45:14","s":["mb8stgr4q7"]}],"23":[{"m":"The God who takes revenge in action here... He is a just God.\n\nWe may not always understand his strategy, because sometimes out of the most wicked of souls comes a Saul or Paul who will change the phase of Christianity.\n\nLet us just trust the graciousness and wisdom of God.","dt":"2022-01-10T06:38:11","s":["b0otumpjpd"]}]},"28":{"18":[{"m":"We see wisdom has not anything that can be used to exchange it.\n\nIt's just like the question 🙋 of why man is conscious and more intelligent 🧠 than any other animal.\n\nIt seems all other creatures for some reason just cannot think 🤔.\n\nThat thing that makes us think and conscious, where is it from?\n\nIn the same manner, wisdom even among men cannot be fathomed.\n\nWhy are some people just wise?\n\nWell, it is the Lord that giveth wisdom\n... Out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding.","dt":"2024-01-10T07:51:35","s":["yu79zgee8w"]}],"28":[{"m":"Mmmm mm... So though popularized by Solomon in Proverbs, it is actually Job who first said 📖 it.\n\nThe fear of God is wisdom 🤔\n\nTo depart from evil is indeed understanding.\n\nSo for the hyper-grace movements in error, who sin and do evil and claim cleansing by the blood 🆎 of Jesus.\n\nYes, they are cleansed and forgiven, but are not walking 🚶 in wisdom.\n\nAnd guess what, their folly will soon come to light.","dt":"2022-01-10T06:45:06","s":["s3ax3whmc8"]},{"m":"Wow, the question is answered. How to obtain wisdom and understanding.\n\nNot by folly and learning through experience. What then is the benefit of understanding when you have already suffered the loss that understanding was supposed to bring?\n\nRather, shun evil 😈 and you will later gain the understanding for which you took this instruction.\n\nAs you see the reward on those who refused to heed.","dt":"2024-01-10T07:54:18","s":["t6fi6uyy2y"]}]},"29":{"6":[{"m":"The Good News rendering tallies and better reflects my understanding of this verse.\n\nThat even in the most rocky of places, impossible situations... he prospered.\n\nNo wonder Job feared God so much. He knew his prosperity was as a result of the secrets of God.\n\nHe talks of his longing for the times when the secrets of God were upon his tabernacle.","dt":"2022-01-10T07:15:03","s":["f4n4oh1wbk"]}],"10":[{"m":"This was a man who had a hedge of fire 🔥 about him and everything of his.\n\nLittle wonder he had this effect on people, even on nobles and princes 🤴.\n\nHe was divine, divinely assisted.","dt":"2024-01-11T07:13:37","s":["k7egkjavxd"]}]},"31":{"33":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔. Leko nemanda...\n\nAdam's story passed down from generation to generation 💎.\n\nJob was indeed a very righteous man 👨. He confessed his sins often.","dt":"2022-01-11T08:21:11","s":["ct6fzpfd0k"]}]},"32":{"14":[{"m":"Okay, nice intro. Let's see what Elihu has to say in his discourse 🕺... It's his time to dance.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:26:48","s":["lrf8s2o6xr"]}],"21":[{"m":"Was he at this point talking to God, or was he using pray in the sense of a request and plea 🙏?\n\nLooks like pray was being used in the sense of plea, and other verses support that view.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:28:57","s":["4kgaw9csa9"]}]},"33":{"1":[{"m":"Looks like pray was being used in the sense of plea, and other verses support that view.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:31:12","s":["mlfixa20ge"]}],"6":[{"m":"Interesting angle that Elihu took.\n\nJob wished to speak to God, and Elihu says, I grant you your wish — let me be in the stead of God.\n\nThen he goes ahead to imply that since he is flesh like Job, Job would not be frightened of him.\n\nThus Job can freely listen to his reason and counter him.\n\nMaybe that's why God didn't rebuke him as he did the other friends.","dt":"2024-02-09T10:14:07","s":["lrpd535rmz"]}],"26":[{"m":"AND this was prophetic, for indeed Job was restored to his former state and even better.","dt":"2024-02-09T10:17:36","s":["2gkfpi5kcc"]}],"33":[{"m":"Wow... This younger man is bold. He must have something up his sleeves. Let's see.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:35:43","s":["y4mkxlahd9"]}]},"34":{"12":[{"m":"So Elihu's strategy is that he stood in the place of God to speak for him. Smart 🧠, and very poetic the angle of his thoughts 💭 and speech 🗨 patterns.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:39:05","s":["viywmb8i7q"]}],"19":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 Elihu was making some strong 💪 points here. Advocating for some more respect and honour for God, and at least his sovereignty.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:42:32","s":["up3kwzoctg"]}],"23":[{"m":"That's true, and even truer in JOB'S CASE; this was a contest 🦄 of spirit beings.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:43:43","s":["yom32srfl5"]}]},"35":{"8":[{"m":"Very true... Indeed our wickedness and our righteousness profit or hurt men, not God.\n\nHowever, God, being God by nature, cannot behold wickedness without just recompense in this life or thereafter.\n\nELIHU is making some really strong points.","dt":"2024-02-09T10:27:21","s":["lub23urpjg"]}],"14":[{"m":"Another good point there. Trust thou in him...\nHaving the perspective that this was a test, I see where Elihu was on point.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:48:15","s":["a79m69w9al"]}]},"36":{"2":[{"m":"Who was Elihu, and what manner of relationship did he have with God that he should seek to speak in the stead of God?\n\nGod?? 😳 A speaking dares to speak for him.\n\nThen that man must indeed know God, and have such intimate knowledge and fellowship with him.\n\nI ASK AGAIN, WHO... WAS ELIHU?","dt":"2022-01-13T07:50:26","s":["1fzfk5jf5r"]}],"12":[{"m":"So Israel being blessed in the times of kings who served and loved the Lord was not new.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:52:49","s":["z6rgmfce85"]}],"31":[{"m":"True... Through the forces 💪 of nature God judges.\n\nBlessing with abundance or cursing with lack.","dt":"2022-01-13T10:06:59","s":["m5aj4aj91k"]}],"4":[{"m":"His confidence 🔏 and certainty is mind-boggling.","dt":"2022-01-13T07:51:06","s":["62t4vmgvsj"]}]},"37":{"5":[{"m":"The discourse of Elihu in hindsight sounds like the discourse of God when he appeared before Job.","dt":"2022-01-13T10:09:05","s":["l3vwwrvou1"]}],"16":[{"m":"God is perfect 👌 in knowledge, so also in this matter concerning Job he has a depth of knowledge and perspective that Job cannot appreciate, and that was indeed so.","dt":"2022-01-13T10:12:06","s":["fqoiofn6un"]}]},"38":{"2":[{"m":"The words of God here are like the words of Elihu... No wonder God did not condemn Elihu but did the others.","dt":"2024-02-11T20:06:26","s":["9izsf8f1me"]}],"7":[{"m":"Man is a creature wonderful and fantastic.\n\nAfter having spoken of the 🌎 earth in all its complexities and glamour,\nhow difficult it is to fathom,\n\nhe comes to the sons of God, of whom man is part.\n\nThat is how super complex and super powerful we are.\n\nThat the sons of God are one of the questions 🙋 posed to Job to answer and fathom out.\nIf he could nkwaa di3","dt":"2022-01-17T07:25:57","s":["nt9bweofz6"]}],"41":[{"m":"A thought struck me: the raven's young wander for lack of meat.\n\nThey've done no wrong, yet God permits them to wander at the peril of their innocent lives until their mother comes with food.\n\nThis also is the wisdom of God, and Job cannot answer why that is so.\n\nHe, like the young ravens, without cause suffereth violently and knoweth not why, but his sufferings were not without cause, as we are in hindsight made to know that there were bigger stakes going on beyond him.","dt":"2026-01-14T13:47:39","s":["r07unnomac"]}]},"41":{"5":[{"m":"Why did God choose to use the display of his wisdom, might and pomp to answer Job, rather than tell him he has a bargain on...\n\nHere God shows Job his works of wisdom and is pointing to him that whatever he does is for a reason, and a just one for that matter.","dt":"2024-02-12T07:18:18","s":["h65zcz003w"]}],"18":[{"m":"What beast is this?","dt":"2022-01-20T06:22:40","s":["xlf2h8hqbt"]}]},"42":{"6":[{"m":"Oh okay, so this is where that expression is from — dust and ashes.","dt":"2024-02-12T07:22:32","s":["07v24vqi1m"]}],"7":[{"m":"Heheh 😅... Job was indeed God's favorite... God had rebuked him, yet he told Job's friends that Job was right, and thus they need to apologize.\n\nCharlie, we all are not equal before God.\n\nIt appears our ranking with God is dependent on how close we are to him and how much we reverence him.\n\nThe same it is in the natural.","dt":"2024-02-12T07:24:57","s":["ob7hp0u2ej"]}],"8":[{"m":"This is similar to Abraham and Abimelech. God indeed has favorites.\n\nThough these examples are Old Testament, I wonder if the same applies to the New Testament.\n\nThough I don't doubt it does.\n\nJust that in the New Testament we all are children of God, and like earthly fathers, we love all our children, but some are just preferred to others because of their availability and service.\n\nIt's just that way... That does not take away the love we have for the others, but we know who belongs where.","dt":"2024-02-12T07:27:07","s":["lae4g9p9cd","tp0fq0y5tj"]},{"m":"There is someone else in scripture, I think Abraham, whom the Lord rebuked the king — Pharaoh, or was it Abimelech? — for his sake.\n\nWhy seven bulls and rams? It seems ere was the law of Moses, knowledge of sacrifices was known, and the significance of numbers in approaching God.","dt":"2026-01-15T09:41:40","s":["7ont0g1pls"]}],"11":[{"m":"He that hath, smh 🤦‍♂️ when he had not and needed it the most, no man gave.\n\nYet in his abundance, more was given him.\n\nIndeed he that hath, more will be given.","dt":"2022-01-20T06:40:30","s":["bc5zxo2oq5"]},{"m":"How was Job able to dwell with them when they had abandoned him in his lowest moment?\nBut he, being a man of wisdom, understood that it was all the doing of the Lord, and they just acted as is natural to men.\n\nThe loss of his first family 👪 also he did commit into the hands of the knowing God. I'm sure he mourned them as any father would, but he knew the wisdom of God is greater than man.\n\nAnd see, 4 thousand years and we still speak of Job.","dt":"2024-02-12T07:33:28","s":["4z8ijovu7b"]},{"m":"He that hath... indeed more is given.","dt":"2026-01-15T09:44:59","s":["np0oqfqp0s"]}]}},"Joshua":{"2":{"2":[{"m":"How did he know? Even in their times, though there was no camera 📸, men were stationed to ensure spies were kept out.","dt":"2024-05-09T16:45:49","s":["1l4hdvh2ae"]}],"4":[{"m":"We celebrate Rahab as making a wise choice, but was she not a betrayer?\n\nOr she was wise, not being blinded by loyalty to a failing state.\n\nShe aligned herself with God and his purposes, though she was a harlot.\n\nThis does not mean God approves of harlotry, but after she aligned and finally joins Israel, she is married to an Israelite, and from her genealogy comes the Christ.\n\nNo record again is made of her harlotry. Indeed, harlotry was prohibited in Israel 🇮🇱","dt":"2022-03-25T00:07:57","s":["84ch56d1y1"]}],"10":[{"m":"40 years ago and the story persists... It's difficult to shake off such a story, especially when eyewitnesses were still alive.\n\nNow here comes this dreaded people to take your land. You are done for indeed.\n\nRahab was wise and she shine her eyes 👀.\n\nShe was smart and no idiot to continue her allegiance to a failed state.\n\nMore so, being a prostitute, she knew men and how vain they were. She plied her trade by wisdom, stealth and deceptive manipulation.\n\nShe would not be fooled by statedom and its lure.\n\nLike almost all states, the people are just tools in the hands 👐 of the mighty, fed with lies 🤥 to keep them humble.\n\nShe slept likely with men of repute and she heard stories. She knew it was a game of thrones. Kings 👑 and ♟ pawns.\n\nHer opportunity had come. She would not be fooled.","dt":"2022-03-25T00:17:36","s":["gy02i3jnz7"]}],"14":[{"m":"Oh, this marked a true sign 🤘 for them that the people feared them and that the land was theirs.\n\nIt was such personal interactions that the 12 spies lacked, because from the crossing of the Red Sea, these heathen had heard what the Lord had done and feared.\n\nThis was forty years ago; if only they had believed the Lord. The people of Canaan's hearts ♥ always melted, and yet the people also feared 😨 that which feared them.\n\nWhat an irony 😏. What wasted opportunity and years.\n\nNo wonder the Lord was so wroth with them.","dt":"2024-05-09T17:04:02","s":["t52mja7cjw"]},{"m":"SHE WAS A PROSTITUTE, SHE WAS A BELIEVER","dt":"2026-03-23T05:57:14","s":["0h3rsfki6m"]}],"15":[{"m":"Strategic location for business.","dt":"2022-03-25T00:14:20","s":["rp10qomd43"]}],"21":[{"m":"SHE betrayed her own people, she changed allegiance, she was now a Jew, she and her household. She was now born again. She too will now behold the cloud of God's glory.\n\nShe also will at last see HIS SHEKINAH","dt":"2026-03-23T06:03:21","s":["qcx5y7j4ef"]}],"11":[{"m":"They heard these victories and attributed it not to the men of Israel but to God.\n\nThis was God's strategy, that through Israel he would root out all evil 😈, and the remnant of men, seeing the wisdom, holiness and blessedness of serving the Lord, would willingly come to him and be adopted into Israel.\n\nOnly a fool after seeing all this would not.\n\nBut alas, Israel also failed the Lord woefully and delayed the plan of uniting man to God. All of the world 🗺 to God.","dt":"2024-05-09T16:53:34","s":["r5sek3wd8a"]}],"19":[{"m":"Interesting imagery...\n\nImagine as Israel raided the other houses 🏘, burning 🔥 them down and breaking them.\n\nYet there conspicuously stood this house, which stood obviously unscathed. Whose house 🏡 was that?\n\nThe house of Rahab the prostitute, and all in there were safe.\n\nImagine the weeks preceding this event, Rahab seemed to be having a family reunion as all friends and family 👪 came to her home 🏡 and refused to return or go too far from her home.\n\nI wonder what excuse they coined for this number of people coming to her home...\n\nHer house became like Noah's ark.","dt":"2024-05-09T17:11:20","s":["kwpqj207s2"]}]},"3":{"5":[{"m":"Probably God had already told him what he, God, was about to do.","dt":"2024-05-10T06:16:52","s":["eipt5ml8gx"]}],"7":[{"m":"Yep, so that is it. God had already spoken to Joshua about what he was about to do.\nThat's why Joshua could give such specific instructions as staying 3000 cubits behind the ark of the covenant.","dt":"2024-05-10T06:18:22","s":["901c3epvcw"]},{"m":"THOUGH he wasn't a priest or Levite, he could still command the priests, because he was the leader and God thus communicated to him directly. He was like a king; he was a king, but this rulership was not hereditary.","dt":"2026-03-23T06:06:42","s":["ak59s2xrng"]}],"13":[{"m":"What a sight 🤯... Now imagine the people of Jericho watching this scene from afar.\n\nThey knew they were done for.","dt":"2022-03-25T00:36:06","s":["z4qgerts9y"]}]},"4":{"7":[{"m":"Memorials are a good thing. I've got to pass on our history to our children 🧒.\n\nThe Martha and Henry story.\n\nNow to the Bible: God knew men forget easily; men die off, but physical symbols live on and will serve as a good reminder.","dt":"2022-03-25T00:38:51","s":["ah627444be"]}],"8":[{"m":"God was putting up memorials everywhere so that the children of Israel do not forget what he had done, and their children will have a witness and testimony to what the Lord had done in time past.\n\nSo that when they are at rest in the promised land and do not need that many divine miracles and interventions, they have the stories, and not just stories but physical evidences of the stories.\n\nThat way they will know the stories really happened and not folklore.\n\nBut we have a witness of the happenings in the Bible and of the scriptures. The witness is the Holy Spirit in our hearts.\n\nWe can't deny him. HE lives right inside us. Even when the wind is contrary and we hear different stories and so-called scientific evidences contrary to the word of God, which in reality is not science but agendas of men, our faith still stands strong, because we cannot deny the Spirit that lives in us and whom we fellowship with day in and day out,\n\nfor our fellowship is with the Father and with his Son.","dt":"2026-03-23T06:16:47","s":["kh99prap9z"]}],"9":[{"m":"Who asked him to? No one, we are not told. Or the interplay of wisdom. As God gave instruction as a witness to the children of men, he also thought it wise to leave a witness to the Spirit, to GOD. SO that witness was under the river where no man can see but God can.\n\nBut wait, these stones were not just a witness to the Spirit but to men, the children of Israel unborn. Anyone can take up stones and arrange them and claim they were from under the river as a result of miraculously being stopped by God for the people to walk on dry ground.\n\nBut if you should dive into the river, you will see twelve stones, intelligently arranged under the bank of the river, maybe even with names of the tribes of Israel etched in them.\n\nA feat that could only be achieved if someone dived in there who could go that deep down and hold his breath for ages against the current and lift boulders and arrange them etc. Something that is not possible humanly except if the river dried up.\n\nI won't be surprised if these stones were perfectly aligned with the ones on the land.\n\nOh Lord, give us the wisdom to keep memorials of divine and key moments of our lives for the future generations.","dt":"2026-03-23T06:28:08","s":["uvthgl1eby"]}],"16":[{"m":"How did the Lord speak, was it audibly?\nSecondly, why did he speak to Joshua and not the priests? For Joshua was not a Levite.\n\nHe spoke to Joshua because he was the leader.","dt":"2022-03-25T00:44:38","s":["42d586qff6"]}],"23":[{"m":"They came out of Egypt and slavery through the dry ground of the Red Sea, and entered the promised land of Canaan through the dry ground of the river Jordan.","dt":"2026-03-23T06:35:28","s":["2xel8btyow"]}],"24":[{"m":"Now the purpose of the memorial is stated.\n\nGod knew he was not going to be appearing to everyone and to Israel 🇮🇱 in such dynamic fashion always, but the memorial will always be present 📦 to represent God.","dt":"2022-03-25T01:21:37","s":["58rlbmg5tt"]}]},"5":{"7":[{"m":"Could age also be a factor in the kind of respect the children of Israel had for Joshua?\n\nJoshua at this stage was 80 years, about the same age as when Moses delivered Israel from the hands of Pharaoh.\n\nAt this stage, Joshua and Caleb were the only people of that age.\n\nOf course this was not the only reason, in fact not even the main reason, as this people had shown that they could disrespect even God, the Ancient of Days.\n\nMuch less an 80-year-old man. But it did play a role somewhat, I believe.\n\nAs it served as a grim reminder of what had happened to their fathers, and only two lived this long — because of obedience.","dt":"2024-05-10T06:28:25","s":["eq7daaoqgy"]}],"8":[{"m":"This was a perfect opportunity for their enemies to strike at them, as the sons of Jacob did to Shechem, but they were too scared to dare attack.\n\nThey only hid themselves, awaiting their doom.","dt":"2026-03-24T15:25:40","s":["idvjky5vpp"]}],"12":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔","dt":"2022-03-25T01:24:16","s":["or86f4vsv2"]},{"m":"Ah wait oo... so manna was following them everywhere, think of it. When they moved, the manna would rain in the new location, not the old.\n\nThey even crossed the Jordan and manna followed them, only to cease the morrow after they ate the old corn of the land.","dt":"2026-03-24T15:30:45","s":["vvc6sx7qce"]}],"14":[{"m":"How did Joshua discern that this was God and not man?\n\nIs it not because of his encounters with God under Moses?\n\nGod had come to them and sat down to meat 🥩 with them in bodily form.\n\nHe knew, as did Abraham, and had EXPERIENCED God to know that this man 👨 is not man, though 💭 he looks like one.","dt":"2022-03-25T01:27:00","s":["fli035xgv0"]}],"15":[{"m":"How do they know when a true angel or spirit appears to them? He paid obeisance to him. How do they know? Same thing with Abraham when God visited him. How did he know?","dt":"2026-03-24T15:51:43","s":["voim7is0lp"]}],"1":[{"m":"Only God knows the kind of incantations that these pagan nations did for their gods when they heard this.\n\nOnly God knows the number of human sacrifices and bloodshed that was done to strengthen themselves for the war they saw coming. And none of them thought to default to the side of Jehovah. Yes, they believed, just as demons believe in God and tremble, yet they did not mix with faith what they had heard, so none defaulted to the side of JEHOVAH save Rahab the prostitute.","dt":"2026-03-24T14:59:00","s":["mn4ghmdqrw"]}],"9":[{"m":"Oh Lord God, when will you roll away the reproach of our colonial masters from us?\n\nThe disorder, division and foolishness of our ways.","dt":"2024-05-10T06:29:51","s":["vy3dnt0muq"]}]},"6":{"6":[{"m":"You indeed need to be bold and courageous, because at any point in time God can come up with a command for the people and it must be executed.\n\nIt takes a strong 💪 leader to lead such a great flock of God in line with God's dictates.\n\nOf course, that does not mean God's commands are erratic.","dt":"2022-03-25T01:29:59","s":["6p3y3ixg7c"]}],"9":[{"m":"Armed men protecting the most powerful and dangerous presence on earth. Why did the ark need protection? Why?","dt":"2026-03-25T16:54:59","s":["7d2lk13w9d"]}],"13":[{"m":"Such work was for young, vibrant men. No wonder old men were taken out of service of the tabernacle.","dt":"2026-03-25T16:56:25","s":["qfdv75fr64"]}],"16":[{"m":"I can imagine the fear 😱 as the Israelites compassed the city, once and then twice and then three times and then four 4⃣...\n\nAt this time the inhabitants of Jericho wondered what was going on; they knew today was different.\n\nThey could feel it that this march was going to crescendo into something, but this something they could not tell.\n\nUntil the seventh march... Their fears heightened with each march.\n\nThen the people shouted and down came the walls of Jericho.\n\nALL the while Rahab's house had the scarlet cloth hanging down and signifying her cover from death ☠ and destruction.\n\nAs it hanged down, the angels 😇 of God saw and forbore, knowing that she was covered and protected from destruction of any sort.\n\nAmazingly, the walls of Jericho came down mightily, yet Rahab the prostitute's side of the wall stayed intact because of covenant.\n\nOh, this our God... This God.","dt":"2024-05-10T07:56:50","s":["3wzhcd7or9"]}],"20":[{"m":"From the sound of things or the look of things, the wall fell down flat before the people at their side, so they had an entrance into the city. I don't know if the wall fell down all round the city. Would that have, in a sense, provided some escape for those on the outskirts, except the army of the Lord had encompassed the city all round?","dt":"2026-03-25T17:24:06","s":["5a1f2z9645"]}],"23":[{"m":"Because they were unclean till they had done the required rituals.","dt":"2024-05-10T08:00:53","s":["7ckly7vq5w"]},{"m":"Just wondering — does that mean Rahab's end of the wall did not collapse when the Lord broke their walls?","dt":"2026-03-25T17:21:01","s":["j31ku3hczo"]}],"3":[{"m":"This was no easy feat, encompassing a city every day for 6 days.\n\nDake's commentary reminds us also that the standing in the rivers of Jordan till all the people passed was also no small feat, possibly took a whole day.\n\nAnd required much physical stamina.\n\nThis brings to mind how spectacular such a sight was. The waters of Jordan heaping up miles away like a dam.\n\nSuch supernatural power, and yet many of the people did not dig deep into God.\n\nThey had the opportunity of a lifetime where God was this close to man, yet they blew it many times.\n\nFor us, how we wish we saw those sights.\n\nBut guess what, here and now as New Testament believers we have also the opportunity of a lifetime... The Spirit of God lives in us for real, and our physical bodies are the temple that God dwells in.\n\nWow. Tell that to the people of old.\n\nThat there was coming a time God will dwell in man...\n\nThey could only imagine and wished they lived to experience that.\n\nI'm sure they wished and imagined how it will feel like for God to be inside you. Kabayaa. Kobeiala. Maroshka.. Mili hatraliski.\n\nGlory.","dt":"2024-05-10T07:48:59","s":["wasriq7col"]}],"21":[{"m":"What happens when the people of God fight an enemy stronger and more numerous than they?\n\nIs it that they suddenly gain supernatural strength like Samson and root out the enemies of God, or the people fight with natural strength but the angels of God are present to be doing damage themselves to God's enemies?\n\nWho, by the way, are God's enemies? The people who disobey the moral laws of God written on every human heart. Obviously not the rituals of GOD as it relates to ceremonial cleansing etc.","dt":"2026-03-25T17:19:17","s":["1pbqhyjzwm"]}]},"7":{"6":[{"m":"He lay down all day till evening 🌃, and at evening was when God spoke to him to get up.\n\nGod came in to him at his own time. I guess he would have laid there for two days if need be, so he could hear the Lord.\n\nAs believers we often think the folks of the Old Testament had God at their beck and call 🤙.\n\nWe don't read in between the lines to see that they really had to wait on the Lord before he spoke.\n\nThey just did not noise the process of waiting that much, but rather just mentioned it simply and moved to give us the details of the results, as we see in this case with Joshua.","dt":"2024-05-10T08:06:51","s":["bxs6czmwma"]}],"9":[{"m":"This invasion was a life and death issue. No wonder they lay before the ark all day. If they joked, they would be dead in no time.\n\nGod was turned to be their enemy in the matter of Achan, not that Ai had special gods who empowered them.\n\nI wonder, the thirty or so men killed, had they committed some sin per chance themselves, causing them to be selected for death? We are not told.\n\nIf I am to assume they were deserving of death because of some secret sin, then that shows men ought to exercise caution and repent.\n\nWhen all went well under the protection of God, all were protected, but the moment God was turned to be their enemies, the laws of justice select the most guilty and deserving of death. Not all men are the same.","dt":"2026-03-25T17:32:59","s":["ao2wg2l54k"]}],"13":[{"m":"Many things to say here.\n\nWhere do I start now.\n\nFirstly, Joshua was reprimanded for lying 🤥 down thus... Akin to Moses when he came crying 😢 to God and God told him to just go divide the Red Sea and stop the crying.\n\nHere it sounds like God was saying, 'No need to lie down thus and overreact.'\n\nYour people have committed a trespass. You should know this, why else would I. It be among you.\n\nVS 12 lets us know God had set a kind of law in motion, i.e.\n\nYou stay in covenant, you are impregnable and invincible. You transgress, you lose out, because I will not be with you.\n\nThe reason laws of nature and spirit exist and work almost automatically and inanimately is because there is a living, animate being behind it ensuring it works.\n\nIt's not all just erratic; there is intelligent 🧠 design ensuring the laws continue to function.\n\nInterestingly, God watched as Joshua strategized etc., showing there is the human aspect of the divine 🔮 will.\n\nThey train and do all they must and leave the giving of the victory ✌️ to God.","dt":"2022-03-26T08:03:09","s":["hsiucb8pgc"]}],"15":[{"m":"Wow, burnt alive 🔥, a human burnt offering.\n\nSounds cruel until you realize that 32 families had lost their fathers.\n\nThe perpetrator definitely cannot live.\n\nIt's strange and makes you ponder the things God allows to happen.\n\nThe pain of such loss. God could not interfere or forewarn Joshua that this is what Achan had done and thus this war they undertake will result in needless deaths.\n\nSame with Adam. Whom he had told the consequences and left man to decide.\n\nAnd man 👨 chose to dare break the law and let the chips fall where they may.\n\nHe had told Israel 🇮🇱 what the consequences of idolatry were and left them to choose.\n\nI SEE THAT WHEN GOD SPEAKS HE LEAVES MAN TO CHOOSE AND WOULD DO NOTHING TO STOP MAN.\n\nIs that how powerful we are, to determine our own life's course 🏇? Free will is a very dangerous power ☣.\n\nGod only comes in after we have made the choice.\n\nIT'S A LAW OF FREE WILL I SEE. God forewarns. Then steps back and man 👨 steps forward to CHOOSE.\n\nAfter man's choice, God steps forward to help restore or promote and complement man, depending on his choice.\n\nBut the consequences must be faced.\n\nI believe if Joshua had consulted with God rather than assume Ai was a small country, he would have gotten help 😣. He would have been forewarned.\n\nThus we ought to pray always.","dt":"2022-03-26T08:15:49","s":["v50vil6beg"]}],"26":[{"m":"God was appeased. Thirty-six men had died; their families had lost breadwinners because of this.\n\nAnd now he was to appease not just God but the families of the lost soldiers, and the blood of the soldiers with that of his own and his family 👪.\n\nNow God was appeased and turned his hot anger away.","dt":"2024-05-10T08:10:55","s":["6zxc8d38t0"]}],"24":[{"m":"Why involve his children 🧒?","dt":"2022-03-29T05:32:15","s":["8auoew4tm5"]}]},"8":{"1":[{"m":"Why was God's choice of numbers greater than that of Joshua?\n\nAi was a small city 🏙 and JOSHUA chose a handful of men to fight them.\n\nWhich he lost anyways.\n\nNow with God almighty on their side, I'm surprised he asked that all the men of war be taken.\n\nCould it mean that though Ai was a small city, their men were very swift and skilled in war??\n\nBecause in the next chapter it is recorded that when the other nations heard of the defeat of Jericho and Ai, they ganged up against Joshua.","dt":"2022-04-07T01:52:20","s":["ffv50bpnsz"]}],"19":[{"m":"So none of the Aians even looked back or sensed something behind them. No, the time of their destruction was come. They sensed nothing.","dt":"2022-03-29T05:38:59","s":["jdolrt7c4j"]}],"26":[{"m":"Just like when Moses held his hands 👐 up in the battle against Amalek.\n\nJoshua 8:26 NKJV\nFor Joshua did not draw back his hand, with which he stretched out the spear, until he had utterly destroyed all the inhabitants of Ai.","dt":"2024-05-11T06:47:25","s":["i1e3s8jrlh","87yiplsx32"]}],"29":[{"m":"What was his offense that he was given this unique treatment?\n\nIt was almost as if he was being shown to the Lord, to appease the wrath of God and show that the vengeance the Lord desired had been carried out.\n\nThe Lord was content now.\n\nJoshua 8:29 NKJV\nAnd the king of Ai he hanged on a tree until evening. And as soon as the sun was down, Joshua commanded that they should take his corpse down from the tree, cast it at the entrance of the gate of the city, and raise over it a great heap of stones that  remains to this day.","dt":"2024-05-11T07:20:39","s":["vpkhc3qj99","mrq2shf0ko"]}],"9":[{"m":"Is this not Bethel, the house of God where Jacob slept when escaping from Esau his brother?\n\nOh that his children would walk this same place in droves, battle ready to take the lands surrounding.\n\nWho would have thought 💭? - God.\n\nJoshua 8:9 NKJV\nJoshua therefore sent them out; and they went to lie in ambush, and stayed between Bethel and Ai, on the west side of Ai; but Joshua lodged that night among the people.","dt":"2024-05-11T06:36:17","s":["lqktrg7pf6","h48xkwt2i9"]}],"18":[{"m":"God was very active in the battles of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nHere Joshua likely heard an audible voice 💭 though there was no bodily presence.\n\nHe knew the voice of God enough to know it was the Lord.\n\nIt is likely that even this ambush strategy was from the Lord, and he might have told Joshua to wait till he, the Lord, had given him the signal to take the city by stretching forth his spear.\n\nAnd then at this moment the ambush will invade Ai and take the city 🏙. Ai will be destroyed just as Jericho was.\n\nAnd this Joshua did.\n\nJoshua 8:18 NKJV\nThen the Lord said to Joshua, “Stretch out the spear that is in your hand toward Ai, for I will give it into your hand.” And Joshua stretched out the spear that was in his hand toward the city.","dt":"2024-05-11T06:43:16","s":["c0qelhwdqm","t6dcfc2pgt"]}]},"9":{"1":[{"m":"What was there about Ai? It was a small city, so its defeat should not cause them to even bat an eye 👁‍🗨.\n\nBut two ✌️ possibilities.\n\n1. The devastation without mercy of the cities Israel fought means that was their modus operandi for warfare.\n\nThis left the people with no option than to unite and fight for their lives.\n\n2. Ai, though small, had such skills that even the other bigger nations avoided them. Probably they were like the honey 🍯 badger among nations.\n\nWe see this in their ability to defeat Israel the first time and in God requesting the entire army to go against them.\n\nJoshua 9:1 NKJV\nAnd it came to pass when all the kings who were on this side of the Jordan, in the hills and in the lowland and in all the coasts of the Great Sea toward Lebanon—the Hittite, the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite—heard about  it,","dt":"2024-05-11T07:32:32","s":["4k7xwt1jir","wfnadhsf4g"]}],"14":[{"m":"Constant enquiry from the Lord is the 🗝 to constant victory ✌️.\n\nI understand Joshua; some things were obvious, so he did not seek the Lord and sought to use his own understanding.","dt":"2022-04-07T01:56:12","s":["4sbvmfs2bo"]},{"m":"And the Lord also said nothing to intercept. Because he probably saw the heart of the people in repentance and genuine fear 😱 of the God of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nSo he accepted to spare them, hence his silence 🤫\n\nJoshua 9:14 NKJV\nThen the men of Israel took some of their provisions; but they did not ask counsel of the Lord.","dt":"2024-05-11T07:39:30","s":["4hqjr2aj61","gxy1mv8eyq"]},{"m":"The Lord said nothing, likely because he had mercy.\n\nBecause see how detailed he was in the matter of Achan, but was completely silent here. Later Joshua could not change their oath, because they swore on the name of the Lord.\n\nAn oath which King Saul would undo, much to the detriment of the people later.","dt":"2026-03-25T17:51:07","s":["n3ovmjz7qe"]}],"19":[{"m":"Back when words were bonds. Now we lie so much and are without honour.\n\nNo wonder we carry so little power and God does not honor our words with power and demonstrations.","dt":"2022-04-07T01:57:54","s":["4erixq0pk9"]}],"4":[{"m":"Same information, different responses.\n\nTo one, they amassed numbers for blind warfare. Blind in that they were going to this war to lose, yet did not even know that was a fact.\n\nThe Gibeonites looked at the strength 💪 of Egypt 🇪🇬 with its chariots, the dividing of the Red Sea 🌊, the breaking of walls by the hand of the God of Israel, and concluded that no confederacy would defeat Israel, whose God fought for them.\n\nJoshua 9:4 NKJV\nthey worked craftily, and went and pretended to be ambassadors. And they took old sacks on their donkeys, old wineskins torn and mended,","dt":"2024-05-11T07:29:00","s":["55wkuplrzp","b17922drjz"]}],"10":[{"m":"They spoke nothing of the current battle with Ai, because presumably word of it was yet to travel to their 'far off country'.\n\nJoshua 9:10 NKJV\nand all that He did to the two kings of the Amorites who were beyond the Jordan—to Sihon king of Heshbon, and Og king of Bashan, who was at Ashtaroth.","dt":"2024-05-11T07:37:39","s":["f5ktud9qpt","fx3kvhlui9"]}],"24":[{"m":"So my reasoning was right... In fact, the people of the land knew full well the mission of Israel... It was no secret nor clandestine.\n\nBut if they knew the instructions of the war, then they knew why God gave such a harsh command.\n\nBecause of their wickedness and worship of devils 👿 and human sacrifice of their babies 🤱.\n\nYet they would not repent nor convert to the God of Israel.\n\nThey loved their wicked ways too much to change.\n\nBut the Gibeonites were wise men; no wonder the Lord spared them.\n\nThey came to reckon that it was better to be servants of the God of Israel, who visibly dwelt with his people, and to repent and defect to the God of Israel than continue to serve these dumb idols.\n\nSmart 🧠 nation they were 👌.\n\nJoshua 9:24 NKJV\nSo they answered Joshua and said, “Because your servants were clearly told that the Lord your God commanded His servant Moses to give you all the land, and to destroy all the inhabitants of the land from before you; therefore we were very much afraid for our lives because of you, and have done this thing.","dt":"2024-05-11T07:46:13","s":["erzegol05a","sux5pma6ml"]}]},"10":{"12":[{"m":"This was a great moment for the Lord to kill several kings at once in a single battle, and the Lord through JOSHUA made the most of the opportunity — I mean, from hailstones, which I can see the angel of God hurling at the people, killing more people that way than by sword, and now to the sun staying still by a full day.\n\nSo victory is wrought completely.","dt":"2026-03-25T17:59:54","s":["h2f0zlk449"]}],"27":[{"m":"This was a testament to the surrounding nations also, that the kings 👑 whom they trusted were shamefully hanged by this Joshua — the Great commander of Israel.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:27:52","s":["nu94nusxl3"]}],"32":[{"m":"Likely a fenced 🤺 city, considering the wording used.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:29:06","s":["ba2z2qcitr"]}],"37":[{"m":"The united kingdoms had lost to him and now he went city by city 🏙 to finish them off completely.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:30:30","s":["0bggolvult"]},{"m":"Looks like Hebron had instated a new king, or maybe it was in reference to the first king who was killed and hanged, or again it may refer to a different city in Hebron with its own king, different from the one Joshua had killed earlier in the cave.","dt":"2026-03-25T18:03:55","s":["x792v3w4dg"]}],"41":[{"m":"God of strategy, this was a four hundred 💯 year strategy now coming to fruition.\n\nMen had fully surrendered to God and he dwelt with them, even as these men also met all the requirements for God to continue to be in their midst.\n\nThe devil 👿 had had a field day, having set up his kingdom 👑 among the heathen centuries prior.\n\nAnd now the kingdom of God was set up and executing God's agenda.\n\nFast forward to now and the world 🗺 lies in rebellion, Christianity is not in full alignment and our ranks have been broken through.\n\nWe are not fully yielded, neither have we set up our altars nor followed the rituals and precepts of our God.\n\nThus God's full will and power is not seen. We see here and there the hand of the Lord, but not his full might.\n\nWe cry 😢 for power and revival, yet we see it not, because we are not ready; we have not repaired our altars nor prepared our hearts 💕 ready for God to fully have his way.\n\nOh Lord, help 😣 us and make us who you want us to be.\n\nOh that God would find men, men in our generation and the generations to come, who would wield power, the power of the Ancient One.\n\nI see Elijah the Tishbite, who popped out of nowhere, now in the heavens.\n\nAnd how would this Elijah come back to the earth 🌎?\n\nI don't see him descending, but just like in the ancient times, this Elijah who just surfaced out of nowhere would again surface out of nowhere.\n\nOnce more Elijah the Tishbite would walk amongst us.\n\nBut why does Elijah the Tishbite have to come back? Would there not be men in the times to come who would be able to wield such power?\n\nMaybe, maybe not... Oh Lord God, have mercy, raise men, we pray, raise men 😭😭","dt":"2024-05-11T08:42:28","s":["7xqf16d6om"]},{"m":"Kadesh Barnea... They had been here for years... Having to wander about in a land that they could have possessed ages ago.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:49:30","s":["5n1dfz57bo"]}]},"11":{"5":[{"m":"Inasmuch as Joshua was literally having automatic guaranteed victories, he waited on the Lord for each battle, because we keep hearing the instructions of the Lord battle after battle.\n\nHere again the Lord speaks after these kings had gathered against them.\n\nObviously Joshua had enquired of the LORD.","dt":"2026-03-25T18:06:16","s":["ulw7l48y3b"]}],"6":[{"m":"Why didn't the Lord make them take it?\n\nTo ensure their continuous dependence on him, likely, and prevent them from multiplying horses 🏇... A thing he had warned them about.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:52:52","s":["5n7ehf0qta"]},{"m":"DID the Lord not like horses and chariots? Or it was to make Israel constantly depend on him for victory rather than weapons of war.","dt":"2026-03-25T18:07:14","s":["3aov4poxbb"]}],"21":[{"m":"Why separate Judah and Israel? It seems this writer lived in the times of the divided kingdom, or maybe later copyists did the at summary of an insertion.","dt":"2024-05-11T09:02:14","s":["zbersredfz"]},{"m":"All the mountains of Israel and all the mountains of Judah — it seems that the person writing this history lived in the times when Israel and Judah had already taken these nations and named them after their nation.\n\nIndeed, the writer of Joshua at this point, or at this part, mentions Judah and Israel as separate nations, meaning the nation was already divided at the time: the line of David and that of the other tribes.","dt":"2026-03-25T18:11:49","s":["r0zewpfvmp"]}],"20":[{"m":"Ahaa... I thought 💭 so... I wondered why they just did not repent, cast away their gods and defect in submission to the God of Israel.\n\nEspecially as their gods had proven incompetent against Israel.\n\nBut alas, the Lord hardened their hearts to their own hurt.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:57:16","s":["s47e8szncv"]},{"m":"They had grown beyond favour and did not deserve it, so God took even the thought 💭 of it from them, lest they gain undeserved favour.","dt":"2024-05-11T08:58:27","s":["vstr0v8229"]}],"22":[{"m":"And from Gath came Goliath of the giants.\n\nIf only they had finished the work centuries before.","dt":"2024-05-11T09:03:03","s":["3swe3t1eqe"]}]},"13":{"14":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔. Is this a comparable inheritance — vast lands as compared to the sacrifice of the Lord by fire 🔥?\n\nThe vast lands will produce the sacrifice of the Lord. A tenth of which is given directly to the priests.","dt":"2022-04-12T13:51:11","s":["x65b9f6a7h"]}],"22":[{"m":"Balaam was a soothsayer... Why was he called such...? Meanwhile, his dealings were with God, though his heart was not right.\n\nI guess because he knew God and how to have access to him, but he traded with his gift 📦.\n\nHe was no man of God though, and obviously he did not consult other gods, but his motives were not right.","dt":"2024-05-13T07:12:11","s":["cvzo0h7bv5"]}],"6":[{"m":"Ei, God was already sharing the property before the time ⌚... Before the Israelites even took possession of it.\n\nHmm 🤔 this tells us something about God and his modus operandi and his way of thinking.","dt":"2022-04-12T13:13:49","s":["mi3f1dxp17"]}],"9":[{"m":"They kept such detailed records — they were indeed building a kingdom to last, so that generations born after will know what is due them, so they can fight for it.","dt":"2026-03-25T23:03:51","s":["h6tbq20g0k"]}],"28":[{"m":"These records have been there even to now, so over 4000 years, and the children of Israel know each their own inheritance and can divide the promised land among themselves without dispute to this day.\n\nThis is a lesson for us all in preserving posterity.","dt":"2024-05-13T07:15:15","s":["89yhtu982e"]}]},"14":{"4":[{"m":"🤔 🤔 🤔...\n\nIs that the reason... That there need be 12 tribes, not 13.\n\nJoseph was two tribes, so one tribe had to be disinherited, and by divine agreement Levi was dispossessed of their inheritance but given another inheritance, arguably better than land.\n\nCould it be that in the selling of Joseph, Levi was a key mastermind — well, just conjecture.\n\nThe tribe of Joseph getting 2 portions was Jacob's choice, and that messed around a bit with God's 12 tribes agenda.\n\nBut he found his way around it, being God.","dt":"2022-04-12T14:00:36","s":["sgxwtcld4s"]}],"12":[{"m":"Caleb was given no easy grounds.\n\nHis faith was great, and thus he was given the tough task of conquering the feared 😨 land of the giants.\n\nWhich he gladly embraced. Very much like him.","dt":"2024-05-13T07:28:50","s":["xfegjlh7xw"]}]},"15":{"26":[{"m":"How did they know all these places, considering that they had not conquered yet?\nWas it by revelation, or they sent surveyors around to map the land?","dt":"2024-05-13T07:46:14","s":["5wsfzzpkhd"]}]},"17":{"18":[{"m":"The blessings of God were in the people; all they needed to do was activate their faith in the word and covenant of the Lord.\n\nAnd they would be victorious. This goes to show that the Lord can give a word or a blessing, but it can lie dormant because there is no man to lay hold of the promise.","dt":"2024-05-13T08:26:42","s":["r49uuxy50h"]}],"15":[{"m":"I am sensing some sarcasm in Joshua's voice and tone. No one wanted the wood country because it was a tough one to claim, but that was their lot to take according to Joshua, and he would not budge when they asked for an easier allotment.","dt":"2026-03-26T20:17:53","s":["etgy3j6nv9"]}]},"18":{"4":[{"m":"Okay, so surveyors of a sort were sent out to map the land.","dt":"2024-05-13T08:28:32","s":["amnmmmnyw9"]}],"9":[{"m":"In a book, that is interesting to note.","dt":"2022-04-13T12:17:03","s":["9uel2ol39w"]}],"10":[{"m":"It was done before the Lord, the Lord witnessed to it, and thus the land was theirs for the taking, for the divine hand of the Lord was upon them.","dt":"2026-03-26T20:20:48","s":["xu8o5dhzf7"]}],"7":[{"m":"So the Levites, for their loss, do not go to war to possess land.\n\nThey go to war as priests carrying the ark and presence of God. There is still risk in that, though, but not the same as those on the frontlines.","dt":"2024-05-13T08:30:19","s":["hobdcxjtmt"]}]},"22":{"10":[{"m":"Firstly, how were they going to cross it? It was not going to be by a miracle. So they likely went at a time the river was low and the current better, and anyways these were men of war, so they could cross over, unlike before, where little ones were involved.","dt":"2026-03-29T05:26:10","s":["md4newtbl2"]}],"12":[{"m":"I mean, without consulting or investigating further, they went to war. It was because at this time they knew the hot anger of the LORD and were not going to take chances.\n\nThey prepared for war so the Lord knows their heart and sees their action, that they stand with him. After this act they now go and enquire, just in case, but were also ready for battle should their worst fears be confirmed.\n\nSecondly, I wonder, why would Israel somehow believe that their brethren, whom they had fought together with and had seen the hand of the Lord, all so suddenly convert and change to another god?\n\nIt was because historically they were known to be quick to worship another god, especially remembering the issue of the golden calf in Sinai.\n\nSo though not likely, yet possible. Totally possible, you can never tell these things.","dt":"2026-03-29T05:30:56","s":["wakeq2z1w4"]}],"20":[{"m":"Ah, this was one of the main reasons. In the matter of Achan, he perished not alone, though he committed the crime alone. Others innocently died because of him.\n\nGod was really hard on them, so now they looked out for each other and for any wrong amongst them. They kept eyes on any defaulters so they save their lives. Knowing very well that if the Lord should come in, he will deal with the negligence of the other camp members in allowing one of their own to go unpunished for their sins.\n\nThe question, however, remains that God did not continue such strict dealing with ISRAEL — he left them at a point as if to see if they would wholly follow him, and they did not after that generation which saw all these wonders passed.\n\nMaybe that was why God was so strict on them. They saw too much and thus had little excuse. Their children only heard stories. Look at, for instance, Gideon — who asked where God was, whom their fathers had told so much about to them.","dt":"2026-03-29T05:37:15","s":["cxsfxevz48"]}],"18":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... The Lord expected collective responsibility from the nation.\n\nIf they saw someone breaking the laws of God, they were to deal with it, lest they risked the Lord being angry 😡 with all of them and dealing with them collectively, not just with the individuals.\n\nBecause by being silent 😶, they have condoned the wrong.","dt":"2024-05-14T08:55:26","s":["gkxq2wj6wr"]}],"33":[{"m":"I can imagine the children of Israel on this side Jordan ☺ smiling and possibly teasing the other 3 tribes that they indeed did not want any trouble with the Lord in the future 🔮.\n\nKnowing how things could turn out in life.\n\nSmart decision to preserve their lot with a memorial altar.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:03:25","s":["zg479hupvs"]}]},"24":{"19":[{"m":"Ei, interesting...\nTimes and seasons indeed change.\n\nThere was a time when a people, in fact his own people, were counselled not to choose him because he doesn't forgive and is jealous, but the people insisted, seeing how blessed this jealous God had made them.\n\nBut now in our time we have been marketed the God that not only forgives sins, but has already forgiven any future sins.\n\nAnd the results: absurdities in the body of Christ.\n\nI understand the reasoning behind such teachings, so people do not walk in so much guilt they refuse to come to the Lord.\n\nIndeed the word lets us know our sins were nailed in the cross.\n\nBut human nature has resulted in excesses and error.\n\nStrange what time reveals.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:32:54","s":["axqoohun79"]}],"25":[{"m":"The number of covenants which were cut, and the number of symbolism, including mountains and stones set up, just so Israel sees and stays true to the Lord.\n\nIt was like their leaders were doing all that was humanly possible so the people and their generations do not forget or get deceived in the future.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:35:53","s":["jbkqnv2llw"]}],"29":[{"m":"Where are the people of Israel 🇮🇱 now... From the little research I did, they have very much preserved their uniqueness as Jews.\n\nThough they have rejected the Messiah.","dt":"2022-04-14T02:03:15","s":["ch4zdgkabn"]},{"m":"So he lived thirty more years in the promised land.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:42:22","s":["jgw2k7upn4"]}],"2":[{"m":"Every Israelite knew their history on their fingertips. Even I, who am not, do know their history.\n\nThis every family should emulate.\n\nOther versions describe the other side of the flood as the river Euphrates.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:22:58","s":["vwe9onakdh"]}],"12":[{"m":"Some versions replace hornet with terror 😰.\n\nSo the Lord sent the fear or terror of Israel 🇮🇱 ahead of their battles to drive the people away, even before Israel drew any sword ⚔ or drew a bow.\n\nJoshua 24:12 AMP\nI sent the hornet [that is, the terror of you] before you, which drove the two kings of the Amorites out before you; but it was not by your sword or by your bow.","dt":"2024-05-14T09:27:38","s":["fdbrxlr4zg"]}],"23":[{"m":"They still carried strange gods with them? Well, it is possible; after all, they were 2 million people, so some few might rebel secretly.","dt":"2026-03-29T06:07:25","s":["o1xfogplf6"]}]},"1":{"8":[{"m":"This verse shows the part of God and the part of man.\n\nJoshua had to be bold\nJoshua had to be courageous\nJoshua had to read and memorize the law\n\nHe was to ensure the law was almost literally on his lips. This would involve careful and deliberate study, and putting in place things to help him remember.\n\nOnce he fulfilled his part, God's ability would give him victory always.\n\nWe are in partnership with God, and there are things only we can do that no spirit will do for us, lest our will is circumvented.\n\nLest we be rendered humanless.\n\nSo our part we must play for the supernatural to work.","dt":"2024-05-09T16:49:12","s":["up4asyyur7"]}],"18":[{"m":"Wow, time changes things. Barely a generation ago, 38 years, and their parents feared 😱, and even with encouragement from the great god-man Moses himself, they could barely be restrained from returning to Egypt.\n\nAnd now here stood their children, ready to take the promised land, and so geared up were they that they rather encouraged Joshua to be strong 💪 and courageous.\n\nA lot can change in just a few decades, and that is what we see in our world 🗺 now with the whole anti-God agenda.\n\nWe have moved from a society that feared God to a godless society.\n\nHmm... Amazing","dt":"2024-05-09T16:44:46","s":["kutf7t6gqi"]}]},"21":{"45":[{"m":"I thought 💭 the children of Israel did not possess all their inheritance as the Lord had commanded.\n\nUnless this verse sought to reveal the perspective from the mind of God.\n\nBecause indeed the Lord had caused all he said to pass. Including giving them all the land he had mentioned.\n\nTheir failure to drive out the inhabitants of the land was based on their appetite or lack thereof.\n\nIn some instances it was said that the children of Israel did not drive the people out completely, but rather allowed them to dwell with them under tribute.\n\nThis was not failure on the part of God; he, God, has done his part.\n\nIt was failure from Israel to not lay hold of that which the Lord had given him.\n\nAnd this happens even now, where God gives us many things but we fail to do our human part to make it a reality.\n\nGod help us.","dt":"2024-05-14T08:41:28","s":["vrayqdh96c"]}]}},"Lamentations":{"1":{"9":[{"m":"Her filthiness is in her skirts? What's the meaning?","dt":"2022-08-26T06:52:20","s":["ke3m9fvfv8"]}],"10":[{"m":"The heathen were not even to enter into the congregation, the gathering of the Lord's people before him, yet they have done worse things, by going beyond the congregation and entering the sanctuary of the Lord.\n\nAn abomination unimaginable.","dt":"2026-09-08T10:44:10.482Z","s":["471gwno56x"]}]},"2":{"4":[{"m":"God poured out his fury like 🔥 fire, and like fire 🔥 it touches everything.","dt":"2022-08-26T06:56:36","s":["tfy4ss91f8"]}],"14":[{"m":"Sad 😔, real sad 😔... When the people to see and hear from God lead the people on in their sins.","dt":"2022-08-26T06:59:44","s":["bu4e8ppee0"]}],"15":[{"m":"The perfection of beauty, the joy of the world 🗺","dt":"2022-08-26T07:00:46","s":["qgm9n90xcd"]}],"19":[{"m":"The 🌃 night watch begins at 6 pm.","dt":"2022-08-26T07:07:36","s":["ju5r5k11h1"]}],"20":[{"m":"They ate their own children, and that a span long — barely a few days or weeks.","dt":"2026-09-09T10:20:50.075Z","s":["6cohfgielf"]}]},"3":{"14":[{"m":"Very common practice amongst us here.\n\nWhere you sing specific songs in mockery of someone's predicament or to communicate something specific.","dt":"2024-10-31T07:14:43","s":["i7m6iualmv"]}],"23":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... So it is in this condition that this statement was made.\n\nIt was not in a state of prosperity... They were really in a very bad place.\n\nAnd they dug around for any glimpse of hope.\n\nAnd finally could clutch at something: that it was because of his mercy that they were even alive in the 👾 first place.","dt":"2022-08-27T14:21:12","s":["gkokp122rp"]}],"22":[{"m":"Verse 22 is a popular verse in Christian circles, but it ought to be read by first reading 21.\n\nThe writer 📝 is talking of the pain and afflictions from the Lord.\n\nAs he laments and moans, he then remembers that because of God's mercy, Israel, though chastised, are not consumed...\n\nThat is to say, they are not utterly destroyed... A remnant was still left behind by the Lord because of his mercies.","dt":"2024-10-31T07:18:13","s":["66et6dpzqj"]}]},"4":{"13":[{"m":"See the calibre of people who did such evil 😈.\n\nNot the ordinary people, not just any leader or person in power.\n\nBut the prophets and priests.\n\nWhat went wrong?\n\nHow did such people get access to the holy office 🏢?\n\nSo every high office must be protected.\n\nProtected from unfit men, from occupying such.\n\nHow else could such cruelty have occupied such office, if not for lack of checks to prevent such?\n\nIn all we do, we must bear in mind that there is an adversary.","dt":"2022-08-27T14:03:20","s":["yt8vmo1n5z"]}],"22":[{"m":"Thus Jacob's woes are ended, and that of Edom begins.","dt":"2022-08-27T14:06:02","s":["1szvtf4tju"]}],"9":[{"m":"Such painful scenes","dt":"2022-08-27T14:01:13","s":["a00u6g32uh"]}]},"5":{"4":[{"m":"Is this not the story of Africa 🌍?","dt":"2022-08-27T13:57:50","s":["op78qs7hay"]}]}},"Ezekiel":{"2":{"3":[{"m":"This reminds me of my call... I am sent out to teach the nations.\n\nIt is easy not to heed, even after knowing in your heart of hearts that you've had encounters with God.\n\nBecause life happens to you, and the challenges of it.\n\nBut after encounters, deep in your heart you know.\n\nIt is important you heed, lest it fades out of your heart ♥ or it tortures your mind.","dt":"2022-08-30T06:41:13","s":["hmfdji6s46"]}]},"3":{"15":[{"m":"Does that mean this experience was in the body, or it only felt that way?","dt":"2022-08-30T07:03:06","s":["jn1h2jyia8"]}],"22":[{"m":"But why could the Lord not just speak to him where he was?\n\nLikely because of what the Lord wanted him to see, and the picture the Lord wanted to have imprinted in his mind.","dt":"2024-11-02T09:45:11","s":["anmyzc0vp4"]},{"m":"I don't get this about GOD... Why can't he speak to his people and prophets where they are, but sometimes he requires them to move to a location to hear him?\n\nIndeed, it obviously is not from his inability to speak, because he actually speaks to his people to move from where they are to where he wants them to be, in order to hear something else.\n\nThis our GOD.","dt":"2026-09-09T17:04:24.558Z","s":["i4frcq6t04"]}],"12":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-08-30T06:54:31","s":["76ce913f77"]}]},"4":{"17":[{"m":"Ezekiel's prophecies were very symbolic, both private prophecies, like how he was to lie down for over a year on one side, and how he was to lie down on the opposite side for the next forty days.","dt":"2024-11-02T09:53:07","s":["tq9taz3lr1"]}],"5":[{"m":"390 years — some search suggests this is the total number of years from the rebellion of Solomon to when Israel went into captivity, and the next verse captures 40 years of the final days of Judah before they went into captivity.\n\nAll of it totalling 430 years, equivalent to the 430 years in bondage in Egypt.\n\nBut for the prophet and priest Ezekiel to go through such agony, well, I don't know, but the imagery of the prophet lying on his side perpetually in the eyes of the people who were in exile was very strong.","dt":"2026-09-10T09:59:34.455Z","s":["3f54zh29dk"]}],"3":[{"m":"So all the while that the remnant of the people not taken captive were in the land, minding their own business and living their lives, though wicked and Godless,\n\nall the while Ezekiel was more or less enchanting against them.\n\nHe had made a physical representation of their gates and walls and was speaking words against the city for its captivity.\n\nLike he was pronouncing spells and curses more or less against them.\n\nThis is very interesting.","dt":"2024-11-02T09:49:11","s":["7yj2tnjc1w"]}],"10":[{"m":"I checked, and this was like taking 6 to 8 slices of bread a day as your food, and the water was just about 3 glasses of water a day.\n\nTo have this as your food and water in the Middle Eastern dry conditions was really extreme.","dt":"2026-09-10T10:01:49.069Z","s":["xha5vwzbvf"]}]},"6":{"4":[{"m":"The mountains of Israel 🇮🇱 were addressed as if animate, or were they?","dt":"2022-08-30T10:17:08","s":["7cb38w1ato"]}],"9":[{"m":"The language of whoredom is used here for idolatry.\n\nBecause that is how God sees and feels about it.","dt":"2022-08-30T10:20:43","s":["i27gjlkkvu"]}],"13":[{"m":"Could it be that in the time of their destruction they will run to their idols and shrines for salvation, but there will be none?\n\nTheir idols will be powerless to save in that day, and so they will be killed and slain before these dumb idols whom the Lord had long warned them about.","dt":"2024-11-02T10:14:46","s":["1ege5afrwm"]},{"m":"They were round about their altars at the time of their death because they likely sought after those idols to deliver them in the time of their war. They clung to their idols unto death.\n\nAnd their idols could not deliver them. They died literally in their iniquity, bowing one more time before their altars. Even in death they sin.","dt":"2026-09-10T10:14:05.719Z","s":["hec2vlvipn"]}]},"7":{"3":[{"m":"God had been forewarning his people all these decades and even centuries,\n\nbut alas, now was the time ⌚.\n\nNow God had attached 📎 a time-line to the whole event.\n\nJust like Abraham's promise of a child 🧒, when the time was due he was given the time-line, according to the time of life.\n\nThis is what the faithful walk is all about, trusting his promises whiles awaiting their manifestation.","dt":"2022-08-31T06:34:36","s":["p1wgq2pkrt"]},{"m":"Are these not the words of the book which he ate... of woes and abominations?\n\nEzekiel 2:10 KJV\nAnd he spread it before me; and it was written within and without: and there was written therein lamentations, and mourning, and woe.\n\nEzekiel 3:1 KJV\nMoreover he said unto me, Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, and go speak unto the house of Israel.","dt":"2024-11-02T10:06:15","s":["kzvs6vkt7o"]}],"20":[{"m":"These idols are carried into battle to offer protection.","dt":"2022-08-30T10:27:21","s":["sp9y4xxnt3"]}],"27":[{"m":"All of these were for one purpose, that they may know that I am the Lord.","dt":"2022-08-31T06:38:05","s":["t0dhpf1z9t"]}],"26":[{"m":"At this point they shall seek the vision they refused when it abounded, and the law of the Lord, but it shall be to no avail.\n\nIt says the law will perish from the priest because they will be taken into captivity and some destroyed.","dt":"2024-11-02T10:13:13","s":["5ix70mdyan"]}]},"8":{"3":[{"m":"What a perspective: from above, God saw this image 🖼 of jealousy.\n\nHe needed Ezekiel to see from his perspective. How that this image of idolatry was constantly before him.\n\nI can imagine the pain; idolatry is adultery to God.\n\nSuch a painful imagery, it's like a man who has to constantly behold his wife's unfaithfulness constantly and yet not be able to do anything about it.\n\nHe, he cannot divorce her, and she also will not change.","dt":"2022-08-31T06:45:17","s":["2pkjeltojl"]},{"m":"This is the image of God he had seen earlier; God had a form of an 🖐️ hand.\n\nBecause of the radiance and brightness, one could not distinctly see what was seen, but could see forms and shapes.","dt":"2024-11-02T10:18:37","s":["m7759bp21j"]}],"12":[{"m":"I ask, why would they do such wickedness?\n\nAnd their reasoning is that the Lord had forsaken them.\n\nIs that not often our own reasoning? When we need help and God does not answer immediately.\n\nWe conclude he is far off. But God is the ancient one of the universe and has his perfect 👌 plan for us.\n\nAlso, these idols and gods might have provided some quick relief 😌.\n\nThere was some deception 😞 that these gods provided that might have made, and makes, those who serve them to prefer them to God Almighty.\n\nIndeed, such gods indulge our flesh and evil 😈 but natural inclination.\n\nThey have no laws against sexual sins and sins in general. Indeed, they encourage such.\n\nSo fleshly, and so man easily falls for them...\n\nSad 😔","dt":"2022-08-31T06:52:42","s":["frjwzs5ika"]}],"18":[{"m":"The Lord is right and justified in this his sentence.\n\nPut the branch 🌿 to the nose 👃 reminds me of Paul kicking against the pricks / goads... Can you imagine that?","dt":"2022-08-31T06:54:33","s":["bh5lgk6ngl"]}]},"9":{"4":[{"m":"Oh good God, you are the one who grants exemption.\n\nLord, exempt your children 🧒","dt":"2022-08-31T06:58:03","s":["t92kao1qu8"]}],"6":[{"m":"Is this not what Peter said, that judgement shall begin in the house of the Lord?","dt":"2024-11-04T18:14:41","s":["lyeilyztqf"]}],"9":[{"m":"Oh Lord, my God!\n\nBecause they concluded in their hearts 💕 that he sees not, he punishes every single sin to show that he sees.\n\nGOD HAS an interesting way of teaching lessons and revenging.\n\nThere is a place where he says that because they have shed blood, he is giving them blood to drink 🍻","dt":"2022-08-31T07:05:08","s":["o5bzs7bf06"]},{"m":"It seems the Lord detests it when men say he does not see and he is dormant.\n\nIt enrages him, it seems, when his longsuffering and mercy are misjudged as absence and impotence.","dt":"2024-11-04T18:28:10","s":["sod7nz568o"]}]},"10":{"2":[{"m":"Oh OK, so the descriptions of some versions are more accurate than others.\n\nThe coals of fire were between the cherubs; some versions, in describing the cherubs in chapter one, do not describe the coals, whiles others do.","dt":"2022-08-31T07:07:15","s":["tb2ei6g5lr"]}]},"11":{"5":[{"m":"Is this falling of the Spirit of the Lord upon him the same as when one senses the presence of the Lord, or maybe it is the same but in a much stronger way, as if the Spirit has literally fallen on you?\n\nA similar wording is used in the Acts of the Apostles, that the Spirit fell upon the disciples... Example: when they preached to the household of Cornelius, it is said that the Spirit fell on them.\n\nSo it is not just sensing the Spirit, but a weight literally of the Spirit on you, as described here.","dt":"2024-11-06T09:06:48","s":["gpnb0m8a9g"]}],"20":[{"m":"Amen... A heart of flesh we need.","dt":"2022-08-31T07:31:08","s":["vwuti8ypty"]}],"22":[{"m":"They are still here.","dt":"2022-08-31T07:30:28","s":["ds3ufg7da9"]}],"24":[{"m":"Wow","dt":"2022-08-31T07:29:51","s":["a54b269008"]}]},"12":{"3":[{"m":"Hmmm 🤔 God did communicate with his people in all possible ways to get them to change on their own accord, but they failed to.","dt":"2022-08-31T07:37:31","s":["dz0irvkzpr"]}],"12":[{"m":"Dig through the wall because the gates are fallen in, and walls broken through.","dt":"2022-08-31T07:34:14","s":["si3t2urqzh"]}],"25":[{"m":"Because of the long suffering of the Lord they say thus.\n\nIt is like the Lord's coming; they say if he would have come, he should have come a long time ago.","dt":"2022-08-31T07:36:05","s":["1hn0efphki"]}],"28":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-08-31T07:47:39","s":["cfc03a46d7"]},{"m":"When the time of GOD's word is not due, the word of the Lord seems like delay. Indeed, it becomes a byword and a reproach.\n\nHowever, when the time is due, it takes the people unaware. And so shall it be in the end of time at the coming of our Lord.\n\nMany say now that the coming of the Lord delays; indeed, there have been many false waitings for the coming of the Lord, but it never happened.","dt":"2026-09-14T10:45:31.492Z","s":["5zggiztokr"]}],"6":[{"m":"Would he not then stumble if he was not to see the ground? What was the purpose of this instruction? The purpose is explained in later verses.\n\nBut literally, Ezekiel was depicting Zedekiah's capture and plucking of eyes. He left the city not seeing anything, because his eyes were plucked out.","dt":"2026-09-14T10:40:08.306Z","s":["wt9mphzill"]}]},"13":{"9":[{"m":"Unlike more genuine prophets, whose writings are held sacred by Israel, these prophets would not be remembered nor go down in the annals of history.","dt":"2024-11-06T09:59:51","s":["sv41ikoqew"]}],"18":[{"m":"Other translations bring out the meaning clearer, that those were magic 🧝‍♂️ kerchiefs and veils for protection and ensnarement.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:40:26","s":["etydmo9bl2"]}],"22":[{"m":"The righteous were made sad because there was no end in sight for the wickedness that was going on daily in the land...\n\nAnd for the wicked, they were assured of no punishment for their ill ways, so they continued.","dt":"2024-11-06T10:03:52","s":["yg6etkd55m"]}],"23":[{"m":"Such wickedness.\n\nThere are very few things as bad as condemning the righteous and acquitting the wicked.\n\nAnd the practice of such magic charms killed and ensnared the whole nation.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:41:59","s":["o89cj6ohnj"]}],"17":[{"m":"GOD says he had not sent them. This should seem obvious, considering that these people were sewing charms and selling their prophecies for gain.\n\nObviously there was no need for GOD to say they prophesy lies, but he had to because they had come in the name of the Lord.\n\nBut their ways and methods alone should have spoken the obvious, that of course GOD has not sanctioned such. But that was not to be; they claim to be GOD-sent.\n\nWe see the same things in our world today, but the rule is, if the methods are not the methods of GOD, we should not be deceived by the words.\n\nThe words also are not the words of GOD.","dt":"2026-09-14T10:59:17.795Z","s":["p6tv68hk0k"]}],"8":[{"m":"Meaning it was their fault they saw lies 🤥. Here Daddy is not denying they saw something; however, he is against them.\n\nBut it has more to do with the state of their hearts 💕.\n\nSo perverse that it opened up for wrong vision.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:32:25","s":["begwbfr1a3"]}]},"14":{"10":[{"m":"No more pardon 🙏, God seems to be saying.\n\nYou prophesy lies 🤥, you are a goner.\n\nYou that go to and listen 👂 to false prophets will likewise be punished.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:47:01","s":["fphtwcn44x"]}],"14":[{"m":"This lets us in on the nature and character of these men.\n\nEspecially of Noah, that they were righteous and were intercessors.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:48:17","s":["euaipv88um"]}],"18":[{"m":"This is quite 🤫 instructive. NOAH was able to save his family 👪, Job prayed for them and sacrificed on their behalf, and Daniel interceded for an entire nation.\n\nBut in this case, things were so bad not even these great intercessors can stand in the gap.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:50:02","s":["f5tlom0r4p"]}],"21":[{"m":"Okay 👌, so we get a peep at God's four sore judgements.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:51:20","s":["5br1v5nhoh"]}],"23":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 so the character of the remnant would be so pure and just that God's wrath in destroying the wicked will be shown.\n\nTo the end that the righteous shall be shown forth as truly righteous, and the remnant shall be refined, having learnt the lesson of the end game of disobedience towards God.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:53:27","s":["0o4kv8zkmp"]}],"13":[{"m":"Which land? Was it referencing the land of Israel only, or is this GOD's judgement on all lands occupied by men?\n\nGOD is judge of all the earth, and as we have seen, he pours his fury on all men. Yes, God's covenant is with Israel, so he keeps his eyes on them perpetually, but he is the creator of the earth, and his judgement touches all men, for he is the father of all flesh.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:16:58.141Z","s":["48h210zwt8"]}],"8":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. The days of God's longsuffering were coming to an end.\n\nHe was going to answer the people that have idols, yet come and enquire of the Lord, by destroying them.\n\nAs a lesson.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:45:30","s":["q39i7j4r5t"]}],"20":[{"m":"Lord, have mercy. This goes to show the extent of wickedness in the land. No amount of intercession was going to deliver the land. All wicked will be punished, and that accordingly.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:27:06.810Z","s":["vupxtfk4x9"]}]},"16":{"14":[{"m":"Perfect because of the handiwork of the Lord to us-ward.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:57:00","s":["zgy57zmgqb"]}],"15":[{"m":"I can imagine the pain. And for a culture given to betrothal, they very much understood God's allegory.","dt":"2022-08-31T17:58:16","s":["z072xjret9"]}],"33":[{"m":"Such a sad 😔 & utterly despicable.","dt":"2022-08-31T18:02:01","s":["orl3offic5"]}],"44":[{"m":"Meaning what? Was that the practice and end of the Hittites?","dt":"2022-08-31T18:05:38","s":["zy3dzlcgp9"]},{"m":"Interesting proverb, didn't know this was in scripture.","dt":"2024-11-06T10:31:07","s":["8l808uaopk"]}],"50":[{"m":"So here again we see in depth the whoredom and other sins of Sodom.","dt":"2022-08-31T18:06:58","s":["7bc2eszoem"]}],"51":[{"m":"God judged Sodom and Samaria terribly for their sins, only for Judah to commit twice, and now it seems the punishment against Sodom and Samaria was unjust, or at least overdone.\n\nWho would have thought that a nation could do worse than these?","dt":"2024-11-06T10:33:00","s":["aee6vkpqz7"]}],"52":[{"m":"Though wicked, yet in comparison to Israel they were righteous.\n\nThat should go to show the extent and degree of depravity that Israel had sunk into.\n\nI mean, for Samaria of Ahab to be described as more righteous, that should tell you how bad the situation was.\n\nYet because Israel was his firstborn son, and here his wife, her punishment was less grievous than her sisters', in that she was spared a remnant and preserved a nation forever before the Lord. That there will always be the nation of Israel for Abraham's sake, and they will not lack a king to sit on the throne of Israel before the Lord for David's sake.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:50:13.979Z","s":["vrgzz4rgzx"]}],"31":[{"m":"At least a harlot gets paid for their services, but an adulterous woman? She gives of the best of herself for free and disdains the house she has built.\n\nShe destroys with her own hands what she has built. Including the very children she travailed in birth for over the years.\n\nGiving children to the fire must have provoked the highest of devotion to these wicked pagan gods.\n\nWhere a woman travails through nine months of pregnancy and eventual labour, only to give of her all to an idol as homage.\n\nThe wicked seem to do wickedly with such devotion it's almost emulatable, except that our GOD hated devotion of wickedness, and he in no way desires such abominations.\n\nHe only desires what is fitting and just for a holy GOD as him. He desires nothing of the abominations of the heathen.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:43:32.829Z","s":["by19n5t9nv"]}],"23":[{"m":"After all this, yet the Lord continued to warn his wife betrothed to him.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:37:40.450Z","s":["nuae2hkf9k"]}],"34":[{"m":"Interesting, and in another sense this is true, in that we have no record much of the heathen nations abandoning their many gods to serve and embrace the GOD of Israel, yet Israel willingly and freely abandons their GOD, who is the real true GOD, to serve others. Even to their own shame, but they still do.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:45:24.902Z","s":["zilg6jndp6"]}],"45":[{"m":"Why this constant connection? There has to be something about the Amorite father and the Hittite mother. This bears more study, or if you know what the true connection is, kindly drop a comment.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:48:12.053Z","s":["69s59y8few"]}],"13":[{"m":"Such ingratitude for such expensive investments over a lifetime. Israel were adopted and given the life of royalty, only to turn back and commit whoredoms with another.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:35:27.976Z","s":["p445y2vpx2"]}],"26":[{"m":"NIV explains “great of flesh” much clearer.\n\nEzekiel 16:26 NIV\nYou engaged in prostitution with the Egyptians, your neighbors with large genitals, and aroused my anger with your increasing promiscuity.\n\nQuite self-explanatory.","dt":"2024-11-06T10:28:22","s":["8o8sjp1ril"]}],"37":[{"m":"Yes, they were to break into Jerusalem and destroy her walls, leaving her bare, naked and exposed. It is a very strong imagery there.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:46:23.917Z","s":["k6rfqlhehk"]}],"56":[{"m":"Meaning what?","dt":"2022-08-31T18:08:35","s":["bjqyfvn1u4"]}]},"18":{"11":[{"m":"In as much as we say blood is thicker than water, here we see that we are individuals in the eyes 👀 of God, and neither sins nor righteousness are transferable.\n\nOf course, that does not rule out transgenerational blessings, as in Abraham and Israel, or curses 🤬.\n\nBut even then it's not automatic, but subject to terms of righteousness.\n\nThe advantage of the covenant is that God leaves a remnant, and in our case as believers, he makes a way of escape.","dt":"2022-09-01T07:27:55","s":["yv5s3czl37"]}],"21":[{"m":"So a beautiful summary of the rules for righteous living is given here.","dt":"2022-09-01T07:31:35","s":["syymqg9ov8"]}],"27":[{"m":"This sounds like the judgement of the afterlife.\n\nBecause it says he shall save his soul alive. To wit, he shall save his soul in this lifetime for all eternity.\n\nLife at death ☠. Death is the great decider of where we go in the afterlife.","dt":"2022-09-01T07:33:20","s":["s7em9k5472"]}],"32":[{"m":"God does not delight in the death of the wicked. Know that.","dt":"2022-09-01T07:38:21","s":["09smj4ctfj"]}],"20":[{"m":"The soul who sins shall die...","dt":"2024-11-06T10:40:18","s":["tp8ayvvilb"]}]},"20":{"10":[{"m":"It appears from here that Israel's 🇮🇱 idolatry started from the very land of Egypt 🇪🇬.\n\nIn that they did not give it up, and God wanted to destroy them, but forbore because he did not want to bring his name to disrepute before the heathen.\n\nIt was the same plea Moses used for them in the wilderness when they built the Baal image 🖼.\n\nI remember I used to wonder 🍃 where they got the idea 💡 from to even create such abomination.\n\nAnd here we have it. They never let go of Egypt's 🏺 idolatry they had learnt.","dt":"2022-09-01T07:53:19","s":["2t2r6d1dty"]}],"11":[{"m":"Oh Lord, have mercy...\n\nGrant us the grace to do thy will. For therein is our life and prosperity.","dt":"2022-09-01T07:47:48","s":["5bvifm7sta"]}],"15":[{"m":"More study needs be made on the promised land and what makes it unique.","dt":"2022-09-01T08:08:38","s":["rh94ccmgju"]}],"21":[{"m":"This is the 3rd time the Lord has repeated this to them.\n\nHe gave them the fountain ⛲ and source of life... Not just life as in existence, but life as in Zoe, with blessings, peace ✌️ and prosperity.","dt":"2024-11-07T23:59:18","s":["3jis0scbeg"]}],"22":[{"m":"Oh, the long suffering of God in his dealings with us as men.","dt":"2022-09-01T08:09:39","s":["j768tjafsk"]}],"25":[{"m":"So GOD LEFT them to do as they wished.\n\nThey thought they were now free to do what they wished. Because I noticed that certain things that God would not countenance in the wilderness, he countenanced in the promised land.\n\nNot knowing he had given them over to death ☠ and destruction.","dt":"2022-09-01T08:12:12","s":["4szwwob0xj"]}],"28":[{"m":"Is this not the sad 😔 story of Africa 🌍 and our many deities under every tree 🎄 and in the forests?\n\nWe have become the scum of the world 🗺. Laughed at, mocked, because of abundance of resources but lack of wisdom.","dt":"2024-11-08T00:05:45","s":["i223s0gdbm"]}],"44":[{"m":"The wonderful longsuffering of the Lord in not punishing us according to what is due us.","dt":"2022-09-01T08:15:08","s":["5us4i0d6dh"]}],"14":[{"m":"So it was not just in the wilderness that the children of Israel were rebellious and forsook the Lord, but even in the land of Egypt they held onto their gods, but the Lord had mercy on them. We see this rebellion in Egypt in verse 8.","dt":"2026-09-17T18:15:33.185Z","s":["wgu1ow6pjp"]}]},"21":{"6":[{"m":"Was he to fake this, or was he to dig deep into himself and the vision of destruction and sigh and weep genuinely?","dt":"2022-09-01T16:42:05","s":["4gi0xzemsa"]}],"14":[{"m":"This scripture has been used to emphasize the need to clap in church ⛪, though contextually this was a specific direction from God.","dt":"2022-09-01T16:48:42","s":["z1djisgafu"]}],"15":[{"m":"See all these vivid descriptions of the looming disaster upon Judah.\n\nIn a vision there were many figures of speech used, but in practice all one saw happen physically was a raid on Jerusalem, a siege and subsequent butchering of its peoples.\n\nYet it had all been predetermined spiritually by God. Even those who were marked out to escape the sword ⚔.\n\nAgain, in practice it seemed random, the deaths of the people at war; after all, people die all the time in war, but in reality every death was predetermined by God.\n\nOh, the wisdom of the Lord.","dt":"2024-11-08T08:35:39","s":["b0m3f2mchn"]}],"20":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... So all this was taking place ere Jerusalem and Zedekiah were finally destroyed.\n\nIt was settled in the realm of spirit prophetically.\n\nIn the natural it looked like Nebuchadnezzar decided and thus executed, but the spirit had already decided it to be so.","dt":"2022-09-01T16:53:18","s":["5p4bfsiwg5"]}],"22":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 Nebuchadnezzar was himself an enchanter 🧙‍♀️ and diviner 🔮.\n\nEven to the appointing of captains he sought after divination.","dt":"2022-09-01T16:54:52","s":["e8nh1brb6y"]},{"m":"Interesting, the heathen divine and seek specific instruction even before wars, and here they do consult for their attack on both Jerusalem and Ammon.","dt":"2024-11-08T08:37:42","s":["egwaoixkor"]}],"25":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. Legality at work here...\n\nThere were legal grounds for Jerusalem's destruction.\n\nTheir iniquity spoke against them. They could not be pardoned 🙏\n\nIniquity in that they served other gods and practiced wickedness.","dt":"2022-09-01T16:56:23","s":["f3s8jukqb3"]}],"23":[{"m":"Those to be taken by his sword saw it as false divination because they also had sworn oaths to keep them from being taken, but then the king of Babylon called to remembrance their sin and iniquity, which could not be pardoned.\n\nSo guess what, though they had made oaths, they were still taken because of their iniquity.","dt":"2026-09-18T09:46:52.182Z","s":["p4yn9foqdj"]}],"31":[{"m":"GOD has from time immemorial judged nations, particularly the inhabitants of Canaan. And he had all the way from Abraham been judging nations, the land of Sodom for instance.\n\nThen in those same times, he did not yet judge Canaan because their iniquity was not yet full, but seeing into the future, he knew their abominations will be over and above and ripe for judgement, and they will seek to strengthen their hands to prevent the judgement of the Lord.\n\nBut way before that time he began the project of forming his own nation, a nation of priests who would execute the judgement of the Lord.\n\nAnd I see the same thing now in our days; nations and superpowers are arming themselves from judgement.\n\nThey sin and do atrocities, but also prevent themselves from suffering the consequences of their sins.\n\nWe commit abortions, we destroy the earth, yet with technology and advancement those in whose hands is the power escape judgement and punishment.\n\nBut the Lord knows; indeed, he knew from of old and has already worked out his punishment to bypass the strong defence they have made for themselves from reaping the punishment of their ways.\nTheir time will come.","dt":"2026-09-18T09:54:27.615Z","s":["g0lqyisjjw"]}]},"22":{"24":[{"m":"Imagine I was an atheist or New Age person reading the Bible and seeing all these moral laws.\n\nMy conclusion would be, it's just nature 🙏 or the universal mind that we as Christians call God, because this chapter is so relevant.","dt":"2022-09-03T08:32:59","s":["zpot03gkk1"]}],"31":[{"m":"The description of the events in this chapter happened ages ago, yet it's eerily the same things happening in our world 🗺 today.\n\nIndeed, there is nothing new under the sun ☀.\n\nAnd in all this, yet God was not willing to destroy the land and sought for a man 👨, but there was none.\n\nI do not know if he sought for a man to pray for the people, or he sought for one who was righteous, such that God will not destroy the good with the evil 😈 and thus pardon 🙏 the whole land.","dt":"2022-09-03T08:31:06","s":["lonoc1qpgc"]}],"10":[{"m":"Other translations describe it as slept on their father's bed with another (I think with their father's wife).\n\nAnd slept with a menstruous woman who was ceremonially unclean.\n\nAs I read these, I ask: are these laws of God required of other nations who know not the Lord?","dt":"2022-09-02T07:31:16","s":["kpe64souv7"]}],"30":[{"m":"But Ezekiel, Jeremiah and others were present to stand in the gap for the land.\n\nI don't think it was just an intercessor God was asking for necessarily, but one so righteous for whom God will not destroy the city, and God found none.\n\nGod himself has said earlier that even if Noah and Job and Daniel were to be in the land, he won't save them.\n\nThey will only save their very own lives, but not the entire city 🏙\n\nOr maybe in this case, post exile, God was willing to pardon if he found a righteous and true intercessor, but there was none.","dt":"2024-11-08T08:48:51","s":["z1or8n7qql"]}]},"23":{"27":[{"m":"This re-echoes earlier scriptures that they brought idols when they came from Egypt 🇪🇬.\n\nAside, of course, the new ones from the people of the promised land.","dt":"2022-09-04T06:50:56","s":["9jv75wji9h"]}],"9":[{"m":"God judges evil of all nations, both his one nation Israel 🇮🇱 and other nations who don't even know him nor serve him.\n\nGod is judge of all.\n\nBut for Israel, they are his covenant nation and have his laws and ways and precepts, so he always leaves a remnant of them to begin the mission work of reaching out to other nations with the ways of Jehovah.\n\nHere they had so corrupted themselves that he hands them over to those who corrupted them.\n\nHe was later to use other nations to punish these other corrupt nations when their cup was full.","dt":"2024-11-09T07:47:33","s":["7szzbsu2nl"]}],"48":[{"m":"So punishment does two things; it's a double-edged sword.\n\n1. It's punishment to the offender\n\n2. A deterrent to others","dt":"2022-09-04T06:51:44","s":["efgwq29xc6"]}]},"24":{"2":[{"m":"So after all the rebukes and warnings, the day had come. No more ambiguity, but a specific day has been mentioned as the day all this will be fulfilled.\n\nJust like Abraham was promised, until a time came God was specific and said, according to this time of life.\n\nSuch is the nature 🏞 of our long suffering God.","dt":"2022-09-04T06:59:26","s":["rdxgrdrlg2"]},{"m":"So whiles Nebuchadnezzar was in real time setting himself up against Jerusalem, the prophecy of the Lord in real time was also taking place. This was at this time more than enough proof that the word of the Lord was true, and that that which was prophesied was now happening in real time before their very eyes.\n\nBut there was still time, time to repent and believe the Lord. I am sure some who believed sent messages to their brethren in Jerusalem to escape, for the end of Jerusalem was at hand.\n\nBecause we read in the book of Jeremiah how some fell to the side of King Nebuchadnezzar.","dt":"2026-09-21T07:31:31.898Z","s":["iwgfom05qt"]}],"3":[{"m":"Ezekiel was in exile.\nWas he giving this prophecy to the hearing of the Israelites in exile, or he went back to the remnant and prophesied this to their hearing?\n\nI think the former is true.","dt":"2024-11-09T08:19:45","s":["9ablg0d4fl"]}],"11":[{"m":"This was purging to the utmost degree, both the content and the container.\n\nFiery hot 🔥 purging.","dt":"2024-11-09T08:36:11","s":["3gheuxtoj9"]}],"13":[{"m":"Judah's situation was bad; she was beyond scourging.","dt":"2024-11-09T08:38:38","s":["19oineu18r"]}],"16":[{"m":"Hmm, sad 😶, but he was not to weep nor cry, for it was a prophetic symbol.","dt":"2022-09-04T07:03:57","s":["cyu6owaba2"]}],"21":[{"m":"This answers my earlier question 🙋. This prophecy was to those in exile.","dt":"2024-11-09T08:40:33","s":["0v2ozg0ksx"]},{"m":"And indeed those in captivity had family who were still left behind, and now they too will be consumed and destroyed.\n\nYou know, I used to wonder the relevance of the prophecies of Ezekiel; why would GOD send Ezekiel to prophesy to the captives about their free brothers in Jerusalem?\n\nIt was because these people were blood, they were relations, so whatever happens to their family who were left behind in Jerusalem would also greatly affect them as well. Indeed, they could send messages to forewarn them.\n\nGOD in his love did all he could to save his people and help them repent, but they would not.","dt":"2026-09-21T07:37:18.318Z","s":["d00jzlu17x"]}],"7":[{"m":"The people made the high places of the rocks a place to shed strange blood to their gods, a sin which could not be covered. Indeed, on the top of the rocks it remained hidden from men, but not from GOD, who is in the heavens.\n\nFrom the heavens he could see their sin; it was not covered, it was exposed in the full glare of GOD and of spirits.\n\nI can imagine GOD, who lives in the heavens and sees every man and city and civilisation, and from this vantage point sees the sins of the people in rearing up strange altars and offering blood upon them.","dt":"2026-09-21T08:27:33.277Z","s":["tb6wwt7pnv"]}],"18":[{"m":"Oh no... Why?","dt":"2024-11-09T08:39:42","s":["fo1lb3uof5"]}],"27":[{"m":"In Ezekiel 3:26 to 27, he had been made mute by the Lord and could only speak when the Lord spoke to him to speak. Now that was to end here.","dt":"2026-09-21T08:11:34.741Z","s":["8up9umz8os"]}]},"26":{"16":[{"m":"Oh, the scenery, imagine it. When a city 🏙 once beautiful and the joy of many suddenly crumbles and is wasted.\n\nA complete scene of desolation.","dt":"2022-09-04T20:03:19","s":["loggc91p2s"]}],"2":[{"m":"Where were these discussions held, like among the kings and elders and princes of those nations in the corridors of power, which then descended to the everyday folks on the streets?","dt":"2026-09-21T08:18:48.227Z","s":["ap8m1crx8i"]}]},"28":{"3":[{"m":"Was just wondering, why was Daniel referenced here rather than Solomon? Was it because in this context of wisdom, revelation of hidden things is what is referenced?\n\nThen, of course, in that sense Daniel was the go-to person.\n\n2ndly, I thought at this time Daniel was yet to go into captivity, or if he had, he was not yet popular??\n\nBut then again, this helps us to appreciate the time-line of these writings...\nLikely at this time Daniel's wisdom was widespread.","dt":"2022-09-05T13:05:14","s":["1w1lqjkrgl"]}],"10":[{"m":"We are shown in scriptures over and over what happens to the proud in heart ♥","dt":"2022-09-05T13:02:10","s":["qails3xmcg"]}],"19":[{"m":"So Satan is like some despised treasonous son cast down to this earth 🌎.\n\nHe is not that glamorous and revered cherub he was back then.\n\nHighly sought after and desired in his days, but now a reject who is trying to gain a name for himself here on the earth 🌎\n\nA scumbag trying to build for himself a kingdom 👑 and riding on men as his tool, through deception.\n\nThe army he leads in this time are not loyal to him for who he is.\n\nThey are loyal to him because of deception 😞.\n\nThey do not know he is behind it. Rulership through clandestine means.","dt":"2022-09-05T13:28:56","s":["6luvyb4922"]}],"26":[{"m":"I wonder whether Israel now, in their own land, do qualify or are experiencing this blessing.\n\nI would say yes, some parts of it, but they are not dwelling securely, though they are dwelling in their own land.\n\nToo many enemies surround them, so for now we wait to see the unfolding events and how this blessing will manifest.","dt":"2024-11-11T08:24:23","s":["jtdxjguldl"]}]},"29":{"5":[{"m":"This I believe alludes to Pharaoh and to his people, he being that great dragon and his people the fish on his scales.","dt":"2024-11-11T08:30:57","s":["jev9deaxfi"]}],"7":[{"m":"Egypt 🇪🇬, whom Israel 🇮🇱 relied upon, were as unreliable as a reed for a staff, and though Israel had been warned, they did not listen 👂.\n\nNonetheless, Egypt was punished justifiably.","dt":"2022-09-05T13:42:07","s":["hrj3y7pp01"]}],"10":[{"m":"This Ethiopia 🇪🇹 is, from some research, in reference to Sudan 🇸🇩 or so.","dt":"2022-09-05T13:43:10","s":["xvel09ue92"]}],"17":[{"m":"This was a long time now... Wow","dt":"2022-09-06T06:13:52","s":["a1vqit0fxo"]},{"m":"At the beginning of this chapter it was the tenth year, and at this point it was 27 years, meaning 17 years had come to pass.\n\nDoes that mean that there was no word from the Lord for all that period, or there was no significant message from the Lord?\n\nEzekiel 30:20-21 KJV\nAnd it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first month, in the seventh day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying, Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt; and, lo, it shall not be bound up to be healed, to put a roller to bind it, to make it strong to hold the sword.\n\nOkay, I just checked, and in the next chapter Ezekiel gives a prophecy that came to him in the eleventh year.\n\nSo he continued to receive prophecies after the tenth year.\n\nThis verse only came to show us the duration between one event and another.\n\nWill check from other chapters onward if anything is said between those years.","dt":"2024-11-11T08:44:36","s":["mistm4v7yl"]}],"6":[{"m":"Israel counted on Egypt for help, much to their own hurt.","dt":"2024-11-11T08:28:49","s":["a5yfpm81j"]}]},"30":{"21":[{"m":"Now was the time of the heathen 🔥\n\nBut then again, since Ezekiel is not chronological in all respects, the date of this prophecy cannot be concluded as following right after the previous chapter's years.","dt":"2022-09-05T14:33:35","s":["t5f2wlmytx"]}],"25":[{"m":"The force 💪 responsible for Egypt's 🏺 downfall was utter and complete.\n\nThe overwhelming force 💪 of God, and it really brought the people low.","dt":"2022-09-05T14:32:44","s":["wojfloobd1"]}]},"31":{"2":[{"m":"Was he to speak to Pharaoh face to 😔, or was he to just prophesy?","dt":"2022-09-06T06:18:39","s":["g2acw5ucg5"]}]},"32":{"8":[{"m":"I think this was in a figurative sense to indicate the gross darkness that will come over them.","dt":"2022-09-06T06:37:03","s":["fz1gujxzt3"]}],"29":[{"m":"Of Edom it is said that they shall lie with the uncircumcised, but with others they lay uncircumcised.\n\nEdom is Esau, son of Isaac, who circumcised his children according to the covenant.","dt":"2022-09-06T06:33:55","s":["x87a6imqny"]}],"4":[{"m":"Imagine a whale trapped on land, helpless as the beasts and birds of the air feed on his flesh. Alive, yet being fed on.\n\nAnd its flesh the birds will carry unto the top of the mountains, and as they carry the flesh, the blood spills and waters all the land. This is the imagery the subsequent verses paint.","dt":"2026-09-22T11:29:56.341Z","s":["7fbuaspjob"]}],"27":[{"m":"If there is the land of the living, then there is the land of the dead, and from what we are told in scripture, the land of the dead is full of people who are alive. Very thought-provoking.","dt":"2026-09-24T08:36:19.437Z","s":["36gvnpq96c"]}]},"33":{"12":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... So we just need to walk 🚶 in righteousness always.","dt":"2022-09-06T06:44:06","s":["ddjaesos78"]}],"21":[{"m":"Sad 😔. The captivity was now personal, \"our captivity\", because they were getting and accepting this was their lot, probably till their death ☠","dt":"2022-09-06T06:46:12","s":["gbfz4sjz7c"]}],"32":[{"m":"Very interesting illustration...\n\nThat the word of the Lord was like music in their ears to them.\n\nThey will hear and enjoy them but will not live by it.","dt":"2024-11-17T12:38:14","s":["zi3v82hudc"]}],"33":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔. That is the only consolation... That indeed he was a true man of God.","dt":"2022-09-06T06:49:27","s":["9w97pyj5xt"]}]},"35":{"12":[{"m":"It seems here that Mount Seir saw the captivity and desolation Israel was experiencing and decided that they had to maximize the opportunity for themselves.\n\nBy invading Israel 🇮🇱 and making their land theirs.\n\nThat was their intention, and God had his own plans for them.","dt":"2022-09-07T06:37:52","s":["3122xj5sh5"]}]},"36":{"3":[{"m":"When you get into trouble and in your lowest moments,\n\nyour case will come on the lips 💋 of talkers.\n\nThat has been the nature of man 👨 from time immemorial towards those in trouble.\n\nExpect it.\n\nIn such moments trust in the Lord, and he shall be your defence.","dt":"2022-09-07T06:43:50","s":["ph61qe11ls"]}],"8":[{"m":"Allegory, similes and storytelling.\nThese are the ways God talks to his people.\n\nGod doth know that you drive home your point to man through images and stories, not just mere words.\n\nGod indeed is the master communicator.\n\nJesus did the same; even atheists know one story or another of Jesus because of his many stories and parables.\n\nQuite a lesson for me. We communicate with man through images.\n\nSee, God does not just say words; he uses stories and word pictures profusely.","dt":"2022-09-07T06:52:38","s":["ga3x5wo499"]}],"9":[{"m":"Such blessed assurance and CONSOLATION. To know that GOD IS WITH US","dt":"2022-09-07T06:53:34","s":["c6ylqtpoic"]}],"15":[{"m":"Already a proverb and a strong 💪 mental hold 👫 had been created that the land devours men 🚹.\n\nThis is a reproach which the Lord wanted to take away. And he did.\n\nThe land was no more permitted to devour men nor cause shame.\n\nNo matter the situation of your life or what you are noted for, God is able to take away our reproach always.","dt":"2022-09-07T06:58:01","s":["1mpa4qj348"]}],"27":[{"m":"It takes a new spirit and heart, which only the Lord can give, to walk 🚶 in the statutes of God.","dt":"2022-09-07T07:12:27","s":["smjqfsghnj"]}],"36":[{"m":"Ah, I love that... I the Lord have spoken it, and I will do it.\n\nHis word and his promises are sure.","dt":"2022-09-07T07:05:12","s":["7xp86jpupj"]}],"38":[{"m":"Such imagery, in one breath bringing again to mind their holy feast and the uncountable flocks, and in another assuring them that he will multiply them as before.","dt":"2022-09-07T07:14:51","s":["a0t17l0cg8"]}]},"37":{"18":[{"m":"Does that imply they asked multiple times without a response, knowing he was a prophet and thus had a message?\n\nUntil finally they blurt out: will thou not show us...?","dt":"2024-11-26T01:37:53","s":["99cihkcvye"]}],"24":[{"m":"They shall walk therein because of the new spirit they now have.\n\nAnd David's family... shall rule over them.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:14:59","s":["omvi667oi8"]}],"12":[{"m":"This makes me wonder, have we no prophets in this nation Ghana to speak the mind of GOD concerning us for real?\n\nA national prophet whose words do not fall to the ground?","dt":"2026-09-26T06:45:22.940Z","s":["th14w401g9"]}]},"38":{"16":[{"m":"This concerns the end of times.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:19:11","s":["hjevgz21sm"]}],"17":[{"m":"Interesting... In other words, God is talking of the future 🔮 and saying he will stand in the future and say that I spoke of you in time past by my prophets.\n\nOh, the omnipresent ONE.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:22:13","s":["t185gyer2m"]}]},"39":{"8":[{"m":"Though this was yet to happen, it was already declared a done deal 🤝 by the Lord.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:42:55","s":["6vsq8bx6vz"]}],"9":[{"m":"Seven years? Then that has to be a very large army for its weapons to be used as fire 🔥 for that long.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:42:10","s":["wdmd5t3b8"]}],"16":[{"m":"When was this day to be... In the future 🔮, because historically such an event is yet to occur.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:44:49","s":["ha0iv1mkwv"]}],"23":[{"m":"GOD wanted it to be made clear that their going into captivity was his judgment against Israel 🇮🇱,\n\nnot any strength 💪 of the enemy.","dt":"2022-09-08T06:50:47","s":["1lhr3rg8je"]}],"28":[{"m":"This has happened many times to Israel... The most recent being their scattering in AD 70 and their regathering in 1948.\n\nBut this chapter is talking of a final judgement on their enemies ⚡ and God dwelling with them in eternal peace ✌️","dt":"2022-09-08T06:48:34","s":["8mi5num2jw"]}]},"42":{"20":[{"m":"From the checks made, this was about 1500 msq.\n\nThat is quite an area. I wonder what the purpose of such a vast area was for.\n\nYes, it is to separate profane from holy, but... Well, let me read on; these questions may be answered in depth.\n\nEzekiel 42:20 CEVUK\nand so the temple area was a perfect square. The wall around this area separated what was sacred from what was ordinary.","dt":"2024-11-27T07:50:40","s":["yjgll9ecvg","kqrbw126oa"]}]},"43":{"9":[{"m":"Like the Egyptians who deified their dead kings, Israel had also picked up that practice.","dt":"2024-11-27T07:55:36","s":["kfblboxj5r"]}]},"44":{"9":[{"m":"Is this New Testament stuff 🧐? God here is saying circumcision of the flesh without that of the heart will not suffice for access into his presence.","dt":"2022-09-11T07:21:21","s":["qakp0djofz"]}],"25":[{"m":"For a sister that hath no husband... otherwise, let her own husband mourn for her.","dt":"2022-09-11T07:25:07","s":["d8blk7114c"]}]},"45":{"9":[{"m":"It seems this temple and the instructions given concerning it are more applicable to Isaiah's time.\n\nIn reading the design of the temple and the fact that God has moved into it post-exile, I thought it was a millennial temple at the end of time.\n\nJust that the way sacrifices are described and the allotment of land for priests and the kings seem archaic, and I wonder how that will pan out practically in the future, considering our modern technology and world.\n\nMention is also made of the crimes of the past, and a caution is thrown to the kings and leaders to stop sinning. But then again, I know there will be no more sin in the future, though there is mention of a 1000-year reign of Christ where rebellion will have to be stamped out.","dt":"2024-11-27T08:17:37","s":["lcrpok74od"]}],"23":[{"m":"I think I'm getting it.\n\nThis is not the end of time, neither is the prince 🤴 Jesus at his coming.\n\nRather, it was to be a temple built in Israel 🇮🇱 if they repented.\n\nBecause the pattern of the temple 🏛 was not to be shown to the people if they did not repent.\n\nAs to whether such a temple was even built, I don't know yet.","dt":"2022-09-11T07:32:58","s":["jt0k1yrpv8"]}],"1":[{"m":"I'm not getting this. This is some future temple which is yet to be built.\n\nNow if it is in the end time, why are we sacrificing sheep 🐑 and needing Levitical priests?","dt":"2022-09-11T07:27:10","s":["iaqzql766s"]}]},"47":{"12":[{"m":"In the previous chapter I talked of this temple not being the millennium.\n\nHowever, a temple with such a river issuing out of it for the healing of the land has not yet existed.\n\nI believe God was revealing his ideal plan for them.\n\nIf, because of the stubbornness of their heart ♥, it was not fulfilled, it may still hold true for a future generation.","dt":"2022-09-11T07:51:27","s":["5y906c2ny0"]}]},"5":{"2":[{"m":"The days of the siege: was the siege of Israel equivalent to 430 days, i.e. a year and a half? If my memory serves me right, it was about a year, so this was not an exact replica of the final siege of Jerusalem.\n\nI checked online, and the actual siege was 540 to 900 days, so it was longer.","dt":"2026-09-10T10:04:25.465Z","s":["vhapzysr3h"]}]},"15":{"7":[{"m":"GOD knew the evil that will befall them, and so he sent constant watchmen and prophets to warn the people severally. But they would not heed.","dt":"2026-09-16T10:30:42.798Z","s":["qivvanf2mu"]}]},"1":{"19":[{"m":"It feels like the wheels were pets or some robotic arm of the creatures, such that it enhanced their abilities.\n\nThe wheels had eyes all over, and thus afforded the creatures the ability to see so much more and in so much more detail.\n\nVerse 21 says that the spirit of the living creatures was in the wheels.\n\nSo there was some very intricate connection between these two.","dt":"2024-11-02T09:25:10","s":["lujc0a0gc6"]}]},"17":{"15":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔... So logical... Such use of allegory.","dt":"2022-08-31T18:12:42","s":["kdtttg9rri"]}],"18":[{"m":"So Zedekiah, I believe, was the one who cut this covenant, yet brake it.","dt":"2022-08-31T18:15:36","s":["hnn993ptdg"]}],"24":[{"m":"Selah","dt":"2022-08-31T18:17:17","s":["ea82798fb6"]}]},"19":{"14":[{"m":"Selah","dt":"2022-09-01T07:40:11","s":["9bea4b02d3"]}]},"25":{"2":[{"m":"Ezekiel was not the only one who prophesied to the enemies of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nSo imagine the multiple curses 🤬 from all angles and different territories against Israel and her enemies.\n\nTo cause the word of the Lord to pass upon them.","dt":"2024-11-09T08:43:08","s":["d1rfc833m4"]}]},"27":{"14":[{"m":"A trade fair","dt":"2024-11-09T08:52:20","s":["0x7gldzyuh"]}]}},"Joel":{"1":{"14":[{"m":"Spiritual death and deafness and dumbness.\n\nInsensitivity to the things of the spirit.\n\nThe mess Israel 🇮🇱 was in merited that the priest lie 🤥 down 👇 all night in sackcloth, and refusing to eat.\n\nLike the way there is a loss of appetite when a loved one dies.\n\nBut here they were, living life as usual.\n\nAnd this sometimes is our state. A state of death, yet we walk 🚶 in darkness and live life as usual.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:24:26","s":["agcpb51ktj"]}],"8":[{"m":"These guys were literally in a deadly situation, and they were acting 🎭 all cool 😎 about it.\n\nGod was shaking them awake to react appropriately.\n\nThey were so blind and dull at heart ♥ that God had to paint 🎨 to them how bad their situation was.\n\nHe told them to weep like a virgin who had lost her husband in her youth.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:14:03","s":["gjyi5ktome"]}]},"2":{"11":[{"m":"The same God who had been coaxing, pleading 🙏 and using all manner of means to get his people to repentance suddenly comes upon them with such an army.\n\nHe himself leading them. With fierceness of wrath and stern, obstinate face 😡.\n\nHe who once pleaded and wept arm 🙋 in arm 🙋, pleading, now came 🏇 with unyielding stubbornness and anger.\n\nCharging at his own people and destroying them.\n\nGod teaches us here how he holds all things in proper perspective. He is in perfect balance ⚖ about issues.\n\nHe knew Israel had to be destroyed, but he also remembered the covenant and the patriarchs and David ✡.\n\nIt was always about balance ⚖. To hold back long enough to allow for repentance, but not too long, such that tenets of justice are destroyed or denied.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:32:04","s":["uqbwy8x4li"]}],"17":[{"m":"Without true repentance, God cannot do his people good.\n\nHe cannot force himself nor his blessings on anyone.\n\nWe have a will, and an unwilling person cannot partake of his blessings.\n\nIt just can't happen.\n\nSo he requires his people to repent and realign themselves with him before he can help them.\n\nSuch is the nature of things, and we ought also to learn from the Lord and not force things on others unduly — depending on the context, of course.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:41:06","s":["yu434hhbvq"]}],"19":[{"m":"This response of God was subject to the people repenting genuinely...\n\nGod would have turned and reversed all the ills for his people, but sadly this was never to be — Israel continued in disobedience and were destroyed.\n\nThis again goes to show that no matter how downtrodden a people are, God will come through for anyone who has truly repented.\n\nSadly, in our days we are crooks and corrupt thieves, yet we still somehow expect God to come through for us.\n\nThe Lord has not changed, and he is a true judge.","dt":"2024-11-19T08:29:00","s":["30im9dam1w"]}],"26":[{"m":"Amen. My people shall NEVER be ashamed.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:42:45","s":["jgzjht9z9n"]}],"27":[{"m":"Oh my God. He again emphasizes. NEVER","dt":"2022-09-13T06:43:09","s":["bt0u1dktny"]}],"28":[{"m":"And this afterwards was a long time ⌚ in coming.\n\nHow that God can compress millennia into one word is amazing.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:44:29","s":["hc9hy88dzo"]}],"31":[{"m":"The day of the Lord, referring to the end of time.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:45:02","s":["bdc526mrfy"]}],"32":[{"m":"This remnant is different from the remnant left after the northern armies, i.e. Nebuchadnezzar and co., invaded Israel.\n\nThis was another remnant, of the future coming of the Lord.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:46:23","s":["3r40va6w54"]}],"8":[{"m":"Lord, have mercy.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:27:11","s":["7kef5tgwgg"]}],"12":[{"m":"With all your heart ♥...\n\nI am reminded of how that I feel the peace ✌️ of the Spirit anytime I make up my mind on full-time ministry and even begin to act thus.\n\nThis is where we are heading to.\n\nFull-time, and the goal is to get there.","dt":"2022-09-13T06:34:55","s":["u6lznuku8k"]}]},"3":{"2":[{"m":"Which place is this... The valley of Jehoshaphat?","dt":"2022-09-13T07:37:06","s":["4aoj4rnsux"]}],"5":[{"m":"God is interesting, i.e. he disdained the gold and silver of his own temple 🏛 because of the harlotry of Israel 🇮🇱, but in their restoration,\n\nhe raises it as a case against the enemies of Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nIt all boils down to context.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:38:47","s":["y4jarbczzk"]}],"10":[{"m":"Ah, I now understand this scripture. I think it was more a call of mockery to the Gentile nations.\n\nTo beat their farming tools into weapons and arm the weak, and let them say they are strong for war.\n\nThis was to mock their strength, really.","dt":"2024-11-19T08:36:34","s":["5dnmhznoal"]},{"m":"And yet, inasmuch as this verse is a mockery call to the enemies of God and of Israel to come for battle, and to arm the weak and tell them they are strong,\n\nyet we have many times taken this out of context and rendered it a clarion call to us, the chosen of the Lord, to declare we are strong even when weak...\n\nYes, the concept of positive faith confessions is biblical and true, just that the verse we have chosen to use is not so apt and appropriate.","dt":"2024-11-28T08:15:25","s":["fk9glkuzdd"]}],"14":[{"m":"Hmm. This part answers my question.\n\nThe valley of Jehoshaphat, which means God judged, was the valley of decisions, where God judged the heathen 🔥 for their sins against God and his people.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:43:18","s":["rwytepg8fj"]}],"16":[{"m":"A double-edged sword: whiles he shook and destroyed others, he was giving strength 💪 by the same.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:44:23","s":["qk4bc2xpy1"]}],"21":[{"m":"Amen, he indeed dwells there.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:46:55","s":["e363imm702"]}],"8":[{"m":"Who are the Sabeans?","dt":"2022-09-13T09:39:22","s":["p1rdnth4ka"]}],"18":[{"m":"Is this not the same stream in Ezekiel's days?","dt":"2022-09-13T09:45:13","s":["v5r2d8gbvk"]}]}},"Daniel":{"1":{"2":[{"m":"Even men are careful to record history and happenings of events.\n\nIt's worth noting that only a part of the vessels of the Lord's house was given to Nebuchadnezzar.\n\nThen in heaven every minute detail of history is noted, including the very hairs 💇 on our head.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:49:38","s":["vj6v54v1xf"]},{"m":"He brought the Lord's treasures into the house of his god because he had conquered Israel 🇮🇱, the people of God Almighty.\n\nLittle did he know it was a set up for him to later recognize and admit that there is only one God, that is the God of Daniel, Meshach and Abednego.\n\nHe thought he had captured the God of Israel 🇮🇱; he did not know it was an infiltration strategy.\n\nAnd next thing, he began to use the most gifted of the children of Israel, but he did not know he was being used.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:41:54","s":["3f7sujfzk9"]}],"9":[{"m":"Now from the macro point of view of God's wrath 😡 against Israel 🇮🇱, he showed favour towards Daniel and others when you zoom 🔎 in to the specifics.\n\nEven in anger some were favoured.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:56:41","s":["d2p5wowl9v"]}],"12":[{"m":"So though the kings were wicked and disobedient to God, there were those of the seed royal 👑 who feared 😱 God and were ready to be thrown into the fire 🔥 alive for him.\n\nYet such ones were not in power, but rather idol and devil 👿 worshipers had taken the throne and the kingdom life.","dt":"2022-09-13T09:59:14","s":["ht6y2uwqe4"]}],"15":[{"m":"Is this medical or divine... Their fresher look?","dt":"2022-09-13T10:26:17","s":["rh58cexn0z"]}],"16":[{"m":"Interesting, what's the science behind this? Divine help, I believe.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:53:48","s":["hhtsyy4b88"]}],"17":[{"m":"These are the kind of students that do well in all subject areas, and you wonder which area is their strength 💪 or weakness really.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:54:48","s":["xz85rvk4st"]}],"21":[{"m":"What a wonderful record. Something so powerful yet defined in a single sentence.","dt":"2022-09-13T10:28:59","s":["eftq1hd76f"]},{"m":"How long did the others last, though? We are not told.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:55:42","s":["5zz3gecn58"]}],"3":[{"m":"This goes to show that Nebuchadnezzar was not all evil 😈.\n\nHe was also very smart 🧠 and very desirous of expanding his own coast and influence, and was willing to take the best gifts.\n\nHe was a king of nations and kings, and so all people were his people from all the respective peoples, states and tribes.\n\nHe was indeed a very wise king 👑.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:43:55","s":["en1i3xhcsq"]}],"4":[{"m":"This description is so much like our school system today — where the best academically have the best chance of excelling in the system of education.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:45:00","s":["64mofc83yn"]}],"5":[{"m":"Their training was to be for 3 years, but it appears they began to serve even in their first year...\nBecause in the very next chapter we see the king have a troubled dream in his second year.","dt":"2024-12-01T08:01:33","s":["ioq5ftg6ae"]}],"20":[{"m":"These 4 young men, I thought they were very intelligent 🧠 students.\n\nNow suddenly they are being compared to astrologers and sorcerers.\n\nHmm 🤔, what kind of wisdom did they demonstrate?\n\nI really wonder, but that goes to show again the content of the educational system of Babylon. It was not just scientific knowledge one was expected to acquire, but to have spiritual knowledge as well.","dt":"2024-12-01T07:58:49","s":["j3c5p5ht9v"]}]},"2":{"9":[{"m":"Wow... This politician of a king 👑","dt":"2022-09-13T10:36:48","s":["1jeclujt6x"]},{"m":"A decree... This means the word of the king could not be changed; they were either going to be killed or rewarded.","dt":"2024-12-01T08:07:57","s":["ytn2jnum4r"]}],"10":[{"m":"These guys were wizards to the core and had divisions in their practice.","dt":"2022-09-13T10:38:57","s":["mazloxm4g3"]}],"13":[{"m":"I can imagine the times.\n\nSuch wicked times upon the land, on any acclaimed wise man 👨.\n\nIt's almost like in Jerusalem, when the newborns under 2 were to be killed in search of Wisdom personified, i.e. Jesus.","dt":"2022-09-13T10:41:48","s":["r19723igye"]}],"16":[{"m":"A law of the spirit realm... The law of time...\n\nDaniel did not control the spirit realm, nor presume so.\n\nHe knew he had to wait, and not knowing how long, but knew that he had to wait before he obtains an answer.\n\nSo he goes to the king and asks for time.\n\nI noticed a similar thing in the book of Jeremiah... I was thinking of it yesterday...\n\nHow that the soldiers of Israel who had escaped captivity sought the face of the Lord from Jeremiah.\n\nAnd though he was a prophet, the word of the Lord came to him 10 days later...\n\nJeremiah 42:7 NIV\nTen days later the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah.","dt":"2024-12-01T08:12:08","s":["yuyyigylkk"]}],"19":[{"m":"Ah Daniel 👽, Daniel the wise one... This Daniel.\n\nThe master of the magicians 🧝‍♂️ and sorcerers 🧙‍♂️","dt":"2022-09-13T10:44:04","s":["kpsejie27g"]}],"20":[{"m":"Wow, so Daniel duplicated another's dream.\n\nHe determined what kind of dream to have. Wow.","dt":"2022-09-13T10:45:26","s":["gci6snofv2"]}],"25":[{"m":"This is so similar to Joseph's story — where his gift brought him before kings.","dt":"2024-12-01T10:50:50","s":["oo5saewa8b"]},{"m":"Why in haste? Had the killings already begun whiles Daniel was waiting on the Lord? Likely so, so that Daniel knows that for every delay real people are dying, or likely also because the king was growing desperate day by day waiting for the answer, and he could run out of patience at any moment and order the killing of the wise men.\n\nArioch came in and spoke to the king that he had found a man of the captives of Judah. Though he had a while back already approached the king, he knew that the king had many matters on his mind, so in wisdom he introduced Daniel again and spoke of the matter as if this was the first time he was meeting the king on this matter.\n\nThat is how we approach busy people and people in the corridors of power and wealth: don't start talking to them expecting them to remember everything from the last conversation. No, start afresh, but in a summary, and then move to the main point.","dt":"2026-09-27T16:05:45.281Z","s":["izhn5f9cbt"]}],"27":[{"m":"Wait oo... So if the thing cannot these men do, why were they soothsayers and magicians in the first place?\n\nParticularly the soothsayers.\nWhat were they soothsayers for?\n\nIt's like a doctor who cannot treat diseases.\n\nBut in hindsight, the soothsayers likely had predicted many things, but the weight of this dream was, and concerned, the eternal future spanning several millennia.\n\nNo soothsayer could know these things. Indeed, no man nor deity could know these things.\n\nThis was a dream in the realm of the Almighty, and he alone.","dt":"2024-12-01T10:57:19","s":["1solmpd00h"]}],"28":[{"m":"These people believed in many gods for different purposes. Daniel had to give and coin an attribute of God to help introduce the God of the Hebrews to them, i.e. 'the God of heaven who reveals secrets' to them.","dt":"2025-09-13T10:53:30","s":["2tyw21cib5"]}],"46":[{"m":"All the while the king was silent; he could have jumped in the moment Daniel got the dream right, but waited until all was said, then he came in.\n\nThe words of the wise made manifest through silence and patient hearing.","dt":"2025-09-13T11:06:28","s":["bvpxbe7rix"]}],"49":[{"m":"One event, one break, and Daniel's life changed, he and that of his friends.\n\nDaniel's family 👪 is never mentioned.","dt":"2022-09-13T10:57:28","s":["mxj0o1isrn"]},{"m":"Much like Mordecai sat at the gates of the king 👑... A great man.","dt":"2024-12-01T11:18:23","s":["axo18mz25l"]},{"m":"I made a comment in 2022 that in all these, Daniel's family was never mentioned. I am later told that it was because they were made eunuchs — I don't know how true that is; I'm yet to investigate that personally.","dt":"2026-09-28T08:23:49.881Z","s":["ww3vb49gke"]}],"1":[{"m":"I just realized that with such bright and GOD-fearing minds in the palace of Judah, who knows, Daniel might have become king 👑 possibly and ruled Judah in righteousness.\n\nIt was in the realm of possibilities, but then again he was not in the direct line of succession, but was of the seed royal. Else he would have been mentioned, possibly.\n\nEven in such a depraved state of Judah, there were still great and GOD-fearing men like Daniel and his friends.\n\nBut the time was up. GOD still sent them to exile.","dt":"2026-09-27T15:54:07.069Z","s":["4ocr34izxa"]}],"11":[{"m":"Who are these so-called gods?","dt":"2022-09-13T10:40:38","s":["obt0w2v496"]}],"26":[{"m":"“The dream which I have seen,” I strongly suspect the king knew the dream very well but just refused to tell them.","dt":"2026-09-27T16:12:33.761Z","s":["tpz7029jw2"]}],"30":[{"m":"Daniel was careful to give God all the glory and honour.\n\nBut today, we see men take upon themselves the glory due God.","dt":"2022-09-13T10:49:30","s":["w53380orth"]}],"45":[{"m":"Daniel 2:34 KJV\nThou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces.\n\nIn verse 34 we are told the stone was cut without hands, and left to our imagination; of course, logically the stone was definitely cut out from another stone, but here in verse 45 we are told specifically where it was cut out of.\n\nIt wasn't just another stone or rock or hill, but it was cut out of a mountain, and after crushing the image, it by itself became a mountain, the mountain of the Lord's house in the last days.\n\nIsaiah 2:2 KJV\nAnd it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the LORD'S house shall be established in the top of the mountains, and shall be exalted above the hills; and all nations shall flow unto it.\n\nAMEN","dt":"2026-09-28T08:18:31.288Z","s":["94w74rnk1i"]}],"48":[{"m":"These Jews, by making him chief, it brought respect to all Jews in the realm.\n\nAnd then in the times of Esther, who was compatriots with Daniel, Mordecai also gained influence and became chief as well, thus giving rest and respect to the children of Israel.\n\nHmm, these Jews — THEY REIGN WHEREVER THEY GO.","dt":"2026-09-28T08:21:04.543Z","s":["s5092nxb3p"]}]},"3":{"11":[{"m":"He thought as long as he was over 👑 kings, he was also god over gods...\n\nGod had to let him know He, God, was the true God of gods.\n\nIt is interesting that we take the very thing that God has taken to spite him and provoke him to jealousy with the very works of his own hands.","dt":"2024-12-01T11:26:55","s":["y72p7m1srx"]}],"12":[{"m":"What inspired such a demonic thought to start with in the first place?\n\nSecondly, where was Daniel?","dt":"2022-09-13T11:00:06","s":["3q1fnvjcrz"]}],"15":[{"m":"Though the scriptures do not mention the image to be that of Nebuchadnezzar — this was a self-made god.","dt":"2024-12-01T11:30:50","s":["o364o0vwy9"]}],"18":[{"m":"Where did such faith come from? Where was Daniel?\n\nThe same God who had saved them in revealing Nebuchadnezzar's dream would save them again.\n\nAnd they were not going to deny him. And even if this time he, God, did not show up, it was not from lack of ability to, but his divine providence.\n\nThus they, the three boys, would not deny the Lord. They would rather die 🎲 for God than save their own skins 🎿","dt":"2022-09-15T09:13:35","s":["blzgq0gdzu"]}],"24":[{"m":"Oh, when in our times and day will we see notable, undeniable miracles in our day and time?\n\nOur world is really in need of it, a miracle that would be viewed and broadcasted by literally the whole world.\n\nTo put an end to the God debate, but oh, that time will come... And the impact of that miracle will be undeniable that there is a God in heaven.","dt":"2024-12-05T08:05:13","s":["a3nebtued6"]},{"m":"NEBUCHADNEZZAR was indeed a tool in the hands of GOD to display God's power.","dt":"2026-09-30T08:20:29.769Z","s":["lxiww59qq1"]}],"25":[{"m":"The form of the fourth was so radiant that the light of a fire 🔥 heated 7 times could not hold his radiance back.","dt":"2024-12-01T11:33:17","s":["a220nankq6"]}],"30":[{"m":"Promotion cometh not from the east nor west; promotion is of the Lord.","dt":"2022-09-15T09:15:39","s":["fzit92ihry"]},{"m":"When you stand for God, he stands for you. And promotion that comes from God serves infinitely greater than any self-engineered promotion.","dt":"2022-09-15T09:32:38","s":["xv1rib5f"]},{"m":"It took demonstration of spiritual power to earn this promotion.","dt":"2026-09-30T08:22:45.849Z","s":["4ww2u3mh8t"]}],"1":[{"m":"So right after he was told he was the head of gold, he decided to make an image, which I believe may be according to the image he saw in his dream.\n\nGoing directly against the GOD of all the earth — sad, but these were polytheists, so what was their way of life.\n\nGOD later dealt with him though.","dt":"2026-09-28T08:48:02.741Z","s":["c1p5v448uc"]},{"m":"A statue 90 feet tall. Is he so vain to be lifted up in such self-exaltation? 90 feet, insane, but it was done. I am presuming the image was probably an image of him, deifying himself essentially.","dt":"2026-09-28T08:50:13.397Z","s":["a4zbc2ityc"]}],"29":[{"m":"Even Nebuchadnezzar came to the conclusion that only the God of the boys delivers in such a manner.\n\nNEBUCHADNEZZAR, even after this remark, did not convert to Jehovah worship.","dt":"2022-09-15T09:31:42","s":["evt5l1czdz"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"Everyone has the place and point they meet God at and surrender to him. After all that King Nebuchadnezzar had experienced, you would have expected him to have converted to the Hebrew God, but no, not until his sanity was taken from him did he surrender to God Almighty. And that is what happens to us. Some change drastically after their first major encounter with the Lord.\n\nOthers take more than one, and yet others multiple encounters to surrender to the Lord, and sadly some never do.","dt":"2025-09-13T11:11:16","s":["4qie4nw87e"]}],"3":[{"m":"I can only imagine what it took for Nebuchadnezzar to get to this point.\n\nHe was a proud man who set up images as gods and decided the whole earth must worship 🛐 it.\n\nHe was a god to himself.\n\nSecondly, why did he have to be asleep in a dream state, where all senses are suspended, for him to have this dream, a portal to the spirit realm?\n\nMind you, his dreams were super accurate. Why did God and the Spirit have to commune with him in a dream state?\n\nCould they not have communed otherwise, directly to him? This is where knowledge into the spirit arises.\n\nOur spirit senses physical things as our everyday default mode. To sense spiritually, we would have to change the mode or engage in some activity that serves as a portal to the spirit.\n\nThere is no way around it; it is deliberate knowledge that must be applied.\n\nBeing in a dream state was how God chose to communicate directly with this pagan king 👑.\n\nIndeed, that was how he dealt with the pagan kings, from Abimelech, Pharaoh and other pagan kings who were not conscious of God and how to access the spirit realm to God...","dt":"2022-09-16T07:46:19","s":["epwywlskw9"]},{"m":"Is King Nebuchadnezzar in heaven? Just thinking aloud.","dt":"2026-09-30T09:30:31.913Z","s":["hyu08nrzdl"]}],"4":[{"m":"The NIV says he was content.\n\nDaniel 4:4-5 NIV\n...contented and prosperous. I had a dream that made me afraid. As I was lying in bed, the images and visions that passed through my mind terrified me.\n\nHe did not have need for anything else and was happy with his life.\nBut little did he know there was a void that only God Most High could fill.","dt":"2024-12-05T07:22:09","s":["3kvbw2qdf2"]}],"8":[{"m":"Why was Daniel the last to be called?\n\nAnd this was not the first time; maybe he was not around at this time.\n\nOr because he was detested for his righteous ways and jealoused over for his many promotions, others tried to get ahead of him.\n\nWhen finally he was needed because all else had failed, then he was called.\n\nAfter which his judgement, which was so impeccable, often led to his promotion.","dt":"2024-12-05T07:27:45","s":["xvb3odu696"]},{"m":"How was Nebuchadnezzar's understanding of who GOD Almighty was? Did he think of HIM as one of the gods, but with superior rank, higher than his own god? Remember, he referred to him as the high GOD in verse 2, and rightly so.\n\nSo GOD was the high one among the gods. Indeed, GOD refers to himself as the Most High GOD, thus acknowledging lower gods.\n\nBut as Christians we know deeper, that there is no god but our GOD and no lord but our LORD — he has no equals. Let's go on.","dt":"2026-09-30T11:00:33.593Z","s":["0uvuya1vqt"]}],"17":[{"m":"In which ways does God rule in the earth, and what is Satan doing here?\n\nWhat laws does Satan function with to give him such power?","dt":"2022-09-18T14:00:14","s":["fclleoe48z"]}],"19":[{"m":"Probably within these times he received the interpretation. An hour ⏳","dt":"2022-09-18T14:31:27","s":["n3ka39o9dx"]}],"26":[{"m":"No wonder he did not believe nor implement the suggestion of Daniel.\n\nThe dream and its interpretation were too fantastic.","dt":"2022-09-18T14:33:41","s":["ik63koy5mc"]}],"27":[{"m":"Despite being forewarned, he did not heed; that is the nature of man, we are so stubborn.\n\nSometimes we can't even help our very own selves and are often led astray by our own desires.\n\nThis was the same by whom his dream of the image was interpreted and by whom the 3 Hebrew boys were delivered from the burning fiery furnace, so he knew God would do what he said he would do, yet Nebu would not heed.","dt":"2024-12-05T07:46:23","s":["dh4h2i7v7g"]}],"33":[{"m":"Hm... Imagine seeing this in the forest.\nA man, yet a beast.\n\nWonders shall never end, and I suspect such decrees and strange events continue to happen up to even this moment of time.","dt":"2022-09-18T14:35:27","s":["zklr7w3cny"]}],"37":[{"m":"Whoever thought that the king 👑 of kings among men would be so humble and come to this point?","dt":"2022-09-18T14:42:51","s":["zcxz7wev1p"]},{"m":"See how God screamed 😱 😡 and raved at Israel 🇮🇱.\n\nYet in captivity he shows favour to them and even gets their captor Nebuchadnezzar into Jehovah worship 🛐.\n\nGod is good and truly loves us as his children 🧒","dt":"2022-09-18T20:52:45","s":["cl6a11euit"]}],"2":[{"m":"These sound like the words of a man who has been humbled and forced to bow the knee and acknowledge a superior power, the power of the Most High GOD.","dt":"2026-09-30T09:25:55.689Z","s":["5dzgmzbqxt"]}],"6":[{"m":"These people and kings were deeply spiritual; indeed, the supernatural was part of the offices and structure of his government, deeply embedded in it.","dt":"2026-09-30T10:35:14.048Z","s":["ctvnn73q72"]}],"9":[{"m":"The holy gods? How many did he think Daniel's GOD was?","dt":"2026-09-30T11:01:51.759Z","s":["0h0mpmimob"]}],"14":[{"m":"The watchers... Who carved out such a story, the imagery and the narrative? Who thought it out?\n\nI can imagine they had counsel, called the heavenly scribes and the artists and communication experts of heaven, to see how best they can communicate and get through to Nebuchadnezzar.","dt":"2022-09-18T13:37:06","s":["jrf7rspt8p"]}],"18":[{"m":"These were polytheists, so why do they call Daniel's God holy?\n\nMaybe because He detested vain practices and idolatry and debauchery and sexual immorality... A practice which other gods relished in.\n\nSo seeing these attributes, they realized that these gods were pleased 😌 with holy living.\n\nThat is how to stir their power and activate their goodness on you.","dt":"2024-12-06T14:20:30","s":["8l63ouxmfw"]}],"30":[{"m":"I suspect he might have been at the top of his palace viewing the expanse of his kingdom and might; I am inferring this from the way he is describing his kingdom.\n\nOr maybe he looked at his own grandeur of a house he had built in Babylon and began praising his own self.\n\nIt is well.","dt":"2026-09-30T11:10:55.624Z","s":["m44ojch90d"]}],"32":[{"m":"Who are the “they”?","dt":"2026-09-30T11:11:21.274Z","s":["rvmgwn1dpk"]}]},"5":{"5":[{"m":"Did the hand wield a pen 🖋 and ink? Just wondering how it was done, and this writing was done strategically at an angle for the king 👑 to see.","dt":"2022-09-19T07:16:12","s":["ka90cuhso9"]},{"m":"I thought GOD did not care about these vessels and had abandoned even the temple and its precious stones to make a statement that morality supersedes external acts of devotion... but apparently he did very much care about them, but in order of preference.","dt":"2026-10-02T11:37:56.361Z","s":["pgaa6h245t"]}],"6":[{"m":"The watchers constantly have their eyes 👀 on what is happening in the earth 🌎.\n\nNothing escapes their watch... I believe they work with reporters 🗺 who give them constant updates...\n\nThey knew what was happening and had plans of their own.","dt":"2022-09-19T07:11:47","s":["z10oae9gk5"]}],"8":[{"m":"Is it not interesting that the solving of mysteries is what brought promotion every single time?\n\nIt was almost like a set up. That which looks like a challenge, a difficulty, was the setup for Daniel and his friends' upliftment.","dt":"2022-09-19T09:10:50","s":["h4ouzpojlp"]}],"11":[{"m":"Oh Daniel... His track record was unbeatable.\n\nTHY father made master of the magicians 🧝‍♂️... Does that mean he had been demoted, probably because of politics and a new 👑?","dt":"2022-09-19T09:12:20","s":["ifvgbjsdhy"]},{"m":"He was in the midst of magic 🧝‍♂️, sorcery and enchantment 🧙‍♀️, yet he wasn't hurt.\n\nHe dominated them and was their master. This was this Daniel of old; how much more we of the new covenant?","dt":"2022-09-19T09:23:06","s":["bpxn7qxb6s"]},{"m":"It seems apparently that at this time, Daniel had likely been demoted by this time.\n\nBut his gift was making room for him.","dt":"2024-12-06T14:24:48","s":["7vaqtwm8c3"]},{"m":"He was made master of the magicians etc., but now it had been taken from him. A new king had come, and likely he had brought in his own people. But Daniel's gift could not be hidden. He had to be called upon because of his gift.","dt":"2025-09-13T12:53:49","s":["bdcxsfalh9"]}],"13":[{"m":"It is worth noting that Daniel maintained his name, even though a whole king Nebuchadnezzar changed it.\n\nEven here in this passage he is called Daniel by Belshazzar instead of Belteshazzar.","dt":"2022-09-19T10:40:50","s":["e95sp4z2af"]},{"m":"He was being called Daniel, never Belteshazzar; he somehow kept his name.","dt":"2026-10-02T12:39:47.826Z","s":["jise063ujy"]}],"14":[{"m":"When foolish children inherit the throne... He hadn't even heard of Daniel nor knew him.\n\nA man of such wisdom and calibre was not known nor among the courtiers of the king 👑.\n\nObviously, looking at his revelries, he had no acquaintance with the wise in heart ♥.\n\nHow can you miss Daniel... Only a fool would.","dt":"2022-09-20T06:22:15","s":["qm6qoxn388"]}],"27":[{"m":"God is interesting: the hand appears and writes not tenses or sentences or phrases, but, like spiritual things often are, it came in patterns with gaps, thus requiring the spirit of wisdom to interpret.\n\nSo the writing goes like\n\nNumbered... numbered\n\nWeighed\n\nDivided\n\nEven if the writing could be read, it will still require interpretation, but here is where it was in a strange dialect, and that was the first barrier needed interpreting, then the meaning of the words as it relates to the kingdom.","dt":"2024-12-06T15:00:31","s":["zspeq25fng"]}],"7":[{"m":"I can just imagine the scene.\n\nThe gods have spoken in writing, and there was no one who understood what it meant.\n\nHence this warning or message would not be understood to be heeded.\n\nThe king knew it was no light message, for the gods did not send a man but came in themselves and wrote... It must indeed be that important for God himself to write it.\n\nThis is frightening... Their end had come, maybe, for the gods to have chosen this manner of communication.","dt":"2024-12-06T14:00:58","s":["nyqyux9mg4"]}],"15":[{"m":"How could such a man with such wisdom not be part of the king's counsel? Obviously some mischievous elements had successfully dropped him from the reins of power, much to the hurt of the kingdom.","dt":"2026-10-02T12:41:34.973Z","s":["llmt25h8cu"]}],"17":[{"m":"What good was such a reward to a kingdom about to be ousted? Indeed, he risked being beheaded or killed when the new rulers took the helm of power.","dt":"2026-10-02T12:42:48.123Z","s":["jrve2lkmx5"]}],"21":[{"m":"This chapter in chronological order should come in chapters 7 to 8 thereabout, but because its content connects with chapter 4, it seems the writers, in keeping with the story line, put this chapter after chapter 4.\n\nThis is seen because Belshazzar was grandson of Nebuchadnezzar — according to Dake's and pagan history (will have to cross check that).","dt":"2024-12-06T14:46:21","s":["kvaxgni63h"]}],"23":[{"m":"The last straw that broke the camel's back seems to be this insolent act against the very GOD who humbled his father and made him a beast.\n\nThe least he could have done was to show some respect to such a GOD, whiles keeping his own gods of iron and bronze, yet he looted the house of GOD without fear.\n\nMaybe, and yes, indeed God's time for his kingdom was up, to be deposed, but HE wanted to take full advantage to send a message to the sons of men. Who knows, maybe GOD would have pardoned him from death if he had some regard for him.","dt":"2026-10-02T12:50:53.094Z","s":["bq1md3vn6o"]}]},"6":{"5":[{"m":"This should be the testimony of the sons of the bond women for all true believers and serious Christians.","dt":"2022-09-20T06:27:58","s":["dp3ftnjsla"]}],"9":[{"m":"Wait oo... How did they know that Daniel would not exchange his prayers for anything, even death ☠?\n\nHow could they trust Daniel to play his part to his own death ☠?","dt":"2022-09-20T09:03:49","s":["cplsexnehh"]}],"10":[{"m":"Such disregard... I love that...\n\nHe did it with attitude. He was like... “Bring it on, devil 👿.”","dt":"2022-09-20T06:31:58","s":["mg8q2f76nt"]},{"m":"They trusted in his consistency for their plan to work, and it did.\n\nThis was how disciplined Daniel was.","dt":"2024-12-06T15:09:53","s":["2x34slx78m"]},{"m":"I can imagine the hatred and anger towards him each time he opened that window of his and prayed.","dt":"2024-12-06T15:10:45","s":["0bzac8czda"]},{"m":"Daniel was a very regimented man and lived a very regimented life.\n\nPraying three times a day.\n\nWhat other parts of his life were non-negotiables and regimented?\n\nThis is wisdom into some of the possible reasons for his excellent results and unrivaled dedication to his work.","dt":"2026-10-03T10:11:10.537Z","s":["gw2a8ihfgp"]}],"12":[{"m":"Politics smh 🤦‍♂️... Even as a king he had been cornered, and he knew it, but could do them no evil 😈 without destroying his own kingdom and authority.\n\nBut could not Daniel have stayed 30 days without prayer?? 🤦‍♂️.\n\nIt is equivalent to death ☠. Unless you are spiritual, you would not understand. And thus no wonder he was ready to die 🎲","dt":"2022-09-20T07:05:23","s":["ouge6htb6x"]}],"16":[{"m":"He knew how much of a loss to his kingdom Daniel was going to be if he died.\n\nThere was going to be irreplaceable responsibility on his head in trying to replace Daniel, because there was none like him.\n\nIn Daniel the king had peace and did not need to bother his head about his realm. Now he was going to lose all that to these politicians.\n\nThey were so heartless and selfish, to the point that though they knew it would cost the kingdom, they did not care.\n\nThey just wanted Daniel out.","dt":"2022-09-20T07:08:24","s":["9nfhly190p"]},{"m":"This was his own way of saying... My hands are clean, Daniel, I have no hand in this... This was not my intention.","dt":"2026-10-03T10:13:42.124Z","s":["rq78aatcqi"]},{"m":"Daniel 6:16 NLT\nThe king said to him, “May your GOD, whom you serve so faithfully, rescue you.”\n\nAnd he did. He knew how faithfully Daniel served GOD, and that was the source of his loyalty to the throne... It was loyalty to GOD, and the king knew the fear of GOD is what accounted for Daniel's exceptional contribution to his kingdom.","dt":"2026-10-03T10:17:13.005Z","s":["deta39buom"]}],"19":[{"m":"Even this action by the king 👑 was of faith, or at least hope, and hope does not disappoint.","dt":"2022-09-20T07:09:53","s":["zi0hcdtbg3"]}],"20":[{"m":"Aw... 😢 😢... A king in lament; he had a heart, and power had not corrupted him.","dt":"2022-09-20T07:10:47","s":["wkij66jgbi"]}],"21":[{"m":"GLORYYYYYY, I can imagine the sigh of relief 😌 that ran down his spine.\n\nAgain, in trials and difficulties, when we stand for God, he uses it to redeem us.\n\nBecause God seeks opportunity for the righteous to shine like the stars ✨ forevermore.\n\nAnd what other way was God going to rid such people from the kingdom justifiably and legally, except through something equally dramatic?","dt":"2022-09-20T07:13:53","s":["qqdxdo8czh"]},{"m":"Oh, what a voice of relief to this weary soul of the king... I can only imagine the tears of the king as he lamented, and as his lament turned to tears of joy at the sound of Daniel.\n\nHe had gone through much suffering, not only because of his lack of sleep and the pain of losing his trusted leader, but also the pain of trying to keep everything under control as a king, and keeping his frame in one piece.\n\nThe king could not be seen to be weak. These courtiers had really gotten the king.","dt":"2024-12-06T15:16:28","s":["zgmxoo32rp"]}],"23":[{"m":"Oh yes, indeed, exceeding gladness.","dt":"2022-09-20T07:15:30","s":["7emsn102a7","qexztceagj"]}],"24":[{"m":"Why involve their wives and children 🧒...\nI guess it was to prevent some form of revenge in the future 🔮","dt":"2022-09-20T07:16:37","s":["ohrn98mbzm"]}],"28":[{"m":"For such a sacrifice Daniel prospered. He was rewarded mightily.\n\nIt was such tests that Saul failed but David passed.","dt":"2022-09-20T07:17:51","s":["0g26qkuqph"]}],"7":[{"m":"Where did such a decree come from? What would make a king accept such a decree concerning himself?\n\nHe was to be exalted above everything, and even GOD.\n\nI'm sure the same excuse was to cement his absolute power, fish out anyone rebellious enough to raise his god over the authority of the king.\n\nAnyone who does that carries rebellion in him and must be ousted out of the king👑dom.\n\nIt all made sense to the king, and he approved purely out of politics, not self-exaltation.\n\nThe things that happen in the corridors of power and the agenda accompanying them.","dt":"2026-10-03T09:43:54.653Z","s":["rowkzpx6t1"]}],"8":[{"m":"I'm sure they came up with some preposterous reason, like it would establish his throne, it will make him feared 😱.\nI realize that it is in times of trial and setups that God uses to promote us, if we stand in faith for him no matter what.\n\nEven as I type this, I find myself guilty of not standing for the Lord always.\n\nIt's been my undoing many times, I believe.","dt":"2022-09-20T06:30:59","s":["8s80smxcpj"]}],"26":[{"m":"Twice Daniel had made the entire men in the entire realm tremble and acknowledge GOD as the one true GOD whose kingdom is forever.\n\nAnd this statement coming from a king is itself a statement.\n\nEvery knee shall bow.","dt":"2026-10-03T10:45:15.863Z","s":["dv8yyepjnn"]}]},"7":{"9":[{"m":"Unless I am mistaken, but this description of God is a bit different from the one Ezekiel saw, where he was brazen in appearance, or maybe the two passages are complementary, i.e.\n\nEzekiel describes his body and Daniel his clothing and hair.","dt":"2024-12-07T10:30:00","s":["spsbz1w2be"]}],"18":[{"m":"Amen... Even forever and ever.","dt":"2022-09-20T08:40:58","s":["kopbke5bea"]}],"22":[{"m":"So the kingdom that the saints possessed was\n\n1. On this earth\n2. It was contended for by another and they overcame him\n3. It is God's kingdom\n4. GOD's kingdom is in the earth 🌎, not just the heavens, and it is a physical kingdom, not just a spiritual","dt":"2026-10-03T19:15:55.578Z","s":["nmhi3ijqyc"]}]},"8":{"16":[{"m":"So it is one thing to see a vision and another to understand it.","dt":"2022-09-21T07:45:18","s":["pkfcmxjulu"]}],"1":[{"m":"Whiles Belshazzar was about his business and engaging astrologers and magicians to run his empire, sidelining Daniel, Daniel was seeing visions of the end, and his gift was shining brighter than ever.","dt":"2026-10-03T19:56:56.915Z","s":["g3sza4sqh2"]}],"2":[{"m":"This man of God, so empowered with visions and gifts from God.\n\nIt is almost difficult to imagine him as a politician, and he was.\n\nA great and high-ranking government official, yet so anointed and spiritual.\n\nDo we have such people today in the corridors of power?","dt":"2024-12-11T07:37:20","s":["twp7nrg98r"]}],"27":[{"m":"So even in the days of Belshazzar, Daniel was active in the corridors of power, meaning the fact that he was called later to interpret the writing on the wall did not necessarily mean he had been sidelined.\n\nMaybe he just wasn't present at the time.\n\nSo my earlier assertion that he may not have been involved in the king's business is not a guaranteed statement, or not true.","dt":"2026-10-05T09:54:25.356Z","s":["2m48z2u3q8"]}]},"9":{"9":[{"m":"Hmm... Such depth of prayer... Acceptance of faults and exaltation of God's divinity.","dt":"2022-09-21T09:07:20","s":["t4cmh64iwi"]}],"18":[{"m":"As Daniel prayed these prayers, God was raising the Ezras and the Nehemiahs in response to Daniel's prayers.","dt":"2024-12-14T08:25:21","s":["bxzhgypgy0"]}],"21":[{"m":"He was not a man, though he looked like one.","dt":"2024-12-14T08:26:53","s":["li23k3d0rh"]}],"25":[{"m":"I was wondering why Gabriel came to reveal events or the future when Daniel's prayer was for the liberation of his people Israel, since the 70 years of their captivity was up.\n\nBut this revelation of the end is apt, as it talks of the fact that a command will be given to rebuild Jerusalem, which is what Daniel prayed about.\n\nBut not only did the angel bring this information, but also gave Daniel further information as to what will happen after.\n\nUntil the Messiah comes — the Messiah — the one king 👑 who would ensure Israel doesn't go into captivity ever again.","dt":"2024-12-21T09:29:31","s":["1pm0hdjkhs"]}]},"10":{"4":[{"m":"Daniel at this stage was very old, yet was very much used of God — likely 80's to 90's.","dt":"2024-12-15T06:19:34","s":["incqjp0a4x"]}]},"12":{"10":[{"m":"That is interesting: same events, same information ℹ, yet some shall understand and others won't.\n\nAnd it is in that same spirit that I believe the events of the end time would be happening as predicted 🔮 in the Bible, and yet some shall recognize it and repent unto eternal life.\n\nWhiles others, though they see it and even read it, will rubbish it to their own damnation.","dt":"2022-09-21T11:00:51","s":["j4q41g9ivi"]}],"13":[{"m":"So all events of the world from Daniel's time ⌚ have already been predestined... 😢.\n\nIndeed, all events from the beginning of time are pre-determined.\n\nIt is already known. There is nothing new.\n\nSo the wise will hear and increase learning and know what to do. And shall choose the good part. Amen","dt":"2022-09-21T10:59:04","s":["810amk1q1k"]}]}},"Ezra":{"2":{"62":[{"m":"Wisdom right there. Here they have records of every family 👪 and genealogy.\n\nThus they kept their ranks, and this prevented them from being exterminated.\n\nSuch wisdom in record keeping.","dt":"2022-09-23T05:28:44","s":["hdnov6ssyc"]}],"4":[{"m":"Israel has had to do this many times throughout its history, being driven out of their homeland in droves, only to return a handful and a remnant at a time, until they finally regroup, then it happens again and again.\n\nIt happened with the Assyrian invasion, then Babylon, then fast forward to AD 70, to 1948, and at the end of time the pattern repeats, but this time they are restored forever.","dt":"2026-10-09T08:20:40.943Z","s":["mo0wqj06gn"]}],"26":[{"m":"So everyone relocated back to where they were born, back to family estates.","dt":"2026-10-09T08:30:09.698Z","s":["591yoksn0l"]}]},"3":{"2":[{"m":"So they began to build not just physical systems but also the spiritual.\n\nCreating the needed atmosphere by sacrifices.","dt":"2022-09-23T05:31:08","s":["x2fmxg5ccd"]}],"8":[{"m":"They were starting the building of a nation afresh.\n\nAnd today we read of the nation of Israel 🇮🇱, a strong nation and dominating the world.","dt":"2022-09-23T05:34:36","s":["l6znj44ew1"]}],"13":[{"m":"Be thou encouraged, though your beginning be small, your latter end shall greatly increase, and the glory of the latter shall greatly exceed the former.","dt":"2022-09-23T05:36:52","s":["9yt6mqzrmu"]}],"3":[{"m":"Morning and evening 🌃 at specific times without fail.\n\nA spiritual cycle, and it was kept sure, and as long as that was so, was their protection and benefits spiritually.\n\nWisdom for us.","dt":"2022-09-23T05:32:48","s":["t8ohu069rq"]}],"4":[{"m":"I can imagine the sobering feeling, many of them old and now returnees to their own country.\n\nThey remembered when they were kids and how they used to come to the house 🏡 of the Lord.\n\nAnd now here they were, old men, few in number and remnants from the war that destroyed their nation.\n\nAnd now here they were, witnesses of the faithfulness of God, who promised to bring them back after 70 years.\n\nThey were back, not to their former glory, but back anyways.\n\nVery sobering.","dt":"2024-12-23T07:45:21","s":["9m3vctnvz8"]}]},"4":{"10":[{"m":"It is in the keeping of records and journals that we have these stories that we now read — beautiful 👌","dt":"2022-09-23T05:50:33","s":["ekte9pnmgq"]}],"3":[{"m":"The Israelites did not tolerate any mixture or pollution of their stock or worship 🛐.\n\nHow come we in Christ do tolerate all manner of inconsistencies?\n\nThe fact that God continues to work with our excesses does not normalize or make them acceptable.\n\nThere is the perfect or ideal that God expects us to work towards.\n\nIsrael was in excess for centuries, yet God worked and loved them, but that never, no matter how long, made it right.\n\nSo also with us. The church ⛪ is filled with such corruption and wickedness.\n\nWe should accept that we have fallen and work towards it, rather than to form new doctrines out of them.","dt":"2022-09-23T05:45:57","s":["xjvqc2xh2z"]}],"24":[{"m":"The children of Israel had been so reduced to nothing.\n\nBecause of their idolatry and immorality.\n\nNo wonder the Lord said that the strange woman will reduce one to a piece of bread, and even an entire nation has fallen prey to this saying because of their immorality towards God.","dt":"2024-12-23T07:55:13","s":["3kpxamiumv"]}]},"5":{"11":[{"m":"Even David and Solomon's name had been erased out of the mind of the heathen, who once feared them mightily.\n\nWe have to be humble because all of us, our time will pass.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:01:13","s":["5ksnxwc0m3"]}],"14":[{"m":"What if this was never recorded? Then would there be no evidence of such a decree?\n\nRecords are very important.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:03:03","s":["csk5ynohyh"]}]},"6":{"10":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. Politicians are smart guys. He knew the spiritual benefits of such a work for the Lord.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:19:27","s":["a9wgutgd6q"]}],"14":[{"m":"I won't be surprised that these prophets prophesied the king's decree will be favorable towards them.","dt":"2024-12-23T08:00:08","s":["4zlqutsezk"]}],"22":[{"m":"Amen... Beautifully done.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:22:05","s":["on5lzidxwq"]}]},"9":{"5":[{"m":"Not again... When one is filled with wisdom, some things are so obvious, and you can easily see a pattern, and the consequences of actions and inactions are so obvious.\n\nThis was what Ezra saw and broke 💔 down.","dt":"2022-10-03T06:29:23","s":["grxaqsgjcb"]}],"9":[{"m":"By reading history and the prophets, it was easy to see God was literally fulfilling his promise and would make one place himself in destiny.\n\nAny student of prophecy becomes almost God-like, for you seem to know and understand what happens and what will yet happen.\n\nYou are able to properly place yourself in time ⌚, know the past and the future 🔮.\n\nProphecy is a very powerful tool. Lord, make me a student of prophecy, and even show unto me what is yet to come.","dt":"2022-10-03T06:33:10","s":["6qrou51gne"]}]},"10":{"17":[{"m":"How come these people, born under the law, knew what to do at all times? Because they had the commands.\n\nBut in these our times the collective mind for his people seems lost,\n\neveryone is doing as seems fit to them, and at an individual level very few know what the will of God is for them.","dt":"2022-10-03T06:38:18","s":["vv2h65ricu"]}],"7":[{"m":"They, by their carelessness and negligence of the word of the Lord, had mingled the holy seed with the profane and risked corrupting the nation of Israel from being God's special seed.","dt":"2024-12-29T21:59:47","s":["g89nxzas44"]}],"10":[{"m":"The kind of covenant Israel 🇮🇱 had with the Lord was such that he owned them and they could not annul it.\n\nThey were committed by covenant by their forefathers even before their birth and could not turn their backs on it, neither would they, considering all the benefits of the Lord.\n\nThough some sons of Belial attempted to in the wilderness and throughout the course of their history.","dt":"2024-12-29T22:03:34","s":["mz46ikze9y"]}]},"1":{"2":[{"m":"Strange, a pagan king supposedly, was now a believer. We are not told the circumstances that led to such strong belief in GOD so as to hear the word of the LORD and to do it.\n\nBut he did do it and fulfilled the law of GOD to him.","dt":"2026-10-08T11:10:10.964Z","s":["d013n9o3xt"]}],"6":[{"m":"They knew what it took and what was required to set up a system for God.\n\nRiches and honour as well as sacrifices.","dt":"2022-09-22T16:09:38","s":["fkw6as054y"]},{"m":"Riches is strength. So they strengthened their hands not with spears and swords but with riches. Money indeed is a defence, wisdom is a defence, and indeed is better than weapons of war.\n\nEcclesiastes 7:12 KJV\nFor wisdom is a defence, and money is a defence: but the excellency of knowledge is, that wisdom giveth life to them that have it.\n\nEcclesiastes 9:18 KJV\nWisdom is better than weapons of war: but one sinner destroyeth much good.","dt":"2026-10-08T11:14:42.545Z","s":["5vffy1qnxw"]}],"7":[{"m":"Wow, that was a long time ago, almost a century had passed, maybe say 70 years according to the prophecy of Jeremiah.\n\nAnd they kept very good records then, just as we do now, so nothing is lost or unaccounted for.","dt":"2024-12-23T07:33:57","s":["oz74ac3kr1"]}],"8":[{"m":"I am wondering where all these vessels of the house of the LORD are. There is a lot of treasure in secret places in the earth.\n\nAll the gold and silver and treasures and precious stones from time immemorial, where are they? Hidden, destroyed, stolen?\n\nGOD knows.","dt":"2026-10-08T11:16:19.882Z","s":["ww4h2u5v44"]}]}},"Esther":{"1":{"19":[{"m":"Unto another that is better than she... That statement is akin to\n\nActs 1:20 KJV\nFor it is written in the book of Psalms, Let his habitation be desolate, and let no man dwell therein: and his bishoprick let another take.\n\nAnd so the bishoprick of Vashti another took.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:29:29","s":["jbswy16six"]}],"22":[{"m":"Every man should bear rule in his own house 🏡.\n\nHow that simple things and actions have a resonance in eternity. A complex web some simple things evolve into.\n\nVashti's actions were going to set a precedence for life.\n\nA precedence which, if left unchecked, will ruin 🏚 house 🏡 holds and even the palace manners of the maidens and women.\n\nIt was a harsh decision, but it needed to be taken to save face 😔 and keep the royal 👑 disciplines intact.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:34:31","s":["8pxqbmmpqd"]},{"m":"The things that men would do to keep their honour and respect.","dt":"2024-12-26T19:16:54","s":["21btt3901t"]}]},"2":{"9":[{"m":"So he favoured her, grooming her to be the one to win this beauty contest.\n\nThe hand of God at work here.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:49:56","s":["3jbnthn1gr"]}],"14":[{"m":"Court manners and protocols. Funded by riches and power.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:54:02","s":["77lrdb0daa"]}],"15":[{"m":"Is this a case of “simplicity is the ultimate sophistication”? Or the chamberlain, knowing what the king loved and hated, gave Esther exactly that to make her win.\n\nNothing is fair in this life; it might have seemed fair in the eyes 👀 of the public, but in reality it was not.\n\nThings happened in the background, all the way from the throne room of heaven, to cause Esther to become queen 👑.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:56:47","s":["05zevchje5"]}],"22":[{"m":"Wisdom at work. Mordecai had worked in the palace and knew the game of thrones and the corridors of Power.\n\nHe knew not to release all secrets, for those secrets are your hidden weaponry.\n\nI'm sure the conspirators confided in Mordecai; little did they know his daughter was the queen 👑.\n\nSuch foolishness of the chamberlain.\n\nIndeed, Mordecai conducted himself so subtly that it was not public news that he saved the king 👑.\n\nEven the king had forgotten about him... However, it was put on record that he did.\n\nAnd all these came to light and played a key role 🗝 in his redemption and ultimate ascension 🇦🇨 to power.\n\nI can imagine how much feared Mordecai's name became.\n\nThe man who arose from a gatekeeper to prime minister, literally.\n\nA master at the game of thrones.\n\nOnly God knows the stories woven of this great achievement and prowess 💪.","dt":"2022-09-26T12:05:16","s":["bclo9t20qe"]}],"23":[{"m":"It was a wise decision of Esther to have the thing reported in Mordecai's name.\n\nA good play of politics, so in the future 🔮, who knows, it might lead to his promotion.\n\nFor Esther had learnt that those in the corridors of Power did not necessarily deserve it but were well favoured to get there.\n\nFavoured by God and man.","dt":"2022-09-26T12:07:16","s":["ycjpwam8e1"]}],"1":[{"m":"So indeed the king 👑 was repentant of his actions, but as king 👑 his orders could not be reversed.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:40:04","s":["22g1k42hom"]}],"2":[{"m":"The king was like a god. Everything revolved around him, including his mistakes and appetites.\nHe could not be wrong; even his mistakes were packaged to preserve the integrity of his office.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:43:29","s":["pxinmno0vk"]}],"12":[{"m":"Wow... After a year of preparation they will look more beautiful, and skin more toned, than any woman of the kingdom.","dt":"2022-09-26T11:51:47","s":["rttk0o8emf"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"Was this not what was sought for Daniel that led to his being thrown into the den of lions? 🦁","dt":"2022-09-26T12:08:12","s":["m0r1ts9jsx"]}],"3":[{"m":"Mordecai was a man of principle.\n\nHis comrades questioned him as to why he was willing to transgress the king's commandment.\n\nBut in truth he was not transgressing the king's commandment; he knew there was only one true king, and that was JEHOVAH, God of Israel.\n\nWhose commandment they had transgressed and were now in exile.\n\nHe was not going to make the mistakes his nation made, and was willing to rather die than transgress the king's command.\n\nIt is interesting that at the same time that Mordecai refused to bow to man-made gods, his brothers in Babylon also likewise refused, i.e. Shadrach, Meshach and co.\n\nAgain, he, like Daniel, was willing to transgress the king's command in keeping with the King of kings' command and his beliefs.","dt":"2024-12-28T08:44:16","s":["abwvvpcqp6"]}],"4":[{"m":"How a little spark can set a whole house ablaze.\n\nJust this reporting of the servants set the stage for a grand showdown.","dt":"2022-09-27T06:26:21","s":["no7mbikx5o"]}],"7":[{"m":"Hm 🤔. This Haman was deep in the occultic.\n\nFor them to cast lots for 12 whole months...\n\nIndeed, his threat to destroy the Jews was not a mere wish. He knew the weight 🏋️ of power needed for such an action, and he was ready to make the sacrifice.\n\nIn the earlier verse he thought it too little a matter to handle Mordecai... That shows how powerful he really was and what it took him by way of sacrifice to get to the realm of power.\n\nLittle wonder he was greatly feared 😱 and revered.\n\nBut the Jews, the Jew called Mordecai, feared no man nor god save Jehovah. Such faith in God, and God came through for him, but it took them down a rabbit 🐰 hole 🕳.\n\nWe need to exercise faith in God and his power if indeed we believe in him.","dt":"2022-09-27T06:36:23","s":["s8dk3r4s8r"]}],"10":[{"m":"I understand why later the king was so wrought with the conspiracy.\n\nThis act could have toppled his kingdom.\n\nIn that his wife was a Jew, and per the royal decree, which was irreversible, his wife would have to be killed, or could have been killed on his blind side, since they do not live together.\n\nThis would have been a very bad omen, because Esther was his second wife; then also other Jews like Mordecai, who had saved his life, would be killed as well.\n\nSo if even those who saved the king's life at a point are killed, then who is the king really loyal to? Who can please him?\n\nHe would have lost trust and loyalty from his trusted associates, because they knew his reckless laws could be their undoing at any point in time.\n\nIt was only a matter of time there would be a plot against him to topple him.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:17:30","s":["1odxjc402f"]}],"11":[{"m":"What a trust that the king has reposed in Haman, to give him such powers that an entire nation was at his whims to do what pleases him to them.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:28:28","s":["2bjfti9g5a"]}],"15":[{"m":"Whenever there is sorrow, pain and affliction... Bear 🐻 in mind that there are others drinking 🍻 and making merry.","dt":"2022-09-27T06:47:38","s":["gv2hferr7o"]},{"m":"There was Shushan the palace, or the palace of Shushan, and Shushan the city.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:20:32","s":["r4v14yynfl"]}],"8":[{"m":"The king was a busy man, and like all leaders with so much going for them yet so little time,\n\nthey rely on the words of close associates and confidants; that is their superstrength when the associate is a good one.\n\nBut a great disincentive and danger to the throne if not.\n\nSuch evil confidants to the king can cause much pain and hurts even in the realm of the king...\n\nAnd sadly the king may never know it.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:01:26","s":["mapywgzrdx"]}]},"4":{"1":[{"m":"Didn't Mordecai feel guilty for bringing such pain upon the people?\n\nHe could have killed himself for such atrocities upon an entire race 🏎.\n\nBut no, he was a firm believer in God; he gingered himself and took action.","dt":"2022-09-27T06:49:47","s":["hwlyb98kl7"]}],"8":[{"m":"Funny, but in the corridors of Power there can be so much insulation from the reality on the ground.\n\nQUEEN 👑 Esther was not even aware that her end was near.\n\nIt took Mordecai to update her. So it's important that in the corridors of Power, you stay in touch with the common people.","dt":"2022-09-27T06:54:54","s":["qejobn2ugz"]}],"14":[{"m":"For such a time as this, when it was you that brought this on all of us, some might have argued.\n\nBut Mordecai was no coward; he stood by his actions and God. And challenged Esther to do the needful.","dt":"2022-09-27T06:58:38","s":["kutn1h01sp"]},{"m":"But one could also blame Mordecai for bringing this upon the Jews — his insubordination was the cause of all this.\n\nThe counter argument would be that because of compromising to the heathen nations and their gods and way of life that the Jews were in captivity in the first place.\n\nWas he therefore to continue in the same manner the ways that brought them into exile?\n\nSo Mordecai was right, and though the consequences were dire, it was in obedience to the Lord.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:25:17","s":["x213wlna1c"]}],"16":[{"m":"Was it that dangerous? What a culture, that to approach the king, your own husband, was a life and death situation.\n\nIt took tact and wisdom, not with mere empty words or attempt to convince,\n\nno, you must not just use words, but you must fashion them in such a way that the king 👑 sees things for what it is.\n\nLest you may risk your head.","dt":"2022-09-27T07:01:17","s":["kctnpgamd5"]},{"m":"A national fast for 3 days and nights. It seems the 3 nights and days of fasting this way was a sure remedy in serious emergencies and astronomical proportions.\n\nI don't know if this is instructive, but we know all scripture is given for learning.\n\nThat is not to say we are to go on a three days dry for any emergency — this was a national crisis — a pending genocide and ethnic cleansing.\n\nIt needed to be done.\n\nSo for anyone using this scripture as a basis for such dry fastings, it is important to consider the context as well.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:33:19","s":["3yhn6co3w0"]}],"11":[{"m":"Without an appointment from the king, you risk your head.\n\nMaybe there had been prior assassination attempts.","dt":"2022-09-27T07:02:11","s":["ag65aoflor"]}]},"5":{"2":[{"m":"Many a time, the children of God enter into crises, and the expectation of God is that his people will come together and humble themselves before him and take advantage of the provision of his mercy.\n\nAnd in such moments of waiting on the Lord, the enemy might seem to be closing in, but the sure mercies of God are present to save.\n\nBut often in such impossible moments, we seek the help of men and systems.\n\nThat is OK if the help of men is not going contrary to the will and word of God. But in such desperate times, the wait on the Lord seems too daunting a task to embark on, so we rather choose the ways of the world.\n\nWays contrary to the ways of God, whiles the Lord waits in hope that we will come to him and obtain mercy.\n\nBut ever so often we fail to and lose both ways: we lose the mercies of God, and the ways of the world also don't save us.\n\nLord, help us and give us the wisdom to excel in all we do.","dt":"2024-12-28T09:40:01","s":["j9emzcbysu"]}],"13":[{"m":"How that we can let one thing steal our joy and every other thing.\n\nLet's be wary of envy and pride... It can lead to discontentment and wickedness.","dt":"2022-09-27T07:06:03","s":["knibp6mz7m"]}],"14":[{"m":"This is why sometimes when a man is caught in wickedness, his entire family 👪 is destroyed as well.\n\nBecause they were in bed, or might have even been the mastermind behind the act.","dt":"2022-09-27T07:07:28","s":["z60si4eqd5"]}]},"6":{"4":[{"m":"It's interesting that Haman could not even wait till morning to ask of this request.\n\nAnd as he hastened to destroy Mordecai, God also hastened to bring the salvation of the Jews.\n\nThe enemy is bent on destroying us, and the more resolved the enemy is, the more bent God is on delivering and blessing us.\n\nHaman came in just in time for the exaltation of Mordecai.","dt":"2024-12-29T06:15:04","s":["vjzb61aytz"]}],"9":[{"m":"Why would he suggest such a thing as honour? It was almost as if he was usurping the throne...","dt":"2022-09-27T08:33:52","s":["f8yxo8sx4t"]},{"m":"It is worth noting that in the king's response he did not include the crown part.","dt":"2024-12-29T06:18:15","s":["akzw0g4dbh"]}],"10":[{"m":"The king was very powerful and skilled in power management.\n\nThough Haman was his right hand man, it never diminished nor bred familiarity.\n\nHe, the king 👑, maintained a posture that he was not weakened in any way by close associates.\n\nSo he could command Haman and not bother about his feelings, nor could Haman interject.\n\nThe king maintained certain protocols that ensured that.\n\nNo wonder a chapter later he ordered for the head of Haman.","dt":"2022-09-28T06:05:45","s":["lpze6fz9q1"]}],"12":[{"m":"Nothing changed for Mordecai; he went back to his humble estate, for he recognized that this was not his level.\n\nHe had only been promoted temporarily; it was his permanent estate.\n\nLord, help us stay humble, we pray.","dt":"2022-09-27T08:30:47","s":["0k0iy99ok3"]}],"13":[{"m":"In the multitude of counselors there is safety, but not in this case, though they were right on their prediction and wisdom.","dt":"2022-09-28T06:08:01","s":["t2e7ent3iq"]}]},"7":{"1":[{"m":"Ah, the stage was perfectly set for the showdown by God.","dt":"2022-09-28T06:09:17","s":["1dcj82fmgr"]}],"6":[{"m":"This was no joke; no one jokes before the king, lest your head goes. So with this statement there was such a rush of information into the king's 👑 head 🤕.\n\nHis own right hand man 👨 dared to plot against the beautiful queen 👑. Then that would mean a 3rd queen 👑... What would that say about his kingdom and reign?\n\nWas that the plan all along? That was why he asked for the Jews to be exterminated, and invariably that would affect the queen and possibly topple the kingdom.\n\nThere was so much at stake with this simple decree.\n\nHe trusted Haman, and these were the possibilities of such an action; his right hand man had betrayed him.\n\nNo wonder he desired the royal robe and crown 👑 and other royalties.\n\nWas all this not a set-up for the insurrection that Haman was probably brewing?\n\nNo wonder the king had to go cool himself up in the next verse from such a rush of information.\n\nEsther might have been a very good wife for the king to be so concerned for her and her safety.","dt":"2022-09-28T06:20:01","s":["1mv872offd"]}],"7":[{"m":"Yeah, he needed to cool it off. Worst of it all was this: imagine on the D-day some insurrectionists come against the queen 👑 and the king got a wind of it.\n\nOnly to be told he can do nothing about it, because he had decreed it.\n\nIt was too late. He would lose his wife right before his eyes, and only God knew who else of value was going to be lost.\n\nThen he hears Mordecai had been hanged on gallows, the Mordecai who saved his life from assassination by the king's door keepers.\n\nWhat a foolish mistake. He could lose his kingdom entirely from infighting.","dt":"2022-09-28T06:29:53","s":["ije14mkeir"]},{"m":"I can imagine the scene: the king felt the set-up of Esther and knew in his heart how that because of Haman it had to take such disguise and shrewdness in order to reach out to him, the king.\n\nAnd she was justified in doing that, because one of his own trusted royals was playing games right under his nose — he was mad with anger at what was happening.","dt":"2024-12-29T06:25:49","s":["pya0q9t0qw"]}],"9":[{"m":"Ei, games and politics. How did he know about the gallows? Smh 🤦‍♂️.\n\nI like also the way he communicated it.\n\nHe knew the king had many matters on his head 🤕, so he said Mordecai who spoke good.\n\nThere was no way the king could have forgotten that. No need for ambiguity. The king was too busy and too much on his mind for such headaches of trying to figure out who.\n\nLord, give me wisdom to speak well, and especially in the corridors of power.","dt":"2022-09-28T06:34:25","s":["pull5eph0f"]}],"4":[{"m":"Oh, palace protocols. To just tell the king, her husband, her petition required such elaborate preparations. Months maybe.\n\nIt was not as simple as just walking up to him and speaking her mind.\n\nAnything goes wrong and it could be a life and death matter.\n\nThough the situation was urgent, she had to keep her cool and present her case in such a way as to paint the picture more clearly, as it deserves...\n\nSuch wisdom.","dt":"2022-09-27T13:24:28","s":["w4w7nrlei4"]}]},"8":{"4":[{"m":"I can imagine the tears of Esther, her pretty face marred by the agony of the loss of her people.\n\nAnd the king stretches for his scepter. It goes to show that though Esther was queen, in the grand scheme of things she had little power.\n\nEven her own husband, the king, barely saw her or knew who she was. Maybe because of ego, and to ensure her constant obedience, he kept her at a distance.\n\nBut now, after these things, I believe he would draw her closer to himself, as a husband should of his wife.","dt":"2024-12-29T06:38:13","s":["xe5mrdi2al"]}],"9":[{"m":"I can imagine the joy when the counter decree was issued, and especially when word got out that the new right hand man of the king was a Jew and the queen also apparently was a Jew.\n\nAnd the circumstance surrounding the sudden change in event could only point to the hand of God.\n\nAll these would put the fear of the Jews on the land and before their enemies.","dt":"2024-12-29T06:41:27","s":["1q38ljrb9o"]}],"17":[{"m":"Only God knows how much fasting Jews of all lands had undertaken.\n\nNow their liberation and deliverance had come.","dt":"2022-09-28T07:00:38","s":["wcaochgg7b"]}]},"9":{"31":[{"m":"At what point they almost died, the Lord came through valiantly for them.\n\nNo one stands with the Lord and falls. The Lord in turn stands for them even much more than they for him.","dt":"2024-12-29T06:48:35","s":["jfz5u2e2cy"]}]}},"Nehemiah":{"1":{"4":[{"m":"So this was how Nehemiah's calling began.\n\nMany people had heard and knew of the broken walls of Jerusalem but were not moved.\n\nHowever, it broke Nehemiah down. He knew he had to do something.\n\nDifferent things move us, and in a way it ties to our purpose.\n\nSometimes you wonder why others seem so apathetic to what is serious to you.\n\nThat is a sign that it resonates with you and you need to do something about it.\n\nPurpose is birthed there.","dt":"2022-10-03T06:49:42","s":["kuu2kpu66b"]}]},"2":{"1":[{"m":"He was the king's 👑 cup bearer; how a foreign slave could get to such a trusted position is amazing.\n\nIt obviously was attained because they saw the fear 😨🤯 not of man in Nehemiah, but rather the fear of God.\n\nSo the king could trust him with his very life.","dt":"2024-12-30T07:03:20","s":["otxin1maqu"]}],"5":[{"m":"Nehemiah, a Jew, was cup bearer to the king.\n\nI suspect Mordecai's influence was still being felt in the courts of Persia almost a century after his being in the courts of the king.\n\nAlso, Nehemiah was a good cup bearer and trustworthy, else he would not have had that position to start with.\n\nAnd on the basis of his good conduct, he was favoured and sent on his way to build the walls of Jerusalem.\n\nImagine he had not served well; there was no way the king 👑 would have favoured him.","dt":"2022-10-03T07:05:38","s":["7hzh3ahsfj"]},{"m":"I wrote two years ago a wonderful thought about Nehemiah being in the courts of the king a century after Mordecai... I would have to fact check ✅ that.","dt":"2024-12-30T07:08:32","s":["lmewldfwa2"]}],"10":[{"m":"The game of politics and taking territories began.\n\nThings are the way they are because there are men who made it so, and there are men ensuring it thus remains.\n\nIndeed, it is in their interest to keep the status quo.\n\nSuch is life, and we must not be ignorant.","dt":"2022-10-03T07:08:38","s":["x5h27u918h"]}],"12":[{"m":"Nehemiah had been in the courts of power long enough to know wisdom and the game of politics.\n\nHe kept his agenda secret and took advantage of the night season to do reconnaissance.","dt":"2022-10-03T07:10:44","s":["ltyfiicb9o"]}],"20":[{"m":"Popular verse.\n\nJerusalem had always been inhabited by different people at different times.","dt":"2022-10-03T07:13:20","s":["155f0efr0p"]}]},"3":{"4":[{"m":"Such detailed records. And now, millennia pass and we have the records.\n\nAt the rising of the dead there will be many wonderful memories.","dt":"2022-10-04T10:55:20","s":["vk0ot2jnfr"]}],"32":[{"m":"They were of one heart ♥ and mind to do the work, and so they did.\n\nEach according to his strength 💪 🧠","dt":"2022-10-04T11:01:59","s":["wa4wfxbfqx"]}]},"4":{"11":[{"m":"To what end?\n\nSeeing they were all under captivity and subjects to the Persians.\n\nYet they still sought to destroy another nation who was rebuilding.\n\nIt is sheer envy.","dt":"2022-10-04T11:04:54","s":["sjppxlg40d"]}],"23":[{"m":"Wow... Day and night they labored, and God was faithful.","dt":"2022-10-04T11:07:13","s":["f0id7rv19u"]}]},"5":{"14":[{"m":"He was a faithful man 👨. Rare they are, and Africa badly needs Nehemiahs.","dt":"2022-10-04T11:09:27","s":["19iqjejqjl"]}],"19":[{"m":"Amen Nehemiah... I am with you on this one.","dt":"2022-10-04T11:10:36","s":["ssbfvyvq4z"]}],"16":[{"m":"He and his workers did not have any land, so they could focus on building the house of the Lord —\n\nelse they be divided in focus and strength 💪.\n\nIt was also a good example of leadership, so the people know that he was all in on this one.","dt":"2025-01-01T15:12:03","s":["69v9vu4x29"]}]},"13":{"12":[{"m":"Oh men...\n\nDespite having returned from painful exile and banishment, and a great revival under Zerubbabel and Ezra many years ago...\n\nAbout 90 years before Nehemiah's coming.\n\nYet they had drifted away, and the Levites were not getting their share of what was due them, so they had to go eke out a living for themselves.\n\nThis continued until Nehemiah came.\n\nYou would have expected that after such exile things would go smoothly, at least for a long while, but no, men are men, and without strong leadership we drift away from what is right.","dt":"2025-01-02T20:47:34","s":["zzy6369ynv"]}],"14":[{"m":"And indeed God remembered him, and today we read his story.\n\nThe whole world 🌍 knows his name and story.\n\nSongs have been sung concerning same.","dt":"2025-01-02T20:48:28","s":["p6r132ehmk"]}],"3":[{"m":"But this law was such a long time ago, centuries and possibly over a millennium, yet they kept it...\n\nSame as when they kept the law of tabernacles, when not even was it kept in the days of Joshua the son of Nun.\n\nThis was a fresh revival, and they kept the law and renewed the covenant.\n\nIt was external, and so long as a generation kept it, the Lord honoured them.\n\nSo also is the promise of God on our lives... It remains ever true as long as we align.","dt":"2025-01-02T20:43:00","s":["gqsm3ae6mz"]}]},"6":{"14":[{"m":"Interesting times for Nehemiah, and it's interesting the things that happen in the corridors of power...\n\nThere were prophets who could be hired to prophesy lies 🤥 and conspire against the progress of their own people.\n\nProbably because Tobiah and co had promised them positions and good things, or they already enjoyed those under the old administration, and now here comes Nehemiah, whom they had no benefits from.","dt":"2025-01-01T15:36:28","s":["rfz4ww3rwt"]}]}},"Malachi":{"1":{"14":[{"m":"God is good and God is love. He had to remind them that he is a real person. He must be honoured, he must be feared and be treated with respect.\n\nThis ties in with the word of the Lord that came to me when I woke up, saying:\n\nThe fear of man is a snare, but whoever trusts in the Lord is kept safe — Proverbs 29:25","dt":"2025-01-04T11:37:23","s":["irf5p5psrd"]}]},"2":{"16":[{"m":"Why did the Lord keep emphasising the need for them to take heed to not their body or soul but their spirit?\n\nAnd he emphasises how that the man and his wife are one, and then right after he cautions the men to take heed of their spirit.\n\nThis goes to show the oneness of spirit of a man and his wife.\n\nSo in order not to corrupt one's spirit, we ought to be careful about putting away and breaking covenant with our wife.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:43:04","s":["vxxe7bmawe"]}],"17":[{"m":"Again, so much like now. It seems good is evil and evil good. Even in the house of the LORD.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:43:38","s":["ac4c3wm1ww"]}],"7":[{"m":"Hmm, this indeed is a word for our priests today.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:38:34","s":["i6qhocbxtf"]}]},"3":{"1":[{"m":"Obvious reference to Jesus.","dt":"2021-12-03T11:37:21","s":["11vramv0a4"]}],"3":[{"m":"THIS book emphasises much on the priests and Levites — the men of God sent to the people.\n\nAnd here the coming of Christ would be to purge the temple and the priesthood.\n\nIt seems what is happening in our world today has happened before, in the sense that God predicts with ease what would happen in the future whiles speaking to men who live in time. He tells them of the events many millennia after their death.\n\nBut it benefits us who live now, as we see it unravel. Needless to say, these ancient men will resurrect to meet us and see what was prophesied happen.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:47:16","s":["07mkz2mkdt"]}],"5":[{"m":"When the priesthood is set in order, and righteousness exalted, then God shall be a swift witness against the workers of iniquity and magicians and sorcerers.\n\nThis goes to explain why many Christians are weak against magicians and sorcerers.\n\nOur righteous altar is not intact.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:50:08","s":["szdgrfrab3"]}],"17":[{"m":"Even if the wicked escape judgement in this life, they will not escape in the day they stand before God when he judges the whole world.\n\nSo also if the righteous receive not a just recompense of reward in this life, he will not miss his blessing in the times to come.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:55:56","s":["oa1ex9q1ol"]}]},"4":{"6":[{"m":"Is it not interesting that virtually every prophet had a word of the end times in his prophecies, even though God was dealing with specific issues in their time?\n\nYet today, we who are closer to the end than they barely talk of the coming of the Lord, that great and dreadful day of the LORD.","dt":"2025-01-04T11:58:13","s":["1egkigltko"]}]}},"Jude":{"1":{"11":[{"m":"The book of Jude has similarities to 2nd Peter, in talking of Balaam, Sodom and Gomorrha, angels etc.","dt":"2025-05-25T06:42:36","s":["f4vkud3h8v","x9oqg0uni5"]}],"24":[{"m":"In his second book Peter emphasises a lot on not falling, but on maintaining a consistent walk with the Lord.","dt":"2025-05-25T06:46:08","s":["lw52e11l1i"]}]}},"Zechariah":{"1":{"3":[{"m":"Words, that is what it takes to bring change, transformation and alignment to the hearts of people.\n\nImmediately his children returned from captivity, the Lord raised men with words — prophets — to align his children to his will.\n\nFor it is only in that alignment that heaven's blessings and backing are brought to bear 🐻 and to the fore.\n\nWords are everything.\n\nThe human man will not do right by himself. He needs words.","dt":"2022-09-23T09:50:01","s":["3mza7ps97h"]}],"7":[{"m":"So particular about dates.","dt":"2022-09-23T09:52:50","s":["15eanyey1k"]}],"11":[{"m":"Hmm 🤔 no more wars, no more strifes...\n\nThe appetite for bloodshed was gone. Aggression had subsided. The whole earth now at peace.","dt":"2022-09-23T09:58:12","s":["dyc3eeav1k"]}],"12":[{"m":"I can imagine that at this time, much prayer and supplication had come to the throne room unanswered.\n\nBecause the time was not yet due, but now the time was due, so the angel cries out, “How long?”\n\nThere are times and seasons.","dt":"2022-09-23T09:55:49","s":["po10j7trj9"]}],"21":[{"m":"So the horns were not just demonic forces, but it was the horns of the heathen that scattered Judah, and now another set of forces 💪,\n\nthe carpenters, have frayed the horns 📯, caused Cyrus to make a declaration and Darius to confirm it.","dt":"2022-09-23T10:02:20","s":["wrpzrnrkgv"]}]},"2":{"5":[{"m":"Glory hallelujah 🙌, the divine protection of the Lord.","dt":"2022-09-23T10:11:39","s":["4nbj4fhaif"]}],"8":[{"m":"Amen, such sweet blessed assurance.","dt":"2022-09-23T10:12:32","s":["szmk8yirzj"]}],"11":[{"m":"And it will happen, for yet we await the Lord dwelling in the midst of his people.","dt":"2022-09-23T10:14:51","s":["cpju25qejy"]}],"13":[{"m":"He is raised up out of his holy habitation to where?","dt":"2022-09-23T10:15:25","s":["b39pcf4v7k"]}]},"4":{"5":[{"m":"It sounds like the angel expected Zechariah to understand, meanwhile, looking at the interpretation, I doubt how it's related to the image.\n\nHmm, matters of the spirit.","dt":"2022-09-23T18:25:03","s":["hrxzm7lp8h"]}],"10":[{"m":"Wow, as these strong 💪 encouraging prophecies were being given, God was working in the background, stirring the heart of kings to favour the cause of Israel.\n\nOne would have also thought that, God having affirmed that Zerubbabel would finish the project, all would go smoothly.\n\nI can imagine when the work came to a halt and Zerubbabel remembered this prophecy. I'm sure he wondered if this was ever going to come true.","dt":"2022-09-23T18:22:53","s":["6ep527uex4"]},{"m":"I believe there should have been a comma at the end of the name Zerubbabel, rather than the word “with” inserted.\n\nThat way it paints the picture of the seven rejoicing when they see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel.\n\nThe rest of the verse then goes ahead to explain what these seven represent — in that sense, the semicolon is apt.","dt":"2025-06-03T09:52:03","s":["jr620a6g1y"]}]},"8":{"17":[{"m":"It is sin that kept God away from the people.","dt":"2022-09-24T06:24:48","s":["1gqm4w8853"]}],"23":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-09-24T06:25:37","s":["ca8536b3bb"]}]},"9":{"9":[{"m":"A messianic psalm... Fulfilled.","dt":"2022-09-24T08:39:45","s":["j1o7u7xiey"]}],"16":[{"m":"This is futuristic.\n\nI am now understanding the Bible... Wow, after all these years of studying it.","dt":"2022-09-24T08:41:22","s":["7oacx4jpvf"]}]},"11":{"12":[{"m":"Need more study as to how this ties in with Jesus's betrayal.","dt":"2022-09-24T09:32:23","s":["rp5yn34fqb"]}]},"12":{"3":[{"m":"Wow... If the Lord be for us, indeed who can be against us?","dt":"2022-09-24T10:17:01","s":["44wgvqvfwh"]}],"10":[{"m":"Indeed they shall mourn and wail 😩 when they realize how grave of a mistake they have made and how they have deferred their salvation for millennia.\n\nSuch needless pain and suffering.\n\nOh, if only they had known.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:20:17","s":["23202w8u1y"]}]},"13":{"8":[{"m":"I believe this has to do with the future of Israel 🇮🇱 in the last days.\n\nI can't believe how much distant into the future 🔮 are these prophecies.\n\nI mean, to prophesy so specifically of 1000s of years into the future. Wow.\n\nBut I guess to the dateless God, it is all still the same.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:24:55","s":["enq2lznpuf"]}],"3":[{"m":"This signifies the level of justice and ⚖ purity in the land in those days.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:22:39","s":["28yjomerc1"]}]},"14":{"5":[{"m":"Why is God talking and saying “the Lord my God”, as if talking of himself in the second person?","dt":"2022-09-24T10:26:28","s":["22971blq0o"]}],"8":[{"m":"No night there, is spoken of in Revelations.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:27:05","s":["jedv3hfzkq"]}],"9":[{"m":"One I am. It is interesting, the many different prophets and prophecies talking of the end of time.\n\nEach bringing on a unique perspective.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:28:08","s":["0k44h8wsfd"]}],"16":[{"m":"Glory to God. Both testaments record the same things.\n\nThis chronological Bible challenge has really been revealing.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:29:44","s":["7ao24q8bih"]}],"17":[{"m":"Kabayaa... Every knee shall bow and every tongue confess that Jesus is Lord.","dt":"2022-09-24T10:30:24","s":["tmjk3rxg89"]}],"21":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-09-24T10:30:59","s":["161d8d8ccd"]}]}},"Habakkuk":{"3":{"2":[{"m":"Wow, what beautiful words... In wrath remember mercy.","dt":"2022-08-19T11:51:56","s":["2hid281tqt"]}]},"2":{"20":[{"m":"Amen","dt":"2022-08-19T07:08:08","s":["cf7ce11ba9"]}]}},"Haggai":{"1":{"2":[{"m":"This now gives us an in-depth into the daily happenings of the temple 🏛 building.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:25:06","s":["h14g35e3f1"]}]},"2":{"5":[{"m":"Oh, this people were a broken people. After such great history, now here were their children, a shadow of their fathers' glory.\n\nBut God told them he understands how they felt, but they should not fear 😱.\n\nGOD was beginning something new, and it was with them.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:32:04","s":["rx2pci50q1"]}],"9":[{"m":"Amen, and this is yet to be fulfilled, but definitely will be.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:34:05","s":["i2z57rdaoh"]}],"19":[{"m":"God states a specific day of his blessings unto them for doing the work of the Lord.","dt":"2022-09-23T06:37:44","s":["q0gs5jna5u"]}],"23":[{"m":"When was this day to be... Is it some time in the future 🔮?","dt":"2022-09-23T06:38:50","s":["f9wvpl1jl8"]}]}},"Obadiah":{"1":{"16":[{"m":"The judgement of the Lord upon the heathen was in this manner:\n\nWhen one nation's cup was full, it was emptied unto the dregs by making them drink of the cup of their own wickedness, by them being destroyed through war and pestilence and captivity by other heathen nations whose cup was not yet full.\n\nWhen that conquering nation's cup of wickedness was also full, then another less wicked nation empties their cup down their own throat unto the dregs, by the Lord, and the cycle continues. But upon Mount Zion there shall be deliverance and holiness...\n\nThat is the foundation of eternal stability and life, and that is the lot of Israel and all they that love her.","dt":"2026-07-11T10:12:45","s":["ykniojnshc"]}]}}};
